{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition","id":114668,"title":"Ask a simple question, Awakened edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-17T05:36:36-07:00","id":114668,"title":"Ask a simple question, Awakened edition","content":"I reopen the thread : (Original author : <u>Archmage Joda</u>)<br /> <br /> To restart : <br /> <br /> Q1 : Camelot was created by Imperium Rite or Practice ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T07:07:20-07:00","id":114694,"title":"","content":"I'm admittedly bad at this, but... Neither? Camelot was created mundanely but with the guidance and help of Merlin who used its rise and fall to &quot;seal his last omen* &quot; or &quot;exalt his flimflam* &quot; and ascend past archmastery. Infuriated, The Ruin (exarch of fate) removed Camelot from the timeline making it so Camelot never happened. Due to the way these rewrites work, there are hints and leftovers that time missed and left in place.<br /> <br /> * I can never keep the technical terms involved with archmastery ascension straight. Hopefully my error will incite corrections for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Continuing to look for a nWoD group in Pennsylvania along 81 near Carlisle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","name":"lunavoco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T13:45:52-07:00","id":114924,"title":"","content":"I'm brand new to Mage : the Awakening, but I enjoyed the core book so much that I want to pick up a second. But... there are a lot of them. Any recommendations on what to get next?<br /> <br /> Also, are Chronicles where the PCs are Seers a thing, or are they just not done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T13:53:10-07:00","id":114926,"title":"","content":"Q2A) Buy them all. (MORE : buy all the White Wolf/Onyx Path books; from all gamelines)<br /> Q2B)If you want to play the Seers; &quot;The Seers of the Throne book&quot; of course (Personally I think it is better for a seer chronic to put the players in a place where Seers are not too dominant); That\u2019s fortunate since you are going to buy them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 04-17-2014, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T14:44:49-07:00","id":114947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=114924#post114924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm brand new to Mage : the Awakening, but I enjoyed the core book so much that I want to pick up a second. But... there are a lot of them. Any recommendations on what to get next?<br /> <br /> Also, are Chronicles where the PCs are Seers a thing, or are they just not done?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a new corebook coming out near this November. Might not want to buy the whole line yet until we see what is still compatible. I suspect that Intruders, Imperial Mysteries, Left Hand Path, and Seers of the Throne will remain useful, tho not totally compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T14:47:59-07:00","id":114950,"title":"","content":"C'mon; I doubt that many will become incompatible ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T16:07:40-07:00","id":115006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=114924#post114924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm brand new to Mage : the Awakening, but I enjoyed the core book so much that I want to pick up a second. But... there are a lot of them. Any recommendations on what to get next?<br /> <br /> Also, are Chronicles where the PCs are Seers a thing, or are they just not done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tome of the Mysteries is pretty much Core Book vol. 2. It's all but required. But as Octavo says, a new core book is coming out in November.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T05:56:59-07:00","id":115237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115006#post115006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tome of the Mysteries is pretty much Core Book vol. 2. It's all but required. But as Octavo says, a new core book is coming out in November.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Tome of the Mysteries doesn't do much in the way of providing story ideas, but it does offer additional explanations on the magic system, which for me was the hardest thing to understand about Mage.<br /> <br /> After that, I think Banishers and Astral Realms were the strongest books I've read so far. I'm pouring through Left-Hand Path right now and it looks to be just as good.<br /> <br /> Both Banishers and Left-Hand Path both expand on Mage's in-house antagonists in creative and insightful ways. The core book wasn't able to devote enough attention to antagonists because of page count. Both books were so good that by the end I wanted to play a character drawn from them.<br /> <br /> Astral Realms expands the Mage cosmology. I admit I originally wasn't impressed with it's theme and left it 'till last to read. Big Mistake! It is an A+ book of ideas that were new to me. It intorduced concepts that I hadn't considered and largely expanded the area mages can operate in. In the mage line, this is my second favorite book.<br /> <br /> Once you think you fully understand what magic is and how it works, pickup Imperial Mysteries. It will blow your mind. This is my single most favorite RPG Book ever. It takes everything you know about mage and expands it to a cosmic muilti-timeline spanning scale. The book includes things like spells with the ability to think and adapt after being cast, contagious spells, and spells that affect reality retroactively (meaning once the spell has been cast, then the entire world's timeline adapts to it. This effect has ALWAYS been inplace.) It's heady stuff and requires a good grasp on the system to get through, but it's worth it!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>New Question: </b>I was considering how various mutant powers can be be replicated in Mage. Most are fairly straightforward, but I ran into one that I couldn't elegantly fit in system: Phasing. Does anyone have any ideas on how you would structure a spell that allows you to walk through walls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Continuing to look for a nWoD group in Pennsylvania along 81 near Carlisle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","name":"lunavoco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T06:23:27-07:00","id":115249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lunavoco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115237#post115237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>New Question: </b>I was considering how various mutant powers can be be replicated in Mage. Most are fairly straightforward, but I ran into one that I couldn't elegantly fit in system: Phasing. Does anyone have any ideas on how you would structure a spell that allows you to walk through walls?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most phasing powers in World of Darkness simply shift you into twilight. So Death 4 Twilight Shift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T06:54:51-07:00","id":115257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115249#post115249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most phasing powers in World of Darkness simply shift you into twilight. So Death 4 Twilight Shift?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where I started too, but i didn't like the inclusion of going to twilight since Twilight has it's own set of things present. <br /> <br /> If Death can be used to grant yourself properties of vampiric undeath, can we do the same for ghostly undeath? Perhaps Death 4 Life 4 to grant insubstantiality like a non-manifest ghost? Or maybe a Space effect to affect collision on your person?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Continuing to look for a nWoD group in Pennsylvania along 81 near Carlisle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","name":"lunavoco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T07:14:11-07:00","id":115261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Death can be used to grant yourself properties of vampiric undeath, can we do the same for ghostly undeath? Perhaps Death 4 Life 4 to grant insubstantiality like a non-manifest ghost? </div> </div> </div>You only need Death 4 - Twilight Shift. Ghosts are insubstantial exactly because they are in Twilight. Twilight is not another world like the Shadow but a state of being, namely being ephemeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;...and then we discovered it wasn't the Robot King after all, it was the real one. Fortunately I was able to reattach the head.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/644-mcbaine","name":"McBaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T17:40:03-07:00","id":115616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115249#post115249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most phasing powers in World of Darkness simply shift you into twilight. So Death 4 Twilight Shift?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't want to go into Twilight, use Space. It lets you cause two objects to occupy the same space without interacting with one another, or with interacting with one another destructively as the mage chooses. That seems pretty close to what you're aiming for with phasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T19:14:46-07:00","id":115646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115616#post115616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you don't want to go into Twilight, use Space. It lets you cause two objects to occupy the same space without interacting with one another, or with interacting with one another destructively as the mage chooses. That seems pretty close to what you're aiming for with phasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That requires Space 5, and has to be cast on every object you want to pass through. By the time you have Space 5, you're better off just teleporting everywhere you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:41:13-07:00","id":115847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lunavoco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=114694#post114694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm admittedly bad at this, but... Neither? Camelot was created mundanely but with the guidance and help of Merlin who used its rise and fall to &quot;seal his last omen* &quot; or &quot;exalt his flimflam* &quot; and ascend past archmastery. Infuriated, The Ruin (exarch of fate) removed Camelot from the timeline making it so Camelot never happened. Due to the way these rewrites work, there are hints and leftovers that time missed and left in place.<br /> <br /> * I can never keep the technical terms involved with archmastery ascension straight. Hopefully my error will incite corrections for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the answer but I do not understand; finally Camelot was created thanks to the mundanely or by omens ? is he broke the Pax Arcanum or not ? this is the generaly result of this kind of omen ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T14:31:32-07:00","id":116683,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q : </b>A ghost-mage can have Numinas based on his Legacy ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 04-21-2014, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:19:50-07:00","id":117014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115847#post115847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the answer but I do not understand; finally Camelot was created thanks to the mundanely or by omens ? is he broke the Pax Arcanum or not ? this is the generaly result of this kind of omen ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Camelot was created mudanely, he did not break the pax arcanum. (if it advances you towards ascention, it can be argued that it doesn't break the pax, since the pax exists to help (or at least to not hinder) Mages' ascent in the first place).<br /> But I haven't gotten around to finishing Imperial Mysteries, so I might be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=116683#post116683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>New Q : </b>A ghost-mage can have Numinas based on his Legacy ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Considering ghost-mages can have &quot;Influence: Mind&quot; in place of Mind (and the same for other arcana), I really don't think there's a problem with Legacy Attainements becoming Influences/Numinae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T15:20:35-07:00","id":117195,"title":"","content":"I would generally not allow an Attainment to be a Numina, at least not as long as I was sticking to the party line of &quot;ghosts are not souls&quot;. Legacies are just too intrinsically linked to the soul. A ghost mage is not fully pulling power from the supernal realms, it just uses a handful of rotes and powers to make echoes of the supernal. <br /> <br /> Rules-wise this is close enough to magic, except on how paradox manifests. Yet this is an important thematic distinction, as the dead hurt those they want to protect most with paradox. Attainments would get around this theme by not inflicting paradox on the anchor. So, that is another reason (beyond the party line) that I'm not a big fan of the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2583-amikaligula","name":"amikaligula","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T09:52:05-07:00","id":117502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amikaligula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=117195#post117195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would generally not allow an Attainment to be a Numina, at least not as long as I was sticking to the party line of &quot;ghosts are not souls&quot;. Legacies are just too intrinsically linked to the soul. A ghost mage is not fully pulling power from the supernal realms, it just uses a handful of rotes and powers to make echoes of the supernal.<br /> <br /> Rules-wise this is close enough to magic, except on how paradox manifests. Yet this is an important thematic distinction, as the dead hurt those they want to protect most with paradox. Attainments would get around this theme by not inflicting paradox on the anchor. So, that is another reason (beyond the party line) that I'm not a big fan of the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be said that since ghosts are shells/echoes of the soul (sort of.. they were described like that a couple times), it's attainement numinae are likewise echoes of what the individual's soul used to be.<br /> <br /> Although thinking on it, it might be better to leave it more like what rotes become - they can use the power, but it's still more like the magic they knew than the soul they were, still causing paradox and whatnot. Mainly because in many cases, the attainements are things that could be accomplished with regular spells (though clearly not in all cases, like the Roses of Eden)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:12:59-07:00","id":118044,"title":"","content":"Another newby question, as I make my way through the books:<br /> <br /> Where exactly do <i>most</i> mages' top-level loyalties lie? Their cabal, their consilium, their order, their legacy (if applicable)? Somewhere else, or is it so individual that there is no standard? It seems like they are pulled in a lot of directions, with different splats making it seem like whatever they are covering takes precedence. For example, I'm reading Guardians of the Veil at the moment, and it strongly implies that Guardians consider their order tops. Conversely, when I was reading Legacies: the Sublime, tight-knit Legacies like the Sodality of Tor or the Daksha make it seem like their legacy is the most important to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:29:36-07:00","id":118051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=118044#post118044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another newby question, as I make my way through the books:<br /> <br /> Where exactly do <i>most</i> mages' top-level loyalties lie? Their cabal, their consilium, their order, their legacy (if applicable)? Somewhere else, <b>or is it so individual that there is no standard</b>? It seems like they are pulled in a lot of directions, with different splats making it seem like whatever they are covering takes precedence. For example, I'm reading Guardians of the Veil at the moment, and it strongly implies that Guardians consider their order tops. Conversely, when I was reading Legacies: the Sublime, tight-knit Legacies like the Sodality of Tor or the Daksha make it seem like their legacy is the most important to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's that.<br /> <br /> Most are attached to their order; but some can being more loyals to their friends,ect...<br /> Some Legacies are very organized with a ideological ideas; more invested than in their order. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T14:16:36-07:00","id":118108,"title":"","content":"<b>NEW Q</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond Ascension </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Ascension the highest state a mage can aspire<br /> to? Most believe so. A smaller number think that if<br /> ultimate enlightenment is possible at all, Ascension<br /> must be its prerequisite. Some religious mages place<br /> the highest realm within the doctrines of their faiths<br /> \u2014 in the afterlife perhaps, though Awakened culture<br /> is biased against believing anything a Sleeper religion<br /> has to say about the cosmos. The best evidence<br /> they have for a realm beyond the Supernal manifests<br /> in beings that speak of a highest Principle and radiate<br /> a power distinct from Supernal Mana.<br /> <b>Sometimes, though, mages encounter phenomena<br /> that point to enlightenment beyond the structure of<br /> Above and Below: holy men and women whose<br /> presence inspires extraordinary transformations and<br /> around whom destiny constructs portentous events.<br /> Despite the fact that these sages are surrounded by<br /> fraudsters and fanatics, they seem to be at peace<br /> with the Lie around them. Some mages envy them.<br /> Some despise their complacency</b>. </div> </div> </div>I don't really get this;what does that refer to ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T17:16:50-07:00","id":118165,"title":"","content":"Most possibly &quot;the principle/empyrean&quot; - check against some promethean <i>saturnine nights</i> and the imperial mysteries box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:41:37-07:00","id":118493,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I missed that there was a second page, so this is largely already answered above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115847#post115847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the answer but I do not understand; finally Camelot was created thanks to the mundanely or by omens ? is he broke the Pax Arcanum or not ? this is the generaly result of this kind of omen ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, assume the same caveats. I'm still grasping at the story myself. But...<br /> <br /> Merlin wanted to seal an omen about a perfect society, a utopia. This omen also included that such a place will fall from within. So he came to the physical where the work getting an Omen going is done. He met Arthur in the flesh, was there when everything started, and stayed (more or less) through to the end. He didn't create it with magic, he used magic like shown in the stories to help those around him create Camelot. Camelot was a real place on the physical world built on the foundation of men and their drives. Merlin was behind the scenes influencing and overseeing the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Merlin didn't wish Camelot into being, he worked very hard with mortals to build it day by day.<br /> <br /> I don't see anything here that breaks the Pax, but I don't have the pieces of the story AND I don't have a perfect grasp on the book Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Camelot itself, it's rise and fall, WAS the Omen. After camelot fell, Merlin was able to Seal the Omen. After it was sealed, he was able to Exalt it using Imperial Rites to permanantly entwine it with reality. Even though an Exarch tried to remove it, we still have stories, legends, and artifacts from Camelot because it was Exalted using an Imperium Rite.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Continuing to look for a nWoD group in Pennsylvania along 81 near Carlisle.","edited":{"userid":1050,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","user":"lunavoco","date":". 04-24-2014, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","name":"lunavoco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T15:27:43-07:00","id":118687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lunavoco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=118493#post118493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I missed that there was a second page, so this is largely already answered above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, assume the same caveats. I'm still grasping at the story myself. But...<br /> <br /> Merlin wanted to seal an omen about a perfect society, a utopia. This omen also included that such a place will fall from within. So he came to the physical where the work getting an Omen going is done. He met Arthur in the flesh, was there when everything started, and stayed (more or less) through to the end. He didn't create it with magic, he used magic like shown in the stories to help those around him create Camelot. Camelot was a real place on the physical world built on the foundation of men and their drives. Merlin was behind the scenes influencing and overseeing the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Merlin didn't wish Camelot into being, he worked very hard with mortals to build it day by day.<br /> <br /> I don't see anything here that breaks the Pax, but I don't have the pieces of the story AND I don't have a perfect grasp on the book Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Camelot itself, it's rise and fall, WAS the Omen. After camelot fell, Merlin was able to Seal the Omen. After it was sealed, he was able to Exalt it using Imperial Rites to permanantly entwine it with reality. Even though an Exarch tried to remove it, we still have stories, legends, and artifacts from Camelot because it was Exalted using an Imperium Rite.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks you too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T16:04:51-07:00","id":118718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=118108#post118108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>NEW Q</b><br /> I don't really get this;what does that refer to ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so imagine if an early first century priest encountered Jesus.<br /> <br /> And Jesus... didn't seem to fit into any other category of supernatural being, and they couldn't really figure out a satisfactory explanation for what he was.<br /> <br /> And Jesus seems to preach a message that posits happiness and fulfillment within the constraints of the Lie, and it seems to work.<br /> <br /> Or, any historical preacher or philosopher. Buddha, Confucius, any modern individuals one might encounter; they seem to have something genuine worked out that doesn't fit in the spiritual perspectives of mages.<br /> <br /> Like, none of these stand directly as proof of God or whichever else, but they make some mages wonder.<br /> <br /> The point is that, despite what mages know, the World of Darkness is big enough and complex enough and mysterious enough that not everything seems to follow their precepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T11:51:06-07:00","id":119201,"title":"","content":"This is a little granular but maybe you all can offer some insight or opinion. The Echo Walkers Legacy are fixated on observing the Angels of the Aether (the Ones Before) in order to emulate them. They customarily resort to a pretty dastardly spell which does potentially serious harm to it's victim. With the material in Summoners, we see that it is possible to summon such an angel. While it is very hard, it would take a depraved Echo Walker to reason that the savings in effort are worth the harm done to an innocent whose soul is dislodged. <br /> <br /> What reason would an Echo Walker have to use the old technique in a post-Summoners world?<br /> <br /> (I am not trying to pick it apart. I really want the legacy to work the way it is written, but I'd like the best rationale for it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2122-montuban","name":"Montuban","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:10:56-07:00","id":119434,"title":"","content":"It's not just about seeing angels, it's about viewing a prototypical form of humanity that they want to shape themselves in emulation of.<br /> <br /> Or rather, that prototypical form is the <i>type</i> of angel they want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T18:40:22-07:00","id":120653,"title":"","content":"I've noticed a few parallels in the game that seem to treat the Abyss as another Arcanum. For example, their is an Exarch of the Abyss (the Gate) and also an Aeon of the Abyss (the Other/Old Man/etc). Why is this? Does this mean that there could be Archmage Siddha of the Abyss?<br /> <br /> There's also a related parallel in Astral Realms. The citadel of the Other is called &quot;The Hollow, Citadel of the <i>Other</i> and the <i>Abyss</i>&quot;. This mimics the naming structure of the citadels of the other Aeons. For example, &quot;~The Fallen Tree of Arcadia, Citadel of <i>Gloriana Temporae </i>and <i>Medraut</i>&quot; is the citadel of the Aeons of Time (Gloriana Temporae) and Fate (Medraut). This is...confusing because it seems to indicate that there are <b>two</b> Aeons in the Hollow. Does this mean that the Abyss itself is the Aeon of the Abyss? Does the Other represent something else? Am I overthinking things tremdously when the writers just copied the structure of the previous citadels for symmetry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T19:35:08-07:00","id":120671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=120653#post120653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed a few parallels in the game that seem to treat the Abyss as another Arcanum. For example, their is an Exarch of the Abyss (the Gate) and also an Aeon of the Abyss (the Other/Old Man/etc). Why is this? Does this mean that there could be Archmage Siddha of the Abyss?<br /> <br /> There's also a related parallel in Astral Realms. The citadel of the Other is called &quot;The Hollow, Citadel of the <i>Other</i> and the <i>Abyss</i>&quot;. This mimics the naming structure of the citadels of the other Aeons. For example, &quot;~The Fallen Tree of Arcadia, Citadel of <i>Gloriana Temporae </i>and <i>Medraut</i>&quot; is the citadel of the Aeons of Time (Gloriana Temporae) and Fate (Medraut). This is...confusing because it seems to indicate that there are <b>two</b> Aeons in the Hollow. Does this mean that the Abyss itself is the Aeon of the Abyss? Does the Other represent something else? Am I overthinking things tremdously when the writers just copied the structure of the previous citadels for symmetry?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The abyss isn't considered an arcana. Anyone who tried to proclaim they were a siddha of the abyss would be branded a Bodhisattva. The Siddha don't like the abyss. They oppose it more than any group because it attempts to destroy reality and by extension the arcana. The abyss doesn't have two representatives because it's not part of the supernal structure it's outside of it. It's powerful enough to have a dream representative because of what it represents but doesn't have symmetry. It was one writer who would have done that section if not the book. So the symmetry is there on purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T04:07:34-07:00","id":120876,"title":"","content":"I don't have the impression that the Siddha really hate the Abyss; they do not touch him; but as their relationship with Exarchs they are satisfied that there is a rough filter to limit the number of Ascendeds and just take away human concepts, (The Exarchs want to rule over humanity and want to become down-to-earth concepts of temporal power, The Siddha affect esoterics symbols want to merge with their favorite arcana and do not care about humanity) they are like businessmen who finance distant dictatorships for their interest without getting their hands dirty.<br /> <br /> They tacitly support the Exarchs; and therefore (even if they probably not admit) the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:52:50-07:00","id":120993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=120876#post120876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the impression that the Siddha really hate the Abyss; they do not touch him; but as their relationship with Exarchs they are satisfied that there is a rough filter to limit the number of Ascendeds and just take away human concepts, (The Exarchs want to rule over humanity and want to become down-to-earth concepts of temporal power, The Siddha affect esoterics symbols want to merge with their favorite arcana and do not care about humanity) they are like businessmen who finance distant dictatorships for their interest without getting their hands dirty.<br /> <br /> They tacitly support the Exarchs; and therefore (even if they probably not admit) the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it works.The siddha don't care about the exarchs but when an exarch goes too far when it comes to twisting an arcana they'll be one of the first ones to oppose them. The reason you can't have a siddha of the abyss is because it's in the nature of the abyss to twist the universe into something entirely alien. Thereby corrupting the arcana, which goes against the siddha philosophy no matter how much you try to twist it. In the end, if the Exarchs want to rule the world it's not a big deal. If the abyss twists reality so it's unrecognizable then yeah it's a big deal. Simply because they don't care about the exarches doesn't mean they'll even remotely support the abyss when it does everything antithetical to the nature of a Siddha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:55:01-07:00","id":121043,"title":"","content":"Where I said they want that the Abyss becomes more important than now ?<br /> In the same way that Tetrarchs aren't pro-abyss for not seeking to destroy the Abyss but to hold him to make a filter; Siddhas let them do even if they not admit it. (See the second &quot;Legends of the Siddha&quot;)<br /> Since they do not care about the policy of the Exarchs and do not fight against them that makes them passive supporters. (as lead the life of a average westerner makes you a passive slave-driver)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:57:43-07:00","id":121044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=121043#post121043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I said they want that the Abyss becomes more important than now ?<br /> In the same way that Tetrarchs aren't pro-abyss for not seeking to destroy the Abyss but to hold him to make a filter; Siddhas let them do even if they not admit it. (See the second &quot;Legends of the Siddha&quot;)<br /> Since they do not care about the policy of the Exarchs and do not fight against them that makes them passive supporters. (as lead the life of a average westerner makes you a passive slave-driver)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... This conversation is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:15:31-07:00","id":121053,"title":"","content":"Remark on slavery was a bit of a joke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ; although I believe that selfishness is supposed to be the great vice of the Siddha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:20:53-07:00","id":121056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=121053#post121053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remark on slavery was a bit of a joke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ; although I believe that selfishness is supposed to be the great vice of the Siddha.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the Siddha is to care about the whole rather than the individual and in that the pursuit of a perfect balance. The Abyss will always threaten this balance that said they aren't proactive because it's impossible to be proactive against something you can barely interact with let alone fight against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:27:31-07:00","id":121164,"title":"","content":"Each Entente have a dark side...maybe the Boddhisatvas have realy creates the Banishers; maybe the Siddha revel in this elitist world and lack of emphaty.<br /> This is not an in-universe common criticism against the Siddha from other Ententes ? (Especially boddhivastavas ?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:49:28-07:00","id":121174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=121164#post121164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Entente have a dark side...maybe the Boddhisatvas have realy creates the Banishers; maybe the Siddha revel in this elitist world and lack of emphaty.<br /> This is not an in-universe common criticism against the Siddha from other Ententes ? (Especially boddhivastavas ?)</div> </div> </div> </div>That they are selfish. Yes. That their selfishness means they ignore and/or traffick with the abyss no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:06:53-07:00","id":134563,"title":"","content":"Why do the Seers of the Throne call themselves the Seers of the Throne?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:34:20-07:00","id":134622,"title":"","content":"They think their purpose is to divine the will of the rulers of the cosmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T12:20:51-07:00","id":160139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ascended Archmasters<br /> Some rare archmasters do achieve the Final Key, Ascending to<br /> the Supernal Realms permanently. These Invisible Masters may<br /> not be able to visit the Fallen World bodily any more \u2013 many<br /> are said to be merged with their Cintamani <b>or Chantry</b> </div> </div> </div>It's probably stupid but i don't get this, Ascended Archmasters aren't supposed to be merged with their cintamanni in the Supernal ? thus why this mention of &quot;merged with their chantry&quot; (a world in their soul) ?<br /> <br /> Maybe a Ascended Archmaster still have a chantry who is integrated in his ascended soul/lustrum (rather than his former golden road) , but why the &quot;or&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 06-06-2014, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:54:14-07:00","id":163863,"title":"","content":"A bit of thread necromancy.<br /> I am fairly new to the MtAw setting so I have some questions about the basic system. I will try to post them one at a time, mostly to make sure that my understanding of the rules is correct.<br /> <br /> <b>New question</b>: <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spell Emotional Urging is Mind 2, it works on one target at sensory range.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now if I wanted to cast it at sympathetic range, I would need 'Mind 3 + Space 2', because it actively affects the target.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I would also have to spend 1 Mana. So far all clear.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If I understand the rules, this spell will also become Vulgar, leading to Paradox roll as well, am I correct?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Another question, if I wanted to affect area instead of just one person, would I need 'Mind 4 + Space 2' ?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And if I wanted to cast it with Advanced Prolongation, would that be 'Mind 5 + Space 2' spell?</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:16:07-07:00","id":163943,"title":"","content":"<b>New Question: </b>Does a Mages use of his Arcana to manipulate things such as magnetic fields, gravity and heat, give him a better understanding of those things, allowing him to purcase dots in Science? Or for an equivalent eksample of a different Arcana/skill, Medicine for Life/Death or social skills for Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:18:09-07:00","id":163944,"title":"","content":"Yes to all. Note that turning a Target afecting spell into an Area one also increases the cost by a point of Mana. So 2 Mana for the sympathetic area of effect Emotional Urging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:30:22-07:00","id":164093,"title":"","content":"@Krobeles: As far as I know the rules only handle the XP cost of raising skills it is not very specific about how you obtained your knowledge, so unless your ST rules otherwise you could gain the appropriate knowledge this way.<br /> <br /> <b>nWoD p. 217</b>: &quot;The Storyteller decides just what he needs to do to qualify. It might take days of study in a library, or enroll- ing in a semester-long night course at the local college. It could be a simple matter of days spent in the wilderness, or a week\u2019s worth of repetitive practice. Most Skills can be self- taught with time and effort, if a character is smart and dili- gent. Otherwise, a teacher might be required.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T09:22:50-07:00","id":164871,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q</b>: <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The spell Temporal Dodge (Time 2) (or other spells like it) has a normal duration one scene. By spending 1 Mana it can be prolonged to whole day. What does it take to have it for indefinite duration, Time 3 or 4?</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:32:29-07:00","id":165177,"title":"","content":"It doesn't, in the current version of the rules, because indefinite-duration spells cannot be cast on living Patterns without archmastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T16:43:58-07:00","id":165351,"title":"","content":"Totally forgot about that one.<br /> <br /> <b>New Q</b>:The spell Reading Outmost Eddies had duration Prolonged(one scene), how does it work? Does it provide one instance of small fortune per cast or does it simply keep sending small fortunes your way for the duration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:34:48-07:00","id":168951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=160139#post160139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably stupid but i don't get this, Ascended Archmasters aren't supposed to be merged with their cintamanni in the Supernal ? thus why this mention of &quot;merged with their chantry&quot; (a world in their soul) ?<br /> <br /> Maybe a Ascended Archmaster still have a chantry who is integrated in his ascended soul/lustrum (rather than his former golden road) , but why the &quot;or&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div><u>No-one knows what exactly happens when you Ascend</u>, or why Ascended Archmasters can't enter the Fallen World in person. Or if they do, they aren't telling.<br /> <br /> However, Archmasters do know that the Golden Road remains behind, including the Cintimanni and any Chantries. And that these retain elements of the Archmage's personality, and that the Seekers of the Throne give Ministers access to them as part of their duties. So it is not unreasonable of them, to suspect that Ascension involves completely merging with one's perfected Soul, and that <u>one might find some remnant of the Ascended within either Lustrum or Chantry</u>.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the rest of the book seems clear - insofar as possible, considering the toolbox nature of the nWoD - that Ascension merges the archmage with their Cintamani, and what remains behind in Chantries is not the Ascended Mage, but semi-abandoned Subsouls. So this is probably <u>not true</u> by default.<br /> <br /> It would, however, be easy to insert into your game - and pretty cool, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:50:26-07:00","id":168959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=168951#post168951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the rest of the book seems clear - insofar as possible, considering the toolbox nature of the nWoD - that Ascension merges the archmage with their Cintamani, and what remains behind in Chantries is not the Ascended Mage, but semi-abandoned Subsouls. So this is probably <u>not true</u> by default.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I think it was a mistake when Chantries were included in the original post, unless the poster uses this in their own games. <br /> <br /> The Golden road of an Ascended mage remains behind, though is unstable and called a Wending. The Chantries and Irises that connect them to the worlds they were Seeded from may still be be entered (though not always), and the golden road can still be observed. &quot;Inhabitants such as orphaned Ochemata or any Chantry population may still be present and rival Seekers may have<br /> claimed the Wending as territory.&quot; Furthermore, &quot;Archmages can absorb Chantries built in Wendings into their own Roads with the Practice of Entities.&quot; Finally, the golden road can crumple and be destroyed if someone tries to cross it, and they would then be dumped into the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:16:00-07:00","id":170840,"title":"","content":"Thanks but I said that because a line from Imperial Mysteries. (My quote in my original post), maybe this is an incorrect assumption from the non-ascended archmasters's viewpoint. (obvisouly, I know about Wendings and the fact that &quot;Ascension is merging with his Cintammani&quot; is almost explicit elsewhere)<br /> <br /> (although the idea of a few archmasters merging with their chantry and become a part of the Phenomenal World* rather than ascend in the Supernal seemed rather cool to me it reminds me of the Selenim's Realms from Nephilim) <br /> <br /> *Essentially use the Seeker's Ascension to harmonize yourself with Reality (Phenomenal World) Rather than the Supernal Truth (a little like the Aswadim who use the Golden Road to no longer be in harmony with the universe)<br /> The &quot;Noumenon&quot; would be like &quot;create and impose a place in the Phenomenal World from his Chantry and become the expression (not the idealization of course, the goal is become more real than true) of this part of the Phenomenal World&quot; I don't think it would be so metaphysically impossible, more &quot;interfere with the thematic of the game or the archmasters are not numerous enough to form Ententes with this kind of Ideas or succeed in this kind of audacity (or far too unique to be know)<br /> But if it was an Entente, the Ethos would be like &quot;The Phenomenal should not be slave of the Supernal's Tyrants or the Abyss and you can reign as good below as above; Anamorphosis is as an Apotheosis as the Supernal Ascension&quot; and takes the realization that the Phenomenal World is no less than the Supernal up to eleven.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T00:13:02-07:00","id":171474,"title":"","content":"What Arcana do you need to turn a person into gold? Matter 5, or 6?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:26:27-07:00","id":171515,"title":"","content":"Life 4 Matter 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T14:57:37-07:00","id":172057,"title":"","content":"Can you get specific isotopes with Matter 5 or would you need higher levels?<br /> Related question: At what level could you create anti-matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T15:07:15-07:00","id":172063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=172057#post172057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question: At what level could you create anti-matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 6, as per Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:20:03-07:00","id":172142,"title":"","content":"Since Satchel already answered the other one...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you get specific isotopes with Matter 5 or would you need higher levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, but anything radioactive needs conjuctional Forces (4-5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:59:40-07:00","id":172187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=172142#post172142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Satchel already answered the other one...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You can, but anything radioactive needs conjuctional Forces (4-5).</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't as it's not making it radioactive but having forces 4-5 would be good so you didn't get radiation poisoning from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T01:15:35-07:00","id":172535,"title":"","content":"Thing is, matter (low case m) at atomic and sub-atomic levels is a grey area of overlap between Matter and Forces (though sub-atomic is mostly Forces). Anyway, not all isotopes are radiocative, and those that aren't need only Matter, but radioactive isotopes (most of them, really) do need Forces, as anything that generates radioactivity needs it. It doesn't matter you are not making it radioactive, the fact that it is is enough to need the conjuctional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> EDIT: now, that's bound to change in the FWC as it seems Conjuctional requirments are way, way, less exigent. It may be just Matter (or just Forces, or any of them indistictly) in the new rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 06-18-2014, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T00:23:17-07:00","id":173796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=172535#post172535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, matter (low case m) at atomic and sub-atomic levels is a grey area of overlap between Matter and Forces (though sub-atomic is mostly Forces).</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that sub-atomic particles are more little bundles of statistical equations than anything you would consider &quot;solid&quot;, I like to think of Matter as being made out of Forces and Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T01:09:42-07:00","id":173811,"title":"","content":"Yeah - creating Matter that then happens to produce radiation shouldn't need Forces going forward, IMO, any more than producing Caesium that you then chuck into water does because it bursts into flame.<br /> <br /> Or, as in the current rules, producing liquids that happen to be toxic, despite &quot;create poison&quot; also being a Life spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T02:50:32-07:00","id":173906,"title":"","content":"And what about altering the state of matter to plasma? Could (and should) be posible with Matter alone? It is one of the 4 basic states after all, but some of the common manifestations as electrical currents or flames are suposedly covered by Forces.<br /> <br /> By the way, I hope is posible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 06-19-2014, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T03:10:35-07:00","id":173916,"title":"","content":"You can use Forces to ionize a gas through a couple different methods that mirror the mundane techniques, and you can probably use one of the top levels of Matter to decrease the temperature at which a gas will reach the threshold of heat-induced ionization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T03:21:00-07:00","id":173920,"title":"","content":"Maybe Weaving or Patterning to change the pressure and/or temperature needed for an state shift? Sounds doable but I have no idea about how to measure the Potency of the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T03:31:43-07:00","id":173921,"title":"","content":"I'd use the same scale that lower-dot Forces spells use to spend successes on degrees of air temperature change. It's going to demand more than, say, turning a room into an oven, but I don't know the details relevant to this phase transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:27:30-07:00","id":174506,"title":"","content":"Q. Could an archmaster teach the 6th dot in an arcana to a normal mage? I was looking at pg. 132 in the core and it made me wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:04:21-07:00","id":174590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=174506#post174506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q. Could an archmaster teach the 6th dot in an arcana to a normal mage? I was looking at pg. 132 in the core and it made me wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div> In my games, I don't let this happen, at least not directly. An archmage could guide you to your threshold seeking, which can then let you achieve your 6th dot, but all the rules seem to point out that anything beyond 5 dots requires archmastery first. I always consider that the 6th-10th dots of arcana require a a proper Centinami acquired through a construction of a Golden Road. So, an archmage can teach a 6th dot to a normal mage... by teaching him how to become an archmage. That said, I think it comes down to your ST, and how you want to interpret the rules for your own game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T01:37:22-07:00","id":175063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=174506#post174506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q. Could an archmaster teach the 6th dot in an arcana to a normal mage? I was looking at pg. 132 in the core and it made me wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Become Archmage is more than &quot;learning&quot;, obtain a sixth dot in an Arcanum and get the Archmaster Template request to broke the Threshold, you <i>change</i> the universe to allow your archmaster-hood.<br /> <br /> Of course, a Archmaster can help a Seeker. (in the limits of the Pax Arcanum) <br /> <br /> So for me (and I think canonically), you cannot makes a Archmaster so directly; although personnaly I think it's technicaly possible but with nothing less than a 10th spell to grant archmastery in the corresponding arcanum. (rewrite the laws of reality/arcanum to allow his archmastery in a similar way to the Threshold.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T02:05:46-07:00","id":175074,"title":"","content":"That's the thing, it wouldn't be giving them the archmaster template, they'd still be a normal mage, just with a sixth dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always consider that the 6th-10th dots of arcana require a a proper Centinami acquired through a construction of a Golden Road. </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty reasonable assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T02:42:12-07:00","id":175098,"title":"","content":"Official answer: No. The 6s on the corebook's Gnosis chart are the result of not having worked out all the details of archmastery at time of writing. Fallen World's version of it will only go up to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T04:38:26-07:00","id":175132,"title":"","content":"Wait, so in <i>FWC</i> will there still be Gnosis 10 Mages who aren't arch-masters? I know it's been mentioned a few times that Gnosis 10 doesn't necessarily imply arch-mastery, but now I'm confused from the last couple posts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T04:52:25-07:00","id":175136,"title":"","content":"He's referring to the arcana mastery table on pg.76 of the corebook. It says that Gnosis 6 magi can learn a 6th dot in an arcana. That's no longer going to be the case because you need to gain the Archmaster template as of IM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T04:56:26-07:00","id":175139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=175074#post175074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing, it wouldn't be giving them the archmaster template, they'd still be a normal mage, just with a sixth dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepers cannot learn the five first dots of the arcana because you have to be a mage by definition.<br /> It is the same for 6+ dots; you have to be a archmaster. (even if technicaly, you get the archmaster template and the sixth dot together)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:25:53-07:00","id":175182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepers cannot learn the five first dots of the arcana because you have to be a mage by definition.<br /> It is the same for 6+ dots; you have to be a archmaster. </div> </div> </div>That's an implied definition which the actual rules don't synch up with, due to as DaveB said, the core and IM being written years apart. The arcana mastery table says you can do exactly that when you have gnosis 6.<br /> <br /> Now, you'd still lack a golden road to cast imperial practices and you wouldn't have all the features of the Archmaster template, but there are a few little grey areas you would get access to like advanced prolongation on 5-dot spells which could be kinda cool.<br /> <br /> Funny thing is, I originally meant this as a bit of idle curiosity about an interesting rules discrepancy but I kinda like the idea now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T07:39:55-07:00","id":175246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=175136#post175136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's referring to the arcana mastery table on pg.76 of the corebook. It says that Gnosis 6 magi can learn a 6th dot in an arcana. That's no longer going to be the case because you need to gain the Archmaster template as of IM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. I see it now. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T18:37:58-07:00","id":177526,"title":"","content":"Is there a place where I can find more info on Abyssal Verges? I've heard the term mentioned here and there but can't seem to find substantial info on the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T03:54:50-07:00","id":177814,"title":"","content":"We've mentioned them occassionally throughout the game line, but they've never been described! They had to be cut from Left Hand Path for space. Mage is sometimes odd about what got picked up and expanded on and what didn't - it took until Imperial Mysteries to actually describe what the Abyss looks like &quot;inside&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, they're Verges to the Abyss. Think an Anomaly, but bigger, spawning Gulmoth, and if you can survive going &quot;through&quot; them you end up in the Abyss. They're on the list of things to describe in Fallen World Chronicle, and we'll try not to cut them for space this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T09:45:06-07:00","id":178037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=177814#post177814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've mentioned them occassionally throughout the game line, but they've never been described! They had to be cut from Left Hand Path for space. Mage is sometimes odd about what got picked up and expanded on and what didn't - it took until Imperial Mysteries to actually describe what the Abyss looks like &quot;inside&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, they're Verges to the Abyss. Think an Anomaly, but bigger, spawning Gulmoth, and if you can survive going &quot;through&quot; them you end up in the Abyss. They're on the list of things to describe in Fallen World Chronicle, and we'll try not to cut them for space this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here comes &quot;<b>In the Mouth of Madness</b>&quot; for <b>Mage</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T13:14:06-07:00","id":178177,"title":"","content":"My simple question: How the heck do you &quot;hang&quot; a counterspell?? I was reading the intro in the Mysterium book (page 9) and have been flummoxed since. I thought you had to <i>identify</i> the spell first to counterspell it... so if you're hanging the counterspell..... ???<br /> Fate 2, so that it's an &quot;if/then&quot; situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2802-dreamtide","name":"Dreamtide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T13:27:13-07:00","id":178183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreamtide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=178177#post178177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My simple question: How the heck do you &quot;hang&quot; a counterspell?? I was reading the intro in the Mysterium book (page 9) and have been flummoxed since. I thought you had to <i>identify</i> the spell first to counterspell it... so if you're hanging the counterspell..... ???<br /> Fate 2, so that it's an &quot;if/then&quot; situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read that piece of fiction, but as far as I know hanging a counterspell is possible.<br /> <br /> You need the spell &quot;Counterspell Prime&quot; (Prime 2) as it can be used without first identifying the spell you are using it against. Setting a conditional trigger (&quot;hanging the spell&quot;) is Fate 2 + Time 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T08:24:44-07:00","id":187996,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to hear your opinion about a piece of creative thaumaturgy:<br /> <br /> A character with Space 3 runs at a closed door and tries to squeeze through the tiny crack between door and doorframe. Is Space 3 enough to become nearly two dimensional for a split second or would that require adept or even master level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;...and then we discovered it wasn't the Robot King after all, it was the real one. Fortunately I was able to reattach the head.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/644-mcbaine","name":"McBaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T08:53:03-07:00","id":190339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McBaine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to hear your opinion about a piece of creative thaumaturgy:<br /> <br /> A character with Space 3 runs at a closed door and tries to squeeze through<br /> the tiny crack between door and doorframe. Is Space 3 enough to become nearly two dimensional for a split second or would that require adept or even master level?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Transitory effect I'd see no problem with it, though I'd probably rule that at space 3 it can't increase its duration yet (successes would go to potency, which would work towards adding dice to infiltrate, for example.)<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Question: Shoud / Do computer programs count as being in the same conceptual space as &quot;ideas&quot; for the purposes of spell targeting? I.e. one can target People, Places and Things, not thoughts or concepts. Should computer programs be targetable by (e.g.) Forces, or are they too conceptual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 07-07-2014, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T09:01:54-07:00","id":190358,"title":"","content":"No, they're just writing. In an electric medium, but writing nontheless. Forces/Mind Conjunctional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T09:05:34-07:00","id":190384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McBaine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=187996#post187996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to hear your opinion about a piece of creative thaumaturgy:<br /> <br /> A character with Space 3 runs at a closed door and tries to squeeze through the tiny crack between door and doorframe. Is Space 3 enough to become nearly two dimensional for a split second or would that require adept or even master level?</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems pretty awesome to me. This is the magical equivalent of picking a lock and going through the door then locking it again. It's nothing too outrageous. So go for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T09:44:24-07:00","id":190402,"title":"","content":"Bending space that hard would be Making, just Weaving wouldn't handle such a drastic change.<br /> With space 3 however you can bypass a door, just not that specific way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:50:11-07:00","id":190481,"title":"","content":"I have two:<br /> <br /> 1) In the middle of combat, an NPC points an RPG at an Obrimos Adept of Forces. The Obrimos says &quot;I use Telekinesis to hit the RPG, triggering it.&quot; Now, from the ST's standpoint, where said RPG was, an explosion would take out 80% of the enemy combatants, all mooks. From the player's point of view, it's damned cool and if he doesn't do something, he'll get an RPG to the face. The ST expects him to re-direct the RPG off to the side, out of combat. The player wants to end combat PDQ.<br /> <br /> My question: barring Time 2 Perfect Timing to get the Telekinesis *just* as the RPG is activated or Fate 2 to do similar, (there were no Acanthoi involved), how would you adjudicate this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2) Same Adept of Forces wants a Force Field spell. A standing barrier a la Star Trek. What level, if at all, would you adjudicate this? Notice Death 3's ability to do exactly this with shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T11:53:05-07:00","id":190579,"title":"","content":"For #2, there are a couple ways to handle this, based on how other arcana do it: you could base it off Phantasms, Death walls, or Wards/Bans.<br /> personally I'd probably base it on Bans and make it an instant transitory spell, where if anything exerts more Strength/Successes against penetrating it than it has Potency, it passes through and lowers the potency. (e.g. if you are being shot at by 3 guys and the second one shoots hard enough to penetrate it, the 3rd one gets to deal with less potency)<br /> I don't think it's unreasonable to allow this to be made out of kinetic energy at 3, and other forces at higher levels - electricity at 4 (dealing bashing damage on contact) and fire at 5 for example.<br /> <br /> Or you could make it work exactly like an AoE Mage Armor, adding Armor to anyone covered by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 07-07-2014, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:21:53-07:00","id":190663,"title":"","content":"For your second question see the Adamantine Arrow book, I believe the spell is called Repel or something similar. It's a mobile ban that the caster projects around himself, the duration is Concentration and it's Vulgar.<br /> <br /> Obviously other arcana should be able to achieve similar effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:22:18-07:00","id":190664,"title":"","content":"So, I have a character who specializes in Life, and has a theme of 'magical martial arts'. I want a Rote that is, basically, attacking their life force with soft style martial art's attacks (ala <i>Jyuuken</i>), as his really distinctive magical offense. It will probably be something learned in-game. Now, I'm at a loss how to do this without making it worse than a normal Brawl attack, or making it stupid to not just Life Force assault rote that is ranged. To be clear, we are using the GMC update with DaveB's stop-gap. The simplest way I can see is just a Dexterity + Brawl + Life rote, This runs into a few problems, 1) things are assumed to be Sensory range... which is not a martial arts move. 2) It's obviously worse than making it ranged, because Defense would apply and adding two stats (dex or wits + Athletics) is worse than just one (Stamina). <br /> <br /> There's the 'Law of Embodiment' merit, but I don't see how it's useful. It's a regular Dex + Brawl roll, then IF you hit you roll Life (- Stamina). I'm... not sure how that is worth five merit dots. You have the same number of dice as above, and a greater chance to hit. Unless I completely misunderstood the merit, of course. <br /> <br /> So any help with making a flavorful magical attack that's not obviously worse than what I can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:28:25-07:00","id":190670,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Adamant Hand fighting merit from the Adamantine Arrow book? That's useless if you're not playing an Adamantine Arrow of course, but if you are you might find what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:54:14-07:00","id":191005,"title":"","content":"There's also a Life 3 + Prime 4 spell (Adamantine Arrow too, I think, but since it's a spell it can be improvised by anyone) that has a scene-long duration and allows you to deal aggravated damage with your hands. Since it's magical, you could fluff it as soft style MA attacks that happen to deal devastating damage, using the same pools as fists or kicks.<br /> It only augments your damage type though, so you don't get a die bonus, and it costs 1 mana per attack (still, dealing agg at a sub-master level is pretty scary; at Prime or Life 5 you could possibly do something like add the primary arcana as a weapon bonus)<br /> <br /> If your character doesn't have Prime you could do something conceptually similar - using spells that don't deal damage themselves, but augment the character's damage-dealing capabilities for the scene at the cost of Mana, like spreading rashes, fungi, infections, contact poisons or whatever with a touch, essentially just changing the aesthetics of the attack without changing the mechanics of it. (You could justify it with things like &quot;Using the Life arcana, I transfer my muscle strength into concentrated bursts of life force, thereby not having to punch to deal damage, as anything that touches my fingers feels the pain my body can inflict&quot;). Though just that might actually be just Life 2 (Ruling) as it doesn't actually do anything besides cosmetically change the appearance of attacks without changing their capabilities. (it might even be argued to be Veiling, as you're hiding physical aggression, something that does fall under the Life arcana).<br /> <br /> At higher levels (i.e. 3, 4 and 5) you could add on to it with more powerful or longer-lasting effects, like adding your Life rating to attacks, making them lethal/aggravated or inflicting penalties due to warts/fungi/etc. I'm not sure about the actual balance though, as it's not exactly a direct-damage situation, so tweak the ratings as necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  Correction: It's Prime 4 + Life 3, not Life 4 07-08-2014, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T19:06:48-07:00","id":191012,"title":"","content":"Mm. Not playing an Arrow. =/ I've looked at it. (5th dot allows you to cast a spell and attack on the same turn separately.), but as you stated, it's useless as a non-Arrow mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T22:31:43-07:00","id":212112,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing that there were non-explicit crossover hints wth Mummy: The Curse in Left Handed Path. Can anyone point these out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T23:05:32-07:00","id":212156,"title":"","content":"They're in the Scelesti chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T00:02:42-07:00","id":217934,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if I'm missing something obvious-it's late and I don't have the patience to go through my books- but I've often seen Prime used as the arcana to interact with the God Machine and its servants. For example, in Dave's stop-gap GMC mechanics, targeting an Angel, its Numina, rewriting the Pattern of someone claimed, etc, requires equal parts Prime and Spirit. What's the rationale behind this?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, another one: why do mages join the Seers? I mean okay, I've heard the explanations of &quot;they're joining the winning side&quot;/&quot;it's easier than joining the Pentacle&quot;/&quot;you get lots of hookers and blow, but those don't really ring true for me. Previous posts on the subject for why:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/198283-can-the-seers-of-the-throne-be-heroic?p=199547#post199547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, I don't see the perks. The Seers have to be motivated by more than just the money, because mages who just care about money can get it any number of ways. They're mages.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs demands aren't small or inocuous. Knowing the order may come down to sacrifice your own children Abraham and Isaac style at any time means you need to be getting something out of this deal you couldn't get on your own, and I don't see what.<br /> <br /> If they aren't ideologically motivated, it reminds me of the human villain from the Fifth Element who decided to help destroy the universe (with him in the universe) for the money.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/198283-can-the-seers-of-the-throne-be-heroic?p=199655#post199655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, being a Seer is actually really hard. The hardcore Darwinism and evil inherent in the Seer hierarchy breeds immense amounts of paranoia and serves as a fertile breeding ground for mental health problems. Knowing that the people in your organization both above and below you are untrustworthy and could very well be planning your demise is not the kind of thing that allows one to sleep well at night.<br /> <br /> And while the Seers might claim that the Exarchs &quot;rule the universe&quot;, it's not really obvious. They're just as restrained by the Pax as everyone else. How much of a practical difference would there be for the average Seer if they got their dreams and artifacts from a few Archmasters instead of the Exarchs? I don't think equating the Seers to servants of actual tyrannical rulers in RL works that well. I might be misreading or misremembering the books but it seems like the Seers and the Pentacle are pretty evenly matched. It's hard to be the small, oppressed underdogs when you are actually bigger in size than the oppressors no:?</div> </div> </div> </div>And I know theirs a ton of lies in Seer propaganda and 1984-style erasing of the past but that strikes me as a lot less effective when the people you're trying to do that too are willworkers. Mages are magical detectives after all. They are nearly unparalleled in ability when it comes to gathering information. Once one strips away all the bull, joining the Seers seems like a pretty crappy deal. Other than genuine zealots for the Exarchs, I could maybe see a mage that really enjoyed abusing Sleepers but also wanted the benefits of a large and old magical organization joining. Other than that...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":2713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","user":"123456789blaaa","date":". 08-04-2014, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T00:13:26-07:00","id":217938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=217934#post217934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if I'm missing something obvious-it's late and I don't have the patience to go through my books- but I've often seen Prime used as the arcana to interact with the God Machine and its servants. For example, in Dave's stop-gap GMC mechanics, targeting an Angel, its Numina, rewriting the Pattern of someone claimed, etc, requires equal parts Prime and Spirit. What's the rationale behind this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because Prime is the &quot;magic&quot; Arcana, it's used for all the weird shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T02:26:44-07:00","id":217980,"title":"","content":"Prime is the Arcanum covering (among other parts of its purview) raw symbolism, meanings, and Truth - it's why it's used for Mana resonance manipulation, ley line moving, and creates &quot;illusions&quot;.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is built out of hidden meanings and symbols.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T03:10:43-07:00","id":217987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=217934#post217934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Also, another one: why do mages join the Seers? I mean okay, I've heard the explanations of &quot;they're joining the winning side&quot;/&quot;it's easier than joining the Pentacle&quot;/&quot;you get lots of hookers and blow, but those don't really ring true for me. Previous posts on the subject for why:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I know theirs a ton of lies in Seer propaganda and 1984-style erasing of the past but that strikes me as a lot less effective when the people you're trying to do that too are willworkers. Mages are magical detectives after all. They are nearly unparalleled in ability when it comes to gathering information. Once one strips away all the bull, joining the Seers seems like a pretty crappy deal. Other than genuine zealots for the Exarchs, I could maybe see a mage that really enjoyed abusing Sleepers but also wanted the benefits of a large and old magical organization joining. Other than that...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the most likely reason is simply that most mages join whichever side gets to them first since if you've just gone through a life-changing revelation, the first people who turn up and give you some answers drastically affect what you think is going on with Magic, the Lie and everything. Imagine if you suddenly awaken and then five minutes later a bunch of friendly chaps turn up and explain how magic is all to do with these crazy god-like beings and that you should join them to protect the world from these absolute nutters who keep trying to mess everything up. Then if you realise the seers are evil, well, they will try to kill you if you leave and the pentacle (who you only know about via seer propaganda) will also probably kill you if they find you.<br /> <br /> One of my only problem with the seers book, which is generally really great, is that i was never able to get fully on board with the average seer being someone who had made the easy or corrupt choice since most mages don't really get a choice in who they join, they just get stuck with whoever finds them first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3497-urbicamortis","name":"UrbicaMortis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T03:38:47-07:00","id":217997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UrbicaMortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=217987#post217987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my only problem with the seers book, which is generally really great, is that i was never able to get fully on board with the average seer being someone who had made the easy or corrupt choice since most mages don't really get a choice in who they join, they just get stuck with whoever finds them first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course the Seers have a choice. The Iron Pyramid is fairly unambiguous about it's moral bankruptcy, and a new Seer very quickly learns what's expected of them. The choice is whether to continue to victimize Sleepers for your continued survival/all the shiny benefits, or make a moral stand and get the hell out of Dodge. The fact that the &quot;serve the Exarchs&quot; choice is corrupt is fairly obvious, and risking your life for what's good and right is certainly harder than not doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T04:07:25-07:00","id":218009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=217997#post217997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course the Seers have a choice. The Iron Pyramid is fairly unambiguous about it's moral bankruptcy, and a new Seer very quickly learns what's expected of them. The choice is whether to continue to victimize Sleepers for your continued survival/all the shiny benefits, or make a moral stand and get the hell out of Dodge. The fact that the &quot;serve the Exarchs&quot; choice is corrupt is fairly obvious, and risking your life for what's good and right is certainly harder than not doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, in that staying in the Seers after you've realised they're a horrible organisation is the easy choice, but I guess i feel to an extent that they got unlucky. I mean, your other choices are defect to the pentacle (who you've heard nothing but bad things about) or flee an organisation filled with powerful people who can magically find you. That doesn't excuse making the morally bankrupt choice but I've always felt that most pentacle mages would make the same choice if they hadn't got lucky and been found by less evil people first. My basic point, I suppose, is that anyone who chooses to leave the seers is an exceptional individual willing to risk almost certain death to make a moral stand whereas generally pentacle mages have not undergone the same test of character since they lucked into being recruited by the (more or less) good guys.<br /> <br /> It just makes it hard to judge the Seer rank and file too harshly, at least in comparison to the Pentacle. They made the easy choice, sure, but the other side didn't even have to make it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3497-urbicamortis","name":"UrbicaMortis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T04:25:03-07:00","id":218015,"title":"","content":"Which gives Pentacle mages just enough pause when fighting low-ranking Seers for the high-ranking Seers to exploit.<br /> <br /> Look at the sample characters in Seers of the Throne - there's the one who really doesn't want to be a Seer but is terrified of his Pylon, and the one who's facing his first Exarch-given commandment with the wide-eyed knowledge that he'll cross a moral event horizon but can't see a way out.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic cannon fodder makes the best cannon fodder!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 08-04-2014, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T04:48:24-07:00","id":218029,"title":"","content":"If you ever read the Mage demo Gloria Mundi, the last antagonist in it is explicitly referred to in these terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:09:12-07:00","id":240870,"title":"","content":"So lets assume Mage X has ritually cast a potency 50 ward on himself (Space 5, Mind 5, Gnosis 7, maxed out rote stats via gain skill and stuff), he also has a ritually cast Shield of Chronos spell on him and the has rank 3 occultation merit. Basically he doesnt want to be found and can roam the place as a mental projection. He has broken the Lex Magica and the ruling council need to make an example of him.<br /> <br /> Now assume the council can go all out, have unlimited resources and enough time to find somebody able to breach the ward or find him through other means, but they might only get 1 attempt. Can Mage X even detect when his ward is breached or would he need to scrutinize his spell every so often (and require probably more successes than he can acquire without serious intelligence/occult boosting.)<br /> <br /> What do they cast at Mage X? What other non-awakened things could be used to help find/catch him. A Spirit perhaps? Giests have a finding ceremony, but need part of the mage, perhaps time magic could bring a part of him back from the past thats assuming the council would be even aware of it.<br /> <br /> A few current ideas are either a combined dispel magic / ward spell, that'll dispel Mage X's ward (the dispel magic spell would have to changed to be area effect right as it targets a spell and lets assume that zero mages have any sympathetic connection to the Mage X's ward spell so casting an area effect version centered on Mage X is how it'd have to work. It also has the added bonus that it'll dispel every spell on him thats lower than potency 51 since that is the min potency needed to breach the ward) &amp; the ward will stop him from just teleporting away unless he beats this new ward long enough for another space master to open a portal to the location and swarm him.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps a controlled dispel making at least 1 person immune to the ward and then they can cast other things at him without the ward. Or a ritually cast geas spell (probably needing the to the limit rule as you cant normally cast lvl 5 spells at sympathetic range) the spell will require him to leave the city and never return in any form etc or suffer the -5 penalty to rolls if he breaks it.<br /> <br /> Does anybody else have any other ideas? If the ruling Council are not able to do anything they they will look like complete fools and others might start thinking they can get away with breaking the rules etc etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:33:25-07:00","id":240884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=240870#post240870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now assume the council can go all out, have unlimited resources and enough time to find somebody able to breach the ward or find him through other means, but they might only get 1 attempt. Can Mage X even detect when his ward is breached or would he need to scrutinize his spell every so often (and require probably more successes than he can acquire without serious intelligence/occult boosting.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Space 2, Prime 2 thingy that tells you when your spells are being messed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:49:43-07:00","id":240896,"title":"","content":"You should note too that wards are anchored to locations, there's an AA example of a mobile ward/ban but its duration is Concentration and it's vulgar. So basically, he could throw up this huge ward, sure and then he'd be under self-imposed house arrest (Which had awesome plot implications in Broken Diamond), eventually completely mundane search methods would find him and then unless he's added Bans the Ward would do him absolutely no good at all.<br /> <br /> Even with Bans there is almost assuredly a work around.<br /> <br /> There are ways that are safer and take up a lot less effort than creating a giant ward though. Personally if I was a Master of Space I'd just pop bodily into my Oneiros and then use apportation to get what I need from time to time. It's almost like a mini-Golden Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-25-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T17:04:37-07:00","id":240901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=240896#post240896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should note too that wards are anchored to locations, there's an AA example of a mobile ward/ban but its duration is Concentration and it's vulgar. So basically, he could throw up this huge ward, sure and then he'd be under self-imposed house arrest (Which had awesome plot implications in Broken Diamond), eventually completely mundane search methods would find him and then unless he's added Bans the Ward would do him absolutely no good at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, he has Creative Thaumaturgied a variant of ward for people who want to avoid getting scried on the move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T17:07:41-07:00","id":240904,"title":"","content":"You don't need to do creative thaumaturgy to do that, just Sever the Threads or Conceal your Sympathies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:20:18-07:00","id":241085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=240904#post240904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to do creative thaumaturgy to do that, just Sever the Threads or Conceal your Sympathies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manually destroying ALL your sympathetic connections seems like a pain, and it doesn't stop people from knowing you exist, so they're going to reform Described connections pretty much instantly while talking about you. If someone knows your name, they can still use sympathetic magic, including scrying.<br /> <br /> Or you could do it all. Keep up a shield of Chronos against Time stuff, a ward against Space stuff, and <i>also</i> destroy all your sympathetic connections. This mage criminal doesn't look like he's sparing much effort for his counter-measures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T01:27:26-07:00","id":241175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;There's a Space 2, Prime 2 thingy that tells you when your spells are being messed with. &quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Thanks i knew i remembered reading something like that once, just couldnt remember it.<br /> <br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You should note too that wards are anchored to locations, there's an AA example of a mobile ward/ban but its duration is Concentration and it's vulgar. So basically, he could throw up this huge ward, sure and then he'd be under self-imposed house arrest (Which had awesome plot implications in Broken Diamond), eventually completely mundane search methods would find him and then unless he's added Bans the Ward would do him absolutely no good at all. </div> </div> </div></i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <i>Even with Bans there is almost assuredly a work around.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>So yeh as Kazorh implied a creative thaum personal ward is being used, mastery of space and all, the repel spell was looked over when coming up with it. There is also instances of objects being warded in reign of the exarchs and while probably just the writers not reading ward properly does give weight to the possibility of a personal ward.<br /> Another way would be to have a persistant imbued item with an area effect high potency area ward around it which could be movable, the question was to assume he is mobile with a high potency ward what 1 spell could somebody cast that would help the council bring him to justice not pick holes in how the ward works <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;There are ways that are safer and take up a lot less effort than creating a giant ward though. Personally if I was a Master of Space I'd just pop bodily into my Oneiros and then use apportation to get what I need from time to time. It's almost like a mini-Golden Road. &quot;<br /> <br /> Hmm, so is there any precedent for bodily going into the astral thats not archmastery? I always assumed it required archmastery to physically enter the astral and while it could be handwaved as creative thaum would it not also require mind X to open a portal into somebodys oneiros maybe?<br /> <br /> Its one of the annoying parts of Space that a master of space cant apport items without matter, has always seemed really stupid to me. Again not really answering my question, it wasnt how else can Mage X avoid the council <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Manually destroying ALL your sympathetic connections seems like a pain, and it doesn't stop people from knowing you exist, so they're going to reform Described connections pretty much instantly while talking about you. If someone knows your name, they can still use sympathetic magic, including scrying.<br /> <br /> Or you could do it all. Keep up a shield of Chronos against Time stuff, a ward against Space stuff, and also destroy all your sympathetic connections. This mage criminal doesn't look like he's sparing much effort for his counter-measures.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Indeed, paranoia (its not as people are after him) means habitual use of sever threads etc. a described connection with rank 3 occultation knowing the real name is a whopping -13 dice penalty.<br /> <br /> Assuming one were to find a mage with a rote, stat 4 skill 4 and arcanum 5 thats a only 13 dicepool leaving a chance dice. Assume he could have his stat and skill boosted via mind to 6 or higher and is given either 8 again or rote actions for the entire ritual casting its still probably not enough dice to pierce a stupidly high ward potency.<br /> Max number of rolls is base dicepool of 13, so even 13 rolls of 4-6 dice with rote action doesnt give enough successes.<br /> <br /> Maybe sympathetic casting at Mage X isnt they route to go down. Hence why i was asking what other options a council could come up with.<br /> <br /> I did think of another one. Knowing that mage X usually has his intelligence boosted with mind magic perhaps a wide enough area effect Sense Consciousness spell convering as much range as possible (we can probably cover an entire city with enough successes) that only registers highly intelligent minds would narrow down the field.<br /> There is a spell that does something similar in tome of mysteries called Supernal sense, it requires space though and wards provide protection for it. My understanding of changing a spell to area affect and casting it where you are was that you didnt need space even if the area effect extends past sensory range? The spell itself is being cast in sensory range its just its area of effect is for miles around you right?<br /> Hence why im confused by the space requirement for supernal sense, maybe because that spell provides constant info on the locations of active magic.<br /> <br /> Also casting a spell over an entire city causes other headaches, if the spell is not cloaked then every mage in the citys unseen senses will go off, do they all get the chance to counterspell it?<br /> <br /> Ugg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T05:01:01-07:00","id":241223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=240870#post240870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does anybody else have any other ideas? If the ruling Council are not able to do anything they they will look like complete fools and others might start thinking they can get away with breaking the rules etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life mages could use large area scent detecting spells to find him or enchant a few thousand rats or birds to look for him. If a species of vulture can smell a dead body through dense foliage from miles away then a Master of life should be able to smell your mage from a few cityblocks away.<br /> Death mages send lots of ghosts. Did the PC ever do anything that might have anchored a Ghost to him?<br /> Spirit mages can ask and send spirits.<br /> Prime mages can cast large area spell detecting spells to find high powered wards. A potency 50 ward will be like a giant firework to any Prime Master with a good spell of the knowing practice. A prime spell with enhanced area factors cast by a master with several acolytes should be able to cover several blocks or even most of a city to find a specific casters signature or a specific spell.<br /> I don't remember if shield of Chronos protects against Fate spells? A Master of fate could probably walk through the city, throw a coind or something else to decide which direction to go at any street corner and find your Mage by &quot;chance&quot;.<br /> Forces master with fate to send a lifefeed to the Master's smartphone each time your PC walks into view of any Camera in the city.<br /> Mind masters know they can't affect him directly (as he is a Master himself), but a large area knowing spell for the PC's image in the minds of sleepers might detect him. If any sleeper ever sees him, the Masters will know instantly. They might also try to find his Oneiros, though that is risky against a Master of Mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T06:34:33-07:00","id":241293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=241223#post241223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life mages could use large area scent detecting spells to find him or enchant a few thousand rats or birds to look for him. If a species of vulture can smell a dead body through dense foliage from miles away then a Master of life should be able to smell your mage from a few cityblocks away.<br /> Death mages send lots of ghosts. Did the PC ever do anything that might have anchored a Ghost to him?<br /> Spirit mages can ask and send spirits.<br /> Prime mages can cast large area spell detecting spells to find high powered wards. A potency 50 ward will be like a giant firework to any Prime Master with a good spell of the knowing practice. A prime spell with enhanced area factors cast by a master with several acolytes should be able to cover several blocks or even most of a city to find a specific casters signature or a specific spell.<br /> I don't remember if shield of Chronos protects against Fate spells? A Master of fate could probably walk through the city, throw a coind or something else to decide which direction to go at any street corner and find your Mage by &quot;chance&quot;.<br /> Forces master with fate to send a lifefeed to the Master's smartphone each time your PC walks into view of any Camera in the city.<br /> Mind masters know they can't affect him directly (as he is a Master himself), but a large area knowing spell for the PC's image in the minds of sleepers might detect him. If any sleeper ever sees him, the Masters will know instantly. They might also try to find his Oneiros, though that is risky against a Master of Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of using animals with life, spirits via spirit and ghosts via death is a possibility, and while it could take weeks or longer depending on the area to search it might eventually pay off.<br /> <br /> Predatory spirits with numina similar to Know the Path or Communion with the Land gifts from werewolf would have the best chance i think.<br /> As far as i know ghosts have nothing special other than being able to go just about where ever they want in twilight it might also be hard work for them to search for someone if they cant stray far from anchors but lighten anchor spells and would work along with maybe arming ghosts with spells that'd help with the search.<br /> Animals adding extra eyes/noses etc to the search would also help out, it'd just be a matter of time/effort involved.<br /> <br /> So yeh wards themselves are not of the practice of veiling so should show up under prime detections spells, though the example of supernal sense from tome of mysteries suggests otherwise which threw me. As long as you are not using space and then perhaps trying to detect mana possibly with life to detect it in humanoids would narrow the search down.<br /> <br /> A friend suggested that a Fate master could throw a dart at a map and find him easily but that seems a bit far fetched to me. The spell gift of fortune can send items to anybody anywhere so fate can surely find people alright but it requires space. I personally would allow it vs sleepers maybe awakened who you wanted to bump into randomly as long as they were not specifically going to any great lengths to hide themselves, fate can only be stretched so far. Bumping into somebody in his pocket realm is also unlikely which is fortunate that said mage hasnt the matter or life to be able to stay inside his pocket realm without breathing equipment for extended periods of time.<br /> <br /> Oh and its not my PC, its an others. We have been discussing possible methods of finding him for weeks now and its come down to deciding that with enough time and effort Mages can make anything happen (who knew right?) and that a lot of reasons why something doesnt happen is because of the time/effort and motivation involved, abit like a nuclear stand off in a cold war.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T07:02:22-07:00","id":241304,"title":"","content":"Nah, not a spirit.<br /> <br /> Your best bet is a <i>Shade</i>. Have the Consilium put together a team of Moros and summon a supernal entity to find him. Potentially very risky indeed, and using a sledgehammer to crack a nut, but when a job's worth doing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T08:21:09-07:00","id":241369,"title":"","content":"In the Astral Realms book there's a Space spell that lets you cast Space spells during it's duration to move between layers of the Astral. At mastery you can also cast space spells between the Fallen and the Astral, so yeah you can go bodily to the Astral without being an Archmaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T13:23:14-07:00","id":241647,"title":"","content":"Actually, no, you can't. That spell just lets you directly enter a layer of the Astral as usual but without the long meditation, so you can just cast the spell and enter a particular Temenos realm. Your body is still behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T17:45:09-07:00","id":241854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nah, not a spirit.<br /> <br /> Your best bet is a <i>Shade</i>. Have the Consilium put together a team of Moros and summon a supernal entity to find him. Potentially very risky indeed, and using a sledgehammer to crack a nut, but when a job's worth doing... </div> </div> </div>Forgot all about summoning supernal beings and all the cool stuff in the summoners book though ochema had been discussed had it been the seers problem. Doh. Any particular reason for a shade? Guessing any supernal being, or even royal avatars etc could do the job?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, no, you can't. That spell just lets you directly enter a layer of the Astral as usual but without the long meditation, so you can just cast the spell and enter a particular Temenos realm. Your body is still behind. </div> </div> </div>Thats what i thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T04:03:13-07:00","id":242144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=241854#post241854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgot all about summoning supernal beings and all the cool stuff in the summoners book though ochema had been discussed had it been the seers problem. Doh. Any particular reason for a shade? Guessing any supernal being, or even royal avatars etc could do the job?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I somehow picked up the notion that the mage they were looking for was a Moros.<br /> <br /> A supernal being of whichever path your fugitive is would be best. After that, probably an Angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:25:21-07:00","id":250743,"title":"","content":"This is ridiculously newbie but...<br /> <b>New Question</b>: What the hell is magic? Is it drawing down the supernal, bending reality to your will, using higher truths to alter reality or something different? And are the supernal realms actual realms, or just metaphors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T08:19:27-07:00","id":250772,"title":"","content":"Ok, short opinions because I tend to ramble otherwise. A lot. <br /> <br /> Magic isn't really knowable. Mages know it exists, they think they kind of get how it works, but magic is just as magical to them as it is to us which is one of the reasons they're so obsessed with finding answers to all their crazy questions. Make up a theory or use a metaphor that seems to accurately describe what's going on.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you've been following the devblogs but there's some hints for the Supernal Realms. There are realms in the sense of &quot;not on earth&quot; only because they exist purely in the abstract because they're idealic forms that are too pure to touch the Fallen world at all. It's not like you can just point to a cosmological map though and say, &quot;Here's Supernal Australia.&quot; Most of the time Mages are dealing the Supernal World which is kind of like Twilight if you imagine Twilight to be a different frequency of existence rather than a place you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T13:34:39-07:00","id":251023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DahQueenDiva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=250743#post250743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it drawing down the supernal</div> </div> </div> </div>yes<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> bending reality to your will </div> </div> </div>yes<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> using higher truths to alter reality </div> </div> </div>yes<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or something different? </div> </div> </div>yes<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And are the supernal realms actual realms </div> </div> </div>no<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or just metaphors? </div> </div> </div>kinda<br /> <br /> Edit: On the subject of the Supernal, I reccomend <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/falling-down/\" target=\"_blank\">those</a> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\">two</a> blog posts from Dave Brookshaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 09-06-2014, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T06:57:52-07:00","id":251434,"title":"","content":"As my player plans committing murder by magic - is Postcognition ( Time 2 ) needing to touch target to discern it's timeline? Is advanced mages of Time could cast it without the target - like &quot;we know Mr X is gone, let's look for him in timestream&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T07:11:17-07:00","id":251438,"title":"","content":"Postcognition requires you to know exactly what time you want to be looking at, Space would be required if you don't have the target whose past you're looking at present. So if you can figure out the last time the target was seen in order to get as close to the time of his disappearance as possible then you can keep casting Postcognition or ritual cast it for a much longer vision until you see what happened to him to make him disappear. Provided of course that the reason he's gone didn't involve a Shield of Chronos or a Time Erasure spell at some point anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T10:19:07-07:00","id":251547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=251434#post251434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As my player plans committing murder by magic - is Postcognition ( Time 2 ) needing to touch target to discern it's timeline? Is advanced mages of Time could cast it without the target - like &quot;we know Mr X is gone, let's look for him in timestream&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you know someone that is planning to commit murder, via any means, and they think mages might be investigating it the best advice would be to change his mind. Mages will find you and Time would be the least of your problems. Time 2s Post-Cognition power is a really versatile recording device, but it's little more than that. You cast the spell at a location and can view almost any point in time at that location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T17:05:08-07:00","id":251767,"title":"","content":"It's more a dilemma - can mage assasinate a mage? Victim-to-be is local Curator. From my own all analyzis, once body is found any Adept level Awakened can solve a crime in one evening. So what if there wouldn't be any body to begin with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T19:53:02-07:00","id":251879,"title":"","content":"Even if there is no body, there are still sympathetic connections. So anybody with Time could figure out what happened. &quot;If&quot; they asked the right questions. You could obfuscate the event with magic, even set booby traps if somebody starts snooping.<br /> <br /> The other way would be to manipulate events so that somebody else would be blamed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T14:32:23-07:00","id":252665,"title":"","content":"The Guardians will tell you it's entirely possible to assassinate a Mage and get away with it, and if you do get caught make sure you have lots of real or convincing fake evidence for why it was a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:48:31-07:00","id":252897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=252665#post252665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guardians will tell you it's entirely possible to assassinate a Mage and get away with it, and if you do get caught make sure you have lots of real or convincing fake evidence for why it was a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>Guardians</i> can... they have a whole support system in the form a religious mafia cartel to help them do it. A lone mage doing the same thing would need to be at least an Apprentice in each of the Arcana to have a ghost of a chance of going after a <i>Curator</i>... of all people... A Curator is not going to be easy to get the drop on. She would have gotten to her position by, most likely, doing this very same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T21:36:36-07:00","id":252978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=252897#post252897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, <i>Guardians</i> can... they have a whole support system in the form a religious mafia cartel to help them do it. A lone mage doing the same thing would need to be at least an Apprentice in each of the Arcana to have a ghost of a chance of going after a <i>Curator</i>... of all people... A Curator is not going to be easy to get the drop on. She would have gotten to her position by, most likely, doing this very same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By doing this very same thing.... do you mean being an apprentice of all the arcana, or murdering the previous Curator?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:58:21-07:00","id":253233,"title":"","content":"In agreement with the others here, a successful murder of another mage that doesn't get traced back requires a well coordinated team of at least Adepts and if at all possible the target should not have many friends and weak cabalmates.<br /> Between the target's cabal, Legacy-mates, friends in the Order, their old teacher and possible students, the victim's Ghost (or, worse, if they were a Death mage their Revenant) the list of highly skilled people that might comer after you can be long and powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T05:09:20-07:00","id":253239,"title":"","content":"Question: What's the difference between Azazel described in <i>&quot;Astral Realms&quot;</i> and Azazel described in &quot;<i>Inferno&quot;</i>? Or they are the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2511-broskandar","name":"Broskandar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T06:00:08-07:00","id":253260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broskandar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=253239#post253239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: What's the difference between Azazel described in <i>&amp;quot;Astral Realms&amp;quot;</i> and Azazel described in &amp;quot;<i>Inferno&amp;quot;</i>? Or they are the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Astral Realms are the (sometimes collective) subconscious of living things. As such, Azazel in AR is the archetypal Azazel that living creatures imagine Azezal to be ... Sort of.<br /> <br /> Inferno Azazel would be the &quot;real&quot; Azazel, insofar as there is such a being (compared to an abyssal entity that would call itself such, or a creature from the underworld, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T07:11:39-07:00","id":253281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=252978#post252978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> By doing this very same thing.... do you mean being an apprentice of all the arcana, or murdering the previous Curator?</div> </div> </div> </div>By doing whatever it takes to recover, protect, and preserve magic. The Mysterium is &quot;worse&quot; than the Guardians of the Veil. You can trust the Guardians to do their duty, to uphold their morality in service to their cause. The Mysterium is amoral. Knowledge has a price. Knowledge is power. Knowledge must be preserved. That's their morality. Notice that there is nothing in there about people ... which is different from ALL the other Orders.<br /> <br /> How do you think you recover a relic from a Seer stronghold? How do you stop the Guardians of the Veil from destroying a grimoire?<br /> <br /> You break a few eggs.<br /> <br /> That's what I meant about the Curator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T00:15:15-07:00","id":258831,"title":"","content":"I have two Mastigos in my gaming group. One specialized in Mind, one in Space (both are masters and have 5 dots in their chosen specialty Arcana). I give you the scenario and want to know if it is possible:<br /> <br /> They encountered an enemy Mage of the Seers who used a Profane Urim. The Mind mage wants to read the Seers mind to get the memory of where the real body is. Once he got the mental image of the cellar, he wants to give the Space mage this image in his mind via telepathy. The Space mage would then use this image to teleport them both to the Seers real body and coup-de-grace him while his mind is in another body.<br /> <br /> The questions:<br /> 1) Is this possible?<br /> 2) If yes, what would the connection be? (They are aiming for a -4 becaue of the picture in the mind, but that doesn't sit well with me. But it is definately more than described... so, -6? -8?)<br /> 3) What happens if the body dies? Living on in the hijacked body till the spell from the Profane Urim wears out? Ghost Mage? Other?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;...and then we discovered it wasn't the Robot King after all, it was the real one. Fortunately I was able to reattach the head.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/644-mcbaine","name":"McBaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T01:29:19-07:00","id":258855,"title":"","content":"1. Totally possible IMHO, i don't see any abuse in this.<br /> 2. I'd say -6. A bit worse than currently scrying the location<br /> 3. Your guess. I'd say it depends on where the seers soul is. If it is in his original body then he dies, If it occupies the hijacked body when he lives till the spell ends and then ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T03:57:25-07:00","id":258907,"title":"","content":"1. You can totally do that, it's actually a pretty cool teamwork solution. Kudos on those players.<br /> <br /> 2. -4 I'll count a direct mind image as seeing it remotely, like a picture or a tv program.<br /> <br /> 3. By default, the Seer just gets violently back to his own body. He could get some penalties due to shock or even gain a permanent derangement for the experience at the Storyteller's discretion. Maybe, and just maybe, you can work a Mind-Space(maybe also Death) spell so it gets trapped in the pupetted body and dies with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T07:26:24-07:00","id":258973,"title":"","content":"Thorbes he's talking about killing the seers original body. I find it hard to believe that returning to a corpse with say it's head cut off would end with just an derangement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T08:14:23-07:00","id":258985,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow, my bad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's trickier. Technically he dies, but maybe he can live on in the stolen body. He probably stop being a mage. A ghost mage is also an option, or he can live as a Morphean into the sleeper's body's Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T10:27:44-07:00","id":259034,"title":"","content":"Theres a spell that allows you to share sympathetic connections you have with other people, i dont remember the book but it is pretty OP. Also once you have even the weakest of links to something be sure to cast new threads asap to raise your connection up to intimate.<br /> <br /> So the spell is in the seers of throne book and is space 3 its called duplicate sympathy and causes me all sorts of headaches in games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 09-17-2014, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T00:14:57-07:00","id":259592,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers. I guess I settle for -5 as a sympathetic connection (even a clear memory is IMHO not as good as seeing something on a photo or in a scrying window, but it is the next best thing I guess).<br /> I will go with the ghost mage. Should open up some interesting story oportunities. <br /> One other thing: They will have access to the Profane Urim the Seer uses... are there any drawbacks? Is possessing someone a Wisdom sin? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;...and then we discovered it wasn't the Robot King after all, it was the real one. Fortunately I was able to reattach the head.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/644-mcbaine","name":"McBaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T02:52:06-07:00","id":259637,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Sympathetic penalties are always even. Either -4 or -6.<br /> <br /> Yeah, of course possesing someone is a Wisdom sin, you are stealing his body and bullying his consciounes into a corner. There are few things more horrible that you can do to a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T04:44:34-07:00","id":259691,"title":"","content":"what is more powerful the Aeons,or Ascended Mages<br /> <br /> and what is the Old Gods","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T12:46:29-07:00","id":259966,"title":"","content":"I have no idea which is more powerful between the Aeons and an Ascended Mage but probably the Mage if only by virtue of flexibility.<br /> <br /> The Old Gods are the gods that ruled in the Supernal Realms before the Exarchs came upstairs and kicked them out. Quite a few of them are still around, just elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T00:54:15-07:00","id":260414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=259966#post259966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Old Gods are the gods that ruled in the Supernal Realms before the Exarchs came upstairs and kicked them out. Quite a few of them are still around, just elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>And probably part of them are True Fae of <b>Changling</b>'s Arcadia, at was implied in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T02:34:05-07:00","id":262732,"title":"","content":"Quick question: As my players might visit the Underworld during our next game in need to get to know that place a bit better. Where can i find something about it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T03:54:23-07:00","id":262755,"title":"","content":"Book of the Dead has both info about the underworld and some sidebar mechanics for including Mages. Maybe somebody can point out more specific pages? I don't happen to have it in front of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/825-magiuspendragon","name":"magiuspendragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T18:06:42-07:00","id":265834,"title":"","content":"What exactly are the Dur-Abzu, from what I can recall they are Abyss reflections of the Watchtowers but can't remember if that's it. also what is the Sixth Watchtower, there have clues about that in the core book but was it ever confirmed and if it was what is it.<br /> <br /> And just a fun little question, what would you think would happen if one would write their name on te Sixth Dragon( the Tremere Watchtower of vampires)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T01:37:49-07:00","id":266051,"title":"","content":"The Dur-Abzu are indeed the Abysal and twisted reflections of the 5 Watchtowers. They turn the lemental asociations of the originals upside down, among other things (the one from the Aether originally heavily asociated with Fire is a cold, dark, underwater dwellling, for example).<br /> <br /> The sixth Watchtower remains a mystery (Mystery?) though the Tremere will tell you its the Soul one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T08:57:53-07:00","id":268288,"title":"","content":"How many mages die of natural causes (old age, disease) vs. being eaten by their experiments/ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T18:18:00-07:00","id":268646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=268288#post268288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many mages die of natural causes (old age, disease) vs. being eaten by their experiments/ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever works in your story for old age versus accidents. There are very few archmages though, usually described as less than 100. And since they are immortal (or essentially are, since they no longer have a physical body that will die), we don't know how many mages reach archmastery at a time (those 100 could be composed of a pool from several centuties). And even though they may not have a physical body per se, even archmages can be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Ascension itself is a rare event, and as written, the setting pot rays it as something only a few mages have ever succeed in. Even archmasters, who have a path layer out for their possible ascension, aren't guaranteed success. <br /> <br /> In the end, it depends on how you and your storyteller build your games setting. That said, as the original setting potrays it, expect lots of mages to die from conflicts/accidents/hubris with a good number dying from old age, a small minority achieving archmastery, and only a few ascending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:15:21-07:00","id":269095,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget Tremere and life-stealing Moros; they probably wonk the numbers a bit, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T14:13:57-07:00","id":269486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=268646#post268646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever works in your story for old age versus accidents. There are very few archmages though, usually described as less than 100. And since they are immortal (or essentially are, since they no longer have a physical body that will die), we don't know how many mages reach archmastery at a time (those 100 could be composed of a pool from several centuties). And even though they may not have a physical body per se, even archmages can be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Ascension itself is a rare event, and as written, the setting pot rays it as something only a few mages have ever succeed in. Even archmasters, who have a path layer out for their possible ascension, aren't guaranteed success.<br /> <br /> In the end, it depends on how you and your storyteller build your games setting. That said, as the original setting potrays it, expect lots of mages to die from conflicts/accidents/hubris with a good number dying from old age, a small minority achieving archmastery, and only a few ascending.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand that I can tweak per story needs, I was just wondering what the default assumption was. (It's been a while since I've done more than just flip-reference the source material.) My reason for asking was because it would strongly influence how mentors approach apprentices - and how mages might assess their own mortality.<br /> <br /> For example, a mentor probably isn't likely to invest much time / effort into students if they've witnessed 10 of their former students pass away. (Whether out of a desire to avoid watching another one die, or just not wanting to waste their time.)<br /> <br /> It also influences how one interprets sample cabals like the Ebon Noose... where only ~ two members seem to remain from a cabal which has had a roster since at least the 80s (if not far, far longer). What happened to the rest of the Nemean's (approximate) contemporaries, or even the apprentices of the 90s (considering Tiamat is more of a transfer, and the Axe seems a relatively recent arrival - and the rest of the members are relatively young, iirc). Did they die, move on to new cabals, get eaten, etc. The assumed answer leans with the conceit.<br /> <br /> Additionally, some might feel like they should be constantly pruning their NPCs, if it's rare for mages to make it past a certain mark.<br /> <br /> Etc., etc., I'm tired and dumb, don't mind me and my minutia b***s***.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T15:21:40-07:00","id":269529,"title":"","content":"No, no I think it is a good question. I think it is a triple spike of mortality: pre-/early apprenticship, when the mage knows nothing and thus has no control. Then a lull while they learn under a mentor. After they establish themselves and have enough skill to really get into trouble, it spikes again as the more hubristic mages burnout. The final spike is late into mastery, as age and skill make the mage more willing to pursue risky and complex spells and acts so as to achieve their end goals before they pass (whether these goals be archmastery, immortality, ascension) and thus face greater mortality (plus, they are old so they die of old age).<br /> <br /> I also think it is order dependent. For example, the AA is likely to have a higher attrition rate than say, the SL, as their nature is conflict and their role is warrior sages.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think we could expand this more, but I am on call and need to get back to the wards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:28:36-07:00","id":270141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=269529#post269529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I think we could expand this more, but I am on call and need to get back to the wards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get to it! We don't want pervy outsiders scrying our sanctum!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:57:30-07:00","id":270154,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q:</b> Is there a nWoD LFG post anywhere? Does anyone have recommendations on how to find a group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Continuing to look for a nWoD group in Pennsylvania along 81 near Carlisle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","name":"lunavoco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T12:28:59-07:00","id":270271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=270141#post270141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get to it! We don't want pervy outsiders scrying our sanctum!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, medical wards. I realized that after I posted it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T20:26:13-07:00","id":273446,"title":"","content":"What Rank is Ascended beings(Oracles,Exarchs,etc),? I would guess at least 8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T23:12:19-07:00","id":273498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=273446#post273446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Rank is Ascended beings(Oracles,Exarchs,etc),? I would guess at least 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the 10th Arcanum dot in Imperial Mysteries is equated with Ascension... I'd put them around Rank 8 as well. They're at that point unchallenged in their influence over 1/10th of reality. Assuming that the hypothetical Rank 10 has complete control over all reality, I think it could then also be assumed that Rank 9s would have that level of mastery over multiple aspects of reality... so Rank 8 would be the point around which an Ascended Archmaster would fit in.<br /> <br /> In Imperial Mysteries it also lists Gaea as Rank 9 and says that no Archmaster has ever encountered Her, or if any have, none have survived to tell of it... which indicates that all Archmasters are below Rank 9 in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 10-06-2014, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T12:46:37-07:00","id":281386,"title":"","content":"So in 2E a Seer Prelate can turn a demense into a Supernal Verge keyed to their patron Exarch. What happens when their patron Exarch is the Gate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:38:33-07:00","id":281419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=281386#post281386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in 2E a Seer Prelate can turn a demense into a Supernal Verge keyed to their patron Exarch. What happens when their patron Exarch is the Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Abyssal Verge maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T11:32:03-07:00","id":283995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=281419#post281419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Abyssal Verge maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first thought as well. I'm curious as to whether the Developers had something different in mind though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T21:36:54-07:00","id":284611,"title":"","content":"Question! What's the mechanical difference between lesser and greater spirit summons? What's the benefit of using the vulgar spell vs. the lower covert one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3905-llewyd42","name":"Llewyd42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T02:20:14-07:00","id":284787,"title":"","content":"As far as i remember without looking in the book:<br /> Lesser summons a spirit that's on this side of the Gauntlet, either materialized or in twilight.<br /> Greater summons a spirit from across the Gauntlet from the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T07:42:55-07:00","id":284944,"title":"","content":"I've read a wonderful peace of fanfiction couple of months ago but can't find it anymore. It was a story from the age of Atlantis told from the perspective of Father. Can someone provide me a link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T23:02:53-07:00","id":288365,"title":"","content":"New Question: Is there a half decent collection of all the rotes published so far for me to print out for my players? I've seen a couple kicking around online, but I was wondering if there was a definitive resource that folks consider reliable.<br /> <br /> My players are coming from 2 years of Vampire: the Masquerade and a list of rotes might help them acclimatise to their new power and potential!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3126-matlock-mcguthers","name":"Matlock McGuthers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3126_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T23:12:38-07:00","id":288370,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Spells\" target=\"_blank\">Right here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:44:08-08:00","id":301019,"title":"","content":"New here! Hello to y'all.<br /> My question might seem stupid, but I can't find the freaking dmg mechanics for acid/corrosive substances. Lethal, aggravated, progressive, healable?<br /> Regarding acidic spatter, it mentions that it's bashing dmg, but it also says that it's a weak acid... In higher levels of the ars, i could make it quite the nasty one. And then?<br /> <br /> Sry for the newbieshness! <br /> <br /> PS:Just created a Life + Matter tamer of rivers, and I'm in love with her :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4230-faustvii","name":"FaustVII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4230_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T03:04:54-08:00","id":301995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FaustVII</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=301019#post301019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New here! Hello to y'all.<br /> My question might seem stupid, but I can't find the freaking dmg mechanics for acid/corrosive substances. Lethal, aggravated, progressive, healable?<br /> Regarding acidic spatter, it mentions that it's bashing dmg, but it also says that it's a weak acid... In higher levels of the ars, i could make it quite the nasty one. And then?<br /> <br /> Sry for the newbieshness!<br /> <br /> PS:Just created a Life + Matter tamer of rivers, and I'm in love with her :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly don't think it has been codified anywhere. <br /> I'd base the mechanics on fire, actually. Three stats instead of two, though. <br /> Coverage: How much of the victim is covered in acid. From 0 to 3, where 0 is just a small drop, and 3 is completely drenched. <br /> Strength: How much damage the acid does per turn. From 0 to 3. With three being highly concentrated sulphuric acid, or aqua regis, or so. <br /> Type: What type of damage does it do. From Bashing to Aggravated. Although I would keep Agg acid for the magically created stuff and so. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, after exposure it to the acid, you decide how much coverage the victim got, and the strength of the acid, and apply that amount of damage of the chosen type, repeat every turn until the acid is washed away, or the victim dead. <br /> <br /> Armor reduces coverage, possibly down to none, depending on how much it covers, but the acid will work on that to...<br /> <br /> Overpowered? Probably, but I just pulled this off of the top of my head, so don't expect perfection. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T07:03:46-08:00","id":302111,"title":"","content":"There should also be some kind of max damage per acid exposure based on the amount spilled (Coverage) and the Strength of the acid, because the acid is being used in the chemical reaction.<br /> So no infinite damage as long as the person does not clean the acid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:30:34-08:00","id":302438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=302111#post302111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should also be some kind of max damage per acid exposure based on the amount spilled (Coverage) and the Strength of the acid, because the acid is being used in the chemical reaction.<br /> So no infinite damage as long as the person does not clean the acid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean like fire isn't an infinitely ticking thing now? Yes, the acid will eventually stop burning through the vic, but will she be still alive by then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:18:38-08:00","id":356964,"title":"","content":"The Read Matrices (Forces 1) spell explicitly mentions things like gamma and radio waves, but at -3 difficulty. Then there is spell Tune In, that lets you listen in on any electromagnetic noise. There is also Nighsight that lets you<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She can essentially perceive the infrared or ultraviolet spectrum and detect electromagnetic radiation, or sonic or kinetic energy. </div> </div> </div>1. Would it be possible to have Forces 1 Gamma Sight, that would let you see through walls?<br /> 2. Would that spell let you cast spells on target withing locked room as sensory as long as you are in the 200 yards range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:21:40-08:00","id":357081,"title":"","content":"You would be able to change your perceptions to be able to see ambient gamma radiation in the area. If that's a type of radiation that's ambient and clings to forms or is shaped in some way in order to allow you to see things on the other side of solid objects then yes. I know nothing about gamma radiation and I'm assuming that's x-Ray radiation and that it's not actually ambient so while possible it's kind of a niche case. If I'm wrong then it's just damn clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T20:04:46-08:00","id":357165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=356964#post356964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Read Matrices (Forces 1) spell explicitly mentions things like gamma and radio waves, but at -3 difficulty. Then there is spell Tune In, that lets you listen in on any electromagnetic noise. There is also Nighsight that lets you<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Would it be possible to have Forces 1 Gamma Sight, that would let you see through walls?<br /> 2. Would that spell let you cast spells on target withing locked room as sensory as long as you are in the 200 yards range?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes. But there's very litlle ambient gamma (or anything higher than near UV, really) in most Terran environments, and almost nothing reflects it, so lokking through a wall won't be useful since anything that penetrates the wall will also penetrate whatever's beyond the wall.<br /> 2. I'd say no. You couldn't get a clear enough image for targetting.<br /> <br /> One way to get around the need for a conventional sightline would be to use a Space 1/Life 1/Matter 1 conjunctional spell to give yourself something like the &quot;sense of perception&quot; from the Lensman novels. You can &quot;see&quot; in every direction, directly aware of every living and non-living thing within that volume (limit yourself to living things larger than ants, just for your own sanity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T05:41:35-08:00","id":357425,"title":"","content":"You really only need 1 dot of whichever arcana is the purview of the thing you want to target to create an Unveiling effect that locates the desired target(s) inside of sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T05:51:52-08:00","id":357427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=357425#post357425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really only need 1 dot of whichever arcana is the purview of the thing you want to target to create an Unveiling effect that locates the desired target(s) inside of sensory range.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll need a dot of Space to pinpoint exactly where those are though. The Unveiling spell will only inform you of the number and roughly the &quot;type&quot; of the pattern (say, Life could tell you that in a radius of X yards around you there are 3 life forms, two of wich are human, and another is a dog but not where they are with respect to you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T06:21:46-08:00","id":357434,"title":"","content":"That seems unlikely. Occasions where spells demanded multiple Arcana to cover all of their apparent effects were always an awkward holdover from Ascension, and Dave has stated that they'll be basically excised. A spell to detect things (which would be a Knowing, not an Unveiling, mind) but don't give you a sense of where they are is silly. Space Knowings should be about detections of things to do with spatial relations, just as the entire Arcanum should be, not something you use to supplement other spells so that you can actually range them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T09:47:38-08:00","id":357556,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I heard that in the Second Edition, Atlantis is a story instead of a real place. What do I do if I want to include characters from First Edition that originate from Atlantis, such as the Somnia Draconis (Night Horrors - The Unbidden)? Do Mages in the Second Edition have a mostly agreed upon origin, or multiple conflicting theories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T09:58:51-08:00","id":357563,"title":"","content":"The real place was erased from the timeline through magic of the highest level (Imperium). <br /> <br /> The erasure was not perfect, ruins, remnants and artifacts are still found, even though atlantis never existed in this timeline.<br /> <br /> This was the case for 1. Edition. It is still the case in 2. Edition.<br /> <br /> Those characters are as fine as they were in first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI have long since forsaken mortal blood. It offers me nothing but the stale taste of mayflies. I have partaken of Luna's ever-changing children and dined on the scholars of Magic. I have bled monsters, born and created. No more. Tonight I drink the blood of gods and slake my thirst for another thousand years of night.\u201d","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/312-grunt","name":"Grunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T10:04:58-08:00","id":357566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grunt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=357563#post357563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real place was erased from the timeline through magic of the highest level (Imperium).<br /> <br /> The erasure was not perfect, ruins, remnants and artifacts are still found, even though atlantis never existed in this timeline.<br /> <br /> This was the case for 1. Edition. It is still the case in 2. Edition.<br /> <br /> Those characters are as fine as they were in first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T16:08:23-08:00","id":357862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=357427#post357427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll need a dot of Space to pinpoint exactly where those are though. The Unveiling spell will only inform you of the number and roughly the &quot;type&quot; of the pattern (say, Life could tell you that in a radius of X yards around you there are 3 life forms, two of wich are human, and another is a dog but not where they are with respect to you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Per <b>MtAw p.114</b> it is possible to cast spells as &quot;sensory range&quot; using hearing or smell (at penalty).<br /> <br /> My idea was to use Forces 1 to bypass the &quot;veiling&quot; effect of solid wall to normal light by using &quot;x-ray|gamma lengths&quot;.<br /> If the ambient radiation is not enough secondary (combined) effect similar to Nightsight could be used.<br /> If that is not enough, Forces 2 lets you increase|decrease the intensity further.<br /> At that point you should have direct sensory range at even better resolution than normal sight. (Inspiration here is Superman and his x-ray vision.)<br /> Something similar should be possible for sound to give you sensory perception similar to Daredevil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T05:04:00-08:00","id":358215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=357434#post357434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems unlikely. Occasions where spells demanded multiple Arcana to cover all of their apparent effects were always an awkward holdover from Ascension, and Dave has stated that they'll be basically excised. A spell to detect things (which would be a Knowing, not an Unveiling, mind) but don't give you a sense of where they are is silly. Space Knowings should be about detections of things to do with spatial relations, just as the entire Arcanum should be, not something you use to supplement other spells so that you can actually range them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree, but I was under the impresion the question pertained to 1st edition mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T14:00:03-08:00","id":358552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=358215#post358215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree, but I was under the impresion the question pertained to 1st edition mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't it work under 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T03:59:23-08:00","id":360098,"title":"","content":"In 1st edition the &quot;Detect whatever&quot; spells need a dot of Space to exactly pinpoint the location of each relevant pattern in the area. As Isator pointed out, thats highly likely not to be the case in 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T08:35:15-08:00","id":360221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=360098#post360098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1st edition the &quot;Detect whatever&quot; spells need a dot of Space to exactly pinpoint the location of each relevant pattern in the area. As Isator pointed out, thats highly likely not to be the case in 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. It's like the difference between walking into a room and picking up a strange smell... You might even know what that spell is... &quot;It smells like a wet dog in here...&quot; And then it takes effort on your part to track the smell down to it's source. If you had Space 1, you wouldn't need to expend all that effort. You would be able to know, see, follow what you've detected directly to its source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T08:25:17-08:00","id":369758,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit to the amount you can increase the gauntlet strength by using spells or abilities. I know the chart stops at 5 but it doesnt say anywhere that the max is 5? Ofc its moot for the purpose my player wanted to use it for (to stop a spirit escaping back through the gauntlet) as the materialize numina doesnt even give penalties to the spirits attempt to cross the gauntlet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T10:11:10-08:00","id":369832,"title":"","content":"I believe that's because Materialize doesn't allow them to cross the Guantlet at all unless the Spirit also has the Reach numen. Materialize normally is used in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T10:52:34-08:00","id":369870,"title":"","content":"The implied max, from my reading, is 6. Under most normal circumstance, it only goes to 5, however conditions can make an area spiritually deadened, or the gauntlet can be supernaturally raised. The result of it getting bolstered is a Barrens (Book of Spirits, 73): a place of spiritual emptiness, resulting from a strong disconnect between Material and Shadow. Ordinarily this only happens with supernatural bolstering (ie, the Azlu), but they naturally occur in tn the most bleak parts of dense cities: mostly office farms, and possibly hospitals where people are kept too heavily medicated to act. I don't think going beyond this would be possible, as Barrens are pretty much &quot;there is nothing in this part of the Shadow&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:59:15-08:00","id":370156,"title":"","content":"<b>MtAw p. 283</b> describes the rules for Paradox in Shadow Realm, I remember that somewhere were rules for Paradox in Twilight and Astral, but I could not recall where. Could you point me in the right direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:39:02-08:00","id":370218,"title":"","content":"Check Astral Realms for rules on Paradid there. Usually you'll only suffer Paradox in the Oneiros of a Sleeper, or Banisher or if Abyssal Astral Entities crop up.<br /> <br /> I don't know the rules about Paradox in Twilight, my guess is that it either stays the same or is a -2 as in Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T06:44:32-08:00","id":372473,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q</b>: What dice pool would you use for mundane &quot;magic&quot; card and coin tricks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T06:50:59-08:00","id":372488,"title":"","content":"Dexterity or Manipulation + Larceny (maybe Subterfuge)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T11:12:35-08:00","id":375398,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q:</b> The <b>Magic Shield, MtAw 222</b> is a nice thing against other Mages, but it is totally useless against normal Sleepers. If I want to add the effect of <b>Unseen Shield, MtAw 167</b> (or shield from any other Arcana), do I cast it as conjuctional or as combined spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T09:00:03-08:00","id":376307,"title":"","content":"This requires a combined casting of two spells. You have two separate effects that need to happen, so two spells, so Combined spells.<br /> <br /> Conjunctional is ONE spell that takes knowledge of another arcana to pull off. Want to cast a life spell on a ghost? You need to know how ghosts tick, so add Death \u2022\u2022 to the Life spell and fire away. Speaking of fire, do you want to turn into a ball of fire? Life allows you to change your shape, but Fire isn't governed by life. So you need to add Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 to the spell and your good. Either way, it's One spell with an effect that requires knowledge of multiple arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Continuing to look for a nWoD group in Pennsylvania along 81 near Carlisle.","edited":{"userid":1050,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","user":"lunavoco","date":". 01-20-2015, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1050-lunavoco","name":"lunavoco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:23:06-08:00","id":382233,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q: </b>Can Aponoia prevent awakenings? To be clear: If an archmage (or other equivalent being) messes with the Tellurian and alters events, can a previously awakened person become a sleeper in the changed world? Or does it requires specifically going to the watchtower and erasing that persons's name, or killing him in the past before he awakens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:33:04-08:00","id":382243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=382233#post382233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>New Q: </b>Can Aponoia prevent awakenings? To be clear: If an archmage (or other equivalent being) messes with the Tellurian and alters events, can a previously awakened person become a sleeper in the changed world? Or does it requires specifically going to the watchtower and erasing that persons's name, or killing him in the past before he awakens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the story describing how the threshold process unfolds specifically has the mage return to a world where the apprentice that he failed never existed without him intending to wipe him from existence, and a mage he banished as an oathbreaker seems to be some guy on the street (Though his awakened status isn't clarified). I could definitely see Aponia resulting in mages losing their awakened status... while sleepers become mages who had awakened years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T09:59:18-08:00","id":385224,"title":"","content":"Does use Mind for seduce someone's is a Wisdom Sin 10 if the mage don't do it hid/her pleasure and would be unable to seduce this person without magic ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:12:27-08:00","id":385237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=385224#post385224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does use Mind for seduce someone's is a Wisdom Sin 10 if the mage don't do it hid/her pleasure and would be unable to seduce this person without magic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if I fully understand the question, so apologies beforehand if the answer is not what you were looking for:<br /> <br /> Wisdom 10 means using magic for something you could do just as fine without it is a sin, yes. The mage couldn't ever seduced that somene without magic, so it is arguable it doesn't count against that. Is still a Wisdom sin at Wisdom 10 because manipulating the emotions of someone with magic is a sin way down that scale, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:43:06-08:00","id":385348,"title":"","content":"Adding on to that if you use Mind to buff -yourself- to succeed at seducing someone then I don't think it's a Wisdom sin at all. I could be wrong, but it would still be a less &quot;bad&quot; sin than manipulating the other person with Mind directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:58:18-08:00","id":385426,"title":"","content":"Ah, now that's a grey area!<br /> <br /> Yeah, I completely forgot about the social boosting spells of Mind and directly asumed Sulery Drals meant something like Love Spell when they talk about using magic to seduce someone (wich they might not be refering to).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T13:17:01-08:00","id":385479,"title":"","content":"Agreed. The question if what defines &quot;using magic to achieve something you could do without magic&quot; can go both ways with the example. On one hand, if you read it as the action, most people can attempt to get better at seduction with practice, and thus boosting that skill magically dings Wisdom 10.on the other hand, you could argue that succeeding at seduction is one thing you could never do without magic (...ouch) or at least not with said person, and thus you are indirectly using magic to succeed at a task impossible without magic (the direct method being the much worse wisdom sin of directly altering their view of you). Honestly, no idea where this falls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T03:37:39-08:00","id":386115,"title":"","content":"I was thinking, maybe the Social boost could be equated to those profesional athletes that cheat using drugs to increase their performance. It is morally questionable. Not sure where in the Wisdom scale it should fall though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:35:46-08:00","id":386201,"title":"","content":"I don't have my books at the moment, so does dishonesty fall on the scale anywhere?<br /> <br /> I know selfish thoughts are a Wisdom 10 sin though and boosting yourself with magic for a goal like seduction probably qualifies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:39:18-08:00","id":386204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386115#post386115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking, maybe the Social boost could be equated to those profesional athletes that cheat using drugs to increase their performance. It is morally questionable. Not sure where in the Wisdom scale it should fall though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The counter would be that you are using a natural talent to make yourself more desirable. Not your fault that not everyone can warp reality, am I right?<br /> <br /> (Note that I actually take your view on the moral grayness. I just am using what a player in a similar situation argued in my game)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:39:20-08:00","id":386205,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Wisdom 10 prohibit you from using any magic ever though? I mean, you can (potentially) achieve pretty much everything without using magic. Want to save a dying person? Perform first aid or call a doctor. Want to kill a person? Use a gun. Want a rare grimoire from the astral realms? Find a professional astral explorer. In a world where other mages exist you can (potentially) achieve anything you want without using magic yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:42:08-08:00","id":386211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386204#post386204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The counter would be that you are using a natural talent to make yourself more desirable. Not your fault that not everyone can warp reality, am I right?<br /> <br /> (Note that I actually take your view on the moral grayness. I just am using what a player in a similar situation argued in my game)</div> </div> </div> </div>The counter to that would be that you are using magic instead of working out, practicing your oratory skills and being a nicer person in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:47:07-08:00","id":386238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386205#post386205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Wisdom 10 prohibit you from using any magic ever though? I mean, you can (potentially) achieve pretty much everything without using magic. Want to save a dying person? Perform first aid or call a doctor. Want to kill a person? Use a gun. Want a rare grimoire from the astral realms? Find a professional astral explorer. In a world where other mages exist you can (potentially) achieve anything you want without using magic yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;find an astral explorer&quot; is false on 2 fronts (The rest lead into an argument of whether &quot;using magic for things achievable without magic&quot; is talking in absolutes or if it is circumstantial). The Astral Realms are only accessible to mages, so it is something that arguably only magic can achieve. And while another mage could explore it, they would be using magic, and thus you are simply using magic by proxy, which would count in my book if we interpetation things as you put it (It is why you still would roll for a Wisdom degeneration if you ordered your retainer to kill someone...) <br /> <br /> The way I look at it: could I achieve this with the same level of effort (or less) than going to the local store to buy something. So boiling tea while home would be a hit, while summoning a pot of tea and heating it while trapped in a blizzard in Antarctica... not a sin (though raises questions about their priorities). <br /> <br /> The issue with the current example is that while most people cannot raise their abilities instantly, people can normally attempt seduction. So while asking a girl out (at least in my mind) is easier than grabbing milk from the grocery store, making myself good at it is not... so not sure how to handle this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 01-30-2015, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:53:42-08:00","id":386246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386238#post386238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;find an astral explorer&quot; is false on 2 fronts (The rest lead into an argument of whether &quot;using magic for things achievable without magic&quot; is talking in absolutes or if it is circumstantial). The Astral Realms are only accessible to mages, so it is something that arguably only magic can achieve. And while another mage could explore it, they would be using magic, and thus you are simply using magic by proxy, which would count in my book if we interpetation things as you put it (It is why you still would roll for a Wisdom degeneration if you ordered your retainer to kill someone...)<br /> <br /> I think the better way to look at it is: could I achieve this with the same level of effort (or less) than going to the local store to buy something. So boiling tea while home would be a hit, while summoning a pot of tea and heating it while trapped in a blizzard in Antarctica... not a sin (though raises questions about their priorities).</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can go out into the blizzard to find a nearest settlement and get the tea from them. It's suicidal, but you <i>can</i> do it. Instead of finding a rare grimoire in the astral realms you <i>can </i>go and do the research yourself. Since Wisdom sins generally punish you for using magic to make life easier (Wisdom 4 to kill a man with magic, to commit manslaughter without magic, or to perform goetia to fight your flaws with magic) I'd say that at Wisdom 10 you just don't do magic, because pretty much everything selfless you can imagine doing you can do without magic by devoting more time and effort to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:56:26-08:00","id":386248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386238#post386238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with the current example is that while most people cannot raise their abilities instantly, people can normally attempt seduction. So while asking a girl out (at least in my mind) is easier than grabbing milk from the grocery store, making myself good at it is not... so not sure how to handle this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems clear cut to me. Wisdom 10 sin is &quot;using magic to achieve something you could do without magic&quot;. You can seduce a girl by using Life magic to grow bulging muscles and perfect face. Or you can go to the gym and get them naturally. You can raise your intellect with Mind and learn top 10 love poems through the astral. Or you can read a book and finish university. By taking a shortcut with magic you commit a Wisdom sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T06:52:05-08:00","id":386303,"title":"","content":"It is worth noting that the actual writting says:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Using magic to accomplish a task that could be achieved <b>just as well</b> without it</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The bolded part is key, I think.<br /> <br /> For example, if I found out a loved one is in danger<i> right now</i> in the <i>other side of the world</i>, there's no mundane mean for me to get there in time, so using Teleport wouldn't count as an act of Hubris even at Wisdom 10. Using it to cross the street because you don't want to wait for the trafic light to get green is another thing.<br /> <br /> If a disease is imposible to heal with current medical treatments, using Life to heal it is not a Wisdom sin. Using it to get rid of a mild common cold that is not bothering you may be though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:12:53-08:00","id":386321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386303#post386303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worth noting that the actual writting says:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Using magic to accomplish a task that could be achieved <b>just as well</b> without it</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The bolded part is key, I think.<br /> <br /> For example, if I found out a loved one is in danger<i> right now</i> in the <i>other side of the world</i>, there's no mundane mean for me to get there in time, so using Teleport wouldn't count as an act of Hubris even at Wisdom 10. Using it to cross the street because you don't want to wait for the trafic light to get green is another thing.<br /> <br /> If a disease is imposible to heal with current medical treatments, using Life to heal it is not a Wisdom sin. Using it to get rid of a mild common cold that is not bothering you may be though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that justifying doing everything with magic? You can boil tea normally, but tea brewed with exactly right temperature provided by Forces would be better. You can pick up girls in the bar, but mind controll would do things faster and emotional urging would make feelings better. You can call the police/Order/friends on the other side of the world and ask them to help you, but Teleporting and blowing shit up yourself is faster and easier. You can get a biology degree to develop a cure, but Life provides a convenient shortcut, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> What you are suggesting is a slippery slope. Can a researcher use Mind and Life instead of sleeping and eating, because he has more time to work on cancer cure this way? Can a detective mind read the suspect, instead of putting effort into investigation? Where do we draw the line where using magic to acomplish something becomes acceptable?<br /> <br /> Although I would make an exception for using legacy Attainments. They incorporate magic into mundane reality, and using them should be extremely natural for legacy members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:24:22-08:00","id":386337,"title":"","content":"You are not getting it. Even the example in the book mentions using a <i>nearby</i> teapot.<br /> <br /> No, it doesn't justify doing anything with magic. The &quot;just as well&quot; is not about <i>quality</i> but about <i>availability</i>.<br /> <br /> If time is of the essence, then not all options are equal. Can the patient wait till you get your degree in medicine and a job at that hospital? Probably not, then you cannot do it &quot;just as well&quot; without magic. If your friends in the other side of the world are just a call away, then teleport is not needed, yes. In that case it would be a sin as there are other methods justs as effective and efficient available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:32:51-08:00","id":386343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386337#post386337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not getting it. Even the example in the book mentions using a <i>nearby</i> teapot.<br /> <br /> No, it doesn't justify doing anything with magic. The &quot;just as well&quot; is not about <i>quality</i> but about <i>availability</i>.<br /> <br /> If time is of the essence, then not all options are equal. Can the patient wait till you get your degree in medicine and a job at that hospital? Probably not, then you cannot do it &quot;just as well&quot; without magic. If your friends in the other side of the world are just a call away, then teleport is not needed, yes. In that case it would be a sin as there are other methods justs as effective and efficient available.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using magic to accomplish a task that could be achieved just as well without it (i.e., boiling tea with Forces instead using the nearby stove). </div> </div> </div>So if you are a jobless hobo, then making food out of thin air with Matter and brewing tea with Forces is ok?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Don't take me wrong, I don't mind the world where hobo wizards make themself grand feasts every day. But it's kind of a strange morality system that encourages a mage to avoid interaction with human society so he can provide for himself with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 01-30-2015, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:43:26-08:00","id":386347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386343#post386343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you are a jobless hobo, then making food out of thin air with Matter and brewing tea with Forces is ok?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as you probably have no other means to do so.<br /> <br /> If you are creating food out of thin air because the alternative is to starve, then is not a sin. Conjuring food out of thin air just because you are too lazy to go to the shop downstairs, is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:50:07-08:00","id":386350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386343#post386343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Don't take me wrong, I don't mind the world where hobo wizards make themself grand feasts every day. But it's kind of a strange morality system that encourages a mage to avoid interaction with human society so he can provide for himself with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you've reached Wisdom 10, then you are most likely an experienced mage. Probably a Master at something. And what you are saying is that Life masters <i>must</i> go around the world and heal the sick with magic, because &quot;selfish thoughts&quot; is also a Wisdom 10 sin, and clearly the sick people won't wait until someone finds a cure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T08:26:48-08:00","id":386355,"title":"","content":"Wisdom 10 is supposed to be difficult to maintain, a Mage with Life who is Wisdom 10 and who is confronted with someone who needs healing best provided via magic will probably need to heal them or face a breaking point. It's unlikely he has to go out of his way to find such people though unless that's part of who he is. Because, ignoring the vast masses of people you don't know isn't really selfish, it's just part of being human. We're really only equipped to care about people close to us, some people are better at empathizing with the rest of humanity too, but that doesn't make those who don't or can't bad or selfish people automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T08:39:38-08:00","id":386363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386350#post386350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if you've reached Wisdom 10, then you are most likely an experienced mage. Probably a Master at something. And what you are saying is that Life masters <i>must</i> go around the world and heal the sick with magic, because &quot;selfish thoughts&quot; is also a Wisdom 10 sin, and clearly the sick people won't wait until someone finds a cure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one there is a difference between &quot;selfish&quot; and &quot;different priorities&quot;. A Master of Life could spend their time &quot;better&quot; (at least subjectively) than that, while not doing so for selfish reasons. Even if they were also a Master of Time and Space, there is only so much you can do.<br /> <br /> Consider too that most of the 1e Morality stats were prohibitive in nature. You suffered potential degeneration for acting badly, for things that harm or could harm. Not doing something, even if that something would be a &quot;good&quot; thing, is generally not a concern.<br /> <br /> And also, one could even make a case that saving too many people with magic is actually unwise too. Using magic constantly to break the Natural Order Of Things (TM) is a bit sketchy, doubly so for a Thyrsus (who is the most likely to be a Master of Life) or Moros. Even if that particular part of the Natural Order of Things is an unpleasant part of Creation (i.e. people dying from illness).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:34:41-08:00","id":386384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386363#post386363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for one there is a difference between &quot;selfish&quot; and &quot;different priorities&quot;. A Master of Life could spend their time &quot;better&quot; (at least subjectively) than that, while not doing so for selfish reasons. Even if they were also a Master of Time and Space, there is only so much you can do.<br /> <br /> Consider too that most of the 1e Morality stats were prohibitive in nature. You suffered potential degeneration for acting badly, for things that harm or could harm. Not doing something, even if that something would be a &quot;good&quot; thing, is generally not a concern.<br /> <br /> And also, one could even make a case that saving too many people with magic is actually unwise too. Using magic constantly to break the Natural Order Of Things (TM) is a bit sketchy, doubly so for a Thyrsus (who is the most likely to be a Master of Life) or Moros. Even if that particular part of the Natural Order of Things is an unpleasant part of Creation (i.e. people dying from illness).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thyrsus are not exempt from murder being a sin, so don't try to pull this &quot;Natural Order&quot; shit on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:37:53-08:00","id":386389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, if you've reached Wisdom 10, then you are most likely an experienced mage </div> </div> </div>That's kinda a logical fallacy. There's no direct relationship between Wisdom and Arcana mastery. If anything you are more likely to have high Wisdom as an Apprentice than a Master.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what you are saying is that Life masters <i>must</i> go around the world and heal the sick with magic, because &quot;selfish thoughts&quot; is also a Wisdom 10 sin, and clearly the sick people won't wait until someone finds a cure. </div> </div> </div>I don't remeber saying that but I suposse one could take that from what I said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, back to your hobbo wizard example, creating a grandiose feast day after day would be a sin none the less because creating food past the actual needs is just gluttony and hubris.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:42:26-08:00","id":386413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386384#post386384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thyrsus are not exempt from murder being a sin, so don't try to pull this &quot;Natural Order&quot; shit on me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you are being rude for no reason. Up to this point I thought you were actually arguing in good faith, I'm not so sure anymore.<br /> <br /> And for your information, Thyrsus did have acces to a Merit that actually gave them a pass on killing as long as it was clean and with a purpose related to survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:45:30-08:00","id":386414,"title":"","content":"Picking girls in a bar might not be the best &quot;sin-less&quot; example. How about creating sculpture. You could do it through mundane means without magic, but if you boost your skills with magic, the result will be better. If your goal it to create the finest sculpture, would using magic be Wisdom 10 sin or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:28:41-08:00","id":386521,"title":"","content":"That's a better example. If what you are aiming for is beyond normal human capacity, then I will err on not being a sin. On the other hand it is dificult to adjudicate if something is truly beyond human skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-30-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:33:29-08:00","id":386523,"title":"","content":"I assume that if you're magic-ing for the sake of practicing, say, Rotes and Yantras and such it wouldn't count as a sin either?<br /> <br /> Granted, you tend not to actually roleplay scenes where your characters are practicing, so I guess that's kind of a pointless question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T12:09:52-08:00","id":386563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386523#post386523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that if you're magic-ing for the sake of practicing, say, Rotes and Yantras and such it wouldn't count as a sin either?<br /> <br /> Granted, you tend not to actually roleplay scenes where your characters are practicing, so I guess that's kind of a pointless question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think in another thread it was decided that practicing magic automatically passes since you couldn't ever do it mundanely. Though there was a caveat that other Wisdom harming things still would be counted (practicing a lightning rote in the woods on a dead tree vs on a neighbors dog, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T12:34:10-08:00","id":386580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=386521#post386521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a better example. If what you are aiming for is beyond normal human capacity, then I will err on not being a sin. On the other hand it is dificult to adjudicate if something is truly beyond human skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also depends on the action you are evaluating in the &quot;just as well&quot; part. Specifically, if you are viewing this in terms of raising a skill or sculpting a statue. If you view the Stat boost as part of sculpting, it could fall under being a sin, as you are you using magic for something you could do mundanely (sculpt a statur). On the other hand, if you view it as two seperate actions (&quot;boost skills&quot; then &quot;sculpt statue&quot;) I would rule that there is no Wisdom penalty, as there really is no &quot;just as well&quot; from going to mortal dexterity and crafting skill to the peak of human ability (or higher with gnosis 6+) in a matter of minutes-hours. <br /> <br /> I also think you should seperate quality/outcome as a qualifier though, especially in a storytelling system. A mundane mortal could theoretically achieve a divine result with enough luck on a roll, just as a mage with the skills of a god fail miserably if the dice don't fall his way. While both are unlikely scenarios, I don't think it is fair to punish morality based on the outcome of a die roll (at least one that isn't for morality/derangement that is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T06:22:24-08:00","id":387270,"title":"","content":"-Can a archmaster turns a Banisher into a regular mage or it's impossible because the abyssal shard don't depends of the Supernal Magic and the only way would be dangerous or hazardous indirect abyssal manipulation or seek for the help of powerfull abyssal beings (who maybe can remove the abyssal since it's in their domain) ?<br /> <br /> -Can a archmaster infiltrate a Entente ? like a former Guardian of Veil who was infiltred in a another order and still fake it except for a few allies ? Or a Seer pretending to be a Examplar ? (The opposite seems impossible since the Exarchs test themselves the Seers who pass the Threshold)<br /> <br /> -Can eventually the Gate become a Archgenitor ? he would give a Prelacy close to his legacy ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 01-31-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T06:52:48-08:00","id":387332,"title":"","content":"Don't know about the last two, but for the first consider that usually when an Archmage tries to create a Mage he gets a Banisher. So yeah, he might be able to turn a Banisher into a regular Mage, but it would probably have similarly nasty unforeseen consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T08:27:47-08:00","id":387430,"title":"","content":"About it...does a Sleepwalker still have an abyssal shard ? If you force te the awakening of a sleepwalker, he is still likely to become a Banisher ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T08:49:06-08:00","id":387443,"title":"","content":"The Abyssal shard is what causes the sleeping curse and triggers paradox when casting in front of sleepers. Since both are absent with sleepwalkers, I would say no. <br /> <br /> Also, the idea that Banishers have an Abyssal shard is a theory put forth in their book and astral realms. There isn't anything saying that said theory is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T21:03:41-08:00","id":394411,"title":"","content":"Not quite a simple question but: a friend of mine has recently asked me about MtA passages on nazi germany. I can only remember the Daksha, so... can you help me sending more references?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T09:24:39-08:00","id":397660,"title":"","content":"What is the justification of the Bodhisattvas to use Imperium Rites if they want to ascent ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:22:03-08:00","id":397744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=394411#post394411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite a simple question but: a friend of mine has recently asked me about MtA passages on nazi germany. I can only remember the Daksha, so... can you help me sending more references?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book Mage Noir has a lot on the period, mostly from the post-war perspective. Definitely something to look into for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:32:57-08:00","id":429159,"title":"","content":"An omen that modify the physical laws to increase the maximum potential technology level, is Earthly or Profane ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:49:04-07:00","id":555131,"title":"","content":"Sorry for necroposting, but considering it's either that or make a new thread with just one simple question, well...<br /> <br /> Anyways, looking at the Adamantine Hand Fighting Style, one of the prerequisites state that you have to have 1 dot higher in the Arcanum than the maneuver you're purchasing. If that is the case, does that mean you have to be an archmaster to purchase the 5th dot in the style, since it does say 1 dot higher, or can you just purchase it anyway if you've mastered the Arcanum?<br /> <br /> It just seems kinda weird to me that you have to become a frakking archmaster just to master a magical fighting style, especially considering that, once you get to that point, plain combat is trivial at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:36:31-07:00","id":555803,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that would mean having the 5th dot requires having the 6th dot of the Arcana. And it's a little more than &quot;just mastering&quot; a fighting style, since the 5th dot lets you <i>ignore Paradox</i>. So long as the spell is delivered through touch, though, but still. That's insanely huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:47:53-07:00","id":555811,"title":"","content":"If I remember reading some commentary in the past correctly, the fifth dot needing Archmastery is working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:52:38-07:00","id":555817,"title":"","content":"And I will speak as someone who waved it (made it Arcana Dots=Level) and it quickly breaks the game if your players are even slightly clever with its application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:14:13-07:00","id":555829,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think that it would be much better if the fifth dot was replaced to be a little less insane and then bump down the requirements (because I'll grant that it DOES suck to not be able to finish out your fighting style unless the game brings you up to Archmastery).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:37:07-07:00","id":555845,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Both on it needing a rehash and for why. <br /> <br /> Though the AH fighting style as a whole needs some rebalancing. For example, the 3rd dot is much more beneficial than any other save the 5th dot, even with its willpower cost. The 4th (damage-&gt;1 time casting bonus, w/9 again if damage is made resistant) can either drastically be abused (an orphan of proteus with this was... amusing) or very underwhelming. The first dot giving a -1 to any shield struck in melee of the same arcana as the AH's and the shield redistribution are okay. But the 1st is limited to a 1/10 chance unless you take it multiple times (thus having 2 dots in many arcana). The 2nd is pretty decent as long as you aren't silly about its use. <br /> <br /> The fact that it needed to be retaken for each arcana and required a decent number of prerequisites to take in the fist place meant that a lot of my players never bothered with it (except that orphan who realized he could use his 1st attainment to abuse the damage effect, or when I made the HR on arcana=merit level). <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I think it was a cool idea. It just didn't seem to mechanically work for my players enough to not just take law of embodiment with more fighting styles (or at least go past the 3rd dot in something they they combined a lot, such as using it to shoot and heal on the same turn)<br /> <br /> Hopefully, if it returns in 2e, it will see some love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:48:38-07:00","id":555853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=555845#post555845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully, if it returns in 2e, it will see some love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave's already indicated that AH will return in 2e. He referenced it in his Order spoilers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\"> New Order &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Adamantine Arrow: Adamant Hand. Arrow mages of good Status may learn a Fighting Style to combine spellcasting with combat. The Hand allows mages to use full dodges, and unarmed and armed strikes, as Yantras for instant spells.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:54:36-07:00","id":555856,"title":"","content":"Oh, duh. Thanks Branford. It has been awhile since I read that X)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:56:49-07:00","id":555857,"title":"","content":"That's awesome! Good news. Order-specific stuff like that is always cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:12:48-07:00","id":558393,"title":"","content":"(That's all 2e questions)<br /> <br /> 1) Jerry the Thyrsus wants to transform into a Reptilian (as per DtD) so he can impregnate one he's been sleeping with for some time already (so Fantasia + Hereditary Change iirc). Maybe he's in love with this particular Reptilian, maybe he wants to make HPL's ghost cry. Maybe both. How much Reach and what additional Arcana (for Attainments) can he expect to need?<br /> <br /> 2) Do any parts of the Awakened Template remain functional during the Soul Loss condition? If so, which (unreleased ones don't have to be mentioned)?<br /> <br /> 3) '30s time! Jack the British Acanthus wants to curse the Falangists (disregarding the penalties for excessive Factors and Reach for now). Can he donate 13 pounds to them and use the amount of money as a Yantra? If so, what kind(s) of Yantra? If no, does he need to pay the equivalent of 13 pesetas instead (and see the intermediate question)?<br /> <br /> 4) What Arcana/Attainments are neccessary to create a potion that heals the drinker once ingested (beyound Imbue Item/Prime 4 and Life Weaving/3)?<br /> <br /> 5) Could Dr. T the Thyrsus with Life 3 cast a Life Knowing spell to gain the Informed Condition for the mundane treatment roll (Dex+Med)? Or even Healing Heart?<br /> <br /> Edit: 6) What do I need to do if I want my Familiar to pretend to be a spirit of Death while she's just a run-on-the-mill scavanger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 06-17-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:56:00-07:00","id":558432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=558393#post558393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That's all 2e questions)<br /> <br /> 1) Jerry the Thyrsus wants to transform into a Reptilian (as per DtD) so he can impregnate one he's been sleeping with for some time already (so Fantasia + Hereditary Change iirc). Maybe he's in love with this particular Reptilian, maybe he wants to make HPL's ghost cry. Maybe both. How much Reach and what additional Arcana (for Attainments) can he expect to need?</div> </div> </div> </div>*the Nobody Knows alarm goes off* At a GUESS, assuming Reptilians are fundamentally living, changing a human into another animal is *probably* Weaving, so you're looking at baseline Life 3. At least one reach for advanced duration. No idea about what it would take to make the impregnation take properly, I'm afraid. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=558393#post558393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Do any parts of the Awakened Template remain functional during the Soul Loss condition? If so, which (unreleased ones don't have to be mentioned)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know we know this one... I'm dredging memory here, but I think you lose a dot of effective Gnosis each day until you have a soul again.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=558393#post558393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) What Arcana/Attainments are neccessary to create a potion that heals the drinker once ingested (beyound Imbue Item/Prime 4 and Life Weaving/3)?</div> </div> </div> </div>... None? In fact, you need Prime 4 to access the Imbue Item attainment and only Life 2 to heal now (healing is a natural function of the body which you are Ruling to work immediately, and that's been explicitly spoiled)<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=558393#post558393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: 6) What do I need to do if I want my Familiar to pretend to be a spirit of Death while she's just a run-on-the-mill scavanger?</div> </div> </div> </div> You've got options, but if you just want to *pretend*, you can definitely do it with a Spirit 2 spell, as that's Veiling. It's not something I think spirits can do - I think approx. Rank and Choir pings to them pretty much naturally - but I can imagine spoofing your Rank/Choir to be a reasonable numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:25:49-07:00","id":558537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crabbadon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=558432#post558432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we know this one... I'm dredging memory here, but I think you lose a dot of effective Gnosis each day until you have a soul again....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's how it is now. In 2E you'll lose your ability to contain paradoxes. And probably other fun stuff as well!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:34:38-07:00","id":558834,"title":"","content":"For complete transformation into something else, it would be Patterning (life 4). If you just want some of the features, such as sperm that can impregnate a non-human, then it is weaving. Regardless, probably at least 1 reach fo advanced as mentioned, and possibly a +2 for an advanced, magically based lifeform. <br /> <br /> To make the impregnation work (assuming you overcome the compatability issues) maybe just Life 2, as you are controlling a process the species is capable of (hence, ruling). Besides advanced to keep it working till delivery, I don't know if you would need much reach (though maybe, as it is a mystical being, you might)... but since pregnancy itself isn't too supernatural, I would be okay with it not requiring it.<br /> <br /> But these are all guesses, so I would say we wait till 2e is off the presses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:51:11-07:00","id":558999,"title":"","content":"If you're biologically compatible, the practice of Compelling is probably enough to ensure conception happens (or doesn't happen, whichever you prefer). It's something that could have happened naturally. Ruling if you don't want to wait for the lady's normal cycle. And the conception is a non magical thing you've brought about using magic, so you wouldn't need to keep the spell going more than... however much time there is between the sexual act and the conception. (I'm sure I've heard how much time it takes at some point in my life, but I can't say I remember.) Once your Knowing spell tells you that fertilization has occurred, you can let the spell lapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:35:34-07:00","id":603200,"title":"","content":"Just how complex can something you transform into via Life 4 be? Living beings are already pretty complex (and we have example of transforming into weird stuff like living flame) but could someone with Matter 4 Life 4 transform into, for example a fully working computer or other high-tech device?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">okay, I admit it, it's actually about transforming into an F16</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T19:44:33-07:00","id":603382,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not, the Guardian legacy called the Austere do something very similar with their attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:20:01-07:00","id":611402,"title":"","content":"What might be the effects of using spells in non-standard environments, like underwater, falling through the sky etc? I had several thoughts about this, but I wanna know if I am missing something important.<br /> <br /> You probably can't benefit from most Yantras while underwater and such. You can't shoot fireballs either, even with Forces. However, the celestial fire of Prime probably works. A weird fuel created through Matter 4+ could work too, but that might require Reach and thus greater Paradox risk. Avoiding all falling damage from thousands of meters probably requires Forces to bypass gravity, Life to make your bones super durable, Matter to make the ground soft or Fate to make you fall in a convenient pillow truck. All of those would require 3+ Arcana dots and/or Reach, thus running into the problem of the strange water-resistant fire mentioned before. Oh, and news of your miraculous survival will likely spread very fast without the help of the clean up crew.<br /> <br /> I'd say a genuinely clever Mage plans ahead to avoid the need of spells in these situations, or even avoids these situations entirely. On the other hand, a more ostentatious, high ranking member of the Silver Ladder might have his own planes and helicopters that are Imbued/Enhanced with just about everything so he won't have to worry about Scrying, Sympathetic Fraying or worse.<br /> <br /> What else should I know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T16:57:21-07:00","id":616889,"title":"","content":"I have another question. When you use Arcana like Matter and Life to alter objects and living beings, the way their return to their original forms might be weird. If you used Life 2 to turn a big tree into a swarm of wasps with a roughly equal NWOD Size, what happens to the wasps when the spell wears off? Does each wasp become a leaf, piece of bark and the like, then fall to the ground like a thousand pins? Do the wasps become an intact tree again, but since its roots are no longer inside the ground, it falls and later dies? I mean, you could tell the wasps to go back to the original spot of the tree and reshape themselves into the tree's normal form, but that carries great risk of Paradox. And you might need to leave in a real hurry for some reason, or just be a very irresponsible person. What is the standard effect then? My hunch is &quot;ST fiat, probably the most inconvenient thing you can think of, with limits&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the various transformations from one of the 3 main states of matter to another, it might leave behind weird evidence too, if you don't bother to manually revert the changes.<br /> <br /> Could I hide such strange evidence with illusions through the Mind Arcanum as I revert the transformations? If not, I might need the help of a Guardian Of The Veil, but that has its own risks.<br /> <br /> Did I miss anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T22:01:06-07:00","id":617140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=611402#post611402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avoiding all falling damage from thousands of meters probably requires Forces to bypass gravity, Life to make your bones super durable, Matter to make the ground soft or Fate to make you fall in a convenient pillow truck. All of those would require 3+ Arcana dots and/or Reach</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 2 to Shield yourself from gravity. Wait for air resistance to slow you down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=616889#post616889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could tell the wasps to go back to the original spot of the tree and reshape themselves into the tree's normal form, but that carries great risk of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. Paradox is only a risk at the moment you cast the spell. What happens afterward doesn't matter. If it happens in front of Sleepers, there will be what was Disbelief in 1e and will be Dissonance in 2e. Fortunately, you don't care about them destroying your spell, since you're ending it anyway. So pretty much the only effect is they'll edit the weirdness out of their memories later.<br /> <br /> Also they might freak out and they'll suffer through an Integrity breaking point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=616889#post616889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I hide such strange evidence with illusions through the Mind Arcanum as I revert the transformations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you Veil the transformation so nearby Sleepers won't notice it happening? Sure. Could you hide the evidence afterward so they don't notice that either? Also yes. You have a limited number of spells you can keep active at any one time, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 08-06-2015, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T22:17:50-07:00","id":617148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=617140#post617140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Force 2 to Shield yourself from gravity. Wait for air resistance to slow you down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 2 to Shield yourself from Inertia. Hit as fast as you want and perfectly and instantaneously match velocities with the planet Earth with no damage to yourself, then cancel the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T23:03:01-07:00","id":628240,"title":"","content":"What are the properties of Thaumium and other &quot;perfected metals&quot;? <br /> If there's a difference between them in 1st or second edition that we know of yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T23:26:39-07:00","id":628244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=628240#post628240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the properties of Thaumium and other &quot;perfected metals&quot;?<br /> If there's a difference between them in 1st or second edition that we know of yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been stated to be planned for coverage in Signs of Sorcery, the first 2e supplement for Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T23:35:34-07:00","id":628249,"title":"","content":"Alright thanks for letting me know. <br /> <br /> <br /> Would like to know what they are for the mean time in 1e as the 2e answer might take a few months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T23:55:43-07:00","id":628253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=628249#post628249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright thanks for letting me know.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would like to know what they are for the mean time in 1e as the 2e answer might take a few months.</div> </div> </div> </div>We get the properties of Thaumium in the core book, I honestly don't remember if there were any written effects from the other perfected materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:04:39-07:00","id":628265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=628253#post628253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We get the properties of Thaumium in the core book, I honestly don't remember if there were any written effects from the other perfected materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacies: the Ancient covered the properties of orichalcum, lunargent, hermium, and siderite in the Forge Masters entry (page 76, specifically), though the effects of perfected tin, copper, and lead have not been covered, nor have the effects of <i>electrum magicum</i> beyond its role in the ceremony behind learning the Legacy's third Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:09:49-07:00","id":628271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=628265#post628265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Legacies: the Ancient covered the properties of orichalcum, lunargent, hermium, and siderite in the Forge Masters entry (page 76, specifically), though the effects of perfected tin, copper, and lead have not been covered, nor have the effects of <i>electrum magicum</i> beyond its role in the ceremony behind learning the Legacy's third Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I had some fuzzy memory about that they HAD mechanics, but I couldn't remember if it was something official, or something I made up for a chronicle myself. (Let alone where the rules were, a Legacy book would be the LAST place I check. :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:37:53-07:00","id":640243,"title":"","content":"I may be mixing things up, but are the Lower Depths the same plane or pseudo-plane of existence as the Inferno? The sample Lower Depths entity from Summoners (page 63) makes bargains much like a demon from the Inferno supplement would. However, Summoners says that the entities from the Lower Depths despise all things, but Inferno says that they have a sort of twisted love for humans. Maybe each Lower Depths/Inferno demon looks upon humans differently. It's more likely that they are simply lying, and whatever they feel for humans lies in a third category outside love and hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:58:13-07:00","id":640271,"title":"","content":"Thaumium is like nMage's version of cMage's Primum - it's magic-resistant metal. It's an alloy of Oricalcum and Lunargent (IIRC) - those are two of the seven perfected metals.<br /> <br /> In Legacies: The Ancient, it's explained that you make Perfected Metal by shifting a quantity of metal into Twilight and back again dozens of times. We might change that in 2e (we're outlining the book that will include them right now).<br /> <br /> There's supposed to be seven different perfected metals, one for each of the classically-known metals: gold, silver, tin, lead, copper, mercury, and iron. L:TA explains that Thaumium is only one form of perfected alloy, and there's several different ones you can make with Matter Mastery.<br /> <br /> The actual materials aren't inherently magical, but have qualities above and beyond their impure versions<br /> <br /> Perfected Gold is Orichalcum - it's imperishable, conducts energy, impervious to acid.<br /> Perfected Iron is Siderite - it's memory-morphic, in that it doesn't break but *bends*, then reforms to its forged shape. It never dulls its edge, and can cut diamond.<br /> Perfected Mercury is Hermium, a superliquid - stir it and the circular current never stops. put it in a container and it will crawl up and out.<br /> Perfected Silver is Lunargent - highly malleable and chemically inert<br /> <br /> tin, lead, and copper are not described, but Perfected Lead might be Apeiron, the matter of Stygia Matter-based Supernal Entities are named after.<br /> <br /> And above them all, above Primum, is Adamas, the utterly indestructible, magic-resistant material Atlantean temples are made out of, which is made by a 7-dot spell Excising the capacity of a material to be damaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:58:48-07:00","id":640273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=640243#post640243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be mixing things up, but are the Lower Depths the same plane or pseudo-plane of existence as the Inferno? The sample Lower Depths entity from Summoners (page 63) makes bargains much like a demon from the Inferno supplement would. However, Summoners says that the entities from the Lower Depths despise all things, but Inferno says that they have a sort of twisted love for humans. Maybe each Lower Depths/Inferno demon looks upon humans differently. It's more likely that they are simply lying, and whatever they feel for humans lies in a third category outside love and hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Inferno is one of the Lower Depths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T09:28:24-07:00","id":640355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=640271#post640271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumium is like nMage's version of cMage's Primum - it's magic-resistant metal. It's an alloy of Oricalcum and Lunargent (IIRC) - those are two of the seven perfected metals.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Mage 1e, p. 203, Thaumium is comprised of perfected gold (orichalcum), silver (lunargent) and mercury (hermium). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T09:52:21-07:00","id":640372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=640243#post640243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be mixing things up, but are the Lower Depths the same plane or pseudo-plane of existence as the Inferno? The sample Lower Depths entity from Summoners (page 63) makes bargains much like a demon from the Inferno supplement would. However, Summoners says that the entities from the Lower Depths despise all things, but Inferno says that they have a sort of twisted love for humans. Maybe each Lower Depths/Inferno demon looks upon humans differently. It's more likely that they are simply lying, and whatever they feel for humans lies in a third category outside love and hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, &quot;Lower Depth&quot; is kind of a catch-all name Mages use for places that don't work the way they should, based on Mages' current understanding of the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:28:19-07:00","id":640424,"title":"","content":"Regarding the lower depths. DaveB on Giant in the Playground:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Actual spoiler for Awakening 2e: The Lower Depths</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;Places so far from the light they shouldn\u2019t be able to exist, but do. Wormholes under a rotting log of Creation. The Lower Depths consist of countless realms, because the region lacks even the energy to contain a unitary reality. The Lower Depths are to the Fallen World what the Fallen is to the Supernal, and are therefore a Lie of the Lie. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Some mages believe that the petty symbols of the human psyche take on great importance in certain of the Depths, just as Supernal signs cast their shadows in the ordinary world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Each Lower Depth is unable to retain a critical constituent of existence; it\u2019s either absent or has been distorted into something hostile to ordinary existence. Sometimes the lack can be defined by an Arcanum. A Depth realm without Death might be choked with endless knots of imperishable flesh and plant matter. Other depths lack less definable principles, such as Shape, Identity and Righteousness. Some mages situate Hell here, because the entities known as akathartoi (\u201cunclean ones\u201d) closely resemble the demons of Abrahamic legend, feeding from human depravity. Mages have catalogued numerous Lower Depths, but only by interrogating and examining their inhabitants. No reliable source speaks of a mage returning from the Lower Depths, but it\u2019s possible to summon an inhabitant upward. Their denizens find it difficult to manifest. They must satisfy signature hungers, and find it extremely difficult to take material form.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Canonical Lower Depths: The Inferno (lack and feed from human Vice), wherever it is Strix come (lack and feed from Vitae), Duat from Mummy (lack and feed from Sekhem). And those are three &quot;Depths&quot; relatively close to the Fallen World. Mage's gameline has included creatures like The Tutor, an immobile, hurts-to-look-at half-Materialized *thing* the Paternoster Ministry of Seers have imprisoned that rips the human capacity for individual identity away as a sting reflex, The Decay, a Lower Depths being that manifests as everything material crumbling as it eats Durability, and the Hounds of Annwn, vaguely canid (but entirely invisible, as they don't have a Pattern) beings that eat Patterns, used by a Left-Handed Legacy to build their own pocket world in the Lower Depths from the things the Hounds eat.<br /> </span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:36:37-07:00","id":640429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=640271#post640271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumium is like nMage's version of cMage's Primum - it's magic-resistant metal. It's an alloy of Oricalcum and Lunargent (IIRC) - those are two of the seven perfected metals.<br /> <br /> In Legacies: The Ancient, it's explained that you make Perfected Metal by shifting a quantity of metal into Twilight and back again dozens of times. We might change that in 2e (we're outlining the book that will include them right now).<br /> <br /> There's supposed to be seven different perfected metals, one for each of the classically-known metals: gold, silver, tin, lead, copper, mercury, and iron. L:TA explains that Thaumium is only one form of perfected alloy, and there's several different ones you can make with Matter Mastery.<br /> <br /> The actual materials aren't inherently magical, but have qualities above and beyond their impure versions<br /> <br /> Perfected Gold is Orichalcum - it's imperishable, conducts energy, impervious to acid.<br /> Perfected Iron is Siderite - it's memory-morphic, in that it doesn't break but *bends*, then reforms to its forged shape. It never dulls its edge, and can cut diamond.<br /> Perfected Mercury is Hermium, a superliquid - stir it and the circular current never stops. put it in a container and it will crawl up and out.<br /> Perfected Silver is Lunargent - highly malleable and chemically inert<br /> <br /> tin, lead, and copper are not described, but Perfected Lead might be Apeiron, the matter of Stygia Matter-based Supernal Entities are named after.<br /> <br /> And above them all, above Primum, is Adamas, the utterly indestructible, magic-resistant material Atlantean temples are made out of, which is made by a 7-dot spell Excising the capacity of a material to be damaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumium is actually an alloy formed by Orichalcum, Lunargent <i>and </i>Hermium, at least as far as the core says (and I think L:tA doesn't contradict it).<br /> Can we take it then that in 2e Thaumium is just made from alloyed Orichalcum and Lunargent?<br /> <br /> Edit: and Apeiron is described in Imperial Mysteries as the &quot;Pure Lead of Stygia&quot;, Matter in it's purest sense, cabable of taking any property whatsoever. It's something only Archmasters can make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 08-26-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:11:55-07:00","id":642001,"title":"","content":"I was wondering: How is it with Gnosis dots and Arcana limitations in 2e? When I was thinking about it, I realized that if we go with the idea that getting a dot in an Arcanum is basically about learning an information (you have the option to pay for the dot with normal exp), the strength of your connection with the supernal shouldn't matter that much.<br /> <br /> This is especially visible when you can have 2 mages - both have the same Arcana and mage 1 decides to learn a dot in Arcanum A. He does so and can't learn dot in Arcanum B because of the limit. The other mage learns dot in Arcanum B and can't learn the dot that mage 1 did. Why would the simple act of learning an information prevent those mages from learning the other one?<br /> <br /> Now, I understand the need for some basic limit, so we don't have Gnosis 1 Masters running around, but that could be solved by, say, making the upper limit mage's Gnosis +2 for non-Archmasters. That would basically create the same kind of limit like 1e core for the first Arcana new mage gets and wouldn't require that half page long table that doesn't make much sense to me from a roleplaying perspective...<br /> <br /> So, how does 2e deal with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:23:10-07:00","id":642013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=640429#post640429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thaumium is actually an alloy formed by Orichalcum, Lunargent <i>and </i>Hermium, at least as far as the core says (and I think L:tA doesn't contradict it).<br /> Can we take it then that in 2e Thaumium is just made from alloyed Orichalcum and Lunargent?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say &quot;If I recall Correctly&quot;, no you may not take it that I mean &quot;I'm changing to this&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, you <i>may</i>, but be prepared to be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:24:13-07:00","id":642015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=642001#post642001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering: How is it with Gnosis dots and Arcana limitations in 2e? When I was thinking about it, I realized that if we go with the idea that getting a dot in an Arcanum is basically about learning an information (you have the option to pay for the dot with normal exp), the strength of your connection with the supernal shouldn't matter that much.<br /> <br /> This is especially visible when you can have 2 mages - both have the same Arcana and mage 1 decides to learn a dot in Arcanum A. He does so and can't learn dot in Arcanum B because of the limit. The other mage learns dot in Arcanum B and can't learn the dot that mage 1 did. Why would the simple act of learning an information prevent those mages from learning the other one?<br /> <br /> Now, I understand the need for some basic limit, so we don't have Gnosis 1 Masters running around, but that could be solved by, say, making the upper limit mage's Gnosis +2 for non-Archmasters. That would basically create the same kind of limit like 1e core for the first Arcana new mage gets and wouldn't require that half page long table that doesn't make much sense to me from a roleplaying perspective...<br /> <br /> So, how does 2e deal with this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're simplified (no more giant table), and slightly harsher than in 1st ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:26:47-07:00","id":642017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=642015#post642015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They're simplified (no more giant table), and slightly harsher than in 1st ed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do the new limits still extend to Arcana 6-9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 08-27-2015, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:42:06-07:00","id":642034,"title":"","content":"Dave, would you be willing to spoil us on details of those limits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:57:15-07:00","id":642116,"title":"","content":"Is rampant speculation allowed in this thread? I have some rampant speculation on that one but I don't want to transgress any social norms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:15:04-07:00","id":642134,"title":"","content":"I think you are safe. Speculate away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:25:07-07:00","id":642144,"title":"","content":"So, simplifying and tightening up the Gnosis-to-Arcana limits. The obvious way to simplify without just going to a straight cap is to use things the system already has in it: the Ruling, Common and Inferior Arcana.<br /> <br /> My guess is that it's something along the lines of Gnosis 1: Ruling 3, Common 2, Inferior 1 (or even 0) - a few more 2s available but fewer 3s shakes out to be more of a limit in my eyes.<br /> <br /> If it's staying fairly close to the 1e version, I'd expect Ruling 4 at Gnosis 2, Common 3 at 2 or 3, Ruling 5 at 3 or 4, and proooooobably Common 4 at 4 or 5; choose the latter of all the &quot;or&quot; options and you get a nice progression.<br /> <br /> That means no Masters of non-Ruling Arcana below Gnosis 6, but that may not be as much of a problem as I initially thought - I'm probably too used to Exalted's Essence track, where the jump from 5 to 6 is much harder to cross than it is for nWoD power stats. In general it does make Ruling Arcana a notable chunk more important than they are in 1e, and specialising in non-Ruling ones that bit harder (without Legacies to help).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I'd fit the Inferior Arcanum in but it'd be on a similar sort of track.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I may be totally wrong in every way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:34:28-07:00","id":642148,"title":"","content":"I find it plausible. Dave said something akin to Gnosis being the splat stat that mages tend to have higher than other splats have their respective stats (like Blood Potency). I think he said that Gnosis 7 or 8 isn't that uncommon and it's the Gnosis 9 and 10 mages that are really scary (I guess mainly because of the sharp Mana increase, if we go by the 1e numbers). These comments should be somewhere in the comments section of one of the dev blogs or their respective threads. It may have changed, though. It was posted some time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:46:17-07:00","id":642154,"title":"","content":"That in mind, it may well be a slower progression than I have down there - though actually that track (Ruling increasing at even scores and Common at odd ones) would allow Archmastery at 6 and Mastery of Common Arcana at 7, which might match that &quot;not that uncommon&quot; you mention.<br /> <br /> I fully expect the actual way it works to be clever and subtle in a way I haven't thought of...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T06:56:26-07:00","id":647941,"title":"","content":"Would an active defensive mage spell provoke Clash of Wills if a supernatural power was used against the mage? Example: Mage has a Mind spell up to protect them from mind control, and a vampire attempts to use Dominate. Would that provoke a Gnosis + Mind vs. Blood Potency + Dominate roll or would the Dominate just bounce off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:03:23-07:00","id":647944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=647941#post647941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an active defensive mage spell provoke Clash of Wills if a supernatural power was used against the mage? Example: Mage has a Mind spell up to protect them from mind control, and a vampire attempts to use Dominate. Would that provoke a Gnosis + Mind vs. Blood Potency + Dominate roll or would the Dominate just bounce off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not many spells in 1ed provoke Clash of wills. They generally act as dots of armor against effects, subtracting dice from the attempt to, say, mind control the mage. I expect this will change in 2ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:09:43-07:00","id":647950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=647944#post647944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not many spells in 1ed provoke Clash of wills. They generally act as dots of armor against effects, subtracting dice from the attempt to, say, mind control the mage. I expect this will change in 2ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure that might be how it actually works, since I have been reading Clash of Wills as a sort of...blanket rule for dealing with edge cases. I figure the rules for a Mind Shield spell will indicate how exactly it interacts with attempts to alter the mind via magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T21:07:20-07:00","id":690857,"title":"","content":"These questions might not be simple, but this seems like the best thread to ask.<br /> <br /> What options to Archmages have to become immortal, that is, never die from old age? I figured that, rules as written, they would need to use the Practice Of Excision to remove some part of their Pattern linked to the process of aging. Life, Time and Death all sound fitting for this, but what other Arcana might work? If I remember correctly, you can stop the aging process with 5 dots of Time and Reach in 2ED, but you'd be one dispellation away from being reduced to a pile of ash and bone chunks, like an elder vampire suffering Final Death. A spell cast with an Imperial Practice is much more sturdy, I bet. That being said, creative use of magic could achieve the same goal with &quot;just&quot; the Practice Of Dynamics. Again, Life, Time and Death sound like the most likely options.<br /> <br /> If the Potency of spells in 2ED is Withstood by Stamina, Resolve or Composure, does that mean a Rank 5 entity with the Simplified Resistance Attribute at 15 is nigh impossible to affect without tons of Reach and Yantras? It is appropriate for a being of such power, I admit, but it seems even a Rank 3 entity with Resistance 9 could prove very hard to control without a lot of Paradox risk. Am I reading the 2ED rules right?<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries says that entities of Rank 6+ can duplicate the effects of the Common Practices of any Arcanum, as long as the effect is related to its Influences. All Mana costs are converted to Essence. So a Rank 6 entity is treated as having an initial Primary Factor of 6 for all these Influences-As-Arcana, right? What would be their equivalents of Reach and Advanced Spell Factors? What would they have to do if they wanted to imitate an Unraveling spell that deals aggravated damage (which requires 1 Reach + 1 Mana in 2ED)? They already get [Rank] bonus successes on rolls related to their Influences, but could they spend Essence to boost their Power and Finesse to improve dice pools for Influences? Am I looking at it from the wrong angle and missing something obvious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-06-2015, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T00:11:09-07:00","id":690938,"title":"","content":"Two dots, a Mage in 2e can stop aging with 2 dots in Time.<br /> <br /> Good, a Rank 3 entity is supposed to be powerful, it's in line to be difficult to control. It has nothing to do with Paradox though, increasing Reach doesn't make your spell stronger in terms of the Withstand mechanic.<br /> <br /> Hard to say, but the folks in the W:tF forum could probably give you a better answer anyways. Spirits almost certainly don't use Reach or any other Mage mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T00:38:49-07:00","id":690947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=690938#post690938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good, a Rank 3 entity is supposed to be powerful, it's in line to be difficult to control. It has nothing to do with Paradox though, increasing Reach doesn't make your spell stronger in terms of the Withstand mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main way to pump your Potency is by Reaching, right? So not all Reach makes you stronger for that mechanic, but you need that specific Reach to get over a high Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T00:49:41-07:00","id":690951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=690947#post690947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main way to pump your Potency is by Reaching, right? So not all Reach makes you stronger for that mechanic, but you need that specific Reach to get over a high Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>They way I understand it so far Potency is still a spell factor, which means you raise it by taking dice penalties to your casting dice pool, not by using Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T01:08:26-07:00","id":690959,"title":"","content":"What BlueBiscuit said. <br /> <br /> Potency and Reach only interact by using a Reach for Advanced Potency which only makes your spell harder to dispel and has no effect on its ability to overcome Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:57:09-07:00","id":690996,"title":"","content":"Oh, hmm - I was under the impression that improving your Spell Factors was another type of Reach. Guess I'm waiting for the book to see if I was wrong. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T03:22:19-07:00","id":691000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=690996#post690996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, hmm - I was under the impression that improving your Spell Factors was another type of Reach. Guess I'm waiting for the book to see if I was wrong. ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the devblog on Reach and Paradox, as well as Creative Thaumaturgy and the various example spells, I'm curious were you got that idea from (I honestly am, I could be wrong after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T03:40:05-07:00","id":691007,"title":"","content":"Not sure; most likely cause is the line in The Creative Arts about &quot;most Reach is spent to manipulate spell factors,&quot; which I now see could just be referring to Advanced factors.<br /> <br /> Having poked around a bit more, the Ivan Tischenko Must Die spellcasting example in The Man Comes Around has me pretty convinced I was wrong - Cowl's pulling extra Potency, but he &quot;is spending one Reach to cast the spell in a matter of seconds rather than taking an hour, another to use Advanced Duration, and another to cast at sensory range.&quot;<br /> <br /> No mention of Potency in the Reach section, so it looks like it's just a dice penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:46:43-07:00","id":693963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=691007#post691007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure; most likely cause is the line in The Creative Arts about &quot;most Reach is spent to manipulate spell factors,&quot; which I now see could just be referring to Advanced factors.<br /> <br /> Having poked around a bit more, the Ivan Tischenko Must Die spellcasting example in The Man Comes Around has me pretty convinced I was wrong - Cowl's pulling extra Potency, but he &quot;is spending one Reach to cast the spell in a matter of seconds rather than taking an hour, another to use Advanced Duration, and another to cast at sensory range.&quot;<br /> <br /> No mention of Potency in the Reach section, so it looks like it's just a dice penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ivan Tishchenko Must Die</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it Advanced Potency... He doesn't think anyone's going to try to Dispel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had an idea.<br /> <br /> Advanced Potency adds Potency to the dispellation Clash of Wills. So Gnosis+Arcanum vs Gnosis+Arcanum+Potency.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't, I play a Mystagogue in my next Mage game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:50:50-07:00","id":693968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=693963#post693963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had an idea.<br /> <br /> Advanced Potency adds Potency to the dispellation Clash of Wills. So Gnosis+Arcanum vs Gnosis+Arcanum+Potency.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't, I play a Mystagogue in my next Mage game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know that dispellation (as opposed to Countering, which definitely is a Clash) is a Clash of Wills? I could see it being a straightforward &quot;potency of Dispel subtracts from potency of the spell it targets,&quot; or something similar; there are a few possibilities for what Advanced Potency could do if it's not a Clash, including &quot;can't subtract, it's totally nuke the spell or nothing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T11:05:03-07:00","id":694066,"title":"","content":"Dispelation is not a Clash of Wills. Countermagic is a Clash of Wills - Dispel Magic is just a Prime spell, Withstood by the Arcanum rating of the mage who cast the spell you're dispelling, plus two if they used Advanced Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T12:01:07-07:00","id":694128,"title":"","content":"Damn. When is Dark Eras expected to come out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T12:25:01-07:00","id":694133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=694066#post694066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dispelation is not a Clash of Wills. Countermagic is a Clash of Wills - Dispel Magic is just a Prime spell, Withstood by the Arcanum rating of the mage who cast the spell you're dispelling, plus two if they used Advanced Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the spoilers, Dave!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T15:59:29-07:00","id":694261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=693963#post693963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I just had an idea.<br /> <br /> Advanced Potency adds Potency to the dispellation Clash of Wills. So Gnosis+Arcanum vs Gnosis+Arcanum+Potency.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't, I play a Mystagogue in my next Mage game.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=694066#post694066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dispelation is not a Clash of Wills. Countermagic is a Clash of Wills - Dispel Magic is just a Prime spell, Withstood by the Arcanum rating of the mage who cast the spell you're dispelling, plus two if they used Advanced Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Tambov, it looks like someone is playing Mystagogue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T04:38:38-07:00","id":694730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=694261#post694261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, Tambov, it looks like someone is playing Mystagogue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I already have a concept - Thyrsus (L3S2P1) focused on &quot;Magic is alive&quot;. Shadow Name Simurgh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T04:39:19-07:00","id":694731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Tambov, it looks like someone is playing Mystagogue <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! AP, or it never happen! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:45:42-07:00","id":694753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=694066#post694066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dispelation is not a Clash of Wills. Countermagic is a Clash of Wills - Dispel Magic is just a Prime spell, Withstood by the Arcanum rating of the mage who cast the spell you're dispelling, plus two if they used Advanced Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>So pumping the Potency up doesn't make it any harder to dispel, and a Master's potency-1 Unveiling spell is harder to dispel than an Apprentice's one, even if they do exactly the same things as far as difficulty to dispel go. Cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:43:07-07:00","id":695037,"title":"","content":"I'm having a really hard time waiting for this to come out. I really want to see how spellcasting balances out without the ability to extended cast and accrue dozens of successes. Impatient!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:31:40-07:00","id":695319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=695037#post695037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a really hard time waiting for this to come out. I really want to see how spellcasting balances out without the ability to extended cast and accrue dozens of successes. Impatient!</div> </div> </div> </div>Extended casting is dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:49:46-07:00","id":695329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=695319#post695319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extended casting is dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, hence &quot;without.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:56:09-07:00","id":695332,"title":"","content":"Didn't Dave say that there were going to be extended casting rules in the book as an alternative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T15:05:41-07:00","id":695399,"title":"","content":"I don't think so. If I remember correctly, all spellcasting is one roll now. That's not to say that it won't take a long time, all spells default to ritual time based on your Gnosis and it takes Reach to cast it in combat time, but even if you take three hours to cast, it will still be just one roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T15:18:52-07:00","id":695404,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the normal rules are as you say. But I'm sure I remember him saying something about there being extended casting as alternate rules. I assume it'd be something like the alternate rules that the other two 2e books have had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:21:58-07:00","id":695436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=695332#post695332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Dave say that there were going to be extended casting rules in the book as an alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We intended to do some when 2e was a writer's bible and an awful lot of private list discussions, but it never made it into the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T17:31:31-07:00","id":695512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=695436#post695436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We intended to do some when 2e was a writer's bible and an awful lot of private list discussions, but it never made it into the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean we can expect it in a supplement at some point down the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T18:14:20-07:00","id":695564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=695512#post695512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean we can expect it in a supplement at some point down the line?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point, probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T07:44:52-07:00","id":697105,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, if ritual casting was so imbalanced (aka, op) as to be removed from the game, what was the reason to default all spells to &quot;ritual&quot; time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T07:59:08-07:00","id":697140,"title":"","content":"Rituals themselves are not the problem, and it's a default assumption of the setting that Mages are scarier with time to plan and prepare than any other splat. The mechanics were what broke so they got fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T08:02:03-07:00","id":697141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=697105#post697105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, if ritual casting was so imbalanced (aka, op) as to be removed from the game, what was the reason to default all spells to &quot;ritual&quot; time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ritual casting wasn't removed from the game at all. As you noted, the default casting time is ritual now. The actual change was that the normal action mechanic will be used instead of the extended action mechanic for ritual spells. Thus ritual spells are now just normal actions that take longer than one turn.<br /> <br /> The problem with extended actions was that the resulting number of successes increases quadratically with your stats, instead of linearly. The obscenely high possible results do not interact nicely with a system mostly based on the normal action mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T08:09:12-07:00","id":697183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=697105#post697105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, if ritual casting was so imbalanced (aka, op) as to be removed from the game, what was the reason to default all spells to &quot;ritual&quot; time?</div> </div> </div> </div>We didn't remove it because it was imbalanced. We removed it because including it means effectively writing the core spellcasting system twice - you need to redo every Spell Factor and Yantra for number-of-successes rather than dice pool penalty/bonus, tweak every Merit that affects spellcasting.<br /> <br /> On top of which, spellcasting isn't something you can do for a while, have a break mid-way through, then return to, like a proper extended action. The second-edition extended action rules include things we would't want (like the timing changes for exceptional successes)...<br /> <br /> We decided it wasn't worth it. Mages still cast in rituals by default, and even get a benefit from taking extra time, but mechanically it's a single roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T08:52:25-07:00","id":697253,"title":"","content":"Glad to read that. I loved the old system of extended rolls for rituals, and I didn't like its elimination. But your explanation has absolutelly convinced me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T10:03:17-07:00","id":697533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=697183#post697183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We didn't remove it because it was imbalanced. We removed it because including it means effectively writing the core spellcasting system twice - you need to redo every Spell Factor and Yantra for number-of-successes rather than dice pool penalty/bonus, tweak every Merit that affects spellcasting.<br /> <br /> On top of which, spellcasting isn't something you can do for a while, have a break mid-way through, then return to, like a proper extended action. The second-edition extended action rules include things we would't want (like the timing changes for exceptional successes)...<br /> <br /> We decided it wasn't worth it. Mages still cast in rituals by default, and even get a benefit from taking extra time, but mechanically it's a single roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>It worked very well in practice, and my players appreciated not having to roll multiple handfuls of dice for their rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T19:49:04-07:00","id":698319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=697183#post697183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We didn't remove it because it was imbalanced. We removed it because including it means effectively writing the core spellcasting system twice - you need to redo every Spell Factor and Yantra for number-of-successes rather than dice pool penalty/bonus, tweak every Merit that affects spellcasting.<br /> <br /> On top of which, spellcasting isn't something you can do for a while, have a break mid-way through, then return to, like a proper extended action. The second-edition extended action rules include things we would't want (like the timing changes for exceptional successes)...<br /> <br /> We decided it wasn't worth it. Mages still cast in rituals by default, and even get a benefit from taking extra time, but mechanically it's a single roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was not aware that you could take a break from an extended action. That would definitely break the fluff of a ritual. Also, I wasn't aware that the new ritual casting time could give you more benefits for taking longer. That definitely fixes (in my understanding) what seemed to be a mistake in the new edition. Also, having to roll multiple times and take into account on each roll for any penalties was a hastle, so fixing that is also nice. Awesome sauce all around. Thanks Dave! (Although the obvious disadvantage is that spells are now defaulted to ritual time instead of instant. Having to reach for instant sounds like a pain, though I suppose that is what you guys are going for, lol.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T20:06:31-07:00","id":698325,"title":"","content":"The benefit Dave is talking about, as far as I'm aware, is the one point of Reaxh you might have spent casting as an instant action. That being said though Reach is important! Grab it safely wherever you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T18:43:41-07:00","id":700377,"title":"","content":"From what I've seen, a mage in 2ED can stop aging with a simple Shielding spell from the Time Arcanum, which requires only 2 dots. If a mage using this spell lives to be 300 years old and another mage manages to dispell it, will the former turn into a skeleton and fall to the ground as the years catch up with him, like an old vampire suffering final death? Could the mage periodically re-cast this Shielding spell as his magical skill increases to make it harder and harder to dispell? Would a similar Time spell cast through the Practice Of Dynamics/Excision/Entities be immune to dispellation from the Common Practices in 2ED?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T18:55:06-07:00","id":700382,"title":"","content":"All I know is that it's been strongly hinted that there are some pretty bad unintended consequences of that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T20:50:28-07:00","id":700426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=700377#post700377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen, a mage in 2ED can stop aging with a simple Shielding spell from the Time Arcanum, which requires only 2 dots. If a mage using this spell lives to be 300 years old and another mage manages to dispell it, will the former turn into a skeleton and fall to the ground as the years catch up with him, like an old vampire suffering final death? Could the mage periodically re-cast this Shielding spell as his magical skill increases to make it harder and harder to dispell? Would a similar Time spell cast through the Practice Of Dynamics/Excision/Entities be immune to dispellation from the Common Practices in 2ED?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes<br /> 2. Yes<br /> <br /> But the second is likely irrelevant given what archmage would ever do that for a non archmage without some price worse than going for archmastery anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:01:58-07:00","id":700724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=700426#post700426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Yes<br /> 2. Yes<br /> <br /> But the second is likely irrelevant given what archmage would ever do that for a non archmage without some price worse than going for archmastery anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... think the answer to that is pretty clearly &quot;that depends on your story!&quot;<br /> <br /> The most obvious one is &quot;an Archmage bargains with a lesser mage - bring her the Quintessences for the big spell she really wants and the (much simpler) immortality spell, and she'll cast the immortality for you in return.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, it's gonna be rare and there'll be a cost, which might be quite unpleasant, but that's all fun and games - I definitely wouldn't write the plot hook off as irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T10:49:22-07:00","id":701099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=700724#post700724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... think the answer to that is pretty clearly &amp;quot;that depends on your story!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The most obvious one is &amp;quot;an Archmage bargains with a lesser mage - bring her the Quintessences for the big spell she really wants and the (much simpler) immortality spell, and she'll cast the immortality for you in return.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, it's gonna be rare and there'll be a cost, which might be quite unpleasant, but that's all fun and games - I definitely wouldn't write the plot hook off as irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Okaay, do whatever you like but don't expect me to buy in to it..<br /> 2. Exactly, the price will probably be too high against just shooting for archmastery themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T14:20:00-07:00","id":701292,"title":"","content":"Why the feeling that &quot;get me some Quintessences&quot; is going to be more painful and unpleasant than becoming an Archmaster? That's really not the way I'd run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:16:16-07:00","id":701335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=701292#post701292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the feeling that &amp;quot;get me some Quintessences&amp;quot; is going to be more painful and unpleasant than becoming an Archmaster? That's really not the way I'd run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why it depends on your story. That said, Quintessence is supposed to be hard to come by and something Arch mage actively work to cultivate.<br /> <br /> And even if not hard from the &quot;magical might&quot; stand point, anything that powerful should be hard for the player seeking such a boon. It could easily be that the spell proposed needs &quot;the life of your firstborn child, freely given, slain by your own hand.&quot; Not impossible to acquire, but... yeah. <br /> <br /> That said, if you want easier access to such boons, go for it. Just pointing out that all archmastery level boons should really make your players ask &quot;how badly do we need this?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:17:32-07:00","id":701336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=701292#post701292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the feeling that &amp;quot;get me some Quintessences&amp;quot; is going to be more painful and unpleasant than becoming an Archmaster? That's really not the way I'd run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just thinking if I'm the one in the position to grant true immortality my price isn't going to be small and the quest for that quintessence likely is going to border on the insane given the price I already paid for my immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T18:06:40-07:00","id":701481,"title":"","content":"A Mage seeking immortality from an archmaster would need to get two Quintessense minimum. One for his immortality and one for the archmaster's benefit. Becoming an archmaster is possibly the first act of imperial magic an archmaster performs and also pretty much requires a Quintessence. So figure that into your calculations I guess.<br /> <br /> Another method of immortality that occurs to me is to make a Pact. It probably counts as a major boon, so there's no reason an Archmaster would charge higher than that really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T20:12:47-07:00","id":701604,"title":"","content":"Could Silence or maybe even Cold be within the purview of Death magic the way Darkness is treated as a tangible thing rather than an absence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T22:00:13-07:00","id":701662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=701604#post701604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Silence or maybe even Cold be within the purview of Death magic the way Darkness is treated as a tangible thing rather than an absence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes to Silence, but would say that Cold would only be incidental or metaphorical. Chill of the grave and chills up your spine, but not ice or snow or freezing things solid. Personal interpretation. Could definitely see extinguishing fires and killing the heat from a heat based attack, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T22:04:43-07:00","id":701665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=701604#post701604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Silence or maybe even Cold be within the purview of Death magic the way Darkness is treated as a tangible thing rather than an absence?</div> </div> </div> </div> I am unsure. Judging from open dev, you would need Forces for that, via sound and heat bending. A Forces Unmaking spell could destroy all the heat inside an area or a person, bringing it to zero Kelvin. Another Forces Unmaking spell could make all sound disappear. For less overt control of sound and heat, there are the Practices Of Compelling and Ruling. There are no &quot;speed bumps&quot; anymore in the dot ratings of the Arcana, so that's good. Death is gonna be mainly about souls, but I don't think the aspects of darkness and ghosts will be removed. Speaking personally, I see nothing wrong with giving some silence and cold spells to Death, but Forces would probably do it better. You could also use Mind to induce deafness and make people feel like the temprature dropped, but it would just be hallucinations. This is just a hunch, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T01:05:21-07:00","id":701831,"title":"","content":"There hasn't been anything to suggest Death is &quot;mainly&quot; about souls. It has been said that it will be the arcanum that deals with souls, but that's just part of its purview.<br /> <br /> That being said, Death can probably do cold and silence via Fraying, Unravelling and Unmaking because Death is also about entropy. It could kill even spells so why not heat and sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T04:09:27-07:00","id":701931,"title":"","content":"The biggest changes to Death is that it won't be dealing with spirits but secrets will be within its purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T05:52:55-07:00","id":702010,"title":"","content":"It never dealt with spirits, it's always been ghosts and will continue to cover ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T08:57:45-07:00","id":702214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=702010#post702010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never dealt with spirits, it's always been ghosts and will continue to cover ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right I was thinking about Spirit and the fact that it did encroach into Death's purview in some cases when I wrote that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T09:41:30-07:00","id":702250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=702214#post702214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right I was thinking about Spirit and the fact that it did encroach into Death's purview in some cases when I wrote that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mostly the stuff dealing with Souls that was perhaps wrongly spread around Death, Spirit and wierdly Prime. Having it all under one Arcana definately makes things simpler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T10:01:12-07:00","id":702283,"title":"","content":"It does screw with the idea that the soul is made up of and influenced by the subtle arcana though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T13:48:29-07:00","id":702492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=702283#post702283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does screw with the idea that the soul is made up of and influenced by the subtle arcana though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;made of the subtle Arcana&quot; was an in setting theory, to explain why the Subtle Arcana each had influence over the soul. Not saying it is a bad theory, but there were other suggested explanations of the nature and composition of the soul, as well as inconsistencies with said theory in the mechanics in 1e. For example, Archmastery of Death (I forget what Dot requirement) allowed wholesale creation of a Soul without other Arcana, which points to Death having sole purview of the soul as a complete entity; this doesn't completely contradict said theory, but raises questions about it.Also, the logic behind the Subtle Arcana making up the soul wasn't always able to supoort how they directly interacted: fate for example was more indirect soul effects, such as being Unfettered and its benefits(i.e. preventing Soul Theft) which stemmed more from it just countering magic that would be to the detriment of a mage destiny rather than being specific to the soul.<br /> <br /> If 2e cleans things up and places the soul primarily under the purview of just Death, it might help mechanically make things more consistent and change up a bit of the cosmology of the soul. Still, it doesn't completely invalidate that idea though, so who knows what 2e will bring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 10-15-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T20:33:57-07:00","id":702960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=702492#post702492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, Archmastery of Death (I forget what Dot requirement) allowed wholesale creation of a Soul without other Arcana, which points to Death having sole purview of the soul as a complete entity; this doesn't completely contradict said theory, but raises questions about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>why do people always remember entities spells of death that way<br /> <br /> when the line is literally <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Create a new soul <b>for a target that has lost their own.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T22:28:17-07:00","id":703004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=702960#post702960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why do people always remember entities spells of death that way<br /> <br /> when the line is literally </div> </div> </div> </div>While I do appreciate the rule clarification, I feel it overlooks my actual point: in 1e, Death, without any other Subtle Arcana, can create a new soul. Even if it is one for someone who has lost there own, as you point out, it is still completely creating a new, complete soul. Unless you are implying that the part that is lost is just the &quot;death fraction&quot; and the other 4 &quot;subtle&quot; fractions remain, I don't see why it undermines the initial point I was making: while the 5 subtle being what makes up the soul is an in-setting theory, it is just that, and other elements have pointed to there being alternative natures and primarily under Death's purview.<br /> <br /> (And if you take the fraction approach, it is raising more questions, as it then means that what Mage's are describing as souls aren't the complete soul, or the 4 other subtle actually aren't part of what Mage's are saying is the soul, which means the &quot;soul&quot; isn't actually made of the 5 subtle arcana anyway, but is just a bit manipulated by Death and a few other things at time, and Mage's don't actually know what the &quot;True&quot; soul is... Which could be really cool, come to think of it...)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, use whatever works for your game. Or better yet, leave the Soul a Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T23:06:40-07:00","id":703013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=703004#post703004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I do appreciate the rule clarification, I feel it overlooks my actual point: in 1e, Death, without any other Subtle Arcana, can create a new soul. Even if it is one for someone who has lost there own, as you point out, it is still completely creating a new, complete soul. Unless you are implying that the part that is lost is just the &quot;death fraction&quot; and the other 4 &quot;subtle&quot; fractions remain, I don't see why it undermines the initial point I was making: while the 5 subtle being what makes up the soul is an in-setting theory, it is just that, and other elements have pointed to there being alternative natures and primarily under Death's purview.<br /> <br /> (And if you take the fraction approach, it is raising more questions, as it then means that what Mage's are describing as souls aren't the complete soul, or the 4 other subtle actually aren't part of what Mage's are saying is the soul, which means the &quot;soul&quot; isn't actually made of the 5 subtle arcana anyway, but is just a bit manipulated by Death and a few other things at time, and Mage's don't actually know what the &quot;True&quot; soul is... Which could be really cool, come to think of it...)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, use whatever works for your game. Or better yet, leave the Soul a Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've felt it was fairly obvious that what Mages describe as &quot;souls&quot; as influenced by the Death Arcanum cannot, in fact, be the entire soul. If a Mage with a Legacy (specifically said to be something that shapes your soul) loses their &quot;soul&quot; due to magic and then reacquires a &quot;soul&quot;, even one from a Mage with a different Legacy <i>or a Sleeper</i>, they keep their Legacy. A Mage that loses their &quot;soul&quot;, becomes a Sleeper, and then regains <i>any</i> &quot;soul&quot; (again, even a Sleeper's), once again Awakens even in 1e; Awakening is also a process that modifies the soul's connection to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Any character that loses their &quot;soul&quot; has the effects of their Virtue and Vice swapped, but <i>they do not replace their Virtue or Vice</i>. This, again, indicates that simply losing their &quot;soul&quot; does not actually affect who they <i>are</i> in any fundamental way any more than losing a hand would. And if a character were to get a new &quot;soul&quot;, from any source, they do not change anything about themselves (i.e. Virtue and Vice and overall personality stay the same or are changed only insofar as events would normally change them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T00:19:50-07:00","id":703067,"title":"","content":"Can we try and trace which &quot;parts of the soul&quot; the Subtle Arcana deal with? Also, I mean to guess at a &quot;regular human soul&quot;. I`m sure the soul of changelings, vampires and others are a bit more complex.<br /> <br /> Death = Integrity and the general health of it.<br /> Fate = Well, its own Fate (call it `free will` or the endless possibilities a person may have in life).<br /> Mind = Vice/Virtue + emotions and memories.<br /> Prime = Its &quot;connection with the Fallen World&quot; as in &quot;not abyssal&quot;. Its possibility to Awaken or not. Its &quot;realness&quot; as in: it possesses a unique supernal symbol for it.<br /> Spirit = Its... instincts? I feel that &quot;Spirit&quot; is a Subtle Counterpart for &quot;Life&quot;, but I don't know how to put it into words :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T02:29:11-07:00","id":703125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=701336#post701336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just thinking if I'm the one in the position to grant true immortality my price isn't going to be small and the quest for that quintessence likely is going to border on the insane given the price I already paid for my immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods*<br /> <br /> I think my difference of approach (noting that I was saying &quot;less difficult than achieving Archmastery&quot; not &quot;not difficult&quot; ;-) ) comes from the fact that immortality, to me, looks like a side benefit of Archmastery - I wouldn't tend to think of Archmasters having paid their price for immortality, I'd be thinking of it as paying their price for VAST(er) COSMIC POWER.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T02:49:43-07:00","id":703150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=703125#post703125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my difference of approach (noting that I was saying &quot;less difficult than achieving Archmastery&quot; not &quot;not difficult&quot; ;-) ) comes from the fact that immortality, to me, looks like a side benefit of Archmastery - I wouldn't tend to think of Archmasters having paid their price for immortality, I'd be thinking of it as paying their price for VAST(er) COSMIC POWER.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you see only a universe of dust, sifting through the motes seems almost casual. Everything crumbles so easily. It's all relative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-16-2015, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T04:21:19-07:00","id":703182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=703013#post703013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've felt it was fairly obvious that what Mages describe as &quot;souls&quot; as influenced by the Death Arcanum cannot, in fact, be the entire soul. If a Mage with a Legacy (specifically said to be something that shapes your soul) loses their &quot;soul&quot; due to magic and then reacquires a &quot;soul&quot;, even one from a Mage with a different Legacy <i>or a Sleeper</i>, they keep their Legacy. A Mage that loses their &quot;soul&quot;, becomes a Sleeper, and then regains <i>any</i> &quot;soul&quot; (again, even a Sleeper's), once again Awakens even in 1e; Awakening is also a process that modifies the soul's connection to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Any character that loses their &quot;soul&quot; has the effects of their Virtue and Vice swapped, but <i>they do not replace their Virtue or Vice</i>. This, again, indicates that simply losing their &quot;soul&quot; does not actually affect who they <i>are</i> in any fundamental way any more than losing a hand would. And if a character were to get a new &quot;soul&quot;, from any source, they do not change anything about themselves (i.e. Virtue and Vice and overall personality stay the same or are changed only insofar as events would normally change them).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want the this thread to get off track, so I suggest we move over to another one of the many soul thread. My entire original point was addressing <i>specifically</i>that component that is now falling under Death's purview in 1e and which is called a &quot;soul&quot; in Mage (both in-setting and in the game mechanics). <br /> <br /> Yes, there is a hell of a lot more going on, as you pointed out (legacies, identity) but the original discussion was on what the thing called the &quot;soul&quot; is made of/ why death was going to be the primary arcana controlling it.<br /> <br /> Plus, we don't know if those other aspects are even tied to a greater soul either. We can assume they are, but they might also be entirely different things (i.e. each element is technically unrelated to the other, such as you Legacy vessel aspect being completely unrelated to the Vice/Virtue part), with these components interacting with and being regulated by the thing called the soul (which acts as a sorta mission command/power source for those things). <br /> <br /> We just don't know enough.... which honestly, I like it being left open as a Mystery. (Though if Dave come in and gives a concrete explanation, I wouldn't be displeased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 10-25-2015, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:18:01-07:00","id":727444,"title":"","content":"are there lay-lines on other world / moons / space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:25:21-07:00","id":727458,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, are you asking if there's something like, I dunno... a galactic leyline? <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://40.media.tumblr.com/1dabc3c02b79faec4e044c76cf72af22/tumblr_nhn1arE1EK1symw83o1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span style=\"font-size:8px\">whatisthydesire</span></div></div> </div> </div></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-25-2015, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:13:56-08:00","id":767917,"title":"","content":"Why dont Time mages just win the lottery? Seers?<br /> <br /> Suppose the cabal is confronted by a mystery. Is there (and should there) be anything preventing time mages from looking into the future where they have already solved the mystery and just short circuit the investigation process? I guess &quot;Who will I discover the murderer to be?&quot; could potentially finger an innocent person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:16:29-08:00","id":768095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=767917#post767917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why dont Time mages just win the lottery? Seers?<br /> <br /> Suppose the cabal is confronted by a mystery. Is there (and should there) be anything preventing time mages from looking into the future where they have already solved the mystery and just short circuit the investigation process? I guess &quot;Who will I discover the murderer to be?&quot; could potentially finger an innocent person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time magic definitely makes things interesting. The lottery one definitely is a tricky one, because it is totally doable within the rules. That said, as you point out, it is also a way to out yourself. As someone who one a sizable ticket once, you need to show multiple ID's, fill out lots of paperwork, etc. (and I only won about $1k). Nevermind that large wins garner media attention, and staying under the radar just makes you more of a focus for the media. I always felt that doing something like this was a good story hook, as all those red tape and public spotlight things make the player stand out (and I bet both diamond and pentacle watch for such manipulations). It is likely the same for things like stock market, if not more so, since not only does exceptional lock in the market make you stand out as exceptional (and evidence shows luck does play a good bit in the market), you are messing with the economy... Which no order would want.<br /> <br /> And the second one is easy: Paradox! As you pointed out, if you solve it by looking to the future to solve it, how did you first solve it? All glimpses of the future will change the present, but peeking to solve a mystery risks a huge conundrum: if current you is looking ahead to see the investigation and learn the answer, then no one would investigate... Which leads to the question of how you found out... In theory, if the police solve the case and you simply act on that future release of info, and never fill the cops in in the present, that could avoid this issue, but it means anything purely supernatural investigated solely by the canal will have some headaches.<br /> <br /> Other reasons I have used is that the future is a nebulous mess that is trickier to pin down the more you look at it and the more troublesome of a question. Lotteries are going to be drawn at a set time and day, but the course of an investigation can lead to numerous turns and outcomes. For example, a player looking ahead could lead them to see the entire cabal dead, Mystery unsolved, which leads to both story hooks (how did they die, what can they do to avoid it) as well as keep the main story hidden. Or how far ahead do the mages know to look? &quot;When I solve the case&quot; isn't a time period you can know until you solve it.<br /> <br /> Another option of it is a magic based mystery is Shields of Cronos and other magic meant to hide the future. It sounds cheap, but remember: the NPCs might be able to use magic too, and if a PC can think of a solution, so clike an NPC, and that means they would seem means to counter said solutions.<br /> <br /> But your questions raise a good point, and the best answer whenever you have this is to:<br /> -if a storyteller look for his to make such tricks lead to more questions and interesting story rather than shut it down. You should try to both create initial plots that aren't simple to solve (political, magical and catspaws all help) with a spell, and fun alternates if someone finds such a gap. Avoid railroading or shutting down creativity, but instead lead to each wrinkle a player creates lead to a new branch of the plot that lets you throw more into the story (like a Paradox Gulmoth summoned by manipulation of games of chance with Time or Fate magic...)<br /> -if a player, not feel like the storyteller is shutting you down but trying to make a more interesting story. It is cool you can create an instant answer, but remember that as a group, that means the game is over if you remove all the challenge, and a ST who makes things not work out perfectly is just trying to create a good story (hopefully... Feel free to call them out if they are railroading all the fun out of it).<br /> <br /> I hope that is somewhat helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 11-17-2015, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T16:23:31-08:00","id":768161,"title":"","content":"There's an issue similar to this that's actually addressed in the legacy write-up for the 11Q for 2e. You can ask questions of the future.<br /> <br /> From what I remember, Dave has said that spells like Prophecy create models of the future which subsequent castings of Prophecy (Even by other Mages) causes to change. So, I think you could certainly check to see the answer to a mystery in the future, but you'd run the risk of the answer suddenly becoming invalidated by time shenanigans from other Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T19:39:51-08:00","id":768240,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T10:17:19-08:00","id":768579,"title":"","content":"Ok another question, this time about Shield of Chronos. In Soul Cages, there was a point where the party tried to use Time magic to predict the next Seer attack on Samael, but they failed because of Shield of Chronos. Does that mean that the Seers were under the shield at the time of the casting of the divination spell, or does that mean that they were time shielded during the actual attack that would take place in the future?<br /> <br /> Option one means that you have to get really lucky or be warded basically all the time to be protected but option two puts you in a weird situation where you are retroactively changing the outcomes of past actions or creating predestination situations, which does not recommend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T11:18:53-08:00","id":768617,"title":"","content":"I don't see why both options aren't possible. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T11:35:28-08:00","id":768629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=768579#post768579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">option two puts you in a weird situation where you are retroactively changing the outcomes of past actions or creating predestination situations, which does not recommend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's any worse than prophecy-type spells <i>without</i> the shield - if your enemies scry for &quot;the next time we're attacked&quot; that depends on when you're currently planning to attack them, so you're still affecting things back in time whether or not you timeward yourself before doing that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T18:51:29-08:00","id":768842,"title":"","content":"You put on the Shield of Chronos when you're doing the thing you don't want people to see. So, it's like when burglars break into your house, they wear dark clothing, come at night, and make sure the lights are turned off. No one can see you. You're going to attack someone, so you cloak yourself in the Shield of Chronos during the attack so that no one looking back on that night or forward to that night will be able to see you do it.<br /> <br /> I don't see how it's retroactively changing the outcomes of past actions or creating predestination situations... Can you elaborate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T19:24:12-08:00","id":768866,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to rob a house in 12 hours. No Shield of Chronos. Owner of the house casts a spell to check if his house is robbed in 12 hours, he sees me, he reacts. Future will change if his actions interact with mine. Or not.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to rob a house in 12 hours. I'm planning on casting Shield of Chronos when I'm inside. Owner of the house casts a spell to check if his house is robbed in 12 hours. Still uncast Shield of Chronos fizzles his spell. He may act upon this knowledge to interfere with the future, for example by being at home when I planned to attack, and thus making me not cast Shield of Chronos at all.<br /> <br /> From game perspective, this might seem like creating retroactive changes, because player's choice of using Shield of Chronos now might affect divinations that happened before player declared that action. So if your player didn't declare that he intends on using that spell beforehand, but remembers about it and casts it &quot;when the time comes&quot;, you may have to retroactively change events that assumed his action was divined properly. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:19:06-08:00","id":768910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=768866#post768866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to rob a house in 12 hours. No Shield of Chronos. Owner of the house casts a spell to check if his house is robbed in 12 hours, he sees me, he reacts. Future will change if his actions interact with mine. Or not.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to rob a house in 12 hours. I'm planning on casting Shield of Chronos when I'm inside. Owner of the house casts a spell to check if his house is robbed in 12 hours. Still uncast Shield of Chronos fizzles his spell. He may act upon this knowledge to interfere with the future, for example by being at home when I planned to attack, and thus making me not cast Shield of Chronos at all.<br /> <br /> From game perspective, this might seem like creating retroactive changes, because player's choice of using Shield of Chronos now might affect divinations that happened before player declared that action. So if your player didn't declare that he intends on using that spell beforehand, but remembers about it and casts it &quot;when the time comes&quot;, you may have to retroactively change events that assumed his action was divined properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is circular. It seems like his reaction is the diviner's reaction is the same whether or not the Shield of Chronos was cast.From a storyteller's or players perspective, you've got to roll with the punches. The NPC divines the crime if there is no Shield of Chronos, or the NPC can't divine the crime because of the Shield. There's what happens in the story and what happens out of the story. It's a good idea to keep them separate. If time being divined can't be seen the storyteller can know that whether or not the player is Shielding or divining, and can therefore plan accordingly. Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> It's getting all Schroedinger's Cat if you start mixing up in-fiction and out-of-fiction things. Either the door's locked or it's not -- whether or not someone plans on robbing you doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:54:51-08:00","id":769027,"title":"","content":"WHW: Shoeld of Cronos doesn't &quot;fizzle&quot; Divination spells for exactly this reason. You get an accurate reading, minus the presence and actions of the shielded Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T03:51:59-08:00","id":769085,"title":"","content":"I'm going to rob a house in 12 hours. The house owner casts divination, sees me robbing their house, and recognises me, so they come and find me in six hours and crack their knuckles menacingly. I decide not to rob the house.<br /> <br /> My future action of robbing the house has made the house owner take an action that then prevents the future action happening. Exactly the same thing - all precognition abilities are weird like that.<br /> <br /> (My two options for how to run it are &quot;what do you intend to do?&quot; and have NPCs act as appropriate, or - and this one is weirder and requires the players to be OK with it - actually running the original scene to see what would happen, then saying &quot;but that doesn't actually happen, because...&quot; and going into an earlier scene where the opposition intervene. There's a subtler option where the opposition turn out to have prepared for it in advance, like finding out the stuff in the safe was replaced with fakes because they knew you were going to rob it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:14:03-08:00","id":769125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=768910#post768910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is circular. It seems like his reaction is the diviner's reaction is the same whether or not the Shield of Chronos was cast.From a storyteller's or players perspective, you've got to roll with the punches. The NPC divines the crime if there is no Shield of Chronos, or the NPC can't divine the crime because of the Shield. There's what happens in the story and what happens out of the story. It's a good idea to keep them separate. If time being divined can't be seen the storyteller can know that whether or not the player is Shielding or divining, and can therefore plan accordingly. Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> It's getting all Schroedinger's Cat if you start mixing up in-fiction and out-of-fiction things. Either the door's locked or it's not -- whether or not someone plans on robbing you doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry but I can't quite parse what you are saying. It might help if you re-read and correct your post. Still, I will try to help to the best of my ability.<br /> <br /> Without a Shield of Chronos, the Diviner knows exactly what will happen and can take exact precautions. He might even contact the burglar to discourage them. If a Shield of Chronos is in place, the Diviner doesn't know what will happen, only that someone will cast this spell in his Sanctum. This is enough to become paranoid, investigate further and improve all of ones defences. In either case, the burglar could be affected by he investigation before he even decides to break in, but that's beside the point.<br /> <br /> The truth is that if you introduce Divination into the game you must learn to think four-dimensionally. You must predict what would have happened had nobody used a Divination spell. Then, if somebody uses a Divination spell, you give them relevant information and change the future accordingly. Also, you must do it each and every time someone casts a Divination spell. It requires you to ask your players about their future plans and about their reactions to most likely outcomes (What do you do if you succeed? What if someone is home? What if you're found out?). Also, whatever the characters do, you must keep in mind that interested parties might have already predicted it and let it go that far. That's a lot of work.<br /> <br /> There is a saving grace in the fact that Divinations stop being accurate the moment they're made. The minuscule changes in timing and the Butterfly Effect can land the characters in situations nobody predicted. If, after casting their spell, the Diviner accidentally inspires you to break into their Sanctum, you have time until their next Divination. Of course, you should have your Shield on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":".  Spelling error. 11-19-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:26:25-08:00","id":769144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=769125#post769125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a Shield of Chronos, the Diviner knows exactly what will happen and can take exact precautions. He might even contact the burglar to discourage them. If a Shield of Chronos is in place, the Diviner doesn't know what will happen, only that someone will cast this spell in his Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mrmdubois points out that that's not how it works - you get an accurate read of what would happen if the Shielded mage wasn't there, so in the analogy, it just looks like nothing happens.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a lot easier to run this sort of thing if you accept that you may need to do some retroactive work as the ST - things like revealing that the NPCs were prepared for what the PCs did in advance, because Divination. Pick ways to do this that wouldn't give any evidence beforehand - teleporting in at a crucial moment rather than being present but invisible, for example, since PCs could detect invisible people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:21:42-08:00","id":769374,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> You're right. My post isn't likely to make much sense. You're also right about the 4th dimensional thinking. I think that's what I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> Take Time magic out of the equation. Insert any other kind of magic and apply it to the problem. Example: You know your house is going to be robbed because you used Space to scry to the planning of the robbery; you used Forces to eavesdrop on the planning of the robbery; you used Spirits or Ghosts to do the same thing; etc. The same sort of issue comes up if the player or storyteller are not prepared for that. As a storyteller, what I do is approach every problem from the perspective of the players and I have an answer, clue, or plot hook for all the way the problem can be solved using magic. &quot;If they use Death, this is what happens...&quot; &quot;If they use Time, this is what they learn...&quot; etc. When Time 2 or greater is introduced in the game, the storyteller has to be prepared to answer those questions and deal with those issues. A murder mystery needs to be able to deal with Post Cognition and pre-cognition magic. Be prepared for that. If you're not prepared for that or you're not flexible, then it seems like a railroad and the players aren't going to have fun and the storyteller isn't either when the players get off the track.<br /> <br /> This question and this issue is not exclusive to the Shield of Chronos.<br /> <br /> Does that make more sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:58:00-08:00","id":769442,"title":"","content":"Unless you have a knack for nonlinear storytelling with en media res, flashbacks and the like then you don't have to generate a headache for yourself about it. Just ask yourself, is this NPC smart, or informed or have the ability to do divinations or counter them? If yes, then when the players make a move make a check to see if he reacts (Whether it's a &quot;future&quot; reaction or not) appropriately or not. Boom done.<br /> <br /> If you're good at nonlinear storytelling then you're already way past the point of worrying about this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, what Troy said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:29:59-08:00","id":769460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=769144#post769144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mrmdubois points out that that's not how it works - you get an accurate read of what would happen if the Shielded mage wasn't there, so in the analogy, it just looks like nothing happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have been thinking about Lynden Chambers' Attainment from &quot;Keys to the Supernal Tarot&quot;. Still, thank you for the correction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:29:07-08:00","id":773986,"title":"","content":"Is there any information on how Astral beings regain essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T14:19:08-08:00","id":776805,"title":"","content":"Will we get more info on the Aeons in 2ED? If the beings that Mages see in the Citadels of the Farthest Reaches next to the Ocean Oroboros are Rank 8 Goetia representing the 10 Arcana and the Abyss, then where are the true Aeons? Inside the Supernal Realms, right? Would they be Rank 9?<br /> <br /> Can the Matter and Prime Arcana be used to conjure or transmute materials to serve as Banes and the like? I remember that I once asked if a Forces spell could be used to deal aggravated damage to a tree spirit with fire as its Bane, and DaveB said that Banes don't have to be acquired through fully mundane means. If I wanted to create true hand-forged iron out of thin air to use against the True Fae, would I need Matter 5 + Prime 5? I think it is more of a case by case basis. Some entities of Rank 5+ or thereabouts might have unique objects as their Banes. I am also pretty sure that the True Fae would forbid magically created hand-forged iron from counting as their Bane if they had any say in the matter.<br /> <br /> If a Mage has Matter 4+, can he turn brute matter like rocks and metal into food and water? If yes, is it any different from normal food and water? Would he need Life 4+ as well to create or transmute food that is actually nutritious instead of just stomach-filling?<br /> <br /> If a Mage has Matter 4 and Life 4, and he turns a Sleeper into a stone, does the Mage choose whether or not they remain conscious? Because if they remained conscious, wouldn't Dissonance eventually cancel the spell? Can the Mage stipulate that this spell kills the target, or does the target always come back to their original, living Pattern when the Duration of the spell ends? If the target was a Sleepwalker, could the Mage make the duration of this spell Indefinite and leave the Sleepwalker conscious as a method of torture? I heard that affecting living Patterns without Archmastery is possible in 2ED, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:19:12-08:00","id":776898,"title":"","content":"I don't think much will be said about the Aeons in 2e. They are one of those things that are cool but not crucial for a core book with a limited page count. Also, I don't think there are Aeons in the supernal. Supernal &quot;inhabitants&quot; are each a kind of Truth, but it is implied in Imperial Mysteries that their shape depends on the interpretation of the observer. Rather than there being a single &quot;Arcana God&quot; it is possible that each Arcana is simply made by a nearly infinite cluster of interconnected Truths.<br /> <br /> Matter 4 can fully create organic matter, because organic chemistry is fully under its purview as long as the end result or the components are not &quot;alive&quot;. There is a distinction between something being organic in origin and being alive. For example, a piece of coal can be organic matter (created from burning wood) but certainly not alive.<br /> <br /> If you turn a person into stone, they are stone. Stone can't think. Perhaps with Mind you could keep someone conscious in this state. Perhaps as little as Mind 2 if you use that Arcana to &quot;shield&quot; their consciousness from being lost during the transformation? If not, probably Mind 4 to allow the stone to think, or something like that. However, perhaps your could only turn them *partially* to stone? I can't say if the transmutation would go back to normal at the end, because I think it hasn't been revealed how those spells work in general for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T21:02:14-08:00","id":776979,"title":"","content":"In one of DaveB's actual plays there is a Mage in that uses a matter/life spell to turn himself into &quot;living steel&quot; and he is capable of running around and fighting while in that state. He explicitly says &quot;body&quot; and not &quot;skin&quot;, which makes me think he is metal all the way through.<br /> <br /> He also explicitly discussed turning people to stone in a manner that is much more in line with what you were asking about, but it is hardly conclusive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -I turned them to Quartz- - Vyvain<br /> -What's required to do that?- - Persphone -<br /> -A high aptitude of the Life and Matter Arcana. But it wears off- - Vyvain<br /> -It does?- - Persephone<br /> -When cast by a Mage. It hurts like hell and is terrifying for the victim, but after a few months at most it will wear off- - Vyvain </div> </div> </div>He doesn't mention a sleeper target auto dispelling the effect, and in context that information could have been important. The victim feeling pain/fear could mean that they feel it as they are being turned into stone (though the transformation may be instantaneous) or it could mean they feel it for the entire duration, in which case a sleeper might be aware enough to dispel the effect. Like I said, inconclusive. It does seem to wear off once it is over though, at least in 1e. I remember reading that permanent effects on living patterns was a possibility in 2e.<br /> <br /> One of the player characters also speculated that the petrified person in the chronicle was the corpse of a victim of a very strange fraying spell that did damage by turning them into stone. DaveB didn't comment on that possibility either way, via gm text or a storyteller character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:13:04-08:00","id":778430,"title":"","content":"So I noticed in the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\">Paradoxical</a> teaser for 2nd Ed, Wolsey gets hit with a -2 penalty on his casting roll for switching to advanced duration for the spell factor. I was looking for where that gets elaborated upon in that and the other teaser blogs, but I can't find it.<br /> <br /> Basically: What caused that -2 penalty (obviously switching to <i>advanced</i> duration, but why?) and can adjusting other spell factors cause penalties? Would using an advanced damage factor change bashing damage to lethal, for instance?<br /> <br /> Danke!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:37:53-08:00","id":778444,"title":"","content":"Whenever you use spell factors you take dice penalties. There isn't a damage factor though, that's just Potency. There are two primary spell factors that I know of, Duration and Potency, your rating in an arcana provides a certain amount of automatic factors in the primary factor of a spell (So if you have Forces 3 your fire spell automatically has Potency 3, or Duration 3). There are other factors for spells that aren't primary, such as Targets and Area, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:48:36-08:00","id":778454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=778444#post778444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever you use spell factors you take dice penalties. There isn't a damage factor though, that's just Potency. There are two primary spell factors that I know of, Duration and Potency, your rating in an arcana provides a certain amount of automatic factors in the primary factor of a spell (So if you have Forces 3 your fire spell automatically has Potency 3, or Duration 3). There are other factors for spells that aren't primary, such as Targets and Area, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought increasing the factors of a spell required spending Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:56:08-08:00","id":778456,"title":"","content":"That's shifting to <i>advanced</i> factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:59:54-08:00","id":778461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=778456#post778456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's shifting to <i>advanced</i> factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, okay. I didn't play enough 1E Mage to know what that means, but I see from the blog post that the difference between regular duration and advanced duration increased Wolsey's spell from turns to weeks, so that makes some sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:08:48-08:00","id":778467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=778454#post778454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought increasing the factors of a spell required spending Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can both reach and take dice penalties. Since reach can be limited you usually use it to cast instantly and go for the advanced duration spell factor chart unless it's a Matter spell, and/or activate the reach options in the spells themselves. <br /> <br /> Damage is tied to Potency which is your arcanum rating and lethal/agg is tied to dot ratings of 4/5 plus mana for agg.<br /> <br /> So you take dice penalties to add further factors like 1e when you're reach is done or it's just better then taking another reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:09:18-08:00","id":778585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=778430#post778430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed in the [URL=&quot;http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/&quot;]<br /> <br /> Basically: What caused that -2 penalty (obviously switching to <i>advanced</i> duration, but why?) and can adjusting other spell factors cause penalties? Would using an advanced damage factor change bashing damage to lethal, for instance?<br /> <br /> Danke!</div> </div> </div> </div>The reach let him use the advanced duration factors, not the penalty. For instance, he could have taken a -2 penalty without reaching to increase the duration from 3 turns to, say, 6 turns or whatever the duration chart says it would be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:13:24-08:00","id":778589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=778461#post778461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, okay. I didn't play enough 1E Mage to know what that means, but I see from the blog post that the difference between regular duration and advanced duration increased Wolsey's spell from turns to weeks, so that makes some sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically you default to these charts where duration is measured in Turns. You take penalties to your casting pool to increase the number of turns your spell will last (if Duration is the Primary factor you already start with some extra turns). If you decide to Reach, you instead use a chart with more narrative time measures, starting with a whole Scene and going up by a day, then a week, then a month, a whole year, etc, etc*). You take penalties to go up that chart instead. So say I cast a spell taking a -6 penalty to go up 3 positions on the chart, without Reach that would net me, say 4 Turns (1 base + 3 extra), with Reach that same spell will last a whole month (starting at a Scene and advancing 3 steps).<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>We don't have the actual chart spoiled,but that seems the idea.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:34:09-08:00","id":781379,"title":"","content":"How hard it would be to use Apportation Spell to borrow fire from Sun, assuming Forces 2 and Space 3?<br /> EDIT<br /> To expand.<br /> I'm a person who never really cared for Space magics, and my players also never really used it, so I remained gleefuly ignorant for most of Space and Sympathetic magic aspects. This time, though, I'm considering experimenting with Mastigos path (never really tried it before other than for my NPCs) and grabbing unusual combination of Space 3, Mind 1 and Forces 2 as starting Arcana dots, getting a lot of Resources and making sure that Craft, Computers and Science skills are keen.<br /> Basically, I want this character to have a home base setup where she can, with a proper command on her tablet/phone, create controlled, powerful energies (for example, large fire or electricity arc) using mundane SCIENCE! at home, apport it with Space, and then control it with Forces. What kind of a setup you need to do this, and why is this better or easier or more efficient than just borrowing from the Sun or whatever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-06-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:27:48-08:00","id":781789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=781379#post781379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard it would be to use Apportation Spell to borrow fire from Sun, assuming Forces 2 and Space 3?<br /> EDIT<br /> To expand.<br /> I'm a person who never really cared for Space magics, and my players also never really used it, so I remained gleefuly ignorant for most of Space and Sympathetic magic aspects. This time, though, I'm considering experimenting with Mastigos path (never really tried it before other than for my NPCs) and grabbing unusual combination of Space 3, Mind 1 and Forces 2 as starting Arcana dots, getting a lot of Resources and making sure that Craft, Computers and Science skills are keen.<br /> Basically, I want this character to have a home base setup where she can, with a proper command on her tablet/phone, create controlled, powerful energies (for example, large fire or electricity arc) using mundane SCIENCE! at home, apport it with Space, and then control it with Forces. What kind of a setup you need to do this, and why is this better or easier or more efficient than just borrowing from the Sun or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I need to know more about this character. How did she Awaken? What's her Order? And why is she doing this and to whom, where?<br /> <br /> No mage question can be answered without context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:53:22-08:00","id":781828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=781379#post781379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard it would be to use Apportation Spell to borrow fire from Sun, assuming Forces 2 and Space 3?<br /> EDIT<br /> To expand.<br /> I'm a person who never really cared for Space magics, and my players also never really used it, so I remained gleefuly ignorant for most of Space and Sympathetic magic aspects. This time, though, I'm considering experimenting with Mastigos path (never really tried it before other than for my NPCs) and grabbing unusual combination of Space 3, Mind 1 and Forces 2 as starting Arcana dots, getting a lot of Resources and making sure that Craft, Computers and Science skills are keen.<br /> Basically, I want this character to have a home base setup where she can, with a proper command on her tablet/phone, create controlled, powerful energies (for example, large fire or electricity arc) using mundane SCIENCE! at home, apport it with Space, and then control it with Forces. What kind of a setup you need to do this, and why is this better or easier or more efficient than just borrowing from the Sun or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, you can't do this for one big reason (at least, according to the developers errata): Sympathy doesn't extend past earth unless an archmage. So no sympathy to appropriate that solar fire. Appropriating in general doesn't ever touch on energy, so you means of pulling in energy from a controlled base would be an interesting one. In 1e, portals did not allow passive transport; in other words, opening to a volcano would only be dangerous if someone walked/was pushed into that portal (the lava would not flow out). <br /> <br /> So this may mean energy can't be pulled through except in conjuntion with forces (appropriation only talks about pulling or dropping objects), though I personally like the idea of a smart mage preparing ready energy supplies.<br /> <br /> As for what 2e has had to say on that... Your guess is as good as mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T18:38:37-08:00","id":781995,"title":"","content":"Freemind, you could however have Apport heat from a volcano or the like which is more active than simply opening a portal and hoping something leaks through.<br /> <br /> I don't really see the point of trying to apport heat from the sun though.<br /> <br /> Basically, the way I see it you could use Forces and generate heat (Or any other energy), or Space and relocate it but does the source matter? Also, even if you assume that you could apport heat from the sun, how would you build up the Sympathetic connection to make it feasible?<br /> <br /> Looking at the Space spells we have available, I wouldn't be surprised to see that active apportation of an energy requires at least 2 dots of Forces. Which at least is way better than it was in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:02:23-08:00","id":782807,"title":"","content":"Ah, I imagined that a scientist who spends a lot of hours working about the sun and actively investigates it (probably an Obsession) would have a way to develop sympathetic connection strong enough. It's fine though, I prefer idea of using techology at home and magitech in general to create interesting and powerful effects.<br /> Spell I was referring to is indeed Apportation. It mentions that in order to move forms of energy I need Forces 2 (which we have covered), and that I can Apport energy of Size one-per-Space-dot. Which means that I can Apport Size 3 Fire...which is an Inferno.<br /> There are only size limitations, but what about actual intensity of ported energy? While Size 3 Inferno with 1 intensity is still 4 damage, I imagine that Size 1 fire with Intensity 3 is much easier to arrange safely at home in technomagic kitchen space. Are there any limiters I forgot about, for example in Forces write up somewhere? Or at least a precedence I can look into?<br /> <br /> I might be horribly misreading Apportation and misunderstanding how it works, so I would also be grateful for a &quot;working example&quot; of Apporting something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also not sure how exactly Sympathy with energy works. Do I need a Sympathetic link to my workshop to Apport from it? Do I need a Sympathetic connection to the Forge I'm keeping fire in? Should I have connection to specific tesla coils? Or do I need a connection to specific fire, that needs to be reset every time fire dies and is rekindled? This would force me to keep flame constantly alive, which is...actually kinda neat imagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-09-2015, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:58:41-08:00","id":782840,"title":"","content":"At the very least you could certainly use magic to create a fire that's small, but very intense. <br /> <br /> Any of those sympathetic examples could work I think. Though for something as removed from the flame as &quot;my workshop&quot; I'd probably say that you would have to open a Scrying window or something similar to target specific things in it. Essentially, the more specific and direct your sympathetic link is to what you want to affect the easier it would be to affect directly. Which means an flame you keep constantly lit that you're connected to would be the easiest method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:06:07-08:00","id":782845,"title":"","content":"I also really like the constant flame thing because it has certain symbolic meaning, and there are some traditions of keeping fire lit no matter what for religious reasons; adding to that some sacraments and sympathetic fuel (burning my own blood, photos, hair, etc) should be cool enough.<br /> Also, it provides me with interesting, very mundane problem - a stupid power outage can kill my eternal flame, forcing me to personally lit a new one and forge new bond with it :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T10:28:19-08:00","id":782903,"title":"","content":"Power outages don't affect magical fires. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:15:33-08:00","id":787773,"title":"","content":"Can you cast Quicken Corpse on someone who is under the effect of Suppress Other Life? I don't see any reason why you can't, and it is actually pretty cool and useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T20:35:05-08:00","id":787810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=787773#post787773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cast Quicken Corpse on someone who is under the effect of Suppress Other Life? I don't see any reason why you can't, and it is actually pretty cool and useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Someone under the effects of that spell isn't truly a corpse -- they just appear to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T21:46:42-08:00","id":787847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=787773#post787773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cast Quicken Corpse on someone who is under the effect of Suppress Other Life? I don't see any reason why you can't, and it is actually pretty cool and useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a tricky question and it's hard to say for certain. If I was storytelling my answer would be no however. The reason is that the target is composed of a (disguised) Life pattern, whereas that particular spell is meant to target a Death pattern.<br /> <br /> In theory it might be possible for a Mage who knows that they're casting the spell on someone with Suppress Other Life active to design a spell that instead manipulates the Death pattern of the Suppress Other Life spell to move the target's &quot;Corpse&quot;, but it'd be a fiddly act of creative thaumaturgy and I would rule that you couldn't benefit from the Quicken Corpse rote. It seems like a different spell to me<br /> <br /> As a completely personal call as well rather than anything from the book, If they were cast by different mages I'd probably also say that there should be a clash of wills. If the caster of Suppress Other Life succeeds then the veiling part of the Suppress Other Life spell would fool the caster of Quicken Corpse into not detecting that the spell failed due to an invalid target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T23:04:37-08:00","id":787870,"title":"","content":"I would handle it as a Clash of Wills too. Your intention is to raise the corpse so it kinda clashes with the intention of the mage that suppressed it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, I would make them roll the spell and on a success, they realize something is off: the imago should have worked but it didn't, time to investigate more. Death Sight would probably reveal what's up after some scrutiny and once you know what happened, you could probably create a custom version of Quicken Corpse to work on Suppressed people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T06:45:55-08:00","id":788045,"title":"","content":"Now you are getting me interested into possibilities of using Death to become so undead, that you can buff yourself with Quicken spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T06:56:46-08:00","id":788055,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a tricky question. From a purely metagame point of view it is letting someone do something that their Arcanum really isn't built for and so feels a little like an exploit. However at the same time, it's doubling up on spells, has to be done in a very specific way and makes it much more obviously magical. That's so many downsides that I feel like it's managing to balance itself out pretty well. Mages trying to exploit loopholes and getting hit with major consequences is pretty much what the game is all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T09:50:52-08:00","id":788165,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that sounds like one for the &quot;if you do this I will think of <i>interesting consequences&quot; </i>school of STing - there's a lot that could happen, from other mages getting the wrong impression to other mages getting the <i>right</i> impression and breaking out the 'control undead' spells; after all, if you make yourself a valid target for Death magic, you make yourself a valid target for Death magic...<br /> <br /> That and I'd probably have it make you <i>look</i> kind of dead if people know what they're looking for, which has its own pile of Fun.<br /> <br /> Might need Life to combine with it, I'd have to have a read of the new book to decide. When it's out. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T10:00:23-08:00","id":788170,"title":"","content":"Life+Death 4 could be used to effectively turn yourself into a Revenant, or Ghost, maybe even a Kerbori or Cthonian, some kind of strange vampire imitation etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T10:14:00-08:00","id":788179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=788165#post788165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and I'd probably have it make you <i>look</i> kind of dead if people know what they're looking for, which has its own pile of Fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Suppression spell already gives you the appearance of being dead for things like rigor mortis and blood pooling in the extremities. This is the description of the spell which made me think of combining them in this way in the first place &quot;<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The mage can temporarily suppress his own life. <b>While in this state, the mage is well and truly dead.</b> The physical symptoms of death, other than decomposition, set in (the onset and passing of rigor mortis, the receding of the gums and the skin of the scalp and fingertips, the pooling of blood at the bottom of the body). The mind and spirit are absent.&quot;<br /> <br /> I was mostly thinking about using it as an easy way to transport someone you have Suppressed without drawing a lot of attention. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T13:18:59-08:00","id":788300,"title":"","content":"In one of my mage games, one of my players used that trick to kidnap a CEO. They walked out of the place toghether without anyone being none the wiser. I though it was cool and creative and I allowed it because those are the kinds of things I like to encourage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T14:21:30-08:00","id":788338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=788300#post788300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of my mage games, one of my players used that trick to kidnap a CEO. They walked out of the place toghether without anyone being none the wiser. I though it was cool and creative and I allowed it because those are the kinds of things I like to encourage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that is exactly the sort of thing I was thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:42:17-08:00","id":844876,"title":"","content":"In preparation for a legacy,<br /> <br /> What would the appropriate arcana be to interact with Sekhem from Mummy? Not deathless, which bring their own weirdness, but things like relics or vessels, the lifeweb, heka, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:11:11-08:00","id":844924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=844876#post844876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In preparation for a legacy,<br /> <br /> What would the appropriate arcana be to interact with Sekhem from Mummy? Not deathless, which bring their own weirdness, but things like relics or vessels, the lifeweb, heka, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see arguments being made for Fate, Prime, and Life, in that order. We're likely not gonna have a canon answer until the Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:05:03-07:00","id":847293,"title":"","content":"Can anyone give me the quick rundown on the Oracles?<br /> <br /> Are any of them named and described like the Exarchs are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:14:56-07:00","id":847297,"title":"","content":"There are same stories about them in the <i>Silver Ladder</i>, but no names or detailed descriptions. They are basically legends and probably <i>are</i> the Watchtowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:01:03-07:00","id":847407,"title":"","content":"Tome of the Watchtowers talks about them too, but no they've deliberately removed themselves from directly influencing events as a contrast from the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:22:23-07:00","id":847420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=847293#post847293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give me the quick rundown on the Oracles?<br /> <br /> Are any of them named and described like the Exarchs are?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're named in <b>Silver Ladder</b>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Acanthus; The Youthful King of Thorns</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Mastigos; The King of the Burning Voice</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Moros; The Sorrowful King in Gray</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Obrimos; The Star-Cloaked King of Thunder</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Thyrsus; The Throneless King of the Heart<br /> <br /> We write <b>Mage</b> books from the viewpoint that the Oracles never manifest, never identify themselves, and do not meddle in the Fallen World, as the antithesis of the Exarchs. The Watchtowers are plausibly their Subsouls, in a similar fashion to the Exarchs forming Ochemata and Exarchates.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:41:31-07:00","id":847426,"title":"","content":"Kinda sad to see 5 kings and 0 queens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:53:12-07:00","id":847433,"title":"","content":"Are they kings or queens? Who knows- they did/do/will never exist, and the Atlantis they ruled is gone/still to come/never was. Tenses are hard with Archmasters. Doubly so for the Ascended, who are Supernal Symbols now instead of living things. Maybe.<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember Tome of the Watchtowers making some of the Oracles queens of Atlantis, but honestly even the Exarchs change gender every other sentence in references made to them, much like Father-Mother Wolf &amp; Moon. The only one who is <i>definitely </i>male, if only because of the symbol they've become, is the Father- that much is indisputable. Probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-14-2016, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:53:51-07:00","id":847434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=847426#post847426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda sad to see 5 kings and 0 queens.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Tome of the Watchtowers, they spoke of an ancient queen(several i think)whose legend represents the Mastigos path.Also, your perception of gender of now inhuman beings is valid anyway you slice it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:02:06-07:00","id":847439,"title":"","content":"Plus the Oracles might not even exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:05:01-07:00","id":847440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=847439#post847439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the Oracles might not even exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. For all the ST wants to be, the towers could be nothing more than a way for the Exarchs to not be bored after so long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:21:43-07:00","id":847443,"title":"","content":"I was more sad about male figures being used as default pick when needed for characters of &quot;power, wisdom, and/or great importance&quot; (and thus, reinforcing them as the dominant symbols for it) which is strictly a world-building and writing thing, but I'm not sure if this is a good place for this kind of a conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:47:42-07:00","id":847458,"title":"","content":"Nope, almost certainly not a good place for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:17:33-07:00","id":847495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=847458#post847458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, almost certainly not a good place for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also kind of just a knock-on effect of the words coming from different places despite nominal association and the unfortunate appropriation of <i>man</i> by <i>wir</i> \u2014 &quot;king&quot; can be used as signifier of preeminence for things that are not monarchs irrespective of literal or linguistic gender and comes from the same root as &quot;kin,&quot; but &quot;queen&quot; is stuck to strictly feminine words and individuals and is derived from a word that just means &quot;woman.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a problematic consequence of how language has shaken out over the centuries, but it should by no means be taken as a statement of gender for a particular subset of hypothetical Ascended beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T22:31:43-07:00","id":847550,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: my country once had a female king for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T04:24:01-07:00","id":847609,"title":"","content":"Can someone please explain Ascension by Assumption and Ascension by Divine Union? I always wanted to play a character who is trying to ascend by that way but I never quite understood Imperial Mysteries explanation about them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T10:03:23-07:00","id":847748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=847609#post847609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please explain Ascension by Assumption and Ascension by Divine Union? I always wanted to play a character who is trying to ascend by that way but I never quite understood Imperial Mysteries explanation about them</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumption: You know Transfiguration? That, but permanent.<br /> <br /> Divine Union: Find a fallen Supernal god, align yourself with it, and get it home so you can join its retinue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T10:45:25-07:00","id":847762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=847748#post847748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assumption: You know Transfiguration? That, but permanent.<br /> <br /> Divine Union: Find a fallen Supernal god, align yourself with it, and get it home so you can join its retinue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't I become the god itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T11:04:47-07:00","id":847767,"title":"","content":"Merging with the god is one of the ways you can join it. It's basically how Seers Ascend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:18:45-07:00","id":847932,"title":"","content":"If I had to give hints of what the after-life or after-lives might be like in the CoD, what option is closer to what we know about souls?<br /> <br /> The billions of Oneiroi, the Temenos and the Anima Mundi are all one vast soul. Some supernaturals, like the Uratha and the True Fae, appear inside the Anima Mundi sometimes. Those with altered souls might have their own types of Oneiroi and Temenos. I suspect the changeling equivalent of the Temenos is actually the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Ghosts aren't souls, but they go to the Underworld when their Anchors are destroyed, and sometimes they get to move on to their final resting place. Sin-Eaters are often involved in this process, and occasionally Mages.<br /> <br /> Ghosts can also be dragged to the Inferno and come back corrupted. The same can happen to Spirits and Goetia.<br /> <br /> Many Lower Depths have the imagery of bad after-lives. One exception might be Starry A'aru, which seems more peaceful than the rest.<br /> <br /> The Hedge and the Shadow do not seem to be resting places or purgatories, unless you consider the Durances of changelings to be a form of cleansing the soul that has gone very wrong.<br /> <br /> Entering the Supernal might retcon you out of existence, if I remember correctly. The Emanations that split from the Supernal might house souls.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean is a hypothetical opposite of the Inferno. A connection to the Principle/Divine Fire is possible.<br /> <br /> The Ascension into the Supernal that Archmages seek can also be considered an after-life. Other supernaturals might have their methods of passage into the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Did I miss anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:28:32-07:00","id":847937,"title":"","content":"Does it matter? If you want to settle on just one afterlife then use or make up whatever suits your fancy/need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:29:09-07:00","id":851705,"title":"","content":"Mage with prosthethic arm. What arcana do you use to influence It?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:36:16-07:00","id":851707,"title":"","content":"I would say matter. The prosthetic isn't part of his Pattern; while it is fitted for him, it isn't a living part of him. Heck, even that arm he lost became part of Matter's purview as soon as it became detached and stopped counting as living material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:46:05-07:00","id":852659,"title":"","content":"Cool. Next question - someone wants to fuck with the prosthetic using magic. Are any personal traits of the owner (gnosis, resistance attributes, shieldings) applied against mean spells? Ive always ruled that yes, and that ruling covered also stuff like currently worn clothes or jewlery, but i dont actually remember the default rules for this.<br /> <br /> And a follow up question - casting matter spells on artifacts. Any interactions to remember?<br /> <br /> The context: Moros who wants to have their awakening be having a tragic accident that leaves them handless and with some metalglass shards entrenched deep in their chest from the vechicle that crashed. Accepting the prothesis and the fact that shards in their chests are not going anywhere being the final stage of awakening, so there is a idea of either the shards or the hand becoming an artifact (or both). Due to it being a moros with matter 3, that prothesis will be targeted ofteb, so i need to understand all of the quirks involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:20:44-07:00","id":852715,"title":"","content":"Default answer is no, your clothes and prosthetics are valid targets without benefiting from any of your personal resistance.<br /> <br /> I don't think artifacts can normally be targeted by Mages, an Unmaking spell might be able to permanently destroy them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:58:28-07:00","id":859976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=852715#post852715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Default answer is no, your clothes and prosthetics are valid targets without benefiting from any of your personal resistance.<br /> <br /> I don't think artifacts can normally be targeted by Mages, an Unmaking spell might be able to permanently destroy them though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Since clothes can be symbolically tied to your body and how they protect it from the elements as their most important function, you can say that you Withstand spells against them with your Stamina. In 1ED, you can destroy enhanced/imbued items, thaumium and Artifacts with the Matter 5 spell &quot;Annihilate Extraordinary Matter&quot;. The Prime 5 spell &quot;Dead Zone&quot; stops the flow of Mana in an area proportionate to Successes, which can prevent Artifacts from working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:00:27-07:00","id":859977,"title":"","content":"How do you handle Clash Of Wills and Withstand ratings for ephemerals? For the former, I assume Power + Finesse as usual, but wouldn't [Rank + Influence Dots] or [Rank + Simplified Attribute] make more sense? For the latter, I assume they Withstand with their full Resistance. Would it be a good idea to allow the incorporation of an ephemeral's Bane as a Yantra to decrease their Withstand rating? The same could happen if they're low on Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:19:06-07:00","id":859983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=859976#post859976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since clothes can be symbolically tied to your body and how they protect it from the elements as their most important function, you can say that you Withstand spells against them with your Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that, but it doesn't make any sense to. If you're going to do that then you might as well say that the car someone is driving is basically their legs at the moment and benefits from their Withstand score. Your opinion is also not supported by the rules as stated so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=859977#post859977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you handle Clash Of Wills and Withstand ratings for ephemerals? For the former, I assume Power + Finesse as usual, but wouldn't [Rank + Influence Dots] or [Rank + Simplified Attribute] make more sense? For the latter, I assume they Withstand with their full Resistance. Would it be a good idea to allow the incorporation of an ephemeral's Bane as a Yantra to decrease their Withstand rating? The same could happen if they're low on Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Withstand rating for a spirit is their Rank. Clash of Wills will be against whatever you're clashing against. So if they invoke a power that's Rank+Finesse or whatever, then that's what they roll for Clash of Wills against a Mage's Gnosis+Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-05-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:36:25-07:00","id":859993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=859983#post859983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say that, but it doesn't make any sense to. If you're going to do that then you might as well say that the car someone is driving is basically their legs at the moment and benefits from their Withstand score. Your opinion is also not supported by the rules as stated so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Good points. </span></span></span>Now that I think about it, it makes more sense for Objects to not Withstand. If a Mage really cares about his possessions, he should invest into Matter and/or Prime to protect them. Space Wards might help too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=859983#post859983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Withstand rating for a spirit is their Rank. Clash of Wills will be against whatever you're clashing against. So if they invoke a power that's Rank+Finesse or whatever, then that's what they roll for Clash of Wills against a Mage's Gnosis+Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you. I'm glad it's simpler than I thought.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:28:11-07:00","id":860023,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, it could be said in Real Life that a persons car is really an extension of their legs... (or at least, the brain handles it as such)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scientificamerican.com/article/you-are-what-you-touch/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.scientificamerican.com/sciam/cache/file/8EE55DCC-962D-4F4A-AED2AD7CEC191CA1_source.jpg?w=1200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scientificamerican.com/article/you-are-what-you-touch/\" target=\"_blank\"> You Are What You Touch: How Tool Use Changes the Brain's Representations of the Body </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scientificamerican.com/article/you-are-what-you-touch/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scientificamerican.com/article/you-are-what-you-touch/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> How tools become a part of your body </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.livescience.com/9664-brain-sees-tools-extensions-body.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.livescience.com/9664-brain-sees-tools-extensions-body.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Brain Sees Tools as Extensions of Body </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.livescience.com/9664-brain-sees-tools-extensions-body.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.livescience.com/9664-brain-sees-tools-extensions-body.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> After using a mechanical grabber that extended their reach, people behaved as though their arm really was longer. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3223791/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3223791/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T02:27:58-07:00","id":860195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=860023#post860023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.scientificamerican.com/article/you-are-what-you-touch/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scientificamerican.com/ar...hat-you-touch/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.livescience.com/9664-brain-sees-tools-extensions-body.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.livescience.com/9664-brai...ions-body.html</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3223791/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3223791/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Coarse Lie's fabrications <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T18:07:02-07:00","id":866193,"title":"","content":"An Obrimos casts personal invisibility on himself and hides around a corner, the Mastigos following him casts a knowing space spell to know what is in his vicinity. Question: does this cause a clash of wills, reveal the Obrimos's location without piercing the veil, or leave the Obrimos hidden? My assumption is the second outcome since the knowing spell doesn't cause the Mastigos to see everything around him, but I didn't know for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T05:34:00-07:00","id":866352,"title":"","content":"My read would be the second, yeah - the Obrimos is still <i>there</i>, he's just made it so that light doesn't interact with him, but the Mastigos really doesn't care about light at this point.<br /> <br /> A pressure plate or a tripwire would do exactly the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:22:34-07:00","id":870877,"title":"","content":"Just for curiosity, but can Archmages REACH ? The Reach system can break the rule of &quot;only ritual casting for imperial spells&quot;, no ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T03:50:46-07:00","id":871087,"title":"","content":"We don't know.<br /> <br /> Those rules were written for the 1e spell system.<br /> <br /> (Having not actually read them) my base assumption would be yes, you can reach, no, you can't avoid an explicit restriction on Imperial spells just because the 2e system lets you do something you're allowed to do for non-Imperial magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:02:50-07:00","id":871235,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the prosthetic answers. I've decided to consider them a part of the Mage's pattern, like directly wielded tools and clothing, for gameplay reasons mostly.<br /> <br /> Here is a question born from curiosity: Mind magic and strange beings. Would you allow use of Mind magic on following:<br /> 1. A Human.<br /> 2. A Human whose brain is dead but who is alive and still having a functioning mind.<br /> 3. Intelligent brick.<br /> 4. Truly Intelligent Artifical Intelligence<br /> 5. A demon whose physical form is alien and weird<br /> 6. A spirit<br /> 7. A self-aware and intelligent ghost<br /> 8. A familiar<br /> 9. Abyssal entity possesing intelligence<br /> And so on. I'm interested in how people approach these, and why they approach them in a way they do. As for my answer<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Yes on almost everything. That's why I consider Mastigos to be THE WARLOCK, the summoner demonologist, capable of enslaving and controlling most of creatures, even if they don't follow brain rules. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:50:43-07:00","id":871296,"title":"","content":"This is precisely the reason why Mind is one of the most frustrating arcana in the game: Because it lets you bind, control, and generally subdue spirits that <i>Spirit</i> cannot affect.<br /> <br /> Spirit lets you affect spirits. Mind affects humans, animals, spirits, goetia, angels, beings from the Lower Depths, and, as you say, even an intelligent brick. Maybe it can't do things like change their nature but, for the majority of those things, neither can Spirit.<br /> <br /> Ah well. Nothing to be done about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:27:17-07:00","id":871354,"title":"","content":"In our games we've house ruled it that entities primarily controlled by another arcana cannot be controlled by Mind. Otherwise there's not a single reason to not learn Mind and master it as quickly as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T13:55:32-07:00","id":871705,"title":"","content":"I understand the decision from gameplay point of view (and I agree with it!), but how do you explain it in-world and cosmologically? Why a Spirit cannot be controlled, while a dog or human (wouldn't they fall primarly under Life?) can? Isn't it intended for Mastigos to bind big demons and entities in Space created circles of summoning, and then bend them to their will with Mind? <br /> One of explanations I'm thinking about is slightly racist (em, lol) towards ghosts and spirits, but how about considering them so &quot;simple&quot; there is no difference between their &quot;self&quot; and spiritual/ghostly matter big enough to have a fully developed stand alone mind? (Basically, what you could consider their &quot;mind&quot; is just a function of their spiritual constitution, not a Mind-mind).<br /> I'm trying to figure out something to justify why it should not work. But I'm also interested in seeing possible consequences of just saying &quot;ah, fuck it, Mastigos can enslave anything with a good enough spell&quot; and see where it leads and if it really is that bad of a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T16:33:47-07:00","id":871865,"title":"","content":"That's precisely the justification we use. A spirit doesn't have a mind, it's a spiritual expression of the world. Ghosts are basically just left over code from a soul that's moved on and not actually possessed of a mind.<br /> <br /> You could also say it's as easy as the fact that usually, spirits and ghosts don't have a connection to the Astral. Meaning there are some rare and interesting exceptions running around out there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:46:32-07:00","id":873563,"title":"","content":"What Arcana would it take to turn oneself into a ghost mage/spirit/goetia? Could this even be done with a spell, or would it have to be a Legacy thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T02:43:49-07:00","id":873631,"title":"","content":"Life4/Death4, Life4/Spirit4, Life4/Mind4 respectively though it can be dispelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T17:40:11-07:00","id":874128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=873631#post873631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life4/Death4, Life4/Spirit4, Life4/Mind4 respectively though it can be dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safer as an Attainment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:19:53-07:00","id":874183,"title":"","content":"If a mage in the Shadow or Twilight form body is transformed into ephemera, then can Spirit alone change the shape or restore health ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:10:47-07:00","id":874217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=874183#post874183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage in the Shadow or Twilight form body is transformed into ephemera, then can Spirit alone change the shape or restore health ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have turned themselves into a Spirit completely, such as via the final Scions of God attainment? Yeah. Then they are Spirits, and Spirit alone is enough to work on them. Just like Life alone is enough to work on their bodies normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:19:13-07:00","id":874222,"title":"","content":"1) What is a caucus? Is it a gathering of mages of the same Order, or a gathering of mages, period?<br /> <br /> 2) Are there any examples of current Nameless Orders anywhere?<br /> <br /> 3) How responsive is the Temenos and the Anima Mundi to huge events like WWII or 9/11?<br /> <br /> 4) Are there still Omphalos Stones around the world today?<br /> <br /> 5) Is the Labyrinth a global conspiracy that has many other conspiracies in it? Or is it more local? Is there any book that helps you build one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:35:49-07:00","id":874232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=874222#post874222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) What is a caucus? Is it a gathering of mages of the same Order, or a gathering of mages, period?<br /> <br /> 2) Are there any examples of current Nameless Orders anywhere?<br /> <br /> 3) How responsive is the Temenos and the Anima Mundi to huge events like WWII or 9/11?<br /> <br /> 4) Are there still Omphalos Stones around the world today?<br /> <br /> 5) Is the Labyrinth a global conspiracy that has many other conspiracies in it? Or is it more local? Is there any book that helps you build one?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) A caucus is the regional structure of a single Order. Rather than try to fit their hierarchies into a single city (unless it's a really big city, like New York or Tokyo) they cover regions. Convocations are larger gatherings of mages from all Orders.<br /> <br /> 4) Sure! You just have to find them in Vinca archaeological sites; nobody seems to have one yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T21:23:55-07:00","id":874248,"title":"","content":"Cross-over question: do you think that Geniuses interact with the Astral in any remarkable way? I think the Goetia of an Unmada have a habit of wandering into the Temenos (and perhaps other Oneiroi). However, they might not be the same as Manes. Could the Bardos be some kind of mutated Temenos Realms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:25:31-07:00","id":874337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=874183#post874183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage in the Shadow or Twilight form body is transformed into ephemera, then can Spirit alone change the shape or restore health ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind there's more kinds of ephemera than just Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:34:30-07:00","id":874344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=874222#post874222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) What is a caucus? Is it a gathering of mages of the same Order, or a gathering of mages, period?<br /> <br /> 2) Are there any examples of current Nameless Orders anywhere?<br /> <br /> 3) How responsive is the Temenos and the Anima Mundi to huge events like WWII or 9/11?<br /> <br /> 4) Are there still Omphalos Stones around the world today?<br /> <br /> 5) Is the Labyrinth a global conspiracy that has many other conspiracies in it? Or is it more local? Is there any book that helps you build one?</div> </div> </div> </div>2) Tremere Liches<br /> <br /> 3) Kind of an ST call but considering it's a psychoactive realm and something like 9/11 splashes into the public consciousness very quickly and vividly and has a huge impact on the way we think about things, I'd say pretty responsive. <br /> <br /> 5) The Labyrinth is as many cults (or organizations you can mix occult symbolism into easily like the mafia) as the Guardians can take over, big and small. What the Guardians do is manage these, usually with a pretty light touch, and build clues into their occultism that points to other cults in the Labyrinth. The idea being that if a Sleeper feels they figured out all the secrets of one group they can easily find and start digging into the next group. Think of it as a bait trail, but there isn't a trap at the end it just keeps going forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:34:27-07:00","id":874892,"title":"","content":"Since the Mastigos entry in the previews focused so much on stuff that comes off as very goetic, are we going to see the Goetia presented a bit less negatively in the 2e corebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:29:10-07:00","id":874942,"title":"","content":"It was never goetia that were given the negative press, that went to the Mages who attempted to control goetic demons like their Vices. I imagine that won't change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:54:04-07:00","id":875001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=874942#post874942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was never goetia that were given the negative press, that went to the Mages who attempted to control goetic demons like their Vices. I imagine that won't change.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a pretty key thing to Mastigos now, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T17:08:02-07:00","id":875011,"title":"","content":"It has been for a long time, ever since the Astral book came out at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:10:35-07:00","id":875112,"title":"","content":"How do people actually use Zombies? They sound like fun, but in practice they ended up being such a logistical nightmare that nobody ever touched them again with a stick. Main problems seem to be eating up spell control for a poor return, having to order them around, and most importantly, transporting them around; they are never there when you need them the most. It's a sad thing... Making zombies on spot also never really felt attractive, due to them having rather poor stats without putting ritual effort into it.<br /> My best shot for making them actually useful for anything different than sanctum guarding is abandoning human zombies and focusing on animals, especially small ones like birds - basically, zombies you could transport in a suitcase. Anyone with practical experience in necromancing care to share their secrets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:15:05-07:00","id":875120,"title":"","content":"Make a gate to Twilight, march your zombie horde into Twilight. Now you only need a gate to bring out zombies wherever or to drag your enemies into your horde.<br /> <br /> I learned this the hard way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:26:12-07:00","id":875132,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Do you think &quot;follow me&quot; is a valid order for zombies in Twilight when you are not in it? That's a nice idea, I thought that Twilight Invasions were Death 4 stuff, but apparently not. Neat.<br /> EDIT<br /> I guess you would have give your zombies a way to perceive you somehow. Hmmmm.<br /> <br /> EDIT2<br /> Ah, I remembered why I thought it's a Death 4 stuff. It's an Extended Action until Death 4.<br /> <br /> EDIT3<br /> Maybe stick the [exit] Ghost Gate into a Prepared Spell using Time...Death / Time Mage is something I always wanted to do anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-26-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:57:58-07:00","id":875584,"title":"","content":"Give the zombies Ghost Touch, then they can stay in Twilight but also interact with the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:36:32-07:00","id":875616,"title":"","content":"Reverse engineered Touch of the Grave? Hmmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:46:29-07:00","id":875629,"title":"","content":"Going out on a limb, I think if witnessed by Sleepers the zombies would be safe and just lose Touch of the Grave since Sleepers would only be able to detect and react to the impossibility of being torn apart by seemingly nothing.<br /> <br /> By the way, you can perceive the Fallen from Twilight, either way your zombies wouldn't have any trouble keeping track of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:15:19-07:00","id":875652,"title":"","content":"Touchy Zombies sound little too cheesy for my tastes (it's definitely practical, but little too...I don't know, submarine zombies don't have that proper feel), but idea of having a Twilight escort that can pop into existence after you open a gate is definitely iconic, awesome, and not too cheesy. Plus, in 2nd Ed, it will probably be doable by starting character without going through hoops and loops. Thank you! Now I have some cool imagery to work with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:28:07-07:00","id":875665,"title":"","content":"Do like the Necrons do, and teleport metal zombies straight into your opponents face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:22:21-07:00","id":875746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=875665#post875665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do like the Necrons do, and teleport metal zombies straight into your opponents face.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think at that point the zombies go from merely &quot;metal&quot; to &quot;metal as fuck.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:15:49-07:00","id":875779,"title":"","content":"Couple of questions regarding interpreting the practices in the new version of Mage.<br /> <br /> One: Can Compelling of Matter Spells be used to lock/unlock things such as doors and windows, open doors and windows, cause a car to start, make a ball or skateboard roll across the ground, causes dishes to fall off shelves and counters, etc? Y'know, minor poltergeist like stuff. My rationale is that Doors can open and lock as &quot;things they would normally do&quot;, balls can roll as &quot;things they would normally do&quot;, so you can use compelling spells to get these effects. I figured it would be really in theme for the Moros, and help blend together the Necromancer/Alchemist strands.<br /> <br /> Two: Could Ruling of Matter spells, with reach, be used to almost TK effects on objects- pull a glass along a counter, cause a door to refuse to open even if it's unlocked, etc. Normally, glasses don't slide along the counter, doors open when unlocked, and rocks don't fly, but ruling allows you to force something to do something in wouldn't normally do under the circumstances. I'm just thinking, a lot of creepy &quot;ghost-story&quot; effects can be done with matter<br /> <br /> Three, under the interpretation of the Ruling practice, could you puppet a fresh corpse with a ruling of Death Spell? It's still got muscles and everything, so it's got the parts that would let it move, but it just wouldn't normally move.<br /> <br /> Four: Forces spells let you affect the weather. Does that mean that Ruling and Compelling-level forces magic could be used to create a gust of wind?<br /> <br /> Five: In &quot;The Creative Arts&quot; preview, a veiling spell that lets one walk past a camera unnoticed is given as an example of a Veiling spell that conceals something <i>from</i> the arcanum's purview. Does that mean that electronics have been moved to under Forces Purview? <br /> <br /> Six: In Mage 1e, there was a 1 dot spell called Alter Conductivity. It was awesome. If I'm interpreting things correctly, should this be a weaving spell now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:25:48-07:00","id":875791,"title":"","content":"Electronics have been under the purview of Forces for awakening since day one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:36:22-07:00","id":875803,"title":"","content":"Alter conductivity should have always been a Weaving spell IMHO. <br /> <br /> Regardless points 1 and 2 for Matter: Check the Lodestone spell that was spoiled. If what you want feels like it falls under the description, its probably compelling. More complex behavior however I would consider part of the Ruling practice. <br /> <br /> Three might be doable but cumbersome. I would allow the Mage to make the corpse move with Ruling like a crude puppet only. So, you could probably make a corpse open its eyes and scare the shit out of everyone watching, or make it grasp a nearby object, but walking around would probably be very difficult, I would require at least +2 Reach for such kind of fine control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:20:02-07:00","id":875842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azunth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=875779#post875779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of questions regarding interpreting the practices in the new version of Mage.<br /> <br /> One: Can Compelling of Matter Spells be used to lock/unlock things such as doors and windows, open doors and windows, cause a car to start, make a ball or skateboard roll across the ground, causes dishes to fall off shelves and counters, etc? Y'know, minor poltergeist like stuff. My rationale is that Doors can open and lock as &quot;things they would normally do&quot;, balls can roll as &quot;things they would normally do&quot;, so you can use compelling spells to get these effects. I figured it would be really in theme for the Moros, and help blend together the Necromancer/Alchemist strands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two: Could Ruling of Matter spells, with reach, be used to almost TK effects on objects- pull a glass along a counter, cause a door to refuse to open even if it's unlocked, etc. Normally, glasses don't slide along the counter, doors open when unlocked, and rocks don't fly, but ruling allows you to force something to do something in wouldn't normally do under the circumstances. I'm just thinking, a lot of creepy &quot;ghost-story&quot; effects can be done with matter </div> </div> </div>Not as a statted spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Three, under the interpretation of the Ruling practice, could you puppet a fresh corpse with a ruling of Death Spell? It's still got muscles and everything, so it's got the parts that would let it move, but it just wouldn't normally move. </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Four: Forces spells let you affect the weather. Does that mean that Ruling and Compelling-level forces magic could be used to create a gust of wind? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Also Matter.<br /> <br /> [quote]Five: In &quot;The Creative Arts&quot; preview, a veiling spell that lets one walk past a camera unnoticed is given as an example of a Veiling spell that conceals something <i>from</i> the arcanum's purview. Does that mean that electronics have been moved to under Forces Purview?[/quote[<br /> <br /> &quot;moved&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Six: In Mage 1e, there was a 1 dot spell called Alter Conductivity. It was awesome. If I'm interpreting things correctly, should this be a weaving spell now? </div> </div> </div>It's a Matter 3 spell now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:54:26-07:00","id":875879,"title":"","content":"Well, looks like &quot;Dance fight at the morgue&quot; just became a viable concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:48:14-07:00","id":876114,"title":"","content":"Thanks a ton!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T17:18:05-07:00","id":876130,"title":"","content":"Some questions about the Antagonists section for 2e:<br /> <br /> 1) Will we have examples of beings like Morpheans and Ghost Mages? Will we get a sense for what Practices would be needed for a mage to become such a thing?<br /> <br /> 2) Will there be example Gulmoth or Acamoth to make use of? Will we know what someone needs to do in order to summon them?<br /> <br /> 3) Will there be rules for Befouling your own spells with Paradox for power in the corebook, or will we need to wait for that blog post you were talking about?<br /> <br /> 4) (directed at all writers) What is your favorite thing in the Antagonists section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T00:37:50-07:00","id":876330,"title":"","content":"Do you think other supernaturals leave behind a signature akin to a Nimbus, whether as a byproduct of their existence or when they use their powers?<br /> <br /> I can't help but imagine Mummies do, at least; Sybaris is bound to leave a mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T06:36:54-07:00","id":876571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=876330#post876330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think other supernaturals leave behind a signature akin to a Nimbus, whether as a byproduct of their existence or when they use their powers?<br /> <br /> I can't help but imagine Mummies do, at least; Sybaris is bound to leave a mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably rule that anyone who has an aura (such as Vampires and Werewolves) leave something behind to see with Focused Mage Sight. I imagine that for Demons, Embeds do not, but Exploits do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:05:29-07:00","id":876641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=876330#post876330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think other supernaturals leave behind a signature akin to a Nimbus, whether as a byproduct of their existence or when they use their powers?<br /> <br /> I can't help but imagine Mummies do, at least; Sybaris is bound to leave a mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the SoS Mage Sight preview there is stuff that implies that Mage Sight can tell apart the predatory auras of vampires. So probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mysteries with other origins instead reveal the resonance of their source: this might be the aura of a creature like a vampire or werewolf, the flavor of Essence stemming from a locus or spirit, or the resonance of a ley line. Just like a mage's Signature Nimbus, the information revealed should allow a mage to identify the same resonance if she encounters it again. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:25:48-07:00","id":876655,"title":"","content":"Any supernatural power is going to leave a &quot;residue&quot; of some sort, I imagine. Anything that'd ping a Mage's Peripheral Sight when done in front of them is fair game in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:50:08-07:00","id":877164,"title":"","content":"Using magic, what would it take to create a lasting thunderstorm over a large area? Lasting a few hours, at least, before drifting off with the winds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T18:58:24-07:00","id":877222,"title":"","content":"Alright, if the practice determine what spell we can cast with a Arcanum, then a Fireball spell can be done with Patterning (transforming energy into a fireball), Making (creating a fireball ex nihilo) or maybe Ruling (commanding fire ) but never Unraveling, because dont make sense to create/command/transform fire with a practice that destroy the fire ( purview of the Arcanum). This is right or wrong ?<br /> <br /> That said, we can say that some 1st edition direct attack/damage Fraying/Unraveling spells are Patterning/Making/Ruling/other practice that dont do direct damage in 1st edition ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:23:44-07:00","id":877241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=877164#post877164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using magic, what would it take to create a lasting thunderstorm over a large area? Lasting a few hours, at least, before drifting off with the winds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Forces 3 (Weaving) to directly manipulate the local air pressure to cause a storm. Once you get the cycle going to a certain point they're at least semi-self sustaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:51:01-07:00","id":877260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=877222#post877222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, if the practice determine what spell we can cast with a Arcanum, then a Fireball spell can be done with Patterning (transforming energy into a fireball), Making (creating a fireball ex nihilo) or maybe Ruling (commanding fire ) but never Unraveling, because dont make sense to create/command/transform fire with a practice that destroy the fire ( purview of the Arcanum). This is right or wrong ?<br /> <br /> That said, we can say that some 1st edition direct attack/damage Fraying/Unraveling spells are Patterning/Making/Ruling/other practice that dont do direct damage in 1st edition ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand your question, Dave has pointed out that spells that &quot;do x bashing damage&quot; directly to a target still require 3 dots, but no longer are bound to Fraying/Unraveling/Making. For example, perfecting is the practice you would use with time or death to accelerate a demise with 3 dots. And Ruling could let you manipulate existing forces, but it doesn't cause direct harm as the spell effect: you are casting a spell to move the fire, not to harm someone; the harm is tied to the fire, not the spell.<br /> <br /> And there are of course plenty of means to harm and kill with higher practices (as in 1e), if not more so: Masters can kill instantly with spells, such as a Death Making spell. <br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:24:25-07:00","id":877310,"title":"","content":"Yes, only wanted to confirm that damage spells are no longer bounded to Fraying/Unraveling/Making like in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> Like I said, the idea of creating a Force from nothing, like a lightingbolt or Firebolt, to damage a NPC with a Unraveling spell never entered in my head.<br /> <br /> Thanks Freemind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T22:19:55-07:00","id":877351,"title":"","content":"If you perform obvious magic in a place crowded with people who aren't paying attention (say, teleporting from one side of the audience to another during a concert), would it induce paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T23:07:31-07:00","id":877382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=877351#post877351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you perform obvious magic in a place crowded with people who aren't paying attention (say, teleporting from one side of the audience to another during a concert), would it induce paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in an Ascension mindset there. Awakening Paradox only cares about whether or not you're Reaching; all Sleepers do is unravel the spell, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T23:35:48-07:00","id":877392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=877382#post877382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're in an Ascension mindset there. Awakening Paradox only cares about whether or not you're Reaching; all Sleepers do is unravel the spell, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They induce paradox still. If a sleeper sees obvious magic it both unravels the spell and adds 1 paradox die if I recall correctly (so tossing a fireball in front of a sleeper always risks paradox, even if you don't go over your reach limit) . Larger groups adding dice tricks to the roll. But the key is obvious magic, if it wouldn't cause dissonance and unravel the spell, it wouldn't worsen paradox risk either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T23:37:05-07:00","id":877394,"title":"","content":"Nope. Sleepers cause Paradox here too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:19:19-07:00","id":877422,"title":"","content":"The trick here is that the Sleepers are distracted when the obvious magic happens, so they don't really notice it. Another example would be telekinetically pulling a set of keys from the desk to your hand while the drunken gang thug is looking the other way. He doesn't <i>see</i> the obvious spells being cast, but they still happened in his presence. Would this be paradox inducing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:22:25-07:00","id":877425,"title":"","content":"1e RAW, they have to actually <i>witness</i> it. That is, they have to be aware of it somehow. If they don't see it, it doesn't cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> This is a part of why I love the change to 2e with Yantras, because, in 1e, the sanest Mage was the one who stood absolutely still and did nothing while casting that could give away that they're throwing a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T05:05:45-07:00","id":877565,"title":"","content":"They apply dice tricks (9 again, 8 again, rote quality, etc) to paradox pools, and increase it by flat 1 (never more). Basically, if you play safe, they are pretty harmless.<br /> If you play safe. In Mage. While Reaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:46:18-07:00","id":877636,"title":"","content":"I'd say they need to actually notice the magic being done, if they look the other way nothing.<br /> <br /> Actually I find the &quot;obvious magic&quot; part kinda problematic cause sometimes it's hard to say whether an effect is obvious or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:39:51-07:00","id":877804,"title":"","content":"What practice is a Life spell that accelerates natural regeneration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:48:43-07:00","id":877819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=877804#post877804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practice is a Life spell that accelerates natural regeneration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Perfecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:06:15-07:00","id":877837,"title":"","content":"It could easily be argued to Ruling or even Compelling, depending on the strength. Straight healing feels like perfecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:18:20-07:00","id":877855,"title":"","content":"You can heal people with rulling in 2E. Boosting regenation in a way that doesn't seem unnatural could be compelling (say doubling the healing speed for instance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:22:47-07:00","id":877856,"title":"","content":"For healing a slash or a broken bone I would use Ruling. You're controlling the body to do a thing that normally could do by itself, closing an open wound or fixing a broken bone. For nastier wounds as serious burns, amputations or ugly infections like gangrene, I usually require perfecting as the body don't heal this wounds by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T12:07:52-07:00","id":877959,"title":"","content":"I mean accelerate natural healing at the rate of 1:8, so f.e. the body heals 1 bashing damage per 2 minutes, 1 lethal per 6 hours, 1 aggravated per day for the duration of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T14:46:53-07:00","id":878109,"title":"","content":"I'd say Rulling in that case,IMHO Compelling could do something like optimising the healing process, make blood coagulate faster, hasten regenation in a lvl similar to the use of medicine and recieving proper medical care. What you want is beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T13:51:36-07:00","id":879662,"title":"","content":"What happens if you scour your entire Stamina? I know it's not D&amp;D, but does having Stamina 0 kill a character? Or is it simply an Attribute decrease, lowering your maximum Health and connected benefits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T14:46:12-07:00","id":879703,"title":"","content":"I think you cannot Scourge yourself below 1 in an Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T14:54:54-07:00","id":879709,"title":"","content":"Even if you could I'd assume that yes, you die because that's the required minimum attribute to have a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:22:55-07:00","id":880346,"title":"","content":"So do Life spells that heal or transform someone need to be made Indefinite, or is that change already permanent once the spell is cast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:53:23-07:00","id":880379,"title":"","content":"It depends on the spell. Basic healing stays without the need to pump up duration.<br /> <br /> In general, if it's something the body would be able to do by itself given enough time it will stay. Everything else requires to pump up duration.<br /> <br /> So for instance: heal a wound - stays, regenerate a lost limb - nope, cure cancer - stays, cure a genetic deasease - nope, make your hair grow longer - stays, change hair colour - nope. At least that's how I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 05-02-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:29:11-07:00","id":880417,"title":"","content":"Talking about that, we have some spoiler about healing lethal/aggravated damage being Ruling of Perfecting ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:31:16-07:00","id":880476,"title":"","content":"Dave mentioned that healing wounds was Ruling for Life. He didn't say anything about the severity of the wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T16:28:35-07:00","id":880567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=880346#post880346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do Life spells that heal or transform someone need to be made Indefinite, or is that change already permanent once the spell is cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>The healing effects are <i>Lasting</i>, which means they're permanent. Wounds don't reopen when the spell is finished. The spell itself is of momentary Duration (one turn), but its effects persist. Now, for a spell like that, you <i>can </i>cast them with a longer Duration, which means the effects recur at the caster's Gnosis-based ritual casting interval. So in this case, a healing spell cast at a high Duration by a Gnosis 1 mage has its effect every 3 hours. This can be made indefinite with the proper spell factors, and when you do, you heal every 3 hours until the spell is canceled, dispelled, or you die.<br /> <br /> Transforming someone is temporary, as in it doesn't have a Lasting effect. You'd have to make the spell indefinite to make it last forever, though it can still be dispelled or canceled by the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:49:39-07:00","id":880853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=877959#post877959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean accelerate natural healing at the rate of 1:8, so f.e. the body heals 1 bashing damage per 2 minutes, 1 lethal per 6 hours, 1 aggravated per day for the duration of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>thats Body Control a ruling spell. Its +2 Reach to half healing time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:54:03-07:00","id":880855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=880417#post880417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about that, we have some spoiler about healing lethal/aggravated damage being Ruling of Perfecting ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked at my friend, a baker of Beast Ks: Aggravate can be healed with Patterning. Or, so he say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T04:02:11-07:00","id":880859,"title":"","content":"Do spirits/ghost/goetic you create suffer the effect of Dissonance? Or if lets say you give one of the above creatures a manfastation and sleepers see that, would that cause Dissonance? <br /> Because these creatures naturally exist in the world so I'm sure this counts as Obvious Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:40:25-07:00","id":881050,"title":"","content":"Can, or indeed must, a Mage unlearn their Order-based spellcasting specialties if they convert to another order?<br /> <br /> Merely becoming apostate doesn't do it (barring odd circumstances), as it's still techniques that they have learned, but it seems fitting for a new Mystagogue to cast off the trappings of heir former Panopticon masters when they swear new loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T10:51:53-07:00","id":881096,"title":"","content":"They're not <i>spellcasting</i> Specialties -- they're <i>Rote</i> Specialties. A subtle difference, but an important distinction because they only apply to Rotes created by that Order (MtA p.75). Presumably if you wanted to emphasize eschewing 'the old', the Mage would simply stop using the Order's Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:50:34-07:00","id":882465,"title":"","content":"Hold up- serious question here. I was always under the impression that a Hallow was just a Locus, but the Merit in the Mage 2E core shows that this is obviously <i>not </i>the case. What on earth are Hallows then? Isn't Mana just concentrated Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:10:16-07:00","id":882483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=882465#post882465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold up- serious question here. I was always under the impression that a Hallow was just a Locus, but the Merit in the Mage 2E core shows that this is obviously <i>not </i>the case. What on earth are Hallows then? Isn't Mana just concentrated Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana is the stuff of the Supernal. Always has been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:13:17-07:00","id":882596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=882465#post882465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold up- serious question here. I was always under the impression that a Hallow was just a Locus, but the Merit in the Mage 2E core shows that this is obviously <i>not </i>the case. What on earth are Hallows then? Isn't Mana just concentrated Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Loci and Hallows were always different things. Loci were places where the Shadow and the materiel world's Gauntlet was week, Hallows were places where the Supernal World Leaked into the Fallen World. <br /> <br /> They are similiar concepts with completely different results","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:55:08-07:00","id":885041,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain to me importance of Ectoplasm and it's uses? It's a thing important enough to be mentioned as standalone entry in Arcanum's Purview, and has two spells dedicated solely to creating it and shaping, but...it seems to do very little. Why would I care about ectoplasm as a Death 3 Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:18:25-07:00","id":886477,"title":"","content":"Is it posible to design a spell that includes algorithms? For example, a Moros Arrow mage making a Rote that transmutes the substance of his bullets depending on what he's aiming at. (If Vampire, magnesium. Else if Werewolf, silver. Else if Fair folk, iron)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:21:31-07:00","id":886482,"title":"","content":"I think dynamic spells like that are supposed to be Archmastery. You would be better with casting multiple spells on it that only trigger on what you are aiming at: so a spell that works &quot;When aimed at werwolf, turn into iron&quot;, &quot;if aimed at fair folk, turn into iron&quot;), etc. Not a single spell, but a web of spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:57:48-07:00","id":886520,"title":"","content":"Shame, but I suppose that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Another question that popped in to mind soon after that one: Is it possible to use sympathy reactively? For example an enemy mage tries to curse you though a sympathetic link, but your defenses cancel it. Then you reach back though that previously established link and attack them in turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:12:52-07:00","id":887538,"title":"","content":"You could in 1e, you probably have to cast a spell to do it in 2e, but then it would definitely be doable. It looks like Reflexive spells cost a Reach and 1 Mana. Probably what you'd be doing is forcing the link to stay open so you'd actually have the chance to cast back. Benefit is that you can fire away at each other, downside is that unless your Sympathy to your attacker is better than his to you his effective Withstand will be higher than yours giving him the high ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:44:10-07:00","id":887618,"title":"","content":"I posted this in the FAQ thread already, but here we go.<br /> <br /> So you have a Gnosis 10 character with 10 Strength, all bought with experience, no Life spell enhancement yet.<br /> <br /> If a Sleeper were to walk by and see this guy hoisting a Honda Civic over his head,<br /> what happens?<br /> <br /> Does the Sleeper start having an abyssal panic attack over how this guy's strength is fairly Supernal,<br /> or does the Sleeper just start recording it for youtube without much difficulty beyond &quot;That guy's not human!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:54:46-07:00","id":887629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=887618#post887618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this in the FAQ thread already, but here we go.<br /> <br /> So you have a Gnosis 10 character with 10 Strength, all bought with experience, no Life spell enhancement yet.<br /> <br /> If a Sleeper were to walk by and see this guy hoisting a Honda Civic over his head,<br /> what happens?<br /> <br /> Does the Sleeper start having an abyssal panic attack over how this guy's strength is fairly Supernal,<br /> or does the Sleeper just start recording it for youtube without much difficulty beyond &amp;quot;That guy's not human!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that although this character's supernatural strength is a result of his Gnosis, it's still not supernal magic in the sense of calling down supernal truths to alter fallen reality, so it wouldn't trigger Paradox or Quiessence. That said, this is Chronicles of Darkness, where everyone at least has a friend of a friend who saw a ghost one time and the supernatural remains an open secret more due to humanity's own doubt than effort on the part of supernatural conspiracies. So most likely the Sleeper is going to assume there's some kind of trick going on. Obviously that guy's not <i>really</i> lifting a car - that would be impossible. Must be some kind of street magician with a huge budget for practical effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:10:24-07:00","id":887646,"title":"","content":"Definetely Youtube recording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:49:16-07:00","id":887810,"title":"","content":"What does the &quot;Add fate <b>\u2022</b>&quot; effect on Dispel Magic... uhh... do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:31:46-07:00","id":887854,"title":"","content":"It allows you to make the spell not work only for a certain group of people. Like you can put a hole in a Ban so that your cabal mates can pass through but no one else. It's the same effect that Prime 3 spell in first edition had forgotthename","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:33:25-07:00","id":887858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=887854#post887854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It allows you to make the spell not work only for a certain group of people. Like you can put a hole in a Ban so that your cabal mates can pass through but no one else. It's the same effect that Prime 3 spell in first edition had forgotthename</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. I would not have gotten that from the text. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:36:31-07:00","id":887864,"title":"","content":"It's great for infiltration, because you can sneak in without turning off the spell. Mission Impossible theme and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T12:32:28-07:00","id":888444,"title":"","content":"How does <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883168-2e-thinking-about-temporal-sympathy\">Temporal Sympathy</a> work?<br /> <br /> I assume that this line in the Attainment: &quot;The spell is Withstood by the fragility of the temporal sympathy (p. 186) between the mage and her subject&quot; is incorrect, as sympathy levels describe the similitude between the subject and its past self.<br /> <br /> Can I apply it only to Time-related spells like Postcognition, or could I theoretically throw a Mind spell back in time so that someone that's bugging me right now decided to do something else earlier that day? Or a Death spell if I'm really serious about not wanting to be disturbed?<br /> <br /> The target of the spell is still the subject's present self, so I'm guessing that I can read where a car has been even if the past location isn't in the spell's range anymore, as long as the <i>present</i> car is in range.<br /> <br /> Likewise, they resist and/or Withstand with their present traits, unless their past had some sort of Time shielding up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:44:22-07:00","id":888694,"title":"","content":"I kind of can't figure out how much reach you need for remote viewing vs sympathy casting. It SOUNDS like both require +2 reach total? but sometimes it sounds like remote viewing needs 2 reach and then sympathy casting needs just 1? I get that you spend 1 on sensory and then can upgrade to remote viewing casting and/or sympathetic casting, but I don't get if either or both of those cost 1 additional reach to get beyond sensory to the &quot;out of your actual presence casting&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:46:54-07:00","id":888698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=885041#post885041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain to me importance of Ectoplasm and it's uses? It's a thing important enough to be mentioned as standalone entry in Arcanum's Purview, and has two spells dedicated solely to creating it and shaping, but...it seems to do very little. Why would I care about ectoplasm as a Death 3 Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to guess its purpose is to give ghosts something to possess without having to claim a person. I dunno if ghosts use the claimed or just the possessed condition but giving them something to utilize without having to sacrifice another person or use a corpse sounds useful enough. I'm guessing this is how giests work too. I dunno if it was ever confronted in canon but I'm guessing the ectoplasm with a bit of work could become plasm for giests and make a moros a huge boon to krewes in a crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T18:07:31-07:00","id":888719,"title":"","content":"Ectoplasm seems to be the substance that a ghost uses to manifest, if a ghost can interact physically with the Fallen world when manifested in a body of ectoplasm then being able to shape it means an infinite variety of tools for you and any ghosts you employ. It also means a Mage in Death Twilight can create tools with which to interact with the physical world, including an ectoplasmic body which might have certain ghost-like benefits. I'm not sure about any of that, it's just my best guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:14:10-07:00","id":889251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=888694#post888694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of can't figure out how much reach you need for remote viewing vs sympathy casting. It SOUNDS like both require +2 reach total? but sometimes it sounds like remote viewing needs 2 reach and then sympathy casting needs just 1? I get that you spend 1 on sensory and then can upgrade to remote viewing casting and/or sympathetic casting, but I don't get if either or both of those cost 1 additional reach to get beyond sensory to the &quot;out of your actual presence casting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Sympathetic Range and Temporal Sympathy require that the spell be at Sensory but don't have any additional Reach mentioned, so I <i>think</i> using just the text you arrive at:<br /> <br /> <b>Sensory Range: </b>+1 Reach<br /> <b>Sympathetic Range: </b>+1 Reach (for sensory), +1 Mana, requires 1 sympathy yantra (or +2 Mana and two yantras for Temporal and Spatial sympathy)<br /> <b>Remote Viewing: </b>+2 Reach (one for sensory plus one more)<br /> <br /> That seems a little odd - but I could imagine a Merit that lets Space 2 people spend 1 mana instead of 1 extra reach to cast on remote viewing (maybe requiring a sympathetic yantra) especially if you wanted to make a Free Councilor or Seer that routinely operated via surveillance networks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:18:57-07:00","id":889252,"title":"","content":"I think in the right circumstances one yantra could pull double duty as temporal and spacial sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:29:08-07:00","id":889256,"title":"","content":"I'd accept that, yeah.<br /> <br /> The only reason you might not let one yantra cover both requirements is that the sympathetics don't provide any dice bonus when used as a necessary element of an Attainment, so part of the &quot;costs&quot; of sympathetic range is &quot;eating up&quot; a yantra slot with no dice payoff - so to use both Attainments you'd normally have to use two yantra slots with no dice gain. Even if I was particularly concerned with that, I'd probably let one object be harnessed twice to cover both requirements as two separate yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:19:15-07:00","id":889287,"title":"","content":"Double-dipping the same object for two different symbolic meanings is explicitly called out as possible, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:15:20-07:00","id":889310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889252#post889252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the right circumstances one yantra could pull double duty as temporal and spacial sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the thing being used as a yantra is used twice or that it satisfies the yantra condition for both forms of sympathy? Because the way I read the rules is that the same &quot;thing&quot; can be used multiple times as yantras, but each one is a separate yantra. Like if you are allowed 3 yantras and you use a photograph of someone for both spatial and temporal sympathy, 2 of your yantras are already sucked up even though its just the one photo, and you're left with 1 yantra left for dice (probably the environment after that or your dedicated tool). What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:34:20-07:00","id":889327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> , that's correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:17:00-07:00","id":889389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889251#post889251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both Sympathetic Range and Temporal Sympathy require that the spell be at Sensory but don't have any additional Reach mentioned, so I <i>think</i> using just the text you arrive at:<br /> <br /> <b>Sensory Range: </b>+1 Reach<br /> <b>Sympathetic Range: </b>+1 Reach (for sensory), +1 Mana, requires 1 sympathy yantra (or +2 Mana and two yantras for Temporal and Spatial sympathy)<br /> <b>Remote Viewing: </b>+2 Reach (one for sensory plus one more)<br /> <br /> That seems a little odd - but I could imagine a Merit that lets Space 2 people spend 1 mana instead of 1 extra reach to cast on remote viewing (maybe requiring a sympathetic yantra) especially if you wanted to make a Free Councilor or Seer that routinely operated via surveillance networks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always viewed that the remote viewing became sympathetic with space 2, as you had a current, visual representation <i>right there in front of you</i> for whatever means you were remotely viewing the target. Thus, why use the remote viewing casting when your skill in space would let you hit the target no matter where he was. <br /> <br /> I viewed the remote viewing extra reach was so that someone couldn't just tap into all the cameras in a city using a rote 1 dot force spell and then start killing people with lightning blasts without ever needing space or to use up a Yantra slot. Sympathetic Casting, with it's Yantra requirement, does lessen the death from elsewhere aspect with its required XP, as well as the need to lessen the spell potential with the loss of a Yantra slot to cast sympathetically (it also keeps space from becoming useless when Forces exists during the age of the internet.) Note, the Blitz* is still feasible, but more prone to paradox without having more reach available (i.e. higher arcana.) <br /> <br /> <br /> *The aformentioned Camera/Lightning combo so named by my Obrimos player based on London's numerous cameras as well as the attacks that befell said city during WWII, which were named after the German word for lightning. Considering the devastation an Obrimos could achieve with this effect, and over a city wide area of they just wished to target structures or indiscriminately, I find the name to be terrifyingly appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-12-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:00:02-07:00","id":889413,"title":"","content":"Don't both Sympathetic Range and Remote Viewing casting require a minimum of 2 Reach, one for Sensory and yet another for the Sympathetic or RV effect?<br /> <br /> The advantage using remote viewing is that it doesn't require a sympathetic Yantra and cost a mana.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:10:03-07:00","id":889419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889413#post889413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't both Sympathetic Range and Remote Viewing casting require a minimum of 2 Reach, one for Sensory and yet another for the Sympathetic or RV effect?<br /> <br /> The advantage using remote viewing is that it doesn't require a sympathetic Yantra and cost a mana.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not as I read it. Remote viewing adds an extra reach on top of casting at sensory range; thus you end up with +2 reach. Sympathetic Range uses adds 1 mana and the yantra requirement to the Sensory Range cost; thus 1 reach, 1 mana, and 1 sympathetic yantra. <br /> <br /> The confusion that arose for my group at first (since why you would do this given the requirements to casts crying) was if you are remotely viewing through a crying window, it doesn't count as Sympathy but remote viewing if you don't use Sympathetic casting, thus +2 reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:15:48-07:00","id":889426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889419#post889419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Not as I read it.</b> Remote viewing adds an extra reach on top of casting at sensory range; thus you end up with +2 reach. Sympathetic Range uses adds 1 mana and the yantra requirement to the Sensory Range cost; thus 1 reach, 1 mana, and 1 sympathetic yantra.<br /> <br /> The confusion that arose for my group at first (since why you would do this given the requirements to casts crying) was if you are remotely viewing through a crying window, it doesn't count as Sympathy but remote viewing if you don't use Sympathetic casting, thus +2 reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't you agreeing with me?<br /> <br /> In order to cast either with remote viewing or sympathetic range, it requires +2 Reach, one to upgrade Touch to Sensory, and a second Reach to upgrade to either RV or Sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Remove viewing doesn't require the sympathetic Yantra or mana expenditure of Sympathetic casting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:22:29-07:00","id":889431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889426#post889426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't you agreeing with me?<br /> <br /> In order to cast either with remote viewing or sympathetic range, it requires +2 Reach, one to upgrade Touch to Sensory, and a second Reach to upgrade to either RV or Sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Remove viewing doesn't require the sympathetic Yantra or mana expenditure of Sympathetic casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read what I wrote? I added up the costs. Sympathetic costs 1 less reach but costs 1 mana and 1 yantra slot which RV does not.<br /> <br /> To review the math:<br /> Sympathetic Casting uses sensory range, but you are sensing the Sympathetic ties and then reinforcing with Mana and the Yantra. <i>Thus, you only spend 1 reach <b>total</b></i>, but also spend 1 mana and must use a Yantra. <br /> <br /> RV uses sensory range, but must spend an extra reach to cast on the target, thus the total of 2 reach. But it costs no Mana and leaves you a Yantra slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:27:39-07:00","id":889439,"title":"","content":"This might have been covered already, but: When doing Teamwork rolls for Ritual Casting, can the Secondary Casters use Yantras? For that matter, can the Primary Caster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:29:07-07:00","id":889442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889431#post889431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you read what I wrote? I added up the costs. Sympathetic costs 1 less reach but costs 1 mana and 1 yantra slot.<br /> <br /> To review the math:<br /> Sympathetic Casting uses sensory range, but you are sensing the Sympathetic ties and then reinforcing with Mana and the Yantra. <i>Thus, you only spend 1 reach <b>total</b></i>, but also spend 1 mana and must use a Yantra.<br /> <br /> RV uses sensory range, but must spend an extra reach to cast on the target, thus the total of 2 reach. But it costs no Mana and leaves you a Yantra slot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's confusing. I hope Dave clarifies RV and Sympathetic casting in the FAQ. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:50:25-07:00","id":889462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889442#post889442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's confusing. I hope Dave clarifies RV and Sympathetic casting in the FAQ. </div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it made sense, but yeah, More clarity is always good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry if I seemed annoyed; just re-read my post and realized it was rather snippy sounding...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889439#post889439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been covered already, but: When doing Teamwork rolls for Ritual Casting, can the Secondary Casters use Yantras? For that matter, can the Primary Caster?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends, and I am taking my best guess here (I would ask Dave in the FAQ):<br /> <br /> -For secondary casters, probably not (especially those who cannot cast the spell due to lacking all necessary arcana). <br /> -The primary caster likely could, but must extend the ritual time if they want to include other Yantras if using <i>mages without the required Arcana as a Yantra</i>.<br /> <br /> I could maybe see letting a secondary caster who can cast the spell and has a ritual time equal to or less than the primary casters ritual time add a single yantra (and only appropriate ones that would play a part in the ritual's symbolism; Rote Mudras likely wouldn't help a ritual) but that would be the ST judgment call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:01:41-07:00","id":889472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889439#post889439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been covered already, but: When doing Teamwork rolls for Ritual Casting, can the Secondary Casters use Yantras? For that matter, can the Primary Caster?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about spellcasting Teamwork (Page 119)?<br /> The final bit notes that the caster<b>s </b>(note plural) may use non-contributing assistants as an environmental yantra, which suggests that both primary and secondary casters may use yantras.<br /> <br /> Near as I can tell the dice pools would be:<br /> <b>Primary Caster: </b>Gnosis + Arcanum + yantras + teamwork successes<br /> <b>Secondary Caster Who Could Cast the Spell: </b>Gnosis + Arcanum + yantras<br /> <b>Secondary Caster Who Can't Cast the Spell but has one dot in all required Arcanum: </b>Gnosis + yantras - 3<br /> <br /> (That looks like rote mudras might cause an issue, but maybe not? Given the conversion ratio of dice to successes to dice to successes, letting the secondaries use high-dice yantras won't get too disgusting.)<br /> <br /> If the spell's being cast as a ritual I guess you'd have to take the slowest possible time from the caster pool to determine how long it takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:01:46-07:00","id":889473,"title":"","content":"You should put that in the FAQ thread so I don't forget it, but yeah - Yantras are essentially equipment bonuses for a casting roll; everyone in a ritual can use their own. Even the same things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:09:40-07:00","id":889478,"title":"","content":"Can you have a chthonian familiar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:17:50-07:00","id":889482,"title":"","content":"Do Sleepwalkers and Proximi participating in teamwork rituals all together count as one environmental Yantra (+1), or does each individual participant count as separate environmental Yantra?<br /> <br /> For instance, if a mage is assisted by both a Sleepwalker and Proximi, would the spell have a +2 bonus and use up 2 Yantra slots, or would both people count as one Yantra for a +1 bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:44:15-07:00","id":890647,"title":"","content":"What is a &quot;noble weapon&quot;? As weapon path tool for Obrimos...? I have problem with this definition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:16:42-07:00","id":890659,"title":"","content":"Lightsabers, obvs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:26:48-07:00","id":890669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=890647#post890647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a &quot;noble weapon&quot;? As weapon path tool for Obrimos...? I have problem with this definition...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Similarly, for Moros, what do &quot;buried materials&quot; encompass. All metals? Anything mined or once buried like bones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-14-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:34:18-07:00","id":890673,"title":"","content":"For Moros is much more easy: crushing weapon are very clear as concept.<br /> There are many modern type.<br /> But &quot;noble&quot;...and modern?<br /> All Obrimos use &quot;Stocco&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-14-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:25:12-07:00","id":890838,"title":"","content":"Noble weapons are probably those types of weapons that are/were traditionally wielded by nobility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:42:14-07:00","id":890843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=890838#post890838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noble weapons are probably those types of weapons that are/were traditionally wielded by nobility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Signet Daggers, foils, longswords, katanas... Likely any sword or other weapon that has authority and &quot;heroic&quot; aspects tied to it, which in turn are often tied to nobility of different nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T23:20:54-07:00","id":891006,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T23:37:41-07:00","id":891015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=890843#post890843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Signet Daggers, foils, longswords, katanas... Likely any sword or other weapon that has authority and &quot;heroic&quot; aspects tied to it, which in turn are often tied to nobility of different nations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How broadly would you define &quot;buried materials&quot; for Moros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T02:02:39-07:00","id":891050,"title":"","content":"If you use Time magic to get more work done in a day, how does that interact with the boundary of the time spell when it comes to things like your utilities? Like if I use a time to write a paper in a matter of minutes that would normally take hours, does the mage's electric bill go up or would the keyboard stop working because you're ghosting from typing too fast? Would your water bill go up or would the water just be really slow?<br /> <br /> Fridge logic question I know :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889478#post889478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have a chthonian familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if the ST doesn't have a problem with it you could? Sorta? Make a custom merit for it. The real problem is not can you, but how you get a cthonian familiar? its as likely to agree to the binding spell as it is to break it and eat you. How would you get it to agree of its own free will and keep it interested in maintaining the bond? It is a nearly unpredictable alien entity. In 1E when you summon them its described that they don't even consciously think about the summoning or the interaction, for them it is like scratching an itch, it is almost a subconscious interaction for them and they don't really interact with the mage in a cerebral fashion.<br /> <br /> TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R , I'd say yes because abyssals have been familiars and they're as alien as it gets---its just not a HEALTHY idea to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-15-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:19:37-07:00","id":891064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891050#post891050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if the ST doesn't have a problem with it you could? Sorta? Make a custom merit for it. The real problem is not can you, but how you get a cthonian familiar? its as likely to agree to the binding spell as it is to break it and eat you. How would you get it to agree of its own free will and keep it interested in maintaining the bond? It is a nearly unpredictable alien entity. In 1E when you summon them its described that they don't even consciously think about the summoning or the interaction, for them it is like scratching an itch, it is almost a subconscious interaction for them and they don't really interact with the mage in a cerebral fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I'm asking because &quot;Chthonians use the same rules as ghosts&quot; now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:56:43-07:00","id":891074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891015#post891015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How broadly would you define &quot;buried materials&quot; for Moros?</div> </div> </div> </div>We had this same question at our table two days ago, when our Moros #2 started reading rules pertaining her characters. We are not English native speakers, so the term confused us a little, and we ended up figuring out this might mean all of the waste products and byproducts, but if someone with actual understanding of what it means in English could explain, we would be grateful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T04:51:56-07:00","id":891089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891015#post891015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How broadly would you define &quot;buried materials&quot; for Moros?</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to look at it through the lens of mage sight. So does it fit thematically within the realm of a Moros. Weapons buried in a crypt, iron and lead hand forged into something symbolic, diamond and other gems in amulets or other tools, etc.<br /> <br /> I actually give No risk the most leeway since their entire world view is shaped by Matter. Wooden/other once living materials or simple primal ones (obsidian daggers), or those things that have been well refined/ascribed to other paths, are usually the only ones that I outright exclude. And even then, it depends: a human skill would fit a Moros, but a leather hide drum might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:17:53-07:00","id":891134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891064#post891064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I'm asking because &quot;Chthonians use the same rules as ghosts&quot; now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what rank they are, I can't find a reference for them below Rank 6 which is right out, but there might be lower examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:00:58-07:00","id":891212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891134#post891134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on what rank they are, I can't find a reference for them below Rank 6 which is right out, but there might be lower examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Which books? There's like 2 in Mage: Summoners, 1e. I don't recall seeing them in Giest but I didn't scour that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:45:26-07:00","id":891237,"title":"","content":"That's what I was saying, I don't know of any chthonians with a low enough rank for the familiar bond to work. You could possibly make your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:26:11-07:00","id":891273,"title":"","content":"Chthonians have explicitly occupied the entire Rank band from 1 to 6 since their introduction; the primary obstacles to keeping one as a familiar are determining whether using ghost mechanics qualifies them as ghosts for the purposes of that specific spell and the question of whether the one-lunar-month time-limit provided in Summoners still applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-15-2016, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T12:23:21-07:00","id":891306,"title":"","content":"The entity you're using has to willingly partake of the Familiar bond and the alien nature of the neverborn might make them incapable of it.<br /> <br /> In any case, Mage says &quot;just use ghost mechanics for them&quot; because that doesn't take up more wordcount than the handful of sentences in our description of the Underworld to note that Cthonians are a thing that exists. In the event of a Geist 2E, they might not end up being that simple. Possibly closer to ghosts than spirits are, but just because a casual Moros doesn't know the difference between a Nephwrack and a Geist, doesn't mean the creatures themselves don't.<br /> <br /> Like everything to do with the Underworld, it's a gamble on my part that Geist will get its turn in the second edition rollout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:23:54-07:00","id":891570,"title":"","content":"So it possible to possess multiple people at once with Mind 5, how would a mage control them all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:25:02-07:00","id":891572,"title":"","content":"One Mind Two Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:44:06-07:00","id":891578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891572#post891572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Mind Two Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I came to that conclusion as well but wouldn't controlling another body count as a physical action? <br /> Thus invalidating One Mind Two Thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:45:58-07:00","id":891579,"title":"","content":"Looking at the fact that you mastered the whole Arcanum, I'm pretty sure you could do some Creative Thaumaturgy to cook something similar but more suited to it. Or maybe just Possession is enough, I mean, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:49:14-07:00","id":891581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891579#post891579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the fact that you mastered the whole Arcanum, I'm pretty sure you could do some Creative Thaumaturgy to cook something similar but more suited to it. Or maybe just Possession is enough, I mean, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, just wanted some feed back on the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T00:39:08-07:00","id":891612,"title":"","content":"What is the benefit of using Mage Armor the Attainment vs relinquishing a spell granting the same effects? One costs a point of mana and lasts a scene, the other costs a point of willpower and lasts until the next chapter. You can even avoid the spell going awry by dispelling it and recasting it. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T02:11:54-07:00","id":891631,"title":"","content":"You can't dispel an attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:47:06-07:00","id":891768,"title":"","content":"I would argue that in the new Practices model imitating what Mage Armor the Attainment does falls in line more closely with Patterning than Shielding. It would be interesting to see what the devs think, if you should still be able to cast the spell-version of Mage Armor at 2 dots... (my personal preference would be no, wait till 4th dot, based on the Apocalypse spell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:31:28-07:00","id":891808,"title":"","content":"Do the Immediate Nimbus Tilts affect the owner as well as the witnesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11689-kokiteno","name":"Kokiteno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:37:23-07:00","id":891814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891768#post891768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that in the new Practices model imitating what Mage Armor the Attainment does falls in line more closely with Patterning than Shielding. It would be interesting to see what the devs think, if you should still be able to cast the spell-version of Mage Armor at 2 dots... (my personal preference would be no, wait till 4th dot, based on the Apocalypse spell).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Arcanum. The ability to extend your mage armor to other people was a three-dot spell last edition, and we currently don't have a 2e equivalent. It's something we'll get to, but *at most* it would be Patterning. Might be Weaving when cast on other mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:38:53-07:00","id":891816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891768#post891768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that in the new Practices model imitating what Mage Armor the Attainment does falls in line more closely with Patterning than Shielding. It would be interesting to see what the devs think, if you should still be able to cast the spell-version of Mage Armor at 2 dots... (my personal preference would be no, wait till 4th dot, based on the Apocalypse spell).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an important distinction, yeah! I mean the Death Armor would be weaving at least, it varies depending on what the attainment does. The Mage Armors are at 2 dots now and work the way they do so that they can be grabbed according to their balance and effect on the game, without disrupting the lore focus of the Practices, which are now balanced using reach.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kokiteno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891808#post891808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Immediate Nimbus Tilts affect the owner as well as the witnesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>gosh that's a good one. I asked that myself in the FAQ topic. The other important question that I'd have, and will repeat here, is how many spells would be involved in making a rank 4 or 5 spirit out of a familiar without losing your familiar bond for its duration and making the spirit from nothing using Making. In 1e it was just the one spell to do this, but in 2e this sounds like it would involve like 3 or 4 spells, which is good balancing but then it raises questions on how reach affect these combined spells, and how the spellfactors affect combined spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-16-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:01:19-07:00","id":891829,"title":"","content":"Your biggest problem is if you raise a Spirit's rank above 2 then it loses the Familiar bond.<br /> <br /> Making the spirit is 5, raising its rank is 3 (Perfecting) so it only ought to take 2 spells to do that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:12:31-07:00","id":891869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891829#post891829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the spirit is 5, raising its rank is 3 (Perfecting) so it only ought to take 2 spells to do that part.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for a second spell. Birthing the Spirit can do that with a reach and 1 mana.<br /> <br /> But I do have my own question about Birthing the Spirit. The spell doesn't say that the spirit goes away after the spell end like the other &quot;create ephemeral&quot; spells nor is the primary factor duration. So does that mean Birth the Spirit is ment to be a lasting spell?<br /> <br /> Also by increasing the number of subjects for a spell would that let you create more spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:18:51-07:00","id":891878,"title":"","content":"Good point.<br /> <br /> It would seem so, and yes respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:01:10-07:00","id":891902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891829#post891829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your biggest problem is if you raise a Spirit's rank above 2 then it loses the Familiar bond.<br /> <br /> Making the spirit is 5, raising its rank is 3 (Perfecting) so it only ought to take 2 spells to do that part.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't clear to me from the book if this is the case or if that's just an interpretation. A spirit that is naturally over rank 2 DEFINITELY cannot be bonded, but of what I speak is binding a spirit of rank 2 and then, only afterwards, increasing its rank. Whether that immediately breaks the bond or if it holds because you were already bonded to the spirit, I do not know, and at this point it sounds like it has to fall to the ST to decide that per given chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:05:22-07:00","id":891906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891902#post891902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't clear to me from the book if this is the case or if that's just an interpretation. A spirit that is naturally over rank 2 DEFINITELY cannot be bonded, but of what I speak is binding a spirit of rank 2 and then, only afterwards, increasing its rank. Whether that immediately breaks the bond or if it holds because you were already bonded to the spirit, I do not know, and at this point it sounds like it has to fall to the ST to decide that per given chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spirit that becomes rank 3+ is disqualified for the familiar manifestation, so the bond is broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:16:31-07:00","id":891914,"title":"","content":"Under the new rules, do instant spells (IE ones that lack a duration) count against the number of active spells you can have up at any one time?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if my Gnosis 1 mage needs to spend reach to cast, say, Kinetic Strike whilst having Pierce Deception up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1218,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","user":"Taejix","date":". 05-16-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","name":"Taejix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:38:45-07:00","id":891927,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Instant spells have to Reach if you're already at your Gnosis limit. On the bright side it automatically stops counting against your limit immediately after you cast it because it was only an Instant effect and so the Reach only stacks transiently.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> , Dave answered this one before the game was released. Anything that raises an entity above rank 2 also disqualifies it as a Familiar. You could still keep it as an ally, retainer, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:39:08-07:00","id":891928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taejix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891914#post891914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the new rules, do instant spells (IE ones that lack a duration) count against the number of active spells you can have up at any one time?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if my Gnosis 1 mage needs to spend reach to cast, say, Kinetic Strike whilst having Pierce Deception up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You should post that question in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread/page16\">FAQ thread</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:40:34-07:00","id":891930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891927#post891927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Instant spells have to Reach if you're already at your Gnosis limit. On the bright side it automatically stops counting against your limit immediately after you cast it because it was only an Instant effect and so the Reach only stacks transiently.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> , Dave answered this one before the game was released. Anything that raises an entity above rank 2 also disqualifies it as a Familiar. You could still keep it as an ally, retainer, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, crap. When did he say this, was this awhile ago or was it close to the publication date? do you remember where this was I would like to see the context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891906#post891906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A spirit that becomes rank 3+ is disqualified for the familiar manifestation, so the bond is broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well aside from what Mrmbudois is saying about the word of god, as far as the book goes the manifestation does not say that the bond is broken, nor what the level of the spirit is. The Merit is clearly built around rank 1-2 entities and that's obvious, but then the spell that actually builds the merit and the manifestation condition only says that the spirit being cast on has to be rank 1 or 2 to be the valid subject of the spell. Sans what DaveB says, this implies to me that the spell is concerned about the spirit at the time of casting and not during its duration??<br /> <br /> See, the reason this is a concern of mine is, say, what happens if a Moros has a rank 2 familiar that they got from character creation, then some thyrsus casts bolster spirit and destroys the bond without having to be arcana 4 in anything. If this works and the bond is terminated, how is the player going to get their familiar back in the context of the story without potentionally losing it? Like the suggestion of the merits being turned to retainer the Moros can put the 4 dots from familiar into retainer I guess, but they still couldn't fix this in the story without a thyrsus handy on the moros's cabal or friends, not without wasting time from other players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-16-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:51:07-07:00","id":891938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891930#post891930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, crap. When did he say this, was this awhile ago or was it close to the publication date? do you remember where this was I would like to see the context.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well aside from what Mrmbudois is saying about the word of god, as far as the book goes the manifestation does not say that the bond is broken, nor what the level of the spirit is. The Merit is clearly built around rank 1-2 entities and that's obvious, but then the spell that actually builds the merit and the manifestation condition only says that the spirit being cast on has to be rank 1 or 2 to be the valid subject of the spell. Sans what DaveB says, this implies to me that the spell is concerned about the spirit at the time of casting and not during its duration??<br /> <br /> See, the reason this is a concern of mine is, say, what happens if a Moros has a rank 2 familiar that they got from character creation, then some thyrsus casts bolster spirit and destroys the bond without having to be arcana 4 in anything. If this works and the bond is terminated, how is the player going to get their familiar back in the context of the story without potentionally losing it? Like the suggestion of the merits being turned to retainer the Moros can put the 4 dots from familiar into retainer I guess, but they still couldn't fix this in the story without a thyrsus handy on the moros's cabal or friends, not without wasting time from other players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DaveB posting on 4chan for your reference:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543437\" target=\"_blank\">http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543437</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#117743\"><b>DaveB</b></span> <span style=\"color:#117743\">!!kn3vuELOelB</span> Fri 08 Apr 2016 12:43:47 <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543437\" target=\"_blank\">No.</a><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#q46543437\" target=\"_blank\">46543437</a> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#\" target=\"_blank\">Report</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#888888\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Quoted By: <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543621\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;46543621</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#789922\"><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543226\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;46543226</a></span><br /> We're up to doing the Page XXes. Fortunately, I have a list.<br /> <br /> Yes, your Familiar remains your Familiar even if it uses another Manifestation effect, including Claim, but Familiars have a hard cap of Rank 2 Making the entity Rank 3 through magic destroys the Familiar bond.<br /> <br /> Claim requires the entity to also have Fetter and Possess - a Rank 2 spirit doesn't actually have enough Manifestation slots to Claim someone, unless it starts dropping Numina.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:57:31-07:00","id":891946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891938#post891938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> DaveB posting on 4chan for your reference:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543437\" target=\"_blank\">http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46528164/#46543437</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey I remember that. I was asking about familiar and the claimed condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:10:15-07:00","id":891953,"title":"","content":"That was a good question to ask. Well thanks you two. That answers my concerns pretty effectively. And I guess sanctity of merits covers the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:44:32-07:00","id":891976,"title":"","content":"A ghost can't have Bolster Spirit cast on it since it's not a spirit. Your concern is valid if a Moros does it. I'd assume if you're playing a Moros though then you could Dispel the Bolster Ghost effect and either the Familiar bond would automatically kick back in, or you could have it recast.<br /> <br /> I think the Familiar Bond spell would be entitled to a Clash of Wills at the very least since its effect is in direct opposition to the effects that a Bolster (Entity) spell would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-16-2016, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:09:33-07:00","id":892093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taejix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891914#post891914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the new rules, do instant spells (IE ones that lack a duration) count against the number of active spells you can have up at any one time?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if my Gnosis 1 mage needs to spend reach to cast, say, Kinetic Strike whilst having Pierce Deception up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, and yes - you assess how many active spells you have before casting. Doesn't matter how long the spell over your limit will last for. If you're at your limit already you have to Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:48:44-07:00","id":892115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=891976#post891976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost can't have Bolster Spirit cast on it since it's not a spirit. Your concern is valid if a Moros does it. I'd assume if you're playing a Moros though then you could Dispel the Bolster Ghost effect and either the Familiar bond would automatically kick back in, or you could have it recast.<br /> <br /> I think the Familiar Bond spell would be entitled to a Clash of Wills at the very least since its effect is in direct opposition to the effects that a Bolster (Entity) spell would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to imply that the moros had a familiar that was a Ghost. The familiar would be from the Shadow. An obrimos isn't limited to familiars of the godmachine angels or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:58:52-07:00","id":892154,"title":"","content":"Oh, no that's true. It's just kind of the natural fit. For some reason I got it in my head that you were talking about a Moros with a ghost familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T18:28:17-07:00","id":892176,"title":"","content":"Legacy questions for 2e:<br /> Are the attainments for spells of equal or less dots? It provides an example of a (**) spell being used as a (***) attainment but not the other way around.<br /> So, is it possible to have an attainment achieve a higher dot spell? (I feel this is a 'no')<br /> <br /> Next question but related; I don't believe it is by the currently presented rules but; could a legacy utilize two arcana? I ask because I am considering a mage developing a legacy to mimic werewolves with shape changer(life ****) being the only non spirit spell I feel it'd require to be complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T19:30:16-07:00","id":892202,"title":"","content":"The reason you see a 2 dot spell as a 3rd attainment is because the attainment is using Reach that wouldn't be available at a lower level since attainments can't use any Reach above the arcana cap.<br /> <br /> Legacies can use two arcana, one main arcana and one optional arcana which frequently provides secondary effects to the main one. Shape changing would just be Life 4 though, unless you're trying to more perfectly mimic the effects of being half spirit and half flesh like true werewolves, in which case you'd probably need a conjunctional Spirit 4 effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T03:34:07-07:00","id":892410,"title":"","content":"I wanted to ask something about Abyssals that I'm not sure has an official answer, but its something I'd be curious about. So, when say a werewolf sees an Abyssal, they'll tend to think its some form of corruption Magath or the like. However, what does a Spirit think when it sees an Abyssal. Do they recognise it as a spirit, or do they consider it something other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T03:46:17-07:00","id":892415,"title":"","content":"It would depend entirely on the Abyssal in question's actual nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T08:13:00-07:00","id":892523,"title":"","content":"Yes, Abyssal entities can be of any Arcana or Arcana combination &quot;internally&quot; even if for rules purposes Gulmoth are handled as Spirits. So if a particular Gulmoth is taking in some Spirit-based characteristics, other Spirits should be able to recognize those. However the Abyss is rarely consistent, thus Spirits may detect another of their Kin, but possessed of an unreal Essence, or maybe it has an impossible Rank, maybe feeding from it causes anomalous behaviors. <br /> <br /> Other Gulmoth may not have any Spirit nature at all, they would be like ghosts are to spirits, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:41:37-07:00","id":893253,"title":"","content":"A Mage 2nd Edition question:<br /> <br /> How do you determine the Potency of a spell? Where is this explicit in the book?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:52:18-07:00","id":893262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893253#post893253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mage 2nd Edition question:<br /> <br /> How do you determine the Potency of a spell? Where is this explicit in the book?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the spellcasting rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:58:05-07:00","id":893305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893262#post893262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In the spellcasting rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that's what I thought, too, and I'm having trouble finding it. I'm reading pages 111 - 117 so far...There is a definition of Potency and the explanation that each spell description tells you what the Potency is for. The example in the book uses a damage spell. There are many references to how to increase Potency and how to alter it and how it interacts with other Spell Factors and Reach and Withstanding. All that makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> If the Potency of my spell is 2, how did I determine that number? And on what page in the book does it describe how to calculate the Potency of your spell? My Potency is always 1 ... and then I take dice penalties to increase it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","user":"Troy","date":". 05-18-2016, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:05:03-07:00","id":893362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893305#post893305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the Potency of my spell is 2, how did I determine that number? And on what page in the book does it describe how to calculate the Potency of your spell? My Potency is always 1 ... and then I take dice penalties to increase it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. You also get free moves down the table equal to your highest Arcanum in the spell minus 1. So if you're casting a Life 1 spell with Potency as the Primary Factor and you have Life 3, you can automatically cast it at Potency 3 (1+3-1). If you want Potency 4, that's -2 to dice to the pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo","name":"griffalo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8871_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:31:12-07:00","id":893424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffalo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893362#post893362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. You also get free moves down the table equal to your highest Arcanum in the spell minus 1. So if you're casting a Life 1 spell with Potency as the Primary Factor and you have Life 3, you can automatically cast it at Potency 3 (1+3-1). If you want Potency 4, that's -2 to dice to the pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. So all the references to successes on your spell rolls are superfluous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:43:52-07:00","id":893431,"title":"","content":"If I want to cause a gun to misfire the next time it is fired, what are the considerations?<br /> <br /> If it's done outside of combat but anticipating violence is the duration based on how long the spell will be in effect, waiting for the gun to fire to trigger the effect or is it the duration of the gun not being usable?<br /> <br /> What is the ideal practice if you're using Fate for this?<br /> <br /> Can this spell be safely released once the gun is cursed or must it be maintained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:53:48-07:00","id":893437,"title":"","content":"Exceptional Luck if it's just a &quot;singular&quot; happestance of gun being unable to fire due to many circumstances, Monkey's Paw if it's long term issue with the gun itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:31:10-07:00","id":893480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893424#post893424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent. So all the references to successes on your spell rolls are superfluous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, unless you roll an Exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:56:11-07:00","id":893733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893437#post893437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Luck if it's just a &quot;singular&quot; happestance of gun being unable to fire due to many circumstances, Monkey's Paw if it's long term issue with the gun itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would I spend Reach to make the spell endure until its needed or is the duration factor based on how long the spell effect (in this case the gun jamming) itself lasts? So is it advanced duration to make it last about a day because I anticipate violence with the holder of the gun at some point (lets say its a hostage situation) or is it instant (standard) duration because the gun is only being jammed the next time its fired rather than the gun being made totally inoperable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:14:26-07:00","id":893796,"title":"","content":"This might have already been answered, but why are Sever Soul and Sever the Awakened Soul different practices? I'm assuming that the former is either fraying or weaving and the later is unmaking. Why aren't they the same but maybe separated by requiring reach for an awakened soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:20:29-07:00","id":893800,"title":"","content":"I have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:28:00-07:00","id":893807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flux</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893796#post893796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have already been answered, but why are Sever Soul and Sever the Awakened Soul different practices? I'm assuming that the former is either fraying or weaving and the later is unmaking. Why aren't they the same but maybe separated by requiring reach for an awakened soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably there is something qualitatively different about an Awakened Soul that makes a difference... but yeah, now that you mention it why wouldn't that just be due to Reach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T01:10:13-07:00","id":893891,"title":"","content":"I try to ask also here cause we are going to play a little crossover game tomorrow night and we need to know - do the tilts caused by an hex heal with supernatural regeneration? Like arm wreck or leg wreck blind ecc.. by RAW they shouldn't cause u can solve the tilt only by healing the associated damage that caused it. If that's the case that means that a mage spending mana a vampire spending blood.points and a werewolf in war form regenerating all damage each turn won't free himself from my curse for the duration of my spell. Pretty scary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T01:29:11-07:00","id":893901,"title":"","content":"I will say yes: counter example.<br /> An Obrimos cast nightvision on herself: a vicious stryx, materialized , torn her eyes away.<br /> She is blinded BUT with darkvision? I will say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:19:21-07:00","id":893914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893807#post893807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably there is something qualitatively different about an Awakened Soul that makes a difference... but yeah, now that you mention it why wouldn't that just be due to Reach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason destroting a connected sympathetic connection requires Unmaking.<br /> <br /> Mages have their Gnosis clinging onto and into their souls, which a Reaper has to pry loose. Sleepers don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:20:49-07:00","id":893915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893891#post893891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I try to ask also here cause we are going to play a little crossover game tomorrow night and we need to know - do the tilts caused by an hex heal with supernatural regeneration? Like arm wreck or leg wreck blind ecc.. by RAW they shouldn't cause u can solve the tilt only by healing the associated damage that caused it. If that's the case that means that a mage spending mana a vampire spending blood.points and a werewolf in war form regenerating all damage each turn won't free himself from my curse for the duration of my spell. Pretty scary</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes, as a hex works by misfortune. If Fate twists to make you trip and break your leg, you should still be able to regenerate it if you're a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T03:16:45-07:00","id":893933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893915#post893915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say yes, as a hex works by misfortune. If Fate twists to make you trip and break your leg, you should still be able to regenerate it if you're a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much I was thinking the same but coming from u dave I now have the certainty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> appreciate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T04:15:37-07:00","id":893937,"title":"","content":"<b>Q: </b>About spell stacking. Lets say that i boosted my Socialize skill with mind magic by 2. If i add a spell from faith magic with potency 1 do i have Socialize bosted by 3 or? One spell is making me clever while other makes me lucky in choosing topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:21:48-07:00","id":894030,"title":"","content":"Okay so here's a weird question. If I use Ground-Eater, I presume my momentum remains unchanged even though I am going faster, because it bypasses the usual newtonian mechanics. But what if someone casts it on someone or something that is on a moving vehicle, the vehicle NOT being the subject of Ground-Eater? How will that interact with the vehicle? Let's say I want to mess with someone and put Ground-Eater on them so that they're moving slow, but then they get into a car. Does the car move them with no attention to something like Ground-Eater, or does the person riding the car continue to move slightly less space than the car, causing them to press uncomfortably into the back of the seat?<br /> <br /> And if not, would a Weaving/Fraying version of Ground-Eater cause this problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:58:48-07:00","id":894058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=893937#post893937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: </b>About spell stacking. Lets say that i boosted my Socialize skill with mind magic by 2. If i add a spell from faith magic with potency 1 do i have Socialize bosted by 3 or? One spell is making me clever while other makes me lucky in choosing topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have two extra dots in the Skill and a +1 bonus to Socialize rolls, which is not the same thing as have three extra dots in the Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:52:54-07:00","id":894116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=894058#post894058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have two extra dots in the Skill and a +1 bonus to Socialize rolls, which is not the same thing as have three extra dots in the Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while mind gives me temporary Skill dots fate grants me a bonus to Socialize roll(its always suposed to be a condition?) which is in my opinion the same thing but avoids stacking.<br /> We have attribute, skill and a bonuses. <br /> <br /> Is casting Life spell to boost muscle Strength +1 and second Life spell that gives me a +1 bonus to Strength roll a correct formula?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:29:25-07:00","id":894148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=894030#post894030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so here's a weird question. If I use Ground-Eater, I presume my momentum remains unchanged even though I am going faster, because it bypasses the usual newtonian mechanics. But what if someone casts it on someone or something that is on a moving vehicle, the vehicle NOT being the subject of Ground-Eater? How will that interact with the vehicle? Let's say I want to mess with someone and put Ground-Eater on them so that they're moving slow, but then they get into a car. Does the car move them with no attention to something like Ground-Eater, or does the person riding the car continue to move slightly less space than the car, causing them to press uncomfortably into the back of the seat?<br /> <br /> And if not, would a Weaving/Fraying version of Ground-Eater cause this problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the simplest way to rule it would be that since they're not moving under their own power they're unaffected. That assumes they're not the ones operating the vehicle. Imagine how small the spatial tweak would need to be for their foot to hit the gas instead of the brakes. So I'd consider penalizing their Drive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:47:04-07:00","id":894163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=894148#post894148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the simplest way to rule it would be that since they're not moving under their own power they're unaffected. That assumes they're not the ones operating the vehicle. Imagine how small the spatial tweak would need to be for their foot to hit the gas instead of the brakes. So I'd consider penalizing their Drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>wow, thank you! that's a really good answer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:06:53-07:00","id":894261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=894116#post894116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So while mind gives me temporary Skill dots fate grants me a bonus to Socialize roll(its always suposed to be a condition?) which is in my opinion the same thing but avoids stacking.<br /> We have attribute, skill and a bonuses.<br /> <br /> Is casting Life spell to boost muscle Strength +1 and second Life spell that gives me a +1 bonus to Strength roll a correct formula?</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't the same thing though, for example, when doing an extended action, your number of attempts is based on your unmodified dice pool (Attribute + Skill) so the + 2 dots would count, while the +1 bonus die would not. It would come into play when making the actual rolls though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:11:08-07:00","id":894307,"title":"","content":"My group is considering treating zero successes on the wisdom roll for containing paradox as a released paradox. The downsides to containing don't seem to have enough teeth otherwise. Is there anything we should consider before making this change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:15:30-07:00","id":894549,"title":"","content":"According to Dark Eras:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p58</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pangaeans can delve into the Oneiros of individual humans by first entering the Temenos then finding their way to the target <b>in the same way that Awakened can.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The nearest thing to this that I can find in Mage 2e Core is the &quot;tenuous bridge made of shared thoughts&quot; described on p247, which is explicitly complicated by things sufficiently well-known to involve the Temenos. What am I missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:17:08-07:00","id":895096,"title":"","content":"Okay, Second Edition question:<br /> <br /> The Time 2 Attainment Temporal Sympathy has strange language.<br /> <br /> Can anyone give me an example of how it is used? Why would I need to cast a spell on a subject in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:33:50-07:00","id":895114,"title":"","content":"To affect the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:46:53-07:00","id":895131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895114#post895114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To affect the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems strange that they just throw that ability out there without much more on how it works or what the ramifications are. And why only the Past and not the Future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:48:08-07:00","id":895133,"title":"","content":"You know that a monster is going to get you through that door, so you use your magic to lock it in the past so he never got to you. Your friend is going to be killed, so you send a SMS to the past telling him that you really need him to go buy you some groceries so he won't run into a psychokiller in the dark alley. You want to give past-you some hints, so you write in a notebook some clues for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:00:07-07:00","id":895145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895133#post895133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that a monster is going to get you through that door, so you use your magic to lock it in the past so he never got to you. Your friend is going to be killed, so you send a SMS to the past telling him that you really need him to go buy you some groceries so he won't run into a psychokiller in the dark alley. You want to give past-you some hints, so you write in a notebook some clues for yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like that opens up the possibility to be more annoying than Shifting Sands, though. I mean, I totally love the idea of the Bill &amp; Ted &quot;My dad lost keys -- no, we stole them and hid them right here moment&quot; but I don't think that was the intention of the authors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:11:18-07:00","id":895158,"title":"","content":"...Time Magic allowing you to affect past not being the intention of the authors???? I'm not sure what do you mean, because I don't know Bill &amp; Ted so maybe I'm missing some reference.<br /> We didn't try it out yet, but Time Magic seems to be balanced by the fact that you need to have fuckaton of Factors to make it work. You need both a lot of Potency to pierce Withstand(s), and a lot of Duration to actually make changes last enough to &quot;stay&quot;. This probably means that a lot of annoying TimeAbuses is not possible or realistic simply due to Spell Factors restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-20-2016, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T18:48:44-07:00","id":895211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895131#post895131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems strange that they just throw that ability out there without much more on how it works or what the ramifications are. And why only the Past and not the Future?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can affect the future, that's what Divination, Prophecy and the like are for. <br /> <br /> For how to handle the ramifications though look at the section of the book that talks about narrative effects of spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:23:18-07:00","id":895231,"title":"","content":"Question about Matter's Ruling practice. Fairly easy to get things to do stuff they wouldn't normally do, yeah? Water flowing up walls, shaping wood into splintery ineffective tools, making household objects do all sorts of poltergeisty things... So I'm assuming you can get a rug to float into the air.<br /> <br /> Can you ride the rug while floating it with Ruling?<br /> Can I be the necromancer that can show you the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T21:24:14-07:00","id":895281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895158#post895158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what do you mean, because I don't know Bill &amp; Ted so maybe I'm missing some reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Bill &amp; Ted's Excellent Adventure, Bill and Ted must rescue their friend from jail, but have no idea how they'd be able to do that. Since they have a time machine, they propose that after their adventure is over, they'll get the jail key, travel back in time, and place it behind the bush that Bill is pointing to. They then inspect the bush, and find the key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T13:14:22-07:00","id":895656,"title":"","content":"With the spell Deny the Reaper, are the healing effects lasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T13:49:37-07:00","id":895669,"title":"","content":"Why is the Gauntlet stronger in urban areas when there are just as many or even more spirits in cities than there are in the wilderness? It isn't like oWoD where you can blame Consensus or the Weaver for it, and it seems silly to handicap urban Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Do Death spells to interact with ghosts worry about the Gauntlet at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-21-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T14:25:37-07:00","id":895681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895669#post895669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Gauntlet stronger in urban areas when there are just as many or even more spirits in cities than there are in the wilderness? It isn't like oWoD where you can blame Consensus or the Weaver for it, and it seems silly to handicap urban Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Do Death spells to interact with ghosts worry about the Gauntlet at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gauntlet is only relevant to the Shadow Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T15:34:52-07:00","id":895709,"title":"","content":"Teleportation (Space 4) has a Primary Spell Factor of Potency. What exactly does this Potency correspond to, number of targets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T15:38:56-07:00","id":895712,"title":"","content":"That would be Scale. I'm not a Space Buff, but I think it was either mislabeled, or it's used to pierce Sympathetic Withstand rating of a place/thing you are teleporting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T16:08:54-07:00","id":895727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895669#post895669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Gauntlet stronger in urban areas when there are just as many or even more spirits in cities than there are in the wilderness? It isn't like oWoD where you can blame Consensus or the Weaver for it, and it seems silly to handicap urban Thyrsus.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is not mage exclusive. The actual mechanics and descriptions of the 'physics' of the place are from Forsaken and the Book of Spirits.<br /> <br /> If I remember right, Forsaken 2e basically explained it that humans produce a huge amount of essence and that churns the gauntlet up making it harder to cross through. I'd infer that it's not actually thicker, that's just what it feels like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T16:20:22-07:00","id":895732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895709#post895709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleportation (Space 4) has a Primary Spell Factor of Potency. What exactly does this Potency correspond to, number of targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>As WHW said, it is because of withstand. Teleportation needs to over come withstand (often of sypethetic cause) to suceed so that is why potency is the primary spell factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T16:30:21-07:00","id":895736,"title":"","content":"Uh, how do I play with Exceptional Luck and Hexes in general without them being totally bonkers? Tilts you get to impose are pretty mean; game mentions that they last until Duration is over (which can be quite easily buffed to &quot;A Scene&quot; with Reach) or until the subject resolves the Tilt, but...how are they supposed to resolve it? Should I assume it's a Looney Tunes type of tilt where I don't know, someone get's their leg caught in a chair and all it takes to resolve the Tilt is to smash the chair or something? Exceptional Luck is Reflexive, and this means you can shutdown opponents - even Mages - without giving them a chance to make their move. <br /> <br /> Also...<br /> I cast a Hex that inflicts Sick and Poisoned on my opponent. That opponent is Gravely Misfortune. I assume both tilts &quot;tick&quot; the Grave Misfortune?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T17:32:06-07:00","id":895764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895231#post895231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Matter's Ruling practice. Fairly easy to get things to do stuff they wouldn't normally do, yeah? Water flowing up walls, shaping wood into splintery ineffective tools, making household objects do all sorts of poltergeisty things... So I'm assuming you can get a rug to float into the air.<br /> <br /> Can you ride the rug while floating it with Ruling?<br /> Can I be the necromancer that can show you the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895709#post895709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleportation (Space 4) has a Primary Spell Factor of Potency. What exactly does this Potency correspond to, number of targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>To overcome Sympathetic Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T18:19:41-07:00","id":895787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895669#post895669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Gauntlet stronger in urban areas when there are just as many or even more spirits in cities than there are in the wilderness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that the Shadow is not a Mage-exclusive dimension, regions of collective human presence (and other less-known factors) tend to thicken the Gauntlet regardless of what the terrain is like. It has no impact on Essence-generation outside the context of deliberate harvesting; urban spirits still get their daily point from proximity to suitable Resonance and Loci still operate as wellsprings and easy crossing-points.<br /> <br /> It seems silly to call it a handicap just because places where you're more likely to run into people are also places where you're incentivized to make use of places of power or go the long way when trucking with Spirit in cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T01:26:08-07:00","id":895983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895709#post895709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleportation (Space 4) has a Primary Spell Factor of Potency. What exactly does this Potency correspond to, number of targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's almost always Withstood by sympathy, and while you could maybe think of a way to use teleport with a long duration, it doesn't exactly scream primary factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T05:37:50-07:00","id":896026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flux</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=895656#post895656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the spell Deny the Reaper, are the healing effects lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that question. But based on spells like Cut Threads and Create Sympathy, it should be Lasting, because it has Potency as its Primary Factor. Any spells that can be dispelled usually have Duration as Primary, while those where the Duration isn't needed have Potency. It's just not spelled out loud in this case.<br /> <br /> Besides, a spell that does what Deny the Reaper does, and that would not be Lasting immediately makes one think of Duration, and not the number of months of damage you can erase. Also, if you want to eliminate a grave injury as a mage, it probably is a recent one anyway. Who would wait/could not find a Master for months, before healing themselves anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:03:10-07:00","id":896040,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Reach option mentions that it end's when Duration runs out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T07:00:07-07:00","id":896064,"title":"","content":"Chaos Mastery is dumb. Fate has probably worst spell-writing in the entire game. It's not a single spell, it's Fate+Potency of different Spells that can be activated reflexively (which means you can unleash multiple of them at once, as there is no RESTRICTION ON HOW MANY YOU CAN UNLEASH AT ONCE). There are so many problems with this spell that I can't even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T07:20:36-07:00","id":896071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=896040#post896040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Reach option mentions that it end's when Duration runs out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Reach options often modify the spell well beyond what it was doing originally. Like the Lasting effect of Create Sympathy can instead with Reach become at most Indefinite spell that gives you a new Sympathetic Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T08:22:52-07:00","id":896097,"title":"","content":"So, just so I understand, since Veiling magic like Cloak Nimbus makes active perception go to Clash of Wills, and because mages always know when their spells are clashing, the best one can hope for in a situation like Supernal Vision vs Cloak Nimbus is that the person using active perception spells know that -something- is wrong, but not quite what? <br /> <br /> Does &quot;a mage always knows when his spells are clashing&quot; apply to Active Mage Sight, or is this an advantage of revelatory spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:39:23-07:00","id":896115,"title":"","content":"A stupid thing that bugs me: what would be names of the Arcana in Japanese (preferably romanised) ?. I tried google translate but it gives a few results for somes and I don't know which would work best. Just out of curiosity.<br /> <br /> @Deny the Reaper: I would make the healing effect lasting If only to prevent it from being a worse Temporal summoning. But it also makes sense with the spell and that's how other healing spells work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 05-22-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:46:05-07:00","id":896119,"title":"","content":"How much influence the Life 2 spell Control Instincts can have on humans?<br /> <br /> Can it put a person to sleep or just make him or her sleepy? Or not even that?<br /> <br /> I suppose it can induce thirsty (since it can induce hungry) and maybe sexual desire (?).<br /> <br /> Can it make someone have goosebumps or start sweating as he or she were in a cold or hot environment?<br /> <br /> Can it make someone run in fear or just induce an adrenaline rush (and the response is up the person affected)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11809-vilevader","name":"Vilevader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:17:15-07:00","id":896139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=896115#post896115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A stupid thing that bugs me: what would be names of the Arcana in Japanese (preferably romanised) ?. I tried google translate but it gives a few results for somes and I don't know which would work best. Just out of curiosity.<br /> <br /> @Deny the Reaper: I would make the healing effect lasting If only to prevent it from being a worse Temporal summoning. But it also makes sense with the spell and that's how other healing spells work.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u6642\u7a7a Jikuu : generally it means a concept of time-space<br /> \u56e0\u7e01 Innen: direct cause and indirect conditions which underlie the actions of all things (buddhist term)<br /> \u7cbe\u795e Seishin\uff1a mind, soul, heart, spirit<br /> \u7a7a\u9593\uff1a Kuukan: void+space, how cool is that :P<br /> \u6b7b Shi: death. plain and simple<br /> \u7269\u8cea Busshitsu: material, substance<br /> \u751f\u6c17: Seiki: life, vitality, vigor<br /> \u795e\u660e: Shinmyou: spirits of heaven and earth (term from Shinto, meaning all kinds of lesser and greater gods)<br /> \u7406\u5ff5: Rinen: (platonic) ideal, how things ought to be, foundational principle, idea, conception (characters: logic/reason/justice+idea/thought)<br /> \u529b\uff1a Chikara: force, energy \uff08character used in contexts like electric power and such)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-22-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:24:59-07:00","id":896143,"title":"","content":"So Seishin covers both Mind and Spirit and you have to use context to figure out which is meant? That sounds about right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:28:09-07:00","id":896145,"title":"","content":"Nah, Spirit would be Shinmyou. I missed it in the initial post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:42:43-07:00","id":896152,"title":"","content":"Cool. Although considering how conflated the meaning of Ki is I wouldn't be surprised if Japanese Mages did that with other magically oriented words as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:44:32-07:00","id":896195,"title":"","content":"Bonus content from my players, who decided that they had fun with the &quot;Arcana in Japanese&quot; request; this time, it's Chinese. <br /> \u65f6\u95f4\uff1a Sh\u00edji\u0101n, the concept of time<br /> \u56e0\u679c\uff1a Y\u012bngu\u01d2: cause and effect, karma (buddhism)<br /> \u7cbe\u795e\uff1a J\u012bngsh\u00e9n: mind, conciousness, mental<br /> \u7a7a\u95f4\uff1a K\u014dngji\u0101n: void+space<br /> \u6b7b\u4ea1\uff1a S\u01d0w\u00e1ng: death+perish<br /> \u7269\u8d28\uff1a W\u00f9zh\u00ed: matter, substance<br /> \u7406\u60f3\uff1a L\u01d0xi\u01ceng: ideal<br /> \u529b\uff1a L\u00ec: force, power<br /> \u751f\u610f: Sh\u0113ngy\u00ec: life and vitality<br /> \u795e\u602a\uff1a Sh\u00e9ngu\u00e0i: spirits and devils (name for all spiritual beings)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T15:36:37-07:00","id":896351,"title":"","content":"Could you inscribe a rote on skin like a tattoo with scribe grimoire as it is a surface that can be written upon with just scribe grimoire or should it need a level of life arcana in this usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T15:46:26-07:00","id":896358,"title":"","content":"I think Prime is enough. As far as I understand new Arcana, Life would only get involved if you wanted to make the Rote form in the DNA or modify a specimen to manifest the Rote in it's fur pattern or something crazy like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T15:52:32-07:00","id":896361,"title":"","content":"Page 71 of the 2nd Edition: Unless I missed something, shouldn't the Convocation that Silver Ladder wants to organize be Grand, not Great? This should probably belong to errata, but since the thread is closed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:18:29-07:00","id":896371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=896358#post896358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Prime is enough. As far as I understand new Arcana, Life would only get involved if you wanted to make the Rote form in the DNA or modify a specimen to manifest the Rote in it's fur pattern or something crazy like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of writing a rote in dna is interesting to say the least. How one would read it is an interesting thought as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:51:39-07:00","id":896390,"title":"","content":"So, I have a firearm worth 5 dots of availability. Anyone willing to cook me something up? It should be a handgun with STR requirement of no more than 2, semi-automatic. It's not an Enchanted Item, so it's special qualities shouldn't be magical, but can be a product of magical gunsmithing. I remember that Hurt Locker spoilers had some rules about upgrading items based on their cost...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T18:09:38-07:00","id":896427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=896361#post896361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 71 of the 2nd Edition: Unless I missed something, shouldn't the Convocation that Silver Ladder wants to organize be Grand, not Great? This should probably belong to errata, but since the thread is closed...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Send a private message to Dave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T04:32:05-07:00","id":896681,"title":"","content":"Could the &quot;transform life&quot; spell cover bringing supernatural traits to a creature?<br /> <br /> From how it is written one could interpret that it can because other creatures exist with these traits but another way of reading it is that you can only mimic mundane traits. Based on the examples given it also does seem to be more in line with the later interpretation. <br /> <br /> What I'm wanting is to kind of get a mix of Transform life and the crypid creation from demon so I can have a mad scientist like mage who replicates myths and legends. I'm just uncertain if transform life would function in a way that could manifest supernatural traits and be the solution. If it cant then i am uncertain of what spell practice and arcana that'd fall under.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:38:42-07:00","id":896803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=896681#post896681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the &quot;transform life&quot; spell cover bringing supernatural traits to a creature?<br /> <br /> From how it is written one could interpret that it can because other creatures exist with these traits but another way of reading it is that you can only mimic mundane traits. Based on the examples given it also does seem to be more in line with the later interpretation.<br /> <br /> What I'm wanting is to kind of get a mix of Transform life and the crypid creation from demon so I can have a mad scientist like mage who replicates myths and legends. I'm just uncertain if transform life would function in a way that could manifest supernatural traits and be the solution. If it cant then i am uncertain of what spell practice and arcana that'd fall under.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the actual way you do this is with archmastery, but the other way you do this is probably by adding other arcana to infuse the thing with powers--course, any number of those will be spells that can be dispelled, wear off, may require mana that need to be infused in the creature, etc etc. With magic you can do all sorts of crazy things, but the crazier it is the more dots in other arcana you might need to balance things out, like a fire breathing dragon probably needs a force spell combined in (not as just conjunctional arcana, but a separate, triggerable spell), and I'm not sure but I'm sure a few people would need you to have Prime 4 so you could &quot;imbue&quot; a living thing with these spells.<br /> <br /> But the easy way is archmastery, cuz one of archmastery spells is literally &quot;mess with a supernatural template.&quot; You could literally add and remove facets of a supernatural template using those, its weird! They kinda almost don't truly count as spells either, at that point they're more like attainments or features of a supernatural template--they're lasting and are considered natural. Archmages are way powerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I have another question myself now. How does Dispellation work if you have multiple subjects in a single spell and they are spread out? Like say you cast a +2 strength spell on your cabal and then everyone spreads out over the city, then an Obrimos tries to dispel the +2 strength on the one person they see. Is only the one instance of the spell removed or are all instances of the spell removed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-23-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:30:29-07:00","id":897006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=896681#post896681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the &quot;transform life&quot; spell cover bringing supernatural traits to a creature?<br /> <br /> From how it is written one could interpret that it can because other creatures exist with these traits but another way of reading it is that you can only mimic mundane traits. Based on the examples given it also does seem to be more in line with the later interpretation.<br /> <br /> What I'm wanting is to kind of get a mix of Transform life and the crypid creation from demon so I can have a mad scientist like mage who replicates myths and legends. I'm just uncertain if transform life would function in a way that could manifest supernatural traits and be the solution. If it cant then i am uncertain of what spell practice and arcana that'd fall under.</div> </div> </div> </div>See Wonderful Machine, p157-8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:33:42-07:00","id":897010,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> that could be an interesting mix with transform life, thank you I hadn't concidered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:56:15-07:00","id":897149,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So I have a question about demesnes! &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Furthermore, as long as a spell that<span style=\"color:#000000\"> qualifies for the bonus doesn\u2019t leave the Verge, it doesn\u2019t risk<span style=\"color:#000000\"> Paradox unless a Sleeper is present at some point during the<span style=\"color:#000000\"> spell\u2019s duration.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think I understand this. There was also a section that said that spells were paradox-free if they didn't leave the verge, or I think it was that spells in your onieros are paradox free if they do not leave your onieros.<br /> <br /> This is really weird because paradoxes are supposed to occur during casting right? Not after the fact. Why would these spells suddenly cause paradox when the spell leaves those areas, but when in a normal situation if a sleeper finds a spell laying around after it was cast, it only causes dissonance and rips the spell apart?<br /> Is this actually an errata maybe? Maybe it meant causes paradox during casting and not duration, or it meant to say dissonance instead of paradox...<br /> <br /> So is the idea that the spells have more power inside a demense/verge/onieros, but then they become even more vulnerable than normal spells outside of them when chanced upon by sleepers because they're supernally charged or something? Or are these errors?<br /> <br /> Like, is a spell paradox free if it doesn't leave the demense supposed to mean &quot;scale doesn't leave demense?&quot; Or does it mean that if I make a luminescent duck and carry it with me out of my demesne then someone sees it it causes a paradox instead of dissonance and then everything's bad?</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:29:29-07:00","id":897190,"title":"","content":"I think that might be cause for errata. Or they mean that the spell is vulnerable to Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T15:25:30-07:00","id":897256,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Dave answered this one somewhere, they're just subject to Dissonance unless Paradox is a concern because of circumstances as usual in a way that the Demesne doesn't supersede.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:54:59-07:00","id":897391,"title":"","content":"I think it means that if you are targeting something outside of the Verge, it will risk Paradox. So it prevents paradox free sympathetic or remote view castings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:07:09-07:00","id":897395,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> He answered it in a thread when I pointed it out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/896101-paradox-persistant-spells-the-psychotic-and-psychonautics\">here</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not sure if it was mentioned at any other point.<br /> <br /> From what I can now gather from his statement, paradox's are supposed to occur during the casting, not at any other point.<br /> <br /> Besides that, they haven't embellished on what it was meant to mean, but using 1.0 as a reference I imagine that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2813_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2813\" data-vbnamecard=\"2813\">Freemind</a> is correct, as it simply used to be that spells cast in a demesne could not be sympathetically cast and remain paradox free. I'm also presuming that the reference to sleepers is meant to refer to them being present at any point during the spells casting. Again, not a hundred percent sure but that's what I'm thinking at this point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:24:34-07:00","id":897464,"title":"","content":"So, I have a dumb question, bear with me...<br /> <br /> I want to use Locate Object to find an object that I can't actually see or know where it is, as often is the case. Do I have to cast it at sympathetic range to do so? I mean, I can't touch it to target it. I might be able to use an Aimed spell to center Locate Object's area from a certain point, but I'm still not sure if that works. I -might- be able to use sensory since I'm theoretically in range to sense it, but I am not already doing so directly, so maybe that's out. So, I might have to use Locate Object sympathetically in order to use it on something I can't see, but if I do so, I assume the range for Locate Object centers around the lost object...so that's out I guess?<br /> <br /> I think I'm overthinking this, but I'm trying to figure out the rules as written in cases like this so no nasty surprises pop up. Someone help me figure out how to find my car keys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:36:18-07:00","id":897477,"title":"","content":"It has to be inside the area of the spell when you cast it to be able to find it, if it's outside that area then I'd say you have to cast Sympathetically. The spell doesn't appear to require being able to see the object though, and that makes sense since what you're doing is targeting yourself with a Knowing effect with limited range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:12:38-07:00","id":897512,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you -are- targeting yourself. A specific thing is the subject of the spell, which makes it useful for casting on an object and using it as a tracking device with the Reach option, but I'm still not 100% sure how the basic effect works for lost, unseen things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:23:47-07:00","id":897519,"title":"","content":"Knowing spells generally target the recipient even if they are trying to know about something else, it's just that what is known in this case appears to require you covering an area of possible things whose locations could be known in. If the thing isn't in the area the spell essentially fizzles, but casting Sympathetically effectively changes the scale to infinity in regards to the one thing whose location you wish to know about.<br /> <br /> That's how I'd run it anyway, though I agree it could stand to be clearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:40:28-07:00","id":899579,"title":"","content":"Are items pulled out of Twilight good enough as a +3 Sacrament Yantra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:00:27-07:00","id":899643,"title":"","content":"Depends on the item probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:14:32-07:00","id":899650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=899579#post899579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are items pulled out of Twilight good enough as a +3 Sacrament Yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since twilight is technically apart of the material realm it may only count for the +2 since it is not truly a seperate realm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:51:16-07:00","id":899865,"title":"","content":"How do I determine Potency for spells in Enhanced Items?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T02:35:06-07:00","id":899882,"title":"","content":"I would go with the minimum Potency required for the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:13:29-07:00","id":900434,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Twilight would be probably too easy. I guess it should be Underworld, Shadow and Astral World (and other, but these 3 are easiest to get into).<br /> <br /> Ok, what happens:<br /> 1. I see someone.<br /> 2. I cast Shadow Crafting targeted above their head.<br /> 3. I assign Advanced Scale to the spell and, like, 3 or 4 spell factors to it.<br /> 4. I create Shadow Spikes or some other dangerous item that has bad synergy with people on which it falls.<br /> 5. I let it fall.<br /> <br /> ???????","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:43:12-07:00","id":900539,"title":"","content":"Can magic create a synthetic soul? I know it is a debated topic but I'm wondering if there is a solution to restoring your soul other than stealing another's or retrievin what you gave lost. <br /> <br /> Though death deals with matters of the soul I feel that death 5 probably wouldn't be enough to create a synthetic soul","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:45:17-07:00","id":900541,"title":"","content":"It's specifically stated that you cannot create soul without going into Archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:20:41-07:00","id":900563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=900541#post900541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's specifically stated that you cannot create soul without going into Archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn't seen that. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:29:03-07:00","id":900847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=899882#post899882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go with the minimum Potency required for the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's because one of my players, an Obrimos of the Weret-Hekau, following the Omphalos school, lost an arm battling a creature of the Abyss as part of his backstory, and wants to have a golem-arm to replace the one he lost, made with a Matter 4 and Mind 2 conjunctional spell as according to the spells: Golem and Telepathy so he can give it orders with his mind.<br /> <br /> This golem would, have a Potency of 1, meaning that he would roll 2 dice whenever he would use this arm, which is kind of sad. So I was wondering if, saying that a character has (Dot rating of Enhanced Item/2, rounded up and unable to exceed five) would be fair?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind, I realised that if we use the Retainer rating as an Attribute rating, it'd work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:25:32-07:00","id":901547,"title":"","content":"How does withstand work for counterspell?<br /> <br /> In the withstand section it says it applies the arcana as withstand to counterspelling but withstand reduces potency which the counterspell attainment doesn't seem to need. By the counterspell attainment it also looks to simply be a clash of will contested roll so withstand wouldn't factor in.<br /> <br /> Didn't notice this in the errata or FAQ appoligies if I missed it there however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:27:35-07:00","id":901550,"title":"","content":"Counterspell doesn't care about Withstand. Dude A wants to cast a spell, you sacrifice your action if you have one available to Coutnerspell. You both go into a Clash of Will. If you win, spell is countered. Maybe you misread Dispellation for counterspelling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:32:17-07:00","id":901556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=901550#post901550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterspell doesn't care about Withstand. Dude A wants to cast a spell, you sacrifice your action if you have one available to Coutnerspell. You both go into a Clash of Will. If you win, spell is countered. Maybe you misread Dispellation for counterspelling?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...but spells themselves Withstand dispella-tion using the Arcanum rating of the caster\u2019s highest Arcanum used in the spell...&quot; pg 114<br /> <br /> Is the reason for my confusion since it doesn't line up with the rules for counterspelling.<br /> <br /> Edit: unless Dispellation is a different thing entirely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:35:55-07:00","id":901559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=900539#post900539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can magic create a synthetic soul? I know it is a debated topic but I'm wondering if there is a solution to restoring your soul other than stealing another's or retrievin what you gave lost.<br /> <br /> Though death deals with matters of the soul I feel that death 5 probably wouldn't be enough to create a synthetic soul</div> </div> </div> </div>The book has a sidebar on this topic. It says that to attempt to create a soul would require Mastery of all five subtle arcana, and that of the very few masters skilled and willing enough to attempt it, none succeded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:41:26-07:00","id":901569,"title":"","content":"Check out 1st dot Prime spell &quot;Dispel Magic&quot;. What you quoted refers to dispelling spells, which is done using Dispel Magic or Supernal Dispellation Spell.<br /> <br /> How would people imagine dispelling magic using Death? I remember it was possible in 1st edition, and it fits thematically a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:42:22-07:00","id":901570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=901556#post901556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;...but spells themselves Withstand dispella-tion using the Arcanum rating of the caster\u2019s highest Arcanum used in the spell...&quot; pg 114<br /> <br /> Is the reason for my confusion since it doesn't line up with the rules for counterspelling.<br /> <br /> Edit: unless Dispellation is a different thing entirely</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterspelling stops a spell as it is being cast. Dispellation is removing the spell after it has already taken effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:48:19-07:00","id":901577,"title":"","content":"@WHW <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar168_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"168\" data-vbnamecard=\"168\">Aiden</a> I was thinking that counterspell was used even after a spell had been cast not as a reaction to a spell being cast. Thank you both for clearing that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:24:06-07:00","id":901608,"title":"","content":"So obviously summoning things from the astral is Mind, and Goetia can be given manifestation with Death or Spirit.<br /> <br /> But what if you want to summon items and objects from the astral? Would it still be Death of Spirit? Or should it be Matter? <br /> <br /> Could Matter even create some items, like a star fighter from star wars? Would it not be allowed because Matter can't normally do it, or would it just be giving form to a concept and get around that rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:48:58-07:00","id":901619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=901569#post901569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would people imagine dispelling magic using Death? I remember it was possible in 1st edition, and it fits thematically a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was weird that Dispellation talked about how all spells have a capacity to end (A very Death thing to say), and that Dispellation takes advantage of that. I'd run the Death version as pretty much exactly the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=901608#post901608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So obviously summoning things from the astral is Mind, and Goetia can be given manifestation with Death or Spirit.<br /> <br /> But what if you want to summon items and objects from the astral? Would it still be Death of Spirit? Or should it be Matter?<br /> <br /> Could Matter even create some items, like a star fighter from star wars? Would it not be allowed because Matter can't normally do it, or would it just be giving form to a concept and get around that rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default objects from the Astral would also appear in Twilight, but you could probably combine them with Death or Spirit to give them a &quot;Manifestation&quot; and you could certainly use Matter to make them a Mind+Matter hybrid in much the same way that Life+Forces can turn you into a living being of flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-27-2016, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:58:42-07:00","id":901628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=901619#post901619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was weird that Dispellation talked about how all spells have a capacity to end (A very Death thing to say), and that Dispellation takes advantage of that. I'd run the Death version as pretty much exactly the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> By default objects from the Astral would also appear in Twilight, but you could probably combine them with Death or Spirit to give them a &quot;Manifestation&quot; and you could certainly use Matter to make them a Mind+Matter hybrid in much the same way that Life+Forces can turn you into a living being of flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright thanks.<br /> <br /> Edit: so I looked into Spirit 4 and found the spell that would do exactly what im looking for. So now I feel silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 05-27-2016, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:02:21-07:00","id":902145,"title":"","content":"Another question about mage.<br /> <br /> One option for Mana expenditure is to gain 1 success, so could that be used on a spell? How would this work for spells that are at a chance die? <br /> Or could a mage spend 5 mana to get a exceptional success and regain all the spent mana for the spell casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:10:15-07:00","id":902153,"title":"","content":"There isn't any option for spending mana to achieve a succes on a roll. Where did you find that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:23:40-07:00","id":902171,"title":"","content":"Thats for Scrutiny and Scrutiny only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T12:03:56-07:00","id":902202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902153#post902153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't any option for spending mana to achieve a succes on a roll. Where did you find that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I reread the section and I now understand I miss read the section (Pg. 125) and I realized that its was talking about spell options that would NEED mana to cast. Instead of an extra option for mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:01:30-07:00","id":902301,"title":"","content":"So, I have a question about Incognito Presence. In the text of the spell, it mentions that anyone wanting to focus on the subject under the effects of the spell or remember the subject must make a clash of wills. Then the reach option requires that the person/thing doing the clash must have a supernatural ability that specifically allows clash of wills. However, in order to do clash of wills in the first place, you have to have a supernatural ability. Does this mean that the spell automatically causes all sleepers and other &quot;muggles&quot; to completely ignore you, no chance of piercing your veil? Also, if so, what's the point of the reach option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:05:40-07:00","id":902304,"title":"","content":"I've read way to many spells at once. I know fate magic can give Boons, what spell do I need o use to grant the Charmed Condition? The boon section at the start says it can be done with spells but which spells? Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1510-mysticjackal","name":"MysticJackal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:15:06-07:00","id":902309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MysticJackal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902304#post902304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read way to many spells at once. I know fate magic can give Boons, what spell do I need o use to grant the Charmed Condition? The boon section at the start says it can be done with spells but which spells? Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under Boon pp 134<br /> Grant a number of beneficial Conditions (such as Charmed,<br /> Informed, Inspired, or Steadfast) equal to Potency for the<br /> Duration of the spell. None of these Conditions grant<br /> Beats when the subject resolves them (unless the caster<br /> achieved an exceptional success in the casting).<br /> <br /> Boon can be granted with exceptional luck","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:16:50-07:00","id":902311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MysticJackal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902304#post902304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read way to many spells at once. I know fate magic can give Boons, what spell do I need o use to grant the Charmed Condition? The boon section at the start says it can be done with spells but which spells? Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any spell that can grant a boon can create that condition. From the top of my head Exceptional Luck can do it and it's a reach effect on Monkeys paw..<br /> <br /> @Falcon777: The wording is somewhat poor.but. I'm sure that Sleepers aren't able to notice when u use the Reach effect but other than that I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:23:23-07:00","id":902348,"title":"","content":"A player of mine upon reading GotV's Masque came up with this idea of having 5 masques (at level 5) where each would have Status 5 in each Order.<br /> <br /> This doesn't seem wrong per the way rules were written but... is that ok? Has this been asked before?<br /> <br /> Thanks, folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:32:03-07:00","id":902355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902348#post902348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A player of mine upon reading GotV's Masque came up with this idea of having 5 masques (at level 5) where each would have Status 5 in each Order.<br /> <br /> This doesn't seem wrong per the way rules were written but... is that ok? Has this been asked before?<br /> <br /> Thanks, folks!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is allowed by the RAW, I think. But it also would be Damn hard, and may be a case where it doesn't make sense for the setting. But if it is okay for your story, go for it.<br /> <br /> Remember, the ChroD Golden Rule: The setting is what you, the ST, want it to be; their stuff is to offer you a base to make into whatever you wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-28-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:07:26-07:00","id":902376,"title":"","content":"Just double checking, but after chargen, Rotes cost 1xp -per dot- of the rating of the Rote, while Praxes are 1xp -total-, right?<br /> <br /> Edit: Except it clearly states in the Spellcasting thing that Rotes cost 1xp each. So, I guess they only have dot ratings during chargen? Well, darn. That was one thing I thought Praxes had over rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 05-28-2016, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:50:14-07:00","id":902398,"title":"","content":"Does the Lex Magicka merit's bonus to Doors and prevention of Willpower spending count in Duels Arcane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:51:53-07:00","id":902425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902376#post902376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just double checking, but after chargen, Rotes cost 1xp -per dot- of the rating of the Rote, while Praxes are 1xp -total-, right?<br /> <br /> Edit: Except it clearly states in the Spellcasting thing that Rotes cost 1xp each. So, I guess they only have dot ratings during chargen? Well, darn. That was one thing I thought Praxes had over rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is unclear. One section says one. The other says something different. To keep it consistent (as with other games, where now chargen is balanced to prevent the need to optomize, such as the old &quot;buy 3 in your inferior Arcana&quot; trick), my group goes with the XP per dot, and gives a refund if you form your own rote, minus the XP to create the rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:53:25-07:00","id":902456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902425#post902425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is unclear. One section says one. The other says something different. To keep it consistent (as with other games, where now chargen is balanced to prevent the need to optomize, such as the old &quot;buy 3 in your inferior Arcana&quot; trick), my group goes with the XP per dot, and gives a refund if you form your own rote, minus the XP to create the rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only charge my players 1 XP for a Rote or Praxes and allow them to purchase 6 Rotes at character creation. Rotes and Praxes are inherently more limited than a full arcana dot so I don't mind giving them the leg up. If I were going to change it then I'd just make it equal to half the arcana dots rounded down so most Rotes and Praxes would only cost 1 XP but 4th and 5th dot Rotes would cost 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T21:10:30-07:00","id":902474,"title":"","content":"Do Imbued and Enhanced Items you make yourself cost Experiences to make?<br /> <br /> Are Enhanced Items with spell effects on them made with the persistent effect of Imbue Item?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:32:10-07:00","id":902511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902456#post902456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I only charge my players 1 XP for a Rote or Praxes and allow them to purchase 6 Rotes at character creation. Rotes and Praxes are inherently more limited than a full arcana dot so I don't mind giving them the leg up. If I were going to change it then I'd just make it equal to half the arcana dots rounded down so most Rotes and Praxes would only cost 1 XP but 4th and 5th dot Rotes would cost 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that alternative.<br /> <br /> I use it to enforce the rote economy. Keeping Praxes at 1 XP regardless of level allows me to emphasize that a Praxes is personal and easier. Meanwhile, having a high level rote cost more reflects learning a possibly unfamiliar and codified system, where the more complex the spell (higher dots) the greater the time and understanding that needs to be dedicated.<br /> <br /> I have implemented a System to reduce the cost. Having a Grimoire with the Rote on hand or finding a Mentor reduced the cost by 1xp, and also having a Praxes of the same spell reduced it a further 1xp (minimum Rote cost is 1xp). That way players were rewarded for seeking out mentors, magical lore, etc., cause if a Master, they get a refund based on the max cost, not the actual price paid. So a Mage who formed a praxes, sought and found a willing mentor, and had a Grimoire who learned an adept Rote would pay 1xp and get back 3 (4xp as max cost, minus 1 for creating a Rote) if they ever created their own Rote. <br /> <br /> But like I said, I like yours too. Figured I would just explain my system a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:35:08-07:00","id":902512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902474#post902474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Imbued and Enhanced Items you make yourself cost Experiences to make?<br /> <br /> Are Enhanced Items with spell effects on them made with the persistent effect of Imbue Item?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the first, I don't require it. What I do make a point to my player is that without the XP expenditure, they have no protection of their time and resources if the item is lost somehow; no sanctity of Merits unless the XP is paid for. I do let them pay overtime though, and refund any invested if something happens before they finish paying their premium. I find this prevents wanton magic item creation.<br /> <br /> I am not quite sure what your second question is getting at. Are you asking how to make an enchanted item?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:45:10-07:00","id":902514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902512#post902512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not quite sure what your second question is getting at. Are you asking how to make an enchanted item?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am asking, given the following\u2026<br /> <br /> 1. The Imbued Item Merit makes reference to triggering an imbued item's activation<br /> 2. The Imbue Item Attainment makes reference to determining whether the imbued spell is contingent (i.e. activated by a trigger) or persistent (i.e. always active)<br /> 3. The Enhanced Item Merit makes reference to &quot;persistent Duration&quot; spells that permanently modify the item<br /> 4. The Enhanced Item Merit can explicitly be combined with the Imbued Item Merit<br /> <br /> \u2026 whether this means that using Imbue Item to imbue a persistent effect makes an Enhanced Item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:01:16-07:00","id":902522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902514#post902514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am asking, given the following\u2026<br /> <br /> 1. The Imbued Item Merit makes reference to triggering an imbued item's activation<br /> 2. The Imbue Item Attainment makes reference to determining whether the imbued spell is contingent (i.e. activated by a trigger) or persistent (i.e. always active)<br /> 3. The Enhanced Item Merit makes reference to &amp;quot;persistent Duration&amp;quot; spells that permanently modify the item<br /> 4. The Enhanced Item Merit can explicitly be combined with the Imbued Item Merit<br /> <br /> \u2026 whether this means that using Imbue Item to imbue a persistent effect makes an Enhanced Item.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, makes sense.<br /> <br /> Short answer is no, Imbued is not needed for enchanted.<br /> <br /> Imbued is only when you grant a magical effect to an item. For example, a persistent effect that causes anyone who slips a gold ring on to turn invisible would be imbued. Essentially, you have encoded a Supernal Imago that the item activates and it's effects alter some subject other than the item itself. This requires the imbuing attainment, as Prime let's that item trigger that effect as if it was casting.<br /> <br /> Enchanted items reflect a spell that alters an item but doesn't grant the item an ability to create its own magical effect. Think of enchanted as any spell that boosts the equipment or functionality of a spell, permanently. For example, apersistent effect that causes a gun to never jam due to being perfectly machined and impervious to wear and tear due to a Matter spell (or possibly fate) would be enchanting. The gun itself grants no powers and creates no effects, but it does have a permanent effect cast on it that makes it much more than an ordinary gun.<br /> <br /> Enchantment can be performed by any arcana, if the effect changes the item, doesn't grant it the ability to create its own effects, and is made indefinite or lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:02:19-07:00","id":902524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902522#post902522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer is no, Imbued is not needed for enchanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the opposite of what I asked.<br /> <br /> I am asking if <i>using the Attainment to make a persistent effect qualifies as an Enhanced Item rather than an Imbued Item</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-29-2016, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:11:05-07:00","id":902528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902524#post902524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the opposite of what I asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I misread it just after I hit send.<br /> <br /> My post still answers it. If it doesn't change the items properties beyond granting it the ability to create an effect, it is called an imbued item. Enhanced/enchanted refers to those with actual improvement of some aspect of the item.<br /> <br /> I guess you could argue being imbued improved the item to make it enhanced, as technically an indefinite effect has been cast in it. I wouldn't though, as a gold ring that grants invisibility still otherwise is a simple gold ring and would melt, break/bend or otherwise act as if any other gold ring. I also think you have them gotten into semantics, and it might confuse others as they don't understand which type of item you made. Unless the item was both enchanted to grant it itself different attributes, and then also was imbued to create an effect, Imbued would refer to Effect producing items, and enchanted would refer to attribute/quality improvement.<br /> <br /> Is that more what you Are asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:25:39-07:00","id":902535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902528#post902528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My post still answers it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It markedly does not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think you have them gotten into semantics, </div> </div> </div>An Imbued Item, per the Merit, has a triggered effect that costs Mana to use.<br /> <br /> A persistent effect is by definition not a triggered effect outside of the broadest of timescales.<br /> <br /> An Enhanced Item can contain spells in a manner near-identically described as Imbued Items and specifically has persistent effects.<br /> <br /> Imbue Item, per the Attainment, allows you to create items with persistent magical effects.<br /> <br /> Given the apparent disjunction between the Merit and the Attainment, the question of what an item imbued with a persistent effect is remains unanswered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:01:11-07:00","id":902547,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't giving the spell you imbue indefinate duration do what you want ?That way once you activate the item it's going to stay active for as long as you need ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:14:20-07:00","id":902654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=902535#post902535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It markedly does not.<br /> <br /> An Imbued Item, per the Merit, has a triggered effect that costs Mana to use.<br /> <br /> A persistent effect is by definition not a triggered effect outside of the broadest of timescales.<br /> <br /> An Enhanced Item can contain spells in a manner near-identically described as Imbued Items and specifically has persistent effects.<br /> <br /> Imbue Item, per the Attainment, allows you to create items with persistent magical effects.<br /> <br /> Given the apparent disjunction between the Merit and the Attainment, the question of what an item imbued with a persistent effect is remains unanswered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, 3am posts can be a bit iffy. I apologize for missing what you were getting at. I will take another stab; if I am off again I apologize.<br /> <br /> So, regarding enhanced, the merit specifically states:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Effect: Your character owns an item enhanced by persistent <br /> Duration spells, which <b>permanently modify the item\u2019s properties.</b> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. <br /> <br /> In other words, the point I was trying to make was that enhanced items refer specifically to items with indefinite spells that change the aspects of that item. Imbued items grant the ability to create a magical effect, but that is layered onto a mjnane item; besides the effect it can grant, there is no change to that items properties. <br /> <br /> So while the imbued item section is inconsistent, the enhanced item seems to be consistent in that it simply means any item that has a spell that directly alters the items properties (the gun that never jams, the unbreakable sword, etc.) and only grant their benefits to the user whatever manner the item was modified when it is utilized as said item. Numerous spells can achieve this and only require enough reach and a dot of willpower to make said spells indefinite, versus imbued traits which encode an Imago of a spell into the item and thus require the prime 4 attainment to have enough skill to encode whatever effect you want the item to manifest.<br /> <br /> But your right. The idea of a permanent magical effect that the item bestows an Effect is technically not covered under the imbued merit. I see that you could argue that an item permanently modified with imbued item to grant a constant magical effect would fit the enhanced items definition (as it has permanently altered properties.) However, I personally think the merit cost would be better described by the imbued item merit, even though it is permanently active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-29-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:40:35-07:00","id":902985,"title":"","content":"Dumb question : does ghost gate destroy your clothes?<br /> It says &quot;Items can be carried through the gate, but doing so destroys their material forms...&quot; so that seems to cover clothes as well. I assume RAI means more like taking a knife with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:41:25-07:00","id":903171,"title":"","content":"There is a post, i dont know if its here or in rpg.net, where Dave writes an example of a mage casting a curse on a guy. Does anyone has that link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:45:45-07:00","id":903173,"title":"","content":"A mage takes a legacy whose fourth attainment (or even fifth) is shifting sands. Because its an attainment it cannot be countered or dispelled. How would might one counter a legacy with this particular attainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:41:04-07:00","id":903217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903173#post903173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage takes a legacy whose fourth attainment (or even fifth) is shifting sands. Because its an attainment it cannot be countered or dispelled. How would might one counter a legacy with this particular attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can counter its direct effects in a normal fashion, you just can't stop them from using it. So, if a Mage used Shifting Sands to travel back in time they would still light up under Time Mage Sight and ping all forms of PMS. You could then do something like cast Constant Presence, or use Temporal Stutter to boot them back to the present or other similar methods for thwarting time travelers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T20:12:55-07:00","id":903235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903171#post903171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a post, i dont know if its here or in rpg.net, where Dave writes an example of a mage casting a curse on a guy. Does anyone has that link?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?591295-Mage-the-Awakening-The-Man-Comes-Around&amp;p=19183548#post19183548\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Ivan Tischenko Must Die</b></a>, from the RPGnet thread for his current AP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:50:08-07:00","id":903444,"title":"","content":"So, for practical reasons, a Souless Mage is pretty safe and not in a much of danger if they have a good source of Willpower restoration that does not rely on Vice, like spells that restore a point per casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T07:25:22-07:00","id":903483,"title":"","content":"Apart from all their spells risking Paradox","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T07:49:37-07:00","id":903503,"title":"","content":"I knew I was missing something just by refferring to Condition rules. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:00:07-07:00","id":903513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903173#post903173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage takes a legacy whose fourth attainment (or even fifth) is shifting sands. Because its an attainment it cannot be countered or dispelled. How would might one counter a legacy with this particular attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can try slow-acting poison, preferably when they're asleep. Time-Veiled explosives will also do the trick. Even if they survive they're still injured. Make sure you have stalked them for the previous day. If your mark spontaneously manifests injuries it means your future self got to them and you have an advantage. Again, Veiling spells are a must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:04:13-07:00","id":903586,"title":"","content":"<b>Q: What would happen when i move a duration factor to make these spells last for a few turns or a scene?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Telekinetic Strike (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Athletics, Firearms, Science<br /> The mage manipulates kinetic forces to crush subjects or<br /> form a \u201cball\u201d of highly pressurized air and kinetic energy that<br /> she can hurl at foes. The spell inflicts bashing damage equal<br /> to its Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell inflicts the Knocked Down or Stunned Tilt. </div> </div> </div>A spell that deals damage equal to potency every turn?<br /> A spell that deals damage equal to potency over few turns?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Call Lightning (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Athletics, Firearms, Science<br /> With a gesture the mage can conjure lightning down from<br /> a stormy sky to strike her foes. She must use this spell with<br /> an existing storm or one she sets into motion with \u201cControl<br /> Weather\u201d (see p. 143), since she cannot create lightning from<br /> nothing at this level.<br /> While the lightning bolt itself is all but unavoidable, the<br /> crackling build-up of energy gives a target warning. The bolt can<br /> only strike a target it could actually reach, so the target must<br /> be exposed in some way. With multiple subjects, the lightning<br /> forks, striking each simultaneously. It does damage according<br /> to the Electricity rules on p. 224. </div> </div> </div>Would it reliably send a lightning from the sky every turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:13:08-07:00","id":903594,"title":"","content":"Spell effects like that recur at a time interval equal to that of your ritual casting time. In other words, if you're Gnosis 3 and cast the spell, poor John Q. Gotinmyway would get struck by lightning every hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:24:51-07:00","id":903635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903594#post903594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell effects like that recur at a time interval equal to that of your ritual casting time. In other words, if you're Gnosis 3 and cast the spell, poor John Q. Gotinmyway would get struck by lightning every hour.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. Where can i find that rule? And also how i can create a spell that sends lightnings a little more often than once every hour?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:37:46-07:00","id":903646,"title":"","content":"The simplest way would be to simply re-cast the spell, or increase your Gnosis to lower your ritual casting time interval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:51:49-07:00","id":903656,"title":"","content":"Best way to portray it in game would be creating a spell that creates a Condition for it's duration, and that condition would then proceed to shock you using it's internal logic rules. Look at &quot;Sick&quot; and &quot;Poisoned&quot; tilts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:58:03-07:00","id":903659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903635#post903635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Where can i find that rule? And also how i can create a spell that sends lightnings a little more often than once every hour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 113, under duration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:27:38-07:00","id":903674,"title":"","content":"I guess i can add some reach effects like:<br /> <b>+1 Reach </b>Target gets the Always Strike Twice Tilt for the number of turns equal to potency<br /> <br /> <b>Always Strike Twice Tilt</b><br /> The character acts like a magnet to the lightnings and boy its not fun.<br /> <b>Effect</b>: As long as there is storm in the area the character is treated as main target of free flowing electricity. It does not cause lightnings, only moves character closer to the Supernal symbol of Thunder. Its up to ST to determine when and how the strike will happen (or not).<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Pissing of a deity, bad luck, curse and any relevant supernal fenomena.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> Wait for it to stop, get some lucky item, or get shocked for a second time.<br /> <br /> Is this any good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:44:09-07:00","id":903686,"title":"","content":"It seems cool. In combat, I would just make it a flat 1 Bashing per turn and some riding effect on that (like &quot;lightning always target you first&quot; :P)<br /> But you are definitely going into a good direction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:05:48-07:00","id":903729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903686#post903686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems cool. In combat, I would just make it a flat 1 Bashing per turn and some riding effect on that (like &quot;lightning always target you first&quot; :P)<br /> But you are definitely going into a good direction</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean that <b>+1 Reach</b> adds 1 bashing per turn for a number of turns equal potency (body is still in shock) ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:55:41-07:00","id":903790,"title":"","content":"Ey mates! I have one question i've posted in the FAQ thread, but given that it will take time to get an answer, thought i might aswell ask it here: In a magically dead area (such as the ones caused by Prime), can a Mage still use his Arcana Attainments?<br /> <br /> I ask this seemingly stupid question as the book says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attainments do not require Imagos and as such cannot be countered by Counterspell, Universal Counterspell, or any other Attainments that affect spells </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:47:02-07:00","id":903812,"title":"","content":"They should still work since they're not even magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:34:22-07:00","id":903843,"title":"","content":"To calculate the paradox dice for a Supernal being, would rank be equal to gnosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:42:49-07:00","id":903849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=903790#post903790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ey mates! I have one question i've posted in the FAQ thread, but given that it will take time to get an answer, thought i might aswell ask it here: In a magically dead area (such as the ones caused by Prime), can a Mage still use his Arcana Attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm mistaken, the dead zones Prime creates doesn't stop Arcana or Magic from being used; If your talking about the Ansho which are listed in tokyo which prevent spells from being cast, then no - attainments still work fine according to them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:32:37-07:00","id":904452,"title":"","content":"Control Heat ramps up extreme environments. At Potency 5 it can move from room temperature to a Level 5 Extreme Environment. A hot or cold one.<br /> <br /> The list in Extreme Environments lists them up to 4, is there even a level 5 or is 4 max? And what would a level 4/5 heat environment be like if caused by a spell that affects a house? (as per advanced scale)<br /> Would it be on fire? Or just very hot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:37:47-07:00","id":904551,"title":"","content":"What kind of magic would be needed to replicate hospital &quot;stuff&quot; in order to use Medicine skill to degrade Lethal to Bashing?<br /> Asking because we probably won't get to Arcanum 4 anytime soon (if ever), and rewarding a Life (Or Death) Mage for having Medicine skill is something we would like. Just not sure how to portray it using spell mechanics.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> This should make it more clear:<br /> How would a spell that manipulates the Medical Care look like?<br /> Things that constitute Medical Care:<br /> - Proper place to do it (&quot;Hospital stuff&quot;); this is binary. <br /> - Extended Intelligence+Medicine roll; could be possibly boostable?<br /> - ^ roll intervals of 1 hour; could be shortened using Potency?<br /> - Target Number of Successes to downgrade damage; could be reduced by Potency?<br /> - 1 Wound per day limit; could be lifted using Potency?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-31-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:14:39-07:00","id":905534,"title":"","content":"How would the merit Closed Book (CofD pg 50.) Apply to certain spells? If the storyteller allow it to apply to magic of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:07:13-07:00","id":905572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening 2e Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coaxing the Spirits (Spirit \u2022)<br /> Practice: Compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Composure or Rank<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Politics, Athletics, Expression<br /> Though most spirits are but slumbering motes that have no will or sapience, the mage may coax them to brief activity in accordance with their natures. She may compel the spirit (or its physical representation) to take a single instant action in accordance with its nature. A frightened animal might attack or flee, a car might start up, or a cliff face might start a small avalanche.The spell is Withstood by the Rank of the spirit coaxed or the Composure of a living representation, whichever is higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that anything has a physical representation? Could this spell affect people and awakened mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:24:11-07:00","id":905580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=905572#post905572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean that anything has a physical representation? Could this spell affect people and awakened mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't have spiritual reflections, so no. People have always curiously been absent from the Shadow--we fertilize and produce essence like crazy, but there's no &quot;human spirit&quot;--just goetia.<br /> I guess technically it could &quot;work&quot; on astral entities but the goetia wouldn't be able to do anything since they're &quot;further&quot; away from our world than the Shadow is. If you use Mind 1 and the ST is being kind, it miiiight work on someone's onieros goetia, but at that point you'd just be casting a harder spell that is Withstood by a trickier entity for something that normal Mind 1 magic would do to the actual mind of the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T13:18:43-07:00","id":905908,"title":"","content":"Where can I read about Abyssal Awakenings and are they, as written, One Ticket Way to Evilville?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:10:37-07:00","id":905941,"title":"","content":"Time of the Mysteries I believe, and Left Hand Path probably talk at them too.<br /> <br /> It's a one way ticket to being aligned with the Abyss. Any Scelesti will tell you that doesn't necessitate evil though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T18:50:04-07:00","id":906116,"title":"","content":"Does the sleepwalker merit 'fitful slumber' cause one to become a sleepwalker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:10:46-07:00","id":906359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=905941#post905941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time of the Mysteries I believe, and Left Hand Path probably talk at them too.<br /> <br /> It's a one way ticket to being aligned with the Abyss. Any Scelesti will tell you that doesn't necessitate evil though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I have access to both of these, so I will look at them later. Though at first I was baffled that I didn't know what Time of Mysteries was <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Imagine that you are a Cult-Master of a Mystery Cult that grants a Supernatural Merit as it's benefit. You, as a Mage, obviously can't benefit from it. What happens? Do you just pick Merit of appropiate value, due to Sancticy of Merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:14:19-07:00","id":906361,"title":"","content":"Why can't a Mage benefit from a supernatural merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:39:43-07:00","id":906373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=906361#post906361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't a Mage benefit from a supernatural merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>'These Merits require the character remain human (non-supernatural.) If the character becomes a vampire, ghoul, mage, or any other supernatural character type, these Merits disappear.'<br /> <br /> Still protected by Sanctity of Merits, so you can get something else from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:40:28-07:00","id":906374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=906359#post906359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine that you are a Cult-Master of a Mystery Cult that grants a Supernatural Merit as it's benefit. You, as a Mage, obviously can't benefit from it. What happens? Do you just pick Merit of appropiate value, due to Sancticy of Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> Per chronicle of darkness, page 56 under supernatural merits<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These Merits require the character remain human [...] If the character becomes a [...], mage, [...] these Merits <br /> disappear. <b>Per the Sanctity of Merits [...], these Merits can be reallocated</b>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:18:15-07:00","id":906422,"title":"","content":"Thanks. My concern is that because these merits are granted from Mystery Cult Initiation, not something character purchased &quot;herself&quot;, they might not be appropiate for this rule.<br /> <br /> Fun thing: There is no way to perceive things moved to Twilight other than being in T wilight yourself, as written. All of the &quot;you can see Twilight!&quot; spells and Attainments specifically mention ghosts and souls. Probably not intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:29:04-07:00","id":906580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=906422#post906422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. My concern is that because these merits are granted from Mystery Cult Initiation, not something character purchased &amp;quot;herself&amp;quot;, they might not be appropiate for this rule.<br /> <br /> Fun thing: There is no way to perceive things moved to Twilight other than being in T wilight yourself, as written. All of the &amp;quot;you can see Twilight!&amp;quot; spells and Attainments specifically mention ghosts and souls. Probably not intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that too. I just houseruled it to be &quot;[spirit/ghost/goetia] and associated epherma.&quot; Otherwise it makes a lot of the abilities to interact with the epherma, or to covert things to/from epherma, seem odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:02:15-07:00","id":906612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=906422#post906422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun thing: There is no way to perceive things moved to Twilight other than being in T wilight yourself, as written. All of the &quot;you can see Twilight!&quot; spells and Attainments specifically mention ghosts and souls. Probably not intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage detects ghosts and deathly Twilight phenomena with her Periphery, and can automatically see souls and ghosts in Twilight with her Death Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think you wouldn't be able to see things, in this case ghosts and deathly phenomena, in Twilight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:08:28-07:00","id":906615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=906359#post906359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I have access to both of these, so I will look at them later. Though at first I was baffled that I didn't know what Time of Mysteries was <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Imagine that you are a Cult-Master of a Mystery Cult that grants a Supernatural Merit as it's benefit. You, as a Mage, obviously can't benefit from it. What happens? Do you just pick Merit of appropiate value, due to Sancticy of Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen Mystery Cults as breaking the 'mortal only' rule for merits granted, and that it would likewise work if you had such a cult grant a vampire/mage/whatever else merit. Anyone can benefit, but you need to have 3 dots of the Mystery Cult merit, which means you're in fairly deep. Granted, Mages do have Mystery Cult Influence as an option, but they still need to have a cult available that has the merit that they want; it's ultimately up to the ST what can be accessed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T01:14:18-07:00","id":907516,"title":"","content":"Would a pocket dimension have a reflection in the shadow?<br /> <br /> Since it is still technically apart of the material plane it does seem to be possible but if by default it doesn't, with enough resonance could a reflection in the shadow be developed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T01:25:45-07:00","id":907519,"title":"","content":"I see. I will then just convert these Merits into something else, as they are redundant with Mage template anyway (Medium and Unseen Sense aren't very useful for Death Mage : P)<br /> <br /> People keep talking about a rule that allows developing new and alternate Arcana Attainments (not Legacy Attainments). Where is it located? I can't find it.<br /> EDIT<br /> Derp, found it. Still, I'm not sure; is it supposed to mean that a Mage can have multiple 2nd Dot Utility Attainments for one Arcanum? If so, it's incredibly interesting way to make character growth horizontal instead of vertical, assuming locking Gnosis at certain levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-05-2016, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T02:07:56-07:00","id":907532,"title":"","content":"<b>Q: </b>If I cast e.g. &quot;Honing the Form&quot; with Potence 4 and Reach to Advanced Scale do I have to divide Potence or can I use it all on each target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T02:20:40-07:00","id":907536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=907532#post907532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: </b>If I cast e.g. &amp;quot;Honing the Form&amp;quot; with Potence 4 and Reach to Advanced Scale do I have to divide Potence or can I use it all on each target?</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell affects each target with all spell factors of the spell. You don't divide them but rather affect all with the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:37:24-07:00","id":907797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=907516#post907516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a pocket dimension have a reflection in the shadow?<br /> <br /> Since it is still technically apart of the material plane it does seem to be possible but if by default it doesn't, with enough resonance could a reflection in the shadow be developed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no by default, but yes if there's a plot possibility in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:51:49-07:00","id":907939,"title":"","content":"I'd say no by default, but yes with Spirit 5 Making, or a Space+Spirit Co-Location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T18:56:58-07:00","id":908033,"title":"","content":"I could swear I've read it somewhere but my memory is a fickle thing. Dear folks, where did I read about the methods of finding a newly awakened mage? Where can I find this information? Was it the Core book? Sanctum and sigil? Tome of the Mysteries?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:28:01-07:00","id":908052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=908033#post908033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could swear I've read it somewhere but my memory is a fickle thing. Dear folks, where did I read about the methods of finding a newly awakened mage? Where can I find this information? Was it the Core book? Sanctum and sigil? Tome of the Mysteries?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the Mysterium book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:39:11-07:00","id":908233,"title":"","content":"Question about teamwork casting: Do the secondary actors suffer penalties from spell factors ?<br /> <br /> If yes then i find the option to help with casting a spell even if you can't cast it yet somewhat useless. You roll Gnosis -3 further lowered by spell factors meaning that you'll be rolling a chance die meaning the reward isn't worth it (succeding for 1 die is as likely as dramatically failing for -4 dice). And in case you actually manage to have a positive dice pool that means that the caster has at least around 4 more dice than you so he doesn't need your help. Plus each caster rolls her own paradox, which means that the apprentices are going to roll a lot of dice due to having no free reach.<br /> <br /> So how is it ?<br /> <br /> I like the image of a Master calling his apprentices to help with a spell but it seems either harmfull/dangerous to do so or absolutely unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Currently thinking about making it: &quot;If can't cast the spell roll Gnosis+Arcanum without modifiers, if you get at least one success add one die to the main actors casting pool&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 06-06-2016, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:41:01-07:00","id":908234,"title":"","content":"They also get Yantra bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T04:21:44-07:00","id":908253,"title":"","content":"Can a multiple spell be made into a Rote or Praxis, and therefore be made into a Legacy Attainment? [The thing i had on my mind was a Mind spell who could detect minds nearby and inform at the same time of said minds prevalent emotion. I wanted to add Space 1 as the Optional Arcanum, in order to be able to locate them.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:02:55-07:00","id":908365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=908234#post908234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also get Yantra bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does the main caster. Half my point was that if the secondary agent gets a possitive dicepool it also means that the main caster gets a large enough dice pool that the few bonus dice aren't needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:03:59-07:00","id":908366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=908253#post908253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a multiple spell be made into a Rote or Praxis, and therefore be made into a Legacy Attainment? [The thing i had on my mind was a Mind spell who could detect minds nearby and inform at the same time of said minds prevalent emotion. I wanted to add Space 1 as the Optional Arcanum, in order to be able to locate them.]</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a combined spell is still two separate spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:28:08-07:00","id":908419,"title":"","content":"So quick question, when casting a spell that effects a ephemeral entities patteren do you need add its corresponding Arcane? <br /> <br /> Such as reading a ghosts thoughts with Mind do need to add Death to the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 06-06-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T11:13:19-07:00","id":908446,"title":"","content":"In that specific example, no, reading a mind falls entirely within the purview of Mind. You don't need Life to read a person's mind, and sure ephemeral entities are different than people but the phenomena of consciousness isn't different in spite of its alien makeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:27:24-07:00","id":909015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=908419#post908419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quick question, when casting a spell that effects a ephemeral entities patteren do you need add its corresponding Arcane?<br /> <br /> Such as reading a ghosts thoughts with Mind do need to add Death to the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't need Death, but you do need some way to see the ghost to target it. Typically that means having Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:03:34-07:00","id":909023,"title":"","content":"Does natural Tass spoil?<br /> <br /> Does Mana Sensitivity sense other mages, by their mana?<br /> <br /> The section on Hallows says that Hallows trigger peripheral mage sight. Is that a typo, since it contradicts Mana Sensitivity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:39:29-07:00","id":909585,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a><br /> <br /> Organic Tass spoils. The other sorts don't.<br /> Apple tass will rot, but River Rock tass will not.<br /> <br /> It seems Mana Sensitivity would sense a nearby Mage with Peripheral Sight if they have Mana in their patterns.<br /> <br /> The Hallows section doesn't seem to specifically mention Peripheral Sight.<br /> It says Mystic Senses. It probably needs to be more specific.<br /> Based on the Active Sight for Prime and the Mana Sensitivity Merit,<br /> I'd assume when it says mystic sense it's referring to Prime Active Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 06-07-2016, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:51:00-07:00","id":909796,"title":"","content":"I did a quick search and didn't find anything, but has there been any talk about additional rules for Scelesti past what's found on page 239 about rolling Gnosis to gain control of Reach from Paradox? I feel like Dave said he was going to do a write-up for Scelesti on the blog/website at some point after release -- has he mentioned any details about that yet? Not trying to be impatient (though I'll always hunger for more Mage stuff) it's just becoming relevant here in a few days for me.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:04:49-07:00","id":909805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=909796#post909796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a quick search and didn't find anything, but has there been any talk about additional rules for Scelesti past what's found on page 239 about rolling Gnosis to gain control of Reach from Paradox? I feel like Dave said he was going to do a write-up for Scelesti on the blog/website at some point after release -- has he mentioned any details about that yet? Not trying to be impatient (though I'll always hunger for more Mage stuff) it's just becoming relevant here in a few days for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave did indeed state he wanted to post some cut material about Mage antagonists like Scelesti and the Mad, as well as converting about four legacies for 2e.<br /> <br /> However, I assume he's been very occupied with finishing the errata for the final Mage 2e PDF and PoD and writing the FAQ.<br /> <br /> New material will almost certainly have to wait until the core product is finalized and clarified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:10:24-07:00","id":909809,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, absolutely! I don't expect the full write-up anytime soon (relatively) seeing as how Mage 2E isn't even finished, AND Signs of Sorcery is in the works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:24:09-07:00","id":909816,"title":"","content":"So what's the advantage to using Self-Repairing Machine?<br /> Nigredo and Albedo at a high Duration at even just 1 Gnosis seems to proc the Structure healing more often than a Self-Repairing Machine that doesnt have a reach effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T06:09:33-07:00","id":910013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=909816#post909816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the advantage to using Self-Repairing Machine?<br /> Nigredo and Albedo at a high Duration at even just 1 Gnosis seems to proc the Structure healing more often than a Self-Repairing Machine that doesnt have a reach effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its the fact you can take the machine for granted and not have to sweat about routine maintenance, but if you're a machine-savvy mage you probably wouldn't use it anyway for the pleasure of working on the machine anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:49:07-07:00","id":910108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=910013#post910013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its the fact you can take the machine for granted and not have to sweat about routine maintenance, but if you're a machine-savvy mage you probably wouldn't use it anyway for the pleasure of working on the machine anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the implied subtlety of &quot;this object heals itself over time&quot; in contrast to &quot;this object has a repair spell on it that procs every couple of hours.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:15:45-07:00","id":910240,"title":"","content":"Basically, Nigredo and Albedo is a &quot;you can have the bumper pop back into place after a fender bender, but that wont stop the engine from getting clogged up&quot; sort of deal?<br /> <br /> Aside from the inside of the vehicle, I don't think either of these spells have subtlety. If someone scratches your paint job and dents your door, then either one procs, all that damage is suddenly gone. Someone watching could see all the paint regrow and the dent slowly un-dent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 06-08-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:38:46-07:00","id":910251,"title":"","content":"That's when Dissonance would occur I imagine. Honestly, I could easily see bumping into someone and scratching their paint, only to realize the damage isn't that bad, and then not even being able to find the scratch later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:56:07-07:00","id":910259,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> I can see the advantages now.<br /> Thank you all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:37:37-07:00","id":911043,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to transfer temporal sympathy between different subjects without archmastery, or are those connections entirely limited to individual specimens and their own past selves within the normal game mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:14:34-07:00","id":911081,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. Except then you could manage jumping back much further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:59:33-07:00","id":911172,"title":"","content":"can spells held within hung spell be individually activated only only all at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:33:39-07:00","id":911195,"title":"","content":"All at once since the trapped spells activate when the &quot;hung spell&quot; spell ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:27:22-07:00","id":911228,"title":"","content":"Then I guess is there any way to have each spell activate separately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:41:44-07:00","id":911246,"title":"","content":"Yes, by having Multiple Hanged Spells. If you are afraid of spell control, just relinquish it unsafely.<br /> EDIT<br /> This one is interesting, because while you can have multiple Hung Spells at once, only the most Potent one will be &quot;active&quot; at a time. It's tricky. You would have to activate them in a specific chain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-09-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:07:13-07:00","id":911274,"title":"","content":"Would anything implode if you added a +1 reach option to Hung Spell for selective firing? Or maybe a Fate-reliant Reach option (deliberate exemption from a spell effect, etc.?) I don't see too much peril in the prospect - they're still in spell control, there's mana costs involved, Hung Spell itself has to be robust enough to hold them all - but I may be missing something obvious.<br /> <br /> Here's one that struck me recently:<br /> <br /> How might a mage predict the future or fate of, say, a city or nation? It seems as though spell-based options trip over the limitations of having to have distinct targets (and being limited in area). Am I missing a spell option that has unusual targeting? Can a mage predict a natural disaster in the city they live in without having to divine the future of a neighborhood or resident that would be affected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:13:48-07:00","id":911279,"title":"","content":"You would probably need to do what psychology always had to deal with, and target a representative group. Or area. Still, Factors are there as much as to empower your magic, as they are to limit it. Limitless magic is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:32:45-07:00","id":911329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911246#post911246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, by having Multiple Hanged Spells. If you are afraid of spell control, just relinquish it unsafely.<br /> EDIT<br /> This one is interesting, because while you can have multiple Hung Spells at once, only the most Potent one will be &quot;active&quot; at a time. It's tricky. You would have to activate them in a specific chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darn, Thank you. I am trying to build a mage who utilizes vancian spell casting by choice and trying to see how I could make it work. It does seem odd to me that all spells are activated when the hung spell ends though I do understand that it makes sense. If there was a way to activate each spell within a casting of hung spell individually it'd make this concept far easier because of the issue with spell control as you mentioned.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a> Having the spells be able to be activated separately for a reach would be interesting. Kind of like having a key set to release each spell. Maybe this would interact with conditional duration in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:38:59-07:00","id":911530,"title":"","content":"Why is Channel Mana a 3-dot spell, but Channel Essence is a 2-dot spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:48:24-07:00","id":911531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911530#post911530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Channel Mana a 3-dot spell, but Channel Essence is a 2-dot spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is because essence is more mutable than mana. I mean we never talk about &quot;different types&quot; of mana, but there are thousands, countless forms of essence and the wrong kind of essence can be damaging to the wrong kind of spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:25:02-07:00","id":911671,"title":"","content":"Is 1e Matter: Reconfiguration still a Patterning spell or is it Weaving now? If i want to change a car into a different car i am not changing it completely. Its still a car. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:45:04-07:00","id":911684,"title":"","content":"One thing into another thing of the same type is probably just Weaving, Ruling if it's just cosmetic. Look at Life for some handy parallels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:24:36-07:00","id":911710,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried using Creative Thaumaturgy rule about Narrative effects being limited by Potency with spells like Psychic Domination, Lying Maps and so on? On one hand I can see it solving a lot of potential troubles, on the other hand I don't have enough information to make a good Potency threshold for these effects just yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also, is there really anything stopping Ruling Life or Death from just making something die? It seems to fall within their Purviews and &quot;what can Ruling do&quot;; would it be &quot;be dead for the duration of the spell&quot; kind of deal? Are there any reasons, outside of obvious game balance, for it not being possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-10-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:51:47-07:00","id":911723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911710#post911710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried using Creative Thaumaturgy rule about Narrative effects being limited by Potency with spells like Psychic Domination, Lying Maps and so on? On one hand I can see it solving a lot of potential troubles, on the other hand I don't have enough information to make a good Potency threshold for these effects just yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also, is there really anything stopping Ruling Life or Death from just making something die? It seems to fall within their Purviews and &quot;what can Ruling do&quot;; would it be &quot;be dead for the duration of the spell&quot; kind of deal? Are there any reasons, outside of obvious game balance, for it not being possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't tried it, but that might be a good idea for things like Psychic Domination.<br /> <br /> As for Ruling Life/Death, I think it's pretty much been said that to kill someone, you're either fully unmaking their life or making a death that isn't there yet. You can't rule Death to kill someone because it's not there to rule (at least not in the form that'd allow it to be used to kill them, yes all patterns have some bits of each arcana blah blah blah), and you can't rule Life to stop being life because that'd be Unmaking it, which is not Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:58:44-07:00","id":911725,"title":"","content":"You can make Mind unmake itself while Ruling by giving it a suicide command, so what stops you from Ruling subject's heart to operate in a way that will lead to it's demise? <br /> And yeah, I was tinkering with the Psychic Domination; assigning Potency thresholds to commands sounds like a good compromise for the style I'm aiming for. But I don't like relying on common sense (it kills people, common sense is not common and often is wrong), and I'm not sure how to estabilish a scale of Potencies, because for that, I need to what is much and what is not much, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:14:55-07:00","id":911738,"title":"","content":"How do clashes of will and dice boni work? Leaving the bonis from advanced potency and duration aside, are there other bonis that apply or is it just a straight Gnosis + Arcana vs whatever, if neccessary rolling one roll for the spell itself with boni and one without for the clash?<br /> <br /> Example : Peter (Gnosis 3, Forces 3) casts a Forces 3 Fraying spell (a kinetic blow) on his opponent Dave (Gnosis 3, Forces 2), who has put up a barrier shielding him from kinetic attacks. A clash of will ensues. Peter rolls 6 dice versus Daves 5 dice. So far so easy.<br /> <br /> Now what if Peter used a reflexive Yantra to add a die to his spell? Does that die count for the sake of the clash of wills or just for the spell? What if a Prime 2 spell was used to infuse said Yantra he used reflexsivly in his spell to give him the 8-again quality? Or a Fate spell to give him rote quality? Does that all work for the clash of wills or does he roll his let's say 7 dice with rote quality and 8 again for the clash?<br /> <br /> Or the flip side what if Dave the defender cast his Forces shield with 8-again quality, does said 8-again apply to all clashes of will that shield will triggers automatically?<br /> <br /> What if either side chopped dice off to cast the spell with higher potency, would those dice be missing for the clash aswell?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:48:56-07:00","id":911763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911725#post911725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make Mind unmake itself while Ruling by giving it a suicide command, so what stops you from Ruling subject's heart to operate in a way that will lead to it's demise?<br /> And yeah, I was tinkering with the Psychic Domination; assigning Potency thresholds to commands sounds like a good compromise for the style I'm aiming for. But I don't like relying on common sense (it kills people, common sense is not common and often is wrong), and I'm not sure how to estabilish a scale of Potencies, because for that, I need to what is much and what is not much, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh commanding someone to commit suicide isn't telling the Mind to unmake itself, it's telling the Mind to do something that may ultimately end in it no longer existing through outside forces the Mind happens to have control over (it wouldn't do much on a paralyzed or comatose victim, for instance, since they CAN'T perform a suicidal command).<br /> <br /> You could probably use Life Ruling to stop someone's heart, but isn't that already covered by Body Control (I don't have my book open to check if it still allows that in 2e)? Which if I recall keeps you alive with that limited or missing heart rate. So I think the implication there is if you're just using Ruling, you can manipulate the parts but without being able to Unmake or at least heavily Fray, it doesn't actually degrade or work like it might if the heart stopped normally.<br /> <br /> Also, Life for whatever reason needs 4 dots to make someone perform suicidal commands for reasons I can't quite comprehend (or rather, I can, I just don't see why that's Patterning for Life and not for Mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:52:19-07:00","id":911765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911738#post911738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do clashes of will and dice boni work? Leaving the bonis from advanced potency and duration aside, are there other bonis that apply or is it just a straight Gnosis + Arcana vs whatever, if neccessary rolling one roll for the spell itself with boni and one without for the clash?<br /> <br /> Example : Peter (Gnosis 3, Forces 3) casts a Forces 3 Fraying spell (a kinetic blow) on his opponent Dave (Gnosis 3, Forces 2), who has put up a barrier shielding him from kinetic attacks. A clash of will ensues. Peter rolls 6 dice versus Daves 5 dice. So far so easy.<br /> <br /> Now what if Peter used a reflexive Yantra to add a die to his spell? Does that die count for the sake of the clash of wills or just for the spell? What if a Prime 2 spell was used to infuse said Yantra he used reflexsivly in his spell to give him the 8-again quality? Or a Fate spell to give him rote quality? Does that all work for the clash of wills or does he roll his let's say 7 dice with rote quality and 8 again for the clash?<br /> <br /> Or the flip side what if Dave the defender cast his Forces shield with 8-again quality, does said 8-again apply to all clashes of will that shield will triggers automatically?<br /> <br /> What if either side chopped dice off to cast the spell with higher potency, would those dice be missing for the clash aswell?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yantra bonuses and other things that affect spellcasting dice pools specifically (like factors) do NOT affect Clash of Wills, though dice tricks that affect ALL rolls (including spell rolls) usually would, but it'd be an entirely separate roll for the purposes of if you only can add a benefit to X rolls.<br /> <br /> As DaveB has mentioned, a Mage's best bet when they expect their spell to Clash is to pump extra duration into it (which adds built in bonuses to the Clash dice pool).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:10:05-07:00","id":911773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911765#post911765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yantra bonuses and other things that affect spellcasting dice pools specifically (like factors) do NOT affect Clash of Wills, though dice tricks that affect ALL rolls (including spell rolls) usually would, but it'd be an entirely separate roll for the purposes of if you only can add a benefit to X rolls.<br /> <br /> As DaveB has mentioned, a Mage's best bet when they expect their spell to Clash is to pump extra duration into it (which adds built in bonuses to the Clash dice pool).</div> </div> </div> </div>So it would be possible to cast a version of As Above, So Below that affects Clashes of Will?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:40:29-07:00","id":911792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911710#post911710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Also, is there really anything stopping Ruling Life or Death from just making something die? It seems to fall within their Purviews and &quot;what can Ruling do&quot;; would it be &quot;be dead for the duration of the spell&quot; kind of deal? Are there any reasons, outside of obvious game balance, for it not being possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would rule that you can &quot;Rule&quot; someone already dying (all health boxes with lethal, rapid-killing disease, suicide tentions, etc) to die right now {Potency Ruling Death Spell}, or someone with a serious heart issue to have a heart attack {Potency Ruiling Life Spell} the same way as &quot;Rule&quot; can affect a bored worker to take a break now (Potency Ruling Mind Spell). But without pre-existing firm conditions, &quot;Rule&quot; can't cause aneurisms or decomposition to deal damage or make stuff happen. This falls under &quot;Fraying&quot;<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Devil, with Fraying (and other Practices) one can for example &quot;Fray&quot; someone with Death, decomposing his flesh until he is dying. Then he can affect him with the Ruling Practice to die. Or first mark him with a Ruling Duration &quot;Die Faster&quot; spell, then Fray him and take his victim by surprise<br /> <br /> As already said, Ruling magic cant fray by itself, but maybe it can give conditions like &quot;Heart Attack&quot;, &quot;Speed Decomposition&quot; or &quot;Fasten&quot; that are damaging with their own effects but requires some setup like people with existing chronic heart disease, people that became angry in this scene etc...<br /> <br /> To sum up, here is my interpretation of the &quot;Cool&quot; Practices:<br /> Compel is for &quot;I slightly nudge stuff&quot;<br /> Rule is &quot;Turn existing stuff into Environmental/Situational Advantage&quot;<br /> Fray is &quot;average Firebending control&quot;<br /> Pattern is &quot;Taste my lightning sucker&quot;<br /> Make is &quot;You're my bitch&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:42:28-07:00","id":911794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911710#post911710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried using Creative Thaumaturgy rule about Narrative effects being limited by Potency with spells like Psychic Domination, Lying Maps and so on? On one hand I can see it solving a lot of potential troubles, on the other hand I don't have enough information to make a good Potency threshold for these effects just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>For self-harming or suicidal commands you could simply treat it like an extraordinary damage spell. Forcing the target to deal 2x/3x remaining Potency in damage to themselves.<br /> <br /> For Lying Maps, think up some base distance and multiply it by remaining Potency to see just how far off the subject is lead at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:57:14-07:00","id":912089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=911773#post911773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it would be possible to cast a version of As Above, So Below that affects Clashes of Will?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T01:43:36-07:00","id":912147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912089#post912089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>As above, so below bestows it's bonuses to a specific yantra, so I can't see how it can affect clashes when yantra bonusses don't affect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:01:40-07:00","id":912159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912147#post912147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As above, so below bestows it's bonuses to a specific yantra, so I can't see how it can affect clashes when yantra bonusses don't affect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yantra bonuses themselves don't affect a Clash, but there's no reason a spell can't say that it affects a Clash of Wills if the spell Clashing was cast using a specific Yantra. That's not a yantra bonus in that case, it's just a condition of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:34:00-07:00","id":912169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912147#post912147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As above, so below bestows it's bonuses to a specific yantra, so I can't see how it can affect clashes when yantra bonusses don't affect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only question is if Clash of Wills can be affected at all. If it can it means that Prime can do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:16:54-07:00","id":912275,"title":"","content":"Can bonus dices granted by fate (like exceptional luck) be used also to win or boost a clash of wills?<br /> <br /> also, my 2 cents on the clash of wills prime bonus- i would allow prime to power up a clash of wills only if its related to two spellcasters clashing and i mean two awakened mages, not to win a clash of wills against other supernaturals. This is because in my opinion prime can apply his power only on awakened magic and supernal powers, and has no influence or very little on other kind of special discipline or gitfs.. etc..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 06-11-2016, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:43:30-07:00","id":912307,"title":"","content":"What is the benefit of joining the Seers? Wealth and power I can get with a bit of creative magecraft, prestige and fame I can get much the same way. I'm not sure what benefits they offer that I either can't get myself or outweigh the whole &quot;become a slave to the Exarchs&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:51:09-07:00","id":912311,"title":"","content":"Can you be affected by Sympathetic Magic when in other worlds/Twilight?<br /> <br /> As for Seers, this is going to be brutal, but - remember Samuel L Jacksons character from <i>Django</i> ? Consider him and his motivations Seer-ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:05:38-07:00","id":912325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912307#post912307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the benefit of joining the Seers? Wealth and power I can get with a bit of creative magecraft, prestige and fame I can get much the same way. I'm not sure what benefits they offer that I either can't get myself or outweigh the whole &quot;become a slave to the Exarchs&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one thing you can actually <i>live it</i>. The advantage of being mundanely rich (criminally or not) is that you do not have to explain it. Furthermore, Pentacle mages have to specifically work on their riches, for a Seer it is a benefit of just doing their job. Mechanically, this is represented by the essentially &quot;free&quot; Resources they get (making their Order Status more valuable than the Pentacle's). Also, do not forget the comfort in knowing that very Concepts are on your side (or rather you on theirs). Finally, you get to benefit of nobody ragging on you for using your magic to get even more luxury, where an Arrow's superiors might scoff or a th\u00e9arch's colleagues wonder whether she fucked up her priorities. Being a greedy bastard is not just tacitly accepted, but encouraged. That is good for the soul, if you are so inclined anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:27:52-07:00","id":912344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912311#post912311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be affected by Sympathetic Magic when in other worlds/Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly, yes, and I don't believe the separation of realms provide any protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:39:29-07:00","id":913286,"title":"","content":"So, can we make a Bullet Shield with Matter?<br /> Would it be blocking bullets completely, or would it just be downgrading the damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T05:00:19-07:00","id":913344,"title":"","content":"You will still get hit by all the kinetic force behind them, I would wager. Unless you mean shield made out of bullets, then yes, that's actually pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:57:38-07:00","id":913557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912344#post912344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Explicitly, yes, and I don't believe the separation of realms provide any protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source ? Can you give us the page number ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:47:18-07:00","id":913696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=913344#post913344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will still get hit by all the kinetic force behind them, I would wager. Unless you mean shield made out of bullets, then yes, that's actually pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds pretty awesome actually. Shield made of bullets.<br /> Like a reach option could be that the bullets fire back at anyone hitting your shield too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:04:44-07:00","id":913733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=913557#post913557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source ? Can you give us the page number ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looked it over, it's not explicit, it is implied though by mentioning things like spells cast inside a Mage's Oneiros by the Mage never risk Paradox unless they leave the Oneiros. Since you only check for Paradox only when casting the spell, and the only way to cast outside of your Oneiros would be Sympathetically, it can be done.<br /> <br /> Also, I know Dave has mentioned that you can cast Sympathetically into or out of the Realms Invisible but spells may provoke Paradox as normal if they breach the bounds of the Realm, for instance casting a Death spell Sympathetically from the Underworld into the Physical would risk Paradox as normal instead of at the -2 the realm normally grants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:33:28-07:00","id":913744,"title":"","content":"Questions about Shifting Sands.<br /> <br /> The subject retains the same health and such as when the spell was cast on them, right?<br /> Could this be used to send an enemy back in time with like half their health and resources spent?<br /> Essentially allowing the cabal to have the upper hand at the beginning of the fight,<br /> preferably played straight because the cabal would be just meeting an already wounded enemy.<br /> <br /> Moreover, do you run the fight from the beginning again with the wounded enemy,<br /> or should the ST just change things accordingly while the cabal is left unawares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:08:37-07:00","id":913849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912311#post912311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be affected by Sympathetic Magic when in other worlds/Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight yes. You can be affected. If you're on a different realm of existence, (Underworld, Shadow, etc...) and the caster is not, they need 2 dots of the appropriate arcanum to cast on you. See the Teleportation spell (Space 4) for precedent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T08:25:48-07:00","id":914104,"title":"","content":"Question: Ward and Signs gives a Withstand protection against spells that target the mage pattern, but it works against a aimed spell like the Thunderbolt ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T08:51:50-07:00","id":914116,"title":"","content":"A quick question: What in the nine hells is a &quot;Perfected material?&quot; Steel I understand (It's Iron, but better), but I can't think of much else that logic would extend too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:12:01-07:00","id":914128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=912307#post912307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the benefit of joining the Seers? Wealth and power I can get with a bit of creative magecraft, prestige and fame I can get much the same way. I'm not sure what benefits they offer that I either can't get myself or outweigh the whole &quot;become a slave to the Exarchs&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a slave to the Exarchs no matter what you do, friend. You might as well accept the benefits of serving directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azunth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914116#post914116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question: What in the nine hells is a &quot;Perfected material?&quot; Steel I understand (It's Iron, but better), but I can't think of much else that logic would extend too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfected Metals aren't things like Steel, but a. . .damn, I can't remember if they're Platonic Ideals of a metal or what. But in any case, it's way more hype than Steel. Thaumium was the example we had in 1E, and it let someone holding an item made of it use mana store in it to counter spells and (maybe) weapons made of it were better at blasting through magical protections. But it's some pretty wild shit. We're supposed to get a handful of examples in Signs of Sorcery, and thus likely in that book's Open Dev blogs as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:16:02-07:00","id":914129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azunth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914116#post914116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question: What in the nine hells is a &quot;Perfected material?&quot; Steel I understand (It's Iron, but better), but I can't think of much else that logic would extend too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Steel and gold both have qualities that are symbolically resonant with persistence (one's name literally derives from the same root as &quot;stay&quot; and the other is notable for being nonreactive to a lot of chemicals) and petrified wood is a type of fossil where the shape of a plant has been entirely filled in with minerals. Diamond is the first other substance that comes to mind that fits that metric, but I'm sure you could find others with some digging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:25:07-07:00","id":914134,"title":"","content":"Legacy Attainments: If one doesn't want to spend the Reach for Sensory Casting, could an Attainment be thrown (instead of using touch-range)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:30:03-07:00","id":914141,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:34:15-07:00","id":914145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914128#post914128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfected Metals aren't things like Steel, but a. . .damn, I can't remember if they're Platonic Ideals of a metal or what. But in any case, it's way more hype than Steel. Thaumium was the example we had in 1E, and it let someone holding an item made of it use mana store in it to counter spells and (maybe) weapons made of it were better at blasting through magical protections. But it's some pretty wild shit. We're supposed to get a handful of examples in Signs of Sorcery, and thus likely in that book's Open Dev blogs as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what's been spoiled so far there will be more perfected elements than just metals, Dave specifically mentioned Perfected Fire and Water. I suspect that these could tie into the Tamer legacies, where perhaps Perfected Fire becomes not just a source of energy, but also a physical representation of Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:02:30-07:00","id":914160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914129#post914129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steel and gold both have qualities that are symbolically resonant with persistence (one's name literally derives from the same root as &quot;stay&quot; and the other is notable for being nonreactive to a lot of chemicals) and petrified wood is a type of fossil where the shape of a plant has been entirely filled in with minerals. Diamond is the first other substance that comes to mind that fits that metric, but I'm sure you could find others with some digging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Right off the bat, Noble Gases would fit the bill, if not be practical. Titanium might be right as well. Granite, maybe? Or Brick? Maybe even plastic, given how tough hard plastic can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914128#post914128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfected Metals aren't things like Steel, but a. . .damn, I can't remember if they're Platonic Ideals of a metal or what. But in any case, it's way more hype than Steel. Thaumium was the example we had in 1E, and it let someone holding an item made of it use mana store in it to counter spells and (maybe) weapons made of it were better at blasting through magical protections. But it's some pretty wild shit. We're supposed to get a handful of examples in Signs of Sorcery, and thus likely in that book's Open Dev blogs as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually asking about the path symbolism Obrimos. But thanks anyway!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:46:21-07:00","id":914202,"title":"","content":"Ok questions about attainments:<br /> <br /> Universal counterspell: it states that for a point you can counter the lowest Arcanum of the spell. But what if the opposing mage knowledge of the lowers arcanum is greater than it's his knowledge of it's highest. Say a mage with Matter 3, Forces 4, Prime 2. Casts a Matter 3/Prime2/Forces1 spell. By RAW by paying a point of mana you coulnd counter only the Forces portion of the spell (making it harder) and couldn't counter the Prime portion (would make it easier).<br /> Or maybe for this specific type of Clash you use the Arcana dots of the spell and not of the mage (so an Adept casting a 2 dot spell would only roll Gnosis+2 dice) ?<br /> <br /> Space mage armor - it increases your defense and it says you add Space to your dodge pool. Does it mean your dodge pool becomes (oldDef*2)+Space or [(oldDef+Space)*2]+Space ?<br /> Seems to lack the word &quot;intead&quot; somewhere. Asking partially because other types of similar mage armor have no such info. Also &quot;you can't use this bonus if you can't apply defense&quot; - does this mean other types of similar Mage armor can apply the bonus because they have no such info in their description ?<br /> It seems like it's just that someone has put a few reminders in the description of this type of MA and didn't put them in others but asking to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:27:02-07:00","id":914274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azunth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914160#post914160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was actually asking about the path symbolism Obrimos. But thanks anyway!</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha geez I COMPLETELY misread Materials as Metals.<br /> <br /> Probably because I'm so damned excited about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T16:30:52-07:00","id":914458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914104#post914104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Ward and Signs gives a Withstand protection against spells that target the mage pattern, but it works against a aimed spell like the Thunderbolt ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The spell only takes effect once it reaches its target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T04:16:47-07:00","id":914739,"title":"","content":"If you throw a Temporal Pocket over a large area, can you interact with other things within the pocket without cancelling the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:16:25-07:00","id":914759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=914739#post914739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you throw a Temporal Pocket over a large area, can you interact with other things within the pocket without cancelling the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You cannot interact with things frozen in time, but multiple subjects under the same spell can interact amongst themselves, you certainly can extend this to be a whole area and not a list of individual subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T08:11:06-07:00","id":914836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you throw a Temporal Pocket over a large area, can you interact with other things within the pocket without cancelling the spell? </div> </div> </div>This made me think of an idea where a restaurant is extremely fast at making food, and running a lot of sit down restaurants out of business. No one is allowed in the back to see what is going on in the kitchen, only the staff. The Mages go to check it out and find out what is going on and have to decide what they want to do with this situation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:21:02-07:00","id":915071,"title":"","content":"Are we talking about a temporal pocket where time OUTSIDE the pocket is frozen but everything INSIDE is running at player time? I think that would work as long as you don't touch anything outside the pocket.<br /> <br /> I actually don't remember if someone answered this question but I think at one point I asked the same question and asked how such a spell would interact with utilities like gas, electric, internet, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:33:20-07:00","id":915085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually don't remember if someone answered this question but I think at one point I asked the same question and asked how such a spell would interact with utilities like gas, electric, internet, etc. </div> </div> </div>Well, I am thinking they would actually just be cutting ingredients and doing prep work. The actual cook time would still be the same, but if you have all the time you need to prepare 100 meals it would go pretty quick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:16:43-07:00","id":915331,"title":"","content":"Learning your Order's Mudras is part of initiation. Is this information considered confidential? Could a Mystagogue get in trouble for asking their Free Council cabal-mate to make a copy of a Mysterium Grimoire? Moreoever, is the Free Councilor even capable of doing that without knowing the Mysterium's Mudras?<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------<br /> <br /> What arcanum would your Shadow Name fall under? Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-15-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T23:16:26-07:00","id":915425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=915071#post915071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking about a temporal pocket where time OUTSIDE the pocket is frozen but everything INSIDE is running at player time? I think that would work as long as you don't touch anything outside the pocket.<br /> <br /> I actually don't remember if someone answered this question but I think at one point I asked the same question and asked how such a spell would interact with utilities like gas, electric, internet, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best way to handle that would be to gloss over it, honestly, just like time travel glosses over temporal paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:10:52-07:00","id":915834,"title":"","content":"When targeting via Temporal Sympathy, how do you have to describe the time period you want to effect?<br /> <br /> Can you say you want to target Jim one day before he ever met Bob, if you don't know when that day was?<br /> or do you have to say &quot;I want to target Jim as he was exactly a week ago&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T20:38:32-07:00","id":916603,"title":"","content":"Do Paradox Conditions give two arcane beats if you let them lapse? It says Resolution: Let the condition lapse, and also Arcane Beat: Let the condition lapse.<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> Why can Death transform people to Shadow, but Matter can't transform people to metal without Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T15:45:24-07:00","id":918279,"title":"","content":"So Peripheral Mage Sight senses all unconcealed supernatural effects. Peripheral Mage Sight is, in itself, an always active supernatural effect. Does this mean that mages trigger each other just by being around one another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T15:51:59-07:00","id":918282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=918279#post918279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Peripheral Mage Sight senses all unconcealed supernatural effects. Peripheral Mage Sight is, in itself, an always active supernatural effect. Does this mean that mages trigger each other just by being around one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>When their nimbus flares, I think. Also when they use an attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:00:18-07:00","id":918284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=918279#post918279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Peripheral Mage Sight senses all unconcealed supernatural effects. Peripheral Mage Sight is, in itself, an always active supernatural effect. Does this mean that mages trigger each other just by being around one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>Peripheral Sight doesn't sense things that are &quot;dormant&quot;. Ghost is supernatural, but Peripheral Sight won't alert you to it; it might alert you to Ghost using numina, however. Under this logic, Sight won't sense another Sight, but will a Sight that Sighted something can be Sighted by Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:05:29-07:00","id":918289,"title":"","content":"Right. Now say that five times fast. :-p <br /> <br /> Really, it was a good point one of my players mage; technically mage sight is stated to always be active, rather than activating in response to other effect. So it brought some confusion as to how to actually conceal oneself from another mage (which already is not easy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:08:03-07:00","id":918291,"title":"","content":"I would say it's a part of Mage's nature as much as unholy blood sustaining a Vampire or ephemera keeping Ghost together. I would leave the &quot;ping, something is going on&quot; for Active uses of Mage Sight, not Peripheral.<br /> <br /> Leave a &quot;Peripheral Mage Sight of other Mages pings my Peripheral Sight&quot; for a Banisher who went mad due to <i>all the noise, all the noise, the neverending noise.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:41:09-07:00","id":918308,"title":"","content":"Since mage sight is never stated as being activated, but instead the language is &quot;requires more concentration&quot; and &quot;put all attention on one target&quot;, I would say mage sight at any level doesn't meet the &quot;activated power&quot; trigger of Peripheral Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-20-2016, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:19:23-07:00","id":919585,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused on Rotes. The book says this: &quot;The caster of a Rote is considered to have five dots in the highest Arcanum used for purposes of how much free Reach she has.&quot;<br /> <br /> A friend of mine said that is only the case if the caster is casting it from a Grimoire or if you made the Rote yourself (I don't see the point of that considering you have to be a Master of the Arcanum anyways, so it wouldn't give you a boost). Is this true, or do you just get it from any Rote casting?<br /> <br /> If it's the latter, then that seems <i>waaay</i> overpowered in my eyes. I'm probably missing something though, so could someone fill me in on how it would not be overpowered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:28:00-07:00","id":919588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=919585#post919585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused on Rotes. The book says this: &quot;The caster of a Rote is considered to have five dots in the highest Arcanum used for purposes of how much free Reach she has.&quot;<br /> <br /> A friend of mine said that is only the case if the caster is casting it from a Grimoire or if you made the Rote yourself (I don't see the point of that considering you have to be a Master of the Arcanum anyways, so it wouldn't give you a boost). Is this true, or do you just get it from any Rote casting?<br /> <br /> If it's the latter, then that seems <i>waaay</i> overpowered in my eyes. I'm probably missing something though, so could someone fill me in on how it would not be overpowered?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get it from any rote casting. That's the primary reason you buy rotes.<br /> <br /> It's not overpowered because for the cost of four rotes, you could instead buy a whole arcana dot. First edition rotes didn't have anything like bonus Reach, and so were considered mostly worthless, and people hardly ever bought them. They're powerful in 2nd edition in order to make them worth buying. They allow you to take one or two dots in an arcanum, then take Rotes of the spells you care about most. In 1st edition, you didn't have this option and simply had to master the arcanum to get those benefits, which was a major disappointment, and also encouraged players to rush straight for 5 dots in an arcanum which caused all kinds of other problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-23-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:32:16-07:00","id":919589,"title":"","content":"Any Rote will give you this benefit. If you have an access to Grimoire, you may decide to double the ritual casting time to get a rote quality on the spell (reroll failed dice once).Masters can get this rote quality on any Rote they design themselves.<br /> Basically, your friend misremembered it.<br /> <br /> As for being overpowered, reach isn't really that strong, unless spell gives a really good unique reach options, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-23-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T05:04:20-07:00","id":919647,"title":"","content":"Nevermind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-23-2016, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T07:00:49-07:00","id":919683,"title":"","content":"Is the xp cost of buying new rotes 1xp flat straight or is it 1xp per dots of the spell? Example- buying a mind 3 rote costs 3 esperiente, 1 dot rote 1...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T07:05:42-07:00","id":919686,"title":"","content":"1 XP per Rote, so regardless of Spell Level is my understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T07:10:35-07:00","id":919687,"title":"","content":"1 XP per Rote is how I run it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T19:41:12-07:00","id":920731,"title":"","content":"According to the Experiences chart, it's 1 XP per dot, as the section above the number says &quot;Experiences per Dot&quot;. But then, in the Rote section of Spellcasting, it says that Rotes may be purchased at 1 XP a pop. Way to stay consistent, corebook!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:43:57-07:00","id":921200,"title":"","content":"Apart from Spells that rely solely on Potency, is there a good reason not to choose Praxes over Rotes? The Beat Economy doesn't look too slow to make them a viable alternative to Rotes, I just wonder if the benefits granted by them is worth foregoing the negotiation and/or personal sacrifice involved in learning Rotes instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:55:59-07:00","id":921207,"title":"","content":"From my understanding, it seems more of a story thing. That a Praxis is self taught via repeated use where a Rote is taught by another mage (or learned from a Grimoire). So, if there is no one in the region that knows the 'Pierce Deception' Rote, for example, then learning it as a Praxis might be your only choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T16:01:22-07:00","id":921210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=921200#post921200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from Spells that rely solely on Potency, is there a good reason not to choose Praxes over Rotes? The Beat Economy doesn't look too slow to make them a viable alternative to Rotes, I just wonder if the benefits granted by them is worth foregoing the negotiation and/or personal sacrifice involved in learning Rotes instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>This question feels like it flipped around in the middle somewhere.<br /> <br /> A Praxis is part of your Gnosis, with all the attendant upshots and downsides that entails, and you develop them for free as you strengthen your Gnosis. Rotes are most useful to characters who can't make them themselves, but the benefits of a Rote are still major enough that Masters will likely consider the investment made in any spell they codify as a Rote to be worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T17:17:25-07:00","id":921240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=921200#post921200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from Spells that rely solely on Potency, is there a good reason not to choose Praxes over Rotes? The Beat Economy doesn't look too slow to make them a viable alternative to Rotes, I just wonder if the benefits granted by them is worth foregoing the negotiation and/or personal sacrifice involved in learning Rotes instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotes benefit from the ability to use a skill as a mudra, which depending on your rank in a skill, is basically a Yantra that is anywhere between +1-+6, whereas most things are +1-+2 Yantras. In addition, the amount of Free Reach they have is equal to that of a master, even if you have an initiate rank in that rote. If you are a master, any rote that you make yourself has the rote quality aspect to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:08:10-07:00","id":921439,"title":"","content":"Might be the wrong thread to ask, but I didn't find another one, so: do we have an ETA when the PoD will become available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:05:35-07:00","id":921570,"title":"","content":"Is there any additional benefit to extra successes on a spellcasting roll besides getting an exceptional success? That is, is there any situation where it would matter that I got 4 successes rather than 1? Not counting situations where 3 successes grants exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:20:50-07:00","id":921577,"title":"","content":"Nope, extra successes have no benefit if they don't get you up to exceptional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:57:56-07:00","id":921601,"title":"","content":"No unless u use the dirty and down spellcasting sysyem in which case to my understanding successes are used to determine scale duration ecc... (?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:57:59-07:00","id":921602,"title":"","content":"What would it take to exchange momentum between targets? e.g. betweena human and a train to send a poor fellow flying into a wall with 150km/h. <br /> Is it 3rd dot Reach effect? Adept spell or do i need a additional 2 dots in Space?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:47:30-07:00","id":921638,"title":"","content":"Im not even sure Adept would be required. Your not changing the force in any, only changing what it affects. Either way Space not required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:01:23-07:00","id":921642,"title":"","content":"Yea, I thought so too but you can't really switch positions with your friend using Life. On any level. You need Space. Orrr I might be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 06-26-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T05:48:28-07:00","id":921946,"title":"","content":"If you start with the Familiar merit, does your familiar gain the Familiar Bond condition or is that reserved for those who use the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:24:18-07:00","id":922027,"title":"","content":"It would start with that Condition because starting with the Merit presumes that someone cast the spell for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:46:38-07:00","id":923035,"title":"","content":"Given how easy it is for mages to make money via magic, would it damage anything to let a mage treat half the most relevant Arcana (round up) as resource dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:02:13-07:00","id":923046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=923035#post923035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how easy it is for mages to make money via magic, would it damage anything to let a mage treat half the most relevant Arcana (round up) as resource dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no, because using magic to make money tends to lead to fun plot hooks and complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T20:40:52-07:00","id":923673,"title":"","content":"noticed Enchanted Items on the character sheet but where are the rules for enchanting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:49:48-07:00","id":923701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=923673#post923673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">noticed Enchanted Items on the character sheet but where are the rules for enchanting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of these items are talked about in the Merits section of Chapter 3, but generally require Prime 4 and 2-3 dots of an appropriate Arcana for the effect you're after. Matter 2 makes it easier to temporarily alter Items for a longer time, but at that level, only a few effects in the book are really handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-30-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T21:41:05-07:00","id":924293,"title":"","content":"For newly Awaken mages, what would be some interesting Mysteries to have them do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:33:06-07:00","id":924472,"title":"","content":"A mage in USA can summon a Tengu spirit from Japan Shadow with only SPIRIT 3 or need SPIRIT3+SPACE 3/4 to &quot;teleport&quot; the Spirit from Japan to Usa ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:55:17-07:00","id":924483,"title":"","content":"He needs Space 2 to inform the spirit ( it then must travel to the mage by foot) or Space 3/4 ( i dont remember) to teleport it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:15:27-07:00","id":924515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=924293#post924293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For newly Awaken mages, what would be some interesting Mysteries to have them do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slashers/Suicides, impossible robberies, the ever-popular fifth-degree Masquerade Breach (with or without crossover), towns unstuck in time, &quot;haunted&quot; houses, Mad Kings...<br /> I could go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:07:16-07:00","id":924576,"title":"","content":"Is the Opacity rating of a given Mystery supposed to be something a mage can just tell at a glance, before they do any of the deeper investigation actions? Like should I just be stating &quot;this weird idol is Opacity 5&quot; when my PCs show interest in poking it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:27:41-07:00","id":924586,"title":"","content":"No, you shouldn't. Its a Mystery so keep it hidden. But maybe some spell could Unveil how deep the Mystery is - Prime or Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:01:48-07:00","id":924605,"title":"","content":"Now that I think of it, should I not be explicitly telling them the Opacity rating at all? In my first few sessions I've been walking them through the new rules by saying &quot;okay so this thing has Opacity 4&quot; as they start to do Scrutiny, and explicitly telling them when they break through a layer and how many more successes they need to get to the next one. Plus, I would think it would be obvious what the Opacity is as soon as someone attempts Revelation and I say &quot;take a -4 penalty&quot;. But even that might be better than an explicit statement.<br /> <br /> My concern is that if I don't tell them the Opacity and let them know when they break through a layer, there isn't going to be a sense of progression or getting closer to the answer. I also don't really want to &quot;trick&quot; my players by having them waste Mana to add successes when they only needed one, for example. On the other hand, they aren't supposed to know automatically how much Health an enemy has left, and combat seems to work well enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 07-01-2016, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:38:22-07:00","id":924626,"title":"","content":"Revelation is a one roll per player and you can do it yourself, iguess. With Scrutiny just describe what they found when they breach level of Opacity.<br /> This thread might be of some help: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/923119-2e-what-mage-sight-can-show\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...sight-can-show</a><br /> The important thing is that I prefer words then numbers on dices so I try to describe without using system specific language whenever I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:57:35-07:00","id":924633,"title":"","content":"I don't think the &quot;betting&quot; mechanic of spending mana really works right unless you tell them the Opacity. I mean, I wouldn't have mages going around and saying &quot;yeah, this Mystery is Opacity 3&quot; but it's good to be explicit about mechanics with players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:17:36-07:00","id":924640,"title":"","content":"Successes from mana are not lost except the case when you already went through all the layers of Opacity. Which is kind of normal when you bruteforce the Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:46:07-07:00","id":924651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=115616#post115616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you don't want to go into Twilight, use Space. It lets you cause two objects to occupy the same space without interacting with one another, or with interacting with one another destructively as the mage chooses. That seems pretty close to what you're aiming for with phasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of twilight like Frequencies, with different kinds of being as either sharing bandwidth (and thus can interact) or not. Death is the bandwidth of ghost, and possibly if adjusted properly, Strix on a different bandwidth within the same arcanum. While both are beings of death I think they'd appear drastically different through Death Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Detective Lawrence 'Morgan Freeman' Appleton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I don't know very much about other dimensions and all that. I'm an old school Catholic. I believe in Hell. I believe that it's more than just murderers and rapists down there. I believe in demons and worms, vile shit in the grease trap of the Universe. And the more I think about it, the more I think that it's not just some place down there. Oh no, that it's right here with us. We just can't perceive it. It's kinda like the country music radio station. It's out there in the air, even if you don't tune into it.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:57:49-07:00","id":924657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=924651#post924651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think of twilight like Frequencies, with different kinds of being as either sharing bandwidth (and thus can interact) or not. Death is the bandwidth of ghost, and possibly if adjusted properly, Strix on a different bandwidth within the same arcanum. While both are beings of death I think they'd appear drastically different through Death Mage Sight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Strix are not in Twilight (unless they use the one specific power which does put them into it).<br /> <br /> They're made out of shadows and Vitae, though, so the Death Arcanum works on them. Just utilising an entirey different part of Death's purview to casting sells on ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:58:46-07:00","id":924659,"title":"","content":"Just a heads up about Strix: They are completely physical albeit made of shadows and smoke. They don't have a Twilight frequency of their own. At a high level of Shadow Potency, they do have gifts that allow them to be immaterial and even jump into the Shadow, but most Strix don't have that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:35:31-07:00","id":924672,"title":"","content":"That does bring up the question of what &quot;frequency&quot; of twilight Strix are in when they DO use the twilight form embodiment; can they interact with any other ephemeral entities, like ghosts for instance, or do they create yet another spectrum entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T17:22:32-07:00","id":924686,"title":"","content":"Blood &amp; Smoke p207, 'While in Twilight, the Strix enjoys complete intangibility \u2014 it may pass, unnoticed, through solid objects, and the damage it suffers fro banes is reduced by one type (to nothing if already Bashing.) It can perceive and interact with ghosts and spirits, attack them as though it were Materialized, and even feed on their Corpus by eating their \u201cflesh,\u201d gaining one Vitae per three Corpus consumed.'<br /> <br /> There's another mention of them using it to feast on ghosts and spirits, so presumably they hop on and overlap their frequencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-01-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:18:26-07:00","id":924698,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think they Twilight form spans all Twilight frequencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:10:30-07:00","id":924724,"title":"","content":"Ah, I hadn't actually read it in a bit. That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:23:48-07:00","id":924748,"title":"","content":"Quick question on Legacies: I'm a little confused with the qualifiers. Do you have to be a member of a specific Path, and a member of (a) certain Order(s), or is it a bit more freeform?<br /> Using the Eleventh Question as an example, the corebook says, &quot;Moros, Guardians of the Veil, or Mysterium.&quot; So do you have to be a Moros, but be of any Order? Could you be a member of those two Orders, but any Path? Or do you have to be a Moros of one of those two Orders?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:31:51-07:00","id":924752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=924748#post924748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question on Legacies: I'm a little confused with the qualifiers. Do you have to be a member of a specific Path, and a member of (a) certain Order(s), or is it a bit more freeform?<br /> Using the Eleventh Question as an example, the corebook says, &quot;Moros, Guardians of the Veil, or Mysterium.&quot; So do you have to be a Moros, but be of any Order? Could you be a member of those two Orders, but any Path? Or do you have to be a Moros of one of those two Orders?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to hit at least one of the three criteria on top of the Knowledge and Indoctrination requirements for initiation, but you don't need to hit all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Path, Order or Praxis:</b> All Legacies possess an originating Path, and many (though not all) are connected to an Order. <b>Normally, your mage must either belong to the Legacy\u2019s Path <u>or</u> Order. However, it is possible for a mage of any Path or Order to join a Legacy if she learns a Praxis that duplicates the Legacy\u2019s first Attainment, and utilizes one of the Legacy\u2019s Yantras.</b> She develops the understanding to join without other requirements. Note that some Legacies possess unusual Attainments that make this impossible. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:35:03-07:00","id":924753,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I forgot that bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:39:33-07:00","id":924755,"title":"","content":"As far as Twilight bandwidth frequencies go, I think Mummies break it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T21:40:12-07:00","id":924769,"title":"","content":"First edition didn't have separate frequencies, so Mummy is working off the idea that Twilight is a state where all ephemerals freely interact with each other as well as with solid matter entities that can enter Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T15:44:51-07:00","id":925076,"title":"","content":"Are Veiling spells trigring peripheral mage sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:17:59-07:00","id":925119,"title":"","content":"Probably, but you don't know what's triggering your PMS, and apparently Mages are under an incessant deluge of PMS triggers so they won't necessarily think anything of it unless they're suspicious already. Prime, Mind or Death could be used to Veil a spell so it doesn't trigger PMS though.<br /> <br /> Alternatively I'd allow Reach clauses on Veiling spells like, Reach +1: When a Mage loses the Clash of Wills against your Veil he doesn't realize there was a CoW. Reach: +2 Your Veil doesn't ping PMS, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-02-2016, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:31:14-07:00","id":925153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=925119#post925119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, but you don't know what's triggering your PMS, and apparently Mages are under an incessant deluge of PMS triggers so they won't necessarily think anything of it unless they're suspicious already. Prime, Mind or Death could be used to Veil a spell so it doesn't trigger PMS though.<br /> <br /> Alternatively I'd allow Reach clauses on Veiling spells like, Reach +1: When a Mage loses the Clash of Wills against your Veil he doesn't realize there was a CoW. Reach: +2 Your Veil doesn't ping PMS, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't help myself, it's just too good to let it pass \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/c9/6a/51/c96a514ba188b403710969a55f743584.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 07-02-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T01:26:01-07:00","id":925263,"title":"","content":"I thought veiling and similarly concealing powers didn't ping PMS?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T01:28:31-07:00","id":925266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=924769#post924769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition didn't have separate frequencies, so Mummy is working off the idea that Twilight is a state where all ephemerals freely interact with each other as well as with solid matter entities that can enter Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading somewhere that Twilight is not a place, it's a state of being. Essentially, anything that is insubstantial or incorporeal is considered to be 'in Twilight' and that any being in Twilight can only interact with others of its own kind, or who became that way via similar methods. For example; if a mage uses Death to become incorporeal, they won't be able to physically interact with one who uses Spirit to become an incorporeal spirit, because they're in different versions of Twilight.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can get a quote and page number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T03:54:14-07:00","id":925293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=925263#post925263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought veiling and similarly concealing powers didn't ping PMS?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it was the case in 1ed (but I might be wrong). Prime was able to conceal any spell cast by you and it cost 1 mana - but it was an attainment. <br /> <br /> \u200bI like that way of thinking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>. I would personally go with +2 Reach: Spend 1 mana call upon Supernal symbol of Veiling to make sure that this (Veiling) spell does not trigger PMS<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spells that directly call upon the perfection of<br /> the Supernal Realms require a point of Mana. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T05:41:40-07:00","id":925308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=925263#post925263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought veiling and similarly concealing powers didn't ping PMS?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2E, page 90</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any supernatural attempt at concealment<br /> hides the effect from the mage, without a Clash of Wills or any<br /> other mechanical effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T06:59:04-07:00","id":925320,"title":"","content":"I must have missed that part... Thanks!<br /> <br /> So if i veil targets equilibrioception he just falls down without PMS and can suspect that he has a stroke? Unless he activates Mind or Life Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:12:17-07:00","id":925371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CarnivalCash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=925266#post925266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere that Twilight is not a place, it's a state of being. Essentially, anything that is insubstantial or incorporeal is considered to be 'in Twilight' and that any being in Twilight can only interact with others of its own kind, or who became that way via similar methods. For example; if a mage uses Death to become incorporeal, they won't be able to physically interact with one who uses Spirit to become an incorporeal spirit, because they're in different versions of Twilight.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can get a quote and page number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's how it works in second edition, including Mage the Awakening second edition. In first edition there were no different frequencies, and everything interacted with everything else. Mummy is a first edition game.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken first edition core book, p252, 'Ghosts, as described in the World of Darkness Rulebook, share several qualities in common with the spirits of the Shadow Realm, but are not the same thing. Both are ephemeral entities \u2014 when present in the physical world, they do not have a solid, material form, but are instead in an intangible, ephemeral state (that of Twilight). A ghost and a spirit can see, touch or otherwise interact with one another, as they are in the same ephemeral state.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:30:36-07:00","id":925379,"title":"","content":"I thought that Veiling spell being cast pings PMS like any other effect, but once it starts working, it becomes less detectable as a part of it's effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:45:11-07:00","id":925387,"title":"","content":"No a Veiling spell does not ping PMs, if it would it would be kinda useless. Remember there is a Prime 2 spell that can veil spells from triggering PMS, if that spell pinged PMS by itself it would be completely pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T10:38:20-07:00","id":925405,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the Spell does not ping PMS but the act of casting the veiling spell would if it were cast within range of the PMS. This would still not tell the Mage what was cast, but that -something- supernatural was just actively used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:04:19-07:00","id":925412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Peripheral Mage Sight is always active. The mage sees \u2014 rather,<br /> perceives \u2014 magical occurrences through the lens of her Path and<br /> Nimbus. Many mages experience the Periphery through senses<br /> other than sight. A sensual Mastigos might feel brushing, light<br /> touches on his skin, while an Acanthus might hear mercurial<br /> laughter. Many Moros sense the supernatural through their<br /> sense of smell, tasting decay and chemicals on the air. Deeper<br /> levels of Mage Sight rely on knowledge of the Arcana, but the<br /> Periphery<b> responds to all supernatural events.</b><br /> Note, however, that Peripheral Mage Sight notices only active<br /> supernatural effects. <b>Any supernatural attempt at concealment<br /> hides the effect from the mage, without a Clash of Wills or any<br /> other mechanical effect.</b> Peripheral Mage Sight, for instance,<br /> doesn\u2019t detect a ghost lurking quietly in Twilight. If the ghost<br /> spends Essence, activates a Numen, or Manifests, however, this<br /> attracts the mage\u2019s attention.<br /> Nor does Peripheral Mage Sight give any clues as to what just<br /> happened \u2014 only that magic is afoot. If the mage doesn\u2019t have<br /> the Death Arcanum to use Active Mage Sight with, the ghost<br /> will remain a nagging sensation of something out of place at<br /> the edge of the mage\u2019s perceptions. </div> </div> </div>It goes deeper then spell and is changing the game dramatically. Any splat that is activating concealment power is undetectable by PMS.<br /> Other effects trigger PMS only on activation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:36:35-07:00","id":925430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CarnivalCash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=925266#post925266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember reading somewhere that Twilight is not a place, it's a state of being. Essentially, anything that is insubstantial or incorporeal is considered to be 'in Twilight' and that any being in Twilight can only interact with others of its own kind, or who became that way via similar methods. For example; if a mage uses Death to become incorporeal, they won't be able to physically interact with one who uses Spirit to become an incorporeal spirit, because they're in different versions of Twilight.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can get a quote and page number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage: the Awakening, Pp. 253-4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T13:48:48-07:00","id":925482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=925412#post925412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It goes deeper then spell and is changing the game dramatically. Any splat that is activating concealment power is undetectable by PMS.<br /> Other effects trigger PMS only on activation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is correct. Thanks for adding the quote. <br /> <br /> Personally, this is not a dramatic change for me as I remember some part of 1E also mentioned something very similar. Although it might have been from errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:14:28-07:00","id":926875,"title":"","content":"Something I've wondered ever since the CT development blog was published and haven't gotten a solid answer in the official book: Can a Master of Forces create a nuclear explosion through the practice of Making? In 1E, Nuclear Cascade was a 6-dot Forces spell, but I suspect that might've been done due to the &quot;speed bumps&quot; of 1E's spell design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:19:46-07:00","id":926879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=926875#post926875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've wondered ever since the CT development blog was published and haven't gotten a solid answer in the official book: Can a Master of Forces create a nuclear explosion through the practice of Making? In 1E, Nuclear Cascade was a 6-dot Forces spell, but I suspect that might've been done due to the &quot;speed bumps&quot; of 1E's spell design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuclear forces aren't treated specially by the system in 2E, so Making can create them, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T00:34:54-07:00","id":926898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=926879#post926879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuclear forces aren't treated specially by the system in 2E, so Making can create them, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuclear Cascade messes with the process of fission, not the existence of radiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T00:42:05-07:00","id":926902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=926898#post926898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuclear Cascade messes with the process of fission, not the existence of radiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay?<br /> <br /> It still wouldn't require Dynamics to 'create a nuclear explosion' in 2E. You can create <i>any</i> force from nothing with Making.<br /> 'Messing with' a nuclear process wouldn't even require that much. This was one of the most major effects of switching to strict adherence to the Practices instead of arbitrarily saying 'this one thing under your Arcanum's purview is harder', such as Nuclear forces, Median Life, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T00:55:28-07:00","id":926906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=926902#post926902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was one of the most major effects of switching to strict adherence to the Practices instead of arbitrarily saying 'this one thing under your Arcanum's purview is harder', such as Nuclear forces, Median Life, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may notice that the Arcanum's 2e purview does not list &quot;nuclear forces&quot; and that the spell specifically interacts with the chain reaction that makes a nuclear explosion actually produce an explosion instead of just a lot of radiation.<br /> <br /> You may further note that Create Energy has rules for simply generating radiation across an area that do not fit the described effects of Nuclear Cascade's explosive option and that chain reactions are exactly the kind of thing that Dynamics spells specifically handle.<br /> <br /> Not all nuclear energy is a nuclear explosion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T01:09:27-07:00","id":926912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=926906#post926906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may notice that the Arcanum's 2e purview does not list &quot;nuclear forces&quot; and that the spell specifically interacts with the chain reaction that makes a nuclear explosion actually produce an explosion instead of just a lot of radiation.<br /> <br /> You may further note that Create Energy has rules for simply generating radiation across an area that do not fit the described effects of Nuclear Cascade's explosive option and that chain reactions are exactly the kind of thing that Dynamics spells specifically handle.<br /> <br /> Not all nuclear energy is a nuclear explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why you keep focusing on Nuclear Cascade, the question wasn't whether one could duplicate its effects, it was about creating a nuclear explosion, and mentioned Cascade as the only published option to do so in 1E.<br /> <br /> An explosion (nuclear or otherwise) is still a force (or rather, a combination of several forces), and still under the purview of Forces via Creative Thaumaturgy. The following isn't really debatable; A nuclear explosion results in radiation, sound light, heat, fire, and movement. All of this explicitly falls under Forces.<br /> <br /> <b>You don't have to cause a nuclear reaction</b>, you can create all of those forces ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to cause a nuclear reaction leading to an explosion, then yes, Dynamics would be required. It would also be Matter (imo) more than Forces, but that's not really relevant to the discussion.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, it'd be a lot simpler to just use Advanced Scale + Unmaking to destroy everything within the area with the force of your choice and combine it with a spell (using the combined spell rules) to create radiation in a larger area, if you really want to duplicate the mechanical effects of Cascade without archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 07-06-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T06:02:04-07:00","id":927009,"title":"","content":"You definitely can create something like a nuclear explosion with forces, though you might run into scale and/or potency problems relatively quick. Just for the blast alone without radiation or heat you need about a 5 km radius from the explosion center for a small nuclear bomb. You might also say you create a small explosion which has enough potency to create a 5 km blast radius, but I don't really know how I would handle that as a ST. Probably 100 potency or something like it? If you want to duplicate a real nuclear explosion you have to add the radiation, heat and x-rays on top of it. So for a single mage, probably not a thing before archmastery.<br /> So it is probably far easier to go through a real nuclear chain reaction. For that you would need matter 4 or 5 to get enough material for a critical mass and forces 5 to start the reaction via neutron bombardment. And probably space to get the hell outta there or rather cast the forces spell via scrying.<br /> <br /> If all you want is destroy a lot of area:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=926912#post926912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Actually, it'd be a lot simpler to just use Advanced Scale + Unmaking to destroy everything within the area with the force of your choice and combine it with a spell (using the combined spell rules) to create radiation in a larger area, if you really want to duplicate the mechanical effects of Cascade without archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: Just realized that area is capped at &quot;campus / small neighborhood&quot;, so creating your own magical nuclear bomb, might actually be the way to go for mass destruction as a single mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 07-06-2016, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T06:20:32-07:00","id":927019,"title":"","content":"Calling for 100 Potency to make a nuclear blast sounds very arbitrary, do you have any actual grounding in the rules to make that call?<br /> <br /> Also, Scale isn't capped, at the bottom of the chart is a guideline for continuing to increase Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T06:29:17-07:00","id":927020,"title":"","content":"Creative Thaumaturgy mentions that effects which have multiple possible states and scales of success could and sometimes should be gated by Potency. Of course, it doesn't provide you with actual guidelines for that, so his 100 Potency is as good as someone else's 5 Potency.<br /> I think it would be definitely possible to create a guideline for this, but it would require picking and sticking to a &quot;target mood&quot;, and doing some analysis of how numbers work in the game to get the feel of what is a lot and what is not a lot. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:13:32-07:00","id":927030,"title":"","content":"As someone pointed out to me, I told a small lie - the book suggests you a guideline; the extended action difficuilty one.<br /> That would put easy tasks at 5 Potency, &quot;Professional tasks&quot; at 10 Potency, and &quot;hard tasks&quot; at 20 Potency, which doesn't seem to play with Potency ranges too well, as you probably will never see a Potency +10 Spell in a standard game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:27:29-07:00","id":927039,"title":"","content":"Not without group casting anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:03:14-07:00","id":927108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=927019#post927019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling for 100 Potency to make a nuclear blast sounds very arbitrary, do you have any actual grounding in the rules to make that call?<br /> <br /> Also, Scale isn't capped, at the bottom of the chart is a guideline for continuing to increase Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Area is capped, but then why would you need more than a few tens of square miles to simulate a nuclear blast? That would be the equivalent of a low-yield strategic device, with consequences of its own.<br /> <br /> Also, Potency 30 on a combined Forces 5 Making, Matter 5 Unmaking spell, with max Advanced Scale, should do the job, and give the appropriate cosmetics. Might also need Life 5 to kill the organics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 07-06-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:49:51-07:00","id":927137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=927108#post927108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might also need Life 5 to kill the organics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The current Forces 5 unmaking spell kills organics just fine, so I don't think this should be necessary.<br /> <br /> Honestly, unmaking via almost any of the Arcana can be used to kill people creatively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T03:19:26-07:00","id":928038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=927108#post927108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Area is capped, but then why would you need more than a few tens of square miles to simulate a nuclear blast? That would be the equivalent of a low-yield strategic device, with consequences of its own.<br /> <br /> Also, Potency 30 on a combined Forces 5 Making, Matter 5 Unmaking spell, with max Advanced Scale, should do the job, and give the appropriate cosmetics. Might also need Life 5 to kill the organics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need more than a couple of tens of square miles to simulate a small nuclear blast, but that is by far exeeding the scale factors. Highest scale factor is a small neiborhood or a campus. Paris e.g. has 105 km\u00b2 of actual area! Bombing away 25 km\u00b2 of those is one quarter. And that is kilometers not miles. So the highest scale factor is somewhere in between 1 and 10 km\u00b2/miles\u00b2, roughly ten times smaller, than an actual nuclear blast.<br /> You CAN actually go via subjects. If you take Hiroshima as example you actually only need -19 for scale for the 80.000 victims. But that would mean a nuclear blast spell is fairly easy in an unpopulated area, which makes no sense at all to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway your argument might be now: I don't need that scale, I just create an explosion in an 1 m\u00b3 cube with such a force, that the resulting blast wave travels about 5 km from the point of origin. THAT blast, would in my opinion need something like 100 potency. This number IS totally arbitrary, beside the fact, that it should be really high in my opinion. But it also is kind of a really stupid spell imho.<br /> <br /> In any case, if you don't just aim for max destruction, but for some kind of reason really want a nuclear blast, going the route to just create a critical mass via matter and setting it of, seems to be by far the easiest solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T04:23:11-07:00","id":928052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=928038#post928038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, if you don't just aim for max destruction, but for some kind of reason really want a nuclear blast, going the route to just create a critical mass via matter and setting it of, seems to be by far the easiest solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my ignorance of nuclear principles talking, but would it be possible to create a critical mass that doesn't need any further action to detonate as soon as it exists? Do all critical mass require action by an outside force to detonate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T05:05:54-07:00","id":928063,"title":"","content":"Usually yes. As far as I am aware every material which is able to sustain a nuclear chain reaction radiates neutrons in it's decay and is therefore able to detonate. If you got enough material so that the natural decay sets of the chain reaction, you got a critical mass. If you use outside neutron radiation this critical mass simply gets smaller and you can set of the chain reaction more precisely. You could also use a second kind of material with a stronger natural decay and therefore more radiation to set of your fissile mass. And you kind of need a neutron reflector if you don't want to use outside radiation. But overall: a mage with matter 5 and some science background can create a nuclear bomb pretty easily without even needing forces to set it of, yes.<br /> On that notion: a mage with matter 5, can probably also just create antimatter. That would... well scale up the destruction quite a bit. This is actually a really really scary thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T05:27:20-07:00","id":928070,"title":"","content":"Matter 4 would work as well, possibly even just Matter 3 if it's simply placing a particular quality of possible fission onto a normally non-fissile material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:52:45-07:00","id":928225,"title":"","content":"Of course, if you're more interested in massive destruction than fallout, casting a sympathetic range Patterning Forces spell on a couple dozen satellites would do the job, as would a Making spell conjuring a 30 ton spar of heavy metal (I vote Tungsten or Uranium) into a decaying orbit, with less necessary Arcana levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:08:18-07:00","id":928325,"title":"","content":"Can I use Mind on spirits without having conjuctional Spirit dots? E.g Incognito Presence spell<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Incognito Presence </b>(Mind \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> The mage causes people to look past the subject, their minds<br /> forgetting her the moment they stop looking at her. In essence,<br /> people believe she is not there. When people look at her, they<br /> want to avert their eyes, or barely notice her presence. People<br /> cannot remember seeing her when they are no longer looking<br /> her way. Anyone attempting to maintain his gaze on her or<br /> remember her may do so with a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach: </b>Only beings with Active Mage Sight, or a supernatural<br /> ability that allows a Clash of Wills may concentrate on<br /> the subject to notice her. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:10:19-07:00","id":928326,"title":"","content":"By the book yes, and on ghosts or anything else with a mind as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:13:19-07:00","id":928329,"title":"","content":"Thanks! What in the case of SI?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:35:50-07:00","id":928344,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the question. Do you mean AI? If so, yes, if it has a mind then Mind works on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:38:19-07:00","id":928346,"title":"","content":"Im sorry... Thats an abreviation from my language... I meant Artificial Inteligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T18:25:04-07:00","id":928543,"title":"","content":"Are ruling spells really supposed to create effects that mimic increasing skills and Merits? Example of a Creative Thaumaturgy Ruling spell working in such way is &quot;raising a corpse to follow your commands&quot;, but in actual spell lists, such a spell is a Weaving Spell. That One Mind Spell which increases your Skill is also a Perfecting Spell. <br /> <br /> Also,I'm failing to understand why Exceptional Luck is a 2nd Dot spell - Tilts are supposed to require Fraying or Patterning,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T21:48:52-07:00","id":928587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=928543#post928543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are ruling spells really supposed to create effects that mimic increasing skills and Merits? Example of a Creative Thaumaturgy Ruling spell working in such way is &quot;raising a corpse to follow your commands&quot;, but in actual spell lists, such a spell is a Weaving Spell. That One Mind Spell which increases your Skill is also a Perfecting Spell.<br /> <br /> Also,I'm failing to understand why Exceptional Luck is a 2nd Dot spell - Tilts are supposed to require Fraying or Patterning,</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see your example in the pdf, so this may be a version difference. That Perfecting spell you talk of has very broad application that goes beyond what comparable Ruling spells, especially those in Mind, are capable of. Most of the Ruling spells adhere to an internally consistent theme, related to the Arcana in question, so in the case of Mind, you are using magic to nudge other minds to respond in a more desirable fashion, which is why most of the example Mind Ruling spells boost Social Skills or manipulate the Social Maneuvering system, among other things; Enhance Skill, on the other hand, is more akin to reprogramming a computer, hence it being a Perfecting spell. The thing that you have to keep in mind is that the Practices are there at different levels to give you an idea of how limited a given Practice is.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: the Awakening, Second Edition, Ch.4: Magic, Practices; Pp. 126</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Conditions &amp; Tilts</span><br /> As pre-packaged blocks of rules already designed to fit into a lot of different systems, Conditions are an excellent source of inspiration for long-lasting spells. Because the effects of Conditions and Tilts are so broad, it\u2019s difficult to assign hard-and-fast rules for Practices that inflict them. Use the Practice descriptions and the following list as a guideline:<ul><li>Compelling (\u2022) spells can\u2019t create Conditions out of whole cloth, but can intensify phenomena that already exist to inflict Conditions. A Compelling spell can make someone who\u2019s already nervous Spooked, for example, but can\u2019t make someone who\u2019s uninterested in the mage romantically Swooning.</li> <li>Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spells can create <u>most non-Persistent, mundane</u> Conditions. Supernatural Conditions, such as the Soulless Condition and its sequelae or Manifestation Conditions, generally require a Weaving (\u2022\u2022\u2022) spell.</li> <li>Creating a <u>Persistent Condition</u> is almost always a Patterning (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Unraveling (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) effect.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>None of the Conditions and Tilts created by Exceptional Luck are Persistent, nor are they supernatural in of themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T02:00:22-07:00","id":928651,"title":"","content":"Read a bit further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tilts are usually created by applying a Reach to an attack <br /> spell, but if you want to create one on its own, it\u2019s usually <br /> a Fraying (\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Patterning (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) spell. </div> </div> </div>Ex!Luck creates Tilts without being either an attack spell, a Fraying Spell, or a Patterning Spell. <br /> <br /> And according to the Creative Thaumaturgy, Ruling is enough to give you Merit or Skill dots, so stuff like Enhance Skill should be Ruling. This lack of internal consistency is killing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:27:17-07:00","id":928800,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't see an inconsistency, because both spells are on theme, but YMMV. and then there's this wrinkle:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Many Roads</span><br /> Astute players will likely figure out a multitude of ways to accomplish similar effects with different Arcana, sometimes at different dot levels. This is okay. Just because a Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022 spell can do a thing doesn\u2019t mean a Forces \u2022 spell that does a similar thing is \u201cbroken\u201d or should be disallowed. Take for example influencing the outcome of a coin toss. A simple Compelling of Fate can easily tip the odds toward either heads or tails, but it\u2019s theoretically possible to use a Forces Fraying spell to alter the kinetic energy imparted to the coin, causing it to spin slower, or use a Matter Weaving spell to change the coin\u2019s center of mass. Both are perhaps more complicated than the Fate approach, but they\u2019re valid within the purview of their respective Arcana. Similarly, a Mind Weaving spell could force a target to feel love, while a Life Ruling spell could cause the target\u2019s brain to release dopamine and other hormones that create a similar effect. </div> </div> </div>Of course, the other thing to keep in mind is that Fate, Mind, Space, and Time are the most gamest Arcana of the 10, despite the depth of narrative potential those Arcana provide. They most directly engage and modulate the System, often times well before the other Arcana come close, so of course what their practices can accomplish may seem a little out of sync with the other Arcana. I think you aren't considering that different Arcana are better at dealing with different things than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 07-09-2016, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:02:31-07:00","id":931079,"title":"","content":"I actually found the answer to the Enhance Skill thing; Dave mentioned in errata thread that the &quot;gain a skill&quot; thing was initially at 2nd dot, but was moved to 3rd, and current CT is bugged in that regard.<br /> <br /> Quick question:<br /> Bolster Spirit and Quicken Ghost allow you to give target ephemeral a new Manifestation. One of possible Manifestations is Possession. While possesing someone, ephemeral beings can heal their vessel by spending Essence.<br /> Does this basically mean that you can get your Familiar or commanded Entity, Quicken it with Possession, allow them to posses yourself or someone else, and use it as a healing tool?<br /> Our group has a Thyrsus, but she has Life 1, and I wonder if we can use her Familiar as a creepy healbot this way. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-13-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:16:05-07:00","id":931086,"title":"","content":"I'm STing a new PbP game and I'm trying to refine my knowledge on some of the new 2E rules for some miscellaneous topics.<br /> <br /> First, do ghouls still count as Sleepers for the purpose of Dissonance/Quiescence and increasing paradox? I assume not, as they're pseudo-supernatural beings, but they're still human. What about wolfblooded?<br /> <br /> Second, are mages affected by conditions caused by Kindred feeding (scarred/swooning)? What about the predatory aura conditions? What happens, if anything, to Kindred who feed on mages?<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'll have more, but those were ones I was trying to make sense of as I skim through multiple 2E CoD books at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:26:07-07:00","id":931089,"title":"","content":"Anything that has some kind of Supernatural power - be it a merit, a template, and so on - counts as not-Sleeper for Dissonance/Quiescence and Paradox. <br /> Mages are not immune to the Lashing Out - they oppose it with their Nimbus. Rules for that are in nimbus chapter, under something titled like &quot;Nimbus and Other Auras&quot;.<br /> There are no specifics on what happens when Kindred feeds on Mage, so it's your choice. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:29:43-07:00","id":931091,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks!<br /> <br /> Another one that I'm sure is answered somewhere, but not sure where to look...What is the easiest way to look through a crowd and see who is a supernatural creature (Kindred, werewolf, mage, etc.)? Is that something you can do with Active Sight, Focused Sight, or some kind of Unveiling/Knowing spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:30:02-07:00","id":931092,"title":"","content":"....<br /> Ok. Banishers don't get their Integrity replaced with Wisdom. So, basically, they can take the Sleeper Merits from Sleeper chapter, ones with requirements of &quot;Integrity&quot;, am I correct?<br /> They are SCAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAARY. Look what a Banisher with &quot;Liar&quot; and a &quot;Communal Sleeper&quot; can do. Hohohohhohohohohohohohohohoh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-13-2016, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:38:02-07:00","id":931095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931091#post931091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thanks!<br /> <br /> Another one that I'm sure is answered somewhere, but not sure where to look...What is the easiest way to look through a crowd and see who is a supernatural creature (Kindred, werewolf, mage, etc.)? Is that something you can do with Active Sight, Focused Sight, or some kind of Unveiling/Knowing spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no easy way. Supernal Vision allows you to modify your sight to divine up such things, but you need to STUDY the target. You can't just look at a crowd and see if someone is glowing; you need to study each one individually, and that takes minimum of one turn per person. Generally, if you *suspect* that someone might be supernatural, it's pretty easy, but it's hard to pick the right guy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-13-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:52:00-07:00","id":931100,"title":"","content":"From Active Mage Sight section: Death Sight allows a mage to detect the presence of the<br /> Anchor Condition (p. 258) or manifested ghosts and related<br /> phenomena. With a glance, a mage using Mage Sight can tell if<br /> someone has a soul, or if a body is, in fact, dead.<br /> <br /> Active Mage Sight is specifically the phase before scrutinizing an individual subject, so yes, I imagine they can pick a vampire out of the crowd pretty easily. They won't -know- it's a vampire though, just that this corpse seems to be walking around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:55:40-07:00","id":931102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931095#post931095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no easy way. Supernal Vision allows you to modify your sight to divine up such things, but you need to STUDY the target. You can't just look at a crowd and see if someone is glowing; you need to study each one individually, and that takes minimum of one turn per person. Generally, if you *suspect* that someone might be supernatural, it's pretty easy, but it's hard to pick the right guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, so it's something that you can do with Focused Sight? Scrutinize the target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T18:27:26-07:00","id":931118,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, undead have it harder because both Life and Dead sights should pick them up.<br /> Stuff like Claimed might be detectable by Spirit glance. Not comfortable with Werewolf. z<br /> <br /> Focused Sight can potentially tell you everything and nothing, depending on involved Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:06:04-07:00","id":931205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931102#post931102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotcha, so it's something that you can do with Focused Sight? Scrutinize the target?</div> </div> </div> </div>Focused sight/scrutiny would work if you used the appropriate Arcanum for their supernatural nature (such as Death for a vampire or their ghoul), it's just a question of whether you as ST want that to be Surface or Deep information. But &quot;Supernal Vision&quot; refers specifically to a Prime 1 spell of that name which can reveal supernatural natures, not a Mage Sight effect. Mind 1 &quot;Mental Scan&quot; and Life 1 &quot;Analyze Life&quot; can also tell you that a target is supernatural in various ways.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Unrelated question about spells like Ghost Shield and Ephemeral Shield that grant a Clash of Wills against certain powers. When does that Clash happen if the power already has a resistance roll?<br /> <br /> For example, Bill has Ghost Shield active. A ghost uses Awe on him, and rolls Power+Finesse versus Bill's Presence+Composure+Gnosis. When does Bill roll Gnosis+Death for the Clash, before or after the power's inherent resistance roll? What order do those rolls resolve in?<br /> <br /> I think the easiest way to do this would be to just give Bill two separate chances to resist, and use the ghost's initial Power+Finesse successes as the target for both rolls. Is that how it's meant to work?<br /> <br /> Also, when a ghost or spirit or goetia rolls a Clash, do they use Power+Finesse or something involving their Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T01:44:16-07:00","id":931245,"title":"","content":"Clashes always go off last - they're when an effect has worked, but is in conflict with another. So, first you get your resistance roll against the Numen's activation and then, if it activates, it has to beat the spell on your Pattern that has the effect of &quot;Numina don't work on me&quot;: which is resolved in system by a Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T01:50:58-07:00","id":931246,"title":"","content":"Remember that Clash doesn't always mean that one of the effects is eradicated - sometimes it just means that both powers went off, but one of them made other practically irrelevant or worked around it. Kind of like how you don't destroy Vampire's Obfuscate by piercing it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:39:32-07:00","id":931381,"title":"","content":"Can death magic force a disembodied soul to materialize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:56:48-07:00","id":931427,"title":"","content":"Do you mean to Manifest? Probably, it'd be Death 4 if you can do it as you'd be morphing ephemera into a vessel that can Manifest and morphing the soul to essentially keep it from rejecting such a merger with that Manifested ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:17:36-07:00","id":931438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931427#post931427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean to Manifest? Probably, it'd be Death 4 if you can do it as you'd be morphing ephemera into a vessel that can Manifest and morphing the soul to essentially keep it from rejecting such a merger with that Manifested ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, wondering if you can force the soul itself into using the Materialize Manifestation. Not putting it into a shell that you then cause to materialize. Although I suppose that could have similar results.<br /> <br /> Naturally you'd have be able give it the materialize manifestation as iirc disembodied souls have no manifestations, other than twilight form obviously, by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:33:56-07:00","id":931450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931438#post931438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naturally you'd have be able give it the materialize manifestation as iirc disembodied souls have no manifestations, other than twilight form obviously, by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>A disembodied soul doesn't have a Twilight Form, being not made of ephemera; you need to have some manner of supernatural power that allows you to manipulate souls to interact with them unless you're a Supernal being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:50:02-07:00","id":931461,"title":"","content":"I think they do exist in Twilight but have no stats, not sure if that does or doesn't count as not having a Twilight Manifestation. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> is right about souls not being made of ephemera though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:15:35-07:00","id":931472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931450#post931450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A disembodied soul doesn't have a Twilight Form, being not made of ephemera; you need to have some manner of supernatural power that allows you to manipulate souls to interact with them unless you're a Supernal being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I'd somehow got it into my head that souls used the rules for ephemeral beings. Skimming through the mage book shows no evidence for this. It seems I was confusing the traits of a soul imprisoned by the Idigam as the standard traits of souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:26:36-07:00","id":931478,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they don't:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e, p. 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls are insubstantial constructs, wholly invisible except to Death Sight when properly integrated into a person, and visible as vague humanoid auras in the Mage Sight of the five subtle Arcana when removed from a host. They are clearest when viewed under magic that reveals subjects in Twilight resonating with Death (such as the Death 2 Attainment), but are not made of ephemera, so remain insubstantial to ephemeral beings unless they have Numina or Influences allowing them to manipulate souls. All Supernal beings may spend one Mana to physically interact with unattached souls. Mages must use spells to manipulate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:28:40-07:00","id":931480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931461#post931461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they do exist in Twilight but have no stats, not sure if that does or doesn't count as not having a Twilight Manifestation. I think <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> is right about souls not being made of ephemera though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That raises an interesting question, does something have to be composed of ephemera to exist in the state of twilight? I would argue that twilight and materialized are states of ephemera, just as solid, liquid, gas, and plasma are states of matter. By that interpretation, a thing must be made of ephemera to be in the state of twilight. But an argument could be made that twilight might simply be a state of non-materiality, and any substance be it ephemera, matter, or something else is theoretically capable of becoming non-material by magical means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:33:05-07:00","id":931486,"title":"","content":"My understanding of Twilight is that it simply describes things that currently do not interact with matter. Ephemera is just one example of a substance that tends to exist in a state of twilight.<br /> <br /> Would this mean that Dark Matter/Energy exist in Twilight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:36:15-07:00","id":931518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931480#post931480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That raises an interesting question, does something have to be composed of ephemera to exist in the state of twilight? I would argue that twilight and materialized are states of ephemera, just as solid, liquid, gas, and plasma are states of matter. By that interpretation, a thing must be made of ephemera to be in the state of twilight. But an argument could be made that twilight might simply be a state of non-materiality, and any substance be it ephemera, matter, or something else is theoretically capable of becoming non-material by magical means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter 4 Ghost Wall makes objects non-material without shifting them into Twilight. The fact that souls can be perceived via any subtle arcana implies that actually souls don't reside in Twilight. So Satchel was right, again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:59:13-07:00","id":931525,"title":"","content":"Wow, that image of souls is creepy as anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:15:55-07:00","id":931535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931525#post931525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that image of souls is creepy as anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:23:10-07:00","id":931538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Pg.98.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls are insubstantial constructs, wholly invisible except to<br /> Death Sight when properly integrated into a person, and visible as<br /> vague humanoid auras in the Mage Sight of the five subtle Arcana<br /> when removed from a host. They are clearest when viewed under<br /> magic that reveals subjects in Twilight resonating with Death<br /> (such as the Death 2 Attainment), but are not made of ephemera,<br /> so remain insubstantial to ephemeral beings unless they have<br /> Numina or Influences allowing them to manipulate souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is kind of vague on the issue honestly. You can see them without seeing into twilight but viewing death twilight gives you a much clearer view of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:44:34-07:00","id":931552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931535#post931535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I always imagined them as just a glowing ball of energy or something like that. Kinda dull.<br /> <br /> But a vague ethereal figure just seems really creepy to me. I guess it's basically the way ghosts are portrayed in a lot of places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T20:24:26-07:00","id":931780,"title":"","content":"Other random question...<br /> <br /> So using a Dedicated Tool allows you -2 on a paradox roll when used as a Yantra in a spell. If the tool would also work as a Path/Order tool (+1 Yantra), and I want it to &quot;double dip&quot; in the spell casting, do I have to count it as using 2 Yantra? Or is it 1 Yantra that also happens to give a penalty to paradox rolls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T02:35:29-07:00","id":931894,"title":"","content":"You can use a single item as many times as you want up to your Yantra/Gnosis limit but every time you do you need to invoke different aspect. Dedicated Tool and Order Tool are two different aspects thus it would take 2 Yantras to apply both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T03:19:52-07:00","id":931903,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks! That's what I figured. <br /> <br /> I also see from the book that you can choose to cast a spell as an aimed spell, which lets you hit someone close by but without needing to spend a Reach to cast it at sensory range. Can you cast any spell this way? Or does it need to be some kind of fraying or unraveling spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T03:24:57-07:00","id":931904,"title":"","content":"You can cast any spell but the drawback is that you can miss and hit someone or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T03:41:10-07:00","id":931907,"title":"","content":"Sweet. That's exactly how I figured it might work. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:01:46-07:00","id":932155,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit on how much Essence a Resonant Condition creates? Because:<br /> 1. Get a Familiar<br /> 2. Find a Resonant Condition<br /> 3. Ask your Familiar to give you it's Essence in form of Mana<br /> 4. Use Channel Essence from Resonant Condition to your Familiar until it's full<br /> Gives you a pretty easy access to All Mana You Need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:26:22-07:00","id":932168,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure spirits can only harvest Essence once a day<br /> <br /> Wait, nevermind I see what you're doing, that might work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:47:10-07:00","id":932182,"title":"","content":"I would probably rule that it works like spell stacking, with the &quot;duration&quot; being a scene or maybe a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:27:38-07:00","id":932266,"title":"","content":"While I like your solution, I don't like the way of doing it. Maybe I should just go with excessive Ephemeral Channeling creating some Condition for that?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Still, I would love to get advice on how much Essence before putting down Condition to make it less and less and less efficient would be proper. We don't have much experience in dealing with Spirits, so I don't know how much Essence is too much.<br /> <br /> Context: Other players asked me what are good ways for them to get Mana with their current setups, so I started checking things out. Our Thyrsus has Spirit 3 and a Familiar, and loooooooooves doing stuff with her Familiar, so I started searching for something using that angle, and well, arrived here, because while it's a cool idea and our GM likes it too, neither of us want it to be limitless. Managing resources is fun! Finding a way to milk 10 Mana per Scene is fun, finding a way to milk infinite Mana is counter productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-15-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T19:28:24-07:00","id":932331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=931894#post931894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use a single item as many times as you want up to your Yantra/Gnosis limit but every time you do you need to invoke different aspect. Dedicated Tool and Order Tool are two different aspects thus it would take 2 Yantras to apply both.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not clear. It says under dedicated tool:<br /> <br /> &quot;Effect:Using a Dedicated tool as a Yantra penalizes any Paradox dice pool by \u20132; the mage can also use it as a Path or Order tool.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dedicated tools are unlike any other Yantra, and it's therefore entirely possible that they're an exception to the usual rules. I could easily read this quote as saying that a Dedicated tool is simultaneously a path or order tool, and also comes with the +1 yantra bonus, so long as the tool's symbolism is applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=932155#post932155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit on how much Essence a Resonant Condition creates? Because:<br /> 1. Get a Familiar<br /> 2. Find a Resonant Condition<br /> 3. Ask your Familiar to give you it's Essence in form of Mana<br /> 4. Use Channel Essence from Resonant Condition to your Familiar until it's full<br /> Gives you a pretty easy access to All Mana You Need.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not RAW, but personally I just prohibit players from converting Essence to Mana at all. It leads to an unlimited mana engine via Create Essence, and that in turn breaks down a good deal of the setting's assumptions.<br /> <br /> This example just seems to be another way it breaks the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-15-2016, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T20:00:45-07:00","id":932343,"title":"","content":"Mana / Essence conversion between Mage and their Familiar is one of defining gameplay features for Familiar, though, and we don't want to take it away from her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T03:08:40-07:00","id":932456,"title":"","content":"About the Sanctum merit: if a Cabal buys this merit together, how does it work with spell-control? Lets say in a cabal there is 3 members, A, B &amp; C.<br /> A&amp;B have both the Sanctum merit at 2 dots and C at 1 dot, bringing their sanctum up to 5 dots. Can each mage in the Cabal use the 5 dots and get 5 extra active spells as long as they where cast in the sanctum or does they get + 2, +2 ,+1 spell-control respectively ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T04:10:18-07:00","id":932462,"title":"","content":"They get +2 +2 +1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T04:30:13-07:00","id":932466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=932343#post932343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana / Essence conversion between Mage and their Familiar is one of defining gameplay features for Familiar, though, and we don't want to take it away from her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just go with your point about making it lead to a new condition or possibly some other setting weirdness. <br /> <br /> In general, I have started just turning any potential gamebreaking aspects that are allowed by RAW into &quot;allowable, but there is a reason not every mage does it&quot; scenarios. Not to punish them (some gimicks led to positive aspects) but turn them into plot hooks and Mysteries. A the very least, I don't leave the events in a vacuum: change the shadow, get spirit court upheaval and werewolfs; make yourself ungodly lucky, the Seers notice you disrupting the local lottery/economy; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T07:38:00-07:00","id":932499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=932462#post932462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They get +2 +2 +1</div> </div> </div> </div>I am probably missing something, but I am not seeing the benefit of sharing the Merit then. This looks like exactly the same result as if each one of them had a separate Sanctum for themselves expect for being able to base it on the same Safe Place. I originally assumed you would simply have 5 spell slots for the entire cabal that they can use however they like. Meaning A alone could use it for 5 additional spells (but leaving none for B and C) or B could have 3 extra and C could have 2 extra, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T08:14:22-07:00","id":932518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=932499#post932499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am probably missing something, but I am not seeing the benefit of sharing the Merit then. This looks like exactly the same result as if each one of them had a separate Sanctum for themselves expect for being able to base it on the same Safe Place. I originally assumed you would simply have 5 spell slots for the entire cabal that they can use however they like. Meaning A alone could use it for 5 additional spells (but leaving none for B and C) or B could have 3 extra and C could have 2 extra, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can still combine the dots for size and security as well as pool more dots for a demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T08:30:09-07:00","id":932525,"title":"","content":"It saves you that one dot for Safe Place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:18:35-07:00","id":933016,"title":"","content":"So, imagine I want to raise myself a undead army.<br /> I gather bodies in small room. I want them all, and I want them now. Intuitive way to do it seems to be &quot;use Advanced Scale to get more subjects&quot; for the spell. But...isn't &quot;Use Advanced Scale to target all corpses in the building&quot; the more efficient route, allowing me to bind potentially hundreds of Zombies in a single casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:56:04-07:00","id":933040,"title":"","content":"Yep. Scale usually funtions better as Area rather than Targets when you want cuantity. Your Storyteller may dictate that Area is only to affect places, so you'll need to use Targets in this instance. I'd rather make that distiction so each Scale type has its own uses, but YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T02:41:06-07:00","id":933324,"title":"","content":"I usually run Adv. Scale as &quot;area if touch range (or thrown), targets if sensory range&quot;, unless that doesn't make sense for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:34:21-07:00","id":933411,"title":"","content":"Description of Area as Scale mentions that it basically affects every viable subject in it, so I think RAISE ZOMBIES! would raise all corpses in the area. Obviously, it's not that useful for spells like BURN WITH FIRE!.<br /> <br /> Another find:<br /> 1. Get yourself a Demesne.<br /> 2. In Demesne, your magic doesn't Risk Paradox, period.<br /> 3. This means you can Reach as many times as you want<br /> 4. So you go, get yourself a Time 3, cast Shifting Sands...and you can travel to any point in your past. How?<br /> The amount of time you travel depends on Reach, one scene (hour) per Reach. As you can Reach infinitely, you can travel infinitely too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T08:01:30-07:00","id":933423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933411#post933411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Description of Area as Scale mentions that it basically affects every viable subject in it, so I think RAISE ZOMBIES! would raise all corpses in the area. Obviously, it's not that useful for spells like BURN WITH FIRE!.<br /> <br /> Another find:<br /> 1. Get yourself a Demesne.<br /> 2. In Demesne, your magic doesn't Risk Paradox, period.<br /> 3. This means you can Reach as many times as you want<br /> 4. So you go, get yourself a Time 3, cast Shifting Sands...and you can travel to any point in your past. How?<br /> The amount of time you travel depends on Reach, one scene (hour) per Reach. As you can Reach infinitely, you can travel infinitely too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well only as far as your own timeline goes. Once you are talking about times during which you didn't exist I'm guessing that's a bit beyond a Disciple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T08:04:22-07:00","id":933426,"title":"","content":"I'd argue you also can't travel to before the Demesne was established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T08:06:17-07:00","id":933427,"title":"","content":"The fact that blanket-targeting an area allows you to hit more people than using a strict number of subjects is entirely intentional - it's the difference between &quot;curse everyone in this room&quot; and &quot;cures him, him, her, her, him, him, her, but noone else&quot;<br /> <br /> The former's both easier for the Mage <i>and</i> potentially less Wise. Feature, not bug!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T08:51:32-07:00","id":933435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933426#post933426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue you also can't travel to before the Demesne was established.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd second this argument. Still, a pretty nifty method of early-onset time traveling hijinks within that boundary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T15:33:34-07:00","id":933610,"title":"","content":"Can a Legacy use an inferior Arcanum as it's Ruling one? I am curious because I have come up with quite a cool Legacy idea for an Obrimos involving Death (basically tying into the symbolic power of a Sun or Sky divinity/concept being sacrificed in part or full or slain in the course of a classically heroic act, Thor falling after the slaying of the World-Serpent, stuff like that)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T15:40:38-07:00","id":933611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933610#post933610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Legacy use an inferior Arcanum as it's Ruling one?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mind-focused Dreamspeakers are an example Thyrsus Legacy, so I should assume so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-18-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T16:43:47-07:00","id":933638,"title":"","content":"And Dreamspeakers aren't the only example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:20:36-07:00","id":934299,"title":"","content":"Trying to clarify something. In the book, it says when you scrutinize something using Focused Sight, failure can run the risk of adding to the opacity for other mages, and you can even add to others' opacity on an exceptional success. <br /> <br /> Does this mean when you strip down opacity through repeated rolls and accruing successes, it also reduces the opacity for other mages trying to scrutinize the same subject? In other words, how do you handle opacity of a subject when multiple mages are scrutinizing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:37:57-07:00","id":934317,"title":"","content":"I beliebe is independent (each mage reduces the opacity for themselves, unless they work in t\u00e1ndem) The increase of Opacity by Nimbus Contamination is for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:34:55-07:00","id":934335,"title":"","content":"Say you want to use a damage spell to punch a size 15 hole into a size 80 building. Would you need to apply scale factors for size 80 (the size of the targeted object) or size 15 (the size that you actually want to affect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T01:54:26-07:00","id":934352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934335#post934335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say you want to use a damage spell to punch a size 15 hole into a size 80 building. Would you need to apply scale factors for size 80 (the size of the targeted object) or size 15 (the size that you actually want to affect).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that comes down to ST discretion quite a lot. If you're punching a hole in the building I'd argue that you're only targeting the specific section of the building and so don't need to aim the spell at the whole thing so it'd only need size 15 not size 80 in factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:15:25-07:00","id":934356,"title":"","content":"Then on the other hand the closest you come to an official ruling on this is in the Forces section where they mention that to slow a semi you have to target the whole truck not just a tire(s). Supposedly though, that's to slow the truck, if you just want to rip its wheels off then you could just target the wheels. So I'd take the same logic to a building, you can target the whole building and minimize the chance of collapse when you put a hole in it, or you can just punch a hole in it and hope for the best. This also stays inside the games themes so I'd be comfortable with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:11:54-07:00","id":934389,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it won't break the game to allow for targeting parts of large things by using a smaller size factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:12:05-07:00","id":934390,"title":"","content":"Can you get extra dice to your spellcasting pool by Reaching? I have <i>seen </i>it mentioned somewhere, but can't find it for the love of God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:23:36-07:00","id":934392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934390#post934390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you get extra dice to your spellcasting pool by Reaching? I have <i>seen </i>it mentioned somewhere, but can't find it for the love of God.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only been mentioned by people who keep forgetting that's not how factors work. No, Reach doesn't give dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:24:28-07:00","id":934393,"title":"","content":"Nope, that's not one of the uses of Reach. You can, however spend more time casting ritually to get bonuses, that's the closest thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:42:18-07:00","id":934398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934393#post934393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, that's not one of the uses of Reach. You can, however spend more time casting ritually to get bonuses, that's the closest thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934392#post934392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only been mentioned by people who keep forgetting that's not how factors work. No, Reach doesn't give dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah well. It's rather sad, that was one of the last things I needed to make 2E usable. Might have to house-rule it in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:45:00-07:00","id":934399,"title":"","content":"What? Why? You can get dice by using Yantras, WP, and ritual casting, why would you need Reach to add dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:48:04-07:00","id":934400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934399#post934399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Why? You can get dice by using Yantras, WP, and ritual casting, why would you need Reach to add dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those are capped and don't allow for major workings. Mages generally feel like conjurors of cheap tricks now, a lot more than before. I was trying to remedy that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:09:49-07:00","id":934412,"title":"","content":"How is that? Those are capped <b><u><i>after appling penalties</i></u></b> is an importnat distinction. You can have an uber spell (with lots of penalties to increase factors) and still get a net +5 to your unmodified dice pool of Gnosis+Arcanum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:12:48-07:00","id":934413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934400#post934400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of those are capped and don't allow for major workings. Mages generally feel like conjurors of cheap tricks now, a lot more than before. I was trying to remedy that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understand how the spell casting system works. What do you mean a &quot;major&quot; working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:24:44-07:00","id":934418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934413#post934413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you understand how the spell casting system works. What do you mean a &quot;major&quot; working?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that encompasses a city. Materials durable enough to create a space elevator. Going back in time several days (without the above demesne trick).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934412#post934412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that? Those are capped <b><u><i>after appling penalties</i></u></b> is an importnat distinction. You can have an uber spell (with lots of penalties to increase factors) and still get a net +5 to your unmodified dice pool of Gnosis+Arcanum</div> </div> </div> </div>Our definition of &quot;uber&quot; spells are probably different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:34:49-07:00","id":934420,"title":"","content":"You can't encompass a city anyway because Advanced Scale is capped, the rest is all doable with the way the system works now though, so I still don't see your problem.<br /> <br /> Wait, do you think rolling more dice somehow makes a spell stronger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-20-2016, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:44:28-07:00","id":934424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934420#post934420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't encompass a city anyway because Advanced Scale is capped,</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I admit, I missed that. That still only supports my point more. The best you can do is a &quot;campus&quot;. That's not much at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934420#post934420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the rest is all doable with the way the system works now though, so I still don't see your problem.<br /> Wait, do you think rolling more dice somehow makes a spell stronger?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you have the potential to roll more dice, you can take more -2 shifts for extra potency, so yes, the spell becomes more powerful. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:48:26-07:00","id":934426,"title":"","content":"Doesn't change the fact that what you consider major workings can usually still be done without granting extra dice via Reach. The unlimited dice booster is group casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:25:06-07:00","id":934445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=934426#post934426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't change the fact that what you consider major workings can usually still be done without granting extra dice via Reach. The unlimited dice booster is group casting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Group casting requires your GM either actively help you, or your cabal be really focussed, or you derail the game to find enough NPC mages, so it's pretty eh. Even if I can see how it can be RP fodder. But I guess we need to end this discussion, I am not sure this thread is appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:37:14-07:00","id":934451,"title":"","content":"Yeah, especially since you apparently aren't able to address my point that your &quot;major&quot; magic can actually be achieved without changing the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:15:36-07:00","id":934476,"title":"","content":"You can &quot;force&quot; GM to give you ritual help by using your Order Status to borrow Retainers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T08:32:52-07:00","id":935086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933427#post933427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that blanket-targeting an area allows you to hit more people than using a strict number of subjects is entirely intentional - it's the difference between &quot;curse everyone in this room&quot; and &quot;cures him, him, her, her, him, him, her, but noone else&quot;<br /> <br /> The former's both easier for the Mage <i>and</i> potentially less Wise. Feature, not bug!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like how it makes stuff like &quot;I want me and thins on my person to be less vulnerable to magic&quot; or &quot;I want to turn myself invulnerable to fire, but I also need to target my clothes, argh&quot; not a problem anymore; just stick Area on it, and you turn &quot;ability to make zombies&quot; into something you just devote a spell control slot to, without bothering to micro manage how many zombies you can make and if it's worth it with and where is the sweet spot between scale and potency and arrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrgh, this just lets me assume I'm a necromancer, I can turn small room of corpses into zombies, what do I do with that? <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it makes buff sharing even easier, and if there is something I fear, it's the logical conclusion of &quot;we can share our buffs very easily, there is pretty much no real reason to be stingy; let's just perform our buffs in one space and use Area to make it target all of us&quot;. Cabals whose members all are Accelerated, Mentally Perfected, Wards-And-Signed, Physically Perfected and so on make me want to kill myself.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> Small challenge:<br /> Books provide Equipment bonus. Figure out a &quot;fluff reason&quot; for MatterMagic to interact with Book's Equipment rating - decreasing it, increasing it, applying dice tricks, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:38:30-07:00","id":935097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935086#post935086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like how it makes stuff like &quot;I want me and thins on my person to be less vulnerable to magic&quot; or &quot;I want to turn myself invulnerable to fire, but I also need to target my clothes, argh&quot; not a problem anymore; just stick Area on it, and you turn &quot;ability to make zombies&quot; into something you just devote a spell control slot to, without bothering to micro manage how many zombies you can make and if it's worth it with and where is the sweet spot between scale and potency and arrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrgh, this just lets me assume I'm a necromancer, I can turn small room of corpses into zombies, what do I do with that?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it makes buff sharing even easier, and if there is something I fear, it's the logical conclusion of &quot;we can share our buffs very easily, there is pretty much no real reason to be stingy; let's just perform our buffs in one space and use Area to make it target all of us&quot;. Cabals whose members all are Accelerated, Mentally Perfected, Wards-And-Signed, Physically Perfected and so on make me want to kill myself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since you are targeting the area you can't target anyone specifically. So if your zombie ever leaves the area it'll just collapse to the ground.<br /> I guess you can encompass the area around a person or object so when it moves the spell moves also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:50:22-07:00","id":935103,"title":"","content":"Nah, when you target an area, spell that would check for number of subjects just checks for any and all subject in the area and applies spell to it. So Advanced Scale:Subjects1 will target these 5 specific zombies, while Advanced Scale:Area1 will target all corpses in this room. Kinda like spell &quot;pulse&quot; that affects anything viable in it's path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines <br /> how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell <br /> effect to anyone or anything within. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:15:26-07:00","id":935146,"title":"","content":"You are right ... But , that makes me wonder how this area cast spell That Affects only targets That are currently inside . So that every one entering is affected but when they leave the effect ceases. <br /> For example matter magic that gives everyone arriving a map of a mansion which would then disappear after leaving. Maybe a +2 Reach and 1 Mana for a spell to &quot;recast&quot; itself in such a way? Its not realy recasting, just a characteristic of an area.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:18:52-07:00","id":935153,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a different spell, Fate or Space probably. Remember, one of Mage 2 goals is to make each spell &quot;one effect&quot; - if you want a spell that does multiple things, cast another one or combine them. Life spell that makes you stronger and gives you regeneration should be Stronger!+COMBINE+Regeneration!, not &quot;StrongerRegeneration&quot;, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don\u2019t think of this section as a \u201cmenu\u201d; any individual spell <br /> should have a single, clear effect. If you start designing a spell <br /> that deals damage and grants bonus dice and imposes a Con-<br /> dition, you\u2019re probably creating a combined spell (see p. 118), <br /> not a single spell. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:31:22-07:00","id":935158,"title":"","content":"Im talking about one effect actually. You are making a banquette in a big house and dont want your guest to lose themselves. So you print a physical map, on paper.<br /> Then you cast a spell around a house that makes a copy of said map and places it in guests hands. Space and Fate can use Keys to determine who would be affected but Matter can surely place it in a pocket since its, you know, made of inorganic matter. <br /> But the question is &quot;Can I add new targets in such a way?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:03:53-07:00","id":935181,"title":"","content":"It'd probably be easier just to cast a spell on the area that makes it impossible for people within to get lost? A Perfecting of Space, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:17:25-07:00","id":935187,"title":"","content":"The easiest thing to do would be placing a pile of maps on a table next to front doors. Im asking how to make this particular effect to work. It's about being fancy hence you want to impress the guests.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:18:25-07:00","id":935188,"title":"","content":"A Matter spell to make copies of the map, and Space spell that takes copied maps into hands of your guests. Add Fate to create &quot;if, then x&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:27:40-07:00","id":935196,"title":"","content":"So basically you need fate to include more targets into your spell after its been cast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:58:18-07:00","id":935216,"title":"","content":"No, it just determines who or what in the area gets a map by meeting a particular condition such as entering the area that's affected. Spells cannot change target factors on their own without the practice of Dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:37:30-07:00","id":935234,"title":"","content":"That makes them targets of a Space spell that hands them a map. But really you just used area scale factor so the target doesnt change.<br /> <br /> Another case (or previous): A pit that revives dead pidgeons. You make a spell that targets an area that revives every pidgeon that you will throw there as long as the spell lasts. Is it possible with Death on non-Dynymics level?<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sorry if I sound rude or anything. I'm just trying to understand this particular nuance.<br /> Edit 2: Or Mind spell that shuts down everyone that enters your home. Impossible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 07-21-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:53:57-07:00","id":935241,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, the two main roadblocks to these ideas are:<br /> <br /> 1. You can't really have a spell recast itself on command. You <i>can</i> have it recast itself every ritual interval, but you can't have it go off, say, every time you snap your fingers, or every time someone walks into the area.<br /> 2. You can't have a spell exclude people from its effect that it didn't exclude before, and you can't exclude someone based on a Key (as far as I can tell). The only way to exclude someone from an area <i>at all</i> is by casting <i>Wards and Signs </i>on them beforehand.<br /> <br /> For the pigeon hole to work, I think you'd have to be satisfied with all dead pigeons reviving every (ritual interval). (EDIT: assuming that the revival was Lasting, rather than subject to the duration of the spell. If the duration determines how long they're alive again, the spell won't re-cast)<br /> <br /> For the map generator, if you just cast it yourself, you could combine it with <i>Wards and Signs</i>, then exclude all previous targets from the casting so that no one gets a second map. There's no way for it to be completely automated and send a map to someone who just walked in, though. The closest you can get is a 5-minute ritual interval with Gnosis 9.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: You <i>can </i>have a spell go off <i>once</i> in response to a trigger with <i>Hung Spell</i> and Conditional Duration. So with booby trapping your home, it would work if you were OK with resetting it after it went off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 07-21-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:25:31-07:00","id":935261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935241#post935241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> For the pigeon hole to work, I think you'd have to be satisfied with all dead pigeons reviving every (ritual interval). (EDIT: assuming that the revival was Lasting, rather than subject to the duration of the spell. If the duration determines how long they're alive again, the spell won't re-cast)<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I figured about that ritual interval can help in this case even before you replied but I don't understand a part about Lasting... Only Lasting effects can be recast?<br /> <br /> <br /> About booby traping a house, thats a cool way of doing it. But what about &quot;wall&quot; of Mind effect that is just harmfull? Its not recasting , right? Its just a spell that makes a hostile environment for a brain. Ive seen a spell in Creative Thaumaturgy Thread that dealt damaga every time you went through the Gountlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:45:13-07:00","id":935271,"title":"","content":"No, Lasting has nothing to do with whether or not a spell can be recast. Lasting is a piece of terminology to describe permanent effects of a spell. For instance, if I use magic to smash a vase it isn't suddenly going to repair itself after the spell is cast (Barring other supernatural effects) so the fact that the vase is broken is a Lasting effect.<br /> <br /> Without looking at the spell you're referencing I assume that damage dealt via passing through the Gauntlet is not the effect of the spell. The actual effect of the spell is probably to place a Condition or Tilt which has that effect. Thus, instances of damage are not a result of the spell being cast again. If that's not how the spell works it's likely not a spell that complies with the actual rules of the game and shouldn't be used as an example for how to do things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-21-2016, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:50:41-07:00","id":935277,"title":"","content":"Your best bet would be to target the house, and slap a Condition on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:07:46-07:00","id":935286,"title":"","content":"I found it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883859#post883859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vicious Gauntlet (Spirit 4)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Survival, Stealth, Brawl<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> This spell alters the nature of the gauntlet, adding bitting fangs, snarling thorns and vicious claws to its &quot;surface&quot;. The subject of this spell is the gauntlet itself as it covers the area affected by the spell. While the alteration lasts, whenever an entity attempts to cross it, roll Gauntlet Strength x 2, resisted by the entity's Stamina (or Resistance if a Spirit or similar entity). Each success causes a point of lethal damage to the crossing entity. Once the gauntlet has performed a number of attacks equal to the spell's Potency, the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The gauntlet deals aggravated damage instead of lethal. Costs 1 Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The gauntlet may be altered by the spell in one direction only.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You may designate a Key that prevents the gauntlet from attacking it's holder.</div> </div> </div> </div>So number of attacks equal to the Potency? <br /> <br /> @WHW Thank! I always forget about Conditions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:15:32-07:00","id":935289,"title":"","content":"That spell works, though honestly they could have just dropped the bit about Potency for number of attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:35:55-07:00","id":935303,"title":"","content":"But without that bit the spell a really poor job in guarding the passage. So a Mind spell that inflicts Sleep condition for number of attack equal to Potency is possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:38:53-07:00","id":935307,"title":"","content":"In fact I included the Potency bit just because a lot of spells in the core book have it. Since then, I've thought more about the uses of Potency, and removed it almost completely from all spells except those that actually provide/remove dots or inflict/heal damage. My current version of this spell is:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vicious Gauntlet</span></span></b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Patterning<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Survival, Animal Ken, Brawl</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The spellcasting roll for this spell is always penalized by the Gauntlet Strength.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell alters the nature of the Gauntlet, adding biting fangs, snarling thorns and vicious claws to its &quot;surface&quot;. The subject of this spell is the Gauntlet itself as it covers the area affected by the spell's Scale. While the spell lasts, whenever any entity attempts to cross it or use a supernatural power to reach across it, roll a dice pool equal to twice the Gauntlet Strength contested by Stamina or Rank. Each success inflicts a level of lethal damage to the crossing entity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Only one side of the Gauntlet is affected (the mage chooses which one).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You may designate a Key that protects its holder from being attacked.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the entity takes damage from the Gauntlet, it fails to cross over or reach through the Gauntlet. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach and 1 Mana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Gauntlet deals aggravated damage instead of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> You might notice that there is something weird with this spell: instead of Withstand, I apply the Gauntlet Strength as a straight penalty. In my rules I apply Gauntlet Strength as a penalty instead of raising Withstand, so that it is compatible with blue book Spirits and Werewolf. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","user":"arthexis","date":". 07-21-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:49:43-07:00","id":935312,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason you don't have a Primary Factor listed either <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2535_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2535\" data-vbnamecard=\"2535\">arthexis</a> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:51:51-07:00","id":935313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935312#post935312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason you don't have a Primary Factor listed either <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2535_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2535\" data-vbnamecard=\"2535\">arthexis</a> ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got rid of primary factors completely. You can take a look at my ruleset if you are interested:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:06:23-07:00","id":935328,"title":"","content":"While it might be annoying to do, I think that if you are posting custom spells, adding a note that they follow your houserules would be good to avoid confusion for people wanting to use them. Just a thought, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:23:26-07:00","id":935396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935271#post935271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Lasting has nothing to do with whether or not a spell can be recast. Lasting is a piece of terminology to describe permanent effects of a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can have to do with whether or not a spell's duration means the effect is repeated. Damage spells repeat for the duration essentially because the damage is Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:27:59-07:00","id":935401,"title":"","content":"That has nothing to do with the effect being Lasting and everything to do with it being produced instantly and Potency primary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-21-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:35:39-07:00","id":935406,"title":"","content":"Sure. But most of the time it's the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T19:19:40-07:00","id":935419,"title":"","content":"I don't see what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T20:28:37-07:00","id":935433,"title":"","content":"Making a spell Lasting usually also means the effect is instantaneous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T00:29:52-07:00","id":935477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935396#post935396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can have to do with whether or not a spell's duration means the effect is repeated. Damage spells repeat for the duration essentially because the damage is Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no direct damage spells in the book that can be made to be Lasting outside of ST fiat, for good reason. Most of the spells that create Lasting effects generally make fundamentally irrevocable changes to the targets, although a few exist to clarify the difference between suppressing an element of the game versus eliminating it entirely. Duration already grants repetition as follows: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: the Awakening, 2nd Edition, Chapter 4: Magic, Spell Factors, Duration</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duration Duration is simply how long a spell lasts once cast. Standard spell Durations are measured in turns, while using a Reach to use the Advanced Duration chart makes the spell last much longer. I<b>f a spell would logically have an immediate effect but is cast with Advanced Duration, the effect recurs at every multiple of the character\u2019s Gnosis-based ritual casting time, until the Duration runs out.</b> For example, a Gnosis 1 character\u2019s healing spell with a Duration of a day heals its Potency in Health boxes every three hours. The highest level of the Advanced Duration chart is \u201cindefinite,\u201d meaning the spell lasts until dispelled or the caster cancels it. Moving to indefinite requires a second Reach, and the caster must also spend a point of Mana</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:13:08-07:00","id":935488,"title":"","content":"To get to the Astral from a Hallow, you have to &quot;absorb and spend&quot; a certain amount of Mana from that Hallow. Does Tass count, or just the Mana you get directly from oblations (or Prime)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:45:13-07:00","id":935492,"title":"","content":"If the tass has been generated by the Hallow then I don't see why not. Arguably, you could also take mana and cycle it through the Hallow back into yourself in order to attune that mana to the Hallow, or maybe just change the resonance on mana in your Pattern to match the Hallow with Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-22-2016, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T05:24:26-07:00","id":935532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935477#post935477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no direct damage spells in the book that can be made to be Lasting outside of ST fiat, for good reason. Most of the spells that create Lasting effects generally make fundamentally irrevocable changes to the targets, although a few exist to clarify the difference between suppressing an element of the game versus eliminating it entirely. Duration already grants repetition as follows:</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct damage spells are Lasting by definition because the damage doesn't go away when the spell's Duration is up.<br /> <br /> Yes, Duration grants repetition when the spell &quot;<b>would logically have an immediate effect.</b>&quot; What I'm saying is that if you make a spell's effect Lasting, you also make it have &quot;an immediate effect.&quot; For example, <i>Clear Thoughts </i>is Duration primary, and suppresses a Condition for the Duration. But if you make it Lasting, the Condition resolves; it's an immediate effect now, so the spell will repeat if its given enough Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:39:03-07:00","id":935855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935492#post935492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the tass has been generated by the Hallow then I don't see why not. Arguably, you could also take mana and cycle it through the Hallow back into yourself in order to attune that mana to the Hallow, or maybe just change the resonance on mana in your Pattern to match the Hallow with Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I ask because it has implications for what rating of the Hallow merit can be used to access the Astral, and I don't want to make things <i>too </i>easy for my players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:56:58-07:00","id":935861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935855#post935855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. I ask because it has implications for what rating of the Hallow merit can be used to access the Astral, and I don't want to make things <i>too </i>easy for my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, how is that making it harder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T17:20:03-07:00","id":935870,"title":"","content":"Just thinking out loud. What I meant was &quot;if only Mana received from oblations (IE, the daily allotment granted by the merit) counts, then characters would need to buy a higher Hallow rating to access the Astral from their own home base.&quot; In 1E you just explicitly needed access to a 5 dot Hallow, in 2E the sliding scale of spending (6-Hallow rating Mana) is a little more complicated. If characters can use collected Tass or some other means, then they have a larger number of places from which they can access the Astral, because even a 2 dot Hallow could collect enough condensed Tass for a journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T17:54:12-07:00","id":935879,"title":"","content":"Did you mean you didn't want to make things too hard for your players then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T23:25:38-07:00","id":935953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935532#post935532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Direct damage spells are Lasting by definition because the damage doesn't go away when the spell's Duration is up.<br /> <br /> Yes, Duration grants repetition when the spell &quot;<b>would logically have an immediate effect.</b>&quot; What I'm saying is that if you make a spell's effect Lasting, you also make it have &quot;an immediate effect.&quot; For example, <i>Clear Thoughts </i>is Duration primary, and suppresses a Condition for the Duration. But if you make it Lasting, the Condition resolves; it's an immediate effect now, so the spell will repeat if its given enough Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem logical to me. I suppose that's the reason that the book emphatically advises against allowing players to improvise spells with Lasting effects. And nothing in the rules explaining Lasting effects specifically and explicitly make the claim that their effects are immediate by dint of being Lasting effects. Only a handful of spells behave the same way as <i>Clear Thoughts.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:00:19-07:00","id":936107,"title":"","content":"I mean, there are only a handful of spells in the book that explicitly mention that their effects are Lasting or have an option to make them so. And yeah, the book never says &quot;Lasting effects = immediate effects&quot; but the book also doesn't bother to define &quot;immediate effects&quot; because it uses natural, not technical, language. But I challenge you to find a spell that has an immediate effect that isn't Lasting, or a spell that when made Lasting doesn't have an immediate effect.<br /> <br /> I do find that a lot of Lasting spells don't have significant effect when recurring unless they're affecting an area. Erasing a memory over and over with <i>Mind Wipe</i> isn't really useful unless you bind it to an area and cycle subjects through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T01:17:12-07:00","id":936454,"title":"","content":"Does Ghost Gate really leave a Mage naked after it ends?<br /> <br /> Could you use it to destroy any item, regardless of it's durability and structure? Does its destructive effect extend to magic items and artifacts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T02:57:45-07:00","id":936475,"title":"","content":"Question about Forces: What Practice is making an illusion? In this case, bending light around a person to make them look like a totally different person with different clothes. I'd guess it's Weaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T03:39:15-07:00","id":936481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=936475#post936475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Forces: What Practice is making an illusion? In this case, bending light around a person to make them look like a totally different person with different clothes. I'd guess it's Weaving.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True illusion will most likely be a Prime spell but a mirage is definitely a Force Weaving. Possibly mimicking Mutable Mask (Life \u2022\u2022)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T06:22:03-07:00","id":936515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=936481#post936481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True illusion will most likely be a Prime spell but a mirage is definitely a Force Weaving. Possibly mimicking Mutable Mask (Life \u2022\u2022)?</div> </div> </div> </div>True illusion is Forces, this has been stated by Dave more than once, and if you look at Platonic Form you'll notice that you have to add Forces in order to make the Platonic Form not appear overtly supernatural.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> : Considering it'd require changing the wavelengths of light and how it's reflected and so on, yeah, probably Weaving at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T06:25:16-07:00","id":936516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=936454#post936454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Ghost Gate really leave a Mage naked after it ends?<br /> <br /> Could you use it to destroy any item, regardless of it's durability and structure? Does its destructive effect extend to magic items and artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the use of the word destruction is a mistake. I mean, technically, yes it's physical form is &quot;destroyed&quot; because it's ephemeral and no longer has a physical presence, but there's no reason it would remain that way if taken back from Twilight to the Physical. That being said, if it isn't a mistake it probably works on magic items, but not on artifacts. Awakened magic doesn't seem to be capable of destroying artifacts that easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:10:25-07:00","id":936601,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Animal Minion(Life 0000) be a Weaving spell instead of Patterning? It just controls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:15:21-07:00","id":936603,"title":"","content":"The Ghostgate got rewrriten, so the whole&quot;destroy&quot; thing might not be a case anymore. Maybe. We shall see.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> So, as a Necromancer Not-Yet-Extraordinaire, our heroine wants to use her zombies and ghost familiar with some nice efficiency. Is following setup right?<br /> <br /> 1. Get a good, strong human corpse. Use some veiling magic to make it appear cute, alive and in general, not suspicious.<br /> 2. Reinforce it with some Matter to make it overall stronger (for example, use Wondrous Machine with added Death 3 to combine the body with some wondrous machinery), etc<br /> 3. Raise it as a powerful zombie.<br /> 4. Ask your familiar to claim it. <br /> 5. Use your Claimed Zombie as a proxy, messenger and enforcer, representing your interests while you sit safely in your Sanctum, using the Familiar sensory link to provide magical backup without being yourself in danger.<br /> <br /> Other than being heavy on spell control, is there something un-working with this idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-24-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:51:59-07:00","id":936613,"title":"","content":"Nope, seems a good way to act by proxy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T11:05:33-07:00","id":936626,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how to make the &quot;Corpse is first raised as a Potent, Reached Zombie&quot; relevant; the spell turns them into Retainer, and Claimed Corpse Familiar would use normal stats, so...any ideas? Using current mechanics, end result seems to be identical, zombie or no zombie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:02:13-07:00","id":936645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=936601#post936601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Animal Minion(Life 0000) be a Weaving spell instead of Patterning? It just controls.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read the description it's basically a consciousness transference like Possession, so since it takes the Mage's control of their own body and rewrites that control onto a different subject it's Patterning. It's similar to rewriting your spatial location via Teleport being Patterning except instead of rewriting across space your rewriting across organisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T02:14:41-07:00","id":936986,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That was helpfull actually. 2ed is a lot more intuitive but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T07:17:19-07:00","id":937072,"title":"","content":"Can a mage use Twilit Body to change himself or someone else into ephemera and then use Shape Spirit to heal/change said subject as it is now made up of ephemera? So can a spirit mage heal himself in twilight or change someone else into a mouse by transforming him into ephemera first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:29:32-07:00","id":937217,"title":"","content":"Since Spirit magic allows you to shape ephemera, my response would be to say yes, but that the transforming of someone into another shape would fail as soon as they became physical again. So, say, if you cast Twilit Body and then a Spirit Patterning spell to turn someone into a mouse, it'd work, but if you then canceled Twilit Body, the other spell would come undone as well as the person is transformed back into flesh and it can no longer affect them.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=936626#post936626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how to make the &quot;Corpse is first raised as a Potent, Reached Zombie&quot; relevant; the spell turns them into Retainer, and Claimed Corpse Familiar would use normal stats, so...any ideas? Using current mechanics, end result seems to be identical, zombie or no zombie.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. Your best bet would be to find a corpse you like (creepy) and restore it with Death magic so that it's fresh as a newly deceased cadaver. Then, you have your ghost buddy claim it and make it their new home.<br /> <br /> After that, what's important is the following spells:<br /> <br /> -Death Veiling to hide that they are dead. This could give the corpse a mere semblance of life or it could give them back all the rough functions of a living being.<br /> -Death Perfecting or Fraying to remove the effects of decay. In practice, this is a healing spell, set to ping every time your ritual cast time comes up. Since Claimed corpses decay fast, this is an absolute necessity.<br /> -Death Perfecting to enhance the corpse in ways you find useful for your purposes.<br /> <br /> Third one's optional but the first two are mandatory unless you want to get a new meatbag every week.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I've got a Thyrsus who used a magical anomaly to do something similar; carving a clay statue into a guardian demon and then filling it with a spirit that now patrols near her sanctum. The thing is an absolute beast. It makes being a solitary way more viable when you have that sort of firepower at your back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 07-25-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:29:55-07:00","id":937218,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say no, because despite the fact they're now made of ephemera they're still not spirits.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> has a pretty good response too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:35:01-07:00","id":937221,"title":"","content":"What if you cast a spell that translates them into ephemera, shape them, then cast spell that translates ephemera into flesh, while still maintaining previous two magics? <br /> I would guess that as long as the whole chain is intact, something could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:40:40-07:00","id":937227,"title":"","content":"While that's theoretically possible, translating an object into ephemera is a simple act of shifting it into another plane of existence. Transforming ephemera directly into flesh would be a compound Spirit + Life spell and, since it'd require Life 4, you might as well skip a step and just cast Life 4 Patterning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:53:16-07:00","id":937230,"title":"","content":"Stuff like Touch of the Grave allows you to pull out ephemeral objects from Twilight into material, though, so...instead of Ephemera-To-Flesh, retrieve it using a Touch of the Grave/similar spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:00:03-07:00","id":937235,"title":"","content":"That's reasonable, yeah. Though I feel like it's the basis for a cautionary tale, given that ephemeral objects have a Durability of 1 when pulled out of Twilight. You don't really want to shatter your friend like glass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:53:51-07:00","id":937419,"title":"","content":"Talking about Durability...<br /> Someone annoys me, I decide to Shadow Craft a coffind directly around them. How to figure up Structure and other game-relevant stats?<br /> EDIT<br /> Or, more accurately, how do I figure out stats needed for the dude to interact with it, and his means of busting out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-25-2016, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T22:02:58-07:00","id":937475,"title":"","content":"Size is 5 or 6, Durability is 2 by default, Structure is the sum of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T02:51:07-07:00","id":937525,"title":"","content":"Does peripheral mage sight pick up ongoing supernatural effects that is not concealed? For instance IF a mage uses a spell to enhance her perception for a scene. Could another mage notice it with her peripheral mage sight? Or does it only trigger the turn its cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 07-26-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T03:09:10-07:00","id":937529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=937525#post937525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does peripheral mage sight pick up ongoing supernatural effects that is not concealed? For instance IF a mage uses a spell to enhance her perception for a scene. Could another mage notice it with her peripheral mage sight? Or does it only trigger the turn its cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd ping PMS as soon as the other Mage walks into sensory range, but that doesn't mean the Mage knows where it's coming from, or what it is, and they are apparently having their PMS pinged pretty near frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T05:20:48-07:00","id":937554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=937525#post937525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does peripheral mage sight pick up ongoing supernatural effects that is not concealed? For instance IF a mage uses a spell to enhance her perception for a scene. Could another mage notice it with her peripheral mage sight? Or does it only trigger the turn its cast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Peripheral mage sight is triggered by unconcealed ongoing magical effects or the activation of effects. So yeah, in that situation the mage would trigger peripheral mage sight on other mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:25:44-07:00","id":937616,"title":"","content":"Last I checked, that's explicitly <i>not</i> the case, isn't it? That Mage Sight is only triggered by active effects? A Mage's peripheral sight is only set off by someone, say, casting a spell near them, not casting a spell a mile away and then sneaking up close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:28:02-07:00","id":937617,"title":"","content":"A spell that is still running is an active effect, it's either being consciously maintained by a Mage or has had a part of his will imparted into it in order to keep it active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:32:48-07:00","id":937622,"title":"","content":"I thought it's like with Ghosts - just being there and existing isn't active. Like, Accelerated Mage who is moving at normal pace isn't pinging Sight, but the instant he uses his ability to overwrite initiative, *ping*.<br /> So I would say - it sends a ping when it's first cast, and every time it does something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:35:40-07:00","id":937623,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was my understanding, too; once a spell is cast, it's a part of the world and hence no longer an active, changing effect.<br /> <br /> I could swear Dave talked about this at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T18:35:49-07:00","id":937856,"title":"","content":"So we don't seem to have a conclusive view about PMS here then i take it. I as well find it weird if PMS allowed to detect &quot;passive&quot; magical powers that are being used. But then again im not completely in the mage mindset as of yet.<br /> Although i find it really weird if a mage could sense another mages (or other supers) powers just by being in proximity later on (while it's still in duration). If PMS is triggered by everything, how does mages even remotely trust each other? Like every member in the Consilium has at lest one spell more or less always active it seems. Why would I use Mental Shield if I'm worried about Goetia and then try to get help from my fellow mages when they can't know if im gonna murder them with that spell that tingles their feelings (PMS) or if it's just a spell to keep him clean in the rain without scrutinizing him thoroughly with mage sight. <br /> At least, if it doesnt trigger PMS all the time, it gives other mages a bit of reasonable doubt. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:55:34-07:00","id":937985,"title":"","content":"Guess this is one of those things that we'll need Dave or one of the writers to comment on, until then &quot;go with what feels better to you&quot; is valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T02:32:22-07:00","id":937998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=935477#post935477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no direct damage spells in the book that can be made to be Lasting outside of ST fiat</div> </div> </div> </div>All Direct Damage spells are pretty heavily implied to be Lasting, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T04:15:08-07:00","id":938015,"title":"","content":"They aren't. Consequence of their influence (damage) is, but spells themselves aren't - otherwise Tilts inflicted by them wouldn't short out after their Duration is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T04:22:09-07:00","id":938017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=937998#post937998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Direct Damage spells are pretty heavily implied to be Lasting, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/JK4UPPM.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Now that we're discussing Lasting, I have trouble with this thing here. What does it mean? I mean, there are ways to revert most spell effects, including healing (which is lasting and can be reverted by just wounding the same place again in the same manner, and direct damage which can be reverted by healing and repair). For example, if I use Matter \u25cf\u25cf &quot;Shaping&quot; should it have this +2 Reach option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:58:46-07:00","id":938081,"title":"","content":"It's for when a spell effects are ongoing, not its side effects, as far as I can tell. The way a block of metal looks after you shape it is a side effect of the spell that grants you the power to shape it in the first place so it requires no extra Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:54:59-07:00","id":938110,"title":"","content":"I'm just realizing this. If I give a dog gills with transform life, make that spell indefinite and add the reach option, I can breed puppys with permanent (lasting) gills from it right? This adds some horrifying possibilities for fucked up mages breeding weird chimeras for whatever purposes.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:09:28-07:00","id":938115,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I want to comment on the &quot;only spells without any way to revert them&quot; aspect, because I can't think of many - maybe any - spells where that is the case. Even a spell like, say, Shaping, could theoretically have all the shaping done by the Mage magically reverse. There's not really any spell I can think of where the universe can't hit a reset button.<br /> <br /> For the record, in practice, I follow the &quot;Consequences of the spell do not disappear&quot; mantra; the effects of the spell in the world don't vanish after the spell ends. It's just the whole criterion for what is a good basis for making something Lasting doesn't seem right or clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:10:05-07:00","id":938117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938110#post938110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just realizing this. If I give a dog gills with transform life, make that spell indefinite and add the reach option, I can breed puppys with permanent (lasting) gills from it right? This adds some horrifying possibilities for fucked up mages breeding weird chimeras for whatever purposes.....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well. You can even make human chimeras. I'm 100% sure that some mages managed to make a colony of &quot;special purpose&quot; people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T13:01:21-07:00","id":938288,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about the breeding thing. Are you actually affecting their genetic information? Would you have to rewrite their Symbolic Ideal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:41:21-07:00","id":938395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +2 Reach: The bestowed traits, if made indefinite, can be<br /> passed on to the creature\u2019s descendants. </div> </div> </div>Since purview of Life Arcanum includes evolution - yes, you are affecting genetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:24:27-07:00","id":938504,"title":"","content":"Hoo that's cool, I actually forgot they called this specific option<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Question.<br /> <br /> Spells in Demesnes and Verges don't risk Paradox. How does it interact with unsafe Relinquishment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-28-2016, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:31:12-07:00","id":938637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938504#post938504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hoo that's cool, I actually forgot they called this specific option<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Question.<br /> <br /> Spells in Demesnes and Verges don't risk Paradox. How does it interact with unsafe Relinquishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's a solid answer anywhere, but I think that as long as the spell doesn't effect anything outside of the bounds of the verge or demesne, it wouldn't start building Paradox. But if you buff yourself inside of it, unsafely relinquish, and then leave, it'd work as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T03:09:46-07:00","id":938710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938504#post938504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells in Demesnes and Verges don't risk Paradox. How does it interact with unsafe Relinquishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>It functions as normal because the warping of a spell that's unsafely relinquished has nothing to do with Paradox other than the fact that it recycles some rules from Paradox. A spell that's unsafely relinquished that goes haywire has nothing to do with the Abyss, and we've had this conversation already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T05:10:53-07:00","id":938742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938637#post938637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's a solid answer anywhere, but I think that as long as the spell doesn't effect anything outside of the bounds of the verge or demesne, it wouldn't start building Paradox. But if you buff yourself inside of it, unsafely relinquish, and then leave, it'd work as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it not have Paradox, since Paradox is checked for at the casting, but just accrue dissonance effects?<br /> <br /> Also, separate question I asked in the errata thread and received 1 answer to regarding interpretation of a specific application before temporal sympathy discussion took over:<br /> <br /> Do attainments stack with spells? Legacy attainments have transient stacking rules, and I didn't see whether stacking at all is unique to them or whether being transient is. Specifically, I'm looking at mage armors that grant armor (forces and matter) stacking with mundane armor that has been magically enhanced by matter magic or a scaly hide granted from life magic.<br /> <br /> Edit: adding to the mix, life armor defense bonus stacking with honing the form to increase dex and/or enhance skill increasing athletics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","user":"Ifisa","date":". 07-28-2016, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T05:48:08-07:00","id":938755,"title":"","content":"Stacking attainments with spells is Transient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T05:56:58-07:00","id":938760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938755#post938755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stacking attainments with spells is Transient.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't understand. Can you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:12:07-07:00","id":938771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938760#post938760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't understand. Can you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like a cite on that, but there are rules under legacy attainments for transient stacking. When you activate the attainment, it can stack with a spell, but the spell it is stacking on is cancelled after a number of turns equal to your dots in the spells highest arcana. However, it's under the legacy attainment specific rules, and I didn't see it for normal attainments. Since I'm going over this issue with my ST, a cite would really help us.<br /> <br /> Our dilemma is this: Gnosis 5 Life Master with Mind 3 wants as high as defense as he can get. He normally has 6, with 3 wits and dex and 3 athletics.<br /> <br /> He activates his life armor attainment, granting 3 defense and allowing him to use the higher of dex and wits.<br /> <br /> He casts honing the form, and reaches to ignore his attribute cap, gaining 5 dex (I'm just going to call potency equal to his dots despite duration primary, because it isn't relevant to the discussion)<br /> <br /> He casts Enhance Skill to grant himself 3 more athletics, reaching to ignore the cap.<br /> <br /> This is pretty good, but he also doesn't want to get hurt if he is hit. He already has 3 general armor from the attainment, but casts Transform Life to grant himself a scaly hide with 2/1 armor. Edit: then he calls his matter master friend and has her cast aegis on his suit to grant *that* 5 armor.<br /> <br /> What is the end defense and armor he gets, and which spells are contributing to this? I like examples, sorry that this is long and annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","user":"Ifisa","date":". 07-28-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:15:11-07:00","id":938773,"title":"","content":"Why does Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf &quot;Telekinesis&quot; not require Mastery of Forces? You are making a force to act on an object <i>ex nihil</i><i>.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:20:45-07:00","id":938776,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11862\" data-vbnamecard=\"11862\">Ifisa</a> there's isn't a citation other than the legacy attainment rules you just pointed to. From there though we can build a reasonable assumption that if the devs didn't intend to create easily abused doubling up of benefits via a spell/attainment combo (Spells don't combo like that either, explicitly and can be used as a parallel example for this argument) then spells that stack with arcana attainments are also only transient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:21:35-07:00","id":938777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938773#post938773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf &amp;quot;Telekinesis&amp;quot; not require Mastery of Forces? You are making a force to act on an object <i>ex nihil</i><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You're changing a property of the object from potential to kinetic, problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:22:47-07:00","id":938779,"title":"","content":"Those stack - general armor from a Mage Armor spell stacks with the Matter spell that gives clothing an armor rating, and the attainment giving you the higher of two attributes for defense works fine with boosting those attributes.<br /> <br /> Only when the same stat is being altered does it get limited to the highest potency spell;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:25:23-07:00","id":938782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938773#post938773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf &amp;quot;Telekinesis&amp;quot; not require Mastery of Forces? You are making a force to act on an object <i>ex nihil</i><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You're altering the properties of the many forces at work on your subject to stop them flying off the planet as it plunges through space at many million miles per hour.<br /> <br /> (Forces is one of those arcana where mastery is only needed for very specific cases - you're *always* covered in forces.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:25:26-07:00","id":938783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938779#post938779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those stack - general armor from a Mage Armor spell stacks with the Matter spell that gives clothing an armor rating, and the attainment giving you the higher of two attributes for defense works fine with boosting those attributes.<br /> <br /> Only when the same stat is being altered does it get limited to the highest potency spell;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dave, can I ask for the clarification regarding the &quot;cannot revert&quot; rules for Lasting? It is fairly unclear.<br /> What's the criterion that makes the result of Matter \u25cf\u25cf &quot;Shaping&quot; Lasting and the result of Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf &quot;Transubstantiation&quot; not Lasting? Is it purely from a game balance standpoint of not letting people make easy gold and other valuables with Adepthood in Matter?<br /> <br /> I'm asking this because this is one of the points that for me makes the internal logic of the magic system sort of go out of whack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","user":"Altasaire","date":". 07-28-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:32:55-07:00","id":938787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938779#post938779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those stack - general armor from a Mage Armor spell stacks with the Matter spell that gives clothing an armor rating, and the attainment giving you the higher of two attributes for defense works fine with boosting those attributes.<br /> <br /> Only when the same stat is being altered does it get limited to the highest potency spell;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I am loving the Mage book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:34:13-07:00","id":938788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938782#post938782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're altering the properties of the many forces at work on your subject to stop them flying off the planet as it plunges through space at many million miles per hour.<br /> <br /> (Forces is one of those arcana where mastery is only needed for very specific cases - you're *always* covered in forces.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so you're modifying the resultant vector of the object? okay, that's fair. Would be cool if it said so in the spell, though.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf &quot;Gravitic Supremacy&quot;, can we have some sort of guideline regarding what &quot;real-life&quot; numbers that effect would boil down to? What's the potency to make an area with Jupiter's gravity, or something? (The effect as it is is fine and dandy, but it only effects &quot;actors&quot; in the scene (modifying their effective attributes, Speed, and such) and isn't really conducive to interesting things that logically should be able to be done with it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","user":"Altasaire","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T09:55:47-07:00","id":938914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938782#post938782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're altering the properties of the many forces at work on your subject to stop them flying off the planet as it plunges through space at many million miles per hour.<br /> <br /> (Forces is one of those arcana where mastery is only needed for very specific cases - you're *always* covered in forces.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would a Forces 5 gravity, kinetic energy or inertia Unmaking spell therefore cause a subject to fly off the planet at many millions of miles per hour? Would this be the Forces gravity version of a Withstand or die spell?<br /> <br /> Also, if Forces are so uniquely ubiquitous and powerful, shouldn't spells like Earthquake only require Forces 4 or below?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T17:45:48-07:00","id":939232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=938914#post938914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Forces 5 gravity, kinetic energy or inertia Unmaking spell therefore cause a subject to fly off the planet at many millions of miles per hour? Would this be the Forces gravity version of a Withstand or die spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Velocity is relative, not just in an Einsteinian sense, but in a simpler sense too, Galileo knew this for instance. In a very real way, sitting in a house is just as stationary as sitting in a supersonic jet in horizontal flight (ignoring turbulence). Therefore an Unmaking velocity spell needs to nullify relative velocity, and thus nullifies velocity relative to whatever, in context, is symbolically stationary. This is usually the earth surface but a vehicle they are inside of would probably work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 07-28-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T01:53:01-07:00","id":940004,"title":"","content":"So have I gotten this correctly :<br /> <br /> At Gnosis 1 you can only increase <b>one</b> Arcanum to 3 dots, this is not a typo and meant ruling Arcana, right? So if I am a Mastigos and start out with Gnosis 1, Mind 3, Space 2 and Death 1 I have to increase Gnosis to 2 before I can reach Space 3 in any fashion.<br /> <br /> The Limits of Arcana give costs for buying Spheres beyond your limit. This only applies to the limits given in the adjacent chart (above 5 for ruling, above 4 for common, above 2 for inferior) and <b>not for </b>learning Arcana above your allowed Gnosis limit, correct? So aforementioned Mastigos could not spend 5 xp to increase his Space to 3 at Gnosis 1 (or his Mind to 4 for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T02:24:00-07:00","id":940016,"title":"","content":"How does the Indomitable merit from the base rulebook interact with Withstand, or spells in general?<br /> <br /> My assumption is that since Indomitable works on contesting and resisting supernatural affects and the Withstand rules specifically say spells are not resisted or contested unless, for instance, Counterspelled, Indomitable would not apply here. However, would it work on Counterspell? Counterspell says it is a Clash of Will, which afaik do not benefit from Indomitable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T02:24:48-07:00","id":940017,"title":"","content":"It doesn't do anything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T02:28:24-07:00","id":940019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940004#post940004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So have I gotten this correctly :<br /> <br /> At Gnosis 1 you can only increase <b>one</b> Arcanum to 3 dots, this is not a typo and meant ruling Arcana, right? So if I am a Mastigos and start out with Gnosis 1, Mind 3, Space 2 and Death 1 I have to increase Gnosis to 2 before I can reach Space 3 in any fashion.<br /> <br /> The Limits of Arcana give costs for buying Spheres beyond your limit. This only applies to the limits given in the adjacent chart (above 5 for ruling, above 4 for common, above 2 for inferior) and <b>not for </b>learning Arcana above your allowed Gnosis limit, correct? So aforementioned Mastigos could not spend 5 xp to increase his Space to 3 at Gnosis 1 (or his Mind to 4 for example).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not a typo You can't have a Gnosis 1 character with two 3-dot Arcana.<br /> <br /> The Gnosis cap on how high your highest and other Arcana are doesn't get overridden by the experiences cost increase for going beyond your Path's limitations. It costs a Mastigos an extra Experience to buy his third dot of Matter, but if he's only Gnosis 1 and has Space 3 and Matter 2 he can't buy a third dot of <i>anything</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T02:49:45-07:00","id":940021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940017#post940017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't do anything</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you had previously said merits like Indomitable would grant half their normal dice to a character's Withstand rating? So, +1 in this case?<br /> <br /> Or did you just mean it doesn't do anything for Counterspell specifically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:01:14-07:00","id":940022,"title":"","content":"Can you elaborate on how Lasting works? Says spells that can't be undone but what does that mean? Anything can be undone, can it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:18:03-07:00","id":940026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940022#post940022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you elaborate on how Lasting works? Says spells that can't be undone but what does that mean? Anything can be undone, can it not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lasting is more about effect of the spell than the spell itself. When you shape matter you end up with Lastingly shaped matter. When you heal someone the effect is Lasting because it can be sustained naturally. When you don't need the spell to exist to maintain the effect - the spell is Lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 07-30-2016, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:27:51-07:00","id":940029,"title":"","content":"So, using something like Conditioning would also be lasting? Or a Matter transformation? I mean, obviously you can't have an eternally burning fire because that's obviously requiring magic to keep running. But, if it's fairly mundane it can stick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:39:00-07:00","id":940032,"title":"","content":"Well yes, they can be made Lasting with indefinite duration, +2 Reach and 1 mana. But only with ST approval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:47:24-07:00","id":940034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940004#post940004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So have I gotten this correctly :<br /> <br /> At Gnosis 1 you can only increase <b>one</b> Arcanum to 3 dots, this is not a typo and meant ruling Arcana, right? So if I am a Mastigos and start out with Gnosis 1, Mind 3, Space 2 and Death 1 I have to increase Gnosis to 2 before I can reach Space 3 in any fashion.<br /> <br /> The Limits of Arcana give costs for buying Spheres beyond your limit. This only applies to the limits given in the adjacent chart (above 5 for ruling, above 4 for common, above 2 for inferior) and <b>not for </b>learning Arcana above your allowed Gnosis limit, correct? So aforementioned Mastigos could not spend 5 xp to increase his Space to 3 at Gnosis 1 (or his Mind to 4 for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>I must note, it is not limited to Ruling Arcana. You can have an Starting Mastigos with Gnosis 1 and Spirit 3, Mind 2 and Space 1, if you want. You will have to wait to Gnosis 2 to have any other Arcanum at 3, Ruling or not Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T04:34:20-07:00","id":940045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940022#post940022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you elaborate on how Lasting works? Says spells that can't be undone but what does that mean? Anything can be undone, can it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Say that you use a Matter spell to change the shape of a rock. After you are done, do you need any magic for the rock to stay in the shape that you gave it? Not really, the laws of nature will do that for you, it would require more energy to change the rock than to keep it the same, and thus the effects of the spell are Lasting. Or when you throw fire at a pile of hay, causing it to start burning. When your spell ends, the pile will still be burning, and without an external force to snuff it out you would need more energy to stop it than to let it continue, so it keeps burning like a natural fire. The fire will eventually die out, Lasting does not mean &quot;eternal&quot;, it just means the effects of the spell will keep on carrying on like a natural effect.<br /> <br /> So wounds from a spell are Lasting not because they will never heal (they will heal naturally), but because they will not spontaneously heal. You would need more magic to heal them again, so it would not make sense for that effect to vanish when your spell does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:25:39-07:00","id":940188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940032#post940032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes, they can be made Lasting with indefinite duration, +2 Reach and 1 mana. But only with ST approval.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having an Indefinite Duration does not make a spell Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:31:45-07:00","id":940301,"title":"","content":"My bad. I confused a few things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T19:18:10-07:00","id":940389,"title":"","content":"Okay, so we're having trouble parsing a spell. Specifically Incognito Presence and it's new Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Option 1) Withstand is there to affect the subject of the spell - that is, the person being turned invisible against their will. Precedent exists in Vampire, Geist and I think Demon. Pretty straightforward.<br /> <br /> Option 2) Withstand is a rating for everyone that would see the invisible person, and the spell's Potency is constantly checked against the Withstand ratings of everyone in an area. Makes some sort of sense, but changes the utility wildly.<br /> <br /> Which is it?<br /> <br /> Edit: Question 2: Can a mage maintain a spell relinquished with a WP to keep it safe? I always thought so because of this line:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without maintenance from the caster, the spell may go awry if left for very long periods. </div> </div> </div>...but now I'm not sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 07-30-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:48:10-07:00","id":940424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940389#post940389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so we're having trouble parsing a spell. Specifically Incognito Presence and it's new Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Option 1) Withstand is there to affect the subject of the spell - that is, the person being turned invisible against their will. Precedent exists in Vampire, Geist and I think Demon. Pretty straightforward.<br /> <br /> Option 2) Withstand is a rating for everyone that would see the invisible person, and the spell's Potency is constantly checked against the Withstand ratings of everyone in an area. Makes some sort of sense, but changes the utility wildly.<br /> <br /> Which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. it autosucceds at hiding the person, which is why it costs Mana. Withstand is always the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Question 2: Can a mage maintain a spell relinquished with a[ WP to keep it safe? I always thought so because of this line:<br /> <br /> ...but now I'm not sure. </div> </div> </div>No. You can only maintain spells still in your spell control. The sentance you quote is the consequence of relinquishing; without maintenance (which you can't perform any more...) the spell can go haywire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:24:44-07:00","id":940479,"title":"","content":"Why is Incognito Presence (autosuccess at hiding a person) different enough to warrant a Mana cost compared to, say, Hidden Hoard (autosuccess at making my sword beneath notice so i can stab unsuspecting people)? Both make me autosucceed at a skill (Steatlh to hide a person, Larceny to hide a weapon), and both render mundane attempts at detection auto fails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:25:45-07:00","id":940565,"title":"","content":"The question about Incognito Presence popped up in here already three or more times and Dave is ignoring it a little bit.<br /> <br /> Q: Lets say that you are falling from stratosphere (really fast) and you cast Ban on yourself without adding Forces to the spell. Will you suddenly stop in midair? And in this case will you die from all the kinetic energy that you gathered which can't escape your Ban?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:45:47-07:00","id":940573,"title":"","content":"Appreciate it, thanks Dave!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T05:03:37-07:00","id":940577,"title":"","content":"The description of the Amnion says it counts as equipment and takes physical form like a diving suit or a scaled hide.<br /> Because of how the Astral works Arcana affect stuff based on how they look, so anything that looks like a living being can be affected by Life, objects by Matter, etc.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that depending on what form your Amnion takes you could use Matter or Life to increase its armor bonus like any other equipment bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:06:57-07:00","id":940595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940565#post940565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question about Incognito Presence popped up in here already three or more times and Dave is ignoring it a little bit.<br /> <br /> Q: Lets say that you are falling from stratosphere (really fast) and you cast Ban on yourself without adding Forces to the spell. Will you suddenly stop in midair? And in this case will you die from all the kinetic energy that you gathered which can't escape your Ban?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be stuck in a falling loop, but your kinetic energy which is also trapped wouldn't increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:39:24-07:00","id":940601,"title":"","content":"A question regarding Pattering and Unmaking Spells regarding the Life/Matter/Forces Arcana.<br /> <br /> To turn a human into a statue I need Life 4 and Matter 4 , because the gross matter he is made up of is alive, thus turning it into a Life pattern rather than a Matter pattern. Now if I wish to use transform energy (Forces 4) with a human as the target to turn all his bodyheat into say sound, turning him into a frozen (and thus quite dead) corpse, does that require conjunctional Life 4 aswell, since the Forces pattern inside a living human are a Life pattern?<br /> <br /> Let's go to unmaking : Forces 5 can kill a human with eradicate energy (eliminating all the energy in the body, killing the target) without conjunctional Life. Does that mean that a Matter 5 unmaking practice like annihilate matter can be used on living human targets aswell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:49:05-07:00","id":940603,"title":"","content":"I have run a few play test scenarios yesterday to check if everyone understands how mechanics works before we play the actual game. Aand we figured out that teleporting wont help because you wont get rid of your speed and Ban would just hold you without losing speed either (or even kill you depending on interpretation). <br /> <br /> So we came up with a spell that changes kinetic energy to potential energy by virtually suspends your altitude on 10.000 metres leting you land like nothing happend. Kind of Shield of Chronos but for Space? And if the spell runs out you just end up splashed on the ground wherever you are in that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:54:52-07:00","id":940636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940601#post940601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> You need Forces to change kinetic to potential energy, but you could also fray or unravel the down vector that's exerting itself on your body in order to slow or stop before hitting the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:55:18-07:00","id":940637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940603#post940603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">teleporting wont help because you wont get rid of your speed</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that? The other side of the planet is going over 2000 miles/hour if you are at the equator but you can teleport there just fine. Also you can probably teleport onto a moving airplane fine too. The spell is probably capable of making you arrive stationary relative to your target.<br /> <br /> If you don't like that, then bend space so up and down are switched. Then you will start to fall upwards, but because you were already moving downwards, gravity will need to slow you down first, then once you are at a complete stop, teleport away and cancel the other spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T09:34:24-07:00","id":940655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940636#post940636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's correct.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> You need Forces to change kinetic to potential energy, but you could also fray or unravel the down vector that's exerting itself on your body in order to slow or stop before hitting the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing it directly - yes. But when you keep the height at the same value you are holding the energy as potential.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940637#post940637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does it say that? The other side of the planet is going over 2000 miles/hour if you are at the equator but you can teleport there just fine. Also you can probably teleport onto a moving airplane fine too. The spell is probably capable of making you arrive stationary relative to your target.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when put a space door in an airplane the door is moving with the same speed as an airplane and if you emerge from them you are gaining all the speed factors of a plane.<br /> But if you are jumping through you end up few feet further from the portal. The momentum is preserved. Thinking of it... you are right in some way. If you would enter the portal very, very slowly it would be just fine. So you need to cast it in front of an make it go slightly slower than you. +1 Reach probably? Thanks. Thats neat.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940637#post940637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like that, then bend space so up and down are switched. Then you will start to fall upwards, but because you were already moving downwards, gravity will need to slow you down first, then once you are at a complete stop, teleport away and cancel the other spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>We thought about it but virtually suspending height seemed way cooler <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:43:05-07:00","id":940688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940655#post940655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing it directly - yes. But when you keep the height at the same value you are holding the energy as potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fraying the vector so you slow down by not travelling as easily along the path of down would still work then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:15:30-07:00","id":940708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940688#post940688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fraying the vector so you slow down by not travelling as easily along the path of down would still work then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it would work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:36:41-07:00","id":940752,"title":"","content":"What are the requirements for creating a Demesne, now? There was a mention of an Attainment in the pre-errata PDF file, but the official mechanical errata document doesn't mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:53:53-07:00","id":940768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940752#post940752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the requirements for creating a Demesne, now? There was a mention of an Attainment in the pre-errata PDF file, but the official mechanical errata document doesn't mention it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainment in this case basically just means &quot;Magical thing that can be done without casting a spell.&quot; So the system for establishing a demesne hasn't changed. Considering it's almost certainly just a terminology slip it may have been changed (Assuming it was caught) without bothering to mention it in the errata document because nothing was actually made different in terms of mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:13:10-07:00","id":940789,"title":"","content":"Demesne creation rules are on page 99.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T16:29:49-07:00","id":941496,"title":"","content":"How many dots of Space,Mind and Reach do i need to do a higer version of one mind two thougths and mind control to control several people and make them do different things.<br /> Example, my char is studing in the basemant, mind puppet #1 is fixing the roof, mind puppet #2 is cooking, mind puppet #3 is socializing with the neighbour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 08-01-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T18:39:10-07:00","id":941576,"title":"","content":"That's just the basic 2 dot psychic control spell with extra Scale factors, you only need Space if you're going to cast the spell on targets that you can only access via Sympathy.<br /> <br /> Extra tracks of thought via One Mind Two Thoughts is also just an increase in Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T04:33:59-07:00","id":941834,"title":"","content":"This thread is huge and I just started mage. Apologies if it's been covered.<br /> <br /> The Familiar Manifestation states that it lasts until one of the parties cancel it. It also says only the Familiar spell grants it. This kind of feels like it's implying that the Condition is Lasting.<br /> <br /> The Familiar spell says the Familiar Manifestation lasts as long as the Duration, or until one of the two involved decide to end it.<br /> <br /> Does the Condition outlast the Duration or not? How does this apply to the Familiar Merit, which somehow gives you a Familiar that's immune to having the Familiar spell dispelled? I get spending the XP for the merit should have a bonus over just casting the spell, I'm just curious how you would ICly explain buying the merit and making the spell (seemingly) impossible to dispel.<br /> <br /> Related: It says it must affect two subjects. Do you have to increase Scale for this, thus making the spell always have a -2 penalty to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:08:45-07:00","id":941856,"title":"","content":"The merit doesn't make your bond immune to Dispellation it just refunds the merit dots if that happens. <br /> <br /> Additionally, yes, the effect of the spell will go away if the Duration lapses, but it's not that difficult to achieve Indefinite so just do that.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, you would have to take the -2 dice penalty to increase Scale to two targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:54:25-07:00","id":942775,"title":"","content":"A mage lost his soul and replace it with a sleeper soul. He can now slowly recover his gnosis and arcana.<br /> Will the soul also transform to become an awakened soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:09:50-07:00","id":942783,"title":"","content":"It's effectively Awakened as soon as it's put in a Mage and the Mage may use his magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:03:07-07:00","id":942816,"title":"","content":"So, a tremere using a mage to farm awakened souls could happen then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:16:39-07:00","id":942824,"title":"","content":"It seems to be less important if the soul itself is awakened than if the vessel you put it in has Gnosis in the current edition. Awakened Soul seems to be &quot;Soul + Gnosis-Containing Vessel&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:39:18-07:00","id":942850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=941834#post941834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is huge and I just started mage. Apologies if it's been covered.<br /> <br /> The Familiar Manifestation states that it lasts until one of the parties cancel it. It also says only the Familiar spell grants it. This kind of feels like it's implying that the Condition is Lasting.<br /> <br /> The Familiar spell says the Familiar Manifestation lasts as long as the Duration, or until one of the two involved decide to end it.<br /> <br /> Does the Condition outlast the Duration or not? How does this apply to the Familiar Merit, which somehow gives you a Familiar that's immune to having the Familiar spell dispelled? I get spending the XP for the merit should have a bonus over just casting the spell, I'm just curious how you would ICly explain buying the merit and making the spell (seemingly) impossible to dispel.<br /> <br /> Related: It says it must affect two subjects. Do you have to increase Scale for this, thus making the spell always have a -2 penalty to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Familiar Bond isn't lasting: the Merit assumes whoever cast the spell for you bought it up to indefinite and then relinquished it safely, but even then if someone dispels it, no more familiar bond. (and one pissed-off ephemeral entity now suffering essence bleed)<br /> <br /> But you, the player of the mage who now has an ex-familiar would get your merit dots back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:52:58-07:00","id":942868,"title":"","content":"Another counter intuitive thing for Familiars is that you can only have Rank 2 Familiars, so anything that boosts them to Rank 3 (Say, Bolster Spirit) would logically cancel the spell [or at least supress it until virtual rank is over].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:57:57-07:00","id":942875,"title":"","content":"That is indeed what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:13:59-07:00","id":942901,"title":"","content":"Daaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaave<br /> Are meditation bonuses to Breaking Points supposed to work on Acts of Hubris checks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:39:06-07:00","id":942921,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if I should answer because you have evoke the name of the developer, but I will give it a shot. According to the rules, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After successfully meditating, the character gets a +1 bonus to her next breaking point roll </div> </div> </div>Of course, ST has ultimate say, but RAW that player gets that bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:42:05-07:00","id":942925,"title":"","content":"Acts of hubris are not breaking points. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:02:15-07:00","id":942978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=942925#post942925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acts of hubris are not breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can spend WP to get +3 on AoH, so another +1 isn't a big deal. It might even be in theme if you're meditating on the AoH you're most likely to commit next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:52:39-07:00","id":943359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=942850#post942850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Familiar Bond isn't lasting: the Merit assumes whoever cast the spell for you bought it up to indefinite and then relinquished it safely, but even then if someone dispels it, no more familiar bond. (and one pissed-off ephemeral entity now suffering essence bleed)<br /> <br /> But you, the player of the mage who now has an ex-familiar would get your merit dots back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming the spirit would be amenable to reestablishing the bond, though, if a hostile force dispelled it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T02:30:28-07:00","id":943499,"title":"","content":"That's dependent on the context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:18:06-07:00","id":943532,"title":"","content":"Some Questions on Area scale spells:<br /> <br /> - &quot;Range&quot; talks about Subjects. For instance, at standard range you have to &quot;touch&quot; the subject, at advanced it is anyone you can see, hear... How does this interact with Area spells? If I do not use advanced range, must the Area by necessity be directly around me? If I use Sensory, can the area start further out from me instead? Do only people I have sensory contact with get affected?<br /> <br /> - Can you use Runes Yantra when using an Area spell? The area spell you use is not your Subject, and Runes states it needs to be put directly on the Subject, so... no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-04-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:34:10-07:00","id":943535,"title":"","content":"You have following options:<br /> - Touch Range + Area Scale: Stuff explodes with you in the center.<br /> - Sensory Range + Area Scale: Stuff explodes from any point you can perceive in the center<br /> - Touch Range + Area Scale + Aimed Spell: You pick a target spot and shoot it with your spell, if you succeed with the Aimed Spell roll, it hits and explodes as if you had touched that spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:43:50-07:00","id":943539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943535#post943535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have following options:<br /> - Touch Range + Area Scale: Stuff explodes with you in the center.<br /> - Sensory Range + Area Scale: Stuff explodes from any point you can perceive in the center<br /> - Touch Range + Area Scale + Aimed Spell: You pick a target spot and shoot it with your spell, if you succeed with the Aimed Spell roll, it hits and explodes as if you had touched that spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall Dave saying you could touch any point inside the area, not just the center (so if you wanted to cover an entire room, touching the door would be enough), but can't seem to find it right now :S<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:52:04-07:00","id":943543,"title":"","content":"Well, that would make shooting kamehamehas with spells much easier, as you would literally just touch the edge of the spell area and be safe yourself while dodging need to do aimed spells or sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:46:11-07:00","id":943564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943532#post943532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Questions on Area scale spells:<br /> <br /> - &quot;Range&quot; talks about Subjects. For instance, at standard range you have to &quot;touch&quot; the subject, at advanced it is anyone you can see, hear... How does this interact with Area spells? If I do not use advanced range, must the Area by necessity be directly around me? If I use Sensory, can the area start further out from me instead? Do only people I have sensory contact with get affected?<br /> <br /> - Can you use Runes Yantra when using an Area spell? The area spell you use is not your Subject, and Runes states it needs to be put directly on the Subject, so... no?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any part of the area has to be within touch / sensory range, not all of it. You can make D&amp;D like cones if you want to.<br /> <br /> If a player described covering an area with runes like something from a horror movie, I'd let them use the Yantra, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:50:27-07:00","id":943565,"title":"","content":"Can Life shape change you into extinct animals?<br /> Is boosting your attribute in that new form a subject to spell stacking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:53:55-07:00","id":943566,"title":"","content":"By the way, on the subject of runes, despite them being mentioned as tattoos, the rule that changing the perfect alignment of the symbols breaks the spell seems to counter that. Most movements will change the structure of your body enough to change the alignment, often considerably.<br /> <br /> Can you draw runes ahead of time, or do you need to do it at the same time as casting the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:57:08-07:00","id":943567,"title":"","content":"The runes thing then gives you another cool feature, because you can literally cover a room in runes, use it to cast Advanced Scale spells that target whole room, and then take things you casted spells on outside the room.<br /> Practical Example:<br /> NecroMcNecro dedicates a room in their sanctum to ritual spells. NecroMcNecro gathers his corpses once every month in the room, and uses runes inside to improve his magic. Then, after animating is done, he takes all of the corpses outside and proceeds with his mysterious plans.<br /> <br /> AntiUndeadMsAntiUndead doesn't like zombies pouncing around and conquering the world, so she takes a daring mission and sneaks into the sanctum of NecroMcNecro and distrubs the runes to end the undead army prematurely.<br /> It turns runes from &quot;really really not that useful&quot; to &quot;something you will probably be using a lot in your sanctum shaeningans&quot;, because hey, +2 yantra! <br /> And dedicated ritual rooms covered in evil runes are just in genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:05:50-07:00","id":943568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943567#post943567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The runes thing then gives you another cool feature, because you can literally cover a room in runes, use it to cast Advanced Scale spells that target whole room, and then take things you casted spells on outside the room.<br /> Practical Example:<br /> NecroMcNecro dedicates a room in their sanctum to ritual spells. NecroMcNecro gathers his corpses once every month in the room, and uses runes inside to improve his magic. Then, after animating is done, he takes all of the corpses outside and proceeds with his mysterious plans.<br /> <br /> AntiUndeadMsAntiUndead doesn't like zombies pouncing around and conquering the world, so she takes a daring mission and sneaks into the sanctum of NecroMcNecro and distrubs the runes to end the undead army prematurely.<br /> It turns runes from &quot;really really not that useful&quot; to &quot;something you will probably be using a lot in your sanctum shaeningans&quot;, because hey, +2 yantra!<br /> And dedicated ritual rooms covered in evil runes are just in genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good for flavour, though purely by RAW it would not work as runes need to go on their subject, not the area you cast in. Could grant a +1 Place yantra, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:18:10-07:00","id":943576,"title":"","content":"Well, I was assuming the Dave's ruling of &quot;make it look like it's from a horror movie and it will work&quot; and checked for consequences. Then I liked them :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:21:03-07:00","id":943608,"title":"","content":"For Lasting effects, is there a more hard rule for finding out which spells have Lasting effects? I find the theory easy to grasp, but in practice it is difficult.<br /> <br /> Let us take Matter as an example.<br /> <br /> The Crucible spell makes an object a more perfect version of itself. perfecting is the opposite of Fraying, so this would be Lasting, correct? The first Reach option in its description wears off, since it calls for a duration, but the base effect seems lasting to me? The object won't degrade itself again without an outside force.<br /> <br /> That one seems clear to me, but what about Wonderful Machine? Does it just blow itself apart once the duration ends? Seems... a bit odd? But I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:27:43-07:00","id":943644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943565#post943565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Life shape change you into extinct animals?<br /> Is boosting your attribute in that new form a subject to spell stacking?</div> </div> </div> </div>After giving it some more thought: Are they extinct because supernal says so? Blueprints are still there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:53:56-07:00","id":943841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943608#post943608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Lasting effects, is there a more hard rule for finding out which spells have Lasting effects? I find the theory easy to grasp, but in practice it is difficult.<br /> <br /> Let us take Matter as an example.<br /> <br /> The Crucible spell makes an object a more perfect version of itself. perfecting is the opposite of Fraying, so this would be Lasting, correct? The first Reach option in its description wears off, since it calls for a duration, but the base effect seems lasting to me? The object won't degrade itself again without an outside force.<br /> <br /> That one seems clear to me, but what about Wonderful Machine? Does it just blow itself apart once the duration ends? Seems... a bit odd? But I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if you still have Duration on Crucible, when the Potency runs out you get no further benefit from the spell, other than possibly availability rating bonus. Once the Duration runs out that would also go away. It's really not any different from a particularly good knife getting dull over time, and the effects bestowed by the Potency of the spell are anything but natural which is why they're not Lasting.<br /> <br /> Blow apart, falls apart, become useless junk, whatever, as long as it's no longer operable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T01:09:33-07:00","id":944185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943567#post943567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The runes thing then gives you another cool feature, because you can literally cover a room in runes, use it to cast Advanced Scale spells that target whole room, and then take things you casted spells on outside the room.<br /> Practical Example:<br /> NecroMcNecro dedicates a room in their sanctum to ritual spells. NecroMcNecro gathers his corpses once every month in the room, and uses runes inside to improve his magic. Then, after animating is done, he takes all of the corpses outside and proceeds with his mysterious plans.<br /> <br /> AntiUndeadMsAntiUndead doesn't like zombies pouncing around and conquering the world, so she takes a daring mission and sneaks into the sanctum of NecroMcNecro and distrubs the runes to end the undead army prematurely.<br /> It turns runes from &quot;really really not that useful&quot; to &quot;something you will probably be using a lot in your sanctum shaeningans&quot;, because hey, +2 yantra!<br /> And dedicated ritual rooms covered in evil runes are just in genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't sound right to me - if you're using runes as a rune yantra to delineate an area, you're saying &quot;Here is a spell which works on things in this area. Just, whatever is in this area while the spell is running.&quot; If you want it to work on your zombies, even if they're not in the room, and not on other corpses, even if they're in the room, you should probably be inscribing the runes on the zombies directly.<br /> <br /> Absolutely works as a place yantra though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:00:40-07:00","id":944380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943841#post943841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Even if you still have Duration on Crucible, when the Potency runs out you get no further benefit from the spell, other than possibly availability rating bonus. Once the Duration runs out that would also go away. It's really not any different from a particularly good knife getting dull over time, and the effects bestowed by the Potency of the spell are anything but natural which is why they're not Lasting.<br /> <br /> Blow apart, falls apart, become useless junk, whatever, as long as it's no longer operable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it says that items such as gold become incredibly pure when the spell is used on them. Very pure gold is naturally possible. The spell has changed the nature of the object in question through the energy applied. Perfecting also governs repair spells, and if you can create lasting matter with magic to replace broken parts/fill up holes and what not, I don't see why a spell of the same nature could not wipe out impurities and leave a &quot;perfected&quot; bar of gold, for instance. Making something better is really just repairing it past its original state, in a way.<br /> <br /> A new source of power would be needed to degrade it, so it doesn't make sense for that to happen from the duration being up.<br /> <br /> So I agree that the 8-again and such would fade, but I see no reason why the increased value of valuable items would fade again once they have been perfected.<br /> <br /> And yes, completely pure gold becoming very impure again instantly *is* &quot;quite different&quot; from a knife going dull. :P One is a process resulting from use and natural processes, the other a mystical event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-05-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:58:30-07:00","id":944443,"title":"","content":"In the case of purifying gold you can assume that gold perfected via magic is more than mundanely perfect so when the spell wears off it reverts to its highest level of mundane purity. That would be a reasonable Lasting effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:02:45-07:00","id":944447,"title":"","content":"Huh. I just make the stuff magically go &quot;poof&quot;, like Cinderella's gear; duration lapsed out, your Availability goes back to what it was initially. Without you arguing here, I would honestly never ever thought about a possibility of Crucible having any Lasting effects at all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:31:50-07:00","id":944563,"title":"","content":"Continued from other thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=944478#post944478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some cases it's not but it seems to generally be the case that Lasting works because its effects can be sustained without further magic. That's how I understand it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I also understand it. The key to take away there being that reverting a change that has been made through magic back to its prior state would essentially take as much energy to accomplish as changing it in the first place, and so in the absence of such an energy source the effects Last, because they really have no other choice than to obey the laws of nature once the magic wears out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=944443#post944443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of purifying gold you can assume that gold perfected via magic is more than mundanely perfect so when the spell wears off it reverts to its highest level of mundane purity. That would be a reasonable Lasting effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds perfectly logical and acceptable to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=944447#post944447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I just make the stuff magically go &quot;poof&quot;, like Cinderella's gear; duration lapsed out, your Availability goes back to what it was initially. Without you arguing here, I would honestly never ever thought about a possibility of Crucible having any Lasting effects at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting to note, Crucible reads:<br /> <br /> &quot;As long as the spell\u2019s Duration lasts, its wielder may spend one<br /> point of Mana at any time to \u201crecharge\u201d this effect, granting<br /> the rote action quality on an additional number of rolls equal<br /> to the spell\u2019s Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why would the author feel the need to point out you can only recharge the effect as long as the Duration lasts, if every effect of the spell poofs out of existence when the Duration ends? Obvious answer: because not every effect does.<br /> <br /> I would even say that you can use the Rote charges after the Duration ends, as that seems to be the intent here. You may only recharge as long as the duration goes, but the only limit on using the charges seems to be Potency, not Duration. Seems implicitly stated in how it is written. I'm not overly attached to that interpretation though, will not bother to sustain a debate on that point. The important part is whether or not people agree that anything resulting from magic that is naturally sustainable in our world persists under the laws of nature, the rest is just a peculiarity of one particular spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here is basically the important part: A Moros takes an ice cube out of the fridge and uses State Change to turn it into liquid water for a minute. What happens when the duration is up? Will it spontaneously and instantly freeze again?<br /> <br /> My take on it: It will stay at the very least partially liquid, as no force is siphoning off the energy it would need to lose to become compeltely solid again. State Change preserves the temperature of things so some small bits of the water may refreeze, but the not-ice cube would have been basically absorbing heat from the environment and moving further away from where it needs to be to freeze from the very moment it was taken out the freezer and melted. Its temperature alone would not be sufficient to enact the change in heat content (which is not the same as temperature) needed to freeze fully, so it does not. IF you purposefully heat it during its time as a liquid, it definitely does not go back to solid after the duration ending.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you use magic to turn concrete into a gas it will contract fully back into a solid as soon as the spell ends, since concrete cannot exist as a gas under room temperature (or at all, ever, for that matter?).<br /> <br /> Maybe State Change isn't the best example, seeing as the description itself says it returns to its &quot;natural state&quot;, making it not much of a debate...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-05-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:56:06-07:00","id":944581,"title":"","content":"Since you don't want to debate about Crucible I'll just say that I disagree with your take on it. The spell requires Potency and Duration to be effective, and the Reach is to further increase the usefulness of the Potency investment in the spell, but any of the effects of the spell will lapse along with the Duration is how I see it. As a sidenote though, damn, that's the kind of spell you bump up to Indefinite and safely relinquish for a permanent, awesome magic item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T16:18:46-07:00","id":944588,"title":"","content":"State change will revert when spell ends, no matter what you changed into what. Magic is not physics. It doesn't care about lack of energy or other natural laws.<br /> Remember that &quot;Ice cube --&gt; Liquid&quot; won't give you &quot;water&quot;. It will give you &quot;Liquid ice cube&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=944581#post944581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you don't want to debate about Crucible I'll just say that I disagree with your take on it. The spell requires Potency and Duration to be effective, and the Reach is to further increase the usefulness of the Potency investment in the spell, but any of the effects of the spell will lapse along with the Duration is how I see it. As a sidenote though, damn, that's the kind of spell you bump up to Indefinite and safely relinquish for a permanent, awesome magic item.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even unsafely relinquishing is interesting now, due to the new paradox table. Unless your GM wants to get rid of the item and removes Advanced Duration (boooohooooo), item is going to become subject of new weird conditions, which fits mage wonderfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-05-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T06:54:02-07:00","id":944818,"title":"","content":"So, Shared Fate.<br /> <br /> 1. Can I link Fates of subjects of different type? Example: Vodoo Doll and a Person.<br /> 2. Is the transferred damage decided based on what happens to the Subject A (subject A is hit with a knife; Subject B suffers like she was hit with a knife too), or the results that happen to Subject A? (Subject A is wearing armor, so knife strike doesn't do much, so Subject B doesn't get hit for much too)<br /> Practical scenario: I link myself to Dude X. I activate Death Armor, thus turning all kinetic damage into Bashing. I shoot myself in the head, dealing Killing Blow of damage that would be lethal but is bashing. Dude's X head explodes - as he has no Death Armor - or is his Damage &quot;just&quot; my massive Bashing?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Talking about Killing Blow...<br /> Premeditated Murder is better than Murder of Passion; Premeditated Murder is only a Sin against Falling Wisdom. Yet, Killing Blow - which is a &quot;Premeditated attempt at ending a sentient life&quot; in one, clear and cut go is an Act of Hubris against Enlightened and Understanding Wisdom, but not against Falling Wisdom???????????????????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????<br /> I get contradictory signals here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-06-2016, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:00:54-07:00","id":944820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=944818#post944818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Shared Fate.<br /> <br /> 1. Can I link Fates of subjects of different type? Example: Vodoo Doll and a Person.<br /> 2. Is the transferred damage decided based on what happens to the Subject A (subject A is hit with a knife; Subject B suffers like she was hit with a knife too), or the results that happen to Subject A? (Subject A is wearing armor, so knife strike doesn't do much, so Subject B doesn't get hit for much too)<br /> Practical scenario: I link myself to Dude X. I activate Death Armor, thus turning all kinetic damage into Bashing. I shoot myself in the head, dealing Killing Blow of damage that would be lethal but is bashing. Dude's X head explodes - as he has no Death Armor - or is his Damage &quot;just&quot; my massive Bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I think, yes<br /> 2. I think this just transfers mechanical damage. If you stab a voodoo doll with a knife, it will probably only be capable of taking a point or two of damage due to low structure. So that point or two of damage is inflicted on the linked subject.<br /> Scenario - As written, they take the damage that you take, not the damage you 'should' take. If your armor reduces it, they take the reduced damage.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:10:51-07:00","id":944827,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. What about Tilts? Imagine I:<br /> a) put Doll on fire (using some kind of ON FIRE tilt)<br /> b) start twisting it arms hoping for, I don't know, Arm Wrack<br /> c) put the Doll in Extreme Environment<br /> d) Shoot it up with a Decay Death Spell that turns it into goo by reducing it's Structure directly to 0<br /> <br /> I like imagery of Arrow who confronts their fear of death by shooting themselves in the head to drop people unconcious due to being subject to something like 9 Bashing damage in one go. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:11:12-07:00","id":944852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=944827#post944827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. What about Tilts? Imagine I:<br /> a) put Doll on fire (using some kind of ON FIRE tilt)<br /> b) start twisting it arms hoping for, I don't know, Arm Wrack<br /> c) put the Doll in Extreme Environment<br /> d) Shoot it up with a Decay Death Spell that turns it into goo by reducing it's Structure directly to 0<br /> <br /> I like imagery of Arrow who confronts their fear of death by shooting themselves in the head to drop people unconcious due to being subject to something like 9 Bashing damage in one go.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Inflicting Tilts like that feels like a very good Reach effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T19:26:21-07:00","id":945229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=944827#post944827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. What about Tilts? Imagine I:<br /> a) put Doll on fire (using some kind of ON FIRE tilt)<br /> b) start twisting it arms hoping for, I don't know, Arm Wrack<br /> c) put the Doll in Extreme Environment<br /> d) Shoot it up with a Decay Death Spell that turns it into goo by reducing it's Structure directly to 0<br /> <br /> I like imagery of Arrow who confronts their fear of death by shooting themselves in the head to drop people unconcious due to being subject to something like 9 Bashing damage in one go.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidenote: this sounds like you're trying to kill a fly with a sledgehammer. A sympathetic range Death, Forces, or Fate spell, using the doll as a Yantra, is a lot less convoluted to pull off.<br /> EDIT: I read the spell. Go nuts, because this doesn't really need Space to be mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 08-06-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:59:25-07:00","id":948522,"title":"","content":"Can Ascended Mages be summoned as Supernal beings?<br /> <br /> Additionally, can they be the Supernal beings that sometimes mess with Mages using Focused Mage Sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:34:27-07:00","id":948533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=948522#post948522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Ascended Mages be summoned as Supernal beings?<br /> <br /> Additionally, can they be the Supernal beings that sometimes mess with Mages using Focused Mage Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would say not summoned, you can only normally summon beings up to Rank 5. Ascended (Arch)masters are far more powerful than that. Although maybe 2E allows for a Rank 5 Avatar, like 1E did.<br /> <br /> If you can see, say, Metatron, who is pretty high Rank, I think you could observe and interact with an Ascended mage as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:41:18-07:00","id":948536,"title":"","content":"Not every Mage who has Ascended was necessarily powerful enough to hit Rank 5+ on Ascension though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:47:01-07:00","id":948537,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I don't know where I got the idea then. Maybe I've red it somewhere and absorbed it as a canon piece of lore.<br /> <br /> I wonder by what standard is the Rank of the Ascended determined anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:59:18-07:00","id":948545,"title":"","content":"Probably archmastery being necessary for Ascension that was erroneously held as true from 1e.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how Rank is determined for Ascended though. <br /> <br /> Next question, Supernal beings know almost everything about their Path and arcana, what's stopping a Mage from asking them for a path to follow to Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:17:55-07:00","id":948553,"title":"","content":"I think it's two things: One is that every Supernal symbol is unique and so is every path to become one, every Ascension. And two, connected to that, it is likely that as long one isn't a symbol, the Supernal being literally cannot imagine that symbol's existence and so doesn't know the path to become said symbol. It makes sense in a sort of roundabout, convoluted way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-11-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:24:43-07:00","id":948559,"title":"","content":"I think your second point makes the most sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:46:02-07:00","id":948869,"title":"","content":"This makes me wonder about the scope of the Supernal Watcher merit in SoS. I think Dave mentioned something about getting Allies dots with a Supernal being that will always be apparent in your Sight, but no details are known, like the effect of the merit on attempts to summon the being, or the general relationship with the being. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Spoilers Dave pls.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-12-2016, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:32:37-07:00","id":950864,"title":"","content":"Does inuring allows a mage to not suffer wisdom degeneration from spells that <br /> <br /> A) Could be used in a way that risk wisdom. Say, i inure fireball and i can fireball people to death and no degeneration from that. But were i to kill them with ice beams then i would risk degeneration.<br /> <br /> B) Only from spells that it mere casting is a wisdom check no matter what i do with it. Say, stealing a soul or making a soul stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:22:15-07:00","id":950880,"title":"","content":"A) Right.<br /> <br /> B) What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:47:00-07:00","id":950889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=950880#post950880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B) What?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant, that casting a fireball is not by itself an act of hubris. I can blow a wall with it, set a tree on fire or various other uses besides the one, killing/harming, that causes degeneration check.<br /> <br /> Creating a soulstone, sever an awakened soul or magic with the abyss (though we dont have rules for them yet), on the other hand is always a degeneration check. There is no &quot;harmless&quot; (in the sense of the PC wisdom) use for those. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:17:12-07:00","id":950991,"title":"","content":"Creating a soul stone is, but that's not a spell. Severing a Mage's soul is a spell so it can be Inured. Not sure what you mean by making Abyssal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:43:40-07:00","id":951002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=950991#post950991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating a soul stone is, but that's not a spell. Severing a Mage's soul is a spell so it can be Inured. Not sure what you mean by making Abyssal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they're talking about how a mage can invite the abyss into their magic in order to control the resulting paradox (you roll gnosis and each success gives the caster total control over a single paradox reach).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:47:17-07:00","id":951004,"title":"","content":"No idea, but LRS says there isn't rules for it, and that's clearly a rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:58:08-07:00","id":951009,"title":"","content":"I think they might just have missed it. I can't see anything else that could constitute magic with the abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T04:29:59-07:00","id":951041,"title":"","content":"Rules for it are hidden at the end of Scelesti section of the antagonist chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T04:38:39-07:00","id":951044,"title":"","content":"If that's what LRS is talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:02:31-07:00","id":951477,"title":"","content":"yup, pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:31:37-07:00","id":951920,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#004F6D\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\">Hidden Hoard (Matter<span style=\"font-family:ArialMT\">\u2022\u2022<span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\">)<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Practice: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Veiling<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Primary Factor: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Duration<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Larceny, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> This spell renders Matter difficult to detect. It isn\u2019t invisibility,<br /> precisely; rather, the spell veils the subject\u2019s connection to the<br /> Supernal truths, making it seem insignificant and beneath notice. Mundane attempts to detect the subject fail automatically.<br /> Spells and powers that would detect the veiled object are subject<br /> to a Clash of Wills.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> How do I cast this spell without making the item invisible to myself?<br /> <br /> Generally, how do I cast veiling or shielding spells while excluding certain phenomena from their effects (like teammates)? It's not an option of Fate as far as I can gather, and I can't find it in the spell factors or anywhere. How is it supposed to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:47:02-07:00","id":951937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=951920#post951920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#004F6D]How do I cast this spell without making the item invisible to myself?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule you can see through your own Veilings.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generally, how do I cast veiling or shielding spells while excluding certain phenomena from their effects (like teammates)? It's not an option of Fate as far as I can gather, and I can't find it in the spell factors or anywhere. How is it supposed to work? </div> </div> </div>Check Warding Gesture, Fate 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:53:03-07:00","id":951940,"title":"","content":"If you haven't relinquished it then you're aware of the spell which ought to be enough to bypass it for yourself. If you don't think that's good enough then just cast a Matter Unveiling or use Mage Sight and purposely cause your spell to fail the Clash of Wills. Since you haven't relinquished it you can do that.<br /> <br /> There is a Fate effect that allows you to exempt people from being targets of your spell by the way. It's the Warding Gesture spell and it would be simple to do a little creative thaumaturgy or add a Reach clause to make it function the way you're asking after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:18:02-07:00","id":951958,"title":"","content":"Another thing. Can I not throw a bunch of fireballs at several targets through Scale/targets option? It seems to say I _must_ use Area, which is fairly sad, and I don't get why it is impossible. Am I not getting it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:57:45-07:00","id":951995,"title":"","content":"I don't understand. Why is it impossible? You can use Scale as either Area (everything in target area gets affected, and any point of the target area - be it center, or be it edge - must remain in your Range), or as Subjects (you get to affect up to appropiate number of subjects that are in your Range).<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Ohhh, I see. Aimed spells.<br /> That's because you would need to make multiple Athletics+Gnosis rolls, and <br /> a) 2nd ed doesn't like multiple attacks per turn<br /> b) with things like &quot;20 subjects&quot; your group would kill you for rolling it 20 times<br /> c) Adamantine Arrows would pick Adamant Hand: Athletics and then argue that they get 5 instances of it off when throwing 5 fireballs at 5 subjects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-16-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:34:47-07:00","id":952036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=951995#post951995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand. Why is it impossible? You can use Scale as either Area (everything in target area gets affected, and any point of the target area - be it center, or be it edge - must remain in your Range), or as Subjects (you get to affect up to appropiate number of subjects that are in your Range).<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Ohhh, I see. Aimed spells.<br /> That's because you would need to make multiple Athletics+Gnosis rolls, and<br /> a) 2nd ed doesn't like multiple attacks per turn<br /> b) with things like &quot;20 subjects&quot; your group would kill you for rolling it 20 times<br /> c) Adamantine Arrows would pick Adamant Hand: Athletics and then argue that they get 5 instances of it off when throwing 5 fireballs at 5 subjects</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are reflexive, so fine, no? Besides, you could, like, make autofire with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:40:38-07:00","id":952041,"title":"","content":"It's basically a principle rule for 2nd editions - no more than one attack roll (and no more than one attack, though hurt locker and similar things try to flirt with this forbidden fruit) per turn. Mage already breaks one of the rules - because these attacks are done as a *reflexive action* - and breaking another one probably would be too much.<br /> It's already amazing that Dave decided that you can throw the spell in the same turn you cast it - I remember being super worried that you would have to cast it in one turn, and then throw in the next, because that would make Aimed spells very weak and rarely used option. <br /> <br /> But now? Now Aimed Spells are amazing. They save you soooooooooo muuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuch reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:14:10-07:00","id":952064,"title":"","content":"Btw, I've seen it said that Aimed spells are not withstood, is that true?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=952041#post952041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But now? Now Aimed Spells are amazing. They save you soooooooooo muuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuch reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do they? I feel like I am missing something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","user":"Altasaire","date":". 08-16-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:19:01-07:00","id":952071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=952064#post952064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, I've seen it said that Aimed spells are not withstood, is that true?</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct-damage spells \u2014 that is, spells that deal their Potency in damage of a type dependent upon their Practice \u2014 are not Withstood, but Aimed spells do still have their effects subject to the appropriate Withstand rating in addition to needing to roll to hit their target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:26:30-07:00","id":952083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=952071#post952071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Direct-damage spells \u2014 that is, spells that deal their Potency in damage of a type dependent upon their Practice \u2014 are not Withstood, but Aimed spells do still have their effects subject to the appropriate Withstand rating in addition to needing to roll to hit their target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. So what is the point to even having them, then? I am probably not following the intent behind the mechanics, here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=952041#post952041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's basically a principle rule for 2nd editions - no more than one attack roll (and no more than one attack, though hurt locker and similar things try to flirt with this forbidden fruit) per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Btw, what is the in-narrative basis for not being able to attack several times while you are under heavy Acceleration? Or is it purely &quot;you cannot because you canNOT&quot; with no in-game reason given?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","user":"Altasaire","date":". 08-16-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:37:42-07:00","id":952093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=952083#post952083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. So what is the point to even having them, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Aimed spell does not require a Reach to affect a target outside of Touch range, which allows you to use that Reach on something else, or at least save yourself some Paradox dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:41:30-07:00","id":952095,"title":"","content":"You don't need to spend Reach on Sensory Range. Which might mean difference between &quot;My spell invokes Paradox&quot; and &quot;It doesn't&quot;, which may stop you from snowballing into Paradox Ville. <br /> Their practical use is that outside of combat, you pretty much always can use them in place of Sensory Range. In combat, well, they allow you to basically use spells like magical grenades - if your enemies are bunkering inside a room and you can't see them, you can't target them...but you can just throw an Aimed Spell fireball inside and use AoE to target them this way. And because you are targeting and unmoving spot in space, you probably aren't going to care about penalties to your Athletics+Gnosis roll. <br /> For Admantine Arrows, they can help use their Order merit without taking breaks from casting on all spells after first in the scene pretty much. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T04:48:39-07:00","id":952429,"title":"","content":"Seers of the Throne Status adds to Resources when pursuing mundane services and objects. Can the combined score go beyond 5? For practical reasons, it could mean things like unlimited purchases of 4 and 5 availability that were not possible previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:36:13-07:00","id":952443,"title":"","content":"Yup. There's no real game mechanical effect once you go above an effective resources of 8, but &quot;can get as much availability 5 stuff as needed&quot; is pretty good. And the ST should allow for things like funding everyone who wants to sue a website you don't like or running for president.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:54:35-07:00","id":952450,"title":"","content":"Thanks for reminding us in the U.S. about who really runs things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:12:23-07:00","id":952462,"title":"","content":"No wonder that Seers triumph over the Pentacle. Thank for clarifying! This definitely makes playing a Seer a pretty unique experience from multiple angles; it's nice to see such caution to gameplay patterns. I think I like this solution more than the old Luxury merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T09:34:49-07:00","id":952567,"title":"","content":"Combined Spells, are they just two spells, like say a Damage Spell from Forces, and a Veiling Spell from Mind, or are they a combination of multiple effects from different Arcanum? Like for example, to see a certain supernatural being associated with Fate and Prime, you would need to cast a 1 dot spell that incorporated both Arcanum but not any different effects other then Unveiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:07:59-07:00","id":952585,"title":"","content":"They are two spells like in your first example.<br /> <br /> A spell that requires multiple arcana in one Practice like in your second example is conjunctional. It's only limited by your arcana rather than your Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:03:09-07:00","id":953030,"title":"","content":"I asked a question about dispelling the Familiar spell a few posts back.<br /> <br /> Today, I found a section saying:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Familiar Manifestation lasts until the mage<br /> or the Familiar chooses to end it, or until another<br /> mage severs the bond (this requires an Unmaking<br /> spell using the appropriate Arcanum). </div> </div> </div>(Page 253)<br /> <br /> Which is in conflict with the spell claiming:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage gains the Familiar Merit and the<br /> spirit the Familiar Manifestation Condition for the Duration of<br /> the spell. </div> </div> </div>The only way to get the Manifestation is via the spell, so...<br /> <br /> I'm confused again.<br /> <br /> Do you need 5 Spirit to revoke a Spirit familiar (which goes back to implying the bond is a Lasting effect until one of the parties ends it or it's broken by force)) as the first quote says, or so you just use Dispel Magic (with 1 dot in Prime and 1 dot in Spirit instead of 5) to dispel the spell that caused the bond (which makes me wonder why the Ephemera section specified you need 5)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:34:04-07:00","id":953039,"title":"","content":"No, you need Spirit 5 to be an asshole to someone else with a Familiar. In other words, although their bond will only last for as long as the duration of the spell or one of them decides to part ways it's still an incredibly strong connection that requires Unmaking for an outside party to break. Nothing about the quoted sections there imply Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:39:37-07:00","id":953042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=953030#post953030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked a question about dispelling the Familiar spell a few posts back.<br /> <br /> Today, I found a section saying:<br /> <br /> (Page 253)<br /> <br /> Which is in conflict with the spell claiming:<br /> <br /> <br /> The only way to get the Manifestation is via the spell, so...<br /> <br /> I'm confused again.<br /> <br /> Do you need 5 Spirit to revoke a Spirit familiar (which goes back to implying the bond is a Lasting effect until one of the parties ends it or it's broken by force)) as the first quote says, or so you just use Dispel Magic (with 1 dot in Prime and 1 dot in Spirit instead of 5) to dispel the spell that caused the bond (which makes me wonder why the Ephemera section specified you need 5)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The familiar bond exists only so long as the spell does and when you're buying the merit it represents an indefinite duration on a relinquished spell but it is still a spell so it can be dispelled like any other. So no, you don't need to use unmaking spirit to sever the bond. I suspect the reason it has that requirement of 5 dots in the ephemera section is either an artifact from an earlier draft or it is talking about targeting the bond itself for destruction rather than trying to dispel the spell that creates it (because you don't have any prime dots for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:51:30-07:00","id":953047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=953039#post953039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you need Spirit 5 to be an asshole to someone else with a Familiar. In other words, although their bond will only last for as long as the duration of the spell or one of them decides to part ways it's still an incredibly strong connection that requires Unmaking for an outside party to break. Nothing about the quoted sections there imply Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But why would the spell that creates the familiar bond somehow be so much more resilient that it can't be dispelled like any other? If you have spirit 1 and prime 1 and come across a spell that has created the resonant condition for a fire spirit it shouldn't be any more resistant to dispellation than a spell that makes a fire spirit into a mage's familiar.<br /> <br /> At least it makes no sense if the familiar bond isn't lasting. If it is a lasting effect, then yeah, it should be 100% immune to regular dispellation and require unmaking to remove. As it is though you can't make the familiar bond lasting, it's just a spell and there is no spell that cannot be dispelled by having prime 1 and 1 dot of all the arcana involved in the spell, not matter how expensive the merit representing it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:21:39-07:00","id":953058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=952443#post952443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. There's no real game mechanical effect once you go above an effective resources of 8, but &quot;can get as much availability 5 stuff as needed&quot; is pretty good. And the ST should allow for things like funding everyone who wants to sue a website you don't like or running for president.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It'd still have a mechanical effect when it comes to blocking social merits with other social merits (the vampire chronicler's guide went into detail on one way of running it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:22:14-07:00","id":953059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=953047#post953047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why would the spell that creates the familiar bond somehow be so much more resilient that it can't be dispelled like any other? If you have spirit 1 and prime 1 and come across a spell that has created the resonant condition for a fire spirit it shouldn't be any more resistant to dispellation than a spell that makes a fire spirit into a mage's familiar.<br /> <br /> At least it makes no sense if the familiar bond isn't lasting. If it is a lasting effect, then yeah, it should be 100% immune to regular dispellation and require unmaking to remove. As it is though you can't make the familiar bond lasting, it's just a spell and there is no spell that cannot be dispelled by having prime 1 and 1 dot of all the arcana involved in the spell, not matter how expensive the merit representing it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're correct in your previous post, Unmaking is required to dispel the bond itself, not the spell maintaining it (Which if that spell was targeted and dispelled would dispel the bond as well). In other words, dispelling the bond rather than the spell creating the bond is a brute force approach that requires Unmaking. Spirit 1/Prime 1 would do it with more finesse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:50:09-07:00","id":953207,"title":"","content":"How do I give Acamoth and Gulmoth spells-as-numina now? You could before, not sure what do they roll now. Is it Power+Finesse, as in 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:25:42-07:00","id":953237,"title":"","content":"You can still do it, and its whatever the roll normally is for an ephemeral entity to activate a Numina. What you'll have to wrestle with is how to determine Reach. I'd limit them to taking no more than Reach equal to Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:30:38-07:00","id":953390,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers so far.<br /> <br /> Here is another: can you use Material Sympathy Yantra on self-targeting spells? That is, can you pluck your own hair or something to get +2 to cast Knit on yourself or something?<br /> <br /> And another: Can indirect results of your spell that are obvious trigger paradox? Specific example: Say you Compel a rank 5 dog spirit to Mass Create a pack of dogs. Compelling the spirit isn't obvious magic; Sleepers can't see spirits. But the Spirit's use of its Influence is obvious. Does casting the Compelling spell qualify for Paradox for obvious magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:19:15-07:00","id":953576,"title":"","content":"You can just use yourself, you don't really even need to pluck your own hair.<br /> <br /> The Compelling spell isn't obvious and won't trigger Paradox. A spell without an obvious effect when cast that lasts long enough that produces results that -are- obvious after casting run the risk of being Unraveled by Sleeper witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T00:55:24-07:00","id":954262,"title":"","content":"Another one! I'm playing a spirit-focused Thyrsus if you can't tell.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm asking it here rather than the werewolf or CofD forums.<br /> <br /> The book indicates that there is a spirit for mostly everything.<br /> <br /> What happens if a spirit for an object or animal is destroyed, rather than just forced to hibernate?<br /> <br /> Does it harm the object/animal in any way? Will a new spirit eventually take its place?<br /> <br /> I'm kind of leaning towards the latter if most things have spirits, given the dog-eat-dog nature of the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:27:31-07:00","id":954271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=954262#post954262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one! I'm playing a spirit-focused Thyrsus if you can't tell.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm asking it here rather than the werewolf or CofD forums.<br /> <br /> The book indicates that there is a spirit for mostly everything.<br /> <br /> What happens if a spirit for an object or animal is destroyed, rather than just forced to hibernate?<br /> <br /> Does it harm the object/animal in any way? Will a new spirit eventually take its place?<br /> <br /> I'm kind of leaning towards the latter if most things have spirits, given the dog-eat-dog nature of the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more appropriate to say that there's a spirit for every <i>kind </i>of thing. Thus, if the spirit governing dogs in a given area is destroyed, and a suitably similar proxy can't be found, dogs in the area may move on, start behaving erratically, sicken, and in general disappear. But at the point where the spirit's destruction starts having a noticeable impact on the Fallen World, you aren't dealing with the Shadow patron of one dog, but rather the patron of all dogs within a given area. As for those it influences, I'd imagine losing or coming to a place where the spiritual makeup doesn't support dogs, for example, would be akin to moving into a new neighborhood, in that there'd be a need for adjustment, but eventually a new spirit would arise to take the reins. But losing a patron wouldn't necessarily harm those that it influences, beyond possibly impacting their behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:49:43-07:00","id":954453,"title":"","content":"If the spirit of a thing dies it doesn't necessarily damage the thing. Without a spirit though it might become a thing that no one will bother wasting any emotional energy on so it could easily get worn down or thrown away. It could get a new spirit inside it in the unlikely event that someone managed to fight against the spiritual ennui it naturally generates and take care of it enough for a mote to take hold and grow from there.<br /> <br /> Another, similar way to look at it is as if the thing that lost its spirit has become soulless. It becomes a thing without &quot;purpose&quot;, fortunately for most things they're either inanimate or can run on instinct so it may not appear to affect them that much. Metaphysically speaking though, they're dead on the inside. On the bright side, like a soulless person they can have that intrinsic spark restored. Even more fortunately, they can have it more easily restored than a soulless person can have a soul restored to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-20-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:07:47-07:00","id":954687,"title":"","content":"So after a bit of a hiatus whilst waiting for 2E to come out, I'm finally back and have picked up a copy of the book. First off, huzzah to Dave and team for doing so well! I'm a bit miffed about the glossing-over of a few important things, but understand page count limitations account for a lot. Looking forward to new supplements to flesh things out.<br /> <br /> Anyway, now to the question: After reading that Death now includes cold as a concept under its purview (woot!) I'm trying to figure out coldfire, a la C.S. Friedman's eponymous series. Basically, a force/reaction that is in every way the inversion of fire -- i.e. it's endothermic, creates brilliant light that obfuscates rather than illuminating, and freezes on contact instead of burning. I've been trying to figure out whether it's thematically appropriate to limit its use to Masters of Death, and if not then to figure out which Practices it should come from and thus its Arcanum rating. I know that Making would allow it to be summoned whole-cloth, but can anyone posit a different Practice or combination thereof that would allow for its creation?<br /> <br /> EDIT: for what it's worth, coldfire does behave as a material substance, acting like a non-Newtonian fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","user":"Raikirah","date":". 08-20-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T18:41:27-07:00","id":954719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raikirah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=954687#post954687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So after a bit of a hiatus whilst waiting for 2E to come out, I'm finally back and have picked up a copy of the book. First off, huzzah to Dave and team for doing so well! I'm a bit miffed about the glossing-over of a few important things, but understand page count limitations account for a lot. Looking forward to new supplements to flesh things out.<br /> <br /> Anyway, now to the question: After reading that Death now includes cold as a concept under its purview (woot!) I'm trying to figure out coldfire, a la C.S. Friedman's eponymous series. Basically, a force/reaction that is in every way the inversion of fire -- i.e. it's endothermic, creates brilliant light that obfuscates rather than illuminating, and freezes on contact instead of burning. I've been trying to figure out whether it's thematically appropriate to limit its use to Masters of Death, and if not then to figure out which Practices it should come from and thus its Arcanum rating. I know that Making would allow it to be summoned whole-cloth, but can anyone posit a different Practice or combination thereof that would allow for its creation?<br /> <br /> EDIT: for what it's worth, coldfire does behave as a material substance, acting like a non-Newtonian fluid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just looking at how to do it with death I can see patterning on an existing death thing doing it. Like turning a corpse or some ectoplasm into a pile of cold fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:20:45-07:00","id":954772,"title":"","content":"Patterning would let you take ambient cold and &quot;ignite&quot; it as well. I have no idea how coldfire works, but an idea I have could involve igniting ashes by Weaving the property of &quot;burning&quot; (Which is a process that fire does, but not necessarily what fire is so could be argued to fall under Forces) onto it. Maybe that would be more like a ghost flame. No idea. *Shrugs.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:59:55-07:00","id":954787,"title":"","content":"Can anyone help me think of a good Skill to use for a Rote version of Stealing Fire (Prime 3) that involves branding the subject? <br /> <br /> I'm working on an Obrimos with low Wisdom who thinks he's helping Sleepers by branding them with runes in order to cast indefinite versions of Stealing Fire and Apocalypse in the hopes of forcing them to Awaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:02:12-07:00","id":954789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=954719#post954719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just looking at how to do it with death I can see patterning on an existing death thing doing it. Like turning a corpse or some ectoplasm into a pile of cold fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, ectoplasm. Hadn't thought of that. Ectoplasm behaves like a non-newtonian fluid, iirc -- i.e. it flows as a liquid, but does so uphill.... hell, with that in mind it could be done as a Weaving effect, adding the descriptors &quot;darkening&quot; and &quot;supercooled&quot;. Hrmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:05:39-07:00","id":954791,"title":"","content":"Depending on how they go about it, Crafts, Medicine or even Weaponry could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:11:14-07:00","id":954848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=954787#post954787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone help me think of a good Skill to use for a Rote version of Stealing Fire (Prime 3) that involves branding the subject?<br /> <br /> I'm working on an Obrimos with low Wisdom who thinks he's helping Sleepers by branding them with runes in order to cast indefinite versions of Stealing Fire and Apocalypse in the hopes of forcing them to Awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>This qualifies as sadistic torture to me, so I vote Intimidate. have him join a pain cult so he can gain it as a Rote skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:18:20-07:00","id":954976,"title":"","content":"I actually really love this Left-Handed Obrimos idea. I may steal it for a villain some time. For the rote, I'd go with Crafts, Medicine, or Intimidation, as already suggested. <br /> <br /> A guide for which to choose would be to figure out how the thaumaturge thinks of the spell. Is it an act of artisanship in crafting this symbol? An act of healing for their soul (or at least one where they need to be careful with the flesh)? Or a violent act, either against the target or the Lie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:03:42-07:00","id":955430,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm confused. What does Supernal Veil -do-? I've always read it as a ward against magical detection but now that I'm rereading it, it seems like it wards it from -all- detection - including mundane stuff like sight and whatever - as long as the subject is supernatural. Can someone else explain this to me because for the life of me I cannot parse it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:08:20-07:00","id":955432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=955430#post955430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm confused. What does Supernal Veil -do-? I've always read it as a ward against magical detection but now that I'm rereading it, it seems like it wards it from -all- detection - including mundane stuff like sight and whatever - as long as the subject is supernatural. Can someone else explain this to me because for the life of me I cannot parse it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I read it at magical detection, but it wouldn't be outside of prime's purview to also veil magical things from mundane detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:06:17-07:00","id":955496,"title":"","content":"Depends on if you consider mundane senses an ability. If you do then it would be simple enough to say that people not actively looking for the weird auto-fail and people who are provoke a CoW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:43:47-07:00","id":955504,"title":"","content":"Damnit, I just had an awesome idea for a spell: A Prime spell that gives non-Supernal things the magical signiature of mage spells, so Sleepers react with a breaking point and quiescence.<br /> <br /> Weaving or Patterning, probably. Also, obvs, a Wisdom sin. But fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:24:42-07:00","id":955516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=955504#post955504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnit, I just had an awesome idea for a spell: A Prime spell that gives non-Supernal things the magical signiature of mage spells, so Sleepers react with a breaking point and quiescence.<br /> <br /> Weaving or Patterning, probably. Also, obvs, a Wisdom sin. But fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an excellent way to make sure you aren't remembered!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:56:30-07:00","id":955526,"title":"","content":"A neuralyzer spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:21:44-07:00","id":955530,"title":"","content":"Now, see, you *could* just learn the Mind Arcanum. But that wouldn't be using Prime 4 to crack a nut without due care and attention to bystanders' souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:59:58-07:00","id":955540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=955504#post955504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnit, I just had an awesome idea for a spell: A Prime spell that gives non-Supernal things the magical signiature of mage spells, so Sleepers react with a breaking point and quiescence.<br /> <br /> Weaving or Patterning, probably. Also, obvs, a Wisdom sin. But fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that just be variant of Apocalypse? Are you making the supernatural thing &quot;Supernal&quot;-ish, or just cloaking it in &quot;Supernal&quot; (which would trigger the Breaking Points itself)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah, the goal is to forget the thing (by leveraging the Quiescence mechanism), not to just provoke Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T06:05:43-07:00","id":955542,"title":"","content":"Question: Stealing the Fire lets you make someone a Sleepwalker while it is in effect (Breaking Points are deferred until the spell expires, when they have to reconcile their memories of the Supernal while now lacking the ability to do so). Do spells they witnessed then suffer Dissonance, or no, because they are not actually observed?<br /> <br /> If so, could you set up triggered spell effects to temporarily apply Stealing the Fire to Sleepers while they are in the area to protect the spells from Dissonance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T06:16:41-07:00","id":955545,"title":"","content":"I actually can see this spell used by, let's say Mysterium, to make sure that certain things and places are never remembered.<br /> And if you want to be a dick, equip the victim with contact lenses and cast this spell on the lenses. Or one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:09:51-07:00","id":955632,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the Mysterium would be thrilled with it, hiding things is one thing, but it smacks of spreading Pancryptia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:55:58-07:00","id":956033,"title":"","content":"Okay, so Supernal Veil -does- make one invisible to mundane senses? I'm trying to be clear on what the spell actually does because it's come up in game and our group has wildly different interpretations, so how it's supposed to work might have an impact as early as next session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:48:53-07:00","id":956059,"title":"","content":"To me, it looks like it's written that it hides supernatural things. Supernatural detection powers provoke Clash of Wills as per usual. While that seems pretty potent, it's pretty much how every other Veiling spell works. So you can cast it on anything supernatural and it conceals them from everything, but detection powers provoke CoW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T00:23:55-07:00","id":956189,"title":"","content":"So, the Spirit 2 Command Spirit spell adds in towards the end '<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Commands that go against the spirit\u2019s self-interest (including abandoning a host or Fetter) provoke a<br /> Clash of Wills.' But, what exactly does that mean? Basically any form of mind control is going to be against most spirit's self interest. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">If it does just generally apply unless the spirit was going to do the thing you asked anyway it basically comes down to &quot;BEHOLD! I AM THE MIGHTY MASTER OF SPIRIT, SHMEBULOK! OBEY ME, RANDOM RANK 2 SPIRIT!&quot; &quot;No.&quot; &quot;DAMN YOU, INFERIOR DICE POOL!&quot; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">So, I don't think that's the intent. Can we get a clearer distinction as to where the line is drawn?</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 08-23-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T01:37:28-07:00","id":956205,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I agree with your assumption that most commands you can give a spirit are against its self-interest. If you work within a spirit's purview then in most cases you will not be working against its interest you'll just be focusing its efforts. So in other words, don't send a fire spirit into water to check out a wreck, that would provoke a CoW. Command a water spirit instead, no CoW most of the time. The more specifically appropriate for a task a spirit is for a task the less likely there will be a CoW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:36:14-07:00","id":956339,"title":"","content":"Spirits don't generally do things for free, even if it's within their purview: like a fire spirit burning things down. I'd only count it as against the spirit's self-interest if it involves going against its nature (like Mrmdubois's example) or something that harms the spirit (as per the book's abandoning a host example).<br /> <br /> So the spell is mostly useful for things a spirit would do anyway, but you can skip paying them or doing them favors in exchange for their efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:08:32-07:00","id":956355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=956339#post956339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the spell is mostly useful for things a spirit would do anyway, but you can skip paying them or doing them favors in exchange for their efforts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, you can be a cheapskate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:44:53-07:00","id":956495,"title":"","content":"Is the 2E book lacking the definition of a conjunctional spell? I was trying to explain the difference between a conjunctional and a combined spell to players and it was fairly hard (especially because it's fairly unclear in places \u2014 Life 5 Mind 5 to create a mind-ful creature, why not a combined Create Life and Create Mind?) but I could not find a good explanation of conjunctionals in the book. Am I just missing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:53:45-07:00","id":956567,"title":"","content":"I didn't see them mentioned by name this time around. What used to be conjuctional effects are now listed as optional Arcana among Reach options. But basically a &quot;Conjuctional&quot; spell is a single whole effect that needs knowledge of several Arcana, while combined spells are discrete, diffferent effects that you cast all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:57:48-07:00","id":956604,"title":"","content":"Yeah but how do I make new ones and how do i use the &quot;Add Space 2&quot; things to the spell. Just have space 2 and say i use it or is it a penalty of sort when i cast it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:28:15-07:00","id":956617,"title":"","content":"Depends on what your spell is getting out of Space 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:35:55-07:00","id":956620,"title":"","content":"I get that you get out different thing depending on the spell. But how do I incorporate that extra conjunction of an extra arcanum (or arcana?) into the spell. Just say i add it (if i have the preq.) or do i roll spellcasting with a penalty or do i use the lower of the arcana as my dice pool, or? The system dosen't tell me how to incorporate the &quot;add arcana&quot; things that some spells have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 08-23-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:02:51-07:00","id":956803,"title":"","content":"Just having it does the trick for a conjuctional use. No penalties or caps to the rolls or extra Reach (usually*) or Mana cost of any kind.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:9px\">Unless it is a Reach effect that happens to need the addition of another Arcanum.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:05:37-07:00","id":956805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=956620#post956620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I get that you get out different thing depending on the spell. But how do I incorporate that extra conjunction of an extra arcanum (or arcana?) into the spell. Just say i add it (if i have the preq.) or do i roll spellcasting with a penalty or do i use the lower of the arcana as my dice pool, or? The system dosen't tell me how to incorporate the &quot;add arcana&quot; things that some spells have.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't change the roll at all, just increases the requirements to cast to including arcana other than the primary one at the required dot rating. So for example prime 1 dispel magic with fate 1, forces 1 and life 1 is still just a 1 dot spell which has the dicepool of gnosis + prime + yantras but it requires the caster to know fate, forces and life all at 1 dot or higher rather than just knowing prime at 1 dot or higher. A hypothetical 5 dot spell with all other arcana at 5 dots or lower involved in it is still just a 5 dot spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T01:31:38-07:00","id":956854,"title":"","content":"Would you say a &quot;Pain&quot; yantra of &quot;I deal X resistant lethal to myself to gain a +X yantra&quot; would be balanced?<br /> <br /> Sacrifice of others and of inanimate objects is there, but no sacrifice of self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T03:03:40-07:00","id":956863,"title":"","content":"I personally go with<br /> - Just a wound is +1<br /> - LETHAL Wound that turns resistant due to being used as a Sacrament in the spell is +2<br /> - LETHAL Wound that turns resistant AND bestows a negative condition that lasts until the wound is healed bestows +3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T23:45:21-07:00","id":957435,"title":"","content":"A question about the Banishment spell: How does it work on Claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:33:24-07:00","id":957513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957435#post957435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about the Banishment spell: How does it work on Claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the wording, I'd say it works normally. An argument could be made for Claimed being a more potent condition, though, since it's not accounted for in the Mage core, in which case you'd maybe need to add a Reach, but that'd be more of a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:36:28-07:00","id":957515,"title":"","content":"Are damaging spells subject to spell stacking by RAW or RAI?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:00:54-07:00","id":957522,"title":"","content":"You can't combine damage spells to do two sets of damage but if they also inflict secondary effects you can stack those. Check the errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:12:36-07:00","id":957533,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm reading it wrong but the errata talks specifically about combined spells.<br /> What if one mage casts Rotting Flesh (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) and the second casts Warp (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022) on the same target in the same turn? Both are damaging spells. Is only the highest in effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:16:33-07:00","id":957535,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe. That would be possible logical reading. And honestly, it might be the sanest (even if very counter intuitive) option, because it also solves the issue of &quot;my party bombed a god in one turn help&quot;. If you want a narrative reason, I don't know, symbols of violence and hurting grapple each other and only the strongest prevails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:26:53-07:00","id":957541,"title":"","content":"I'm really ok with that. It's a great rule actually because it forces players to play creatively. And with so easily achievable advanced scale factor (5 targets) the mages are no longer destroyers of the worlds( I mean they are still but nerfed in case of direct damage). It was 5 players x 5 targets x 3 potency (starting characters) = 75 damage in one turn! <br /> Thanks for confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:05:20-07:00","id":957550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957515#post957515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are damaging spells subject to spell stacking by RAW or RAI?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - it's just that you almost never notice, as losing a health level is instantaneous. But if you combined two direct-damage spells, they would only do the combined potency in damage, not double it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:07:20-07:00","id":957551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957533#post957533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm reading it wrong but the errata talks specifically about combined spells.<br /> What if one mage casts Rotting Flesh (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) and the second casts Warp (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022) on the same target in the same turn? Both are damaging spells. Is only the highest in effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, both work.<br /> <br /> (characters!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:08:57-07:00","id":957552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957435#post957435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about the Banishment spell: How does it work on Claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Works normally. Probably kills the poor sumbitch whose body is now so mutated it can't survive without its ephemeral passenger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:19:18-07:00","id":957556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957551#post957551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, both work.<br /> <br /> (characters!)</div> </div> </div> </div>You lost me there. If two casters choose one target with the damaging spells and they both work does that mean that e.g you can double boost attribute as long as there were two casters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:38:47-07:00","id":957565,"title":"","content":"No, because the boost only works while the spell is still there, so the second incoming spell finds something already boosting it.<br /> <br /> Damage is done and over in an instant shorter even than a turn. The spell that injured the target first has gone by the time the next one comes in, even if they're both within the same game turn (an abstract unit of time that's about three seconds long).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Although, now you have me thinking about what happens if you *do* cast a damaging spell with a Duration, such that it inflicts its potency every tickaround of your casting interval. That *would*, indeed, suppress other incoming direct damage spells with lower Potency.<br /> <br /> Huh. neat. That's going into the faq, then. I'm sure someone will think of a cunning use for it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:39:06-07:00","id":957566,"title":"","content":"No, that wouldn't work because the effects of attribute boosting isn't instantaneous, it has Duration.<br /> <br /> Ninja'd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:51:31-07:00","id":957577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957565#post957565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because the boost only works while the spell is still there, so the second incoming spell finds something already boosting it.<br /> <br /> Damage is done and over in an instant shorter even than a turn. The spell that injured the target first has gone by the time the next one comes in, even if they're both within the same game turn (an abstract unit of time that's about three seconds long).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that every spell lasts at least a turn (Core p.111).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spellcasting results in the following general effects, but each<br /> of these can be increased through changing spell factors or<br /> risking Paradox.<br /> \u2022 The spell grants a one-die bonus or penalty, deals one point<br /> of weapon damage, or heals one wound.<br /> \u2022 The spell lasts for one turn.<br /> \u2022 The spell hits one subject of Size 5 or less, or an area equal<br /> to an arm\u2019s-length circle around a point.<br /> \u2022 The mage must be touching the subject of the spell, or be<br /> casting on herself.<br /> \u2022 The spell takes an amount of time to cast based on Gnosis. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 08-25-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:04:14-07:00","id":957590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957552#post957552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Works normally. Probably kills the poor sumbitch whose body is now so mutated it can't survive without its ephemeral passenger.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you use for Rank for the Claimed? I was always under the impression that Claimed weren't entirely spirits anymore but a hybrid. None of the example Claimed in any of the books have a Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:17:35-07:00","id":957602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957565#post957565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because the boost only works while the spell is still there, so the second incoming spell finds something already boosting it.<br /> <br /> Damage is done and over in an instant shorter even than a turn. The spell that injured the target first has gone by the time the next one comes in, even if they're both within the same game turn (an abstract unit of time that's about three seconds long).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Although, now you have me thinking about what happens if you *do* cast a damaging spell with a Duration, such that it inflicts its potency every tickaround of your casting interval. That *would*, indeed, suppress other incoming direct damage spells with lower Potency.<br /> <br /> Huh. neat. That's going into the faq, then. I'm sure someone will think of a cunning use for it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We already talked about that. I think it ended with making sure that each time the casting interval comes, you have Charmed condition on you and expend it to reduce the Super Potent Damage to 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:06:05-07:00","id":957625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957590#post957590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you use for Rank for the Claimed? I was always under the impression that Claimed weren't entirely spirits anymore but a hybrid. None of the example Claimed in any of the books have a Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're expelling the spirit rather than the Claimed as a whole so it would be the rank of the spirit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> not all spells require 3 seconds in which to occur. A turn is the smallest amount of time that matters to the mechanics, but it's still an abstraction of actual time. It might be better to assume that in the case of damage spells it requires a turn to put together the Imago, but the results happen instantly right at the end of that turn. Reflexive spells take even less time to throw together the Imago and get the result. I'm not even sure it makes sense to say that a damage spell (Or other transitory spells) last for the full turn. That would lead to some weird attempts at negating damage because the target didn't burn for a whole 3 seconds or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:45:52-07:00","id":957671,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Effect takes place entirely at the beginning of said turn but the spell lasts in pattern at least a whole turn. <br /> I know Dave said that it last for a shorter time than a turn but I'm still tempted to house rule it. 5 starting mages can deal 75 bashing damage in a turn, not even prepared and with default potency. Take - 2 penalty and its 100 bashing damage per turn. Without staging or preparing the situation.<br /> 5 mages on 5 vampires in an white room scenario(I know, I know) leaves vampires devastated in one turn.<br /> <br /> Damn, its tearing me. I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:55:34-07:00","id":957709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957565#post957565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because the boost only works while the spell is still there, so the second incoming spell finds something already boosting it.<br /> <br /> Damage is done and over in an instant shorter even than a turn. The spell that injured the target first has gone by the time the next one comes in, even if they're both within the same game turn (an abstract unit of time that's about three seconds long).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Although, now you have me thinking about what happens if you *do* cast a damaging spell with a Duration, such that it inflicts its potency every tickaround of your casting interval. That *would*, indeed, suppress other incoming direct damage spells with lower Potency.<br /> <br /> Huh. neat. That's going into the faq, then. I'm sure someone will think of a cunning use for it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if I like the direction of this rules interaction. I mean, damaging spells shouldn't be a shield against other damaging spells, because that could be all too easily exploited by someone with the right selection of Healing spells or Mage Armor. Heck, with a long enough Interval, a spell that inflicts just enough Bashing to go over Armor every interval is not even a risky move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 08-25-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:44:19-07:00","id":957745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=957671#post957671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Effect takes place entirely at the beginning of said turn but the spell lasts in pattern at least a whole turn. <br /> I know Dave said that it last for a shorter time than a turn but I'm still tempted to house rule it. 5 starting mages can deal 75 bashing damage in a turn, not even prepared and with default potency. Take - 2 penalty and its 100 bashing damage per turn. Without staging or preparing the situation.<br /> 5 mages on 5 vampires in an white room scenario(I know, I know) leaves vampires devastated in one turn.<br /> <br /> Damn, its tearing me. I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can house rule it, but the game isn't designed with vampires in mind. Beating the crap out of them under the right circumstances is par for the course with Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T09:57:30-07:00","id":958273,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering. How far back can Forenzic Gaze(Death 1) look? Can you look 2000 years back without using Temporal Sympathy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 08-26-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:36:45-07:00","id":958312,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:14:57-07:00","id":958335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=956495#post956495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the 2E book lacking the definition of a conjunctional spell? I was trying to explain the difference between a conjunctional and a combined spell to players and it was fairly hard (especially because it's fairly unclear in places \u2014 Life 5 Mind 5 to create a mind-ful creature, why not a combined Create Life and Create Mind?) but I could not find a good explanation of conjunctionals in the book. Am I just missing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always explain it as such:<br /> -Combined is casting 2 effects at the same time.<br /> -Conjunctions is using 2 different arcana to create a singular effect that wouldn't normally be possible with just one of them. <br /> <br /> So, for example:<br /> -A spell that both healed lethal damage and also shielded the subject from further damage by projecting a force field would be a Combined Spell, with life and forces as the Arcana used, because the effects are entirely different (life to heal and then forces to shield.)<br /> -A spell that transforms a man into the Human Torch would be a Conjunctional Spell, as you require life to transform living beings but fire is outside its purview. It is a singular effect though (I am now a man who is composed of fire) <br /> <br /> As for the question of complex effects such as the (Create Life/Mind) example you suggested, I would usually ask: what is the final product? Creating a living being with a complex mind would be conjunctional, as you want to create a single effect that could only come about with both life and Mind. But say I wanted to create multiple different types of beings with different types of complex minds (say I wanted to create an Orc, Dwarf, and Elf) all as part of a single spell; then it would be a combined spell, as I am getting more than 1 effect (3 different beings) with a single spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:04:47-07:00","id":958405,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> Another question. Can you cast The Outward and Inward Eye on a camera?<br /> <br /> Can you cast Scrying on a camera to photo things you'd scry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:12:56-07:00","id":958411,"title":"","content":"I don't think you'd cast it on the camera, you wouldn't need to anyway since it opens up a window in space right in front of you, raise the camera, click.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:30:40-07:00","id":958419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958411#post958411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you'd cast it on the camera, you wouldn't need to anyway since it opens up a window in space right in front of you, raise the camera, click.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lets you perceive things. At no point it lets actual light through, as far as I was able to ascertain. At least without additional Arcana, I guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:24:24-07:00","id":958453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958312#post958312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neat. I can see a moros that visits museums all over the world and just looks at those few precious moments before death. He even knows how the dinosaurs looked and hunted. <br /> <br /> Next questions if you don't mind.<br /> Is GoogleMaps sufficient sympathetic connection and yantra for a mastigos to travel the world?<br /> What Life needs to shapechange into extinct animal? Is +1 Reach enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:03:31-07:00","id":958468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958419#post958419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lets you perceive things. At no point it lets actual light through, as far as I was able to ascertain. At least without additional Arcana, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She creates a<br /> \u201cwindow\u201d that allows her to perceive the subject, much like<br /> a television screen. When she casts the spell, she may choose<br /> whether the spell is one way, or whether people at the location<br /> can see back through the window. </div> </div> </div>If it weren't an actual warp in the fabric of space it'd just be Unveiling instead of Ruling. We know that warps in Space can effect energy because of the example given by Ban which bends light as part of its effect without the addition of other arcana. The fact that the spell can work both ways (Meaning an unaware actor not directly targeted by the spell can still see through it, much like a camera would be) &quot;like a tv screen&quot; suggests to me that light can indeed pass through in either direction.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> No. Google maps would make a good representational Yantra but probably has barely any Sympathetic connection to the places it displays. As far as I know Mastigos haven't made a habit of borrowing the sympathy of maps to go planet hopping ever.<br /> <br /> To shapechange into extinct organisms you probably just need Life 4 Shapechanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:30:11-07:00","id":958482,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Question: if you are mute or otherwise can't vocalize, are </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">you</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> shit out of luck regarding High Speech?<br /> <br /> I've found a description of it \u2014 &quot; In a sense, High Speech revolves around the concept of projecting the higher truths of the Supernal Realms through speech, which is a collection of sounds given meaning by the speaker to be projected outwards and interpreted by listeners&quot; \u2014 and it feels needlessly limiting. Is it a critical thing, something I miss, symbolically, or allowing a Mage to write out their thoughts in a notepad during spellcasting, or letting a mute Arrow weave High Speech sign language into his rote katas is fine?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:47:24-07:00","id":958524,"title":"","content":"A couple of things regarding Nimbus. One, is mage affected by his own Long-Term Nimbus? Two, how well does using a Shadow Name protect against a mage's Long-Term Nimbus from affecting his mundane life- is it largely perfect as long as a mage is careful, or will a powerful mage see some bleed-through of his nimbus no matter or exacting he is? Three, does using a Shadow Name reduce the affects of a Mage's Long Term Nimbus when he's in his mundane identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:04:12-07:00","id":958534,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10091_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10091\" data-vbnamecard=\"10091\">Altasaire</a> High Speech that's written are Runes. I'd let a player get away with using a High Sign Language too though.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8045\" data-vbnamecard=\"8045\">Azunth</a> Did you see the bit about a Mage taking the name Odin shouldn't expect to keep both eyes? Mages can be affected by their Long Term Nimbus. The level of protection against it provided by Shafow Name is determined by Wisdom. Answer to 3 is yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:08:55-07:00","id":958535,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Can Death determine if someone's possessed by a Spirit/Gulmoth with Soul Marks?</div> <br /> </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:11:31-07:00","id":958536,"title":"","content":"Not what's possessing them, but that they're possessed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:12:23-07:00","id":958537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958536#post958536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not what's possessing them, but that they're possessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:21:02-07:00","id":958538,"title":"","content":"What Sphere is used to determine if someone's a Sleepwalker? Prime? Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:25:33-07:00","id":958541,"title":"","content":"So a question about nimbus.<br /> <br /> Can you get a sense of which mages nimbus is sensed by peripheral mage sight? And does spell subjects have the casters nimbus on it when it takes effect ? <br /> <br /> In the story The Door. it is implied that both Outis and another mage recognizes the Hierarchs nimbus when Outis is the target of a sympathic spell cast on him. <br /> <br /> &quot;He never gets to finish insisting. We both feel the magic incoming, as foreign thoughts enter my mind. From<br /> his expression, he recognizes the nimbus. Good. I couldn\u2019t have timed this better if I\u2019d tried.<br /> I hold up my hand for him to wait, as though I were taking a phone call instead of entering telepathic<br /> communion with the Hierarch.&quot; p204 2ed Mage Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:36:37-07:00","id":958543,"title":"","content":"Peripheral MS isn't that precise. Yes to the 2nd question. In the story when targeted by magic they would have immediately brought up their AMS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T00:37:22-07:00","id":958629,"title":"","content":"Since there was some talk about Shadow Names, I had a question about mage culture.<br /> <br /> Using your Shadow Name around your mundane friends and family is a no-go, because it apparently forms sympathy between that name and them, which is bad.<br /> <br /> Using a Mage's mundane name around them is considered very taboo.<br /> <br /> What do mages do in mixed company? What if they go to university together and have to talk in the halls? At the library? What if they go to the same party by chance?<br /> <br /> I kind of figured sympathetic names weren't a big deal anymore, given how complicated such interactions are and the fact that the penalty for sympathetic magic without a sympathetic name is so mild now, but then I saw the bit about how super taboo it is.<br /> <br /> How do mages deal with cases where mundane and magic friends collide? It's bound to happen. Is it covered in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:15:03-07:00","id":958637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958629#post958629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do mages deal with cases where mundane and magic friends collide? It's bound to happen. Is it covered in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless your Shadow Name is Honorific Surname, Diminutive Nickname, Middle Name, or Pronoun, there's not really a whole lot of unavoidable overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:32:14-07:00","id":958640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958538#post958538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Sphere is used to determine if someone's a Sleepwalker? Prime? Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're called arcana and prime can definitely do it with a knowing spell, but if you use mind to scan deeper memories and find obvious magic that the person clearly remembers, but it wouldn't be as definitive as the prime spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:10:58-07:00","id":958651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958468#post958468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> No. Google maps would make a good representational Yantra but probably has barely any Sympathetic connection to the places it displays. </div> </div> </div> </div>What about a picture taken directly on the scene? Is it enough? Can it be digital? I can understand how digitalization of data and puting it on the internet strips it of original sympathy. But maybe it doesn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:41:12-07:00","id":958688,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> if your mundane and magical friends meet then you aren't doing a great job of using the shadow name properly anyway since its purpose is to help you separate the magical and part of your life from the mundane. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> A picture is still pretty much just representational (It's practically the definition of representation) in my opinion, good as a yantra weak as a source of sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:28:50-07:00","id":958699,"title":"","content":"You can boost sympathy with a single spell. I kinda know what's the difference between yantra and sympathy. The thing I don't get is this thin line between zero and weak sympathy. Does a photo of a place have weak sympathy to the place if it didn't change too much since it was taken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:58:15-07:00","id":958705,"title":"","content":"I figure a photo has the same sympathy to a place as a person does to a cup that they're holding. In other words, in the moment of taking it there's a really fragile connection that breaks apart at the end of the scene. At that point the photo works well as a representational Yantra but no longer has any useful Sympathetic connection the location it represents. Naturally, if you have Space you can reinforce its Sympathy before that breakdown occurs and get some more use out of the picture as a result. I wouldn't be surprised if there are Space Mages who barter Sympathetically enhanced photos with each other. In other words a photo is about as important to a place as a paper cup is to a person (Look at Web-Weaver). For a weak sympathetic connection to a place you'd have to take a replaceable object from it, like say a wood chip from a playground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-27-2016, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:53:54-07:00","id":958720,"title":"","content":"Thanks! So live video should be enough to have weak sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:58:58-07:00","id":958723,"title":"","content":"I don't know, it's basically the same as a picture the only thing that's different is that it's continuous instead of a snapshot. It's probably the same as the paper cup, as soon it gets shut off it'll no longer have a sympathetic connection at all. Although if you have a live video feed you can also just skip Sympathy and use remote casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:33:40-07:00","id":958731,"title":"","content":"Neither of these really answered my question. I gave some examples where it would happen, so &quot;it wouldn't&quot; isn't really helpful a response. 2/3rds of the mages in my game are all students at the same university. Meeting them in mundane situations around mundane folks is going to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:37:06-07:00","id":958733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958731#post958731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of these really answered my question. I gave some examples where it would happen, so &quot;it wouldn't&quot; isn't really helpful a response. 2/3rds of the mages in my game are all students at the same university. Meeting them in mundane situations around mundane folks is going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not covered in the books but I would probably throw together some kind of mind or prime spell so that anybody who hears your shadow name in your presence without you personnaly telling them first hears your mundane name instead and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> Or maybe simply anyone not knowing one of the two and hearing it would hear a third name. And then a HUGE social pressure on the young mage to stick to using the shadow name in magic circonstances, the nickname in public and to not inquire about the real name, possibly with some kind of geas/curse attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12295,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","user":"Lokiel","date":". 08-27-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:44:17-07:00","id":958739,"title":"","content":"Just use mundane names in mundane situations and mage names in mage situations.<br /> EDIT<br /> It's taboo to call Merlin The Gremlin &quot;Bob&quot; when he is pouncing around with a fake beard and in mage robes, because he is literally wearing a Merlin Gremlin persona; you would be basically assaulting his Shadow Name and polluting it. It's ok to call him Bob when he ditches the costume and is running around as his normal self. In fact, calling him Merlin The Gremlin when he is in mundane identity would probably also be a no no because it would be polluting the Shadow Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-27-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:04:40-07:00","id":958741,"title":"","content":"As long its continouos and it's happening now it has weak sympathy. Remote casting, I forgot about it.<br /> <br /> What about temporal? Is enough to have well preserved 1900's newspaper to look back into every second of those hundred years? What do I see? The place where I'm standing or the surroundings of newspaper at the time of my choosing? How far I can &quot;walk&quot; in my vision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:05:46-07:00","id":958742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958739#post958739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just use mundane names in mundane situations and mage names in mage situations.<br /> EDIT<br /> It's taboo to call Merlin The Gremlin &quot;Bob&quot; when he is pouncing around with a fake beard and in mage robes, because he is literally wearing a Merlin Gremlin persona; you would be basically assaulting his Shadow Name and polluting it. It's ok to call him Bob when he ditches the costume and is running around as his normal self. In fact, calling him Merlin The Gremlin when he is in mundane identity would probably also be a no no because it would be polluting the Shadow Name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think his problem is when you have mages who only know your shadow name and not your mundane one whom you meet on a daily basis. So your suggestion doesn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:15:12-07:00","id":958744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958731#post958731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of these really answered my question. I gave some examples where it would happen, so &quot;it wouldn't&quot; isn't really helpful a response. 2/3rds of the mages in my game are all students at the same university. Meeting them in mundane situations around mundane folks is going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>How it gets handled when it does happen is dependent on the story and the actors. So many possibilities.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> You could look back at the paper's past, but it's not going to show you all the events that's described in the paper. The area around the paper that's revealed could be handled with Scale and would be the surroundings of the paper at each point in its history. So you could cast Postcognition on it in your Sanctum but its history and your vision would start where it was printed and move along to where it was sold and so on until it ended up in an archive or wherever you got it from assuming you were able to pull together a Postcog with enough Duration to witness its entire history from past to present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:27:23-07:00","id":958748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958744#post958744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your vision would start where it was printed and move along to where it was sold and so on until it ended up in an archive or wherever you got it from assuming you were able to pull together a Postcog with enough Duration to witness its entire history from past to present.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Add Space 2 to Postcognition to travel wherever you want(by &quot;foot&quot; or following space sympathy)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 08-27-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:32:01-07:00","id":958749,"title":"","content":"Then it's like meeting people you know only by online name offline. Awkward and begging to ask &quot;so, I should call you how...?&quot;<br /> EDIT<br /> Then again, it isn't that hard to communicate with people without using their names or handles. Just go for &quot;you&quot; and &quot;it's his&quot; instead of &quot;John&quot; and &quot;it's John's&quot;?<br /> There were like 3 or 4 people in our dorm that I *knew* but *didn't knew their names* and it would be awkard to ask for them, so I just communicated with them without using them, for like, months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-27-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:40:09-07:00","id":958753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958731#post958731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of these really answered my question. I gave some examples where it would happen, so &quot;it wouldn't&quot; isn't really helpful a response.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response was not &quot;it wouldn't.&quot; My response was &quot;Neither 'Becky' nor 'Mister Anderson' nor 'You' are sympathetic names or Shadow Names, so there's your workaround.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:41:44-07:00","id":958754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=958749#post958749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it's like meeting people you know only by online name offline. Awkward and begging to ask &quot;so, I should call you how...?&quot;<br /> EDIT<br /> Then again, it isn't that hard to communicate with people without using their names or handles. Just go for &quot;you&quot; and &quot;it's his&quot; instead of &quot;John&quot; and &quot;it's John's&quot;?<br /> There were like 3 or 4 people in our dorm that I *knew* but *didn't knew their names* and it would be awkard to ask for them, so I just communicated with them without using them, for like, months.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree that a social norm would be enough, with maybe a little bit of magic added in for the most cautious. I think his problem is how can mages avoid giving out sympathy to rivals they meet in their mundane life. Frankly, there's no way. But anyway, I think a determined enough mage can easily find the true name of most of his rivals anyway. Between Mind reading, happening upon it by cha... Fate, using postcognition to hear a conversation you've participated in, scrying, and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:01:03-07:00","id":958760,"title":"","content":"Yeah, using Shadow Names seems to be more about having a magical identity that empowers your magic and about keeping your mundane connections safe from it than about protecting your Sympathetic identity. If you really want to protect that then invest in Occultation or Fame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:19:13-07:00","id":958763,"title":"","content":"Nah, I don't really care about rivals finding out. Having a Sympathetic name really does very little in the grand scheme of things. Just +1 to Withstand level without it, which is just a -2 penalty to compensate for. I was just curious how the major taboo interfaces with day-to-day life when you share that day-to-day life with other mages. Friendly or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:33:08-07:00","id":958770,"title":"","content":"Basically, if your Cabal mates refuse to call you Lord Dark Of Doom And Mystery even when you actively trying to be Lord Dark Of Doom And Mystery (by equipping your trappings, by using appropiate speech pattern, by CASTING MAGIC), you might have problems building up that Shadow Name to 3. You could probably do a plot about this, where someone is waging a memetic war against their rival by undermining their Shadow Name in order to reduce their power by eroding the Shadow Name and making the merit weaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T01:23:47-07:00","id":959146,"title":"","content":"Mage 2ED: ,for heal a vampire, a mage need Life AND Death too? Death 2 or 3 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T02:11:00-07:00","id":959153,"title":"","content":"Life does nothing to a vampire. To heal a dead body you need Death 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T02:46:00-07:00","id":959156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=959153#post959153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life does nothing to a vampire. To heal a dead body you need Death 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a vampire , undead, body is valued as a zombi corpse, yeah. <br /> On first edition, mage used life and death for vampire body: now i dont know...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:02:50-07:00","id":959168,"title":"","content":"Most of those akward conjuctional requirements have benn cleaned up in 2nd ed. Healing an undead is a Perfecting Death spell.<br /> EDIT: you may even be able to improve their &quot;natural&quot; healing capabilities, maki g each Vitae count as 2 or more, as an alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 08-28-2016, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:02:45-07:00","id":959335,"title":"","content":"Spirits have Know Spirit. Ghosts have Speak with the Dead.<br /> <br /> How would you determine rank/nimina/ban/bane/etc for other Ephemera?<br /> <br /> Supernal, Abyssal (this is most relevant right now), or the various Ephemera designed for other game lines like Strix?<br /> <br /> While we're at it, would Horrors be handled mostly with Life or some other Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:24:41-07:00","id":959347,"title":"","content":"Well, Supernal beings aren't ephemeral, but there's no reason why the arcana that it corresponds to couldn't judge the strength (Rank) of its existence.<br /> <br /> Abyssal entities might be able to be diagnosed by arcana, but they might not be either depending on their specific natures and also because of the fact that Abyssal beings defy codification you can't really class them all as ephemeral either. They use the rules for ephemeral creatures, but that's not what they are.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about Horrors, but it probably depends on the Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:39:55-07:00","id":959426,"title":"","content":"For Horror, I would say Mind, since they're mostly Super-Goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:16:00-07:00","id":959459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=959335#post959335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits have Know Spirit. Ghosts have Speak with the Dead.<br /> <br /> How would you determine rank/nimina/ban/bane/etc for other Ephemera?<br /> <br /> Supernal, Abyssal (this is most relevant right now), or the various Ephemera designed for other game lines like Strix?<br /> <br /> While we're at it, would Horrors be handled mostly with Life or some other Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely Strix would be covered by Death since they're sort of animate shadows. I remember DaveB saying something like &quot;Death works on Strix, but for different reasons than it works on vampires or ghosts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to say that Abyssal creatures shouldn't be readable by the Arcana directly, or maybe doing so costs Mana and/or always invokes Paradox. Maybe a &quot;Supernal Vision&quot;-ish Prime 1 effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-28-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:28:07-07:00","id":959478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=959426#post959426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Horror, I would say Mind, since they're mostly Super-Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about Horrors, the astral creatures that dwell in the Primordial Dream from Beast, yeah. But, I think Maina was talking about Horrors, the generic non-ephemeral monsters from the CofD core. In that case, it would depend on the Horror. Living creatures would require Life, undead would require Death, stuff like the evil house would probably require Matter, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T05:04:58-07:00","id":959759,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> <br /> After the errata, unsafely relinquished spells can &quot;apply a condition&quot; to spell's subject, as per Paradox Options Table. My questions is: how do you decide how long the Condition will persist? Normally, this would be based on spellcasters Wisdom, but it feels weird that the spell can &quot;check&quot; your Wisdom after you release it. So:<br /> a) do you use Wisdom as normal to determine Condition's duration?<br /> b) do you use Wisdom-when-released to determine Condition's duration?<br /> c) do you use &quot;Wisdom of 0&quot;, as there is no Wisdom to keep the spell in check at all?<br /> d) something else?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T14:57:32-07:00","id":960031,"title":"","content":"Somewhere on these forums, someone posted their houserules where emotions were the purview of Spirit, not Mind. Can anyone help me track those houserules down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:43:29-07:00","id":960058,"title":"","content":"Doesn't really need it, Spirit can manipulate Essence and its effects on Spirits. Want people to get angry? Whip up some anger Essence and the spirits that govern it will come to do your bidding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:15:58-07:00","id":960070,"title":"","content":"Is spending Reach for precision a thing? For example, so as to replicate a chip with alter conductivity?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T19:50:35-07:00","id":960184,"title":"","content":"Closest correlation I can think of is Zoom In, but that depends on if you think of it as precision or amplifying the spell's original effect. I prefer the latter. Reach is for go big or go home, imo. So, if I was ruling it and you wanted a piece of material to act like a computer chip it would require a different spell than Alter Conductivity. It would still be at the same level though since it's basically using Wonderous Machine on a rock or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:33:03-07:00","id":960317,"title":"","content":"What do you think would it take to cut a wood log into fine pieces for your fireplace? Matter Fraying spell with potency equal to the Structure?<br /> How to cut an arm off with Life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 08-30-2016, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T03:12:40-07:00","id":960324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=960184#post960184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closest correlation I can think of is Zoom In, but that depends on if you think of it as precision or amplifying the spell's original effect. I prefer the latter. Reach is for go big or go home, imo. So, if I was ruling it and you wanted a piece of material to act like a computer chip it would require a different spell than Alter Conductivity. It would still be at the same level though since it's basically using Wonderous Machine on a rock or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea here isn't to make a wooden table work like a computer by magically mashing the two things together, but rather to give it the properties of a computer's circuitry by manipulating it's conductivity. Basically, it comes down to &quot;could you use <i>Alter Conductivity</i> to affect an object in such a way that only parts of the whole object gain or lose said conductivity?&quot;. For example, could you cast it on a chess board so only the black tiles are conducive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:17:04-07:00","id":960336,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd just make that a Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T07:17:55-07:00","id":961039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=960317#post960317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think would it take to cut a wood log into fine pieces for your fireplace? Matter Fraying spell with potency equal to the Structure?<br /> How to cut an arm off with Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make cutting a wood log into pieces for a fireplace a narrative effect - it's just plain not worth mechanizing - unless it's a tree, in which case, sure, you can measure it that way.<br /> <br /> Severing an arm with Life, meanwhile, is an upgraded form of the Arm Wrack tilt. If you want a quick spell...<br /> <br /> <b>Splinter (Life or Space oooo)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Practice:</i> Unraveling<br /> <i>Primary Factor:</i> Duration<br /> <i>Withstand: </i>Stamina<br /> <i>Suggested Rote Skills:</i> Medicine, Firearms, Brawl<br /> <br /> All things are dependent on the Supernal for their reality. By unraveling the threads of a subject's Tapestry, the Mage denies their opponent the very existence of their parts.<br /> <br /> With this spell, the Mage may inflict one Tilt affecting the target's limbs (Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Blinded, Deafened) per dot of Potency. Applying the tilt twice affects both bodily members. This may manifest as nerve damage, sapping of strength, or even the limbs simply turning cold and dead.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The spell is not clean and gentle; the unraveled threads explode outwards and turn the subject's limbs into a shower of gore. For each Tilt inflicted, the subject suffers one lethal health level. The damage does not disappear when the Tilts end.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: Rather than merely sapping the strength from the target's limbs, the Mage severs them entirely. This renders the effect Lasting. This costs 1 Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T07:52:33-07:00","id":961055,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> Yeah, me too. It' not a stressful situation so Down and Dirty spellcasting or narrative effect would suffice. I was wondering more about Arcana requirements of cleanly and purposely splitting things apart. And your spell is very helpfull, thanks! <br /> My take on it was to allow to attach this kind of &quot;lasting tilt&quot; to any spell that deals aggravated damage. So +1 Reach to deal agravated +1 Reach to apply Wrack Tilt + 1 Reach severe limb permanently. <br /> Your's better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T07:56:09-07:00","id":961058,"title":"","content":"You could easily modify the existing damage spell to allow the Tilt application as a +1 Reach effect and a +2 to make that Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:09:55-07:00","id":962679,"title":"","content":"I've heard a few mentions of a Legacy whose end-game is turning into a Spirit, but I can't find the name. Does this exist?<br /> <br /> Similarly, can magic grant Numina to people? Maybe Spirit+Life? Or while the person is in Ephemeral Form (like with Twilight Body)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:18:24-07:00","id":962681,"title":"","content":"You're talking about the Scions of God, they're in the Legacies the Sublime book. In that book turning into a spirit is the &quot;end-game&quot; but it's not part of their attainments (Except possibly their ascendant attainment).<br /> <br /> And yes, magic can. The Katsinam Tsuukya (Can't remember the book, Tome of the Watchtowers I think) actually grant Influences and Numina as part of the attainments. If translated into a spell it'd indeed be a Spirit+Life Patterning spell. Nothing about becoming ephemeral inherently grants you Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:45:02-07:00","id":962691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=962681#post962681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Katsinam Tsuukya (Can't remember the book, Tome of the Watchtowers I think)</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:47:26-07:00","id":962694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=962679#post962679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, can magic grant Numina to people? Maybe Spirit+Life? Or while the person is in Ephemeral Form (like with Twilight Body)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say, without Honorary Rank, a Conjunctional Spirit + Life Patterning spell would be necessary, otherwise, I'd argue that Shape Spirit could be cast upon yourself, although, TBH, unless the target is a plain-Jane mortal, most splat powers are more versatile than Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:56:53-07:00","id":962697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=962694#post962694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say, without Honorary Rank, a Conjunctional Spirit + Life Patterning spell would be necessary, otherwise, I'd argue that Shape Spirit could be cast upon yourself, although, TBH, unless the target is a plain-Jane mortal, most splat powers are more versatile than Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't get Honorary Rank till Spirit 4 anyway so your point is moot. Even if it were correct Honorary Rank doesn't mean that you're part Spirit (A requirement for having a Numina) it just means that spirits treat you with caution and respect because you can make their existence pretty awful if they don't.<br /> <br /> Even if Numina aren't as versatile as arcana, rotes, etc, they are still powers that wouldn't induce Dissonance. Though if I were running it then even though the Numina and its effects were immune to Dissonance the spell that granted the Numina would be subject to Dissonance after a Sleeper witnesses or is subjected to the Numina.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T05:15:03-07:00","id":962775,"title":"","content":"How does gravity work in a space created by Ban?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T05:31:31-07:00","id":962781,"title":"","content":"Presumably, the same way it did before. Gravity is still there, doing the same thing. Mage treats forces (and Forces) more like liquids you can gather in a bucket and pour on people than particles in motion or molecular interactions. Otherwise, the Zoom In spell would create enormous black rings around the eyes of the Mage using it as it funnels light into a single point like a telescope, and an Invisibility spell would also make you blind.<br /> <br /> Think symbolically, not physically. An area under a Ban is basically the same place it was before; cut-and-pasted into a blank white void. Lighting conditions, gravity, all that jazz, should theoretically change, but since it's symbolically the same place, I'd treat it as no different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:59:45-07:00","id":962929,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> <br /> A bucket full of gravity.<br /> \u200bMakes sense in that respect.<br /> Otherwise the air wouldn't be in there either,<br /> nor Time.<br /> <br /> Imagine that though.<br /> Taking a bucket full of gravity and pouring it over someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T01:24:45-07:00","id":963128,"title":"","content":"A question about Spirits and Influences.<br /> The description of the level 5 influence mass creation also elaborates that a spirit can now create a single permanent manifestation of its influence, implying it wasn't possible before. Looking at the duration chart, every spirit with a rank 4 influence can allready do that. Which one is true?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T02:33:08-07:00","id":963142,"title":"","content":"It can't. You sum up the dots of the Influence Effects and Duration to determine the possible outcome. So creating (4 dots) a permament (4 dots) effect would normally require 4+4=8 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T04:27:53-07:00","id":963162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=963142#post963142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can't. You sum up the dots of the Influence Effects and Duration to determine the possible outcome. So creating (4 dots) a permament (4 dots) effect would normally require 4+4=8 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that, as mentioned, 5 dots does bypass this particular requirement for creating a single, permanent effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:28:49-07:00","id":963191,"title":"","content":"Okay good, that's what I thought reading the duration rules too... but I thought I probably was wrong. I mean by that system you need (apart from influence 5 being able to do it on their own) and Influence rating of 6+ to make anything besides a Strengthening influence permanent, meaning such feats are actually more or less impossible for spirits (apart from Influence 5 just circumventing that rule)? If thats the intent then why give the option in the table at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 09-04-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:00:48-07:00","id":963203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=963191#post963191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay good, that's what I thought reading the duration rules too... but I thought I probably was wrong. I mean by that system you need (apart from influence 5 being able to do it on their own) and Influence rating of 6+ to make anything besides a Strengthening influence permanent, meaning such feats are actually more or less impossible for spirits (apart from Influence 5 just circumventing that rule)? If thats the intent then why give the option in the table at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This [phenomenon] will be significantly more resilient for as long as the lesser Incarna sponsoring it exists&quot; is expected. &quot;This persistent change to the particulars of this [phenomenon] will stick around basically forever&quot; is more the domain of godlike entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T19:52:59-07:00","id":964030,"title":"","content":"hello all...<br /> <br /> i have a couple questions...if they have already been answered, forgive me and point me the right direction.<br /> <br /> 1. in nWoD is there a way to lower spellcasting difficulty???<br /> <br /> 2. what is this praxis thing i was reading about?? the concept for my mage about casting the same spell/rote all the time makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> 3. after character creation would the xp cost for striking looks at the 2 point level be 6 xp?<br /> <br /> 4 when you learn a new sphere ( yes i know i'm using the wrong term) does one get a rote for free???<br /> <br /> 5 how long does it take after awaking for someone to be trained as a mage??<br /> <br /> thank you all,<br /> <br /> Rtemplar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12391-rtemplar","name":"rtemplar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:21:33-07:00","id":964080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rtemplar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=964030#post964030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hello all...<br /> <br /> i have a couple questions...if they have already been answered, forgive me and point me the right direction.<br /> <br /> 1. in nWoD is there a way to lower spellcasting difficulty???<br /> <br /> 2. what is this praxis thing i was reading about?? the concept for my mage about casting the same spell/rote all the time makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> 3. after character creation would the xp cost for striking looks at the 2 point level be 6 xp?<br /> <br /> 4 when you learn a new sphere ( yes i know i'm using the wrong term) does one get a rote for free???<br /> <br /> 5 how long does it take after awaking for someone to be trained as a mage??<br /> <br /> thank you all,<br /> <br /> Rtemplar</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Do you mean lowering the target number? If so, no. Hell no. Hell no not in a million years no. Mummy is the only gameline that has messed with target numbers and that was a pretty bad idea then.<br /> <br /> 2. Praxis are spells that you've cast a hell of a lot of times and the casting is near second nature to you, it's easier to do really well when you cast a praxis and praxis are pretty much iconic of your character. They're pretty well explained in the book.<br /> <br /> 3. Nope. Xp costs in 2e are flat, so if you want to buy 1 dot of a merit it costs 1xp, 2 dots of a merit costs 2xp. Having 3 dots in a merit and buying the fourth and fifth dot for example still only costs 2xp. So for buying striking looks 2 after character creation it would cost 2xp.<br /> <br /> 4. No. You have to buy rotes or find a grimoire with the rote contained inside and then buy the rote anyway if you want to know it and cast it without the grimoire. Rotes can only be made by masters of the relevant arcana as well.<br /> <br /> 5. Depends. Usually a month or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:50:55-07:00","id":964089,"title":"","content":"damn.....makes everything really tough to do then if base difficulty is 8. as for the xp cost for striking looks..i must have the 1e version...cuz it says new dot times 2. please tell me page number for praxis...thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12391-rtemplar","name":"rtemplar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:19:52-07:00","id":964100,"title":"","content":"If you have 1st edition, you won't find Praxis in the book, those are a second edition thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:56:20-07:00","id":964167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rtemplar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=964089#post964089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">damn.....makes everything really tough to do then if base difficulty is 8. as for the xp cost for striking looks..i must have the 1e version...cuz it says new dot times 2. please tell me page number for praxis...thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>8 isn't that hard to hit, most of the time you're only looking for a single success anyway and where you'd get a difficulty lowering in CWoD you'd get a number of bonus dice in CofD, outside of contested rolls, extended actions and combat you'll only ever need to get 1 success to do a thing.<br /> <br /> Ah yeah, you're using 1e. So praxis aren't a thing in 1e and the cost is 6xp for a 2 dot merit bought after creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:29:31-07:00","id":964187,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it's been asked.<br /> <br /> If you lower a target's Withstand trait with a spell,<br /> and then you cast a second spell with a low potency on the weakened subject,<br /> does the second spell stop working when the first spell wears off due to a returning withstand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:47:46-07:00","id":964196,"title":"","content":"I would assume yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:15:51-07:00","id":964229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=964187#post964187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it's been asked.<br /> <br /> If you lower a target's Withstand trait with a spell,<br /> and then you cast a second spell with a low potency on the weakened subject,<br /> does the second spell stop working when the first spell wears off due to a returning withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> (characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:23:26-07:00","id":964233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=964187#post964187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it's been asked.<br /> <br /> If you lower a target's Withstand trait with a spell,<br /> and then you cast a second spell with a low potency on the weakened subject,<br /> does the second spell stop working when the first spell wears off due to a returning withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the opposite works as well, so if the withstand has been raised above the potency by magic and the withstand raising magic stops for whatever reason then the spell will take effect as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:39:24-07:00","id":965740,"title":"","content":"HI guys,<br /> <br /> i have a question about abyss environment tilt, can someone tell me where is it in the book or what is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:48:52-07:00","id":965776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=965740#post965740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HI guys,<br /> <br /> i have a question about abyss environment tilt, can someone tell me where is it in the book or what is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on a search through the book and a glance at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885141-abyssal-environmental-tilt\">this thread</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880989-abyssal-environmental-tilts\">this thread</a> I think they're not in the book and something you have to come up with on your own. It's possible the upcoming supplement has some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:11:42-07:00","id":965822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=965776#post965776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on a search through the book and a glance at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885141-abyssal-environmental-tilt\">this thread</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880989-abyssal-environmental-tilts\">this thread</a> I think they're not in the book and something you have to come up with on your own. It's possible the upcoming supplement has some.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is as I feared, but thank you for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:17:56-07:00","id":966079,"title":"","content":"What other penalties apply to the spellcasting pool besides self imposed (for factors) and enemy spells?<br /> <br /> Like do effects that make it hard to concentrate do anything?<br /> <br /> Likewise, does a supernatural effect penalize the pool? For instance, casting a spell to find and/or follow a werewolf through a crowd while it is in human form. Is that all just handled by the withstand system or maybe clash of wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:55:24-07:00","id":966091,"title":"","content":"Officially, none.<br /> <br /> You may wish to have effects that penalize concentration work on magic, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:53:03-07:00","id":966359,"title":"","content":"I am not sure but...<br /> Situation: Obrimos with Prime 2 Time 2 Force 2<br /> 1) If my mage use post cognition... can he use other spell for &quot;scan&quot; npc's lies with Pierce Detection?<br /> 2) Can use Nightvision for have better vision ?<br /> 3) His peripherical magic sight, activate if a ghost ,unseen, use a numina on the scene ?<br /> 4) Can use focused mage sight too?<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:02:13-07:00","id":966362,"title":"","content":"You can use Mage Sight with Postcognition just fine. The other spells have to be Combined with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:27:18-07:00","id":966380,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> Shouldn't it work like Scrying and count as viewing them remotely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:42:19-07:00","id":966388,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> Based on the errata to Temporal Sympathy, casting spells back in time requires a Combined Spell, combining one Time spell that uses Temporal Sympathy and one spell for effect. This errata makes it harder for mages to throw magic back in time at low Gnosis, by my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:43:26-07:00","id":966390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=966380#post966380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> Shouldn't it work like Scrying and count as viewing them remotely?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't an option to remote cast on things in the past, and since the errata came out you can't use Temporal Sympathy on a spell that doesn't specifically call for it. Using Combined Casting with Postcognition or another spell that requires Temporal Sympathy effectively makes the non-Time spell into a Time spell, thus qualifying it for casting into the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfSilkAndStone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=966388#post966388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> Based on the errata to Temporal Sympathy, casting spells back in time requires a Combined Spell, combining one Time spell that uses Temporal Sympathy and one spell for effect. This errata makes it harder for mages to throw magic back in time at low Gnosis, by my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninja'd. I don't know if that's the reason it was done. It just complicates the method by which magic can be sent into the past, it doesn't actually resolve the questions that were raised because of the ability to do it. Usually along the lines of, how do you resolve that? Though maybe it does help since you have guidelines in those Time spells about how to resolve their effects and you can thus pair those guidelines with the combined spell that just got winged out and maybe come more easily to a resolution.<br /> <br /> By the way, I think it would be more interesting if you could Remote Cast on subjects in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-09-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:01:27-07:00","id":966425,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3547\" data-vbnamecard=\"3547\">SonOfSilkAndStone</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Ow right. I forgot about that (still before my first run of 2e). <br /> So if you can use Mage Sight does that mean that you can use attainments without combining? Also why couldn't you add one dot of Forces to reveal more like in Goetic Summon when you just add Spirit or Death to materialize? <br /> Summon and Materialize are related to self in the same way like Postcognition and Nightvision IMO. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:16:59-07:00","id":966432,"title":"","content":"Hard to say, but I think I'd rule that it only works with Mage Sight. <br /> <br /> You can't just add a dot in Forces because you're getting one complete spell effect at the same time that you're getting another complete spell effect.<br /> <br /> So, with Goetic summon, what you're doing there the Death or Spirit component is not a complete Death or Spirit effect that stands alone by itself, it's modifying the Goetia's &quot;body&quot; with ephemera from Death or Spirit to be able to materialize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:27:25-07:00","id":966436,"title":"","content":"With Forces you are just slightly modifying sensory input granted by Postcognition while in Goetic Summon Death grants entire new &quot;body&quot;. And yes, this Death or Spirit component can be cast as stand alone spell on a ghost or spirit.<br /> <br /> Edit: Let's just take an easier example (I dont want to argue about this one) <br /> Sacred Geometry reaveals things but if you add Spirit or Death it reaveals also diffrent things. Those are clearly two stand alone spells casted not by by combining but by conjoining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 09-09-2016, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:09:26-07:00","id":966454,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would think that conjoined spells generally all have precisely the same end, with all parts of the spell intending the same purpose. By definition, the Time spell in the combination is intended only to part the veil of time; a specialized postcognition intended to reveal, say, the local history of ley line movement, that seems like a reasonable conjunction to me. This would, however, bend towards Knowing spells being pretty reasonable to combine into postcognitive spells, so I guess I generally agree that 'postcognition + Prime' or whatever should let you get limited past knowledge without a full Combined spell by default (unless word of designer is otherwise).<br /> <br /> On a related note, I just love that magic in Awakening is governed by symbolism - it makes it relatively easy to adjudicate, as a new ST to any Mage game. The Practices and attainments all make a certain grammatical sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:43:44-07:00","id":966541,"title":"","content":"What would it take to get a satellite view of the earth with a scrying window?<br /> <br /> Not with all the bells and whistles of Google Maps or anything, just to look at it from that high up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:50:35-07:00","id":967227,"title":"","content":"What do Proximi do Clashes with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T06:50:23-07:00","id":967287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=966541#post966541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would it take to get a satellite view of the earth with a scrying window?<br /> <br /> Not with all the bells and whistles of Google Maps or anything, just to look at it from that high up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having Sympathy with an area already grants an overview, the larger the area the &quot;higher&quot; your Scrying window would presumably be set.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10091_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10091\" data-vbnamecard=\"10091\">Altasaire</a> I believe they clash with the same dice used to activate their Blessings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:15:49-07:00","id":967294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=967287#post967287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having Sympathy with an area already grants an overview, the larger the area the &quot;higher&quot; your Scrying window would presumably be set.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Prelate of the Eye could get a view of Earth with an orbital scrying window?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:37:26-07:00","id":967298,"title":"","content":"I don't think so since you'd still be bound by the upper limits of Advanced Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:15:17-07:00","id":967319,"title":"","content":"You could cast scrying window facing up, repeat the proces starting from the last one casting spell remotely and after couple of times just rotate the last window making it look down.<br /> I'm also sure that you can cast a moving scrying window. Add 1 Reach or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:12:01-07:00","id":968920,"title":"","content":"How many Awakened is a good range for a large city, like, say, London, Toronto, or Seattle? Those examples aren't pulled from the air, either, so if you want to be specific, they have populations just shy of 9 million, around 5 million, and just shy of 700,000 respectively. All cities have vibrant and active Mysteries for the sake of this question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:55:57-07:00","id":969012,"title":"","content":"Are you including Seers, apostates and banishers? Secret mages no one knows about, or those who have just travelled there to explore one of the vibrant and active Mysteries?<br /> <br /> Or just a traditional consilium?<br /> <br /> In addition, is it the primary stomping grounds of the players, or someplace they might visit and pass through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:43:18-07:00","id":969030,"title":"","content":"I'll take numbers with and without each, but it should be local Mages only (i.e. people only there long-term). Consilium is the focus here, though.<br /> <br /> And yes, these are primary stomping grounds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:10:57-07:00","id":969172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=968920#post968920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Awakened is a good range for a large city, like, say, London, Toronto, or Seattle? Those examples aren't pulled from the air, either, so if you want to be specific, they have populations just shy of 9 million, around 5 million, and just shy of 700,000 respectively. All cities have vibrant and active Mysteries for the sake of this question.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city\"> How many monsters are in your city? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The new Beast corebook, in background section of SAS The Morning After, have first official monsters numbers per capita in nWoD! Finally you can make sound </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:14:25-07:00","id":969206,"title":"","content":"Interesting... That should be useful in general, and I'll definitely be making use of that in future! That said, I was curious if anyone had anything more Mage-specific since Mages are perhaps the second-most migration-prone of the major splats (Prometheans obviously taking the crown).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:47:06-07:00","id":969314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969206#post969206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... That should be useful in general, and I'll definitely be making use of that in future! That said, I was curious if anyone had anything more Mage-specific since Mages are perhaps the second-most migration-prone of the major splats (Prometheans obviously taking the crown).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you have Splintered City: Seattle? The Mage section mentions that they are a strong Consilium but not the most powerful group of supernaturals in the area. Not a hard number but gives some idea of the relative populations maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:01:07-07:00","id":969405,"title":"","content":"Splintered City is Demon, yeah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:24:05-07:00","id":969418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969405#post969405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splintered City is Demon, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. But there is a small section for each other splat as well. Just a taster of what it might be like for them in Seattle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:36:14-07:00","id":969427,"title":"","content":"I've put a lot of thought into this over the years, and my own estimates are that a full Consilium made up of one Caucus of each Pentacle Order (where there isn't too much hat-collecting going on with some mages having multiple roles, except for heads of Orders being Councillors) is about 70 mages. <br /> <br /> Plus Seers and Nameless, you're looking at about 120 mages for a major city that's interestingly Mysterious enough, somewhere the size of Vegas, maybe, or Seattle.<br /> <br /> Bigger metropolies like LA and London will have nearly 200. New York is, in our semi-canon, the most populous Consilium in the world, but it's technically the New York City / Long Island / New Jersey Consilium, covering everything from Shelter Island to Princeton. It has multiple caucuses of most Orders, and an Arch-Heirarch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:04:14-07:00","id":969440,"title":"","content":"That sounds about right. Been batting this about in my head between meetings today, and I took to devising a method of &quot;chunking&quot; the supernaturals; finding a natural number a region might support and which going over will result in major tensions and possible civil war. For me, I figure that number is about 100 for the Awakened. Any large population center may have near that amount, with the rest chunked out into surrounding areas.<br /> <br /> For Toronto, I ended up figuring a number of about 250 being a reasonable population relation, but that's too high for one Consilium. So, parcel off about 50 for Barrie and Parry Sound, 25 for Waterloo and Stratford, and 75 for Niagara. These groups get their own Mysteries and Consilia and schisms but ultimately link up to Caucuses split between these regions. Naturally, this gets pretty dilute and these represent most of the Awakened in Ontario.<br /> <br /> It's a method that deliberately ignores the populations of those surrounding regions, but they're ostensibly not the main area of play and only exist as far as they're interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969418#post969418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. But there is a small section for each other splat as well. Just a taster of what it might be like for them in Seattle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nifty. Must've missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:04:54-07:00","id":969480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969427#post969427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've put a lot of thought into this over the years, and my own estimates are that a full Consilium made up of one Caucus of each Pentacle Order (where there isn't too much hat-collecting going on with some mages having multiple roles, except for heads of Orders being Councillors) is about 70 mages.<br /> <br /> Plus Seers and Nameless, you're looking at about 120 mages for a major city that's interestingly Mysterious enough, somewhere the size of Vegas, maybe, or Seattle.<br /> <br /> Bigger metropolies like LA and London will have nearly 200. New York is, in our semi-canon, the most populous Consilium in the world, but it's technically the New York City / Long Island / New Jersey Consilium, covering everything from Shelter Island to Princeton. It has multiple caucuses of most Orders, and an Arch-Heirarch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Using Seattle as an example, with a population of approx. 650,000, that would mean there's one mage for approx. every 5,400 people. Absent some super-Mystery in a particular locale, isn't that proportion of Mages to regular humans extremely high?<br /> <br /> Do you believe the other major supernatural splats (e.g., vampires, werewolves, changelings) have comparable numbers to mages?<br /> <br /> While these types of questions have arisen for years an have only lead to vague conjecture, now that OPP intends to release a actual crossover chronicle book, we'll hopefully receive more substantive guidance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:21:49-07:00","id":969486,"title":"","content":"Expand it to Seattle's metro area, which bloats to eat Tacoma too, and the ratio falls considerably. Mind you, if you do the same for London, you take an extra four million souls on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:28:56-07:00","id":969490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969486#post969486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expand it to Seattle's metro area, which bloats to eat Tacoma too, and the ratio falls considerably. Mind you, if you do the same for London, you take an extra four million souls on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but even with a Seattle metro population of about 3.7 million, that's still one mage for about every 30,000 normal humans. It's still a pretty big proportion, and assuming that other major supernaturals have similar numbers, to say nothing of other splats and minor supernaturals like psychics and thaumaturges and various supernatural entities like claimed and spirits, that's one heck of a LOT of supernatural beings and activity. <br /> <br /> If I was some regular Joe or Jane normal, I wouldn't want to get out of bed in the morning, no less do something suicidal like ride the bus or subway at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:33:34-07:00","id":969493,"title":"","content":"There's 650,000 people in Seatle the city. The urban area is much much bigger.<br /> <br /> Most large cities are surrounded by other towns and cites which are ffor practical purposes a part of the core city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:42:45-07:00","id":969501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969493#post969493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's 650,000 people in Seatle the city. The urban area is much much bigger.<br /> <br /> Most large cities are surrounded by other towns and cites which are ffor practical purposes a part of the core city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, I live and work in Manhattan and grew up in the NY and NJ suburbs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's why I expanded the population numbers of Seattle to 3.7+ million, the population of the entire metropolitan area. The assumed supernatural proportions dropped from an original &quot;Are you effing' kidding me?&quot; enormous from only counting Seattle proper, to a still extremely high &quot;my math must be wrong?!&quot; huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:56:43-07:00","id":969507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969480#post969480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Using Seattle as an example, with a population of approx. 650,000, that would mean there's one mage for approx. every 5,400 people. Absent some super-Mystery in a particular locale, isn't that proportion of Mages to regular humans extremely high?<br /> <br /> Do you believe the other major supernatural splats (e.g., vampires, werewolves, changelings) have comparable numbers to mages?<br /> <br /> While these types of questions have arisen for years an have only lead to vague conjecture, now that OPP intends to release a actual crossover chronicle book, we'll hopefully receive more substantive guidance?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mages clump. Population ratios assume that the supernatural beings in question are evenly spread; something that <i>might</i> work for vampire if you're ignorant of how vampire society works but definitely doesn't work for mages.<br /> <br /> There's whole areas that should have one or two or ten mages that don't, because they <i>move</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T17:02:33-07:00","id":969540,"title":"","content":"Flawed though they may be, population ratios do give people a rough sensation of how &quot;common&quot; supernatural beings are, which is pretty important for people to help feel how crowded a given magical scene is. It's never going to be good for books to give exact numbers but guidelines on how to emphasize different levels of crowding might be fun.<br /> <br /> Plus, you can limit the biases of assumptions by expanding the area under observation and then sub-dividing, and/or by emphasizing that the areas players go are automatically interesting and, thus, will contain more magic people by default.<br /> <br /> Once someone gets used to the game, it's not as necessary to have guides, but they help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T17:05:25-07:00","id":969541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969507#post969507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mages clump. Population ratios assume that the supernatural beings in question are evenly spread; something that <i>might</i> work for vampire if you're ignorant of how vampire society works but definitely doesn't work for mages.<br /> <br /> There's whole areas that should have one or two or ten mages that don't, because they <i>move</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Understood, although a lot of other major supernaturals will similarly clump for a variety of reasons, such as vampires and changelings, for food and security, respectively. &quot;Mysteries&quot; will also likely attract some other supernatural types, as well as potentially being a source itself.<br /> <br /> My primary point was that in many urban areas, particularly mid-size and even some smaller cities, the supernatural, both splat and other weirdness, will be extraordinarily dense where you effectively can't swing a dead cat without hitting something that goes bump in the night.<br /> <br /> I definitely understand why so many mortals become Hunters or join the innumerable cults in the CofD. It's often that or quickly becoming a missing person or violent crime statistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T17:12:29-07:00","id":969546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969540#post969540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flawed though they may be, population ratios do give people a rough sensation of how &quot;common&quot; supernatural beings are, which is pretty important for people to help feel how crowded a given magical scene is. It's never going to be good for books to give exact numbers but guidelines on how to emphasize different levels of crowding might be fun.<br /> <br /> Plus, you can limit the biases of assumptions by expanding the area under observation and then sub-dividing, and/or by emphasizing that the areas players go are automatically interesting and, thus, will contain more magic people by default.<br /> <br /> Once someone gets used to the game, it's not as necessary to have guides, but they help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another point to consider is not just the absolute numbers or general geographic distribution of given supernatural types, but also power level distribution, to get a sense of what's happening in a locale.<br /> <br /> For instance, the hypothetical medium-sized city with about 120 mages will feel a lot different if over 20% are masters than if less than 1-2% achieve that kind of power. Similarly, a perceived excess of lower-level disciple and below mages will result in a lot more character opportunities, but with fewer sources of information or safety and security mechanisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:04:59-07:00","id":969712,"title":"","content":"How the fuck do I give stats to a creature created by the &quot;Create Life&quot; spell? Do I just arbitrarily allocate some, or what?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ended up ruling that it counts as a Potency (Potency of spell) Horror for the purposes of Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 09-15-2016, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:57:49-07:00","id":969735,"title":"","content":"The book says that it has whatever attributes are typical for a creature of that type. That is, just use the Bestiary entry. For things that don't actually exist, using the Horror rules as you are is probably as good a method as any if you can't just eyeball stats that make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:00:49-07:00","id":969737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969735#post969735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says that it has whatever attributes are typical for a creature of that type. That is, just use the Bestiary entry. For things that don't actually exist, using the Horror rules as you are is probably as good a method as any if you can't just eyeball stats that make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was my conclusion as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:38:25-07:00","id":969861,"title":"","content":"Does a Safe Place merit grant withstand rating if combined with Sanctum? Do you have any magical bariers build in or is Sanctum just for granting additional spell slots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:50:03-07:00","id":969869,"title":"","content":"I'm still coming to grips with 2E - are there any practical mechanical differences between Practices of the same dot level? I just read a thread, for instance, where people were going back and forth over whether a particular effect fell under Perfecting or Weaving. Is that important in any context other than being as correct as possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:06:05-07:00","id":969876,"title":"","content":"Not really, but it helps to build consistency into your rulings for your own and your player's understanding of the game and the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:13:35-07:00","id":969878,"title":"","content":"Could Pattern Restoration help a Mage get rid of an addiction he developed before Awakening? Rules-wise, I think the answer's Yes, but saying No would make a more interesting story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:26:57-07:00","id":969885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969876#post969876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, but it helps to build consistency into your rulings for your own and your player's understanding of the game and the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, cool. It's something I try to be aware of but I'm perpetually wary of being caught out by some merit or little-known rule from supplement X that would end up hinging an important roll or story point on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:26:57-07:00","id":969928,"title":"","content":"What happens in the following cases:<br /> <br /> You turn something into a gaseous state, someone breathes in some of it, and the spell wears off.<br /> <br /> You transform a poison into water and someone drinks it. Then the spell wears off.<br /> <br /> You turn water into a poison and someone drinks it. Then the spell wears off before they're too ill to recover.<br /> <br /> You create tea or cake with Ex Nihilo and consume it. Then the spell wears off.<br /> <br /> Does Matter even cover food? I know it covers drinks.<br /> <br /> Is there any way to make Lasting food/drink? Whether via Making or transforming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:30:57-07:00","id":969933,"title":"","content":"So, Abyssal beings are built roughly using the Spirit (for Gulmoth) and Goetia (for Acamoth) rules (even if they are not quite those things). This means they have the Attribute trio of Power-Finesse-Resistance, Rank, Essence, Influences, Manifestations, and Numina. They use the Conditions of their appropriate type (except as noted).<br /> <br /> So does this mean a Gulmoth (or Acamoth with adequate warping) can Claim things and people? Maybe even pick up the Familiar Manifestation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:32:53-07:00","id":969936,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Yup.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> Generally, use your best judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:02:40-07:00","id":970007,"title":"","content":"Has anyone written up any stat-blocks for Supernal or Abyssal entities in second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:20:23-07:00","id":970100,"title":"","content":"Anyone officially? Not to my knowledge. Abyssal is a template now, though; you can take existing entities and just slap it on them and bam. Abyssal critter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:09:09-07:00","id":970140,"title":"","content":"Gonna throw in my own question: Does Supernal magic work on Abyssal entities? Can Supernal fire an incarnate demon? Can Spirit command a gulmoth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:12:12-07:00","id":970145,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Abyssal entity has always been my answer. I prefer the Abyss to defy categorization.<br /> <br /> I thought the New York Consilium was going to be in the book, but it isn't, has anyone consolidated the details about it floating around? I know it has moving buildings and that the Seers have partially weaponized the Mystery of that, and that it's huge and that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:50:28-07:00","id":970181,"title":"","content":"New York is the setting for Travis Stout's own Mage chronicle, and we've been dropping references to it since Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> It is the largest Consilium in the Western world, maybe in the whole world; its territory covers half of New Jersey, the Boroughs of New York City itself and all of Long Island. It has eleven Pentacle Order Caucuses (each Order has at least one full Caucus, most two, some three) and a functioning Nameless Order for the apostates who want to swap rotes but otherwise be left alone. The various sub-Consilia are working on Mysteries of their own, but the big one is that Manhattan is so charged with ley energies its evolving into something. Whole city blocks move, sliding around, but the changes are subject to Quiescence so only the Awakened and Sleepwalkers are aware of it.<br /> <br /> After 9/11, Manhattan became an unexploded bomb. The Seers and Pentacle worked out a short-lived truce to deal with it, but the Seers screwed the Pentacle mages (including the Consilium's arch-Hierarch) over and somehow took control of Manhattan's Mystery. Now the island itself is hostile to Pentacle mages trying to set up shop there, so the Consilium keeps to the other Boroughs and the wider New York / New Jersey states, with some cabals raiding into Manhattan to try to figure out what's going on or recover lost treasures. The locals call what happened &quot;The Folly&quot;.<br /> <br /> Awakening second ed's chapter fiction is set in New York. It will get its proper writeup in Tome of the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Other random facts:<br /> <br /> There's a Free Council cabal of punk musicians called &quot;Join The Seers.&quot;<br /> The new arch-Hierarch is a thearch named Sheshat<br /> The Interfector is called Outis, and his schtick is he accidentally prevented his own birth during a disastrous time-travel jaunt when an apprentice.<br /> Various of the Brooklyn-Queens Silver Ladder Caucus have appeared in the Fallen World Anthology and M2e<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:02:51-07:00","id":970193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New York is the setting for Travis Stout's own Mage chronicle, and we've been dropping references to it since Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> It is the largest Consilium in the Western world, maybe in the whole world; its territory covers half of New Jersey, the Boroughs of New York City itself and all of Long Island. It has eleven Pentacle Order Caucuses (each Order has at least one full Caucus, most two, some three) and a functioning Nameless Order for the apostates who want to swap rotes but otherwise be left alone. The various sub-Consilia are working on Mysteries of their own, but the big one is that Manhattan is so charged with ley energies its evolving into something. Whole city blocks move, sliding around, but the changes are subject to Quiescence so only the Awakened and Sleepwalkers are aware of it.<br /> <br /> After 9/11, Manhattan became an unexploded bomb. The Seers and Pentacle worked out a short-lived truce to deal with it, but the Seers screwed the Pentacle mages (including the Consilium's arch-Hierarch) over and somehow took control of Manhattan's Mystery. Now the island itself is hostile to Pentacle mages trying to set up shop there, so the Consilium keeps to the other Boroughs and the wider New York / New Jersey states, with some cabals raiding into Manhattan to try to figure out what's going on or recover lost treasures. The locals call what happened &quot;The Folly&quot;.<br /> <br /> Awakening second ed's chapter fiction is set in New York. It will get its proper writeup in Tome of the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Other random facts:<br /> <br /> There's a Free Council cabal of punk musicians called &quot;Join The Seers.&quot;<br /> The new arch-Hierarch is a thearch named Sheshat<br /> The Interfector is called Outis, and his schtick is he accidentally prevented his own birth during a disastrous time-travel jaunt when an apprentice.<br /> Various of the Brooklyn-Queens Silver Ladder Caucus have appeared in the Fallen World Anthology and M2e</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we have a teeny nugget to wildly speculate on regarding the local Nameless Order? It's really exciting to see one take a major role in a canon setting for once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:10:05-07:00","id":970201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New York is the setting for Travis Stout's own Mage chronicle, and we've been dropping references to it since Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> It is the largest Consilium in the Western world, maybe in the whole world; its territory covers half of New Jersey, the Boroughs of New York City itself and all of Long Island. It has eleven Pentacle Order Caucuses (each Order has at least one full Caucus, most two, some three) and a functioning Nameless Order for the apostates who want to swap rotes but otherwise be left alone. The various sub-Consilia are working on Mysteries of their own, but the big one is that Manhattan is so charged with ley energies its evolving into something. Whole city blocks move, sliding around, but the changes are subject to Quiescence so only the Awakened and Sleepwalkers are aware of it.<br /> <br /> After 9/11, Manhattan became an unexploded bomb. The Seers and Pentacle worked out a short-lived truce to deal with it, but the Seers screwed the Pentacle mages (including the Consilium's arch-Hierarch) over and somehow took control of Manhattan's Mystery. Now the island itself is hostile to Pentacle mages trying to set up shop there, so the Consilium keeps to the other Boroughs and the wider New York / New Jersey states, with some cabals raiding into Manhattan to try to figure out what's going on or recover lost treasures. The locals call what happened &quot;The Folly&quot;.<br /> <br /> Awakening second ed's chapter fiction is set in New York. It will get its proper writeup in Tome of the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Other random facts:<br /> <br /> There's a Free Council cabal of punk musicians called &quot;Join The Seers.&quot;<br /> The new arch-Hierarch is a thearch named Sheshat<br /> The Interfector is called Outis, and his schtick is he accidentally prevented his own birth during a disastrous time-travel jaunt when an apprentice.<br /> Various of the Brooklyn-Queens Silver Ladder Caucus have appeared in the Fallen World Anthology and M2e</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Tome of the Pentacle, will you reveal the secrets behind the Manhattan Mystery and how the Seers took control of it?<br /> <br /> Does the New York Consilium include the whole Hudson Valley, including the suburbs of counties like Rockland and Westchester in NY north of NYC, with their sizable populations? <br /> <br /> And lastly, a request. Any chance either Khonsu or Hal from <i>Premeditation</i> might make an appearance in TotP?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:51:40-07:00","id":970248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> Thank you. Definitely something to look forward to when Tome of the Pentacle comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:54:08-07:00","id":970310,"title":"","content":"Consilia are still, by default, about the size of a city or so in populated areas, right? I somehow got it stuck in my head that like Caucuses, Consilia are bigger but now I'm not sure where I got that idea and I'm trying to figure that out before I start dividing my state up into Consilia, Caucuses &amp; Assemblies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:19:36-07:00","id":970326,"title":"","content":"Yes, by default they're a single city, and a Order Caucus will stretch over multiple Consilia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:37:35-07:00","id":970587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970326#post970326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, by default they're a single city, and a Order Caucus will stretch over multiple Consilia.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=874334#post874334\">my unofficial 2E take on Boston setting</a> I made Boston proper Consilium, but whole Massachusets ( and parts of New England ) terrain of Orders Caucuses. Silver Ladder have something very different than rest of Orders.<br /> <br /> Tearchs of New England are both divided and united \u2013 they started as network of Favors leading to <i>Chariot of Epona</i> cabal in beginning of European colonization. With each Favor the Nameless mages of region took, each come closer to Star Precept and many finally embraced traditions of Silver Ladder and Greco-Celtic mysticism of Epona Awakened. Still, new converts stayed very independent in their ways, leading to tradition of local Tearchs to be very separated from Order. This resulted in the unorthodox way the Magisterium works \u2013 organization is splinted in to regions ruled by one Grand Magister each - Vermont, New Hampshire, and Maine under one. Connecticut and Rhode Island in to second. And Massachusetts as last one. They are filled with local Magisters, but they have lower standing in Order as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:24:34-07:00","id":970619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=969861#post969861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Safe Place merit grant withstand rating if combined with Sanctum? Do you have any magical bariers build in or is Sanctum just for granting additional spell slots?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really, really sorry for double posting this one. I can rule that half of dots rounded up spend on sanctum counts as withstand rating but I'm curious if any one put more thought on this. <br /> You can put a prime spell on it but it would still take spell slot if you are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:21:30-07:00","id":970646,"title":"","content":"If it does it would only add +1 as an additional source of Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:21:37-07:00","id":970647,"title":"","content":"There's nothing I've found that indicates that Safe Place (a Mundane merit, not a magic one) provides Withstand.<br /> <br /> That said, there's no qualifiers on the penalty to breaching. RAW is that it would also provide a penalty to magical attempts to breach the Safe Place, even if that might not be RAI.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm missing something obvious, but I've checked everywhere I can think.<br /> <br /> Edit: You can also Relinquish the aforementioned Prime spell if you want to ward the place. It won't take a slot then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:47:25-07:00","id":970653,"title":"","content":"It would add +1 to e.g. attacks based on sympathy, yes. But breaching magicaly when e.g. targeting door would suffer full withstand from merit.<br /> <br /> So Sanctum merit just grants you a space to work more safe magic but only when you are there. <br /> I remember that in 1e it granted some protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:09:52-07:00","id":970667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970326#post970326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, by default they're a single city, and a Order Caucus will stretch over multiple Consilia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, since you offered a &quot;fully stocked Consilium&quot; outline, do you have one for a Caucus too? I'm curious what a typical one would be like. I recall mentions in the past that, say, a Mysterium Caucus might cover two or three Consilia and have as many athenaeums, etc., but I'm curious how big and active the membership of a Caucus is assumed to typically be.<br /> <br /> Not even hard numbers, necessarily, but a general sensation of how often a Mage might interact with their Caucus, how crowded it should feel at a given rank, etc. Does a Caucus end up feeling like a second Consilium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:13:55-07:00","id":970670,"title":"","content":"1) a) To cast a given spell, does a mage need to have dots in a relevant Arcanum equal to that spell's level, or can an apprentice try their hand at casting Making and Unmaking spells if they want?<br /> <br /> If the answer to the above is &quot;yes, the apprentice can try casting 5-dot spells&quot;...<br /> <br /> b) ...is there any mechanical difference between that apprentice, with 1 dot in the Arcanum, trying to cast a 2-dot spell vs a 5-dot spell?<br /> c) ...can one attempt a spell from an Arcanum in which one has no dots at all?<br /> <br /> 2) Am I correct in thinking that the damage inflicted by an attack spell, and the ability of a Withstood spell to overcome Resolve/Composure/Stamina/Sympathetic connections, is entirely set at casting by the Potency that the caster chooses? And cannot afterwards be changed, except by an exceptional success used increase a spell factor? So if you underestimate the resistance or overestimate the strength of a sympathetic connection, and don't pick a high enough Potency, you're just out of luck?<br /> <br /> 3) When you take Mystery Cult Initiation (or gain it from Mystery CultInfluence), am I correct in thinking that you get all the benefits for dot levels equal to or less than you posses? E.g. if you have four dots in Mystery Cult Initiation, you get a three-dot Merit, <i>and</i> a two-dot Merit or a skill, <i>and</i> a one-dot Merit, <i>and </i>a Skill Specialty or one-dot Merit pertaining to initiation?<br /> <br /> 4) When and where are we going to see more Legacy writeups? They were one of my favourite elements of 1e Mage, and I really like the new format for them, but alas, the new setup makes it difficult to translate them directly from 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:19:19-07:00","id":970673,"title":"","content":"1) You need Arcanum 5 to cast Making spells.<br /> <br /> 2) Correct.<br /> <br /> 3) Correct. Also, consider the unwritten disadvantage of Mystery Cult Initiation: you belong to a friggin' cult.<br /> <br /> 4) Soon\u2122. YMMV on that last bit, I personally find it easy to create new / update Legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:48:43-07:00","id":970689,"title":"","content":"Is there any reason that every single spell in the Spirit Arcanum that targets spirits couldn't be transplanted wholecloth into Mind and used to effect/shape/channel stuff from/etc Goetia instead? <br /> <br /> Mind covers Goetia entirely, but there aren't a lot of spells governing boosting/altering them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:04:19-07:00","id":970699,"title":"","content":"That's because it'd be pointless to waste word count on essentially duplicate spells, but yes, Mind can do to goetia what Spirit does to spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:05:10-07:00","id":970701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970689#post970689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reason that every single spell in the Spirit Arcanum that targets spirits couldn't be transplanted wholecloth into Mind and used to effect/shape/channel stuff from/etc Goetia instead?<br /> <br /> Mind covers Goetia entirely, but there aren't a lot of spells governing boosting/altering them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume that the relevant Practice effects for Spirit and Mind concerning spirits and goetia, respectively, would be similar, if not identical (as would Death Practices for ghosts).<br /> <br /> Remember that the included spells are only examples of effects, not limits of what can be creatively achieved. Given that goetia are less prevalent for most mages than far more ubiquitous spirits, it's not surprising that the sample spells for Mind generally focused on other effects.<br /> <br /> However, you question does highlight the need for a Mage FAQ. Hopefully, Dave will have some time between real life and developing Deviant and other writing projects to soon finish the FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:28:28-07:00","id":970745,"title":"","content":"Actually, a lot of Spirit spells have options for affecting goetia by adding Mind. It seems like you need both to fully manipulate goetia, not Mind alone. Even the Mind spells require Spirit added in to handle goetia outside of the Astral (such as granting Materialized with Goetic Summons).<br /> <br /> Probably because Goetia don't naturally exist outside the Astral, so you need Spirit to interface them with Twilight and the like.<br /> <br /> Channel Essence was one of the examples in your post. It explicitly requires both Spirit and Mind for Goetia, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:48:36-07:00","id":970809,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and more than a few of the &quot;Add X arcana&quot; don't make sense. Channel Essence also requires Death 2 to affect ghosts, which seems counterintuitive to your Twilight interface assumption. Also the spell makes no differentiation for goetia found in the Astral, so the Twilight angle makes no sense. Maybe it makes sense if what fuels goetia and ghosts is different than what fuels spirits, and the spell draws off and converts those individual fuel sources, but a) That would be Patterning, and b) Essence seems to be the catch all fuel source name.<br /> <br /> Every spell with the &quot;Add arcana X&quot; frankly annoys me, it sets this undefined precedent and doesn't match up with the rules for conjunctional spells which say that the primary and secondary arcana have to be at the same level. At least that's what Dave said would be the rule, but since we don't actually have rules on conjunctional spells, and Dave said the core has no examples of conjunctional spells (But maybe that's what those are?) I find the whole thing unnecessarily confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:57:08-07:00","id":970812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970809#post970809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and more than a few of the &quot;Add X arcana&quot; don't make sense. Channel Essence also requires Death 2 to affect ghosts, which seems counterintuitive to your Twilight interface assumption. Also the spell makes no differentiation for goetia found in the Astral, so the Twilight angle makes no sense. Maybe it makes sense if what fuels goetia and ghosts is different than what fuels spirits, and the spell draws off and converts those individual fuel sources, but a) That would be Patterning, and b) Essence seems to be the catch all fuel source name.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Essence is the catch all fuel source, it is a Spirit 'thing,' and it's creation wouldn't make sense in Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:16:29-07:00","id":970823,"title":"","content":"Doesn't clarify the problem, and it doesn't help with a solution to it either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-16-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:08:14-07:00","id":970863,"title":"","content":"Essence is literally listed under the &quot;Purview&quot; for Spirit. There's really no inconsistency there.<br /> <br /> It's the other ones like granting the Materialized condition that are weird.<br /> <br /> Now another question:<br /> <br /> Say you cast an Indefinite spell that grants a Boon to everyone within a building. Or damage. Or healing. Whatever, it's an example.<br /> <br /> Say everyone in the building leaves and a new set of people arrives before the next Ritual Interval.<br /> <br /> Does the refreshing of the boon happen to the original set of people even though they left the house (meaning that Scale only determines who is originally hit with the spell), or does the refreshing of the boon happen to the new set of people within the house (meaning that Scale determines the area of the ongoing effects, and the targets change as the people within the area changes)?<br /> <br /> I assumed it was the latter, but I've seen a few posts on this forum that indicate it might be the former. The book is unclear. If it's the latter, can it be centered on a moving object (like a train or a person), or does it have to be anchored in a place that doesn't move, like a spot on the ground?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:55:11-07:00","id":970897,"title":"","content":"The fact that Essence falls under Spirit is literally not the thing I'm talking about, I have no idea why you aren't comprehending that. Eh, whatever, no one knows.<br /> <br /> Boons don't refresh, they just last as long as their Duration allows with as many uses as their Potency grants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:13:55-07:00","id":970964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970809#post970809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Channel Essence also requires Death 2 to affect ghosts, which seems counterintuitive to your Twilight interface assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of this post was about Channel Essence. Channel Essence requires Spirit because Essence is under the purview of Spirit. It requires Death 2 to give to Ghosts because Ghosts are under the purview of Death. It's that simple.<br /> <br /> Also instant spells cast with long durations refresh themselves every [ritual interval based on gnosis]. Pedantry like this is why I also listed damage and healing as examples. Either way it doesn't answer the question, which was about Scale and Area of Effect. Your dismissive non-answers to my questions are really starting to rub me the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:42:31-07:00","id":971062,"title":"","content":"I'm not giving you dismissive non-answers. Anyways, alright, so adding Death or MInd 2 allows you to channel Essence (For spirits) from Ghosts of Goetia. That would make sense. My default assumption was that it channeled whatever energy fuels Ghosts or Goetia from them and was requiring Spirit erroneously. This might change my assumption that there are some spells which seem to require &quot;Add X arcana&quot; erroneously. I'll have to look them over again.<br /> <br /> All of the Boons and Hexes in their text explicitly say that they grant such and such an effect equal to Potency or a number of times per Potency for the Duration of the spell. This implies that spells that grant Boons and Hexes aren't &quot;instant&quot;, and that would mean that they do not auto-recast when their Duration is up. Many Fate spells run on this dynamic, requiring dice penalties to be sunk into Duration and Potency in order to be effective and basically nullifying the auto-recast. Since your example didn't fit with your question I was pointing out the error. Granted, I fixated on the one example.<br /> <br /> So, on to your actual question, if your spell is cast in an area and it will recast itself every Gnosis Ritual Interval (GRI) then it will affect the individuals present in the area at the time of the casting since the actual target is the area not the persons that were originally affected when the spell was cast, unless you were using Scale to increase the number of individual targets of the spell and not the area of the spell. Seems pretty cut and dry to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:56:57-07:00","id":972015,"title":"","content":"Is there a quick list or anything of cabals in the various books? Trying to just pull some useful ones for a game I'll be starting soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:06:45-07:00","id":972058,"title":"","content":"Not that I can think of, but if you're looking for premade characters, any of the Order books will have lots of easily usable content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:15:59-07:00","id":972063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=972015#post972015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a quick list or anything of cabals in the various books? Trying to just pull some useful ones for a game I'll be starting soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Chicago </a>and <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Boston_Unveiled\" target=\"_blank\">Boston </a>books have fully made cabals with stats, information about the cabal as a whole and their relationships with others. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_The_Unbidden\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors</a> has a Left-Hand Path cabal, the Golden Quorum. There's also a <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/63046\" target=\"_blank\">Ready Made Mage Characters pdf</a> available on DriveThru RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:10:37-07:00","id":972562,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I don't know if this has been asked before (it's a long thread), but I've been trying to wrap my head around the spellcasting system, and one doubt still lingers:<br /> <br /> On the sidebar of Common Reach Effects (pages 112 and again in 326) it says, &quot;If at sensory range, allow the Mage to cast on a subject she is viewing remotely.&quot; However, in the description of the Sympathetic Range Attainment (page 193) there's no mention of any Reach needed, only that in order to cast the spell the mage has to cast at sensory range, have a Sympathetic connection and a Sympathetic yantra, and pay 1 Mana.<br /> <br /> <i>So, is an extra Reach needed for casting sympathetically (at least 1 Reach is already needed for Sensory casting)?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 09-19-2016, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:34:13-07:00","id":972574,"title":"","content":"No, it's an extra Reach to cast via Remote Viewing. One Reach to move the spell to Sensory Range (Which you also need to do to cast Sympathetic spells), and then one more Reach to cast via Remote Viewing (A Sympathetic spell requires a mana and a Sympathetic Yantra instead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:11:18-07:00","id":972584,"title":"","content":"I'm still confused, then. What is the difference between Sympathetic casting and casting through remote viewing? I could use an example, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:19:35-07:00","id":972586,"title":"","content":"I think that casting sympathetically works just as you described, using one reach to bring you to sensory range.<br /> <br /> The way I understand casting remotely is this : Say you scry on someone else [A] (probably via a sympathetic link) and he walks up to another person [B], to which you have no sympathy. You now want to cast a spell on the person [B]. You don't have a sympathethic link, so you can't cast sympathetically. You can however still cast a spell through your scrying window. To do so you need to cast a spell on a subject you are viewing remotely. To do so you need to expend two reaches, one to bring it to sensory range and then another to cast on a subject you are viewing remotely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:25:33-07:00","id":972589,"title":"","content":"It's basically two sets of requirements for doing the same thing so that you can do one or the other depending on convenience.<br /> <br /> So, if you're watching a live feed and want to hit that annoying news person with a lightning bolt you spend 1 Reach to achieve Sensory (Because obviously you can't touch him, or throw a spell at him that can hit him) and then you spend another Reach to use Remote Casting. Then you finish setting up your lightning bolt and let it fly.<br /> <br /> Another way is you've tracked this news person down to his home, snapped a few covert photos of him or broken into his house and stolen the stub of the first paycheck he ever got doing the news or obtained something else that could be used to symbolize him. You've either built up Sympathy to him or Borrowed the Threads of it from your symbol of him. Now you can hit him with a lightning bolt wherever he is whether you can see him or not. You're on vacation in Malay and want to lightning bolt him at his desk at home. So you spend a Reach for Sensory Range (Same reason as for Remote Casting) and then spend 1 mana to activate the Sympathy Casting attainment and use the symbolic object or photo or whatever that you have to represent him as a Yantra in your spell, set the spell up and boom, lightning bolt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:35:36-07:00","id":972594,"title":"","content":"You have a voodoo doll. You make the doll look like Bob. You want to make Bob explode. You want to make Bob explode without leaving your room while Bob is on the other side of town. You use the doll that looks like Bob to cast a spell at him when he's far away and you can't see him. This is Sympathetic casting. Instead of the doll you could use a piece of Bob's hair or Bob's sympathetic name or any other Sympathetic Yantra.<br /> <br /> You are looking at someone who isn't here. You do this with a scrying spell or live video feeds or using your Familiar's senses. This is Remote Viewing. You want to cast a spell on them. You can see them, but they are not physically here. You must cast via Remote Viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:40:45-07:00","id":972654,"title":"","content":"Can nimbus affect mechanicly the person it belongs to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:42:17-07:00","id":972656,"title":"","content":"That seems to be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:50:38-07:00","id":972660,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't see why it couldn't, but the book mentions comparing the Resolve of witnesses, which usually means spectators, not the actor themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:55:04-07:00","id":972665,"title":"","content":"What do you think about +1 to perpetrators attribute and -1 to spectators attribute? Is it to much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:47:11-07:00","id":972696,"title":"","content":"I think it's not that helpful, to be honest; games are assumed to be group affairs, and it means that groups of Mages basically weaken their allies by casting spells in their vicinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:53:56-07:00","id":972790,"title":"","content":"I am actually starting a Mage game.<br /> <br /> One of the things that's always piqued my curiosity is the concepts of libraries. And using said libraries to learn or research spells. Awakened magic has always seemed sort of sandboxy to me, but having read a bit more I think I got it. <br /> <br /> When it refers to a mage researching a spell in a book, it's basically the same as when a person on the forum asks how to do a certain thing. The mage is looking for information to explain what Practices and Arcana would be involved in such a spell, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:42:31-07:00","id":972822,"title":"","content":"Or he's looking through an aethenaeum or lore house for a grimoire with the particular spell he wants to cast. Since a grimoire can teach you the Rote and give you the rote quality on your roll when casting it's a fairly potent resource.<br /> <br /> I think Mages sort of inherently know the kinds of things their arcana can do, but a library would be a useful resource for digging up less obvious applications as well. So in that sense, yeah, like this forum. Practices are learned instead of instinctual as they're a byproduct or direct result of Mages trying to teach other Mages, so a library could certainly be useful for looking into what arcana might be able to achieve via which Practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:03:39-07:00","id":972850,"title":"","content":"Also, Mages don't inherently know High Speech (after all, most of it is lost). So it's possible that when your Mage is reading up in the library, he's looking up ideas for words or runes that can help him cast the spell. I assume this is a lot of what Mages get up to in their downtime and that's why they have unrestricted access to the High Speech and Runic Casting Yantras during play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:28:02-07:00","id":972862,"title":"","content":"Actually, Mages do inherently know High Speech, that was changed from 1e. Though I suppose it's might be more understanding of it than the ability to speak or write it. What the Orders provide is training to use it in the spoken word or in runes as part of casting a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:31:55-07:00","id":972865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=972850#post972850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Mages don't inherently know High Speech (after all, most of it is lost). So it's possible that when your Mage is reading up in the library, he's looking up ideas for words or runes that can help him cast the spell. I assume this is a lot of what Mages get up to in their downtime and that's why they have unrestricted access to the High Speech and Runic Casting Yantras during play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All mages know High Speech. Their peripheral mage sight acts as a translator.<br /> <br /> Mages need to be trained in order to incorporate High Speech into spellcasting for use as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:03:31-07:00","id":972876,"title":"","content":"Speaking of High Speech, I recall it being said for 1e that High Speech was mostly a language of magical jargon, and as such couldn't really be used effectively as an actual language. Has that changed at all in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:34:08-07:00","id":972886,"title":"","content":"Not really, but not because it's magical jargon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the instant of Awakening, all mages can comprehend<br /> High Speech, the Supernal symbol of \u201clanguage\u201d that serves as<br /> the platonic ur-tongue. The Orders all teach their students to<br /> use High Speech as a Yantra in Spellcasting (the High Speech<br /> Merit, p. 102) but it is useable in spoken and written form as<br /> a crude form of communication. Because it\u2019s more the symbol<br /> of a language than a real language, though, High Speech has<br /> some restrictions \u2014 it is very good at communicating facts, but<br /> can\u2019t be used to deliberately lie (it\u2019s possible to be mistaken).<br /> It also contains no metaphors or symbols, as it is its own Supernal<br /> concept. High Speech may be used for Persuasion and<br /> Intimidation rolls, but reduces all Expression and Subterfuge<br /> rolls to chance dice. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T03:34:25-07:00","id":973021,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a>, thank you! I had somehow conflated both methods of casting into one. Now, it seems the magic systems in 2nd Ed have more wrinkles than I had thought. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:18:28-07:00","id":973249,"title":"","content":"Quick question: Say that I want to take control of a zippo flame as per Influence Fire for three turns. The goal is to make the mote of flame travel around, but it will eventually leave my Touch Range. Do I need just 1 Reach for the Instant Casting, or do I need an extra Reach for Sensory Range, even though I'm touching the flame on the turn the Spell was cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:30:32-07:00","id":973254,"title":"","content":"Nah, you're touching it when you cast the spell, so it's under your control even after you let go of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:23:17-07:00","id":973801,"title":"","content":"How do sympathetic Yantras work with multi-target spells?<br /> <br /> I'm casting Telepathy on Jill and Jess. <br /> <br /> A) Does it not work at all?<br /> B) Can I use strands of their hair, each taking a yantra slot, for a +4 bonus from material sympathy?<br /> C) Can I intertwine the strands, using it as only a single yantra that still gives the +2 bonus?<br /> D) Can I choose freely between options B and C?<br /> E) If I can only get Jill's hair, can I still use the Yantra despite not having representations of <i>each</i> subject, just one?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:41:42-07:00","id":973816,"title":"","content":"Material Sympathy only gives a bonus on spells not cast at non-Sympathetic range, not sure if that pertains to the question. I'd rule you only get the +2, and only if you had the material from each target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:59:55-07:00","id":973854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=973816#post973816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Material Sympathy only gives a bonus on spells not cast at non-Sympathetic range, not sure if that pertains to the question. I'd rule you only get the +2, and only if you had the material from each target.</div> </div> </div> </div>This hypothetical is non-sympathetic range.<br /> <br /> Would you require two yantra slots to benefit from that +2 bonus? Or just one, despite using two 'items'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:03:13-07:00","id":973855,"title":"","content":"I'd require 2 I think, same reason an AA can't double down on bonuses when using a dedicated tool that's also a weapon without using more Yantra slots. Well, not quite the same, but it's a similar philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:19:03-07:00","id":974300,"title":"","content":"A question about AMS and counterspelling.<br /> Which one do you need to see? Casters nimbus, caster, target of the spell or just be in the vincinity without actually seeing anything beside the &quot;spellwave&quot;? E.g you stand on one side of the wall and the caster on the other. Can you counter or just feel the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:35:09-07:00","id":974304,"title":"","content":"&quot;the countering mage must see her rival casting in Active Mage Sight.&quot; 2ed p192. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T04:41:58-07:00","id":974333,"title":"","content":"How could I miss it? Thanks!<br /> Sooo Imago is clearly visible under the AMS. Is it in, umm, brain or in the nimbus?<br /> <br /> Display of Power makes <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagos formed by mages within the<br /> spell\u2019s effect become visible in the Supernal World to all forms<br /> of Active Mage Sight </div> </div> </div>and if I'm reading it right it means that only the AMS of the same arcanum as the cast spell is able to see Imago natively. Rest of AMS just sees the effect.<br /> Or maybe without Display of Power counterspelling doesn't involve rivals Imago at all?<br /> What do the mage counter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:06:07-07:00","id":974342,"title":"","content":"I think it's only the nimbus that flares and is visible in AMS. The counterspelling mage knows it is a spell being cast if he uses AMS, and with the right arcana used with AMS in what arcanum being used and if capable can counter it. I don't think AMS can show what kind of spell being cast or more precisely what spell or even practice being in use. If you want to be able to perceive your enemies imago (or your own) you need Display of Power. As i understand it, Display of Power , gives form in High Speech glyphs to the imagos being imagined by mages inside the area of effect. To see these glyphs you need active mage sight but they show up in all arcana.<br /> I guess that those glyphs from Display of Power that mages got their practice and arcana symbols/glyphs from. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:46:35-07:00","id":974351,"title":"","content":"Mages get the glyphs (well, kinda, it's in the same way that we get the letter A from a cow's head) from what Mana looks like when you spend it during Scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:01:54-07:00","id":974358,"title":"","content":"gies if this has already been asked....<br /> <br /> My group has recently started using the Duel Arcane (aren't politics fun), and we have a few confusions:<br /> <br /> 1) does failing to open a Door with an Arcanum mean that you can't use that Arcanum for the rest of the Duel, or for the current Door?<br /> <br /> 2) This is more of a comment. We found that rolling for Initiative for every round shakes the Duel up a bit every round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:24:24-07:00","id":974365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=974351#post974351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages get the glyphs (well, kinda, it's in the same way that we get the letter A from a cow's head) from what Mana looks like when you spend it during Scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So these glyphs gained from spending mana while using Scrutiny as per page 93 is the glyphs that mages use to talk about the Arcana? Is that the glyphs being used as background art in the spell pages 128-191 ? Like the glyph for Time kinda looks like a Y and Prime kinda looks like a T? <br /> <br /> What about Practices and different parts of magic, like attainment, does those have similair glyphs made up from mana or?<br /> <br /> And more important, if you only get the glyphs from scrutinizing mana realeased into the fallen world as per page 92-93, what does the spell Display of Power show with it's &quot;magical runes&quot; and &quot;symbols&quot; flashing around the mages that use an imago. How does those things look?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:58:10-07:00","id":974443,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar417_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"417\" data-vbnamecard=\"417\">the_duck</a><br /> 1) I would rule that it is only for current door but if you wish more dramatic and unforgiving take on a Duel you could make it that Arcanum is locked for the rest of the duel. Maybe a Dramatic Failure effect?<br /> 2) Thats a great way of ST any conflict scene if you and your players are willing to sacrifice some some game time for rolling and noting it down every round.<br /> <br /> I think that using Prime AMS would be able to discern practice of any arcana. And back to the case. If the spell being cast can be read from nimbus does that mean that supressing nimbus(or casting from Twilight/anything that veils your nimbus) would make you uncounterable?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 09-22-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:30:53-07:00","id":974466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Active Mage Sight of any Arcanum also reveals all Awakened<br /> spells as they are being cast. The mage can see another will-<br /> worker\u2019s Nimbus flare as he forms the Imago and casts the spell<br /> (which, in turn, gives the observant mage a chance to use the<br /> Counterspell Attainment if she knows the Arcanum involved). </div> </div> </div>This would suggest that <i>any </i>AMS can see spells being cast, and that it is tied to the Nimbus. By that reading, Cloak Nimbus would require a Clash of Wills before you could counterspell anything under its protection.<br /> <br /> Which leads to some lingering CoWs questions I've had:<br /> <br /> What pool would you use for AMS against Cloak Nimbus? I don't imagine it's going to be the Arcana used for AMS, because you'll almost always be using more than one. Prime or the primary Arcana of the spell being cast? What if the Mage doesn't have that Arcana at all?<br /> <br /> What do Ephemera use for CoW? Annihilate Spirit lists Power + Finesse, but that's a ridiculously potent CoW considering that Spirits hit 5s in those stats a lot easier than other things, and Rank is their Supernatural Tolerance stat like Gnosis for Mages. It also contradicts Werewolf. Let's use the various [Ephemera] Shield spells as an example there, since they work against both Numina and physical attacks. Command Spirit is another good one, since they have no resisting power in the first place in such a situation.<br /> <br /> Then there is Body Autonomy. As written, it can protect against an attack (the other options specify Supernatural, this one does not) that inflicts a Personal Tilt with a Clash of Wills. This could mean entering a Clash of Wills with Sleepers and other non-Supernatural sources. How is this handled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:45:21-07:00","id":974704,"title":"","content":"Alright, I got Left-Hand Path. And DriveThruRPG is apparently operated by someone who seems to check out oddities.<br /> <br /> House Tremere absorbs other Reaper legacies into sub-Houses. The Tremere Legacies and Houses mentioned seem more straightforward reapers, but would the Cloud Infinite and [Legion] also be edible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:03:43-07:00","id":974717,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they would, so would the SL reaper legacy the Carnival Melancholy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:32:40-07:00","id":974955,"title":"","content":"Who are Nemeans? Or where I can find more information?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:38:45-07:00","id":974956,"title":"","content":"?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Nemean&quot; (named after the Greek myth of the Nemean Lion) is the Thyrsus signature character, if that's what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T04:08:10-07:00","id":974978,"title":"","content":"Aw, sorry. I've googled it up before and figured out what its named after but thought that its some kind of legacy and The Nemean from FWCA was one of them. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T04:15:19-07:00","id":974981,"title":"","content":"What do you need to spot an awakened mage (without any active spell) ? Is prime or any AMS enough (seems like other supernaturals like vampire can be spotted with death AMS) or do you need to cast knowing/unveiling spells on the area to find out ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12418-ponobo","name":"ponobo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:15:01-07:00","id":975193,"title":"","content":"Mage sight won't tell you if someone is awakened. You need either: a way to see their Soul (death), or use prime 1 Supernal vision (spell). There are some other more indirect methods: you can scan their mind for instance (Mind 1 Mental scan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:53:21-07:00","id":975221,"title":"","content":"Death Sight says that you can see if someone has a soul, I'm not sure you can see the soul itself otherwise it would be phrased more simply (like, you can see the soul of people) and Death Sight would then allow to spot most supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm okay with being able to spot mages only with spells. It makes looking for seers/banishers/reapers far more tense because they'll know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12418-ponobo","user":"ponobo","date":". 09-23-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12418-ponobo","name":"ponobo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:06:03-07:00","id":975225,"title":"","content":"Where can I find out about Goetic mages, I guess the term is? I recall in first edition there were mages who would summon reflections of parts of themselves, like their lust or greed.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for whatever book would tell me why this was done, and go further into detail about how, perhaps with some benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2016, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T12:12:36-07:00","id":975639,"title":"","content":"Summoners has the most recent info on goetia from 1e, but Goetic Summons is a 3 dot spell in 2e and goetia are in the ephemeral entities section of the book, and there's also a brief discussion about the Astral. The Astral also has information on Goetia. Benefits: You have a goetic servant, Negatives: If you pulled it out of a person they can no longer feel or be affected by the thing you pulled out, so if you pull out their Lust they no longer feel lust.<br /> <br /> I have a question, I'm planning to use the Chupacabra from Summoners in a session next week. I glanced it over and am wondering if I really need to change anything to use it in 2e. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:02:41-07:00","id":975663,"title":"","content":"Seems like no one asked before, so I'm asking now. Can a Mage have more than one Familiar at a time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:14:17-07:00","id":975673,"title":"","content":"In 1e the answer is no (Sort of), in 2e yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:24:39-07:00","id":975678,"title":"","content":"Currently got a Thyrsus with five. Nothing in the rules says just one. That said, keeping a stable of spirits fed and happy is an extreme effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T05:29:55-07:00","id":975916,"title":"","content":"Do mages gain a Beat for having their rightmost health box filled with damage? If so, does it need to be lethal, like vampires/werewolves, or bashing, like mortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T07:10:51-07:00","id":975934,"title":"","content":"They do and bashing would be enough.<br /> <br /> Q: Why is Death adept able to change into shadow but Matter adept cant change into stone without Life arcanum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:22:54-07:00","id":975949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=975934#post975934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do and bashing would be enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Source please?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:58:14-07:00","id":975963,"title":"","content":"p.79 in M:tA 2e rulebook<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Mage: The Awakening, mages are essentially human,<br /> with one major difference; they can choose to wield magic.<br /> The following rules show how to create your Mage characters,<br /> and some of the few differences between mages and Sleepers. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:18:39-07:00","id":976042,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but nothing in that statement says anything about mages getting Beats when their last health box is filled with damage. Humans get it, but every other way for humans to get beats are in the rules about mages as well, except the damage thing. That way of getting beats is absent from mages. The other ways are normal for all game lines, however the damage thing is different between them. As said, there is nothing that says mages should get beats from damage like normal mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:12:13-07:00","id":976064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976042#post976042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but nothing in that statement says anything about mages getting Beats when their last health box is filled with damage. Humans get it, but every other way for humans to get beats are in the rules about mages as well, except the damage thing. That way of getting beats is absent from mages. The other ways are normal for all game lines, however the damage thing is different between them. As said, there is nothing that says mages should get beats from damage like normal mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was so, then Mages can't take beats from Persistent Conditions since they cannot be &quot;solved&quot;, but do award beats when something happens. Also, damage awarding beats is pretty consistent throughout the game lines. All game lines have the exact same 6 categories that award beats (except for Mage and the taking lethal one):<br /> - Fulfilling an Aspiration or making headway towards one;<br /> - Resolving a Condition;<br /> - Persistent Conditions when they negatively affect you;<br /> - Turning a failure into a dramatic failure;<br /> - Taking lethal damage on one of your last health boxes;<br /> - At the end of a session;<br /> But, since you can include &quot;taking damage on the last health boxes&quot; and negative impact from Persistent Conditions as fulfilling the &quot;Any major dramatic event the Storyteller deems appropriate can award a Beat.&quot; condition, it can be included in the list from Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:22:39-07:00","id":976069,"title":"","content":"Can Imbued Items cast spells enhanced by Attainments? For example, could I make an item Imbued with Hung Spell with a Conditional Duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:41:57-07:00","id":976076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976064#post976064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that was so, then Mages can't take beats from Persistent Conditions since they cannot be &quot;solved&quot;, but do award beats when something happens. Also, damage awarding beats is pretty consistent throughout the game lines. All game lines have the exact same 6 categories that award beats (except for Mage and the taking lethal one):<br /> - Fulfilling an Aspiration or making headway towards one;<br /> - Resolving a Condition;<br /> - Persistent Conditions when they negatively affect you;<br /> - Turning a failure into a dramatic failure;<br /> - Taking lethal damage on one of your last health boxes;<br /> - At the end of a session;<br /> But, since you can include &quot;taking damage on the last health boxes&quot; and negative impact from Persistent Conditions as fulfilling the &quot;Any major dramatic event the Storyteller deems appropriate can award a Beat.&quot; condition, it can be included in the list from Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually again, not true. Persistent Conditions give beats to mages. P.230 M:tAW 2ed. <br /> But yeah i do think it's a typo that mages don't get beats when they got damage in their last health boxes. However it seems weird that they would just forget to copy-paste the ways to get beats.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:43:42-07:00","id":976077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976069#post976069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Imbued Items cast spells enhanced by Attainments? For example, could I make an item Imbued with Hung Spell with a Conditional Duration?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They can be if the attainment changes the spell in some way. So Conditional Duration is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:06:43-07:00","id":976085,"title":"","content":"Are mages really able to switch out their Aspirations after the Scene instead of after the Chapter/session like very one else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:23:40-07:00","id":976184,"title":"","content":"I imagine that's a typo.<br /> <br /> When you include a secondary arcanum/arcana for casting a spell, does it cost Mana if it's not primary?<br /> <br /> Say, for example, a Thyrsus casts a Life 2 Veiling spell to transform their appearance. If they added Matter 2, so that their clothing was likewise changed to match this new appearance, does that cost Mana or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:12:34-07:00","id":976402,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the primary arcanum is what determines if it uses mana.<br /> The conjunction just adds to the spell.<br /> Tough though when deciding if something is a conjunctional or a combined effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've got a question about the three-favors rule for getting your soul stone back.<br /> Do you have to do it for sleepers or just for other mages?<br /> Cause it might be interesting to find a mage's stone as a sleeper,<br /> then all you've gotta do is rub the lamp and make a wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:34:26-07:00","id":976410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976402#post976402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that the primary arcanum is what determines if it uses mana.<br /> The conjunction just adds to the spell.<br /> Tough though when deciding if something is a conjunctional or a combined effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've got a question about the three-favors rule for getting your soul stone back.<br /> Do you have to do it for sleepers or just for other mages?<br /> Cause it might be interesting to find a mage's stone as a sleeper,<br /> then all you've gotta do is rub the lamp and make a wish.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does the rule get enforced is a good follow-up question. Can a Sleeper, with no capacity to do anything at all to the Soul Stone, really get those three favours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:51:16-07:00","id":976413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976410#post976410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the rule get enforced is a good follow-up question. Can a Sleeper, with no capacity to do anything at all to the Soul Stone, really get those three favours?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking pentacle mages,<br /> perhaps they're being resticted to the genie act as penance for something they did in the past,<br /> so as a result they have to go through with it to regain some trust from their order.<br /> <br /> Anyway, a good point.<br /> The favor system seems much more serviceable when a mage has the stone,<br /> less hoops to jump through to get it to work out logically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:33:13-07:00","id":976424,"title":"","content":"It's not a metaphysical law of the universe, it's a legal convention shared by the Pentacle and Seers - one's Soul Stone is so important that holding on to one you've filched is dirty pool (or bad cricket, for us Brits).<br /> <br /> So... Depends on the indulgence of the owner, or how liable the local Lex Magica they're a member of is to look poorly on them just smiting a Sleeper. You could luck out and get the stone of a Thearch or Libertine, or you could be up shit creek and have the stone of a hardcore Mystagogue or Seer.<br /> <br /> The law's for people. How much does the mage think of Sleepers as people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:48:43-07:00","id":976426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976424#post976424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sleepers as people</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop believing the Libertine propaganda, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:57:56-07:00","id":976470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=889482#post889482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Sleepwalkers and Proximi participating in teamwork rituals all together count as one environmental Yantra (+1), or does each individual participant count as separate environmental Yantra?<br /> <br /> For instance, if a mage is assisted by both a Sleepwalker and Proximi, would the spell have a +2 bonus and use up 2 Yantra slots, or would both people count as one Yantra for a +1 bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As Branford has said... I have been searching in the forums, and this question, that hasn't been answered, is bugging me :P. In the book at pg. 119 it says &quot;Mages<br /> without the Arcanum used at all, Sleepwalkers, and Proximi may also assist in the casting, but do not roll. Instead, the casters may use their participation in the ritual as an environment Yantra.&quot;, but how does it works exactly? Does anyone knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11688-marciano666","name":"marciano666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:00:07-07:00","id":976483,"title":"","content":"All together - proximi are a subset of sleepwalkers. Any number of sleepwalkers involved is one environment yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:00:57-07:00","id":976484,"title":"","content":"Environment Yantra are described along with all the others. It works like any other Yantra. It's just 1-die, so you'll almost always have better options (High Speech, Material, Runes, etc), but it is an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:00:53-07:00","id":976521,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11688-marciano666","name":"marciano666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:20:29-07:00","id":976532,"title":"","content":"I definitely looking forward to the Mage FAQ. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:12:52-07:00","id":976555,"title":"","content":"Yeah any ETA on the FAQ ? Or perhaps if there is enough done on it get the things thats done up ? =) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:30:27-07:00","id":976565,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting for the errata'd book to drop. I've done most of the FAQ already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:48:22-07:00","id":976578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=976565#post976565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm waiting for the errata'd book to drop. I've done most of the FAQ already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. <br /> <br /> Given the myriad questions from the original FAQ thread and later inquires, how large is the draft FAQ document?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:16:20-07:00","id":977107,"title":"","content":"For attainments, can you use conjunctional effects of a spell you're duplicating without dedication the 'optional' slot to it? I'm designing a Life legacy for Warlocks. The 5th level attainment is Create Life, and I'd like the created life to have a Mind appropriate to its type, per the Mind 5 conjunctional effect.<br /> <br /> The optional arcana for the Legacy <i>is</i> Mind, but I'd wanted to use the optional slot for a Reach-heavy version of Telepathy, not just to add a conjunctional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:22:08-07:00","id":977111,"title":"","content":"Could you have the Optional just be a straight Psychic Genesis and simply add the option of making it last as long as any Created Life it's tied to? Since it's a goetia you could also dump telepathy and the like into it as its Numina or Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T05:22:38-07:00","id":977128,"title":"","content":"For the &quot;Awe&quot; Numen (p. 261), it reads, &quot;Anyone gaining fewer successes than the entity is unable to move or speak for a turn. If the entity gains an exceptional success, the effect lasts three turns.&quot; The description of the Numen suggests that this effect is due to paralyzing fear, although I imagine it could also be something like overwhelming euphoria, ecstasy, or whatever you want it to include.<br /> <br /> In game terms, though, does this prevent targets from taking instant actions? If someone is &quot;unable to move or speak,&quot; can they still apply their defense, cast spells, or take other mental actions? Do you apply something like the Insensate tilt (p. 322), or something else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Insensate (p. 322)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The character shuts down, either due to extreme fear or sudden pleasure. He may huddle in a corner, cringe away from sudden noises, or stare into space as waves of pleasure lap over him.<br /> <br /> Effect: The character can\u2019t take any actions until the Tilt is resolved. He can apply Defense to incoming attacks, and if he takes any damage from an attack, he\u2019s knocked free of whatever fogged his brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 09-27-2016, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T05:34:34-07:00","id":977137,"title":"","content":"Good question. I believe it means they can't do anything, but the way it's worded allows a lot of room for lawyers to argue, 'It says unable to move, but I'm not moving I'm just casting a spell.'<br /> <br /> And yeah I'm sure it can be things other than fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-27-2016, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T07:18:41-07:00","id":977167,"title":"","content":"In that particular case, I would say no spellcasting. If it just froze them still but able to think, they would be able to cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:17:24-07:00","id":977209,"title":"","content":"So how well does the 1ed St screen work with 2nd ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:37:32-07:00","id":977271,"title":"","content":"Now that the errata is out I have a couple of questions about the duel arcane:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Failing to open a Door means the character must change tactics, and cannot use the same Arcanum a second time on a closed Door.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean it's possible for a character to be unable to attack again in the duel due to failing several rolls? E.g. if the character has Mind, Space and Time and fails an attack with each arcanum against the same door does that mean they can no longer attack? Does this also mean that a duel can result in a draw?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dueling character may not use Yantras or spend Reach beyond that she gains for Arcana mastery, and must still account for spell factors and resistance. </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to what a character would spend reach on? Do they need to account for spell factors like Casting Time and Range in the Duel? The rules seem to suggest that (mechanically) you just roll Arcanum + Attribute until someone wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:20:45-07:00","id":977292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977271#post977271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm curious as to what a character would spend reach on? Do they need to account for spell factors like Casting Time and Range in the Duel? The rules seem to suggest that (mechanically) you just roll Arcanum + Attribute until someone wins.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess that the duel can have more rules or take place in a setting that aint just 1 meter apart from one another. Maybe the duel takes place on the top of different mountainpeaks. And if guess the rules in the duel usually don't say &quot;you do one spell, i do the next&quot; but is usually taking place in real time ( eg. initiative) so instant spellcasting would be a good thing to spend reach on. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:08:07-07:00","id":977333,"title":"","content":"This is undoubtedly somewhere in this thread or the FAQ thread, but the former is 250+ posts long and this one is 1500+. They really need a FAQ document somewhere. So here is my question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage,2nd ed.,pg.112</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A character receives a <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>free </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Reach \u2014 which does <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">add Paradox dice \u2014 per dot of her highest-rated Arcanum that meets or<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">exceeds the spell\u2019s requirement. For example a mage with four<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">dots of the Mind Arcanum gains two free Reaches when casting<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">a spell that requires Mind 3.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This makes no sense to me.The mage has Mind 4 which is higher the Mind 3 required by the spell. Therefore they get a free Reach per dot of the highest rated Arcanum that exceeds the requirements. I'm going to presume this is Mind as its the only Arcanum referenced in the example. As they have four dots in Mind they should receive four free reaches, not two.<br /> <br /> Explain, please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:13:48-07:00","id":977335,"title":"","content":"I think there's a chart that goes with that. Look on page 326.<br /> <br /> They receive two because they have two dots of Mind that 'meet or exceed' the spell's requirement. Mind 3 meets it, Mind 4 exceeds it. Two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:15:46-07:00","id":977337,"title":"","content":"For each dot that meets or exceeds.<br /> <br /> So the spell requires dots:<br /> 1, 2, 3<br /> <br /> You have dots:<br /> 1, 2, 3, 4<br /> <br /> 3 meets the requirement and 4 surpasses it. You get one Reach for each. So you get two Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:31:22-07:00","id":977349,"title":"","content":"Thanks both. That's really unclear. If that's what they meant it should say something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage gets a free Reach for each dot by which their Arcanum equals or exceeds the spell's requirement. </div> </div> </div>Short and less ambiguous. Would it kill them to put a couple of parentheses and a formula in there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:40:40-07:00","id":977359,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A character receives a <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>free </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Reach \u2014 which does <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">add Paradox dice \u2014 per dot of her highest-rated Arcanum that meets or<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> exceeds the spell\u2019s requirement.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage gets a free Reach for each dot by which their Arcanum equals or exceeds the spell's requirement. </div> </div> </div><br /> Are these two sentences not making the same statement, save that the book quote above allows for instances with multiple Arcana?</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:23:55-07:00","id":977396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Midgardener</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977359#post977359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Are these two sentences not making the same statement, save that the book quote above allows for instances with multiple Arcana?[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>The misleading part is this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A character receives a <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>free </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Reach <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">per dot of her highest-rated Arcanum that meets or<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> exceeds the spell\u2019s requirement.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> It's meant to say that a character receives a free Reach <b>per Acanum dot</b> that meets or exceeds the spell's requirements. But what it actually says is that a character receives a free Reach <b>per dot in the Acanum</b> that meets or exceeds the spell's requirement. I.e. if the Arcanum meets or exceeds the spell's requirement you get a free reach per dot in it.<br /> <br /> It's what is called a Dangling Modifer. I.e. the &quot;meets or exceeds&quot; qualifier can attach to either the number of dots or the Arcanum itself and as it follows from the Arcanum would more properly be attached to the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:00:02-07:00","id":977419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977396#post977396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's meant to say that a character receives a free Reach <b>per Acanum dot</b> that meets or exceeds the spell's requirements. But what it actually says is that a character receives a free Reach <b>per dot in the Acanum</b> that meets or exceeds the spell's requirement. I.e. if the Arcanum meets or exceeds the spell's requirement you get a free reach per dot in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Sticking with the Mind 3 spell when you have Mind 4. If the spell also has Life 1 and Death 1, and you have Life 3 and Death 3, you aren't getting extra free Reach for those.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T22:35:56-07:00","id":977608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977292#post977292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess that the duel can have more rules or take place in a setting that aint just 1 meter apart from one another. Maybe the duel takes place on the top of different mountainpeaks. And if guess the rules in the duel usually don't say &quot;you do one spell, i do the next&quot; but is usually taking place in real time ( eg. initiative) so instant spellcasting would be a good thing to spend reach on. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't need reach in any of these circumstances as you aren't actually spellcasting using the Magic system, the Duel is something separate entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:10:31-07:00","id":977656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977271#post977271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that the errata is out I have a couple of questions about the duel arcane:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does this mean it's possible for a character to be unable to attack again in the duel due to failing several rolls? E.g. if the character has Mind, Space and Time and fails an attack with each arcanum against the same door does that mean they can no longer attack? Does this also mean that a duel can result in a draw?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm curious as to what a character would spend reach on? Do they need to account for spell factors like Casting Time and Range in the Duel? The rules seem to suggest that (mechanically) you just roll Arcanum + Attribute until someone wins.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I second these questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I thought that if you failed the roll, you couldn't open the Door with the Arcanum in the following turn (but you could try with it in the next one), but now that I reread the text, it doesn't say so... And also, the Reach part get me really confused, moreover you need to account for resistance? What kind of resistance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dueling character may not use Yantras or spend Reach beyond that she gains for Arcana mastery, and must still account for spell factors and resistance </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11688-marciano666","name":"marciano666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:33:01-07:00","id":977659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977608#post977608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wouldn't need reach in any of these circumstances as you aren't actually spellcasting using the Magic system, the Duel is something separate entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes? And in the duel you still spend Reach... Not every magical Duel needs to take place in a small space 15 feet from one another. And even if it's 15 feet you still need a Reach for instant as well as sensory range at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> M:tAw 2ed p 294</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A dueling character may not use Yantras or spend Reach beyond<br /> that she gains for Arcana mastery, and must still account for<br /> spell factors and resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T04:25:46-07:00","id":977684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=977349#post977349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks both. That's really unclear. If that's what they meant it should say something like this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage gets a free Reach for each dot by which their Arcanum equals or exceeds the spell's requirement. </div> </div> </div>Short and less ambiguous. Would it kill them to put a couple of parentheses and a formula in there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still upset they didn't went with something like <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your Grasp equals your Arcana Rating +1, and every spell has a base Reach equal to its dot rating. If your Reach exceeds your Grasp... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T04:50:26-07:00","id":977689,"title":"","content":"Grasp isn't a term in Mage. Honestly, it's way too late to still be complaining about the wording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:31:49-07:00","id":978629,"title":"","content":"Can Proximi mitigate Paradox with mana?<br /> <br /> Edit: Found it. They can and I dont even know why I asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:10:56-07:00","id":978881,"title":"","content":"What do entities that use Power/Finesse/Resistance roll in a Clash of Wills? I'm surprised that the book doesn't explicitly say it. Is it Power+Finesse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:59:19-07:00","id":978893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=978881#post978881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do entities that use Power/Finesse/Resistance roll in a Clash of Wills? I'm surprised that the book doesn't explicitly say it. Is it Power+Finesse?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Werewolf 2e pg 115:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A spirit in a Clash of Wills uses its Rank as its dice pool.<br /> If the Clash comes from the spirit using an Influence, it adds<br /> its dots in that Influence to the dice pool. </div> </div> </div>Strix use Power + Shadow Potency.<br /> <br /> A ghost would probably use its Rank just like a Spirit would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:08:42-07:00","id":979225,"title":"","content":"Do i use the ruling practice if i want to put a ban on someone?<br /> Eg. forbidden someone from performing an action or talking about a certain subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:46:56-07:00","id":979242,"title":"","content":"Psychic Domination is Ruling but I can imagine hiding posibility of a certain action from someone with Veiling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:52:51-07:00","id":979246,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that'd be Ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:48:20-07:00","id":979272,"title":"","content":"How can you specify a target of spell or exempt it without its presence? I can't find it.<br /> E.g. 1. Incognito Presence that works only on my colleagues. Do I need Fate 2 like in 1e?<br /> 2. Knit casted on an area that targets only my cabalmates. Prime 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:01:33-07:00","id":979278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979272#post979272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you specify a target of spell or exempt it without its presence? I can't find it.<br /> E.g. 1. Incognito Presence that works only on my colleagues. Do I need Fate 2 like in 1e?<br /> 2. Knit casted on an area that targets only my cabalmates. Prime 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate 2 &quot;Warding Gesture&quot; does that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:12:16-07:00","id":979280,"title":"","content":"So conjoining 2 dots of fate to a spell is an universal way. Hmm, but wouldn't it be possible with Prime 2 to work only on targets with special set of aura characteristics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:48:38-07:00","id":979296,"title":"","content":"It's not conjoining 2 dots of Fate, you cast a Fate (Wards and Signs) spell and then during its Duration can designate targets or exemptions for other spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:08:46-07:00","id":979308,"title":"","content":"I think you meant &quot;Fate (Warding gesture)&quot;. And yeah, the spell works in a way you described but by conjoining 2 dots of Fate you could make a lesser version of the effect that only affects a single spell that is conjoined with. Maybe some +2 Reach and mana to balance it. <br /> Space keys are a version of this principle. Do you think that every arcanum could use its respective kind of a Key?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:26:44-07:00","id":979480,"title":"","content":"What would be the best way to get for a Mage to get to another planet? Let's assume they have a piece of rock from whatever planet to supply the sympathetic connection.<br /> <br /> Could a space mage build a stargate to this other world? Or would it be easier to go into the Shadow world using spirit, visiting a representation of Mars and crossing back over there?<br /> <br /> In essence, is there a distance limit to teleportation/portal magics (mostly asking for 1e, but also answers for 2e would be nice)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:50:37-07:00","id":979496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979480#post979480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or would it be easier to go into the Shadow world using spirit, visiting a representation of Mars and crossing back over there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you feel like almost literally fighting God, this would be grossly infeasible.<br /> <br /> 1e generally operates under the tacit assumption that magic below the level of archmastery doesn't reach beyond the lunar sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:19:14-07:00","id":979506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979480#post979480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the best way to get for a Mage to get to another planet? Let's assume they have a piece of rock from whatever planet to supply the sympathetic connection.<br /> <br /> Could a space mage build a stargate to this other world? Or would it be easier to go into the Shadow world using spirit, visiting a representation of Mars and crossing back over there?<br /> <br /> In essence, is there a distance limit to teleportation/portal magics (mostly asking for 1e, but also answers for 2e would be nice)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a canon answer to this one. The book Astral Realms details a Temenos realm of humanity's dreams and fantasies about Mars, and it has this sidebar on page 160:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Connections to the Planet Mars</b><br /> In the early 21st century, the surface of<br /> Mars is relatively well-known to researchers<br /> and those members of the general public<br /> who are interested. As a result, the portions<br /> of the realm of Mars that are most similar<br /> to the physical reality of the planet Mars are<br /> actually quite close. Spending time in the<br /> most realistic version of Mars can be used<br /> as a Known (\u20134) sympathetic connection to<br /> the planet Mars for purposes of using Space<br /> magics to scry or visit the planet. However,<br /> the same is true of high-resolution photographs<br /> or a meteorite from Mars. Of course,<br /> any mage interested in doing this must first<br /> ask herself why she is interested in visiting a<br /> lifeless and hostile world. </div> </div> </div>---<br /> <br /> Separate question. Can you use temporarily boosted Skills and Merits to qualify for buying things with Experiences?<br /> <br /> Example 1: I use an Indefinite spell to raise my Wits from 2 to 3. Can I buy Trained Observer with Experiences? If I do, and the spell is cancelled, what happens?<br /> <br /> Example 2: I want to join the Eleventh Question, but I only have Investigation 1. I boost it to 2 with an Indefinite spell, meet the other prerequisites, and study the Legacy from a soul stone. Can I buy the first Attainment with an Arcane Experience? If I do, and the spell is cancelled, what happens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:30:23-07:00","id":979542,"title":"","content":"Sympathy does not work like that any more, though - the old chart conflated both how good a symbolic representation of the target you had and how good your personal sympathy to it was. Second edition splits them into two different things. You could use Temenotic Mars as sympathetic yantra, but you'd need something that's actually been to the planet and retains enough of a sympathetic link for you to use a Space spell on to copy its link, or to have been to Mars yourself.<br /> <br /> This means most of the solar system is right out, Space-wise, but the Moon is possible for a mage determined to be a space explorer - moon rock samples are kept uncontaminated, in special environments in a handful of research centres in the US. Break into the White Sands facility, and you could get yourself a sympathetic connection to the moon.<br /> <br /> Watch out for Idigam, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 10-01-2016, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:37:15-07:00","id":979544,"title":"","content":"As for the other question - officially, trait-buying goes off permanent ratings, not boosted ones. Unofficially, I'd allow a player to buy the Merit in your first example, but the character would lose said Merit when the spell ended and she no longer met the prerequisites. Sanctity of Merits would then refund the xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T02:07:18-07:00","id":979557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979542#post979542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy does not work like that any more, though - the old chart conflated both how good a symbolic representation of the target you had and how good your personal sympathy to it was. Second edition splits them into two different things. You could use Temenotic Mars as sympathetic yantra, but you'd need something that's actually been to the planet and retains enough of a sympathetic link for you to use a Space spell on to copy its link, or to have been to Mars yourself.<br /> <br /> This means most of the solar system is right out, Space-wise, but the Moon is possible for a mage determined to be a space explorer - moon rock samples are kept uncontaminated, in special environments in a handful of research centres in the US. Break into the White Sands facility, and you could get yourself a sympathetic connection to the moon.<br /> <br /> Watch out for Idigam, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martian_meteorite\" target=\"_blank\">you could go to Mars too</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:54:33-07:00","id":979595,"title":"","content":"Oh, awesome! Be sure to stock up on Forces and Matter spells to protect from the radiation and Martian atmosphere, and don't get caught on camera.<br /> <br /> The way sympathy works now was designed so that &quot;I have a photo of it!&quot; is not sufficient. Its an okay yantra, but you won't get a link out of it. This means we don't need the thing from first edition where magic stopped working at the limits of Earth's atmosphere. If you want to go on a heist to get your hands on the mineral samples needed to banish some poor fucker to Utopia Planetia, then godspeed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:24:53-07:00","id":979621,"title":"","content":"You'd be better off with Time, Life and Forces for exploring space. Transform yourself into light, shut off your ability to age and then achieve escape velocity. Learning Space would be useful for the return trip though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:58:14-07:00","id":979757,"title":"","content":"Or use Forces to trap photons and steal their sympathetic connection to the star that send them. If you can see a star's light, you should be able to get a sympathetic connection to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:55:44-07:00","id":979834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979595#post979595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way sympathy works now was designed so that &quot;I have a photo of it!&quot; is not sufficient. Its an okay yantra, but you won't get a link out of it. This means we don't need the thing from first edition where magic stopped working at the limits of Earth's atmosphere. If you want to go on a heist to get your hands on the mineral samples needed to banish some poor fucker to Utopia Planetia, then godspeed!</div> </div> </div> </div>So a representation of something no longer has sympathy with the thing it represents? A person's portrait or picture has no sympathetic connection (that can be borrowed for casting) to them? That isn't something I'd have found intuitive, especially since a picture acts as material sympathy for yantra purposes.<br /> <br /> You mind clarifying this a bit? It feels like something that could also do with being in the FAQ.<br /> <br /> Edit: For clarity's sake, I'm asking why a representation wouldn't have some sort of sympathetic connection. Is there no mystical connection there, especially when a representation has the semiotic connection described in the Yantras section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 10-01-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:23:02-07:00","id":979853,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear in the book; it's just people assuming it works like it used to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:52:58-07:00","id":979866,"title":"","content":"I had a look in the book to try and see if I'm missing something, and the book's definition of a sympathetic link is that the two share a strong emotional, physical, or mystical connection. You must admit, the last one that's pretty open-ended, especially when this is a setting where everything is described as being composed of symbols connected to higher Truth.<br /> <br /> It's a nice change, I just don't think I'd have expected it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:58:47-07:00","id":979869,"title":"","content":"Is it me, or is the Arrow the oldest order?<br /> <br /> It makes sense, considering their philosophies are somewhat old fashioned and likely more required in older times. And based on other posts about the other Orders, specifically their appearances in Dark Eras, it seems like the other Orders required a lot more trial and error before they found something that worked.<br /> <br /> This is keeping in mind that you can do whatever you want with the system. The question is based off of second edition material, of course, not first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:02:14-07:00","id":979872,"title":"","content":"They're the youngest. They were formed in 1945.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:04:15-07:00","id":979873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979872#post979872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're the youngest. They were formed in 1945.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either I was way off or needed to word my question better. Dark Eras mentions the 'Vajrastra, the school of the Adamantine Arrow.' Did it exist in a non-Order state longer than the others?<br /> <br /> Oh I see. 'The Order lats reorganized itself in 1945.' It's all in the book, apologies I was thinking this stuff was in their Order book.<br /> <br /> Anyways as, I hope, a question that isn't available in the book, when was the Scelesti-Kish thing going on? Wikipedia suggests Kish grew to prominence in 3100 BC, was that about it? In other words, well before the orders or the schools of thought that would later become them?<br /> <br /> I'm plotting out something in the game that, very loosely, ties back to that time and the Arrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:15:07-07:00","id":979883,"title":"","content":"I think that's originally from Mage Noir, actually. The idea is that the experience of World War II led Arrow caucuses from around the world to convene in Tibet and fundamentally reevaluate their practices, especially how involved they were with Sleeper cultures and warfare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:16:14-07:00","id":979884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979873#post979873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking this stuff was in their Order book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamantine Arrow, pages 31 and 32<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also Mage Noir, but it was in the Arrow Orderbook first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:29:11-07:00","id":979890,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I got it, and about the Kish thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979873#post979873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways as, I hope, a question that isn't available in the book, when was the Scelesti-Kish thing going on? Wikipedia suggests Kish grew to prominence in 3100 BC, was that about it? In other words, well before the orders or the schools of thought that would later become them?<br /> <br /> I'm plotting out something in the game that, very loosely, ties back to that time and the Arrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:32:12-07:00","id":980166,"title":"","content":"Can someone clarify for me how the &quot;mix and match&quot; process for boons works when you use something like Exceptional Luck to grant boons? I think I understand it, but wanted to double check some things. <br /> <br /> Let's say I have Potency 3 on my spell overall. I know you can pick one of the three options on p. 134: either gain 3 uses of 9-again on mundane rolls, +3 on a specific action or Skill for 3 different uses, or 3 beneficial conditions. Easy enough. <br /> <br /> But what if I want to mix and match? Do you kind of just allocate Potency to the things you want? For example, again with Potency 3, what if I wanted each effect? Would that be 1 instance of 9-again, +1 to one specific action/skill for 1 roll, and one condition? Or am I missing something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:58:27-07:00","id":980266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979542#post979542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy does not work like that any more, though - the old chart conflated both how good a symbolic representation of the target you had and how good your personal sympathy to it was. Second edition splits them into two different things. You could use Temenotic Mars as sympathetic yantra, but you'd need something that's actually been to the planet and retains enough of a sympathetic link for you to use a Space spell on to copy its link, or to have been to Mars yourself.<br /> <br /> This means most of the solar system is right out, Space-wise, but the Moon is possible for a mage determined to be a space explorer - moon rock samples are kept uncontaminated, in special environments in a handful of research centres in the US. Break into the White Sands facility, and you could get yourself a sympathetic connection to the moon.<br /> <br /> Watch out for Idigam, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Also remember: using Spirit to effect interplanetary travel is best attempted after dark, due to the baleful influence of a certain jealous, radioactive Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:40:34-07:00","id":980299,"title":"","content":"Just a thought, but there is no longer a hard cap on Sensory range, and zoom in allows you to ignore atmospheric conditions and even see molecular bonds! <br /> Shouldn't that be more than enough magnification to do Sensory range teleports to any planet in our solar system? <br /> <br /> Related, say you got a live feed from a camera on a satellite around Mars. Would that count as remote viewing for spellcasting or is the time delay thanks to distance too great?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:45:25-07:00","id":980304,"title":"","content":"You'd probably have to make it a series of hops, zoom in, teleport, zoom in, teleport, but yeah that could work.<br /> <br /> For the live feed from Mars, even if it is too great a time delay you could reduce it via a Time spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:49:42-07:00","id":980309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=980166#post980166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone clarify for me how the &quot;mix and match&quot; process for boons works when you use something like Exceptional Luck to grant boons? I think I understand it, but wanted to double check some things.<br /> <br /> Let's say I have Potency 3 on my spell overall. I know you can pick one of the three options on p. 134: either gain 3 uses of 9-again on mundane rolls, +3 on a specific action or Skill for 3 different uses, or 3 beneficial conditions. Easy enough.<br /> <br /> But what if I want to mix and match? Do you kind of just allocate Potency to the things you want? For example, again with Potency 3, what if I wanted each effect? Would that be 1 instance of 9-again, +1 to one specific action/skill for 1 roll, and one condition? Or am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it right. You kind of just allocate Potency to the things you want. It's like casting Exceptional Luck/Monkey's Paw/Sworn Oaths/whatever grants you a master pool of Potency, and then you divide that between up to 3 distinct spell effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=980299#post980299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought, but there is no longer a hard cap on Sensory range, and zoom in allows you to ignore atmospheric conditions and even see molecular bonds!<br /> Shouldn't that be more than enough magnification to do Sensory range teleports to any planet in our solar system?<br /> <br /> Related, say you got a live feed from a camera on a satellite around Mars. Would that count as remote viewing for spellcasting or is the time delay thanks to distance too great?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first one actually somewhat came up in my game! A scientifically-inclined Obrimos was using Zoom In on Venus during a conversation about astrology with a Thrice-Great.<br /> <br /> With a Reach, Zoom in can specifically see clearly out to one mile per dot of Forces. I assume &quot;see clearly&quot; means &quot;sensory range.&quot; Unless you made up a Reach effect, it wouldn't work for the same reason that you can't see the Moon in a microscope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:07:36-07:00","id":980371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=979595#post979595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, awesome! Be sure to stock up on Forces and Matter spells to protect from the radiation and Martian atmosphere, and don't get caught on camera.<br /> <br /> The way sympathy works now was designed so that &quot;I have a photo of it!&quot; is not sufficient. Its an okay yantra, but you won't get a link out of it. This means we don't need the thing from first edition where magic stopped working at the limits of Earth's atmosphere. If you want to go on a heist to get your hands on the mineral samples needed to banish some poor fucker to Utopia Planetia, then godspeed!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So in the far off future, when humanity reaches for the stars, mages will be able to set up interplanetarian portals!!??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:07:45-07:00","id":980396,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really have to be the far off future for Mages. Nah, the main thing is that the setting is developed to be humanocentric and while space exploration is a human endeavor once you're out in the stars it can be more difficult to keep your mind on the problems of humanity at large back home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:55:34-07:00","id":980419,"title":"","content":"Q how many dots in the mentor merit should you have for your mentor to be able to induct you into his/her legacy.<br /> RAW under the strictest interpetation seems to say that you have to have a 4 dot mentor (pc has gnosis 2, mentor has PC gnosis plus half the merit rating).<br /> Is the mentor merit necessary to join a legacy via mentor or is most mentors not represented by the merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:03:10-07:00","id":980421,"title":"","content":"You don't need the Mentor merit. You could optionally buy it to represent an especially involved and dedicated relationship with the other mechanical benefits of Mentor, but it isn't required to join a Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:28:36-07:00","id":983760,"title":"","content":"I'm building a goetic familiar, and I have some questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 258</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goetia do not naturally possess Manifestations. They can be granted<br /> physical bodies through the Death and Spirit Arcana; Goetia can<br /> be granted the ability to possess victims through the Mind Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a mage casts Goetic Summons (without the Spirit or Death effect) to call something down from the Astral, what form does the entity take? Does it automatically get Twilight Form? If not, where is it exactly?<br /> <br /> Is Twilight Form one of the manifestation conditions that can be granted by whatever the Mind 4 version of Bind Spirit is? Or would granting that and other Manifestations be the province of a Mind 4 version of Shape Spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:36:56-07:00","id":983763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=983760#post983760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm building a goetic familiar, and I have some questions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When a mage casts Goetic Summons (without the Spirit or Death effect) to call something down from the Astral, what form does the entity take? Does it automatically get Twilight Form? If not, where is it exactly?<br /> <br /> Is Twilight Form one of the manifestation conditions that can be granted by whatever the Mind 4 version of Bind Spirit is? Or would granting that and other Manifestations be the province of a Mind 4 version of Shape Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Twilight Form is the default ability an Ephemeral Entity possesses to give it &quot;form&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:49:28-07:00","id":983766,"title":"","content":"That's what I was thinking too, but the text seems to go out of its way to exclude Goetia from that. This is on 258:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Spirits and ghosts begin with the Twilight Form Manifestation<br /> and a number of Manifestation Effects from the list below equal<br /> to Rank.</b> They may increase their capabilities by reducing the<br /> number of Numina they possess, at the cost of one Numen per<br /> Manifestation Effect.<br /> <br /> Many Manifestation Effects have prerequisite Influence or Manifestation<br /> Conditions \u2014 a spirit can only Fetter to something with an<br /> Open Condition, for example.<br /> <br /> All Manifestation Effects require a Power + Finesse roll to use. Most<br /> have an associated cost in Essence, and some are contested or resisted.<br /> <br /> <b>Goetia do not naturally possess Manifestations.</b> They can be granted<br /> physical bodies through the Death and Spirit Arcana; Goetia can<br /> be granted the ability to possess victims through the Mind Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:36:15-07:00","id":983785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=983766#post983766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I was thinking too, but the text seems to go out of its way to exclude Goetia from that. This is on 258:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably the nature of an Astral entity is that it exists in us, or through us, via the Astral.( Oneiros, Temenos, etc.) Thusly, I guess they don't have a form beyond an inherent Thought-Body.<br /> <br /> My best thought is, if you want to give it a Manifestation, you use a Weaving Practice of Spirit or Death to Weave in a new frequency for it to take on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:51:40-07:00","id":983791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=983766#post983766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I was thinking too, but the text seems to go out of its way to exclude Goetia from that. This is on 258:</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight Form is a logical exception, given that it is costless, has no prerequisite Condition, and explicitly has a corresponding band of Twilight, to say nothing how how the &quot;no Manifestations&quot; sentence only specifically refers to the effects of Materialize and Possess.<br /> <br /> The takeaway is that goetia need magic or exceptional circumstances to stay out of the Astral for any significant length of time rather than that goetic summoning is an exercise in contradictory states of ephemerality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:36:37-07:00","id":983811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=983791#post983791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">goetic summoning is an exercise in contradictory states of ephemerality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put. Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:00:12-07:00","id":984139,"title":"","content":"Just a quick query about counter spell. Where in the casting process does the clash of wills roll fall. I recall Dave mentioning that clash of wills happened last so that it only kicks in on things that would otherwise be successful. This also means a Mage can see a spell is not worth countering and not use up there action. One noteworthy thing I noted is that as casting rolls are made after paradox, you can't stop another mages paradox by countering the triggering spell.<br /> <br /> This seems fairly fitting but I thought I should check if I have this right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T04:54:19-07:00","id":984351,"title":"","content":"This might not be the best place to ask, but it's relevant. I purchased the Mage 2E book and recently downloaded the revised version with errata. I tried to upload it to Google Drive so I could access the file on my iPhone in my preferred app, for when I'm not at my PC. However, although the file ends in .pdf, Google Drive doesn't recognize it as an actual PDF format. As a result, I can't view it on my phone, even though I can open it correctly from my Google Drive account on other PCs.<br /> <br /> How do I fix this? Already tried deleting and downloading again, and downloading the Dropbox account version and downloading it from there to transfer to Google Drive. If there is a good forum here to post or someone else to ask so I don't need to use this thread, please let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-09-2016, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:24:36-07:00","id":984382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984351#post984351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might not be the best place to ask, but it's relevant. I purchased the Mage 2E book and recently downloaded the revised version with errata. I tried to upload it to Google Drive so I could access the file on my iPhone in my preferred app, for when I'm not at my PC. However, although the file ends in .pdf, Google Drive doesn't recognize it as an actual PDF format. As a result, I can't view it on my phone, even though I can open it correctly from my Google Drive account on other PCs.<br /> <br /> How do I fix this? Already tried deleting and downloading again, and downloading the Dropbox account version and downloading it from there to transfer to Google Drive. If there is a good forum here to post or someone else to ask so I don't need to use this thread, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's strange. I've done the same and have had no trouble. Have you tried restarting your computer and then redownloading or tried using a different internet connection? It sounds like the file is getting corrupted in transmission somehow. Does the file open on your computer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:14:37-07:00","id":984410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984382#post984382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's strange. I've done the same and have had no trouble. Have you tried restarting your computer and then redownloading or tried using a different internet connection? It sounds like the file is getting corrupted in transmission somehow. Does the file open on your computer?</div> </div> </div> </div>The file opens just fine. It's not corrupted, it just isn't recognized by Google Drive as a PDF, even though it ends in .pdf and opens in Adobe.<br /> <br /> It loads on my phone on the Dropbox app, so I might just use a different app if necessary. Just trying to see if I can fix the issue another way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:05:53-07:00","id":984447,"title":"","content":"If i use Life 5 to create life, that life has children, and then the spell expires/ is dispelled. What happens to the children?? Are they real?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:54:29-07:00","id":984472,"title":"","content":"The book talks about adding Reach to make an effect Lasting. How much Reach would you guys require for the spell Regeneration to be made Lasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:00:58-07:00","id":984473,"title":"","content":"P127, 'Making a spell Lasting always costs +2 Reach, but you should think carefully before allowing it - only spells without any way to revert them should have the option.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:19:18-07:00","id":984546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984447#post984447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i use Life 5 to create life, that life has children, and then the spell expires/ is dispelled. What happens to the children?? Are they real?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are a natural side-effect of the spell and thus persist after the spell ends. It's no different than if you use Life 5 to create something and it kills someone, or creates a tool, or poops in the woods, the consequences don't go away just because the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:50:40-07:00","id":984557,"title":"","content":"Do Spirits made through &quot;Birth Spirit&quot; develop naturally after their creation, like through acquiring new Influences? If they transform themselves sufficiently, can they still be dispelled or do they become side-effects of their own creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T23:01:39-07:00","id":984759,"title":"","content":"I think my take on it would be that, yes, a spirit can develop over time but its Nature will always contain a core of what was used in the spell. If the spell is ever unraveled, the spirit will lose one (or two if Reach was used) Rank and see its nature change towards whatever it's been feeding upon. This might mean no real change in its Nature, or it might change radically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T23:14:27-07:00","id":984762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984557#post984557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Spirits made through &amp;quot;Birth Spirit&amp;quot; develop naturally after their creation, like through acquiring new Influences? If they transform themselves sufficiently, can they still be dispelled or do they become side-effects of their own creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, even to the point of becoming a magath, but the spirit remains the product of a spell and will vanish if that spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:11:23-07:00","id":984885,"title":"","content":"If you turned someone into something like a car, would they have some semblance of control over their new form?<br /> If not, would a reach option be appropriate for bestowing that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T10:46:05-07:00","id":984944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984885#post984885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you turned someone into something like a car, would they have some semblance of control over their new form?<br /> If not, would a reach option be appropriate for bestowing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we always turned vampires into lawn furniture in older editions. Zero mobility. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:37:40-07:00","id":984970,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have an idea on how to do temporary magical items? Specifically like bullets from Outlaw Star's caster gun (unoriginal of me, but I'm in a Wild West setting, so fuck it). Basically something fun like a bullet that when it hits it's target, does Control Gravity in the area around the impact. Stuff like that. Am kind of at a loss other than Fate 2 + Time 2 and and having the target of an AoE spell be the bullet using Hang Spell and Conditional Duration. <br /> <br /> In addition, Body Control (Page 148) states that for every potency the healing time of bashing is halved. . then says that at Potency 3 the healing time is 1 minute per bashing. But shouldn't it be 15 minutes, down to 7.5 minutes, down to 3.75 minutes? Or am I just not understanding the math here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:20:32-07:00","id":984992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984970#post984970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have an idea on how to do temporary magical items? Specifically like bullets from Outlaw Star's caster gun (unoriginal of me, but I'm in a Wild West setting, so fuck it). Basically something fun like a bullet that when it hits it's target, does Control Gravity in the area around the impact. Stuff like that. Am kind of at a loss other than Fate 2 + Time 2 and and having the target of an AoE spell be the bullet using Hang Spell and Conditional Duration. </div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could just imbue the buller with the spell and the trigger for the imbued spell could be that the bullet hits something. Sure it counts against your spell controll but that is why you make your magic bullets in your sanctum right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7463,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","user":"Toine","date":".  Fixed a wrong word. 10-10-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:21:42-07:00","id":984994,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Imbued item is just a bit away for me, as I'm a starting character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:01:54-07:00","id":985018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=984970#post984970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have an idea on how to do temporary magical items? Specifically like bullets from Outlaw Star's caster gun (unoriginal of me, but I'm in a Wild West setting, so fuck it). Basically something fun like a bullet that when it hits it's target, does Control Gravity in the area around the impact. Stuff like that. Am kind of at a loss other than Fate 2 + Time 2 and and having the target of an AoE spell be the bullet using Hang Spell and Conditional Duration.<br /> <br /> In addition, Body Control (Page 148) states that for every potency the healing time of bashing is halved. . then says that at Potency 3 the healing time is 1 minute per bashing. But shouldn't it be 15 minutes, down to 7.5 minutes, down to 3.75 minutes? Or am I just not understanding the math here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The base bashing healing time is 15 minutes per point, so at Potency 3 you'd need to half it 3 times. So the base 15 would be cut to 7.5, then to 3.75, then to 1.875. At that point I'd assume the writers round down for simplicity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:00:40-07:00","id":985110,"title":"","content":"Trying to think up setting. Wanted some clarification.<br /> <br /> Default consilium is a single city. Presumably in regions with more spread-out mysteries and cabals you might have a more broadened consilium, perhaps more influenced by caucuses?<br /> <br /> Basically, while mages clump, the world is still large. If for whatever reason there's two cabals in Elfers, a small census-designated 'place' of 13,000 people, and some cabals up and down the coast but none within twenty miles of each other and nothing else within a hundred miles. Would there be a Consilium, centered in Elfers, with territory spread out to encompass the other cabals? Or would they all just be 'lone' cabals, mostly influenced by Caucuses? Or would some Silver Ladder bigwig from Orlando, just over 100 miles away, step in and say that they're going to have to move? Would they all be consilium-designated solitary cabals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-10-2016, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:46:16-07:00","id":985476,"title":"","content":"I'd say your first priority in deciding what should be the case is what you feel would work best for your game. If you want the cabals to be interacting in some way or another as regards local Mysteries or resources, make them a part of a Consilium. If you want to encourage more of a feeling of isolation, don't have a Consilium at all. It's such a small group to begin with, everyone knows one another, and there wouldn't <i>really</i> be much of a need for a Consilium to resolve disputes.<br /> <br /> If the big Mystery of the region affects everything along the coast, that'd be more incentive to have a Consilium. One of my games is set in Oregon and there is a state-wide Mystery called the Great Western Whorl that makes state-wide cooperation pretty important (if I'd had the Silver Ladder book when I started the game, I'd have simply made Convocations in the state reasonably common but live and learn). However, if the Awakened there don't <i>need</i> to discuss Mysteries - maybe the guys up the coast are spying on a Supernal Verge, while those way down the coast are chasing swamp vampires - then there's no need for a Consilium; the two groups might as well not exist from the perspective of the rest.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that there's simply an agreement for each cabal to have a leader or representative meet to discuss things and have a round-table rather than a Consilium. If every cabal has at least one thearch member in it, this process would be decidedly easier to produce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:04:37-07:00","id":985483,"title":"","content":"I was mostly offering up that example for terms, I'm not sure why I made it so different from my idea for a setting. I thought Elfers was a good place to start because it's a ridiculously small town. Place.<br /> <br /> Anyways the idea is there's a consilium, but a small one. A few cabals spread out in a large town, not quite a city. But there's some rather intriguing mysteries spread out across the region, two or three cabals here, one cabal here, for hundreds of miles. Not enough to really warrant each becoming their own consilium, so I figured they would be 'folded into' the larger one, just due to technicalities and a desire to keep everyone under the consilium umbrella, so the Guardians, Mysterium, and Arrow can jump into action when they need to and the Silver Ladder can regulate disputes.<br /> <br /> A sense of isolation is a priority, as well as the idea that there's a lot out there in the world mages at large will never see or know about, even in this backwoods area. But I also wanted a lot of travel. Impending conflict is a further concern, as there's a couple powerful Free Council Assemblies on one side, in larger cities, and what's believed to be the nerve center for a Tetrarch on the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-11-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:59:00-07:00","id":985572,"title":"","content":"The Orders can jump into action independently of a Consilium. In a remote enough area a caucus might be stretched pretty thin, but if there are Mages ther then the Orders they're trained in have some kind of foothold. Take Tucson, at the very least the local Arriw caucus meets in the airplane graveyard, but Order representatives are still thin enough on the ground that no one has bothered to set up or join up with a Consilium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:13:02-07:00","id":986081,"title":"","content":"Page 118 for Combined Spells: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">&quot;Free </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Reach is determined as normal.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> RAW it appears that a Mastigos with Space 4 and Mind 2 casting a combined Space 1 and Mind 2 spell would get 3 Reaches as Space is the highest Arcanum in the spell, and the Mind 2 practice would be the highest requirement, but that would make it easy for Gnosis 3+ Mages to gain more free Reaches than they'd normally get from low-rated Arcana. Casting the Mind spell alone would normally only receive a single Reach, but by combi-casting it with their highest Arcanum the Mastigos get two additional Reaches for a measly -2 dice penalty.<br /> <br /> The way I've assumed it to work (before re-reading the rules on page 112) is that you determine which spell would net you the fewest Reaches if cast individually, and that would be the Reaches for your combined spell.<br /> Can someone clarify how it's supposed to work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:39:54-07:00","id":986126,"title":"","content":"You would get 3 Reach for the Space spell and one Reach for the Mind spell that you are combining. That's for determining Reach clauses though I think since Factor improvements via Reach are shared by both spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-12-2016, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:00:56-07:00","id":986169,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's how it works, myself. I think you had it right before, Tessie; you use the lowest relevant arcanum for everything else, so I imagine that you'd use it to determine the overall Reach for a spell. Reach effects are shared by each spell, which, if you had to spend them individually, would mean you'd get <i>more</i> powerful through combined castings, not less.<br /> <br /> So yeah, go with what you understood originally. That is, to use your example, the Mage with Space 4 and Mind 2 casting a combined Space 1/Mind 2 spell would have <i>one</i> free Reach, and would roll Gnosis + Mind - 2 as their dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:37:30-07:00","id":986354,"title":"","content":"I know this has come up on the forums before and even in this thread, but I'm having some issues with understanding the Duel Arcane rules.<br /> <br /> First, I'm ignoring this part of the 2E core book, which I am pretty sure should have been removed during errata? Am I right about that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dueling character may not use Yantras or spend Reach beyond that she gains for Arcana mastery, and must still account for spell factors and resistance. </div> </div> </div>Second, is it true that you only need 1 success on your attack roll (if the opponent does not defend) to open a Door, and that extra successes contribute extra dice on the next roll? If so, what's stopping the win from going to whoever has the most Doors (assuming large enough rolls to consistently get 1 success/roll)? Is there any passive defense you need to incorporate when rolling, or target number you need to reach to open the Door other than 1 success?<br /> <br /> Third, can you spend Willpower on the rolls? It seems like Willpower is already very closely related to your ability to win the Duel, because Doors are based on Resolve + Composure. Letting you add WP to a roll seems to very heavily weigh in favor of the combatant with higher Resolve + Composure.<br /> <br /> Fourth, can you have exceptional successes and dramatic failures on these rolls, and so they cause conditions or tilts like usual?<br /> <br /> It just seems really non-interactive to me, and I'm trying to make sure I'm understanding the rules as written correctly. As it stands, it seems to me like even a newly Awakened mage could reliably win the Duel if they just have higher Resolve + Composure because they'll typically outlast their opponent's Doors. If there was some other target you needed to hit for opening a Door, or if every roll was contested, or if you could open multiple Doors with higher rolls, it would make more sense to me -- but Defending takes away your option for Attacking that turn.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something really important?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-12-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:23:05-07:00","id":988061,"title":"","content":"Bump? Maybe it's not a simple question? :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T21:56:25-07:00","id":988128,"title":"","content":"(EDIT: I wrote up some houserules for expanding the Duel Arcane in response to this, feel free to check them out: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988166-expanded-duel-arcane-rules\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...l-arcane-rules</a> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988061#post988061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bump? Maybe it's not a simple question? :/</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're reading this DaveB, I and others would love to see some clarification of the Duel Arcane when the Mage FAQ comes out! Until then, here's an effortpost about my interpretation of it. (now that it's no longer a conflict of interest for me to answer)<br /> <br /> First:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dueling character may not use Yantras or spend Reach beyond that she gains for Arcana mastery, and must still account for spell factors and resistance. </div> </div> </div>The conceit of the Duel Arcane in 2E is that you're (dramatically and poetically) modeling a specific spell effect which you are capable of actually casting, it's not like the 1E Duel where it's a totally abstract display of power. I believe the intent of this sentence here is that you should look to a spell which you could actually cast, spend 1 Reach on Instant casting, and then maybe 1 Reach on sensory range if necessary? You could also assume that you're casting as an aimed spell, but that may be a moot point because you aren't actually completing the spell and so you wouldn't need to make a &quot;throwing&quot; roll. I suppose it depends on how far the attacks/defenses are going? Depending on how you read it, it could be that you need to fully cast and complete the effect, it just doesn't actually have a mechanical impact because it's purely in the Supernal World.<br /> <br /> Possibility 1: it's as simple as Attribute+Arcanum for all attacks and defenses.<br /> Possibility 2: you account for Reach as if actually casting the spell you're using, which might require a Gnosis+Athletics/Firearms-Defense roll for your Attack to make contact if you're not devoting Reach to Sensory Range. If the spell effect you want to recreate is Withstood, you may need to take dicepool penalties on your Attack or Defense as usual to raise Potency, and the Attack/Defense fails if Potency isn't high enough.<br /> <br /> Possibility 2 would raise some issues because, since the spells aren't actually taking effect, there would be no real reason not to use 1 or 2 dot spells that aren't Withstood. But that might just be a flavor issue.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Second: I think your initial read is correct, there is no target number or Defense or Withstand rating or anything like that, only the other mage choosing to Defend on their turn. The way the rules are written suggest to me that you only add extra successes as dice on your next roll (whether Attack or Defense) if you Attacked. Fortune favors the bold.<br /> <br /> Third: I don't see why you couldn't spend WP in the Duel. Usually the rules will explicitly state when you can't spend WP on a roll, such as for Wisdom degeneration, so I assume it's possible by default. I think it's a feature, not a bug, that the Duel favors high Resolve+Composure. It's no different from a gunfight favoring high Dexterity+Firearms, except that it requires less Skill specialization and so is open to more characters.<br /> <br /> Fourth: Again, I don't think the Duel is different from any other roll that has exceptional success/dramatic fail and ensuing Conditions. Tilts and Conditions usually make combat and other challenges more exciting and dynamic.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Having said all that, when you look at the rules, there's an emergent strategy for the Duel that isn't really called out explicitly.<br /> <br /> When you make an attack roll and fail, you can't use that Arcanum to attack again until the Door in question opens. This implies that it's possible to put your opponent in check by blocking all of their attacks until they run out of Arcana to use. If they can't use their Arcana to attack, they either have to Negotiate and offer a concession (probably a big one since they have almost no leverage) to open your current Door, or Defend until you're placed in the same position as they are.<br /> <br /> That, along with the possibility of imposing Tilts (a magical version of Arm Wrack, for instance), would seem to make the Duel more dynamic. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-16-2016, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:28:26-07:00","id":988138,"title":"","content":"So, here is a question about the interaction of Enhanced Item and a spell like Sever the Awakened Soul?<br /> So reading it Sever the awakened soul rips out someones soul when they hare hit by the spell. Let's assume I made a sword, and placed this spell in as an enhanced item. According to my reading of enhanced item, I now have a 5 dot item that I no longer have to cast sever the awakened soul with, and it separates supernatural beings from the souls just by wounding them. Unlike an imbued item I don't have to cast the spell and worry about it failing it is always on, and always ready to go. It is a permeant feature of that item. Am I understanding that correctly?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:44:43-07:00","id":988170,"title":"","content":"I don't think so. Enhanced Item is for equipment that's the subject of a spell like Monkey's Paw or Aegis. Sever the Awakened Soul targets a person, not an object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T06:55:47-07:00","id":988232,"title":"","content":"Going by the wording any spell that can have its effect extended to indefinite duration qualifies for this. Though perhaps the example spell might not work for enhancement because extending duration extends the souls minium separation from the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:23:29-07:00","id":988241,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> is right, spells that are used to create an Enhanced Item are spells that target the object to enhance it, not spells placed on the object that target something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:40:31-07:00","id":988559,"title":"","content":"If I'm casting a spell on myself, can I automatically use a Material-level sympathy Yantra, or do I have to separate a chunk from myself somehow? What if I take a second to look at myself in a mirror? Or if a mirror is too impermanent, take a selfie on my phone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:36:40-07:00","id":988602,"title":"","content":"In what part of the 2ed core are the rules to taint spells with the abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:45:43-07:00","id":988615,"title":"","content":"P239, upper left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:12:44-07:00","id":988645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988559#post988559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm casting a spell on myself, can I automatically use a Material-level sympathy Yantra, or do I have to separate a chunk from myself somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889464-question-on-the-flexibility-of-yantras?p=889614#post889614\">There's an established joke here</a>, but semiotics beats semantics; you'll want to incorporate a relevant piece of yourself, a recent record, or something you made in the last month into the casting, depending on the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:05:46-07:00","id":988795,"title":"","content":"Where can I find general guidelines for creating stats for NPCs? How high should their Gnosis, Arcana, attributes/skills, etc. be?<br /> <br /> I feel like it would help if there were &quot;tiers&quot; with general guidelines on creating higher level characters. The 1E books used to have this: you'd get so much bonus XP at character creation for &quot;experienced&quot;, &quot;elite&quot;, etc. characters. Anyone have tips for that in 2E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:43:52-07:00","id":988809,"title":"","content":"Those xp guidelines severely lowballed everyone anyway.<br /> <br /> The short answer is &quot;nowhere&quot;. The long answer is that we're looking at it as maybe being something to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:46:53-07:00","id":988810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988602#post988602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what part of the 2ed core are the rules to taint spells with the abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The barest bone is in the scelsti section, but omits the addictive effects of befouling your spells and the risk of ripping your Path into abyssal form. We're working on those. (1e versions are in Tome of the Mysteries and Left Hand Path)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:02:11-07:00","id":988816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988809#post988809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those xp guidelines severely lowballed everyone anyway.<br /> <br /> The short answer is &quot;nowhere&quot;. The long answer is that we're looking at it as maybe being something to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, do you (or anyone else here) have any general suggestions for Gnosis/Arcana ratings for NPCs, then? I found a reference in the 1E Adamantine Arrow book that suggested the Adamant Sage should be a second-degree Master, but may be first-degree Master with multiple Adept Arcana ratings. That kind of guideline helps me figure out how strong to make certain NPCs like the Hierarch and council. And I guess I could look through the 1E core book for stats on the Numean and other Council members, too. Just wondering if others had tips for that in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:17:50-07:00","id":988823,"title":"","content":"There's the Mentor Merit that proposes how powerful a given Mage will be in comparison to the character with a Mentor. Here's the actual text:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a guideline, Mentors who are Awakened mages bought for Mage characters should have Gnosis and Arcana higher than the character \u2014 at least half their dot rating higher Gnosis than the character, and twice the dot rating in Arcanum dots above the number of Arcanum dots the character has, while still obeying the rules for how high Arcana may rise with Gnosis. </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"> Most Mentors will have an Order or Consilium Status of their own as well. </span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 10-17-2016, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:36:30-07:00","id":988876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988809#post988809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those xp guidelines severely lowballed everyone anyway.<br /> <br /> The short answer is &amp;quot;nowhere&amp;quot;. The long answer is that we're looking at it as maybe being something to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Colour me as genuinely interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:38:19-07:00","id":988953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988559#post988559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm casting a spell on myself, can I automatically use a Material-level sympathy Yantra, or do I have to separate a chunk from myself somehow? What if I take a second to look at myself in a mirror? Or if a mirror is too impermanent, take a selfie on my phone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've asked this before. You can use yourself as Material Yantra. By that logic, I imagine you can use other people as Material-level yantra for spells targeting them if you can touch them for it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12483\" data-vbnamecard=\"12483\">ale137</a> Page 239 has the only rules we have for it so far. It's under Chapter Six: Left-Handed Mages - Scelesti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:53:07-07:00","id":989052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=988816#post988816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, do you (or anyone else here) have any general suggestions for Gnosis/Arcana ratings for NPCs, then? I found a reference in the 1E Adamantine Arrow book that suggested the Adamant Sage should be a second-degree Master, but may be first-degree Master with multiple Adept Arcana ratings. That kind of guideline helps me figure out how strong to make certain NPCs like the Hierarch and council. And I guess I could look through the 1E core book for stats on the Numean and other Council members, too. Just wondering if others had tips for that in 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think you should consider that by considering how many mages you think exist in the world or in the country of your setting, and then the surrounding area of the main location. I personally consider anyone whose dice pool with improvised magic to be 6 dice to be a &quot;professional&quot; for whatever magical tasks they get up to. Gnosis 3 is when your rituals get really short, and you've finally got access to combined spells, as well as decent headway for legacy progression, with that in mind, I personally consider mages with gnosis 3 and path arcana 3 to be the meat of any consilium--anyone above that are major players and actively shape the politics and research and captain the resources for the local area. Even if you have thousands or tens of thousands of mages world-wide, I personally think that Masters of any arcana should be rare enough that you could count them on your hands.<br /> <br /> The more important the players should be in addition to making a suppressive, &quot;we're alone or outnumbered&quot; kind of scenario, the less powerful mages you might want to have. If you want Mage society to be positively active and exciting, like a secret world where there's constantly stuff going on and lots of interesting people to meet, then you might have dozens of isolated Masters who specialize in specific things and pull the weight of mentor's and teachers and top-researchers in various fields--but I personally feel that runs the risk of sometimes making the player characters seem unnecessary if they get caught up in a conflict that would be better resolved by the masters.<br /> <br /> Unless the conflict is totally personal and related to the PC's obsessions so there's a clear reason why only the PC cabal(s) are involved in the drama of your chronicle. I dunno if that is helpful or too much to take in, and it is all just my opinion, but if that helped at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:26:00-07:00","id":989066,"title":"","content":"I use two guidelines for generating NPC stats in my game. These are totally just a model that I almost always fine-tune, but it helps to have some kind of skeleton to work from.<br /> <br /> First, decide if the NPC is simple or complex. This isn't so much a reflection of importance to the story as whether or not I expect to roll complex dice for them during a scene. My PCs have/had an important and powerful mentor who I never fully statted, and a more minor mage who's just their friend and sometimes joins in during action scenes, so I gave them full stats.<br /> <br /> All named NPCs (ideally) get a Concept, Virtue/Vice, one Aspiration and one Obsession.<br /> <br /> In both cases, arbitrarily rate their power from 1-5 dots. 1 dot is equivalent to a freshly created PC, 3 dots is a &quot;rival&quot; whom they can be challenged by as a party but expect to win, 5 dots is a major force.<br /> <br /> Simple NPCs: use Retainer as a guide for dicepools. Choose a number of tasks/abilities equal to their dots that they're skilled at. Choose Gnosis/Arcana ratings based on the Mentor merit relative to a generic starting character.<br /> <br /> Complex NPCs: make a starting character. Add Gnosis dots equal to NPC's dot level. Add Experiences as follows:<ul><li>1 dot: 5 XP</li> <li>2 dot: 10 XP, 5 AXP</li> <li>3 dot: 15 XP, 10 AXP</li> <li>4 dot: 25 XP, 15 AXP</li> <li>5 dot: 30 XP, 20 AXP</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:50:23-07:00","id":989552,"title":"","content":"I have a few questions about the Seers and how much influence they have. <br /> <br /> Do the Seers control the british crown?<br /> Do the Seers keep the metric system down?<br /> Do the Seers keep Atlantis of the maps?<br /> Do the Seers keep the Martians under wraps?<br /> Do the Deers hold back the electric car?<br /> Do they make Steve Gutenberg...a star?<br /> Do they rob cavefish of their sight?<br /> Do they rig every Oscar night?<br /> Do they?<br /> Do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:56:13-07:00","id":989556,"title":"","content":"Dammit now the song will be stuck in my head for a while. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:03:08-07:00","id":989638,"title":"","content":"There are many times I find missing pop culture references is more benefit than problem.<br /> <br /> I met a former roommate's current roommates once and they asked if I knew what a fox said, so I explained their various calls. They went really weird and quiet as my former roommate busted up laughing. They showed me the music video and then spent about half an hour after listening to different fox calls.<br /> <br /> It was educational for all of us.<br /> <br /> Re: Dave's response on XP: That's about the best attitude I could hope for.<br /> <br /> <br /> My simple question is:<br /> <br /> How should you handle legacy attainments that make sense to be something that gets superceded by straight arcana attainments at higher levels? (say, a first attainment that unveils something that the arcana at 2 just allows.<br /> <br /> (I'm leaning towards making the legacy attainment improve on learning a later attainment that guarantees that the attainment has become redundant, but not using up that attainment to achieve it, but this seems like stretching or breaking the rules as stated. Alternately, you could word the attainment in such a way as to have it slide things over naturally. E.G. 1st Attainment improves the ability to see spirits and related phenomena without a spell by a step. If the mage normally requires deep scrutiny or an active spell to see a thing, it is now visible to Active Mage Sight If they normally can see something with Active Mage Sight, the attainment boosts that up to Peripheral Mage Sight, but with full clarity.)<br /> <br /> Wait: Better questions:<br /> <br /> <b>Where (or what) are the rules for when a Yantra can be used? </b><br /> <br /> Area isn't consistent about mentioning the rules. Demesnes seem to assume that you will cast from inside to get the benefit, but I don't see it actually state this anywhere. Environment actually says you need to cast from within in its Benefit section. Supernal Verge makes the point only in the first bit, but it actually says so. Presumably, that's intended, but it could help to say so. <br /> <br /> Conceivably, some area Yantra effects could apply based off of the location of the target, though, rather than the caster. Still, skip area.<br /> <br /> Actions seem pretty clear all the way through.<br /> <br /> <i>Tools </i>are where intent becomes vague. Pretty sure that actually holding a tool was intended by &quot;use&quot; but that is far from clear. This applies to pretty much all of the Tools section. There's a bit of debate over whether or not a guy counts as Representational Yantra of himself. Reading that section, the only suggestion that such a maneuver might not work is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Mage: The Awakening 2nd Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...allowing the mage to build it into the Imago or access an Attainment to use her own sympathetic connection to the subject in order to cast across Space or Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, without any particulars on how specific &quot;use&quot; is supposed to be, we're left with a lot of calls by ear.<br /> <br /> Incense would be a sacrament, presumably. A wand should be waved around deliberately and appropriately for the spell, but couldn't be used if someone knocked it out of the mage's hand. A lucky coin might need to be flipped into the air, so somebody grabbing it could cancel it.<br /> None of those is very well-defined by the rules.<br /> <br /> If a player can argue that their wand is symbolic for a spell when it's in an enemy's hand should it still apply? <br /> <br /> I get why this is vague---authors didn't want to paint people into a corner---but it's a bit much. <br /> <br /> <b>What are valid conditions for Keys? </b><br /> <br /> There is almost no explanation in the Space section on the topic. Is there someplace that actually explains more?<br /> <br /> An example given is &quot;Those of my bloodline&quot;. &quot;Those who mean me well and are under their own control.&quot;---Would that be a 2 Potency Key? If I include &quot;Only open for people I want admitted.&quot; would that be legitimate? The clauses being limited by Potency is a good idea, but the scope of the clauses is not particularly defined, there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-19-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:50:04-07:00","id":989899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=989638#post989638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many times I find missing pop culture references is more benefit than problem.<br /> <br /> I met a former roommate's current roommates once and they asked if I knew what a fox said, so I explained their various calls. They went really weird and quiet as my former roommate busted up laughing. They showed me the music video and then spent about half an hour after listening to different fox calls.<br /> <br /> It was educational for all of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 Like<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=989638#post989638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm leaning towards making the legacy attainment improve on learning a later attainment that guarantees that the attainment has become redundant, but not using up that attainment to achieve it, but this seems like stretching or breaking the rules as stated. Alternately, you could word the attainment in such a way as to have it slide things over naturally. E.G. 1st Attainment improves the ability to see spirits and related phenomena without a spell by a step. If the mage normally requires deep scrutiny or an active spell to see a thing, it is now visible to Active Mage Sight If they normally can see something with Active Mage Sight, the attainment boosts that up to Peripheral Mage Sight, but with full clarity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help with your question, but the preview of &quot;Signs of Sorcery&quot; has a few Merits that enhance Mage Sight. Perhaps they'll be of interest:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\">Advanced Mage Sight Rules</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:17:12-07:00","id":990418,"title":"","content":"Are the origins of Atlantean dragons ever expanded upon? As far as where they are from, where they actually went, what their goals were, etc. The most I ever personally saw was speculation from other mages in books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:24:07-07:00","id":990425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990418#post990418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the origins of Atlantean dragons ever expanded upon? As far as where they are from, where they actually went, what their goals were, etc. The most I ever personally saw was speculation from other mages in books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Closest came in <i>Left Hand Path</i>. That wasn't much of an explanation or origin story.<br /> <br /> (Well, I suppose it's possible that I missed a reference in <i>Seers of the Throne</i>, <i>Silver Ladder</i>, or <i>Guardians of the Veil</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:43:05-07:00","id":990432,"title":"","content":"I kind of quietly ignore 90% of the Atlantis stuff from 1E, especially the core book, so I'm not sure whether they went into any detail there.<br /> <br /> However! I happen to know this because I was just reading the book. <i>Summoners</i> has an otherworldly creature (or category of creature?) called la Vouivre which may be related to the Atlantean dragons. Modern mages summon it so they can hunt and kill it and harvest its venom for Magic Heroin. Summoners is a good book, y'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:45:37-07:00","id":990434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990418#post990418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the origins of Atlantean dragons ever expanded upon? As far as where they are from, where they actually went, what their goals were, etc. The most I ever personally saw was speculation from other mages in books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in second edition, no. In fact, Second Edition is much more clear about the fact that Atlantis is a myth, and the Awakened City never existed in the reality the game takes place in. The Fall wasn't just the collapse of Atlantean civilization, it was a cosmological retcon that erased Atlantis and the entirety of the Time Before from history. So, the origins and fate of the dragons is largely academic. They never really existed, at least not in the version of history that Mages currently exist in. There weren't giant winged reptiles that walked the earth long ago and brought magic posthumously to the Atlanteans, but the story of the dragons is significant to Mages as a symbol of predecessors to the Awakened, who's being was one with magic, and existed in a time <i>before</i> the Time Before, to which modern Awakened owe their knowledge of magic.<br /> <br /> My pet answer, is that the dragons were to the Time Before as the Exarchs are to the current reality - sentient Supernal symbols which defined the laws of that reality, and may or may not have been Mages in a previous reality that was removed from history when they Ascended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:00:22-07:00","id":990446,"title":"","content":"What's the generally agreed upon reason for the Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> I'm going to guess that mages dismiss the whole Father Wolf thing out of hand, but I suppose it's possible. Do they just see it as evidence of the damage the Fall has caused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:07:57-07:00","id":990450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990446#post990446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the generally agreed upon reason for the Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> I'm going to guess that mages dismiss the whole Father Wolf thing out of hand, but I suppose it's possible. Do they just see it as evidence of the damage the Fall has caused?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would mages dismiss the Father Wolf story out of hand?<br /> <br /> Not every event of cosmological significance needs a supernal source or reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:20:59-07:00","id":990453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990450#post990450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would mages dismiss the Father Wolf story out of hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a far-fetched story with little evidence to support it that is held to be true mostly by beings that aren't well known to mages and even then there's a variety of different versions of it. And it happened so long ago that it, along with a number of other things from the period, aren't even mentioned or seem to be known by mages in modern days.<br /> <br /> Can you point me to where the question is answered?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not every event of cosmological significance needs a supernal source or reason. </div> </div> </div>I don't recall saying it did. It is an easy fallback, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:30:51-07:00","id":990457,"title":"","content":"&quot;Just so you know, 'This Story is True' is kinda just a werewolf figure of speech.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:42:36-07:00","id":990460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990453#post990453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's a far-fetched story with little evidence to support it that is held to be true mostly by beings that aren't well known to mages and even then there's a variety of different versions of it. And it happened so long ago that it, along with a number of other things from the period, aren't even mentioned or seem to be known by mages in modern days.<br /> <br /> Can you point me to where the question is answered?<br /> <br /> I don't recall saying it did. It is an easy fallback, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing that the myth is true, only questioning why it would be dismissed out of hand.<br /> <br /> As you acknowledge, no one alive really has any idea about what really happened and the supernatural rarely has easy or simple answers. In fact, Dark Eras even provides a canon basis for for the truth of the myth.<br /> <br /> Moreover, at least in 2e, it has been made clear that mages know that most mysterious phenomena have no supernal basis at all. Mages as a group would not use a supernal explanation as a &quot;fallback&quot; explanation for matters they might not understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:46:27-07:00","id":990462,"title":"","content":"I don't know as Mages have an agreed upon reason for the Gauntlet, any more than physicists have an agreed upon &quot;reason&quot; for gravity. It's just a phenomenon of the Fallen World, and they can describe exactly how that phenomenon works in terms of their models, but why it works the way it does is kind of beyond the scope of their inquiry. By th same logic that says modern Mages probably aren't aware Father Wolf actually existed, they probably also aren't aware there was actually time when there was no Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:48:03-07:00","id":990463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990434#post990434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in second edition, no. In fact, Second Edition is much more clear about the fact that Atlantis is a myth, and the Awakened City never existed in the reality the game takes place in. The Fall wasn't just the collapse of Atlantean civilization, it was a cosmological retcon that erased Atlantis and the entirety of the Time Before from history. So, the origins and fate of the dragons is largely academic. They never really existed, at least not in the version of history that Mages currently exist in. There weren't giant winged reptiles that walked the earth long ago and brought magic posthumously to the Atlanteans, but the story of the dragons is significant to Mages as a symbol of predecessors to the Awakened, who's being was one with magic, and existed in a time <i>before</i> the Time Before, to which modern Awakened owe their knowledge of magic.<br /> <br /> My pet answer, is that the dragons were to the Time Before as the Exarchs are to the current reality - sentient Supernal symbols which defined the laws of that reality, and may or may not have been Mages in a previous reality that was removed from history when they Ascended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you. I've yet to really dive much into 2E, so this is the kind of answer I was hoping for, in a way. Though, it does disappoint me in some regards as I (as a fantasy nerd) tend to like dragons.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:19:14-07:00","id":990476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990463#post990463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thank you. I've yet to really dive much into 2E, so this is the kind of answer I was hoping for, in a way. Though, it does disappoint me in some regards as I (as a fantasy nerd) tend to like dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some day I want to run a ChroD fantasy game set in the Time Before. It would be on the low-fantasy side, where things like elves and dwarves are these semi-mythical races that are thought to have existed long ago but died out. As I mentioned, ragons would occupy a similar conceptual space as Atlantis and the Exarchs do in the modern setting, as creatures from a mythical Time Before that left the world and became one with the Supernal, but in doing so made magic work the way it does now. Though, they would likely be seen as rather more benevolent than their eventual successors, sacrificing their physical existence to make magic accessible to all of humanity, rather than conquering the Supernal realms to take it for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:28:32-07:00","id":990479,"title":"","content":"I'd wind up making a lot of Exalted jokes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:20:00-07:00","id":990505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990479#post990479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wind up making a lot of Exalted jokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never played Exalted. Is it a lot like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:24:45-07:00","id":990508,"title":"","content":"Well, there are a bunch of dragons who kind of embody the building blocks of reality, and they are the source of the vast majority of Exalted's magic power. Albeit not the really powerful ones you generally play.<br /> <br /> I just kind of meant in general regarding the Time Before though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:28:46-07:00","id":990509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=990505#post990505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never played Exalted. Is it a lot like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I think he just meant that a fantasy game that takes place in the mythic prehistory time &quot;before&quot; the normal gamelines with added magic makes it a lot like Exalted. In the days of WoD when Exalted was new there was an implication that Exalted was the prehistory of the WoD, which could make it a parallel to CofD's Time Before.<br /> <br /> Every edition of Exalted is over-the-top fantasy action, much like Scion or Dudes of Legend. Not to say it's inherently silly: obviously White Wolf/Onyx Path wouldn't put anything out that didn't include some opportunity for heavy themes, in Exalted mostly about power, responsibility, cosmic rebellion, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:51:18-07:00","id":990517,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could do an Awakening version of Magma Kraken...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:08:17-07:00","id":990533,"title":"","content":"Neat! I guess you could make it kind of a &quot;New Exalted&quot; like ChroD was a &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;. I probably wouldn't though. I'd just make it something between a Fantasy Shard and an Atlantean Dark Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:19:38-07:00","id":990865,"title":"","content":"Maybe not a simple question, but in that case you can resend me in right direction.<br /> How you understate shooting penalty?<br /> Even when your cover is 3/4 (Head-sholders figure) enemy receive only -3 (yes, if he wont hit head itself he need add -3 for head). It's understandable - simplification is our all.<br /> But when it come for long range i lose the logic. When you need to hit fullheight target on fourth distant your mighty dicepool of 6 (from 8) reduced to zero. Even if you are sniper (my starter one can accumulate in aiming up to +7 dices).<br /> Do i understand correctly, that distants penalty sacrificed for sake of hitting target (and hitting specific part of target)?<br /> <br /> PS. Sorry for wrong number: i searched shooting penalty and this theme popup. I see that is a mage theme afterward. How to delete it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 10-21-2016, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:48:16-07:00","id":991031,"title":"","content":"If OP did an atlantean dark era, I'd prefer it as some kind of &quot;time vortex&quot; situation, set in a weird dimensional anomaly with a bunch of time periods all crashed together. I mean, actually setting something during Atlantis would be neat, but that would require major rule changes (it'd be pre-Abyss) and would force them to nail down a time, place, and nature for what Atlantis actually was, which I really don't think Second Edition would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:09:04-07:00","id":991040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991031#post991031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If OP did an atlantean dark era, I'd prefer it as some kind of &quot;time vortex&quot; situation, set in a weird dimensional anomaly with a bunch of time periods all crashed together. I mean, actually setting something during Atlantis would be neat, but that would require major rule changes (it'd be pre-Abyss) and would force them to nail down a time, place, and nature for what Atlantis actually was, which I really don't think Second Edition would do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, this would be a homebrew setting. I can't imagine Onyx Path ever doing an official Atlantean err... &quot;era&quot;... (I'm just gonna call it a shard cause &quot;era&quot; has connotations of being a historical period in post-Fall history), except <i>maybe</i> in a VII-style &quot;here are three sugggestions for what it might have been like&quot; kind of book. And even that is a huge maybe.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think a Time Before shard would necessarily require pinning down a time or place. It could be set at any time, since it's effectively in a completely different timeline than the one we live in, which makes a convenient excuse for the generic semi-medieval-european-ish-mishmash fantasy setting. And given that there were no Exarchs shaping the way the universe works, the Time Before may very well have had entiterly different geography, even entirely different laws of physics. It could have been, for all intents and purposes, a completely different universe. It also doesn't necessarily mean no Abyss. I mean, modern Mages think that the Abyss didn't exist in the Time Before and the Fall created it. But then, modern werewolves think the bane of silver didn't exist before the Sundering and it was punishment for killing Father Wolf. They were wrong, and they had the benefit of speculating about a time that actually happened in human history. Who's to say Mages aren't wrong about how they think things worked in the Time Before as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-21-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:19:18-07:00","id":991041,"title":"","content":"Honestly, any combination of those approaches would make for a pretty fun setting. I'd like some werewolf crossover stuff, too. It's interesting to note that while a lot of ChroD's cosmology is humanocentric, Werewolf is the biggest exception. And the humanocentricity isn't an inherent nature of the universe, it seems to be because humanity made such an impression on the metaphysical landscape of the cosmos with all their stories and dreams and sapience that they gave birth to all sorts of supernatural phenomena. It would be very interesting to set something before that period so we could do some stuff with the transition. That's been a major theme in Werewolf already- part of the background elements of the game is about how werewolves and their culture have had to adjust to humans taking over the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:49:56-07:00","id":991054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991041#post991041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, any combination of those approaches would make for a pretty fun setting. I'd like some werewolf crossover stuff, too. It's interesting to note that while a lot of ChroD's cosmology is humanocentric, Werewolf is the biggest exception. And the humanocentricity isn't an inherent nature of the universe, it seems to be because humanity made such an impression on the metaphysical landscape of the cosmos with all their stories and dreams and sapience that they gave birth to all sorts of supernatural phenomena. It would be very interesting to set something before that period so we could do some stuff with the transition. That's been a major theme in Werewolf already- part of the background elements of the game is about how werewolves and their culture have had to adjust to humans taking over the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. I'd definitely include werewolf crossover, which would draw a lot from the Sundered World Era; using the Border Marches instead of the Gauntlet, the lack of Tribes as we know them in the modern setting, etc. I'd actually really like to include a lot of Mummy influence as well, if I knew anything about Mummy. I joked about the generic medieval European fantasy setting, but I would actually prefer more of an ancient Egyptian influence. It would be a cool opportunity to reconcile the Iremite fivefold soul concept with the Awakened idea of the soul being made up of the five subtle Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:42:06-07:00","id":991128,"title":"","content":"Plotting something out.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever ran an encounter with an enemy or other NPC who could use Shifting Sands or another similar ability allowing themselves to basically go back in time with the awareness of how things are going to happen?<br /> <br /> Do you just 'gm it up,' have them seem to know the capabilities of the players? Or do you run it through, 'Forget the last two rounds,' and go back to where you were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:53:43-07:00","id":991138,"title":"","content":"Whatever approach you go for, you should always read JJBA before playing/STing a character with time powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:04:25-07:00","id":991160,"title":"","content":"Does Ban prevent entering from or to the Twilight or Shadow? Or moving through it in Twilight form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 10-21-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:39:45-07:00","id":991227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991160#post991160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Ban prevent entering from or to the Twilight or Shadow? Or moving through it in Twilight form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, when the Ban is encoded with Spirit and/or Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:17:38-07:00","id":991263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991160#post991160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Ban prevent entering from or to the Twilight or Shadow? Or moving through it in Twilight form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Space alone affects them, but the shift from the other world automatically permits a Clash of Wills.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Magic that manipulates space, like a teleportation power or the ability to step from one world to another... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:51:13-07:00","id":991273,"title":"","content":"To clarify: Twilight is a state of being, not a world. Beings in Twilight may not enter or exit the affected area and does not provoke a Clash of Wills if they try.<br /> Trying to enter the affected area from the Shadow provokes a Clash of Wills without any other Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T11:45:51-07:00","id":991463,"title":"","content":"Correspondence states that it lists sympathy connections through the lens of which the subject thinks of them. What if the subject doesn't think, such as the ring example given in it's reach effects? Or if the subject is a plant? How would these sympathy connections come through? Similarly, would correspondence reveal images with names defining them, or would it reveal what was the oldest and most important things to the subject (and if those things are there now?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:03:43-07:00","id":991605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991463#post991463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence states that it lists sympathy connections through the lens of which the subject thinks of them. What if the subject doesn't think, such as the ring example given in it's reach effects? Or if the subject is a plant? How would these sympathy connections come through? Similarly, would correspondence reveal images with names defining them, or would it reveal what was the oldest and most important things to the subject (and if those things are there now?)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of inanimate or non-sentient objects I'd have the sympathetic connections be defined by their function. For example: The ring's connection to the owner could be defined as &quot;Wearer&quot; while the plants connections could be &quot;Nourishment&quot; and/or &quot;Anchor&quot; about the soil it's planted in, or &quot;Host&quot; if the plant is parasitic.<br /> I don't understand what you mean with your last question so I can't try to answer it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:55:46-07:00","id":991667,"title":"","content":"*considers* Say that in the case of the plant, you used correspondence to get a tie to the plant's owner (however weak that may be). Would you then have enough information about the owner to target them sympathetically?<br /> <br /> A similar case to this question would be that say you used correspondence on a gun, and then found two sympathetic links defined as 'holder' and 'target'. The target is revealed to be the body next to you. Could you scry the 'holder' to determine who murdered a person? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:22:51-07:00","id":991682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991667#post991667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*considers* Say that in the case of the plant, you used correspondence to get a tie to the plant's owner (however weak that may be). Would you then have enough information about the owner to target them sympathetically?<br /> <br /> A similar case to this question would be that say you used correspondence on a gun, and then found two sympathetic links defined as 'holder' and 'target'. The target is revealed to be the body next to you. Could you scry the 'holder' to determine who murdered a person? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That could relate to if the weapon was oft used by the holder, but a quickly picked up and discarded firearm would have a poor link, if any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:12:00-07:00","id":991701,"title":"","content":"So I just came across the section for Aspiration in Mage 2E, and realized its says pick a new aspiration after the scene you complete it instead of the chapter.<br /> Was this a typo, or was it done on purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:47:07-07:00","id":991758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991682#post991682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That could relate to if the weapon was oft used by the holder, but a quickly picked up and discarded firearm would have a poor link, if any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems relevant: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: The Awakening - Second Edition, pg 172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...while a murder weapon retains links to both killer and victim for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T03:13:19-07:00","id":991791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991701#post991701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just came across the section for Aspiration in Mage 2E, and realized its says pick a new aspiration after the scene you complete it instead of the chapter.<br /> Was this a typo, or was it done on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Purpose!<br /> <br /> (characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:37:27-07:00","id":991926,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked before, but it's not clear to me from the core book wording. Can you convert your own mana to Essence using Spirit 2 (e.g., Channel Essence or some other spell) to offer it as a gift or bribe to a spirit? If not, what is the simplest way to give Essence willingly to a spirit or ephemeral entity?<br /> <br /> Also, is the Regeneration Numina an instant or reflexive action? If it is reflexive, can it be used multiple times per turn if in a combat or initiative situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:31:12-07:00","id":991948,"title":"","content":"Mana can't be converted to Essence without Prime+Spirit 4 (Or passing it to your familiar in which case the conversion is automatic). Note that when you channel Essence into yourself it doesn't convert the Essence into Mana, it just makes you a convenient storage place for Essence. If you have Essence in your Pattern you can use Channel Essence to give some or all of that Essence to a spirit. It's pretty easy to create Essence though, for instance, to create Fire Essence, you light a fire and then a spirit that consumes Fire Essence can harvest from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:40:19-07:00","id":991955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=991926#post991926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has been asked before, but it's not clear to me from the core book wording. Can you convert your own mana to Essence using Spirit 2 (e.g., Channel Essence or some other spell) to offer it as a gift or bribe to a spirit? If not, what is the simplest way to give Essence willingly to a spirit or ephemeral entity?<br /> <br /> Also, is the Regeneration Numina an instant or reflexive action? If it is reflexive, can it be used multiple times per turn if in a combat or initiative situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording of the spell only mentions drawing Essence into yourself and channeling Essence from yourself into something else. Nothing about converting Mana into Essence.<br /> <br /> The Regeneration Numen should be the same kind of action as all other Numina since nothing else is written. I assume it's an instant action, but I can't find anything about what kind of action the activation of a Numen actually is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:12:49-07:00","id":991978,"title":"","content":"Channel Essence just says &quot;from a resonant condition&quot;. You know what's generally got the Resonant condition? <i>Literally Everything.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:46:50-07:00","id":991993,"title":"","content":"When someone aims a spell, instead of using sensory range, it says it usually manifests as a bolt of energy and the like.<br /> <br /> Is there a possibility that one such bolt could be ricocheted or hit back toward the caster?<br /> <br /> Assuming it can happen, my thoughts are on it being in a scene where two Arrows play a game of table tennis with a spell in bolt form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:08:10-07:00","id":992084,"title":"","content":"What does adamas look like? I have it in my head that it's like perfected diamond - its immutability suggested that to me - but I don't remember anything from an official source one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:43:28-07:00","id":992280,"title":"","content":"I think I remember it described as marble with cristal veins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:18:55-07:00","id":992313,"title":"","content":"Ooh, sweet, okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:42:21-07:00","id":993610,"title":"","content":"Can Mind Patterning transform your entire body into psychic ephemera?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:55:22-07:00","id":993619,"title":"","content":"You would think so, but the Patterning spell Psychic Projection specifically leaves your body comatose. I suppose it makes sense that Mind would affect the mind only, not the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:34:26-07:00","id":993634,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure anything where you turn stuff covered by one arcarnum to stuff covered by the other generally requires both. There are some loopholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:22:03-07:00","id":993663,"title":"","content":"Yea. Its some kind of deeper principle I guess. Death can turn you into shadow but Matter needs life to grant you iron skin (or bunsen burner in mouth). Why is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:45:15-07:00","id":993674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=993619#post993619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would think so, but the Patterning spell Psychic Projection specifically leaves your body comatose. I suppose it makes sense that Mind would affect the mind only, not the body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet Death allows you to physically enter Twilight with a Weaving spell, which is the same as becoming ephemera. I find that to be a bit inconsistent since all three ephemeral Arcana (Death, Mind, and Spirit) should have the same effects on ephemera, Essence and Twilight relating to their purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:50:35-07:00","id":993678,"title":"","content":"Technically Spirit can also turn you into Ephemera on it's own, because that's what happens if you enter the shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:02:07-07:00","id":993689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=993674#post993674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet Death allows you to physically enter Twilight with a Weaving spell, which is the same as becoming ephemera. I find that to be a bit inconsistent since all three ephemeral Arcana (Death, Mind, and Spirit) should have the same effects on ephemera, Essence and Twilight relating to their purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind not being able to give goetia the ability to Materialize is not inconsistent with the way goetia work and I can see no reason the reverse should be the case that is not wholly rooted in arbitrary symmetry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T02:10:21-07:00","id":993943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=993689#post993689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind not being able to give goetia the ability to Materialize is not inconsistent with the way goetia work and I can see no reason the reverse should be the case that is not wholly rooted in arbitrary symmetry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe you are right with Mind Ephemera but changing into thought or memory and nesting yourself in somebody's mind should be perfectly doable. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T02:43:55-07:00","id":993950,"title":"","content":"You'd have to use Mind+Life or start in a different Twilight State and then use the corresponding Mind+Death/Spirit to pull it off. Although what you just described sounds more like hiding out in someone's Oneiros, which still leaves your body behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:38:28-07:00","id":993962,"title":"","content":"I think that we at some point talked about entering Astral with body and pros/cons of it. The question is still: Why Death doesn't need Life to change subject into shadow? It doesn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:47:29-07:00","id":993967,"title":"","content":"I think it's because you're not actually changing them <i>into</i> anything. Twilight is a frequency of existence. They're not becoming a ghost or a spirit, they're still a human, just out of sync with material reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:48:57-07:00","id":993968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=993962#post993962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that we at some point talked about entering Astral with body and pros/cons of it. The question is still: Why Death doesn't need Life to change subject into shadow? It doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea, it makes no sense to me either and I intend to run it requiring Life 4 as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:56:40-07:00","id":993969,"title":"","content":"That would make it a Life spell requiring conjunctional Death 3. Does that feel right to you?<br /> <br /> Actually looking at it, the key difference is when the target is a conscious entity. Shifting inanimate stuff <i>does</i> require matter 4, plus 3 in whatever frequency you aim at, and is listed under matter. <br /> <br /> But making a human ephemeral requires just death or just spirit, and making an ephemeral solid likewise requires just death or just spirit, except for goetia who also require mind, and that's because they can't manifest themselves otherwise it would just need mind on it's own, probably. <br /> <br /> It seems a consistent rule of magic: Entities can just flip between matter and ephemera. It's not something you need another arcarnum to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-27-2016, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T04:08:12-07:00","id":993973,"title":"","content":"Life 3 and Death 3 would allow to transport properties of shadow to living object (e.g. flatness, being hurt with light, &quot;floating&quot;) but not entirely. Patterning of both is required to change living into shadow entirely with one spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T08:44:44-07:00","id":994037,"title":"","content":"Will there are simple rules for sorcerers? Or use Grimoire rules for sleepwalkers?<br /> <br /> I ask about rules where sleepwalkers can cast a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T08:47:08-07:00","id":994039,"title":"","content":"If you want Sleepwalkers who can cast a spell, you either want Proximi who are born with some magic, or magic items. Anyone can use Imbued Items, and there's a merit that lets sleepwalkers use Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T08:53:56-07:00","id":994048,"title":"","content":"If you just want hedge magic the psychic merits do a pretty good job doubling for those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:10:27-07:00","id":994139,"title":"","content":"Can Arcana Attainments be applied to Legacy Attainments? For instance, could an 11th Question use Sympathetic Range for their &quot;Postcognition&quot; Attainment? Could they use Time in a Bottle to extend the Duration of their &quot;Shaping&quot; Attainment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:30:40-07:00","id":994160,"title":"","content":"For Sympathy I think the answer is yes, but Reach has to be spent to make the attainment function at Sensory Range. Remember Potency is fixed at either your arcana rating or half that depending on Primary factor so depending on the attainment it might never be a viable option for Sympathetic use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:10:06-07:00","id":994211,"title":"","content":"Do grimoires reveal their nature through Active or Focused Mage Sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:18:04-07:00","id":994213,"title":"","content":"It's an active spell, so yes. If the spell is made Lasting, you're still imprinting Mana into the world. Even if that weren't the case, I'd still say yes for drama's sake, too, since it means Sleepers can degrade grimoires into worthless gibberish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:48:23-07:00","id":996360,"title":"","content":"Normally, when you use Corridors of Time you can only send a target back on its own timeline, and temporal Sympathy doesn't &quot;web&quot; like spatial Sympathy does because Sympathy is maintained between a target and its past selves. Do you think it's possible though to alter your own temporal Sympathy sufficiently to be able to send yourself back in time in someone else's place? Say you have a friend Jim, who's 90, and you're only 30, can you beg, borrow or steal his temporal Sympathy, apply it to youself, and then cast Corridors of Time to go back to when Jim was 20? If you do, who is affected by changes you made in the past? Do you go back and inhabit Jim's 20 year old self, or is his presence temporarily annihilated by yours? Can you think of any other obvious repercussions? What level of Time would this take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:07:55-07:00","id":996367,"title":"","content":"I'd say that's normally beyond Time mastery, but I love the idea, Mrmdubois. It's <i>just</i> stretching sympathy, though.<br /> Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:17:12-07:00","id":996371,"title":"","content":"I say you could combined cast it with Possession, and all the restrictions that has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:59:22-07:00","id":996429,"title":"","content":"How many ranking officials are there on a given Consilium for a large city?<br /> <br /> The core book gives some suggestions, and maybe I'm overthinking this, but it says &quot;Traditionally there are four or five Councilors in addition to the Hierarch, and each Path has a single representative.&quot; Does that mean the 4-5 Councilors are all generally representatives from different Paths, or are there 4-5 Councilors + another 5 Councilors who are appointed based on their Path? Also, is there traditionally just one Herald, Sentinel, and Interfector per Consilium, or can there be multiple of those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:05:11-07:00","id":996432,"title":"","content":"In 2e, (non-Legacy) Attainments seem to be something you simply gain once you hit the appropriate level of expertise. So, the secrets of Sympathetic Range do not need to be revealed to you or discovered via trial and error upon attaining Space 2 - you know that attainment immediate. Is that correct?<br /> <br /> Does that mean there are no Attainments that are the result of secret training among the Wise outside of Legacy Attainments? In other words, all non-legacy attainments are universally common attainments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:43:48-07:00","id":996444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=996429#post996429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many ranking officials are there on a given Consilium for a large city?<br /> <br /> The core book gives some suggestions, and maybe I'm overthinking this, but it says &quot;Traditionally there are four or five Councilors in addition to the Hierarch, and each Path has a single representative.&quot; Does that mean the 4-5 Councilors are all generally representatives from different Paths, or are there 4-5 Councilors + another 5 Councilors who are appointed based on their Path? Also, is there traditionally just one Herald, Sentinel, and Interfector per Consilium, or can there be multiple of those?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keeping in mind this is my understanding from 1e, but I believe what it's saying here is that the traditional setup is one of the following:<br /> <br /> 1) A Hierarch (1), plus a Counciler (4 total) for each path that is not already taken by the Hierarch's path for a total of 5 Mages.<br /> 2) One Counciler for each path (5 total) plus a Hierarch (1), who can be of any path for a total of 6 Mages.<br /> <br /> I believe there can be more than one herald or sentinel, but the traditionally there is only one Interfactor at a time in a consilum. I say at a time, because sometimes it's one Guardian who serves as a dedicated, full-time Interfactor, but in some Consiliums it is a responsibility that rotates between multiple Guardians, so that no one Guardian has to bear the burden of the sins an Interfactor must commit alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:05:00-07:00","id":996450,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> There's 4-5 Councilors total, and each one (potentially including the Hierarch) represents one Path. There's no Order requirement unless the Consilium is especially egalitarian.<br /> <br /> There are as many of the other offices as you like, depending on the size and volatility of the Consilium. Listing 3 or 4 Sentinels and Heralds by name and leaving room to introduce more in play is a pretty safe and common approach. In the games I've played there's usually just one Interfector (at least officially/ritually), but the 2E writeup doesn't suggest this is a requirement. Fun fact: the chapter fiction in the 2E book is partially about an Interfector and gives a picture of what their job involves.<br /> <br /> A large number of Heralds might suggest a disorganized and widespread Consilium where every Herald only knows a few people well. A lot of Sentinels suggests a serious problem with magical crime, or a paranoid Council. A lot of Interfectors suggests a Council that actively enforces its will on its constituents and has a good rapport with the Guardians.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar358_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"358\" data-vbnamecard=\"358\">EmanantVolition</a> Yeah, I think the listed Arcana Attainments are inherently things you learn by virtue of learning Space 2 or whatever. It's just a thing you can do now.<br /> <br /> There aren't any such secret Attainments listed, but I don't see why they couldn't exist. If you wanted to make custom Arcana attainments, I would price them the same as Legacy attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:05:46-07:00","id":996964,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to grant Goetia Manifestations/Manifestation Conditions other than Familiar and Materialized (from Goetic Summons, Add Death 2 or Spirit 2)?<br /> <br /> It hit me that it would be interesting to see a Walker from the Temenos possess the person it's based on, but that only works if it can be granted or forced into the Possessed Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:24:16-07:00","id":996973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=996964#post996964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to grant Goetia Manifestations/Manifestation Conditions other than Familiar and Materialized (from Goetic Summons, Add Death 2 or Spirit 2)?<br /> <br /> It hit me that it would be interesting to see a Walker from the Temenos possess the person it's based on, but that only works if it can be granted or forced into the Possessed Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Astral Realms, that's just a thing that happens sometimes without Mage intervention, in 2E especially in Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> I assume that you can use a Mind 4 spell to recreate the effects of Bind Spirit/Revenant with Goetia, or maybe it requires a Mind 4 requisite for those spells and can't be done with Mind alone. Astral Realms has some artifacts and imbued items that you could adapt to 2E which bring goetia into the physical world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:37:43-07:00","id":996979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=996973#post996973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Astral Realms, that's just a thing that happens sometimes without Mage intervention, in 2E especially in Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> I assume that you can use a Mind 4 spell to recreate the effects of Bind Spirit/Revenant with Goetia, or maybe it requires a Mind 4 requisite for those spells and can't be done with Mind alone. Astral Realms has some artifacts and imbued items that you could adapt to 2E which bring goetia into the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read some more and found that Bind Spirit has &quot;Add Death or Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: The spell\u2019s effects extend to ghosts or Goetia.&quot;<br /> So I think Spirit is intended to be the primary Arcanum for handling the ephemeral part of ephemeral entities. I'm not fond of that, but I think I understand the reasoning behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:55:40-07:00","id":997026,"title":"","content":"Revenant (Death 4) also has optional Mind 4 to affect Goetia and can grant any one Manifestation per each dot of Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T01:58:54-07:00","id":997053,"title":"","content":"Mind 4 has Possession, if cast on a goetia it would presumably skip the Manifestation rules entirely to shove it into a target and follow the rules of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:14:00-07:00","id":997074,"title":"","content":"Hmm. The way Possession is worded makes it clear it's the caster that possesses the victim. I wonder if a Prime spell can change who's considered the caster for the purpose of spell effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:30:26-07:00","id":997078,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Prime is necessary for this effect. Just increase the target factor to include giver and receiver of consciousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:38:07-07:00","id":997081,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd have a hard time convincing my ST the same, but it's technically not possible unless I've missed some obscure passage in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:49:24-07:00","id":997082,"title":"","content":"Why is it not possible? The thing is that the book has limited word count and the spell is described this way because it allows to spend mana - since you have to be a mage. But nothing stops you from throwing some reach on it and possessing 5 people at a time. If you want to you can say that only the caster can spend mana to boost the spell as described and add reach effect to take even that away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:00:08-07:00","id":997086,"title":"","content":"Spending Mana is not a prerequisite of casting the spell. What I mean is by RAW it's not possible since the possessor is clearly defined as not being a subject of the spell, meaning changes to the scale factor does not grant the ability to change who the possessor is. That said it could be possible to redefine the possessor as a subject with a Reach option. In that case you'd be required to up the scale factor unless the subject is going to possess themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:11:21-07:00","id":997089,"title":"","content":"The mana is a prerequisite of using the effects of the spell other than possession. Yes, you are correct and by RAW the spell works in a very non flexible way but there is whole chapter about creative thaumaturgy that states what are RAI. Of course you can say that it is what it is and unless you are a master you can't grant possession to someone else buut... look at all this hubris. It's beautiful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:37:21-07:00","id":998471,"title":"","content":"Lets say that you have some kind of artifact or spell that allows to see spirits in Twilight. Would it be possible to cast spells on them remotely and/or via sympathy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:51:11-07:00","id":998477,"title":"","content":"You can always cast sympathetically whether or not you can perceive the target provided you can fulfill all requirements for sympathetic targeting. If the spell or artifact allows you to look directly into Twilight it's sensory range. If the spell or artifact allows you to look into Twilight through some sort of lens or viewport it's remote casting since you're not perceiving the target directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:06:46-07:00","id":998485,"title":"","content":"1. But spirits are immaterial for you if you are not ephemeral too. You need 2 dots of Spirit to touch them. Wouldn't it be a Reach effect to this spell that allows you to cast spells on them? Because, you know, you can't e.g conjure an ephemeral fire inside of them alone with Forces.<br /> Also:<br /> 2. Im wondering. Can you walk inside a burning building unharmed if you are ephemeral?<br /> 3. Is it possible to cast a spell past The Gountlet with Space alone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:47:18-07:00","id":998500,"title":"","content":"1: You don't need to be able to touch whatever it is you're targeting if you don't cast at the touch range. Certain effects however might not have any effect on ephemeral entities. You can't burn something that is affected by fire, but you can teleport it someplace else with Space without a problem as long as you can target it.<br /> 2: Yes. Being ephemeral makes you immune to all physical effects.<br /> 3: Yes, Withstood by the Gauntlet Strength. You'd have to cast either sympathetically or via remote viewing since effects that allows you to see through the Gauntlet functions like a lens or viewport in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:53:14-07:00","id":998504,"title":"","content":"You need the Spirit (or Death or Mind) Arcanum to create something directly in Twilight, but not to target something that already is in Twilight. A Forces fire is not ephemeral in nature so it's not affecting ephemeral entities as long as they don't materialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:48:39-07:00","id":998547,"title":"","content":"If I'm using my dedicated tool to get the paradox break and the yantra bonus for using a tool does it count as one yantra or two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:08:34-07:00","id":998557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=998547#post998547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm using my dedicated tool to get the paradox break and the yantra bonus for using a tool does it count as one yantra or two?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two, I think. I use a similar example for my character(Silver Pen that's Dedicated. 3 Yantras in one!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:12:17-07:00","id":998603,"title":"","content":"Essentially always, using a Yantra in multiple ways requires a slot per, but in this case, you are using a dedicated tool as a dedicated tool and a path or order tool.<br /> There actually is a case to be made that those tool bonuses stack. The use section itself suggests that you can use it as both in the description of the effect.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning 2, but I'd certainly not mind running it either way unless I discovered abuse from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:35:36-07:00","id":998836,"title":"","content":"The book says &quot;Using a Dedicated tool as a Yantra penalizes any Paradox dice pool by \u20132&quot;. It doesn't say that a mage can choose to forego the dice bonus it would provide to get that instead, it just does it whenever it's used as a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:59:37-07:00","id":998873,"title":"","content":"I've been pondering Mage Sight some and am a bit stuck on Deep Information. Specifically, the revelation of how the arcanum used is related to the Mystery.<br /> <br /> The example in the book mention a vampire's ghoul and Death Sight to reveal Deep Information about the undead blood in their system, as well as any powers the ghoul has gained from its presence. It also has the example of Fate Sight revealing that the powers of the fae are drawn from mystical bargains.<br /> <br /> My problem is the question of sorting out how much detail to reveal. For example, I've got a character scrutinizing a werewolf using Life and Spirit Sights. On its surface, this seems relatively straight-forward; revealing the shapeshifting and healing powers of werewolves, and perhaps that they contain essence. Yet I find myself wondering about more specific elements of this. For example, would it detect that werewolves can only change into certain forms? Would it detect that they are hurt by some material more than others? That said material is silver? Would it reveal that they have Gifts and, if so, would it say what those Gifts are? Would it show that the can slip between the Shadow and fleshy reality?<br /> <br /> How deep, in other words, does Deep Information go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:07:03-07:00","id":998884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=998873#post998873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been pondering Mage Sight some and am a bit stuck on Deep Information. Specifically, the revelation of how the arcanum used is related to the Mystery.<br /> <br /> The example in the book mention a vampire's ghoul and Death Sight to reveal Deep Information about the undead blood in their system, as well as any powers the ghoul has gained from its presence. It also has the example of Fate Sight revealing that the powers of the fae are drawn from mystical bargains.<br /> <br /> My problem is the question of sorting out how much detail to reveal. For example, I've got a character scrutinizing a werewolf using Life and Spirit Sights. On its surface, this seems relatively straight-forward; revealing the shapeshifting and healing powers of werewolves, and perhaps that they contain essence. Yet I find myself wondering about more specific elements of this. For example, would it detect that werewolves can only change into certain forms? Would it detect that they are hurt by some material more than others? That said material is silver? Would it reveal that they have Gifts and, if so, would it say what those Gifts are? Would it show that the can slip between the Shadow and fleshy reality?<br /> <br /> How deep, in other words, does Deep Information go?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might say it depends on what Arcanum you Scrutinize with. Spirit might tell you about their Gifts, Essence, Banes, etc. where Life would tell you more about their regeneration and shapeshifting. Death might show you that their souls seem to be covered in elaborate scarification patters, whereas Prime might reveal the meaning of their Renown brands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:27:16-07:00","id":998887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=998836#post998836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says &quot;Using a Dedicated tool as a Yantra penalizes any Paradox dice pool by \u20132&quot;. It doesn't say that a mage can choose to forego the dice bonus it would provide to get that instead, it just does it whenever it's used as a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The full quote is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Effect: Using a Dedicated tool as a Yantra penalizes any<br /> Paradox dice pool by \u20132; the mage can also use it as a Path or<br /> Order tool. </div> </div> </div>Which, combined with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To reflect this,<br /> the number of Yantras she can apply to a given spellcasting pool<br /> is limited by her Gnosis. If she uses one ritual item in many ways,<br /> each individual use counts as one Yantra for this limit. </div> </div> </div>seems like two to me. It seems like the object can be a Dedicated tool and a Path (or Order) tool at the same time, and you choose which to use it as each time you use it. So if you use it as a Dedicated tool, you get the -2 to Paradox dice pools. You can then also use it as a Path or Order tool if it qualifies, taking an additional Yantra slot. You could also just use it as a Path or Order tool for a particular casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:43:08-07:00","id":998918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=998884#post998884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might say it depends on what Arcanum you Scrutinize with. Spirit might tell you about their Gifts, Essence, Banes, etc. where Life would tell you more about their regeneration and shapeshifting. Death might show you that their souls seem to be covered in elaborate scarification patters, whereas Prime might reveal the meaning of their Renown brands.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much do you think it should share, do you think? I don't feel like Mage Sight should give an exhaustive list of Gifts. Should it describe that they have Banes or say what they are? Would Life Sight tell you <i>what</i> they turn into or merely that they can shapeshift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:56:27-07:00","id":998926,"title":"","content":"Well, the big &quot;WOLF&quot; symbol floating around them is probably a big clue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:13:41-07:00","id":998931,"title":"","content":"Unless they are in Hishu, then things get muddier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:36:25-07:00","id":998958,"title":"","content":"With Life, you might still see them in dalu, or even a smaller form of gauru. I think you end up using both your visions with Mage Sight, so with spirit you might get a sense of 'hunter,' however that may be projected to the mage. I'd really suggest any 'wolf' imagery be muddied, if you want to stick to Werewolf the Forsaken lore, as 'wolf' and 'human' are just masks for the Hunter. Plus there's abilities that allow for deviation of the standard five forms. That might be the type of thing that would only come up after long scrutiny, though.<br /> <br /> I don't believe you'd get a list of Gifts, but Spirit would, providing you could watch them long enough, let you read a lot about a werewolf. You might be able to make out their Renown Brands, and what they're for. Gift Marks and Renown Brands tell a story about a werewolf, and reading them would probably give you a general idea of it's history. It might just be as simple as, 'They're considered a glorious warrior among the spirits.' Or, 'Marks carved into her soul describe aspects of the woman, claiming they're a cunning and wise hunter, who defeated the Crimson Tenth and imprisoned the Host of the Killing Word.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T01:58:06-08:00","id":999127,"title":"","content":"I would say that the presence of gifts as a class of native spiritual ability can be perceived with Life and Spirit scrutiny together. Specific counts would be a separate mystery about that particular wolf and would require studying other werewolves to see which patterns are common, and so forth.<br /> <br /> As to wolf, well, yeah, that should shine through along with the moon. Hints of totem and auspice should be visible, too. Those should only require Spirit. That there is a lunar tie related to what it is would be part of the basic mystery about a werewolf, say, with the mysteries of shapechange and so forth revealed as new, deeper mysteries suggested by the answers.<br /> <br /> That seems about right. Don't want to hold out or fold too early on the revelations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T05:21:21-08:00","id":999176,"title":"","content":"Scrutiny is supposed to be an pretty difficult when using more than one arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:24:13-08:00","id":999186,"title":"","content":"Also you wouldn't get a list of gifts so much as a general gist of what sort of stuff those gifts let them do, at most. <br /> <br /> If a werewolf knows the Gift of Strength, then the mage would perceive channels in his essence that provide spiritual power to reinforce his muscles. If they had the Gift of Insight they might instead perceive a lupine-looking third eye. It's up to them to figure out what all that means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:28:09-08:00","id":999260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=998547#post998547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm using my dedicated tool to get the paradox break and the yantra bonus for using a tool does it count as one yantra or two?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, a Yantra bonus is always a dice bonus. That's what a Yantra IS, mechanically speaking. A dedicated magical tool, the way I see it, is a Yantra (=bonus dice) with an extra benefit. Said benefit does not count against the Yantra limit, it's an add-on.<br /> <br /> An official confirmation either way would be greatly appreciated, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:45:10-08:00","id":999269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=999260#post999260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, a Yantra bonus is always a dice bonus. That's what a Yantra IS, mechanically speaking. A dedicated magical tool, the way I see it, is a Yantra (=bonus dice) with an extra benefit. Said benefit does not count against the Yantra limit, it's an add-on.<br /> <br /> An official confirmation either way would be greatly appreciated, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use of a sympathetic yantra to cast sympathetically does not add any bonus dice. The same thing probably applies when &quot;breaking in&quot; a new dedicated tool or you'd be stuck with the limited options of path and order tools for a dedicated tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:53:28-08:00","id":999274,"title":"","content":"They way I read the rules is that you need to use your dedicated tool as two yantras to gain both benefits. A rule that has flown straight out the window in my group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T03:45:34-08:00","id":1000201,"title":"","content":"Do Legacy Attainments suffer from &quot;spell control&quot;? Or are you capable of maintaining multiple instance of each Attainment's effect? e.g. If I had a Legacy with Forge Destiny as its 5th Attainment, will I be able to have multiple instances of it at active at once? Such as one for each member of your Cabal, and then perhaps using it for other people as a bargaining chip or gift which can be granted to even Sleepers?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, does Magical removal/suppression of memories before the end of the scene and the onset of Quiescence save a Sleeper witness from suffering a Breaking Point, as the memories would otherwise be scoured from his mind by the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Clarity of Expression 11-08-2016, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:09:04-08:00","id":1000209,"title":"","content":"Attainments, any attainment, don't count toward spell control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:51:18-08:00","id":1001414,"title":"","content":"What are the initial sympathetic ties of a freshly written rote added to a grimoire with Scribe Grimoire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:56:13-08:00","id":1001415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1000201#post1000201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, does Magical removal/suppression of memories before the end of the scene and the onset of Quiescence save a Sleeper witness from suffering a Breaking Point, as the memories would otherwise be scoured from his mind by the Abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope: Quiescence doesn't remove the memory, it alters it so that &quot;magic&quot; isn't the cause of things. It's still traumatic and potentially world-altering though. Even if the memory is suppressed, the person will still be left with whatever Condition they'll have: they'll be left feeling Shaken but they can't understand why, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:10:02-08:00","id":1001422,"title":"","content":"Is the Arcadia from Changeling and Arcadia in the Supernal Realm one and the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:49:05-08:00","id":1001435,"title":"","content":"No. <br /> <br /> Ten characters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:03:43-08:00","id":1001449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001422#post1001422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Arcadia from Changeling and Arcadia in the Supernal Realm one and the same?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakenin