e Gnosis 2+ could still think they are literally the same place.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:45:50-08:00","id":1001503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001414#post1001414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the initial sympathetic ties of a freshly written rote added to a grimoire with Scribe Grimoire?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage gets weak sympathy towards the subject of their spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001422#post1001422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Arcadia from Changeling and Arcadia in the Supernal Realm one and the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short explanation: Officially they're not connected, but I don't think giving them a connection goes against any written material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:07:27-08:00","id":1001640,"title":"","content":"Can a Supernal entity be summoned into the Astral?<br /> Can there be Artifacts which exist within the Astral (perhaps left by the aforementioned Supernal visitor)?<br /> What is the extent of the <i>Daimon</i>'s power? Would it be wise to consider it as being a Goetia of Rank equal to Gnosis with Influence (Oneiros) at an equivalent level?<br /> Information on the Temenos references travel within it as being a game of association, however does the lack of information about travel within the Oneiros mean it is as being a simple as willing yourself into another scene? Can the Daimon use its Influence to stop this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:29:40-08:00","id":1001646,"title":"","content":"Has anyone yet created an unofficial update of the House of Ariadne Legacy to Second Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T01:16:49-08:00","id":1001668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001640#post1001640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Supernal entity be summoned into the Astral?<br /> Can there be Artifacts which exist within the Astral (perhaps left by the aforementioned Supernal visitor)?<br /> What is the extent of the <i>Daimon</i>'s power? Would it be wise to consider it as being a Goetia of Rank equal to Gnosis with Influence (Oneiros) at an equivalent level?<br /> Information on the Temenos references travel within it as being a game of association, however does the lack of information about travel within the Oneiros mean it is as being a simple as willing yourself into another scene? Can the Daimon use its Influence to stop this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd let you summon Supernal entities to the Astral, but I don't think there's a canon answer.<br /> <br /> There are Astral artifacts, yeah. A daimon's rank probably still caps out at 5 for non-archmasters so I'd make it Gnosis/2. It's Influence (It can have Oneiros) who ups increase accordingly. Technically, everything that happens in the Astral is just an act of will that just looks like taking action, Astral travel looks like that. You move through a scene, find an exit with a promising association and then move through it. A Daimon could stop you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T03:45:53-08:00","id":1001702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001640#post1001640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the extent of the <i>Daimon</i>'s power? Would it be wise to consider it as being a Goetia of Rank equal to Gnosis with Influence (Oneiros) at an equivalent level?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Daimons have Influence: Oneiros 3 for their own Oneiros. They also have Influences for the same Arcana as their Mage at the same levels. I.e. a Moros with Matter 3, Death 2 and Time 1 will have a Daimon with the following Influences: Oneiros 3, Matter 3, Death 2 and Time 1. On top of that it also has the same Arcana as Numina. It can cast every spell that the Mage can cast (rolling Power+Finesse) including Rotes (which in 2E I guess would be represented by adding the Mage's Mudra as a bonus to the roll). Mana is substituted with Essence if the casting calls for it. Since it's Numina and not actual Arcana I guess they get unlimited Reach since they never cause Paradox.<br /> Rank seems to be set at 2 in all the examples, but I think Rank 3 is a bit more appropriate. Especially for people with Gnosis 6+ despite Rank not being directly tied to Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T04:30:09-08:00","id":1001711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001646#post1001646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone yet created an unofficial update of the House of Ariadne Legacy to Second Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Troy took a stab at it: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=896338#post896338\">Link</a><br /> <br /> Also, Dave gave us this snippet:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929912#post929912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, the House of Ariadne were a Seer Legacy that had a Diamond-based offshoot appear via stolen soul stones. (Why should such things always be portrayed as going the other way? This isn't Masquerade's Antitribu)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:21:23-08:00","id":1001749,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, i'm new on the forums here and i have a couple of rule questions about 2ed awakening:<br /> <br /> 1) if a mage with forces hurls a classical AOE fireball, everyone caught in the blast suffer full potency (before armors, spell, whatever), right?<br /> Then, if a mage with life buffs a stat in an area, everyone gets the full potency buff (So the spell potency is copied on every subject because of area) or the mage must divide the potency between targets inside the area?<br /> <br /> 2) If a mage with life casts body control like this:<br /> Gnosis 3<br /> Life 2<br /> +3 medicine because of rote<br /> +2 Mudra bonus<br /> +1 another yantra<br /> <br /> Total dice: 11<br /> <br /> Then uses 1 free reach for advanced duration, steps it to 1 week duration (because of the arcanum -1 primary factor rule) and subtracts 10 dice to get +5 potency (to a total of +6) and rolls a success with the only dice left, he gets a +5 in everything listed in the spell without limits even if it is only ruling practice?<br /> I mean, in 1ed tome of mysteries told that ruling could not grant more than a +2/+3, if i'm not mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:47:04-08:00","id":1001754,"title":"","content":"Yes, if you target an area it effects everyone in an area including allies or enemies.<br /> <br /> Your reading of Body Control appears correct, limits on Ruling from Tome of the Mysteries are defunct as it's from 1e and this is 2e. By the way, you could spend WP on that spell and roll 4 dice instead of just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:54:33-08:00","id":1001757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001754#post1001754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if you target an area it effects everyone in an area including allies or enemies.<br /> <br /> Your reading of Body Control appears correct, limits on Ruling from Tome of the Mysteries are defunct as it's from 1e and this is 2e. By the way, you could spend WP on that spell and roll 4 dice instead of just one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the fast answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, it is correct to gain a +6 in everything the spell lists? And, moreover, everyone in an aoe cast would actually receive the same potency effect?<br /> And the aoe cast does no more need to have a dot higher than the level of the spell the mage wishes to cast like in 1ed? (i remember that a mage needed life 3 to cas a life 2 spell with aoe)<br /> <br /> Sorry if I repeat myself but i'd like to be 100% sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:43:25-08:00","id":1001775,"title":"","content":"Yup, that's correct. I just noticed though you haven't assigned any dice penalties to increase Scale. So your friends would have to come in for a group hug to be able to effect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:56:57-08:00","id":1001783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001775#post1001775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, that's correct. I just noticed though you haven't assigned any dice penalties to increase Scale. So your friends would have to come in for a group hug to be able to effect them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but they are already willing to do that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:22:57-08:00","id":1001801,"title":"","content":"Another question about a massive Time spell a player of mine (who min maxed a lot but does not know that it will backfire greatly) casted (then i'm done for today, i swear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> He did this:<br /> Casted Time 3 Acceleration in order to boost his dodge.<br /> His base defense is 5 (min maxed, ofc) + Time Armor (3) = 8.<br /> Added then weaponry (instead of athletics because of defensive combat merit) -&gt; +5 (Always min maxed) = 13<br /> Acceleration potency -&gt; 5<br /> For a total of 18 defense.<br /> <br /> As per dodge defense, he then multiplied by 2, gaining 36 dodge dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> A part being massive, did he everything according to rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:33:30-08:00","id":1001806,"title":"","content":"Not sure, but I can tell you it doesn't matter. Bigger dice pools start to see diminishing returns in successes rolled, and there are lots of ways to get around a high Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:41:14-08:00","id":1001811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001801#post1001801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question about a massive Time spell a player of mine (who min maxed a lot but does not know that it will backfire greatly) casted (then i'm done for today, i swear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> He did this:<br /> Casted Time 3 Acceleration in order to boost his dodge.<br /> His base defense is 5 (min maxed, ofc) + Time Armor (3) = 8.<br /> Added then weaponry (instead of athletics because of defensive combat merit) -&gt; +5 (Always min maxed) = 13<br /> Acceleration potency -&gt; 5<br /> For a total of 18 defense.<br /> <br /> As per dodge defense, he then multiplied by 2, gaining 36 dodge dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> A part being massive, did he everything according to rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>What, no +1 Reach on Acceleration to add Rote Quality to the dodge roll? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, that all checks out. The only room I see for error is base defense. He has 5 Wits and 5 Dexterity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T10:02:11-08:00","id":1001825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001811#post1001811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, no +1 Reach on Acceleration to add Rote Quality to the dodge roll? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, that all checks out. The only room I see for error is base defense. He has 5 Wits and 5 Dexterity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, he added the rote quality, i just did not mention it ^_^<br /> <br /> And yes, he min maxed Dexterity and Wits. A lot. Since my players had a transition from a Requiem Campaign to a mage one (very long but sound story), they had extra points to allot around their new mages.<br /> He has a thing for extremely defensive and stealthy character bundled with the need to constantly do non lethal jokes around.<br /> <br /> [And he never ever played anything different anywhere, he is disconcerting. In last Scion campaign he played a scion of Loki without even looking at the other gods and even if I had already chose to try a Scion of Loki (I tried a Scion of Vidar in the end, because a double Scion of Loki would have been quite annoying and I would not back down <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).]<br /> <br /> So, he boosted defense attributes and ran down acanthus thorny road because of the joke thing.<br /> Funny that he chose the guardians of the veil as order. Well, he actually chose them for the masque merit and a bit for the philosophy.<br /> Anyway, I advised him not to minmax, since is a very bad practice that will inevitably backfire on him, but... Well, nothing<br /> <br /> Aaaaah... New Players.<br /> He'll learn, soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Btw, all that dodge was useless, since i got him anyway dribbling defense. Still alive because it was a tutorial session <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T10:07:05-08:00","id":1001827,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with minmaxing, and punishing your players for it isn't very sporting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:18:29-08:00","id":1001852,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible for a mage to make &quot;holy&quot; water using prime or matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5951-cayros","name":"Cayros","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:24:49-08:00","id":1001854,"title":"","content":"It'd be possible for them to make it with a lot of arcana, depending on what you want it to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T12:46:56-08:00","id":1001884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001827#post1001827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing wrong with minmaxing, and punishing your players for it isn't very sporting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait wait, i'm not going to punish anyone for minmaxing nor I ever did. What I meant was that lacking any versatility, outside the extremely narrow and ultra specialized set of abilities the minmaxer chose, will be a severe drawback, maybe a lethal one (already seen this happen many times, actually, in larp too).<br /> Well, at least if the story/Chronicle is not the usual &quot;kick down the door, roll the dice, kill the monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> I agree that, from a mechanical point of view, there's nothing wrong with minmaxing.<br /> But regarding character consistence, minmaxing rarely makes sense and mostly generates very shallow characters unable to add anything to a chronicle except high, and highly specialized, dice pools.<br /> I personally advise against it, but else the player can have it his own way.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:03:54-08:00","id":1001893,"title":"","content":"He is an Acanthus. You can say a lot of things about Time and Fate, but &quot;lack of versatility&quot; isn't one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:10:53-08:00","id":1001899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001749#post1001749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If a mage with life casts body control like this:<br /> Gnosis 3<br /> Life 2<br /> +3 medicine because of rote<br /> +2 Mudra bonus<br /> +1 another yantra<br /> <br /> Total dice: 11<br /> <br /> Then uses 1 free reach for advanced duration, steps it to 1 week duration (because of the arcanum -1 primary factor rule) and subtracts 10 dice to get +5 potency (to a total of +6) and rolls a success with the only dice left, he gets a +5 in everything listed in the spell without limits even if it is only ruling practice?<br /> I mean, in 1ed tome of mysteries told that ruling could not grant more than a +2/+3, if i'm not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage can also spend Willpower on a Spellcasting roll to get +3 dice, putting you from 1 dice to respetable 4 dice. 4-6 dice is &quot;around optimal&quot; dicepool to aim at unless you are fishing for Exceptional Success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:20:03-08:00","id":1001905,"title":"","content":"Do people have tricks for Mage NPCs that might get into combat scenarios?<br /> <br /> Do you have them rely on rotes, while taking advantage of any environmental opportunities? Cause there's a lot of versatility in their spells and whipping things together on the fly can seem daunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-11-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:04:39-08:00","id":1001925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001899#post1001899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage can also spend Willpower on a Spellcasting roll to get +3 dice, putting you from 1 dice to respetable 4 dice. 4-6 dice is &quot;around optimal&quot; dicepool to aim at unless you are fishing for Exceptional Success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, it was only an example to be sure about the cast rule mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:07:14-08:00","id":1001990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001905#post1001905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people have tricks for Mage NPCs that might get into combat scenarios?<br /> <br /> Do you have them rely on rotes, while taking advantage of any environmental opportunities? Cause there's a lot of versatility in their spells and whipping things together on the fly can seem daunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, the first rules of combat are:<br /> <br /> 1. Don't get into combat.<br /> 2. If you break rule 1, try to get away if doing so would likely prevent serious injury or death.<br /> 3. If you cannot comply with rule 2, go for the jugular.<br /> <br /> (Optional rule 4: If you must fight, do it where you have home-field advantage.)<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, as a Mage gets more powerful, the kinds of pain they can inflict on an enemy are really limited only by their imagination and their ethics. There are some truly <i>awful</i> things you can do to someone with Life magic that make the prospect of facing a Thyrsus Adept with a grudge pretty brutal. As a result, winning a fight between the Awakened becomes less and less a question of how you'll win and more and more how you <i>want</i> to win.<br /> <br /> Weaker Awakened, meanwhile, will rely on combat rotes, skill-boosting rotes, and &quot;debuffs&quot;. Truth is, of course, that some Ruling spells are so vicious as to be fight-enders in their own right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:16:34-08:00","id":1001993,"title":"","content":"In general, figure out a spell effect that cannot be easily counteracted without having ability to manipulate Arcanum used to cast it, and then use it to win fight by creating unfair situations. &quot;Ban&quot; is poster spell for this, so is gravity manipulation, Darkness spamming, Twilight Gating opponents, and so on. Put your opponents in a position from which they can't fight, and they will be dead, eventually.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Combat Mage is a Mage who:<br /> 1. Knows how to disable their enemies with one reliable spell<br /> 2. Has easy way to compensate for lack of sensory input. If you are a combat mage, it's not unreasonable for you to have always-running spell that will allow you to still cast spells even when your mundane senses are impossible to use<br /> 3. Even when forced to use magic defensively in fight, can use it to gain progress towards victory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 11-11-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:30:28-08:00","id":1002000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001905#post1001905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people have tricks for Mage NPCs that might get into combat scenarios?<br /> <br /> Do you have them rely on rotes, while taking advantage of any environmental opportunities? Cause there's a lot of versatility in their spells and whipping things together on the fly can seem daunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The different approach to combat in 2E is really helpful here. If you're getting into a combat situation, remember to ask what everyone's Intent is. It might be &quot;kill/injure the other guys,&quot; yeah, but it also might be &quot;get the hell out of here&quot; or &quot;capture someone&quot; or &quot;make my enemies lay down their arms&quot; or &quot;distract them while my friend finishes the ritual.&quot; When you know what everyone is thinking, it narrows down their options.<br /> <br /> With NPCs, it also might be good to play loose with the spellcasting rules a little bit and use Down and Dirty Spellcasting. You don't need to overthink a specific player-focused spell effect, just look at the NPC's dot rating and decide what they're trying to do (kill someone, hinder them, escape, etc), then describe it in a cool way and roll Gnosis+Arcanum+2 for whatever Yantra they're assumed to use. If it's a damage effect, it does [Arcanum rating]+[successes] damage. If it's a dice penalty or bonus, it gives [successes] dice for [Arcanum rating] turns, or vice versa. If it's a narrative effect like teleportation or dimension shifting, it just happens how you want unless the players counterspell it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:55:17-08:00","id":1002011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1002000#post1002000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The different approach to combat in 2E is really helpful here. If you're getting into a combat situation, remember to ask what everyone's Intent is. It might be &quot;kill/injure the other guys,&quot; yeah, but it also might be &quot;get the hell out of here&quot; or &quot;capture someone&quot; or &quot;make my enemies lay down their arms&quot; or &quot;distract them while my friend finishes the ritual.&quot; When you know what everyone is thinking, it narrows down their options.<br /> <br /> With NPCs, it also might be good to play loose with the spellcasting rules a little bit and use Down and Dirty Spellcasting. You don't need to overthink a specific player-focused spell effect, just look at the NPC's dot rating and decide what they're trying to do (kill someone, hinder them, escape, etc), then describe it in a cool way and roll Gnosis+Arcanum+2 for whatever Yantra they're assumed to use. If it's a damage effect, it does [Arcanum rating]+[successes] damage. If it's a dice penalty or bonus, it gives [successes] dice for [Arcanum rating] turns, or vice versa. If it's a narrative effect like teleportation or dimension shifting, it just happens how you want unless the players counterspell it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> To reiterate because apparently I didn't explain in my first post: I don't have any problem running mage characters, but as the mechanics are kind of bulky I was asking if anyone uses any tricks to make it go faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:57:42-08:00","id":1002014,"title":"","content":"Figure out their Shadow Name. Good Shadow Names usually lead to fairly &quot;obvious&quot; and &quot;intuitive&quot; method of attack. Darcy The Sun Lord will whip you with a fireball, Nancy The Undying Shadow will probably have a favorite shadow spell. So it's a good habit to figure out few spells for each important NPC that they like to use, not only for combat, but for other situations too.*<br /> <br /> *<br /> I'm a person who believes that each thing you write down and prepare beforehand will help you immensely when &quot;improvising&quot;, so my advice for &quot;how to improvise on fly&quot; is to &quot;prep beforehand&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Quick and Dirty: <br /> Figure out beforehand typical magic pool for your casters, assuming &quot;probable&quot; yantra budget <br /> Next, check how many spell factors you can squeeze out of it before going down to 4/5/6 dice (pick one of these options)<br /> Write down the trimmed down spell pool and number of factors to spend <br /> Now you can spend factors fast and down bother with calculating the whole thing over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 11-11-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T10:44:44-08:00","id":1002266,"title":"","content":"Can a person move from their own Oneiros to someone else's, either directly or through connection to a shared Temenoic realm?<br /> <br /> That is, to say, could a cabal member enter the Oneiros of another cabal member by, say, following the threads of symbolism of their cabal and/or its sanctum into the Temenos and then following it out into another member's Onerios from there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:03:44-08:00","id":1002271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1002266#post1002266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a person move from their own Oneiros to someone else's, either directly or through connection to a shared Temenoic realm?<br /> <br /> That is, to say, could a cabal member enter the Oneiros of another cabal member by, say, following the threads of symbolism of their cabal and/or its sanctum into the Temenos and then following it out into another member's Onerios from there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There's definitely some spells in Astral Realms to do it, although those really need to be adapted to 2E. You can also enter someone else's Oneiros instead of your own if you're linked with Telepathy while you both meditate.<br /> <br /> In 2E there's a way to do it with no special spells. There's a sentence tucked in the Astral section somewhere that says you can enter another Oneiros if both of you are currently thinking about a very specific thing while meditating or dreaming. You follow the symbolism about that specific thing in your own Oneiros, and then presumably when you reach the shared &quot;cell&quot; about that subject, you can transfer over to theirs. This would be easy enough to arrange with your cabal, and you could spy on other people too if you know what's on their mind.<br /> <br /> I'm not totally clear on how the Temenos interacts with individual Oneiroi. I don't know if there are naturally direct portals, you probably have to use spells or Numina to break into someone's dream vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:47:38-08:00","id":1002668,"title":"","content":"Can a combined spell be a Praxis or rote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:56:36-08:00","id":1002674,"title":"","content":"I don't think Rotes can be, and a Praxis can only combine with another Praxis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:43:39-08:00","id":1002719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1002674#post1002674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Rotes can be, and a Praxis can only combine with another Praxis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are correct, on both counts. Rote Imagos are considered too rigid to be combined, even and especially with other Rotes. Praxes also have a similar effect, but I think you can infuse them with another, you just lose the Praxis benefit if they're not being fused with another Praxis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T21:40:19-08:00","id":1002766,"title":"","content":"The way I read the question (which may or may not be correct, but I would be interested in an answer, regardless), it's: if you cast a particular combined spell a lot, can you make the combined spell into a praxis or rote? E.g. if a Fate mage's signature combat move is to hit enemies with a combined Shared Fate + Grave Misfortune, can they turn the combination into a rote, gaining the benefits of a rote when and only when they're casting the spells in combination?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Feel free to correct me, Khalendas, if I read your question wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:21:30-08:00","id":1003099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1002766#post1002766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I read the question (which may or may not be correct, but I would be interested in an answer, regardless), it's: if you cast a particular combined spell a lot, can you make the combined spell into a praxis or rote? E.g. if a Fate mage's signature combat move is to hit enemies with a combined Shared Fate + Grave Misfortune, can they turn the combination into a rote, gaining the benefits of a rote when and only when they're casting the spells in combination?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Feel free to correct me, Khalendas, if I read your question wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are correct, that was the question ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T19:02:18-08:00","id":1003197,"title":"","content":"How are attainments gained? I've read the chapter but I don't remember reading how and when you get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T20:09:58-08:00","id":1003212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1003197#post1003197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are attainments gained? I've read the chapter but I don't remember reading how and when you get them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get them automatically, all you need is the appropriate number of dots in the appropriate Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T06:56:18-08:00","id":1003369,"title":"","content":"Could someone explain combined spells to me?<br /> <br /> Let's say at character creation I opt to get Mind 3 and Gnosis 3; I want to combine Augment Mind with Enhance skill. Augment Mind has potency as primary factor and Enhance Skill has duration. Which of the spell factors gain the bonus from my Arcana rating? Let's I cast the spell at a potency of 4; does this mean I divide my potence between the two effects (e.g +1 resolve and +3 investigate), or do I get +4 in each?<br /> <br /> Are there any particular Arcana/spells you feel give that bit of extra oompf in combination? Like, which spell combinations are your favourites when playing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:01:58-08:00","id":1003428,"title":"","content":"I think both spells should have the same Primary factor to be cast combined. A Reach will fix that. <br /> Both spells have Potency 4 if you change Enhance Skill's Primary factor to align with Augment Mind, or 1 if you go the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:29:10-08:00","id":1003440,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the community would answer 'yes,' but I figured I'd ask.<br /> <br /> If you get an Exceptional Success with a spell, one of your options is a Mana refund. Specifically, 'All Mana spent on the spell is refunded, and the mage receives one more point of Mana.'<br /> <br /> Does this include Mana spent to mitigate Paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:32:14-08:00","id":1003444,"title":"","content":"I would assume yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:44:11-08:00","id":1003644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1002668#post1002668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a combined spell be a Praxis or rote?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anyone? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:51:28-08:00","id":1003648,"title":"","content":"Probably, in first edition they could be rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:51:58-08:00","id":1003649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1003644#post1003644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anyone? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The book doesn't mention it specifically. I don't think anything would break if you let mages do that, apart from making it slightly easier for them to cast powerful spells with fewer drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> yeah, it includes Paradox Mana. There aren't a ton of other things you can spend Mana on for a spell in the first place.<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:30:31-08:00","id":1003898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1003649#post1003649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book doesn't mention it specifically. I don't think anything would break if you let mages do that, apart from making it slightly easier for them to cast powerful spells with fewer drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> yeah, it includes Paradox Mana. There aren't a ton of other things you can spend Mana on for a spell in the first place.<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, thanks, i'll house rule that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:06:34-08:00","id":1003920,"title":"","content":"Page 118 in the book (Combined Spells): Rotes cannot be combined, but Praxes can if the caster has all of the spells being combined as Praxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:09:42-08:00","id":1003921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1003920#post1003920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 118 in the book (Combined Spells): Rotes cannot be combined, but Praxes can if the caster has all of the spells being combined as Praxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question isn't about combining Rotes, it's about creating a Rote for a Combined spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:07:59-08:00","id":1004013,"title":"","content":"Is there anything stopping a player from just improvising a spell that uses potency as a primary spellfactor instead of duration if the spell they are trying to cast usually lists duration as its main factor? The book suggests that to change the primary factor you have to spend one reach, which could be avoided this way. The book sadly doesn't give a clear awnser wether some standart primary factor is mandatory to certain spells. Personally I've followed the idea that any spell that'd last longer than an instant push would autmatically take duration as its primary factor, but the book is riddled with spells that contradict this assumption, picking spellfactors seemingly at random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:24:29-08:00","id":1004024,"title":"","content":"I don't play much mage. Is there any spell that can (without extreme difficulty) detect mages who aren't actively using any magic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:29:19-08:00","id":1004026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004024#post1004024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't play much mage. Is there any spell that can (without extreme difficulty) detect mages who aren't actively using any magic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supernal Vision can detect Mages(who are not Veiling themselves of this sort of detecting) via their Patterns. It also detects Sleepers and Sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:42:05-08:00","id":1004031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004013#post1004013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything stopping a player from just improvising a spell that uses potency as a primary spellfactor instead of duration if the spell they are trying to cast usually lists duration as its main factor? ... The book sadly doesn't give a clear awnser wether some standart primary factor is mandatory to certain spells. Personally I've followed the idea that any spell that'd last longer than an instant push would autmatically take duration as its primary factor, but the book is riddled with spells that contradict this assumption, picking spellfactors seemingly at random.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering about that myself but it does have an answer. It's on p127, right before the list of spells.<br /> <br /> 'Determine which Factor is the Primary Factor. This is either Potency or Duration, with the rule of thumb of \u201cwhichever Factor you immediately think of when you think of a more powerful version of the spell.\u201d <i>The Primary Factor of a given spell effect is always the same; you can\u2019t make a creative thaumaturgy spell that\u2019s identical to another spell except with a different Primary Factor.</i>'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:57:41-08:00","id":1004038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004031#post1004031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cwhichever Factor you immediately think of when you think of a more powerful version of the spell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is..... extremly subjective and will just end in different people not being of one opinion which should be the primary factor for one given spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:14:19-08:00","id":1004050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004038#post1004038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is..... extremly subjective and will just end in different people not being of one opinion which should be the primary factor for one given spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most (but not all) of the spells in the book seems to adhere to this guideline:<br /> <br /> Does Potency do more than overcoming a Withstand Rating?<br /> Yes: Potency is the Primary Factor<br /> No: Next question<br /> <br /> Does Duration increase the usefulness of the spell?<br /> Yes: Duration is the Primary Factor<br /> No: Potency is the Primary Factor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:15:46-08:00","id":1004080,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think it's terribly difficult to figure out what a spell's primary factor would be - which ever is the more direct way to scale up the spell's effect. That said, I think the provision against creating a spell that's identical to another but with a different primary factor is silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:45:23-08:00","id":1004101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004080#post1004080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think it's terribly difficult to figure out what a spell's primary factor would be - which ever is the more direct way to scale up the spell's effect. That said, I think the provision against creating a spell that's identical to another but with a different primary factor is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The alternative would be having to set a Primary Factor for Rotes, Praxes and Legacy Attainments. It would not be a bad house rule, but as much as I love how elegant creative thaumaturgy is I prefer having one less variable to worry about when putting together a spell during play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:48:36-08:00","id":1004103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004101#post1004101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The alternative would be having to set a Primary Factor for Rotes, Praxes and Legacy Attainments. It would not be a bad house rule, but as much as I love how elegant creative thaumaturgy is I prefer having one less variable to worry about when putting together a spell during play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T15:08:06-08:00","id":1004132,"title":"","content":"Remember that Duration increases usefulness of a spell not only when it leads to it lasting longer, but also when it might be Clash-of-Willed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:21:23-08:00","id":1004715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004038#post1004038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is..... extremly subjective and will just end in different people not being of one opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the general design philosophy of Mage 2e. Have fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T22:44:23-08:00","id":1004813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1004715#post1004715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welcome to the general design philosophy of Mage 2e. Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...pretty much spot on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T11:26:59-08:00","id":1005039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1003369#post1003369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone explain combined spells to me?<br /> <br /> Let's say at character creation I opt to get Mind 3 and Gnosis 3; I want to combine Augment Mind with Enhance skill. Augment Mind has potency as primary factor and Enhance Skill has duration. Which of the spell factors gain the bonus from my Arcana rating? Let's I cast the spell at a potency of 4; does this mean I divide my potence between the two effects (e.g +1 resolve and +3 investigate), or do I get +4 in each?<br /> <br /> Are there any particular Arcana/spells you feel give that bit of extra oompf in combination? Like, which spell combinations are your favourites when playing?</div> </div> </div> </div>MtA2e p118: &quot;Rotes cannot be combined, but Praxes can if the caster has all of the spells being combined as Praxes.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:22:37-08:00","id":1005162,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to make sure I understand potency as a primary spell factor. By default a spell with potency as a primary spell fact is one. So through creative thaumaturgy a mage casts a fire dart attack spell it does 1 damage (bashing or lethal depending upon practice). To make that damage increase a -2 for each extra point of potency would be applied. <br /> <br /> But what about rotes? Telekinetic blasts does 1 bashing? or does it do 3 based one the dots? If it does 3 where in the book does it make this clarification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:49:34-08:00","id":1005173,"title":"","content":"Being a Rote doesn't change primary spell factor. Telekinetic Blast Rote uses whatever thing basic version of Telekinetic Blast used as primary factor.<br /> <br /> Primary factor, before spending any dice, is equal to your Arcana rating. Mage with Forces 3 casting Fire Darts (Potency: Primary) has Potency of 3, other Mage casting the same spell with Forces 5 has Potency 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:27:22-08:00","id":1005198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005173#post1005173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Rote doesn't change primary spell factor. Telekinetic Blast Rote uses whatever thing basic version of Telekinetic Blast used as primary factor.<br /> <br /> Primary factor, before spending any dice, is equal to your Arcana rating. Mage with Forces 3 casting Fire Darts (Potency: Primary) has Potency of 3, other Mage casting the same spell with Forces 5 has Potency 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok sorry for seeming so dense but I'm not able to find this in the book. This is what I've read in the spell casting chapter on page 113<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"> All spells have a </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">primary spell factor </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">of either Potency or Duration. After penalties have been applied for the desired spell factors, the player may move the primary factor up its chart a number of steps equal to the character\u2019s rating in the spell\u2019s highest Arcanum minus one. </span>&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The effect of a spell\u2019s Potency is described in the individual spell write-up \u2014 each level of Potency increases the spell\u2019s main effect. Each level of Potency beyond the first imposes a \u20132 penalty to the casting roll&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I don't seem to be able to find it anywhere that states the potency of 1 can be increased without taking a penalty and I couldn't find anything about rotes and potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:33:13-08:00","id":1005200,"title":"","content":"Rotes calculate Potency the same as any other spell, what makes Rotes different are its use of Reach and the ability to use a Mudra as a Yantra. That quote you just used from page 113 says exactly how to move up Potency without taking a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:56:25-08:00","id":1005206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005198#post1005198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok sorry for seeming so dense but I'm not able to find this in the book. This is what I've read in the spell casting chapter on page 113<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"> All spells have a </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">primary spell factor </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">of either Potency or Duration. After penalties have been applied for the desired spell factors, the player may move the primary factor up its chart a number of steps equal to the character\u2019s rating in the spell\u2019s highest Arcanum minus one. </span>&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The effect of a spell\u2019s Potency is described in the individual spell write-up \u2014 each level of Potency increases the spell\u2019s main effect. Each level of Potency beyond the first imposes a \u20132 penalty to the casting roll&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I don't seem to be able to find it anywhere that states the potency of 1 can be increased without taking a penalty and I couldn't find anything about rotes and potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are 2 ways of interpreting your first quoted bit of text there. The first way, which I assume is how you're reading it, is that a primary factor of potency simply allows you to raise potency up to the dot rating of the arcana by taking penalties and so conversely you would be unable to raise potency unless it is primary factor, otherwise there would be no difference between primary and normal spell factor. And even further it implies that only the primary factor can be raised by taking penalties.<br /> <br /> The other interpretation is that you can make potency any number between 1 and your arcana rating for free without taking penalties (the 'may' referring to the player having the option, so they don't have to pump out the spell at full power if they don't want to).<br /> <br /> So if the first interpretation were true then we'd expect that in your second quote it'd mention that potency has to be the primary factor in order for you to take the penalty, which isn't the case, it instead says you can raise the potency by taking a penalty, no qualifiers or limitations. So there are a few indicators which imply the first interpretation should be used which are missing, whereas the only issue with taking the second interpretation is that the second quote has the wording '...Potency beyond the first...' which implies that any raising of potency requires a -2 penalty, however it can also be taken to mean that 'the first' means free potency, though that is a bit of a stretch I think it's more reasonable than implying additional swaths of words that by all rights should have been included if they were intended. Given the lack of conflicts and much lower amount of bookkeeping and restrictions with the second interpretation I think it's the only one that can be reasonably taken in the situation.<br /> <br /> In addition rotes won't change anything about potency automatically, the effects of a rote are: you gain access to the mudras yantra (which can be up to about +11 outside of the use of magic for more skill dots), you can cast non-ruling arcana spells without spending mana, you can roll with rote quality if casting at double ritual time from a gimoire (or you are the master who encoded the rote), it cloaks you nimbus and you are treated as having 5 dots in the primary arcanum of the spell for the purposes of free reach only. So the rote just gives more option to raise potency (can spend more reach without risking paradox, which means you can make potency primary factor with less risk and the mudras bonus is a very powerful yantra which means you can raise potency far higher while still being sure you'll succeed the casting roll.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:06:18-08:00","id":1005209,"title":"","content":"I can't help you right now with quotes, but reducing the process to simple steps:<br /> <br /> 1. All non-primary factors start at 1.<br /> 2. Primary factor can start as high as your Arcanum rating.<br /> 3. Moving a factor up by one step costs you 2 dice. <br /> <br /> It's that simple. From my point of view, text states it in a little overcomplicated way, but I wonder if it's a native vs non native speaker problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T03:01:58-08:00","id":1005287,"title":"","content":"I think it's a lot clearer in the Quick Reference in appendix four.<br /> <br /> Potency works just like any other spell factor. They just didn't bother with a table because it's totally linear and they were saving space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T04:47:44-08:00","id":1005304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005209#post1005209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help you right now with quotes, but reducing the process to simple steps:<br /> <br /> 1. All non-primary factors start at 1.<br /> 2. Primary factor can start as high as your Arcanum rating.<br /> 3. Moving a factor up by one step costs you 2 dice.<br /> <br /> It's that simple. From my point of view, text states it in a little overcomplicated way, but I wonder if it's a native vs non native speaker problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I was born and raised here in the U.S so it's not a native speaker so much as thick headed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's finally sunk in so I'm good now. Thanks to everyone for helping to clear that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12662,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","user":"bestial Warlust","date":". 11-19-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T04:56:04-08:00","id":1005305,"title":"","content":"I think it's a question of the writers knowing what they mean so they have a hard time realizing that their writings can be interpreted more than one way or when it's not clear for those who read it for the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:00:38-08:00","id":1005350,"title":"","content":"I've got a question about the transform life rote. The spell is able to grant more subtle aspects of life as well right? Like you could give a person cat like agility, the reaction time of a fly, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:12:07-08:00","id":1005352,"title":"","content":"Ehh... kind of. Life is a very physical arcarnum. It mucks about with actual biological processes so to give someone stuff like that you need to actually alter their body in the right way. The end result might not actually be all that subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:16:44-08:00","id":1005355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005350#post1005350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question about the transform life rote. The spell is able to grant more subtle aspects of life as well right? Like you could give a person cat like agility, the reaction time of a fly, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no. For that sort of thing, you want Honing the Form. All the examples given in Transform Life are for giving the subject extra organs and other capabilities that don't fit into the standard list of Attributes; if what you want would be most sensibly described as a bonus to e.g. Dexterity (like &quot;cat-like agility&quot;), it's probably HtF instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:17:52-08:00","id":1005357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005350#post1005350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question about the transform life rote. The spell is able to grant more subtle aspects of life as well right? Like you could give a person cat like agility, the reaction time of a fly, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I feel I should point out, because it seems to be causing some confusion, or at least ambiguity. The example spells in chapter three are not necessarily Rotes. Transform Life, for example, can be cast as a Rote, as a Praxis, or as an improvised spell. Rote has a specific mechanical meaning beyond just being a pre-written spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:23:00-08:00","id":1005360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005357#post1005357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I feel I should point out, because it seems to be causing some confusion, or at least ambiguity. The example spells in chapter three are not necessarily Rotes. Transform Life, for example, can be cast as a Rote, as a Praxis, or as an improvised spell. Rote has a specific mechanical meaning beyond just being a pre-written spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the response, I was thinking along those lines but I wanted to double check. As a guy who watches way too many nature documentaries the scope and power of this spell is staggering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:03:46-08:00","id":1005377,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you took it as a rote it <i>would</i> just be <i>one</i> rote, and it is pretty damn useful so it's a good rote to have. <br /> <br /> But, like overall a Life mage is no more versatile than any other mage, because they can <i>all</i> do a similar variety of things, just spread out over more distinct spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:45:40-08:00","id":1005389,"title":"","content":"The Gaolers of Ialdabaoth grew out of a cabal of Mysterium and Guardians of the Veil mages detailed in Grimoire of Grimoires. They're a legacy devoted to the capture, imprisonment and study of ephemeral entities, namely ghosts and spirits, tainted by the Abyss. Would they be considered a heresy among the Diamond Orders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:57:20-08:00","id":1005393,"title":"","content":"I remember that being the tone of their writeup.<br /> <br /> The Gaolers would be a good chance to highlight that Left-Handed is sometimes a matter of perspective. The Diamond is wary and distrustful of them because of what they do, which is indeed very dangerous, but a neutral observer might not call it evil or malevolent. Foolhardy, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-19-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:10:45-08:00","id":1005399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005389#post1005389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gaolers of Ialdabaoth grew out of a cabal of Mysterium and Guardians of the Veil mages detailed in Grimoire of Grimoires. They're a legacy devoted to the capture, imprisonment and study of ephemeral entities, namely ghosts and spirits, tainted by the Abyss. Would they be considered a heresy among the Diamond Orders?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Varies. What's considered heretical in one place is not necessarily in another( The Bokor, for example). A surefire way to be near univerally heretical is when you use souls for power. That's a sure fire way to get branded as Left-Hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:01:31-08:00","id":1005487,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of forbidden magic, let me just make sure: when a Guardian with the Masque merit chooses two Acts of Hubris they don't have to roll for, that can include dealing with the Abyss? There's room for a deep-cover Scelestus, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T17:38:23-08:00","id":1005521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1005487#post1005487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the subject of forbidden magic, let me just make sure: when a Guardian with the Masque merit chooses two Acts of Hubris they don't have to roll for, that can include dealing with the Abyss? There's room for a deep-cover Scelestus, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like it. You could go either way, having a Scelestus in the Guardians or having a Guardian go undercover as one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:23:35-08:00","id":1006057,"title":"","content":"A couple of players of mine are arguing about the subject scale option.<br /> For what I read in the manual, if you choose to affect a number of subjects they are chosen randomly unless fate 2 is brought into the spell equation.<br /> My players instead say that you can choose subjects by default.<br /> <br /> What is the final verdict? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:27:57-08:00","id":1006058,"title":"","content":"You can choose them. I don't have the book on me right now but yea. Trust me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:38:02-08:00","id":1006062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1006058#post1006058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can choose them. I don't have the book on me right now but yea. Trust me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh uh, you're right. I did a little re-read and noticed I've missed the &quot;specific subjects&quot; part.<br /> Thanks ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:50:19-08:00","id":1006277,"title":"","content":"Yep, <i>Everyone</i> gets to simply select targets if casting via Sensory. If you want Scale on an aimed spell, it's AoE, and you now need to cast Warding Gesture to cheat with AoE. <br /> <br /> That's a lot simpler to adjudicate that the criteria thing in 1e. Thumbs up for a decided rule improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T06:38:58-08:00","id":1006680,"title":"","content":"I need a sounding board,Veiling appears to be able to present partial cosmetic changes to a subject like in Mutable Mask for Life. How extensive can that be in other arcana? For instance could Matter 2 make $1 present as a bill of a different denomination or feel like sandpaper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T06:58:41-08:00","id":1006686,"title":"","content":"Veiling generally just hides something rather than changing how it appears, but if Life can make something appear different then all the other Arcana should be able to as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:00:23-08:00","id":1006688,"title":"","content":"I think that you can Veil a knife as a sledgehammer but it won't change anything else besides look and maybe feel with a reach. It won't change weight, damage, structure or conductivity. Sandpaper bill will feel like a sandpaper but it won't actually smooth anything if used as a tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:06:34-08:00","id":1006690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1006686#post1006686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veiling generally just hides something rather than changing how it appears, but if Life can make something appear different then all the other Arcana should be able to as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that comparable effects exist for other Arcana:<br /> <br /> - Corpse Mask (Death 2) changes the apparent cause of death of a corpse.<br /> - Fabricate Fortune (Fate 2) can create fake destinies and fake Fate-based trigger events.<br /> - Alter Mental Pattern (Mind 2) gives the subject a fake set of thoughts, emotions etc if someone tries to use supernatural powers to read their mind.<br /> - Lying Maps (Space 2) alters the subject's sense of direction to direct them down a desired route.<br /> <br /> So I'd say the use of Veiling to cosmetically alter the subject is well-established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:46:53-08:00","id":1006708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1006688#post1006688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you can Veil a knife as a sledgehammer but it won't change anything else besides look and maybe feel with a reach. It won't change weight, damage, structure or conductivity. Sandpaper bill will feel like a sandpaper but it won't actually smooth anything if used as a tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Veiling a knife as a sledge hammer would be going too far. A person stays a person just a different looking one.<br /> <br /> Ok, thanks everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T08:06:38-08:00","id":1006711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1006690#post1006690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'd say the use of Veiling to cosmetically alter the subject is well-established.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll have to admit I didn't look at too many spells before writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T07:12:33-08:00","id":1008900,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if I understand the wording of Momentary Flux correctly. Is it possible to inform your past self about the outcome of the spell? e.g. you got shot entering a room and cast it tell your past self that going there is bad for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-27-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T07:32:15-08:00","id":1008902,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything in the description of Momentary Flux suggesting that it can be used to send information backwards in time. You can cast it before going in to determine whether the room is good or bad for you, or you can cast it after going in (with Temporal Sympathy) to determine whether <i>having</i> gone in will be good or bad for you, but the spell reveals information to your <i>present</i> self, not your past self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T07:57:16-08:00","id":1008906,"title":"","content":"Original:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages with Time \u2022\u2022 may use the Temporal Sympathy Attainment<br /> to cast this spell on a subject in the past, but the spell still<br /> reveals positive or negative outcomesfor the <b>future</b>. </div> </div> </div>Google Translate can't help me with this but shouldn't it be like that if it were to only work for your present self?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages with Time \u2022\u2022 may use the Temporal Sympathy Attainment<br /> to cast this spell on a subject in the past, but the spell still<br /> reveals positive or negative outcomes for the <b>present</b>. </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/b9/b9ec74d2993d1b484a352ea1ef660837762a2ab98b1667f6a727a30857ae661e.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:10:00-08:00","id":1008908,"title":"","content":"My reading of that is that the spell exists to tell you about <i>future events</i> caused by the subject, whether the subject is something in the present or something in the past. In the case of walking into the room, for instance, you could cast the spell first to determine whether the room bodes well for you. If someone's waiting inside to shoot you, the answer will probably be &quot;no&quot;. Alternatively, if you've already gone in, and someone is about to shoot you from hiding but hasn't done so yet, and you cast the spell with Temporal Sympathy, you can ask &quot;does the fact that I entered the room bode well or ill for me?&quot; and the answer, again, will probably be &quot;ill&quot;. In all cases, though, it's you in the present who casts the spell and receives the information.<br /> <br /> Does that clarify things for you at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:18:14-08:00","id":1008910,"title":"","content":"Yes it does. Thank you for answer! I don't think that the Temporal Sympathy is very usufull in this spell though. You could just ask &quot;is staying here a better or worse choice?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:19:09-08:00","id":1008913,"title":"","content":"The subject of the spell is the thing you want to know about, not the person who gets the information. You can't grant the knowledge to anyone but your present self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:24:51-08:00","id":1008917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1008913#post1008913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of the spell is the thing you want to know about, not the person who gets the information. You can't grant the knowledge to anyone but your present self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ow! Because its a Knowing spell right? What does it take to make someone a recipient of a Knowing spell? Higher practice or just increasing the scale factor to include both target and recipient?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:28:18-08:00","id":1008920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1008910#post1008910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it does. Thank you for answer! I don't think that the Temporal Sympathy is very usufull in this spell though. You could just ask &quot;is staying here a better or worse choice?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In that instance, sure, it doesn't help very much. There are other scenarios where it could be useful, though. For instance, suppose you're out for a walk and you happen to be caught on CCTV near where a crime was being committed by unknown parties, causing you to be regarded as a suspect. You could cast on that location with temporal sympathy and determine that <i>having been</i> there bodes ill for you, whereas casting on that location <i>now</i> would tell you nothing, because the relevant event is past. Or, to use an example from the spell description itself, maybe you meet a stranger who has a cold and he infects you with it; casting the spell on him afterwards wouldn't tell you anything, because he's <i>already</i> given it to you and therefore bodes neither well nor ill for you now, whereas casting it on his past self could tell you that meeting him was bad for you (because you're about to come down with a cold).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:56:14-08:00","id":1008932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1008917#post1008917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ow! Because its a Knowing spell right? What does it take to make someone a recipient of a Knowing spell? Higher practice or just increasing the scale factor to include both target and recipient?</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher practice, no. Targets, you can give the info to yourself or someone you touch by default. Increasing the scale to include two targets would allow you and someone else to receive the information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:56:46-08:00","id":1008933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1008917#post1008917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ow! Because its a Knowing spell right? What does it take to make someone a recipient of a Knowing spell? Higher practice or just increasing the scale factor to include both target and recipient?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yknow, I don't think it ever really specifies.<br /> <br /> I'd go with it adding another target for the spell, which I guess means that you <i>might</i> be able to use Momentary Flux to send information to your past self, but Temporal Sympathy is usually very specific about what you can use it on so I think in this case when they say &quot;subject&quot; they mean <i>just</i> the subject mentioned in the spell description, ie the one being assessed.<br /> <br /> Basically if a mage wants to alter a past decision they need to do it the hard way, with more dots of Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:05:54-08:00","id":1008937,"title":"","content":"Just combine casting Postcognition with Quantum Flux targeting your past self would allow you to send the information to your past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:24:12-08:00","id":1008946,"title":"","content":"I don't think postcognition allows you to <i>affect</i> the past, just see it. It doesn't count as remote viewing because it's basically a recording and remote viewing has to be in real time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:11:03-08:00","id":1008957,"title":"","content":"Yeah, probably combine cast with a spell that actually goes backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:17:11-08:00","id":1008961,"title":"","content":"At that point you can just, like, go back in time though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T11:03:24-08:00","id":1008977,"title":"","content":"Obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T21:25:32-08:00","id":1009165,"title":"","content":"I know I've seen it asked a few times in the past but I don't think I've ever seen an answer to it, but are mages supposed to be able to top themselves off with Willpower and Mana by spamming their Praxis? I know I've seen it mentioned that mages in setting afflict themselves with conditions to resolve in order to gain beats, but I'm curious as to whether this was also intended. So is this a thing that mages do in-setting or just a mechanical quirk? Or hell, am I wrong and does it not work this way post errata or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T21:47:49-08:00","id":1009174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1009165#post1009165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I've seen it asked a few times in the past but I don't think I've ever seen an answer to it, but are mages supposed to be able to top themselves off with Willpower and Mana by spamming their Praxis? I know I've seen it mentioned that mages in setting afflict themselves with conditions to resolve in order to gain beats, but I'm curious as to whether this was also intended. So is this a thing that mages do in-setting or just a mechanical quirk? Or hell, am I wrong and does it not work this way post errata or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your question is &quot;Are mages supposed to be heavily incentivized to use their Praxes \u2014 i.e. their signature spells \u2014 very often?&quot; then the answer is yes.<br /> <br /> If your question is &quot;Can you just cast your Praxes over and over for no reason without making even a token effort to connect this kind of casting about for a viable result like a proper addict to the narrative draw of 'I am low on resources and my internal dealer has these handy levers built into my Gnosis to offer me my fix'?&quot; then the answer is no with the caveat that that token effort is something it helps to build towards through Obsessions and choice of Praxes and Storyteller discussion in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you've got a Praxis based around transmutation then you're sure as hell going to want to do some transmuting when you're low on Mana or Willpower, but that's an action that doesn't exist in a vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:15:39-08:00","id":1009182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1009174#post1009174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your question is &quot;Are mages supposed to be heavily incentivized to use their Praxes \u2014 i.e. their signature spells \u2014 very often?&quot; then the answer is yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's really more of a question of if it is a setting assumption that most (intelligent) mages should generally be running around with full Willpower/Mana unless having literally just moments ago spent a lot of either? I know mechanics-wise it's a thing and should be taken advantage of as much as possible, but again, is it a mechanical quirk or an intentional setting aspect. <br /> <br /> Having less than full Willpower/Mana seems reason enough to spam Praxes regardless of what they are and what your Obsessions might be. It could be argued that even if not specifically for the sake of Obsessions, and even without them in mind at all, replenishing your resources is something that could only help you accomplish whatever it is you may or may not want to do in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:29:24-08:00","id":1009185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1009182#post1009182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having less than full Willpower/Mana seems reason enough to spam Praxes regardless of what they are and what your Obsessions might be. It could be argued that even if not specifically for the sake of Obsessions, and even without them in mind at all, replenishing your resources is something that could only help you accomplish whatever it is you may or may not want to do in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't getting at &quot;for the sake of Obsessions&quot; so much as &quot;your Obsessions are likely to shape your choice of Praxes as a given game goes on, and the nature of Praxes as individual spells, combined with the way Yantras work and the nature of Paradox as a thing that is brought into prominence through the presence of Sleepers, is going to inform any given mage's coping mechanisms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Praxes are, in a sense, Mage's loose equivalent of the more overtly monstrous gamelines' Anchor Traits \u2014 if you're low on Willpower and have most of your Praxes allocated to spells that affect electronics, you're going to prioritize seeking out some viable targets, Yantras, and secondary reasons for you to use those Praxes on some electronics; depending on how careful and/or desperate you are, you may or may not care that a given application of magic is wildly inappropriate to the nearest convenient setting and/or serves no purpose other than to refill your stores of energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T23:00:17-08:00","id":1009196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1009185#post1009185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't getting at &quot;for the sake of Obsessions&quot; so much as &quot;your Obsessions are likely to shape your choice of Praxes as a given game goes on, and the nature of Praxes as individual spells, combined with the way Yantras work and the nature of Paradox as a thing that is brought into prominence through the presence of Sleepers, is going to inform any given mage's coping mechanisms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Praxes are, in a sense, Mage's loose equivalent of the more overtly monstrous gamelines' Anchor Traits \u2014 if you're low on Willpower and have most of your Praxes allocated to spells that affect electronics, you're going to prioritize seeking out some viable targets, Yantras, and secondary reasons for you to use those Praxes on some electronics; depending on how careful and/or desperate you are, you may or may not care that a given application of magic is wildly inappropriate to the nearest convenient setting and/or serves no purpose other than to refill your stores of energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Praxes-as-Anchor is not an angle I've ever considered, but this makes a lot of sense, and leaves the whole Praxis-spam issue feeling much less like a gamey exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T03:49:57-08:00","id":1009264,"title":"","content":"Yes. Rather than alternate anchors, think of it as all mages having an additional Vice of &quot;using magic feels good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which helps when so many of their mechanics are precluded on spending willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:32:40-08:00","id":1009803,"title":"","content":"So, weird thought I had looking over the rules for Ephemeral Beings today in Mage 2E. Seeing as Goetia and Spirits both use Resonant as their base Condition, could a Spirit with the Essence Thief Numen completely consume a Goetia the way they would consume another Spirit, merging their two natures without becoming an unstable magath? What would such a hybrid ephemeral look like? Would the Spirit become more self-aware, even at low Rank, taking up some of the humanity that comes with the Essence of a being from the Astral Realms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:54:38-08:00","id":1009813,"title":"","content":"It could only happen if they were in the same frequency of Twilight, otherwise they typically don't interact with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:01:28-08:00","id":1009817,"title":"","content":"That's the entire basis of the Ghost Eater Numen, ain't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:23:07-08:00","id":1009830,"title":"","content":"It is, but I think it was renamed Essence Thief in the new 2E material, Post-God-Machine Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:25:08-08:00","id":1009848,"title":"","content":"Tomayto, tomahto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:08:53-08:00","id":1010222,"title":"","content":"If you pick up a weapon (or other piece of equipment), and then cast shifting sands on yourself, reaching for a scene, are you still holding that item in the past? If so, what happens to the item once you catch up to the present? AKA: can you duplicate items?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:34:39-08:00","id":1010229,"title":"","content":"No, you can't. The item has its own past and when Shifted follows its own time sympathy. But I can see a Weaving spell that spins the time and temporarily duplicates an object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-30-2016, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:38:02-08:00","id":1010230,"title":"","content":"You don't take <i>anything</i> back with you with shifting sands. You only end up clothed because your past self was already wearing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:40:55-08:00","id":1010233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1010230#post1010230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't take <i>anything</i> back with you with shifting sands. You only end up clothed because your past self was already wearing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could however target an item and send it back in changed condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:05:58-08:00","id":1010293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1010233#post1010233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could however target an item and send it back in changed condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an idea. If you were mortally wounded and had no access to healing in the recent past, you could send your torn and bloody clothes or equipment back in time before the crisis as a warning to your past self, and hope you do better the second time around. Or if you learned something mind-shattering or made a horrible mistake and couldn't bear to continue in your current iteration, you could do the same thing and trick your past self into trying something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-30-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:37:40-08:00","id":1010307,"title":"","content":"Yes, but even better then that - you could send your cabalmate back in time if he is in better shape then you &quot;Remember what will happen... *coffs blood* Save us all... Now go... *zzap*&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:37:33-08:00","id":1010328,"title":"","content":"You could send monster/opponent too strong to take down in a single go back in time after damaging it. Or set up a situation where you send something into a frame of time where something damaging happens; set up an explosion in Round A and keep shuffling the target back to it in Round B, until it's defeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:33:04-08:00","id":1010625,"title":"","content":"How would you construct a spell that deflects direct magical attack to the attacker? Is Prime Weaving enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:46:38-08:00","id":1010638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1010230#post1010230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't take <i>anything</i> back with you with shifting sands. You only end up clothed because your past self was already wearing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This makes sense. Do you always end up in the same place you were in the past?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:50:53-08:00","id":1010642,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar61_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"61\" data-vbnamecard=\"61\">Octavo</a> Yes. Unless you combine it with Teleportation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:55:31-08:00","id":1010646,"title":"","content":"Redirecting a spell is essentially mucking about with it's spell factors. That sounds like weaving to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T08:33:30-08:00","id":1010664,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> When typing a digital Grimoire (so that touch range applies) where can the data write to (the local machine, a distant server with where the data base is?), and can it be copied via normal electronic means?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1001884#post1001884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that, from a mechanical point of view, there's nothing wrong with minmaxing.<br /> But regarding character consistence, minmaxing rarely makes sense and mostly generates very shallow characters unable to add anything to a chronicle except high, and highly specialized, dice pools.<br /> I personally advise against it, but else the player can have it his own way.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. Mechanics are not detached from realities within what some would call the &quot;fluff&quot; of the story; they are the bones and muscle over which the skin of the story rests. Imbalance under the skin can leave terrible disfigurement of the entire body. Attachment to the setting is defined not by description, but by mechanics like Status, Allies, Retainers, Mystery Cults, Safe Places, Contacts and so forth, and if neglected leave a character not connected to the setting. Task completion (focusing on die pools) can be important (but not always) to story progression, but interconnection is so much more rich palette for dramatic purposes.Sanctity of Merits takes the sting out of investing in those connections to the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T08:49:04-08:00","id":1010673,"title":"","content":"Some people find connections dull in comparison to ability to influence the setting themselves. Not everyone is interested in investing into external things like those. I also don't think that this has anything to do with minmaxing or not, but then again, I think that many people would be surprised at seeing what exactly a CofD &quot;minmaxed&quot; character is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T10:44:13-08:00","id":1010701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1010673#post1010673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that many people would be surprised at seeing what exactly a CofD &quot;minmaxed&quot; character is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like a Mage with no extra starting XP who can shiv people with 36 dice 9-Again Rote Action?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T10:54:49-08:00","id":1010706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1010701#post1010701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like a Mage with no extra starting XP who can shiv people with 36 dice 9-Again Rote Action?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More like a member of a legacy that sacrifices its enemies by co-locating them into the Volcano. Instant kill and mana for sacrifice. Add an Obsession with Volcano and some Justice Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:40:14-08:00","id":1011044,"title":"","content":"Question regarding page 242:<br /> <br /> &quot;An Exarchate Verge only provides its Yantra bonus and Paradox immunity to spells that use the Arcanum connected to its ruling Exarch. On the other hand, it provides +1 Reach to such spells by exploiting the Exarchs\u2019 mastery of the Lie...&quot;<br /> <br /> Does anyone understand this? What does it mean to provide both paradox immunity as well as +1 reach? If you're immune to paradox, reaching beyond arcana limits can't add paradox dice, right?<br /> Thanks<br /> <br /> Edit: found the answer. The reach is meaningless unless the spell leaves the area. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/919627-exarchate-verges?p=919656#post919656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if the spell doesn't leave the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 12-02-2016, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:49:19-08:00","id":1011054,"title":"","content":"Paradox immunity only applies if the spell stays in the verge, right? Maybe the +1 reach works all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:52:09-08:00","id":1011056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011054#post1011054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox immunity only applies if the spell stays in the verge, right? Maybe the +1 reach works all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's when the spell leaves the area via something like Remote Casting or Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:35:08-08:00","id":1011251,"title":"","content":"Sorry to butt in, I'm just wondering what exactly the requirements are for a being to be viable as a familiar. As far as I know there is a choice between spirits, ghosts, and goetia but does that entail that a familiar-to-be need be one of these or what? Can a Strix be coaxed into familiar-hood? Is it limited to sapient ephemeral beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:53:35-08:00","id":1011257,"title":"","content":"The familiar bond would be near-useless for a strix, because they don't suffer essence bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:43:17-08:00","id":1011672,"title":"","content":"1. Can you make a memory of someone so vivid (with Mind) that it can be used as representational yantra for spellcasting?<br /> 2. Can Signature Nimbus be used as sympathy yantra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:51:39-08:00","id":1011678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011672#post1011672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Can you make a memory of someone so vivid (with Mind) that it can be used as representational yantra for spellcasting?<br /> 2. Can Signature Nimbus be used as sympathy yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, in either case. I'm pretty sure Sympathy Yantras have to be actual, tangible <i>things</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:47:48-08:00","id":1011737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011672#post1011672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Can you make a memory of someone so vivid (with Mind) that it can be used as representational yantra for spellcasting?<br /> 2. Can Signature Nimbus be used as sympathy yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind treats thoughts as acceptable subjects for spells, much like Matter treats objects as acceptable subjects for spells. I would allow a memory to serve as a representational Yantra. You have to somehow &quot;have it on hand.&quot; which will probably require an active spell like Perfect Recall though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T18:47:59-08:00","id":1011777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011257#post1011257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The familiar bond would be near-useless for a strix, because they don't suffer essence bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are other reasons to form a familiar bond than essence bleed. Otherwise ghosts wouldn't bother. My question is what entities qualify for familiar bonding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T19:40:25-08:00","id":1011793,"title":"","content":"Ghosts have essence bleed too. It's negated by hanging around their Anchor, but if that's removed they'll lose Essence and get sucked into the Underworld. It really looks like just the primary three ephemeral entities can be made familiars. 'The spirit may not be greater than Rank 2,' implies they have to have Rank.<br /> <br /> I'd say strix couldn't be made familiars, what with them not being ephemeral entities, not having Rank, and not using Mana or Essence.<br /> <br /> If you would allow strix, you might as well allow vampires and prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2016, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:05:30-08:00","id":1011855,"title":"","content":"Would Space 1 and Forces 1 be sufficient for finding someone using a space knowing spell, a Forces unveiling spell, and a phone call?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:59:03-08:00","id":1011874,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has been asked before, but...<br /> <br /> Q: Using the &quot;Change Primary Spell Factor&quot; reach effect, can any spell factor be made primary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T01:31:49-08:00","id":1011904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011874#post1011874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been asked before, but...<br /> <br /> Q: Using the &quot;Change Primary Spell Factor&quot; reach effect, can any spell factor be made primary?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, by RAW only potency or duration can be primary spell factor (I personally run with it so any factor can be, but that's a homerule).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T03:50:05-08:00","id":1011936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011678#post1011678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so, in either case. I'm pretty sure Sympathy Yantras have to be actual, tangible <i>things</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Symbolic Yantras section speaks about sympathetic names, drawings, and carricatures. Signature Nimbus is a very personal thing for a mage and resides where he cast a spell (which creates sympathy). Nimbus is a unique representation of a mage... And I'm a little torn by this because it would mean that you can have sympathetic link to every caster of the every spell you came across.<br /> <br /> But yea, Sympathy Yantra:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Material sympathy represents the subject as he is now, or at<br /> the time the mage wants to affect him. It could be a piece<br /> of the target\u2019s physical substance, or a recent photograph<br /> or recording; an item the subject created within a month<br /> is also acceptable.<br /> \u2022 Representational sympathy is something that represents<br /> the subject though she has changed since \u2014 an old lock<br /> of hair or photo of the subject as a child, for example.<br /> \u2022 Symbolic sympathy includes indirect representations of<br /> the subject \u2014 a person\u2019s sympathetic name, drawings,<br /> caricatures, or posed and costumed photographs </div> </div> </div>Basically you need to see or gather part of the subject to have a sympathy yantra? (This nimbus thing bothers me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T03:54:05-08:00","id":1011937,"title":"","content":"I'd say a nimbus is more a signature than a representation. Certainly not something you can use as a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T04:26:09-08:00","id":1011943,"title":"","content":"Questions about mysteries:<br /> <br /> Is every single spell cast by other mages a (little) mystery that needs scrutinizing to determine which spell actually is? (excluding superficial information)<br /> And, if a mages does not have the right sight for a mystery, how much information could/should gain when opacity is removed?<br /> <br /> Opacity, btw, is personal? I mean, while scrutinizing, a mage lowers Opacity only for himself or for everyone else (I think it is the first, but just to be sure...)<br /> <br /> And, lastly, opacity could &quot;ramp back up&quot; on its own if enough time is spent away between one attempt at scrutinize and the other?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T05:30:24-08:00","id":1011956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011937#post1011937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a nimbus is more a signature than a representation. Certainly not something you can use as a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. You know that signature is a sympathy yantra, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T05:59:48-08:00","id":1011967,"title":"","content":"I don't, because it isn't.<br /> <br /> The thing they signed probably would be, but the signature itself isn't unless it's their sympathetic name.<br /> <br /> Anyway, a better comparison might be fingerprints. Saying the nimbus counts is like saying you can use anything somebody has ever touched as a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-04-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:01:11-08:00","id":1011971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011855#post1011855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Space 1 and Forces 1 be sufficient for finding someone using a space knowing spell, a Forces unveiling spell, and a phone call?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What's the Forces spell doing? Just dial the number and cast a Space 1 Locator spell remotely.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:11:08-08:00","id":1011977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011967#post1011967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't, because it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just gonna have some fun for a second: A person's sympathetic name counts as a sympathetic representational yantra, a signature is a person writing their own name, thus it would make sense to say that the signature nimbus is the person scrawling their magical name down when they cast spells. The question becomes is the magical name enough to cast on them sympathetically? I would say no because the whole point of a shadow name which is a magical identity with a magical name (That the signature nimbus is tied to) is to make using sympathetic magic on you more difficult.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> The memory as representational Yantra thing would have to be drawn from memories where you met the target or have other means of symbolically identifying him with your memories. Of course once you have that kind of thing in your memories you might as well make it easier to keep on hand by writing it down or making a drawing. That doesn't give you Sympathy to your target though, it's just the Yantra you need to work into your spell, you'll still have to get Sympathy somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T08:00:25-08:00","id":1012012,"title":"","content":"If you want to create a Rote for a spell that will basically always be a Wisdom Sin, does the act of creating the Rote itself constitute a Wisdom Sin?<br /> Case in question: My Moros wants to create a Rote for Create Ghost, but as creating an intelligent being without giving it indefinite Duration is a Wisdom Sin my ST ruled that because creating the Rote would require casting the Spell a several times to work out the Rote it would also involve several rolls for Acts of Hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T08:12:54-08:00","id":1012015,"title":"","content":"Just create really stupid ghosts. I wouldn't call a rank 1 &quot;intelligent&quot; by any stretch of the imagination.<br /> <br /> Yeah, in fact, this is explicit in the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Manes: Rank 1 ghosts. Most Manes are not truly<br /> intelligent, but can speak and act according to<br /> patterns complex enough to fake it. When confronted<br /> with something beyond their obsessions,<br /> their limitations become clear. </div> </div> </div>I don't know how the rote for an always-hurbistic spell would work, but Create Ghost definitely isn't one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-04-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:04:10-08:00","id":1012029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011793#post1011793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts have essence bleed too. It's negated by hanging around their Anchor, but if that's removed they'll lose Essence and get sucked into the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know that. Where is it mentioned? I thought they just literary could not move beyond their anchors in the mortal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:08:21-08:00","id":1012031,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's first edition. They changed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:23:57-08:00","id":1012037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1012029#post1012029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know that. Where is it mentioned? I thought they just literary could not move beyond their anchors in the mortal world.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the ephemeral entities section under Essence. In Mage it's on page 254.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits, Goetia, and ghosts outside of a suitable Condition bleed one point of Essence per hour. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:30:07-08:00","id":1012105,"title":"","content":"What does failing casting a spell represent?<br /> <br /> It says, 'The magic does not work,' and specifically for a Dramatic Failure, 'The magic does not work. The caster gains a Condition based on the intended outcome of the spell.' How much does it 'not work.' Is this just a failure like hoping for something to happen and it not happening? Or casting fireball and instead making an illusion of your deepest, darkest desire? What kind of Conditions pop up from this, specifically based on the intended outcome of the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:51:19-08:00","id":1012114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1012105#post1012105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does failing casting a spell represent?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO: Failure to properly enact the Imago, resulting in a whole lot of nothing. In the cases of a Dramatic Failure, you enact the Imago, but the Imago itself is faulty, resulting in a 'backfire'. In the case of a fireball, you might end up suddenly burned. In the case of a spell to control someone's mind, perhaps you suddenly become infatuated with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:33:12-08:00","id":1012183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1011971#post1011971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What's the Forces spell doing? Just dial the number and cast a Space 1 Locator spell remotely.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Given the subject of the spell isn't necessarily within range and that a sympathetic connection wasn't available either, I thought it might be necessary to have Forces in order to be able to see the radio waves used. But if it isn't necessary, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:24:56-08:00","id":1012208,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> Well. By RAW it is. If signature is handcrafted by the subject it is a Sympathy Yantra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>\u2022 Material sympathy represents the subject as he is now, or at</i><br /> <i>the time the mage wants to affect him. It could be a piece</i><br /> <i>of the target\u2019s physical substance, or a recent photograph</i><br /> <i>or recording;<b> an item the subject <u>created</u> within a month</b></i></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>is also acceptable</b></span>.</i> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Yes, yes. I'm aware that Sympathy Yantra is not the same as Sympathy. And I like explanation about why the mages Nimbus is not a Sympathy Yantra. It would mean that if mage works magic while he is not under a Shadow Name he leaves a lot of trails which is another reason for using those Names","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:54:24-08:00","id":1012226,"title":"","content":"That's <i>really </i>stretching the definition of &quot;created&quot;. And &quot;Item&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:16:45-08:00","id":1012273,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd say that it's less of an item created and more of a fingerprint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:22:52-08:00","id":1012457,"title":"","content":"I thought a little about arguing about what is created and what is an item but... there is no point in it. Lets look at it from the other side: isn't signature made/designed to <i>represent</i> a signee? Isn't it a <i>symbol </i>of someone? The only thing that can represent you more is a photography or a painting. Signature for me is like a country flag but for a person - and a flag is like a definition of 'representing' and 'symbolizing'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:31:45-08:00","id":1012460,"title":"","content":"...aren't you literally leaving a signature on your Watchtower to represent your new bond (sympathy) to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:44:44-08:00","id":1012462,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I totally forgot about this. I'm wondering though. I can see now why Signature Nimbus might not be a good Sympathy Yantra - wait - when I wrote it down I'm lost again. Signature. Nimbus. It represents your Magical Persona. It can't be used as Sympathy Yantra to your mundane self but targeting you by Shadow Name should be possible. Looks like tracking a culprit is a piece of cake if he is not a prime, space and time user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:46:02-08:00","id":1012463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1012460#post1012460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...aren't you literally leaving a signature on your Watchtower to represent your new bond (sympathy) to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is signing your Sympathetic name the same as leaving your signature nimbus? I reckon it's similar but is actually not useful as a source of Sympathy or it would lessen the value of a shadow name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:49:16-08:00","id":1012464,"title":"","content":"Now I wonder if Without a-race of Death should get a Reach option that literally make you leave no trace, including time and magical imprints (Supress Aura already kills your magical &quot;signals&quot;, so I don't think it's a stretch) . Definitely going to meditate that for my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:50:31-08:00","id":1012465,"title":"","content":"You can't cast on a mage's magical persona by speaking their shadow name aloud. This is no different. The nimbus is not a thing. It's a shape embedded into spells. You can't use a spell as a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T02:51:57-08:00","id":1012466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1012464#post1012464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I wonder if Without a-race of Death should get a Reach option that literally make you leave no trace, including time and magical imprints (Supress Aura already kills your magical &quot;signals&quot;, so I don't think it's a stretch) . Definitely going to meditate that for my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it. Different Reach clauses though, one for signature nimbus and another for time stamp and I think I'd allow a CoW against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-05-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T03:07:41-08:00","id":1012470,"title":"","content":"Reach for signature nimbus - why not, a death mage can observe it with his mage sight. But for time stamp? How do you supress it if you have no sense that can target it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:38:42-08:00","id":1012785,"title":"","content":"Can you use the same rote mudra for each of your Yantra slots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:45:53-08:00","id":1012791,"title":"","content":"No. You can use Yantra only once in a given way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:54:54-08:00","id":1012797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1012791#post1012791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. You can use Yantra only once in a given way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, good. That's what I thought. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:55:11-08:00","id":1012798,"title":"","content":"No. You can't use any Yantras for multiple slots. The closest is using the same tool as two or more different Yantras because it has more than one symbolical interpretation, but I find that to be quite rare. This can not be done with Mudras because they're symbols for specific spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T21:58:12-08:00","id":1014157,"title":"","content":"Since the updated version of Incognito Presence prevents those without supernatural senses from detecting the person under the veil, could such a veiled person safely cast a spell on himself that has obvious supernatural effects without suffering from the paradox effects of sleeper witnesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T00:04:23-08:00","id":1014197,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. That's acting with care and Wisdom. What you do from there might induce Dissonance though if you don't continue to be careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:47:01-08:00","id":1015574,"title":"","content":"Does using magic to apply a Manifestation Condition with Advanced Duration supercede the normal timeout resolutions of those Conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T00:40:50-08:00","id":1015589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1015574#post1015574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does using magic to apply a Manifestation Condition with Advanced Duration supercede the normal timeout resolutions of those Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think so, at least to some extent. Some of the Conditions are ended by the 'source of the Condition' being removed, which in this case would be the spell. Otherwise I'd be going off of p184's 'Bind Spirit' description. While you have to create the prerequisite Conditions, if they aren't already present, 'The entity immediately enters the Manifestation of the mage's choice, and may not leave it while the spell remains in effect.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:00:58-08:00","id":1015920,"title":"","content":"Are there any limitations as to what abilities an Ephermal entity can use to influence the physical world while in a state of twilight?<br /> I would imagine Influences can be used, but what about Numina? Especially stuff as potentially dangerous as Blast or Drain.<br /> <br /> Can Mages also cast Magic at Twilight entities, and out of Twilight at physical entities at will? Or does it require a conjunctional Arcana on the relevant frequency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:10:49-08:00","id":1015922,"title":"","content":"How does spending dice from your dice-pool work, specifically in regards to the many different variables Scale contains?<br /> <br /> I spend 2 dice on the Advanced Chart: The borders of my area-of-effect spell are as large as a small warehouse or parking lot; but if any target is larger than size 10 they're immune, and it can only impact 10 people inside that range?<br /> <br /> Or do I need to spend Scale dice twice in order to impact 10 subjects (-2 dice) of size 10 or lower (-2 more dice)?<br /> <br /> Does nuking 2 dice simply let my spell TARGET someone size 10 or lower; TARGET 10 individuals without impacting a huge area, or hit everyone inside the small warehouse or parking lot's area?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:20:29-08:00","id":1015923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1015922#post1015922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does spending dice from your dice-pool work, specifically in regards to the many different variables Scale contains?</div> </div> </div> </div>You choose between Area or Number of Subjects; Area Scale affects all applicable subjects within the area and needs Warding Gesture to exempt specific targets, while Number of Subjects sets the upper limits of both size and quantity of targets \u2014 taking a two-dice penalty on Advanced Scale lets you affect either everything the spell can effect within a small warehouse/large or up to ten individual targets of Size 10 or less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:32:12-08:00","id":1015961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1015920#post1015920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any limitations as to what abilities an Ephermal entity can use to influence the physical world while in a state of twilight?<br /> I would imagine Influences can be used, but what about Numina? Especially stuff as potentially dangerous as Blast or Drain.<br /> <br /> Can Mages also cast Magic at Twilight entities, and out of Twilight at physical entities at will? Or does it require a conjunctional Arcana on the relevant frequency?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Entities in Twilight can only attack or be attacked by other entities in the same phase of Twilight, or beings that are able to touch them through magic or other supernatural means (unless the attack utilizes the entity's bane).'<br /> <br /> Regarding the first part of your question, only if they see them, with certain exceptions. Something like Awe requires the ephemeral to be seen, so not unless they're able to see you in Twilight. Blast is an attack, so no. But Left-Handed Spanner allows you to just superimpose your Twilight form over the target.<br /> <br /> For the second part, you need to be either in that Twilight state, or have a power that lets you interact with them despite it. Spirit and Death, for instance, have powers that let you interact with and see ghosts despite not being in Twilight. Some of these powers last on a duration so don't require other spells used against ephemerals to be conjunctional, but if you're in a hurry and don't have anything set up like that yes you would have to use multiple arcana. A key exception is banes. A Matter mage can fill a room with knives and it won't harm an entity in Twilight, but if that entity has knives as a bane it will affect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T21:30:00-08:00","id":1015979,"title":"","content":"I'm confused about causing conditions/tilts with creative thaumaturgy. Two dot magic can create most mundane non-persistent conditions and four dot magic can create persistent conditions and a tilt is a reach effect on an attack spell. However, since conditions presumably end when the spell ends and tilts are how conditions work in combat the distinction seems semantic. <br /> <br /> For example say I use a life ruling spell to preemptively blind a known hostile member of the local seer pylon I spot at a nightclub for a week (very naughty of me). If he turns around and starts shooting at me blindly he should be under the blinded tilt and if he runs off and is unable to dispel the magic he'd be blinded for the entire week presumably as a persistent effect.<br /> <br /> Or is it that anything that could act as a persistent condition can't be recreated with ruling magic? e.g. I can't have duration longer than a scene or an effect like blindness/deafness/ataxia/sleep/etc that has a persistent variant. Similarly does this mean I can't cast like a sleep spell (life/mind) in the middle of combat and I'd have the condition as a reach effect on a direct attack spell? Because it seems odd to take a hostile action to end a conflict non-violently.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T02:57:48-08:00","id":1016041,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Ephemeral entities are not absent, they are immaterial - which is different. So even if you can't see them you can affect them by area casting. Fire or projectiles can't hurt them but Mind, Fate etc can affect them regardless of Twilight Frequency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:08:20-08:00","id":1016299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1016041#post1016041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Ephemeral entities are not absent, they are immaterial - which is different. So even if you can't see them you can affect them by area casting. Fire or projectiles can't hurt them but Mind, Fate etc can affect them regardless of Twilight Frequency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly more interested in what ephemeral entities can do really.<br /> So basically a Spirit can use any Numina to affect a physical entity, so long as it's not an &quot;attack&quot;, and any internal requirements are fulfilled?<br /> So Awe could be activated, but would then require a manifestation such as Image for it to affect material beings, Blast cannot be used to affect material beings unless the Spirit has used Materialize to exit Twilight, and Drain can be used against physical beings from Twilight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:27:29-08:00","id":1016304,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> Awe requires that people be able to see the entity using the Numina, Blast doesn't require a being Materialize or exit Twilight, which is the same as Drain. Technically, Awe doesn't require a spirit to leave Twilight either, but a Materialized spirit is usually visible by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-12-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T04:56:20-08:00","id":1016984,"title":"","content":"How obvious must be incorporating a Yantra into a spell? Is it enough to touch you dedicated tool or do you need to point it and weave?<br /> E.g. a dedicated cross pendant... <br /> 1. Touching your bare chest skin<br /> 2. Pushing chest forward and saying &quot;BY THE POWER OF MY CROSS!!!11one&quot;<br /> 3. Holding it in hand and pointing at your water to change it in wine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:39:57-08:00","id":1017001,"title":"","content":"I would say you have to use it, the use may be subtle but it still has to actually interact with you or the subject of the spell, which is why each Yantra beyond the one reflexive one takes an entire Instant Action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:32:36-08:00","id":1017270,"title":"","content":"Do Familiars have Bans and Banes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:41:24-08:00","id":1017285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1017270#post1017270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Familiars have Bans and Banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, on account of the Familiar Condition not causing them to stop being what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:41:39-08:00","id":1017286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1017270#post1017270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Familiars have Bans and Banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T01:19:48-08:00","id":1017540,"title":"","content":"<u>Time question:</u><br /> <br /> My acanthus player asked if is it possible to have the second level spell &quot;choose the thread&quot; ramped up from its two rerolls to potency rerolls as a level 3 spell (Weaving?)<br /> Is it possible or is patterning needed in order to do that?<br /> <br /> <u>Questions about mysteries:</u><br /> <br /> Is every single spell cast by other mages a (little) mystery that needs scrutinizing to determine which spell actually is? (excluding superficial information)<br /> And, if a mages does not have the right sight for a mystery, how much information could/should gain when opacity is removed?<br /> <br /> Opacity, btw, is personal? I mean, while scrutinizing, a mage lowers Opacity only for himself or for everyone else (I think it is the first, but just to be sure...)<br /> <br /> And, lastly, opacity could &quot;ramp back up&quot; on its own if enough time is spent away between one attempt at scrutinize and the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T02:04:04-08:00","id":1017545,"title":"","content":"Time question: Perfecting allows you to apply rote action quality and thats the power level you should have buut... I discovered that 3rd dot lets you do things that 2nd can but stedilly. So you could have two rolls for every action for the rest of the scene. Or if you still wan't more rerolls I would cap it on Time dots so Weaving would give you three rolls from which you can choose but still on a number of actions equal to potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:31:30-08:00","id":1017568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1017540#post1017540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Questions about mysteries:</u><br /> <br /> Is every single spell cast by other mages a (little) mystery that needs scrutinizing to determine which spell actually is? (excluding superficial information)<br /> And, if a mages does not have the right sight for a mystery, how much information could/should gain when opacity is removed?<br /> <br /> Opacity, btw, is personal? I mean, while scrutinizing, a mage lowers Opacity only for himself or for everyone else (I think it is the first, but just to be sure...)<br /> <br /> And, lastly, opacity could &amp;quot;ramp back up&amp;quot; on its own if enough time is spent away between one attempt at scrutinize and the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, every spell is a Mystery with an Opacity rating and everything. If a Mage doesn't have the right Sight for a Mystery I don't think they gain any benefit from it (Top of pg. 92). So they receive no Surface information and can't use Scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Opacity lowering is personal, Opacity increasing isn't.<br /> <br /> Opacity ramping back up isn't normally how that works, but it could if that's part of the Mystery's function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:07:50-08:00","id":1017578,"title":"","content":"Many thanks to both of you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T12:46:07-08:00","id":1017756,"title":"","content":"Assuming one wants to play a Sleepwalker in a group of full-fledged Mages, are there any options to help avoid getting tossed around like a ragdoll by enemy Mages? Sleepers get some psuedo-options, I'm aware, but Sleepwalkers can't take them due to no longer triggering Paradox and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T12:58:07-08:00","id":1017765,"title":"","content":"Get enchanted by your buddies and carry a fully charged trinket of Thaumium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:22:56-08:00","id":1017796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1017756#post1017756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming one wants to play a Sleepwalker in a group of full-fledged Mages, are there any options to help avoid getting tossed around like a ragdoll by enemy Mages? Sleepers get some psuedo-options, I'm aware, but Sleepwalkers can't take them due to no longer triggering Paradox and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well by definition any of the other splats is a sleepwalker but even then a mage can do so much beyond what a standard character can.<br /> If you just want to play a mortal and be on the same level face to face I can pretty much guarantee that you won't be. However, if you were to get the equivalent xp as a starting mage is worth compared to a base human you may be able to do something by building up an organization and investing in other social networks. This organization could be run under the rules of a mystery cult. I may suggest looking at witch finder (hunter) for something to give this cult if the ST allowed. It is low magic but being able to access any magic would be a great asset in this situation.<br /> One of the best defences a sleepwalker could have in this situation is to ALWAYS be surrounded by sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T09:49:48-08:00","id":1018128,"title":"","content":"How does one recharge an Artifact's Mana? Is Channel Mana the only way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:01:40-08:00","id":1018131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1018128#post1018128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one recharge an Artifact's Mana? Is Channel Mana the only way?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:10:23-08:00","id":1018133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1018128#post1018128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one recharge an Artifact's Mana? Is Channel Mana the only way?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can just transfer the Mana in, presumably \u2014 &quot;[you] can access and refill the item's Mana as if it were [your] own&quot; doesn't suggest any spell-dependent requirement to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:52:16-08:00","id":1018261,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Artifact's mana battery function got nerfed - it was self-regeneratiing in 1Ed. You can't use it for free mana regen any more, and it's a good thing, I think - that function honestly was more of an system artifact that intended feature (because people kept buying cheap Artifact as a mana source and mana pool extension, instead as anything else). 2nd ED Artifacts still can extend your mana pool as a side bonus to main dish of being, duh, an artifact. I think it's healthier for the game.<br /> <br /> *Extended mana pool is still a great benefit. Because it's so easy to regenerate mana while you are not chased by abyssal horrors or whatever, ability to have some extra mana on your person can be much more useful than another source of mana regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T23:28:51-08:00","id":1019633,"title":"","content":"Making sure I'm parsing the fine print of Sanctum correctly:<br /> <br /> If you have Gnosis 3 and Sanctum 3, and you have two spells sustained through the extra spell control the Merit gives you and three running on your regular spell control, will casting another spell outside of your Sanctum will cost you three extra Reach instead of the one Reach it would cost if the spells on your Sanctum's control didn't exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T01:47:17-08:00","id":1019663,"title":"","content":"That's how I understood it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T02:53:08-08:00","id":1019674,"title":"","content":"Question about Incognito Presence: if a person under said spell enters a grapple, with the intent of pummeling his foe unconscious, does the spell still keep on working? Is the opponent now grappling with an invisible foe (using the blinded tilt)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T03:36:45-08:00","id":1019686,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to recover from turning into one of the Mad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T03:59:28-08:00","id":1019694,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2648_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2648\" data-vbnamecard=\"2648\">TelperionST</a> I would say that this is a viable Reach effect.<br /> <br /> Edit: It could work for number of actions equal to Potency withstood by Resolve if you are looking for more balanced take, but I don't think it's necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-20-2016, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:07:33-08:00","id":1019699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1019686#post1019686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to recover from turning into one of the Mad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not permanently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:16:36-08:00","id":1019705,"title":"","content":"Here's another question: a character with 7 health boxes has 6 magically resistant bashing damage and gains 8 regular bashing damage. Does the magically resistant bashing damage get removed from the character sheet once the damage is upgraded to lethal? I.e. does the character now have 6 points of magically resistant lethal damage and 1 point of regular lethal damage, or just 7 points of regular lethal damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:21:48-08:00","id":1019707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2648_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2648\" data-vbnamecard=\"2648\">TelperionST</a> Upgraded means that it's still the same kind but worse. In other words, it stacks. So you'll end up with 6 points of resistant lethal damage and 1 regular lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:46:16-08:00","id":1019848,"title":"","content":"In the Verges section of the 2E, there is a mention of the spells not risking Paradox, except for when a Sleeper is present during the *duration* of the spell. I take it duration is supposed to be &quot;casting&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:55:14-08:00","id":1019850,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sounds like a typo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:55:24-08:00","id":1019851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1019848#post1019848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Verges section of the 2E, there is a mention of the spells not risking Paradox, except for when a Sleeper is present during the *duration* of the spell. I take it duration is supposed to be &quot;casting&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the nature of risking Paradox as mentioned in page 298's sidebar on obvious magic, almost certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:44:50-08:00","id":1019877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1019686#post1019686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to recover from turning into one of the Mad?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Get an archmaster to weld you a new Wisdom trait together. Otherwise, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:31:18-08:00","id":1019905,"title":"","content":"Player was casting a Veiling from Ghosts spell last session, but they have a ghost familiar. Is there any way to opt the familiar out? Also, they would still be able to use their familiar-sense-sharing to see through each others senses, right?<br /> <br /> It ended with a fail-to-Dramatic Failure that turned them into a beacon for ghosts but I'd like to know for next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:37:31-08:00","id":1019919,"title":"","content":"Fate and Space both seem to add options for keying spells with exemptions. Fate, for example, lets you Scry a one-way window. Space lets you key wards. Just use those as examples.<br /> <br /> Seeing through each others' senses should be unaffected, though I imagine the ghost still wouldn't see the Mage when borrowing their vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:40:33-08:00","id":1019922,"title":"","content":"Don't know about the exemption but I'd be inclined to say it doesn't matter since it wouldn't block their connection and senses swapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T13:19:34-08:00","id":1019945,"title":"","content":"I go with a rule that every arcanum can exclude their respective purview with a reach. Space and Fate are just very broad in their sympathy and intentions. So you can Key Life spell to affect only humans but you can't make it affect only every man that has a red coin in his pocket, thats up to Fate or Space","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T22:31:55-08:00","id":1020189,"title":"","content":"Another parsing check, this time for combined spells: Does &quot;Free Reach is determined as normal&quot; mean that, for instance, a boilerplate Matter 5 Spirit 2 Moros could cast Opener of the Way on an object with four free Reach by combining it with Find the Balance albeit with the substantially lower base pool of Gnosis + Spirit - 2?<br /> <br /> Also, how is the primary spell factor determined for combined spells whose primary factors are different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-21-2016, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T00:11:52-08:00","id":1020210,"title":"","content":"Couple of newbie questions (although I feel weird asking them as I play Awakening since it's beginning) about the 2E which I'm discovering right now:<br /> 1. Is there any limits to how many times can you Reach with one spell?<br /> 2. The Yantra limit imposed by Gnosis are max. Yantras per spell or total Yantras a character has?<br /> 3.Can someone explain me in &quot;for dummies&quot; version the thing with primary spell factor and modifiers, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T00:31:17-08:00","id":1020216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1020210#post1020210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of newbie questions (although I feel weird asking them as I play Awakening since it's beginning) about the 2E which I'm discovering right now:<br /> 1. Is there any limits to how many times can you Reach with one spell?<br /> 2. The Yantra limit imposed by Gnosis are max. Yantras per spell or total Yantras a character has?<br /> 3.Can someone explain me in &quot;for dummies&quot; version the thing with primary spell factor and modifiers, please?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. No, you can reach up to infinity, provided you're willing to risk the paradox for over-reaching.<br /> 2. Yantra per spell. So at gnosis 1 you can use High Speech and your Shadow Name and that's it (2 yantra), in a completely different casting (maybe the same spell, maybe not) you could use a magical tool and an environment yantra.<br /> 3. I'm a little drunk right now and I can't remember all the info needed to answer this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T03:39:40-08:00","id":1020255,"title":"","content":"3.<br /> Each spell factor starts at 1. Primary spell factor - which is either Potency or Duration, based on spell - may start at your Arcana. You may buy spell factors by reducing your spellcasting dicepool, 1 spell factor per 2 dice spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:09:52-08:00","id":1020965,"title":"","content":"Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. In the Learning Legacy Attainments table, the first rank Minimum Ruling Arcanum is supposed to be 2, not 1 right?<br /> <br /> 2. How is it with the Soul Marks spell and the 3rd Attainment detection, if you are the creator of the Legacy? Do you already detect the Attainment without Reach, or is the Gnosis level important only as a requirement for the Attainment and you still need to Reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:52:38-08:00","id":1021052,"title":"","content":"Sympathetic Connections can be affected and detected by Space, so is it possible to create a Space spell that alerts you when a Sympathetic Connection is active? For the purposes of such a spell, what counts as active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:12:54-08:00","id":1021079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021052#post1021052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathetic Connections can be affected and detected by Space, so is it possible to create a Space spell that alerts you when a Sympathetic Connection is active? For the purposes of such a spell, what counts as active?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems a bit vague, honestly. I guess it would be narrowed specifically to only when a Sympathetic Connection is being &quot;tapped&quot;, as in it's being used for a spell or is a subject for a spell. Otherwise, I don't know how a Connection can be made active, such as when a child thinks about their parent and how they're doing( in my mind that causes a tug or flash to go through the connection, but that just makes it seem like such Connections are always active once they exist in the first place).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:31:58-08:00","id":1021084,"title":"","content":"I suppose by active I mean that the Connection is in a state where it could potentially increase, which basically boils down to when the two people having a connection to each other are interacting. I figure that while all of your Connections hang about on you and diminish over time from inactivity then there must be an inverse state that Space might be able to detect though I hesitate to say that moving from one level of Connection state to another should be the minimum requirement for a detectable &quot;event.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:53:25-08:00","id":1021088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021084#post1021084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose by active I mean that the Connection is in a state where it could potentially increase, which basically boils down to when the two people having a connection to each other are interacting. I figure that while all of your Connections hang about on you and diminish over time from inactivity then there must be an inverse state that Space might be able to detect though I hesitate to say that moving from one level of Connection state to another should be the minimum requirement for a detectable &quot;event.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That works something akin to Oaths Fulfilled, so yes, I'd think it's possible as a Knowing Practice. Name ideas include His Heart Grew 3 Sizes, and Loves Me Not, like the little song","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:53:28-08:00","id":1021089,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure such a spell exists in 1E in Seers of the Throne. Either way, I'd allow it as an Unveiling spell cast on a specific connection that alerts you when it's activated during the duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:06:15-08:00","id":1021293,"title":"","content":"Still think it should be Knowing, not Unveiling. Maybe I'm just nitpicking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T00:07:26-08:00","id":1021487,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for Mages to detect Infrastructure from Demon? I'm guessing no, but I'd find it very useful if anyone can remember off-hand where in what books it discusses this. My current mode for running as ST is that I have Embeds and Infrastructure hidden even from Mages second senses and sights, but having more evidence for doing this would be useful.<br /> <br /> If Mages can though, <i>how</i> they can will become my next question--for example does it require archmastery or can ordinary mages have a hope of finding and interacting with Infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T02:04:47-08:00","id":1021497,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the Demon Storyteller book have a section on the Awakened? There was some stuff on their interaction in the old thread with temporary 2e rules in it... but that seems to have gone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T05:24:39-08:00","id":1021535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021487#post1021487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for Mages to detect Infrastructure from Demon? I'm guessing no, but I'd find it very useful if anyone can remember off-hand where in what books it discusses this. My current mode for running as ST is that I have Embeds and Infrastructure hidden even from Mages second senses and sights, but having more evidence for doing this would be useful.<br /> <br /> If Mages can though, <i>how</i> they can will become my next question--for example does it require archmastery or can ordinary mages have a hope of finding and interacting with Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Infrastructure&quot; is just normal stuff, until it moves into the correct configuration to produce Output, and it's that that triggers Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> And no, Embeds also trigger Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T11:21:30-08:00","id":1021624,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/74456-detecting-god-machine-infrastructure-with-awakened-magic?p=75888#post75888\">There's a whole thread about it</a>. It's pretty helpful but technically I believe pre-second edition mage, from the stopgap rules. I linked directly to Dave's post.<br /> <br /> There's a section in the Demon Storyteller's Guide talking about how Demons view mages and how to sort of plan their powers from the viewpoint of a Demon game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-24-2016, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T21:15:33-08:00","id":1021810,"title":"","content":"How does <i>Words of Truth (Prime 2) </i>actually work?<br /> <br /> The spell itself states that &quot;The mage speaks with tongues of fire, and the world listens. So long as the words the mage speaks are objectively true and the mage herself knows them to be true, all subjects of this spell can hear her and understand her clearly, regardless of distance, noise, or language barriers&quot;.<br /> <br /> However it then states that the spell cannot be used for the testing of theories, such as stating &quot;Frank died when he fell off that cliff&quot;, when the result is ambiguous, the spell failing if you do not know the Truth. However this itself causes more issues with regards to the potential for the spell to actually be used for Truth detection when yo u consider the phrase &quot;So long as the words the mage speaks are objectively true&quot;. If you truly believe that Frank died when he fell off that cliff, say for instance you saw his broken and mangled body below, then the spell should function and you should seem to be stating the truth when you make that claim.<br /> <br /> However what happens if he in fact did not die, but instead had weaved a cunning illusion? Would the objective truth that he is alive disrupt the spell and render it incapable of being used? This may in many situations not be available for use for theory testing, however when you apply judicious usage of memory modification, you can quickly ensure that you believe whatever you say, and would thus be able to use the spell.<br /> <br /> So instead, is <i>Words of Truth </i>only capable of communicating sincerity of intention and belief? If so, then the objective, Supernal nature of Prime's Truth aspect seems to be flawed from the beginning and open to rampant abuse by less than perfectly moral and forthright Mages, who wish to trick others into believing that their sincerely, personally held opinions and perspectives (including those which they fabricate to serve their needs) are the truth.<br /> <br /> Apologies, this may be a less than &quot;simple&quot; question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:57:30-08:00","id":1021892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021810#post1021810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does <i>Words of Truth (Prime 2) </i>actually work?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I recall that DaveB spoiled this spell particular spell during open development. Your questions and more resulted in many, many pages of discussion with little resolution. The actual release of the book has done little to settle the issues.<br /> <br /> The spell will hopefully be more fully explained in the promised Mage 2e FAQ.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T02:19:57-08:00","id":1021906,"title":"","content":"I'd personally have it be that the spell only works on statements that are both objectively true and the mage believes to be true, but that would make it a bit too easy for truth-testing for some people, because the mage can challenge their beliefs through it. At the same time though, the mage needs bloody good reason to use the spell in that fashion if it's something they actually believe to be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T02:25:06-08:00","id":1021907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021906#post1021906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time though, the mage needs bloody good reason to use the spell in that fashion if it's something they actually believe to be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a very simple reason for them to do that with a belief that they believe to be true: <i>they want to convince someone else</i>.<br /> <br /> Suppose, for instance, we have a devout Muslim Obrimos with Prime 2. He, wishing to spread knowledge of the truth to his friends, casts the spell and proclaims <i>&quot;There is no God but God and Mohammend is his Prophet.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Now what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T03:36:51-08:00","id":1021923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021907#post1021907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a very simple reason for them to do that with a belief that they believe to be true: <i>they want to convince someone else</i>.<br /> <br /> Suppose, for instance, we have a devout Muslim Obrimos with Prime 2. He, wishing to spread knowledge of the truth to his friends, casts the spell and proclaims <i>&quot;There is no God but God and Mohammend is his Prophet.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Now what?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...and the mage herself <i>knows</i> them to be true...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that the difference between &quot;knowing&quot; someone is dead and &quot;knowing&quot; the truth about your religion is that one instance allows you to figure out the truth, at least in theory (a literal &quot;reality check&quot; for the possibility of the ideas' existence in context of the rest of the world, the rules of the world must allow the check), while the other is inherently about what may be a very sincere faith, but at its core is still just faith.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's about the faith/proof dichotomy. There is a reason for why the Obrimos tend to be so logically minded. Prime is the Arcanum of Truth and truth has to be internally consistent by definition, *always*. And logic is pretty much a mental exercise about keeping things consistent. By trying to persuade someone about something that you can't logically connect to reality, you are already leaving out a key component of the spell symbolism. What you believe might even be true, but without that ability to link it all together, you can't cast the spell. You also need to believe in what you are saying, because not standing by what you are saying, you pretty much go against yourself. For Prime, that's a big no-no, too.<br /> <br /> At least that's what I keep telling myself to justify how the spell can be used without breaking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 12-25-2016, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:39:04-08:00","id":1021934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021907#post1021907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a very simple reason for them to do that with a belief that they believe to be true: <i>they want to convince someone else</i>.<br /> <br /> Suppose, for instance, we have a devout Muslim Obrimos with Prime 2. He, wishing to spread knowledge of the truth to his friends, casts the spell and proclaims <i>&quot;There is no God but God and Mohammend is his Prophet.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Now what?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The spell would fail, because Islam isn't objectively true (unless the ST is running a world where it is of course), which is why I said it'd have to be both objectively true and thought to be true by the mage. So you wouldn't get stuff like proving your religion through a spell, because that isn't an objective truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:10:07-08:00","id":1021958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021923#post1021923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;...and the mage herself <i>knows</i> them to be true...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that the difference between &quot;knowing&quot; someone is dead and &quot;knowing&quot; the truth about your religion is that one instance allows you to figure out the truth, at least in theory (a literal &quot;reality check&quot; for the possibility of the ideas' existence in context of the rest of the world, the rules of the world must allow the check), while the other is inherently about what may be a very sincere faith, but at its core is still just faith.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's about the faith/proof dichotomy. There is a reason for why the Obrimos tend to be so logically minded. Prime is the Arcanum of Truth and truth has to be internally consistent by definition, *always*. And logic is pretty much a mental exercise about keeping things consistent. By trying to persuade someone about something that you can't logically connect to reality, you are already leaving out a key component of the spell symbolism. What you believe might even be true, but without that ability to link it all together, you can't cast the spell. You also need to believe in what you are saying, because not standing by what you are saying, you pretty much go against yourself. For Prime, that's a big no-no, too.<br /> <br /> At least that's what I keep telling myself to justify how the spell can be used without breaking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens is that the game stops while the players have a philosophical debate about the nature of knowledge? :P What exactly counts as &quot;knowing&quot; something remains a highly contested question in epistemology - what level of certainty do you need to have in order to be able to say &quot;I know X&quot; rather than just &quot;I believe X&quot;? Can you &quot;know&quot; X when the truth is actually not-X, if you had excellent reasons for believing X to be true but were wrong through no fault of your own? If you believe X for spurious reasons but happen to be right through dumb luck, can you be said to &quot;know&quot; X?<br /> <br /> In any case, I think the definition of &quot;faith&quot; you are working with is a bit muddled - or at least, is not the sense that the religious people I know would use it in this context. As I read it (and feel free to correct me if I've misinterpreted you), you seem to be proposing &quot;faith&quot; as a sort of epistemic category in which a) &quot;faith&quot; statements are not subject to the same standards of proof or disproof as other statements, and b) they cannot be held with the same level of certainty as other statements. This would seem to put them in a similar category to, say, statements of personal preference, like &quot;pineapple is the best fruit&quot;; it would be silly to ask whether that statement is &quot;objectively true&quot;, and if someone cast Words of Truth and then said that, I would expect the result to be a big fat nothing.<br /> <br /> The thing is, in my experience, the vast majority of people who <i>hold</i> religious beliefs don't regard their beliefs that way. <i>They</i> think that their beliefs are objectively true (even someone holding a belief along the lines of &quot;all gods are real for the person believing in them&quot; believes that <i>that</i> is objectively true). And they think that they have compelling reasons to do so, whether those be elaborate intellectual systems, historical accounts, personal experience, or what-have-you. You don't have to find their reasons convincing - I don't - but I don't think it's reasonable to say that the truth or falsehood of those beliefs is intrinsically unknowable. They are, after all, making a more-or-less specific claim about the cosmos: that it contains a being or beings fitting the description in the Qu'ran (or in the Bible, or the Talmud, or whatever body of religious doctrines they hold to), which has done such-and-such things and will do other things. These claims are difficult (to put it mildly) to empirically test with the tools available to us in the real world, but that doesn't mean that that they are <i>in principle</i> things impossible to know. (Indeed, in the case of religions that promise an afterlife, we all perform a fairly unambiguous check of their truth at some point: we die. We are not, thereafter, in any position to communicate our findings, but either we experience the predicted afterlife, or we don't.) So if you have a spell that explicitly checks against <i>objective truth</i> (and a lot of religions <i>define</i> their deity or deities as the foundation of all truth), I don't think &quot;well, that's just faith&quot; works as a justification for the spell not to apply. If &quot;just faith&quot; puts religious beliefs in the same category as statements like &quot;the colour blue is awesome*&quot;, then in the sense that's relevant to their adherents, &quot;just faith&quot; means they are false.<br /> <br /> Now, I agree that allowing Words of Truth to test religious beliefs breaks the setting horribly. I just don't think this approach works as a way to get around it. (My personal solution is to houserule out all references in the spell to &quot;objective truth&quot;, full stop; it convinces people that you are sincere. Much easier to fit into the setting, and, IMO, also more interesting. YMMV, naturally.) <br /> <br /> * It is, by the way. OBJECTIVE TRUTH! *Casts Words of Truth*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021934#post1021934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell would fail, because Islam isn't objectively true (unless the ST is running a world where it is of course), which is why I said it'd have to be both objectively true and thought to be true by the mage. So you wouldn't get stuff like proving your religion through a spell, because that isn't an objective truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so now you have a world in which either:<br /> <br /> a) Islam is objectively true, and everyone listening knows it;<br /> b) Islam is objectively not true, and at least one person (the caster) knows it, because if it <i>were</i>, then the spell would have worked.<br /> <br /> (You can fill in any religion you please in place of Islam, with the same result; I picked it because it has a very short and catchy statement of its central doctrine.)<br /> <br /> Either way, the truth or falsehood of that religion in now a settled question. And this can be repeated by any mage with Prime 2 and religious convictions of any sort. Any new mage can be told, with absolute assurance, &quot;oh, yeah, that's the One True Faith&quot;, or, alternatively, &quot;yeah, we haven't found the One True Faith yet, but <i>these</i> definitely aren't it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:32:26-08:00","id":1021965,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12425\" data-vbnamecard=\"12425\">General Tacticus</a><br /> <br /> To clarify, I generally consider the word &quot;belief&quot; to mean &quot;personal stance on a certain matter, rational or irrational&quot;, while &quot;faith&quot; would be a subgroup of that definition meaning &quot;irrational belief in the existence or capabilities of something or someone&quot;. So faith would deal with issues of objective existence, not with what is generally considered personal preference.<br /> <br /> I pretty much agree with you regarding changing the definition of the spell, though. As I mentioned before, what I wrote is pretty much just a flimsy excuse to try not to break the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 12-25-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:40:48-08:00","id":1021968,"title":"","content":"Heh, I can see an argument just like this heating up the nights of many Obrimos and confusing the hell out of them - in-game characters don't even have the privilege of access to the spell descriptions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T19:38:23-08:00","id":1022173,"title":"","content":"Simple answer: The statement is too broad for a true/false statement. Conceptual breadth/depth is important. If I say &quot;My son is a good person&quot;, there are so many possible definitions of &quot;good&quot; that the statement cannot be ruled objectively true or false.<br /> <br /> If someone states &quot;There is a God&quot; as a part of the spell, they must know what they mean by God, clearly and unambiguously, and that definition WILL be conveyed in their words.<br /> <br /> Same with the Muslim statement of faith. If the deity a Muslim Mage sees in the shahadah is in any way real, it'd turn up true or mangled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:31:48-08:00","id":1022545,"title":"","content":"What would it take to change another Mage's Shadow Name?<br /> Archmastery in Prime? Mind? Both?<br /> <br /> Alternatively could you just mundanely or mystically convince them to change their mystic identity? <br /> Thinking of story where a Mage flew too close to Helios and was branded &quot;Icarus&quot; for his impudence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T20:13:30-08:00","id":1022595,"title":"","content":"To change your shadow name you just have to convince people to start using your new shadow name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T20:17:49-08:00","id":1022598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022595#post1022595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To change your shadow name you just have to convince people to start using your new shadow name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I was asking, but that also sounds like rubbish. There's no way your mystical identity is determined by popular opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T21:47:44-08:00","id":1022613,"title":"","content":"Mages generally choose their own Shadow Name, and are free to use a different name if they want.<br /> <br /> Changing a Shadow Name might only present a problem if a mage possesses the Shadow Name Merit, and then he or she would just redistribute the dots under Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:19:30-08:00","id":1022620,"title":"","content":"A shadow name isn't some fundamental aspect of your character's metaphysical self, it's a title and persona that they use around other mages and other mages will use to refer to them. To change it all you'd really need to do is say &quot;yeah, I'm no longer Arsenic, I'm now Golden-Eye&quot;. It's as hard as playing a different character in an rpg when you get sick of your old one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T22:43:32-08:00","id":1022624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022620#post1022620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A shadow name isn't some fundamental aspect of your character's metaphysical self, it's a title and persona that they use around other mages and other mages will use to refer to them. To change it all you'd really need to do is say &quot;yeah, I'm no longer Arsenic, I'm now Golden-Eye&quot;. It's as hard as playing a different character in an rpg when you get sick of your old one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The metaphysical significance afforded to the persona nevertheless suggests it's not a change made lightly, particularly if you aren't yet far-gone enough to only value your time spent Not Being A Mage for the stealth benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T02:59:33-08:00","id":1022667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022620#post1022620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A shadow name isn't some fundamental aspect of your character's metaphysical self, it's a title and persona that they use around other mages and other mages will use to refer to them. To change it all you'd really need to do is say &quot;yeah, I'm no longer Arsenic, I'm now Golden-Eye&quot;. It's as hard as playing a different character in an rpg when you get sick of your old one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really mesh though with how your shadow name apparently influences your fate. To use the provided example, no Mage known as Odin should expect to keep both eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:02:47-08:00","id":1022670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022667#post1022667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't really mesh though with how your shadow name apparently influences your fate. To use the provided example, no Mage known as Odin should expect to keep both eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That comes from you taking the set of symbols that you associate with your shadow name into yourself. It totally meshes with it when you consider it like that, cause changing shadow name is just replacing the symbols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:50:31-08:00","id":1022684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022598#post1022598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not what I was asking, but that also sounds like rubbish. There's no way your mystical identity is determined by popular opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Shadow Name is still a name, and even though it carries mystical significance it isn't necessarily any harder to change than your mortal name and probably it's less difficult. If you want a name change to stick though that includes convincing other people that you should be called differently. Hence my comment.<br /> <br /> What were actually asking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T04:04:52-08:00","id":1022687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022670#post1022670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That comes from you taking the set of symbols that you associate with your shadow name into yourself. It totally meshes with it when you consider it like that, cause changing shadow name is just replacing the symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was originally asking however, and which I'd like to know, is whether it's possible to change and fix someone else's symbols.<br /> If it's only so transitory a part of themself that they can change it at will, perhaps that wouldn't require Archmastery to manipulate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T04:35:08-08:00","id":1022689,"title":"","content":"No, it wouldn't. It doesn't even require magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T04:54:05-08:00","id":1022690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022687#post1022687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I was originally asking however, and which I'd like to know, is whether it's possible to change and fix someone else's symbols.<br /> If it's only so transitory a part of themself that they can change it at will, perhaps that wouldn't require Archmastery to manipulate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's such a transitory part of themselves that they can change it with little effort. If you were to use magic to change it it'd likely just require patterning or even weaving (in mind I'd say).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T06:07:41-08:00","id":1022708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1022667#post1022667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't really mesh though with how your shadow name apparently influences your fate. To use the provided example, no Mage known as Odin should expect to keep both eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's if a mage takes the Shadow Name Merit. Virtually all mages take one or more shadow names, not all of them so incorporate that name into their magical symbolism that it becomes an actual merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:29:15-08:00","id":1022771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1021907#post1021907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a very simple reason for them to do that with a belief that they believe to be true: <i>they want to convince someone else</i>.<br /> <br /> Suppose, for instance, we have a devout Muslim Obrimos with Prime 2. He, wishing to spread knowledge of the truth to his friends, casts the spell and proclaims <i>&quot;There is no God but God and Mohammend is his Prophet.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Now what?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to bring up an old question but I'm going to throw my two-bits in because I didn't see anyone address this.<br /> <br /> When big problems come up, well, maybe some will see it as a cop-out but I'd just remind players somehow of the existence of Exarchs. For me, this isn't even a cop-out, as it seems vitally important to understanding and preparing for high-level play or really important world-spanning mysteries to include how the Exarch's are controlling or veiling various aspects of the world.<br /> <br /> Thus, all religious questions must be ambiguous or impossible to dissect due to the influence of the Father. The Father will no doubt have made sure that no Mage can tip any religion away from subtly serving Him by using his own arcanum against him--and that would be the goal of the Father, to slowly pervert all religions to somehow serving Him, no matter what the religion is supposed to be about. Or that's how I did things.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the Prophet does much of the same. If you try to use the Time Arcanum to empirically test and observe Jesus of Nazareth to justify or fight Christianity, you're going to get disappointing results, because there is no way two or even three (Ruin) Iron Seal Exarch's are going to let you find a linch-pin detail for a religion that has affected almost the entire world for over millennia. The same with the Muslim faith. It wouldn't matter if Islam is the true faith or not--The Father doesn't want anyone knowing for certain, as it would thwart the Father's method for controlling humans.<br /> <br /> My players tended to use the truth spell for interrogations, by-the-by.<br /> <br /> The only problem I ever had with my own approach is that any religious players or characters will then want to know how or why God allows the Exarch's to twist or hide His truths, but I guess that's no different than asking about the &quot;problem of evil&quot; so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:26:36-08:00","id":1022997,"title":"","content":"I'd tend to go with the devout muslim not exactly surviving the Awakening. You can't really go through a transcendant mystical experience and then just go on as you were. Either their religious beleifs are ripped apart, or they'll be pretty radically reinterpreted.<br /> When a sleeper says &quot;There is not God but God and Muhammad is his prophet is Muhammad' they're effectively repeating a religious slogan, when an Awakened says that I'd imagine it'd be closer to expressing some fundamental truth about the world. That's not something you want to do to a sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T18:05:07-08:00","id":1024591,"title":"","content":"Do Aimed Spells have to be thrown immediately, and if not not, how long does the proto-spell exist before it fizzles? Or does it fizzle? Could you theoretically hold unto such a spell indefinitely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T18:13:11-08:00","id":1024592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1024591#post1024591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Aimed Spells have to be thrown immediately, and if not not, how long does the proto-spell exist before it fizzles? Or does it fizzle? Could you theoretically hold unto such a spell indefinitely?</div> </div> </div> </div>The throwing is a part of the casting, unless you use Fate 2's &quot;Hung Spell&quot; to hold onto that Fireball for later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T19:56:40-08:00","id":1024606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1024592#post1024592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The throwing is a part of the casting, unless you use Fate 2's &quot;Hung Spell&quot; to hold onto that Fireball for later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 2 is Hung Spell, but otherwise you're correct. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> If you decided to hang onto an Aimed Spell at the very most it would only last in order to be thrown until its Duration runs out. In the case of spells with instantaneous effects that tick on GRI then it would be available to throw only once per GRI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T05:42:00-08:00","id":1025382,"title":"","content":"Wolf Blooded: count as humans for paradox effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:42:46-08:00","id":1025409,"title":"","content":"Are there any Abyssal entities in 2e Core? what should I look to for creating them on paradox? also do you address casting rules as normal for NPCs or something simpler?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:45:51-08:00","id":1025410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1025382#post1025382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf Blooded: count as humans for paradox effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are Sleepwalkers just as anyone who has at least 1 dot of supernatural merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:04:27-08:00","id":1025438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1025409#post1025409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any Abyssal entities in 2e Core? what should I look to for creating them on paradox? also do you address casting rules as normal for NPCs or something simpler?</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't any Abyssal creatures. I think though there's an Abyssal template, so you follow the rules for making an ephemeral entity and then add that.<br /> <br /> When it comes to casting rules for NPCs I tend to do the same thing that I do for my players, I figure out the Reach first and then if there's a risk of Paradox I'll roll it out, if there isn't then I ask myself if this is a high pressure situation if it is then I roll it out, but if it isn't I handwave it and say it succeeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:06:26-08:00","id":1025560,"title":"","content":"What would a mage need to use to make &quot;Poison Ivy&quot; vines attack from nothing or a seed? I ended up improving a character, and trying to map it back to something. For the game I just used the rules for the snare dread power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:25:43-08:00","id":1025565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1025560#post1025560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a mage need to use to make &quot;Poison Ivy&quot; vines attack from nothing or a seed? I ended up improving a character, and trying to map it back to something. For the game I just used the rules for the snare dread power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Life 3 seems most appropriate. The 3 dot spells are the first spells that allow you to directly harm other mages, and they seem to be most appropriate here. At the 3 dot level, every Arcanum has a &quot;you deal [potency] amount of bashing damage&quot; spell (except for Fate, but Fate's spell can piggy-back on another Arcanum), with +1 reach upgrading it to lethal damage. At the 4 dot level, all Arcana have a &quot;you deal [potency] amount of lethal damage&quot; spell, with +1 reach allowing you to upgrade it to aggravated damage. Game-wise I'm fine with this, because of the Wisdom degeneration it entails, but sometimes it's hard to imagine exactly what happens. For example, it's easy to imagine a 4 dot Mind spell causing lethal damage to anyone who looked at the mage wrong (aneurysm, stroke, straight Phineas Gage level brain damage), but Mind-based aggravated damage is a whole other story altogether. You can't really write about glowing-green scum covered swathes of neurons, because that's just instant death no matter how you look at it. There's no real 'up' from lethal-level strokes. Once you've had a stroke, you're fucking fried, you're done. For the Life Arcanum the Lethal -&gt; Aggravated level makes sense, but for Mind (and a fortiori most other Arcana) it does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:34:33-08:00","id":1025592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1025565#post1025565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Life 3 seems most appropriate. The 3 dot spells are the first spells that allow you to directly harm other mages, and they seem to be most appropriate here. At the 3 dot level, every Arcanum has a &quot;you deal [potency] amount of bashing damage&quot; spell (except for Fate, but Fate's spell can piggy-back on another Arcanum), with +1 reach upgrading it to lethal damage. At the 4 dot level, all Arcana have a &quot;you deal [potency] amount of lethal damage&quot; spell, with +1 reach allowing you to upgrade it to aggravated damage. Game-wise I'm fine with this, because of the Wisdom degeneration it entails, but sometimes it's hard to imagine exactly what happens. For example, it's easy to imagine a 4 dot Mind spell causing lethal damage to anyone who looked at the mage wrong (aneurysm, stroke, straight Phineas Gage level brain damage), but Mind-based aggravated damage is a whole other story altogether. You can't really write about glowing-green scum covered swathes of neurons, because that's just instant death no matter how you look at it. There's no real 'up' from lethal-level strokes. Once you've had a stroke, you're fucking fried, you're done. For the Life Arcanum the Lethal -&gt; Aggravated level makes sense, but for Mind (and a fortiori most other Arcana) it does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if I were describing an aggravated brain damage it'd end up looking like hemorrhagic fever, and the post mortem would probably show brain stew left on the burner for too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T15:54:17-08:00","id":1025601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1025592#post1025592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if I were describing an aggravated brain damage it'd end up looking like hemorrhagic fever, and the post mortem would probably show brain stew left on the burner for too long.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In game terms, however, that would not be different from what you could inflict at 4 dots, without the upgrade to aggravated. My point wasn't that you couldn't make mental lethal damage worse-looking, it was that lethal mental damage was as far as you could go, aggravated mental damage wouldn't make it worse. Going back to the comparison to Life, glowing, irradiated gangrene (aggravated) is clearly much worse than a degloved (lethal) hand. My point is that Mind doesn't have comparable afflictions. A blown blood vessel is as bad as an irradiated metal brain insert, when considering the Mind descriptions. That's what at issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:03:19-08:00","id":1025608,"title":"","content":"A degloved hand is probably aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:09:03-08:00","id":1025612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1025608#post1025608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A degloved hand is probably aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I only have the Mage 2nd edition core rulebook, so if this is contradicted by the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook I wouldn't know, but: degloving is something that can happen simply by the mechanical procedures of something a hand could come into contact with, so it would be lethal damage by definition. In the rulebook, aggravated damage is described as either inflicted by supernatural beings or sources, or nuclear power. Degloving usually happens either because of the intervention of a machine or due to high-pressure mineral oil, so it wouldn't be aggravated in either case. We can go into specific google image search examples if you wish, but I don't think anyone is waiting for that so let's just skip it.<br /> <br /> edit: Thanks bruh, I just spent 30 minutes looking at degloving pictures on google. Conclusion: lethal, not aggravated. If you want to see some grim shit, google harlequin fetus. Alright, logos out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","user":"logos","date":". 01-02-2017, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:36:07-08:00","id":1025621,"title":"","content":"Google image search wouldn't really be a way to settle it anyway. I'll concede that might be the what aggravated damage is for, personally I envision it as basically anything that could take a very long time to heal from or requires special intervention to recover from at all. So by that definition degloving would fit, but if that's not the RAW, eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T17:53:50-08:00","id":1025647,"title":"","content":"You all miss that Mind damage effects don't physically damage the brain. That would fall under Life. What the spell says is that the effects looks like a stroke, but physically the brain is completely healthy.<br /> <br /> Edit: I re-read the damage spells from Mind. It's the bashing version that is described as mimicking the effects of a stroke (temporarily, I assume). The lethal/aggravated version does not mention any physical trauma at all. It directly targets your psyche and deals purely mental damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-02-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T23:56:44-08:00","id":1025761,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Like, there is no brain to fry when you are targeting that Intelligent Car, but you stil deal damage to it with Mind just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:57:37-08:00","id":1026407,"title":"","content":"Two simple questions that I would like some help with:<br /> <br /> 1) Does Incognito Presence work in combat? Are you effectively invisible to enemies, if they fail the Clash of Wills? Even if you attack someone?<br /> <br /> 2) Can you force a target of Sleep of the Just to fall asleep in the middle of combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T02:05:32-08:00","id":1026411,"title":"","content":"1) Sure.<br /> <br /> 2) If you read Sleep of the Just closely you'll see that it doesn't actually say it puts someone to sleep, it just effects whether or not they can and also what happens if they do. It probably can be used as a general sleep inducing spell though since Psychic Domination has &quot;Sleep&quot; as one of its example commands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:32:18-08:00","id":1026472,"title":"","content":"Can I hex someone (or use an Arcanum other than Fate) to boost their next Paradox roll (using the +2 Reach to affect spellcasting, of course)?<br /> <br /> Unrelated: I watched Swan Lake yesterday. What would be reasons to not relinquish a transformation of such a massive Scale as Rotbart's?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:22:12-08:00","id":1026497,"title":"","content":"I don't think magic should be able to increase the chance of Paradox.<br /> <br /> 2) You wouldn't relinquish it so that you could drop the effect of the spell when you choose not when its Duration runs out or before it gets taken apart by Sleeper Dissonance or a Mage's dispelling at an inconvenient time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:20:31-08:00","id":1026534,"title":"","content":"Nothing in the rules says you can't, but I wouldn't let magic affect Paradox without some special Abyssal twist. That's Joining territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:30:23-08:00","id":1026564,"title":"","content":"Would it be ok to use a reach to make the target of the mind control spell think that the command was his idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:32:32-08:00","id":1026566,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. Trying to rationalize it could do the target a lot of long term psychological damage, but that's not really your problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:19:49-08:00","id":1026590,"title":"","content":"Well, it's a potential Act of Hubris which might be your problem unless you're at Falling already, but other than that it seems like a perfectly reasonable Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:01:40-08:00","id":1026614,"title":"","content":"As a general question of curiosity, how frequent are Consilium/Caucus meetings in your games? Meetings with mentors? Is it a regular deal - meetings once a month or so - or only when there's a big fuck-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:01:19-08:00","id":1026790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026614#post1026614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general question of curiosity, how frequent are Consilium/Caucus meetings in your games? Meetings with mentors? Is it a regular deal - meetings once a month or so - or only when there's a big fuck-up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regular, but it's accepted for members to skip attendance out of personal excuses, or send delegates. Emergency calls see almost all members attend.<br /> <br /> Some mentors keep contact in a schedule, much like a doctor's appointment. Some meet when they get free time to hang out, much like friends do. Some are dicks and leave cryptic advices on critical moments, or worse, when there's no apparent critical moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:49:16-08:00","id":1026827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026614#post1026614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general question of curiosity, how frequent are Consilium/Caucus meetings in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't had one but we're gearing up. I'd say a consilium meeting every couple months, but more casual, with a important one twice a year.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meetings with mentors? Is it a regular deal - meetings once a month or so - or only when there's a big fuck-up? </div> </div> </div>Really depends on the players. One of them has an Infamous Mentor, the Morrigan, who's been called in to town and is going to have some tasks for them once she deals with the player's problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:25:09-08:00","id":1026835,"title":"","content":"This may be a silly question but is the Spirit arcana 'better' at manipulating essence than Mind or Death? I ask because essence is specifically listed as being under the purview of spirit on pg. 179 but the other arcana have examples of ways to manipulate ephemeral phenomena under their domains so I assume they can control their variants of essence as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:28:45-08:00","id":1026837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026835#post1026835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a silly question but is the Spirit arcana 'better' at manipulating essence than Mind or Death? I ask because essence is specifically listed as being under the purview of spirit on pg. 179 but the other arcana have examples of ways to manipulate ephemeral phenomena under their domains so I assume they can control their variants of essence as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Essence is part of Spirit. Death spells alone will, for the most part, allow for the manipulation and control of ghosts but not specifically their Essence. Looking through Spirit you can see that you need it and Death or Mind to use a lot of its abilities on ghosts or goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:55:58-08:00","id":1026841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026837#post1026837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Essence is part of Spirit. Death spells alone will, for the most part, allow for the manipulation and control of ghosts but not specifically their Essence. Looking through Spirit you can see that you need it and Death or Mind to use a lot of its abilities on ghosts or goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally find that ridiculous. Spirit shouldn't be the only arcana that can properly deal with its ephemerals. I always rule it that you just use the relevant arcana for dealing with an ephemeral being (so no spirit dots will ever be needed to deal with ghosts). Like, I don't see why it is that to do anything with regard to a ghost or death ephemerals, being who are entirely death, should require anything but death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:02:05-08:00","id":1026844,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6365_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6365\" data-vbnamecard=\"6365\">Fumus</a> agreed, for instance if it was limited to only ghosts and such a &quot;channel ghostly essance&quot; would make sense to be a death spell because it is more about the manipulation of ghosts and death Resonant energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:23:31-08:00","id":1026847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026841#post1026841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit shouldn't be the only arcana that can properly deal with its ephemerals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't.<br /> <br /> Like I said, all you need it for is to deal with Essence.<br /> <br /> If you look in the Death section, you can 'properly deal' with its ephemerals. You can craft with ectoplasm, see, speak, interact with and sculpt ghosts and ghost matter, damage, summon, command, weaken or empower ghosts, enter Twilight with, exorcise them, make them possess, make them a familiar, enter their Underworld, create new anchors and create ghosts from scratch.<br /> <br /> All you need Spirit for is to Channel Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-05-2017, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:56:24-08:00","id":1026861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026841#post1026841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit shouldn't be the only arcana that can properly deal with its ephemerals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit is the only Arcanum whose ephemerals <i>have Essence as a legitimate concern</i>. Ghosts are kept at equilibrium by their basic Manifestation Condition, Goetia don't naturally wind up outside the Astral with any concrete means of sticking around, and both of them are native to veritable lands of plenty compared to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Channel Essence is a Ruling spell. Literally everyone who's not a Thyrsus has an identical requisite investment to eventually learn it \u2014 the worst the Moros have going for them is that they have to get there from zero dots in the Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:20:02-08:00","id":1026879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026861#post1026861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit is the only Arcanum whose ephemerals <i>have Essence as a legitimate concern</i>. Ghosts are kept at equilibrium by their basic Manifestation Condition, Goetia don't naturally wind up outside the Astral with any concrete means of sticking around, and both of them are native to veritable lands of plenty compared to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Channel Essence is a Ruling spell. Literally everyone who's not a Thyrsus has an identical requisite investment to eventually learn it \u2014 the worst the Moros have going for them is that they have to get there from zero dots in the Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still don't see why that means essence in a ghost, produced by a ghost just sitting around or being transferred from one ghost to another should require spirit. Essence should be under the purview of whatever arcana is associated with the thing that the essence came from in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:36:26-08:00","id":1026884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026879#post1026879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see why that means essence in a ghost, produced by a ghost just sitting around or being transferred from one ghost to another should require spirit. Essence should be under the purview of whatever arcana is associated with the thing that the essence came from in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any essence naturally produces or inherited by ghosts anyway? Information on ghosts is kind of thin in the books I own. If ghost produce essence it's likely the same way humans do it, by influencing a certain area and that would let this essence be produced in the shadow and make it a part of the shadow. And even death essence, is only relevant to death spirits and has basically no meaning for ghosts afaik.<br /> Isn't in general essence basically part of the shadow? I think the &quot;material&quot; ghosts are from and what you seek for is ectoplasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:51:13-08:00","id":1026888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026837#post1026837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Essence is part of Spirit. Death spells alone will, for the most part, allow for the manipulation and control of ghosts but not specifically their Essence. Looking through Spirit you can see that you need it and Death or Mind to use a lot of its abilities on ghosts or goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't what Add Death or Mind means. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...num-to-a-spell</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:12:43-08:00","id":1026895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026879#post1026879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see why that means essence in a ghost, produced by a ghost just sitting around or being transferred from one ghost to another should require spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. Ghosts are entirely capable of being given new Anchors and/or induced to take each other's Essence and/or exposed to the Underworld and Channel Essence does not move Essence in a fashion that is not run through the mage's Pattern.<br /> <br /> The primary use of Essence (fueling basic activity) is circumvented by the way Awakened magic interacts with the Manifestation system to begin with (forcing an ephemeral being into a particular mode of existence \u2014 all of which cut its upkeep down to the same rate as a ghost with an Anchor and two of which actively limit the scope of its powers). Adding the general phenomenon to the Arcana governing realms of existence in which its discrete storage and theft is not a meaningfully common concern means you have to deal with the broader implications of sticking Craft Fetish in Death and Mind even though the Astral and the Underworld offer no issues with interacting with the material world that would not be more readily managed by manifesting them and using more thematically appropriate methods to feed them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essence should be under the purview of whatever arcana is associated with the thing that the essence came from in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Essence does not come from ephemeral beings in the first place. That's kind of the point of it.<br /> <br /> Having Death 5 and Spirit 2 means you have a ready wellspring of Death-Resonant Essence to feed your ghosts with by opening an Avernian Gate, and the Mastigos have historically trended toward Spirit for the purposes of physical goetic evocation for more reasons than just aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:12:00-08:00","id":1027002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026895#post1026895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence does not come from ephemeral beings in the first place. That's kind of the point of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Essence isn't something ephemeral beings produce; it's something they take from the world.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting that Essence is outright the very first purview listed under the Spirit arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:19:40-08:00","id":1027005,"title":"","content":"Spirit and Death and Mind entities rarely interact directly, so they each have to have developed independent methods of gathering and manipulating Essence. It seems strange to me that only Spirit is capable of emulating these mechanisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:33:28-08:00","id":1027012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA, page 253</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Collectively, Goetia, spirits, and ghosts are known as ephemeral entities, after the substance their bodies are made of when in the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA, page 254</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral entities subsist on Essence, while Supernal beings use Mana</div> </div> </div> </div>In the mechanical part of the game they are all 3 Ephemeral Entities and they all 3 subsist on Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027002#post1027002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Essence isn't something ephemeral beings produce; it's something they take from the world.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting that Essence is outright the very first purview listed under the Spirit arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all three are made of Ephemeral substance governed by their respective realms, all 3 need to find essence from sources both in the material world and in their respective realms. However Spirits do not get Essence from the Shadow and must always find external sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-05-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:47:58-08:00","id":1027019,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> Also the claim that Essence is under Spirit so it must require spirit to manipulate is weak as hell. It's like saying you can't ever induce cold with Forces by fraying Heat in the area unless you include Death because Cold is under Death's purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:56:42-08:00","id":1027028,"title":"","content":"I have not made my judgment yet but I see wyhy it could be the case. Its like with Life, Prime and mana.Life can control a mage and even make him spend mana, but Prime can do it directly.<br /> With Death, Spirit and essence case can be similar. You could connect ghosts and force them to channel essence but not by affecting essence directly. (Unless it has a death/decay resonance??)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:01:09-08:00","id":1027031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1026888#post1026888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't what Add Death or Mind means. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...num-to-a-spell</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Your quote, all the posts in there, don't refute what I said. Though I certainly overestimated the spells mentioned.<br /> <br /> Channel Essence says, 'Add Death \u2022\u2022 or Mind \u2022\u2022: The spell may be cast on a ghost or Goetia.' And as I said, you need to add Death or Mind to use it on a ghsot or goetia. how is that not what Add Death or Mind means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:07:02-08:00","id":1027035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027028#post1027028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not made my judgment yet but I see wyhy it could be the case. Its like with Life, Prime and mana.Life can control a mage and even make him spend mana, but Prime can do it directly.<br /> With Death, Spirit and essence case can be similar. You could connect ghosts and force them to channel essence but not by affecting essence directly. (Unless it has a death/decay resonance??)</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is true, you could also channel essence with life resonance with Life or fire essence with Forces. I think I rather have all essence under the purview of Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:11:00-08:00","id":1027036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027031#post1027031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Channel Essence says, 'Add Death \u2022\u2022 or Mind \u2022\u2022: The spell may be cast on a ghost or Goetia.' And as I said, you need to add Death or Mind to use it on a ghsot or goetia. how is that not what Add Death or Mind means?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacred Geometry sys 'Add Death \u2022 or Spirit \u2022: The mage\u2019s senses are also attuned to the presence of Avernian Gates or Loci, respectively. Other Arcana may reveal stranger sacred spaces, as well.' but that doesn't mean that you can't locate Avernian Gates alone.<br /> <br /> Add Death or Mind in Channel Essence means that you need Spirit and Death to channel essence between spirit and ghost. Which is also a leftover from 1e that shouldn't be here, imo. If you have Essence in your purview you shouldn't need any other arcana to manipulate essence just like you don't need Life or Matter to manipulate Fate of men and chairs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:12:41-08:00","id":1027037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027031#post1027031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your quote, all the posts in there, don't refute what I said. Though I certainly overestimated the spells mentioned.<br /> <br /> Channel Essence says, 'Add Death \u2022\u2022 or Mind \u2022\u2022: The spell may be cast on a ghost or Goetia.' And as I said, you need to add Death or Mind to use it on a ghsot or goetia. how is that not what Add Death or Mind means?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's your conclusion then you didn't understand what I was saying or what the phrase Add Arcana X means. The Add Arcana X clause doesn't preclude the use of Death or Mind by itself to gather or manipulate Essence in the way that the ephemeral entities under their respective purviews do.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> I don't think Life can be used to force someone to spend their mana. I could be wrong though, source?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-05-2017, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:17:52-08:00","id":1027039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027036#post1027036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add Death or Mind in Channel Essence means that you need Spirit and Death to channel essence between spirit and ghost. Which is also a leftover from 1e that shouldn't be here, imo. If you have Essence in your purview you shouldn't need any other arcana to manipulate essence just like you don't need Life or Matter to manipulate Fate of men and chairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't, but if you look at the Channeling Essence spell, it's not just a matter of blowing out energy, it's taking it into your Pattern in the place of your Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:22:39-08:00","id":1027042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027035#post1027035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is true, you could also channel essence with life resonance with Life or fire essence with Forces. I think I rather have all essence under the purview of Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for you to see where I come from: I run a very broad interpretation of the arcana. When Fate can affect everything, Death can weaken and destroy everything I don't see why Life couldn't heal everythink that can be healed (healing =/ repairing). So in my game you can heal spirits for example. &quot;If you can perceive something you can alter it with applicable purview&quot; - if you can perceive sympathetic connetion with Space 1 you can then deaden it with Death 3 or 4.<br /> <br /> But yea, essence is not dead nor alive just like mana is a quality on its own. So death should't be able to command it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:24:10-08:00","id":1027044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027037#post1027037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's your conclusion then you didn't understand what I was saying or what the phrase Add Arcana X means. The Add Arcana X clause doesn't preclude the use of Death or Mind by itself to gather or manipulate Essence in the way that the ephemeral entities under their respective purviews do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts and Goetia don't gather Essence. 'In their home realms, Goetia, ghosts, and Supernal entities regain their Rank in Essence or Mana per day. Spirits are not sustained by the Shadow; they must always find sources of Essence even when in their own world.' Just like ghosts are sustained by their anchors. They can steal Essence from other ghosts, but their primary method of gaining Essence is not losing it by being close to their anchors.<br /> <br /> Beyond the generation of Death-related Essence via Death-related acts, Death has nothing to do with Essence. Though you could easily justify some sort of draining or decaying of Essence in a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:26:36-08:00","id":1027045,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Sure. It's in the purview text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Life and Spirit rule the Primal Wild. Life is the gross Arcanum<br /> of the pair, a term made literal by some of its more visceral spells.<br /> Life magic governs all living things, in fact, from viruses to titanic<br /> whales, e<b>ven the nerve cells that allow thoughts to form Imagos.</b><br /> Life is tenacious in the extreme, capable of surviving anywhere,<br /> developing any trait to weather environmental stresses, and<br /> Life mages are comparably tough. By harnessing the endless<br /> adaptability of living forms, mages can gain perspectives on the<br /> world otherwise lost even to Awakened senses<br /> </div> </div> </div>It is not said directly but I'm sure that it is possible if explained by a clever player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:30:10-08:00","id":1027047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027044#post1027044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts and Goetia don't gather Essence. 'In their home realms, Goetia, ghosts, and Supernal entities regain their Rank in Essence or Mana per day. Spirits are not sustained by the Shadow; they must always find sources of Essence even when in their own world.' Just like ghosts are sustained by their anchors. They can steal Essence from other ghosts, but their primary method of gaining Essence is not losing it by being close to their anchors.<br /> <br /> Beyond the generation of Death-related Essence via Death-related acts, Death has nothing to do with Essence. Though you could easily justify some sort of draining or decaying of Essence in a target.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still have a means of accumulating and storing it regardless of whether or not that's passive. They may not use exactly the same method, but to that degree that ghosts or goetia interact with essence so should Death and Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:36:47-08:00","id":1027051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027047#post1027047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They still have a means of accumulating and storing it regardless of whether or not that's passive. They may not use exactly the same method, but to that degree that ghosts or goetia interact with essence so should Death and Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that they interact with the Entities that interact with the essence not the essence directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:28:51-08:00","id":1027078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027042#post1027042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for you to see where I come from: I run a very broad interpretation of the arcana. When Fate can affect everything, Death can weaken and destroy everything I don't see why Life couldn't heal everythink that can be healed (healing =/ repairing). So in my game you can heal spirits for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such an interpretation would be a house rule, though. Officially Life can't affect ephemeral entities. A Thyrsus in the Underworld is shit out of luck when it comes to Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> It appears that Essence is exclusively something handled by Spirit. At least directly. Mind can always &quot;convince&quot; an ephemeral entity to use Essence in various ways, and 3+ dot spells can change the size of Essence pools by changing the entity. There's no mention of Essence in any Death or Mind spells, and Essence is specifically listed as a purview under Spirit. It's quite clear what the devs intended.<br /> It kinda blows, though. It hasn't come up at our table yet, but I'm pretty sure it's going to get house ruled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:36:42-08:00","id":1027081,"title":"","content":"Once again something being under the purview of an arcana doesn't exclude interaction with the thing by another arcana. It could just as easily be that since other ephemeral entities aren't normally starved for Essence it's less of a factor in dealing with them and thus no one bothered to write a spell for it in Death or Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:39:05-08:00","id":1027082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027081#post1027081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again something being under the purview of an arcana doesn't exclude interaction with the thing by another arcana. It could just as easily be that since other ephemeral entities aren't normally starved for Essence it's less of a factor in dealing with them and thus no one bothered to write a spell for it in Death or Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then like with Familiar, they would have written 'Substitute Death or Mind.' And Essence would be under the purview of Mind and Death. And Spirit wouldn't be the only place where spells like Howl from Beyond would exist.<br /> <br /> Frankly this seems like an overreaction. You're not kept from dealing with ghosts by not having Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-05-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:40:30-08:00","id":1027083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027078#post1027078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such an interpretation would be a house rule, though. Officially Life can't affect ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that it's a house rule, I don't mind.But spirits are alive so I don't see why they can't be healed by Life just like Mind affects <i>all </i>kinds of minds. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027078#post1027078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Thyrsus in the Underworld is shit out of luck when it comes to Ruling Arcana.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If Thyrsus can affect essence he is not really powerless there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:48:30-08:00","id":1027087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027082#post1027082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not kept from dealing with ghosts by not having Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, but there shouldn't an artificial gate to interacting fully with an arcana's ephemeral entities either.<br /> <br /> Plus, again the Add Arcana X doesn't mean that the arcana Y that's being added to is a prerequisite for a similar effect that targets only entities that fall under X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-05-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:50:57-08:00","id":1027089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027087#post1027087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, but there shouldn't an artificial gate to interacting fully with an arcana's ephemeral entities either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hardly an artificial gate. Spirit has been involved with Essence since the creation of spirits and not being able to spontaneously Channel Essence doesn't keep you from 'interacting fully' with ghosts or Goetia. Even if you really believe that it's because ghosts use Essence, that's not the entirety of the picture, as Ghosts and Goetia just require very specialized Essence, while spirits can take anything. Ghosts don't just gather up Essence like spirits, they get them from their anchors, which is something you can create for them in Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:52:31-08:00","id":1027090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027083#post1027083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Thyrsus can affect essence he is not really powerless there</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Underworld has no regularly occurring Essence. Ghosts (and stranger beings) get Essence from just being there. The only Essence to be found is in ghosts, and Channel Essence provides the precedent that you can't affect Essence in ephemeral entities without adding the corresponding Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-05-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:56:10-08:00","id":1027092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027037#post1027037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's your conclusion then you didn't understand what I was saying or what the phrase Add Arcana X means. The Add Arcana X clause doesn't preclude the use of Death or Mind by itself to gather or manipulate Essence in the way that the ephemeral entities under their respective purviews do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ostensibly, given that the text refers in the singular (&quot;cast on a&quot;, rather than &quot;may include&quot;), that's precisely what it's doing isn't it? Because otherwise, there'd be no need to include that addendum; equivalent spells at the Ruling level would already exist for those arcana.<br /> <br /> Essence is Spirit's purview. You can be a decent necromancer or demonologist without it, but you can't be a great one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:59:26-08:00","id":1027094,"title":"","content":"No spirits are still limited to interacting with Essence of the appropriate type. A spirit can not interact with a ghosts essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA: page 255</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral entities can attempt to steal Essence or Mana from beings of the same type \u2014 ghosts from ghosts, spirits from spirits, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-05-2017, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:00:29-08:00","id":1027096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027092#post1027092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence is Spirit's purview. You can be a decent necromancer or demonologist without it, but you can't be a great one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make an end run about the limitation by using Death or Mind's Familiar ability. Not only does this allow you to channel Essence back and forth, but it lets you see through the target's eyes.<br /> <br /> Do you really think not being able to Channel Essence is some barrier that keeps 'decent' necromancers from being great ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:01:14-08:00","id":1027097,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> Ghost are made of essence. I might be wrong with this but they are destroyed when essence is depleted in them. I think that this kind of multiarcana restrictions are a sad land ridiculus leftover from 1e. You can influence destiny with Fate? - You don't need Matter to affect weapons destiny. You can influence minds with Mind? - You don't need Spirit to affect spirits. You can affect mana with Prime? - You don't need Death to steal mana from a ghost mage. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:01:20-08:00","id":1027098,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> And to that I call bullshit because it makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:04:12-08:00","id":1027102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027097#post1027097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> Ghost are made of essence. I might be wrong with this but they are destroyed when essence is depleted in them. I think that this kind of multiarcana restrictions are a sad land ridiculus leftover from 1e. You can influence destiny with Fate? - You don't need Matter to affect weapons destiny. You can influence minds with Mind? - You don't need Spirit to affect spirits. You can affect mana with Prime? - You don't need Death to steal mana from a ghost mage. And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When they run out of essence they hibernate and are pulled back to their anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:04:16-08:00","id":1027103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027097#post1027097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> Ghost are made of essence. I might be wrong with this but they are destroyed when essence is depleted in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. Ghosts are made of ephemera. They take a single point of damage without Essence and falls into hibernation, but that's less lethal than starvation in living beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:06:24-08:00","id":1027104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027097#post1027097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost are made of essence. I might be wrong with this but they are destroyed when essence is depleted in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts don't seem to be made of Essence. When they Manifest, their Manifestation uses ephemera, but that's about the extent of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:07:17-08:00","id":1027105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027103#post1027103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not true. Ghosts are made of ephemera. They take a single point of damage without Essence, but that's less lethal than starvation in living beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. I don't have a rulebook on me now. So all that Thyrsus could do would be cursing ghosts with starvation by Shielding them from essence. Or make essence in them poisonous.<br /> <br /> Edit: Isn't destroing ephemera only possible when corpus <i>and </i>essence are depleted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:09:37-08:00","id":1027110,"title":"","content":"And even that might not be possible without adding Death to the spell, just like Channel Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:10:49-08:00","id":1027111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027110#post1027110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even that might not be possible without adding Death to the spell, just like Channel Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? Essence is essence. Either yo can control it or you can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:14:45-08:00","id":1027113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027105#post1027105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks. I don't have a rulebook on me now. So all that Thyrsus could do would be cursing ghosts with starvation by Shielding them from essence. Or make essence in them poisonous.<br /> <br /> Edit: Isn't destroing ephemera only possible when corpus <i>and </i>essence are depleted?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How is life shielding them from essence. A ghost is not living and does not has a living body. Its corpus in made of ephemera and not living material Life affects living thing and since the ephemera not the essence is living I don't see the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:15:11-08:00","id":1027114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027094#post1027094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No spirits are still limited to interacting with Essence of the appropriate type. A spirit can not interact with a ghosts essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit and spirits are different things. There is a reason we add arcana here, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027096#post1027096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make an end run about the limitation by using Death or Mind's Familiar ability. Not only does this allow you to channel Essence back and forth, but it lets you see through the target's eyes.<br /> <br /> Do you really think not being able to Channel Essence is some barrier that keeps 'decent' necromancers from being great ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Familiar bonds also require Spirit to forge if we're reading Add as indicative of a requirement. It doesn't really pose a problem.<br /> <br /> And, yes, when Essence is one of the major bartering tools with ephemeral entities, that is a challenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027098#post1027098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> And to that I call bullshit because it makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why doesn't it? A human drinks water to survive but Life can't bend a stream. Why is this so unfathomable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:16:14-08:00","id":1027115,"title":"","content":"Good question, but the book has already set the precedent with Channel Essence. You can't channel Essence without the right Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:18:07-08:00","id":1027119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027114#post1027114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiar bonds also require Spirit to forge if we're reading Add as indicative of a requirement. It doesn't really pose a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Familiar doesn't say Add Death or Mind, it says Substitute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, yes, when Essence is one of the major bartering tools with ephemeral entities, that is a challenge. </div> </div> </div>It's not something they hunger and hunt for like spirits do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:18:27-08:00","id":1027120,"title":"","content":"My copy of the PDF (pretty sure it's the final copy) says Substitute for the Familiar spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:18:28-08:00","id":1027121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1027115#post1027115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question, but the book has already set the precedent with Channel Essence. You can't channel Essence without the right Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this for you to channel essence you need the appropriate arcanum as a conjunctive effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid"