-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:22:46-08:00","id":1058491,"title":"","content":"Page 249: &quot;The dream form may look nothing like the sorcerer, because this is her self-image as influenced by contact from the Supernal, and divorced from the limitations of flesh. Characters with the Shadow Name Merit often appear radically different in age, race, sex, or fitness, as their dream forms conform to their magical selves&quot;<br /> <br /> The only limit I'd set is that the character is supposed to look mostly human.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:19:25-08:00","id":1058536,"title":"","content":"I just wanna say, that's actually a pretty rockin' image and would like to know where you found it.<br /> <br /> As Tessie says, &quot;be roughly humanoid&quot; is probably a good limit to set for it, but if the character so heavily identifies with a wolf totem or something that they manifest as an actual wolf, go for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:59:34-08:00","id":1058868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1058536#post1058536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanna say, that's actually a pretty rockin' image and would like to know where you found it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pinterest, search for &quot;Mage&quot; and &quot;Spirit&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:04:02-08:00","id":1058905,"title":"","content":"I managed to dig up the source of that picture,<a href=\"https://www.artstation.com/artwork/lOOKO\" target=\"_blank\"> in higher resolution as well</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:30:11-08:00","id":1059087,"title":"","content":"If Weaving Prime can cause an object to be solid in every frequency of Twilight, could not Unveiling Prime allow a subject to see Twilgiht?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:38:43-08:00","id":1059240,"title":"","content":"Another Rune Casting question.<br /> <br /> As estabilished previously, Runes can be used with Area of Effect option of Scale Factor, basically targeting any viable target within the runic circle. Until now, I mostly used this as a way to milk more power out of sanctum while also gaining some extra Spell Control Slots that can be easily revoked by breaking the circle when spell is not needed anymore / starts being corrupted. <br /> <br /> However, I wonder...why not put these runes on carriable objects? Runic rings, runic bracelets, runic necklaces; basically anything that can form a &quot;circle&quot; around a part of your body. This would allow you to &quot;prep&quot; runes for self-targeting spells, and you would need to have specific spells prepared for specific runic trinkets. Still, I don't think there is anything in rules forbidding this kind of equipment? It's another +2 Yantra, coupled with ability to easily end spells without having access to Dispelling Magic, which in turn helps you manage your Spell Control limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:42:44-08:00","id":1059244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059240#post1059240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Rune Casting question.<br /> <br /> As estabilished previously, Runes can be used with Area of Effect option of Scale Factor, basically targeting any viable target within the runic circle. Until now, I mostly used this as a way to milk more power out of sanctum while also gaining some extra Spell Control Slots that can be easily revoked by breaking the circle when spell is not needed anymore / starts being corrupted. <br /> <br /> However, I wonder...why not put these runes on carriable objects? Runic rings, runic bracelets, runic necklaces; basically anything that can form a &amp;quot;circle&amp;quot; around a part of your body. This would allow you to &amp;quot;prep&amp;quot; runes for self-targeting spells, and you would need to have specific spells prepared for specific runic trinkets. Still, I don't think there is anything in rules forbidding this kind of equipment? It's another +2 Yantra, coupled with ability to easily end spells without having access to Dispelling Magic, which in turn helps you manage your Spell Control limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it. The way I read runes I assume they're only good for the spell they were created for, and subsequent castings of the same spell, but that just means you need more bangles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:12:34-08:00","id":1059262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059240#post1059240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Rune Casting question.<br /> <br /> As estabilished previously, Runes can be used with Area of Effect option of Scale Factor, basically targeting any viable target within the runic circle. Until now, I mostly used this as a way to milk more power out of sanctum while also gaining some extra Spell Control Slots that can be easily revoked by breaking the circle when spell is not needed anymore / starts being corrupted.<br /> <br /> However, I wonder...why not put these runes on carriable objects? Runic rings, runic bracelets, runic necklaces; basically anything that can form a &quot;circle&quot; around a part of your body. This would allow you to &quot;prep&quot; runes for self-targeting spells, and you would need to have specific spells prepared for specific runic trinkets. Still, I don't think there is anything in rules forbidding this kind of equipment? It's another +2 Yantra, coupled with ability to easily end spells without having access to Dispelling Magic, which in turn helps you manage your Spell Control limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand. Could you give an actual example? I don't get what's the utility of doing that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:38:17-08:00","id":1059269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059262#post1059262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand. Could you give an actual example? I don't get what's the utility of doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imagine that you find yourself casting, let's say, Incognito Presence upon yourself pretty often. It's a spell that benefits a lot from Super Duration, but it's also very inconvenient to leave it &quot;on&quot; for large periods of time, because it interferes with your activities quite a bit. You don't like the idea of burning a spell control slot on it - maybe your Gnosis is low, or maybe you expect yourself to cast other long duration spells (maybe you want to increase your skills, for example). You like the idea of Unsafely Relinquisinh the spell to save on spell slots, but you don't have Prime - so you can't dispel the spell when you are done with it. <br /> So you get yourself a ring with a movable segment and carefully place Runes on it, reflecting imago of this specific spell. The ring won't be helpful for any other spell, but you don't mind. <br /> Next time you cast the spell, you use Runes placed on it as a Yantra. This gives you a +2 Yantra that can be used only for this spell (already a pretty good benefit for spending 3 hours working on a piece of jewlery), and only when spell targets &quot;anything encircled by the Runes&quot; - which, in this case, will be you. After casting the spell, you spend a Willpower point to unsafely relinquish the spell - you probably invested a lot of duration into it, because you wanted to be safe against Clash of Will detecting powers. Normally, this would be really unfortunate, because being invisible for a year is actually a curse, and if you are a Mastigos, your starting Arcana spread won't allow you to dispel it! But that's why you are using Runes.<br /> You see, spells that used Runes as a Yantra stop working the moment Runic circle is disturbed. That's why you specifically picked a ring that has some kind of movable part - when the spell outlives its usefulness, you can move the movable part so the runic circle is broken. This terminates the spell, and you can reuse the Ring in future castings of Incognito Presence, because you actually didn't destroy the runes - you just temporarily disturbed their continuity. <br /> If you were, let's say, a Gnosis 1 Mage, this allowed you to have Incognito Presence running without interfering with your normal spell casting, as your Spell Control limit is pretty small at the beginning phase of the game. This saves you from having to Reach to simply cast a spell. <br /> <br /> This tactic loses some of it's potency at Gnosis 3, where you probably already picked up Dispel Magic. It also dosen't play well with Combined Spells - simply because you would need to create new items for each combination, which limits your flexibility a little.<br /> <br /> I like the image this invokes, though - mages creating and carrying bags fulls of trinkets. It also gives you an interesting trade off, because by anchoring spell in this way, you are risking someone or something figuring it out - or worse, something happening by pure accident! - which in turn allows them to potentially disrupt your spells by targeting the trinkets. Which...is good, as it creates temptation of lazy hubris. It encourages you to rely on unsafely relinquished spells, too, which is another temptation that helps Mages hang themselves with their own hands. <br /> <br /> This also seems to have great affinity with Matter magic, as you can reinforce the trinkets, change their shape and do other interesting things that allow introduction of &quot;magic items&quot; into Matter playstyle from the get-go, even if they aren't really magical items. Artificer archetype!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:22:39-08:00","id":1059283,"title":"","content":"Now I get it, thanks. But I do belive it's stretch, though. Runes have to be inscribed into the subject, If the subject is an area, it is a specific area. If you cast the spell on the area inside a ring's circunference, when you move the ring the spell would end because that altered the arrangement of the runes around the area. At least that's my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:37:21-08:00","id":1059285,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily, though - you are targeting everything inside target area, not the area itself. It's kinda like how you can target a room and make every body inside it a zombie, and these zombies won't stop being zombies after they leave the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T18:07:20-08:00","id":1059294,"title":"","content":"My understanding was area effect spells target the area. If you cast Acceleration on an area, for instance, everyone in the area is accelerated, but stops being so when they leave (but anyone new entering the area is similarly made Accelerated).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T18:47:40-08:00","id":1059305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059269#post1059269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Imagine that you find yourself casting, let's say, Incognito Presence upon yourself pretty often. It's a spell that benefits a lot from Super Duration, but it's also very inconvenient to leave it &quot;on&quot; for large periods of time, because it interferes with your activities quite a bit. You don't like the idea of burning a spell control slot on it - maybe your Gnosis is low, or maybe you expect yourself to cast other long duration spells (maybe you want to increase your skills, for example). You like the idea of Unsafely Relinquisinh the spell to save on spell slots, but you don't have Prime - so you can't dispel the spell when you are done with it.<br /> So you get yourself a ring with a movable segment and carefully place Runes on it, reflecting imago of this specific spell. The ring won't be helpful for any other spell, but you don't mind.<br /> Next time you cast the spell, you use Runes placed on it as a Yantra. This gives you a +2 Yantra that can be used only for this spell (already a pretty good benefit for spending 3 hours working on a piece of jewlery), and only when spell targets &quot;anything encircled by the Runes&quot; - which, in this case, will be you. After casting the spell, you spend a Willpower point to unsafely relinquish the spell - you probably invested a lot of duration into it, because you wanted to be safe against Clash of Will detecting powers. Normally, this would be really unfortunate, because being invisible for a year is actually a curse, and if you are a Mastigos, your starting Arcana spread won't allow you to dispel it! But that's why you are using Runes.<br /> You see, spells that used Runes as a Yantra stop working the moment Runic circle is disturbed. That's why you specifically picked a ring that has some kind of movable part - when the spell outlives its usefulness, you can move the movable part so the runic circle is broken. This terminates the spell, and you can reuse the Ring in future castings of Incognito Presence, because you actually didn't destroy the runes - you just temporarily disturbed their continuity.<br /> If you were, let's say, a Gnosis 1 Mage, this allowed you to have Incognito Presence running without interfering with your normal spell casting, as your Spell Control limit is pretty small at the beginning phase of the game. This saves you from having to Reach to simply cast a spell.<br /> <br /> This tactic loses some of it's potency at Gnosis 3, where you probably already picked up Dispel Magic. It also dosen't play well with Combined Spells - simply because you would need to create new items for each combination, which limits your flexibility a little.<br /> <br /> I like the image this invokes, though - mages creating and carrying bags fulls of trinkets. It also gives you an interesting trade off, because by anchoring spell in this way, you are risking someone or something figuring it out - or worse, something happening by pure accident! - which in turn allows them to potentially disrupt your spells by targeting the trinkets. Which...is good, as it creates temptation of lazy hubris. It encourages you to rely on unsafely relinquished spells, too, which is another temptation that helps Mages hang themselves with their own hands.<br /> <br /> This also seems to have great affinity with Matter magic, as you can reinforce the trinkets, change their shape and do other interesting things that allow introduction of &quot;magic items&quot; into Matter playstyle from the get-go, even if they aren't really magical items. Artificer archetype!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually pretty nice. It's like a makeshift way of imbuing items without the need for high levels of Prime. Pretty clever actually. I also love how disastrously bad this can potentially go if things were to go wrong. This is totally one of those 'enough rope to hang themselves with' things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-06-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T19:05:54-08:00","id":1059308,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1130_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1130\" data-vbnamecard=\"1130\">falco1029</a> <br /> <br /> Sounds like two different uses of Scale: one to make X number of subjects into zombies, and one to make an area of X size where people become zombies as long as they're in it. Both effects last for the Duration of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:17:05-08:00","id":1059385,"title":"","content":"Could a Mage learn an extinct Legacy no longer practiced or even really understood by any living Mage by travelling to its lost Temenos realm, and perhaps bargaining with the Goetia it finds there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:48:56-08:00","id":1059392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059385#post1059385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Mage learn an extinct Legacy no longer practiced or even really understood by any living Mage by travelling to its lost Temenos realm, and perhaps bargaining with the Goetia it finds there?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd have to find something to serve as a mentor like a clue to the location of a daimonomicon or soul stone, but yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T03:24:32-08:00","id":1059419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059392#post1059392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They'd have to find something to serve as a mentor like a clue to the location of a daimonomicon or soul stone, but yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could they recreate it &quot;from scratch&quot; with Goetia guidance, without a soulstone or a daimonomicon, but with high enough stats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T03:32:58-08:00","id":1059421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059419#post1059419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could they recreate it &amp;quot;from scratch&amp;quot; with Goetia guidance, without a soulstone or a daimonomicon, but with high enough stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with RAW, I think. But you the Storyteller can always say that some of the last survivors of the Legacy somehow 'encoded' the Legacy into the Goetia, as if it were a soul stone or grimoire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T05:10:03-08:00","id":1059443,"title":"","content":"If you can study a legacy thoroughly you should be able create a new legacy based on the old one by using the rules for creating a legacy. However, it will not be the same legacy and might actually have substantial differences if the new creator comes up with different &quot;solutions&quot; to the hidden inner workings of a legacy that can't be studied without a soul stone or daimonomicon.<br /> Or the goetia could actually have the daimonomicon inscribed in their minds and be able to recite it. In which case they should act like a daimonomicon for purposes of joining the legacy and learning attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T05:22:29-08:00","id":1059447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059419#post1059419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could they recreate it &amp;quot;from scratch&amp;quot; with Goetia guidance, without a soulstone or a daimonomicon, but with high enough stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be similar to a Mage forcing his way into a legacy that's current. He'd have to develop the Praxes and hit Gnosis 3. There's a lot of stuff in the astral though, you could find a Daimonomicon there and all kinds of stuff. Theoretically, if you learned enough from the temenotic realm you could develop Sympathy to it and then summon up or have someone else summon up a Supernal entity that could use that connection to help you hunt down relics, ghosts or soul stones from the legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:25:28-08:00","id":1059860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059308#post1059308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1130_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1130\" data-vbnamecard=\"1130\">falco1029</a><br /> <br /> Sounds like two different uses of Scale: one to make X number of subjects into zombies, and one to make an area of X size where people become zombies as long as they're in it. Both effects last for the Duration of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's little different than that. Using are as a Scale Factor doesn't mean you are targetting an area - it means that you are targeting everything inside that area. For example, it allows you to do a DnD-esque &quot;Burning Hands&quot; cone effect without making the spell Sensory. Trade off here is that you have no power over what get's targeted and what doesn't - anything that's a viable subject for the spell in the target area (which probably can't be shaped into swiss chesse pattern; I'm running under assumption that the shape has to be balanced and with no holes) is getting targeted. Which means possibilities of friendly fire and other unfortunate implications. It's a trade off that allows really cost efficient use of Spellfactors and Reach, in exchange of being very dangerous and leading into Low-Wisdom behavioral patterns. Again, it does that Mage 2nd Edition thing where you totally can be a diligent spellcaster and cast all of your spells as Sensory or Touch spells, but once you figure out that you can not only skip Sensory by doing a &quot;kamehameha spell cone&quot; using area, but also potentially hit extra targets, you will cringe every time you will have to Reach for Sensory. And some day, you will be tired of doing so and just unleash collateral damage. Which is perfectly good emerging gameplay feature.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was looking at Shifting Sands and...I'm not sure if I understand it correctly. Could someone give me like 10 different examples of the thing? Mostly about what carries over with the subject to the past and what does not. I'm a fan of casting this spell at anything *other than yourself*, and I want to know how much exactly I can do with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Specific question: Imagine I have a book. I scribe something on the book, and then Shifting Sands it 2 scenes ago. Previous-Me looks at the book 2 scenes ago. Will it contain anything In-Between-Me has written into it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:51:07-08:00","id":1059869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059860#post1059860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I was looking at Shifting Sands and...I'm not sure if I understand it correctly. Could someone give me like 10 different examples of the thing? Mostly about what carries over with the subject to the past and what does not. I'm a fan of casting this spell at anything *other than yourself*, and I want to know how much exactly I can do with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Specific question: Imagine I have a book. I scribe something on the book, and then Shifting Sands it 2 scenes ago. Previous-Me looks at the book 2 scenes ago. Will it contain anything In-Between-Me has written into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>My knee-jerk interpretation is that you just sent yourself a note from the future. Earlier You then can't help but change the future, and those changes become Lasting once the book reaches the time in which it was sent to the past. You do not have to ensure that the book reaches the past again, as Time doesn't mind paradoxes (with a little P, that is).<br /> <br /> That said, I could see a Storyteller ruling otherwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:53:57-08:00","id":1059871,"title":"","content":"The subject of shifting sands arrives at the past in whatever state it was when you sent it back. The only exception are spells. Spells afecting the subject cast by the caster remain, while spells actively effecting the subject not cast by the caster disappear. You'd have to be a Disciple of Time to rationalize why it works like that aside from meta reasons like playability, book keeping and game balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T19:03:06-08:00","id":1059877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059871#post1059871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of shifting sands arrives at the past in whatever state it was when you sent it back. The only exception are spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true. A truly strict reading of the spell is that only injuries, Conditions, spent Mana, spent Willpower, and spells the subject cast on herself are definitely unchanged. There's plenty of ground there for a Storyteller or group of players to disagree with us on the rest, for all those meta reasons you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T19:47:37-08:00","id":1059890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059871#post1059871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells afecting the subject cast by the caster remain, while spells actively effecting the subject not cast by the caster disappear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells affecting the subject cast by the <i>subject</i> remain, for which the most sensible justification is &quot;spells don't begin before they're cast&quot; combined with Travelers' time travel working on destructive principles rather than the positional rewriting of archmagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T21:43:18-08:00","id":1059930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059890#post1059890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells affecting the subject cast by the <i>subject</i> remain, for which the most sensible justification is &quot;spells don't begin before they're cast&quot; combined with Travelers' time travel working on destructive principles rather than the positional rewriting of archmagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T00:49:58-08:00","id":1059983,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to stack dedicated tool Yantra bonuses? A mage gets one actual dedicated tool, but for example a soul stone can also be used as a dedicated tool. It's not clear whether not you could use both and get a -4 to Paradox. I'm inclined to think yes, at least at first glance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T01:19:30-08:00","id":1059986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059983#post1059983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to stack dedicated tool Yantra bonuses? A mage gets one actual dedicated tool, but for example a soul stone can also be used as a dedicated tool. It's not clear whether not you could use both and get a -4 to Paradox. I'm inclined to think yes, at least at first glance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This works very well for pre-Gnosis 3 characters who want to overreach and can &quot;cancel&quot; two reaches worth of Paradox per extra DedicatedTools-equivalent. It loses steam at Gnosis 3 and more, where you start picking up 2 paradox dice per Reach, but at this point you probably have enough Arcana or/and Rotes to not be desperately risking paradox. Gameplay problems shift from &quot;how do I cast this spell without potentially blowing myself up&quot; to &quot;how do I amass enough dice to turn ocean into coffee without wasting a whole evening on it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T01:21:59-08:00","id":1059987,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Shifting Sands tips! It seems like what I plan on doing isn't massively unfound in the rules. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T02:17:11-08:00","id":1059997,"title":"","content":"Here's another question: Is it possible to create a Prime Shielding spell that forces a Clash of Wills against Dispel Magic or Supernal Dispellation? That spell is Withstood by the Arcanum rating, which means any mage with 4 or 5 dots in Prime will have a pretty easy time dispelling anything they want. I suppose you could protect important spells in layers of Wards and Signs to increase their Withstand though. But what about Clash of Wills? The creative thaumaturgy rules say that a Shielding spell can protect against a number of supernatural attacks equal to Potency, requiring Clash of Wills for each one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:04:34-08:00","id":1060006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1059997#post1059997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The creative thaumaturgy rules say that a Shielding spell can protect against a number of supernatural attacks equal to Potency, requiring Clash of Wills for each one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds reasonable. Establishing a Prime Shield around your spells to attempt to prevent someone from Compelling their Flaws to the point of destruction or Unravelling them.<br /> Of course, there's nothing to stop someone from Dispelling THAT spell, and it doesn't help should someone try and brute-force a contradictory power into existence over the top of yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:10:02-08:00","id":1060007,"title":"","content":"These Creative Thaumaturgy rule is wrong but didn't get errated sadly. Shielding spells provide blanket immunity to mundane sources of harm, and supernatural attacks induce CoW. That's it. Potency only adds a dice to CoW if its Advanced. And yea, you could build a spell that gives you a CoW for every attempt to dispel it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here is my take on it<br /> <br /> <b>Royal Guard </b>(Prime 2)<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Shielding<br /> Wise Willworker knows that spells are a fragile creatures and must be protected. This spell provides immunity from Dissonance and CoW for every attempt to tamper with targeted spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>This spell is also guarded by CoW against the dispelation<br /> <br /> <br /> I think you could push CoW or immunity from Dissonance to a Reach effect.<br /> <br /> Edit: It would be better to cost 1 mana (maybe eveen for every spell). And if you worry about the setting you can change &quot;blanket immunity from Dissonance&quot; to &quot;additional Dissonance withstand equal to potency&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-08-2017, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:13:08-08:00","id":1060008,"title":"","content":"A Prime Clash of Wills spell would be very potent compared to other Arcana's Shielding spells, but the drawback would be that beneficial spells also would trigger it.<br /> The &quot;number of supernatural attacks per Potency&quot; thing is most likely an error and should be ignored since the final version removed that from the text of all Shielding spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:23:22-08:00","id":1060010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060007#post1060007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These Creative Thaumaturgy rule is wrong but didn't get errated sadly. Shielding spells provide blanket immunity to mundane sources of harm, and supernatural attacks induce CoW. That's it. Potency only adds a dice to CoW if its Advanced. And yea, you could build a spell that gives you a CoW for every attempt to dispel it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here is my take on it<br /> <br /> <b>Royal Guard </b>(Prime 2)<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Shielding<br /> Wise Willworker knows that spells are a fragile creatures and must be protected. This spell provides immunity from Dissonance and CoW for every attempt to tamper with targeted spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>This spell is also guarded by CoW against the dispelation<br /> <br /> <br /> I think you could push CoW or immunity from Dissonance to a Reach effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This spell seems reasonable, although I do agree with Tessie that a Clash of Wills Shielding spell is very potent. There is probably a reason why Wards and Signs grants Withstand instead of Clash of Wills against magical attacks. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure the drawback Tessie mentions would really be a factor when protecting spells against dispellation this way. Hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:38:13-08:00","id":1060013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060007#post1060007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell provides immunity from Dissonance and CoW for every attempt to tamper with targeted spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells should not be immune to Dissonance. Supernal Power is eroded by the Abyss, you shouldn't be able to negate that with Prime 2.<br /> Especially when sometimes with powerful Indefinite spells, that might be the only reliable (albeit immoral) way to destroy it.<br /> <br /> I'd just change that to &quot;Any Magical attempt to erode, modify or destroy the targetted spell provokes a Clash of Wills&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Me am no spell good 03-08-2017, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:45:25-08:00","id":1060015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060013#post1060013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells should not be immune to Dissonance. Supernal Power is eroded by the Abyss, you shouldn't be able to negate that with Prime 2.<br /> Especially when sometimes with powerful Indefinite spells, that might be the only realiable (albeit immoral) way to destroy it.<br /> <br /> I'd just change that to &amp;quot;Any Magical attempt to erode, modify or destroy the targetted spell provokes a Clash of Wills&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal Veil already negates the Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:49:30-08:00","id":1060017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060015#post1060015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Supernal Veil already negates the Dissonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty liberal reading of that spell.<br /> I think it's supposed to work as a &quot;hide my augmentation spells from mystical detection&quot; spell, not a &quot;hide my 100m tall fire-breathing rainbow coloured dragon from all perception, including the eternal tearing shards of the abyss that reside within the soul of every sleeper&quot; spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T03:52:13-08:00","id":1060019,"title":"","content":"Hiding spells might help a spell not to trigger Dissonance, but when Dissonance does trigger it should be a lot more difficult to handle it with Supernal magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:55:09-08:00","id":1060204,"title":"","content":"If you combine a Spell with &quot;Supernal Veil&quot; would it hide that casting from Peripheral Mage Sight? What if you combine your Spell with a Veiling Spell of the same Arcanum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:01:56-08:00","id":1060210,"title":"","content":"Is mass under the domain of Matter or Forces? One of my players wants to cast a spell to remove the speed penalty on some armor, It's clearly a perfecting spell but I'm not sure what Arcana could do it. Right now I'm inclined to say both can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:09:50-08:00","id":1060215,"title":"","content":"Both could do it, but works differently. Matter would be to actually change the mass of an object. Forces, however, could change how gravity acts upon an object, making it weigh less despite retaining mass. Forces would be the easier route to take since Matter would require changing one attribute of the object (mass) while retaining other properties depending on the first property (structure, durability and armor rating).<br /> <br /> Edit: With Matter it would be simpler to get a lighter armor and just increase its armor rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-08-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T13:22:13-08:00","id":1060248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060215#post1060215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both could do it, but works differently. Matter would be to actually change the mass of an object. Forces, however, could change how gravity acts upon an object, making it weigh less despite retaining mass. Forces would be the easier route to take since Matter would require changing one attribute of the object (mass) while retaining other properties depending on the first property (structure, durability and armor rating).<br /> <br /> Edit: With Matter it would be simpler to get a lighter armor and just increase its armor rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I'm following you correctly Forces 2 or Matter 3. That makes a lot of sense. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T22:28:58-08:00","id":1060419,"title":"","content":"Can a mage throw a spell-based Legacy Attainment as an Aimed Spell? Gut feeling says no, but I can't find exact rules on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T23:49:39-08:00","id":1060430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060419#post1060419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage throw a spell-based Legacy Attainment as an Aimed Spell? Gut feeling says no, but I can't find exact rules on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments are derived from Praxes, Praxes can be Aimed, the changes a Praxis undergoes upon becoming an attainment don't say you can't still Aim them. I'd allow them to be Aimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T05:43:10-08:00","id":1060485,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much time players spend on specific values of Gnosis and Arcana. Anyone cares to share their experience? I'm curious what is this games &quot;sweet spot&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T05:58:01-08:00","id":1060488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060485#post1060485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much time players spend on specific values of Gnosis and Arcana. Anyone cares to share their experience? I'm curious what is this games &quot;sweet spot&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because XP costs are linear, the game will tend to advance at a normal pace. I have 4 players. 3 of them have Gnosis 5 and at/near Arcanum 5, while one of them was on Gnosis 3 for a long time until recently. I feel like once you start getting Arcanum 4, you tend to be able to handle many situations and may not feel like it's necessary to go further as quickly. Of course, my players are starting to explore Chantries and the like, so the Imperial Mysteries are starting to appeal to them...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T06:59:52-08:00","id":1060500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060007#post1060007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These Creative Thaumaturgy rule is wrong but didn't get errated sadly. Shielding spells provide blanket immunity to mundane sources of harm, and supernatural attacks induce CoW. That's it. Potency only adds a dice to CoW if its Advanced. And yea, you could build a spell that gives you a CoW for every attempt to dispel it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here is my take on it<br /> <br /> <b>Royal Guard </b>(Prime 2)<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Shielding<br /> Wise Willworker knows that spells are a fragile creatures and must be protected. This spell provides immunity from Dissonance and CoW for every attempt to tamper with targeted spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>This spell is also guarded by CoW against the dispelation<br /> <br /> <br /> I think you could push CoW or immunity from Dissonance to a Reach effect.<br /> <br /> Edit: It would be better to cost 1 mana (maybe eveen for every spell). And if you worry about the setting you can change &quot;blanket immunity from Dissonance&quot; to &quot;additional Dissonance withstand equal to potency&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Returning to the &quot;Prime Clash of Wills&quot; spell, I think this makes sense but perhaps it'd be more balanced to require having 2 dots in all the Arcana required by the spell you're trying to protect. That's how basic Dispel Magic works, so it makes sense that if you're trying to Shield a spell of a given Arcanum, you need to manipulate how Prime works with it. I'm not sure other Prime spells require this, but from a balance perspective it's probably OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T16:20:07-08:00","id":1060690,"title":"","content":"You could do that spell as a Veiling Spell, under logic that Dispel finds and exploits flaws in the spell, and you veil these flaws so they are harder to find and anyone trying to do so needs to pierce the Veil. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T21:17:15-08:00","id":1060752,"title":"","content":"Shifting Sands and a few other powers send you back in time. When Shifting Sands sends you back do you go back where you were an hour ago? (Assuming you spend the reach to go back that far) Or do you stay where you are it's just an hour earlier? I feel like the answer might be buried in the timeline section but I can't seem to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T21:27:43-08:00","id":1060753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060752#post1060752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting Sands and a few other powers send you back in time. When Shifting Sands sends you back do you go back where you were an hour ago? (Assuming you spend the reach to go back that far) Or do you stay where you are it's just an hour earlier? I feel like the answer might be buried in the timeline section but I can't seem to find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are specifically traveling back in your own timeline, so I'd say your location reverts back to where you were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T21:39:50-08:00","id":1060754,"title":"","content":"If it's outside sensory range 'where I was' do you need the Space 2 Attainment for Spatial Sympathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T22:07:41-08:00","id":1060756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060754#post1060754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's outside sensory range 'where I was' do you need the Space 2 Attainment for Spatial Sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. The spell works on the basis of the timeline, allowing you to sidestep spatial limits. So theoretically, if you were on another continent an hour ago (usually well outside sensory range), you'd return to that time and place.<br /> <br /> Or are you saying you want the mage to turn up in a location that he was not at when traveling back in time, despite the spell's normal effects? Unlike Temporal Stutter (travel to the future) which does mention using Sympathetic Magic to do just that, past-traveling spells don't mention that. Which leads me to believe the only way to end up in a different location in the past is to bodily travel back to the past, ending up with both you and your past self running around. This feat, in turn, is explicitly called out as Archmastery and is unavailable for most mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T22:19:58-08:00","id":1060758,"title":"","content":"I think I found the answer I was looking for to confirm what you said Hermit.<br /> <br /> See here from Corridors of Time:<br /> <i>Without temporal sympathy, the subject may only be sent<br /> back to a period with an Unchanged temporal sympathy to the<br /> present. By using temporal sympathy, the mage may allow her<br /> subject to revisit old decisions and make different choices. <b>The<br /> subject arrives in whatever location he was in at the time chosen.</b><br /> By including the Sympathetic Range Attainment, the mage may<br /> send him somewhere else, but subjects cannot be sent back to<br /> periods outside their own lifetime.</i><br /> <br /> The bolded part describes the mage arriving being transported to wherever they were at the chosen time. If they were at a coffee shop a year ago and they send the target it seems they are at the coffee shop if they don't have Spatial Sympathy to change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T22:24:11-08:00","id":1060759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060756#post1060756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leads me to believe the only way to end up in a different location in the past is to bodily travel back to the past, ending up with both you and your past self running around. This feat, in turn, is explicitly called out as Archmastery and is unavailable for most mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corridors of Time does mention that Sympathetic Range can be used to send targets back to different locations, but yes, doing so without actually changing your past self's location is the stuff of archmagic.<br /> <br /> Dave's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/902581-questions-about-temporal-sympathy-and-time-magic?p=904306#post904306\">mentioned</a> some salient details before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T23:00:23-08:00","id":1060765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060759#post1060759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corridors of Time does mention that Sympathetic Range can be used to send targets back to different locations, but yes, doing so without actually changing your past self's location is the stuff of archmagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, now that I see it again, Corridors of Time <i>does </i>mention you can use S.Range to end up in other locations. Which means that anyone who looks at you will think you teleported or something, from that time's point of view.<br /> <br /> ... So that's how a certain lazy pun-loving skeleton does his teleporting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T01:37:24-08:00","id":1060787,"title":"","content":"How would you explain Imago and process of forming a spell to someone with blind mind's eye and unability to form mental images?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T10:22:08-08:00","id":1060926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060787#post1060787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you explain Imago and process of forming a spell to someone with blind mind's eye and unability to form mental images?</div> </div> </div> </div>Focus on other sensory details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:38:59-08:00","id":1060980,"title":"","content":"By &quot;blind mind's eye&quot; I meant pretty much unability to conjure images, tastes, sounds and other &quot;mindspace like you see in movies&quot; style imagination. Basically, aphantasia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T13:29:35-08:00","id":1061000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1060980#post1060980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By &quot;blind mind's eye&quot; I meant pretty much unability to conjure images, tastes, sounds and other &quot;mindspace like you see in movies&quot; style imagination. Basically, aphantasia.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could describe it as the process of intensely thinking about the effect of the spell, as though their inner narrator was using words that describe higher-order magical concepts in extreme detail, such that a single syllable described an entire causal relationship, for example.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure how far aphantasia goes though, but since most at least have an inner voice I think this should be possible. I'm not 100% sure.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T01:13:11-08:00","id":1061162,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I do posses an inner narrator, it's just that it doesn't...sound. It's hard to explain. I like the &quot;intense, extensive exploration of the concept&quot; though. It makes much more sense to me than mind's eye. Thanks [exclamation mark, RIP my keyboard].<br /> <br /> AND FOR SOMETHING TOTALLY DIFFERENT<br /> I was annoyed for a moment that Status Merit creates a chargen system mastery trap. How? Well, you can use Status to requisit things. Add two dots to their Availability Rating, and you can get them for forever. Merits have Availability Rating equal to their Merit dots, which means that with Status of three, you can systematically grab all the One Dot merits and claim them for yourself for forever, at tempo one merit per week. So why bother grabbing Sanctum One, Grimoire One and Alternate Identity One if you can just take three weeks of game time to have them all?<br /> That was from character generation standpoint.<br /> <br /> But now I can see a merit in it...when your characters progress from Status One to Status Three in game, this is a really neat upgrade that gives you one time feel of &quot;bling bling&quot; when you look at your character sheet, and decide to permanently requisit things you already own...after which you use Sancticity of Merits to recover XP you invested in these things and suddenly, you have like five dots of merits you can spend on something else. It definitely makes you want to climb the ladder of Status.<br /> <br /> ...on the other hand, I hate how Sanctum Requires Safe Place merit. I never saw Safe Place in use. Getting one dot Sanctum eats 20 percent of your starting Merits. Feels like a tax, especially when you know that you could invest these two merit dots into Status to bump it to three and get these and many others for free.<br /> [My favorite way of spending unused Status Requisitions is to order fuckaton of temporary [so worth one dot of requisitions] Grimoires and go on a SCRIBE GRIMOIRE binge.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-11-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T03:29:54-08:00","id":1061187,"title":"","content":"If Safe Place never comes up it's because by it's mere presence most NPCs never show up at your door. But actually with a just a one-dot Safe Place, your Sanctum is pretty easy to breach. You may compensate with a couple of spells, but then that's either a lot of maintenance or 1 XP per spell. It might be worth it if that kind of spell comes naturally to you, but for example in my current game my cabal can't do very much about it so when Seers inevitably come knocking, I think our Safe Place will be useful.<br /> <br /> And the reason I don't have a problem with characters using Status like that it's because 1) it comes with responsibility 2) It's certainly useful, but not a better option than pooling for Hallow, Sanctum, Library, etc. as a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T09:28:12-08:00","id":1061265,"title":"","content":"On this second edition, how is the Aegis Kai Doru reacting to the Atlantis Myth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T09:43:34-08:00","id":1061273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_containe