":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:10:15-08:00","id":1061438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061431#post1061431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What systems would/should the Mage considerations of Cryptids operate under in Mage 2e?<br /> Spirits with a perpetual Materialized form? Something stranger? Horrors with Dread Powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd build them using the spirit rules and then simply not worry about Essence or Manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:10:23-08:00","id":1061439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061431#post1061431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What systems would/should the Mage considerations of Cryptids operate under in Mage 2e?<br /> Spirits with a perpetual Materialized form? Something stranger? Horrors with Dread Powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any of the above depending on the specific creature in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:40:44-08:00","id":1061449,"title":"","content":"Quick question, can you use willpower for spellcasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7108-satcom","name":"Satcom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T01:20:24-08:00","id":1061476,"title":"","content":"What does potency do for the Mind 5 spell Psychic Genesis?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satcom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061449#post1061449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, can you use willpower for spellcasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes you can. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T01:50:06-08:00","id":1061481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061476#post1061476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does potency do for the Mind 5 spell Psychic Genesis?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> yes you can.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, which is why in the most up to date version the primary factor is duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T03:15:43-07:00","id":1061487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061265#post1061265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this second edition, how is the Aegis Kai Doru reacting to the Atlantis Myth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tooth and Nail would lead me to believe that any potential source of Relics, be it from the Dreamtime, or even fragments of deleted timelines, would be of interest to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T05:30:49-07:00","id":1061516,"title":"","content":"If a Mage uses Sever Soul on someone right before said someone dies does the soul disappear upon their death or does it no longer count as theirs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-12-2017, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T07:06:28-07:00","id":1061532,"title":"","content":"A soul &quot;belongs&quot; to whomever it was attached to last, so ostensibly it remains theirs, metaphysically. Whether this means it vanishes with them into oblivion is another question entirely. Best guess is... Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T09:41:07-07:00","id":1061562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061516#post1061516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Mage uses Sever Soul on someone right before said someone dies does the soul disappear upon their death or does it no longer count as theirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it or liches would have more trouble creating stock-piles. The soul never goes through the process of dying with the body either which feels to me like it'd be a necessary metaphysical component for it to move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T13:00:35-07:00","id":1061590,"title":"","content":"The matter of stockpiles is easily solved by Soul Jars. The Spell to make them can be explicitly made Lasting. &quot;Sever Soul&quot; on the other hand has a Duration, and the Soul returns to its owner after the Spell lapses. I always assumed the Soul finds its final destination if there are no Spells holding it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T16:56:44-07:00","id":1061648,"title":"","content":"Would a Mage be able to at any point be able to use a Spiritual being's powers? I understand in many cases these would seem less powerful and also inconsistent with a Mage's interest in retaining purely Supernal power, but I'm currently writing a Parazoologist Legacy and their Fourth Attainment is normally about taking on biological traits of other animals (through visual inspiraiton from seeing stuff like Wyverns, Barghests, and Kelpies).<br /> <br /> However I was also wondering if as the Optional Arcanum they could borrow some of their innate Spiritual powers as well for a short while, having to spend Essence in the same was as the creature to use them.<br /> <br /> Or is this too much? Certainly perhaps too much for the Spirit Arcanum, but what about for the 4th attainment of a Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T17:13:15-07:00","id":1061651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061648#post1061648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Mage be able to at any point be able to use a Spiritual being's powers? I understand in many cases these would seem less powerful and also inconsistent with a Mage's interest in retaining purely Supernal power, but I'm currently writing a Parazoologist Legacy and their Fourth Attainment is normally about taking on biological traits of other animals (through visual inspiraiton from seeing stuff like Wyverns, Barghests, and Kelpies).<br /> <br /> However I was also wondering if as the Optional Arcanum they could borrow some of their innate Spiritual powers as well for a short while, having to spend Essence in the same was as the creature to use them.<br /> <br /> Or is this too much? Certainly perhaps too much for the Spirit Arcanum, but what about for the 4th attainment of a Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Pacting from the Summoners book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T23:06:21-07:00","id":1061733,"title":"","content":"Is creating a mental illness basically a persistent condition that resolves when the magic no longer acts on the person?<br /> <br /> By extension, could you give yourself mental illnesses and resolve them for beats?<br /> <br /> Also, would you need Patterning to do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T00:03:11-07:00","id":1061741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1061733#post1061733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is creating a mental illness basically a persistent condition that resolves when the magic no longer acts on the person?<br /> <br /> By extension, could you give yourself mental illnesses and resolve them for beats?<br /> <br /> Also, would you need Patterning to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can generate conditions with Ruling, and you can most certainly do that. The book in fact directly mentions that possibility is popular with Mastigos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T00:22:30-07:00","id":1061745,"title":"","content":"If a condition ends because the spell ends the condition does not resolve. However, you can still gain beats when you fulfil the beat criteria of the condition.<br /> <br /> And yes, persistent conditions are most often created with 4 dot spells, but not necessarily so. For example, the condition Obsession is considered a persistent condition, but I find that a simple Mind 2 spell should be able to grant it for the duration of the spell (i.e. as long as it's not Lasting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-13-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T03:30:27-07:00","id":1061771,"title":"","content":"You could craft a condition that generates another one. Something like Unstable -&gt; 'Kind of mental illness'. That way only Unstable ends with the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:28:51-07:00","id":1062605,"title":"","content":"is there any reason a supernal fae couldn't use Time 2- Veil of Moments to extend the length of time it can manifest in the fallen world, potentially indefinitely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:49:42-07:00","id":1062616,"title":"","content":"Can Mages no longer spend Willpower on Wisdom rolls? I know that even Dave said you could a while back but after reading through the book just now it explicitly says you can't. Is that just something that changed in the final version of the book or is it a mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:56:20-07:00","id":1062620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062616#post1062616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages no longer spend Willpower on Wisdom rolls? I know that even Dave said you could a while back but after reading through the book just now it explicitly says you can't. Is that just something that changed in the final version of the book or is it a mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something they changed in the final version.<br /> Sensible too, as spending Willpower would be a massive boost to what is normally quite a small dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T23:00:25-07:00","id":1062671,"title":"","content":"can a mage learn multiple versions of a rote in order to use multiple different mundra yantras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T23:27:36-07:00","id":1062682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062671#post1062671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can a mage learn multiple versions of a rote in order to use multiple different mundra yantras?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see why not, although I see little in-universe reason to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T02:33:37-07:00","id":1062717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062605#post1062605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there any reason a supernal fae couldn't use Time 2- Veil of Moments to extend the length of time it can manifest in the fallen world, potentially indefinitely</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Fae in question, they'd need to be able to get thE Duration up to Indefinite, but most Fae probably could extend their stay. I doubt most would though since the Fallen is very high risk for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T02:35:04-07:00","id":1062718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062671#post1062671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can a mage learn multiple versions of a rote in order to use multiple different mundra yantras?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mudra yantras are exclusive to their rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T04:26:00-07:00","id":1062728,"title":"","content":"I guess you mean you can only use one mudra per spell even if you know several? Makes sense since each rote comes with a unique imago and the mudra is created to strengthen that particular imago.<br /> Since it's relevant to the question I can point out that you don't need to use any mudra at all to gain access to the extra Reaches. Just learning a rote is enough to get that bonus as long as you use the rote's imago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T05:24:05-07:00","id":1062738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062728#post1062728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's relevant to the question I can point out that you don't need to use any mudra at all to gain access to the extra Reaches. Just learning a rote is enough to get that bonus as long as you use the rote's imago.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't? Source?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T05:31:46-07:00","id":1062741,"title":"","content":"&quot;When casting a Rote from memory, using an Order\u2019s recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra.&quot;<br /> <br /> The mudra (or at least the yantra bonuses) is implied to be a choice when casting a rote. In fact, it actually implies you can't use the mudra when casting from a grimoire.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's not written very clearly, but looking at the list of yantras it never mentions free Reach for mudras; only extra dice. Contrast to dedicated tools where using one as a yantra has the explicit additional benefit of reducing paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-15-2017, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T13:57:18-07:00","id":1062962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062738#post1062738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't? Source?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's written perfectly clearly. You <i>may</i> use a Mudra Yantra when you've memorized a rote (and as Tessie points out, not when you're just borrowing a Grimoire.) You don't <i>have</i> to.<br /> <br /> You usually will, though, because as Yantras go Mudra is exceptionally effiicient. 1-5 dice for a few seconds' Tutting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T14:03:23-07:00","id":1062967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062962#post1062962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You usually will, though, because as Yantras go Mudra is exceptionally effiicient. 1-5 dice for a few seconds' Tutting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Related question: Does the extra die from an Order's Rote Skills come before or after the five-dice cap on Mudra's bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T23:15:05-07:00","id":1063128,"title":"","content":"Is there a rule of thumb for &quot;spells to prefer as a praxis&quot; versus &quot;spells to prefer as a rote&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T23:32:55-07:00","id":1063133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063128#post1063128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a rule of thumb for &quot;spells to prefer as a praxis&quot; versus &quot;spells to prefer as a rote&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotes are for pushing your limits, Praxes are for spells you cast often.<br /> <br /> The reduced exceptional threshold of a Praxis effectively turns its use into an extra Vice for the mage thanks to the universal Willpower recovery of an exceptional casting, whereas the ability to use grimoires (or, for Masters, personal mnemonics) to gain the rote quality effectively doubles a spell's baseline odds of success without relying on extra spells or Destiny dots.<br /> <br /> (Rotes do also have a somewhat higher chance of exceptional success than regular castings, which further helps with squeezing extra factors and other benefits out of a spell, but a single reroll of any failed dice is more useful for just getting the spell to work than fishing for providence.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T23:44:52-07:00","id":1063135,"title":"","content":"Remember that this use of Grimoire requires you to cast the spell as a Ritual and doubles the total ritual time you take to cast it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T14:15:34-07:00","id":1063502,"title":"","content":"It really depends on how you use magic and whether you have Fate buffs. Personally I use free Praxis to remove the Mana cost from spells I need in an emergency. I use Rotes when I need the free reach and/or every drop of potency. Rotes become less useful when you get combined spells.<br /> <br /> Rotes are also good when you don't want to max out an arcana, but you want to use one or two spells from it. If you are only ever taking Prime 1, then Dispel Magic is an excellent rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T20:22:03-07:00","id":1063732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063502#post1063502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really depends on how you use magic and whether you have Fate buffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate buffs are limited to the same effects as the Prime spell As Above, So Below and grimoire-based long-casting \u2014 the boon overview lists &quot;add two Reach to apply the benefit to spellcasting rolls&quot; bit is listed under the dice-trick effect specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T20:37:15-07:00","id":1063735,"title":"","content":"When selecting a legacy, if the primary arcanum of the legacy is Common or Inferior for the mage, it elevates to Ruling. If it's already Ruling for the mage, when the mage buys a dot of that arcanum she gets an Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> Is it just me or does that latter option really pale in comparison to the former in most cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T21:31:41-07:00","id":1063744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063732#post1063732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate buffs are limited to the same effects as the Prime spell As Above, So Below and grimoire-based long-casting \u2014 the boon overview lists &quot;add two Reach to apply the benefit to spellcasting rolls&quot; bit is listed under the dice-trick effect specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The fate buff you want is the 9-again turn a chance die into a single die combined with Steadfast to autopass the roll. This lets you tank your dicepool to -4 and still guarentee one success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T22:04:40-07:00","id":1063746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063744#post1063744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fate buff you want is the 9-again turn a chance die into a single die combined with Steadfast to autopass the roll. This lets you tank your dicepool to -4 and still guarentee one success.</div> </div> </div> </div>That this is a blatant exploit which obviously defeats the purpose of having the spellcasting system work the way it does and glides past the thing I just pointed out about what part of the boon breakdown specifies applicability to spellcasting rolls should tell you plenty about how much stock I put in this interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T03:29:33-07:00","id":1063787,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing that it isn't against the spirit of the system, but it's how it works by RAW. Exceptional Luck has a specific +2 Reach option that allows <i>all</i> boons to affect spell casting rolls, and one of those boons can be Steadfast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T03:56:43-07:00","id":1063795,"title":"","content":"Do you require spirit arcanum when using the space 2 Attainment for sympathetic targeting on a target in the shadow(when you're in the mortal world).<br /> And similarly for other worlds like death for the underworld ect.<br /> It makes sense for it to require it, but I can't seem to find anything in the book besides one specific spell's added effects that would indicate so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:07:53-07:00","id":1063802,"title":"","content":"No, you do not require it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T06:37:21-07:00","id":1063826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063746#post1063746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That this is a blatant exploit which obviously defeats the purpose of having the spellcasting system work the way it does and glides past the thing I just pointed out about what part of the boon breakdown specifies applicability to spellcasting rolls should tell you plenty about how much stock I put in this interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about Steadfast inherently excludes spellcasting. You could use it on spellcasting without reach. The only thing being made to affect spellcasting is the 9-again part, which is in line with what you are saying.<br /> <br /> Steadfast not being allowed to apply to Spellcasting rolls is a houserule, and one I would likely make for my games, but when answering the question of what makes a good praxis or a good rote it bares mentioning that it depends on what else you have going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T06:54:31-07:00","id":1063830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063746#post1063746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That this is a blatant exploit which obviously defeats the purpose of having the spellcasting system work the way it does and glides past the thing I just pointed out about what part of the boon breakdown specifies applicability to spellcasting rolls should tell you plenty about how much stock I put in this interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players used this exploit and I also ruled that the only boons / hexes that could be applied to spellcasting were the ones specified in the boons / hexes section. I agree that that's what the rules text was trying to get across in its very concise way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T06:59:34-07:00","id":1063833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063735#post1063735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When selecting a legacy, if the primary arcanum of the legacy is Common or Inferior for the mage, it elevates to Ruling. If it's already Ruling for the mage, when the mage buys a dot of that arcanum she gets an Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> Is it just me or does that latter option really pale in comparison to the former in most cases?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pale in comparison? It downright sucks since most mages will already have developed their Path's Ruling most of the way or they wouldn't be interested in that particular legacy anyway.<br /> My understanding is that many people on this forum houserule that legacies has a secondary Arcanum that is granted as Ruling in case the primary Arcanum already is Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T07:34:20-07:00","id":1063843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063826#post1063826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing about Steadfast inherently excludes spellcasting. You could use it on spellcasting without reach. The only thing being made to affect spellcasting is the 9-again part, which is in line with what you are saying.<br /> <br /> Steadfast not being allowed to apply to Spellcasting rolls is a houserule, and one I would likely make for my games, but when answering the question of what makes a good praxis or a good rote it bares mentioning that it depends on what else you have going on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you are using Fate Exceptional Luck to give yourself the Steadfast condition you need to use reach to allow it to affect Spellcasting rolls. the exceptional luck itself states this. Conditions from Exceptional Luck also do not grant beats unless the spell roll achieved an exceptional success. Not a house rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> The mage blesses the subject\u2019s endeavors or curses them<br /> with misfortune. Whether good or bad, the subject\u2019s luck is<br /> truly exceptional. This spell bestows a boon or inflicts a hex<br /> on the subject (see p. 134). The subject may Withstand a hex<br /> with Composure.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>+2 Reach: The boon or hex can affect spellcasting rolls.</b></span><br /> +2 Reach: Spend a point of Mana. The mage can cast this<br /> spell as a reflexive action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T08:31:02-07:00","id":1063871,"title":"","content":"Boons specify that the 9-again and 8-again options only apply to mundane rolls without extra reach. Boon specify that adding potency to dicerolls only affects mundane rolls. The section on conditions makes no such distinction. Exceptional Luck does not speciy it only works on mundane rolls, but it does include a +2 reach option to affect spellcasting. Either that is a really weird way to harken back to the reach options included in the boon section, in which case no particular restriction is given in the spell itself, or it is an option to make everything about the spell apply to spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Either interpretation allows Steadfast to be used with spellcasting rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T09:13:09-07:00","id":1063891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063787#post1063787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing that it isn't against the spirit of the system, but it's how it works by RAW. Exceptional Luck has a specific +2 Reach option that allows <i>all</i> boons to affect spell casting rolls, and one of those boons can be Steadfast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrary to what the Simpsons may have told you, &quot;technically correct&quot; is not actually the best kind of correct. The nature of how these books are put together and the constraints under which errata are compiled mean some common sense needs to be exercised in interpreting the mechanics regardless of the presence or absence of explicit forbiddance against particular rules interactions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063826#post1063826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing about Steadfast inherently excludes spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909046-breaking-exceptional-luck?p=909627#post909627\">This conversation has been had before</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-17-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T09:46:29-07:00","id":1063909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1063891#post1063891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909046-breaking-exceptional-luck?p=909627#post909627&amp;quot;]This</a> conversation has been had before[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>That thread primarily talks aboit the Informed condition, which I agree does not work RAW. I believe that was clarified later, even.<br /> <br /> Resolving two conditions... page 126 is for creative thaumaturgy and I'm not sure it takes into account spells that grant multiple conditions. Even if you take that to be true, just don't use Inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T11:15:28-07:00","id":1063941,"title":"","content":"I've been considering throwing in a houserule in my games to ban spells from affecting spellcasting. Otherwise, you get the Nuclear Acanthus problem, where two Acanthus can cast Exceptional Luck back and forth on one another in an infinite loop until they achieve enough dice to bypass all problems everywhere forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T12:01:53-07:00","id":1063964,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that problem got worked out already that it doesn't take long to hit a point of diminishing returns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T12:20:50-07:00","id":1063970,"title":"","content":"You might boost yourself (dunno why you'd need to have more than one mage) so much that such a houserule still makes sense, but as Mrmdubois says it's certainly not possible to get an infinite loop when every bonus die costs two dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T14:00:54-07:00","id":1064022,"title":"","content":"Does an attack spell apply the stunned tilt if it does sufficient damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","user":"Enlightened_Milkman","date":".  grammar is hard 03-17-2017, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T14:59:01-07:00","id":1064046,"title":"","content":"It seems likely, but should probably be determined on a case to case basis to see if it makes sense for any specific attack spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T18:26:56-07:00","id":1064112,"title":"","content":"Stunned is facet of taking damage, not the damage's source. Unless you're immune to it, you take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:26:46-07:00","id":1064163,"title":"","content":"Do Postcognition spells also exist in the past you're perceiving?<br /> So for example, say you utilise Postcognition to perceive a scene where there's a Mage present. Will they (in the past) detect its formation in Peripheral Mage Sight?<br /> As a continuiation from this, can that past version of the Mage with the use of the correct Arcana dispel your Postcognition spell? Or utilise Focused Mage Sight to determine when you're casting from?<br /> Furthermore, as the future is unwritten, if that Mage understands that element of temporal physics, they'll likely understand at that point they're existing within an alternate history, and that their actions are so important that they'll echo through time to that future point.<br /> <br /> The most important factor to me though is that if Mages in the past can detect Postcognition, how dangerous is it for a Mage to use Postcognition on any scene where they know a Mage will be present?<br /> Say for instance you scry the casting of a concealment spell which a Mage seeks to use in order to hide his Sanctum from detection.<br /> His peripheral Mage sight will trigger, alerting him to the fact that someone is likely attempting to determine what he's doing, even if he doesn't have the Arcana to perceive the Postcognition spell specifically.<br /> As such, he may completely change his plans to protect his sanctum, likely changing events for a significant period of time after that, triggering the butterfly effect, and quite possibly leaving the present that the Mage exists in radically different.<br /> <br /> Even if you interpret the caster themselves as benefitting from the protection against Temporal Retcons formed from their own spells, you're still potentially causing horrific consequences for the present.<br /> <br /> With a simple use of Apprentice Time magic (Temporal Sympathy needed to view more than Unchanged pasts), you could though simply casting the spell redefine the present in such drastic ways such that you, and hundreds of thousands, perhaps even millions or billions of people might not even exist (albeit perhaps replaced with alternate history versions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Me no am spell gud 03-17-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:39:27-07:00","id":1064168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064163#post1064163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Postcognition spells also exist in the past you're perceiving?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, much like how Temporal Summoning doesn't alter something's past just because a past version of it is being made to exist in the future \u2014 Time spells that aren't time travel aren't subject to the complications of time travel. It's a reference copy, not an active window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:39:30-07:00","id":1064169,"title":"","content":"Postcognition does not exist in the past. It simply allows you to view the past.<br /> <br /> Edit: What Satchel said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:45:27-07:00","id":1064173,"title":"","content":"Right, that makes more sense.<br /> <br /> So up until the point at which you're using Unmaking to unmake everything that's already happened and &quot;force&quot; your way back into the Past, every spell which uses Temporal Sympathy really isn't messing with the past, more summoning a verison of it, or affecting the present by overlaying an alternate version of history over it (a la Rewrite History).<br /> <br /> So until you use Corridors of Time (or perhaps Shifting Sands to a much lesser extent) you don't have to worry about the Butterfly effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T22:32:27-07:00","id":1064188,"title":"","content":"Simple Question:<br /> <br /> Since major changes to things cause a noticeable shift in Temporal Sympathy, could you just cast a a knowing Time spell to detect the exact moment in the past such a shift in Temporal Sympathy took place? Such as a death, birth, item Imbuing, ect... like noticing you're suddenly going up a much steeper inclune?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T01:42:19-07:00","id":1064220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064188#post1064188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple Question:<br /> <br /> Since major changes to things cause a noticeable shift in Temporal Sympathy, could you just cast a a knowing Time spell to detect the exact moment in the past such a shift in Temporal Sympathy took place? Such as a death, birth, item Imbuing, ect... like noticing you're suddenly going up a much steeper inclune?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I understand it correctly, the answer is maybe. If you are protected from the time change then you know what you are looking for and can focus on the events of that change. If you where affected by the time change then you don't even know to look for a change let alone what to look for in the past as it would look normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T06:52:08-07:00","id":1064276,"title":"","content":"I don't think Pale_Crusader meant &quot;when did a timeline change occur&quot;, but rather &quot;when did the last major change to this thing happen&quot; - like, say, finding out the exact date of someone's Awakening by using Time magic to check for when their temporal sympathy drops off a cliff.<br /> <br /> And the answer, I think, is yes. Seems reasonable to me. It will only detect the last major change, though, but you could use another Arcanum to search for a specific change. The Moros Eleventh Question in my chronicle uses a Death 1 Time 1 Praxis called &quot;Time of Death&quot; to get the precise moment a corpse died all the time. (So he can then use his postcognition attainment on it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T06:56:26-07:00","id":1064277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064220#post1064220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I understand it correctly, the answer is maybe. If you are protected from the time change then you know what you are looking for and can focus on the events of that change. If you where affected by the time change then you don't even know to look for a change let alone what to look for in the past as it would look normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize. My question isn't about detecting magical alterations to the timeline, it's about using the fact that Temporal Sympathy changes when a subject becomes/was less like the moment you are using as a Temporal Sympathetic Yantra.<br /> <br /> Hypothetically it'd let you know when changes of particular magnitudes enough to change the subjects Temporal Sympathy happen even if you have no idea what the change was.<br /> <br /> Like using Spirit to notice changes in the Gauntlet while you travel to pin point thicker spots (like Prime sacred geometry, but search for the opposite of normal searches).<br /> <br /> Envision the spell as a Time knowing, with Withstand being the connection because your observing to connection not the subject, thus making it super easy to find the time of major changes and difficult to find the moment of minor changes to the sibject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-18-2017, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T06:57:43-07:00","id":1064278,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T11:22:02-07:00","id":1064392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064276#post1064276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the answer, I think, is yes. Seems reasonable to me. It will only detect the last major change, though, but you could use another Arcanum to search for a specific change. The Moros Eleventh Question in my chronicle uses a Death 1 Time 1 Praxis called &quot;Time of Death&quot; to get the precise moment a corpse died all the time. (So he can then use his postcognition attainment on it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't Death 1 Forensic Gaze be able to determine the exact moment a corpse died without any need for conjunctive use of Time<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forensic Gaze (Death\u2022)<br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Investigation, Expression<br /> The mage can determine the state of a corpse. She determines<br /> the exact method of its demise <b>as well as exactly when it died</b>.<br /> For each level of Potency, the mage reveals contributing factors<br /> to the cause of death. For example, a man found burned in a<br /> car might have died from asphyxiation, but might have gotten<br /> that way because he was unconscious due to a head wound from<br /> crashing his car into a tree while driving drunk. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T11:30:50-07:00","id":1064395,"title":"","content":"It would. &quot;Time of Death&quot; doesn't seem to fall into mindset of 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T21:02:26-07:00","id":1064635,"title":"","content":"Are the effects of Life 2's Purge Illness inherently Lasting? If so, is it possible to have a Mind 2 version of the spell that can rid someone of their addictions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T21:17:31-07:00","id":1064637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064635#post1064635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the effects of Life 2's Purge Illness inherently Lasting? If so, is it possible to have a Mind 2 version of the spell that can rid someone of their addictions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that resolving mental Conditions already has a spell, Clear Thoughts (Mind 3), I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T21:29:07-07:00","id":1064638,"title":"","content":"And so it does, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T07:30:26-07:00","id":1064744,"title":"","content":"Spirits and goetia has Influences relating to their natures, meaning often types of objects, forces, feelings and abstract concepts. It seems to me that souls would hit both the object and abstract concept categories. Is it possible to have Influence: Souls? And, in that case, does that mean that they would be able to create souls with Create and Mass Create when regular mages can't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T07:39:13-07:00","id":1064747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064744#post1064744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits and goetia has Influences relating to their natures, meaning often types of objects, forces, feelings and abstract concepts. It seems to me that souls would hit both the object and abstract concept categories. Is it possible to have Influence: Souls? And, in that case, does that mean that they would be able to create souls with Create and Mass Create when regular mages can't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically yes, but I'd be very interested in how the spirit or Goetia got that Influence in the first place.<br /> <br /> And by interested I mean, &quot;How the hell are you justifying it within the narrative?!&quot; There being no spiritual reflection of humans, the only creatures who naturally possess souls, seem to imply that souls are not the usual stuff the Shadow interacts with. And since the Oneiros and the Temenos are inside/ made of souls, I doubt Goetia of there having Influence over souls (it'd be like a spirit having Influence over Ephemera, or the Shadow)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T07:54:29-07:00","id":1064750,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a Reaper stored enough stolen souls in soul jars to create the Resonant Condition for souls?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or, perhaps, a Reaper with Spirit just created or gave a spirit Influence: Souls just because they wanted the spirit to create souls for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-19-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T08:00:37-07:00","id":1064754,"title":"","content":"The problem with Resonance and souls is that no mattet how much souls there are and active they are, souls don't seem to produce Soul-Resonance. Otherwise, we'd already be producing soul-spirits by just living, and a city would be a maelstrom of soul-spirits. <br /> <br /> Hmm... maybe artificially synthesizing Resonance could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T20:23:59-07:00","id":1065070,"title":"","content":"Do you think a modern version of the old Mind 3 spell Eternal Now would still be possible? If so, do you think it would still be a Fraying spell or something else?<br /> <br /> Edit: For those who don't know/remember what the spell did, it suppressed the ability for the target to form new memories for the duration of the spell. It would obviously need to be modernized, for example, Withstood by either Resolve or Composure, but is the basic concept still sound and appropriately assigned Practice-wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-19-2017, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T23:49:25-07:00","id":1065119,"title":"","content":"Is there any room or precedent in the CofD combat system for making split attacks, hitting multiple targets at once?<br /> I primarily ask because I've been wanting for a while for a Fate legacy of mine to be able to &quot;fan the hammer&quot; and take a few people out of the fight (assuming Beaten Down is in effect).<br /> Would it be something like a negative dice penalty equal to the number of targets, then having to divide any successes as equally as possible between them?<br /> <br /> So say for instance you wanted to cause some painful but not life-threatening wounds to take 3 goons out of the fight, you could suffer a -3 to your attack roll, and with 3 successes would deal 2 damage (light revolver, 1 damage + 1 success each) to each of the individuals. Hopefully enough to deal the single point of lethal needed to hopefully dissuade them from violent action.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, if you're a Mage and a lucky son of a gun, you could potentially suffer as high as a -5 penalty and get really lucky with 5 successes, and people thinking twice about taking you on.<br /> <br /> Not quite a &quot;mage&quot; question, but perhaps only feasible for the most skilled and lucky of mortals, or a reasonably prepared Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T00:17:33-07:00","id":1065120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1065119#post1065119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any room or precedent in the CofD combat system for making split attacks, hitting multiple targets at once?<br /> I primarily ask because I've been wanting for a while for a Fate legacy of mine to be able to &quot;fan the hammer&quot; and take a few people out of the fight (assuming Beaten Down is in effect).<br /> Would it be something like a negative dice penalty equal to the number of targets, then having to divide any successes as equally as possible between them?<br /> <br /> So say for instance you wanted to cause some painful but not life-threatening wounds to take 3 goons out of the fight, you could suffer a -3 to your attack roll, and with 3 successes would deal 2 damage (light revolver, 1 damage + 1 success each) to each of the individuals. Hopefully enough to deal the single point of lethal needed to hopefully dissuade them from violent action.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, if you're a Mage and a lucky son of a gun, you could potentially suffer as high as a -5 penalty and get really lucky with 5 successes, and people thinking twice about taking you on.<br /> <br /> Not quite a &quot;mage&quot; question, but perhaps only feasible for the most skilled and lucky of mortals, or a reasonably prepared Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>For spellasting attacks, you need only increase the Spell Factor for Scale - Number of Subjects.<br /> <br /> For basic combat, you generally cannot hit multiple targets except using automatic firearms with the autofire rules or possessing an applicable Merit (e.g., Martial Arts 3 (Whirlwind Strike), Staff Fighting 4 (Tornado Strike - Hurt Locker) or Two Weapons Fighting 4 (Double Strike - Hurt Locker)).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T04:17:35-07:00","id":1065185,"title":"","content":"You could probably get away with a spell that enforces Down and Dirty Combat on the targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T04:28:28-07:00","id":1065189,"title":"","content":"For firearms, use Covering Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T19:22:46-07:00","id":1065547,"title":"","content":"Hey quick question, shouldn't the damage from Devour the Slain spell be Resistant Damage since it's Scouring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T19:59:29-07:00","id":1065554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1065547#post1065547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey quick question, shouldn't the damage from Devour the Slain spell be Resistant Damage since it's Scouring?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> <br /> There's been a debate over how whether this makes Death better at inflicting damage, and the Scouring rules and damage-from-spells rules in general. What I remember of the consensus is that yes, inflicting resistant damage and gaining Mana while doing it is awesome, but not that overwhelmingly so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T20:06:45-07:00","id":1065558,"title":"","content":"But the spell itself doesn't say it is resistant damage. Do you have a source that says it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T20:13:13-07:00","id":1065563,"title":"","content":"Just inferring it, since the spell is still a variant of Scouring without saying anything about the resistant bit being altered, and how Dave never bothered to correct people assuming the spell inflicting resistant damage in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025432-devour-the-slain-knit-endless-loop\">this thread</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T20:47:43-07:00","id":1065578,"title":"","content":"OK it seems that Dave has implied it's Resistant Damage. So thank for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T21:24:12-07:00","id":1065587,"title":"","content":"It wasn't implied, it was actually quite explicit.<br /> <br /> &quot;The lethal damage from Scouring is resistant. You can't heal it with Knit. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:22:51-07:00","id":1065745,"title":"","content":"My book isn't with me. Prime Mage Armour protects against purely supernatural attacks, that I recall, without a physical component (a blast of ethereal fire yes, werewolf claws no). Does that include purely supernatural supernal attacks? Would Prime Mage Armour apply against the practice of fraying for example? Unmaking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:26:43-07:00","id":1065782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1065745#post1065745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My book isn't with me. Prime Mage Armour protects against purely supernatural attacks, that I recall, without a physical component (a blast of ethereal fire yes, werewolf claws no). Does that include purely supernatural supernal attacks? Would Prime Mage Armour apply against the practice of fraying for example? Unmaking?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's specifically what it's for, yes. It would probably provide less protection against Unmaking though since those frequently bypass Health and Armor, and deal with Withstand or CoW, success equals death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:31:22-07:00","id":1065785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1065782#post1065782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's specifically what it's for, yes. It would probably provide less protection against Unmaking though since those frequently bypass Health and Armor, and deal with Withstand or CoW, success equals death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, as I thought. Much appreciated. Do you think Prime 5 could provide more effective protection against making and unmaking? Increase withstand against such practices maybe? Like a kind of extended duration unmake spell, er, spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:32:11-07:00","id":1065787,"title":"","content":"Prime Armor would protect against all damage spells regardless of Practice. A damaging Weaving or Perfecting spell would be countered just as much as a Fraying spell just as long as the spell deals damage. It would not protect against Unmaking because Unmaking doesn't deal damage. It succeeds or it does not succeed at unmaking something.<br /> <br /> Edit: Bluuuh. I tend to open up several tabs and read them in order. That's why I miss replies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:00:52-07:00","id":1065810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1065785#post1065785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, as I thought. Much appreciated. Do you think Prime 5 could provide more effective protection against making and unmaking? Increase withstand against such practices maybe? Like a kind of extended duration unmake spell, er, spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wards and Signs already increases Withstand, it's Shielding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:21:31-07:00","id":1065939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1064747#post1064747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically yes, but I'd be very interested in how the spirit or Goetia got that Influence in the first place.<br /> <br /> And by interested I mean, &quot;How the hell are you justifying it within the narrative?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>An Adept Re-Weaving an existing Spirit, or a Master Making one whole cloth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:21:18-07:00","id":1066025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1065939#post1065939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Adept Re-Weaving an existing Spirit, or a Master Making one whole cloth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it, Spirit mages can already cast Shape Spirit (Spirit 4).<br /> <br /> This is why the Uratha get antsy when they hear about Spirit mages. Even when you think you know all about them, they still manage to catch you off guard, and the next second they're wrecking the Shadow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:31:29-07:00","id":1066028,"title":"","content":"It's weird to think about a mage being able to create a being with intrinsic powers that the mage could not grant to himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:44:23-07:00","id":1066034,"title":"","content":"Combined Spell question:<br /> Devouring The Slain SET TO HEALTH SCOURING plus Rotting Flesh equals no no?<br /> Devouring The Slain SET TO WILLPOWER DRAIN plus Rotting Flesh equals yes yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T18:17:37-07:00","id":1066081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066034#post1066034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combined Spell question:<br /> Devouring The Slain SET TO HEALTH SCOURING plus Rotting Flesh equals no no?<br /> Devouring The Slain SET TO WILLPOWER DRAIN plus Rotting Flesh equals yes yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of? <br /> <br /> My rationale:<br /> No matter the fluff saying how the damage is done, Devouring The Slain does deal damage directly, which doesn't combine-stack with other damage. Apply highest damage and resolve the rest of the effects normally. It's ... not a no no, in that you can cast it, it's just not useful for damage, but you do get the mana and deal damage and, if Reach used for Rotting Flesh, apply penalty to Social rolls equal to Potency for the Duration of the combined spell (which, I don't know, a round? a scene if you're into overReaching? seems like a Potency-heavy combo) <br /> <br /> The Willpower version has no overlap, rott'n'drain away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T18:44:11-07:00","id":1066087,"title":"","content":"That's my train of logic, yeah.<br /> <br /> Another Shifting Sands question:<br /> <br /> I cast a spell preventing someone from dying [let's say from bleeding, it's not that important]. That spell is only thing keeping them alive. Or they are one turn away from bleeding out.<br /> I cast Shifting Sands on them, sending them back X time. My spell gets canceled due to Shifting Sands rules. Or they bleed out in the past, doesn't matter. What's important, they die in the past.<br /> ...what's now?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And a variant:<br /> I cast Shifting Sands combined with Weight of Years. It's damaging enough to kill the subject, and it has enough Reach to send it, dunno, few hours back in time. Do I kill them in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T20:45:04-07:00","id":1066109,"title":"","content":"Actually, it someone inhabits their past self, you could just target theur corpse after its died and send it back in time. It now occupies the same space as the alive person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T21:17:39-07:00","id":1066116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066087#post1066087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my train of logic, yeah.<br /> <br /> Another Shifting Sands question:<br /> <br /> I cast a spell preventing someone from dying [let's say from bleeding, it's not that important]. That spell is only thing keeping them alive. Or they are one turn away from bleeding out.<br /> I cast Shifting Sands on them, sending them back X time. My spell gets canceled due to Shifting Sands rules. Or they bleed out in the past, doesn't matter. What's important, they die in the past.<br /> ...what's now?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And a variant:<br /> I cast Shifting Sands combined with Weight of Years. It's damaging enough to kill the subject, and it has enough Reach to send it, dunno, few hours back in time. Do I kill them in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they die in the past they stay dead and the timeline accepts it as a Lasting change when the corpse catches up to the present. So the same as if you sent yourself back and died.<br /> <br /> Not sure about Weight of Years, the principle of a spell not being able to exist before it existed might still apply. I think I'd prefer to rule it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T00:01:41-07:00","id":1066153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066087#post1066087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cast Shifting Sands on them, sending them back X time. My spell gets canceled due to Shifting Sands rules. Or they bleed out in the past, doesn't matter. What's important, they die in the past.<br /> ...what's now?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And a variant:<br /> I cast Shifting Sands combined with Weight of Years. It's damaging enough to kill the subject, and it has enough Reach to send it, dunno, few hours back in time. Do I kill them in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>ooh Time shenanigans!<br /> <br /> I don't think the variant changes anything. Except maybe making the caster think themselves clever - &quot;ooh I damage you by blasting your body forward, then I send you back, haha&quot;<br /> <br /> Here we come to the point of &quot;Aeryes reads spells in a certain way&quot; again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Unlike some other spells (like Rewrite History) I would say Shifting sands is an instantaneous one, more like the mentioned Weight of Years in that you just affect the target, the effect is instantaneous and that's all the spell does: the target is shunted back and the rules of Time apply from then onward. By this I mean to imply the spell is effectively without Duration and cannot thus be cancelled, like damage. (the proof is in trying the opposite: A casts spell on B, B goes backwards and the spell is immediately cancelled because B was not the caster) <br /> <br /> Unless you also protect yourself from Time shenanigans, at this point the effect becomes &quot;The person died in the past and the Storyteller decides how far back the narrative has to go to account for this.&quot;<br /> If you do protect yourself from Time alterations, you stay with your current knowledge and location, while everyone else percieves it as though you suddenly teleported (unless Plot Power demands that you would be in the same place anyway), and are clueless as to &quot;current&quot; circumstances that differ from your unaltered timeline. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066116#post1066116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about Weight of Years, the principle of a spell not being able to exist before it existed might still apply. I think I'd prefer to rule it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Weight of Years is &quot;I damage you using Time!&quot; and it happens the instant the combinedSpell(it's a single spell with 2 effects now) hits, I'd rule that the damage does get done, and, like other damage, is kept in the journey backwards.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just for personal amusement, alternative ruling to this combination spell would be that you temporally rip apart the target by sending them forwards and backwards in time simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T00:11:05-07:00","id":1066160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066153#post1066153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Weight of Years is &quot;I damage you using Time!&quot; and it happens the instant the combinedSpell(it's a single spell with 2 effects now) hits, I'd rule that the damage does get done, and, like other damage, is kept in the journey backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't had the chance to reference the spell when I responded. I thought it might be a sustained aging spell like the Life one. I agree, the effects would occur simultaneously and the subject would be damaged and shunted back in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:03:06-07:00","id":1066349,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'll get more luck posting here. How does Sleepwalkers holding spells for multiple Mages work?<br /> <br /> 1) Is it max two spells from any combination of Mages?<br /> 2) Is there one &quot;Medium+&quot; slot and one &quot;Strong+&quot; slot.<br /> 3) Can each Mage have a Sleepwalker hold spells for them, regardless of other Mages?<br /> 4) Something else?<br /> <br /> I.e. Lets say there are three Mages conveniently named A, B and C. A and B have a Medium connection to the sleepwalmer. C has a strong connection. The Sleepwalker holds a spell for A.<br /> <br /> Can B have the Sleepwalker hold a spell?<br /> <br /> Can C have the Sleepwalker hold a spell? If yes, how many?<br /> <br /> If the Sleepwalker can and does hold a spell for B as well, can C have the Sleepwalker hold a spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:09:04-07:00","id":1066353,"title":"","content":"I...intuitively assumed that &quot;corpse&quot; and &quot;a living person&quot; are symbolically distinct enough that it wouldn't replace the living person that was a source for the corpse. I honestly don't know how to resolve this idea [as you probably can see, my example questions tried really hard to make sure that subject reaches the past alive and dies there], because this immediately makes me ask: if I have a table made out of many trees, which one do I replace when I send it back enough &quot;from before&quot; it was made? <br /> <br /> I think for our groups sanity we will assume that there are certain &quot;points of no return&quot; for purpose of this continuity, simply to avoid problems like these, and add some restrictions to time travle, but...uhhhh...I have no idea what should be &quot;canon default&quot; resolution for the corpse / table shifting. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:19:21-07:00","id":1066363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066349#post1066349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'll get more luck posting here. How does Sleepwalkers holding spells for multiple Mages work?<br /> <br /> 1) Is it max two spells from any combination of Mages?<br /> 2) Is there one &quot;Medium+&quot; slot and one &quot;Strong+&quot; slot.<br /> 3) Can each Mage have a Sleepwalker hold spells for them, regardless of other Mages?<br /> 4) Something else?<br /> <br /> I.e. Lets say there are three Mages conveniently named A, B and C. A and B have a Medium connection to the sleepwalmer. C has a strong connection. The Sleepwalker holds a spell for A.<br /> <br /> Can B have the Sleepwalker hold a spell?<br /> <br /> Can C have the Sleepwalker hold a spell? If yes, how many?<br /> <br /> If the Sleepwalker can and does hold a spell for B as well, can C have the Sleepwalker hold a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are two interpretations. <br /> First is that Sleepwalkers hold spells on sympathetic bonds. So A and B can have each one spell; C can have 2 of them. <br /> Second is that Sleepwalkers have slots So if A has taken the 'medium' B is shit out of luck. C still can use the 'strong' one.<br /> And as far as I know those are interpretations and theres nothing official to back it up. It's up to a ST. For example I went with the first one because of a player Proximi that I wanted to empower in the cabal of normal mages. She became a fierce warrior with all those spells hanging on her. Sort of a bodyguard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:31:10-07:00","id":1066373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066353#post1066353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I...intuitively assumed that &quot;corpse&quot; and &quot;a living person&quot; are symbolically distinct enough that it wouldn't replace the living person that was a source for the corpse. I honestly don't know how to resolve this idea [as you probably can see, my example questions tried really hard to make sure that subject reaches the past alive and dies there], because this immediately makes me ask: if I have a table made out of many trees, which one do I replace when I send it back enough &quot;from before&quot; it was made?<br /> <br /> I think for our groups sanity we will assume that there are certain &quot;points of no return&quot; for purpose of this continuity, simply to avoid problems like these, and add some restrictions to time travle, but...uhhhh...I have no idea what should be &quot;canon default&quot; resolution for the corpse / table shifting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know what is canon default for this but, damn... this would be hell of a good Mystery. &quot;Your mage sights are tingling. Instinctively you start looking around. Twig, sentinel that came to talk with you about the thing and now stood behind you looks like a victim of a terrible car crash. Blood all over him, left arm is missing, multiple wounds. He falls down. Most likely dead before collapsing.&quot;<br /> Extra points if you prepared a note for your acanthus that explains everything that happened in alternative timeline one week from now. And be sure that he can't tell anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-22-2017, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:42:01-07:00","id":1066386,"title":"","content":"When using Wards and Signs at Advanced Potency, does the +2 Withstand also apply against the spells W&amp;S protects you from, or is it <i>only</i> for dispellation purposes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:57:12-07:00","id":1066404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066386#post1066386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Wards and Signs at Advanced Potency, does the +2 Withstand also apply against the spells W&amp;S protects you from, or is it <i>only</i> for dispellation purposes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It only applies against dispellation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:41:52-07:00","id":1066447,"title":"","content":"Does a sleeper with no soul suffer Quiescence or cause Dissonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:00:34-07:00","id":1066462,"title":"","content":"How specific are Artifacts' effects supposed to be? Are all Potency/Reach spent when the Artifact is used, or when it is created? Let's say with Honing the Form as an example; when is the decision made to bump a specific attribute? <br /> <br /> And if all of the Reach are spent during creation and not casting, does that mean that a hypothetical Artifact that grants +3 Strength will lose some of its effectiveness when someone with Strength 3+ uses it, unless there is perpetually one Reach spent on exceeding natural maximums?<br /> <br /> In a similar vein, do all Artifacts follow the same rules for casting time as spellcasting, needing to spend 1 Reach to work instantly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:17:15-07:00","id":1066479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066447#post1066447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a sleeper with no soul suffer Quiescence or cause Dissonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's ever said, but I would personally rule that yes, they do still cause Dissonance/Quiescence. In fact, I'd probably say that without a soul in place, all they have is that unfiltered abyssal shard left in its place and their affect on Paradox and other Abyssal forces would be enhanced. But to be fair I'm a bit of a dick at times so that probably isn't how most people would handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T18:23:48-07:00","id":1066652,"title":"","content":"Could you use a Ruling Practice of Death to manipulate the cold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T19:52:57-07:00","id":1066680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066652#post1066652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use a Ruling Practice of Death to manipulate the cold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Judging by the existence of Cold Snap, probably. Just keep in mind that it's not <i>ice</i> manipulation (as that would be Matter), but rather &quot;absence of heat&quot; manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T19:59:34-07:00","id":1066682,"title":"","content":"Though Cold Snap does create ice, so creating ice through the cold of Death is a possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T22:20:02-07:00","id":1066707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066652#post1066652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use a Ruling Practice of Death to manipulate the cold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. &quot;Cold&quot; is one of the explicitly listed purviews of the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> So you could do it as directly manipulating cold (which is symbolically different from temperature, not using Forces here), as causing an absence of heat, as moving closer to an ending of something.<br /> <br /> So, copy the Control Heat spell into Control Cold for Death, make it work only to make things colder (or, you know, be high-concept and remove cold to add heat, whatevs, &quot;lifting the icy grasp of death&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T03:21:20-07:00","id":1066760,"title":"","content":"If two people swapped souls what would the do, Just what transfers from one body to the other when this swap occurs. Is the soul the center of the magical self? The last condition in the souless chain, Thrall, states that when a mage reaches this level of souless that they lose that ability to use will or cast magic. Is that because they can no longer exert there will on the world or is it because their soul controls their magic. For instance if you yank the soul of a mage out of his body and replace that soul with that of a sleeper, just what happens?<br /> <br /> My personal thought is that nothing would happen on a physical or magical level, only on a metaphysical level. The mage would continue to be able to cast spells and use/regain wisdom. Gnosis and willpower control spellcasting. What I personally feel would happen is the swapping of inner traits, like vices and virtues would swap, your inner voice (Conscience), the sense of right and wrong (Morals), those intangible traits of the human soul. I feel that is all that would transfer.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T03:55:14-07:00","id":1066767,"title":"","content":"From what I've gathered the soul will adapt to fit the new person. For example, legacies shapes the soul, but if you replace your soul with someone without or with a different legacy the soul would transform to fit you and you'd still belong to the same legacy.<br /> Vices and Virtues are affected by soul loss, but since you do retain them (at least the Vice) after losing your soul it makes me think it's a part of your mind a lot more than it's part of your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:06:41-07:00","id":1066780,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Legacies don't so much shape your soul as they shape your soul-socket. The soul itself is more of a battery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:35:40-07:00","id":1066796,"title":"","content":"I would say that just like Shadows are &quot;corpses&quot; of Light, Ice is &quot;corpse&quot; of Water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:30:52-07:00","id":1067232,"title":"","content":"Souls are fungible commodities, with these exceptions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Using them to learn legacies via Soul Study</li> <li>Soul stone sympathetic connection</li> </ol>For all other purposes, one soul cannot be differentiated from another. If a mage loses her soul, she can replace it with any other soul and there's no intrinsic consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:40:22-07:00","id":1067235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1066780#post1066780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your soul-socket.</div> </div> </div> </div>There needs to be a better term for this. It's not even a mage-only phenomenon. \u0100tman, maybe? I mean in the Buddhist sense but it does refer to the soul in Hindu and Jainism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:33:55-07:00","id":1067254,"title":"","content":"The way I picture soul stones working is that basically a soul is like clay. It moulds itself to the container but it will keep it's shape if you take it out until you put it in another one. <br /> <br /> Creating a soul stone basically snips a bit off and bakes it, so it stays in a shape that signifies you and your Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:41:04-07:00","id":1067262,"title":"","content":"That's a damn good explanation.<br /> <br /> But there's something I'm wondering about<b></b>: How does soul stones work when their owner is suffering from soul loss?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what happens to the Oneiros during soul loss? I don't remember if the book said anything about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:03:43-07:00","id":1067272,"title":"","content":"Since 1 soul stone = 1 point of gnosis, it could be argued that a mage whose soul has been taken could reabsorb a soul stone in order to function as a mage who has made nine soul stones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:33:31-07:00","id":1067284,"title":"","content":"Soul Stones really to me don't seem like they're made of Soul at all.<br /> They decrease Gnosis potential, and you can't stick a bunch of them together to make a new soul.<br /> <br /> Instead they're Gnosis-fragments.<br /> Bits of your soul-container that you haven't figured out how to use yet to better channel your soul's power, so you break them off for other powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:48:44-07:00","id":1067293,"title":"","content":"I feel that a Soul Stone, even though implicates a piece of the soul, is not actually part of a Soul and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> is pointing out it is a piece of Gnosis. As a piece of Gnosis can it be used to awaken someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:06:11-07:00","id":1067302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1067293#post1067293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a piece of Gnosis can it be used to awaken someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, unless it's serving as Quintessence in an Archmage spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:12:32-07:00","id":1067375,"title":"","content":"In 2e, the definition of a soul shrunk a bit and refers to a certain ineffable spark that is common to all ensouled beings. The soulstone, on the other hand, is clearly connected more to other anima concepts (yeah: gnosis is more related); while the name <i>is </i>fitting, it's also going to be a bit confusing because Awakening 2's &quot;soul&quot; isn't everything about a person that people consider to be &quot;soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> The ways of dealing with the discrepancy that I consider are: 1. Consider that magi have come up with a more specific technical term of art. 2. Treat the term &quot;soul&quot; as a sloppy one, and multiple senses rule the day. If I ever get to run a game, I'll probably use some of each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:56:39-07:00","id":1067801,"title":"","content":"If you have sympathy to them somehow, can you use Space alone to teleport or colocate to other realms? (I.e the shadow, etc) Or do you need another Arcana to create a portal first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:36:03-07:00","id":1067859,"title":"","content":"When you go back using Shifting Sands, &quot;current&quot; Initiative shift to the subjects, and if it's the caster, then he doesn't get &quot;another&quot; turn to play with because it's technically continuation of the turn where he cast the spell and thus his instant action is already used up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T18:21:35-07:00","id":1067876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1067801#post1067801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have sympathy to them somehow, can you use Space alone to teleport or colocate to other realms? (I.e the shadow, etc) Or do you need another Arcana to create a portal first?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to say yes-Arcana, no-portal \u2014 the non-Space component is there to handle the necessary metaphysical translation for shifting to another realm, which doesn't necessitate a separate changeover point but does mean you need more than just three dots in an Arcanum and a guy who knows a guy to be able to jump the Gauntlet or break a ghost out of a Deep Dominion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:55:34-07:00","id":1067913,"title":"","content":"It's mentioned that Artifacts can cast spells by themselves, without the assistance of a Mage.<br /> Does that mean that an Artifact has its own spell control?<br /> <br /> For example, I want my next character to have an Artifact called the Reliquary of Animation, which animates Golems, and potentially binds Ghosts into them, as well as related powers.<br /> If for example, its Golemn animating ability functions if left &quot;inside&quot; the Golem for long enough (such as a carved mouth, eye socket, or simple socket designed for that purpose, for one hour given ritual speed and Gnosis 3) and it uses its ability independently, does that mean that (assuming 6 dots and Gnosis 3) it can maintain only 3 Golems at a time due to spell control?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:08:37-07:00","id":1067929,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at the spell Perfect Sympathy, the reach option that begins &quot;The subject\u2019s sympathetic connection is so great that it can fool even magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Could I design a spell with conjunctional Space 3 and +1 reach that can manage a sympathetic range &quot;bank shot&quot;?<br /> <br /> For example, suppose I'm in possession of Mage A's soul stone (sympathy yantra). Mage A is strongly connected to his legacy mentor Mage B. Could I improvise a sympathetic range spell with Fate 2, Space 3, +1 reach to bank a hex off Mage A to affect Mage B as the spell's subject?<br /> <br /> If not, is there any other way to manage a sympathetic range bank shot that doesn't involve changing the sympathetic connections in play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:14:45-07:00","id":1067931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1067801#post1067801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have sympathy to them somehow, can you use Space alone to teleport or colocate to other realms? (I.e the shadow, etc) Or do you need another Arcana to create a portal first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its odd that the Teleport spell specifically mentions needing Death or Spirit 2 to get to other realms, yet co-locate and even scry has no mention of it. Personally im going with if you want to view/get to/contact another realm of existance you need to add Death or Spirit to any space spell. (Mind to teleport directly into the Astral???)<br /> <br /> Not sure how this applies to twilight as its not another realm..not quite sure how i feel about just space being able to scry folk in twilight. Somebody asked earlier if its possible and my first instinct was to say no but somebody else replied yes. I think it'd be possible but you'll only see the location the twilight thing is in and would need some other way to actually &quot;perceive&quot; the thing in twilight (like death/spirit sight or a spell or something), (like scrying an invis person)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-25-2017, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:25:13-07:00","id":1067933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1067929#post1067929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, is there any other way to manage a sympathetic range bank shot that doesn't involve changing the sympathetic connections in play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with that qualifier, no. Perfect Sympathy's Reach effect works because you're shuffling an effect targeting the subject to instead target someone the spell enhances the subject's relation to, and there wouldn't be much point to doing so anyway since at three dots you have the ability to both duplicate and strengthen sympathies.<br /> <br /> That being said, Correspondence and Borrow Threads are both valid spells for use with Sympathetic Range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T02:23:01-07:00","id":1067952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1067801#post1067801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have sympathy to them somehow, can you use Space alone to teleport or colocate to other realms? (I.e the shadow, etc) Or do you need another Arcana to create a portal first?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can. Kind of. Its the same principle as in &quot;every mind is a mind and you don't need Spirit to affect spirits mind&quot;.<br /> So when you superimpose material and shadow with co-location you can do it just fine but since you can't see ephemera the other place will be 'empty' for you. And now I tell you why.<br /> It works on the same principle as Loci. It doesn't have a power of translating you inteligently back and fourth when you cross it. It's just an absence of Gountlet and translation is a feature of reality. In the shadow theres only Spirit ephemera so you must adapt and translate. On the other hand when spirits cross to our side they are welcomed by our multitude of Twilights and don't have to translate. <br /> So if you wan't to you can add Gauntlet strength as a withstand to this spell but it's up to you.<br /> Now to the &quot;but teleportation requires 2 dots of the other arcanum&quot; part. Teleportation needs to rewrite your pattern and do all the heavy lifting. It's fast but more complex and must do the work entirely by itself, thus conjunctionals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:31:00-07:00","id":1067973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1067929#post1067929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking at the spell Perfect Sympathy, the reach option that begins &amp;quot;The subject\u2019s sympathetic connection is so great that it can fool even magic.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Could I design a spell with conjunctional Space 3 and +1 reach that can manage a sympathetic range &amp;quot;bank shot&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> For example, suppose I'm in possession of Mage A's soul stone (sympathy yantra). Mage A is strongly connected to his legacy mentor Mage B. Could I improvise a sympathetic range spell with Fate 2, Space 3, +1 reach to bank a hex off Mage A to affect Mage B as the spell's subject?<br /> <br /> If not, is there any other way to manage a sympathetic range bank shot that doesn't involve changing the sympathetic connections in play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like the answer is yes, what's unclear is if the Mage gets to choose the connection the spell redirects too, but I'd assume yes if they know it ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T22:40:05-07:00","id":1068188,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this has been asked a hundred times, and I think I even saw the answer to this question before (but I forgot it), but would anyone be kind enough to tell me what the automatic successes thing is all about on Legacies?<br /> <br /> &quot;If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes,<br /> it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the<br /> mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.&quot;<br /> <br /> As long as the game has been out I still haven't gotten into a session yet where anyone's used an attainment. I presume these successes are used for the sake of, say, another gameline where another power needs to know how many successes the Mage rolled.<br /> But I just wanted to make sure--is this refering to a clash of wills, as in, the Mage gets Primary Arcanum dots in successes in a clash of wills? I'm guessing no.<br /> And the other very important question that I got was <i>does this or can this count as an exceptional success.</i> Because that would be horrifying!<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question 1st Attainment is what got me thinking about this, because of this part here.<br /> <br /> &quot;Optional: Matter 1<br /> The Querent also may engage Active Mage Sight (Matter)<br /> upon arrival. If it must pierce any form of supernatural concealment,<br /> it automatically scores successes equal to the mage\u2019s<br /> Matter dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this is from the legacy section proper, instructions bits.<br /> <br /> &quot;For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who<br /> possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency<br /> automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as<br /> per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone who has the answer, oh thank you thank you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T03:54:43-07:00","id":1068231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1068188#post1068188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this has been asked a hundred times, and I think I even saw the answer to this question before (but I forgot it), but would anyone be kind enough to tell me what the automatic successes thing is all about on Legacies?<br /> <br /> &quot;If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes,<br /> it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the<br /> mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.&quot;<br /> <br /> As long as the game has been out I still haven't gotten into a session yet where anyone's used an attainment. I presume these successes are used for the sake of, say, another gameline where another power needs to know how many successes the Mage rolled.<br /> But I just wanted to make sure--is this refering to a clash of wills, as in, the Mage gets Primary Arcanum dots in successes in a clash of wills? I'm guessing no.<br /> And the other very important question that I got was <i>does this or can this count as an exceptional success.</i> Because that would be horrifying!<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question 1st Attainment is what got me thinking about this, because of this part here.<br /> <br /> &quot;Optional: Matter 1<br /> The Querent also may engage Active Mage Sight (Matter)<br /> upon arrival. If it must pierce any form of supernatural concealment,<br /> it automatically scores successes equal to the mage\u2019s<br /> Matter dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this is from the legacy section proper, instructions bits.<br /> <br /> &quot;For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who<br /> possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency<br /> automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as<br /> per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone who has the answer, oh thank you thank you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If the attainment allowed for a contested roll then you would need to know how many successes were rolled, like Clash of wills, The answer to the second question is no, not a exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-26-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:03:44-07:00","id":1068267,"title":"","content":"Hmm. If it works for Clash of Wills, then Attainments have a really good niche. One autosuccess per highest Arcanum is better than most of Clash of Will dicepools, assuming ratio of one success average per 3 dice. Arcanum 3 Clash of Will attainment is better than 9 dice pool Clash of Will due to it's reliability. I wonder when it's mathematically better to go for CoW Attainments, and when it's better to rely on classic spell CoW...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:11:05-07:00","id":1068270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1068267#post1068267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder when it's mathematically better to go for CoW Attainments, and when it's better to rely on classic spell CoW...</div> </div> </div> </div>When you want more spell factors or Reach options.<br /> <br /> A Shielding spell on yourself could render you virtually invulnerable to supernatural attacks from a particular arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:21:02-07:00","id":1068271,"title":"","content":"I am by no means an expert at this game and the Clash of Will could be wrong, Were a measure of success would come is is if the attainment was built of a spell like Gravitic Supremacy (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022) it will increase jumping distance <b>per success rolled</b> by the spell\u2019s Potency. So instead of the <b>per success rolled</b> that would be replaced by <b>per dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T07:49:42-07:00","id":1068289,"title":"","content":"Except the successes rolled in the spell refers to a mundane roll and the attainment grants a number of successes on the Gnosis+Arcanum roll that would've been if the attainment was cast as a spell.<br /> <br /> I personally think that the successes gained has no functional purpose in just Mage as of now, but is a way to keep their backs clear should a future supplement or another gameline contain a power that somehow modifies the result of supernatural power activation rolls. For example a potential Endowment from Hunter 2E that reduces the amount of successes rolled on supernatural power activation rolls. That would then affect attainments because attainments do have a degree of success despite having no roll.<br /> As far as I know no such powers currently exists, but there's a few gamelines I don't know much about ruleswise, and there's several corebooks (both new editions and a new gameline) in the works that may introduce such things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:23:25-07:00","id":1068300,"title":"","content":"Could be just that simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:39:03-07:00","id":1068308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1068270#post1068270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you want more spell factors or Reach options.<br /> <br /> A Shielding spell on yourself could render you virtually invulnerable to supernatural attacks from a particular arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. I wonder how CoW Attainment Shield and CoW Spell Shields interact. Attainments and Spells should stack, but how do you stack a CoW? My intuitive solution is just roll CoW twice, once for each shield. This would allow for some incredible burst shields when you know that there is big spell coming in 2 rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:55:13-07:00","id":1068314,"title":"","content":"Rolling twice makes sense, but in a game where multiple CoW shields are somewhat common you might want to use the highest and add a bonus based on the other one, somewhat like Withstand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T09:30:40-07:00","id":1068327,"title":"","content":"Or I could just make it so you roll it once, but CoW Attainment + CoW Shield also has automatic successes equal to the Arcanum. It's incredibly mindboggingly strong, but it would require transient stacking, so you need to specifically prepare for it and make it happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T21:47:06-07:00","id":1068547,"title":"","content":"Would it possible to obtain a sympathetic connection to another planet by communing with it in the Sidereal Wastes, so as to Teleport to it? It would be pretty cool to have a moon of Jupiter or an exotic exoplanet as a setting.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the affect of Velocity Control is Lasting, you can eventually get close to lightspeed in space where you're traveling almost without friction. Could have a Spelljammer campaign Mage 2E style.<br /> <br /> I get why this isn't explored in the game setting, but is it possible? IIRC in Ascension Awakened magic only worked within the boundary of the orbit of the moon. I don't remember reading any such limitation in Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T00:33:40-07:00","id":1068573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1068547#post1068547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it possible to obtain a sympathetic connection to another planet by communing with it in the Sidereal Wastes, so as to Teleport to it? It would be pretty cool to have a moon of Jupiter or an exotic exoplanet as a setting.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the affect of Velocity Control is Lasting, you can eventually get close to lightspeed in space where you're traveling almost without friction. Could have a Spelljammer campaign Mage 2E style.<br /> <br /> I get why this isn't explored in the game setting, but is it possible? IIRC in Ascension Awakened magic only worked within the boundary of the orbit of the moon. I don't remember reading any such limitation in Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has been mentioned by DaveB that 1st editions limit of lunar orbit of spells (or around that range) is no longer the case so if you can somehow get a connection to a planet then you can teleport there, i wouldnt allow a connection by communing with it in the sidereal wastes tho. You'd need something physically from it and then borrow its sympathy.<br /> <br /> 1st Editions Astral book actually discussed getting sympathy with mars from spending time in a realistic astral version of mars but its sympathy rules were different obviously. 2nd edition might allow that as its Yantra, but id still say you need a physical real actual link.<br /> <br /> I think it really comes down to what sort of Mage game your wanting, i can see myself allowing it for some campaigns and not for others depending on the story im trying to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-27-2017, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T00:44:38-07:00","id":1068575,"title":"","content":"On that note, if anyone wants an idea for why you won't run into aliens in World of Darkness, might I suggest that the God Machine or the Exarchs limited intelligent life in the universe to just Earth, so the only extra-terrestrials you will meet <i>are</i> from the Sidereal Wastes, but otherwise everything is dead or kept primitive by the influence of the numerous Exarchs<br /> <br /> Probably not a popular idea but I currently think of Idigam as castaways from other planets after the Fall.<br /> <br /> But I always liked the idea of going to the Sidereal Wastes and seeing the Animal Masters of other planets...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T04:02:35-07:00","id":1068602,"title":"","content":"It's quite possible to explore other planets, but it requires some planning and a cabal that has the right Arcana. Forces and Matter seems to be the most important since they can protect against vacuum, grant local gravity, recycle air, keep a space vessel together, etc. Life might also be good to not starve. Space can get you to some bodies in the solar system, but that's kinda it for Space. Spirit is a must, though, if you plan on visiting the Moon in a game where WtF is used. The idigam should be pretty keen on tagging along when you leave, and probably won't take no for an answer when it comes to escaping their prison.<br /> <br /> There are at least two mentions of aliens, as in beings that are not originally from Earth (or other realms of existence).<br /> First of all we've got the Visitors from Dark Eras Companion. They're the classic brain parasite puppeteers from the movies. They have the line &quot;Very few Visitors exist on Earth, yet for some reason, they choose this era to dispatch a reconnaissance mission.&quot; in their part of the text box. It's not explicitly said they're from space, but they are obviously designed to invoke that feeling.<br /> Then we got the &quot;alien spirits&quot; that the Moon-Banished idigam can call down from &quot;the void and the stars beyond Luna's boundary&quot;. However, they take just a week to arrive and does so on meteors and other physical objects. Unless they're capable of accelerating physical mass to several times the speed of light they wouldn't be able to originate from outside the Oort Cloud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T05:48:00-07:00","id":1068625,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear that there isn't a rule I missed that outright eliminates outer space and interstellar settings. &quot;Seer's secret moon base&quot; and &quot;Moros archmage's safehouse on the moon Charon&quot; are pretty neat locations to spend a chapter or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:06:22-07:00","id":1068632,"title":"","content":"But since it's only possible to get sympathetic connections to bodies that have samples here on Earth you'd have to physically travel to those bodies instead of just teleporting. And even when it comes to the Moon and Mars you'd have to find the samples first before you can teleport or co-locate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:26:15-07:00","id":1068637,"title":"","content":"Don't need sympathetic connections for a couple of the planets in our solar system, just a decent telescope(or an electric one for more reach for the not close ones). <br /> It looks like they removed the limit on sensory being 200. If you can see it you can target it. Just steal something link that's already there. Then take a picture of said object. You got both the link and the yantra right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:34:20-07:00","id":1068640,"title":"","content":"Or just teleport via Remote casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:41:24-07:00","id":1068643,"title":"","content":"Depends on how the ST rules it. For a very broad definition of sensory range you'd be able to travel to other stars. But if you limit how clearly you have to see a subject to be able to cast on it, and how long time delay a &quot;live&quot; feed can have before it acts like a recording rather than remote viewing, then even getting to the moon might be a challenge.<br /> For example, you might be able to target the moon via sensory range, but then you'd have to account for its Size, which is probably a lot higher than any mage can target. But if you want to target an area on the moon instead I'd say you'd have to be able to visually distinguish that area, which, depending on the size of the area, could require a telescope more powerful than the Gran Telescopio Canarias. And even for a mage it would be difficult at best to borrow such telescopes. And I'm not sure if you can get a live feed from those anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:18:34-07:00","id":1068682,"title":"","content":"&quot;For ease of space travel we recommend hiring a certified Beamer. Our guides are proficient in Space, Time and Forces Arcana that shorten voyages tremendously.&quot;<br /> Forces and Space should be able tweak cheapest of telescope into interstellar beast. Add a sprinkle of Time to get rid of relativity. Alohamora. You are there with a remote Co-location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:42:26-07:00","id":1069382,"title":"","content":"Teamwork Spellcasting Rolls.<br /> <br /> Can I use them with instant spell rolls? Or just with Ritual Spellcasting?<br /> I don't see anything that specifically calls for Ritual Spellcasting only, so I just want to be sure about this.<br /> <br /> Cause Egregore will be way more powerfull with this.<br /> <br /> <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T09:06:28-07:00","id":1069396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1069382#post1069382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Teamwork Spellcasting Rolls.<br /> <br /> Can I use them with instant spell rolls? Or just with Ritual Spellcasting?<br /> I don't see anything that specifically calls for Ritual Spellcasting only, so I just want to be sure about this.<br /> <br /> Cause Egregore will be way more powerfull with this.<br /> <br /> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>Page 114, &quot;Casting Time,&quot; last line of Paragraph 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:43:17-07:00","id":1069671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068319-mtaw-1st-edition-sensory-range-sensory-magic-and-the-200-yard-rule?p=1069359#post1069359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is addressed by RAW. Note that most of the spells that reveal in-area out-of-senses information <b>are</b> Knowing spells (such as Sense Life or Sense Consciousness) which <i>specifically</i> <i>do not</i> impart Sensory information:<br /> <br /> <i>An important detail to note is that <b>Knowing magics specifically</b> <b>do not bestow sensory information</b> upon the mage. The Practice of Knowing deals in facts, not the senses.</i><br /> -- Tome of the Mysteries, p.19<br /> <br /> Using the rule of thumb that Sensory Range can only be extended via Unveiling should address most situations. Hope that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this still relevant for 2nd ED rules? Are senses bestowed using magic good enough to target something, or are they actually worse than TV Screen? I don't actually mind either answer (they just change the emergent gameplay in different ways), but I want to know for future relevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:17:35-07:00","id":1069694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1069671#post1069671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this still relevant for 2nd ED rules? Are senses bestowed using magic good enough to target something, or are they actually worse than TV Screen? I don't actually mind either answer (they just change the emergent gameplay in different ways), but I want to know for future relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, if you can sense it you can cast on it, but your ability to do so is limited by the sensory information available. You may sense a mind with Mind, but that isn't enough information for warping their face with Life for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:34:11-07:00","id":1069707,"title":"","content":"Imagine my opponent shrouded me with Eternal Darkness of Seven Midnights (i.e. they killed all the light so I can't see them), and I use my Force Magic to perceive by attuning myself to gain &quot;Gravity Sense&quot;. Can I target them, and if yes then with what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:10:36-07:00","id":1069724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1069707#post1069707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine my opponent shrouded me with Eternal Darkness of Seven Midnights (i.e. they killed all the light so I can't see them), and I use my Force Magic to perceive by attuning myself to gain &quot;Gravity Sense&quot;. Can I target them, and if yes then with what?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be some highly tuned gravity sense, but if that's the case and you have no other arcana with which to sense them, then I imagine, you'd only be able to target them with Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:22:27-07:00","id":1069730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1069671#post1069671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this still relevant for 2nd ED rules? Are senses bestowed using magic good enough to target something, or are they actually worse than TV Screen? I don't actually mind either answer (they just change the emergent gameplay in different ways), but I want to know for future relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;[...]sensory, meaning that the mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject.&quot;</i> -- 2E, p.114<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Unveiling spells expose hidden things <b>to the mage\u2019s senses</b>.&quot;</i> -- 2E, p.123<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Knowing spells deliver <b>knowledge </b>about something directly to the mage (or to another target).&quot;</i> -- 2E, p.123<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure if you were posing the question to me or just quoting me. 2E isn't my wheelhouse since I found the system a bit too clunky/unwieldy and so I'm not as familiar with it nor do I own all the books. You'll notice a lot of what I originally cited came from Tome of the Mysteries which clarified a lot of 1E core. All I could find were these bits which suggest a similar relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 03-28-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:24:04-07:00","id":1069762,"title":"","content":"For a kind of Sleeping Beauty spell. I want to put my target to Sleep with a Hex or another Fate magic. Is this possible?<br /> If so, it's just Exceptional Luck(Hex version) plus Fate 2dot Attainment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:10:29-07:00","id":1069775,"title":"","content":"That is what I would place it as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:56:14-07:00","id":1070066,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any decent guidelines for the availability ratings of stuff you can requisition via Order Status?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:10:42-07:00","id":1070076,"title":"","content":"Maybe use guidelines from Resources merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:15:22-07:00","id":1070079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070076#post1070076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe use guidelines from Resources merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't because there isn't a direct correlation. It's essentially eyeball work so I'm curious if anyone has put in the effort before I try to tackyit myself.<br /> <br /> If it were that simple and obvious then I wouldn't be asking the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:24:58-07:00","id":1070096,"title":"","content":"I think there is. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character\u2019s position affords her certain access to her Caucus<br /> or Consilium\u2019s stores. She can access Artifacts, Imbued Items, mentors,<br /> libraries, Grimoires, and other magical resources. <b>The Storyteller<br /> should assign an Availability rating to the item your character seeks,</b><br /> related to the power level or regular Merit rating. <b>Consider your character\u2019s<br /> Status dots <u>as Resources</u> for the purpose of procuring these<br /> magical resources</b> (see Acquiring Services, p. 228). Availability ratings<br /> assume the service or Merit will be assigned on a temporary basis (for<br /> a single story); add \u2022\u2022 for permanent requisitions. The group assumes<br /> she\u2019ll return it when done with it, or make amends if it\u2019s destroyed<br /> or lost. Merits suitable for requisition include Alternate Identity, Retainer,<br /> Imbued Item, Artifact, Grimoire, Mentor, Hallow, Sanctum,<br /> Library, Advanced Library, Safe Place, Familiar, and Resources, all<br /> with Availability equal to their dot rating. The Storyteller decides if<br /> your character\u2019s group has access to a particular magical resource;<br /> rank doesn\u2019t summon magical storehouses into being. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every item has an Availability rating. Once per chapter, your<br /> character can procure an item at her Resources level or lower,<br /> without issue. Obtaining an item one Availability above her<br /> Resources reduces her effective Resources by one dot for a full<br /> month, since she has to rapidly liquidate funds. She can procure<br /> items two Availability below her Resources without limit (within<br /> reason). For example, a character with Resources \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 can procure<br /> as many Availability \u2022\u2022 disposable cellphones as she needs. </div> </div> </div>So if you have Status 3 once per chapter you can ask for temporary access to all the weak hallows(1 dot each) in the area(if such exist). Or one imbued item (3 dot or lower). Or burn your Status temporarily to acquire 4 dot Grimoir.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:27:03-07:00","id":1070097,"title":"","content":"Yes, I've read that, I'm not sure there's a direct 1:1 correlation between a merit dot and an availability rating. By that measure Mage society would find 1 dot Imbued Items as common as batteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:30:30-07:00","id":1070102,"title":"","content":"Or you could ask for 1 dot Hallow permanently, and do that once per game session. If you had Status 5, you could technically ask for unlimited permanent 1 Hallows - 1 Availability for &quot;Hallow 1&quot;, 2 availability for permanent requisition, and another 2 availability to skip the limits. More realistically, it would allow you to not count that for this sessions requisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:33:45-07:00","id":1070106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The Storyteller decides if</i><br /> <i>your character\u2019s group has access to a particular magical resource;</i><br /> <i>rank doesn\u2019t summon magical storehouses into being.</i> </div> </div> </div>Imbued items start at two dots. And actually after X thousand years of mages crafting them I believe they should just lay in repositories in crazy abundance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:34:07-07:00","id":1070107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070097#post1070097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I've read that, I'm not sure there's a direct 1:1 correlation between a merit dot and an availability rating. By that measure Mage society would find 1 dot Imbued Items as common as batteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are as valuable as batteries. Not as common. You can have Status 5, but you are still limited by the number of these &quot;merits&quot; inside the setting - there are only that many Imbued Items 1 in the bank for you to borrow, even if they are relatively weak. You are restricted by what other people are willing to &quot;put in&quot; the shared pool, or what they are obliged to put in due to laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:36:23-07:00","id":1070108,"title":"","content":"They start at one dot. Sorry. I messed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:10:18-07:00","id":1070431,"title":"","content":"Okay, a question about Artifacts. The text in 2e mentions adding Utility Attainments to a spell. Is it possible to add non-Utility Attainments to an Artifact?<br /> <br /> E.g: Some sort of Deathly artifact that grants the user an Inviolate Soul as long as they are using it, using the rules for Death/Gnosis combos for it? <br /> <br /> Or are the Attainments like that not meant to be obtainable, even by an Artifact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:21:55-07:00","id":1070439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070431#post1070431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, a question about Artifacts. The text in 2e mentions adding Utility Attainments to a spell. Is it possible to add non-Utility Attainments to an Artifact?<br /> <br /> E.g: Some sort of Deathly artifact that grants the user an Inviolate Soul as long as they are using it, using the rules for Death/Gnosis combos for it?<br /> <br /> Or are the Attainments like that not meant to be obtainable, even by an Artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Attainment abilities can be replicated through spells, but no, under current Artifact creation rules you can't do that.<br /> However if you talk to your GM I don't see any reason why you couldn't make an exception to that rule.<br /> I think DaveB's mentioned that there will be expanded rules for Artifacts in Signs of Sorcery, when it comes out.<br /> But I wouldn't hold my breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:27:23-07:00","id":1070528,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble finding a rule again. I could have sworn I had read this before but I just can't find it!<br /> <br /> What happens if you try to mix attainments? Like if you try to mix a Legacy Attainment with something broken like Time in a Bottle? What happens? Is that possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T02:33:01-07:00","id":1070545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070528#post1070528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble finding a rule again. I could have sworn I had read this before but I just can't find it!<br /> <br /> What happens if you try to mix attainments? Like if you try to mix a Legacy Attainment with something broken like Time in a Bottle? What happens? Is that possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>You risk going Mad, but I don't think it would work since legacy attainments can't be modified after you've learned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:43:41-07:00","id":1070555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070545#post1070545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You risk going Mad, but I don't think it would work since legacy attainments can't be modified after you've learned them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I misspoke, sorry. I meant, an attainment already cooked into it. Like the Eleventh Question 4th attainment apparently has the time utility attainment of temporal sympathy as part of the spell.<br /> <br /> So for example, an attainment that has the Everywhere effect from Space 4's greater utility attainment, but in exchange, the mana cost has to be at least 1, and the Everywhere effect <i>has to</i> go into play. Is there anything about this in a rule or a FAQ or errata that I've overlooked? Or is it one of those &quot;ST domain&quot; things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:02:29-07:00","id":1070563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070555#post1070555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I misspoke, sorry. I meant, an attainment already cooked into it. Like the Eleventh Question 4th attainment apparently has the time utility attainment of temporal sympathy as part of the spell.<br /> <br /> So for example, an attainment that has the Everywhere effect from Space 4's greater utility attainment, but in exchange, the mana cost has to be at least 1, and the Everywhere effect <i>has to</i> go into play. Is there anything about this in a rule or a FAQ or errata that I've overlooked? Or is it one of those &quot;ST domain&quot; things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Sympathy only works with the past of a subject not it's future so none of the attainments in the 11Q writeup use it. The Reach was spent on Sensory because it's a combined effect with the Optional Matter attainment below it that could have a Representational Yantra crop up anywhere within Sensory Range.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it though, a legacy attainment could probably include arcana attainment or it would neuter some legacies like the Threnodists. I know that legacy attainments are supposed to give a mana break, but you should probably still pay the requisite mana for the arcana attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-30-2017, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:41:28-07:00","id":1070631,"title":"","content":"Would you consider Casting magic a &quot;Mental roll&quot; with regards of the penalties from the Madness Condition? I am erring on yes due to the need to acurately form an Imago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T12:40:19-07:00","id":1070803,"title":"","content":"Technically, no - a Mental roll is one including a Mental Attribute, and magic isn't Wits + Arcanum or anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:10:20-07:00","id":1070818,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> Technically...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Life and Spirit rule the Primal Wild. Life is the gross Arcanum<br /> of the pair, a term made literal by some of its more visceral spells.<br /> Life magic governs all living things, in fact, from viruses to titanic<br /> whales, <b>even the nerve cells that allow thoughts to form Imagos.</b><br /> Life is tenacious in the extreme, capable of surviving anywhere,<br /> developing any trait to weather environmental stresses, and<br /> Life mages are comparably tough. By harnessing the endless<br /> adaptability of living forms, mages can gain perspectives on the<br /> world otherwise lost even to Awakened senses. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:23:08-07:00","id":1070823,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Thorbes asked about Mental rolls, not Nerve Cell rolls.<br /> <br /> What you want are things that inflict penalties to 'all rolls,' like extreme environments after a few hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:31:03-07:00","id":1070831,"title":"","content":"Instead of going for the dice roll penalty in case of Madness, I think expecting appropiately Madness Induced Imago would be more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:37:43-07:00","id":1070833,"title":"","content":"It's very much a mental thing. It's just not a Mental thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T14:52:05-07:00","id":1070868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070833#post1070833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very much a mental thing. It's just not a Mental thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. But it would be a waste not to have something like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:27:38-07:00","id":1070886,"title":"","content":"I'm very torn. On one hand forming an imago should just be a mental process that should be affected by negative conditions (lower-case c) that affects your mental process, but on the other hand no rules actually support that view. Your Mental Attributes does not matter in the slightest, and it seems you need to spend 2 Reach to also affect spell casting rolls with spells that affect mundane rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:32:23-07:00","id":1070888,"title":"","content":"That is quite a dichotomy but I go with mental magic giving penalties only with reach but on the other hand drugs and alcohol work without any help. Just so you could be irresponsible drink&amp;cast type of mage. Or just drugged by a hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:34:25-07:00","id":1070889,"title":"","content":"A Mental Roll penalty doesn't mean you can't think thoughts. It suggests a challenging mental bout.<br /> <br /> Thinking Imagos is clearly the easiest part of it, as it's not part of any Mental roll. It's getting the magic through that's the hardest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:42:29-07:00","id":1070894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070889#post1070889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mental Roll penalty doesn't mean you can't think thoughts. It suggests a challenging mental bout.<br /> <br /> Thinking Imagos is clearly the easiest part of it, as it's not part of any Mental roll. It's getting the magic through that's the hardest.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it comes from there so if Fate can brake your bones and blinding you just by randomizing chemical reactions in the body...so Mind should be able to affect spellcasting rolls with some reach.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By directing once-random biochemical changes within a<br /> subject, cause seizures, hallucinations, and physical events,<br /> imposing suitable Conditions such as Blind or Disabled. </div> </div> </div>Drugged Tilt applies to all rolls, not just mental, just like wound penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:44:17-07:00","id":1070895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070894#post1070894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it comes from there so if Fate can brake your bones and blinding you just by randomizing chemical reactions in the body...so Mind should be able to affect spellcasting rolls with some reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it can, as you noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Drugged Tilt applies to all rolls, not just mental, just like wound penalties. </div> </div> </div>You just need to penalize more than Mental rolls to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:48:50-07:00","id":1070898,"title":"","content":"We agree then. I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T16:23:39-07:00","id":1070914,"title":"","content":"Good discussion, thanks guys. Now it's clear to me RAW is Madness does not affect magic. Still a good idea for it to factor in the spells somehow, even if only as a purely narrative effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T16:38:20-07:00","id":1070919,"title":"","content":"Oh absolutely.<br /> <br /> I've no idea what it's like from the writing or development level but seeing other people talk about it there's a sharp divide between people who believe RAW and RAI, where Madness only exists as a dice penalty decided upon by the ST once per chapter or it has broader effects, like being a madperson. And there's certainly a loud contingent who don't seem to be want to be told what to do or 'how to play' their character but in my opinion the books could go further in explaining how people would or should act under certain Conditions beyond 'trying to find dicepools that don't have penalties to them.'<br /> <br /> Though I guess part of the problem with that is something that's come up a lot in the past. In going with the Madness example, 'what is madness?' and the myriad of ways to depict it and it's not something easily narrowed down in a Condition meant to affect a myriad of different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2017, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:10:18-07:00","id":1070937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070563#post1070563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporal Sympathy only works with the past of a subject not it's future so none of the attainments in the 11Q writeup use it. The Reach was spent on Sensory because it's a combined effect with the Optional Matter attainment below it that could have a Representational Yantra crop up anywhere within Sensory Range.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it though, a legacy attainment could probably include arcana attainment or it would neuter some legacies like the Threnodists. I know that legacy attainments are supposed to give a mana break, but you should probably still pay the requisite mana for the arcana attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't the 4th Attainment a duplication of Prophecy, which affects the future? Actually looking at it, it only says sympathy yantra, so I guess it is actually space.<br /> Which means that an arcana attainment can be added to a legacy attainment even if the arcana isn't used in the spell.<br /> <br /> So I guess that begs the question if this is only true for attainments that simply <i>will not function</i> without it. A spell to summon spirits using the Everywhere arcana attainment probably isn't needed for the <i>bare minimum</i>, it only makes it more powerful. So I dunno.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: two cents, or perhaps a handful of change, on the above discussion.<br /> <br /> If I had to suggest how to roll play madness, then &quot;what is madness&quot; is probably just something dysfunctional <i>for that character</i>. What is madness could vary by culture or condition, but for Mages I guess it is a bit easier cuz you just have to make the characters obsessions and vice all the stronger. Its whatever makes the character themself feel afflicted.<br /> <br /> I can see Mind or Forces causing dice penalty conditions through distractions, like annoying sounds or making someone feel drunk. Life probably could be used to MAKE them drunk.<br /> <br /> And last, I'm guessing Madness doesn't affect spells because the Imago needs to be able to get started in the mind, but it doesn't have to end there--the soul is also involved and the soul doesn't go Mad unless your Wisdom is kaput. So as long as you can still think, you can make a spell.<br /> <br /> So, the distractions I suggested, their dice penalty would be situational. They'd apply to complex imagos or trying to single out a target you can't see... but if the character got frustrated and wanted to just cast an AoE spell with themself as the epicenter, they probably won't take a dice penalty for that (just probably a wisdom roll for very probably about to do something very much unwise.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 03-30-2017, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:46:26-07:00","id":1070976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1070937#post1070937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But isn't the 4th Attainment a duplication of Prophecy, which affects the future? Actually looking at it, it only says sympathy yantra, so I guess it is actually space.<br /> Which means that an arcana attainment can be added to a legacy attainment even if the arcana isn't used in the spell.<br /> <br /> So I guess that begs the question if this is only true for attainments that simply <i>will not function</i> without it. A spell to summon spirits using the Everywhere arcana attainment probably isn't needed for the <i>bare minimum</i>, it only makes it more powerful. So I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually doesn't say it's a Sympathy Yantra, but a Representational Yantra, I know that typically that would be used for Sympathetic magic, but it's actually a way of limiting the purview of Prophecy for the attainment to a target that the Mage is studying. Prophecy is typically cast without Sympathy because 1) the future doesn't require temporal sympathy, and 2) the caster uses it on &quot;time&quot; to ask theoretical questions about the future of any subject they can come up with. Even when used Socially to reduce Doors it doesn't have a Withstand so it must not be a spell you cast on another subject which eliminates the need for space sympathy.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nevermind, I didn't read carefully enough, yes the attainment incorporates the Space Sympathy ability, apparently bypassing the need for Space for that attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-30-2017, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:10:07-07:00","id":1071305,"title":"","content":"Can you add a Withstand rating to a spell that normally lacks it? Would you consider it Reach-worthy? Or should I assume that a lot of spells have Withstand ratings that are not listed due to being irrelevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:49:57-07:00","id":1071321,"title":"","content":"The reason many spells don't have Withstand ratings is because they don't affect the target negatively. If it can be used negatively against the subject you should actually add a Withstand rating regardless of whether the caster wants it or not. There are a few published spells that say that if the spell is used negatively it will be Withstood by whatever Attribute is relevant despite not having a separate line for Withstand above the effect text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:06:40-07:00","id":1071329,"title":"","content":"I know that. But I'm specifically asking about making something that lacks Withstand gain it. I assume it's not possible for Rote version of the spells, or not without a Reach, but I think it's something that could be possibly done with Improvised Spells or as a Reach option. <br /> (Yes, there is a reason why having a Withstand on spell with no negative conesquences might be positive)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:11:00-07:00","id":1071332,"title":"","content":"If you wan't to weaken the spell by a Reach effect you should go for it. And I don't see a reason why you couldn't use it with Rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:14:18-07:00","id":1071333,"title":"","content":"Could you present a theoretical situation wherein a mage would want their spell to face a Withstand rating? It would help me think about the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:21:50-07:00","id":1071336,"title":"","content":"Imagine your Invisibility spell has Withstand rating. You put 1 Potency into it. Now you can turn it on and off at will, as due to Dave's clarification about how Withstand works, Withstand is rechecked on turn-per-turn basis...which means you can decide to reflexively not Withstand the spell when you want to be Invisible, and Withstand it when you don't want to be. <br /> This already works for all spells if you can afford to have Wards and Signs running on you, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:26:53-07:00","id":1071338,"title":"","content":"It's completely possible to change an existing Withstand rating (which is why Withstand is re-checked), but I'm not sure if it's possible to decide after the spell is already cast whether or not a Withstand rating will apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:31:36-07:00","id":1071345,"title":"","content":"Maybe with some merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:44:56-07:00","id":1071350,"title":"","content":"Mmm. Maybe it's a language quirk, but I feel that &quot;Withstanding&quot; is an active effort - you keep resisting (or not). At worst, I think you can force Withstand re-check by spending a Willpower point, to raise your Withstand by 2. &quot;Willpower point to turn spell on/off&quot; sounds OK.<br /> This would also *finally* make Choose the Thread somewhat practical to me, because the way the spell is constructed was killing me (mostly because you had very little control about what it will actually affect) - now I can precast, keep it suppressed and surrender to visions of future when I know that I need this specific roll to be rolled twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:57:10-07:00","id":1071357,"title":"","content":"Withstand ratings aren't limited to thinking beings. Durability, Gauntlet Strength, Sympathy (both when using them and casting on them), Hallow Rating etc. are also possible Withstand ratings. Those things can't choose to resist a spell. They do so because it's simply harder to affect them. On the other hand a conscious person who knows a spell is cast on them can choose not to use their own Withstand rating but that makes <i>not</i> Withstanding more of an effort than Withstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:34:10-07:00","id":1071490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1071336#post1071336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine your Invisibility spell has Withstand rating. You put 1 Potency into it. Now you can turn it on and off at will, as due to Dave's clarification about how Withstand works, Withstand is rechecked on turn-per-turn basis...which means you can decide to reflexively not Withstand the spell when you want to be Invisible, and Withstand it when you don't want to be.<br /> This already works for all spells if you can afford to have Wards and Signs running on you, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you do that with Fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T17:05:45-07:00","id":1071507,"title":"","content":"I think the decision whether or not to withstand is still a one-time thing.<br /> <br /> What you <i>can</i> definitely do is set the potency to your withstand score + 1 and switch the spell off for a turn with a point of willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T06:31:25-07:00","id":1071697,"title":"","content":"Or just boost the Withstand score with a spell to suppress the other spell for as long as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T10:04:44-07:00","id":1071743,"title":"","content":"That works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T08:33:56-07:00","id":1072031,"title":"","content":"Does Geomancy (Prime 3) let one change the gross arcanum associated with a node by way of changing the resonance? And is it necessary that the mage casting the spell have ability in said arcanum? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":".  corrected spell name 04-02-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:31:35-07:00","id":1072050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072031#post1072031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Geomancy (Prime 3) let one change the gross arcanum associated with a node by way of changing the resonance? And is it necessary that the mage casting the spell have ability in said arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you could do that, and no it wouldn't appear to require a use of a conjunctional arcana to choose which flavor of arcana is put there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:11:29-07:00","id":1072172,"title":"","content":"Like, since Legacy attainments are Immune to Countering and Supernal Dispellation and Free from the Lie, is there anything that stops a mage from creating a legacy trying to become immortal if he is a Seer?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T16:33:57-07:00","id":1072239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072172#post1072172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, since Legacy attainments are Immune to Countering and Supernal Dispellation and Free from the Lie, is there anything that stops a mage from creating a legacy trying to become immortal if he is a Seer?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing that stops any Mage from devising a legacy to become immortal. There's more than one in fact, the Tremere are the most famous is all, which is one of the reasons other Mages are wary of the concept. Scions of God do it for instance, and they keep the immortality bit a very quiet secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T16:34:48-07:00","id":1072241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072172#post1072172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, since Legacy attainments are Immune to Countering and Supernal Dispellation and Free from the Lie, is there anything that stops a mage from creating a legacy trying to become immortal if he is a Seer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from other Seers becoming jealous of you and trying to keep you checked and undermine you? Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T21:31:48-07:00","id":1072355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072172#post1072172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, since Legacy attainments are Immune to Countering and Supernal Dispellation and Free from the Lie, is there anything that stops a mage from creating a legacy trying to become immortal if he is a Seer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see many Pentacle Mages actually wanting to do that. But as per standing Pentacle policy, they'd likely be ostracised eventually.<br /> <br /> There's also the difficulty of designing such Attainments on your own. Though doubtless the Mysterium has an odd dozen soul-stoles stolen from those Mages who achieved such a feat, and then eventually died.<br /> <br /> Really there's no reason you can't make yourself unaging. However the problem is that ultimately, without the 6th Attainment, you can't make yourself Undying, and at that stage, you've got the potential to Ascend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T23:38:47-07:00","id":1072381,"title":"","content":"Is there a set of rules for having a character undergo an Awakening during play? Like if I took a mortal character and made him Awakened mid-game, what the immediate post-awakening template would look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T02:37:19-07:00","id":1072420,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Arcana levels, but no Rotes since they have to be taught. Same with the free Occult dot and High Speech Merit since those are gained through Order membership.<br /> The neolithic era (that I don't remember what it's named right now) in Dark Eras has character creation rules for mages before the creation of the Orders that you could take a look at.<br /> I'm not assuming that the character won't be part of an Order, but what's taught by an Order will take at least some time before the character gains access to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-03-2017, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:11:27-07:00","id":1072457,"title":"","content":"Can you &quot;trick&quot; your way past Withstand? Imagine for example you're going to Hex someone, but you need them relaxed because your potency isn't that great.<br /> If you convince them to relax while you &quot;read their fortune&quot; and that's enough for them to take the effort to lower their Withstand, does that still count despite the fact it's something completely different to what you claimed?<br /> <br /> Also I seem to remember someone saying something about this, but can someone raise their Withstand against a spell after it's been cast on them, once they realise what it actually does?<br /> Would it be possible to use a conjunctive Mind effect perhaps to &quot;encourage&quot; someone not to raise their Withstand again? Such as perhaps by distracting them from the actual effects of the spell so they never actively consider it something working against them, and don't try and cancel it, or provoke Dissonance?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think up a Mastigos Fate Legacy about making predictions and cursing people, and it would work SO much better if there was some way to &quot;sneak in the back door&quot; and avoid Withstand.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. While not playable yet in 2e, I'm assuming an Archmaster's understanding of their Arcana's Imperial Practices (6+ dots) enhances their Attainments beyond the capacity of even the most potent Master, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Spelling 04-03-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:15:21-07:00","id":1072481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072457#post1072457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I seem to remember someone saying something about this, but can someone raise their Withstand against a spell after it's been cast on them, once they realise what it actually does?<br /> Would it be possible to use a conjunctive Mind effect perhaps to &quot;encourage&quot; someone not to raise their Withstand again? Such as perhaps by distracting them from the actual effects of the spell so they never actively consider it something working against them, and don't try and cancel it, or provoke Dissonance?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. While not playable yet in 2e, I'm assuming an Archmaster's understanding of their Arcana's Imperial Practices (6+ dots) enhances their Attainments beyond the capacity of even the most potent Master, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>So Dave posted saying that you can spend willpower while say mind controlled to raise the withstand stat and if it decreases the potency of the spell to zero then you are no longer effected by it for 3+ seconds per willpower spent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Withstand reduces the effect of a spell's Potency, it doesn't remove the spell. If someone's withstand rating changes part-way through a spell's Duration, up OR down, it gets reassessed. If your mind-control spell that isn't potent enough to beat someone's resolve is still active when something else reduces their resolve to below Potency, your mind control spell begins to work. Alternatively, if you mind control someone to kill themselves, they *can* spend Willpower at the last minute to up their Resolve for a turn. Or another mage can cast a spell that increases their Resolve, with a longer duration than your mind-control one. </div> </div> </div>This means that spells such as &quot;Befuddle&quot;, &quot;Degrading the Form&quot;, and &quot;Alter Integrity&quot; behave oddly...so probably need different withstand traits. Personally i see no reason not to add an additional command of &quot;Dont resist&quot; to all mind control spells now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-03-2017, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:23:40-07:00","id":1072484,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but can somebody decide once they're feeling a spell's effects to reapply with Withstand to it, when they'd originally lowered it to permit the spell to affect them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:26:26-07:00","id":1072486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Withstand reduces the effect of a spell's Potency, it doesn't remove the spell. If someone's withstand rating changes part-way through a spell's Duration, up OR down, it gets reassessed. If your mind-control spell that isn't potent enough to beat someone's resolve is still active when something else reduces their resolve to below Potency, your mind control spell begins to work. Alternatively, if you mind control someone to kill themselves, they *can* spend Willpower at the last minute to up their Resolve for a turn. Or another mage can cast a spell that increases their Resolve, with a longer duration than your mind-control one. </div> </div> </div>What happens to the extra returned potency gained when one casts &quot;Degrading the form&quot; with a potency 1 higher than the victims withstand rating and you use that 1 potency on stamina, reducing it to 1 meaning you gain some points back. Do you get to use it to lower another stat?<br /> <br /> Example victim has stamina 3, strength 3 and dexerity 3, i cast a potency 4 degrading the form on him. I beat the withstand by 1 so i lower his stamina, withstand gets ressessed and it drops his stamina/withstand to 1 meaning that i now beat withstand by 3 and have 2 extra potency, which i can use to reduce his strength to 1 also? It also applies to the befuddle spell.<br /> <br /> Also any spell that increases the same stat as its withstood by will continually flicker on and off, so obviously these need different withstand stats, i just dont know what..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-03-2017, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:28:34-07:00","id":1072487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072484#post1072484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but can somebody decide once they're feeling a spell's effects to reapply with Withstand to it, when they'd originally lowered it to permit the spell to affect them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that spending willpower to raise the withstand stat (i dont think you can just use willpower to raise any withstand) is them trying to reapply withstand, they get 3 seconds per willpower and only if it overcomes the spells potency again, if it doesnt or they dont spend willpower then no, they cant just reapply withstand whenever they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-03-2017, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:17:05-07:00","id":1072550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072486#post1072486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happens to the extra returned potency gained when one casts &quot;Degrading the form&quot; with a potency 1 higher than the victims withstand rating and you use that 1 potency on stamina, reducing it to 1 meaning you gain some points back. Do you get to use it to lower another stat?<br /> <br /> Example victim has stamina 3, strength 3 and dexerity 3, i cast a potency 4 degrading the form on him. I beat the withstand by 1 so i lower his stamina, withstand gets ressessed and it drops his stamina/withstand to 1 meaning that i now beat withstand by 3 and have 2 extra potency, which i can use to reduce his strength to 1 also? It also applies to the befuddle spell.<br /> <br /> Also any spell that increases the same stat as its withstood by will continually flicker on and off, so obviously these need different withstand stats, i just dont know what..</div> </div> </div> </div>This already had been asked on this topic. Seems like one of the most common questions.<br /> If I remember correctly, you don't count(upgrade) the effects of the same spell on the withstand rating against itself.<br /> If you did, all spells that buff your stats to &quot;Potency&quot; would be in a constant &quot;withstand/don't withstand&quot; state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-03-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T09:11:21-07:00","id":1072565,"title":"","content":"Are Perfected Materials subject to Dissonance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T16:58:00-07:00","id":1072777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072565#post1072565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Perfected Materials subject to Dissonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no, unless created by a spell.<br /> If only because they can be refined in the complete absence of Supernal Magic by passing them through naturally formed Irises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:05:47-07:00","id":1072783,"title":"","content":"Yet they are still considered Supernal by the open dev document for Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\"