ell Create Thaumium creates a type of matter that proects its wielder by triggering a CoW. I assume that an indefinite duration adds +4 dice to the dice pool as usual, but what happens if the Thaumium is made Lasting by the listed +2 Reach option? Does it lose the +4 bonus due to not having a duration, or does the Lasting option always grant +4 bonus dice?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072789#post1072789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then you have your answer.<br /> Assign a Withstand, and if Dissonance successes are in excess of that, deal damage to its structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> Would you say Size or Durability being the better choice of Withstand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-03-2017, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:16:40-07:00","id":1072838,"title":"","content":"Can you use a Sensory range spell in the past through Postcognition if you pay the cost for casting Sensory through an indirect means (albiet, at a painful cost in Reach and a decent bit of Mana)? After all, you can see their pas selves when you're Postcogniting, and you can use Sensory spells on anyone you see...<br /> But on the other hand, the errata to Temporal Sympathy seems to indicate it's not meant for you to be able to casually use any spell in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13216-yamidamian","name":"yamidamian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:23:49-07:00","id":1072846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072790#post1072790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: Generally spells that leads to Clash of Wills can't be made Lasting so it's not much of an issue, but reading the Sheer Perfection document again I saw that the spell Create Thaumium creates a type of matter that proects its wielder by triggering a CoW. I assume that an indefinite duration adds +4 dice to the dice pool as usual, but what happens if the Thaumium is made Lasting by the listed +2 Reach option? Does it lose the +4 bonus due to not having a duration, or does the Lasting option always grant +4 bonus dice?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> Would you say Size or Durability being the better choice of Withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div>With regards to your first question, Dave's said he's ditching all of those Lasting reach options.<br /> <br /> With regards to your second question, talk to your GM. I'd actually go with a combination of both, as that's what you've got to consider when actually making the stuff the hard way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:02:35-07:00","id":1072893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072846#post1072846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With regards to your first question, Dave's said he's ditching all of those Lasting reach options.<br /> <br /> With regards to your second question, talk to your GM. I'd actually go with a combination of both, as that's what you've got to consider when actually making the stuff the hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Perfected Metals, right? Or more general stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:23:37-07:00","id":1072903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072893#post1072893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Perfected Metals, right? Or more general stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd thought I was pretty clear given context, but only for Perfected materials.<br /> It was decided that it was otherwise too easy to create massive numbers with a simple Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T23:14:20-07:00","id":1072962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072550#post1072550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This already had been asked on this topic. Seems like one of the most common questions.<br /> If I remember correctly, you don't count(upgrade) the effects of the same spell on the withstand rating against itself.<br /> If you did, all spells that buff your stats to &quot;Potency&quot; would be in a constant &quot;withstand/don't withstand&quot; state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what? I did alot of googling/searching for this answer and ive only seen one or two suggested methods of fixing it (changing the withstand rating to something else i think is the simplest) and no RAW answer.<br /> <br /> Most spells that buff stats arnt actually withstood. Only spells that boost the same thing that as it withstands are broken (along with things that lower the same stat as withstand)<br /> <br /> If its no trouble could you link the other questions/answers please as my google-fu may not have been good enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T01:53:22-07:00","id":1072999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yamidamian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072838#post1072838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use a Sensory range spell in the past through Postcognition if you pay the cost for casting Sensory through an indirect means (albiet, at a painful cost in Reach and a decent bit of Mana)? After all, you can see their pas selves when you're Postcogniting, and you can use Sensory spells on anyone you see...<br /> But on the other hand, the errata to Temporal Sympathy seems to indicate it's not meant for you to be able to casually use any spell in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Postcognition doesn't travel to or change the past it effectively summons a vision of the past forward for viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T01:55:09-07:00","id":1073000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072962#post1072962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait what? I did alot of googling/searching for this answer and ive only seen one or two suggested methods of fixing it (changing the withstand rating to something else i think is the simplest) and no RAW answer.<br /> <br /> Most spells that buff stats arnt actually withstood. Only spells that boost the same thing that as it withstands are broken (along with things that lower the same stat as withstand)<br /> <br /> If its no trouble could you link the other questions/answers please as my google-fu may not have been good enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a really long, contentious thread on this <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7210_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7210\" data-vbnamecard=\"7210\">Horodrigo</a> is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:10:42-07:00","id":1073012,"title":"","content":"Actually, no official answer was given regarding how to deal with such a situation unless I'm completely misremembering how that thread went.<br /> But it was commonly accepted that the most simple way of dealing with it would be to ignore the spell's own effect on a Withstand rating when rechecking Withstand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:24:59-07:00","id":1073106,"title":"","content":"Why is it called Withstand when rolling for Dissonance when it doesn't actually work like Withstand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:37:57-07:00","id":1073114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1073012#post1073012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, no official answer was given regarding how to deal with such a situation unless I'm completely misremembering how that thread went.<br /> But it was commonly accepted that the most simple way of dealing with it would be to ignore the spell's own effect on a Withstand rating when rechecking Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember it similarly. There was that infobit about how Withstand work, people started asking questions about loops and other things, and then started figuring out hotfixes for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:43:48-07:00","id":1073120,"title":"","content":"A spell can't withstand itself. Pretty logical, when you think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T13:25:03-07:00","id":1073331,"title":"","content":"Somewhere on these forums I saw a post about a spirit mage getting a Spirit Boon.<br /> What is a spirit boon? Is like a favor from a spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:54:20-07:00","id":1073569,"title":"","content":"What practice is fusion?<br /> Not of subatomic particles, but of beings, objects, minds?<br /> What would it take for two Mages to work together, and pool their Arcana to construct an imago neither of them could individually form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:00:36-07:00","id":1073572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1073569#post1073569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practice is fusion?<br /> Not of subatomic particles, but of beings, objects, minds?<br /> What would it take for two Mages to work together, and pool their Arcana to construct an imago neither of them could individually form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Patterning might work with a stretch. If this isn't something the Imperial Practices cover, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:43:53-07:00","id":1073584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1073569#post1073569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practice is fusion?<br /> Not of subatomic particles, but of beings, objects, minds?<br /> What would it take for two Mages to work together, and pool their Arcana to construct an imago neither of them could individually form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about literal fusion or group casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:48:40-07:00","id":1073586,"title":"","content":"One Mage has Matter 4, Life 1.<br /> The other has Life 4, Matter 1.<br /> <br /> What does it take for them to be able to work together and Pattern a frog into a cabinet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:58:31-07:00","id":1073590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1073586#post1073586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Mage has Matter 4, Life 1.<br /> The other has Life 4, Matter 1.<br /> <br /> What does it take for them to be able to work together and Pattern a frog into a cabinet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, I don't think it's really been covered.I think there was a merit for it in 1e, but currently I don't think it's mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T00:37:20-07:00","id":1073609,"title":"","content":"It's Ritual Synergy from TotM p.74 but only with ST approval since it made a lot things trivial. Like teleporting a fridge for which you needed something like Space 4, Matter 3 (I don't remember exactly). I believe it should be cheaper for 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T01:17:25-07:00","id":1073617,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was it. So that existed in 1e, but as for 2e I have no idea. I feel like it should be a thing that can be done, cabals getting together to ritually cast a spell they couldn't manage alone, but it hasn't really been addressed so I don't know whether such things would be officially supported nowadays. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T01:53:40-07:00","id":1073624,"title":"","content":"A Merit building off Cabal Symbolism, perhaps? So that only spells that fit with the cabal's shared symbolism can be cast beyond an individual's Arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:08:20-07:00","id":1073629,"title":"","content":"Is this what you are talking about?<br /> <br /> Egregore<br /> Mysteriorum Arche (\u2022): In a teamwork spellcasting roll (see p.<br /> 119) in which the character is participating, she does not suffer<br /> the \u20133 penalty to contribute without the necessary Arcanum<br /> rating, and adds an automatic success if a full participant. All<br /> members of the ritual team must possess this Merit.<br /> <br /> Teamwork<br /> Mages may work together towards a common goal for spellcasting.<br /> This is handled like any other action where characters combine<br /> their efforts (see \u201cTeamwork,\u201d p. 214). The mages involved<br /> in the spellcasting must all have at least one dot in the Arcanum<br /> required to cast the spell, while the leader must have the required<br /> Arcanum rating to cast it himself. If the leader knows the spell as a<br /> Praxis or Rote, the spell gains the benefits of those methods. Any<br /> secondary caster who meets the Arcanum requirements rolls her<br /> own casting and adds her successes as bonus dice to the leader.<br /> If a secondary caster does not meet the Arcanum requirements,<br /> she rolls Gnosis (no Arcanum) with a \u20133 penalty, and provides<br /> any successes as bonus dice to the leader. Each participant must<br /> roll for Paradox separately; if any one of the casters releases a<br /> Paradox instead of containing it, it affects the entire spell. Mages<br /> without the Arcanum used at all, Sleepwalkers, and Proximi may<br /> also assist in the casting, but do not roll. Instead, the casters may<br /> use their participation in the ritual as an environment Yantra.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or is the question about; In a teamwork condition the leader has the life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 requires Shapecahnge a frog into a cabinet, but doesn't have the required matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 to do it, however a participant has the required Life \u2022 to be counted as a full member and has the required Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 to add. As an ST I would have a teamwork situation and the leader would take a -2 or -4 for a combination spell, as they are both Co-Leaders each being a leader in their own section of the combined spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 04-05-2017, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:17:24-07:00","id":1073631,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that doesn't quite work for this, because the spell would effectively need two leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:22:39-07:00","id":1073633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1073629#post1073629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this what you are talking about?<br /> <br /> Egregore<br /> Mysteriorum Arche (\u2022): In a teamwork spellcasting roll (see p.<br /> 119) in which the character is participating, she does not suffer<br /> the \u20133 penalty to contribute without the necessary Arcanum<br /> rating, and adds an automatic success if a full participant. All<br /> members of the ritual team must possess this Merit.<br /> <br /> Teamwork<br /> Mages may work together towards a common goal for spellcasting.<br /> This is handled like any other action where characters combine<br /> their efforts (see \u201cTeamwork,\u201d p. 214). The mages involved<br /> in the spellcasting must all have at least one dot in the Arcanum<br /> required to cast the spell, <b>while the leader must have the required<br /> Arcanum rating to cast it himself</b>. If the leader knows the spell as a<br /> Praxis or Rote, the spell gains the benefits of those methods. Any<br /> secondary caster who meets the Arcanum requirements rolls her<br /> own casting and adds her successes as bonus dice to the leader.<br /> If a secondary caster does not meet the Arcanum requirements,<br /> she rolls Gnosis (no Arcanum) with a \u20133 penalty, and provides<br /> any successes as bonus dice to the leader. Each participant must<br /> roll for Paradox separately; if any one of the casters releases a<br /> Paradox instead of containing it, it affects the entire spell. Mages<br /> without the Arcanum used at all, Sleepwalkers, and Proximi may<br /> also assist in the casting, but do not roll. Instead, the casters may<br /> use their participation in the ritual as an environment Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Elfive said, since what we're looking at is a conjunctional spell requiring Matter 4 + Life 4, but without none of the mages actually having that ratings. One has Matter 1 and Life 4, the other has Matter 4 and Life 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:22:51-07:00","id":1073634,"title":"","content":"Edited the above post, you responded before I finished my thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:43:10-07:00","id":1073642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1073633#post1073633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Elfive said, since what we're looking at is a conjunctional spell requiring Matter 4 + Life 4, but without none of the mages actually having that ratings. One has Matter 1 and Life 4, the other has Matter 4 and Life 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think I would allow it to work as a Combined Spell (Not a conjunctive effect) with each one a Co-Leader of they section of the effect, Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Shapechange and Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Transubstantiation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T03:56:57-07:00","id":1073658,"title":"","content":"You'd probably need to use Display of Power at least, so that both mages contributing to the shared Imago can see what the other is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:20:53-07:00","id":1073732,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. I think that is a good requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:48:31-07:00","id":1073741,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Time as well to hang the Imago as it's forming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T11:24:45-07:00","id":1073804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1072172#post1072172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, since Legacy attainments are Immune to Countering and Supernal Dispellation and Free from the Lie, is there anything that stops a mage from creating a legacy trying to become immortal if he is a Seer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, being in direct control over your place in the Chain of Causality is a better end game, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T05:35:00-07:00","id":1074098,"title":"","content":"It's possible to kill or render unconscious without using Unmaking and without using the suggested &quot;direct damage&quot; spells, right? Like using a Life Ruling spell to cause a person to require more oxygen than his environment can possibly supply so that he dies of oxygen deprivation (basically flipping Body Control on its head)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T05:52:55-07:00","id":1074099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074098#post1074098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible to kill or render unconscious without using Unmaking and without using the suggested &amp;quot;direct damage&amp;quot; spells, right? Like using a Life Ruling spell to cause a person to require more oxygen than his environment can possibly supply so that he dies of oxygen deprivation (basically flipping Body Control on its head)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, see the sidebar for Ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T05:55:39-07:00","id":1074101,"title":"","content":"Space has a sidebar about how much oxygen is breathed by an average adult person. Cast Ban on someone and let them use up all oxygen and you have yourself an unconscious (and possibly brain damaged) person. Also Mind and Life should both be able to force someone to just fall asleep/become unconscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T06:13:43-07:00","id":1074105,"title":"","content":"Spells cast in a detrimental manner directly on a target like the Transform Life suggestion should contend with Withstand though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:06:06-07:00","id":1074171,"title":"","content":"Can you use Remote Control to shoot someone? Or to draw a masterwork picture? What are example uses of Remote Control that would substitute for a Skill check?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:11:50-07:00","id":1074177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074171#post1074171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Remote Control to shoot someone? Or to draw a masterwork picture? What are example uses of Remote Control that would substitute for a Skill check?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it could paint a picture (Unless it was via some kind of auto-drawer or a printer), but it could substitute for some Science, most of Computers, some Drive, you could shoot a gun, but I don't think you could substitute the Guns skill, it's pretty case by case, but my assumption is that it works best on objects that don't absolutely require physical manipulation (Because the magic intervenes) in order to perform a function like a sword or a pencil would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:15:41-07:00","id":1074181,"title":"","content":"I thought that too, but a friend pointed out to me that examples include &quot;flipping&quot; a switch and making industrial press &quot;slam downwards&quot;, which, in his mind, means that the spell can force certain degree of physical manipulation. <br /> Would you allow doing it if the object you want to compel is in your hand (so you can input the needed physical movement), or would you just bump the &quot;remote pencil&quot; to Matter 2 and make it Ruling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:47:14-07:00","id":1074197,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is that you could manipulate all moving parts of an object, but you can't directly move the object. (In the case of cars you'd turn the wheels which leads to movement instead of giving it a push in the direction you want it to move.) You could turn off the safety of a gun, cock the hammer of a revolver, load a round in the chamber of a pistol, and pull the trigger, but you can't actually aim the gun with Remote Control.<br /> <br /> Edit: The spell points out that the object have to be mechanical. A paintbrush or a pencil aren't mechanical. A ballpoint pen is mechanical, but I believe the only things Remote Control would be able to do is to rotate the ball and extend/retract the point if it's a retractable pen. Otherwise why would there be a limit on what object you can manipulate with Remote Control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-06-2017, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:10:45-07:00","id":1074206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074101#post1074101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space has a sidebar about how much oxygen is breathed by an average adult person. Cast Ban on someone and let them use up all oxygen and you have yourself an unconscious (and possibly brain damaged) person. Also Mind and Life should both be able to force someone to just fall asleep/become unconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend and i are having a running argument/discussion over which could cause people to die quicker a oxygen or a carbon dioxide ban over an area...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:14:57-07:00","id":1074209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1041377#post1041377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can a Mage use Matter's &quot;Remote control&quot; spell on a firearm and then use the spells potency as successes to use it?<br /> <br /> The spell says &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><i>Anything that\u2019s within the bounds of a</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><i> single instant action, and which the subject device is capable of</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><i> performing, is fair game. Should the action require a Skill roll,</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><i> treat the spell\u2019s Potency as its successes</i>.&quot; Seems a bit silly as on its own the gun can only fire right? But then if a mage cant drive and remote controls a car why should he be allowed to have potency in successes to drive it? Maybe the mage just waves the gun at his target and it fires at the right time?<br /> <br /> I can totally see a mage being able to remote control enemy firearms and having them not fire but the &quot;</span></span><i>Should the action require a Skill roll,</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><i> treat the spell\u2019s Potency as its successes</i>.&quot; part of this spell bothers me with firearms, maybe only firearms that can move themselves ie on some form of motor system can be controlled like this?</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I asked this in January and didnt get a reply.<br /> <br /> Making guns go off in somebody's hand when pointing at people: yes, Stopping a gun from firing: yes, having god like ability (potency successes) to shoot people: no since part of the roll to hit somebody is about aiming which comes from a person, tho if the gun is held by some mechanical arm/motor then yes you now have some super accurate automatic gun. (ignoring the fact about how the gun detects its target blah blah....its magic!!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-06-2017, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:33:40-07:00","id":1074223,"title":"","content":"Say Mage A casts co-locate using 2 locations, his bedroom and a empty field. The spell mentions that folk with active mage sight (or the reach effect) see items inside the area as translucent but what about outside the area?<br /> <br /> Mage B is standing in the field outside the area of the spell, does he see 4 walls and a door, basically a box appear in the field or does he see the inside of the room as if there were no walls? I suppose it depends if the walls are in the area of the spell or not? Mage A could define the area his bedroom up to 1cm from the walls or right into the walls? I suppose if he had range for an entire house then it'd appear translucently in the field to those who can see it.<br /> <br /> What about Mage A, he only see's anything in the aoe of the spell in the field as translucent but he cant see though the walls of his room? He might see translucent grass on his hardwood floor now, maybe even a translucent cow will walk though his wall and into his room but thats it, he wont see Mage B outside his room?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:40:34-07:00","id":1074228,"title":"","content":"The mage would only see the area that is overlapping. How much that overlaps depends on the mage who cast the spell. And yes, the wall would be in the way for Mage A.<br /> <br /> However, a mage could cast the Outward and Inward Eye with the Reach option to see through Irises and then be able to see the surroundings of both overlapping areas, and not just the one they're currently in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:25:47-07:00","id":1074295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074206#post1074206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A friend and i are having a running argument/discussion over which could cause people to die quicker a oxygen or a carbon dioxide ban over an area...</div> </div> </div> </div>The suffocation reflex is caused by acidification of the blood not lack of Oxygen. So banning Oxygen would be a more 'humane' way to kill somebody as they would go hypoxic breathing pure nitrogen with out suffocating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway a weird situation came up in my game. My players stole a car and cast 'Hidden Hoard' and I'm trying to parse what that means to an outside observer. Would it look like the invisible jet from Superfriends era wonder woman with 5 grown people in the seated position tearing down the highway? Or would they be invisible while inside the car?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:40:11-07:00","id":1074302,"title":"","content":"Most of the Veiling spells don't make the subject invisible per se, but make the onlookers mindlessly &quot;surf&quot; their sight past it without actually acknowledging it's existence. So I don't think you would be floating in midair like it's an invisible jet, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:24:22-07:00","id":1074314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074171#post1074171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Remote Control to shoot someone? Or to draw a masterwork picture? What are example uses of Remote Control that would substitute for a Skill check?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoot a gun held and pointed by someone else yes, use make the gun move in a curtain direction before shooting no. Get a pincil to draw I would say no even if held by someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:33:39-07:00","id":1074319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074295#post1074295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The suffocation reflex is caused by acidification of the blood not lack of Oxygen. So banning Oxygen would be a more 'humane' way to kill somebody as they would go hypoxic breathing pure nitrogen with out suffocating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway a weird situation came up in my game. My players stole a car and cast 'Hidden Hoard' and I'm trying to parse what that means to an outside observer. Would it look like the invisible jet from Superfriends era wonder woman with 5 grown people in the seated position tearing down the highway? Or would they be invisible while inside the car?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell mentions that the on lookers still see the object but they put no value to it &quot;making it seem insignificant and beneath notice&quot; so no they are not invisible and neither is that car, but no one feels the car and its passengers are worth noticing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:45:12-07:00","id":1074328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074295#post1074295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it look like the invisible jet from Superfriends era wonder woman with 5 grown people in the seated position tearing down the highway? Or would they be invisible while inside the car?</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-Forces Veiling spells are SEP fields.<br /> You're not invisible, you're just irrelevant.<br /> You can drive on a road with a Matter veiling spell on your car without risk of crashing, it's just nobody will pay your vehicle any mind, regardless of if it's bright pink, covered in blood, is a rolling wreck, or has a plasma cannon mounted on the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T15:11:50-07:00","id":1074343,"title":"","content":"SEP field?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T15:15:28-07:00","id":1074347,"title":"","content":"Somebody Else's Problem field. It's a Hitchhiker's Guide To The Galaxy reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T15:51:47-07:00","id":1074368,"title":"","content":"Huh, Matter 2, four way intersection pileup with a simple Veiling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T16:22:01-07:00","id":1074387,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input. Now I'm know what to expect when my PC's put on scuba suits and try the same stunt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T18:15:46-07:00","id":1074437,"title":"","content":"Can people have sympathetic connections to concepts or abstract entities? For example, suppose a person has been the sole occupant of a particular address -- does she have a sympathetic connection <i>to the address</i> rather than just the house that sits there? Does a retired professional baseball player have a sympathetic connection to his lifetime statistics? Does a child have a sympathetic connection to the electronic record of his complete gene sequence? These are arrangements of symbols that correspond uniquely to specific individuals. They seem similar in nature to a person's sympathetic name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T20:23:02-07:00","id":1074491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074437#post1074437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can people have sympathetic connections to concepts or abstract entities? For example, suppose a person has been the sole occupant of a particular address -- does she have a sympathetic connection <i>to the address</i> rather than just the house that sits there? Does a retired professional baseball player have a sympathetic connection to his lifetime statistics? Does a child have a sympathetic connection to the electronic record of his complete gene sequence? These are arrangements of symbols that correspond uniquely to specific individuals. They seem similar in nature to a person's sympathetic name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of those things could be used for Sympathy Yantras (which a sympathetic name doubles as), but most abstract entities aren't discrete enough to be connectable \u2014 simply being well-known to a wide variety of people is enough to scramble a person's accessibility to sympathetic magic down to a weaker connection or stop a subject from being used to bridge Oneiroi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T21:30:19-07:00","id":1074506,"title":"","content":"Would you allow an esoteric rote created by a particular master and known only to a vanishingly small number of mages to serve as a sympathy yantra for that master? I would think that a rote would have a particularly strong connection to the one who created it.<br /> <br /> I think this is a neat plot device for finding or magically interacting with a master -- you learn an esoteric rote that he created from one of her students, and just knowing that rote give you the means to form a connection to her. It seems on par with &quot;a mage and an item she has imbued&quot; (Strong connection), but there's no physical item in play.<br /> <br /> It also gives mages a reason to think twice about sharing the rotes they create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T23:44:16-07:00","id":1074537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1074506#post1074506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you allow an esoteric rote created by a particular master and known only to a vanishingly small number of mages to serve as a sympathy yantra for that master? I would think that a rote would have a particularly strong connection to the one who created it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's part of the purpose of Legacy members having material sympathy to each other and the master-student bond constituting a Strong connection and therefore this can be viewed as another case of rotes not serving the same function as Legacy Attainments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this is a neat plot device for finding or magically interacting with a master -- you learn an esoteric rote that he created from one of her students, and just knowing that rote give you the means to form a connection to her. It seems on par with &quot;a mage and an item she has imbued&quot; (Strong connection), but there's no physical item in play. </div> </div> </div>Half the point of a rote is that it's sufficiently impersonal to diffuse your Signature Nimbus into deep information; you'd have better luck using a grimoire she scribed or the student she taught as the source of the connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also gives mages a reason to think twice about sharing the rotes they create. </div> </div> </div>Between rotes being a major chunk of the personal bargaining power any given Master has at their disposal and Scribe Grimoire being a one-dot spell, this is already incentivized in a manner that doesn't push Masters to focus on Space above other Arcana with greater incentive than their students have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:11:01-07:00","id":1074998,"title":"","content":"Is there guidance somewhere for determining the difficulties of various common uncontested actions?<ul><li>Lift or move various heavy things using Strength + Stamina</li> <li>Run for a really long time using Stamina + Athletics</li> <li>Stop someone from bleeding out with Wits + Medicine</li> </ul>The only thing I can find in the rules says that the ST can apply up to a -5 dice penalty based on challenging circumstances. This... doesn't feel totally sufficient. A high-gnosis mage can boost her strength high enough to possibly lift a car over her head; I'm pretty sure that's more than a -5 penalty to the dice roll and I have no idea how large a penalty to apply. Someone who is bleeding out due to a missing hand is easier to stabilize than someone with internal bleeding due to a bullet in their liver.<br /> <br /> I don't understand how to determine the difficulties of uncontested rolls in a systematic and consistent way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":".  Removed firearms example as it's covered in the combat rules for range penalties 04-08-2017, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T01:07:51-07:00","id":1075041,"title":"","content":"there used to be a table for first eddition mage, there probably is one in the core book(Cant find mine right now) for lifting weights and the Strength plus Stam increasses your effective strength for a little bit. I think for exhaustion that can stack beyond -5, at least i would let it. For running long distances why would you need to roll? If its a race its contested, if its time based do a flat X successes needed(possibly exstended).<br /> Stopping someone from bleeding out depends on the wound, with certain wounds simply being impossible to actually first aid like most internal wounds(You can apply pressure all you want, but you aren't doing it to the wound, since it's inside them), surgery would be required which is extended vs a target successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T01:23:35-07:00","id":1075042,"title":"","content":"I have something <a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/21304220/NLWC7b2bATEoDw3ZAVsLTA/max.jpg?1469554468\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Remember that you can apply multiple penalties to a single roll and exceed the -5 limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 04-08-2017, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:25:13-07:00","id":1075113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075042#post1075042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have something <a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/21304220/NLWC7b2bATEoDw3ZAVsLTA/max.jpg?1469554468\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Remember that you can apply multiple penalties to a single roll and exceed the -5 limit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, wow! Thanks! That cheatsheet looks useful for many things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T16:36:08-07:00","id":1075295,"title":"","content":"Soul Marks - are souls by RAW exclusive to human(ish) beings? Does Soul Marks give any info. if turned on a dog or deer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T18:09:08-07:00","id":1075316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075295#post1075295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Marks - are souls by RAW exclusive to human(ish) beings? Does Soul Marks give any info. if turned on a dog or deer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Animals might have souls by some gameline definition, but apparently not by the Mage definition. Soul like demon is one of those terms that's very common even though the things it's applied to might not have much else in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T18:41:13-07:00","id":1075317,"title":"","content":"The mage definition of souls only include human souls and awakened souls. The two types of souls that have an Oneiros and are connected to the Temenos. Soul Marks probably only applies to those kinds of souls. But being able to read the souls or soul equivalents of other creatures could be as easy as requiring a Reach and possibly adding another Arcanum (such as Spirit for werewolves, since they're half spirit). Exactly what kind of beings you could do that to would be up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:25:32-07:00","id":1075410,"title":"","content":"Only humans (and select exhuman beings) have souls as mage defines them; animals don't.<br /> <br /> Yes, animals appear within the soul of the world / anima mundi. Yes, mages are aware of this apparent contradiction. Most interested mages go for &quot;nonhuman life shares a communal spiritual element, which we can't perceive in the Fallen World because it surrounds us&quot; and Obsessed mages make plan about reaching other planets or lifeless Lower Depths to try to make external measurements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T03:26:09-07:00","id":1075426,"title":"","content":"Is there a repository of stuff that has been put out in Open Development, Kind of a One Stop Shop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T06:04:34-07:00","id":1075445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075410#post1075410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only humans (and select exhuman beings) have souls as mage defines them; animals don't.<br /> <br /> Yes, animals appear within the soul of the world / anima mundi. Yes, mages are aware of this apparent contradiction. Most interested mages go for &quot;nonhuman life shares a communal spiritual element, which we can't perceive in the Fallen World because it surrounds us&quot; and Obsessed mages make plan about reaching other planets or lifeless Lower Depths to try to make external measurements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what you said in another thread I'm wondering if the Tremere might actually be a good place to hunt down more information on this kind of thing since they're the soul experts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:07:12-07:00","id":1075462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075410#post1075410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only humans (and select exhuman beings) have souls as mage defines them; animals don't.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which &quot;select exhuman's qualify? I didn't realized werewolves etc., didn't have souls. What kind of info. does a mage get if he uses Soul Marks on a werewolf or something else that looks human but has no soul? Do they look like a normal human being suffering soul loss? Or do they just identify the creature immediately as non standard but not recognized?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:39:49-07:00","id":1075474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075462#post1075462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which &quot;select exhuman's qualify?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess archmasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:51:18-07:00","id":1075478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075462#post1075462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which &quot;select exhuman's qualify? I didn't realized werewolves etc., didn't have souls. What kind of info. does a mage get if he uses Soul Marks on a werewolf or something else that looks human but has no soul? Do they look like a normal human being suffering soul loss? Or do they just identify the creature immediately as non standard but not recognized?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have <i>something</i>, which comes about as a result of their bipartite natures, but they don't have a human soul. Death magic would probably reveal that something is hippity-jibbity where their soul <i>should be</i>, but it probably won't tell you more than that. Spirit, though, would likely be able to produce a Soul Marks type spell to avail you of more information about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T14:34:07-07:00","id":1075587,"title":"","content":"Hello, i have a question about Space 2 &quot;Break Boundary&quot;.<br /> The spell talks about Physical obstructions, then it says that the caster can slip through a roaring fire blocking the road ahead.<br /> <br /> Now, as I see it, fire is an energy which cannot be physically interacted with (aka, you can't grab it and manipulate), so the spell shouldn't work because it is not a real obstruction since, except for the possibly lethal fire damage, you could wade through.<br /> <br /> So, one of my players got surrounded by a cage made of lightning by an Obrimos and I did not let him pass through with the spell because of the aforementioned reason, did i do wrong? (noticed way later that the example in the description included fire)<br /> <br /> And, were he able to use the spell to get out, did his spell have to beat the Obrimos' spell potency, win a clash of wills or simply get out of jail free?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T14:45:03-07:00","id":1075590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075587#post1075587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, i have a question about Space 2 &quot;Break Boundary&quot;.<br /> The spell talks about Physical obstructions, then it says that the caster can slip through a roaring fire blocking the road ahead.<br /> <br /> Now, as I see it, fire is an energy which cannot be physically interacted with (aka, you can't grab it and manipulate), so the spell shouldn't work because it is not a real obstruction since, except for the possibly lethal fire damage, you could wade through.<br /> <br /> So, one of my players got surrounded by a cage made of lightning by an Obrimos and I did not let him pass through with the spell because of the aforementioned reason, did i do wrong? (noticed way later that the example in the description included fire)<br /> <br /> And, were he able to use the spell to get out, did his spell have to beat the Obrimos' spell potency, win a clash of wills or simply get out of jail free?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be an issue if the major issue with the space spell was Matter, but it isn't, its a short bit of Space. The Space spell doesn't care what you are blinking through cuz space is space, no matter what is occupying it. You can technically wade through a steel wall if you're the juggernaut too.<br /> <br /> If you need to keep your continuity, say that your Obrimos put a Spatial Ward on the lightning box. If the Obrimos already knows ahead that the person they're trying to trap is a mastigos (less obvious if the character in question isn't a mastigos and just had space 2 on-hand), then the Obrimos would know better than to use <i>just</i> a lightning cage.<br /> <br /> The lightning cage itself would not withstand or clash out the Break-Boundary spell, but the Obrimos using a Ward would provoke a clash of wills for sure. The precise target of Break Boundary isn't the lightning cage itself, but rather the space it is occupying. The spell also gets more versatile with the use of reach--as the base version lets you get through any obstruction you do not want to mess with, provided it blocks an actual, technical path--be it blocked by a window, fire, or you just do not want cob webs on your nice coat.<br /> <br /> After using reach you just laugh at space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:08:16-07:00","id":1075593,"title":"","content":"Obrimos could probably use Prime to weave a Platonic Idea of RAGE CAGE PERFECT PRISON NO ESCAPE into the construct, which would IMHO be symbolically enough to pose as a valid obstacle for Break Boundary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:08:22-07:00","id":1075594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075587#post1075587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, i have a question about Space 2 &amp;quot;Break Boundary&amp;quot;.<br /> The spell talks about Physical obstructions, then it says that the caster can slip through a roaring fire blocking the road ahead.<br /> <br /> Now, as I see it, fire is an energy which cannot be physically interacted with (aka, you can't grab it and manipulate), so the spell shouldn't work because it is not a real obstruction since, except for the possibly lethal fire damage, you could wade through.<br /> <br /> So, one of my players got surrounded by a cage made of lightning by an Obrimos and I did not let him pass through with the spell because of the aforementioned reason, did i do wrong? (noticed way later that the example in the description included fire)<br /> <br /> And, were he able to use the spell to get out, did his spell have to beat the Obrimos' spell potency, win a clash of wills or simply get out of jail free?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't grab fire, but you can still interact with it by getting burned. That's enough to qualify as physical. <br /> <br /> The rest is as Scarlet Witch said; the lightning cage does nothing, unless the enemy mage took preemptive measures specifically against Space magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:39:21-07:00","id":1075681,"title":"","content":"Has there been any direction as to what extent you can sculpt AoE spells? Line, cones, funnels, walls and so forth?<br /> Or is it always just one roughly spherical burst?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:45:30-07:00","id":1075686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075681#post1075681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any direction as to what extent you can sculpt AoE spells? Line, cones, funnels, walls and so forth?<br /> Or is it always just one roughly spherical burst?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943564#post943564\">Asked and answered roughly eight months ago</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:21:50-07:00","id":1075718,"title":"","content":"To be fair, 8 months is a long time on a topic with nearly 200 pages, and the search bar isn't always helpful.<br /> On that note...<br /> I thought I asked this before but I can't find it in this topic via the search bar. Dedicated Magical Tools do not stack do they? Specifically referring to pages 98 and 122. The yantra description very much wants you to only have a single dedicated tool, but Matters of the Soul makes it sound like you could possibly get more than one dedicated tool provided that the extras were your soul-stones--only 1 dedicated tool can be a previously-mundane-object.<br /> <br /> Course, that matters little if the -2 paradox dice do not stack. The benefit could just be geared more toward a split-second fix if your dedicated tool gets stolen or destroyed and you need a new one, or if you wanted back-ups. Which are viable ideas too.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could get more ideas from Tome of Mysteries but since it is 1E its kinda ST territory y'know? So what do some of you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:02:10-07:00","id":1075935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075590#post1075590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that would be an issue if the major issue with the space spell was Matter, but it isn't, its a short bit of Space. The Space spell doesn't care what you are blinking through cuz space is space, no matter what is occupying it. You can technically wade through a steel wall if you're the juggernaut too.<br /> <br /> If you need to keep your continuity, say that your Obrimos put a Spatial Ward on the lightning box. If the Obrimos already knows ahead that the person they're trying to trap is a mastigos (less obvious if the character in question isn't a mastigos and just had space 2 on-hand), then the Obrimos would know better than to use <i>just</i> a lightning cage.<br /> <br /> The lightning cage itself would not withstand or clash out the Break-Boundary spell, but the Obrimos using a Ward would provoke a clash of wills for sure. The precise target of Break Boundary isn't the lightning cage itself, but rather the space it is occupying. The spell also gets more versatile with the use of reach--as the base version lets you get through any obstruction you do not want to mess with, provided it blocks an actual, technical path--be it blocked by a window, fire, or you just do not want cob webs on your nice coat.<br /> <br /> After using reach you just laugh at space.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer, that clarified it. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd have another question regarding Time 3 Acceleration: the description says that those under the spell's effect can move up to the multiplied speed.<br /> Does this mean any of the following?<br /> <br /> 1 - You can modulate the effect, going at normal speed or maximum speed when you want, changing it reflexively (i guess).<br /> 2 - You are always at set multiplied speed and, thus, attracting unwanted sleeper attention is unavoidable.<br /> 3 - Other mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:17:41-07:00","id":1075944,"title":"","content":"Is there a pre-existing resource for handling Spirits and the Spirit Arcanum as a storyteller beyond what's the in the 2E core sourcebook?<ul><li>How to incorporate Spirits into every setting (planning ahead)</li> <li>How to adjudicate unexpected uses of Spirit by creative players (rules of thumb for what's reasonable and what isn't)</li> </ul>The material for Spirit feels a little abstract and unintuitive for me to handle consistently. I'd love it someone could point me to a play-book or blog post or something from a ST who has it down pat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:18:23-07:00","id":1075945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075935#post1075935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have another question regarding Time 3 Acceleration: the description says that those under the spell's effect can move up to the multiplied speed.<br /> Does this mean any of the following?<br /> <br /> 1 - You can modulate the effect, going at normal speed or maximum speed when you want, changing it reflexively (i guess).<br /> 2 - You are always at set multiplied speed and, thus, attracting unwanted sleeper attention is unavoidable.<br /> 3 - Other mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to ask the same!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13208-babbaleo","name":"Babbaleo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:45:44-07:00","id":1075962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075935#post1075935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd have another question regarding Time 3 Acceleration: the description says that those under the spell's effect can move up to the multiplied speed.<br /> Does this mean any of the following?<br /> <br /> 1 - You can modulate the effect, going at normal speed or maximum speed when you want, changing it reflexively (i guess).<br /> 2 - You are always at set multiplied speed and, thus, attracting unwanted sleeper attention is unavoidable.<br /> 3 - Other mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the &quot;up to&quot; qualifier. It says &quot;Multiply the subject\u2019s Speed by Potency.&quot; I'm looking in 2E. Spell factors are determined at casting time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:59:28-07:00","id":1075966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075962#post1075962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see the &quot;up to&quot; qualifier. It says &quot;Multiply the subject\u2019s Speed by Potency.&quot; I'm looking in 