iner\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075966#post1075966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have to agree with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but since it is Speed and not speed, like in Velocity Control, I would think that you can control it just as precisely as you can your normal, unaccelerated Speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:21:32-07:00","id":1075983,"title":"","content":"I since it is controlled by potency and potency is set then it is also set. So I respectfully disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:46:53-07:00","id":1076004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075962#post1075962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see the &quot;up to&quot; qualifier. It says &quot;Multiply the subject\u2019s Speed by Potency.&quot; I'm looking in 2E. Spell factors are determined at casting time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh lol, it's true. I must have misread it :O<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:49:28-07:00","id":1076005,"title":"","content":"Basically I could slow walk but I would still have slow walk speed x potency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13208-babbaleo","name":"Babbaleo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:08:37-07:00","id":1076023,"title":"","content":"It will still look unnatural to sleepers, which is the main thrust of the question. Really, try to walk with your normal form but three times slower. It's hard to judge how fast to move, and it's more tiring because you have to stand on one leg with the other extended for much longer. If you encounter a sleeper, just end the effect early and recast later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:42:01-07:00","id":1076050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076023#post1076023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will still look unnatural to sleepers</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I wasn't trying to say that, walking Benny Hill style IT'S obvious magic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13208-babbaleo","name":"Babbaleo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:42:22-07:00","id":1076079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076023#post1076023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will still look unnatural to sleepers, which is the main thrust of the question. Really, try to walk with your normal form but three times slower. It's hard to judge how fast to move, and it's more tiring because you have to stand on one leg with the other extended for much longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, I didn't think about it that way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:51:13-07:00","id":1076085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075944#post1075944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a pre-existing resource for handling Spirits and the Spirit Arcanum as a storyteller beyond what's the in the 2E core sourcebook?<ul><li>How to incorporate Spirits into every setting (planning ahead)</li> <li>How to adjudicate unexpected uses of Spirit by creative players (rules of thumb for what's reasonable and what isn't)</li> </ul>The material for Spirit feels a little abstract and unintuitive for me to handle consistently. I'd love it someone could point me to a play-book or blog post or something from a ST who has it down pat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of Spirits, it's 1e and doesn't touch much on Mages interacting with spirits but it helps, also Forsaken 2e probably has a lot of info on spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:29:00-07:00","id":1076113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075944#post1075944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a pre-existing resource for handling Spirits and the Spirit Arcanum as a storyteller beyond what's the in the 2E core sourcebook?<ul><li>How to incorporate Spirits into every setting (planning ahead)</li> <li>How to adjudicate unexpected uses of Spirit by creative players (rules of thumb for what's reasonable and what isn't)</li> </ul><br /> The material for Spirit feels a little abstract and unintuitive for me to handle consistently. I'd love it someone could point me to a play-book or blog post or something from a ST who has it down pat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the purviews in the Spirit Arcanum section and you will get a sense for what Spirit can cover.<br /> <br /> My own advice is to remember that spirits are omnipresent but also follow a kind of path of least resistance. Most spirits are little more than animals and don't have grand plans or thoughtful schemes. They influence the world, but they do so by perpetuating and strengthening resonances, rather than by possessing people or deliberately scheming. Now, don't get me wrong, those things also definitely happen, but they're the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br /> For example of how this works, and how important Resonance is as a concept, consider the following scenario:<br /> <br /> You are out hiking in the forest in winter, when suddenly a storm you didn't prepare for picks up and blankets the area in frigid winds and deep snow and you totally lose your way. Seeking shelter, you stumble across an old log cabin and decide it's better to shelter there and wait for the storm to pass rather than risk freezing to death. You light a fire in an old iron stove and find an old bed. Snuggling up under your emergency blanket, you settle in for the night.<br /> <br /> Now, we consider a divergence. In one scenario, the cabin has Resonances of warmth and comfort. In another, it has Resonances of isolation and desolation.<br /> <br /> In the former case, when you settle into the cabin, you'll hear winds whistling outside and the crackle of the fire and feel strangely cozy; like the cabin is a fortress and you're safely secure from the natural dangers outside. It's oddly peaceful and serene and you enjoy an evening with your thoughts. Then, outside the window, you spot the shape of a stranger approaching. They come to the door and bang their fist upon it.<br /> <br /> In the latter case, when you settle into the cabin, you can practically hear the holes in the old sealing; the shriek of wind as it slips through and bites at any skin you have exposed. The fire feels low and barely radiates heat more than a few feet, no matter how much fuel you give it, and the cabin itself feels like a solid gust might simply save the storm the trouble of freezing you and bring a roof down on you instead. You can't sleep, because you feel utterly alone and terrified that your end is coming. And then, from the darkness, a stranger approaches the cabin. Raising their fist and smashing it against the door.<br /> <br /> Nothing materially has changed here. But in the former scenario, you're more likely to assume it's a wayward traveler, like yourself, in need of shelter, and not a threat for which you should ready your gun.<br /> <br /> That's how spirits affect the world. They take resonances like that and they amplify them; strengthening them; feeding on the essence they produce in a constant feedback loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:27:56-07:00","id":1076149,"title":"","content":"Thank you both! Didn't know about that book; I'll check it out.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly having trouble putting a box around what Spirit magic can and cannot do.<br /> <br /> Coaxing the Spirit for example seems like it can duplicate the effects of any Compelling spell and some Ruling spells from Life (applied to animals), Matter, or Forces. For example, compare the description of Coaxing the Spirit to the description of Control Instincts -- there's clearly strong overlap in capability.<br /> <br /> Command Spirit seems like it can for-sure duplicate the effects of any Ruling spell from Life (animals), Matter, or Forces.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the book has some concrete guidance or vignette examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:36:30-07:00","id":1076156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076149#post1076149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you both! Didn't know about that book; I'll check it out.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly having trouble putting a box around what Spirit magic can and cannot do.<br /> <br /> Coaxing the Spirit for example seems like it can duplicate the effects of any Compelling spell and some Ruling spells from Life (applied to animals), Matter, or Forces. For example, compare the description of Coaxing the Spirit to the description of Control Instincts -- there's clearly strong overlap in capability.<br /> <br /> Command Spirit seems like it can for-sure duplicate the effects of any Ruling spell from Life (animals), Matter, or Forces.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the book has some concrete guidance or vignette examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Coaxing the Spirits only work to amplify existing stuff. Which is largely Compelling territory. Making a scared animal bolt for it, or attack firsthand. Making an open fire burn a bit brighter. More overt things that would arguably be Ruling, like shaping fire into dazzling shapes or making a perfectly tame animal frenzy in panic, would still fall under Ruling spells of their respective Arcanum. <br /> <br /> Command Spirit looks nice on paper, but remember you need a spirit to affect. Which might not even exist yet, if the phenomena you're trying to target is brand new or just weak. The spirit might also be on the other side of the Gauntlet, since most spirits can't cross at will. This means the spell is Withstood by local Gauntlet Strength. Even after that, there's still the narrative factors of spirits not being fond of fleshy mortals bossing them around and potentially holdih a grudge, and the Storyteller being comfortable with including spirits in the game in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:52:48-07:00","id":1076164,"title":"","content":"Something to remember is that most physical objects have a spirit in them, but it's a very weak and quiescent spirit. That's the basis of Coaxing the Spirits, which lets you do things like make doors open or engines start or guns jam, or what have you, because these are all things within the purview of the spirit of the object and something that could reasonably be affected by said spirit were it active. You're essentially casting a spell to tell the spirit of that object to use its Influence on that object.<br /> <br /> The thing about that power is that it doesn't actually scale up, because the target is ultimately the same weak spirit. So, for example, a casting of Coaxing the Spirits could make a burning flame move in a given direction or grow more intense, but a Spirit Ruling spell couldn't command it to go out. Likewise, a Spirit Ruling spell couldn't make water run uphill. The spell is still targeting the same weak spirits and they don't get stronger just because you have.<br /> <br /> Spirit's a very powerful arcanum, though. In no small part because it's the <i>only</i> one that can move essence, regardless of the type of entity involved (though you need dots in the relevant arcanum to affect entities other than Shadow spirits). That means that Thyrsus are in a unique position to bargain with alien entities, regardless of type. A Thyrsus can snatch essence from Resonant Conditions and feed it to their pet spirit pretty much as much and as often as they want, which makes them unmatched for chiminage.<br /> <br /> Likewise, while big and powerful spirits are rare, small and weak ones are common, and most anything you could care to find is available somewhere. A Disciple or Adept of Spirit can, with relatively little effort, gather up an obedient servant that most other Mages can't even detect, yet alone effect, before even considering how powerful such things are compared to Sleepers. Even a Rank 1 spirit with the right Manifestations or Numina is a world-class thief.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Really, Spirit is a fairly potent arcanum. The only real question is how unWise your player(s) (is/are) willing to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:44:44-07:00","id":1076201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076164#post1076164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to remember is that most physical objects have a spirit in them, but it's a very weak and quiescent spirit. </div> </div> </div> </div>Going off on a tangent - it just occurs to me that based on the abilities of Spriit 1, and the description of the spirits, it seems all these numberless quiescent spirits are on the material side of the gauntlet. Are spirits actually born in the material world and then shift into shadow as they awaken?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:51:56-07:00","id":1076206,"title":"","content":"Uuugh I looove spirit. But it doesn't seem like ST's care much for the arcanum or down-right hate it. I thought it would get better when I tried to get a werewolf game started and play as a mage, but then it became about forsaken vs pure and then the spiritual landscape just disappeared from thought.<br /> <br /> But hey! I've got two cents to spend on the Acceleration spell thing.<br /> I can understand having difficulty controlling your speed if you are using forces or space, but why Time? Isn't the shtick that you are slowing down time slightly except for yourself? So you'd be able to control your speed just fine, what you're not controlling is the illusion of your speed cuz how much you are affecting time is set. So you're not at risk of losing control of how fast you are going, but you are going to need to recast the spell if you do not want time to be moving as slowly. The spell does seem to care about concentration. I think it is one of those strange instances where a spell is still very similar to a previous one but given more powerful effects simply because it is a different practice, like how if you want gross control of a lifeform you need life 4 and not just life 2, as opposed to Mind 2's control just requiring reach...<br /> <br /> but I do freaking love the spirit arcanum. If I may, I think there are two arcanum that are pretty much double-edged sword, catch-all types, which will get varying amounts of ire out of your ST because their nature is able to get things done the other arcana are better suited or more appropriate for.<br /> Those are Fate and Spirit. However, they <i>are</i> double-edged swords. If you want to start a storm, the appropriate arcanum is Forces. However, if your ST is okay with it, I personally see a lot of justification for Fate and Spirit being able to cause storms too. The problem is in the details, and I think that's why it is a problem for ST's and their players. Players want their spells to get the effects they want as soon as possible, and ST's want to further the plot.<br /> A Fated storm is going to take longer to show up than one made with Forces, or it may appear under very different amounts of control or purpose than your Forces storm would. You asked Fate, and Fate delivered, but it does so under <i>its</i> terms, not that of your Imago, unlike the Forces version.<br /> Spirit has the same issue, except it would work faster, cuz it uses another creature(s) magic. The storm may happen much faster, but it is going to come under the terms of the creature who you compelled/asked/bribed to make the storm. The next issue is that all your spirit-magic is going to involve you in the vicious, feudal politics of the Shadow. Unless you're prepared to maneuver that delicately, or are already in a position to, as Axelgear said, be unWise and just be a Shadow-tyrant yourself, all your spirit spells are going to build yourself a dangerous reputation with other powerful Shadow monstrosities.<br /> <br /> So Fate can get almost anything you need done, but it will require a lot of grease, a little more effort from you, and may not show up the way you wanted it to, or take significantly longer to produce results.<br /> Spirit will get almost anything you want done quickly, but its going to come with a lot of Shadow-related baggage as you entrench yourself deeper into an alien world's doings and goings-on.<br /> <br /> And these are the reasons why those arcana are both frustrating, and very fun. But they can also feel like cheating to some people. If your ST lets you make fetishes like crazy you're going to have an armory of paradox-free spirit-magic, and that's just unfair to other players.<br /> Unless the ST arranges for something to go disastrously wrong for your cache and you fail to protect it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Wouldn't it be awful if you, say, pissed off the Seers of the Throne or the Guardians for using Quiescence-free magic in public using fetishes, and they just so happened to tip off a tribe of Pure-werewolves with a powerful totem that would just <i>love</i> to have a new slave/pet-mage. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:30:16-07:00","id":1076284,"title":"","content":"Spirit's a great arcanum, but it requires you to remember the presence of an entire spiritual ecosystem. That's an extra hassle on the ST sometimes. Me, personally, I love it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076201#post1076201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going off on a tangent - it just occurs to me that based on the abilities of Spriit 1, and the description of the spirits, it seems all these numberless quiescent spirits are on the material side of the gauntlet. Are spirits actually born in the material world and then shift into shadow as they awaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a big ol' Maybe. In all likelihood, though, probably not. Spirits of objects rarely awaken. Instead, you get concentrations of resonances in a region sustained for long enough that the essence coalescing in the Shadow forms into a spirit.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Shadow isn't Twilight but nor is it another world, totally disconnected from ours. The Shadow is, to our plane of existence, as the layer of dust coating everything in our world is to us; it holds a similar, recognizable shape, but is ultimately of an entirely separate nature and composition. So whatever happens to one makes echoes in the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:01:36-07:00","id":1076300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075962#post1075962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see the &quot;up to&quot; qualifier. It says &quot;Multiply the subject\u2019s Speed by Potency.&quot; I'm looking in 2E. Spell factors are determined at casting time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont see the &quot;up to &quot; qualifier in the normal speed description either. <i>&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:EscalidoGothico\">Movement<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> take an instant action. He can give up his action to move at<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">double his normal Speed.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot; </i>so that means everybody always moves their exact speed and cant go slower right too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:32:16-07:00","id":1076312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076300#post1076300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont see the &quot;up to &quot; qualifier in the normal speed description either. <i>&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:EscalidoGothico\">Movement<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> take an instant action. He can give up his action to move at<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">double his normal Speed.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot; </i>so that means everybody always moves their exact speed and cant go slower right too?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what they meant was that you can control your speed, but you can't control what the potency of the spell is doing to your spell after the fact.<br /> <br /> But again, I think that the Time spell isn't a spell you lose control over. You're not going to go flying into a wall because from the caster's perspective, the world will be slowing down, instead of them speeding up out of control. The character can control their own speed from their own perspective, but they cannot control how it will appear. If your potency is giving you 3x speed, you will seem to be going 3x faster than you think you are to all observers, period. That's what I think, and I think it works well.<br /> <br /> A space equivalent though probably definitely would send you plowing through a wall if you're going too fast to control what you're doing, but in that scenario instead of altering time, you're traveling several steps further for each step you take, so your perception will have to keep up with your actions. In Acceleration, since it is time based, your perception matches your speed so you can just take a casual walk and everyone else will see you zipping around. If not, then, well, you could probably just Reach for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:39:13-07:00","id":1076336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1075935#post1075935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the answer, that clarified it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd have another question regarding Time 3 Acceleration: the description says that those under the spell's effect can move up to the multiplied speed.<br /> Does this mean any of the following?<br /> <br /> 1 - You can modulate the effect, going at normal speed or maximum speed when you want, changing it reflexively (i guess).<br /> 2 - You are always at set multiplied speed and, thus, attracting unwanted sleeper attention is unavoidable.<br /> 3 - Other mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>So while spell factors are locked on casting remember mages can lower potency anytime during the duration.<br /> <br /> I think there are two ways to do this, either while under the effects of the spell it'll always cause dissonance even when travelling at your former non magic speed, or that it only looks magical if you go at speeds over your normal. Using the dodge effect or using defence vs firearms will always look like Neo/agents dodging bullets tho and obviously be magical. Maybe always going first also qualifies as this spell looks odd/magical all the time??<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:48:01-07:00","id":1076340,"title":"","content":"Oh gosh, I forgot about the lowering potency after the spell is cast thing. I don't think you can bring it back up to the original value though. Was that only in 1E or is that in 2E again? I forget and I was unable to find it just now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:49:38-07:00","id":1076341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076340#post1076340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh gosh, I forgot about the lowering potency after the spell is cast thing. I don't think you can bring it back up to the original value though. Was that only in 1E or is that in 2E again? I forget and I was unable to find it just now...</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only lower spell factors after casting yep not increase them. Was in 1e too but you couldnt increase em in 1e either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:39:21-07:00","id":1076480,"title":"","content":"Are there any legacies (published or fan made) which specialize in healing spells? I can't imagine mages not inventing one (even if they do end up hunted by Seers), but I haven't found any that seemed related","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T08:21:15-07:00","id":1076501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076480#post1076480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any legacies (published or fan made) which specialize in healing spells? I can't imagine mages not inventing one (even if they do end up hunted by Seers), but I haven't found any that seemed related</div> </div> </div> </div>Tamers of Rivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:17:36-07:00","id":1076567,"title":"","content":"Tamers of Rivers are just the best. I actually did a conversion for them for 2e, because my Thyrsus is trying to join that Legacy. It ended up structured as follows:<br /> <br /> All primary attainments require Matter. All secondary attainments require Life.<br /> <br /> <b>1st Attainment: Revealing the Obstruction</b><br /> <br /> The Traveler's eyes are open at last, and she sees the flowing of the rivers of energies through all things. She can see their clarity with uncanny perfection; sensing any distortion in their flow as clearly as she might see a wall in front of her.<br /> <br /> This attainment functions as Discern Composition, though it only works on a liquid or predominantly liquid substance (i.e. wet sludge oozing out of a factory's run-off drain would trigger it, but a pile of mud would not). It activates reflexively when the Mage encounters any sort of liquid, and communicates its composition directly. While the Mage doesn't know the scientific terms of the substances within the solution (unless they have sufficient Science or Medicine dots to suggest that they are), they get a general sense of the &quot;meaning&quot; of the solution. That is, a seemingly pure stream contaminated with heavy metals will register to a Traveler as unsafe to drink, regardless of if they're aware of the dangers of heavy metal poisoning or even that such a thing as heavy metals exist.<br /> <br /> In case it isn't obvious, this attainment means it's near-impossible to poison a Tamer's drink. Even poisons in their food become instantly noticeable once the mouthful mixes with their saliva.<br /> <br /> <u>Optional Attainment:</u> The Unifying Truth<br /> <br /> The Rivers - the waters - are a metaphor which is also true. As the Traveler can see the flow of water in the living world, they can see the flow of live in the waters of the body.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles Analyze Life. Unlike the previous attainment, it is not <i>usually</i> automatic. In most cases, to properly analyze someone's health, the Tamer must touch the subject's forehead to feel the heat of their blood or examine the colour of their urine or otherwise take a moment to get a sense of the flows of the person's body.<br /> <br /> The special exception to this is extreme illnesses and the undead. If a person carries a severe and potentially fatal illness, or one that is in any way supernatural, the Traveler's senses pick them out instantly. Something about the rasping breathing or the faint sheen of sweat tips them off. Likewise, the undead stand out because they <i>aren't</i> alive; like a bubble in an otherwise empty sea, they stand apart. Tamers recognize them on sight.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Attainment: </b><b>Dowsing the Depths</b><br /> <br /> The Traveler's senses expand. One does not need to <i>see</i> the River to know its presence; one can hear it; one can smell it; one can taste it. The scenery changes before one ever sees the waters, as life draws deep from its source.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles Detect Substance, but it may only target liquids. It has the Instant and Advanced Duration Reach effects applied. One unique characteristic of this attainment is that bodily fluids are an acceptable target of the spell, provided the Mage also has Life 1 (as just about every Traveler does). Said fluids do not need to be <i>outside</i> the body to be targeted, either, meaning that this spell can allow the Mage to, say, detect a hiding person through a wall.<br /> <br /> <u>Optional Attainment:</u> Purifying the River Within<br /> <br /> The Tamers of Rivers command the waters of life, just as they are commanded by them. This attainment starts within, and then, gradually, moves without.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles Purge Illness with the Instant Reach effect applied. The Tamer can technically apply this effect with nothing but a touch, but many choose to perform some kind of washing ritual with it, like a baptism, to wash away the sickness.<br /> <br /> This attainment activates reflexively any time the Tamer is exposed to a contagion. For this reason, none of them ever seem to be sick.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd Attainment: Commanding the Waters</b><br /> <br /> The Tamer truly begins to <i>tame</i>. With this level of progress, the Tamer has become one with the waters enough that her will is its will. She bends and the River bends with her.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles Shaping, with the Instant and Sensory Range Reach effects applied. It may only effect liquids (surprise), but once waters are shaped by this attainment, they hold the shape given to them. Such shapes have a Structure of 1 (it isn't hard to break water) but a Durability equal to the Mage's dots in Matter.<br /> <br /> This attainment's Duration resets automatically every turn the Mage is in contact with the liquid in question. Yes, this means Travelers can walk on water.<br /> <br /> <u>Optional Attainment:</u> Flesh as Water<br /> <br /> A miraculous property of water is that it cannot be broken. Run it through with a knife and it does not notice. Scatter droplets on a sizzling rock and they shall turn to vapour, condense as clouds, fall as rain, and become the River once more. Water is an eternal and contiguous whole. By practicing this truth, the Tamers can perform their most famous miracles: The sealing of flesh, as water.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles Knit, with the Instant Reach effect. Tamers are able to extend the effects of this spell further, applying any one of the Reach effects listed with the spell (restoring Lethal instead of Bashing; healing Personal Tilts; undoing deprivation; reproducing a full night's rest). However, doing so costs a point of Mana and inflicts a point of Resistant Bashing damage on the Traveler, as exerting the level of &quot;force&quot; required mangles their own flows of living energy. Multiple effects may be applied at once but the cost must be paid for each, to a maximum of 4 Mana and 4 Resistant Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>4th Attainment: Reshape the Vessel</b><br /> <br /> The River is all things and all things are the River. The Traveler passes through their limited understanding of what it is to be as liquid and emerges on the other side, transformed. After all, are not all things transitory? All shapes merely the latest mask worn by every piece of the cosmos through time and space? Every droplet of water has been in the sea; the sky; the earth; the body; the soul. It has been stone and ice and flesh and blood and everything else. The Traveler need only remind it of its birthright.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles State Change, with the Instant and Advanced Duration Reach effects. The Traveler may touch any solid object and convert it into a liquid state. Once it is in its liquid state, it may be commanded with a spell, or with the Commanding the Waters attainment. As with that attainment, the Duration automatically resets so long as the Traveler is in contact with the substance in question. Once the effect wears off, it retains whatever shape it held before.<br /> <br /> This attainment may also be used to target water, turning it into one of its many solid forms or directly into vapour.<br /> <br /> <u>Optional Attainment:</u> Into New Wineskins<br /> <i>Special Prerequisite: This optional attainment requires the Long-Shifting Merit.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> What the Traveler does for objects, she may also do for herself. Her flesh is as mutable as the world around it, and it answers her will as surely as the waters of the River.<br /> <br /> This attainment resembles Shapechanging. It may only target the Traveler herself, and has both the Instant and Advanced Duration (thanks to the Long-Shifting merit) Reach effects applied. Since this attainment requires Matter 4 anyway, the Mage has the option of their gear changing to fit her new form, or simply blending into her flesh.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> That's all of the attainments. I never made a fifth because it didn't seem likely the game would make it to Gnosis 8.<br /> <br /> The prerequisites for joining were changed to needing Empathy 2 and at least one dot in both Medicine and Occult. The third attainment requires Empathy 3 and Medicine at least at 2.<br /> <br /> Oblations are unchanged, as is the method of initiation. You die so that you can be reborn, by drowning in the river and becoming one with the source of all things.<br /> <br /> Legacy Yantras: Washing a wound or ailment mark (+1); immersion, particularly in flowing water (+1, or +2 if this inflicts a nasty Tilt); succeeding on an Empathy roll to understand the target's emotional state (+1); taking ego-suppressing drugs like LSD (+2, so long as the adverse effects aren't suppressed).<br /> <br /> Naturally, Tamers also have a lot of associated sacrament and environment yantras; things like sacred pools, water from holy springs, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T14:47:11-07:00","id":1076666,"title":"","content":"Arcana Attainments. How do you get them? The Orders teach you? You need to pay exp for them?<br /> <br /> On the Exp table there are Legacy Attainment costs, but nothing about Arcana Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T15:25:08-07:00","id":1076677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076666#post1076666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcana Attainments. How do you get them? The Orders teach you? You need to pay exp for them?<br /> <br /> On the Exp table there are Legacy Attainment costs, but nothing about Arcana Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you have the requisite level of an arcanum, you have the appropriate Arcanum attainment. Once you reach Death 2 for instance, ghosts lurking in twilight start to ping your peripheral mage sight. Its pretty much instinctive.<br /> <br /> Edit: Upon re-reading, it does say the orders instruct you on how to use them, but I still read that to mean you don't pay for them, the orders (or whoever you have to teach you) just helps advise you on them.<br /> <br /> From the book:<br /> &quot; the instruction bears more resemblance<br /> to conditioning in athletics or fundamental principles<br /> in mathematics.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 04-11-2017, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T16:00:23-07:00","id":1076687,"title":"","content":"Arcana attainment seems to be pretty much automatic mechanically speaking. I think there was some hint that it might be possible to develop more arcana attainments and that the list in the book isn't actually exhaustive. I'd make those the endpoint of an Obsession and charge 1 AXP to develop it, but it could then be passed on to future students. It would make sense for instance for an Adept of Space to be able to reflexively CoW with any power that attempts to manipulate or use one of their Sympathetic connections or for an Adept of Time to reflexively CoW with any incidental change to their past instead of increasing Scale or decreasing casting time for a mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T17:09:37-07:00","id":1076716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076567#post1076567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tamers of Rivers are just the best. I actually did a conversion for them for 2e, because my Thyrsus is trying to join that Legacy. It ended up structured as follows:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This I could use for my next (well, next of next) Legacy conversion... Thanks for sharing in advance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Never mind, found how Abyssals work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-11-2017, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T20:30:23-07:00","id":1076776,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the referral, all. I'm not sure why I missed that Legacy. Actually, it works amazingly well for the PC I'm shopping for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076716#post1076716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This I could use for my next (well, next of next) Legacy conversion... Thanks for sharing in advance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be very interested to see your take on it as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:11:29-07:00","id":1076924,"title":"","content":"So, uh, another Shifting Sands question.<br /> <br /> I have no soul. I have Death 3 and Time 3. I'm very sad. I reap a Soul of a sleeper. I'm not sad anymore. I put it into myself using Soul Jar and it's 2 Reach + 1 Mana option. I shifting sands myself to round before I reaped the sleeper Soul.<br /> <br /> Am I a happy reaper or am I unhappy reaper? Or, more straightforward, did I just eat a soul without eating a soul?<br /> <br /> Take two:<br /> <br /> I have a soul. My friend has no soul. He is unhappy. I am happy. I have Death 3 and Time 3. I Sever Soul of a random Sleeper, put it into my friend using Soul Jar and it's 2reach+mana option, and then Shifting Sands my friend to a moment before I Sever Souled the sleeper. Is my friend soulless or is he happily soulfull?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:47:41-07:00","id":1076938,"title":"","content":"The answer to both questions is that the soul is now a part of you and, when you cast Shifting Sands, it's affected by the spell in the same way you are. Just as you go back in time and find that there's no second you waiting for it, it does the same.<br /> <br /> In other words, no, there's no ability to duplicate souls here. In the first scenario, you go back in time and the Sleeper's soul vanishes from them at the moment of your arrival, from their perspective. In the second scenario, same story.<br /> <br /> Now, does this have to be the way it works? Of course not. You could have fun with this and make a Mystery out of it. Maybe, instead of vanishing retroactively, the Sleeper has a kind of temporal ghost of their soul. It looks like a soul, but it's fluxed to hell with Time magic and, as soon as the time comes when it would have been harvested, it vanishes.<br /> <br /> Naturally, your curious Reaper might then start experimenting with this; reaping people's souls, then hopping back a few minutes to watch the process. Maybe simultaneously examining the soul in the soul jar while this happens; examining Time and Space sympathies, etc.<br /> <br /> And what happens when you try detaching a temporally stuttered soul and cast a Time Shielding spell on it? What happens if you then put that soul back in the Sleeper?<br /> <br /> Before you know it, a small coastal town is being destroyed by an enormous tornado, there's two moons in the sky, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:49:43-07:00","id":1076939,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, I will run a mage game, but i'm with some trouble to understand &quot;The Symbols&quot;. When a mage cast a magic he needs to build a imago and support this imago with his knowledge of the Arcana and the symbols of her Path, but how does this symbols work? Then a Thyrsus can only do his magic if he put some shaman way to do it?<br /> <br /> Can someone give me a exemple?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:00:05-07:00","id":1076945,"title":"","content":"Imagine that you are writing a code to do a specific thing, and your each Watchtower gives you slightly different language to work with.<br /> <br /> Or that you are trying to solve a math problem, but depending on your Watchtower, you get to work with different symbols and operations.<br /> <br /> Or imagine that you are trying to write a short story, and each language poses different opportunities and challenges to your writing process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:12:29-07:00","id":1076953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1076938#post1076938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer to both questions is that the soul is now a part of you and, when you cast Shifting Sands, it's affected by the spell in the same way you are. Just as you go back in time and find that there's no second you waiting for it, it does the same.<br /> <br /> In other words, no, there's no ability to duplicate souls here. In the first scenario, you go back in time and the Sleeper's soul vanishes from them at the moment of your arrival, from their perspective. In the second scenario, same story.<br /> <br /> Now, does this have to be the way it works? Of course not. You could have fun with this and make a Mystery out of it. Maybe, instead of vanishing retroactively, the Sleeper has a kind of temporal ghost of their soul. It looks like a soul, but it's fluxed to hell with Time magic and, as soon as the time comes when it would have been harvested, it vanishes.<br /> <br /> Naturally, your curious Reaper might then start experimenting with this; reaping people's souls, then hopping back a few minutes to watch the process. Maybe simultaneously examining the soul in the soul jar while this happens; examining Time and Space sympathies, etc.<br /> <br /> And what happens when you try detaching a temporally stuttered soul and cast a Time Shielding spell on it? What happens if you then put that soul back in the Sleeper?<br /> <br /> Before you know it, a small coastal town is being destroyed by an enormous tornado, there's two moons in the sky, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I missed that, sorry! I didn't mean to ignore you.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> <br /> What if I steal a soul from a baby<br /> that's about to born<br /> and then go back to from before it's born<br /> is it born soulless<br /> ???????????????????????????????????????????<br /> <br /> <br /> ...BABY SOUL REAPER antics always give me a headache.<br /> Though, shouldn't that argument be extended to other things? Like, if I steal mana from you and then go back, should the mana of current you suddenly evaporate and end up in my hands?<br /> Imagine: I'm a Time Wizard Lord of Consilium. I get my Mana Tax from my delicious Consilium members. I eat it all, and then I Shifting Sands to a week ago, cackling madly trying to see what happens with all the mana I ate in the future that tries to un-replicate in the current present.<br /> <br /> ...I think SHIFTING BABY SANDS cause worse headaches that BABY SOUL REAPERS.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> <br /> ...what if I have donated organs/ate someone/went Revolver Ocelot and grafted myself a new hand/stuff and then Shifting SanNNNNNNNNNNOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO MY HEAD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T04:42:41-07:00","id":1077636,"title":"","content":"So, about Legacy Attainments. They're developed from spells, so excluding the special qualities of Attainments (Free from the Lie, Immunity to Dissonance/Dispellation, Transient Stacking, etc), they should work like spells. I asked something similar before regarding if Attainments can be aimed/thrown. The answer was yes.<br /> <br /> However, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> reminds me that Legacy Attainments are developed from not just normal spells, but Praxes. So, does this mean that Legacy Attainments also achieve exceptional success on three successes? And if so, since Legacy Attainments score automatic successes equal to the mage's Arcanum dots when required, does this mean that Disciples and above always get exceptional successes on their Attainments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:21:55-07:00","id":1077642,"title":"","content":"The rules don't say, but I don't think I'd allow attainments the option to grant WP, Mana, or Conditions that grant Arcane Beats, but I think I would allow the bypass of Withstand after the Mage hits arcana 3 which would give attainments a highly prized niche ability on a very select range of abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:38:48-07:00","id":1077652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077636#post1077636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, about Legacy Attainments. They're developed from spells, so excluding the special qualities of Attainments (Free from the Lie, Immunity to Dissonance/Dispellation, Transient Stacking, etc), they should work like spells. I asked something similar before regarding if Attainments can be aimed/thrown. The answer was yes.<br /> <br /> However, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> reminds me that Legacy Attainments are developed from not just normal spells, but Praxes. So, does this mean that Legacy Attainments also achieve exceptional success on three successes? And if so, since Legacy Attainments score automatic successes equal to the mage's Arcanum dots when required, does this mean that Disciples and above always get exceptional successes on their Attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me double-up on this one! Can this result in someone piercing a defender's Withstand?<br /> <br /> edit: eek, nevermind. well, actually, maybe, I guess does anyone have any second opinions ontop of mrmdubois?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:44:56-07:00","id":1077655,"title":"","content":"The clause about the number of successes on activation is for other powers that mess with that. I know of a couple that minus successes from another power, or simple override other abilities if they have more successes. That would be the case when that comes into play. Since you aren't actually rolling you can't get an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:48:01-07:00","id":1077658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077642#post1077642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules don't say, but I don't think I'd allow attainments the option to grant WP, Mana, or Conditions that grant Arcane Beats, but I think I would allow the bypass of Withstand after the Mage hits arcana 3 which would give attainments a highly prized niche ability on a very select range of abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that certainly would make Legacies worth investing past 1st Attainment, which not being a case leads to an awkward situation for us right now. Almost &quot;anything an Attainment can do, spellcasting can do better&quot;, so no one is interested in initiating deeper than frontloaded non attainment benefits. Could you elaborate about consequences of such ruling, so I can meditate upon homeruling it this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:55:17-07:00","id":1077664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077658#post1077658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that certainly would make Legacies worth investing past 1st Attainment, which not being a case leads to an awkward situation for us right now. Almost &quot;anything an Attainment can do, spellcasting can do better&quot;, so no one is interested in initiating deeper than frontloaded non attainment benefits. Could you elaborate about consequences of such ruling, so I can meditate upon homeruling it this way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it means that Potency is going to matter -way- less for attainments that would otherwise have to contend with Withstand so attainments could focus more on switching valuable secondary factors to primary. So psychic domination for instance would become a good long term ability because Withstand is ignored. I'd assume mental protection abilities would still grant a CoW, but yeah you'd be a serious threat to the unprotected. Disciples would absolutely dominate various ephemerals for long periods of time unless directly contradicting their natures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:12:21-07:00","id":1077680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bonreu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077655#post1077655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clause about the number of successes on activation is for other powers that mess with that. I know of a couple that minus successes from another power, or simple override other abilities if they have more successes. That would be the case when that comes into play. Since you aren't actually rolling you can't get an exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, other than the potential involvement in a clash of wills, which also seems in the air, it sounds like the automatic successes only comes up against other game-line powers. If attainments don't &quot;crit&quot; so to speak and can bypass withstand, if they do not do that, then they don't seem to ever matter in-mage because the number of successes won't matter to most things--potency does instead, given Withstand. In 1E this would have been huge, but 2E simplified things by trying to splice resisted and contested rolls and just use Withstand instead, except for Clash of Wills like Ward.<br /> <br /> Legacies are so complicated that it really does sound like the attainments are best left for show and instead focus on oblations and the 3rd ruling arcanum...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:20:20-07:00","id":1077681,"title":"","content":"Mmmm. I'm not sure if I want a jump from &quot;your potency related attainments rarely work&quot; to &quot;your potency related attainments just flat out always work with no form of counterplay allowed&quot;...<br /> I have a really hard time finding a place for legacy attainments <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:26:46-07:00","id":1077685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077681#post1077681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmm. I'm not sure if I want a jump from &quot;your potency related attainments rarely work&quot; to &quot;your potency related attainments just flat out always work with no form of counterplay allowed&quot;...<br /> I have a really hard time finding a place for legacy attainments <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense if it is a Master's situation, like Hermit suggested, but if that doesn't work then really should just be <i>not at all</i> huh?<br /> I mean the praxis thing is just a reward for mages preparing for their attainments. They're not <i>actually</i> praxis because you do not need the praxis to get the attainment, it just gives you a reward-incentive. A praxis is like a signature spell anyway, but an attainment is your gnosis re-shaping itself to draw on your soul as a mystical source of power instead of the supernal. The praxis is just consumed and helps reshape your gnosis, it isn't really upgraded per ce right?<br /> <br /> If anyone has attainments able to crit at all, it sounds like it should only be when the mage is a master, at the very least, but it sounds like it is more meant for clash of wills or to quick-fix against situations where some other splat's powers want to count the mages successes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:32:21-07:00","id":1077690,"title":"","content":"Funniest thing about the praxis thing is something that made me really laugh:<br /> &quot;I get an XP and 1 beat...but lose my Praxis?<br /> [thinking]<br /> [thinking]<br /> Can I refuse the XP and keep my Praxis? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:42:08-07:00","id":1077693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077690#post1077690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funniest thing about the praxis thing is something that made me really laugh:<br /> &quot;I get an XP and 1 beat...but lose my Praxis?<br /> [thinking]<br /> [thinking]<br /> Can I refuse the XP and keep my Praxis? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like a pretty serious question, honestly. For me, I want attainments that I can use in front of sleepers. That sounds like the most important thing you would need an attainment for is either the wisdom break, the mana break, or, the quiescence break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:30:32-07:00","id":1077884,"title":"","content":"About Attainments and Withstand - additional Spell Factors might be used to boost Potency. Admittedly, the Corebook can be read two ways on that, but if it's true, with Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span> or <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span>you can boost your Potency to 3 and 4, respectively. With Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can boost it to 6 and 7. At this point even the most strong-willed human beings have no chance to resist, short of spending Willpower. Even the most powerful Spirits might have trouble, since they Withstand with Rank.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:54:27-07:00","id":1077904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077884#post1077884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Attainments and Withstand - additional Spell Factors might be used to boost Potency. Admittedly, the Corebook can be read two ways on that, but if it's true, with Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span> or <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span>you can boost your Potency to 3 and 4, respectively. With Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can boost it to 6 and 7. At this point even the most strong-willed human beings have no chance to resist, short of spending Willpower. Even the most powerful Spirits might have trouble, since they Withstand with Rank.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>From the book:<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> <br /> To get an additional spell factor you need a -2 penalty dice.<br /> So, having the Lowest Arcana involved at level 2 or 4 will give you +1 or +2 secondary spell factors.<br /> The examples showed in the book backup this, as having a Arcana of 5 involved you can bump +2 spell factors, to get Duration 3 (since it is already 1), and having Arcana 3 involved you only get +1 spell factor and get Duration 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-13-2017, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:54:53-07:00","id":1077943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077884#post1077884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Attainments and Withstand - additional Spell Factors might be used to boost Potency. Admittedly, the Corebook can be read two ways on that, but if it's true, with Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span> or <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span>you can boost your Potency to 3 and 4, respectively. With Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can boost it to 6 and 7. At this point even the most strong-willed human beings have no chance to resist, short of spending Willpower. Even the most powerful Spirits might have trouble, since they Withstand with Rank.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Factors for an attainment will not exceed the rating of your arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:07:54-07:00","id":1077954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077884#post1077884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Attainments and Withstand - additional Spell Factors might be used to boost Potency. Admittedly, the Corebook can be read two ways on that, but if it's true, with Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span> or <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span>you can boost your Potency to 3 and 4, respectively. With Arcanum <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can boost it to 6 and 7. At this point even the most strong-willed human beings have no chance to resist, short of spending Willpower. Even the most powerful Spirits might have trouble, since they Withstand with Rank.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting that you add the secondary spellfactor bonus to the primary spellfactor instead? I don't think that's intended, the secondary spellfactor bonus that Horodrigo broke down is something that is used &quot;when required&quot; so attainments apparently do not need even <i>that</i> to work. I think adding the spellfactors you'd use for a short duration (3 turns) to potency instead (increasing max of 5 pot to 7 pot) is allowed. If an ST was down with it in order to make an atypical attainment or something, an attainment that just flat out won't <i>work</i> without high potency, I could understand, but at that point you're in &quot;ignore the rules to make the story better&quot; territory and it is out of any player's hands...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:40:36-07:00","id":1077978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077904#post1077904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the book:<br /> <i>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</i><br /> <br /> To get an additional spell factor you need a -2 penalty dice.<br /> So, having the Lowest Arcana involved at level 2 or 4 will give you +1 or +2 secondary spell factors.<br /> The examples showed in the book backup this, as having a Arcana of 5 involved you can bump +2 spell factors, to get Duration 3 (since it is already 1), and having Arcana 3 involved you only get +1 spell factor and get Duration 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the same math as in my post, except I added the Factors to Potency. If it's explicitly disallowed then that's that, but I assumed the example in the book couldn't have covered all the possible uses for additional Factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077943#post1077943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Factors for an attainment will not exceed the rating of your arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that would settle it. Is it stated in the Corebook, on the Forums or would it break the system and as such should be obvious?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:57:27-07:00","id":1077990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077978#post1077978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that would settle it. Is it stated in the Corebook, on the Forums or would it break the system and as such should be obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Primary Factor is equal to Arcana -1, Secondary Factors are worked out differently via &quot;dice penalties&quot; these are two separate things and the Primary factor cannot benefit from the math for the secondary factor. It doesn't require explaining in the book because it's an incorrect reading of the given rules that leads you to the conclusion that it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:33:29-07:00","id":1078019,"title":"","content":"I have a question about the Fallen World Chronicles, but it has implications about the Lex Magica and stuff, since it has information about the reading, I'll put it with spoilers.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On &quot;The Intruder&quot; Story, Diamante kills the other mage after discovering that she had probably killed a Sleeper in her attempt of escape. We (the readers) are told that this happens cause she needs to protect her Sanctum. Why? Is there any Lex Magica that killing a sleeper in desperate situations is punishable by death?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:31:03-07:00","id":1078040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078019#post1078019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the Fallen World Chronicles, but it has implications about the Lex Magica and stuff, since it has information about the reading, I'll put it with spoilers.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On &quot;The Intruder&quot; Story, Diamante kills the other mage after discovering that she had probably killed a Sleeper in her attempt of escape. We (the readers) are told that this happens cause she needs to protect her Sanctum. Why? Is there any Lex Magica that killing a sleeper in desperate situations is punishable by death?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It was probably a Silver Law of the local Consilium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:29:28-07:00","id":1078075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1077990#post1077990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primary Factor is equal to Arcana -1, Secondary Factors are worked out differently via &quot;dice penalties&quot; these are two separate things and the Primary factor cannot benefit from the math for the secondary factor. It doesn't require explaining in the book because it's an incorrect reading of the given rules that leads you to the conclusion that it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as a capital-letters-having Secondary Factor. &quot;Additional spell factors&quot; include the Primary Factor in the regular spellcasting mechanics and nothing about the wording of Automatic Activation actually applies this restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:32:25-07:00","id":1078076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078075#post1078075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such thing as a capital-letters-having Secondary Factor. &quot;Additional spell factors&quot; include the Primary Factor in the regular spellcasting mechanics and nothing about the wording of Automatic Activation actually applies this restriction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I capitalized the secondary factor in order to evade confusion, and from what I think you're saying that additional factors could exceed the typical level of the primary factor? I'd take that under advisement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:08:29-07:00","id":1078100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078075#post1078075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no such thing as a capital-letters-having Secondary Factor. &quot;Additional spell factors&quot; include the Primary Factor in the regular spellcasting mechanics and nothing about the wording of Automatic Activation actually applies this restriction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, otherwise that instruction would be in the same paragraph right? There wouldn't be a need to put the &quot;additional spellfactors&quot; clause in a separate paragraph if the writers did not intend for it to be it to be a separate train of thought. If you could put ALL the spellfactors into the primary they'd have kept it as a single paragraph.<br /> I think what it is saying is that if you have forces 5 and your attainment uses potency as the primary spellfactor, your potency will be 5, but you can also get additional factors in separate categories that could incur a dice penalty whose integar is equal or below to Forces dots, in this case, 5. And since spellfactors are purchased at -2's, you can have 2 spellfactors at Mastery.<br /> So you could have Potency 5, Duration 3, or, you could have Potency 5, Duration 2, Scale 2, or something, but Potency 7 is the sort of thing I'd expect if the two paragraphs had stayed as one and were like, one subject.<br /> <br /> Maybe you are right though, but even then, the additional spellfactors are &quot;when required&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T20:51:27-07:00","id":1078158,"title":"","content":"Haha, another way to read that paragraph about &quot;additional spell factors&quot; is that <i>every single non-primary spell factor</i> can get those same ranks simultaneously. So with your Forces 5 example, you could have Potency 5, Duration 3, AND Scale 3.<br /> <br /> Needs an errata imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:49:34-07:00","id":1078173,"title":"","content":"Question: Supernal Veil &quot;wards its subject... from detection.&quot; Period. Does it really mean &quot;from all means of detection&quot; or are we meant to infer &quot;from supernatural means of detection&quot;?<br /> <br /> Assuming that it's limited to magical means of detection, can someone explain what that means or accomplishes when the subject is a person or an object? If you can see someone with Mage Sight, you can also <i>just see them with normal vision</i>. I'm not sure what hiding yourself from Periphreal Mage Site with Supernal Veil accomplishes then except to demonstrate that you have used it (&quot;I can see her, but she doesn't show up in my Mage Site. Guess she's using Supernal Veil. Weird.&quot;).<br /> <br /> How is this power meant to be used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T00:50:58-07:00","id":1078212,"title":"","content":"So my reading of supernal veil doesnt say from all means of detection. Its cloaking the subjects supernatural nature from mage sight and any other spells or abilities that might show something as supernatural, like &quot;Supernal vision&quot;. If you dont want to look like a mage then you cast Veil on yourself and folk will just assume your a sleeper to the supernal vision spell and other powers like it, provoking a clash ofc (You example seems to assume the person already knows somebody is a mage and that them now not showing up on PMS is odd but a mage without any spells on them wont ping PMS too so it could just be a mage with no spells on them? Veiled the person wont ping pms with spells on them, or even appear as a mage to Supernam visial assuming the clash goes in their favor) If you have some buff spells cast on you then you will ping PMS walking down the road and that might attract Seer/banisher/bad attention so you veil yourself to make it harder to detect you. (your not invisible you just dont show up as a mage/magic to anything that detects that. You'll look like Joe blogs walking down the street and not &quot;that dude has magic on him&quot; *ping ping* PMS alert.<br /> <br /> You can cast it on a spell so others wont notice it via PMS or AMS tho yuo probably need to combine it at the same time as casting that spell, it might be useful to hide a spell after its cast too. And hiding artifacts is probably a good use of this spell too right? Folk will still see it, its not invisible but they wont see it glow like a lightbulb to AMS or Supernal vision etc. You area effect spell that turns people into frogs is pretty useless if other mages can see the area lit up like a xmas tree with AMS before entering it right? So you veil it and now its harder to see, if they fail the clash then they might walk into your spell area!<br /> <br /> Basically if you want anything to seem mundane when it isnt you can veil it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-14-2017, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T05:28:49-07:00","id":1078285,"title":"","content":"Thank you, that's very clear and matches my intuition too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:20:43-07:00","id":1078334,"title":"","content":"Now that Satchel backed my interpretation there's little for me to add. Still, I assumed Legacy Attainments work like normal Spells do, except where stated otherwise. Even ordinary spells receive free Spell Factors from the Arcanum rating and then may stack additional Spell Factors on top of it. Since Attainments always work, they need to limit the number of Spell Fctors available, but they don't fix them like they do Reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2nd Ed, p.198</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Like a spell</u>, the Attainment automatically acquires primary spell factor ranks (in Potency or Duration) equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum minus one.<br /> When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:55:41-07:00","id":1078351,"title":"","content":"Still worth noting that due to how Veiling Practice is constructed, you totally can hide anything magical from everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:37:12-07:00","id":1078400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078075#post1078075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no such thing as a capital-letters-having Secondary Factor. &quot;Additional spell factors&quot; include the Primary Factor in the regular spellcasting mechanics and nothing about the wording of Automatic Activation actually applies this restriction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh... ouch... I read this a few more times, then re-read the passage from the rulebook, and now I believe that the allocation of the additional spell factor ranks can be applied to any factor, including the primary. Pardon me while I go re-analyze everything I thought I knew about legacy attainments, including that whole big thread I started which is probably just wrong end-to-end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T10:22:31-07:00","id":1078414,"title":"","content":"Well, remember that in practice, you get up to 2 factors to &quot;spend&quot; in this way - you get a factor for -2 penalty, which means you get +1 factor at Arcanum 2 and another one at Arcanum 4. Arcanum 3 and 5 are dead levels for that. Again, if you are interested in factors, you probably want to cast it as a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:14:00-07:00","id":1078569,"title":"","content":"It would be incredibly powerful if that is true, yeah. I mean this would mean someone could get indefinite duration before they reach archmastery for the purpose of Attainment design. Although I am not sure teatime is correct that the additional spellfactors can be customized per-use of the attainment, I think they're fixed once you set them. It isn't like Disciplines or Gifts get &quot;additional factors&quot; on the fly, they sort of have exact specifications for how they work each and every time, barring very situational creativity like a werewolf using the Shaping gift to climb walls (which was so freaking fun)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:25:47-07:00","id":1078734,"title":"","content":"What exactly are the limits of Postcognition? Can I use it on an item to see the last time it was used? Can I use it on a person to see the same show she saw last night? I need to be on the same place that the specified event happened or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T22:30:40-07:00","id":1078764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078734#post1078734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly are the limits of Postcognition? Can I use it on an item to see the last time it was used? Can I use it on a person to see the same show she saw last night? I need to be on the same place that the specified event happened or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order, you can see the past of a thing you observe, yes you can see the last time it was used but you see it from the item's perspective, no you can't watch the show, but you can see her watching the show, that depends on the event if you have a Temporal Sympathetic Yantra to a person that was at the even then you could see her experiencing the event to see the event itself it would be better to be at the place or have a Temporal Sympathetic (the place) and/or have a Sympathetic link to the place so that you could witness the event that happened there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T00:10:10-07:00","id":1078789,"title":"","content":"Does the portal created with the co-location spell need an act of will to use. Since one needs to see the portal either with Space mage sight or using the reach that lets others see it to use it that means that its not just a gaping hole anybody can pass through right? Without seeing the portal you can walk through the place where it is and not pass through it so i assume there is some form of mental willing that is involvled to go through it that requires being able to see it since even if you somehow know the portal is there without seeing it you still cant pass through it. Since objects cant see the portal does that mean they wont pass through them if thrown/fired? Blind people are fucked? It does say perceive (to become aware of) so not strictly sight could mean just knowing its there lets you use it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Anyone capable of perceiving the portal may pass through it.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Not will pass through it? May pass through suggests that they have a choice? Have nothing against using a portal as a trapdoor or anything since you can just teleport people into danger at Space 4 im just curious as these questions came up when i was explaining co-location to one of my players who played 1e and swore he'd never play again and ive been trying to persuade him that 2e sorted alot of the problems he had with 1e (ritual cast system, vague fluffy descriptions etc) and i think i didnt exactly pull it off explaining co-locate..doh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T05:04:58-07:00","id":1078837,"title":"","content":"Is it me or Charmed Condition doesn't have sense for avoiding direct magical damage? Fate has nothing to do with how good the magical blow will land because it always lands good. I mean, you have 3 options: fail, succeed, ex. succeed. I think that it should downgrade from exceptional to normal but even this feels clunky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T05:09:40-07:00","id":1078840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078789#post1078789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the portal created with the co-location spell need an act of will to use. Since one needs to see the portal either with Space mage sight or using the reach that lets others see it to use it that means that its not just a gaping hole anybody can pass through right? Without seeing the portal you can walk through the place where it is and not pass through it so i assume there is some form of mental willing that is involvled to go through it that requires being able to see it since even if you somehow know the portal is there without seeing it you still cant pass through it. Since objects cant see the portal does that mean they wont pass through them if thrown/fired? Blind people are fucked? It does say perceive (to become aware of) so not strictly sight could mean just knowing its there lets you use it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not will pass through it? May pass through suggests that they have a choice? Have nothing against using a portal as a trapdoor or anything since you can just teleport people into danger at Space 4 im just curious as these questions came up when i was explaining co-location to one of my players who played 1e and swore he'd never play again and ive been trying to persuade him that 2e sorted alot of the problems he had with 1e (ritual cast system, vague fluffy descriptions etc) and i think i didnt exactly pull it off explaining co-locate..doh</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes it does require an act of will but if only thing you see is the other side the step is an act of will that will transfer you. If it's not you should add reach to make it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T05:12:17-07:00","id":1078842,"title":"","content":"I think yes, crossing a portal requires intent coming from awareness of its existence. A Mage or someone else can &quot;provide&quot; the intent for objects or people by touching them and switching their location from one side to the other as a reflexive action. An additional spell could allow you to perform that touch at range if that's necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T05:28:47-07:00","id":1078846,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Or add Reach to change from 'touch' to 'perceive' object/being that you want to switch. It's a reasonable improvement that can be added to a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T06:19:43-07:00","id":1078853,"title":"","content":"Could simply be a use of Sensory Range come to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T06:44:00-07:00","id":1078862,"title":"","content":"Sensory Range allows you to put the portal somewhere else. A separate Reach should be required to will an object through a portal without touching it. Or, which I personally like more, a separate Space Compelling or Ruling spell that forces objects and people through Irises if they're inside them. Possibly with added Arcana depending on the type of Iris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T07:15:49-07:00","id":1078874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078569#post1078569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be incredibly powerful if that is true, yeah. I mean this would mean someone could get indefinite duration before they reach archmastery for the purpose of Attainment design. Although I am not sure teatime is correct that the additional spellfactors can be customized per-use of the attainment, I think they're fixed once you set them. It isn't like Disciplines or Gifts get &quot;additional factors&quot; on the fly, they sort of have exact specifications for how they work each and every time, barring very situational creativity like a werewolf using the Shaping gift to climb walls (which was so freaking fun)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it really so powerful, though? Maybe I'm just too used to selling tons of dice for massive factors when spellcasting, but +1 or +2 bump to primary factor doesn't sound that incredibly powerful, to me. If I wanted a permanent spell, I would probably bite a bullet and just relinquish it safely after supercharging it with reach, factors and probably combining it with something. In both cases you pay 1 XP (Attainment is 1 Xp to learn it, spell is 1 XP to recover lost Willpower), with the drawbacks that one is potentially dispellable (while the second isn't targetable by Dispel Magic...but still can be &quot;dealt with&quot; as a phenomena falling under target arcanum, so it isn't untouchable either), while other is unflexible and basically a permanent unchangeable purchase.<br /> <br /> I guess it would be neat for Indefinite low potency effects that you plan using multiple times on Sleepers or expect to be exposed to Sleepers, but I have hard time coming up with such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T07:30:27-07:00","id":1078881,"title":"","content":"How much would I break (both setting wise and mechanics wise) if I added a caveat to Time Travel Spells, that you need to not only target an individual of which you are jumping into past, but also an area (or subjects) that can be explored and changed during your trip?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, imagine that instead of jumping the entire world into the past because you cast a spell, you create a time-shifted zone in the current, objective present, and only things that happen inside that zone will change as a result of the spell when it ends.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> Yes, we are getting tired of Shifting Sands shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-15-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T07:43:45-07:00","id":1078885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078874#post1078874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is it really so powerful, though? Maybe I'm just too used to selling tons of dice for massive factors when spellcasting, but +1 or +2 bump to primary factor doesn't sound that incredibly powerful, to me. If I wanted a permanent spell, I would probably bite a bullet and just relinquish it safely after supercharging it with reach, factors and probably combining it with something. In both cases you pay 1 XP (Attainment is 1 Xp to learn it, spell is 1 XP to recover lost Willpower), with the drawbacks that one is potentially dispellable (while the second isn't targetable by Dispel Magic...but still can be &quot;dealt with&quot; as a phenomena falling under target arcanum, so it isn't untouchable either), while other is unflexible and basically a permanent unchangeable purchase.<br /> <br /> I guess it would be neat for Indefinite low potency effects that you plan using multiple times on Sleepers or expect to be exposed to Sleepers, but I have hard time coming up with such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sleeper thing is exactly what I'm thinking about, honestly. And as you said they can't be dispelled or countered, just reversed with the opposite effect, like an indefinite Stealing Fire that just flat out turns people into sleepwalkers needs a spell that makes sleepwalkers into sleepers in order to reverse it--and unless that too is attainment then their effect can be dispelled but not your attainment.<br /> <br /> Basically, if an attainment uses Indefinite as its duration, it translates to Lasting. That sounds pretty good! Spells that normally only have dispellation or quiescence as potential weaknesses are now nothing. And as long as you're not going on messianic journies to destroy the Veil the Guardians and Seers won't ring too much of a fuss if you keep your activities low-profile and high-price. From an RP perspective, you could do so much if you charged top-dollar for a 4th attainment ritual that can transform a Silver Ladder mage's loved ones into sleepwalkers. If the additional spellfactors cannot be added to the primary factor, then a Master's attainment(s) will be stuck with a Year duration, which is wicked and anyone you want to make money on will now be needing to update their service from you once a year, allowing for repeat investments, but you could gain sooo much traction with permanent attainment effects that now an adept could perform!<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway that's what I see it as--if an attainment has indefinite duration, it basically can be rephrased as Lasting. Being able to turn almost any spell into Lasting offers so much potential.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:12:08-07:00","id":1078892,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but at that point you could also be chasing Archmastery for quite long time, so I put any 4th and 5th attainment business into &quot;Archmaster type business&quot;. Bumping something from normal duration to Indefinite requires you to:<br /> - Get 10 dice worth of spellfactors using Primary Factor and secondary factors combined<br /> - Get +2 reach above any Reach options you want to get.<br /> <br /> So basically, you need Arcanum 4 to do this (Primary Duration will set it to -6, and Arcanum 4 gives you -4 worth of spending), and to put your spell on an Attainment 2 slots above it's arcanum level (to get +2 reach), +1 per any othe Reach options you want to get.<br /> Which means that:<br /> 1st and 2nd attainment slots can't be used in this way, ever<br /> 3rd, 4th and 5th attainment slots can bear Indefinite 1st level (Gnosis 4 lub 5), Indefinite 2nd (Gnosis 6 or 7) and Indefinite 3rd (8 and 9) level spells.<br /> Note that if you want to use the lower Gnosis requirement, you need to follow a estabilished Legacy *and* have an access to a teacher who knows the target attainment. So you are hunting Gnosis 6 and Gnosis 8 Mages to get your Lasting Fix.<br /> At this point, I would probably surrender and zap my loved ones with breaking points enough times that they would gain Fitful Slumber merit, which seems pretty in line with the theme of Wisdom and Hubris and good way being annoying way :V.<br /> <br /> I'm not very good with the Archmage stuff, because it's way beyond our comfortable powerzone, but can't you become an Archmage at Gnosis 6?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Remember that turning spell Indefinite not only requires 10 dice worth of spell factors, but also 2 Reach - one to bump it into Advanced Duration, and one to bump it into Indefinite - and that Attainments calculate Reach based on attainments rank relative to the spell in question, not your Arcanum.<br /> <br /> EDIT2<br /> So your Stealing Fire would require 5th slot attainment, AND would be Withstood, so you actually do need that Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-15-2017, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:23:36-07:00","id":1078895,"title":"","content":"I want to make sure I understand Inured spells and Legacy Wisdom (which both seem to share the same mechanic).<br /> <br /> In fit of uncharacteristic rage, an Enlightened Wisdom mage uses Telekinetic Strike to crush a baby because he doesn't want to hear it cry anymore. He has previously Inured Telekinetic Strike. There is no possibility of losing Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Same scenario, but rather than having Telekinetic Strike Inurred, the mage has a legacy attainment that duplicates the effect of the spell and uses that to crush the baby. Again, no possibility of losing Wisdom.<br /> <br /> This is correct?<br /> <br /> EDIT: The alternative would be that those mechanics really just apply to spells like the 1E Goetic Magic, where just casting the spell is an act of hubris regardless of intent. With this interpretation, you might not lose Wisdom from the act of casting the spell, but you might still lose Wisdom due to consequences of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-15-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:29:00-07:00","id":1078898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078881#post1078881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much would I break (both setting wise and mechanics wise) if I added a caveat to Time Travel Spells, that you need to not only target an individual of which you are jumping into past, but also an area (or subjects) that can be explored and changed during your trip?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, imagine that instead of jumping the entire world into the past because you cast a spell, you create a time-shifted zone in the current, objective present, and only things that happen inside that zone will change as a result of the spell when it ends.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> Yes, we are getting tired of Shifting Sands shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> House Rule: There are no Thrysus and Acanthus get Fate and Life rather than Fate and Time. The Spirit and Time arcana do not exist. So many difficulties for the ST immediately resolved. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:38:12-07:00","id":1078902,"title":"","content":"Spirit didn't cause us much problems (because we don't get past Arcanum 3 and our Thyrsus isn't really using it to her full potential), but man, if there was a vote &quot;Exarchs decided to deal a major blow to the Awakened! What cosmic damage they deal?&quot;, I have a feeling that at our table, &quot;Acanthuses are retroactively ERADICATED&quot; would win by the landslide :P. <br /> <br /> As for your question, we are not sure. There can be arguments for the both interpretations. I personally run with the &quot;if I decided to permanently attach 2 paradox dice to a spell, it better don't invite Wisdom losses because I used it to kill a LITTLE BABBBBBBBBY&quot; - because otherwise, honestly, any consequences of your spell *still* will cause you to lose Wisdom. Like, sure, you don't provoke wisdom loss on paradox and, say, act of soul stealing...but you still acted against interest of other being...so Wisdom loss for you, mister!<br /> <br /> With how limited Inuring is (1 per Gnosis), how costly, it SHOULD be powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:06:57-07:00","id":1078911,"title":"","content":"I feel like Supernal Magic in general and especially Time come with a &quot;don't be a jerk&quot; clause. It sounds like a situation better handled with the player. On the other hand, the player should have a reasonable expectation of getting to use their cool toys.<br /> <br /> One thing I have found to help this situation is glossing. Assume the timeline will try to stay as close to the original as possible. Handle it more like a spell effect of &quot;change the present ny alterting what I did in the past.&quot; Ask what result they want, how they get it, roll one maybe two dicepools, move on. Except when the action warrents more drama.<br /> <br /> *do not* allow them to use it to save scum and cheat the rng. Jf an action failes the first time, it and all similar actions will fail the second time.<br /> <br /> If you want time travel, save the day by being clever and looking cool in a bowtie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:17:24-07:00","id":1078915,"title":"","content":"I find &quot;Don't be a jerk&quot; clause to be kind of a defeat, because it's not a good deal for anyone involved - Mage in question has to be constantly self policing, while others need to constantly be aware that most of their problems can be solved by just fucking with Time, and generally experiencing disruptive gameplay. I don't want rules that force us to &quot;deal with players&quot;. <br /> That, and quite a lot of characters in the setting should have access to this power (it's Time 3, so a lot of *starting* Witches can grab it from the chargen), so it should be fairly common in the setting, too. And implications of even one in three Cabals having on demand access to time travel is...mind bogglingy setting wrapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:32:58-07:00","id":1079112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1078892#post1078892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but at that point you could also be chasing Archmastery for quite long time,</div> </div> </div> </div>I will admit that I would take archmastery over completing my legacy, but in archmage I personally see attainments as being free from interfering with the Pax Arcanum, which is the mobster-logic driven version of consilium laws that archmages play by. So they'd still be quite valuable. Yeah, you can get archmastery at gnosis 6, you do not need to wait until you're a ridiculous gnosis 8.<br /> <br /> I still think adding the &quot;additional spellfactors&quot; to a primary duration is pretty powerful though. And oh gosh, if a person could add conditional fate triggers to it... and then hiding the trigger with a normal spell because sleepers won't be seeing that part of the effect anyway... In general though I think you are right--the extra factors will not make a huge difference, and the mages who can use the edge cases where they *do* mage a huge difference are likely archmasters already, who can just... do whatever they want almost, assuming no other archmage gets in the way.<br /> <br /> I think you're convincing me though, at low levels those additional factors seem to do less than make an attainment broken more of a make attainments <i>viable?</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:04:10-07:00","id":1079136,"title":"","content":"For me, biggest draw of Attainments was always ability to cast them without a roll, with 100% chance of success. Extra factor can actually mean a lot for instant cast Withstood spells, as for normal targets, their withstand is usually between 1 and 7 (with a caveat that 7 and 6 come from Willpowering a turn). +1 here can not only be a large percentage of what you already have, but also literally a difference between guaranteed failure and guaranteed success.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:24:27-07:00","id":1079146,"title":"","content":"Question regarding the Place of Power spell. This is an interesting spell because it's Withstood by Gauntlet strength, and its effect is to modify Gauntlet strength.<br /> <br /> So let's say I'm at a location with Gauntlet strength 3, and I use Place of Power with the intent of lowering Gauntlet strength. I succeed on a roll with Potency 4, so I can lower Gauntlet strength in the area of effect from 3 to 2. But that's not good enough for me -- I want it lower! So I cast Place of Power again, and this time I'm only WIthstood by the current Gauntlet strength of 2. I again succeed on my roll with Potency 4, so this time I'm able to lower the Gauntlet strength by 2 (4 Potency less the 2 Withstand). Of course <i>after</i> casting the second spell, Spell Stacking comes into play; my new casting replaces my old one. That means that the Gauntlet strength drops to 1 (lowered by 2 from its original 3). And I could do this again to get it to zero.<br /> <br /> Did you follow that crazy mess? Is this how it works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:31:50-07:00","id":1079176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Withstand reduces the effect of a spell's Potency, it doesn't remove the spell. If someone's withstand rating changes part-way through a spell's Duration, up OR down, it gets reassessed. If your mind-control spell that isn't potent enough to beat someone's resolve is still active when something else reduces their resolve to below Potency, your mind control spell begins to work. Alternatively, if you mind control someone to kill themselves, they *can* spend Willpower at the last minute to up their Resolve for a turn. Or another mage can cast a spell that increases their Resolve, with a longer duration than your mind-control one. </div> </div> </div>Dave B said this, so technically it instantly drops the gauntlet to 0 the first time you beat its withstand by 1. (Stats only drop to 1 since Degrading the form mentions to a min of 1) This also breaks afew other spells too, &quot;befuddle&quot;, &quot;state change&quot;, &quot;degrading the form&quot; and &quot;alter integrity&quot;, anything that changes the withstand stat to equal potency or can lower the withstand has problems. Theres no official word on what to do about it, I read that each of the Arcana was done by a different writer so i assume some thought the same as i did that withstand is only checked once when a spell is cast.<br /> <br /> You can just say that spells that alter withstand don't recheck themselves or change the withstand to something else or ignore it and say that spells only check withstand when first cast. I know that is what i am doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-15-2017, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:50:27-07:00","id":1079182,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I understand how to adjudicate this now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T21:50:40-07:00","id":1079231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079176#post1079176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave B said this, so technically it instantly drops the gauntlet to 0 the first time you beat its withstand by 1. (Stats only drop to 1 since Degrading the form mentions to a min of 1) This also breaks afew other spells too, &quot;befuddle&quot;, &quot;state change&quot;, &quot;degrading the form&quot; and &quot;alter integrity&quot;, anything that changes the withstand stat to equal potency or can lower the withstand has problems. Theres no official word on what to do about it, I read that each of the Arcana was done by a different writer so i assume some thought the same as i did that withstand is only checked once when a spell is cast.<br /> <br /> You can just say that spells that alter withstand don't recheck themselves or change the withstand to something else or ignore it and say that spells only check withstand when first cast. I know that is what i am doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I understand this. Do we check which spell takes priority based on the potency before Withstand is applied or after Withstand is applied? Because I thought totalgit's example was correct the first time, because the second casting of Place of Power has the highest potency--that it would result in a gauntlet of 1, and a spell potency of 2. However, if anything else happened to the gauntlet in the meantime, it would force both spells to re-check themselves, and then suddenly both spells would have the same potency at that time, both before and after Withstand. I am very confused how a single casting of Place of Power will drop the gauntlet to 0 if the spell had enough potency to break Withstand... I must have misread that or something, but that's what it looks like to me. Help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T22:15:25-07:00","id":1079236,"title":"","content":"I also have a question about astral stuff, particularly after reading the following thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-astral-wat-do</a><br /> <br /> So... My question is about using Mind magic to get into the astral, and getting other creatures into the astral, and permutations based on practice and the destination layer, and places of power such as hallows or perhaps locii.<br /> <br /> The first is, what practice does a mage need to get into the astral without a hallow? And would the practice change if you were doing it as an instant action or if you still need to meditate? Examples might be if Mind 3 lets you reproduce Astral Adept, but you still need to meditate, or if Mind 4 would just cast you into the astral as a matter of course, as an instant action.<br /> <br /> Next, if this spell works, what permutations does it undergo to use it on a sleeper? For example, if the Mind 3 version works on a sleeper (obviously risking paradox I'd imagine), do they spend a willpower point to enter the astral or does the mage? Or both? As per Astral Adept. If Sleepers cannot gain Astral Adept from Mind magic, does that mean a Mind 4 spell will now work, to Pattern them in? Or is something fundamentally missing, something that can only be Made?<br /> <br /> Similarly for a Changeling. Can I get them into the Temenos using Making Mind, giving them the mind-facet that they're inherently missing? If it is a soul issue entirely, can this be reproduced by adding Conjunctional Death 5? Or is it so severe that you would need 5 dots in all the subtle arcana? Or does it just flat out require archmaster and an alteration to that changeling's template? I am leaning on Mind 5 being enough--although we better hope that spell doesn't wear off before the Changeling can leave the Temenos.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that any spell that works on a sleeper or sleepwalker will work on a changeling for the Anima Mundi, but the Onieros situation is as sticky as the Temenos one.<br /> <br /> Lastly, werewolves. It is said werewolves can sleep into the anima mundi, but this isn't given systems, I think this is just fluff. Perhaps it requires a locus. If so, perhaps we can treat them as Mages for the purpose of getting into the anima mundi, except for a Cahalith, or, except that they do not act lucidly while in the anima mundi, anymore than a human is in in most of their own dreams.<br /> <br /> So, if we allow for this, is Mind 2 enough to allow a werewolf to enter the anima mundi lucidly, or do we need to reproduce astral adept on them to let them enter the anima mundi lucidly and act as a PC character would while in the Anima Mundi, albeit with meditation? If so, I guess the practice is going to depend on if we thought that something like astral adept can be reproduced with Weaving, or if it definitely requires Patterning. Worse case scenario I guess we're looking at Making, but that's only if we're positive that what we need to get a werewolf into the anima mundi lucidly is something that has to be Made. I can see Ruling working but I can also see Patterning being the bare minimum for all of this.<br /> <br /> For the sake of discussion, two other spells that are making me debate what the practices are are Reaching vs World Walker (spirit 3 and 4 respectively), and the interesting interactions between the ruling and perfecting practices (I always thought that increasing a fire's damage would need perfecting, but the book has Control Fire as 2 dots, which tells me that the extra heat is either coming in from the environment or by burning fuel more quickly, ruling fire would be like making a fire &quot;denser&quot; instead of perfecting it.)<br /> <br /> I know that's a lot to read and think about, but, I think it this would be a good exercise in debating the capabilities of the practices, like how Death 3 cannot sever an Awakened Soul because it is the gnosis that is in the way, not the soul itself per ce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T22:52:44-07:00","id":1079249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079231#post1079231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I understand this. Do we check which spell takes priority based on the potency before Withstand is applied or after Withstand is applied? Because I thought totalgit's example was correct the first time, because the second casting of Place of Power has the highest potency--that it would result in a gauntlet of 1, and a spell potency of 2. However, if anything else happened to the gauntlet in the meantime, it would force both spells to re-check themselves, and then suddenly both spells would have the same potency at that time, both before and after Withstand. I am very confused how a single casting of Place of Power will drop the gauntlet to 0 if the spell had enough potency to break Withstand... I must have misread that or something, but that's what it looks like to me. Help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a recursive loop, Original gauntlet/withstand is 3, spells potency is 4 so reduces withstand/gauntlet to 2, gets reassessed so spell now has 2 potency over so reduces gauntlet/withstand to 1, reassessed again potency is now 3 greater so reduces it to 0. This all happens on the first casting if when withstand changes it gets reassessed again.<br /> <br /> Theres also the problem if something has durability 3 and you cast alter integrity on it with potency 10 it'll increase its durability to 10 but its withstand is now 10 so the spell turns off so now its withstand rating is back to 3 so the spell turns on, then off, then on, then off.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-16-2017, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T23:32:52-07:00","id":1079263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079249#post1079249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its a recursive loop, Original gauntlet/withstand is 3, spells potency is 4 so reduces withstand/gauntlet to 2, gets reassessed so spell now has 2 potency over so reduces gauntlet/withstand to 1, reassessed again potency is now 3 greater so reduces it to 0. This all happens on the first casting if when withstand changes it gets reassessed again.<br /> <br /> Theres also the problem if something has durability 3 and you cast alter integrity on it with potency 10 it'll increase its durability to 10 but its withstand is now 10 so the spell turns off so now its withstand rating is back to 3 so the spell turns on, then off, then on, then off.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that sounds really complicated. I don't think it would go recursive though because after the spell successfully applies its potency the first time the spell's imago has been fulfilled. Right? But I can see why that would be a problem. But that definitely gives me an idea. If someone errata'd that or clarified this issue, and fixes this recursive thing, I bet you anything you could MAKE it recursive using your gnosis, like how a healing spell can be made to heal every time the ritual interval passes? I wonder what kind of dots that would take. Probably prime 2? Maybe time 2? both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T23:49:44-07:00","id":1079269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079249#post1079249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a recursive loop</div> </div> </div> </div>The most straightforward reading is that individual spells don't affect themselves \u2014 a casting of Degrading the Form to reduce somebody's Stamina reduces their Stamina by the Potency of the spell minus the Withstand rating accounting for all other factors; a spell that alters a Withstand rating is putting all its metaphorical energy into making that alteration stick for the Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tangentially related question: Does a spell cast with the Sympathetic Range Attainment alter its properties if the subject's Sympathetic Withstand rating changes in relation to the caster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T07:09:28-07:00","id":1079354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079269#post1079269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most straightforward reading is that individual spells don't affect themselves \u2014 a casting of Degrading the Form to reduce somebody's Stamina reduces their Stamina by the Potency of the spell minus the Withstand rating accounting for all other factors; a spell that alters a Withstand rating is putting all its metaphorical energy into making that alteration stick for the Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tangentially related question: Does a spell cast with the Sympathetic Range Attainment alter its properties if the subject's Sympathetic Withstand rating changes in relation to the caster?</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, would you mind sharing your perspective <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079146#post1079146\">on my previous question</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-16-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T07:36:13-07:00","id":1079361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079354#post1079354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, would you mind sharing your perspective <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079146#post1079146\">on my previous question</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>In that example you're using two separate spells with the same effect and the same Potency; having the new spell override the old one means the old spell ceases to have a meaningful effect on any elements covered by the new spell, i.e. the outcome of casting two Potency 4 Place of Power spells on an area with a Gauntlet Strength of 3 results in a Gauntlet Strength of 2 because the first spell's change to the Gauntlet Withstand only applies as long as that spell is the largest/only spell doing that reduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:06:05-07:00","id":1079420,"title":"","content":"You're saying that the second spell overrides the first prior to taking into account Withstand for the second casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:09:16-07:00","id":1079422,"title":"","content":"Think of it like this: A Supernal spell isn't so much a thing you create as it is you giving local rewrite control to a set of Supernal symbol interactions you create in your Imago. When you cast a spell to produce a given effect, it rewrites that local reality to produce the effect of the Imago. If you cast a second spell on top of that, you're not essentially changing anything; you're just recreating the first local rewrite, so the results are the same. In effect, your target is the same underlying physical reality.<br /> <br /> Long and short of it: Supernal spells do not stack; only the most potent effect manifests.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:41:01-07:00","id":1079449,"title":"","content":"I feel like the direct text is ambiguous, but I'm pleased to follow your interpretation since it's more intuitive and makes for better gameplay. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T16:04:13-07:00","id":1079552,"title":"","content":"What happens if a Space master uses teleport on a campus sized area, teleporting everybody in it into a pocket realm the size of a cupboard?<br /> <br /> If he has the campus area in sensory range he only needs to withstand vs his strong connection to his own pocket realm right? His base potency is 5 vs strong sympathetic link of 1 ?<br /> <br /> Even using his reach to instant cast teleport at sensory range on 1 person, teleporting somebody into his timeless pocket realm prison seems really OP? Ok i get everything at 5 dots is awesome but most instant death stuff always gets a withstand and ok this isnt instadeath but its insta stuck frozen in a pocket realm till that spell ends.<br /> <br /> I didnt realise how easy it was to zap people into pocket prison realms. Has anybody had pc's or npc's trap people in them, I can see instances when using one to skip forward days/weeks might be handy in of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T16:20:42-07:00","id":1079558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079449#post1079449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the direct text is ambiguous, but I'm pleased to follow your interpretation since it's more intuitive and makes for better gameplay. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell stacking rules in the book are poorly worded, It says that the highest potency takes effect and the lower one is suppressed but doesnt mention if they are tied. Which one has higher potency???? It also says under withstand that withstood spells reduce the potency by the withstand rating.<br /> <br /> So if the gauntlet is 3 and you cast a potency 4 you have a potency 1 spell left. the gauntlet is now 2 so the second casting at potency 4 minus withstand leaves it at potency 2 which is higher than the first spell so the first spell is suppressed and the gauntlet is lowered to 1 from this second spell and the first is suppressed. (Note you can cancel the first spell as the second spell is lowering the gauntlet by 2, cancelling the first spell has no effect now). The last spell also starts of at potency 4 but after being withstood by a gaunlet of 1 is left with potency of 3 higher than the 2nd spell so it also gets suppressed and the gauntlet is now 0.<br /> <br /> When does one check for Spell stacking? Before or after withstand? before withstand you cant cast multiple potency 4 spells and have them do anything, only the first works the others are suppressed (i assume in the case of a tie on potency its the first spell that gets suppressed, first on, first suppressed?) If after withstand then you can cast multiple potency 4 spells for a cascading effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-16-2017, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T16:31:47-07:00","id":1079560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079552#post1079552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Space master uses teleport on a campus sized area, teleporting everybody in it into a pocket realm the size of a cupboard?<br /> <br /> If he has the campus area in sensory range he only needs to withstand vs his strong connection to his own pocket realm right? His base potency is 5 vs strong sympathetic link of 1 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everything fits.<br /> <br /> He would be have to deal with Sympathetic Range Withstand, not Sympathetic Connection Withstand since he's affecting a thing via Sympathy, not affecting the Sympathy itself. Also, Mages only have a Weak Sympathetic Connection to their own spells.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> If the spells are tied in Potency then I'd say the most recent spell takes precedent and spells still don't stack like that as has been pointed out multiple times now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:51:55-07:00","id":1079589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079449#post1079449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the direct text is ambiguous, but I'm pleased to follow your interpretation since it's more intuitive and makes for better gameplay. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:00:50-07:00","id":1079593,"title":"","content":"Can I re-ask my question and just simplify it to what people think would be the practice for awarding the Astral Adept merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:11:00-07:00","id":1079598,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the spells are tied in Potency then I'd say the most recent spell takes precedent and spells still don't stack like that as has been pointed out multiple times now. </div> </div> </div>Spells dont stack like what?, if multiple spells of different potency are cast on somebody then only the highest potency takes effect the others are suppressed. Im asking at what point do you check the potency for this, since if its after the withstand rating has lowered a spells potency since that is what withstand does, then its possible the spell might start with the same potency but after being withstood now has a different maybe higher than a previous spells potency.<br /> <br /> What is the potency of the spell it starts at 4 but gauntlet 3 withstand lowers it to 1, is it 4 or 1? Its a potency 1 spell since it lowered the gauntlet by 1 right? the next potency 4 spell cast becomes potency 2 since the withstand is now 2, theres no stacking involved as this higher potency takes effect...i cant be clearer really.<br /> <br /> I know spells dont &quot;stack&quot; but casting multiple spells with a potency each higher than the last (which my example shows happens if you check for spell stacking after withstand) would work.<br /> <br /> Sorry i sometimes feel like im in a maths class, people reply on this forum &quot;thats not how it works&quot; but dont show any of their workings....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:13:40-07:00","id":1079599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079593#post1079593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I re-ask my question and just simplify it to what people think would be the practice for awarding the Astral Adept merit?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Increasing a Merit is typically a Ruling (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">) spell. Attributes<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> and Skills can be increased by a Perfecting (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">) spell. Gaining a Skill that has no dots is a Patterning (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">) spell.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Id say gaining a merit is similar to gaining a skill so patterning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:15:44-07:00","id":1079628,"title":"","content":"Well, &quot;Shifting the Odds&quot; is a Fate 2 spell that can give you a merit for a brief period of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:18:05-07:00","id":1079677,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's kind of all over the place, and then Allies requires Mind 5 so its really all oooover the place. My ST is saying that I would need Mind 5 to get a werewolf into the anima mundi but since they can dream into it by chance anyway I was really confused why it would be Mind 5...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T00:40:11-07:00","id":1079709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079560#post1079560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not everything fits.<br /> <br /> He would be have to deal with Sympathetic Range Withstand, not Sympathetic Connection Withstand since he's affecting a thing via Sympathy, not affecting the Sympathy itself. Also, Mages only have a Weak Sympathetic Connection to their own spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I kinda knew they wouldn't all fit...but) Is that then mechanically like the worlds collide 1e spell? Or 2e's collapse spell? Or only the first people hit with the spell get ported the rest dont?<br /> <br /> I keep forgetting both types of sympathy and call them both the same thing, yep so i did mean the range withstand and its actually the first example ive seen with mages sympathy to their own spells. I was assuming that the maaster would spend some time in the realm to increase his sympathy but thats a bad idea, a weak connection is still well within his base potency though anyways making it trivial. The target getting no real option to save himself just seems so good, as long as you win initative, that other master is gone and cant do anything until you end the pocket realm. scary scary stuff, im sure there are other ways masters of other arcana can ruin another masters day but id need to think of them that are as easy. Technically doesnt even need to be your own pocket realm, you just need good sympathy to the frozen time prison realm and have teleport and you remove problem people really easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T03:18:39-07:00","id":1079734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079598#post1079598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> <br /> <br /> Spells dont stack like what?, if multiple spells of different potency are cast on somebody then only the highest potency takes effect the others are suppressed. Im asking at what point do you check the potency for this, since if its after the withstand rating has lowered a spells potency since that is what withstand does, then its possible the spell might start with the same potency but after being withstood now has a different maybe higher than a previous spells potency.<br /> <br /> What is the potency of the spell it starts at 4 but gauntlet 3 withstand lowers it to 1, is it 4 or 1? Its a potency 1 spell since it lowered the gauntlet by 1 right? the next potency 4 spell cast becomes potency 2 since the withstand is now 2, theres no stacking involved as this higher potency takes effect...i cant be clearer really.<br /> <br /> I know spells dont &quot;stack&quot; but casting multiple spells with a potency each higher than the last (which my example shows happens if you check for spell stacking after withstand) would work.<br /> <br /> Sorry i sometimes feel like im in a maths class, people reply on this forum &quot;thats not how it works&quot; but dont show any of their workings....</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easier to say to check before Withstand is applied, in the cases where both spells faces Withstand. Otherwise look at both spells without taking into account the other spell. Which spell would have more Potency in the end? That spell applies.<br /> <br /> But in your example it doesn't really matter when you check which spell has more Potency since once one spell is applied the first stops applying so that the second spell will face the original Withstand rating anyway. So in your example the second Potency 4 spell would still face Gauntlet Strength 3 because it suppresses the first spell.<br /> <br /> Edit: About trying to cram too much into a too small space, you could just limit the spell to not working unless you take such factors into account. Co-location requiring all linked locations to be of the same size, and Teleportation to require all subjects to have unique destinations or both locations for AoE castings to have the same size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-17-2017, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:48:27-07:00","id":1079746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079734#post1079734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But in your example it doesn't really matter when you check which spell has more Potency since once one spell is applied the first stops applying so that the second spell will face the original Withstand rating anyway. So in your example the second Potency 4 spell would still face Gauntlet Strength 3 because it suppresses the first spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second spell will only face the original withstand if withstand gets reassessed when the first spell is suppressed, and if reassessing withstand then 1 casting of potency 4 will lower it to 0 anyways.<br /> <br /> Gauntlet 3. First spell has potency 4 vs withstand of 3 leaving it with a potency of 1.<br /> Gauntlet is now 2. Withstand 2. (withstand should be reassessed here and recur down to zero but if we say spells dont count themselves we continue)<br /> Second spell has potency 4 vs withstand of 2 leaving it with a potency of 2.<br /> Gauntlet is now 0,Withstand is 0, Withstand has changed via a different spell so First spell gets reassessed with new withstand becoming potency 4 vs withstand 0 lowers gauntet to 0/withstand to 0, Second spell gets suppressed but then reassessed also becoming potency 4.<br /> First spell then gets suppressed since its same potency as second spell now, Second spell is still potency 4 vs withstand 0 ? Gauntlet remains 0?<br /> <br /> My head hurts....<br /> <br /> Nope....withstand is checked when a spell is cast. If if changes later, tough....thats what im doing...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-17-2017, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:55:46-07:00","id":1079749,"title":"","content":"Haha my bad for thinking this was &quot;a simple question&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:02:10-07:00","id":1079818,"title":"","content":"Do you need to spend a full turn worth of action (as in, &quot;mechanical&quot; instant action) to use Precise Force attainment? How do you trigger/use it?<br /> As a secondary question, anyone got any experience with this attainment and seeing it in actual play? It's one of these things that looked cool to us on paper, but haven't been used because action economy is a harsh queen and it's restrictions are...very restricting. Gives Obrimos the short stick for the 2nd dot attainments, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:23:06-07:00","id":1079827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079818#post1079818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to spend a full turn worth of action (as in, &quot;mechanical&quot; instant action) to use Precise Force attainment? How do you trigger/use it?<br /> As a secondary question, anyone got any experience with this attainment and seeing it in actual play? It's one of these things that looked cool to us on paper, but haven't been used because action economy is a harsh queen and it's restrictions are...very restricting. Gives Obrimos the short stick for the 2nd dot attainments, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I saw a player use this as a sort of &quot;Iron Fist&quot; escaping the jail thing. He just blew the door open with Precise Force and a kick, since an Attainment is similar to a spell but don't follow the same rules, we play as it not triggering Paradox/Quiescence/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:52:32-07:00","id":1079908,"title":"","content":"Which arcanum actually has Resonance in its purview?<br /> <br /> The 2E core rules lists Prime as the arcanum for Resonance; Spirit has Essence. But if you just search for &quot;Resonance&quot; in the rules, it's really muddled. Just look at the Active Mage Site arcana-specific effects for one example. It almost seems like when you're wondering which arcanum is appropriate for working with Resonance, it depends on the Practice you intend to use.<br /> <br /> I just want to make a custom legacy that's focused on Resonance, where every attainment does something with Resonance: perceiving it, hiding it, bolstering it, changing it. Which arcanum is primary for that legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:17:39-07:00","id":1079926,"title":"","content":"I think you're mixing up the Leyline/Node type of Resonance (Prime), and the Resonant Condition (Spirit). There's some overlap (the presence of one type of Resonance can very well create the other), but they're fundamentally separate things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T13:24:54-07:00","id":1079955,"title":"","content":"Asking this here since I did not want to make a whole thread just for a silly question of mine:<br /> <br /> I want to improve my knowledge and understanding of Mage. It's a line I like but I always feel like I never really did my homework when it comes to it. My ideas about the setting tend to not be true more often than not, so it's rather blatant there's much I need to read. No idea where to start. The books I actually read are the Cores, Intruders, The Free Council One and Left-Hand Path.<br /> <br /> Which ones you'd suggest me to read and why? Or in which order, if you think that could help. Quite an open question, I know.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you think this should belong to a thread of its own instead of here, I'll create it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-17-2017, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:05:59-07:00","id":1079981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079955#post1079955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking this here since I did not want to make a whole thread just for a silly question of mine:<br /> <br /> I want to improve my knowledge and understanding of Mage. It's a line I like but I always feel like I never really did my homework when it comes to it. My ideas about the setting tend to not be true more often than not, so it's rather blatant there's much I need to read. No idea where to start. The books I actually read are the Cores, Intruders, The Free Council One and Left-Hand Path.<br /> <br /> Which ones you'd suggest me to read and why? Or in which order, if you think that could help. Quite an open question, I know.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you think this should belong to a thread of its own instead of here, I'll create it</div> </div> </div> </div>Tomes of mysteries while 1e has alot of stuff in it, but the 2e version is coming soon so alot of info might be moot, also Imperial Mysteries is worth a read, it'll help explain the supernal alot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:28:52-07:00","id":1079996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1079926#post1079926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're mixing up the Leyline/Node type of Resonance (Prime), and the Resonant Condition (Spirit). There's some overlap (the presence of one type of Resonance can very well create the other), but they're fundamentally separate things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha really? Why would they overload a term like that? Particularly when they have the same effect -- the section on leylines and nodes mentions about how Spirits interact with that resonance in the exact same way the interact with resonance elsewhere in the world (&quot;Finally, Resonance generates Essence that spirits at the roots of the Shadow\u2019s ecology devour&quot;). That's bizarre. I'm just going to stay away from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:34:02-07:00","id":1080042,"title":"","content":"I see the source of your confusion. I'd be confused as well if I hadn't been familiar with spirit rules before reading that section. I think it's a classic example of the writer knowing exactly what they mean, but not realising it's not as obvious to the reader.<br /> Anyway, that's what I meant by overlap. Leyline Resonances are one of many sources of Resonant Conditions, which in turn generates Essence. In practice it does mean Leyline Resonances generates Essence; they just omitted one of the steps in how it does that.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's not all that rare that the same terms are used for different things between gamelines. This might be one of those times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-17-2017, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T19:02:10-07:00","id":1080132,"title":"","content":"Cinder, I recommend you read as many of the source books for the diamond orders as you can manage. Each of them provides a perspective on the journey of a mage from pre-Awakening through seniority in an order. For me, those books gave me valuable information on story context, NPCs, and story hooks. Also they're just great reads. The Silver Ladder goes from &quot;Wow these guys are principled leaders&quot; to &quot;Wow these guys are as alien and scary as the old Vampire Antideluvians.&quot; It was a trip! I know you read Free Council, but the books for the diamond orders are just better in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T19:06:26-07:00","id":1080133,"title":"","content":"Outside of the books you mentioned, and the Night Horrors one, I think Dave Brookshaw's actual plays probably helped the most. Especially those collected <a href=\"http://www.pyrron.com/?p=33\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. The PDFs have some inserts, I imagine posts from Dave, explaining why he made certain decisions with the setting and how he saw certain things. It's not a 1:1 match, as something huge and near-apocalyptic happens at the end of one of them that changes the course of their setting (and the repercussions are dealt with in another) but even that's just a good example of how to take a setting and make it 'yours.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:54:45-07:00","id":1080391,"title":"","content":"<b>Simple Question: </b>Can an Imbued Item hold a Combined Spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:24:52-07:00","id":1080411,"title":"","content":"So combined spells count as 1 spell for spell control and only require 1 casting but are still multiple spells going off at the same time, so i would say no. But then theres nothing that states it cant be done, it depends if you think a combined spell is one spell with different effects or many spells only counting as one for control and one casting..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:09:49-07:00","id":1080437,"title":"","content":"I would say you can, but that the merit dot cost should take both spells into account separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:25:44-07:00","id":1081156,"title":"","content":"Does a spell of a given Arcanum count as being under that Arcanum's purview for the purpose of casting spells to affect it?<br /> <br /> That is, can you, say, cast a Life Veiling spell to hide another Life spell from the Peripheral Mage Sight of other Awakened?<br /> <br /> My instinct is to say no, because no Arcanum save Prime includes magic itself under its Purview. Likewise, there'd be no reason for Prime's Dispel Magic spell to exist at all, since every Arcanum could, by itself, manipulate spells of its own Arcanum. Since Dispel Magic requires Prime 1 and one dot in the Arcana used in the targeted spell, this suggests that targeting spells themselves does not naturally fall under the purview of the given Arcana and, thus, hiding spells <i>of</i> that Arcanum don't fall under it either.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any other reasoning or reasons why it would be otherwise, though, I'm interested to hear them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:42:15-07:00","id":1081166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081156#post1081156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a spell of a given Arcanum count as being under that Arcanum's purview for the purpose of casting spells to affect it?<br /> <br /> That is, can you, say, cast a Life Veiling spell to hide another Life spell from the Peripheral Mage Sight of other Awakened?<br /> <br /> My instinct is to say no, because no Arcanum save Prime includes magic itself under its Purview. Likewise, there'd be no reason for Prime's Dispel Magic spell to exist at all, since every Arcanum could, by itself, manipulate spells of its own Arcanum. Since Dispel Magic requires Prime 1 and one dot in the Arcana used in the targeted spell, this suggests that targeting spells themselves does not naturally fall under the purview of the given Arcana and, thus, hiding spells <i>of</i> that Arcanum don't fall under it either.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any other reasoning or reasons why it would be otherwise, though, I'm interested to hear them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal veil hides spells, so yep id agree with your instinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:54:13-07:00","id":1081176,"title":"","content":"It depends on your PMS interpretation. If it detects magic I'd say no, you can't hide Life Spells with Life Arcanum from PMS. But if it detects effects of magic you can Veil them. <br /> Mind should be able to Veil anything, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:02:23-07:00","id":1081227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081176#post1081176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on your PMS interpretation. If it detects magic I'd say no, you can't hide Life Spells with Life Arcanum from PMS. But if it detects effects of magic you can Veil them.<br /> Mind should be able to Veil anything, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont quite understand, what other interpretations of PMS are there? Does PMS detect magic: yes if not of the veiling practice and active and not veiled by the &quot;supernal veil&quot; spell. Does PMS detect the effects of magic: yes if active and not of the veiling practice or veiled with &quot;Supernal veil&quot; spell. While these might be seperate tho i cant think of how, PMS will detect both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-19-2017, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T21:38:48-07:00","id":1081289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081156#post1081156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a spell of a given Arcanum count as being under that Arcanum's purview for the purpose of casting spells to affect it?<br /> <br /> That is, can you, say, cast a Life Veiling spell to hide another Life spell from the Peripheral Mage Sight of other Awakened?<br /> <br /> My instinct is to say no, because no Arcanum save Prime includes magic itself under its Purview. Likewise, there'd be no reason for Prime's Dispel Magic spell to exist at all, since every Arcanum could, by itself, manipulate spells of its own Arcanum. Since Dispel Magic requires Prime 1 and one dot in the Arcana used in the targeted spell, this suggests that targeting spells themselves does not naturally fall under the purview of the given Arcana and, thus, hiding spells <i>of</i> that Arcanum don't fall under it either.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any other reasoning or reasons why it would be otherwise, though, I'm interested to hear them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Death has a spell that hides your nature as a Wizzzzzzzzzard - it makes you register as a Sleeper with no magic business going around you. It's Suppress Aura, 2nd dot. Historically, Death also had access to Supernal Dispel equivalent at 4th dot. <br /> Time also can target spells when using Hung magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T21:51:49-07:00","id":1081291,"title":"","content":"Some STs rule that PMS only detects when a mage casts a spell, not e.g. when a mage previously had a long-duration buff cast on themselves and they walk into view. This is so that mages can be near their cabalmates without PMS constantly making them get goosebumps or whatever, since most mages walk around with wards or enhancements of some kind. People tune out alarms that never stop ringing.<br /> <br /> If your ST goes that way, then you don't have to worry about veiling long-duration effects anyway. They only ping PMS when they're cast, not throughout their durations.<br /> <br /> Life Veiling is for veiling things in the Purview of Life (healing, disease, food, animals, plants, evolution, metamorphosis, physicality, vigor). &quot;Life Spells&quot; is not in that list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T21:58:59-07:00","id":1081294,"title":"","content":"So you wouldn't let Active Magic Sight to see a spell from their Arcanum?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> For clarity, the logic here is:<br /> Spells are not under Arcanum Purview<br /> <br /> Active Magic Sight only shows things falling under Arcanum Purview, and while &quot;supernatural effects falling under Arcanum's purview&quot; is shown by Active Sight, &quot;spells&quot; are not a subject under non-Prime purviews. <br /> <br /> Active Magic Sight shows no spells, unless it's prime, because Prime specifically says it allows you to perceive Awakened Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-20-2017, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:19:05-07:00","id":1081298,"title":"","content":"AMS &quot;highlights all phenomena related to the Arcana used.&quot; That goes beyond the scope of arcanum purview to include spells. However, spells within an arcanum are limited to effecting things in the purview of that arcanum. Two different rules for two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:21:46-07:00","id":1081299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081289#post1081289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death has a spell that hides your nature as a Wizzzzzzzzzard - it makes you register as a Sleeper with no magic business going around you. It's Suppress Aura, 2nd dot. Historically, Death also had access to Supernal Dispel equivalent at 4th dot.<br /> Time also can target spells when using Hung magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death has souls under its purview, and entropy, decay, and endings. The Nimbus is an expression of the character's soul, and there's no reason you can't end magic as readily as you end any other life. Those come from Death playing off its own purviews.<br /> <br /> Hung magic is, likewise, Time monkeying with the temporal component of a spell. It's very much the Arcana acting within their own purviews. Hence why Time can Hang spells from any Arcana, not merely Time spells. Same with Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081294#post1081294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you wouldn't let Active Magic Sight to see a spell from their Arcanum?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> For clarity, the logic here is:<br /> Spells are not under Arcanum Purview<br /> <br /> Active Magic Sight only shows things falling under Arcanum Purview, and while &quot;supernatural effects falling under Arcanum's purview&quot; is shown by Active Sight, &quot;spells&quot; are not a subject under non-Prime purviews.<br /> <br /> Active Magic Sight shows no spells, unless it's prime, because Prime specifically says it allows you to perceive Awakened Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Active Mage Sight shows all magical phenomena. It <i>highlights</i> things that have Supernal correspondences with the Arcana used, including spells and spell-like effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:24:38-07:00","id":1081300,"title":"","content":"Care to find a quote for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:32:27-07:00","id":1081304,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mage Sight highlights all phenomena related to the Arcana used&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Active Mage Sight of any Arcanum also reveals all Awakened spells as they are being cast.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pages 91 and 92 of the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:38:18-07:00","id":1081306,"title":"","content":"Yes. And spells are not phenomena under Arcanum's purview under the discussed interpretation. So if spells are not cast, you can't see them, unless you are using Prime Sight, which specifically mentions that you can see spells. Also, note that you said that ASight shows all &quot;supernatural phenomena&quot;, while it only cares to highlight related ones, which isn't really supported by these quotes. In fact, if the &quot;highlighted&quot; is equal to &quot;registered by Active Sight&quot; (and that would be consistent with how it is used in the text), then it actually ONLY show supernal things that are under your Arcanum's purview...which &quot;spells&quot; aren't.<br /> <br /> &quot;Prime Sight highlights anything the mage can use as a Yantra,<br /> and the presence (if not the composition) of any Awakened spell<br /> or Attainment effect. &quot;<br /> So if you exclude spells of an Arcanum from that's Arcanum purview, logically, you should follow up all the way and make them invisible to Active Sight and to protect the niche of Prime Arcanum, which has &quot;seeing spells&quot; as it's specifically called out Active Sight Effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-20-2017, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:47:11-07:00","id":1081309,"title":"","content":"&quot;related to the Arcana used&quot; is not the same as &quot;under the Arcana's purviews&quot;. A Supernal entity of the Arcanum in question is undoubtedly related to the Arcanum used, but is also undoubtedly <i>not</i> under its purview. Hence, it'd be highlighted, but you couldn't use, say, a Ruling Spirit spell to command a Totem of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> But also of big import here is that Active Mage Sight is a refinement of Peripheral Mage Sight, which alerts a Mage to the presence of <i>all</i> magical phenomena. An Obrimos's Peripheral Sight might cause them to see an ethereal blue flame appear over a strange box that appeared in their Sanctum, which turns into a small bonfire when they expand it to Active Sight, but if the magical effect itself isn't related to Prime or Forces, it won't &quot;highlight&quot; and indicate its connection to that Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Active Mage Sight shows any and all magical phenomena you can sense through the lens of the Arcana you're using it with. &quot;Highlighting&quot; is different to seeing in the first place. Otherwise, there'd be no need to highlight; it'd simply be &quot;shows&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:56:52-07:00","id":1081311,"title":"","content":"It actually is the same, because exact wording is:<br /> &quot;In addition to the above, <b>any supernatural effect falling under <br /> the purview of the Arcanum that the mage can see is highlighted <br /> if she is using the correct Sight. </b>&quot;<br /> <br /> So if a &quot;Life Spell&quot; does not fall under &quot;Life&quot; Purview, you cannot see it. Also, Active Sight doesn't grant you a new sense - it actually only allows you to reinterpret what physical senses give you within symbolism of your Ruling Path. <br /> <br /> &quot;Mage Sight highlights all phenomena related to the Arcana used, <br /> but making sense of the torrent of Patterns is often difficult, and <br /> the <b>mage can only determine the symbols related to phenomena <br /> within her senses</b> \u2014 <b>her Sight won\u2019t let her see through walls <br /> or perceive entities and objects in a state of Twilight. Unveiling <br /> spells and several Attainments allow more specialized analysis of <br /> a mage\u2019s surroundings, either adding capabilities to Mage Sight <br /> or granting extra senses for more information.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you can't see a spell normally, you can't analyze it with Active Sight, because you need to see it with your own eyes in the first place!</b><br /> <br /> Note that the text uses &quot;highlighted&quot; pretty much as a equivalent for, em, &quot;shown by magic sight&quot;. Also, logically, if Active Sight only shows you spells that are currently cast, it doesn't show you spells that are not being cast, which also includes spells that have been successfully cast in the past. <br /> <br /> (By the way, I'm playing a sleep deprived mentally and physically exhausted devil's advocate here. I agree that MSight should show you spells. But I also argue that &quot;Life Spell&quot; should fall under &quot;Life Purview&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T22:58:55-07:00","id":1081313,"title":"","content":"By the way, I love the fact that text talks about Unveiling spells modifying how Magic Sight works, and then you find 0 spells that do that in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:01:05-07:00","id":1081316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081309#post1081309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But also of big import here is that Active Mage Sight is a refinement of Peripheral Mage Sight, which alerts a Mage to the presence of <i>all</i> magical phenomena. An Obrimos's Peripheral Sight might cause them to see an ethereal blue flame appear over a strange box that appeared in their Sanctum, which turns into a small bonfire when they expand it to Active Sight, but if the magical effect itself isn't related to Prime or Forces, it won't &quot;highlight&quot; and indicate its connection to that Arcanum.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Note that Peripheral Mage Sight is triggered by all supernatural events regardless of Arcana, but <br /> unless the mage uses an applicable Active Sight she gains no <br /> information about the phenomenon \u2014 only that it must be <br /> related to an Arcanum she didn\u2019t use.&quot;<br /> So Active Sight doesn't help you with something that Peripheral detected if you didn't look at it with proper Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:05:56-07:00","id":1081319,"title":"","content":"Alright, two things:<br /> <br /> 1. The &quot;In addition to the above&quot; bit you quoted <i>follows</i> the &quot;Mage Sight highlights all phenomena related to the Arcana used&quot; section.<br /> <br /> 2. Mages <i>can</i> see spells normally. Or, at least, sense them. It's how Peripheral Sight works. The reason spells being cast gets brought up is because Peripheral Sight <i>doesn't</i> do that. Nimbus flares happen after the spell is cast, but Active Sight shows you the build-up too.<br /> <br /> The text also doesn't use &quot;highlight&quot; as equivalent for &quot;shown by magic sight&quot;. Animals fall under Life's purview, and, as such, are highlighted by Life Sight. If &quot;highlight&quot; is a synonym for &quot;see&quot;, apparently Mages can't see animals without using Life Sight? Same goes for Prime Sight highlighting Yantras. Why would they need Mage Sight to see a wand?<br /> <br /> Highlight means highlight. It does not mean make visible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:15:34-07:00","id":1081323,"title":"","content":"They don't need a Mage Sight to see a wand, but they need to see a Wand. They also need to see the wand (or touch it, or hear it, or smell it) to see that it's a Wand. Ditto for animal - you see an animal, Life Sight allows you to reinterpret it as a Animal. <br /> <br /> In addition to above follows the &quot;Each Arcanum has a minor mechanical effect, relating to the <br /> base level of perception granted by Active Sight.&quot; section, which lists numerous Active Sight effects for specific Arcana...including &quot; presence (if not the composition) of any Awakened spell <br /> or Attainment effect.&quot; for Prime. <br /> <br /> Look at the sidebar - it actually discusses if Death Sight would &quot;register&quot; a Promethean at all. This alone means that Active Sight doesn't necessarily &quot;register&quot; all supernatural things, only these that fall/relate to their purview. <br /> <br /> If highlight doesn't mean visible, then Active Sight doesn't make *anything* visible, because it doesn't say anything about actually making anything visible. Only that you get to hallucinate connections of the Arcana that...yeah, highlight things.<br /> <br /> &quot;The mage hallucinates, seeing the connections of the Arcana all around her. <br /> Mage Sight highlights all phenomena related to the Arcana used, <br /> but making sense of the torrent of Patterns is often difficult, and <br /> the mage can only determine the symbols related to phenomena <br /> within her senses \u2014 her Sight won\u2019t let her see through walls <br /> or perceive entities and objects in a state of Twilight.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder what a person without preconceptions about Mage and how stuff in Mage works would see this, actually. It doesn't appear to be very helpful to uninitiated and I'm starting to wonder if I'm running it correctly in my home games...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:25:13-07:00","id":1081325,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I'm going to sleep, but here is less facetious note:<br /> I always assumed that &quot;highlight&quot; means that your hallucinations conspire to bring something to your attention using your Path and Nimbus symbolism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:25:37-07:00","id":1081326,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think we've kinda stumbled upon something important here: You're right; Active Mage Sight <i>doesn't</i> show you things (with a few minor exceptions, like Nimbuses, etc.). All it does is highlight things you can see with your Peripheral Sight and your humdrum mortal senses. It highlights phenomena and shows connections, but doesn't actually provide any new sensory data; just information about what is already detected.<br /> <br /> As such, your Peripheral Sight shows you the presence of a spell, and then Prime Sight would say &quot;Yep, this is Awakened magic, alright&quot;. Your mortal eyes show you a shadow in an alleyway, and Life Sight tells you &quot;This is a living creature&quot;. And so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T01:21:55-07:00","id":1081353,"title":"","content":"I asked this in another thread but thought here would be more relevant. So Imbued items, not alot of crunchy rules about them so far, Hopefully SoS will help with them? Anyways the question which tbh might have already been asked, ive not googled this yet, bad me!<br /> <br /> Mage A creates a ring on invisibility imbuing forces 3 &quot;invisibility&quot; spell into the ring, he has its activation be twisting the ring on your finger tho this could be anything. He gives his ring to person B they attempt to use the ring, What happens a) the ring goes invisibile, b) the person goes invisible, c) Person B decides what goes invisible and he could choose person C??<br /> <br /> The attainment says mage A is still in control of the spell and can alter its spell factors, so she decides when the item is imbued and can change it later? When making the ring Mage A decides that option b will happen, but later can make it option a?<br /> <br /> How do spell factors work with imbued items, the dicepool is the arcana level of the spell + users gnosis? This wont let a mortal get many spell factors in so this ring is pretty shit tbh? and thats IF they can actually use spell factors.<br /> <br /> A sleeper twists ring and has 3 dice to become invis for 3 seconds? The making mage controls spell factors but even if they got to choose them it'd be 1 dice for 6 seconds?<br /> <br /> How does reach even work with imbued items? Does the maker or user decide the amount of free reaches? I assume the first is always used for instant casting anyways or do imbued items default of instant casting? You'd obv want to use reach to make the ring Advanced duration so yrou invisible for a useful about of time but is this set at creation or each casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-20-2017, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T15:15:20-07:00","id":1081599,"title":"","content":"If you imbue an item, the item casts the spell essentially as intended. That is, the person (and the ring) turns invisible.<br /> <br /> Being in control of the spell means the Mage can cancel/end it or reduce spell factors at any time. You can't change the spell after the fact in any other way without another spell, and the spell, in this case, is the imbuing itself.<br /> <br /> Spell factors work the same as always.<br /> <br /> Also, Invisibility is Forces 2 now, since it's a Veiling spell.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> My own question: What's the &quot;typical&quot; legal status of Mage cults? Are Pentacle Mages allowed to found cults? Is showing off an attainment a violation of the Lex Magicka?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T15:29:12-07:00","id":1081602,"title":"","content":"Mage cults are probably alright, the GotV and the SL certainly use them frequently for wildly different purposes. FC probably use them a lot to so they can work in their Techne.<br /> <br /> Unless they're specifically prohibited then I assume Mages treat them like any other bits of territory they acquire by marking them somehow and posting a keep out sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:03:52-07:00","id":1081613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081599#post1081599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you imbue an item, the item casts the spell essentially as intended. That is, the person (and the ring) turns invisible.<br /> <br /> Being in control of the spell means the Mage can cancel/end it or reduce spell factors at any time. You can't change the spell after the fact in any other way without another spell, and the spell, in this case, is the imbuing itself.<br /> <br /> Spell factors work the same as always.<br /> <br /> Also, Invisibility is Forces 2 now, since it's a Veiling spell.<br /> <br /> ---</div> </div> </div> </div>The invis spell makes a subject invisible, the caster can determine that subject each casting, can the user of the imbued item do the same or is it set an creation?<br /> What do you base the free reach of the spells on? The arcanum level of the caster (gg sleepers), the arcanum level of the spell? Does the user get to add additional reach making the spell suffer paradox (which the imbued item merit says can happen) but how many dice paradox is base, based on the gnosis of the creator or user? <i>(#edit, its user or 1 if sleeper)</i><br /> <br /> Spell factors work as always? So can the user choose each casting or is it locked in place at creation? Does that mean -2 dice for +1 spell factor makes the ring a chance dice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the item casts the spell essentially as intended. That is, the person (and the ring) turns invisible. </div> </div> </div>Intended by whom, the creator? Does this mean i can setup the invis spell with as many spell factors as i want, imbue it into the spell forcing whoever uses the item to take the penalties when using the item?<br /> <br /> The mage<i> intends</i> for this invis spell to last a month. Lets say he has Gnosis 3 Prime 3 (to imbue) &amp; Forces 2 meaning his base dicepool for Invisibility of 5, he has to use the free reach for instant casting, he has another for advanced duration and would usually take a -4 penalty for a months duration, his intention. How does this translate when another person tries to use this ring? (would need +1 target factor to make both person and ring invis? another -2 penalty?)<br /> <br /> a) they roll arcanum + gnosis always with a -4 penalty and it always causes paradox with a base dice of 2 (gnosis of creator) cos its baked into the item at creation. So a sleeper has a chance dice? Note the -4 penalty is due to the creators free duration from having forces 2, the user doesnt have forces does he get the base -6 because the creator intends for the spell to last a month even tho he doesnt want it too and only needs if for an hour?<br /> <br /> b) each use the user gets to decide for himself how long he wants the spell to last and on whom/what invisibility is cast, he somehow has knowledge of spell factors and reach and can use them as in a normal casting but is limited by a shitty dicepool of the arcanum of the spell?<br /> <br /> Sorry but its still really unclear how this all pans out..but thats for correcting the typo in spell level anyways. Feel free to provide an example imbued item if its easy it'd help alot. Seems to me, all imbued items with a lvl 1 spell effect needing any amount of duration, additional targets or potency to avoid withstand (anything needing sympathy, good luck getting the potency vs withstand for imbued scrying mirrors to work) are going to be close to a chance dice unless the person has a high gnosis??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-22-2017, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T23:19:30-07:00","id":1081722,"title":"","content":"What <i>doesn't</i> count as a temporal sympathy yantra? For example, if you cast a spell targeting a subject's Unchanged past, does their current self not constitute a material yantra? If you cast a spell targeting them 2 days in the past, does their current self not constitute a material yantra? Does it not constitute at the very least, a symbolic yantra? How far can you take this idea? Is a 30-year-old person a symbolic yantra for their 5 year old self? And if you want to target their 5-year-old self, will a photo from when they were seven years old suffice?<br /> <br /> How specific do temporal sympathy yantras have to be?<br /> <br /> It seems weird to me that with Time, you absolutely need a connection to a specific time, but with space, you have the option to use a connection to a person, without needing connections to any of the places that they've been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T03:28:42-07:00","id":1081763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081722#post1081722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>doesn't</i> count as a temporal sympathy yantra? For example, if you cast a spell targeting a subject's Unchanged past, does their current self not constitute a material yantra? If you cast a spell targeting them 2 days in the past, does their current self not constitute a material yantra? Does it not constitute at the very least, a symbolic yantra? How far can you take this idea? Is a 30-year-old person a symbolic yantra for their 5 year old self? And if you want to target their 5-year-old self, will a photo from when they were seven years old suffice?<br /> <br /> How specific do temporal sympathy yantras have to be?<br /> <br /> It seems weird to me that with Time, you absolutely need a connection to a specific time, but with space, you have the option to use a connection to a person, without needing connections to any of the places that they've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal sympathy Yantra? What are you referring to? Both the Sympathetic Range and Temporal Sympathy Attainments requires a sympathy Yantra, which is a subst of Tool Yantras. There is no separate class of sympathy Yantras specific for Temporal Sympathy. You only need an object that represents the subject, which the subject itself never counts as. Thankfully, something simple like a photograph or a lock of hair counts as sympathy Yantra, so you can use that.<br /> <br /> Also, you no longer exactly cast spells &quot;at&quot; the subject in the past, thanks to the errata. In other words, no fireballs from the future suddenly appearing at your face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:06:13-07:00","id":1081916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1081763#post1081763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporal sympathy Yantra? What are you referring to? Both the Sympathetic Range and Temporal Sympathy Attainments requires a sympathy Yantra, which is a subst of Tool Yantras. There is no separate class of sympathy Yantras specific for Temporal Sympathy. You only need an object that represents the subject, which the subject itself never counts as. Thankfully, something simple like a photograph or a lock of hair counts as sympathy Yantra, so you can use that.<br /> <br /> Also, you no longer exactly cast spells &quot;at&quot; the subject in the past, thanks to the errata. In other words, no fireballs from the future suddenly appearing at your face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the section for Sympathy yantras, it specifically distinguishes between yantras for temporal sympathy and for spacial sympathy. For example, Temporal Sympathy yantras have to be tied to the subject, as they were at the time you want to target, while spacial sympathy yantras just have to be tied to the target.<br /> <br /> &quot;Material sympathy represents the subject as he is now, or at the time the mage wants to affect him. It could be a piece of the target\u2019s physical substance, or a recent photograph or recording; an item the subject created within a month is also acceptable.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:13:47-07:00","id":1081922,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> Their Unchanged past is recent enough that the person would still count as a sympathetic Yantra targeting that point in their history. Unchanged for a person is generally somewhere between a scene and a day depending on if anything significant has happened to them. Obviously they can stand in as a Representation or Symbolic Yantra of themselves, and in terms of the Sympathetic casting it makes literally no difference anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-21-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T16:46:27-07:00","id":1082053,"title":"","content":"So in other words, you don't need to do anything to satisfy a the temporal sympathy yantra requirement, except spend a yantra slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:11:08-07:00","id":1082059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082053#post1082053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, you don't need to do anything to satisfy a the temporal sympathy yantra requirement, except spend a yantra slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It has to fulfill the requirements for a Sympathetic Yantra. What you asked about was if the person themselves fulfills that requirement for Temporal Sympathy, the answer is obviously yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T19:15:54-07:00","id":1082095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082059#post1082059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It has to fulfill the requirements for a Sympathetic Yantra. What you asked about was if the person themselves fulfills that requirement for Temporal Sympathy, the answer is obviously yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to cast a temporal sympathy spell, you have to have the person in question available in the first place, unless you're invoking spacial sympathy. So you never actually need to go out of your way to find a temporal sympathy yantra. If you're casting with just temporal sympathy, the person is already there to be used as a yantra. If you're using time and space, the spacial sympathy yantra covers time as well. So either way, the temporal sympathy yantra isn't something you ever need to concern yourself with, except for the yantra slot it consumes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T19:57:32-07:00","id":1082104,"title":"","content":"Do Archmasters age?<br /> Their mortal body is a construct they reform every time they re-enter the Phenomenal world, but does that contruct have to be the same age it was as you last discorporated it?<br /> I'm seeing a very real &quot;Alberto Malich&quot; possibility here. A Mage who has to ration every second he spends back in the physical world, because he's only got so many left.<br /> Spending them one by one, inching closer to the Supernal, and requiring extreme pressure for him to decide to leave the Astral or his Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:01:10-07:00","id":1082106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082059#post1082059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you asked about was if the person themselves fulfills that requirement for Temporal Sympathy, the answer is obviously yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>People <i>don't</i> count as symbolizing themselves for the obvious reason that that's goofy nonsense that defeats the point of having a special category of magical aid. A separated piece of them, sure, relatives, yes, but &quot;I'm using Steve as a symbol of Steve&quot; has never been a terribly sound framing for how to leverage sympathy against people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:11:00-07:00","id":1082109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082106#post1082106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People <i>don't</i> count as symbolizing themselves for the obvious reason that that's goofy nonsense that defeats the point of having a special category of magical aid. A separated piece of them, sure, relatives, yes, but &quot;I'm using Steve as a symbol of Steve&quot; has never been a terribly sound framing for how to leverage sympathy against people.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm not. I'm using Steve as a symbol of younger Steve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:25:44-07:00","id":1082113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082109#post1082109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm not. I'm using Steve as a symbol of younger Steve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Younger Steve is part of the set of all things Steve here referred to as &quot;Steve.&quot; This is pedantry that you do not need to engage in if your aim is to understand how the rules are intended to work to encourage particular character behaviors. The subject of a spell is not their own referent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:53:13-07:00","id":1082122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082113#post1082113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Younger Steve is part of the set of all things Steve here referred to as &quot;Steve.&quot; This is pedantry that you do not need to engage in if your aim is to understand how the rules are intended to work to encourage particular character behaviors. The subject of a spell is not their own referent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's pedantic or goofy nonsense at all. If I understand you correctly, pulling up the camera on your phone, and pointing it at the target of your spell would satisfy a representational sympathetic yantra, but simply looking at them wouldn't. If anything, that explanation seems like the goofy nonsensical interpretation, especially if you're just trying to cast Postcognition on yourself.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to understand what obstacle a temporal sympathy yantra allows the mage to overcome. At first I thought it was meant to be a connection to a specific time in that person's past, since that's what the sympathy yantra description says, but then people told me that it's not a connection to a moment in time, it's a connection to a person. Then I wondered why you would need a special extra connection to the person themselves when they're already physically present. Is it that that you have to be able to touch and manipulate the sympathetic yantra, and people won't usually let you do that?<br /> <br /> The whole point of Yantras is that you use them as an example of what you want your spell to do so that it's easier to visualize exactly what you want, but if a temporal sympathy yantra is meant to represent a person, and not a moment in time, why can't you just visualize the person in your spell from looking at them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 04-21-2017, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:09:55-07:00","id":1082127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082106#post1082106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People <i>don't</i> count as symbolizing themselves for the obvious reason that that's goofy nonsense that defeats the point of having a special category of magical aid. A separated piece of them, sure, relatives, yes, but &quot;I'm using Steve as a symbol of Steve&quot; has never been a terribly sound framing for how to leverage sympathy against people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you fulfill the requirements to be a Material Sympathetic Yantra to yourself, which is the strongest level of connection a Sympathetic Yantra can get, it seems weird to me that you wouldn't then be able to use yourself to fulfill the possibilities of the other two simply because you're pushing further back in time. At the very least nothing can escape its past entirely as its past marks shape its present condition, and you thus carry your past with you on at least the symbolic level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:11:57-07:00","id":1082129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082122#post1082122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first I thought it was meant to be a connection to a specific time in that person's past, since that's what the sympathy yantra description says</div> </div> </div> </div>If you didn't have the person on hand this would be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:15:08-07:00","id":1082130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082129#post1082129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you didn't have the person on hand this would be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that interpretation is that you explicitly HAVE to have the person on hand in order to use temporal sympathy, unless you are also using spacial sympathy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:22:18-07:00","id":1082133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082130#post1082130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that interpretation is that you explicitly HAVE to have the person on hand in order to use temporal sympathy, unless you are also using spacial sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Most Acanthus mostly do Time stuff to themselves by default because it's a lot easier. Though if you've got Space 2 and Time 2 it's just another point of Mana and a more specific Yantra to affect something via Spatial and Temporal Sympathy simultaneously so big whoop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:30:04-07:00","id":1082134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082133#post1082133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much. Most Acanthus mostly do Time stuff to themselves by default because it's a lot easier. Though if you've got Space 2 and Time 2 it's just another point of Mana and a more specific Yantra to affect something via Spatial and Temporal Sympathy simultaneously so big whoop.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't answered the question. Do you need a connection to a time in a person's past, or to a person themselves? The Sympathy yantra description mentions multiple times, having a connection to a time in a person's past.<br /> <br /> And if you do need a connection to their past, how lenient is the system? I can imagine two extremes: one in which a Time mage who wants to cast postcognition regularly has to keep photos of themselves on each day so that they have the right yantra to look back at their past on the day they want, and another extreme in which a Time mage just needs any old photo of themselves in the past.<br /> <br /> For that matter, does Postcognition even require the attainment? It says with Time 2 you can look back further than Unchanged, but doesn't mention needing to use the attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:37:54-07:00","id":1082139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082122#post1082122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's pedantic or goofy nonsense at all. If I understand you correctly, pulling up the camera on your phone, and pointing it at the target of your spell would satisfy a representational sympathetic yantra, but simply looking at them wouldn't. If anything, that explanation seems like the goofy nonsensical interpretation, especially if you're just trying to cast Postcognition on yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Take a picture and focus on the picture&quot; seems like a goofy nonsensical interpretation of the more likely thing to <i>be an instrument for doing better at magic targeting a subject</i>?<br /> <br /> You replied to a statement I made in response to another person that had only a secondary relation to the subject of the Temporal Sympathy Attainment. I don't especially care if your character wants to cast Postcognition on themselves but somehow doesn't know their own sympathetic name. That's your prerogative and quite apart from the matter of whether someone counts as a reference to themselves for the purposes of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just trying to understand what obstacle a temporal sympathy yantra allows the mage to overcome. At first I thought it was meant to be a connection to a specific time in that person's past, since that's what the sympathy yantra description says, but then people told me that it's not a connection to a moment in time, it's a connection to a person. </div> </div> </div>I do not agree with the people telling you this and it is a mistake to engage with me as though I did. That is all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082127#post1082127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you fulfill the requirements to be a Material Sympathetic Yantra to yourself, which is the strongest level of connection a Sympathetic Yantra can get, it seems weird to me that you wouldn't then be able to use yourself to fulfill the possibilities of the other two simply because you're pushing further back in time. At the very least nothing can escape its past entirely as its past marks shape its present condition, and you thus carry your past with you on at least the symbolic level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy Tools are all things that are representations of the spell's subject \u2014 they're magical proxies by definition.<br /> <br /> \u200bStep outside the confines of the Attainment for a moment and look at the role of Yantras in the narrative \u2014 does &quot;the person I'm targeting is right in front of me&quot; have nearly the same symbolic weight and story-significance as &quot;I stole this person's belongings, kidnapped their loved ones, or carved off a physical piece of them&quot; for the purposes of getting a bonus sufficient to offset a step in a spell factor? Does it make any kind of sense to give the standard spellcasting range bands blanket access to a bonus equivalent to drawback-intensive assists like concentration or runes by treating &quot;I can see my target&quot; the same as &quot;I have a lock of my target's hair&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T22:06:15-07:00","id":1082149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082139#post1082139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Take a picture and focus on the picture&quot; seems like a goofy nonsensical interpretation of the more likely thing to <i>be an instrument for doing better at magic targeting a subject</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I still think it's goofy, after reading the opening description of what Yantras are on page 119. It says that a yantra is a mnemonic for focusing a mage's thoughts into an imago. Why would it be easier to focus your thoughts on a picture of a person, than on the actual person in front of you? I can see how a picture would be helpful if you're casting at someone you can't see. I can see how a picture of someone when they were 5 would help you cast through time back to when they were 5. Heck, I can understand how holding onto a lock of their hair could help you even if they're standing in front of you. What I don't see is how a photo of them would help when you can already just see them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You replied to a statement I made in response to another person that had only a secondary relation to the subject of the Temporal Sympathy Attainment. I don't especially care if your character wants to cast Postcognition on themselves but somehow doesn't know their own sympathetic name. That's your prerogative and quite apart from the matter of whether someone counts as a reference to themselves for the purposes of magic. </div> </div> </div>Now hold on. You say in the very next paragraph that you disagree with people who say that temporal sympathy yantras are representative of people, in contrast to those who think that temporal sympathy yantras are representative of times in a person's past. Yet here you say that a person's sympathetic name is sufficient to cast a temporal sympathy spell. How does a sympathetic name relate to some specific arbitrary time in a person's past, that it would help you to focus on that event?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not agree with the people telling you this and it is a mistake to engage with me as though I did. That is all. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so then if you disagree with those people, are you instead saying that to cast a Temporal Sympathy spell, your sympathetic yantra MUST relate to the target at the time you want to target, as it says in the description of Sympathy yantras? If so, how much leeway is there in the time the yantra represents, and the time you want to target? Does this mean that a Time mage must keep photos of themselves from every day in their past to use as yantras?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sympathy Tools are all things that are representations of the spell's subject \u2014 they're magical proxies by definition.<br /> <br /> Step outside the confines of the Attainment for a moment and look at the role of Yantras in the narrative \u2014 does &quot;the person I'm targeting is right in front of me&quot; have nearly the same symbolic weight and story-significance as &quot;I stole this person's belongings, kidnapped their loved ones, or carved off a physical piece of them&quot; for the purposes of getting a bonus sufficient to offset a step in a spell factor? </div> </div> </div>Yes the things you mention have strong weight and story significance, but they're mechanically redundant and unnecessary when you could just point a cell phone camera at someone to get a photo of them. I'm trying to get an idea of how this should work in a way that is first mechanically consistent, so that I can make any changes that are needed to make it thematically consistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it make any kind of sense to give the standard spellcasting range bands blanket access to a bonus equivalent to drawback-intensive assists like concentration or runes by treating &quot;I can see my target&quot; the same as &quot;I have a lock of my target's hair&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I asked whether material sympathy is dependent on physically handling the yantra, for precisely this reason. It would explain why you can't get material sympathy from a person near you, just by looking at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 04-22-2017, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T22:14:04-07:00","id":1082150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082104#post1082104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Archmasters age?<br /> Their mortal body is a construct they reform every time they re-enter the Phenomenal world, but does that contruct have to be the same age it was as you last discorporated it?<br /> I'm seeing a very real &quot;Alberto Malich&quot; possibility here. A Mage who has to ration every second he spends back in the physical world, because he's only got so many left.<br /> Spending them one by one, inching closer to the Supernal, and requiring extreme pressure for him to decide to leave the Astral or his Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says they don't age in their golden road, but nothing about being immortal in the fallen world. So yes, they would age. They would have to excise their ability to age, or prolong their life with magic in order to overcome this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T22:41:12-07:00","id":1082155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082149#post1082149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I still think it's goofy, after reading the opening description of what Yantras are on page 119. It says that a yantra is a mnemonic for focusing a mage's thoughts into an imago. Why would it be easier to focus your thoughts on a picture of a person, than on the actual person in front of you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a picture is a representation and not a moving and changing thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now hold on. </div> </div> </div>No. You dragged me into the temporal sympathy argument when my aim was the specific matter of material sympathy as it relates to its referent subjects. I'm not here for you to interrogate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You say in the very next paragraph that you disagree with people who say that temporal sympathy yantras are representative of people, in contrast to those who think that temporal sympathy yantras are representative of times in a person's past. Yet here you say that a person's sympathetic name is sufficient to cast a temporal sympathy spell. How does a sympathetic name relate to some specific arbitrary time in a person's past, that it would help you to focus on that event? </div> </div> </div>A person's sympathetic name is formed at the point where they start being a person and not having it degrades both forms of sympathy besides. If there was any Sympathy Yantra that I would treat as generally applicable to fairly nonspecific times in a person's life like the vague scenario of &quot;I cast Postcognition on myself,&quot; that would be it. More distinctive periods of time call for greater focus and also actual specificity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, so then if you disagree with those people, are you instead saying that to cast a Temporal Sympathy spell, your sympathetic yantra MUST relate to the target at the time you want to target, as it says in the description of Sympathy yantras? If so, how much leeway is there in the time the yantra represents, and the time you want to target? Does this mean that a Time mage must keep photos of themselves from every day in their past to use as yantras? </div> </div> </div>If they want to go back to every specific day in their lives and they changed frequently from day to day, sure. Collecting mementoes from significant events is exactly the kind of thing you would expect someone who makes regular use of object-dependent time-magic to do, but the game isn't designed under the assumption that characters are going to be aimlessly combing the sands of time as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:16:23-07:00","id":1082225,"title":"","content":"This question has been asked before, but I didn't see a thorough or firm answer...Can someone explain a few things about Ghost Gate? <br /> <br /> 1) If I'm understanding correctly, the duration for the spell refers to how long the gate is open, not how long you remain in Twilight. Is that correct? If you use the Reach option to target a specific subject rather than opening a gate, does this mean you can force someone into Twilight indefinitely if they have no access to spells that help them move back to material form?<br /> <br /> 2) If someone walks through a Ghost Gate into Twilight and then back through it, are their clothes destroyed? What about imbued items? Artifacts? Weapons and Path/Order tools?<br /> <br /> 3) If yes to #2, can someone explain or clarify how to recover your items? Can you cast another spell, and if so, does it need to be an indefinite duration or is it reasonable to make a Reach option that makes the effect Lasting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:53:26-07:00","id":1082239,"title":"","content":"#1) I believe that when the spell duration ends the Gate disappears and the ones that used it reappear in real space. The same for the reach to turn them into a Twilight form, when the spell ends the rematerialize.<br /> #2) It says that the objects are destroyed it doesn't delineate between powerful items, however that being said I would leave that up to the ST, I feel it is one of their purview. I personally would not let something of power be destroyed that easily.<br /> #3) Anything that is destroyed can be recovered by casting Touch of the Grave and reaching into Twilight and bringing it back. As to weather it stays for ever in the fallen world is once again an ST call. I personally would allow it to stay in the fallen world, as they were not naturally destroyed in the first place. This also is in to the article in the Open Development for the upcomming Signs of Sorcery where they make purified substance by passing it through a Ghost Gate and then retrieving it just to repeat the process several dozen time. The final result is a petrified substance that sticks around afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:28:43-07:00","id":1082259,"title":"","content":"Given the descriptions, I'd say you have leeway either way, but I'd disagree with Hardwire.<br /> <br /> 1. I'd say that Ghost Gate, in its non-Reach form, can trap someone indefinitely. Its Reach form cannot. The reason for this is in the structure of the spells; Ghost Gate by itself is a spell which creates a transformative zone that rewrites a part of whatever passes through it, from &quot;Material&quot; to &quot;Ephemeral&quot;. The Gate itself is the spell's creation but the effects of that Gate are not. The same is true for Co-Location, which temporarily rewrites a section of the world so that anything within it has its location rewritten from &quot;Here&quot; to &quot;There&quot;. Once the spell lapses, the changes inflicted are not undone.<br /> <br /> However, the +1 Reach version of Ghost Gate is different; there, the target is that thing which Ghost Gate's regular version rewrites and, like all such magic, its effects are temporary. There, once the Duration wears out, the subject plops back into meatspace.<br /> <br /> 2. Presumably, all mundane objects are destroyed, but bringing them back through the Ghost Gate seems like it'd reverse the process. Artifacts, I feel, are a special class of thing, which cannot be destroyed by this process. Forced into a Twilight state, yes, but... Still themselves. Retrieve it with a spell and it's still an Artifact, not merely an ephemeral copy.<br /> <br /> 3. You can make another Ghost Gate, walk in, walk out. Or you can cast a spell to pull it through as ephemera, in which case it's more prone to breakage. Either works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T08:57:29-07:00","id":1082282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082259#post1082259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the descriptions, I'd say you have leeway either way, but I'd disagree with Hardwire.<br /> <br /> 1. I'd say that Ghost Gate, in its non-Reach form, can trap someone indefinitely. Its Reach form cannot. The reason for this is in the structure of the spells; Ghost Gate by itself is a spell which creates a transformative zone that rewrites a part of whatever passes through it, from &amp;quot;Material&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;Ephemeral&amp;quot;. The Gate itself is the spell's creation but the effects of that Gate are not. The same is true for Co-Location, which temporarily rewrites a section of the world so that anything within it has its location rewritten from &amp;quot;Here&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;There&amp;quot;. Once the spell lapses, the changes inflicted are not undone.<br /> <br /> However, the +1 Reach version of Ghost Gate is different; there, the target is that thing which Ghost Gate's regular version rewrites and, like all such magic, its effects are temporary. There, once the Duration wears out, the subject plops back into meatspace.<br /> <br /> 2. Presumably, all mundane objects are destroyed, but bringing them back through the Ghost Gate seems like it'd reverse the process. Artifacts, I feel, are a special class of thing, which cannot be destroyed by this process. Forced into a Twilight state, yes, but... Still themselves. Retrieve it with a spell and it's still an Artifact, not merely an ephemeral copy.<br /> <br /> 3. You can make another Ghost Gate, walk in, walk out. Or you can cast a spell to pull it through as ephemera, in which case it's more prone to breakage. Either works.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes perfect sense to me and I like it a lot. I know a lot of it comes down to ST interpretation, but this sounds good to me. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T11:40:57-07:00","id":1082327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082139#post1082139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bStep outside the confines of the Attainment for a moment and look at the role of Yantras in the narrative \u2014 does &quot;the person I'm targeting is right in front of me&quot; have nearly the same symbolic weight and story-significance as &quot;I stole this person's belongings, kidnapped their loved ones, or carved off a physical piece of them&quot; for the purposes of getting a bonus sufficient to offset a step in a spell factor? Does it make any kind of sense to give the standard spellcasting range bands blanket access to a bonus equivalent to drawback-intensive assists like concentration or runes by treating &quot;I can see my target&quot; the same as &quot;I have a lock of my target's hair&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but I think that having the person themselves still ought to be able to fill in on the Temporal Sympathy for being a Symbol of their younger selves, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T14:27:20-07:00","id":1082389,"title":"","content":"Another question: Is it possible to cast a spell that makes a Mage forget that they are Awakened, or some other way to temporarily prevent a target Mage from being able to cast spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T15:51:39-07:00","id":1082414,"title":"","content":"The former is a Mind Fraying spell. The latter is a Mind or Prime Unraveling spell, and could probably only inflict a penalty on the target's casting roll, not block it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:06:48-07:00","id":1082421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082389#post1082389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: Is it possible to cast a spell that makes a Mage forget that they are Awakened, or some other way to temporarily prevent a target Mage from being able to cast spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Such wholesale destruction of memory would require an incredible amount of Potency on a Mind-Wipe spell (Mind 5).<br /> However if the Mage decides to cast a spell, there's no magic which can prevent him from attempting to do so, bar counterspelling or archmastery.<br /> What's more, they'd only have to experience peripheral mage sight and they'd be on their way to realising their powers again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:30:29-07:00","id":1082431,"title":"","content":"You probably can destroy an memory of Awakening, or destroy the concept of &quot;Awakened&quot; in the person, leading them to be very confused, but being Awakened is a *state*. You can't stop remembering you are Awakened, because it's like forgetting that you can see. You don't need to understand biochemistry and physics behind your ability to see stuff in order to see stuff, you don't even need to know that what you are doing is &quot;seeing&quot;. Being Awakened is like that, too.<br /> <br /> I assume that a lot of persons understanding and ability to do magic is not stored in memories or brain or muscles or even &quot;general Soul area&quot;, but in the Gnosis insolated by the Soul (or vice versa, I don't remember how Dave explained it when we asked why there is a difference between Sever Sleeping and Sever Awakened Soul), which would mean that in order to fuck with it, you need the same tools that allow you to fuck with Awakened Soul using Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-22-2017, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:22:18-07:00","id":1082499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082327#post1082327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, but I think that having the person themselves still ought to be able to fill in on the Temporal Sympathy for being a Symbol of their younger selves, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in a meaningful sense \u2014 again, step outside the confines of the example for a moment: try applying this logic to things that aren't people.<br /> <br /> The main intersection of my hometown has remained the same intersection for as long as I've lived there, but if I were to show it as it is now to myself fifteen years ago, I would barely recognize it, because the pavement, the street signs, the local businesses, the buildings, and intersection across the bridge have all changed so dramatically that I'm actually having trouble remembering what parts of the walk-up looked like back then. Even if I <i>did</i> have a clear memory of the old layout, I certainly wouldn't consider the current one symbolically relevant to the old one.<br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how semiotic quandaries like Your Grandfather's Axe interact with treating something's present self as an unqualified symbol of all of its past selves \u2014 you may still be driving &quot;the same&quot; car that you got in college, but the muffler replacement you got last August isn't going to help you restore the vehicle to the way it was when it was hot off the lot.<br /> <br /> Symbolism requires significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:29:47-07:00","id":1082501,"title":"","content":"Does Postcognition require temporal sympathy to look into your distant past? The description says you can look further back than Unchanged with Time 2, but never explicitly mentions Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <br /> Do Occultation and Shadow Name make it more difficult for you to cast temporal sympathy-based spells on yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:42:24-07:00","id":1082504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ; &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">By default,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">the caster may only view Unchanged subjects, but with Time<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022 <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">she may view the more distant past, in which case the spell<br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">is Withstood by temporal sympathy.</span></span></b></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Further back than unchanged requires temportal sympathy. Occultation says it &quot;allows&quot; a mage to hide so one assumes the mage has a choice? As for shadow name id say it can also be bypassed by yourself as you know the difference between your magical self and true self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-22-2017, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T21:01:46-07:00","id":1082507,"title":"","content":"Can a single mage use two of his own soulstones in the creation of a Demesne?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A mage can create a Demesne using one or more soul stones</span></span>. </div> </div> </div> Check!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A Demesne is built on the foundation of one or<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> more soul stones. The size of a Demesne is determined by the<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> number of soul stones involved in its creation </span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> Check!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">(or in other words,<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> by the number of mages who contribute to its creation).</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> Shit....In other words? Really?<br /> <br /> There is not other txt that implies its one stone per mage except that annoying last quote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T21:38:53-07:00","id":1082515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082499#post1082499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in a meaningful sense \u2014 again, step outside the confines of the example for a moment: try applying this logic to things that aren't people.<br /> <br /> The main intersection of my hometown has remained the same intersection for as long as I've lived there, but if I were to show it as it is now to myself fifteen years ago, I would barely recognize it, because the pavement, the street signs, the local businesses, the buildings, and intersection across the bridge have all changed so dramatically that I'm actually having trouble remembering what parts of the walk-up looked like back then. Even if I <i>did</i> have a clear memory of the old layout, I certainly wouldn't consider the current one symbolically relevant to the old one.<br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how semiotic quandaries like Your Grandfather's Axe interact with treating something's present self as an unqualified symbol of all of its past selves \u2014 you may still be driving &quot;the same&quot; car that you got in college, but the muffler replacement you got last August isn't going to help you restore the vehicle to the way it was when it was hot off the lot.<br /> <br /> Symbolism requires significance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So if I get this correctly, you still require something that symbolizes the past of the thing you're trying to reach beyond just the thing itself? I'm sorry, I'm terrible without concrete examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T22:06:24-07:00","id":1082518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082515#post1082515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I get this correctly, you still require something that symbolizes the past of the thing you're trying to reach beyond just the thing itself? I'm sorry, I'm terrible without concrete examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Pieces of a target can generally be taken as good for getting back to the point of separation, as can lost personal effects \u2014 if you kicked off a shoe and lost a fingertip running from a rogue chainsaw-devil, the shoe and the fingertip could both be used to return to the scene of the pursuit. Mementoes of significant events likewise serve as markers of a change, whether they're a piece of the rope from an outlaw's hanging or a party hat from a young relative's eighth birthday, and thus can bring you into closer alignment with those spans of time.<br /> <br /> You could even use a person who attended an event as a Sympathy Yantra for scrutinizing the past of the location where it took place, probably, but that's a markedly different thing from using them as an Instrument for enhancing the view of their own past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T02:52:43-07:00","id":1082547,"title":"","content":"What's the quickest and most efficient way to create an explosion using Matter 3 or less and using as least inconvenient resources as possible? I get a feeling that some air targetting Ruling should do the trick...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:45:23-07:00","id":1082580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082547#post1082547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the quickest and most efficient way to create an explosion using Matter 3 or less and using as least inconvenient resources as possible? I get a feeling that some air targetting Ruling should do the trick...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lodestone to create a higher density of water vapor in an area, throw in a nugget of Potassium from a safe distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:50:08-07:00","id":1082582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082547#post1082547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the quickest and most efficient way to create an explosion using Matter 3 or less and using as least inconvenient resources as possible? I get a feeling that some air targetting Ruling should do the trick...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you hadn't asked for least inconvenient resources possible I'd suggest Shrink and Grow on a piece of uranium, plutonium or other fissile material and just increase its mass until you reach critical mass.<br /> The way to do it without specific materials would probably be to compress something to the point where the internal pressure is high enough to cause an explosion. But I'm not sure if it should be a Reach on Shaping, a Reach on Shrink and Grow, or a separate spell altogether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082580#post1082580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lodestone to create a higher density of water vapor in an area, throw in a nugget of Potassium from a safe distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all you'd need a nugget of potassium. Secondly, are you certain that potassium reacts that violently with increased humidity? I personally doubt that, but I'm no chemist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-23-2017, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:03:57-07:00","id":1082589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082582#post1082582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you hadn't asked for least inconvenient resources possible I'd suggest Shrink and Grow on a piece of uranium, plutonium or other fissile material and just increase its mass until you reach critical mass.<br /> The way to do it without specific materials would probably be to compress something to the point where the internal pressure is high enough to cause an explosion. But I'm not sure if it should be a Reach on Shaping, a Reach on Shrink and Grow, or a separate spell altogether.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Does shrink and grow alter mass/weight? If i shrink my car down does it become link a toy car and i pick it up, or does one need to add Forces to alter its weight? I can see two interpretations possible, the car is toy sized but as heavy (in before it'd leave a crater or sommat) or its toy car sized weight and i can pick it up and put it in my pocket. Personally id say you need to add forces (2?) to shrink and grow for that..<br /> <br /> Didnt study chemistry but im sure theres lots of violent reactions possible from stuff you can find in schools so probably not that inconvenient?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:12:42-07:00","id":1082592,"title":"","content":"I think it changes only the size. Leaving you with a very heavy toy car.<br /> Edit: As to explosions. You could possible grant just properties of an explosive. Make a floor flammable as nitroglycerin but leave all other properties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 04-23-2017, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:15:48-07:00","id":1082594,"title":"","content":"Forces governs the force of gravity, but mass is a property of matter and should fall under Matter. Weight is the result of gravity acting upon mass so both Forces and Matter can change weight, but does it in different ways.<br /> <br /> Since Shrink and Grow doesn't specify I'd assume mass changes with size so that density is unaffected. Otherwise I think the language would mention volume instead of just Size. I can also add that the trait Size seems to loosely correspond to weight in addition to volume when reading other rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:18:50-07:00","id":1082596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082582#post1082582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all you'd need a nugget of potassium. Secondly, are you certain that potassium reacts that violently with increased humidity? I personally doubt that, but I'm no chemist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potassium reacts violently with oxygen and even more violently with water, it has to be kept in a special oil that coats it to prevent it from immediately reacting with the normal atmosphere when withdrawn from its container. So yeah, an area of very high humidity would do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:19:26-07:00","id":1082597,"title":"","content":"Both option should be possible with Matter. Depending on your original reading of Shrink and Grow you should be able to Reach for the other option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:46:48-07:00","id":1082609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082596#post1082596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potassium reacts violently with oxygen and even more violently with water, it has to be kept in a special oil that coats it to prevent it from immediately reacting with the normal atmosphere when withdrawn from its container. So yeah, an area of very high humidity would do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that potassium, like all the other alkali metals, reacts with air, but it doesn't normally do so violently. And I thought humidity would have a very marginal effect on potassium in comparison to the oxygen considering that specific humidity at any reasonable air temperatures maxes out at ca 30 grams per cubic metre of air (roughly 1 gram per degree Celsius above 0). And I don't think Lodestone, as a Compelling spell, would be able to oversaturate the air with humidity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:48:34-07:00","id":1082610,"title":"","content":"Can you use Correspondence to find out someone's sympathetic name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:57:21-07:00","id":1082611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082610#post1082610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Correspondence to find out someone's sympathetic name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not directly since it only reveals emotional information not actual information, as for instance it mentions in the spell you could learn that a strong connection is to the subject's childhood home, but that wouldn't give you a street address.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:46:09-07:00","id":1082633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082610#post1082610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Correspondence to find out someone's sympathetic name?</div> </div> </div> </div>However, an ST could allow a Space Knowing spell Withstood Shadow Name (if the subject is currently acting in their magical persona) to find out a character's sympathetic name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-23-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:35:00-07:00","id":1082664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082610#post1082610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Correspondence to find out someone's sympathetic name?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said the answer is no. However how would using mind work to find somebodys sympathetic name? Sleepers probably dont have that as a concept so using &quot;psychic domination&quot; with &quot;tell me your sympathetic name&quot; wont work while &quot;tell me your real name&quot; might work except for people who have changed their name later in life (marriage?).<br /> <br /> Personally I would not allow any space spell to find out somebodys sympathetic name, how does space pull information from somebodies mind exactly or gather information from bits of paper?<br /> <br /> You could maybe find out their name on a birth certificate if you had some link to the person and did some comparing? Sorta like is this bit of hair that person on the birth certificate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:14:30-07:00","id":1082691,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm. I'm kinda tired so my mind isn't working properly. I think the inspiration for this was the effect that happens when, during a fire, opening a door to a burning room might cause an explosion? Wasn't the explosion caused by differences in air between one room and another, being basically a violent sideffect of it trying to attain equilibrium?<br /> Maybe a sudden Shrink targeted at a &quot;Area worth of Air&quot; would cause similar reaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:17:28-07:00","id":1082693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082664#post1082664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As others have said the answer is no. However how would using mind work to find somebodys sympathetic name? Sleepers probably dont have that as a concept so using &quot;psychic domination&quot; with &quot;tell me your sympathetic name&quot; wont work while &quot;tell me your real name&quot; might work except for people who have changed their name later in life (marriage?).<br /> <br /> Personally I would not allow any space spell to find out somebodys sympathetic name, how does space pull information from somebodies mind exactly or gather information from bits of paper?<br /> <br /> You could maybe find out their name on a birth certificate if you had some link to the person and did some comparing? Sorta like is this bit of hair that person on the birth certificate?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sympathetic name is not part of the mind. Someone who has no concept of sympathetic names or doesn't remember their own for whatever reason can't divulge them. But it is part of your Pattern.<br /> The reason Space should work is because the entire concept of sympathy is under the purview of Space. I'd say sympathetic names falls under that concept. It's not like you need Mind to be able to read the subject's sympathetic connections either, despite them most often being defined as relationships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:19:41-07:00","id":1082695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082691#post1082691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm. I'm kinda tired so my mind isn't working properly. I think the inspiration for this was the effect that happens when, during a fire, opening a door to a burning room might cause an explosion? Wasn't the explosion caused by differences in air between one room and another, being basically a violent sideffect of it trying to attain equilibrium?<br /> Maybe a sudden Shrink targeted at a &quot;Area worth of Air&quot; would cause similar reaction?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backdraft\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/USMC-071117-M-1283D-084.jpg/1280px-USMC-071117-M-1283D-084.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backdraft\" target=\"_blank\"> Backdraft - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backdraft\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backdraft </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> um, have no clue tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:30:38-07:00","id":1082702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082693#post1082693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sympathetic name is not part of the mind. Someone who has no concept of sympathetic names or doesn't remember their own for whatever reason can't divulge them. But it is part of your Pattern.<br /> The reason Space should work is because the entire concept of sympathy is under the purview of Space. I'd say sympathetic names falls under that concept. It's not like you need Mind to be able to read the subject's sympathetic connections either, despite them most often being defined as relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, ok yeh. Maybe some form of space knowing spell will reveal the name in the pattern? the difference between knowing the name and not is only 1 potency anyways so its not like hiding it should take up to much of your time, shadow names are there for the yantras and stuff the fact they also hide your name is a smaller side effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T12:51:42-07:00","id":1082740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082691#post1082691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm. I'm kinda tired so my mind isn't working properly. I think the inspiration for this was the effect that happens when, during a fire, opening a door to a burning room might cause an explosion? Wasn't the explosion caused by differences in air between one room and another, being basically a violent sideffect of it trying to attain equilibrium?<br /> Maybe a sudden Shrink targeted at a &amp;quot;Area worth of Air&amp;quot; would cause similar reaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Shrink/Grow assumes that the atmosphere reaches equilibrium at the same time the target achieves its new Size, thus avoiding a pressure wave implosion or explosion during size change. I could see a Reach being added so it does damage inside the area of the spell as a result of pressure differential though. It'd work just like any other direct damage spell at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T06:19:12-07:00","id":1082989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082547#post1082547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the quickest and most efficient way to create an explosion using Matter 3 or less and using as least inconvenient resources as possible? I get a feeling that some air targetting Ruling should do the trick...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd simply go with Windstrike, with an additional Reach for Advanced Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:08:55-07:00","id":1082998,"title":"","content":"Question about magical defense stacking, for example having at the same time a spell that protects against mental compulsion through clash of wills and a prime ward that modifies the incoming spells' withstand.<br /> <br /> Does an incoming spell, which could be halted by both the defense in example, have to pass through both?<br /> <br /> If yes, the spell must first break through clash of wills and then through the whitstand value or vice versa? Or it is mage's choice?<br /> If no, only the one with the greater potency applies?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:28:58-07:00","id":1083005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082998#post1082998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about magical defense stacking, for example having at the same time a spell that protects against mental compulsion through clash of wills and a prime ward that modifies the incoming spells' withstand.<br /> <br /> Does an incoming spell, which could be halted by both the defense in example, have to pass through both?<br /> <br /> If yes, the spell must first break through clash of wills and then through the whitstand value or vice versa? Or it is mage's choice?<br /> If no, only the one with the greater potency applies?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It has to pass both and for the sake of the gameflow I'd say that withstand is applied first. Less rolling = better experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:30:50-07:00","id":1083006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083005#post1083005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has to pass both and for the sake of the gameflow I'd say that withstand is applied first. Less rolling = better experience.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I imagined, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT]<br /> Oh, yes, what about if two or more defense that grant a clash of wills can block an incoming spell? Do they stack or only one can be rolled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","user":"Khalendas","date":". 04-24-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:40:33-07:00","id":1083008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083006#post1083006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As I imagined, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT]<br /> Oh, yes, what about if two or more defense that grant a clash of wills can block an incoming spell? Do they stack or only one can be rolled?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Per spell stacking rules only the highest potency one is in effect. Even if it grants less dice than the lower potency one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:41:52-07:00","id":1083009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083008#post1083008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Per spell stacking rules only the highest potency one is in effect. Even if it grants less dice than the lower potency one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:49:28-07:00","id":1083033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083005#post1083005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has to pass both and for the sake of the gameflow I'd say that withstand is applied first. Less rolling = better experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember that the spell should've Clashed at the time of casting if Withstand is lowered later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T22:48:52-07:00","id":1083348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1082989#post1082989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd simply go with Windstrike, with an additional Reach for Advanced Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>We specifically don't want to go for Windstrike, because it's a Direct Damage spell, and thus deals only Bashing, can't be &quot;combined&quot; with a similar spell, and in general, the player in question want to create an effect where damage is a side-effect and a consequence of &quot;physics&quot; kicking in. Kind of like how controlling electricity to apply environmental rules using Forces isn't a Direct Damage spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T00:17:56-07:00","id":1083372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083348#post1083348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We specifically don't want to go for Windstrike, because it's a Direct Damage spell, and thus deals only Bashing, can't be &quot;combined&quot; with a similar spell, and in general, the player in question want to create an effect where damage is a side-effect and a consequence of &quot;physics&quot; kicking in. Kind of like how controlling electricity to apply environmental rules using Forces isn't a Direct Damage spell</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you could use weaving to increase the reactivity of the air within the spells area and wait for someone to light up a cigarette?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T00:32:27-07:00","id":1083375,"title":"","content":"I like the imagery of the mage throwing a cigarette into the &quot;charged zone&quot; to explode it, yes, hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:40:04-07:00","id":1083442,"title":"","content":"A reason to play a chain smoking John Constantine direct from the comics? Hell yeah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T04:17:35-07:00","id":1083911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083372#post1083372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps you could use weaving to increase the reactivity of the air within the spells area and wait for someone to light up a cigarette?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://data.whicdn.com/images/165211040/large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Edit: The reference might not be obvious to everyone - Roy can change the oxygen content of an area at-will, and his gloves produce sparks. Oxygen-rich environment + ignition source == boom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T04:24:19-07:00","id":1083913,"title":"","content":"Generally this would still be better covered by a damage spell mechanic, though.<br /> Considering lethal damage via &quot;this is now explosive&quot; will usually be patterning, you'll need Matter 4 just the same.<br /> So you can go roy mustang with matter just fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T04:59:32-07:00","id":1083919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1083913#post1083913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally this would still be better covered by a damage spell mechanic, though.<br /> Considering lethal damage via &quot;this is now explosive&quot; will usually be patterning, you'll need Matter 4 just the same.<br /> So you can go roy mustang with matter just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, honestly. We avoid direct damage spells because they are very lackluster when compared to indirect &quot;damage as a consequence of consequences&quot; spells - stuff like Forces ruling, Poison/Sick/Grave Misfortune loops, Shifting-Sands-Into-Unavoidable-Damage loops, &quot;game over&quot; tilts/conditions etc. That, and we play at Arcana hard locked at 3, with 4 being rare mastery.<br /> As for Roy Mustang, I honestly didn't recognize it, because I haven't actually read or watch FMA yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:43:13-07:00","id":1084016,"title":"","content":"He snaps fingers and stuff blows up. Nothing too deep for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Why is the damage spell lackluster?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:48:09-07:00","id":1084021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084016#post1084016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He snaps fingers and stuff blows up. Nothing too deep for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Why is the damage spell lackluster?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't do enough damage. It's just plain better to drop someone into a lava pit or blind and suffocate him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:02:05-07:00","id":1084034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084016#post1084016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He snaps fingers and stuff blows up. Nothing too deep for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Why is the damage spell lackluster?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As Moinen said. 3-8 bashing damage isn't that big of a deal unless you can a) deal it multiple times in a short window (and you can't because they are banned from being Combined, b) people start doing the Wyrdhamster's Players Godkilling Stratagem of going &quot;all four of us casts damaging spell at the same target in the same turn&quot;, especially when compared to damage potential of things like Control Electricity/Heat/Fire, or the power of things like &quot;I Shield you from Oxygen, go suffocate&quot; or other ways to simply manipulate the environment/physics in a way that do the desired amount of disabling and harm. <br /> I mean, why bother casting Windstrike if I can turn all of the oxygen around (and in) you into a solid, probably disabling you outright (as a bonus, I don't even have to care about any kind of Withstand)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:43:46-07:00","id":1084103,"title":"","content":"Also, because using the freeform casting system of Mage to do interesting things by interacting with the environment rather than just direct damage like a DnD Wizard casting fireball is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:45:29-07:00","id":1084104,"title":"","content":"I need some clarification on the Gnosis Chart on page 86, and unfortunately the text that describes the fields isn't much better. The first column labeled as Max, can you only have on Arcanum at that level? and all other Arcanum is limited to the Second Max Column? or is the First Max Column the Max of your ruling Arcanum and all other are limited to the second Column? If it is the first way then there is no 5 Gnosis Double Masters correct?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 15px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Gnosis</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Max</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Max Other</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:54:19-07:00","id":1084109,"title":"","content":"It's as your first interpretation. The &quot;Max&quot; column is the maximum for your highest Arcanum. The &quot;Max Other&quot; column is the maximum for all other Arcana your character knows. So you're correct about there not being any Gnosis 5 Second-degree Masters. Well, unless they manage to drop in Gnosis somehow while still being able to retain their Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:05:06-07:00","id":1084114,"title":"","content":"Ok Thank you for the response.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:34:14-07:00","id":1084321,"title":"","content":"Let's talk a little about Legacies.<br /> Since if a Legacy Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.<br /> <br /> If I'm creating a Attainment and decide to use it as an Aimed spell, I would get some automatic success or would need to roll it?<br /> I know that even 5 sucesses can be evaded with Dodge actions, but for some social Attainments this would be really great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T00:42:44-07:00","id":1084369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084321#post1084321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's talk a little about Legacies.<br /> Since if a Legacy Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.<br /> <br /> If I'm creating a Attainment and decide to use it as an Aimed spell, I would get some automatic success or would need to roll it?<br /> I know that even 5 sucesses can be evaded with Dodge actions, but for some social Attainments this would be really great.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to roll, throwing a spell isn't a part of casting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T00:45:52-07:00","id":1084371,"title":"","content":"Social Attainments might also be somewhat problematic as aimed spells because people tend to don't like being shot with magic lasers in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T03:42:46-07:00","id":1084401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084371#post1084371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social Attainments might also be somewhat problematic as aimed spells because people tend to don't like being shot with magic lasers in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a lot of them likes a firm handshake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:08:19-07:00","id":1084416,"title":"","content":"I have a real problem with Control Weather (Forces \u2022\u2022) and trying to figure out the Scale. Strict interpretation of the scale of spells would mean that the base spell with no reaches applied would cover the area of Arm's reach around the Caster, and frankly makes no sense. Sure you can make it rain, on yourself.Yet to allow it to fill the sky with rain clouds and start a downpour, at just a basic scale, just takes it to the other extreme, yet anything less would be ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Anyone out there have a solution or something that can make sense of the spell. I have a character created Legacy that is wanting to use this, On the surface not a big deal but how much should I let this affect the weather in Phoenix Arizona (A Desert). If I let it affect the entire sky then phoenix just became the next Tropical Forest as the rain finally allows stuff to grow. Yet not letting it affect a good sized scale would turn it into a cartoon. I am at a loss here. And even on a small scale it could disrupt the delicate natural balance that is Phoenix'e weather patterns. Not to mention should be Paradoxal but as a Legacy no Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 04-27-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:22:17-07:00","id":1084420,"title":"","content":"Well the legacy part at least isn't a problem unless they're taking it as the 4th or 5th attainment, otherwise it can only increase or decrease the intensity of existing weather. Control Weather does in fact only hit the inside of the scale factor determined area though. Aimed Spell into the sky, wash, rinse, repeat until the weather over a big overlapping area is affected is how I'd get it to be more than a highly localized weather event. As an attainment that would be surprisingly easy since attainments don't bother with spell control meaning you can have as many instances running simultaneously as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:59:50-07:00","id":1084438,"title":"","content":"It is the 4th level Attainment and That is the whole problem. BTW without a reach in duration it only lasts for 5 turns as a 4th level attainment. The point is that as the attainment stands now he can drastically change the weather in an area the size of his arms in radius for 5 turns. And that is with firing a bolt into the sky every turn, and concentrating in in one area doesn't allow the area to grow the area doesn't stack that way. It would just keep affecting the as area over and over again.<br /> <br /> BTW The attainment isn't at sensory range so it is ether around himself or he continuously fires visible bolts into the the sky to try and affect the weather in the sky. As I said very cartoonish and noticeable. but strangely no paradox.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 04-27-2017, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:18:57-07:00","id":1084446,"title":"","content":"With a Duration that short there wouldn't be much chance of overlapping areas of controlled weather, no. I figure you'd want the Reach spent on Instant, Advanced Scale, Advanced Duration. It eliminates the possibility of creating &quot;impossible&quot; weather, but you can affect pretty large areas for long periods of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:27:43-07:00","id":1084449,"title":"","content":"The reaches were spent on Instant +1 and Drastic Change +2. But even with Instant, Advanced Scale, Advanced Duration it lacks the range so unless aim spell is used it is still limited to touch or self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:31:32-07:00","id":1084451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084449#post1084449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reaches were spent on Instant +1 and Drastic Change +2. But even with Instant, Advanced Scale, Advanced Duration it lacks the range so unless aim spell is used it is still limited to touch or self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aimed Spell doesn't cost Reach so you can have it do Self, Touch, and Aimed. Though I wouldn't bother rolling for Aimed with that since it's basically impossible to miss the sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:41:50-07:00","id":1084455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084449#post1084449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reaches were spent on Instant +1 and Drastic Change +2. But even with Instant, Advanced Scale, Advanced Duration it lacks the range so unless aim spell is used it is still limited to touch or self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since its the 4th Attainment, the first Great Attainment, make it so that he has to make a ritual, like a Rain Dance or something, and spend a Scene making this, now he has one extra Reach, that he uses for Advanced Scale. Now you have some options here:<br /> <br /> You can change the 2 Reach Option for the other one that cost 1 Reach and seems more natural, and them get the other Reach to Advanced Duration. This works like the ritual that he performed for 1 scene has created the climate change, and Advanced Duration here ensures that this is something like Months duration.<br /> <br /> Or, you can maintain the 2 Reach Option, and the Duration is normal. For a Spell that is Duration based, Duration 5 is 10 turns, not 5. So he spent a Scene for invoking a powerfull Blizzard that last for 1 or 2 minutes, on a Desert. Not something bad, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:45:29-07:00","id":1084503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084455#post1084455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since its the 4th Attainment, the first Great Attainment, make it so that he has to make a ritual, like a Rain Dance or something, and spend a Scene making this, now he has one extra Reach, that he uses for Advanced Scale. Now you have some options here:<br /> <br /> You can change the 2 Reach Option for the other one that cost 1 Reach and seems more natural, and them get the other Reach to Advanced Duration. This works like the ritual that he performed for 1 scene has created the climate change, and Advanced Duration here ensures that this is something like Months duration.<br /> <br /> Or, you can maintain the 2 Reach Option, and the Duration is normal. For a Spell that is Duration based, Duration 5 is 10 turns, not 5. So he spent a Scene for invoking a powerfull Blizzard that last for 1 or 2 minutes, on a Desert. Not something bad, tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that it is a duration of 5, this is a 4th level attainment, so it is a duration of 4 which is 5 turn. Now he can use one of the two free spell factors steps that he gets to bump that up to 5. but we haven't gotten there yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:59:39-07:00","id":1084509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084503#post1084503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting that it is a duration of 5, this is a 4th level attainment, so it is a duration of 4 which is 5 turn. Now he can use one of the two free spell factors steps that he gets to bump that up to 5. but we haven't gotten there yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, my bad. Well, but with the spell factors, you can bump it way up to 20 turns. (Duration 6)<br /> But what are his goals? What he wants with the power? Make it rain instantly, or he can spend a scene for activating it? Getting a great area? etc etc.<br /> With some parameters we can try to help him put the Reachs and Spell Factors where he needs most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:35:08-07:00","id":1084526,"title":"","content":"My core problem isn't making it work I can do that it is his write-up and his Homebrew Legacy so I do not want to just change it willy nilly, I want to work with him and see if we can work the way he wants. But my biggest problem is should I allow it to be. As a spell it can have consequences in the form of Paradox, Dispellation, Dissonance, and causing breaking points, Acts of Hubris (Should you disrupt the ecological balance of the desert), plus you can't just continually pop it off. As an attainment it bypasses all of that. Now not saying that it is his intention to do this but when approving a Legacy you need to look at the worse case scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:17:47-07:00","id":1084541,"title":"","content":"Well. I would allow it. To have the Attainment he needs to have Gnosis 6. He is probably a well know mage and the Concillium know him. Even if he does not suffer from Paradox, Dissonance, etc., the Awakened Society will probably call him out if he keeps abusing from the local climate. His Legacy should have a Theory and he probably does not want to damage their reputation. He will not want to be seem as a Mad One.<br /> <br /> Some others legacies have some cool powers like &quot;Fireball&quot;. Take these as an example. Even if they can do it without suffering paradox, and the usual stuff, it is probably for the best if they don't use their powers to wreak havoc all the time, cause this can damage the Veil. This can lure Hunters, Seers and all sort of problems, and also, political problems with the local Concillium. This does not qualifies as acceptable behavior just because he does not loses Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:41:14-07:00","id":1084563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084526#post1084526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My core problem isn't making it work I can do that it is his write-up and his Homebrew Legacy so I do not want to just change it willy nilly, I want to work with him and see if we can work the way he wants. But my biggest problem is should I allow it to be. As a spell it can have consequences in the form of Paradox, Dispellation, Dissonance, and causing breaking points, Acts of Hubris (Should you disrupt the ecological balance of the desert), plus you can't just continually pop it off. As an attainment it bypasses all of that. Now not saying that it is his intention to do this but when approving a Legacy you need to look at the worse case scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the classic problem with Mage, they can do anything and they can do it a lot. There are solutions in the game and outside it, in the game there's social pressure to conform, outside the game there's pretty much the same thing by talking it over with your player. No rules were broken to create the attainment though so I'd personally say it's kosher no matter how often it gets used, and if things got out of hand there'd be a brief visit from the Gaurdians or whoever so there could be some fun drama. If things got out of hand outside the game then I'd talk to my player about the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:55:21-07:00","id":1084613,"title":"","content":"Correct no rules were broken but at the same time I do not want my game to be broken. I am not a big one to telling players that they can't do something and especially if it is within the rules, which this is. I will need to figyer out what it is that i will do with the Attainment and if he really wants to keep it I will just have to figure out a control mechanism that will dissuade misuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:19:04-07:00","id":1084626,"title":"","content":"The easiest thing to do would be to just switch out the extreme weather change for Advanced Duration and Scale honestly. Although at Forces 4 you hardly need an attainment to fuck up the weather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:08:28-07:00","id":1084911,"title":"","content":"Do spells have size that needs to be accounted for when casting on them? For example - if I cast a plain spell on myself and don't factor in scale (because it's one target size 5), it's simple enough for someone to dispel that without needing to add any scale factors- but if the effect were on me and I was size 6 (and therefore needed to take a -2 penalty or reach) would the person casting dispellation need to take that into account as well? For a more extreme example, would they need to account for size for a spell affecting an entire neighborhood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:13:35-07:00","id":1084912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084613#post1084613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct no rules were broken but at the same time I do not want my game to be broken. I am not a big one to telling players that they can't do something and especially if it is within the rules, which this is. I will need to figyer out what it is that i will do with the Attainment and if he really wants to keep it I will just have to figure out a control mechanism that will dissuade misuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joking answer: Welcome to Mage!<br /> More serious answer: Mage, especially when Arcana of 4 and higher are involved, offers storytelling challenges and opportunities that might caught people off guard. They are very specific and quite different from what a lot of games (even other CofD games) entertain. As I had similar problems to you, I've tried to search for a solution that would help me the desired &quot;gamespace&quot; within the game, and discovered that collapsing the Gnosis scale and making anything past 5 mythic, and anything past 3 &quot;rare to the point of being a rarely used plot point&quot; helped immensely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T03:25:58-07:00","id":1084941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084911#post1084911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do spells have size that needs to be accounted for when casting on them? For example - if I cast a plain spell on myself and don't factor in scale (because it's one target size 5), it's simple enough for someone to dispel that without needing to add any scale factors- but if the effect were on me and I was size 6 (and therefore needed to take a -2 penalty or reach) would the person casting dispellation need to take that into account as well? For a more extreme example, would they need to account for size for a spell affecting an entire neighborhood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T03:30:04-07:00","id":1084943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084911#post1084911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do spells have size that needs to be accounted for when casting on them? For example - if I cast a plain spell on myself and don't factor in scale (because it's one target size 5), it's simple enough for someone to dispel that without needing to add any scale factors- but if the effect were on me and I was size 6 (and therefore needed to take a -2 penalty or reach) would the person casting dispellation need to take that into account as well? For a more extreme example, would they need to account for size for a spell affecting an entire neighborhood?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. I wonder what happens when you have a spell that covers multiple targets, too. Do you need to gather them all and target each one of them at once, or is it &quot;dispel on one of them, dispel on all of them&quot; sort of deal? Because if it's the first, then it's another reason for sharing your buffs with Cabalmates.<br /> EDIT<br /> And a goddamn annoying way to fuck someone over. &quot;Oh, I'm going to curse you, and a random person #34242 who will be also veiled, so you will never lift the curse of stinky feets&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-28-2017, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T04:10:50-07:00","id":1084951,"title":"","content":"I assume it would work like Withstand in that case, the spell would no longer affect the one target, but would still be active on the other. In that case it would also mean creating localized areas inside a spell's area where the spell isn't active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T04:12:04-07:00","id":1084952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084943#post1084943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting. I wonder what happens when you have a spell that covers multiple targets, too. Do you need to gather them all and target each one of them at once, or is it &quot;dispel on one of them, dispel on all of them&quot; sort of deal? Because if it's the first, then it's another reason for sharing your buffs with Cabalmates.<br /> EDIT<br /> And a goddamn annoying way to fuck someone over. &quot;Oh, I'm going to curse you, and a random person #34242 who will be also veiled, so you will never lift the curse of stinky feets&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe you can't dispel it permanently this way? The spell would just linger, dormant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T04:20:26-07:00","id":1084954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084951#post1084951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it would work like Withstand in that case, the spell would no longer affect the one target, but would still be active on the other. In that case it would also mean creating localized areas inside a spell's area where the spell isn't active.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. I think it's more like trying to target creature's hand without having enough Size to cover the whole creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T04:31:58-07:00","id":1084959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1084954#post1084954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm. I think it's more like trying to target creature's hand without having enough Size to cover the whole creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you can't make it permanent and dispel it wholesale. You can just exempt this one element.<br /> <br /> Edit: but maybe, if spells are 'nowhere' you could just crank the spell factors blindly(or check the spell with Knowings) to encompass it as a whole.<br /> It's like when you see just half of a target obstructed by wall. You can just imagine that he has size 5 and affect him this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 04-28-2017, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T05:17:27-07:00","id":1084971,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a good compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T05:36:47-07:00","id":1085426,"title":"","content":"How does lucid dreaming work? I know the Mage 2E book has rules for how to start a lucid dream, but what about creating or changing the dream state once you're in it? Rolls and mechanics are probably not needed in most situations where someone is in their own dream, but what if a Mage enters your lucid dream using Mind magic?<br /> <br /> Would Clash of Wills be the primary mechanic to help you resolve issues here? Or maybe contested Resolve + Composure rolls?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking like if you wanted to go into someone's dream to scare or torture them, for example, and try to will them into being tied up or in some kind of danger. Can you do that? How does the person fight back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:33:51-07:00","id":1085449,"title":"","content":"An invading mind could use psychic domination to force the dreamer to make the changes he desires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T09:31:08-07:00","id":1085477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1085426#post1085426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does lucid dreaming work? I know the Mage 2E book has rules for how to start a lucid dream, but what about creating or changing the dream state once you're in it? Rolls and mechanics are probably not needed in most situations where someone is in their own dream, but what if a Mage enters your lucid dream using Mind magic?<br /> <br /> Would Clash of Wills be the primary mechanic to help you resolve issues here? Or maybe contested Resolve + Composure rolls?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking like if you wanted to go into someone's dream to scare or torture them, for example, and try to will them into being tied up or in some kind of danger. Can you do that? How does the person fight back?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the spell Dream Reaching (with the Reach to be a part of the dream) the mage would interact with the dream as if it was physical (albeit by using dream form rules), and the ST should determine whether or not those actions are enough to change the themes of the current dream. You can't just will their dream into anything, but by directly interacting with the dream you can affect their dream self in ways that can change how they dream. Like killing one of the dream actors in front of their eyes will most likely turn a happy dream to a dream of fear and possibly grief. But it might also wake them if it's too jarring.<br /> <br /> The easier way would be to just use the spell Dream of the Just to directly control the dreamscape they're in. That way you can scare them, torture them, and do whatever you like without risking that they wake up.<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills only apply when two conflicting supernatural powers comes up against each other. Unless the subject has a spell or power that protects their dreams and the mage is using a spell to affect their dream there'd be no Clash of Wills roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T23:13:50-07:00","id":1085716,"title":"","content":"Can you set a Conditional Duration that has the possibility of becoming impossible to fulfill? For instance, say that you apply a curse that ends if someone completes a set task -before- a certain time. If they do not complete the task before that time, is the extended duration still applicable? Or if it's something like &quot;Until you give Jon his soul back&quot; but Jon goes and dies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T14:54:23-07:00","id":1085902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1085716#post1085716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you set a Conditional Duration that has the possibility of becoming impossible to fulfill? For instance, say that you apply a curse that ends if someone completes a set task -before- a certain time. If they do not complete the task before that time, is the extended duration still applicable? Or if it's something like &quot;Until you give Jon his soul back&quot; but Jon goes and dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the condition is possible when you cast the spell, it will work for it.<br /> Don't curse a pizza guy with: &quot;Unless you deliver the pizza in under 5 minutes.&quot;<br /> That'd be impossible, and thus would not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T18:30:35-07:00","id":1085988,"title":"","content":"The advantage to using a Conditional Duration is that it grants a free extension to your Duration, depending on the likeliness of the condition. 'The more improbable the condition, the smaller the bonus to Duration.'<br /> <br /> As you can see here. 'An improbable condition (one that is unlikely to happen given current conditions) adds a level of Duration.'<br /> <br /> Impossible conditions are just not an option, as written. But I think a storyteller would be able to allow it, just keeping in mind that it wouldn't add any level of Duration and how many ways there are to make the impossible possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T18:42:29-07:00","id":1085991,"title":"","content":"Impossible Conditional Duration is a nice, clean way to have a built in disable Off Switch for your spell. How to use it? Well, trick the spell into thinking that the condition was fulfilled using Veiling. Great for dissolving unsafely relinquished spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:20:16-07:00","id":1086004,"title":"","content":"Sort of what they did with Samael in Dave Brookshaw's Soul Cage game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:41:31-07:00","id":1086010,"title":"","content":"Well I was watching the new Beauty and the Beast, which is where I got the question on what the plausibility of casting a spell with that kind of duration would be. I wanted to know if you could set up a curse with a duration in order to set a time limit before something became 'permanent'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:44:50-07:00","id":1086012,"title":"","content":"Q: I'm playing a mage in a mixed game and I've decided to go with an alchemist/crafter who's a big nerd and likes to cosplay. My GM recommended picking up Mind so that I could create true duplicates of fantasy weapons by copying their symbols from the temenos and insert it into my crafted weapon. <br /> <br /> It sounded a bit far fetched to me, and I was wondering if something like this would ordinarily be doable? GM permission aside - I'm after a strict reading of potential just so I know wether I'm selling myself short or if my GM is inflating the potential. <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:51:47-07:00","id":1086013,"title":"","content":"I've never seen it. But I get the gist, he's cursed until someone loves him, right? Basically you would set up an Indefinite spell, with a Conditional Duration of Impossible. It wouldn't extend the duration, but it would allow the spell to turn off once the Condition was reached. Though obviously someone loving him isn't impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:20:37-07:00","id":1086028,"title":"","content":"Basically, he remains cursed unless he gets someone to fall in love with him and he love her in return, before the last pedal of an enchanted rose falls. It's not impossible - that would defeat the purpose, and there would be no story. The thing is is that eventually (when the last petal fell) fulfilling the condition would be impossible. Just not initially (and in fact it took many years for that curse to become impossible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:01:41-07:00","id":1086044,"title":"","content":"I take it it's a magic flower?<br /> <br /> I mentioned the impossibility because it came up in your first post on the subject, which suggested to me the hypothetical Condition would be something like impossible, not as much of a time limit.<br /> <br /> But basically you would just make an Indefinite Spell, one that could potentially last forever, and have a Conditional Duration on it that would allow it to end. If the Conditional Duration isn't met, it's never triggered and the spell goes on. It's entirely possible for the Conditional Duration to never be triggered or be really able to be triggered, 'This floor will vanish the second I snap this glass rod.' is an example that would fall short if the glass rod was lost, where it became improbable, or destroyed by another mage.<br /> <br /> That said. If you make a Conditional Duration, and it changes, it does seem like the Duration would change, too. Like if you had a common one, like, see a full moon in a cloudless sky. Then you went and blew up the moon so that it became impossible, or started nuclear war so the atmosphere was going to be clouded over with dust for the forseeable centuries and improbable. It seems like it would no longer be counted as a common one, and might lose the common Conditional Duration. Just because it's tied to Fate, so it does seem to work with that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-01-2017, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T04:03:41-07:00","id":1086124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086012#post1086012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: I'm playing a mage in a mixed game and I've decided to go with an alchemist/crafter who's a big nerd and likes to cosplay. My GM recommended picking up Mind so that I could create true duplicates of fantasy weapons by copying their symbols from the temenos and insert it into my crafted weapon.<br /> <br /> It sounded a bit far fetched to me, and I was wondering if something like this would ordinarily be doable? GM permission aside - I'm after a strict reading of potential just so I know wether I'm selling myself short or if my GM is inflating the potential.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did something similar with Prime instead. Platonic Ideal: Sailor Fuku is perfect for mid-scene transformations into your +99999 mana fueled outfit :P. Anyway, Prime seems to be more in line with what you want than Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T05:00:28-07:00","id":1086138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086012#post1086012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: I'm playing a mage in a mixed game and I've decided to go with an alchemist/crafter who's a big nerd and likes to cosplay. My GM recommended picking up Mind so that I could create true duplicates of fantasy weapons by copying their symbols from the temenos and insert it into my crafted weapon. <br /> <br /> It sounded a bit far fetched to me, and I was wondering if something like this would ordinarily be doable? GM permission aside - I'm after a strict reading of potential just so I know wether I'm selling myself short or if my GM is inflating the potential. <br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter is the way to go as long as the weapon you're trying to duplicate isn't essentially made of psychic energy.<br /> <br /> Your ST seems to be suggesting a Mind version of Fetish, which could be neat but won't make your replicas anymore &quot;true.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:48:29-07:00","id":1086571,"title":"","content":"So yesterday, we had an issue where a player cast Exceptional Luck on an enemy mage, getting an exceptional succes on the roll, breaking through all Withstand, and bestowing 3 tilts for the entire scene. The mage in question was maintaining a spell keeping away giant masses of water, effectively making a &quot;bowl&quot; in the ocean. The tilts chosen were Blinded, Deafened and Insensate.<br /> The Storyteller ruled that he collapsed and was unable to maintain the spell, bringing the water down with a crash.<br /> <br /> I have become unsure whether this is actually what would happen. What happens to maintained spells, when their caster loses consciousness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","user":"HelloCthulhu","date":". 05-02-2017, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:50:51-07:00","id":1086572,"title":"","content":"The only way the spell could be affected is if the mage was using concentration as a yantra. Falling unconscious doesn't do anything to spells otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:27:51-07:00","id":1086621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086572#post1086572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way the spell could be affected is if the mage was using concentration as a yantra. Falling unconscious doesn't do anything to spells otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Spells under your control just don't change what they're doing when you stop controlling them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:06:16-07:00","id":1086731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloCthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086571#post1086571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yesterday, we had an issue where a player cast Exceptional Luck on an enemy mage, getting an exceptional succes on the roll, breaking through all Withstand, and bestowing 3 tilts for the entire scene. The mage in question was maintaining a spell keeping away giant masses of water, effectively making a &quot;bowl&quot; in the ocean. The tilts chosen were Blinded, Deafened and Insensate.<br /> The Storyteller ruled that he collapsed and was unable to maintain the spell, bringing the water down with a crash.<br /> <br /> I have become unsure whether this is actually what would happen. What happens to maintained spells, when their caster loses consciousness?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said thats no how spells work, spells hang around even after death too. Maybe he just decided to go FU instead and ended the spell?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:16:24-07:00","id":1086734,"title":"","content":"Whats the best way to make a anti-magic zone now in 2e?<br /> <br /> Im thinking of a area effect &quot;supernal dispellation&quot; with a potency of 6 would do it meaning all spells would suppressed inside the area, but then the &quot;supernal dispellation&quot; spell will dispel itself as its in its own area? Maybe one needs the fate reach to avoid itself?<br /> <br /> One could technically use a aoe &quot;Dispel magic&quot; along with one dot in whatever, to make a no life magic zone or whatever?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:27:42-07:00","id":1086737,"title":"","content":"Another way to do it is to cast Wards and Signs over the area. You can breach it using excessive Potency or choosing to bypass Withstand on an Exceptional Success, but you'd have to realise or guess that the area actually have a Withstand rating before trying to circumvent it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:37:34-07:00","id":1086743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086737#post1086737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to do it is to cast Wards and Signs over the area. You can breach it using excessive Potency or choosing to bypass Withstand on an Exceptional Success, but you'd have to realise or guess that the area actually have a Withstand rating before trying to circumvent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, wouldnt a wards and signs area effect just stop people from casting spells on that area? As in its shielding the area from other spells that target only the area. &quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Only spells that directly target the subject can be<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> Withstood</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> seems to suggest that it wont protect other subjects in the area? Which seems odd since an area ward should protect everything in it.<br /> <br /> Subject = area, only spells that directly target area does or doesnt mean anything in the area? I can be in an area but not THEE area.....<br /> <br /> Also wards wont suppress spells that enter the area from outside would it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:50:18-07:00","id":1086749,"title":"","content":"Area of Effect spells affects everything within the area. I.e. people and objects within an AoE effect are basically subjects themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086743#post1086743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also wards wont suppress spells that enter the area from outside would it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:16:57-07:00","id":1086854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086743#post1086743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, wouldnt a wards and signs area effect just stop people from casting spells on that area? As in its shielding the area from other spells that target only the area. &quot; seems to suggest that it wont protect other subjects in the area? Which seems odd since an area ward should protect everything in it.<br /> <br /> Subject = area, only spells that directly target area does or doesnt mean anything in the area? I can be in an area but not THEE area.....<br /> <br /> Also wards wont suppress spells that enter the area from outside would it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> said. Plus we had a recent bit of clarification from Dave, he gave an example of casting a spell to turn everyone in the area into frogs. If they failed to Withstand, they would remain frogs until they hopped out of the area, at which point they'd resume being people. If they went back into the area they'd become frogs again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:20:15-07:00","id":1086858,"title":"","content":"Remember when deciding on scale, you choose between affecting an entire area, or affecting a certain number of people in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T18:34:34-07:00","id":1086923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086858#post1086858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember when deciding on scale, you choose between affecting an entire area, or affecting a certain number of people in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, you choose between choosing all applicable subjects in the area for as long as they remain in that area or when they enter it without discretion (For instance a Mind spell is unlikely to affect furniture) or you choose to affect a number of subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:37:21-07:00","id":1086979,"title":"","content":"Alright - this is a silly question but what exactly are Resonance Traits?<br /> <br /> In the 2E book I found this description for Resonance:<br /> <br /> <i>Resonance can typically be described by a keyword<br /> that describes an image, emotion, or theme, such as \u201cSubterranean,\u201d<br /> \u201cWrathful,\u201d or \u201cIchthyoid.\u201d When a sorcerer spends Mana from this<br /> tass on a spell where the effect or manifestation matches the stored<br /> Resonance (\u201cIchthyoid\u201d for growing gills, for instance), it suffuses her<br /> Nimbus, providing a +1 persona Yantra bonus.</i><br /> <br /> My question though is what exactly does Resonance provide to the point that it is fought over for? What exactly does the resonance of &quot;life&quot; provide? I may just be a bit dense but clarification would be great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T21:30:47-07:00","id":1087003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086749#post1086749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Area of Effect spells affects everything within the area. I.e. people and objects within an AoE effect are basically subjects themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, having a potency 6 &quot;honing the form&quot; spell enter a potency 4 &quot;wards and signs&quot; area becomes potency 2? I think the dispel magic spells are probably easier as once you hit potency 6 all 1-5 arcana spells are suppressed and you dont have to worry about thier potency?<br /> <br /> You need fate to make the spell immune to itself though right? Without fate the spell would end up suppressing itself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember when deciding on scale, you choose between affecting an entire area, or affecting a certain number of people in the area. </div> </div> </div>Yep well you either affect an entire area (you dont get to choose without fate) with everything in it OR a number of targets/size equal to the scale in range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T21:34:16-07:00","id":1087004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086979#post1086979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright - this is a silly question but what exactly are Resonance Traits?<br /> <br /> In the 2E book I found this description for Resonance:<br /> <br /> <i>Resonance can typically be described by a keyword<br /> that describes an image, emotion, or theme, such as \u201cSubterranean,\u201d<br /> \u201cWrathful,\u201d or \u201cIchthyoid.\u201d When a sorcerer spends Mana from this<br /> tass on a spell where the effect or manifestation matches the stored<br /> Resonance (\u201cIchthyoid\u201d for growing gills, for instance), it suffuses her<br /> Nimbus, providing a +1 persona Yantra bonus.</i><br /> <br /> My question though is what exactly does Resonance provide to the point that it is fought over for? What exactly does the resonance of &quot;life&quot; provide? I may just be a bit dense but clarification would be great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance goesn on to provide essence to spirits. I dont think its fought over by mages as such (spirits probably do), its just not nice staying in an area covered in &quot;wrathful&quot; resonance since that will attract wrathlike spirits who will feed on it, do wrathlike stuff to generate more essence etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T23:43:32-07:00","id":1087026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086572#post1086572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way the spell could be affected is if the mage was using concentration as a yantra. Falling unconscious doesn't do anything to spells otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086621#post1086621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Spells under your control just don't change what they're doing when you stop controlling them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1086731#post1086731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As others have said thats no how spells work, spells hang around even after death too. Maybe he just decided to go FU instead and ended the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I'll talk to my ST about it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T00:57:04-07:00","id":1087041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1087004#post1087004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resonance goesn on to provide essence to spirits. I dont think its fought over by mages as such (spirits probably do), its just not nice staying in an area covered in &quot;wrathful&quot; resonance since that will attract wrathlike spirits who will feed on it, do wrathlike stuff to generate more essence etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah I see - thanks for clarification of that totalgit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T06:04:36-07:00","id":1087124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1087004#post1087004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resonance goesn on to provide essence to spirits. I dont think its fought over by mages as such (spirits probably do), its just not nice staying in an area covered in &quot;wrathful&quot; resonance since that will attract wrathlike spirits who will feed on it, do wrathlike stuff to generate more essence etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits' concern with Resonance is generally more indirect due to the Shadow's particular scarcity issues; the bigger draw for compatible spirits is going to be that the Resonance generates more weak compatible spirits that can be eaten or exploited by the bigger kids on campus.<br /> <br /> Mages find Resonance work maneuvering for largely as a function of Obsessions and/or projects with preferred real-estate; crossing ley lines or plugging them into Hallows gives the listed Persona boost and can help determine which Gross Arcanum's benefit the space gets, and if, like most mages, you haven't got casual access to pocket dimensions and other expanded personal territories, it's easier to manage this with existing resources than to put off your grand plans until Gnosis 6+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:53:22-07:00","id":1087187,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking it might be explored upon further in Signs of Sorcery, as <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sariras-relics-of-ascension-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">the sarira section</a> from the book seems to get into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:31:52-07:00","id":1087405,"title":"","content":"On pg. 241 what does it mean that spells cast at a ley line can harvest it's Resonance? It doesn't appear to be the same thing as using resonant mana as a Persona Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:34:14-07:00","id":1087408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1087405#post1087405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On pg. 241 what does it mean that spells cast at a ley line can harvest it's Resonance? It doesn't appear to be the same thing as using resonant mana as a Persona Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Offhand I'd say that's a basic Environment Yantra boost; it's more or less the same as the Persona boost without the portability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:55:54-07:00","id":1087427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1087408#post1087408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Offhand I'd say that's a basic Environment Yantra boost; it's more or less the same as the Persona boost without the portability.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:32:16-07:00","id":1088082,"title":"","content":"Where can I find some general tips as a Storyteller for creating balanced conflict scenarios? I have an upcoming scene that pits the newly formed cabal of players (6 mages, Gnosis 1) against a Gulmoth they previously beat but didn't destroy. If I wanted other antagonists there, like more spirits or a Mage, how do I make that fair without it being anticlimactic or an accidental party wipe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:54:17-07:00","id":1088090,"title":"","content":"There really isn't much out there, in the books. Hoping it changes but it's a hard thing to write for. There's probably a lot of advice out there available in RPG blogs.<br /> <br /> Think I can offer two pieces.<br /> <br /> One, know your PCs. It's not that hard to look at their sheet, add the dots and see what they're capable and incapable of, even in mage. If PC A can dominate spirits, a regular spirit antagonist is going to go poorly, even something that can't be dominated like an idigam is likely to have a lot of spirit slaves that can be made to turn against them. If PC B has 6 Health, and your antagonist has a natural weapon with +5L, all the being needs is one success to put them into 'needs medical assistance' mode, providing they're not using armor that reduces damage. Similarly if you have a bunch of antagonists that only have +2B weapons, but PC C decided they'd use Stamina as a dump stat, once they fill him with bashing he's likely going unconscious.<br /> <br /> Two, action economy is a thing. As you noticed, 6 players versus 1 gulmoth, that's 6 chances for the mages to do something to end it versus the gulmoth's 1. Area of effect is a thing but it still comes down to how many turns each side is going to have, giving the players in that example an advantage.<br /> <br /> As a 'not advice but part of the game a lot of people forget not saying you specifically,' keep in mind that you're not limited by the books and nothing is impossible. Magic can be twisted, there's an infinite variety of numina and artifacts and powers that haven't been written down. Your gulmoth can pull tricks out its sleeves that the players would never prepare for, but the more it happens and the more outrageous it is, considering what they know about it, the more you'll test their patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T23:34:26-07:00","id":1088637,"title":"","content":"When a spell goes against multiple other spells, does it clash once - or does it clash multiple times? For instance, if I go and target a person whose warded, whose inside of another ward in their sanctum, who has a mind shield, with a spell that sympathetically reads their mind - am I clashing against every spell here, or just the highest rated one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T00:16:05-07:00","id":1088641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1088637#post1088637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a spell goes against multiple other spells, does it clash once - or does it clash multiple times? For instance, if I go and target a person whose warded, whose inside of another ward in their sanctum, who has a mind shield, with a spell that sympathetically reads their mind - am I clashing against every spell here, or just the highest rated one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gut reaction is that it has to win all Clashes, like falling from a tree and hitting every branch all the way down. Otherwise, there won't be much reason to have multiple defenses in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T01:27:52-07:00","id":1088659,"title":"","content":"Per spell stacking rules. Only the highest Potency spell can apply CoW, even if this means lower dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-06-2017, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:54:00-07:00","id":1088717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1088637#post1088637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a spell goes against multiple other spells, does it clash once - or does it clash multiple times? For instance, if I go and target a person whose warded, whose inside of another ward in their sanctum, who has a mind shield, with a spell that sympathetically reads their mind - am I clashing against every spell here, or just the highest rated one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesnt wards and signs increase withstand and mind shield gives the CoW? So there is no conflict, the spell will have to beat the withstand of the ward and signs spell, then beat a CoW vs the mind shield. The highest potency ward would be the one that takes effect thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:58:36-07:00","id":1088718,"title":"","content":"&quot;Ward&quot; doesn't just refer to the spell Wards and Signs (Withstand). It can also refer to general protective magic, and the spell Ward that does grant CoW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:03:29-07:00","id":1089409,"title":"","content":"If you have two objects, can you cast a spell with Time to determine if their two timelines ever intersected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:23:21-07:00","id":1089481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089409#post1089409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two objects, can you cast a spell with Time to determine if their two timelines ever intersected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say quickly yes. Im not sure what practice etc atm but that seems well within Times purview. You'd need to cast it on both so extra target spell factors and maybe some variation on postcognition, where the spell looks into the path of both objects and finds if they intersected. Knowing practice perhaps, you get a yes/no response but no more info, or it shows you the time/place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:02:59-07:00","id":1089497,"title":"","content":"I seriously cannot think of a way to make such a spell work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:27:03-07:00","id":1089509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089497#post1089497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously cannot think of a way to make such a spell work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not, if you can look into the past to see something then you can search into the past to find out a bit of information. What do you think is stopping it from working?<br /> <br /> Can time see/search along a things timeline? Yes.<br /> Can it tell if that thing has intersected with another thing? Is this the problem? maybe you need to add Fate to detect any sympathy the objects had?<br /> <br /> 2e trying to limit conjunctional effects aside, maybe adding fate (interconnections) to detect the sympathetic connections the objects would have had int he past had they been together (however weak) is they way to do it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:32:24-07:00","id":1089512,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that to cast the spell you're required to intersect their timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:03:45-07:00","id":1089522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089512#post1089512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that to cast the spell you're required to intersect their timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely all that is required to cast the spell is having two objects with enough temporal sympathy to view enough of both of their timelines? The whole point is to find out if they intersected if you were required to intersect thier timelines to do that then the spell would always say yes?<br /> <br /> I think its perfectly plausible that you can use time to look back through 2 or more objects timelines and adding Fate know if any had weak or greater space sympathy with each other? Cast it on x subjects, the spell finds out when/if the subjects ever had space sympathy and shows you that time? Maybe it only determines when it was and you need to then cast postcognition on one of them using that information to see the time itself?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:09:09-07:00","id":1089526,"title":"","content":"I can think of two work arounds, specify a time period during which you suspect they might have intersected, or more simply, just use Postcognition on two subjects if their timelines intersect you'll see it when the visions merge.<br /> <br /> I think the second might be more elegant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:29:39-07:00","id":1089532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089526#post1089526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of two work arounds, specify a time period during which you suspect they might have intersected, or more simply, just use Postcognition on two subjects if their timelines intersect you'll see it when the visions merge.<br /> <br /> I think the second might be more elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to suggest postcog on multiple subjects but im not really sure how that would work. I assume that you witness all events of both subjects superimposed on top of each other? Then yeh you could scan back n forth using the reach to see where they merge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:53:23-07:00","id":1089539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089409#post1089409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two objects, can you cast a spell with Time to determine if their two timelines ever intersected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it as a Time Space effect using time to looks back to see if they intersect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:22:14-07:00","id":1089549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089409#post1089409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two objects, can you cast a spell with Time to determine if their two timelines ever intersected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that this is entirely possible. Create a Knowing effect that reveals one point in time in which the objects have intersected before now - per dot of potency in the spell. Apply a reach to have the spell tell you more vivid information like 'when these times were, how long, etc.' You can then postcog those times if you want even more information to determine the other circumstances surrounding the events :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T11:25:30-07:00","id":1089869,"title":"","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> I need some help to understand better some aspects of sympathy link. The book says: In case of a mage using a sympathetic link to cast a spell in a subject the spell is Withstood by Space itself, but in some cases is easer to cast a spell using sympathetic link instend to do it in the subject directly. E.g.: a subject has stamina 4 and a weak link with the mage, if the mage try to cast a spell to turn him in a pig this spell will be Withstood by his stamina in this case 4, but if the mage use a sympathetic link the spell will be Withstood by the sympathetic link in this case weak so 3.<br /> <br /> Is it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T11:34:43-07:00","id":1089870,"title":"","content":"When you're faced with multiple Withstand ratings (which can happen in a few ways, including casting sympathetically or casting on someone who's subject to the spell Wards and Signs) you simply choose the highest rating and then add one to that per additional rating.<br /> In your example Withstand would be 5 since 4 is the highest and you add 1 because you have the sympathetic Withstand.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's all described in the section &quot;Withstanding&quot; on pages 114-115. Casting sympathetically is not meant to be easier. In fact, it's always more difficult unless you're planning on bypassing Withstand entirely by scoring an Exceptional Success on the casting roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-08-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:14:12-07:00","id":1089878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089870#post1089870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you're faced with multiple Withstand ratings (which can happen in a few ways, including casting sympathetically or casting on someone who's subject to the spell Wards and Signs) you simply choose the highest rating and then add one to that per additional rating.<br /> In your example Withstand would be 5 since 4 is the highest and you add 1 because you have the sympathetic Withstand.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's all described in the section &quot;Withstanding&quot; on pages 114-115. Casting sympathetically is not meant to be easier. In fact, it's always more difficult unless you're planning on bypassing Withstand entirely by scoring an Exceptional Success on the casting roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't see that or just couldn't remember.<br /> <br /> In any way thanks you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:19:30-07:00","id":1089881,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Spirit Summons and related spells - apologies if this has come up before, I've given the forum search engine a chance but we all know what that's like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spirit Summons</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage sends out a call to the nearest spirit within her sensory range. Conversely she can summon spirits she knows personally. She may send a general call and the nearest spirit will answer, or she can specify the type of spirit by Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the ability to summon spirits the mage knows personally:<br /> <br /> 1.) An exception or alternative to the sensory range restriction, allowing a known spirit to be called across any distance?<br /> 2.) A third category of potential targeting (&quot;nearest spirit, specific type, or specific spirit&quot;) within range?<br /> 3.) Something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:31:29-07:00","id":1089892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089881#post1089881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Spirit Summons and related spells - apologies if this has come up before, I've given the forum search engine a chance but we all know what that's like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is the ability to summon spirits the mage knows personally:<br /> <br /> 1.) An exception or alternative to the sensory range restriction, allowing a known spirit to be called across any distance?<br /> 2.) A third category of potential targeting (&quot;nearest spirit, specific type, or specific spirit&quot;) within range?<br /> 3.) Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally without other aids it is impossible to cast spell outside of your sensory range. So you can't summon a spirit that is behind the wall by targeting him directly. You can however cast an aoe that would encompass the entire house and restrict the spell to 'this spirit I know' or 'madness spirits'*. So either target spirit directly or by an aoe, the spell without sympathetic casting can't affect targets that don't meet one of those criteria.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *'<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089954-2e-hack-shutters\">Shutters</a>' again. Yea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:32:23-07:00","id":1089895,"title":"","content":"The 2nd edition merit Adamant Hand functions how?<br /> Is it like, you add your skill dots on Brawl as a Yantra for spells regardless of it being a Rote Spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:44:07-07:00","id":1089899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1089895#post1089895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2nd edition merit Adamant Hand functions how?<br /> Is it like, you add your skill dots on Brawl as a Yantra for spells regardless of it being a Rote Spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Brawl is your Adamant Hand skill then when you make a Brawl attack it can also count as a +1 Yantra on a spell you cast the next turn, and you can do this a number of times equal to your Yantra slots. So if you have Gnosis 3, you could hit a bad guy 3 times with Brawl (The number of Yantra slots you have) and receive +3 Yantra dice to a spell you cast on the fourth turn. Essentially, attacking things boosts your spell's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:39:24-07:00","id":1089969,"title":"","content":"What level of Act of Hubris is blood sacrifice of an animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T16:04:49-07:00","id":1090016,"title":"","content":"I'd say Enlightened, if at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T23:03:13-07:00","id":1090125,"title":"","content":"If you traveled to a point in your life before Awakening you'd be without your magic for the duration of the spell correct? Would it be possible to cast a spell that sends you to a period in your life before Awakening that also summons your present version back into the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T23:56:34-07:00","id":1090135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090125#post1090125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you traveled to a point in your life before Awakening you'd be without your magic for the duration of the spell correct? Would it be possible to cast a spell that sends you to a period in your life before Awakening that also summons your present version back into the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Corridor of Time&quot; already says it sends your present version back into the past to occupy your previous body. So you'd end up in the past in a body with no gnosis, arcana or mana. (But still in control of the &quot;Corridor of Time spell.) So yes your a sleeper for the duration of your time travel...<br /> <br /> Shifting sands in a demense with infinate reachs, might work but thats cheesy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Depends if your ST allows it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-09-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:35:45-07:00","id":1090155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090135#post1090135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Corridor of Time&quot; already says it sends your present version back into the past to occupy your previous body. So you'd end up in the past in a body with no gnosis, arcana or mana. (But still in control of the &quot;Corridor of Time spell.) So yes your a sleeper for the duration of your time travel...<br /> <br /> Shifting sands in a demense with infinate reachs, might work but thats cheesy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Depends if your ST allows it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But how can anybody hold Spell Control over the time traveling spell when they're not a mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:46:16-07:00","id":1090160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090155#post1090155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But how can anybody hold Spell Control over the time traveling spell when they're not a mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepwalkers are able to hold spells for mages. Maybe they count as sleepwalkers ??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:58:16-07:00","id":1090164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090160#post1090160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sleepwalkers are able to hold spells for mages. Maybe they count as sleepwalkers ??</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps? My original thought was that they'd still be Awakened in the future, but their life remains as if they were still Sleepers. No new relationships formed, no old relationships lost. Just the same old life, as if the metaphorical storm in one's life that is the Awakening never happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T01:03:56-07:00","id":1090168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090164#post1090164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps? My original thought was that they'd still be Awakened in the future, but their life remains as if they were still Sleepers. No new relationships formed, no old relationships lost. Just the same old life, as if the metaphorical storm in one's life that is the Awakening never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeh the spell is still being controlled by your future self/body. I wouldnt think to hard about it tbh.<br /> <br /> Personally i think barring demense infinate reach shifting sands malarky, that travelling into the past as an awakened before you awakened is into imperial archmastery territory. But then part of me wants to know what my players would do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T03:31:17-07:00","id":1090207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090135#post1090135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Corridor of Time&quot; already says it sends your present version back into the past to occupy your previous body. So you'd end up in the past in a body with no gnosis, arcana or mana. (But still in control of the &quot;Corridor of Time spell.) So yes your a sleeper for the duration of your time travel...<br /> <br /> Shifting sands in a demense with infinate reachs, might work but thats cheesy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Depends if your ST allows it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sends your -present- self into your past body, and arcana and Gnosis aren't tied to your body. You take your magic with you or the spell makes no sense. You're essentially taking your grown up hand and sticking it in the sock puppet you used to play with when you were five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-09-2017, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:20:20-07:00","id":1090223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090207#post1090207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sends your -present- self into your past body, and arcana and Gnosis aren't tied to your body. You take your magic with you or the spell makes no sense. You're essentially taking your grown up hand and sticking it in the sock puppet you used to play with when you were five.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends, Gnosis is connected to the soul, since you loose access to magic eventually without one if your not sending your awakened soul back that past body wont get given a gnosis or arcana.<br /> Its something for a FAQ really as its not and might never be addressed, i have no real investment either way and the idea of being five with magic sounds cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T08:18:24-07:00","id":1090320,"title":"","content":"What's the difference between the Guardians' Labyrinth and the Ladder's Cryptopolies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T08:39:35-07:00","id":1090324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090320#post1090320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between the Guardians' Labyrinth and the Ladder's Cryptopolies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Purpose. The Labyrinth is to lead people away from Awakening, the Cryptopoly serves the exact opposite purpose. The two Orders poach cults from each other on the sly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T20:48:54-07:00","id":1090581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090320#post1090320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between the Guardians' Labyrinth and the Ladder's Cryptopolies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Guardians want to create a trap for unworthy souls, keeping them from enlightenment by pointing them in completely the wrong direction.<br /> Thearchs want to create a system through which individuals might prove themselves, learn the Elemental Precepts, and hopefully Awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T21:11:50-07:00","id":1090585,"title":"","content":"is the astral threshhold, where you have to spend mana to start walking the astral path still a thing in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T21:15:58-07:00","id":1090586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090585#post1090585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the astral threshhold, where you have to spend mana to start walking the astral path still a thing in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you enter the Astral from a Hallow, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T02:38:09-07:00","id":1090652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090585#post1090585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the astral threshhold, where you have to spend mana to start walking the astral path still a thing in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it's now variable depending on the strength of the Hallow, the cost is 5 mana minus Hallow rating. So at a 5 dot Hallow it's actually free.<br /> <br /> At an Astral verge it's also free, typically you just have to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> I forget how it is with a demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T03:30:29-07:00","id":1090668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090652#post1090652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and it's now variable depending on the strength of the Hallow, the cost is 5 mana minus Hallow rating. So at a 5 dot Hallow it's actually free.<br /> <br /> At an Astral verge it's also free, typically you just have to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> I forget how it is with a demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iit's 6 minus Hallow rating, actually. So Hallows always cost minimum 1 Mana, while Synesi (Astral Irises - is this what you meant by Astral Verge?) and Demesnes are free. But Demesnes have to be created from either 1) your soul stone, 2) a soul stone from the same Path, or 3) any soul stone whose owner permits you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:31:31-07:00","id":1090734,"title":"","content":"If I make a character and spend 5 or all 10 of my starting Merit points on Gnosis. My character starts with Gnosis 2 or 3.<br /> Would it be possible to then start with both Ruling Arcana at Disciple level (3) and no dots of another Arcana?<br /> <br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 characters to have at maximum 1 Arcana at Disciple level (3) and the rest at Apprentice (2).<br /> Gnosis 2 characters may have as many Arcana at Disciple level (3) as they can afford.<br /> <br /> <i>Mage the Awakening Second Edition, page 86.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Your character starts with six total dots in Arcana.<br /> <b>She may only have one Arcanum at three dots at this time</b>.<br /> <b>Three to five of her starting dots must be in her Ruling Arcana</b>, and both Ruling Arcana<br /> must have at least one dot. None of her starting dots can go to<br /> her Inferior Arcana.<br /> The possible combinations are as follows:<br /> Specialist: 3, 2, 1 or 3, 1, 1, 1<br /> Balanced: 2, 2, 2 or 2, 2, 1, 1<br /> Generalist: 2, 1, 1, 1, 1<br /> <br /> <i>Mage the Awakening Second Edition, page 80.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Apologies if this has been asked before. Both the forum search function and google did not lead me to the answer. It did lead me to lots of interesting discussions on the value of those starting Merit points. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:33:54-07:00","id":1090737,"title":"","content":"I would assume no, Mages are considered or supposed to have a third arcana. Frequently this also turns out to be their third ruling arcana when they join a legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:44:01-07:00","id":1090742,"title":"","content":"&quot;She may only have one arcanum at 3 dots at this time&quot; means exactly that, at character creation time only 1 arcanum at 3 no matter what your gnosis max allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T09:52:41-07:00","id":1090757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1090734#post1090734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I make a character and spend 5 or all 10 of my starting Merit points on Gnosis. My character starts with Gnosis 2 or 3.<br /> Would it be possible to then start with both Ruling Arcana at Disciple level (3) and no dots of another Arcana?<br /> <br /> <br /> Gnosis 1 characters to have at maximum 1 Arcana at Disciple level (3) and the rest at Apprentice (2).<br /> Gnosis 2 characters may have as many Arcana at Disciple level (3) as they can afford.<br /> <br /> <i>Mage the Awakening Second Edition, page 86.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Your character starts with six total dots in Arcana.<br /> <b>She may only have one Arcanum at three dots at this time</b>.<br /> <b>Three to five of her starting dots must be in her Ruling Arcana</b>, and both Ruling Arcana<br /> must have at least one dot. None of her starting dots can go to<br /> her Inferior Arcana.<br /> The possible combinations are as follows:<br /> Specialist: 3, 2, 1 or 3, 1, 1, 1<br /> Balanced: 2, 2, 2 or 2, 2, 1, 1<br /> Generalist: 2, 1, 1, 1, 1<br /> <br /> <i>Mage the Awakening Second Edition, page 80.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Apologies if this has been asked before. Both the forum search function and google did not lead me to the answer. It did lead me to lots of interesting discussions on the value of those starting Merit points. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. You can't - your initial six dots are spent according to the above. If you chose 3,2,1, and then your Storyteller gave you XP before the chronicle started, you could concievably get 3,3,1, but the intention is that all mages have at <i>least</i> three Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T03:20:13-07:00","id":1091043,"title":"","content":"Do you allow for affecting off non native but 'right now' attuned ephemera? Lets say Death to shape someone who entered Twilight by Ghost Gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T03:28:54-07:00","id":1091045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091043#post1091043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you allow for affecting off non native but 'right now' attuned ephemera? Lets say Death to shape someone who entered Twilight by Ghost Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>We allow that at our table. I don't know if there's enough information in the books to really say what the 'right' answer is for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T03:54:04-07:00","id":1091047,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes, but you may have to contend with Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:04:00-07:00","id":1091050,"title":"","content":"Yes, if you've turned yourself into ephemera, you are affected by spells that affect ephemera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:06:54-07:00","id":1091051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091050#post1091050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if you've turned yourself into ephemera, you are affected by spells that affect ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! It means that Death and Spirit can heal lastingly - you just need to transpose your target into Twilight state. Mind could do it too if it is possible to mimic principle with something like Mind Gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:17:28-07:00","id":1091055,"title":"","content":"Since Mind can't grant Goetia Manifestations and since both known effects to enter Mind Twilight (i.e. the spell Psychic Projection and Auspex 5) only sends out a projection of yourself I'd say it probably requires Death or Spirit as conjunctional Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:25:20-07:00","id":1091056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091050#post1091050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if you've turned yourself into ephemera, you are affected by spells that affect ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Mind Gate possible with Mind 3 alone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:37:09-07:00","id":1091059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091056#post1091056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Mind Gate possible with Mind 3 alone?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't, assuming you're talking about using it like the Gate from Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:57:04-07:00","id":1091067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091059#post1091059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it isn't, assuming you're talking about using it like the Gate from Death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, I'm talking about exactly that. I just can't grasp why it can't, or rather why Spirit and Death can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:04:30-07:00","id":1091069,"title":"","content":"Question: Why does Incognito presence require Mana expenditure when equivalents like Invisibility or Supernal Veil do not? Is it a pure balance thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:10:44-07:00","id":1091071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091067#post1091067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'm talking about exactly that. I just can't grasp why it can't, or rather why Spirit and Death can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps me to view 'Gates' as a kind of reverse manifestation, and Mind can't do those either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:11:28-07:00","id":1091072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091067#post1091067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'm talking about exactly that. I just can't grasp why it can't, or rather why Spirit and Death can.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reason that goetia can't Manifest naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:32:42-07:00","id":1091078,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> It's an attempt at 'preserving' balance, added in the errata. Mind Veiling is <i>really </i>strong but I don't think that this cost is needed and if you think that it's unjust have it your way.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> That will have to do for me. So you would need to add Spirit or Death 2 for Mind Gate effect. Still it's nice to know that Death and Spirit can heal people or mend objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:34:32-07:00","id":1091079,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=940424#post940424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. it autosucceds at hiding the person, which is why it costs Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:45:37-07:00","id":1091101,"title":"","content":"Would Patterning be good for making a Time spell that places a target <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/JustOneSecondOutOfSync\" target=\"_blank\">Just One Second Out Of Sync</a>?<br /> I'm going off of Temporal Stutter because it seems fairly close to what I'm imagining. Kinda.<br /> I was considering modeling it like a Twilight state attuned to Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:53:02-07:00","id":1091103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091101#post1091101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Patterning be good for making a Time spell that places a target <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/JustOneSecondOutOfSync&amp;quot;]Just</a> One Second Out Of Sync[/URL]?<br /> I'm going off of Temporal Stutter because it seems fairly close to what I'm imagining. Kinda.<br /> I was considering modeling it like a Twilight state attuned to Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put it down as a Reach on either Hung Spell (Very iffy) or a Reach on Temporal Stutter which usually doesn't let you snap an object back from whatever future you've sent it to. Probably +2 Reach either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:42:26-07:00","id":1091122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091051#post1091051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice! It means that Death and Spirit can heal lastingly - you just need to transpose your target into Twilight state. Mind could do it too if it is possible to mimic principle with something like Mind Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something worth exploring: if a mage can heal her body by exploiting a loophole in reality, what is the catch? What can be the unintended consequences?<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, it's completely kosher, but in-setting? Stuffing ectoplasm or ephemera into your wounds and shaping the wound away, then changing back to flesh and blood... What could go wrong, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:55:44-07:00","id":1091124,"title":"","content":"The spells for healing ghosts and spirits are healing a specific kind of ephemeral creature and a being transposed into Twilight doesn't necessarily meet the criteria. I wouldn't allow Death or Spirit to heal you just because you're in Twilight. Besides, you could just recruit a spirit, ghost or goetia that has healing powers, and that would also be Lasting healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:56:44-07:00","id":1091126,"title":"","content":"Temporal Stutter actually hangs around in the area where you initially cast it on someone. If you crank the duration up to indefinite, the target will be &quot;outside&quot; of time until someone dispels it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/884711-how-do-you-imprison-a-mage?p=885772#post885772\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/884711-how-do-you-imprison-a-mage?p=885772#post885772\"> How do you imprison a Mage? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/884711-how-do-you-imprison-a-mage?p=885772#post885772\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/884711-how-do-you-imprison-a-mage?p=885772#post885772 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Ok, a mage is taken into custody for charges by the Consilium. The Consiulium has to make sure the mage doesn't escape or use dangerous magic. How do you do that? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rereading how it is worded in the book makes me think that there is probably another post out there that explains that you aren't so much sending them into the future as removing them from the flow of time for the duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:01:10-07:00","id":1091130,"title":"","content":"If it stays in the area then it can be detected with MS. Can you imagine opening that time capsule? Literally anything could be in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:09:25-07:00","id":1091132,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar216_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"216\" data-vbnamecard=\"216\">Zooroos</a> I could see a few condition based on this fact. I could be fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091124#post1091124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spells for healing ghosts and spirits are healing a specific kind of ephemeral creature and a being transposed into Twilight doesn't necessarily meet the criteria. I wouldn't allow Death or Spirit to heal you just because you're in Twilight. Besides, you could just recruit a spirit, ghost or goetia that has healing powers, and that would also be Lasting healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how would it even be possible to affect attuned ephemera, like Dave said is possible, if you could only affect ghosts or spirits?<br /> It has many applications. Enter your Twilight and be your own master. Bolster your attributes, sharpen your senses, heal and transform. Take a form of a giant spirit fox and chase your enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:14:37-07:00","id":1091137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091130#post1091130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it stays in the area then it can be detected with MS. Can you imagine opening that time capsule? Literally anything could be in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what initially got me thinking about it, as a potential mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:17:30-07:00","id":1091139,"title":"","content":"As stated in the Shape Ephemera spell (which, btw, also states that it's possible to shape beings and objects that became ephemeral through use of Ghost Gate) shaping the ephemera doesn't damage the Corpus. I'm assuming it also can't be used to heal Corpus. Instead you need to use a spell like Shape Spirit, which unfortunately isn't Lasting by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:22:24-07:00","id":1091142,"title":"","content":"Bolster Spirit is Lasting just like Knit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:34:27-07:00","id":1091146,"title":"","content":"So it's possible to use Death and Spirit to heal bashing, if your ST allows you to cast versions of spells that are otherwise only supposed to work on ghosts and spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:37:14-07:00","id":1091147,"title":"","content":"But... Dave just... eh. Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:39:10-07:00","id":1091149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091142#post1091142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolster Spirit is Lasting just like Knit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I was making my point, Mages are not spirits even when they're ephemeral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:45:08-07:00","id":1091150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091147#post1091147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... Dave just... eh. Nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Mrmdubois pointed out there's still a difference between being ephemeral and being an ephemeral entity. I'm not saying it shouldn't be possible to use a version of Bolster Spirit to heal biological entities that are ephemeral, but I still wanted to point out that it's another source of potential judgement differences.<br /> My intention might've been unclear. I blame my fever for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:54:06-07:00","id":1091152,"title":"","content":"I mentioned Bolster Spirit to point out that all healing is Lasting(if not intentionally made non Lasting, I guess). I'm not arguing that you could use it to heal non-native ephemerals but there should be a version of it or Reach that heals them and <i>this </i>can be a table preference. One thing is sure though, either you can affect something or you can't - it should extend to all practices. So if you can reshape something you can also damage or heal it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:51:48-07:00","id":1091180,"title":"","content":"Question: In the Rote &quot;Shapechanging&quot;, the spell's primary factor is Duration. Does that means that the transformation lasts only for the number of turns specified in pg. 113, if no Reach is spent in upgrading the duration to Advanced? I had always assumed that once the spell had effect, the new body was a Lasting effect.<br /> <br /> The reason i ask is because i'm trying to include the Rote as a Legacy Attainment, and i'm having this problem in which i have to choose between the transformation being instant <b><i>or</i></b> having to be recasted once every <i>[insert low number here]</i> turns, which seems kind of cluncky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:56:31-07:00","id":1091184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091180#post1091180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: In the Rote &amp;quot;Shapechanging&amp;quot;, the spell's primary factor is Duration. Does that means that the transformation lasts only for the number of turns specified in pg. 113, if no Reach is spent in upgrading the duration to Advanced? I had always assumed that once the spell had effect, the new body was a Lasting effect.<br /> <br /> The reason i ask is because i'm trying to include the Rote as a Legacy Attainment, and i'm having this problem in which i have to choose between the transformation being instant <b><i>or</i></b> having to be recasted once every <i>[insert low number here]</i> turns, which seems kind of cluncky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very few effects of magic are Lasting, and Shapechanging definitely isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> What you should do for the attainment if you want it Instant and Advanced Duration is make it the 5th attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 