=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T01:47:30-07:00","id":1091458,"title":"","content":"Generally, what can each dot rating of Arcanum can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T01:59:43-07:00","id":1091462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091458#post1091458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, what can each dot rating of Arcanum can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is summarized via Practices, which start on M2E p 123<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:48:07-07:00","id":1091588,"title":"","content":"Can Prime be used in any Scrutinizing roll to scrutinize a Mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:05:25-07:00","id":1091596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091588#post1091588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Prime be used in any Scrutinizing roll to scrutinize a Mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume no, unless it falls under Prime's purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:20:16-07:00","id":1091629,"title":"","content":"But you can cast spell with it that gives you dice tricks. Rote action on scrutiny is neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:54:28-07:00","id":1091643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091629#post1091629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can cast spell with it that gives you dice tricks. Rote action on scrutiny is neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd allow Fate, Time or Prime to buff Scrutiny rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-12-2017, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T13:15:58-07:00","id":1091682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091643#post1091643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'd allow Fate, Time or Prime to buff Scrutiny rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime would be probably cheaper in Reach since Fate and Time(?) needs it to affect spellcasting. While its not really casting I'd say that it still applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T13:24:54-07:00","id":1091683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091682#post1091682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime would be probably cheaper in Reach since Fate and Time(?) needs it to affect spellcasting. While its not really casting I'd say that it still applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime would be the more efficient arcana, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T14:14:01-07:00","id":1091698,"title":"","content":"One of my players cast psychic domination to tell two thugs to go to McDonald's for an hour. I have two questions. Is this a violation of wisdom and at what level? And the spell says that people hear it like a voice in their head. Do you think this voice in their head would provoke dissonance or count as a sleeper perceiving Magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:36:25-07:00","id":1091728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091596#post1091596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume no, unless it falls under Prime's purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic in general is under the purview of Prime so a magical Mystery is in its purview.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:47:05-07:00","id":1091733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091698#post1091698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players cast psychic domination to tell two thugs to go to McDonald's for an hour. I have two questions. Is this a violation of wisdom and at what level? And the spell says that people hear it like a voice in their head. Do you think this voice in their head would provoke dissonance or count as a sleeper perceiving Magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is one or both of them committed vegetarians? If not then I'd say it's probably not an AoH. The voice in their head should trigger Dissonance, but if the Duration was only an hour they won't have time to unravel it, just forget why they went out for fast food, musta been hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:48:00-07:00","id":1091734,"title":"","content":"Ah that perfect point when a question in the 'simple questions for simple answers' thread becomes so complicated it cycles back on itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:48:05-07:00","id":1091735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091728#post1091728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic in general is under the purview of Prime so a magical Mystery is in its purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what's meant by magic, Supernal stuff sure, just generally supernatural doesn't count though imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T19:14:27-07:00","id":1091799,"title":"","content":"Well all Scrutinize need a roll of Gnosis and an Arcanum that places it into the realm of Magic, All though that being said I suppose that other supernatural stuff isn't magic and it would need a scrutinize roll. Well that is why I asked the question. It looks like a play it by ear type of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T20:41:06-07:00","id":1091817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091799#post1091799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like a play it by ear type of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good chunk of Mage is. Gotta keep them players on their toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T22:05:29-07:00","id":1091827,"title":"","content":"Are there any (non-Magic) ways to regain Willpower other than Virtues, Vices, resting, and submitting in combat?<br /> This includes all entities who use Willpower. I remember that Spirits get Willpower back for ever 3 points of Essence they eat (I think).<br /> <br /> Also do animals have Willpower? I don't remember.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think up a &quot;what is Willpower&quot; Mystery, and I'm trying to think of all of the possible sources of it.<br /> I very much like the thought of stealing/generating/storing Willpower.<br /> <br /> I'm totally not going to have some Mind/Prime mage create a bunch of wearable enhanced items which turn their wearers into psychics (using the various merits), containing Willpower reserves, which even Sleepwalker wearers can refill. Totally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 05-13-2017, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T03:54:33-07:00","id":1091885,"title":"","content":"You also regain Willpower when achieving an Exceptional when attacking someone else. Other than that I can think of all the different types of Anchors:<br /> <br /> Vice/Virtue: humans, mages, ghosts, GM-angels, GM-demons, Supernal beings, qashmallim<br /> Mask/Dirge: vampires<br /> Blood/Bone: werewolves<br /> Elpis/Torment: prometheans<br /> Legend/Life: beasts and heroes<br /> Strix only have a Vice.<br /> <br /> Goetia and spirits regain one point of willpower for every third Essence consumed. Strix can spend 3 Vitae to regain a point of Willpower.<br /> In addition all ephemeral entities and Supernal beings regain one point of Willpower each day, similar to having a good night's rest sans having to actually rest. Strix gain one point of Willpower after seeing that the sun has set for the day.<br /> <br /> Horrors from CofD gain Willpower when fulfilling Aspirations, but that's a thing for Storyteller characters as they don't gain beats.<br /> <br /> There's the Drain Numen that all ephemeral entities (and Horrors through the Numen Dread Power) can have.<br /> <br /> Other than that it you can gain Willpower when achieving an Exceptional on certain supernatural power activation rolls (I think BtP had a few of those) and Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-13-2017, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T04:26:02-07:00","id":1091890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091885#post1091885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also regain Willpower when achieving an Exceptional when attacking someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it only with Down&amp;Dirty combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T04:59:35-07:00","id":1091893,"title":"","content":"You're right. My group applies that to regular attacks as well (it fits our playing style and allows for regaining Willpower from more important fights as well), but by RAW it's only Down and Dirty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T06:27:03-07:00","id":1091928,"title":"","content":"But it's a great idea. I think I'll use it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T08:09:20-07:00","id":1091949,"title":"","content":"There is a wolfblooded tell that restores willpower upon engaging in vigorous physical contact. Mind mage sight can see when people spend willpower, so it is definitely an in-universe thing and not an abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T08:13:23-07:00","id":1091953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091733#post1091733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is one or both of them committed vegetarians? If not then I'd say it's probably not an AoH. The voice in their head should trigger Dissonance, but if the Duration was only an hour they won't have time to unravel it, just forget why they went out for fast food, musta been hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but isn't telling them to leave their post an act against their will as it's not really in their interest? Also, isn't triggering Dissonance also cause for a breaking point and thus another AoH?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T08:25:34-07:00","id":1091957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1091949#post1091949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a wolfblooded tell that restores willpower upon engaging in vigorous physical contact. Mind mage sight can see when people spend willpower, so it is definitely an in-universe thing and not an abstraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being an in-universe thing and being an abstraction aren't mutually exclusive. Health is certainly a thing, but health boxes are an abstraction to track health. While we at my table would just say that Irminsul (my Mastigos) sees someone spend Willpower, what Irminsul probably sees is that the other character is mentally exerting themselves more than usual. It's just that mental exortion and health aren't easily quantifiable so we use points and boxes to represent that instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:13:48-07:00","id":1092095,"title":"","content":"Can one change the emotional context of a sympathetic link via Space 3 (the Weaving practice) the same way as one can learn it via Space 1 in Correspondence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:30:13-07:00","id":1092098,"title":"","content":"Probably, but it quickly revert if made Lasting. I don't think redefining a person's home to their office will have any real consequences. The sympathetic bond is a measure of closeness, not a definition of their relationship, so when the spell is cancelled it'd quickly be redefined back to home because that's what it is to the person in the example. If it works like that then Veiling might be the most suited Practice instead of Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T10:13:50-07:00","id":1092361,"title":"","content":"Is their any reason why an Apprentice of Prime cant create a Shielding effect that forces any hostile magic aimed at her to provoke a Clash of Wills (An effect akin to a Space Ward) as a more 'all or nothing' alternative to Wards and Signs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T10:17:28-07:00","id":1092363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092361#post1092361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is their any reason why an Apprentice of Prime cant create a Shielding effect that forces any hostile magic aimed at her to provoke a Clash of Wills (An effect akin to a Space Ward) as a more 'all or nothing' alternative to Wards and Signs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Although Withstand is going to generally be more useful, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T10:25:34-07:00","id":1092366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092361#post1092361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is their any reason why an Apprentice of Prime cant create a Shielding effect that forces any hostile magic aimed at her to provoke a Clash of Wills (An effect akin to a Space Ward) as a more 'all or nothing' alternative to Wards and Signs?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your brave enough make it a Reach effect of Wards and Signs. If not, separate spell is fine. What is even better is to hide yourself <i>from </i>magic with Veiling - make it require one more Reach to target you or even exist for them as viable target only after they Unveil you with a AMS or a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T10:49:29-07:00","id":1092371,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick responses guys, having it be an alternative option should be good for my table. <br /> <br /> While I have your attention, can you guys clarify something for me. 2 questions about Supernal Veil.<br /> 1. My read of this was that if you cast this spell on yourself or another mage, you can be hidden from mundane sense as well as supernatural ones? Along the same principle that a Matter Mage can use the Veiling Practice to make a building unnoticeable. Some players were confused because the description doesn't spell it out. (Also how do you stunt this effect narratively? Are you just unnoticable? Will people walk into me on a busy sidewalk? Or step to one side and not be able to explain why they did if asked about it later?)<br /> <br /> 2. My understanding is that Supernal Veil can be used hide active spells from the scrutiny of other mages Mage Sight, EG I can walk into a meeting covered in Wards and Signs without drawing the attention of other Awakened. Could I use the spell or a variant to conceal the act of spellcasting itself? EG Halfway through the meeting things are getting a little tense and I want to throw up Wards and Signs without pinging everyone's peripheral mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:30:20-07:00","id":1092396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092371#post1092371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. My read of this was that if you cast this spell on yourself or another mage, you can be hidden from mundane sense as well as supernatural ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. This will work for any supernatural creature, not just mages. This makes them undetectable to <i>anything</i>, not just other beings. Cameras etc would also be fooled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will people walk into me on a busy sidewalk? </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you want to run it. With a strict reading of the rules? Yes. However, they wouldn't register that they walked into you (as that would be detecting you). It doesn't break anything if you want to have them sidestep you instead<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My understanding is that Supernal Veil can be used hide active spells from the scrutiny of other mages Mage Sight, EG I can walk into a meeting covered in Wards and Signs without drawing the attention of other Awakened. </div> </div> </div>Correct, but bear in mind that mages have spells all over themselves all the time. On the contrary, it'd be really weird if you walked into a meeting and <i>didn't</i> ping anyone's PMS. They'd probably assume you were up to something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could I use the spell or a variant to conceal the act of spellcasting itself? EG Halfway through the meeting things are getting a little tense and I want to throw up Wards and Signs without pinging everyone's peripheral mage sight? </div> </div> </div>That would require casting it reflexively, which isn't doable as written, no. I wouldn't personally allow a variant option that allowed it either, but if you wanted to, casting reflexively is 'worth' +2 Reach and a point of Mana, if you follow the precedent set by Fate &amp; Death. <s>Of course, even if you did that, the casting of Supernal Veil would <i>also</i> ping PMS. So it's really not doable period.</s>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-14-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:50:40-07:00","id":1092407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092396#post1092396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, even if you did that, the casting of Supernal Veil would <i>also</i> ping PMS. So it's really not doable period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Veilings luckily don't ping so you can cast it in secret. What would cause a problem is the nimbus flare that will be visible to anyone with AMS. If nobody 'looks' at the moment, you're good. <br /> I also run with that, when you know what to look for - and mages know, you can see when someone is casting. Fixed eyes, blank stare, stiffening or relaxing of facial muscles, skilled mages can notice this split second changes. Subterfuge can be involved. This bit is not official though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:54:16-07:00","id":1092408,"title":"","content":"Thanks again! I am looking at starting a game for a bunch of folk new to Mage in a few weeks and I am trying to sort all this stuff out in my head. <br /> <br /> Mind if I throw in a few other questions? <br /> <br /> On the topic of Veiling Spells: How do they work in combat? I get that an opposing Mage can call up his AMS for an instant Clash of Wills, but whats his options after that if he fails? Can I force more Clashes by casting Unveiling Spells searching for the hidden mage? IE A Mastigos who is 'Incognito' takes a pistol shot at a Moros, who calls up his AMS but fails to pierce the illusion. Can the Moros cast a spell like Detect Substance (Gunpowder) to pinpoint the gun and its wielder? Does this call for a second Clash? <br /> <br /> Spells that create servants (Matter 4's Golem and Deaths Quicken Corpse for example) effectively grant dots in the retainer merit= to potency, which informs the created creatures dice pools. For example the Golem I create to protect my Sanctum has a combat dice pool = to Potencyx2. The stock retainer merit caps out at 5 dots, is it fair to say that the same is true for conjured creatures. Can I create a Zombie with 12 or 14 dice if I get the spells potency to 6 or 7?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:00:21-07:00","id":1092414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092408#post1092408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks again! I am looking at starting a game for a bunch of folk new to Mage in a few weeks and I am trying to sort all this stuff out in my head.<br /> <br /> Mind if I throw in a few other questions?<br /> <br /> On the topic of Veiling Spells: How do they work in combat? I get that an opposing Mage can call up his AMS for an instant Clash of Wills, but whats his options after that if he fails? Can I force more Clashes by casting Unveiling Spells searching for the hidden mage? IE A Mastigos who is 'Incognito' takes a pistol shot at a Moros, who calls up his AMS but fails to pierce the illusion. Can the Moros cast a spell like Detect Substance (Gunpowder) to pinpoint the gun and its wielder? Does this call for a second Clash?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would call for CoW, yes. However you should use cumulative -1 penalty for every failure, imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spells that create servants (Matter 4's Golem and Deaths Quicken Corpse for example) effectively grant dots in the retainer merit= to potency, which informs the created creatures dice pools. For example the Golem I create to protect my Sanctum has a combat dice pool = to Potencyx2. The stock retainer merit caps out at 5 dots, is it fair to say that the same is true for conjured creatures. Can I create a Zombie with 12 or 14 dice if I get the spells potency to 6 or 7? </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes. Spells modeled after Retainer merit are very clean and simple and should be used more often. If you wan't to go over 5 dots cap you should spend Reach and Mana, just like in any other spell that goes above this limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-14-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:25:54-07:00","id":1092419,"title":"","content":"I had a thought about High Speech as a yantra. If you use it as a yantra during the casting a spell wouldn't anybody within earshot know exactly what you're casting without the need for mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:31:31-07:00","id":1092423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092407#post1092407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would cause a problem is the nimbus flare that will be visible to anyone with AMS. If nobody 'looks' at the moment, you're good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the spell is considered a part of the subject, that is. It seems logical to me that it'd automatically include itself so you don't have a Nimbus hovering around connected to nothing.<br /> And even if you don't agree with that you could either increase scale factor to include the spell itself, or if you don't like spells targeting themselves you could have a Reach option that hides the Nimbus resulting from this spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:43:06-07:00","id":1092432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092419#post1092419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought about High Speech as a yantra. If you use it as a yantra during the casting a spell wouldn't anybody within earshot know exactly what you're casting without the need for mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they know the Rote they might. Otherwise not, High Speech doesn't convey the whole spell, its just a mnemonic technique that helps with picturing the Imago.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> While I'm not fond of spells targeting itself, its reasonable to add such a Reach, yea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T16:10:53-07:00","id":1092562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092408#post1092408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IE A Mastigos who is 'Incognito' takes a pistol shot at a Moros, who calls up his AMS but fails to pierce the illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Moros in question would need to use Mind AMS to even get a CoW in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T16:23:35-07:00","id":1092565,"title":"","content":"Or Prime. Prime is good for uncovering what's hidden by magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T16:48:36-07:00","id":1092573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092396#post1092396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. This will work for any supernatural creature, not just mages. This makes them undetectable to <i>anything</i>, not just other beings. Cameras etc would also be fooled.<br /> <br /> <br /> [/s]</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesnt supernal veil just veil magical effects from detection so you appear as a sleeper, have no spells, mana blah blah. Pretty sure its not meant as a invisibility cloak. What happens if cast on a sleeper?<br /> <br /> Mind veils minds which has the side effect of incognito presence, forces can hide you from light having the side effect of making you invisible. Prime hides magic this will just make you look like a sleeper, i cant see how that makes one invisible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T16:58:12-07:00","id":1092575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092573#post1092573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesnt supernal veil just veil magical effects from detection so you appear as a sleeper, have no spells, mana blah blah. Pretty sure its not meant as a invisibility cloak. What happens if cast on a sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as written, no. It hides anything supernatural from any sort of detection.<br /> This has been discussed before.<br /> <br /> The other effects your describing belong to a different sort of Veiling Spell - Cloak Nimbus.<br /> <br /> If you cast it on a Sleeper, nothing happens. Sleepers aren't valid subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-14-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T17:37:13-07:00","id":1092586,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that hiding anything supernatural from ever being perceived by anything else at all is not <i>in the </i><i>spirit</i> of Supernal Veil, however. I mean, it seems really weird to me if that's what it's supposed to do.<br /> <br /> Rules As Written the wording is ambiguous, but even it implies something different. It veils the subject from <i>detection</i>, not <i>perception</i>, and the following paragraph elaborates with the example of a <i>supernatural ability</i> which can instinctively detect phenomena like magic, and distinguishes active from passive abilities. Which is... strongly indicative of the intent of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-14-2017, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:12:31-07:00","id":1092595,"title":"","content":"I completely agree with YeOfLittleFaith. It's the only reading that makes sense to me, even if a literal reading says it completely hides mages and such.<br /> Prime Veiling should be able to hide everything supernatural, but it should not be able to hide everything that has supernatural qualities.<br /> <br /> That said the spell has been discussed quite a lot earlier and I don't think people will change their minds. The question has been answered and Katana1515 can chose the answer that makes the most sense to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T19:11:08-07:00","id":1092622,"title":"","content":"How does casting a spell sympathetically on multiple targets at once work? Do I need to spend one Yantra slot on each separate sympathetic link? What's the final Sympathy Withstand rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T19:47:02-07:00","id":1092637,"title":"","content":"Yes, you have to spend one Yantra slot per sympathetic target. Withstand is always calculated per subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T20:53:03-07:00","id":1092646,"title":"","content":"What does it needs to happen for a sleeper to witness magic for paradox? Does it only happens if he is directly watching the magic or just being there is enough?<br /> Can i say &quot;Look at that three headed monkey&quot;, and cast a fireball at his back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T21:28:37-07:00","id":1092657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092646#post1092646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it needs to happen for a sleeper to witness magic for paradox? Does it only happens if he is directly watching the magic or just being there is enough?<br /> Can i say &quot;Look at that three headed monkey&quot;, and cast a fireball at his back?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some cognizance of the magical phenomenon specifically.<br /> Unfortunately, the book isn't quite clear on how much cognizance is required.<br /> <br /> However it's more than mere physical presence, and must involve some actual observation.<br /> If someone turns their back, then unless the audible evidence of the spell's effect is enough to make them think &quot;oh shit, Magic&quot; then Paradox won't apply.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T22:31:40-07:00","id":1092665,"title":"","content":"There are some Rotes who have Reach effects like these:<br /> &quot;+2 Reach: Spend a point of Mana. The mage can cast this spell as a reflexive action.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it possible to use it as a Rote Spell to get the benefits of increased Reachs and Mudra Yantra? Or Mudra Yantras cannot be reflexive?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, how these Reach Effect works? I need to spent 1 Reach for Instant Spell and another +2 Reach and 1 Mana for Reflexive? Or Just 2 Reach and 1 Mana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T22:50:18-07:00","id":1092668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092562#post1092562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Moros in question would need to use Mind AMS to even get a CoW in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on! Have I been mentally doing this wrong! I had it in my head that mage sight let you perceive all spells, regardless of arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T23:06:05-07:00","id":1092669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092622#post1092622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does casting a spell sympathetically on multiple targets at once work? Do I need to spend one Yantra slot on each separate sympathetic link? What's the final Sympathy Withstand rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Withstand is calculated by each subject individually, however - I am of the mind that if you use one spell sympathetically on multiple targets, you only need one Yantra in order to use the Sympathetic Range Attainment. The problem, however, is that that sympathetic range attainment should represent all the targets at once; If it does not, you may need more than one yantra, simply because the first does not apply to the entire list of targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T23:09:10-07:00","id":1092670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092668#post1092668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hold on! Have I been mentally doing this wrong! I had it in my head that mage sight let you perceive all spells, regardless of arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only at the time of the casting. So you can Counter them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T01:09:52-07:00","id":1092692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092668#post1092668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hold on! Have I been mentally doing this wrong! I had it in my head that mage sight let you perceive all spells, regardless of arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Prime has universal Magic sight.<br /> But so long as you can see the spell being cast (requiring AMS of one of the component Arcana, or Prime) you can attempt a counterspell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T01:40:44-07:00","id":1092696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092586#post1092586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that hiding anything supernatural from ever being perceived by anything else at all is not <i>in the </i><i>spirit</i> of Supernal Veil, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. That's just not what it says. FWIW, we'd probably run it your way.<br /> <br /> That said, if 'Mages' or 'Supernatural Creatures' fall under the purview of Prime (they aren't listed, but the fact that Supernal Veil can even target them is evidence that they are) then it is completely valid for a Prime Veiling spell to shield them from detection entirely.<br /> <br /> See 'Hidden Hoard' concealing matter from notice. The same type of invisibility can just as reasonably be accomplished via Life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can conceal things under the Arcanum\u2019s purview from detection </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, they can conceal a target <i>from </i>concrete phenomena under the Arcanum\u2019s purview </div> </div> </div>Supernal Veil reads like it was probably intended to be the latter - shielding a target from magical detection. But the former is still valid - for Creative Thaum, for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T02:46:05-07:00","id":1092709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092665#post1092665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some Rotes who have Reach effects like these:<br /> &quot;+2 Reach: Spend a point of Mana. The mage can cast this spell as a reflexive action.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it possible to use it as a Rote Spell to get the benefits of increased Reachs and Mudra Yantra? Or Mudra Yantras cannot be reflexive?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, how these Reach Effect works? I need to spent 1 Reach for Instant Spell and another +2 Reach and 1 Mana for Reflexive? Or Just 2 Reach and 1 Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW you only need +2 Reach and Mana for Reflexive casting since Reach effects are always self-containing. As to Mudra being Reflexive... I don't know but normal casting allows only for one Yantra that is for this sole purpose made Reflexive. If you strip spellcasting to be also Reflexive it might not have this capacity. ( For what I know only High Speech can't be made Reflexive for this purpose)<br /> <br /> At my table however I run it that Instant is a prerequisite for Reflexive so its +3 Reach and 1 Mana for a whole effect and no Yantra at all is possible since there is not enough time. I made those decisions because I let every spell to be cast that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-15-2017, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:35:27-07:00","id":1092722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092665#post1092665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some Rotes who have Reach effects like these:<br /> &amp;quot;+2 Reach: Spend a point of Mana. The mage can cast this spell as a reflexive action.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Is it possible to use it as a Rote Spell to get the benefits of increased Reachs and Mudra Yantra? Or Mudra Yantras cannot be reflexive?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, how these Reach Effect works? I need to spent 1 Reach for Instant Spell and another +2 Reach and 1 Mana for Reflexive? Or Just 2 Reach and 1 Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW you get to use the Mudra as a reflexive Yantra. However, if your group disallows it for the reason Moinen cited there's still nothing that hinders you from casting the spell as a Rote.<br /> The Mudra is an optional Yantra that isn't needed to cast Rotes. This has been confirmed by Dave Brookshaw (I think it was in this thread) and if you read the section on Rotes you'll find out that casting a Rote from a Grimoire actually removes the possibility of using the Mudra as a Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:16:19-07:00","id":1092751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092668#post1092668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold on! Have I been mentally doing this wrong! I had it in my head that mage sight let you perceive all spells, regardless of arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, Peripheral Mage Sight can detect the use of any supernatural power regardless of arcana, but it doesn't pinpoint who or what or where you just know it's inside sensory range. Active Mage Sight can pinpoint who, what and where, but only if the Arcana used for the Sight is appropriate to the phenomena that the Mage is looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092670#post1092670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only at the time of the casting. So you can Counter them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Active Mage Sight regardless of arcana can notice when a Mage is casting a spell, but it's not because you can see the spell being formed, instead it's because you can witness the flare of the Nimbus. If you don't have the appropriate Mage Sight up you can't counter the spell they're casting unless you have a good guess of what they're about to do and have the appropriate aracana, or you have Prime which can do Universal Counterspell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-15-2017, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:51:16-07:00","id":1092758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092751#post1092751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, Peripheral Mage Sight can detect the use of any supernatural power regardless of arcana, but it doesn't pinpoint who or what or where you just know it's inside sensory range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's an oft repeated error.<br /> <br /> Going by Signs of Sorcery open dev info on Mage Sight, posted here <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for-miles-and-miles-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for...the-awakening/</a> you can tell the location of active effects in your periphery. Even if the subject is in Twilight. And even in records of events. That's right, photographs can trigger your peripheral mage sight.<br /> <br /> What's more, the Keen Periphery (\u2022\u2022) merit will tell you the Arcanum the effect falls under. A pretty helpful investment if I'm going to be honest, as you can make all kinds of wonderful assumptions based on that.<br /> <br /> That is, unless Dave's come back and said that they're not going to have that in the final product. In which case my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:51:37-07:00","id":1092829,"title":"","content":"What's the best way to resolve casting spells on something that's bigger on the inside?<br /> For instance if there was a phone booth with Secret Room cast on the inside of it,<br /> then another mage cast a spell on the outside of the booth to turn the whole booth into water.<br /> Would an area spell cast on the outside effect the inside even if it only fully encompassed the smaller outside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:36:14-07:00","id":1092914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1092829#post1092829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the best way to resolve casting spells on something that's bigger on the inside?<br /> For instance if there was a phone booth with Secret Room cast on the inside of it,<br /> then another mage cast a spell on the outside of the booth to turn the whole booth into water.<br /> Would an area spell cast on the outside effect the inside even if it only fully encompassed the smaller outside?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that spells cast on either side effect the full object on the other side (and no more or less). However, when casting I'd only require the spell to have a Scale Factor meeting that side's perspective: IE, if the phone booth secretly has a 100x100 room inside, you can fill the whole thing with water even if your spell only covers the scale of a phone booth - as long as you're casting from the outside.<br /> <br /> If you're on the inside and you cast the spell with sufficient scale, it fills with 100x100 feet of water, but on the outside it would only appear that the standard volume of the booth is full (no overflow).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T08:34:52-07:00","id":1093667,"title":"","content":"Back with a few more quick questions, this time about how spells interact with Twilight and the Shadow when the caster lacks Death or Spirit.<br /> <br /> If I have a sympathetic link to another mage, who is currently in a twilight form (say via Death Gate) and currently invisible to the naked eye, what do I see when I scry on him? No result, an empty room, or something else? What if they were in the Shadow instead? Or if a friendly mage cast some unveiling spell that let me see into twilight/across the gauntlet first? <br /> <br /> Similar question, If another mage has given me the ability to see a target across the Gauntlet, or in Twilight, can I target them with my own spells? I have the notion that it costs an extra reach in my head somewhere, but can't find anything in the book to corroborate this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T08:56:31-07:00","id":1093674,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Question, about Legacy Attainments:</i></b><br /> <br /> How do you make them Indefinite? ( And by the way, could it be called &quot;Lasting&quot;?) A spell requires 2 reach <i>and</i> a Mana point, but how do you do it in a Legacy Attainment? I was thinking something along the line of spending a Willpower dot, but... well, how would you do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T09:51:18-07:00","id":1093686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1093667#post1093667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back with a few more quick questions, this time about how spells interact with Twilight and the Shadow when the caster lacks Death or Spirit.<br /> <br /> If I have a sympathetic link to another mage, who is currently in a twilight form (say via Death Gate) and currently invisible to the naked eye, what do I see when I scry on him? No result, an empty room, or something else? What if they were in the Shadow instead? Or if a friendly mage cast some unveiling spell that let me see into twilight/across the gauntlet first? <br /> <br /> Similar question, If another mage has given me the ability to see a target across the Gauntlet, or in Twilight, can I target them with my own spells? I have the notion that it costs an extra reach in my head somewhere, but can't find anything in the book to corroborate this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't possess the means to observe a subject then you cannot observe the subject. If you do, regardless of the source, then you can. The Mage who cast the Unveiling spell on you would be the one to CoW if that's necessary. If you can observe a target you can cast on it, though depending on how you're doing so you may need to employ remote viewing casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T09:55:41-07:00","id":1093687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1093674#post1093674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Question, about Legacy Attainments:</i></b><br /> <br /> How do you make them Indefinite? ( And by the way, could it be called &quot;Lasting&quot;?) A spell requires 2 reach <i>and</i> a Mana point, but how do you do it in a Legacy Attainment? I was thinking something along the line of spending a Willpower dot, but... well, how would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>An attainment isn't Lasting. The effects of an attainment can be Lasting if it's modeled off a spell that either has Lasting effects as a byproduct (Damage, healing, etc) or if it has a Reach option to be made Lasting in which case the attainment is required to take that Reach into account.<br /> <br /> Attainments can be moved up to Indefinite by having Duration as the primary and spending the free Dice penalties spent on moving further on the Duration chart, and also spending Reach for Advanced Duration, a Reach on Indefinite and a point of mana upon activation (Though the total mana cost can't rise above 1 in case other mana expenditures would normally need to be taken into account).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T10:25:35-07:00","id":1093697,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1093687#post1093687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attainments can be moved up to Indefinite by having Duration as the primary and spending the free Dice penalties spent on moving further on the Duration chart, and also spending Reach for Advanced Duration, a Reach on Indefinite and a point of mana upon activation (Though the total mana cost can't rise above 1 in case other mana expenditures would normally need to be taken into account).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the quick answer Mrmdubois! So you can make a Legacy Attainment indefinite using just the same rules that spells use. Well, that's a worthy Mana point, that's for sure!<br /> <br /> But wait, here's another related question: Why is it necessary to change its Primary Factor to Duration? I mean, let's take <b>Read the Depths</b>. This spell (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022) has Potency as a primary factor. As i understand it, you could simply leave Potency, and spend the 2 Reach and the Mana point in making it Indefinite. Am i wrong?</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":1349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","user":"Phersus","date":".  A wild new question appeared! 05-17-2017, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:35:34-07:00","id":1093718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1093697#post1093697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thank you for the quick answer Mrmdubois! So you can make a Legacy Attainment indefinite using just the same rules that spells use. Well, that's a worthy Mana point, that's for sure!<br /> <br /> But wait, here's another related question: Why is it necessary to change its Primary Factor to Duration? I mean, let's take <b>Read the Depths</b>. This spell (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022) has Potency as a primary factor. As i understand it, you could simply leave Potency, and spend the 2 Reach and the Mana point in making it Indefinite. Am i wrong?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's wrong, because an Indefinite Duration -also- requires taking -10 in dice penalties. You can't achieve that if you don't have Duration as the primary factor because an attainment only has a number of &quot;dice&quot; to spend equal to arcana, meaning at most 5 dice which is only enough to move you a few steps down the Duration chart. Fortunately, if Duration is the primary factor, it gets the free bump on the chart equal to dots in the primary factor, then if you apply dice penalties you can move the rest of the way to Indefinite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T21:17:53-07:00","id":1093978,"title":"","content":"This is a question for Dave if he is reading this. <br /> I understand that the new idea for the Tremere is for them to me something like a minor template on top of the mage, with legacies as houses. Would they still need to know Death to steal souls or would soul-stealing be a natural power for them?<br /> I want to know if in 2ed it would be possible to have a Tremere with no points in Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:32:32-07:00","id":1093996,"title":"","content":"Is opening locks within the purview of Remote Control (Matter *)? Part of me feels like it falls within wording of the spell, but another part of me feels like it should require at least a practice of Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:59:00-07:00","id":1094033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1093996#post1093996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is opening locks within the purview of Remote Control (Matter *)? Part of me feels like it falls within wording of the spell, but another part of me feels like it should require at least a practice of Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be used to open locks as long as those locks can be opened with a single Instant action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:08:50-07:00","id":1094037,"title":"","content":"You are a gentleman and a scholar, MrmDubois. Thank you very much ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:33:24-07:00","id":1094104,"title":"","content":"The books section on Mage Sight contains the following example, which i am struggling to understand, was hoping you guys could help.<br /> <br /> <i>Concealment magic, of whatever type, can hide a target from Active Mage Sight, but only if the concealment would logically mask the target from the purview of the Arcanum in question. Even then, if the concealment power uses the same magical principles as the detecting Arcanum, the mage still has a chance to see through it. <b>For example, a light-based invisibility spell would conceal a target from Mind Sight, but Life Sight could still detect the living being, with or without the assistance of photons. </b></i><br /> <br /> If Life Sight could detect an invisible mage by picking up on his lifesigns, why on earth does Mind Sight not have a chance to pick up on the presence of a sentient mind? <br /> <br /> This is causing me quite a bit of brain ache, and I was wondering if anyone had sketched out some rough ground-rules as to what 'Sights' would be able to pierce which kind of Veils. If I use Prime to make myself undetectable rather than forces, will Lifesight still have a shot at detecting him? What about using Incognito Presence instead? <br /> <br /> All help is much appreciated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:35:05-07:00","id":1094106,"title":"","content":"It's most likely a typo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:14:46-07:00","id":1094171,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that discussion has been had and it's pretty much got to be a typo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:27:34-07:00","id":1094263,"title":"","content":"So a player has an idea to use a Life 3 spell to give himself iron scales like an iron foot snail and I'm not sure how to represent this in game. I was thinking it would give him the benefits and drawbacks of chainmail applied to his entire body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:39:12-07:00","id":1094268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094263#post1094263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a player has an idea to use a Life 3 spell to give himself iron scales like an iron foot snail and I'm not sure how to represent this in game. I was thinking it would give him the benefits and drawbacks of chainmail applied to his entire body.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more complicated than it needs to be. <br /> <br /> There's already a listed option under Life \u2022\u2022\u2022 Transform Life to give 'Scaly Armor' - which gives 2/1 armor rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:16:43-07:00","id":1094302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094263#post1094263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a player has an idea to use a Life 3 spell to give himself iron scales like an iron foot snail and I'm not sure how to represent this in game. I was thinking it would give him the benefits and drawbacks of chainmail applied to his entire body.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What Inodiv said, improving the armor rating from there would be a Perfecting spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:17:54-07:00","id":1094333,"title":"","content":"That's a very good point. I'd imagine scales of metal would be at least a 3/1 rating though. <br /> <br /> As a bonus question I have another player who wants to take &quot;state change&quot; as a praxis for general utility and capturing someone who's fleeing. (As in change the state of the floor underneath the dude into liquid for a turn so he sinks chest deep before the ground turns back into a solid) Assuming he uses the reach and everything else correctly any reasons why that won't work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T17:42:47-07:00","id":1094362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094333#post1094333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very good point. I'd imagine scales of metal would be at least a 3/1 rating though.<br /> <br /> As a bonus question I have another player who wants to take &quot;state change&quot; as a praxis for general utility and capturing someone who's fleeing. (As in change the state of the floor underneath the dude into liquid for a turn so he sinks chest deep before the ground turns back into a solid) Assuming he uses the reach and everything else correctly any reasons why that won't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's all paid up there's no reason why that wouldn't work. Just be aware of spell factors. This is the essence in a way of Mage, the indirect approach is king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T01:39:34-07:00","id":1094459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094104#post1094104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books section on Mage Sight contains the following example, which i am struggling to understand, was hoping you guys could help.<br /> <br /> <i>Concealment magic, of whatever type, can hide a target from Active Mage Sight, <b>but only if the concealment would logically mask the target from the purview of the Arcanum in question. Even then, if the concealment power uses the same magical principles as the detecting Arcanum, the mage still has a chance to see through it.</b> For example, a light-based invisibility spell would conceal a target from Mind Sight, but Life Sight could still detect the living being, with or without the assistance of photons.</i><br /> <br /> If Life Sight could detect an invisible mage by picking up on his lifesigns, why on earth does Mind Sight not have a chance to pick up on the presence of a sentient mind?<br /> <br /> This is causing me quite a bit of brain ache, and I was wondering if anyone had sketched out some rough ground-rules as to what 'Sights' would be able to pierce which kind of Veils. If I use Prime to make myself undetectable rather than forces, will Lifesight still have a shot at detecting him? What about using Incognito Presence instead?<br /> <br /> All help is much appreciated</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... yes. I'm struggling with Concealment Magic in general. In that particular case, which Active Mage Sight would be fooled? Each time i want to consider these spells, i come out with a headache. I'll elaborate a bit:<br /> <br /> - Life could pierce through it, Mind also,<br /> - Forces... too, i guess? As the mage is using Forces to make herself invisible, that very use of the Arcana should be detectable by another Forces-savvy mage, right?<br /> - Matter could pick up the subtle movement of air in her breathing, so maybe, on an exceptional success? (Also, it coud detect her outfit, so maybe there would be no need for an exceptional success after all)<br /> - Fate could detect the role that hidden character has in that particular situation, so maybe it could, too?<br /> - Time, i don't think so.<br /> - Spirit, only it the subject has some relation to, well, spirits (as in a familiar, or a spirit influencing her actions), or Essence in general.<br /> - Space could pierce it, i think, as a solid body counts as an object and the spatial awareness that Space confers would pretty much locate it as a radar.<br /> - Prime could pierce it, as its very body contains Mana embedded in its Pattern.<br /> - Death, as Spirit. Tough it can be argued that as the mage has a soul, it could be detected by Death. Mmmmm not sure of it after all.<br /> <br /> Some pain in the ass, concealment magic! ^^' What are your thoughts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T01:45:43-07:00","id":1094461,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Incidentally, Mind Question: </b></i><br /> <br /> Would you allow Mind Magic to detect and act upon robots? I am currently accepting it when used on Demons and Angels (which are somewhat that), but i'm not sure of it when it comes to work with lesser machines, Terminator-like, other the God Machine servants, low grade AIs etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T02:12:25-07:00","id":1094463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094461#post1094461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Incidentally, Mind Question: </b></i><br /> <br /> Would you allow Mind Magic to detect and act upon robots? I am currently accepting it when used on Demons and Angels (which are somewhat that), but i'm not sure of it when it comes to work with lesser machines, Terminator-like, other the God Machine servants, low grade AIs etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they have a 'mind'? If so, yes.<br /> <br /> It already works on animals, people, spirits, ghosts, etc by default. It's pretty clear that anything with a 'mind' (sapient or not) falls under its Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T02:12:26-07:00","id":1094464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094459#post1094459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually... yes. I'm struggling with Concealment Magic in general. In that particular case, which Active Mage Sight would be fooled? Each time i want to consider these spells, i come out with a headache. I'll elaborate a bit:<br /> <br /> - Life could pierce through it, Mind also,<br /> - Forces... too, i guess? As the mage is using Forces to make herself invisible, that very use of the Arcana should be detectable by another Forces-savvy mage, right?<br /> - Matter could pick up the subtle movement of air in her breathing, so maybe, on an exceptional success? (Also, it coud detect her outfit, so maybe there would be no need for an exceptional success after all)<br /> - Fate could detect the role that hidden character has in that particular situation, so maybe it could, too?<br /> - Time, i don't think so.<br /> - Spirit, only it the subject has some relation to, well, spirits (as in a familiar, or a spirit influencing her actions), or Essence in general.<br /> - Space could pierce it, i think, as a solid body counts as an object and the spatial awareness that Space confers would pretty much locate it as a radar.<br /> - Prime could pierce it, as its very body contains Mana embedded in its Pattern.<br /> - Death, as Spirit. Tough it can be argued that as the mage has a soul, it could be detected by Death. Mmmmm not sure of it after all.<br /> <br /> Some pain in the ass, concealment magic! ^^' What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am considering just running with any Active Mage Sight can get a shot at piercing a Veiling spell, as it seems to me that every path has ways to justify piercing the veil if you dig deep enough and the language in the book as it stands doesnt give me enough reason to justify turning to my players and saying 'no' when a player points it out. The various 'you cant see me' spells are all still very powerful in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T03:05:48-07:00","id":1094478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094459#post1094459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually... yes. I'm struggling with Concealment Magic in general. In that particular case, which Active Mage Sight would be fooled? Each time i want to consider these spells, i come out with a headache. I'll elaborate a bit:<br /> <br /> - Life could pierce through it, Mind also,<br /> - Forces... too, i guess? As the mage is using Forces to make herself invisible, that very use of the Arcana should be detectable by another Forces-savvy mage, right?<br /> - Matter could pick up the subtle movement of air in her breathing, so maybe, on an exceptional success? (Also, it coud detect her outfit, so maybe there would be no need for an exceptional success after all)<br /> - Fate could detect the role that hidden character has in that particular situation, so maybe it could, too?<br /> - Time, i don't think so.<br /> - Spirit, only it the subject has some relation to, well, spirits (as in a familiar, or a spirit influencing her actions), or Essence in general.<br /> - Space could pierce it, i think, as a solid body counts as an object and the spatial awareness that Space confers would pretty much locate it as a radar.<br /> - Prime could pierce it, as its very body contains Mana embedded in its Pattern.<br /> - Death, as Spirit. Tough it can be argued that as the mage has a soul, it could be detected by Death. Mmmmm not sure of it after all.<br /> <br /> Some pain in the ass, concealment magic! ^^' What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can pretty much be assumed that most of the Mage Sights will have a chance at working around or directly piercing any form of concealment they run up against. As people who perceive what no one else can in order to piece together the mysteries that surround them it fits Mage's theme really well. This is exactly why smart Mages conceal stuff in such a way that no one would think anything is out of the ordinary and worth looking at. You don't use Forces to veil yourself when your opponent shows up at the door, you do it a week ago in a remote area, and preferably have never lived at your given address.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T16:51:37-07:00","id":1094723,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to fold a lesser practice into a greater practice without casting a combined spell?<br /> Say you wanted to turn the asphalt to liquid beneath someone's feet, then wrap it around their body before relinquishing the spell so they're trapped in a cocoon.<br /> That would going by the rules be the Shaping and State Change spells (I don't see the Shaping spell as permitting true fluid dynamics with solids, even with the Reach option), which to cast would be a combined spell.<br /> <br /> However, is there any way to fold those into one spell? Such as by adding a Reach option to State Change?<br /> Or should the bullet just be bit, and wait until Gnosis 3 for such fun Matter manipulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T22:44:21-07:00","id":1094782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094723#post1094723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to fold a lesser practice into a greater practice without casting a combined spell?<br /> Say you wanted to turn the asphalt to liquid beneath someone's feet, then wrap it around their body before relinquishing the spell so they're trapped in a cocoon.<br /> That would going by the rules be the Shaping and State Change spells (I don't see the Shaping spell as permitting true fluid dynamics with solids, even with the Reach option), which to cast would be a combined spell.<br /> <br /> However, is there any way to fold those into one spell? Such as by adding a Reach option to State Change?<br /> Or should the bullet just be bit, and wait until Gnosis 3 for such fun Matter manipulations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If resolving the issue by Reach, I recommend adding Reach to Shaping rather than State Change, since manipulating matter so that it cocoons someone is still under what Shaping does. You could just relax the &quot;affect solids&quot; +1 Reach option so that it does indeed allow fluid dynamics, or leave that one be and include a new, +2 Reach option that does allow completely fluid movement of solids. (I'd go for the former, personally)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T01:19:17-07:00","id":1094801,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your answers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094463#post1094463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It already works on animals, people, spirits, ghosts, etc by default. It's pretty clear that anything with a 'mind' (sapient or not) falls under its Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it can be argued that robots don't really have a mind, they have a pregenerated array of answers to perform when the specified prerequisites apply without cognition, hence the question. But i get the spirit of your answer, thank you lnodiv!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T02:41:06-07:00","id":1094816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094461#post1094461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Incidentally, Mind Question: </b></i><br /> <br /> Would you allow Mind Magic to detect and act upon robots? I am currently accepting it when used on Demons and Angels (which are somewhat that), but i'm not sure of it when it comes to work with lesser machines, Terminator-like, other the God Machine servants, low grade AIs etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you unsure if they have 'mind' but sure that they are not simple programs you could use 'add +1 Reach'. It's a great mechanic for edge cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094723#post1094723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to fold a lesser practice into a greater practice without casting a combined spell?<br /> Say you wanted to turn the asphalt to liquid beneath someone's feet, then wrap it around their body before relinquishing the spell so they're trapped in a cocoon.<br /> That would going by the rules be the Shaping and State Change spells (I don't see the Shaping spell as permitting true fluid dynamics with solids, even with the Reach option), which to cast would be a combined spell.<br /> <br /> However, is there any way to fold those into one spell? Such as by adding a Reach option to State Change?<br /> Or should the bullet just be bit, and wait until Gnosis 3 for such fun Matter manipulations.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have three options. Wait till Gnosis 3 as you said, add Reach to Shaping or wait till Matter 4 that could do it as a single spell (Patterning tends to use sets of effects as a single spell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:46:38-07:00","id":1094936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094723#post1094723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to fold a lesser practice into a greater practice without casting a combined spell?<br /> Say you wanted to turn the asphalt to liquid beneath someone's feet, then wrap it around their body before relinquishing the spell so they're trapped in a cocoon.<br /> That would going by the rules be the Shaping and State Change spells (I don't see the Shaping spell as permitting true fluid dynamics with solids, even with the Reach option), which to cast would be a combined spell.<br /> <br /> However, is there any way to fold those into one spell? Such as by adding a Reach option to State Change?<br /> Or should the bullet just be bit, and wait until Gnosis 3 for such fun Matter manipulations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this effect as a Patterning effect. The problem, however, is that in order to get a Patterning effect, you need Gnosis 3 in order to have Matter 4, and a combined spell is just as good an option for an effect like this.<br /> <br /> This however seems unnecessary to me. By default, the +1 reach option allows you to shape matter in methods you prefer, and while that may not have true fluid dynamics, Asphalt - and most other things - can be granular. That by itself allows you to manipulate the matter in this way while - not being true fluid dynamics - would certainly -seem- so to outside witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T14:47:34-07:00","id":1094949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094936#post1094936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This however seems unnecessary to me. By default, the +1 reach option allows you to shape matter in methods you prefer, and while that may not have true fluid dynamics, Asphalt - and most other things - can be granular. That by itself allows you to manipulate the matter in this way while - not being true fluid dynamics - would certainly -seem- so to outside witnesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this is the best way to handle it. It's how my current Matter mage has been getting things done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T06:42:01-07:00","id":1096275,"title":"","content":"It is possible for a awakened to posses other supernatural magic items and use them? Like Hedge Tokens, Uratha Fetishs and this sorts of things? If yes, them how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T06:44:10-07:00","id":1096277,"title":"","content":"I believe Prime 1 has a spell that allows you to activate any supernatural item, even non mage one, as long as you can add an appropriate Arcanum (so a Hedge Token would demand Prime1+Fate1, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:00:23-07:00","id":1096335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096275#post1096275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is possible for a awakened to posses other supernatural magic items and use them? Like Hedge Tokens, Uratha Fetishs and this sorts of things? If yes, them how?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Mages can <i>create</i> 'Uratha Fetishes' with a published spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:09:33-07:00","id":1096342,"title":"","content":"I think that this mentioned by WHW Prime spell is overdone. There is nothing in Prime that would help to activate the e.g. Fetish. The only aspect that can be argued with is 'truth' but it would mean that Spirit is not 'true' enough which I don't buy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:11:41-07:00","id":1096343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096342#post1096342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that this mentioned by WHW Prime spell is overdone. There is nothing in Prime that would help to activate the e.g. Fetish. The only aspect that can be argued with is 'truth' but it would mean that Spirit is not 'true' enough which I don't buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because 'Magic' is under the purview of Prime, and it can be inferred from the text, and has been clarified outside of it, that 'magic' is not just Awakened Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:16:23-07:00","id":1096350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096343#post1096343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because 'Magic' is under the purview of Prime, and it can be inferred from the text, and has been clarified outside of it, that 'magic' is not just Awakened Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that it has been clarified and since there's been many debates whether its 'magic' or 'Magic' only we must wait for errat, sigh. But even if it's the former case I can't see why Spirit wouldn't be able to activate something that it can create few dots later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:18:07-07:00","id":1096352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096350#post1096350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that it has been clarified and since there's been many debates whether its 'magic' or 'Magic' only we must wait for errat, sigh. But even if it's the former case I can't see why Spirit wouldn't be able to activate something that it can create few dots later.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Compelling Spirit spell probably could.<br /> That's not the only thing the Prime spell does - it also lets you pay Mana instead of the normal activation cost.<br /> <br /> Also - there are 4 published Prime spells that treat other supernatural phenomena as something under its purview. I'll have to check and see if I can find what I'm thinking of re: out of game clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-24-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:18:54-07:00","id":1096353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its purview is the manipulation of magic itself: Mana and tass, the Nimbus<br /> and Hallows, High Speech and the runes of the ancient masters. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that this sentence says only about Awakened Magic, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:22:44-07:00","id":1096355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096352#post1096352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A compelling Spirit spell probably could.<br /> <br /> That's not the only thing the Prime spell does - it also lets you pay Mana instead of the normal activation cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Yes. That certainly is an effect that only Prime can pull off at this level, I agree. Luckily, if I remember correctly, Fetish can hold its own reserve of essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:28:10-07:00","id":1096358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096352#post1096352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Compelling Spirit spell probably could.<br /> That's not the only thing the Prime spell does - it also lets you pay Mana instead of the normal activation cost.<br /> <br /> Also - there are 4 published Prime spells that treat other supernatural phenomena as something under its purview. I'll have to check and see if I can find what I'm thinking of re: out of game clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supernal Veil is the only one that mentions supernatural creatures directly, I think. Its still probably application of 'truth' aspect which is great for Veilings and Unvelings in general.<br /> <br /> Edit: Triple post. Good job me. Sorry for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T09:16:24-07:00","id":1096377,"title":"","content":"Word of Command lets you activate non-supernal magical objects (although requires other Arcana to do so, borderline)<br /> Supernal Veil works on other supernatural creatures explicitly - if it was just truthiness this would work on anything.<br /> Supernal Vision works on non-supernal beings and phenomena.<br /> Word of Making refers to magical objects in the same context that Word of Command does (super, super, super borderline).<br /> <br /> Honestly, Vision + Veil make the intent clear imo, but it's certainly up for interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T09:40:57-07:00","id":1096390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096377#post1096377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word of Command lets you activate non-supernal magical objects (although requires other Arcana to do so, borderline)<br /> Supernal Veil works on other supernatural creatures explicitly - if it was just truthiness this would work on anything.<br /> Supernal Vision works on non-supernal beings and phenomena.<br /> Word of Making refers to magical objects in the same context that Word of Command does (super, super, super borderline).<br /> <br /> Honestly, Vision + Veil make the intent clear imo, but it's certainly up for interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of Command acts counter dogma established by other arcana that work standalone. Fate doesn't need need Matter to affect items or Prime to affect spells, it affects Fate part of them. Death can affect <i>eeevveeerything</i>. Mind.. you know, how it goes. So if 'magic' is under purview of Prime it should act on this aspect alone without need of other arcana. Yea, but lets don't go there(Dispels) again.<br /> Supernal Veil - I'm begining to suspect that its a typo. Supernal creature would be much more inline. <br /> Supernal Vision gives back mostly only a scrambled pictures - also an edgy case.<br /> World of Unmaking... as you said 'super borderline'. Sadly it doesn't define what is magic.<br /> \u200b<br /> Prime Armor talks about other supernatural powers but it's an attainment and this part might be an attempt to balance the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> If your version is correct spell like this should be viable:<br /> <br /> Slumber (Prime 2)<br /> Practice: Rulling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Mage calls forth his command over Magic and all it's iterations to put them dormant. Mages and Proximi fall asleep on the spot, artifacts and imbued items in the area stop working.<br /> + 1 Reach: spell can also affect other supernal creatures and paranormal equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T09:46:18-07:00","id":1096392,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096342#post1096342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that this mentioned by WHW Prime spell is overdone. There is nothing in Prime that would help to activate the e.g. Fetish. The only aspect that can be argued with is 'truth' but it would mean that Spirit is not 'true' enough which I don't buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interpretations of Prime aside, it's totally how the spell is intended to function, so claiming that the spell shouldn't work isn't a helpful answer in a thread about getting answers, imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096335#post1096335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Mages can <i>create</i> 'Uratha Fetishes' with a published spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096350#post1096350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that it has been clarified and since there's been many debates whether its 'magic' or 'Magic' only we must wait for errat, sigh. But even if it's the former case I can't see why Spirit wouldn't be able to activate something that it can create few dots later.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage kind of Fetish works differently from the Werewolf kind of Fetish. It's a case of similar concepts having the same name. The Mage type Fetish doesn't require any kind of spell to be activated, unless you wish to do so from a distance. Also, nothing says Spirit alone wouldn't be able to activate the Werewolf type Fetish just because there's no published spell for doing so. Word of Command would overlap with such a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T10:01:53-07:00","id":1096393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096392#post1096392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Interpretations of Prime aside, it's totally how the spell is intended to function, so claiming that the spell shouldn't work isn't a helpful answer in a thread about getting answers, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't work <i>that way</i>. But you're right, sorry.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Mage kind of Fetish works differently from the Werewolf kind of Fetish. It's a case of similar concepts having the same name. The Mage type Fetish doesn't require any kind of spell to be activated, unless you wish to do so from a distance. Also, nothing says Spirit alone wouldn't be able to activate the Werewolf type Fetish just because there's no published spell for doing so. Word of Command would overlap with such a spell. </div> </div> </div>I just dislike spells that grab other arcana by establishing a rule. Like Shrink and Grow for example - of course Matter is all about transmutations and shaping but the principle of this spell (it's description) could be used by any arcana. Reach effect says that you can't do it without Matter. <br /> <br /> So if we allow Spirit to activate Fetishes, which I would do, and allow Prime to affect supernatural in general, which Inodiv would do, Word of Command can be easily broken into two spells. Except the mana part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T10:56:57-07:00","id":1096409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096393#post1096393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just dislike spells that grab other arcana by establishing a rule. Like Shrink and Grow for example - of course Matter is all about transmutations and shaping but the principle of this spell (it's description) could be used by any arcana. Reach effect says that you can't do it without Matter.<br /> <br /> So if we allow Spirit to activate Fetishes, which I would do, and allow Prime to affect supernatural in general, which Inodiv would do, Word of Command can be easily broken into two spells. Except the mana part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you can use a Reach and Life as a conjunctional Arcanum with Shrink and Grow to affect living beings doesn't necessarily mean you can't just cast Transform Life on living beings to achieve the same effect. So why would you use Shrink and Grow instead of Transform Life? Because that particular mage might have more free Reach with Shrink and Grow, have Shrink and Grow as Praxis or Rote, want to affect both living beings and objects without having to cast a combined spell, or get better Yantra options for Shrink and Grow, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-24-2017, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T11:35:10-07:00","id":1096427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1096409#post1096409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that you can use a Reach and Life as a conjunctional Arcanum with Shrink and Grow to affect living beings doesn't necessarily mean you can't just cast Transform Life on living beings to achieve the same effect. So why would you use Shrink and Grow instead of Transform Life? Because that particular mage might have more free Reach with Shrink and Grow, have Shrink and Grow as Praxis or Rote, want to affect both living beings and objects without having to cast a combined spell, or get better Yantra options for Shrink and Grow, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's how I do it at my table but if you would take a voting here most likely it will go the other way. Hmm. Changing the topic only slightly. Conjunctional Fraying seems like it should work, isn't it?<br /> It's a one goal from multiple angles, like in Transubstantiation or Sacred Geometry.<br /> <br /> Edit: Like in 'I want to destroy you and everything you have!' Life 3 for human + Matter 3 for his clothes and weapon. I would allow that but if you add Prime 3 to damage Mana it gets complicated... You would need to divide potency or something. Weaving should be more fun - mix him up a little, take from mana, give to health, merge him with jacket and possibly give penalty from the 'lack of comfort'. Conjunctionals are weird without rules :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-24-2017, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T15:30:46-07:00","id":1096885,"title":"","content":"New Question: Assume I am an Adept of Death looking to craft a reliable bodyguard. I bind a ghost back into a fresh corpse using the Revenant spell for this purpose. How obviously dead and unnatural is my creation? I want him to be able to pass for alive (at least under light scrutiny) so he can accompany me places or run errands. Could I use Death or Matter spells to make the possessed corpse look more lifelike? Or could it work as an alternative +1 Reach option for the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T16:00:41-07:00","id":1096890,"title":"","content":"If using the Possession Manifestation the resulting revenant would look just like the corpse it was before it was possessed, but it appears it won't further decompose with time. If you wish to hide the effects of blood having pooled in certain parts of the body, or the open wounds (if any) from whatever killed it I suggest using Corpse Mask to make it appear the revenant died of a heart attack a few seconds ago. Other than that you'd have to order your ghost to breathe and you'll probably be able to take your revenant out among people. Just don't have anyone come into prolonged contact (i.e noticing the lack of body heat) or taking the pulse of your revenant or your ruse might be up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Spelling 05-26-2017, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:23:47-07:00","id":1097666,"title":"","content":"Are Temenos Geotia just &quot;actors&quot; for the larger realms?<br /> <br /> Or rather, could you affect the way that mankind percieves a specific Temenos-realm topic, by summoning an important Goetia (even even several/all the Goetia) from that realm out of the Astral, much the way you can affect someone's mind by summoning a Goetia from their Oneiros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T06:55:41-07:00","id":1097762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1097666#post1097666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Temenos Geotia just &quot;actors&quot; for the larger realms?<br /> <br /> Or rather, could you affect the way that mankind percieves a specific Temenos-realm topic, by summoning an important Goetia (even even several/all the Goetia) from that realm out of the Astral, much the way you can affect someone's mind by summoning a Goetia from their Oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're actors since there's no actual difference between a goetia in your Oneiros and one in the Temenos except for location. If you manipulated the actions of goetia that cross temenotic borders though, like the train or the rebel it could have a secondary effect of drawing two realms closer together which would eventually have the impact you're looking for. There are also Astral artifacts that can &quot;pin&quot; one realm to another and force a shift. That was a key point in Soul Cage that nearly allowed the bad guy to pull off his gambit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T03:04:03-07:00","id":1098381,"title":"","content":"Quick Question: Sitting down with a new player to hash out how Control Electricity works when used as a weapon. Two things I am a bit stuck on. <br /> <br /> 1. If I am using the spell to attack someone (Such as a person stood next to a wall outlet) does the spells Duration (which is its Primary Factor) come into account? IE if the spell has 3 turns of Duration will the poor victim take 4 levels of Bashing Damage for the next 3 turns, assuming he cant get away or otherwise change the scenario? The book says &quot;using the electrical current to attack a target usually burns out the breakers or shorts out a device afterward&quot; but I am unsure if this is meant to mean after the first turn, or after the spell is finished. The latter seems much more fun but powerful enough that I wanted other folks thoughts on the matter. <br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Each level of Potency in the spell allows the mage to control one line of power.&quot; Assume the room I am in has 2 wall outlets, could a Potency 2 version of the spell be used to cause each arcs of electricity to strike 2 targets? Or the same one twice for extra damage? <br /> <br /> Thanks for everyone's time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T03:14:56-07:00","id":1098382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1098381#post1098381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question: Sitting down with a new player to hash out how Control Electricity works when used as a weapon. Two things I am a bit stuck on.<br /> <br /> 1. If I am using the spell to attack someone (Such as a person stood next to a wall outlet) does the spells Duration (which is its Primary Factor) come into account? IE if the spell has 3 turns of Duration will the poor victim take 4 levels of Bashing Damage for the next 3 turns, assuming he cant get away or otherwise change the scenario? The book says &quot;using the electrical current to attack a target usually burns out the breakers or shorts out a device afterward&quot; but I am unsure if this is meant to mean after the first turn, or after the spell is finished. The latter seems much more fun but powerful enough that I wanted other folks thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Each level of Potency in the spell allows the mage to control one line of power.&quot; Assume the room I am in has 2 wall outlets, could a Potency 2 version of the spell be used to cause each arcs of electricity to strike 2 targets? Or the same one twice for extra damage?<br /> <br /> Thanks for everyone's time!</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Electricity does damage based on turns of exposure, so yes. If this was a direct damage spell, you'd instead look at the rules regarding spells 'repeating' once per Ritual interval.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T04:41:19-07:00","id":1098399,"title":"","content":"I read that as you can control the flow for the Duration, but causing the electricity to arc can cause a circuit to blow early. What's strange to me is that lines of power control increases by Potency rather than Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T08:52:27-07:00","id":1098444,"title":"","content":"Im not an electrician but how many lines of power does a typical house/room have in it? Arnt two wall sockets usually on the same power line? I think my house would have 2 though, one for the wall sockets and one for the lightbulb? Its been a long time since my circuits have blown a fuse so i cant remember but upstairs and downstairs are on a different circuit i think too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T09:05:33-07:00","id":1098447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1098399#post1098399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's strange to me is that lines of power control increases by Potency rather than Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this would work better if those were controlled by Scale, and Potency determined the strength of the electrical charge you can direct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T09:37:14-07:00","id":1098457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1098444#post1098444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not an electrician but how many lines of power does a typical house/room have in it? Arnt two wall sockets usually on the same power line? I think my house would have 2 though, one for the wall sockets and one for the lightbulb? Its been a long time since my circuits have blown a fuse so i cant remember but upstairs and downstairs are on a different circuit i think too?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll know if you check your circuit breaker, there are usually quite a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T23:16:48-07:00","id":1098669,"title":"","content":"Can you spontaneously create a blast of fire with fraying even though doing so would be creating from nothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T23:22:00-07:00","id":1098670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1098669#post1098669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you spontaneously create a blast of fire with fraying even though doing so would be creating from nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not after the Errata, I think, which reaffirmed the Practices as what the spell is actually doing, rather than the final effects of the spell. A similar instance, the Thunderbolt (name?) spell, has been corrected to Patterning from Unraveling precisely because of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T23:57:29-07:00","id":1098674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1098670#post1098670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not after the Errata, I think, which reaffirmed the Practices as what the spell is actually doing, rather than the final effects of the spell. A similar instance, the Thunderbolt (name?) spell, has been corrected to Patterning from Unraveling precisely because of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would an example of a fraying force spell which does damage be then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-31-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T00:05:04-07:00","id":1098677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">They can also directly attack targets using the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">energies of the Arcanum: inflicting damage via the chill<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of the grave (Death), psychic overload (Mind), or a blast<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of electricity (Forces).</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>A blast of electricity. Probably coming from something and not just made out of thin air though.<br /> <br /> Your basically using it as a special effect of what the damage comes from. So you could use a blast of fire, light, gravity, sound, heat etc and make it a direct damage spell caused by those effects. (not quite sure what the amount of light needed to cause 3 bashing to people by default is though but for that one attack spell you have it. hah)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-31-2017, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T01:16:59-07:00","id":1098689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1098674#post1098674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would an example of a fraying force spell which does damage be then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Damage as in Health damage, or inflicting wear and tear on the energy itself?<br /> <br /> For the latter, the book has the gravity- and velocity- decreasing options of the Gravitic Supremacy and Velocity Control spells as post-Errata examples.<br /> <br /> For the former, the book has no examples. But I suppose you could Fray away body heat or neural signals from a living body to inflict damage, or at least Tilts/Conditions that represent bodily damage.<br /> <br /> If we're looking for 3-dot spells that inflict damage, without being Fraying, then the book has Call Lightning (Weaving) and Telekinetic Strike (Weaving, used to be Fraying pre-Errata). Telekinetic Strike is a direct damage spell, while Call Lightning does exactly what it says.<br /> <br /> If we go to the realm of manipulating the environment so that the enemy is harmed, then nearly every Forces spell can be used to that end in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T01:33:46-07:00","id":1098691,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Spell Stacking and Derived Traits: <br /> If I use Body Control to directly raise initiative mod, but also use Honing the Form to raise Dexterity, does spell stacking come into effect? Both spells do end up causing an increase in Initiative mod, but it's merely a byproduct of the latter spell, not the direct effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T01:49:10-07:00","id":1098698,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I believe so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T01:54:10-07:00","id":1098699,"title":"","content":"They add to different stats (even though one is derived from the other) so I think it should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:18:39-07:00","id":1099204,"title":"","content":"What Arcanum governs Vitae, and what practice is involved in draining it from a subject? I suspect the same practice that governs Essence draining, but am not 100% sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:26:45-07:00","id":1099207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099204#post1099204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Arcanum governs Vitae, and what practice is involved in draining it from a subject? I suspect the same practice that governs Essence draining, but am not 100% sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure at least in 1e you couldnt touch vitae, create it or whatever. I might be misremebering though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:34:56-07:00","id":1099211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099204#post1099204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Arcanum governs Vitae, and what practice is involved in draining it from a subject? I suspect the same practice that governs Essence draining, but am not 100% sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Life, Death or both. The Practice is probably Weaving similar to Channel Mana instead of Ruling as Channel Essence. Essence is naturally freeflowing in a way that neither Mana nor Vitae is.<br /> <br /> If you're interested I wrote a few spells <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1078825\">here</a> around Vitae manipulation with the assumption that Vitae in blood form only requires Life, but that Vitae in shadow form requires Death as a conjunctional Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:40:04-07:00","id":1099215,"title":"","content":"Tome of mysteries said death 5 and prime 3 for 1e to make actual vitae, it woudnt be lasting and wouldnt sustain ghouls but could feed a vampire..but would need a archmaster to make it lasting.<br /> <br /> Life 5 and Prime 3 for human blood (l3+p3 for animal blood) that sustains a vampire, you need the prime to energise it. It also mentions alot of drawbacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:51:49-07:00","id":1099217,"title":"","content":"In keeping with 2E chopping away unnecessary conjunctionals, our table has treated Vitae as solely under Death.<br /> I actually think just Life would be more accurate, in hindsight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T17:11:47-07:00","id":1099336,"title":"","content":"I've got a theory/house rule/head canon that Vitae is what you get if you manage to perfect blood. It's going to be the central Mystery for a future story arc in my current game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T18:34:15-07:00","id":1099347,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of Vitae as Perfect Blood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T04:11:41-07:00","id":1099439,"title":"","content":"Same here, that actually sounds good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T04:29:36-07:00","id":1099445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099336#post1099336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a theory/house rule/head canon that Vitae is what you get if you manage to perfect blood. It's going to be the central Mystery for a future story arc in my current game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While i loved the concept at first, the more i think about all the specifics the less i like it, One thing in particulars bothers me: perfect blood wouldn't be addictive, would it? How do you explain that property? <br /> <br /> I could see it being addictive in the way that would be exhilarating to have it, or to develope some kind of dependence, but that feeling of warped love... i don't think so? The feeling about it is that vampiric Vitae is something... tainted. I would not have that association with perfected blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T05:27:33-07:00","id":1099459,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't even allow Mage stuff to replicate Vitae, its closest equivalent is Essence, but in Vampire lore it's obviously more mystical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T07:48:43-07:00","id":1099515,"title":"","content":"The way Vampire explains why Vitae is addictive is that as basically distilled life it feels absolutely awesome. Is a rush that nothing else can match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:22:26-07:00","id":1099533,"title":"","content":"While the idea of Vitae as Perfected Blood is tantalizing, I can't help but point out that Mage 2E mentions something like this in the Deep Information part of the Focused Mage Sight section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How the Arcanum used relates to the Mystery \u2014 for example,<br /> <b>using Death Sight to scrutinize a vampire\u2019s ghoul will<br /> reveal Deep Information relating to the undead blood in<br /> the subject\u2019s system</b>, and any powers the ghoul has gained<br /> from it. Using Fate Sight to assess a changeling\u2019s powers<br /> will reveal that they are formed by mystical bargains. </div> </div> </div>So Vitae falls under Death, not Life.<br /> <br /> But then again, this is not mutually exclusive with &quot;Vitae is Perfected Blood.&quot; Maybe normal blood always has symbolically registered both to Life and Death in the Supernal, with this being the state of blood being &quot;corrupted&quot; by Life. That'd explain why blood is always so heavily stigmatized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:23:06-07:00","id":1099534,"title":"","content":"At the very least the reason it doesn't work as Perfected Blood is the fact that Vitae isn't actually blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T11:25:27-07:00","id":1099592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099534#post1099534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least the reason it doesn't work as Perfected Blood is the fact that Vitae isn't actually blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would disagree with that. Corrupted, Tainted if you will but all in all still blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T11:39:44-07:00","id":1099596,"title":"","content":"Except when it's not blood at all. Remember that Strix can steal Vitae through the breath of living people, and store it in their own shadow-stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T12:59:40-07:00","id":1099617,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is perfected blood isn't vitae but it counts as vitae for all relevant purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T13:59:56-07:00","id":1099638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099533#post1099533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the idea of Vitae as Perfected Blood is tantalizing, I can't help but point out that Mage 2E mentions something like this in the Deep Information part of the Focused Mage Sight section:</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, sure, but Matter also mentions using it to destroy Vitae so...ehh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T14:23:31-07:00","id":1099643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099592#post1099592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would disagree with that. Corrupted, Tainted if you will but all in all still blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood is the vampire's medium for Vitae, but Vitae isn't blood. The book points this out, and you can draw that conclusion from the fact that as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> said the Strix can steal Vitae from breath. It's also possible for vampires to feed on ephemeral creatures (Though it's rare since there isn't usually much of an opportunity) and gain Vitae that way and ephemeral beings don't have blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T14:49:53-07:00","id":1099650,"title":"","content":"I know it's probably a little weird, but the vampire book defines vitae using a paint analogy - where blood is the oil, the vessel (person) is the water, and the Vitae is the pigment. You can paint with oil/water, but without pigment it's not going to make very good art. Because of this analogy, I've kind of considered Vitae to be less a 'substance' like essence, and more a 'resonance'. A 'flavor', if you will. It's blood, but corrupted with deathly energies. It's breath, but resonating with shadow. It's essence, but filtered by the undead nature of the vampire itself. It's even flesh, if that flesh is colored by that same resonance.<br /> <br /> Just a thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T05:29:43-07:00","id":1099793,"title":"","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> I am having a real problem with space and the Scrying (Space \u2022\u2022) spell. The spell specifically states that it allows the the mage to view other subjects. It does not say that it allows others to view the subjects of the spell through that window. If you use advanced scale it allows multiple subjects but that is subjects of the spell not subjects allowed to view through that spell. I do not feel that it is allowed to have multiple mages to view an area from a remote location and the entire Cabal cast spells at the subject without impunity.<br /> <br /> What is the answer are they allowed to include other mages in the scrying and let them cast spells at a distance as remote viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T06:11:55-07:00","id":1099800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099793#post1099793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all,<br /> <br /> I am having a real problem with space and the Scrying (Space \u2022\u2022) spell. The spell specifically states that it allows the the mage to view other subjects. It does not say that it allows others to view the subjects of the spell through that window. If you use advanced scale it allows multiple subjects but that is subjects of the spell not subjects allowed to view through that spell. I do not feel that it is allowed to have multiple mages to view an area from a remote location and the entire Cabal cast spells at the subject without impunity.<br /> <br /> What is the answer are they allowed to include other mages in the scrying and let them cast spells at a distance as remote viewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say anything about the &quot;window&quot; being only in the caster's mind or something, so,,, yes?<br /> <br /> When in doubt, just limit the spell's base effect and then add a Reach effect. +1 Reach for &quot;Other mages can now also cast spells in remote viewing&quot; or something like that. Or, instead of Reach, expand the Add Fate option to also selectively allow who can share the Scrying vision with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T09:31:26-07:00","id":1099842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099800#post1099800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't say anything about the &quot;window&quot; being only in the caster's mind or something, so,,, yes?<br /> <br /> When in doubt, just limit the spell's base effect and then add a Reach effect. +1 Reach for &quot;Other mages can now also cast spells in remote viewing&quot; or something like that. Or, instead of Reach, expand the Add Fate option to also selectively allow who can share the Scrying vision with you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By means of this spell, the mage parts the curtain of the<br /> Lie and reveals a distant location to her senses. She creates a<br /> \u201cwindow\u201d that allows <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>her</b></span> to perceive the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>subject</b></span>, much like<br /> a television screen. When she casts the spell, she may choose<br /> whether the spell is one way, or whether people at the location<br /> can see back through the window.<br /> <br /> To increase scale it would increase the subjects viewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T13:17:19-07:00","id":1099896,"title":"","content":"Are Clashes of Wills actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T13:44:42-07:00","id":1099906,"title":"","content":"No. They are a method of resolving conflicting supernatural powers. They happen automatically whenever the situation calls for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T13:56:12-07:00","id":1099908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099906#post1099906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. They are a method of resolving conflicting supernatural powers. They happen automatically whenever the situation calls for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, contested actions are reflexive. Is there some sort of official stance on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:02:19-07:00","id":1099909,"title":"","content":"It's a contested roll of sorts, but it's still not an action. Actions are taken. Clashes happens as a consequence to certain conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T20:06:46-07:00","id":1099994,"title":"","content":"Can Mage groups establish their own Mystery Cults within Orders much in the same way Nameless Orders can be represented by the Mystery Cult merit?<br /> Or perhaps even Legacies also having their own Mystery Cults in addition to the benefits gained from membership.<br /> <br /> I feel that could be quite helpful to further represent the benefits of factionalism within Mage society.<br /> Devotion to a group teaching additional secrets, as well as the benefits of being able to requisition objects and favors from your Order and Consilium.<br /> But only so long as you maintain your allegiance, and do your duty to that group.<br /> <br /> Mostly differentiated from the benefits of Mystery Cult Influence through the benefits directly being targeted towards Awakened matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T04:50:34-07:00","id":1100074,"title":"","content":"The answer is yes as long as the ST allows it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T05:24:48-07:00","id":1100079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099994#post1099994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mage groups establish their own Mystery Cults within Orders much in the same way Nameless Orders can be represented by the Mystery Cult merit?<br /> Or perhaps even Legacies also having their own Mystery Cults in addition to the benefits gained from membership.<br /> <br /> I feel that could be quite helpful to further represent the benefits of factionalism within Mage society.<br /> Devotion to a group teaching additional secrets, as well as the benefits of being able to requisition objects and favors from your Order and Consilium.<br /> But only so long as you maintain your allegiance, and do your duty to that group.<br /> <br /> Mostly differentiated from the benefits of Mystery Cult Influence through the benefits directly being targeted towards Awakened matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only obstacle I foresee is how to build a functional Mystery Cult, rather than mere local interpretations of the larger doctrine, inside what are centuries-old Mystery Cults on their own. Splinter ideologies and heresies are likely to be either quickly destroyed or re-assimilated into the Orders.<br /> <br /> Legacies on the other hand I do see doubling as Mystery Cults, instead of having Mystery Cults within them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T05:40:20-07:00","id":1100083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100079#post1100079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splinter ideologies and heresies are likely to be either quickly destroyed or re-assimilated into the Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Order book has a section on factions and cults. Lots of them are pretty old too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T05:44:05-07:00","id":1100084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100083#post1100083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Order book has a section on factions and cults. Lots of them are pretty old too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1E books, right? Dang, I knew should've gotten them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, do they have enough &quot;oomph&quot; to be a Mystery Cult, so to speak, and not just factions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T06:06:37-07:00","id":1100092,"title":"","content":"This is hopefully a simple question, and I can't seem to find it anywhere with my google searching:<br /> <br /> Can an Artifact have set spell factors like Imbued Items? Meaning an Artifact casts a 3rd Dot Death Spell with 5 Potency and Duration of 1 Day.<br /> <br /> So, in this instant it would be a 3rd Dot Spell cast with a Death Arcana of 5 with a Reach spent to make it Advanced Duration and perhaps another for Sensory Range and a final for Instant Casting. I think this would be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Edit: To clarify my meaning. 06-04-2017, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T06:45:37-07:00","id":1100101,"title":"","content":"The merit isnt clear tbh. I think a 3rd dot spell becomes a 3 point artifact, theres no rules as written to upgrade it to a 5 dot effect but only be a 3rd dot spell. I mean it doesnt even mention a dice pool for using it, is it the same as a imbued item?? Do you not even roll to activate it? Who knows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T07:16:25-07:00","id":1100110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100092#post1100092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is hopefully a simple question, and I can't seem to find it anywhere with my google searching:<br /> <br /> Can an Artifact have set spell factors like Imbued Items? Meaning an Artifact casts a 3rd Dot Death Spell with 5 Potency and Duration of 1 Day.<br /> <br /> So, in this instant it would be a 3rd Dot Spell cast with a Death Arcana of 5 with a Reach spent to make it Advanced Duration and perhaps another for Sensory Range and a final for Instant Casting. I think this would be possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The item can store Mana equal to twice the dot rating. The<br /> item\u2019s effective Gnosis is equal to half the dot rating, rounded up.<br /> An owner can access and refill the item\u2019s Mana as if it were her<br /> own, or can use it to fuel the Artifact\u2019s abilities. The Artifact can<br /> also use its Mana as part of its own activation. <b>The Artifact has<br /> effective Arcana equal to the highest Arcanum used in its various<br /> effects</b>. <b>Artifacts cannot Reach beyond the \u201cfree\u201d Reach for their<br /> Arcana ratings on their own.</b> If an Artifact risks Paradox, the user<br /> can spend Mana to mitigate Paradox (in any combination of her<br /> own or the Artifact\u2019s Mana pool, up to her Gnosis-derived limits)<br /> and may choose to contain the Paradox herself. Otherwise, the<br /> Artifact automatically releases it.<br /> <br /> I believe it is answered in the highlighted text above. The reach is fluid and can be assigned on the fly. The Arcana level of the effect is the level of the highest Arcana used in the various effects. So in the example listed the Potency would be 3 and if there was enough reach you could make it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T07:29:40-07:00","id":1100111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100110#post1100110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The Artifact has effective Arcana equal to the highest Arcanum used in its various effects</b>. <b>Artifacts cannot Reach beyond the \u201cfree\u201d Reach for their Arcana ratings on their own.</b><br /> <br /> I believe it is answered in the highlighted text above. The reach is fluid and can be assigned on the fly. The Arcana level of the effect is the level of the highest Arcana used in the various effects. So in the example listed the Potency would be 3 and if there was enough reach you could make it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to indicate you could use Death 5 to cast a Death 3 spell and gain the Reach from having used Death 5, thus the Potency if the Primary Factor was Potency should be 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Edit: Slight adjustment of words being combined horribly, need a Space Master to correct. 06-04-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T08:00:19-07:00","id":1100124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100111#post1100111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems to indicate you could use Death 5 to cast a Death 3 spell and gain the Reach from having used Death 5, thus the Potency if the Primary Factor was Potency should be 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the Artifact had two effects built into it in the first place - a Death 5 spell to give it the Arcanum rating, and a Death 3 spell that benefits from that rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T08:14:42-07:00","id":1100136,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I shall proceed in that fashion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T09:15:02-07:00","id":1100154,"title":"","content":"The only problem i have with it is that say your artifact has a ruling effect, that is a 2 dot practice. You cant just up it to death 5 as its practices are making and unmaking not ruling.<br /> <br /> An artifact of psychic domination would have cost of 3 with a effective gnosis of 2 ending up with a total dicepool to use of 4? (gnosis 2 + mind 2) and 1 free reach, potency of 2 and duration of 1 turn and contains 6 mana. Not exactly mind blowingly awesome but then if you dont have mind as an arcanum and/or are only gnosis 1 its pretty good?? Worth 3 merit points or 5 consil/order stats to requisition it perm? Probably not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T10:41:41-07:00","id":1100176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100154#post1100154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem i have with it is that say your artifact has a ruling effect, that is a 2 dot practice. You cant just up it to death 5 as its practices are making and unmaking not ruling.<br /> <br /> An artifact of psychic domination would have cost of 3 with a effective gnosis of 2 ending up with a total dicepool to use of 4? (gnosis 2 + mind 2) and 1 free reach, potency of 2 and duration of 1 turn and contains 6 mana. Not exactly mind blowingly awesome but then if you dont have mind as an arcanum and/or are only gnosis 1 its pretty good?? Worth 3 merit points or 5 consil/order stats to requisition it perm? Probably not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If the users Gnosis or Arcanum is higher than the artifacts then you can use the Casters instead of the Artifacts. The artifact that you mentioned is not mind blowing but nothing to just dismiss off hand either. The thing that an artifact doesn't allow, at least from what I can see is the use of Yantras to add to the dice pool.<br /> <br /> <b>If an owner accesses the Artifact\u2019s effects, she may use her own<br /> Gnosis and Arcana, the Artifact\u2019s, or any combination thereof.</b><br /> Every Artifact is also a Path tool Yantra worth +1 dice for mages<br /> of the Path of the Artifacts\u2019 highest Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T15:29:58-07:00","id":1100229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100084#post1100084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1E books, right? Dang, I knew should've gotten them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. I admit it's kinda obnoxious when the line is this long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, do they have enough &quot;oomph&quot; to be a Mystery Cult, so to speak, and not just factions? </div> </div> </div>I'd say so. It's kinda a bit of an issue with the books that there aren't really any rules. The Diamond Books divide the Orders into Factions which are broad ideologies/specialisations but within those there are groups sometimes referred to as 'cults' (the style is slightly inconsistent across the books). Those are essentially semi-secret societies within the Orders and they're definitely proper organisations which would offer concrete benefits in the manner of the Mystery Cult Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:56:04-07:00","id":1100395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1099896#post1099896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Clashes of Wills actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breathing is a reflexive action and so is CoW but this changes very little in Mage since spells can defend themselves even when the caster is unconscious.<br /> <br /> Edit: I could see a Time spell that changes reflexive actions into instant ones. And now you need to choose between breathing and participating in a CoW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T04:56:37-07:00","id":1100403,"title":"","content":"I still disagree that CoWs are actions.<br /> First of all it's not even your character who does it, but the power you've already used an action (or several if you incorporated more than one yantra) to activate.<br /> Secondly, you never choose to take a CoW the way you choose to take actions. You don't choose to resist contested powers either, but if you think in such terms everyone involved in a CoW would be resisting since everyone automatically enters the CoW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T05:10:25-07:00","id":1100407,"title":"","content":"Its a roll, yes, and you can choose to fail any roll. You can also add willpower to this roll which indicates that it is a conscious action.<br /> While entering the state of CoW is automatic the roll itself is an action, you can either add WP or fail it - you couldn't do it otherwise.<br /> Edit: Very much like in the grapple. Both participants roll at once and text doesn't really gives you option to not roll. You can however still choose to fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 06-05-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:19:00-07:00","id":1100421,"title":"","content":"If your soul is stolen do you immediately lose the ability to use legacy attainments?<br /> It seems the attainments are issued from the soul, so wouldn't the lack thereof disable usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:19:35-07:00","id":1100438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100421#post1100421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your soul is stolen do you immediately lose the ability to use legacy attainments?<br /> It seems the attainments are issued from the soul, so wouldn't the lack thereof disable usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments aren't effected at all unless your Gnosis drops low enough to cause you to lose access to the attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:29:59-07:00","id":1100639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100407#post1100407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can choose to fail any roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source? This breaks numerous things across multiple gamelines. See the current discussion in Werewolf re: Harmony Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T02:28:10-07:00","id":1100755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100639#post1100639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source? This breaks numerous things across multiple gamelines. See the current discussion in Werewolf re: Harmony Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now when you asked I checked in a book and it turns out I was wrong, you can only change failure into dramatic failure by RAW. Sorry for that. However, I think that a player should have such an option - and don't abuse it, like with everything else. I can imagine that it can be especially troublesome in Harmony rolls so I'll go read the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T02:34:50-07:00","id":1100756,"title":"","content":"Except in atypical cases like Harmony, allowing a player to choose to fail a roll is hardly about to be game breaking. It's a common house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T02:45:12-07:00","id":1100757,"title":"","content":"But it was rooted in my games for so long that I forgot it's a house rule. It's good to discern it, so thank you for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T02:49:06-07:00","id":1100758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100756#post1100756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except in atypical cases like Harmony, allowing a player to choose to fail a roll is hardly about to be game breaking. It's a common house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I tend to allow players to fail conscious actions, but not unconscious ones, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:08:52-07:00","id":1100794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100756#post1100756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except in atypical cases like Harmony, allowing a player to choose to fail a roll is hardly about to be game breaking. It's a common house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also Paradox. Failing Paradox means you don't have any Paradox effects. Hell, if you want then you can take a Dramatic Failure and not only do you not get any Paradox effect, you get a Willpower back, and of course you get your Beat for taking a Dramatic Failure. Choosing to fail rolls is basically giving them a free beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:19:21-07:00","id":1100798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100794#post1100794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also Paradox. Failing Paradox means you don't have any Paradox effects. Hell, if you want then you can take a Dramatic Failure and not only do you not get any Paradox effect, you get a Willpower back, and of course you get your Beat for taking a Dramatic Failure. Choosing to fail rolls is basically giving them a free beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is explicitly rolled by the ST though, so it's not the player's roll to fail even if you allow that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:20:01-07:00","id":1100800,"title":"","content":"I think technically the storyteller rolls for paradox though. And they can totally choose to fail any roll they like.<br /> <br /> Ninja'd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:36:10-07:00","id":1100806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100794#post1100794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also Paradox. Failing Paradox means you don't have any Paradox effects. Hell, if you want then you can take a Dramatic Failure and not only do you not get any Paradox effect, you get a Willpower back, and of course you get your Beat for taking a Dramatic Failure. Choosing to fail rolls is basically giving them a free beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others mentioned Paradox isn't something the player rolls.<br /> <br /> As for downgrading failures to exceptional failures for Beats, I don't see a problem with it. They're still setting themselves up for failure in the moment. Exceptional failure even. It's just a house rule though, you could easily make another: You're only allowed to downgrade a failure to an exceptional failure if you actually made a roll and failed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:55:13-07:00","id":1100810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100806#post1100806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As others mentioned Paradox isn't something the player rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're talking about is an out of character concept to begin with. It isn't a matter of Merlin not wanting to kill his friend so he purposely misses the killshot. It's Merlin's player just wanting to fail for meta-gains. Why can't he fail his Paradox roll, too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">s for downgrading failures to exceptional failures for Beats, I don't see a problem with it. They're still setting themselves up for failure in the moment. Exceptional failure even. It's just a house rule though, you could easily make another: You're only allowed to downgrade a failure to an exceptional failure if you actually made a roll and failed it.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Obviously I wouldn't use the first house rule to begin with. There's a difference in circumstance. As people have already pointed out in the various 'gaming the system' threads you can just choose to take a Dramatic Failure while you're prepping at home, eliminating any need for it to occur in the field where 'Dramatic' means something.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:09:57-07:00","id":1100816,"title":"","content":"Paradox failing is a case when you win actually and that doesn't survive when you apply a little reason to it. You can't decide to win - unless ST decides that too. But also if the group thinks that failure has no sense in here, don't let it happen. The goal of the game is, ironically, to tell the story, no to win per se. Good ST knows the rules and how to apply them, a great one knows when to ignore them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:19:10-07:00","id":1100818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100816#post1100816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox failing is a case when you win actually and that doesn't survive when you apply a little reason to it. You can't decide to win - unless ST decides that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what your whole rule is about. Unless people are randomly deciding to fail for no reason, they're failing because it benefits them, like in the case of Harmony or gaining Beats in an environment where Dramatic Failures are safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But also if the group thinks that failure has no sense in here, don't let it happen. The goal of the game is, ironically, to tell the story, no to win per se. Good ST knows the rules and how to apply them, a great one knows when to ignore them. </div> </div> </div>Yay, snark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:29:56-07:00","id":1100822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100810#post1100810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't he fail his Paradox roll, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>For same reason he can't fail another NPCs roll. <br /> <br /> It's not his roll to make - it's the Storyteller's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:34:50-07:00","id":1100824,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to say that you need to use your best judgement to make the game better. Failing Wisdom? Super cool, get a beat, condition and become more interesting character with less benefits on paradox control and some social repercussions. Failing Harmony? Not cool, it was meant to give you as much bonuses as disadvantages, to strengthen the woofs internal struggle aspect - failing means wining. Unless... The character doesn't want it and you make an interesting story out of it. It depends on the group, really.<br /> I don't allow to change failures into dramatic ones when there is nothing at stake. It wouldn't be very dramatic, imho. Most likely there wouldn't be any roll involved to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:02:31-07:00","id":1100838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100810#post1100810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you're talking about is an out of character concept to begin with. It isn't a matter of Merlin not wanting to kill his friend so he purposely misses the killshot. It's Merlin's player just wanting to fail for meta-gains. Why can't he fail his Paradox roll, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the player doesn't roll for Paradox, as I've already said. I don't know why you're finding that hard to understand, and I don't understand why you're asking me to repeat myself.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not about gaming the system if it's a rule that's applied judiciously. You seem to be discounting the ability of the ST or players to use good sense. Which is a neat bit of condescension I guess, go you.<br /> <br /> Edit: Furthermore it seems amazing to me that I've managed to use this house rule for my entire gaming career without any problem, and you have no experience with it at all, but managed to immediately identify how it's a bad rule. Truly, I wish I had your levels of insight. I could have saved myself a lot of theoretical trouble that's never actually happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-06-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T09:54:25-07:00","id":1100868,"title":"","content":"Alright, sorry about the tone in that last post. I don't like it when answers are given to questions and then promptly ignored so the same question can be asked all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T10:27:37-07:00","id":1100879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100838#post1100838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the player doesn't roll for Paradox, as I've already said. I don't know why you're finding that hard to understand, and I don't understand why you're asking me to repeat myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't ask you to repeat yourself, I pointed out the logical flaw in your argument. It's an out of character decision, it shouldn't matter whether the storyteller rolls it or not. If you want to use Moinen's approach, it's the groups decision, or that of the 'great' ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's not about gaming the system if it's a rule that's applied judiciously. You seem to be discounting the ability of the ST or players to use good sense. Which is a neat bit of condescension I guess, go you.<br /> <br /> Edit: Furthermore it seems amazing to me that I've managed to use this house rule for my entire gaming career without any problem, and you have no experience with it at all, but managed to immediately identify how it's a bad rule. Truly, I wish I had your levels of insight. I could have saved myself a lot of theoretical trouble that's never actually happened. </div> </div> </div>Hi pot, I guess that makes me kettle. Do you think it mattered as much earlier in your gaming career, or just using first edition, when failures were just failures but now using them as a way to grow is a part of the game.<br /> <br /> No need to apologize, your tone's been the same for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:33:22-07:00","id":1100895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100879#post1100879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an out of character decision, it shouldn't matter whether the storyteller rolls it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2022 You don't get to make decisions about rolls that aren't yours.<br /> \u2022 A Paradox roll is no more yours than the roll for another player's action is yours, or an NPC's is yours.<br /> <br /> You keep saying that it is because it's &quot;meta-game&quot; or &quot;out of character&quot; but nothing about either of those concepts actually support the argument that you get to make decisions about rolls that aren't yours (as in, the Player's, not the Character's)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-06-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:35:38-07:00","id":1100896,"title":"","content":"Thematically I prefer ST rolling Paradox. The Abyss being the NPC, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:46:26-07:00","id":1100898,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Not liking the attitude guys. Don't care who started it, if I have to close the thread because it continues suspensions will be in order. Please don't force my hand.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T12:01:44-07:00","id":1100909,"title":"","content":"I've just came from the ban period myself and I know that I am forbidden by rules to answer you when you are red but I need to say that maybe you <i>should </i>care who started and whats being said instead of closing threads and threatening. I know that with that post I'm almost daring you to ban me but what you do, your tone especially, looks like an abuse.<br /> Edit: This topic is a tremendous help for both new and old players. Try to do the right things.<br /> Edit2: Sorry for that post. I wasn't at my best yesterday but I will gladly talk about it in pm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 06-07-2017, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T12:05:17-07:00","id":1100911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1100879#post1100879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't ask you to repeat yourself, I pointed out the logical flaw in your argument. It's an out of character decision, it shouldn't matter whether the storyteller rolls it or not. If you want to use Moinen's approach, it's the groups decision, or that of the 'great' ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>You used a question with no discernible difference from an earlier question after that earlier question had already been answered. If that's not begging for repetition then I don't know what is.<br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;logical flaw&quot; you seem to think you've discovered is in fact not, or at least I don't see how it is. The player can opt to fail a roll != the ST opts to fail rolls in a player's favor. I mean, okay, yes they could, but why would they? If they did, why does that matter?<br /> <br /> From my experience with this rule it's very rarely used. Okay, yes you can gain a Beat if you go for an Exceptional Failure, but that means you failed, badly. There are in story consequences for that, and being successful or trying to shoot for an Exceptional Success is a stronger incentive than getting Beats via failure (Especially when casting spells where Exceptional Success =Beats). If you have the secondary rule I suggested of not allowing a player to convert an opted failure into an Exceptional Failure then use of the original rule is further disincentived. Overall, the option to auto-fail yourself has always been there, and it's never been a problem.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care if you like it or not, it's a house rule. Heck, when I joined the conversation I was just noting that it's a common house rule so it's understandable that Moinen may have forgotten it's just a house rule. I wasn't arguing for or against it, and I'm still not. I'm attempting to clear up your misconceptions about it.<br /> <br /> What ticks me off is that you jumped to a wrong conclusion about how I implement a rule that you're not familiar with and then have persisted in being wrong by not actually paying attention to the replies you're getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-06-2017, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T05:10:52-07:00","id":1101177,"title":"","content":"Hi! A situation came up during my biweekly game, and I'd like your opinion in the matter:<br /> <br /> One of my players tried to use Memory Hole (Mind 2) on a Sleeper with the intent that he would forget a compromising scene that happened a minute before. The problem is, the spell doesn't list any Withstand trait, yet the intent was clearly to act against the target's will. I ruled it at the moment that he would need an extra Reach and face the target's Resolve as the Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Later on, I read again the spells section and I realized that there were a lot of spells without any listed Withstand rating that could be used against a target, while the intent in most cases is to provide some sort of advantage to the target of the spell instead. For example, some Veiling spells don't list any Withstand rating, yet they could be used against a target as a special kind of curse, like Supress Life, or Cloak Nimbus. Do you think I made the right call? Should I consider unintended uses of the spell as creative thaumaturgy (and therefore as a completely different spell? Was the extra Reach a bit too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T05:26:09-07:00","id":1101178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101177#post1101177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! A situation came up during my biweekly game, and I'd like your opinion in the matter:<br /> <br /> One of my players tried to use Memory Hole (Mind 2) on a Sleeper with the intent that he would forget a compromising scene that happened a minute before. The problem is, the spell doesn't list any Withstand trait, yet the intent was clearly to act against the target's will. I ruled it at the moment that he would need an extra Reach and face the target's Resolve as the Withstand rating.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you made a good call.<br /> However in future I wouldn't bother adding an additional Reach requirement.<br /> <br /> Generally I reserve that for elements that go &quot;that little bit extra&quot; in a spell.<br /> So for example in that situation Reach might also convince him not to think about subjects in the general mental &quot;area&quot; of the hidden sections.<br /> Or he would come up with garbled and half-formed explanations for what he can't remember, so he doesn't simply realise that his memory has been tampered with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T05:56:38-07:00","id":1101187,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you're making them go up against Withstand (That was the right call btw) I wouldn't add an extra cost of a Reach unless you're allowing the spell to do more than what it normally does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T09:06:28-07:00","id":1101258,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm still not clear on: If you want to use your dedicated tool to lower Paradox by -2 and as a +1 Path tool do you need to use two Yantra slots or just one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T09:08:13-07:00","id":1101260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101258#post1101258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm still not clear on: If you want to use your dedicated tool to lower Paradox by -2 and as a +1 Path tool do you need to use two Yantra slots or just one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just one. Even if your Dedicated Tool doesn't apply for the +1 you can still use it in a Yantra slot for the -2 to Paradox as well.<br /> <br /> Basically, a Dedicated Tool always takes only one slot, but sometimes you only get one benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T14:34:28-07:00","id":1101371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101177#post1101177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! A situation came up during my biweekly game, and I'd like your opinion in the matter:<br /> <br /> One of my players tried to use Memory Hole (Mind 2) on a Sleeper with the intent that he would forget a compromising scene that happened a minute before. The problem is, the spell doesn't list any Withstand trait, yet the intent was clearly to act against the target's will. I ruled it at the moment that he would need an extra Reach and face the target's Resolve as the Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Later on, I read again the spells section and I realized that there were a lot of spells without any listed Withstand rating that could be used against a target, while the intent in most cases is to provide some sort of advantage to the target of the spell instead. For example, some Veiling spells don't list any Withstand rating, yet they could be used against a target as a special kind of curse, like Supress Life, or Cloak Nimbus. Do you think I made the right call? Should I consider unintended uses of the spell as creative thaumaturgy (and therefore as a completely different spell? Was the extra Reach a bit too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>You made the right call with the withstand, but like the others said the reach wasn't needed. I often use spells that were not intended intended as an attack and as both a Player and an ST I expect/enforce a withstand. As an example using Shadow Crafting (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) offensively to encase a victim in solid skin tight shadows, &quot;Called the Han Solo&quot; so a withstand is completely called for. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T14:41:35-07:00","id":1101375,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go against the grain here and say that adding a Withstand trait to a spell used 100% as described in the book, where it does <i>not</i> include a Withstand, isn't really a great call. When using spells in a creative way that clearly bypasses the assumptions that were made when it was written, I can <i>kind of</i> see doing this, but this seems like a clear cut use of the spell for exactly what it was meant to do.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm missing something about this situation, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T14:58:39-07:00","id":1101379,"title":"","content":"Actually, why does Memory Hole not have a Withstand at all? The primary use to me seems to be something that would be against the targets will. If you are using it on a friendly, they can choose not to Withstand and that would be the edge case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T15:06:33-07:00","id":1101382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101379#post1101379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, why does Memory Hole not have a Withstand at all? The primary use to me seems to be something that would be against the targets will. If you are using it on a friendly, they can choose not to Withstand and that would be the edge case.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good question.<br /> <br /> It seems to fit the type of spell that should have a Withstand. Perhaps the Author was of the impression that being particularly resolved or well-composed wouldn't help you avoid having your memories compartmentalized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T15:17:36-07:00","id":1101385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101379#post1101379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, why does Memory Hole not have a Withstand at all? The primary use to me seems to be something that would be against the targets will. If you are using it on a friendly, they can choose not to Withstand and that would be the edge case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me a case of RAI vs RAW. I too agree that the extra Reach was uncalled for. But I will improvise Withstand ratings for a spell if there's an active manipulation of the target AND it follows the internal logic of the effect. So I'd demand a Resolve Withstand against Memory Hole again, but if the mage turns the target's shirt in solid steel to immobilize him I'll leave it as is, since it would be following the fiction in all respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T16:49:42-07:00","id":1101407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101385#post1101385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me a case of RAI vs RAW. I too agree that the extra Reach was uncalled for. But I will improvise Withstand ratings for a spell if there's an active manipulation of the target AND it follows the internal logic of the effect. So I'd demand a Resolve Withstand against Memory Hole again, but if the mage turns the target's shirt in solid steel to immobilize him I'll leave it as is, since it would be following the fiction in all respects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont worry about suppress life not having a withstand either, its not like it puts the person into a deathlike coma or anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:11:16-07:00","id":1101415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101382#post1101382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good question.<br /> <br /> It seems to fit the type of spell that should have a Withstand. Perhaps the Author was of the impression that being particularly resolved or well-composed wouldn't help you avoid having your memories compartmentalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell's 1e version was self-targeted, much like Suppress Own Life. An appropriate Withstand rating can be assumed necessary if you're targeting someone else with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:15:30-07:00","id":1101416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101407#post1101407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont worry about suppress life not having a withstand either, its not like it puts the person into a deathlike coma or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:16:19-07:00","id":1101417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101407#post1101407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dont worry about suppress life not having a withstand either, its not like it puts the person into a deathlike coma or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't though, it's a Veiling spell that suppresses life signs. It doesn't suppress life.<br /> You appear like a corpse, a walking, talking, corpse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:28:01-07:00","id":1101422,"title":"","content":"To me it seems the lack of Withstand for Memory Hole is just an oversight (possibly due to the 1E version being self-targeting, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> pointed out).<br /> Every spell that is used to alter a person against their will should be Withstood even if the Withstand rating isn't written in the spell description for the published spells. The only exception is purely damage dealing spells with the rationale that they're &quot;Withstood&quot; by Health. Of course, that only applies to spells directly targeting people and other entities. The solid steel shirt example above has no Withstand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:35:16-07:00","id":1101424,"title":"","content":"if a legacy attainment causes a clash of wills, lets say for instance it mimics the Mental Shield spell, does the attainment user actually bother rolling the CoW or do they just automatically acquire successes equal to the highest prerequisite arcana for the attainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:02:50-07:00","id":1101430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101417#post1101417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't though, it's a Veiling spell that suppresses life signs. It doesn't suppress life.<br /> You appear like a corpse, a walking, talking, corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell's 1e counterparts specify a trigger necessary to wake the subject prior to the end of the Duration and that while the spell is active the subject experiences nothing. &quot;Dead for all intents and purposes&quot; isn't &quot;medically dead but still moving.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's Withstood by Composure, if 1e's S.O.L. resistance roll is any indication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:07:19-07:00","id":1101433,"title":"","content":"could a mage use a knowing death spell to find out what a would be necessary for a ghost to &quot;resolve&quot; its anchor/unfinished business?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:12:57-07:00","id":1101437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101430#post1101430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell's 1e counterparts specify a trigger necessary to wake the subject prior to the end of the Duration and that while the spell is active the subject experiences nothing. &amp;quot;Dead for all intents and purposes&amp;quot; isn't &amp;quot;medically dead but still moving.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It's Withstood by Composure, if 1e's S.O.L. resistance roll is any indication.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's not what this spell says.<br /> It says the target appears for all intents and purposes add if she is dead.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to interpret that as a compete biological lockdown when that is not implied by the practice or text, and primarily based on a 1e spell.<br /> Especially when it can instead be read much more aptly as something which veils you into appearing dead, without affecting your physiology in any way.<br /> I really don't see how a veil application to make you seem dead could restrict your own capacity.<br /> That's affecting the innate physiological factors of the subject.<br /> I could see that at Patterning perhaps, but not veiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:14:44-07:00","id":1101438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101433#post1101433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could a mage use a knowing death spell to find out what a would be necessary for a ghost to &quot;resolve&quot; its anchor/unfinished business?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it, Withstood by Rank. Much like Know Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T20:44:54-07:00","id":1101484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101437#post1101437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that's not what this spell says.</div> </div> </div> </div>This spell says that the mage can <i>suppress the subject's life signs</i>, a thing which here means you don't breathe, have a heartbeat, or evince brainwave activity, among other things.<br /> <br /> Not that you don't <i>appear to have</i> those things, that you <i>do not possess those qualities for the duration of the spell</i>.<br /> <br /> People aren't equipped to function through that and its being a raw illusion takes much of the utility out of it \u2014 this is the spell to use when you don't have the luxury of near-Mastery of an Arcanum to deal with air supply but still need someone to be buried alive under six feet of concrete or at the bottom of a lake for retrieval at an indefinite later time, not for when you want to play the world's weirdest game of red-light-green-light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T21:02:41-07:00","id":1101487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101484#post1101484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell says that the mage can <i>suppress the subject's life signs</i>, a thing which here means you don't breathe, have a heartbeat, or evince brainwave activity, among other things.<br /> <br /> Not that you don't <i>appear to have</i> those things, that you <i>do not possess those qualities for the duration of the spell</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the very same sentence the text explicitly says that &quot;suppress lifesigns&quot; does in fact mean that they appear to be absent.<br /> <br /> &quot;The mage can suppress the subject\u2019s life signs; the subject <br /> appears for all intents and purposes as though she is dead. All <br /> physical symptoms of death appear to set in and the soul appears <br /> absent from the body to magical senses.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's easy to interpret &quot;suppress lifesigns&quot; as actually stopping breathing, heartbeats, and brain activity when you completely ignore the second half of the sentence that explains that such things only appear to have stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T21:36:40-07:00","id":1101493,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Suppress Life is a Veiling spell,<br /> which are meant to conceal things.<br /> Not really meant to sever or harm things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T22:15:45-07:00","id":1101497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101487#post1101487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the very same sentence the text explicitly says that &quot;suppress lifesigns&quot; does in fact mean that they appear to be absent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the only absolutely necessary operating distinction between appearing to be dead and being dead is that being actually dead doesn't go away when the spell ends, this does nothing to negate my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's easy to interpret &quot;suppress lifesigns&quot; as actually stopping breathing, heartbeats, and brain activity when you completely ignore the second half of the sentence that explains that such things only appear to have stopped. </div> </div> </div>You've stuck an &quot;only&quot; in there that doesn't exist in the text and the physical symptoms of death include the onset of rigor mortis et al. The 1e spell highlighted this and also provided the basis for the Reach effect allowing you to reflexively use the spell to fake the subject's death via existing circumstances. This is the power you use for plunging subjects into a deathlike sleep or making someone only-mostly-dead or otherwise turning the target indistinguishable from a corpse, and that doesn't work terribly well when you &quot;only&quot; <i>seem like</i> you don't need to breathe anymore.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that there's a Death Veiling spell that makes you simply register as dead to most methods of detection while still retaining mobility, much as I don't doubt there's a Ruling spell in the Arcanum that duplicates some aspects of Body Control, but everything about this spell short of a very technical reading of a single verb suggests Suppress Life is not that spell without incorporating a custom Reach effect into the mix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101493#post1101493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that Suppress Life is a Veiling spell,<br /> which are meant to conceal things.<br /> Not really meant to sever or harm things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Veil Sympathies has a tangible impact on a subject's sympathetic ties despite &quot;only&quot; concealing them. Precedent exists.<br /> <br /> Nobody has been talking about severance or harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T01:24:16-07:00","id":1101526,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Dave's already clarified this one, yes in 1e Suppress Life was an effective takedown spell, but in 2e it isn't. The spell is an illusion and doesn't render the target immobile or unconscious.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the effects of Veil Sympathy on the actual sympathetic ties are also purely cosmetic. The relationships of the subject of the spell aren't actually affected, they just appear to be because that's what Veiling does. The best way to enforce the illusion is to play it straight though, so that could end up degrading those connections over time as you act like you don't have the connections you're trying to hide. That's got nothing to do with the spell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-08-2017, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T04:23:58-07:00","id":1101558,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> can you provide a source? <s>Because the author of that section has also 'clarified' that it does function as a takedown:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917087-what-s-the-purpose-of-advanced-potency-in-instant-spells?p=917355#post917355\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...355#post917355</a></s>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Misattribution 06-08-2017, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T04:53:38-07:00","id":1101566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101558#post1101558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> can you provide a source? Because the author of that section has also 'clarified' that it does function as a takedown:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917087-what-s-the-purpose-of-advanced-potency-in-instant-spells?p=917355#post917355\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...355#post917355</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the same thread, Eric later appears to acknowledge that his interpretation of the spell is really his group's houserule. This is not uncommon for Eric as demonstrated by earlier discussion of his use of Fate effects.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the effect was already clarified by Dave in his &quot;official&quot; errata!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9UUZ4UjZJdEhIM2c/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9UUZ4UjZJdEhIM2c/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9UUZ4UjZJdEhIM2c/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9UUZ4UjZJdEhIM2c/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T04:56:48-07:00","id":1101567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101558#post1101558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> can you provide a source? Because the author of that section has also 'clarified' that it does function as a takedown:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917087-what-s-the-purpose-of-advanced-potency-in-instant-spells?p=917355#post917355\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...355#post917355</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You would have a point, if Eric had actually written Death. But he didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T04:58:01-07:00","id":1101568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101416#post1101416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obv my tone didnt come over, i was agreeing it doesnt work as a takedown.<br /> <br /> The fact the *edit* non author says it does without a withstand obv means he is is mistaken. It would make it stupidly OP and doesnt fit with what a veiling spell actually does. Causing somebody to fall over &quot;fakedead&quot; via veiling? Pull the other one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-08-2017, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:04:00-07:00","id":1101570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101567#post1101567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would have a point, if Eric had actually written Death. But he didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. And I now see the change in the errata doc is more clear than what actually made it into the errata'd PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:09:03-07:00","id":1101574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101497#post1101497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no doubt that there's a Death Veiling spell that makes you simply register as dead to most methods of detection while still retaining mobility, much as I don't doubt there's a Ruling spell in the Arcanum that duplicates some aspects of Body Control, but everything about this spell short of a very technical reading of a single verb suggests Suppress Life is not that spell without incorporating a custom Reach effect into the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the single verb that appears three times in the spell's two sentence description. From my perspective &quot;deathlike coma&quot; is the technical reading; not the natural one. Especially since almost all powers begin with a wide description and then specifies what they actually do. But I can't make you read the spell the way I do so I'll drop the subject now. At least the intended reading has been clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:09:43-07:00","id":1101575,"title":"","content":"What level would the effect of turning somebody into a &quot;corpse&quot; be now then? Weaving maybe? Is a corpse completely different from a living body or is it a just body without life? I't be patterning then if corpses are completely different? It'd obv be withstood by something but if your wanting to capture people without harm then it'd still be useful to be able to drop them where they stand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:22:34-07:00","id":1101578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101575#post1101575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level would the effect of turning somebody into a &quot;corpse&quot; be now then? Weaving maybe? Is a corpse completely different from a living body or is it a just body without life? I't be patterning then if corpses are completely different? It'd obv be withstood by something but if your wanting to capture people without harm then it'd still be useful to be able to drop them where they stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following the guidelines presented for other transformations, you could do it with Life 4 + Death 4.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, shift them into Death-Twilight with Death 3, turning them into Death-Attuned Ephemera, then pattern that from Ephemera to a corpse with Death 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:46:28-07:00","id":1101587,"title":"","content":"As per Shadow Form, it would just be Death 4, not Death 4 +Life 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:47:24-07:00","id":1101588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101578#post1101578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following the guidelines presented for other transformations, you could do it with Life 4 + Death 4.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, shift them into Death-Twilight with Death 3, turning them into Death-Attuned Ephemera, then pattern that from Ephemera to a corpse with Death 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow flesh has long been thought of as a mistake because it doesnt need any Life to turn subjects into shadows. Personally i think needing Life 4 is to high, maybe Life 2 in a similar way that adding X 2 to a ban lets you ban/allow all things under X's arcanas purview. Obv transubstantiation requires life 4 to turn matter into living things so is at the other end, shapechange needs matter 4to change your stuff along with you so one also assumes you woul need matter 4 to turn living things to stone.<br /> <br /> There are no other examples of multi arcana transformation things, like a living person into a fire elemental etc? Perhaps evidence that things changed when 2e tried to remove alot of conjunctional needs?<br /> <br /> Would like more examples of transforming spells to see if shadow flesh is just an anomaly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:51:24-07:00","id":1101592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101588#post1101588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no other examples of multi arcana transformation things, like a living person into a fire elemental etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Referenced in Practices as requiring Life 4 + Forces 4, and is actually the guideline I was referring to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A spell that transforms the target into something that falls within the Purview of another Arcanum, like transforming into a living pillar of fire (Life and Forces), requires a mage to know the Practice of Patterning for the destination Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>However, on a closer reading, it references Life &amp; Forces, but it only says you need Patterning for the <i>destination</i> Arcanum, not both. Not sure what the RAI is here, but I think it's supposed to require both, Shadow Flesh notwithstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-08-2017, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:25:48-07:00","id":1101606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101592#post1101592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Referenced in Practices as requiring Life 4 + Forces 4, and is actually the guideline I was referring to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> However, on a closer reading, it references Life &amp; Forces, but it only says you need Patterning for the <i>destination</i> Arcanum, not both. Not sure what the RAI is here, but I think it's supposed to require both, Shadow Flesh notwithstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally see only requiring the destination Arcanum, Transubstantiation needs Life 4 because living thing is the &quot;destination/final form&quot;. Turning somebody into stone only needs Matter 4. It seems cleaner to me somehow but then its abit confusing that shapechange needs added matter 4 to turn your things along with you but shadow flesh doesnt though. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:28:14-07:00","id":1101608,"title":"","content":"Shadow Flesh got a lot of attention from the forums and no change over at least two editorial passes so I have to assume it's not a mistake.<br /> <br /> In terms of temporarily turning a person into a corpse, everyone definitely has that potential unlike turning yourself into a self-directed, living being of fire so it falls squarely under just Death for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:30:24-07:00","id":1101609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101608#post1101608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Flesh got a lot of attention from the forums and no change over at least two editorial passes so I have to assume it's not a mistake.<br /> <br /> In terms of temporarily turning a person into a corpse, everyone definitely has that potential unlike turning yourself into a self-directed, living being of fire so it falls squarely under just Death for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would fit with only needing the Destination Arcanum, which is technically what is described under Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:34:48-07:00","id":1101611,"title":"","content":"Yet Pillar of Fire, the example given in the description, uses both Life and Forces.<br /> Regardless, I think Death would suffice since I don't believe a corpse is so fundamentally different from a living being that Patterning is needed. I think Weaving or Perfecting could be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T13:07:38-07:00","id":1101710,"title":"","content":"You don't need life to make a living thing into something covered by death because that's something living things do naturally on their own. <br /> <br /> It's a loophole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:21:09-07:00","id":1101732,"title":"","content":"I have another I hope simple question:<br /> <br /> Imbued Items with Persistent effects, do they use Mana constantly? Or do they not use Mana?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:27:18-07:00","id":1101737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101732#post1101732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another I hope simple question:<br /> <br /> Imbued Items with Persistent effects, do they use Mana constantly? Or do they not use Mana?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mana is used when an effect is activated. Ongoing effects on an item are actually Enhanced Items, not Imbued Items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:35:24-07:00","id":1101741,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks! So does that also mean you can have a persistent effect and a contingent effect on an Imbued Item? Since you can combine the two Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:38:04-07:00","id":1101743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101741#post1101741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thanks! So does that also mean you can have a persistent effect and a contingent effect on an Imbued Item? Since you can combine the two Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Imbued Item and Enhanced Item merits note that the merits can be combined on a single item. So yes.<br /> <br /> Also, just for the record you don't need the Imbue Item attainment to create an Enhanced Item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:40:57-07:00","id":1101746,"title":"","content":"This is slightly related, but can you set the spell factors for Imbued Item when created? Or does it simply use the Default Factors unless you still have control over the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:47:03-07:00","id":1101749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101746#post1101746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is slightly related, but can you set the spell factors for Imbued Item when created? Or does it simply use the Default Factors unless you still have control over the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:18:22-07:00","id":1101756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101737#post1101737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mana is used when an effect is activated. Ongoing effects on an item are actually Enhanced Items, not Imbued Items.</div> </div> </div> </div>The imbued item attainment says you can choose <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">gesture, or condition).</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:36:25-07:00","id":1101765,"title":"","content":"I believe Mrmdubois was saying that if you choose to make it persistent it is essentially fulfilling the same purpose as using the Enhanced item. I am not sure why this is, as it seems a round about way to do this honestly since you don't need the Imbue Item Attainment to make an Enhanced Item. *shrugs* This may be a left-over relic from the 1E Imbued Item.<br /> <br /> 1E seemed to have a fine distinction between Imbued and Enhanced that has become more fluid with 2E where Enhanced can mean any spell with an indefinite duration on an item.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T16:24:26-07:00","id":1101782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101765#post1101765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Mrmdubois was saying that if you choose to make it persistent it is essentially fulfilling the same purpose as using the Enhanced item. I am not sure why this is, as it seems a round about way to do this honestly since you don't need the Imbue Item Attainment to make an Enhanced Item. *shrugs* This may be a left-over relic from the 1E Imbued Item.<br /> <br /> 1E seemed to have a fine distinction between Imbued and Enhanced that has become more fluid with 2E where Enhanced can mean any spell with an indefinite duration on an item.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>except its not. Enhanced items are improved items, they never enhance the user directly. You cant get away with having a + strength ring by just casting a indef increase strength spell on a ring and wear it. Its not a enhanced item just because it has any indef spell on it, only if that spell improves the item somehow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T16:40:57-07:00","id":1101785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, dots can be spent to directly enhance the item. A dot can provide +1 to the item\u2019s bonus as a tool, a point of Structure, or a point of Durability </div> </div> </div>Actually that is an additional effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Your character owns an item enhanced by indefinite Duration spells, which permanently modify the item\u2019s properties. Each dot purchased reflects one dot worth of spells the item contains.</b> </div> </div> </div>Is what Mrmdubois and I are talking about, so I believe you can get a +strength ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T16:49:46-07:00","id":1101790,"title":"","content":"Ah, no I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> to create an Enhanced Item is to place a spell on it which empowers the item. A ring of +Str would still be an Imbued Item. I'd actually consider it to be activated by being put on and the effect could be Indefinite from there though. In which case I'd probably tax the item or the Mage a point of mana when donning the ring, but I wouldn't do so afterward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T16:54:44-07:00","id":1101791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101785#post1101785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually that is an additional effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is what Mrmdubois and I are talking about, so I believe you can get a +strength ring.</div> </div> </div> </div>If thats the case why would anybody bother with a persistant imbued item giving + strength to the wearer if they can just use a enhanced item ?<br /> <br /> The additional effect means you can put a fire spell on a sword to make a flaming sword AND also increase its equipment bonus by spending some more dots. (which probably ingame is also another spell to do it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:11:14-07:00","id":1101797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If thats the case why would anybody bother with a persistant imbued item giving + strength to the wearer if they can just use a enhanced item ?<br /> <br /> The additional effect means you can put a fire spell on a sword to make a flaming sword AND also increase its equipment bonus by spending some more dots. (which probably ingame is also another spell to do it) </div> </div> </div>Very true, which is why I had to ask. Seems like you could say &quot;I am going to put a +3 Strength Persistent effect on this sword&quot;. Which, I mean arguably is not against the rules and thus there is no real mana catch here. *shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 06-08-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:35:19-07:00","id":1101810,"title":"","content":"The difference between Enhanced Items and Imbued Items is that the former are items with spells cast on them while the latter are items with spells stored inside them that are cast when the item is used. It is impossible to create an Enhanced Item that can increase the user's Strength because such an effect would have to be cast on the user. Instead you have to create an Imbued Item that casts a spell that increases the user's Strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-08-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:44:43-07:00","id":1101813,"title":"","content":"So, from what I am gathering here, Imbued Item with the persistent effect works like 1E minus the cost of 1 dot, but once you add that persistent effect that is all the &quot;Imbuing&quot; you can do. Your remaining options are to add spells to enhance the item using Matter or other spell effects that affect the material/tool in some direct way.<br /> <br /> For Instance, I could use my Imbue Item attainment to place a +3 Strength persistent effect on my sword then have a Moros mage buddy increase the durability/damage of the item using his Matter magic cast with an Indefinite Duration giving me an Enhanced &amp; Imbued Item that is really awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Added example for clarification. 06-08-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T19:27:11-07:00","id":1101837,"title":"","content":"if you create them yourself after char creation during play you probably also dont need to spend exp tohave the merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T02:31:11-07:00","id":1101894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101813#post1101813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Instance, I could use my Imbue Item attainment to place a +3 Strength persistent effect on my sword</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, you would still have to activate the sword and have it cast the Indefinite spell you placed in it on yourself for this to work. It's not quite going to be an effect where anyone who wields it gets an automatic +3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T03:07:41-07:00","id":1101903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101894#post1101894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, you would still have to activate the sword and have it cast the Indefinite spell you placed in it on yourself for this to work. It's not quite going to be an effect where anyone who wields it gets an automatic +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cant quite see how you can ever reliably get a indefinite duration on a imbued item to be honest. A +3 strength sword is only going to have a Arcana of 3 and assuming a starting char it has dicepool of from 4 to 6 (gnosis 1-3), needing -6 for indefinite, and -4 for potency 3 for a total of -10. I've said it before but any imbued item worth using is going to be a chance dice to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T03:59:24-07:00","id":1101912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be clear, you would still have to activate the sword and have it cast the Indefinite spell you placed in it on yourself for this to work. It's not quite going to be an effect where anyone who wields it gets an automatic +3. </div> </div> </div>This was how the persistent effect worked in 1E, if it doesn't work that way then it is pretty pointless to have a persistent effect that works only for the item, besides that is what Enhanced Item Merit is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:08:44-07:00","id":1101914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101912#post1101912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was how the persistent effect worked in 1E, if it doesn't work that way then it is pretty pointless to have a persistent effect that works only for the item, besides that is what Enhanced Item Merit is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having trouble parsing what you're saying here. So again for clarity:<br /> <br /> 1) Imbued Item gives an item spells that it can cast on another subject. <s>These are not always active - they must be cast from the item.</s><br /> 2) Enhanced item has spells that affect the item itself, with no effect on the wielder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-09-2017, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:27:48-07:00","id":1101917,"title":"","content":"Hey Inodiv,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is <b>persistent (always active)</b> or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition). </div> </div> </div>I have added the quote from the 2E Core, if an Imbued Item casts a spell on another subject, and it is persistent, which as the book indicates always active, then you would gain the effect from holding the sword. Very little else is said about Imbued Items and Persistent Effects, but if I were to use RAI and based on 1E it would seem the effect is provided to whoever holds the item.<br /> <br /> If 2E Imbued Item Persistent does not work this way, and it has to be triggered/activated, then it is not really a persistent effect and is instead a contigent effect.<br /> <br /> If 2E Imbued Item Persistent is a constant effect on the item itself and does not grant it's effects to the wielder/user then to me it is an Enhanced Item since that is exactly what an Enhanced Item is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:46:42-07:00","id":1101924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101917#post1101917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Inodiv,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have added the quote from the 2E Core, if an Imbued Item casts a spell on another subject, and it is persistent, which as the book indicates always active, then you would gain the effect from holding the sword. Very little else is said about Imbued Items and Persistent Effects, but if I were to use RAI and based on 1E it would seem the effect is provided to whoever holds the item.<br /> <br /> If 2E Imbued Item Persistent does not work this way, and it has to be triggered/activated, then it is not really a persistent effect and is instead a contigent effect.<br /> <br /> If 2E Imbued Item Persistent is a constant effect on the item itself and does not grant it's effects to the wielder/user then to me it is an Enhanced Item since that is exactly what an Enhanced Item is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you can build a +strength sword both ways. Either a) a persistent effect that gives its bonus to the holder/user of the sword always (it paid the mana cost at the time of creating the item and its duration is indefinite) or b) as a constingent effect where some gesture casts a +strength spell on somebody, this would probably be shorter duration (a fight) and has the advantage of being able to give +strength to others (depending on range you might have to touch them with the sword the drawback however is that it uses 1 mana each use.<br /> <br /> I also have questions about persistent effects of imbued items, what would happen if the +3 strength sword was wielded by somebody with str 4, if the sword didnt use the reach for going over max would it only increase his str to 5 (his max)??<br /> <br /> What happens when the persistent effect on a imbued item is dispelled? 1e had it so that you couldnt dispell a persistent effect right? But theres no such text saying what happens, does it reactivate at a later time, is it now just a dead imbued item since its not contingent it doesnt have a trigger to recast the spell?<br /> <br /> We need meatier rules for making imbued items, something like preprogrammed arcana strength, reaches, spell factors etc that allows the low dicepools of imbued items to get away with more powerful effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-09-2017, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:48:14-07:00","id":1101925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101917#post1101917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Inodiv,<br /> I have added the quote from the 2E Core, if an Imbued Item casts a spell on another subject, and it is persistent, which as the book indicates always active, then you would gain the effect from holding the sword. Very little else is said about Imbued Items and Persistent Effects, but if I were to use RAI and based on 1E it would seem the effect is provided to whoever holds the item.<br /> <br /> If 2E Imbued Item Persistent does not work this way, and it has to be triggered/activated, then it is not really a persistent effect and is instead a contigent effect.<br /> <br /> If 2E Imbued Item Persistent is a constant effect on the item itself and does not grant it's effects to the wielder/user then to me it is an Enhanced Item since that is exactly what an Enhanced Item is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a long time since I've been this happy to be very wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:56:50-07:00","id":1101928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101925#post1101925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a long time since I've been this happy to be very wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its easy text to miss, its tucked right after the exceptional success description of the imbued item attainment. When i first read it i thought you needed a exceptional success on creating a imbued item to choose to make it persistent or contingent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T05:41:51-07:00","id":1101941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1101924#post1101924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume you can build a +strength sword both ways. Either a) a persistent effect that gives its bonus to the holder/user of the sword always (it paid the mana cost at the time of creating the item and its duration is indefinite) or b) as a constingent effect where some gesture casts a +strength spell on somebody, this would probably be shorter duration (a fight) and has the advantage of being able to give +strength to others (depending on range you might have to touch them with the sword the drawback however is that it uses 1 mana each use.<br /> <br /> I also have questions about persistent effects of imbued items, what would happen if the +3 strength sword was wielded by somebody with str 4, if the sword didnt use the reach for going over max would it only increase his str to 5 (his max)??<br /> <br /> What happens when the persistent effect on a imbued item is dispelled? 1e had it so that you couldnt dispell a persistent effect right? But theres no such text saying what happens, does it reactivate at a later time, is it now just a dead imbued item since its not contingent it doesnt have a trigger to recast the spell?<br /> <br /> We need meatier rules for making imbued items, something like preprogrammed arcana strength, reaches, spell factors etc that allows the low dicepools of imbued items to get away with more powerful effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, unfortunately we don't have a lot of information on their creation. To me when making an imbued item you need to evaluate the pros and cons when deciding persistent or contingent. However, based on what we have provided to us it seems that spell factors are flexible based on the following quote from the 2E core:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The spell imbued into an item remains in the item\u2019s creator\u2019s spell control, even if the item only casts that spell when activated. If an imbued item casts its spell multiple times, however, it still only takes up one spell control \u201cslot.\u201d Most mages relinquish spells after they have imbued them (see p. 118), but if the mage retains control over an item\u2019s spell, she may alter its spell factors when the item casts it, and even cancel it as though she cast it herself </div> </div> </div>Based on this, it seems you can create the spell factors when imbuing the item especially since you can change the spell factors if you have not relinquished it yet. So, in the example of the +3 Strength unless the Reach was spent to increase the effects above the maximum and the mana paid to make this happen the wielder receives the maximum of 5 Strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T19:51:29-07:00","id":1102686,"title":"","content":"Would using Perfect Recall on a Sleeper provoke Dissonance or Paradox? My feeling is no, if it's just to recall a thing or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T20:48:56-07:00","id":1102699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1102686#post1102686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would using Perfect Recall on a Sleeper provoke Dissonance or Paradox? My feeling is no, if it's just to recall a thing or two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the circumstances and the nature of what they're remembering.<br /> However I would point out that Perfect Recall provides literally perfect, exacting recall of a situation.<br /> Something that most people I would say have never, or almost never experienced.<br /> <br /> I would certainly say that in many situations that would provoke Paradox and Dissonance.<br /> Or perhaps only Dissonance if they only a little bit later realised that the memory had been called forth with Magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:20:13-07:00","id":1102730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1102686#post1102686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would using Perfect Recall on a Sleeper provoke Dissonance or Paradox? My feeling is no, if it's just to recall a thing or two.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't provoke Paradox unless you went out of your way to make the casting obvious, since Paradox is only made worse if Sleepers are witnessing a mage cast obvious magic.<br /> <br /> Dissonance is more debatable - it still requires witnessing obvious Supernal magic, but it's not necessary to witness the mage casting it. Whether Perfect Recall counts as obvious magic is going to vary Sleeper to Sleeper, I would think, as well as by the degree to which they used the ability - remembering your breakfast yesterday with freakish clarity probably isn't obvious magic. Being able to relive the first day you were born with perfect clarity probably is.<br /> <br /> I would lean towards it not provoking Dissonance in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:18:26-07:00","id":1102768,"title":"","content":"It will however provoke a breaking point if the thing you make them recall is supernatural in nature. Depends on the individual but sleepers are fragile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T06:39:35-07:00","id":1102790,"title":"","content":"Essentially it was to have the owner of a pawn shop remember with perfect clarity the woman who bought a pendant from him 3 months ago so that he could describe her better. I think I'm going to rule no Paradox or Dissonance or Breaking Point in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T07:56:35-07:00","id":1102808,"title":"","content":"I think in this case any dissonance would kick in long after the spell had done it's job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T21:15:33-07:00","id":1103010,"title":"","content":"Would it provoke an Integrity Breaking Point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T02:11:22-07:00","id":1103044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1103010#post1103010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it provoke an Integrity Breaking Point?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Dissonance is invoked then invariably, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T03:08:08-07:00","id":1103056,"title":"","content":"I believe that in the future castings you could prevent Dissonance by adding reach to smooth the effect or cast some numbing spell beforehand. But other then that the devil's in the detail:<br /> &quot;Look me in the eyes and focus... You see? It's eassssy to rrremmmemberr.&quot; Will probably invoke Dissonance.<br /> &quot; You want a cup of tea? Here. Tea time always helps me to focus. Maybe it'll come to you later *shrugs*&quot; Probably won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T22:50:38-07:00","id":1104621,"title":"","content":"I was looking over Mage 2e in preparation for a game and I had a couple of questions.<br /> <br /> Under Creative Thaumaturgy, page 126, it says that boosting a skill is usually a two dot Ruling spell, but Enhance Skill is listed as Mind 3 Perfecting, just like the spell that boosts mental attributes. Which is correct?<br /> <br /> Imbued Items specifically say they need to have their Mana refilled. Artifacts don't say anything about how they regain Mana. Do they regenerate their own? Or do you refill them just like Imbued items?<br /> <br /> I'm also having a little trouble coming up with good ideas for spells that draw on multiple Arcana at once. Aside from the fairly obvious ones listed in the book, the Arcana don't really seem like they need each other as much as they have in previous games. You don't need the pattern magics to target things anymore, you can resize things without Space, and so on. You don't even technically need to include Space or Time in the spell when using Sympathetic range anymore, you just have to have enough dots to get the Attainment.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong? If so, can you suggest a good source of multi-Arcana spells? Or something else to get my ideas going?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T00:22:56-07:00","id":1104634,"title":"","content":"Your using the pre-errata version on the book. You need to get the post-errata copy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm it says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Increasing a Merit is typically a Ruling (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">) spell. Attributes<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">and Skills can be increased by a Perfecting (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">) spell. Gaining a Skill that has no dots is a Patterning (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">) spell.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> in my book. So 3 dots is correct.<br /> <br /> Unlike in 1e Artifacts dont regenerate their own mana anymore.<br /> As for multi arcana spells, that all depends on the situation. Giving specific examples will be hard because it'll depend on the story. Just remember that 2e requires less &quot;conjunctional&quot; other arcana to do things ans go with the flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-17-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T03:28:36-07:00","id":1104670,"title":"","content":"I need help understanding a Demesne Below is my understanding.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">You can use Multiple Soul Stones to Create a Demesne and the Souls Stones can be from different Mages. It seems that they are Aligned with the Paths associated with the Souls Stones that created them. As stated in the book a Stygian aligned Demesne that is filled with metal but no aspects of Death won\u2019t help death spells but it will help Matter spells. What I do not understand is if they can be filled with Items and Symbols that represent all of the Paths from all of the Soul Stones used to create them at the same time or do you have to prep it with Items and Symbols for a particular Arcana and therefore only aligned to one Arcanum at a time? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Benefits of a Demesne are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">#1) Spells of the Arcana aligned with the Demesne can use the +2 Demesne Yantra.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">#2) Spells of that Arcana aligned with the Demesne do not cause paradox unless they are active when they leave the Demesne.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">#3) Travel to the Astral Realms (I assume the realms that is aligned with the Souls Stones used to create the Demesne) from a Demesne</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">#4) Provide a +2 die bonus to rolls to summon Supernal entities from the realms they\u2019re connected to.<br /> <br /> Also you are to roll for paradox before you roll to cast the spell. if Paradox doesn't kick in until you leave the Demesne when do you roll for the Paradox, during the casting or after you leave the Demesne?<br /> <br /> Also since you do not &quot;Chance&quot; Paradox until you leave the Demesne, When does the additional Paradox build up. In each scene you build additional paradox for each time that you chanced paradox. Example is you chanced paradox 3 times in the scene the 4th time you chance it to add 3 additional paradox dice. When casting spells in a Demesne you do not chance paradox until you leave the demesne and only it that spell is still active. So do you still accrue additional paradox in the scene when you cast the spell or in the scene when the paradox is released? Normally I would say that leaving the Demesne is in the same scene as casting the spells, but that breaks down when using the Hung spell, as the spells do not activate until the Hung Spell is released.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 06-17-2017, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T07:46:19-07:00","id":1104727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1104670#post1104670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells of that Arcana aligned with the Demesne do not cause paradox unless they are active when they leave the Demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells only ever cause Paradox when they are cast. If an appropriate spell is cast in a Demesne, there's no Paradox. When it refers to a spell 'remaining within' a Demesne, it means not casting on something <i>outside</i> of the Demesne. IE - if you're in your Sanctum/Demesne and you cast a spell on someone walking down the street outside, it doesn't benefit from the Paradox immunity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T08:25:41-07:00","id":1104730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1104670#post1104670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need help understanding a Demesne Below is my understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">#3) Travel to the Astral Realms (I assume the realms that is aligned with the Souls Stones used to create the Demesne) from a Demesne</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Also when travelling to the astral realms folk normally arrive first in their oneiros, then proceed to the Tenemos, whatever soul stones used to create the demesne have no say where you end up. While there might be &quot;realms&quot; in the temenos aligned with the arcana you wont arrive there by default just because a demenses soul stone is aligned.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-17-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T09:30:35-07:00","id":1104746,"title":"","content":"Ok thanks for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:52:41-07:00","id":1106644,"title":"","content":"So, with Fate also having &quot;intentions&quot; under its purview would it be appropriate to have it read immediate intentions and Aspirations/Obsessions?<br /> <br /> With Death having &quot;absence&quot; under its purview could you cast a spell to figure out what's missing? Or Veil the absence of something from others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:57:57-07:00","id":1106784,"title":"","content":"hmm, Aspirations and Obessions via fate knowing yep i can see that. Not to keen on using death to figure out whats missing, the whole point is that its missing, maybe unmaking absence using death 5 at tops?<br /> <br /> Unmaking a negative means creating something which is making. Using death unmaking to make something that is absent is abit iffy to me....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T01:11:35-07:00","id":1106916,"title":"","content":"I personally believe that the concept of absence in awakening is more abstract than that. I could see a knowing effect that allowed you to know that something is missing - something is -supposed- to be somewhere, but isn't. I don't think it would define -what- that something was or why it was supposed to be there (maybe with a reach option). By absence, it refers to things that are metaphysically something when nothing is there. Darkness is the Absence of Light. Cold is the Absence of Heat. If something is defined by the absence of another thing, then I would argue that death would be an appropriate arcana to utilize - however, if the absence of something was arbitrary (for instance, I have no daughter), then it would not be something that Death could effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T02:11:42-07:00","id":1106926,"title":"","content":"To clarify on the Death thing, I did mean that you'd be able to tell that something that's supposed to be there is missing. I was specifically thinking of a machine with a missing gear which kept it from running, and Death wouldn't tell you that it's missing a gear, but could notice the gap where the gear was and let you know something was supposed to be in that gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:56:19-07:00","id":1107042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1106926#post1106926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify on the Death thing, I did mean that you'd be able to tell that something that's supposed to be there is missing. I was specifically thinking of a machine with a missing gear which kept it from running, and Death wouldn't tell you that it's missing a gear, but could notice the gap where the gear was and let you know something was supposed to be in that gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, and its connection to Matter through the Leaden Coin shores up that deficiency with Matter showing you what exactly the gear was, and what it did for the machine. A good case of two related Arcana shoring up each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T00:22:48-07:00","id":1107247,"title":"","content":"How would mages go about imprisoning other mages? You can't really contain them through conventional means, so I think it's safe to say that the Awakened have come up with magical means to keep their criminals contained. My question is: what are said magical means?<br /> <br /> \u200bCould the Ban spell with added Prime keep their magic at bay in the space (while conveniently protecting them from any vigilantes)? I suppose a Fraying Prime spell could suppress another mage's magic, though I think that's overpowered. Perhaps an Attainment? At least then you could constrain the casting time to a scene or something to prevent insta-casting and making another mage helpless. Is there something in the actual corebook that actually addresses this? 'Cause if there is, I haven't found it, and the pre-chapter fiction suggests there isn't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T00:58:16-07:00","id":1107252,"title":"","content":"It's not always going to boil down to magic.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you just have to tell someone to go somewhere and hope they stay. Dave had an example in his game, a mage was exiled to a small Father Ted-esque island. Presumably he could leave, if he really wanted to, but then he'd have to deal with word getting out, other members of his order hunting him or attempting to bring him to justice, his word not meaning anything, and so on.<br /> <br /> Generally, mortals put people in prison to protect the public, to punish the criminal, and ostensibly to rehabilitate them. A big inescapable building is just an easy way to do it when you have cities of millions of people. Mages have entirely different and smaller scale problems to worry about. So unless you have a trick up your sleeve or the consilium has some weird fetish for doing things the mortal way you're not going to bother with a 8x10 cell with a cot and three meals a day. If you're going to do that, you might as well just kill them or keep them in stasis. If they're a danger to the public, then kill them or otherwise keep them from it. If they need to be punished, then there's other ways to do so, taking away access to hallows and Order resources, having them be chaperoned by another mage, magical punishments like being made to offer a soul stone or a variety of imbued objects or Mana up to the consilium. If they need rehabilitation then you'll need someone to do the rehabilitating and a safe place to go about it, which can put you on the island mentioned above.<br /> <br /> Mentioning the 'trick up your sleeve' there's likely an artifact that cripples a mage's ability to use magic. There's the soul stones that can cancel out Arcana. There's all manner of pocket dimensions available. You could use spells to trap a mage in a coma or some other situation. But with this kind of thing you're getting an angry mage, potentially one who will go mad. At that point why are they bothering to just keep said mage in a hole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:08:16-07:00","id":1107650,"title":"","content":"It's probably already somewhere I couldn't find but, is it possible to have a Rote made out of a Combined Spell? Or a Praxis for that matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:23:51-07:00","id":1107658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1107650#post1107650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably already somewhere I couldn't find but, is it possible to have a Rote made out of a Combined Spell? Or a Praxis for that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't in the book, but I don't see why you couldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:42:59-07:00","id":1107665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1107650#post1107650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably already somewhere I couldn't find but, is it possible to have a Rote made out of a Combined Spell? Or a Praxis for that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally would say no, and that is based off the 5th level attainment Create Rote. In there is states that a Rote is and improvised spell, not a combined spell, and that it is one that the mage has cast many times. You must be a master to create a Rote, if it were to be allowed you would need to be a master in all Arcana involved and you would need 5 successes per dote of each spell in the Combo for the extended roll. To be a Master in 2 Arcana you would need a min 6 Gnosis so there is an argument that could be made about the requirements just to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:52:54-07:00","id":1107670,"title":"","content":"To create it would be no easy task, yeah, but once it's been created anyone could learn it for 1 XP if they have the minimum arcana requirements for casting it. Praxis also don't need the mastery requirement so it wouldn't be surprising if someone went out of their way to develop a Combined Praxis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:36:01-07:00","id":1107795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1107247#post1107247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would mages go about imprisoning other mages? You can't really contain them through conventional means, so I think it's safe to say that the Awakened have come up with magical means to keep their criminals contained. My question is: what are said magical means?<br /> <br /> \u200bCould the Ban spell with added Prime keep their magic at bay in the space (while conveniently protecting them from any vigilantes)? I suppose a Fraying Prime spell could suppress another mage's magic, though I think that's overpowered. Perhaps an Attainment? At least then you could constrain the casting time to a scene or something to prevent insta-casting and making another mage helpless. Is there something in the actual corebook that actually addresses this? 'Cause if there is, I haven't found it, and the pre-chapter fiction suggests there isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Temporal Stutter them into the future, indefinite duration, have 1 sleepwalker hold the spell for each criminal.<br /> 2) Teleport them into a pocket realm with no time, time wont pass for them and they will be frozen inside until the pocket realm is cancelled. No withstand vs teleporting somebody else, so arguably easier, plus you can fit more than one person in a big enough prison pocket realm. Getting them all out again (if they went in in different places) is another matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-25-2017, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:58:10-07:00","id":1107807,"title":"","content":"In 1e there wasnt a way to determine what an active spell was doing right? (or imbued item if i remember because my players complained about it constantly). You could look at it and work out what potency it was, what arcana was used, what the casters nimbus was blah blah but there wasnt a specific way to determine &quot;this spell is a ban vs frogs&quot; was there? You would see space + life was involved but that was it?<br /> <br /> This has changed in 2e via focused mage sight right? Mages can now use it to determine what the spell is supposed to do, i notice that there isnt a specific entry saying so bit deep information should involve wtf the spell is doing right? The ban vs frog spell would probably be opacity 4 (3 for ban + 1 for extra arcana) etc?<br /> <br /> I need to keep reminding myself about 2e's focus on mysteries and its one of the harder parts of making a story in 2e atm for me atm. Needing to come up with mysteries that keep mages involved in an area or are unfound yet etc is proving tough. (i like the other thread for crowd sourced mysteries)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-25-2017, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T00:41:27-07:00","id":1107928,"title":"","content":"Gah i have alot of questions today but there is nothing stopping a mage using &quot;Hung spell&quot; and then hanging multiple (aoe) damage spells on it at the same time and being able to release them all at the same time right? Coupled with Fate attainment and warding gesture could this be used to create various stupid traps?<br /> <br /> What does it mean when it says it can trap up to its potency in spells? Does this mean it can hold 1 spell per potency or does the hung spell have to match its held spells in total potency?<br /> <br /> Ie: Potency 2 hung spell can hold 1 potency 5 aoe fireball spell and 1 potency 5 aoe bruise flesh spell OR a potency 5 hung spell can hold 1 potency 5 aoe fireball spell and thats it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T01:21:34-07:00","id":1107939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1107928#post1107928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it mean when it says it can trap up to its potency in spells? Does this mean it can hold 1 spell per potency or does the hung spell have to match its held spells in total potency?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Spell per Potency.<br /> <br /> And no, there's nothing stopping you from using it to make traps like you describe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T02:03:30-07:00","id":1107947,"title":"","content":"Assuming its possible to cast &quot;Shared Fate&quot; over an area (the text only mentions two subjects but says increasing scale is needed to remove the mage as one of them) if there are 3 people in the area and they all take one point of damage at the same time do they end up with 2 points of damage or 3? Im imagining an area shared fate hung with a single or multiple area damage spells that'll do a hell of a lot more via shared fate. Ofc its to be expected esp as at master level mages can just unmake things anyways its just something a starting Acanthus (F3, T2) could pull off thats intresting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T03:17:53-07:00","id":1107957,"title":"","content":"They would all have one damage. Shared Fate is for those instances where a source of damage happens to one subject, but not the other, but the other also gets the damage because the spell forces them to share it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T03:23:22-07:00","id":1107958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1107957#post1107957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would all have one damage. Shared Fate is for those instances where a source of damage happens to one subject, but not the other, but the other also gets the damage because the spell forces them to share it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Whenever one subject suffers damage, a Tilt, or an unwanted Condition, any others suffer it as well</span></span> </div> </div> </div>No mention of sharing, straight up says others suffer it aswell. Bill and Bob have a shared fate, an explosion goes of doing 1 lethal to both of them, Bill takes 1 lethal so Bob takes 1 lethal he also has 1 lethal because Bob takes 1 lethal, Bob takes 1 lethal from the explosion &amp; 1 lethal from Bill taking 1 lethal. Both have 2 lethal damage? Both subjects taking damage from the same source at the same time make others suffer it also so its doubly messy. I understand that normally one subject would take damage and the other one gets it if they are far apart or whatever but im talking about both suffering damage at the same time from the same source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-26-2017, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T04:32:41-07:00","id":1107969,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is this: The spell makes one subject suffer the <u>same</u> damage another subject suffers. If that subject already suffers that damage, because it is just close enough to the source, there is nothing to do for the spell. Both subjects already &quot;share their fate&quot; if they get caught in the same explosion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T06:25:39-07:00","id":1108012,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's how I'd interpret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:58:54-07:00","id":1108177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1107969#post1107969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation is this: The spell makes one subject suffer the <u>same</u> damage another subject suffers. If that subject already suffers that damage, because it is just close enough to the source, there is nothing to do for the spell. Both subjects already &quot;share their fate&quot; if they get caught in the same explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yeh i can see that, wish the spell said it that way. It def makes it less lethal. I assume this would also work if you poisoned them both from the same source but what if you poisoned them with the same thing but a different source?<br /> <br /> I assume in a area explosion if one was armoured enough to not take damage and the other wasnt, the armoured one would then take the damage the non armoured one suffered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-26-2017, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:44:11-07:00","id":1108304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1108177#post1108177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, yeh i can see that, wish the spell said it that way. It def makes it less lethal. I assume this would also work if you poisoned them both from the same source but what if you poisoned them with the same thing but a different source?<br /> <br /> I assume in a area explosion if one was armoured enough to not take damage and the other wasnt, the armoured one would then take the damage the non armoured one suffered?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am unsure on the first one. If you poison the same person twice with the same poison, does it get a higher toxicity? If yes, then I think the spell would do the same. For the second one I would say yes, the armored one suffers the same damage as the unarmored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T16:54:45-07:00","id":1109030,"title":"","content":"I'm playing a Transhuman Engineer on a game and I would like to know if it is possible to have a sort of mobile Hallow.<br /> The idea was to create a complex hardware that pumps mana from the internet, but I don't know if the application is indeed possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T01:30:34-07:00","id":1109147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109030#post1109030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a Transhuman Engineer on a game and I would like to know if it is possible to have a sort of mobile Hallow.<br /> The idea was to create a complex hardware that pumps mana from the internet, but I don't know if the application is indeed possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hallows don't move, but you can access them remotely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T01:35:06-07:00","id":1109149,"title":"","content":"Can you use reflexive Yantras when casting a spell reflexively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T02:07:26-07:00","id":1109158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109149#post1109149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use reflexive Yantras when casting a spell reflexively?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume yes, unless you have Adamant Hand you can only use one reflexive Yantra per spell anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:35:03-07:00","id":1109400,"title":"","content":"Are the effects of the Matter 2 spell Shaping Lasting, or does the object go back to its unmodified state when the spell ends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:41:55-07:00","id":1109409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109400#post1109400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the effects of the Matter 2 spell Shaping Lasting, or does the object go back to its unmodified state when the spell ends?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell gives you the ability to shape matter. The new shape of the matter is a side-effect, and side-effects of magic are (generally) Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:55:14-07:00","id":1109416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109409#post1109409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell gives you the ability to shape matter. The new shape of the matter is a side-effect, and side-effects of magic are (generally) Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the spell shape the material for you, or does it just change the material into a shapeable state? I assumed the latter which would support your conclusion, but the fact that intricate shapes calls for a <i>reflexive</i> Wits + Crafts roll implies the spell itself shapes the material, and if so shouldn't it revert to its natural state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T17:10:48-07:00","id":1109485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109416#post1109416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the spell shape the material for you, or does it just change the material into a shapeable state? I assumed the latter which would support your conclusion, but the fact that intricate shapes calls for a <i>reflexive</i> Wits + Crafts roll implies the spell itself shapes the material, and if so shouldn't it revert to its natural state?</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes the subject matter of the spell malleable, but the Mage does the shaping from there which is why you might need to roll Wits+Crafts (Wits+Craft is a skill check, spells don't make skill checks). The shape is the side effect of the subject being made malleable, but the spell doesn't actually change the shape of the subject by itself. Cast at Sensory Range the Mage wouldn't need to be touching the subject in order to shape it, so you might end up with an effect that looks like the spell is doing the shaping, but it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:38:08-07:00","id":1109550,"title":"","content":"Soul Jar creates a 'receptacle' for a soul, where it 'cannot escape and is protected from outside attack,' or lets you jam it into a soulless person. If you actually use a jar, or other non-person container, would someone use Sever Soul, or another 3 dot Death spell, to rip it out of the container?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:01:57-07:00","id":1109584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109550#post1109550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Jar creates a 'receptacle' for a soul, where it 'cannot escape and is protected from outside attack,' or lets you jam it into a soulless person. If you actually use a jar, or other non-person container, would someone use Sever Soul, or another 3 dot Death spell, to rip it out of the container?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Sever souls specifically says from a sleeper? You just destroy the soul jar. The soul is protected from attack while in the jar but you can just destroy the Jar, ir even says in the soul jar spell that destroying the jar releases the soul","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:14:55-07:00","id":1109593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109584#post1109584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Sever souls specifically says from a sleeper? You just destroy the soul jar. The soul is protected from attack while in the jar but you can just destroy the Jar, ir even says in the soul jar spell that destroying the jar releases the soul</div> </div> </div> </div>So there's no Death spell that could just take the soul from a soul jar? They have to destroy or open the jar and Death is incapable of taking the soul through other means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T23:47:59-07:00","id":1109640,"title":"","content":"Seems so that is why being in a soul jar protects the soul from outside harm as only death can probably harm a soul? (or at least interact with it). Dispelling the souljar spell would also work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T00:13:00-07:00","id":1109643,"title":"","content":"So in Reign of the Exarchs there was a variant portal spell called &quot;arcade&quot; that opens 3 portals to 3 different places. Now the new co-location spell allows the creation of a portal but it specifically says to only 2 locations unlike its non portal version. Can anybody think of a good reason one couldnt create portals to all the overlapping spaces via co-location? (apart from that spell saying so)<br /> <br /> Also as part of co-location, if one does merge multiple locations how does the sympathetic yantras work? Does one need one yantra for each other location? So Yantra slots become the cap at how many locations can be merged not potency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T00:51:10-07:00","id":1109649,"title":"","content":"You could create multiple portals, you just can't create one portal that goes to more than one other place, and yes you need a Sympathetic Yantra for each place you're creating a portal to so that's your actual cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:18:36-07:00","id":1109658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109593#post1109593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So there's no Death spell that could just take the soul from a soul jar? They have to destroy or open the jar and Death is incapable of taking the soul through other means?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd let a Ruling Death spell do it, Weaving at maximum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T02:35:37-07:00","id":1109671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1109593#post1109593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So there's no Death spell that could just take the soul from a soul jar? They have to destroy or open the jar and Death is incapable of taking the soul through other means?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that would be a totally valid Creative Thaum spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:56:04-07:00","id":1109807,"title":"","content":"Weaving with a Reach seems right to me for this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T06:52:00-07:00","id":1110142,"title":"","content":"If you cast a spell at touch range and want to apply it with a Dexterity + Brawl attack, at what point during casting do you make the touch attack? And if you miss, is the spell lost or can you try again?<br /> <br /> On a related note, can you keep casting a spell for longer than is mechanically beneficial? In the above example, could you cast the spell and wait a few turns before attempting to touch the subject? Or say I'm waiting for someone to be at the edge of a roof before I push them off with telekinetic blast. Can I spend a few turns using Yantras and spending Mana to amplify the effect and then spend some time doing nothing except holding on to the Imago until my target is in position?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T07:00:48-07:00","id":1110145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1110142#post1110142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cast a spell at touch range and want to apply it with a Dexterity + Brawl attack, at what point during casting do you make the touch attack? And if you miss, is the spell lost or can you try again?<br /> <br /> On a related note, can you keep casting a spell for longer than is mechanically beneficial? In the above example, could you cast the spell and wait a few turns before attempting to touch the subject? Or say I'm waiting for someone to be at the edge of a roof before I push them off with telekinetic blast. Can I spend a few turns using Yantras and spending Mana to amplify the effect and then spend some time doing nothing except holding on to the Imago until my target is in position?</div> </div> </div> </div>You make the touch attack after casting the spell, you may need to up Duration just to be able to hold the spell long enough to land the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T07:04:45-07:00","id":1110146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1110145#post1110145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You make the touch attack after casting the spell, you may need to up Duration just to be able to hold the spell long enough to land the attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the same turn or the turn after?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T07:44:42-07:00","id":1110160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1110146#post1110146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the same turn or the turn after?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's the same turn, whatever the rules are for delivering an Aimed Spell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:02:21-07:00","id":1110204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1110146#post1110146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the same turn or the turn after?</div> </div> </div> </div>p118 mentions combat casting and touch range but only says the mage much use the dex+brawl/weaponry. I assume you do the physical touching part along side forming an imago even when using physical mudras or whatever, id say the roll was the same turn as the casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T12:57:36-07:00","id":1110630,"title":"","content":"Under normal circumstances, it's not possible to wipe away a mage's understanding of the Arcana (or even her Gnosis) using Mind or any other form of magic, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:18:01-07:00","id":1110638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1110630#post1110630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under normal circumstances, it's not possible to wipe away a mage's understanding of the Arcana (or even her Gnosis) using Mind or any other form of magic, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, that's an ingrained part of a Mage's nature, not just a bit knowledge in your brain space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:14:27-07:00","id":1110907,"title":"","content":"If an item acts as an Anchor for a ghost, and you use Temporal Summons to turn it into an earlier version of itself from before it was an Anchor, what happens to the ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:33:20-07:00","id":1110913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1110907#post1110907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an item acts as an Anchor for a ghost, and you use Temporal Summons to turn it into an earlier version of itself from before it was an Anchor, what happens to the ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would posit that the Ghost would start bleeding Essence as normal, or whatever happens to them when they no longer have a connection to their Anchors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:02:49-07:00","id":1111026,"title":"","content":"This maybe beyond the scope of this thread but I may as well ask. I want to create an item that appears to be a jewelers loop with ten lenses. Each lens will grant the wielder mage sight for a specific arcana. I'm not sure how to stat out the item as an imbued item or artifact even after rereading the section in the rule book or how available an item it should be. Right now I imagine it as being akin to a magical smartphone valuable but possessed by nearly everyone. <br /> <br /> Any advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:20:47-07:00","id":1111033,"title":"","content":"Mage Sight is a utility attainment so each Mage Sight is worth a dot. Your real problem is considering who crafted it, because that will determine the Path flavor of the symbols viewed through the loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:32:19-07:00","id":1111037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111033#post1111033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage Sight is a utility attainment so each Mage Sight is worth a dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage Sight isn't an Attainment at all and you can only Imbue Attainments that modify spells besides; Imbuing Apocalypse would seem the most expedient route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:54:21-07:00","id":1111046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111037#post1111037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage Sight isn't an Attainment at all and you can only Imbue Attainments that modify spells besides; Imbuing Apocalypse would seem the most expedient route.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's close enough, a Mage ability that also isn't a spell. I agree just Imbuing Apocalypse would be more expedient, though it still runs into the Path symbol thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T16:01:12-07:00","id":1111050,"title":"","content":"Dev Materials for Signs of Sorcery mention the possibility of Prime 1 + Conjunctive Arcanum 1 being able to grant another Mage access to the Conjunctive (or perhaps just Prime) Mage Sight for the duration at the cost of 1 mana. It can also work on someone who's been granted Mage Sight with Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Why so low in dots? Because they've already got Mage Sight, you're just tinkering with the frequency to help them see what you see.<br /> Should be a fairly cheap and easy to use Imbued item.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:28:40-07:00","id":1111212,"title":"","content":"Question 1: Something thats come up in the last few sessions of this game I am running, where is the boundary between a 'weak' sympathetic link and no link at all. A photo of a location or having seen a persons face are examples of the kind of things my players consider suitable examples of weak links. I am not overly averse to this, but am wondering if thats the intent.<br /> <br /> Where should I draw the line as GM?<br /> <br /> Question 2: Would you allow Know Spirit to work on a Gulmoth or similar abyssal entity? If not, what are some suggestions for other ways an enterprising PC could uncover a Gulmoths ban?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:55:25-07:00","id":1111218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111212#post1111212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 1: Something thats come up in the last few sessions of this game I am running, where is the boundary between a 'weak' sympathetic link and no link at all. A photo of a location or having seen a persons face are examples of the kind of things my players consider suitable examples of weak links. I am not overly averse to this, but am wondering if thats the intent.<br /> <br /> Where should I draw the line as GM?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at the examples in the book, weak links are things like coworkers and stuff that you own but don't care too much about. That's not a very close connection, but it's still <i>way</i> closer than &quot;someone I saw once&quot;. We're talking about things you interact with almost every day, just not on a very deep level. I would rule that you have to at the very least talked to a person to form a sympathetic link to them, and even that decays to nothing before too long if you don't keep associating with that person.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about photographs, though. Just having seen a photo of a place definitely doesn't count, but does the photo itself have enough of a link to the thing it represents that you can Borrow Threads? I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111212#post1111212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 2: Would you allow Know Spirit to work on a Gulmoth or similar abyssal entity? If not, what are some suggestions for other ways an enterprising PC could uncover a Gulmoths ban?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Maybe give the tiniest detail along the lines of &quot;if this is a spirit it's not like any other spirit you've ever seen&quot; accompanied by a nosebleed. As for finding its ban, if it's even possible you have to do it the old-fashioned way - digging through forbidden grimoires, triangulating based on fragmented mortal (or at least non-Awakened) descriptions of similar monsters or, if you're truly desperate, negotiating with other Abyssal entities or scelesti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:03:02-07:00","id":1111223,"title":"","content":"Photos don't have any sympathetic link to whatever they represent as long as the photo hasn't actually interacted with it's subject enough to gain a link (such as a photo of a family being on display in that family's house). But it's a great representation of it's subject and can still be used as a sympathetic yantra despite the lack of sympathetic connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:19:35-07:00","id":1111329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111212#post1111212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 1: Something thats come up in the last few sessions of this game I am running, where is the boundary between a 'weak' sympathetic link and no link at all. A photo of a location or having seen a persons face are examples of the kind of things my players consider suitable examples of weak links. I am not overly averse to this, but am wondering if thats the intent.<br /> <br /> Where should I draw the line as GM?<br /> <br /> Question 2: Would you allow Know Spirit to work on a Gulmoth or similar abyssal entity? If not, what are some suggestions for other ways an enterprising PC could uncover a Gulmoths ban?</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeh Web-weaving explains that just touching stuff (a can) isnt enough for a link so just passing people in the street, seeing their face once probably isnt enough to form any links. I think you need to at least have something more. You need to be able to give that thing some tag or meaning. Like &quot;that blonde girl on the bus&quot; that you see every day, your not anywhere near as close as say co workers but you have given that person some thought and that might create a weak link.<br /> <br /> As for abyss spirits and the spirit arcana, by raw i would say yes, having abyss spirits be immune to spirit/supernal magic just because its so easy for spirit mages (and mind mages) to control them is abit gamey. I might do it for a the big bad in a entire campaign just so it doesnt end the second a mage with mind 2 gets a look at it but just blanket making all abyss spirits immune to supernal control magic because they are abyss and alien is wrong.<br /> <br /> Take spirits from the prince of 100,000 reality, they are still spirits just in a negative/corrupted form. (though it could be argued they are anti-time reflections of normal spirits and not gulmoths, i would need to check my books for the definition of one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T11:30:26-07:00","id":1111367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111212#post1111212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 2: Would you allow Know Spirit to work on a Gulmoth or similar abyssal entity? If not, what are some suggestions for other ways an enterprising PC could uncover a Gulmoths ban?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would vary from Intruder to Intruder. Here are some of the available options:<br /> 1. If the Gulmoth is a Spirit as opposed to just using Spirit rules, &quot;Know Spirit&quot; succeeds without problem. This approach undersells the strangeness of Abyssal beings.<br /> 2. If the Gulmoth incorporates too much corrupt symbolism, &quot;Know Spirit&quot; might succeed, but inflict an Abyssal Condition or Tilt. <br /> 3. If the Gulmoth is something stranger, &quot;Know Spirit&quot; might outright fail. More than that, all Knowing Spells might undergo Havoc when used on the entity.<br /> <br /> If the most obvious route fails, the following methods can be used:<br /> 1. The Ban can be read with a different Arcanum, or a combination of Arcana. For instance Spirit+Prime.<br /> 2. The Ban can be read with &quot;Know Spirit&quot;, but it requires specific circumstances. For instance, having a personal Sympathetic link is necessary to target it with Spells, or you must have caused Paradox earlier that Scene.<br /> 3. Other Spells might work where &quot;Know Spirit&quot; fails. Try &quot;Postcognition&quot; or &quot;Telepathy&quot; and hope you don't get infected with something. You might also find a &quot;friendly&quot; Fang of Mara to cast &quot;Dream Reaching&quot; for you.<br /> 4. Investigation. The Intruder might have encountered its Ban at some point, especially if it existed for some time. An in-depth look into its activities is necessary to discover it. For instance, the only survivors of its attacks were either newborns or the elderly - people without teeth.<br /> 5. If the Intruder has a foothold on reality, or is routinely summoned by Scelesti, someone might have already uncovered the Ban. Left-Handed Mages and Grimoires may hold the key, but may also maliciously mislead you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T18:18:47-07:00","id":1111481,"title":"","content":"So, I do know that Imperial Mysteries at one point calls the number of Archmages &quot;vanishingly small&quot;? Does it ever at any point say how small? Two digits, plus however many Ascended? <br /> <br /> One has to assume that most Tetrarchs aren't Archmasters, because it seems like you'd quickly run towards a hundred if that were so. Though perhaps all Ministers of a major faction are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T18:22:20-07:00","id":1111484,"title":"","content":"Has it been said if Forge Destiny can grant Supernatural merits to those that normally can't have them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T20:17:57-07:00","id":1111528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111481#post1111481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I do know that Imperial Mysteries at one point calls the number of Archmages &amp;quot;vanishingly small&amp;quot;? Does it ever at any point say how small? Two digits, plus however many Ascended? <br /> <br /> One has to assume that most Tetrarchs aren't Archmasters, because it seems like you'd quickly run towards a hundred if that were so. Though perhaps all Ministers of a major faction are.</div> </div> </div> </div>CoD goes out of its way to avoid giving you statistics on supernatural populations. In other words, create as many as you need for your story, no more, no less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T21:22:24-07:00","id":1111543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111484#post1111484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been said if Forge Destiny can grant Supernatural merits to those that normally can't have them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Books even says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The mage grants the subject a Supernatural Merit for<br /> which she qualifies with a maximum rating equal to the<br /> spell\u2019s Potency. Sanctity of Merits <span style=\"color:#004E6D\">(see p. 99) <span style=\"color:#000000\">doesn\u2019t apply<br /> to the loss of this Merit.</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Qualifies one would assume means have prereqs for and doesnt mean is supernatural in the first place. Its also a making spell, so even if forge destiny didnt do it, no reason a creative thaum making spell couldnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:21:18-07:00","id":1111833,"title":"","content":"A Fate spell that effectively renders you invisible by causing things to occur such that no one is looking at you or cameras are turned off or pointed the wrong way when you walk past. What Practice do you think that is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:35:43-07:00","id":1111844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111833#post1111833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Fate spell that effectively renders you invisible by causing things to occur such that no one is looking at you or cameras are turned off or pointed the wrong way when you walk past. What Practice do you think that is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Veiling. Possibly with a Mana cost similar to Incognito Presence.<br /> <br /> Edit: Or maybe not. See post below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-05-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:38:09-07:00","id":1111846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1111833#post1111833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Fate spell that effectively renders you invisible by causing things to occur such that no one is looking at you or cameras are turned off or pointed the wrong way when you walk past. What Practice do you think that is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Patterning. It sounds like it's about on the level (or even an application) of Chaos Mastery, a Fate 4 Patterning spell. Arguably Weaving if you just make yourself supremely unlikely to be detected (\u00e1 la Superlative Luck on Stealth rolls) as opposed to everyone definitely for sure looking away at just the right moment<br /> <br /> It's definitely not Veiling as you suggested in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread, because that Practice refers to hiding things within the Arcanum's purview or hiding <i>from</i> things in the Arcanum's purview. In the case of Fate the means hiding or disguising a destiny, curse or probability. It would also including hiding <i>from</i> destiny, curses or probability, except you are explicitly not allowed to Veil things from abstract concepts short of archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T19:54:26-07:00","id":1112468,"title":"","content":"How does one speed up/slow down time in an area like 1e's &quot;Faerie Glade&quot; spell, there isnt a direct spell written in the book im missing right? One would just have to creative thaum it? A sanctum you can hide in and have 5-6 times as long to come up with ideas/rituals was always useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:46:34-07:00","id":1112616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112468#post1112468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one speed up/slow down time in an area like 1e's &quot;Faerie Glade&quot; spell, there isnt a direct spell written in the book im missing right? One would just have to creative thaum it? A sanctum you can hide in and have 5-6 times as long to come up with ideas/rituals was always useful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tipping the Hourglass (Time \u2022\u2022)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:19:05-07:00","id":1112631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112616#post1112616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tipping the Hourglass (Time \u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't work like Faerie Glade so not the answer they're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:20:49-07:00","id":1112632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112616#post1112616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Tipping the Hourglass (Time \u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a spell that increases or decreases someone's Initiative. It does work by slowing or speeding the passage of time, but the mechanics are so completely unrelated to creating an area where time moves more/less slowly that a version of Tipping the Hourglass that creates a Faerie Glade is effectively Creative Thaumaturgy anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:44:20-07:00","id":1112745,"title":"","content":"The spell <i>Tipping the Hourglass (Time \u2022\u2022), </i>The mage can momentarily alter the flow of Time, causing it to speed up or slow down for a subject, but not drastically. He asked for one that speeds up and slows down time. If he wants something that drastically speeds it up or slows it down then you are correct it would be a Creative Thaumaturgy, However if I am understanding the request then I don't think anything short of Archmastery will allow you to alter time itself. Alter events yes, eradicate timelines yes, but the actual flow of time they stayed away from. Just my observation. Everything I can see in time is altering events, altering perception of time, or moving along a time line. Acceleration and Tipping the Hour Glass comes the closest to actually affecting time itself, Once again My opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#ff0000\">\u200bI just read temporal Pocket and I stand corrected. It actually alters the flow of time within the Pocket. </span></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 07-07-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T11:10:54-07:00","id":1112796,"title":"","content":"Oh right, the 2e Temporal Pocket does the hardcore version of what 1e Temporal Pocket and Faerie Glade do - it effectively <i>stops </i>outside time rather than slowing it. Just add some scale factors and you're all set.<br /> <br /> That's a Making spell though, and simply creating an area of sped up/slowed down time sounds like Ruling to me or at <i>most</i> Weaving. Maybe take a page from the 1e Temporal Pocket and say that the spell makes time in the bubble go 1+Potency times faster/slower?<br /> <br /> <br /> On a side note, this kind of magic freaks me out slightly. Speeding up your own time in relation to the world effectively ages you; an hour spent in a Faerie Glade isn't free, it's borrowed from the end of your life. Make a habit of stretching time to meet deadlines and one-up rivals and you're potentially shaving years off your life. Get stuck on a particularly important, time-limited Obsession and you might end disappearing from your Cabal's view only to instantly reappear, 20 years older.<br /> <br /> Don't do magic, kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:20:54-07:00","id":1112832,"title":"","content":"That's why you'd shield yourself from the effects of time passing during your time in the faster pocket of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:39:46-07:00","id":1112852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112832#post1112832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why you'd shield yourself from the effects of time passing during your time in the faster pocket of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you can't do that, simply because it would make becoming a Lich trivial and risk-free. Just cast &quot;Arrested Development&quot; on yourself with Indefinite Duration and re-apply it if/when it gets knocked off.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about casting Indefinite Duration Time spells on yourself to wind your personal time back, in which case: congratulations, you're a Lich! Try not to make enemies with anyone who has dots in Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T14:44:41-07:00","id":1112929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112852#post1112852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you can't do that, simply because it would make becoming a Lich trivial and risk-free. Just cast &quot;Arrested Development&quot; on yourself with Indefinite Duration and re-apply it if/when it gets knocked off.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about casting Indefinite Duration Time spells on yourself to wind your personal time back, in which case: congratulations, you're a Lich! Try not to make enemies with anyone who has dots in Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you need to read Veil of Moments. Last spell in Time 2, pg. 188.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:04:03-07:00","id":1112941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112929#post1112929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure you need to read Veil of Moments. Last spell in Time 2, pg. 188.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's odd. You have this long review of how challenging and dangerous it is to achieve eternal life and the extreme lengths mages go to to escape death, and then it turns out all you need to extend your lifespan indefinitely is a Time 2 Rote.<br /> <br /> I guess it says you can't spend Experiences while it's on, but the only discussion of how long it takes to spend Experiences is a line that says you can spend the &quot;at any time&quot;, sooo I guess you can drop it for like a second every now and then to spend you exp? I guess my interpretation would be that you have to turn it off while you're practicing your new skill, but that's effectively vetoing long-term use anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:26:55-07:00","id":1112983,"title":"","content":"I would interpret it like this: XP is an accumulation of the effects of time on your person and your actions in it which cause you to change. Applying XP accumulated during your time under the spell after you dispel it thus also causes you to age. After a hundred years of gathering XP you'd likely be turned to dust if you spent it all at once. Arguably though, Temporal Summoning is the actual lichdom spell, become younger with no loss in XP and able to apply it while under the effects of the spell is a no brainer if you don't care that it being dispelled after a long enough time period is an automatic death sentence.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Acanthus obviously run the risk of living very short/long lives with their ability to jump back and forth and speed time up or down subjectively, so Veil of Moments is a pretty sensible safeguard for making sure they don't age too far ahead of where they ought to be (The question becomes, how many Acanthus realize that before aging themselves significantly?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:52:05-07:00","id":1112995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112983#post1112983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would interpret it like this: XP is an accumulation of the effects of time on your person and your actions in it which cause you to change. Applying XP accumulated during your time under the spell after you dispel it thus also causes you to age. After a hundred years of gathering XP you'd likely be turned to dust if you spent it all at once. Arguably though, Temporal Summoning is the actual lichdom spell, become younger with no loss in XP and able to apply it while under the effects of the spell is a no brainer if you don't care that it being dispelled after a long enough time period is an automatic death sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the reason Veil of Moments rubs me the wrong way is that as written it doesn't have the dispellation issue - dispelling it just causes you to resume aging at a normal rate, which makes it relatively risk-free compared to the other simple methods, which revolve around Indefinite Duration spells that instantly kill you if you've gone past your natural lifespan and the spell ends for any reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112983#post1112983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, Acanthus obviously run the risk of living very short/long lives with their ability to jump back and forth and speed time up or down subjectively, so Veil of Moments is a pretty sensible safeguard for making sure they don't age too far ahead of where they ought to be (The question becomes, how many Acanthus realize that before aging themselves significantly?).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also why I don't really like the non-aging clause. I <i>like</i> the idea that messing with time like this is a Faustian bargain. Accidentally aging yourself because you weren't thinking - or better yet, doing it knowingly in pursuit of your Obsessions - is such a fantastically Mage thing to do, and I don't like that you can get out of it with a simple Shielding spell.<br /> <br /> That's just my opinion, though. In the setting as written this'll only happen to inexperienced or desperate Time mages, which is still a pretty interesting story hook or character gimmick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T20:56:45-07:00","id":1113086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112995#post1112995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the reason Veil of Moments rubs me the wrong way is that as written it doesn't have the dispellation issue - dispelling it just causes you to resume aging at a normal rate, which makes it relatively risk-free compared to the other simple methods, which revolve around Indefinite Duration spells that instantly kill you if you've gone past your natural lifespan and the spell ends for any reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrariwise, if you Awaken young and do not rocket through your dots in Time and Gnosis, juggling Veil on and off means you are blowing a spell control slot you can't necessarily spare, which puts you that much closer to courting Paradox or makes you that much more reliant on limited resources to safely maintain it before the point of Mastery.<br /> <br /> I can <i>do things</i> with either specimen \u2014 a character who blights their Nimbus and scars their mind with the whispers of the acamoth in the name of eternal youth and the unaging architect of a grand web of ritual partners and safehouses both manage to produce compelling behaviors without having to fall to dust if they miss a single grain of fallen sand.<br /> <br /> (It is never the one grain you have to worry about \u2014 this is Awakening, after all.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T03:17:48-07:00","id":1113171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113086#post1113086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can <i>do things</i> with either specimen \u2014 a character who blights their Nimbus and scars their mind with the whispers of the acamoth in the name of eternal youth and the unaging architect of a grand web of ritual partners and safehouses both manage to produce compelling behaviors without having to fall to dust if they miss a single grain of fallen sand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. But my concern is this: why would ever do the former when the latter is an option? As presented in the book, the whole reason mages muck about with Abyssal powers, bind theirs souls to their own ghosts and become body-snatchers or soul-thieves for eternal life is that just casting a spell is a bad long-term solution. I mean sure, these are mages we're talking about so they'd still find reasons to turn themselves into ideas and hole up in the Temenos for all of eternity, but I feel the whole idea of a lich as someone driven to morbid, dangerous extremes out of fear of death is rather undercut if the secret to safe, non-transformative longevity is a Time 2 Rote available at character creation.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's broken or anything, and as you point out the idea of a mage, especially an inexperienced one, who carefully (or dare I say Obsessively) maintains their Veil of Moments is very compelling on a one-game basis. I just think it has unfortunate setting-wide implications because it means most liches are just unreasonable gits who eat souls because they're too lazy to learn two dots of Time as opposed to unreasonable gits who eat souls because they're driven to extremes by a relatable human fear of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:29:13-07:00","id":1113197,"title":"","content":"This conversation has been had. I might be able to dig up one of the threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:59:39-07:00","id":1113202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1112983#post1112983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably though, Temporal Summoning is the actual lichdom spell, become younger with no loss in XP and able to apply it while under the effects of the spell is a no brainer if you don't care that it being dispelled after a long enough time period is an automatic death sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>This only works if Temporal Summoning only effects the body. If it effects the mind, you're going to revert in truth to your younger self for the duration, which would presumably include a loss of skills, attributes, powers, etc.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually sure how this one is <i>supposed</i> to work, but in our pre-errata game at least we definitely ran it where Temporal Summoning effected everything about the person - mind, body, and soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:30:10-07:00","id":1113216,"title":"","content":"Veil of moments should have said you dont gain beats &amp; exp AND cant spend exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:52:29-07:00","id":1113226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113216#post1113216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veil of moments should have said you dont gain beats &amp; exp AND cant spend exp.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if it didn't say that it is how I view it and is how I run it in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T09:06:24-07:00","id":1113271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113171#post1113171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. But my concern is this: why would ever do the former when the latter is an option?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be misunderstanding what the former is, but to answer the question: Because the latter takes longer and has more potential points of failure. Setting up a massive infrastructure to allow you to re-apply the same spell to yourself over and over for decades requires time and social capital or unclaimed resources that will either bind you to a locale or hobble your ability to investigate quickly. By contrast, the impatient young Apprentice can drop their Veil, take five to formalize their advanced enlightenment, and roll the dice to restore their bulwark against the ages within the course of an hour.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about the difference between going full Scelestus and casting the spell on a regular basis, I'm talking about the difference between racing to the archetype of unstable Mastery and the archetype of stable Mastery \u2014 it pushes you to either ignore risks or forgo rewards in a way that you don't get from simply shedding your humanity to explore the Invisible Realms.<br /> <br /> (Which reminds me: rote or no rote, having Veil of Moments without Time 5 means you still have to push pretty hard to get a lengthy Duration out of the casting, fortify your Clash rolls for it, or keep any Disciple of Prime from plucking your ersatz immortality off of you. Even a Master's Reach still means you have to choose between Mana, Willpower, and natural healing for a casting that uses Advanced Potency, Instant Casting, or Indefinite Duration outside of a Verge.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:53:03-07:00","id":1113335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113271#post1113271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be misunderstanding what the former is, but to answer the question: Because the latter takes longer and has more potential points of failure. Setting up a massive infrastructure to allow you to re-apply the same spell to yourself over and over for decades requires time and social capital or unclaimed resources that will either bind you to a locale or hobble your ability to investigate quickly. By contrast, the impatient young Apprentice can drop their Veil, take five to formalize their advanced enlightenment, and roll the dice to restore their bulwark against the ages within the course of an hour.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about the difference between going full Scelestus and casting the spell on a regular basis, I'm talking about the difference between racing to the archetype of unstable Mastery and the archetype of stable Mastery \u2014 it pushes you to either ignore risks or forgo rewards in a way that you don't get from simply shedding your humanity to explore the Invisible Realms.<br /> <br /> (Which reminds me: rote or no rote, having Veil of Moments without Time 5 means you still have to push pretty hard to get a lengthy Duration out of the casting, fortify your Clash rolls for it, or keep any Disciple of Prime from plucking your ersatz immortality off of you. Even a Master's Reach still means you have to choose between Mana, Willpower, and natural healing for a casting that uses Advanced Potency, Instant Casting, or Indefinite Duration outside of a Verge.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure what you are talking about here? But<br /> <br /> I think they main point is that having it dispelled doesnt make you rapid age and die if you have had the spell up for 100 years and somebody comes along and dispells it. Ritual casting and eating some paradox is a small price to pay to just recast it probably using a demense too. Being able to gain beats just not spend them but drop the spell and recast just seems like a loophole that may or may not have gone unnoticed by the devs.<br /> <br /> Just makes less sense for people to want to become liches for immortality alone if its possible with Time 2. There has to be other things that Liches have that mages want, that or most are tricked into it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:58:29-07:00","id":1113337,"title":"","content":"Most liches do have an agenda for their immortality, or it's a last ditch resort in the event of an existential crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:31:43-07:00","id":1113516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113335#post1113335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they main point is that having it dispelled doesnt make you rapid age and die if you have had the spell up for 100 years and somebody comes along and dispells it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. Having the spell up for a hundred years would be highly inadvisable for most PCs even without dispellation causing a reaction generally reserved for adaptation to highly rarefied circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ritual casting and eating some paradox is a small price to pay to just recast it probably using a demense too. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understand: if your world works in such a manner that it's a small price to pay, you're not looking at a player character and you're only debatably looking at a mage \u2014 one of the two archetypes I mentioned is the mage who never leaves their sanctum if they can help it and instead works through proxies or students or carefully prepared defensible avenues.<br /> <br /> If diverting a hefty portion of your resources to enabling and maintaining a single spell over and over does not cause problems for you, either you're in downtime or the Storyteller isn't doing their job.<br /> <br /> (Also notable: eating Paradox is going to catch up with you eventually just by virtue of how Wisdom and resistant damage work even with the full suite of Reach effects in play.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just makes less sense for people to want to become liches for immortality alone if its possible with Time 2. There has to be other things that Liches have that mages want, that or most are tricked into it? </div> </div> </div>Many liches tend to have a substantial leg up on the folks running simpleton agelessness in the form of not having to worry about having a squishy mortal body. Time magic just lets you stretch out your available life; liches have greater practice and ability in the realm of <i>not dying</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:02:44-07:00","id":1113612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113516#post1113516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware. Having the spell up for a hundred years would be highly inadvisable for most PCs even without dispellation causing a reaction generally reserved for adaptation to highly rarefied circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>So many words, still have no clue what this means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I don't think you understand: if your world works in such a manner that it's a small price to pay, you're not looking at a player character and you're only debatably looking at a mage \u2014 one of the two archetypes I mentioned is the mage who never leaves their sanctum if they can help it and instead works through proxies or students or carefully prepared defensible avenues.<br /> <br /> If diverting a hefty portion of your resources to enabling and maintaining a single spell over and over does not cause problems for you, either you're in downtime or the Storyteller isn't doing their job.<br /> <br /> (Also notable: eating Paradox is going to catch up with you eventually just by virtue of how Wisdom and resistant damage work even with the full suite of Reach effects in play.)<br /> </div> </div> </div>You seem under the impression that every mage will come up to you and just dispel any spells on you without reason. So maybe if you fight seers all day long it might be a problem but for your average Joe mage who isnt fighting seers every single day, i dont think he will be getting his spells randomly dispelled and even if it is as long as he survives he just recasts it. What hefty portion of resources are we talking about here, you spend afew hours of your time ritually casting, maybe some mana are there other resources im missing that makes casting a rank 2 spell vastly more complex? Plus resistant bashing is still bashing, it heals in 15 mins if you have the reach that allows healing under the Veil, how does this catch up with you exactly? Also just by virtue of being an old mage your wisdom is probably low it really depends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Many liches tend to have a substantial leg up on the folks running simpleton agelessness in the form of not having to worry about having a squishy mortal body. Time magic just lets you stretch out your available life; liches have greater practice and ability in the realm of <i>not dying</i>. </div> </div> </div>I think Tremere can still die, they arnt effectively mummy like are they? They just also dont die from old age? Ive yet to see anything (and nothing has been confirmed in 2e) about how Liches are less squishy than normal, yes they might have some attainment/whatever these are called for tremere but thats not to say normal mages couldnt also have one. One assumes one becomes a Lich to learn secrets about death or the soul rather than just to extend ones lifespan, thats probably a plus but might not be the primary goal of becoing a Lich esp when if you just want to prolong your life span, Mastery in Life/ Death/ (Time) can do that without the Lich part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 07-09-2017, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:38:31-07:00","id":1113621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113612#post1113612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many words, still have no clue what this means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Immediately aging decades over the course of minutes is more appropriate for entities that are part of or entangled with locations so divorced from conventional reality that those locations are the only thing keeping them in their youthful state. Veil of Moments is not an ongoing bargain with an occult force to hold back entropy, it's a construction that stops temporal badness from progressing while it's active; you could sample the CDC's entire stock of horrible diseases and drop the spell to see which started killing you fastest, but aging is a single source of &quot;damage.&quot; There are dozens of more likely ways for a mage to die than old age with or without laminating yourself in magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem under the impression that every mage will come up to you and just dispel any spells on you without reason. </div> </div> </div>I am under the impression that if you depend on a single spell for your agelessness you'll have to be quite careful about making enemies in general, which tends to be difficult to balance with pursuing other obsessions and managing obligations within mage society \u2014 you're not getting that rote and that Sanctum from nowhere, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What hefty portion of resources are we talking about here, you spend afew hours of your time ritually casting, maybe some mana are there other resources im missing that makes casting a rank 2 spell vastly more complex? </div> </div> </div>Demesnes are by definition a limited resource, Sancta do not grow on trees, Sleepwalkers with sympathetic connections to you are not everywhere, and unless you intend to never travel anywhere in the course of pursuing Mysteries you are going to need to be able to access this sort of setup in multiple locales (and the flip side of <i>that</i> is that being ageless younger increases the degree to which you need to either cloister yourself more or invest in ways to falsify aging or reinvent your mortal identity).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus resistant bashing is still bashing, it heals in 15 mins if you have the reach that allows healing under the Veil, how does this catch up with you exactly? </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Demesnes are by definition a limited resource&quot; and note that failing to hit the necessary number of successes means you pick up a Paradox Condition that, unless discharged, will either screw up the rest of your magic or force you to retreat for another two full days to remove an effective cap on your Health. You could release the Paradox instead, but the nature of Paradox Reach is such that you could well wind up building multiple cumulative dice from retries. These things add up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Tremere can still die, they arnt effectively mummy like are they? They just also dont die from old age? Ive yet to see anything (and nothing has been confirmed in 2e) about how Liches are less squishy than normal, yes they might have some attainment/whatever these are called for tremere but thats not to say normal mages couldnt also have one. </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are not the only liches that exist and even before getting into the potential variety implied by &quot;taking on new bodies&quot; there are still at least three categories of lich that just <i>turn themselves into intangible monsters</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-09-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:45:58-07:00","id":1113624,"title":"","content":"TL;DR on &quot;immortality without lichdom&quot;: It sounds workable on paper. Not so much in reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:03:30-07:00","id":1113734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113621#post1113621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immediately aging decades over the course of minutes is more appropriate for entities that are part of or entangled with locations so divorced from conventional reality that those locations are the only thing keeping them in their youthful state. Veil of Moments is not an ongoing bargain with an occult force to hold back entropy, it's a construction that stops temporal badness from progressing while it's active; you could sample the CDC's entire stock of horrible diseases and drop the spell to see which started killing you fastest, but aging is a single source of &quot;damage.&quot; There are dozens of more likely ways for a mage to die than old age with or without laminating yourself in magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes i think you use really long complex sentences just to troll people? I understand all the words but completely miss the content. What does a bargain have to do with anything, are you saying immortality via lichdom is better because of ongoing bargains? (do they even bargain with anything?).What has CDC diseases got to do with anything? We are discussing the viability of a long duration veil of moments spell increasing ones lifespan, this statement applies how?<br /> What about aging is a single source of damage, what does this even mean? Time doesnt catch up with you when the veil is canceled, its paused under it and just resumes when it stops. cast it at 21, keep it up for a 90 years (might be recast but its not down enough to count), your still 21 but really 111 you dont suddenly age to 111. Dying from dozens of other ways applies to every mage not just one with a veil of moments on. Why would this be any more of a problem for a mage with a veil?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this seems harsh but nearly every answer you give is long winded, esoteric almost and i usually have to go lie down in a dark room after reading them, maybe its just me i dunno.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I am under the impression that if you depend on a single spell for your agelessness you'll have to be quite careful about making enemies in general, which tends to be difficult to balance with pursuing other obsessions and managing obligations within mage society \u2014 you're not getting that rote and that Sanctum from nowhere, after all.<br /> <br /> Demesnes are by definition a limited resource, Sancta do not grow on trees, Sleepwalkers with sympathetic connections to you are not everywhere, and unless you intend to never travel anywhere in the course of pursuing Mysteries you are going to need to be able to access this sort of setup in multiple locales (and the flip side of <i>that</i> is that being ageless younger increases the degree to which you need to either cloister yourself more or invest in ways to falsify aging or reinvent your mortal identity).<br /> <br /> See &quot;Demesnes are by definition a limited resource&quot; and note that failing to hit the necessary number of successes means you pick up a Paradox Condition that, unless discharged, will either screw up the rest of your magic or force you to retreat for another two full days to remove an effective cap on your Health. You could release the Paradox instead, but the nature of Paradox Reach is such that you could well wind up building multiple cumulative dice from retries. These things add up.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Again this applies to every other mage also, (not quite sure why you need sleepwalkers to cast a time 2 spell unless you want then hold it for you i suppose) a mage with a perm veil spell has MORE time to collect/save stuff so probably overall will have more resources because they have &quot;lived&quot; longer than another mage. Everything you have said here applies to every single mage. I get the feeling you think any mage with a long duration veil of moments will get victimized MORE than any other random mage? How so? Without going through the mental gymnastics of trying to imbue veil of moments into an item you keep on you thats another possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> The Tremere are not the only liches that exist and even before getting into the potential variety implied by &quot;taking on new bodies&quot; there are still at least three categories of lich that just <i>turn themselves into intangible monsters</i>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:35:51-07:00","id":1113746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113621#post1113621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am under the impression that if you depend on a single spell for your agelessness you'll have to be quite careful about making enemies in general, which tends to be difficult to balance with pursuing other obsessions and managing obligations within mage society \u2014 you're not getting that rote and that Sanctum from nowhere, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you don't. That's the whole point! Because unlike Deny the Reaper or whatever hypothetical Life spell would keep you trucking past your expiration date, you can just re-cast it. Every problem that Veil of Moments has is a problem it shares with the Indefinite &quot;Make Me Not Die&quot; spells the book mentions, except that it's available at a significantly lower dot rating and losing the spell has no immediate consequence whatsoever. Sure you gotta get the Rote from somewhere, but compared to achieving Mastery of Death or discovering a method to transform into a ghost/spirit/Goetia/bodysnatcher without losing your magical abilities, learning a 2-dot Rote is absolute peanuts.<br /> <br /> That's also why you don't really need a Demesne or even a Sanctum. Since the spell timing out or getting dispelled isn't a huge problem you only really need to Reach for Advanced Duration and maybe Instant Casting, spend the rest on being able to heal and regain resources, take a symbolic penalty for Duration factors and re-cast every week.<br /> <br /> Transformative lichdom has its own benefits, but the existence of Veil of Moments as written makes the actions of the Tremere, the hypothetical bodysnatcher liches and those &quot;na\u00efve&quot; mages who put Indefinite Spells of Not Dying on themselves not just dangerous and unethical, but stupid. If you don't want to die, why on earth would you become a Reaper with a constant ticking clock over your head or hinge your moment-to-moment existence on a single, easily-cut thread when there's a 2-dot spell that does essentially the same thing without turning you into a target for every mage with a conscience or opening you up to death by dispellation from any disgruntled Initiate of Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T09:07:16-07:00","id":1113762,"title":"","content":"Agelessness does not look like a good path to immortality, as it only stops one way your (un)timely demise might occur.<br /> <br /> And that's why the Tremere are appealing - they got most bases covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T09:17:09-07:00","id":1113766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113762#post1113762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agelessness does not look like a good path to immortality, as it only stops one way your (un)timely demise might occur.<br /> <br /> And that's why the Tremere are appealing - they got most bases covered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Am i missing something, Are the Tremere Mummy like and undying? You shoot a Tremere with enough bullets and he dies like every other mage right? Most Bases covered, how exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T09:23:12-07:00","id":1113768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113766#post1113766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i missing something, Are the Tremere Mummy like and undying? You shoot a Tremere with enough bullets and he dies like every other mage right? Most Bases covered, how exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact mechanics for the 2E Tremere still haven't been published, but in my game, they can switch bodies with anyone they've stolen the soul of. Even after their current body gives out, if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:20:42-07:00","id":1113817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113766#post1113766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Am i missing something, Are the Tremere Mummy like and undying? You shoot a Tremere with enough bullets and he dies like every other mage right? Most Bases covered, how exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming he's not got a House (Tremere Legacy-lite; Tremere can't have normal Legacies) that makes him undead-ish, yes.<br /> <br /> Well, bullets will work as well as on any other mage. Depends what Mage Armour the Tremere has up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:18:55-07:00","id":1113844,"title":"","content":"I've got a blind mage specializing in space to compensate for her vision. Had the character go blind from her awakening. With going with this character flaw and avoiding to use life magic, what would the character see when using the benefits of space, such as The Outward and Inner Eye or Scrying? I wasn't sure if for the former it would just kind of result in a sort of Daredevil/Spidey-Sense or if she would mentally see something when using it or Scrying. Other players I'm with can't come to an agreement over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T14:57:34-07:00","id":1113884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113844#post1113844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a blind mage specializing in space to compensate for her vision. Had the character go blind from her awakening. With going with this character flaw and avoiding to use life magic, what would the character see when using the benefits of space, such as The Outward and Inner Eye or Scrying? I wasn't sure if for the former it would just kind of result in a sort of Daredevil/Spidey-Sense or if she would mentally see something when using it or Scrying. Other players I'm with can't come to an agreement over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Space technically has the ability to pipe information about the landscape right into your head. That's the province of Matter/Spirit/Forces/Life/etc. as appropriate. It controls distance and direction, and as such its ability to grant &quot;extrasensory&quot; perception actually works by bringing things that would normally be out of your sensory range into it.<br /> <br /> But if it can do that for sight, there's no reason to suppose it can't do it for touch. I'd suggest she just uses a slightly modified version of The Outward And Inward Eye that makes it so that rather than seeing and hearing from every point, she <i>feels</i> and hears from every point. Still blind to colors and patterns, but has more information about texture and temperature. Do something similar with Scrying, let her create a window that projects touch instead of vision.<br /> <br /> Actually, does Scrying transmit sound? The description only talks about visuals. If not, make her Scrying window transmit just sound instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-09-2017, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:39:35-07:00","id":1113905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113746#post1113746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you don't. That's the whole point! Because unlike Deny the Reaper or whatever hypothetical Life spell would keep you trucking past your expiration date, you can just re-cast it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-casting it doesn't turn back the clock. <i>That's the whole point</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every problem that Veil of Moments has is a problem it shares with the Indefinite &quot;Make Me Not Die&quot; spells the book mentions, except that it's available at a significantly lower dot rating and losing the spell has no immediate consequence whatsoever. Sure you gotta get the Rote from somewhere, but compared to achieving Mastery of Death or discovering a method to transform into a ghost/spirit/Goetia/bodysnatcher without losing your magical abilities, learning a 2-dot Rote is absolute peanuts. </div> </div> </div>I really don't care about the particulars of how difficult you think learning a given Rote is \u2014 I'm saying you learned it from somewhere <i>and therefore inhabit a system where you are likely expected to do more than putter around being forever-young.</i> If your character's in an Order they very likely have a mentor who asks them to do things for them in exchange for their instruction, and even without the context of a mentor you aren't picking up magical resources for free. You have better things to do with your spell control slots in that environment than devote them to holding back the longest-term threat to your existence as a young Awakened mystic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's also why you don't really need a Demesne or even a Sanctum. Since the spell timing out or getting dispelled isn't a huge problem you only really need to Reach for Advanced Duration and maybe Instant Casting, spend the rest on being able to heal and regain resources, take a symbolic penalty for Duration factors and re-cast every week. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spending the rest on being able to regain resources&quot; costs you every free Reach that you wouldn't be spending on Advanced Duration with a rote. Rotes in turn do nothing to benefit your dicepool besides provide a Yantra \u2014 a Gnosis 2 Time 2 starting character is going to be leaning on the Mudra bonus and whatever other Yantra they choose to keep their dicepool above a coin-flip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Transformative lichdom has its own benefits, but the existence of Veil of Moments as written makes the actions of the Tremere, the hypothetical bodysnatcher liches and those &quot;na\u00efve&quot; mages who put Indefinite Spells of Not Dying on themselves not just dangerous and unethical, but stupid. </div> </div> </div>Veil of Moments 1) does not un-ring the bell of &quot;I have five days left until I hit my expiration date and every second out of this spell is one I'm not getting back&quot; and 2) is a two-dot effect <i>and therefore will disintegrate with relatively small applications of Dissonance or dispellation</i>.<br /> <br /> The existence of Veil of Moments does not imply the widespread quality of Rote forms of Veil of Moments or the universality of Mastery of Time, and in the meanwhile the world has plenty of forces running around that can age a human years in a minute or cast down magic with a glare, including some Supernal beings.<br /> <br /> (Also, as has been pointed out before, the Tremere are not liches <i>for</i> the immortality. Also also, &quot;inexperienced&quot; and &quot;na\u00efve&quot; are not the same thing and it seems self-evidently dishonest to assume every mage is so preoccupied with living forever that not investing in magic cryogenesis is a rookie mistake.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't want to die, why on earth would you become a Reaper with a constant ticking clock over your head or hinge your moment-to-moment existence on a single, easily-cut thread when there's a 2-dot spell that does essentially the same thing without turning you into a target for every mage with a conscience or opening you up to death by dispellation from any disgruntled Initiate of Prime? </div> </div> </div>Power. Efficiencies. Better fringe benefits. A more robust source of agelessness. An actual honest-to-god Mystery to probe. Most routes to immortality are not as fragile as Veil of Moments. Most Reapers are not just messing with souls for a way to live longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:06:45-07:00","id":1113921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113734#post1113734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a bargain have to do with anything, are you saying immortality via lichdom is better because of ongoing bargains? (do they even bargain with anything?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Much of the literature concerning impossibly old characters aging to dust in a very short period of time is related to those characters having turned into things that only keep their youth as long as specific circumstances are met, most commonly staying in a particular area for the rest of their days or trading some good or service to dark forces to keep in abeyance as leverage or consuming some mysterious substance. (Ghouls hit on the third one in withdrawal, but that's at a rate of one year per <i>week</i>.) These are generally accidents or desperate gambits, not the products of an enlightened magus's attempts to preserve a subject over a long time \u2014 there is no meaningful story purpose to having Veil condense all the time you would have aged into one burst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What has CDC diseases got to do with anything? We are discussing the viability of a long duration veil of moments spell increasing ones lifespan, this statement applies how? </div> </div> </div>Veil of Moments holds back things that get worse over time. Aging is one of those things \u2014 a file cabinet full of deadly illnesses are substantially more than one and therefore will advance your death a lot quicker once there's nothing stopping them, but that's because diseases work faster than aging and can come from multiple sources, not because the syphilis you picked up in a lab mutated into Brain-Eating Hyper-Syphilis over the break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again this applies to every other mage also, (not quite sure why you need sleepwalkers to cast a time 2 spell unless you want then hold it for you i suppose) a mage with a perm veil spell has MORE time to collect/save stuff so probably overall will have more resources because they have &quot;lived&quot; longer than another mage. </div> </div> </div>A mage with a permanent Veil of Moments does not meaningfully <i>have</i> more time outside the context of being able to tell the poison coursing through her veins to wait a bit and managing your spell control is vital to minimizing Paradox. Sleepwalkers and Sancta are the two primary means of safely doing this for long-term spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything you have said here applies to every single mage. I get the feeling you think any mage with a long duration veil of moments will get victimized MORE than any other random mage? How so? </div> </div> </div>Your spells and the subjects of your spells attract supernatural complications through the Long-Term Nimbus and if you're leaving spells on your person outside of the auspices of your Shadow Name then you have no meaningful degree of protection from, say, a manifest Anachronism storming through your family reunion. Veil of Moments provides no defensive benefit to dealing with these intrusions, hampers your ability to expand your capabilities, and also takes up a spell control slot to maintain. It's <i>more viable</i> for mages who completely give up on mortal living, but those mages tend to fall into a place where they've got targets painted on their back anyway, at which point you may as well double down and either pick up extra layers of Not Of Natural Causes in your obituary or go full time-travel and either revise your history or skip over any stretches of time that you don't have plans for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:08:28-07:00","id":1113922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Spending the rest on being able to regain resources&quot; costs you every free Reach that you wouldn't be spending on Advanced Duration with a rote. Rotes in turn do nothing to benefit your dicepool besides provide a Yantra \u2014 a Gnosis 2 Time 2 starting character is going to be leaning on the Mudra bonus and whatever other Yantra they choose to keep their dicepool above a coin-flip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who starts with Gnosis 2? All gnosis 2 gives you is 1 more mana for 5 merit points? Assuming gnosis 3, time 2, no rote and you can get yantras for +5 (tattoo runes, high speech and a tool) plus max extra time is 15 dice, 18 with willpower. Your using 5 reaches, advanced duration +4 from the spell, so your 4 over. You can take -6 for 1 year duration leaving 12 dice, 8 dice for paradox which you can reduce by spending mana. (Even gnosis 2, time 2, +4 yantra, +5 max time + willpower is 15 dice, -6 for year long and its 9 dice to cast still easy peasy, no real hassle except 6 hours of your life, probably all your mana if you want to reduce paradox but worth it.<br /> <br /> <i>Q: During ritual casting can you expend your entire mana pool since its taking 6 hours to cast this you can easily spend 8 mana during this time to reduce paradox to a chance dice?</i><br /> <br /> I really think you are underestimating how easy it is to cast it, without even a rote. Your still coming up with stuff that every other mage has to put up with too. Every mage who joins an order to learn rotes needs to pay it off its not like its a drawback specific to somebody who wants a long duration veil of moments spell on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:22:05-07:00","id":1113928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113921#post1113921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much of the literature concerning impossibly old characters aging to dust in a very short period of time is related to those characters having turned into things that only keep their youth as long as specific circumstances are met, most commonly staying in a particular area for the rest of their days or trading some good or service to dark forces to keep in abeyance as leverage or consuming some mysterious substance. (Ghouls hit on the third one in withdrawal, but that's at a rate of one year per <i>week</i>.) These are generally accidents or desperate gambits, not the products of an enlightened magus's attempts to preserve a subject over a long time \u2014 there is no meaningful story purpose to having Veil condense all the time you would have aged into one burst. </div> </div> </div> </div>What does this have to do with Mage the Awakening exactly? I think you are confused, either you think i think that when veils ends your true age catches up with you, or you think that happens? It doesnt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Veil of Moments holds back things that get worse over time. Aging is one of those things \u2014 a file cabinet full of deadly illnesses are substantially more than one and therefore will advance your death a lot quicker once there's nothing stopping them, but that's because diseases work faster than aging and can come from multiple sources, not because the syphilis you picked up in a lab mutated into Brain-Eating Hyper-Syphilis over the break. </div> </div> </div>One reach means you ignore persistant conditions, probably meaning poisons, diseases etc (they are probably conditions) they wont do a damn thing to you while the veil is up? Alittle care and your fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> A mage with a permanent Veil of Moments does not meaningfully <i>have</i> more time outside the context of being able to tell the poison coursing through her veins to wait a bit and managing your spell control is vital to minimizing Paradox. Sleepwalkers and Sancta are the two primary means of safely doing this for long-term spells.<br /> <br /> Your spells and the subjects of your spells attract supernatural complications through the Long-Term Nimbus and if you're leaving spells on your person outside of the auspices of your Shadow Name then you have no meaningful degree of protection from, say, a manifest Anachronism storming through your family reunion. Veil of Moments provides no defensive benefit to dealing with these intrusions, hampers your ability to expand your capabilities, and also takes up a spell control slot to maintain. It's <i>more viable</i> for mages who completely give up on mortal living, but those mages tend to fall into a place where they've got targets painted on their back anyway, at which point you may as well double down and either pick up extra layers of Not Of Natural Causes in your obituary or go full time-travel and either revise your history or skip over any stretches of time that you don't have plans for. </div> </div> </div>What does having spells outside the auspices of your shadow name, (assuming you have one) do exactly? Mechanically, maybe something Long-Term Nimbus wise i grant you but that is basically St fluff and rarely will have an uber effect on anything. Where are these intrusions coming from and why do they hate a mage who casts a long term veil on himself over other mages who are off doing other random stuff probably much much worse? Your now just pulling stuff out of thin air?<br /> <br /> I give up, by raw its stupidly easy for somebody with time 2 to hold off aging for a really long time, you have come up with various dubious means as to how this would be a hindrance and alot of which baffle me but apart from dick enemy mages dispelling it and you dont survive to recast it, you have yet to convince me it wouldnt be worth doing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:36:51-07:00","id":1113936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113734#post1113734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes i think you use really long complex sentences just to troll people? I understand all the words but completely miss the content. What does a bargain have to do with anything, are you saying immortality via lichdom is better because of ongoing bargains? (do they even bargain with anything?).What has CDC diseases got to do with anything? We are discussing the viability of a long duration veil of moments spell increasing ones lifespan, this statement applies how?<br /> What about aging is a single source of damage, what does this even mean? Time doesnt catch up with you when the veil is canceled, its paused under it and just resumes when it stops. cast it at 21, keep it up for a 90 years (might be recast but its not down enough to count), your still 21 but really 111 you dont suddenly age to 111. Dying from dozens of other ways applies to every mage not just one with a veil of moments on. Why would this be any more of a problem for a mage with a veil?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this seems harsh but nearly every answer you give is long winded, esoteric almost and i usually have to go lie down in a dark room after reading them, maybe its just me i dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rule 2. Respect the conversation.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Don\u2019t try to incite others to break the rules, or distract from the subject at hand. This includes threadcrapping, the posting of short messages or images which add nothing to a thread and serve only to express a user\u2019s displeasure with it.</span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You are not required to read or respond to standard user posts (or even black-text posts by moderators!) within a thread that you are participating in. You are required to be respectful of the conversation and those taking part in it.</span></span></span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":9,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","user":"Sparketh","date":". 07-09-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:04:18-07:00","id":1113944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-casting it doesn't turn back the clock. <i>That's the whole point</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a big deal. Unless something goes horribly wrong you'll never be without the spell for more than a few minutes, hours at the most. Maybe that starts to catch up to you after 1000 years, but good luck existing that long in any form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't care about the particulars of how difficult you think learning a given Rote is \u2014 I'm saying you learned it from somewhere <i>and therefore inhabit a system where you are likely expected to do more than putter around being forever-young.</i> If your character's in an Order they very likely have a mentor who asks them to do things for them in exchange for their instruction, and even without the context of a mentor you aren't picking up magical resources for free. You have better things to do with your spell control slots in that environment than devote them to holding back the longest-term threat to your existence as a young Awakened mystic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dropping the spell for a bit when you need the slots isn't a big deal either, especially if you're young. But this isn't really about Gnosis 1 babies, this is about people who are seriously considering becoming liches. The fact that it's available at character creation is mostly relevant in that it shows how much easier it is to achieve than every other form of lichdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Spending the rest on being able to regain resources&quot; costs you every free Reach that you wouldn't be spending on Advanced Duration with a rote. Rotes in turn do nothing to benefit your dicepool besides provide a Yantra \u2014 a Gnosis 2 Time 2 starting character is going to be leaning on the Mudra bonus and whatever other Yantra they choose to keep their dicepool above a coin-flip.</div> </div> </div> </div>4 dice is already a 75% chance of success. Assuming a modest Mudra skill rating of 2, the use of a Mantra (+2) and taking a -2 penalty to bump the Duration up lands you at 6 dice and ~90% chance of success. Increasing the dice pool through extended ritual casting, higher Gnosis/Time/Skill and more yantras (if available) trivializes the roll completely. It's true you can't safely cast the full version at a moment's notice, but casting an incomplete version (that doesn't let you regain Mana, say) is quite enough until you can get to safety and do a proper ritual casting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veil of Moments 1) does not un-ring the bell of &quot;I have five days left until I hit my expiration date and every second out of this spell is one I'm not getting back&quot; and 2) is a two-dot effect <i>and therefore will disintegrate with relatively small applications of Dissonance or dispellation</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you here. It's not a fantastic solution when you're already at death's door - though still better than any of those Indefinite spells, because 5 days you can dip into in an emergency is much better than no days.<br /> <br /> I hadn't actually considered Dissonance, but it doesn't seem like that big of a deal - it only applies if a mortal realizes you are unnaturally ageless, and any still-human lich will need to take steps to prevent that from happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of Veil of Moments does not imply the widespread quality of Rote forms of Veil of Moments or the universality of Mastery of Time and in the meanwhile the world has plenty of forces running around that can age a human years in a minute or cast down magic with a glare, including some Supernal beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor is there anything that implies it's rarer than a Rote of any other 2-dot spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, as has been pointed out before, the Tremere are not liches <i>for</i> the immortality. Also also, &quot;inexperienced&quot; and &quot;na\u00efve&quot; are not the same thing and it seems self-evidently dishonest to assume every mage is so preoccupied with living forever that not investing in magic cryogenesis is a rookie mistake.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I misread the wiki. I thought it said they were Reapers to sustain their lichdom, but it's the other way around.<br /> That is not my assumption, though. My assumption is that most mages who <i>are</i> preoccupied with living forever would think to check if maybe there exist any simple Time spells that halt aging indefinitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113905#post1113905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power. Efficiencies. Better fringe benefits. A more robust source of agelessness. An actual honest-to-god Mystery to probe. Most routes to immortality are not as fragile as Veil of Moments. Most Reapers are not just messing with souls for a way to live longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still contend that it is more robust than many source of immortality that are harder to achieve, which is my whole beef. It's obviously safer than a Spell Of Not Dying, but recasting a spell every now and then is also a hell of a lot more expedient than stealing souls with about the same frequency - and a hell of a lot less likely to bring the Pentacle hammer crashing down on your head. Even stealing a new body every ~30 years is arguably a bigger hassle, depending on your Gnosis, how badly you need that spell slot and how likely you are to get your spell removed, but Veil of Moments is still hugely more ethical.<br /> <br /> Transformative lichdom is obviously a different story, and while it sidesteps a lot of the issues other liches have, you do have to be willing to give up your humanity.<br /> <br /> Which is ultimately why I don't like Veil of Moments. Llichdom is described as both difficult and either dangerous to the point of idiocy (Spell Of Not Dying), deeply unethical (Tremere, bodysnatching) or requiring you to completely sacrifice your humanity (ghost-liches, spirit-liches etc.). Veil of Moments bypasses every single one of these points, providing an easy, safe, morally uncomplicated and wholly untransformative means of near-indefinite longevity for anyone who wants it. Apart from a few edge cases it completely removes the archetype of the decent human being driven to extremes by the sympathetic motivation of not wanting to die (because that person would just use Veil of Moments rather than resort to any of the other methods) and leaves you only with the dick-pistons who kill for convenience and the weirdos who just really want to be Goetia for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is the last I will say on the matter, because I think we've derailed this thread badly enough as it is. If you still don't see my point of view, I think we'll have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-09-2017, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:53:54-07:00","id":1113962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113884#post1113884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Space technically has the ability to pipe information about the landscape right into your head. That's the province of Matter/Spirit/Forces/Life/etc. as appropriate. It controls distance and direction, and as such its ability to grant &quot;extrasensory&quot; perception actually works by bringing things that would normally be out of your sensory range into it.<br /> <br /> But if it can do that for sight, there's no reason to suppose it can't do it for touch. I'd suggest she just uses a slightly modified version of The Outward And Inward Eye that makes it so that rather than seeing and hearing from every point, she <i>feels</i> and hears from every point. Still blind to colors and patterns, but has more information about texture and temperature. Do something similar with Scrying, let her create a window that projects touch instead of vision.<br /> <br /> Actually, does Scrying transmit sound? The description only talks about visuals. If not, make her Scrying window transmit just sound instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might have to change the way my character acts and does things a little bit if that's how it works. DM tried using a work around with using an artifact necklace with an eye rune on it to occasionally see out of and I'd sometimes consider making the character scry on herself to sort of look around from a third person view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:16:30-07:00","id":1113968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113944#post1113944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this isn't really about Gnosis 1 babies, this is about people who are seriously considering becoming liches. The fact that it's available at character creation is mostly relevant in that it shows how much easier it is to achieve than every other form of lichdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're comparing either a spell that you cast singularly or irregularly or a non-spell that you do regularly or singularly to buy time or obviate the question of age with <i>nigh-constant use of a spell</i> to save up your lifespan. People don't work like that. Mages are not normally ideal automatons prioritizing the long game over more their more immediate fears, desires, and obsessions.<br /> <br /> There's also the obvious fact that most characters are not PCs with relatively free run of the creation mechanics and variable investment in the events of the story \u2014 your Contact in the next Caucus may have no idea where you learned your starting rotes, the story's antagonist doesn't default to severing all ties with the parts of the world he loves just because it would be mechanically optimal, and your fellow Apprentice of Time could have hang-ups about magical stasis that have nothing to do with the effects of Veil of Moments relative to becoming a pure being of manifest Resonance. NPCs don't have the option of choosing their Path or making up Mentors or learning any rote that theoretically exists without cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 dice is already a 75% chance of success. </div> </div> </div>I've had multiple failures come up on higher dicepools and the chances of failure are part of the way that Paradox builds up. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor is there anything that implies it's rarer than a Rote of any other 2-dot spell. </div> </div> </div>Environments vary \u2014 can you honestly claim that, say, a grimoire detailing Psychic Domination would be considered equally lendable to a grimoire containing Soul Armor in the eyes of most mentors? Do you foresee an Acanthus Master prioritizing Veil over something like Choose the Thread or Warding Gesture for spending their time codifying an Imago? Do you imagine that no mage with access to the rote has ever realized its potential for budget immortality and sought to leverage it accordingly? These resources do not exist in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is not my assumption, though. My assumption is that most mages who <i>are</i> preoccupied with living forever would think to check if maybe there exist any simple Time spells that halt aging indefinitely. </div> </div> </div>Your assumption is that most mages who are preoccupied with living forever are more worried about dying of old age in a lifestyle that has biting off more than you can chew as a common hazard of living it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still contend that it is more robust than many source of immortality that are harder to achieve, which is my whole beef. It's obviously safer than a Spell Of Not Dying, but recasting a spell every now and then is also a hell of a lot more expedient than stealing souls with about the same frequency - and a hell of a lot less likely to bring the Pentacle hammer crashing down on your head. Even stealing a new body every ~30 years is arguably a bigger hassle, depending on your Gnosis, how badly you need that spell slot and how likely you are to get your spell removed, but Veil of Moments is still hugely more ethical. </div> </div> </div>It's hugely more ethical if you have that leg to stand on and substantially less viable the instant you run afoul of a creature that eats magic or drinks lifespans or requires magic you haven't learned yet. (And heaven help you if you lose your soul at any point.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Veil of Moments bypasses every single one of these points, providing an easy, safe, morally uncomplicated and wholly untransformative means of near-indefinite longevity for anyone who wants it. </div> </div> </div>And &quot;all&quot; it costs you is your ability to grow while it's active. Raising Gnosis calls for unforgettable milestones of paradigm-shifting developments of your understanding, and doesn't-say argument about the mechanics of spending Experience aside I don't think those mesh well with putting off the expenditure until you have some spare safe downtime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apart from a few edge cases it completely removes the archetype of the decent human being driven to extremes by the sympathetic motivation of not wanting to die (because that person would just use Veil of Moments rather than resort to any of the other methods) </div> </div> </div>Again, the assumption you're very blatantly carrying into this is that every mage prioritizes delving into the mysteries of prophecy and temporal suspension well before they start worrying about their inevitable mortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and leaves you only with the dick-pistons who kill for convenience and the weirdos who just really want to be Goetia for whatever reason. </div> </div> </div>This is the uncomfortable part of the discussion where I remind you what losing Wisdom does to your psychology and what the Awakening already implies for it. These are not mild-mannered people who just so happen to be able to bend the universe around their block, they are obsessive pursuers of mystical power.<br /> <br /> The complications of being a mage and the realities of this being a storytelling game mean Veil of Moments does not actually break the setting's inclusion of less genteel forms of lichdom outside the unlikely scenario of your character seeking to teach every mage they meet Time 2 and the rote in question; nothing prevents a Nameless Order that collectively casts Veil of Moments and Warding Gesture as rotes once a year, but that doesn't do anything to mitigate the existence of soul-eating Reapers or isolated domains without a resident Acanthus. The world goes on suboptimally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T19:21:34-07:00","id":1113989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113844#post1113844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a blind mage specializing in space to compensate for her vision. Had the character go blind from her awakening. With going with this character flaw and avoiding to use life magic, what would the character see when using the benefits of space, such as The Outward and Inner Eye or Scrying? I wasn't sure if for the former it would just kind of result in a sort of Daredevil/Spidey-Sense or if she would mentally see something when using it or Scrying. Other players I'm with can't come to an agreement over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ST might allow the following option to the spell:<br /> +1 Reach: Add Mind \u2022 and receive the information directly into your mind instead of relying on your eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-09-2017, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T19:47:55-07:00","id":1114002,"title":"","content":"Adding an arcana typically doesn't require adding a Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T19:54:27-07:00","id":1114004,"title":"","content":"Most of the time, no, but I thought this added some extra functionality that would merit a Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:22:30-07:00","id":1114012,"title":"","content":"It's just my opinion, but extra function for any spell should be granted either by Reach, or by adding a conjunctional arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:56:46-07:00","id":1114022,"title":"","content":"While my belief is that conjunctional Arcana primarily just extends the purview of the spell, such as Matter on a Life transformation allowing you to transform your clothes along with your body, and the entire Death/Mind/Spirit thing allowing those spells to also function on ghosts/goetia/spirits, rather than adding extra functionality to the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:15:16-07:00","id":1114032,"title":"","content":"I think the point that Satchel is trying to make, is that though the Veil of Moment's does pause the clock of your lifespan for it's duration, it isn't so much immortality as it is prolonging life - as whenever the spell is not active, your clock is still ticking.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, at that particular level, it's a moot point until you reach the point where your walking around for thousands of years.However - this is still not a good form of immortality compared to some of the others. A better alternative than say, the tremere's lichdom, but as was pointed out - if you're a tremere for immortality, you are doing it for the wrong reasons (Tremere are Reapers first and foremost - immortality is just a bonus). That said - with the Veil of Moments, you are sacrificing -something- in exchange for those precious saved seconds.<br /> <br /> You are sacrificing growth.<br /> <br /> Now - mechanically of course, it's easy enough to drop the spell, spend &quot;X&quot; experience, and then put the spell back up. But that's a purely mechanical expression of a significant amount of effort - increasing traits, growing, and moving forward is far beyond the course of simply 'expending experience points'. The narrative is far more in depth when you think about it - your knowledge doesn't increase from an initiates to a disciples over the course of a few seconds - expending that increase represents training, study, and precious effort put into actually trying to grow, things which take time - things that, while the spell is active, are all frozen. No matter how much studying you do - nothing seems to stay. No matter how much exercise you do, you don't grow more healthy or less healthy. You simply 'exist'. For a person, this kind of lichdom might work - simply 'existing', because you are so afraid of death you are willing to be frozen in place. But for a mage, this kind of lichdom is an anathema far worse than altering yourself into a different kind of immortal being, using death mastery to take efforts not to die, or even stealing other people's bodies or years. At least the Lich's who become ghosts or steal bodies have a certain amount of respect and fear from Awakened Society - the mage who chooses not to grow in exchange for life would be viewed with little more than pity and contempt.<br /> <br /> ... At least, that's my view on it anyways, and what the limitation of not being able to spend experiences seems like it's supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> ... Though that kind of explanation does, admittedly, fall flat when a player tries to spend experiences towards raising their contacts or a trait that is not 'internal' and shouldn't be effected by the spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:35:46-07:00","id":1114040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1113844#post1113844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a blind mage specializing in space to compensate for her vision. Had the character go blind from her awakening. With going with this character flaw and avoiding to use life magic, what would the character see when using the benefits of space, such as The Outward and Inner Eye or Scrying? I wasn't sure if for the former it would just kind of result in a sort of Daredevil/Spidey-Sense or if she would mentally see something when using it or Scrying. Other players I'm with can't come to an agreement over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, utilizing the Outward and Inner Eye would effectively allow the blind caster to have a perfect spatial awareness... which basically just means that in combat they don't need to roll in order to figure out where a person is, because the spell will allow for that. I do not believe this would grant the user of the spell sight, however. Instead, it would focus on the other aspect of the spell - sound. The user would be able to take the sounds a person makes - breathing, stepping, etc - and would be able to achieve a perfect sense of spatial relation between themselves and that sound.<br /> <br /> ... So yeah, basically Daredevil I guess. Echolocation and all that jazz. You could be cool about it and use smell in place of sight if you wanted. I wouldn't use touch myself - mostly because touching is a mutual thing and should be felt by both parties rather than just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:36:12-07:00","id":1114042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1114032#post1114032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Though that kind of explanation does, admittedly, fall flat when a player tries to spend experiences towards raising their contacts or a trait that is not 'internal' and shouldn't be effected by the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of those cases where the Arcana really emphasize their patron Path \u2014 the Acanthus archetypically seek to be able to pick and choose their connections, and from an unWise perspective it's not hard to see how rewriting history or Fating some incidental reason for people to do you favors is more appealing than spending normal Experiences you could have put towards branching out in the Arcana or expanding your influence in the Caucus on prosaic benefits like having a legal team on retainer or building a stock portfolio. As with the default spell's caveat for magical healing, there's no need to worry about whether mystical protosympathy can permeate your stasis field to let the relationship solidify.<br /> <br /> (Another point in favor of constant Veiling being better-suited to folks who're shooting for Mastery anyway: Time in a Bottle frees up an entire Reach for setting the thing up quickly, thoroughly, and without fuss.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T07:26:24-07:00","id":1114144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel<