ic Name though...<br /> <br /> If it were me and I were a Mastigos I'd start with Mind flavored Focused Mage Sight which well could give me the identity of the AERW but if not then I would proceed contact a Thyrsus to act as a middle man for a Spirit with Omen/Seek/Pathfinder, or cheat and Summon a Daemon with Omen, Pathfinder, and/or Seek and ask them what the name is or how to find either the name or caster themselves. Or I'd bolster an appropriate Goetia to gain those powers and handle it myself. Then I'd report my findings to the appropriate Mage authorities, which may include myself or not depending on local politics. Ephemeral beings potential abilities are pretty terrifying.<br /> <br /> Also why did nothing with premonition powers detect this before it started? There are so many beings with those powers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-18-2017, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T21:36:02-07:00","id":1118067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1117913#post1117913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds like a Mystery! Focused Mage Sight to break through the levels of Opacity.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> 40 days and nights is a lot of time to investigate. Being under the effect which when I check my Spacial Sympathetic connection chart indicates a Weak connection, but lacking a Sympathetic Name of the Anonymous Emo-Rain Warlock (AERW for short) knocks that down to less than useful...<br /> <br /> Soon as we get a Sympathetic Name though...<br /> <br /> If it were me and I were a Mastigos I'd start with Mind flavored Focused Mage Sight which well could give me the identity of the AERW but if not then I would proceed contact a Thyrsus to act as a middle man for a Spirit with Omen/Seek/Pathfinder, or cheat and Summon a Daemon with Omen, Pathfinder, and/or Seek and ask them what the name is or how to find either the name or caster themselves. Or I'd bolster an appropriate Goetia to gain those powers and handle it myself. Then I'd report my findings to the appropriate Mage authorities, which may include myself or not depending on local politics. Ephemeral beings potential abilities are pretty terrifying.<br /> <br /> Also why did nothing with premonition powers detect this before it started? There are so many beings with those powers...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> not knowing a name only means you need +1 potency, not a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T06:31:24-07:00","id":1118148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1118067#post1118067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> not knowing a name only means you need +1 potency, not a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh? Let me check the page number of that....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA pg 172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sympathetic Names</b></span><br /> In the womb, a human being has only a Connected link to her mother and a Strong one to her genetic father. At birth, this shifts to a Strong link to both parents and other primary caregivers, whether related or not, but babies don\u2019t otherwise form sympathetic links until the sense of self develops. Once the Lie sets in that the world is separate from the self, a child begins to form her own links. Even in adulthood, everyone\u2019s sympathetic links bear a permanent reminder of that early time \u2014 the name that those with links to a baby think of her as becomes indelibly marked in her Pattern as her <b>sympathetic name</b>.<br /> No matter how many times a person changes her name through childhood and adulthood, once she forms links of her own the sympathetic name is set, and is both weakness and protection \u2014 speaking a person\u2019s sympathetic name counts as a Yantra as per <b>p. 122</b>, but not knowing it makes affecting her at range more difficult, increasing the Withstand level against the Sympathetic Range Attainment by one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems your absolutely correct. For some reason I thought it reduced the strength of the connection a step on the table but that isn't so. So in that case it'd be immediately solvable with anyone with the Space 2, and from there they can use the Space 2 Attainment as soon as they get a Yantra (perhaps the massive emo-rain shower would be a good yantra?) to do all sorts of awful things to said being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T06:38:10-07:00","id":1118150,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T11:37:48-07:00","id":1118226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1118150#post1118150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry what?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being under the effects of somebodies spell gives you a weak connection to the caster, if this transfers to being under the effects of non supernal &quot;magic&quot; then all it takes is somebody with space 2 to solve who is causing the 40 days of rain. Technically space 1 can use correspondence to track the connection with its reach effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 07-19-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T12:26:15-07:00","id":1118240,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's unwise to do things that would likely alert those with prophetic ability ranging from Mehket and Cahalith Dreams, Knowing Practice of the Time and Fate Arcanum, the Omen Trance Numina used by Ghosts/Spirits/Geotia/Horrors and even the mortal merits of Cursed and Omen Sensitivity weeks or months in advance.<br /> Maybe it is unwise make an obviously supernatural effect so large it could be called a biblical plague without irony and would alert any beings hunting for the supernatural (which funny enough includes mages and others with build in magic detection ability) to search for you.<br /> <br /> Mostly the first part though be odds of no one catching you before you do that is SLIM.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons the setting (supernatural conspiracies) remains intact, people have those powers but use of those powers are foreseen and thwarted. Yay! Prophetic Plots/Quests!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-19-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:26:58-07:00","id":1118353,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I could've sworn that this was answered somewhere, but I can't find it. If you have a Rote with a given encoded skill, if someone learns it from you do they HAVE to use that same skill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:53:36-07:00","id":1118372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1118353#post1118353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I could've sworn that this was answered somewhere, but I can't find it. If you have a Rote with a given encoded skill, if someone learns it from you do they HAVE to use that same skill?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how an encoded Skill in a Mudra works, yes. There's not much weight to codifying a mnemonic to use knowledge of a certain Skill if that codification doesn't actually use knowledge of that Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T18:57:35-07:00","id":1119138,"title":"","content":"Sanctum grants extra spell control while you're in the space, but the bonus goes away when you're not in the Sanctum. Is that correct? If so, why bother with a Sanctum? When am I ever going to need to cast a bunch of spells with long durations while staying at home for the entire duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T19:19:51-07:00","id":1119141,"title":"","content":"Because you can cast them at the Sanctum and then leave to do other stuff with the spells still active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T20:25:38-07:00","id":1119156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119138#post1119138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctum grants extra spell control while you're in the space, but the bonus goes away when you're not in the Sanctum. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> You can cast spells in your Sanctum as though your spell control were [Sanctum dots] higher, and spells in excess of your normal spell control don't require you to spend extra Reach until you've exceeded your expanded spell control, although subsequent spells still treat the required extra Reach as though your normal spell control had been exceeded by the number of active spells rather than your expanded spell control.<br /> <br /> You can have a normal spell control limit of 3, fill that up with long-term spells, and then you'll need to duck into your Sanctum if you want to cast another spell without spending Reach on exceeding spell control; if, in this situation, you have a two-dot Sanctum and take up both of those extra slots, casting another spell inside or outside your Sanctum is going to cost three extra Reach even though if you had just one fewer spells active you would just have to spend two extra Reach if you were outside your Sanctum and none inside it.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons full-time mages value their ritual spaces, much like how Master-level free Reach makes rotes useful for walking around at maximum holding capacity and still being able to throw a mudra. If you find something interesting and you want to analyze it, you use sensory spells you have in your rotes or specialty Arcana, risk Paradox, or bring it back to the lab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Screwed up the math. 07-21-2017, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T20:27:40-07:00","id":1119157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119141#post1119141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you can cast them at the Sanctum and then leave to do other stuff with the spells still active.</div> </div> </div> </div>And eat lots of paradox if you want to cast anything else? That doesn't seem really helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T20:38:22-07:00","id":1119159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119156#post1119156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> You can cast spells in your Sanctum as though your spell control were [Sanctum dots] higher, and spells in excess of your normal spell control don't require you to spend extra Reach until you've exceeded your expanded spell control, although subsequent spells still treat the required extra Reach as though your normal spell control had been exceeded by the number of active spells rather than your expanded spell control.<br /> <br /> You can have a normal spell control limit of 3, fill that up with long-term spells, and then you'll need to duck into your Sanctum if you want to cast another spell without spending Reach on exceeding spell control; if, in this situation, you have a two-dot Sanctum and take up both of those extra slots, casting another spell inside or outside your Sanctum is going to cost three extra Reach even though if you had just one fewer spells active you'd only have to spend one extra Reach if you were outside your Sanctum and none inside it.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons full-time mages value their ritual spaces, much like how Master-level free Reach makes rotes useful for walking around at maximum holding capacity and still being able to throw a mudra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you said the same thing I did, more or less.<br /> <br /> Ok, I'll be more specific.<br /> <br /> Mad Alice is a starting mage with Gnosis 1 and Sanctum 1. Normally she can have one spell actively controlled before she needs to reach. However, in her sanctum, she can control two spells at once without reaching. However, if she casts two spells in her sanctum, leaves, and then tries to cast another spell, she has to reach as much as she would have to normally as if she didn't have the sanctum.<br /> <br /> And it's that last part that confuses me. Why bother with a sanctum if it doesn't actually let you get &quot;extra&quot; spells? What do you use it for? Defense on your home turf? To sacrifice your flexibility for a bunch of long term buffs? I don't really get the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T20:48:28-07:00","id":1119160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119159#post1119159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's that last part that confuses me. Why bother with a sanctum if it doesn't actually let you get &quot;extra&quot; spells? What do you use it for? Defense on your home turf? To sacrifice your flexibility for a bunch of long term buffs? I don't really get the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is not a death sentence, especially at low Gnosis, and apprentices are not the ones getting the maximum benefit out of Sancta outside the context of having a concrete threshold to drop and resume their Shadow Names.<br /> <br /> Sanctums work in a way that incentivizes powerful mages with a lot of ongoing projects to cloister themselves, learn and codify formalized Imagoes, spend a shitload of Mana, act through proxies and students, and seize/cultivate personal territories where they can freely work their wills. If they are leaving their Sancta, it is often under the sympathetic protection of a nonmagical identity that does not benefit from being conflated with spellcasting.<br /> <br /> It's explicitly a place for you to practice the Art in relative safety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-21-2017, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:01:46-07:00","id":1119165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119160#post1119160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is not a death sentence, especially at low Gnosis, and apprentices are not the ones getting the maximum benefit out of Sancta outside the context of having a concrete threshold to drop and resume their Shadow Names.<br /> <br /> Sanctums work in a way that incentivizes powerful mages with a lot of ongoing projects to cloister themselves, learn and codify formalized Imagoes, spend a shitload of Mana, act through proxies and students, and seize/cultivate personal territories where they can freely work their wills. If they are leaving their Sancta, it is often under the sympathetic protection of a nonmagical identity that does not benefit from being conflated with spellcasting.<br /> <br /> It's explicitly a place for you to practice the Art in relative safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, then you would NOT recommend for a starting character to &quot;waste&quot; their merit dots on a Sanctum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:21:54-07:00","id":1119175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119165#post1119165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then you would NOT recommend for a starting character to &quot;waste&quot; their merit dots on a Sanctum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, the benefit is largely wasted on low Gnosis Mages who don't have much metaphysical breathing room to spare anyway. Depending on the Mage it might be useful to start off, but they'd have to be really good at premeditating what spells might be the most useful to have active that they'd be willing to give up spontaneous casting for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:25:29-07:00","id":1119177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119165#post1119165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then you would NOT recommend for a starting character to &quot;waste&quot; their merit dots on a Sanctum?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend pooling them as part of a cabal or requisitioning them with Order Status and/or Infamous Mentor rather than trying to become totally self-sufficient straight out of the gate. Its primary value is as a place to experiment with your Arcana and exert more of your power than you could bring to bear outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T03:00:45-07:00","id":1119215,"title":"","content":"I apologize if this has been asked before; it seems like a topic that has probably already been discussed to oblivion, but searching the forum did return any pertinent results.<br /> <br /> What is the reasoning behind Hung Spell's being a spell and not an attainment? Is it so that it can be keyed off Duration? To hang a spell, a mage either has to cast it as a combined spell, or (if one's Gnosis is less than 3) requisition help from another Apprentice of Time. Which, I suppose, encourages cooperation, trading of favors, guanxi, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T03:38:42-07:00","id":1119217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119215#post1119215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if this has been asked before; it seems like a topic that has probably already been discussed to oblivion, but searching the forum did return any pertinent results.<br /> <br /> What is the reasoning behind Hung Spell's being a spell and not an attainment? Is it so that it can be keyed off Duration? To hang a spell, a mage either has to cast it as a combined spell, or (if one's Gnosis is less than 3) requisition help from another Apprentice of Time. Which, I suppose, encourages cooperation, trading of favors, guanxi, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, i always just assumed you cast hung spell, then the spell you wanted hung after it. But yeh you may be right in that it needs a combined casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T04:09:04-07:00","id":1119222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119217#post1119217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm, i always just assumed you cast hung spell, then the spell you wanted hung after it. But yeh you may be right in that it needs a combined casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you cast the hung spell and then you cast the spell that is to be captured. The clue to that is in the highlighted portion of the spell that is below. You can capture multiple spells within the Hung spell. You capture your potency in spells. At potency 5 you can capture 5 spells. If you needed to cast the hung spell and the spell that it captures at the same time as a combo spell there is no way that you would be able to cast 5 spells + the hung spell. Also other mages can cast spells in a Hung spell that you cast. Look at the blue section that I highlighted. If you needed to cast it as a combined spell there is no way that another mage could cast a spell to be suspended by your Hung spell.<br /> <br /> The way that the hung spell works is that you cast the Hung spell and then you cast, or other mages if your scale is larger then 1, cast the spell(s) that are to be suspended in the Hung spell until the Hung spell has its potency in spells suspended.<br /> <br /> Hung Spell (Time \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Occult, Expression<br /> With this spell, the mage captures pure expressions of magic \u2014<br /> spells \u2014 at the moment they enter the Fallen World, suspending<br /> them before they take effect but preserving their Duration from<br /> decay. <b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">The subject must be a mage</span>,</b> who must deliberately build<br /> his Imago to take advantage of this spell\u2019s effect and pay one<br /> Mana when casting. <b>Hung Spell may entrap up to its Potency<br /> in spells, which remain in their caster\u2019s spell control but do not<br /> take effect until Hung Spell is canceled or runs out of Duration</b>.<br /> When Hung Spell ceases, the trapped spells immediately take<br /> effect and begin their own Durations.<br /> Many mages use the Fate 2 Attainment to set a Conditional<br /> Duration on Hung Spell, so that it releases the trapped spells<br /> in response to set conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 07-22-2017, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T04:42:27-07:00","id":1119225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119222#post1119222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No you cast the hung spell and then you cast the spell that is to be captured. The clue to that is in the highlighted portion of the spell that is below. You can capture multiple spells within the Hung spell. You capture your potency in spells. At potency 5 you can capture 5 spells. If you needed to cast the hung spell and the spell that it captures at the same time as a combo spell there is no way that you would be able to cast 5 spells + the hung spell. Also other mages can cast spells in a Hung spell that you cast. Look at the blue section that I highlighted. If you needed to cast it as a combined spell there is no way that another mage could cast a spell to be suspended by your Hung spell.<br /> <br /> The way that the hung spell works is that you cast the Jung spell and then you cast, or other mages if your scale is larger then 1, cast the spell(s) that are to be suspended in the Hung spell until the Hung spell has its potency in spells suspended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. It's the &quot;at the moment they enter the Fallen World&quot; line that made me believe that Hung Spell had to be cast simultaneously with the target spell or spells.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T04:49:56-07:00","id":1119228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119215#post1119215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if this has been asked before; it seems like a topic that has probably already been discussed to oblivion, but searching the forum did return any pertinent results.<br /> <br /> What is the reasoning behind Hung Spell's being a spell and not an attainment? Is it so that it can be keyed off Duration? To hang a spell, a mage either has to cast it as a combined spell, or (if one's Gnosis is less than 3) requisition help from another Apprentice of Time. Which, I suppose, encourages cooperation, trading of favors, guanxi, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably because each Arcanum has exactly one 2-dot Attainment (plus mage armor) and Time really needed to have Temporal Sympathy. Warding Gesture is a spell for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> As people have said, you don't need a combined spell - you can cast Hung Spell and then the spells you wish to hang. It's still mainly useful for higher-Gnosis mages at it eats into you spell control, but a novice can always get help, use a sanctum - or eat some Paradox. Come on, what's the worst that could happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T04:55:40-07:00","id":1119229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119225#post1119225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see. It's the &quot;at the moment they enter the Fallen World&quot; line that made me believe that Hung Spell had to be cast simultaneously with the target spell or spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Hung spell is waiting in the background waiting for the spell to enter the Fallen World and then it suspends its duration. Remember you must build the imago of the spell to take advantage of the Hung spell. Meaning that you can not capture someone else's spells in your Hung spell if they do not want you to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T12:29:57-07:00","id":1119601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119228#post1119228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably because each Arcanum has exactly one 2-dot Attainment (plus mage armor) and Time really needed to have Temporal Sympathy. Warding Gesture is a spell for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> As people have said, you don't need a combined spell - you can cast Hung Spell and then the spells you wish to hang. It's still mainly useful for higher-Gnosis mages at it eats into you spell control, but a novice can always get help, use a sanctum - or eat some Paradox. Come on, what's the worst that could happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaaactually, it's for game balance. <br /> <br /> Well, a little of both.<br /> <br /> Yes, we didn'l like Time having two level-2 Attainments, but we experimented with doing it the other way around, making a new Attainment for Space and folding all sympathy up into spell factors. The final set up (sympathy is an Attainment, Hung Spell is a spell) was designed to put effort in the right places, and to take up an extra Spell Control slot for mages using trigger-firing spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T12:36:27-07:00","id":1119602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1119601#post1119601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aaaaaactually, it's for game balance.<br /> <br /> Well, a little of both.<br /> <br /> Yes, we didn'l like Time having two level-2 Attainments, but we experimented with doing it the other way around, making a new Attainment for Space and folding all sympathy up into spell factors. The final set up (sympathy is an Attainment, Hung Spell is a spell) was designed to put effort in the right places, and to take up an extra Spell Control slot for mages using trigger-firing spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks for clarifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:13:41-07:00","id":1120035,"title":"","content":"The Ban and Bane of ephemeral entities seems to function very similarly (In terms of theme not necessarily mechanics) to a Destiny and Doom. Do you think that it's a close enough equivalent that you could manipulate a Ban or Bane with Fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T00:05:24-07:00","id":1122932,"title":"","content":"If your spell lasts 1 turn, and you miss your touch attempt, does it fizzle out?<br /> <br /> If your spell lasts 3 turns, and you miss your touch attempt, does it lose 1 turn off its duration but still allow you to make another touch attempt on your next turn? Meaning you don't have to recast, but it's still occupying a spell slot?<br /> <br /> If you miss an aimed spell, no matter the duration, it's gone - meaning you have to cast it all over again to use it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:20:15-07:00","id":1123040,"title":"","content":"For a spell that grants super senses a la Daredevil would you folks model it as a high reach option on an unveiling spell or a perfecting spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T19:00:50-07:00","id":1123269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1122932#post1122932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your spell lasts 1 turn, and you miss your touch attempt, does it fizzle out?<br /> <br /> If your spell lasts 3 turns, and you miss your touch attempt, does it lose 1 turn off its duration but still allow you to make another touch attempt on your next turn? Meaning you don't have to recast, but it's still occupying a spell slot?<br /> <br /> If you miss an aimed spell, no matter the duration, it's gone - meaning you have to cast it all over again to use it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1: Yes.<br /> 2: Yes.<br /> 3: Unclear. The way I'd rule it though, if it hits an applicable target after you miss then it takes effect on that new target. If it doesn't, and it still has Duration remaining, you might be able to get over there pick it up and throw it again before its Duration runs out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T19:01:46-07:00","id":1123271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123040#post1123040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a spell that grants super senses a la Daredevil would you folks model it as a high reach option on an unveiling spell or a perfecting spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on if you're granting yourself supernatural senses by enhancing the ones you already have or giving yourself new ones that you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T19:02:22-07:00","id":1123272,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Ban and Bane of ephemeral entities seems to function very similarly (In terms of theme not necessarily mechanics) to a Destiny and Doom. Do you think that it's a close enough equivalent that you could manipulate a Ban or Bane with Fate?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T23:27:55-07:00","id":1123328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1122932#post1122932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your spell lasts 1 turn, and you miss your touch attempt, does it fizzle out?<br /> <br /> If your spell lasts 3 turns, and you miss your touch attempt, does it lose 1 turn off its duration but still allow you to make another touch attempt on your next turn? Meaning you don't have to recast, but it's still occupying a spell slot?<br /> <br /> If you miss an aimed spell, no matter the duration, it's gone - meaning you have to cast it all over again to use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally think the targetting process is part of the spellcasting and thus if you can't touch your target the spellcasting automatically fails as you can't satisfy the condition of the spell. Spells don't hang themselves naturally. Though I can see an aimed spell hitting a wrong, applicable target and taking effect as normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123272#post1123272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Ban and Bane of ephemeral entities seems to function very similarly (In terms of theme not necessarily mechanics) to a Destiny and Doom. Do you think that it's a close enough equivalent that you could manipulate a Ban or Bane with Fate?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd say no, but ultimatly it's a ST call. But Bans/Banes are underlying parts of a spirits metaphysical nature and not part of its fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:54:55-07:00","id":1123367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123328#post1123328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally think the targetting process is part of the spellcasting and thus if you can't touch your target the spellcasting automatically fails as you can't satisfy the condition of the spell. Spells don't hang themselves naturally. Though I can see an aimed spell hitting a wrong, applicable target and taking effect as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell in this case isn't hung, it is cast with the target of &quot;the applicable target that I manage to touch with it&quot; regardless of whether or not that's the target you had in mind. It's still ticking down its Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:15:33-07:00","id":1123515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123367#post1123367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell in this case isn't hung, it is cast with the target of &quot;the applicable target that I manage to touch with it&quot; regardless of whether or not that's the target you had in mind. It's still ticking down its Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>You cant just cast a spell that has a duration of x and wait till x-1 and then touch somebody and have the spell take effect thats not how it works. At the moment of casting if you arnt touching the thing you want to cast on then your only other option is to throw it via the aimed mechanic. <br /> <br /> You cant cast a spell like degrading the form to lower a targets strength by 5 for 1 day then sit around for 3 hours till you eventually touch somebody with it. Thats exactly what the Hung spell is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:20:37-07:00","id":1123516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123515#post1123515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You cant just cast a spell that has a duration of x and wait till x-1 and then touch somebody and have the spell take effect thats not how it works. At the moment of casting if you arnt touching the thing you want to cast on then your only other option is to throw it via the aimed mechanic.<br /> <br /> You cant cast a spell like degrading the form to lower a targets strength by 5 for 1 day then sit around for 3 hours till you eventually touch somebody with it. Thats exactly what the Hung spell is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that isn't how it works. Touch at the time of casting or aim it, else you lose it and need to recast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:30:14-07:00","id":1123521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123515#post1123515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cant just cast a spell that has a duration of x and wait till x-1 and then touch somebody and have the spell take effect thats not how it works. At the moment of casting if you arnt touching the thing you want to cast on then your only other option is to throw it via the aimed mechanic. <br /> <br /> You cant cast a spell like degrading the form to lower a targets strength by 5 for 1 day then sit around for 3 hours till you eventually touch somebody with it. Thats exactly what the Hung spell is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't you? First, Hung Spell suspends the Duration, in this case the Duration is still ticking down. Second, the spell will apply itself to the first viable target you touch, so if you forget that you have that up and you pet your dog, your dog is going to be adversely affected. I can't think of why this wouldn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:37:08-07:00","id":1123524,"title":"","content":"Unless you're casting AoE you always specify targets. Otherwise the spell wouldn't distinguish between the person you touch or the clothes you're carrying. The clothes are just as valid for targetting as anything else even if the spell wouldn't have any effect.<br /> And you specify targets during the casting. If you fail to touch someone with a Self/Touch range spell the spell simply won't affect that target. You can't save the targetting until later. It's part of the spell's factors, and spell factors can't be changed after casting. Only decreased if you maintain spell control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-01-2017, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:55:37-07:00","id":1123532,"title":"","content":"What Tessie said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:20:48-07:00","id":1123538,"title":"","content":"The book says Touching an Opponent for the purpose of delivering a touch-range spell requires a Dex + Brawl roll, though. Does this happen before or after casting? How exactly do you work in your Yantra - since you're actively doing something that isn't related to concentrating, like chasing someone down? Is that the point? Touch-range spells aren't really great for combat (especially not offensive, unless you're using magic to make touching people much easier.) and limit the use of Yantra.<br /> <br /> The main benefit of trying to make this work would be not always spending a Reach on upgrading to sensory casting and not taking a chance with a spell that could miss.<br /> <br /> I guess whether the Touch an Opponent roll comes before or after the spell is cast was the source of my confusion. The consensus is you need to touch the target first, then specific that target in your spellcasting while you're still touching them.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with that.<br /> <br /> So to be clear, Touch an Opponent is a reflexive action occurring before you start casting your spell. The page of the book I'm looking at doesn't say if Touch an Opponent is or isn't reflexive, but it would benefit the caster if Touch and Spellcast happened on the same turn. If it is an instant action, forcing you to wait another turn to actually cast - then it further clarifies that Touch-range spells are exceedingly awkward in combat unless your target is willing, ignorant, or inanimate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In contrast, Aimed Spell is a reflexive action that takes place on the same turn as your spellcasting.<br /> <br /> With the Aimed Spell - can you pick it up as Mrmdubois states (upon hitting an &quot;invalid&quot; target, like a wall&quot;) and use it again? I'm not against this idea, but it is something I never thought of. It sounds funny to me. &quot;Oops! Don't mind me, just picking up my death spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or does the Aimed Spell fizzle if you miss and hit an invalid target?<br /> <br /> On the subject of specifying targets for spells, does an Aimed Spell take effect if you hit an unintended target during a miss on a dramatic fail? e.g Fireball aimed at Thing 1 misses and hits Thing 2, so Thing 2 takes damage meant for Thing 1.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 08-01-2017, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:30:49-07:00","id":1123540,"title":"","content":"I would place it at the same as an Aimed Spell, happen after spellcasting rolls and Paradox roll results have been determined, but are reflexive \u2014 they happen on the same turn as the spellcasting roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:33:21-07:00","id":1123569,"title":"","content":"Not as a response to anyone in particular, but a liberal reading of Co-Location would allow the mage to ignore defense when touching an opponent (unless they have Active Space Sight or a similar effect that allows them to see such space distortions) and a Space Fraying spell should be able to remove the need to roll at all. You remove the concept of distance between two subjects (though in a much more controlled manner than Collapse) and they would automatically count as touching for the duration of the spell. If you're one of the subjects you should be able to cast on the other subject as if you're touching them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T12:38:31-07:00","id":1123599,"title":"","content":"I think that would take a very Liberal Reading of Co-Location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:18:15-07:00","id":1123630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1122932#post1122932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you miss an aimed spell, no matter the duration, it's gone - meaning you have to cast it all over again to use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to page 113, &quot;Aimed spells . . . must use area of effect, centered on wherever the mage aims.&quot; That implies that if you miss your mark, the spell goes off wherever it happens to land, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:04:08-07:00","id":1123651,"title":"","content":"That is under the Scale factor that if you are using an aimed spell and have a scale greater than 1 subject that it must use the Area scale and not the subject scale. In other words it is either a streak that strikes a single target or it is a streak that explodes in an area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T22:45:39-07:00","id":1123774,"title":"","content":"I really like the touch and aimed spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:46:57-07:00","id":1123959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123538#post1123538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In contrast, Aimed Spell is a reflexive action that takes place on the same turn as your spellcasting.<br /> <br /> With the Aimed Spell - can you pick it up as Mrmdubois states (upon hitting an &quot;invalid&quot; target, like a wall&quot;) and use it again? I'm not against this idea, but it is something I never thought of. It sounds funny to me. &quot;Oops! Don't mind me, just picking up my death spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or does the Aimed Spell fizzle if you miss and hit an invalid target?<br /> <br /> On the subject of specifying targets for spells, does an Aimed Spell take effect if you hit an unintended target during a miss on a dramatic fail? e.g Fireball aimed at Thing 1 misses and hits Thing 2, so Thing 2 takes damage meant for Thing 1.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Def no to picking up the spell and trying to use it again, if it misses it fizzles, there isnt rules for what happens when you mis a target when shooting them with a gun but its usualyl assumed that nothing else happens unless its a dramatic failure in which case the ST can do whatever nasty stuff he likes with it. If you get a dramatic failure on a fireball spell then the ST should do something like hit thing 2 instead of thing 1 yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:26:56-07:00","id":1124032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1123540#post1123540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would place it at the same as an Aimed Spell, happen after spellcasting rolls and Paradox roll results have been determined, but are reflexive \u2014 they happen on the same turn as the spellcasting roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll keep it the same as Aimed Spell if only for the fact that it keeps things consistent and not confusing. In both cases (touch/aimed) cast + reflexive touch/aim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This next part is aimed at no one in particular:<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to assume you cannot use the Aiming mechanic to grant yourself +1 to +3 on Aimed Spells, like you can with firearms. Am I correct in that assumption?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:37:14-07:00","id":1124038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1124032#post1124032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to assume you cannot use the Aiming mechanic to grant yourself +1 to +3 on Aimed Spells, like you can with firearms. Am I correct in that assumption?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, but it seems like a reasonable Merit. Something like &quot;Each turn your character adds a Yantra that does not require an Instant Action, the mage may use their Instant Action to aim their aimed spell as if he were aiming a firearm.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:05:35-07:00","id":1124102,"title":"","content":"Sorry if it has already been asked, but 250 pages of thread is a bit too much to scour through... The Control Weather Forces Ruling spell (M:tAw 2e p.143). Does the weather change only in an area as per Area of Effect, or does it change the weather itself &quot;naturally&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:29:57-07:00","id":1124131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1124102#post1124102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if it has already been asked, but 250 pages of thread is a bit too much to scour through... The Control Weather Forces Ruling spell (M:tAw 2e p.143). Does the weather change only in an area as per Area of Effect, or does it change the weather itself &quot;naturally&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, Going to say that it uses the area as per area of effect which really limits its power but it is only a 2 dot spell. However defaulting to touch range control weather seems pretty useless so one would always have to cast it with an area of effect seems weird too. The natural change effect is a +1 reach effect, otherwise the change is instant so one assumes this spell is good for small local changes in weather (ie up to campus range) and probably requiring ritual casting to get the full effect (potency for tilts and useful area of effect).<br /> <br /> The idea that a 2 dot spell could change an cities weather system seems abit OP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T00:37:57-07:00","id":1124209,"title":"","content":"So my wife and I have started playing a 2E game and we're utterly perplexed by something -<br /> <br /> What are the options for creating &quot;magic items&quot;? My wife's struggling a bit with the rules as a whole and I don't really know them well enough by myself (being this is the first time I've played any Mage) to really help her out. Is there like a step-by-step process to it? We're both struggling with the very heavy Mage jargon a lot which isn't helping. We know stuff like 1E Changeling's Token/Hedgespinning back to front as a comparison point, but we aren't really sure where to even start the process for Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T01:51:16-07:00","id":1124225,"title":"","content":"You can create a Enhanced Item by casting an Infinite Duration spell on it, If you have Prime 4 you could create an Imbued Item see page 195, and you can not create an Artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T07:05:59-07:00","id":1124285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1124209#post1124209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my wife and I have started playing a 2E game and we're utterly perplexed by something -<br /> <br /> What are the options for creating &quot;magic items&quot;? My wife's struggling a bit with the rules as a whole and I don't really know them well enough by myself (being this is the first time I've played any Mage) to really help her out. Is there like a step-by-step process to it? We're both struggling with the very heavy Mage jargon a lot which isn't helping. We know stuff like 1E Changeling's Token/Hedgespinning back to front as a comparison point, but we aren't really sure where to even start the process for Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK so imbued items and artifacts have some holes in their rules at the moment or maybe not holes per say but they appear to be really really limited in what they can actually pull off. Mainly dealing with reaches and spell factors. Imbued items wanting to pierce any sort of withstand or have any lingering duration are probably going to have only a chance dice to cast, and since they only get 1 free reach it's unlikely to be either a long duration or take ritual time to cast? It seems (at least for artifacts) if you want a 1 dot spell to have any chance of a good dicepool you also have to imbued/add a 5 dot effect into it aswell so it can get the 5 arcana dice.<br /> <br /> Ive tried many times to use whats written to make some imbued items (imbued item for teleport, wand of lightning bolt etc etc) and they all usually have a chance dice because the dicepool you get to cast is so low that any additional spell factors eat it up quickly.<br /> <br /> Hopefully Signs and Sigil will sort this? (any info released about whats in the book cover items?).<br /> <br /> Im happy to be proven wrong, and if somebody can provide an example of a imbued item it might show that i have been doing it wrong all along.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T17:38:06-07:00","id":1124542,"title":"","content":"So I'm looking over the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind...and I notice one of their Yantra is applying the Wisdom of the &quot;Koran of Hagetaka&quot;. Would Quoting the book &quot;70 Maxims of Maximally Effective Mercenaries&quot; count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T02:21:41-07:00","id":1125145,"title":"","content":"Now I've read the mage book but I thought Potency had a cap. I have potential player saying at character start you could make a mage and have them make a &quot; +23 typeless bonus from Exceptional Luck with Potency 23, +26 tool bonus from Monkey's Paw Potency 23 cast on +3 computer, +around 36 dice from assist roll on which I rolled 55 dice with rote action. <br /> <br /> My character had Fate 3(he styled himself as a hero from &quot;Sword and Planet&quot; novels), that gave him 3 base potency. He had Fate 3, Gnosis 1, Mudra Skill 4, High Speech 2, Willpower 3, and lowering dicepool to -4 to add another +9 potency to the roll. That gave him initial potency of 12. Then he added that to another casting of Exceptional Luck, adding another 6 to Potency. Then he added another (18-12)/2=3 Potency in the next cast, getting up to 21. Then I believe it was another iteration of that getting him to 23.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:52:49-07:00","id":1125164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125145#post1125145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I've read the mage book but I thought Potency had a cap. I have potential player saying at character start you could make a mage and have them make a &quot; +23 typeless bonus from Exceptional Luck with Potency 23, +26 tool bonus from Monkey's Paw Potency 23 cast on +3 computer, +around 36 dice from assist roll on which I rolled 55 dice with rote action.<br /> <br /> My character had Fate 3(he styled himself as a hero from &quot;Sword and Planet&quot; novels), that gave him 3 base potency. He had Fate 3, Gnosis 1, Mudra Skill 4, High Speech 2, Willpower 3, and lowering dicepool to -4 to add another +9 potency to the roll. That gave him initial potency of 12. Then he added that to another casting of Exceptional Luck, adding another 6 to Potency. Then he added another (18-12)/2=3 Potency in the next cast, getting up to 21. Then I believe it was another iteration of that getting him to 23.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you are spending 2 turns per cast, spending 1 mana (p126 of mage overcoming max bonus) and 1 willpower to roll a chance dice each iteration, hoping all of them work one after another?<br /> Wheres the extra duration (needs to last at least 4 turns to be able to give bonus to the next casting) for exceptional luck? You need some duration on exceptional luck to be able to take advantage of those extra dice?<br /> Your remembering +1 reach on the 2nd+ casting of exceptional luck because of spell control?<br /> <br /> Monkey paws equipment bonus wont work with spell casting (as in a item with monkey paw cast on it doesnt suddenly count as a path, order or patron yantra tool ) and if you use the reach to give the person using the item a boon that provides extra dice, this wont stack with exceptional luck, only the most potent will be in effect.<br /> <br /> +3 computer? is this a path/order or patron yantra tool? why is somebody getting +3 just from using a computer, yantras listed were mudra, high speech only. No mention of a computer being a yantra tool.<br /> <br /> Assist roll?<br /> <br /> Assuming no mistakes and i already see some, rolling 55 dice with a rote action is overkill when you only need 1 success to cast a spell (3-5 for a exceptional success) more interesting would be what was the end potency/duration/targets of said spell you were rolling 55 dice for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-05-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:00:14-07:00","id":1125165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125145#post1125145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I've read the mage book but I thought Potency had a cap. I have potential player saying at character start you could make a mage and have them make a &quot; +23 typeless bonus from Exceptional Luck with Potency 23, +26 tool bonus from Monkey's Paw Potency 23 cast on +3 computer, +around 36 dice from assist roll on which I rolled 55 dice with rote action.<br /> <br /> My character had Fate 3(he styled himself as a hero from &quot;Sword and Planet&quot; novels), that gave him 3 base potency. He had Fate 3, Gnosis 1, Mudra Skill 4, High Speech 2, Willpower 3, and lowering dicepool to -4 to add another +9 potency to the roll. That gave him initial potency of 12. Then he added that to another casting of Exceptional Luck, adding another 6 to Potency. Then he added another (18-12)/2=3 Potency in the next cast, getting up to 21. Then I believe it was another iteration of that getting him to 23.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well for one thing you are building up paradox very fast with each casting of the Exceptional Luck. Each casting of the exceptional Luck will need to have 4 reaches assigned to it (1 Instant Casting, 1 Advanced duration, 2 affects spellcasting) You can get way without the advanced duration if you take a minus to the die pool to extend the duration (or cast it with the conditional duration attainment and 1 point of mana). The first casting would then have 2 dice of paradox and take the one spell control slot at 1 Gnosis. Each additional casting of the exceptional Luck will then incur paradox at an increased rate. and additional paradox for the reach needed to go over spell control and then additional for chancing paradox previously in the scene.<br /> <br /> Then he must succeed in the casting using a chance die (this can be mitigated by casting exceptional luck and taking the informed condition but you are only compounding the amount of paradox incurred)<br /> <br /> But other then that there is no cap to potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:09:05-07:00","id":1125166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125164#post1125164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you are spending 2 turns per cast, spending 1 mana (p126 of mage overcoming max bonus) and 1 willpower to roll a chance dice each iteration, hoping all of them work one after another?<br /> Wheres the extra duration (needs to last at least 4 turns to be able to give bonus to the next casting) for exceptional luck? You need some duration on exceptional luck to be able to take advantage of those extra dice?<br /> <br /> Monkey paws equipment bonus wont work with spell casting (as in a item with monkey paw cast on it doesnt suddenly count as a path, order or patron yantra tool ) if you use the reach to give the person using the item a boon that provides extra dice, this wont stack with exceptional luck, only the most potent will be in effect.<br /> <br /> +3 computer? is this a path/order or patron yantra tool? why is somebody getting +3 just from using a computer, yantras listed were mudra, high speech only. No mention of a computer being a yantra tool.<br /> <br /> Assist roll?<br /> <br /> Assuming no mistakes, rolling 55 dice with a rote action is overkill when you only need 1 success to cast the spell (3-5 for a exceptional success) more interesting would be what was the end potency/duration/targets of said spell you were rolling 55 dice for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The page that you quoted for costing one mana to go over a trait doesn't pertain to potency as potency isn't a trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:14:22-07:00","id":1125168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125166#post1125166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The page that you quoted for costing one mana to go over a trait doesn't pertain to potency as potency isn't a trait.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. If you give yourself +10 strength via life with a potency 10 spell you still pay the mana for exceeding the trait limit. Its the same here. Exceptional luck is giving more than a +5 bonus to something so it costs a mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:19:10-07:00","id":1125169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125165#post1125165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for one thing you are building up paradox very fast with each casting of the Exceptional Luck. Each casting of the exceptional Luck will need to have 4 reaches assigned to it (1 Instant Casting, 1 Advanced duration, 2 affects spellcasting) You can get way without the advanced duration if you take a minus to the die pool to extend the duration (or cast it with the conditional duration attainment and 1 point of mana).</div> </div> </div> </div>Four free Reaches if it's a Rote, and anyone who has Fate 2 should get Exceptional Luck as a Rote because it's an extremely useful spell even outside spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:22:18-07:00","id":1125170,"title":"","content":"I would disagree with that as it specifically call out a trait of a person( or tool), but that is neither her nor there the point that both of use is trying to make is that it would cost alot to get a +55 dice pool with rote quality when it probably isn't needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:25:10-07:00","id":1125172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125169#post1125169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Four free Reaches if it's a Rote, and anyone who has Fate 2 should get Exceptional Luck as a Rote because it's an extremely useful spell even outside spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true and if it was cast in a Demesne dedicated to Fate it wouldn't incur paradox in the first place. but i was taking just the base statement and missed that it was a rote (to get the Mudra it needs to be a rote).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:26:57-07:00","id":1125173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125165#post1125165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well for one thing you are building up paradox very fast with each casting of the Exceptional Luck. Each casting of the exceptional Luck will need to have 4 reaches assigned to it (1 Instant Casting, 1 Advanced duration, 2 affects spellcasting) You can get way without the advanced duration if you take a minus to the die pool to extend the duration (or cast it with the conditional duration attainment and 1 point of mana). The first casting would then have 2 dice of paradox and take the one spell control slot at 1 Gnosis. Each additional casting of the exceptional Luck will then incur paradox at an increased rate. and additional paradox for the reach needed to go over spell control and then additional for chancing paradox previously in the scene.<br /> <br /> Then he must succeed in the casting using a chance die (this can be mitigated by casting exceptional luck and taking the informed condition but you are only compounding the amount of paradox incurred)<br /> <br /> But other then that there is no cap to potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is using a rote because of the +4 mudra so he has 4 free reach from the rote. The 2nd casting will be 1 paradox (base gnosis 1 is 1?) for the reach from going over spell control and third will be 2 dice? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:29:13-07:00","id":1125174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125170#post1125170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree with that as it specifically call out a trait of a person( or tool), but that is neither her nor there the point that both of use is trying to make is that it would cost alot to get a +55 dice pool with rote quality when it probably isn't needed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. An extra 55 dice mean nothing if the spell is potency 1 vs withstand 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:32:56-07:00","id":1125176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125170#post1125170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree with that as it specifically call out a trait of a person( or tool), but that is neither her nor there the point that both of use is trying to make is that it would cost alot to get a +55 dice pool with rote quality when it probably isn't needed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/BbalGwQ.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:50:09-07:00","id":1125180,"title":"","content":"Ok thanks for the clarification from Dave. I still disagree with it but then it doesn't matter what I think Dave is a developer and that is that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-05-2017, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:54:24-07:00","id":1125182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125173#post1125173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He is using a rote because of the +4 mudra so he has 4 free reach from the rote. The 2nd casting will be 1 paradox (base gnosis 1 is 1?) for the reach from going over spell control and third will be 2 dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>acknowledged already in the post above yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T05:19:23-07:00","id":1125183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125174#post1125174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly. An extra 55 dice mean nothing if the spell is potency 1 vs withstand 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except with an Exceptional (which is exceptionally likely) you can ignore Withstand. Also, why wouldn't you add 10 Potency if you have that many extra dice anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:01:52-07:00","id":1125199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125183#post1125183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except with an Exceptional (which is exceptionally likely) you can ignore Withstand. Also, why wouldn't you add 10 Potency if you have that many extra dice anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yeh ive already asked what the potency/duration etc was on that spell was that had 55 dice on it. My point was number of dice isnt the most important thing in 2e anymore as it was in 1e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:32:02-07:00","id":1125204,"title":"","content":"\u200bCan informed actually be used with spell casting? It specifically says skill roll? Steadfast however just mentions a roll? Maybe giving yourself &quot;an arcane&quot; condition you give yourself a informed like condition that does the same for spell casting?<br /> <br /> Anyway brief napkin maths i can only really squeeze +8 potency out of a first time casting of Exceptional Luck then +12 and it quickly gets diminishing returns after that:<br /> <br /> Dicepool 13 from Gnosis, Arcana, Mudra, High Speech and Willpower.<br /> Base potency 3, duration 1 turn<br /> 1 reach for instant, 1 for advanced duration, 2 for bonus to spell casting<br /> +8 potency for -16<br /> Informed condition for -2<br /> 13-18 = -5, 1 mana, 1 willpower, auto succeed because of informed lasting a scene<br /> <br /> Second cast:<br /> Dicepool 21<br /> 1 reach for instant, 1 advanced, 2 for spell casting, 1 for over control<br /> +12 potency for -24<br /> informed condition -2<br /> 21 - 26 = -5 dicepool, another mana, another willpower, auto succeeds from informed<br /> base paradox of 1 dice from gnosis<br /> <br /> third casting:<br /> Dicepool 25<br /> 1 reach for instant, 1 advanced, 2 for spell casting, 1 for over control<br /> +14 potency for -28<br /> informed condition -2<br /> 25-30 = -5 dicepool, another mana, another willpower, autosucceeds from informed<br /> base paradox of 2 dice, 1 gnosis, 1 from previous casting<br /> <br /> As you can see the diminishing returns stack up quickly. Its already cost you 6+ turns of casting, 3 mana and 3 willpower, with 2 paradox rolls.<br /> <br /> *<i>By the 5th casting you hit the limit, 4th casting can give +15 dice for -30, -2 for informed so is 27 - 32 for -5 dicepool, 5th is +16 for -32, -2 for informed, 28-34 is -6 so an illegal cast, you top out at +15 dice or an extra 7 potency on the next spell you cast within the next scene after 8+ turns, 4 mana, 4 willpower, multiple paradox rolls, of 1, 2, 3 dice, </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-05-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:46:34-07:00","id":1125213,"title":"","content":"Sorry I was looking at beats, resolving the condition grants a beat if the Exceptional Luck was an exceptional success, But the base spell allows for the exceptional luck to affect spellcasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-05-2017, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:12:13-07:00","id":1125229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125213#post1125213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I was looking at beats, resolving the condition grants a beat if the Exceptional Luck was an exceptional success, But the base spell allows for the exceptional luck to affect spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The disagreement is that can the boons granted by exceptional luck to spell casting be the gain bonus dice or condition options. Some interpret it to only be the +8/9 again options<br /> <br /> Which is another thread so ignore me :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:30:47-07:00","id":1125236,"title":"","content":"If you are referring to the section in the Hex/Boon that specifically calls out the &quot;+2 reach to affect spellcasting&quot; (impose dice penalty (hex), 9 again/8 again (Boon)) that is in those sections to cover other spells that give a hex or a boon (specifically Monkeys Paw, Sworn Oath, Divine Intervention, Pariah, ect...) the Exceptional Luck covers all categories with the +2 reach option.<br /> <br /> But if this discussion is in another thread you are right it doesn't need to be discussed here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T09:12:09-07:00","id":1125252,"title":"","content":"Ok, you cast temporal stutter on somebody with a indefinite duration and then release it. I assume some form of temporal residue/mystery is left behind that those with time mage sight will be able to decipher but later you or others want to dispel it. Does the spell stick around at the point where the subject vanished or does the spell vanish along with the subject of the spell meaning its not there to dispel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T09:57:16-07:00","id":1125259,"title":"","content":"The spell sticks around where they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:28:38-07:00","id":1125327,"title":"","content":"Can Correspondence be broken down into simpler spells? I mean, maybe I don't care about all of the Sympathetic connections, maybe I just want to see the strength of the Sympathetic connection between me and the subject and the emotional context. If I used Correspondence to do that then at Instant and Sensory Range that would take five Reach which seems kind of excessive for digging up one specific piece of information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:50:11-07:00","id":1125335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125327#post1125327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Correspondence be broken down into simpler spells? I mean, maybe I don't care about all of the Sympathetic connections, maybe I just want to see the strength of the Sympathetic connection between me and the subject and the emotional context. If I used Correspondence to do that then at Instant and Sensory Range that would take five Reach which seems kind of excessive for digging up one specific piece of information.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be four Reaches for Sensory (1), Instant (1), and specified connection (2). And in that particular example you could just cast on yourself instead, reducing it down to three Reaches.<br /> But it makes a whole lot of sense to be able to cast a Knowing spell directly on a Sympathetic Connection to gain more in depth information about that particular Connection. I'd allow it as ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:59:55-07:00","id":1125343,"title":"","content":"Good point on casting it on yourself to reduce Reach cost, still bothersome in how high it is to me though. Basically, I'm trying to wrangle a useful ability out of Space 1 that might be the basis for an attainment in a legacy that deals more with Sympathy than spatial distortion and I am really struggling.<br /> <br /> Though, I wonder...other arcana have spells you can cast on yourself in order to perceive certain aspects of the arcana's phenomena, Exorcists' Eye, Pierce Deception, etc, shouldn't Space be able to do something like that? I imagine it would only perceive currently active sympathetic connections (Active meaning you're having an interaction with a person/place/thing). If you're talking with someone, obviously you have a Sympathetic connection with them in that moment, but perhaps this type of Unveiling spell could reveal the strength of the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:00:15-07:00","id":1125344,"title":"","content":"How does Area Scale interact with Duration?<br /> <br /> For example, suppose Alice and Bob are standing in a room. Timmy Thyrsus is standing outside the room and casts Shapechanging to turn everyone in the room into a frog. He casts the spell with an Area that covers the room and a Duration of one month. Has Timmy just turned Alice and Bob into frogs for a month as if he had targeted the mdirectly, or has he created a Zone of Frog such that for the next month you become a frog upon entering the room and return to human form when you leave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:03:18-07:00","id":1125346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125344#post1125344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Area Scale interact with Duration?<br /> <br /> For example, suppose Alice and Bob are standing in a room. Timmy Thyrsus is standing outside the room and casts Shapechanging to turn everyone in the room into a frog. He casts the spell with an Area that covers the room and a Duration of one month. Has Timmy just turned Alice and Bob into frogs for a month as if he had targeted the mdirectly, or has he created a Zone of Frog such that for the next month you become a frog upon entering the room and return to human form when you leave?</div> </div> </div> </div>The second one, he created a Zone of Frog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:55:26-07:00","id":1125364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125346#post1125346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second one, he created a Zone of Frog.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd contend it's the first, because the entire point of Area Scale having a higher number of potential subjects is that it reduces the amount of control you have over the outcome without oversight.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: does regular spell control let you end the spell for specific targets if you use Area Scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:57:38-07:00","id":1125365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125364#post1125364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd contend it's the first, because the entire point of Area Scale having a higher number of potential subjects is that it reduces the amount of control you have over the outcome without oversight.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: does regular spell control let you end the spell for specific targets if you use Area Scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Dave has commented that it's actually the second, and it still has a high number of potential subjects since anyone walking into the zone is going to be subject to the spell and then suffer a breaking point when exiting it. Your chances of having unintended targets is actually higher, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T19:49:07-07:00","id":1125462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125364#post1125364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd contend it's the first, because the entire point of Area Scale having a higher number of potential subjects is that it reduces the amount of control you have over the outcome without oversight.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: does regular spell control let you end the spell for specific targets if you use Area Scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also remember Dave saying its the second. If there are 50 people in that room then they all become frogs (after withstand checks) and anybody entering the area of the spell gets turned into frogs too. If Timmy only wanted to shapechange Alice &amp; Bob he should have used number of targets instead to target just them.<br /> <br /> Spell controls says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">but although<br /> she can reduce the number of subjects if the spell used that form of<br /> Scale, all spell factors must still apply equally to all subjects \u2013 she can\u2019t<br /> weaken a spell for a specific individual without further magic</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So i would say that you can lower the Area Scale spell factor of that spell to cover a smaller area or lower the potency spell factor so less people get shapechanged but all subjects in the area are still covered by the spell. You cant pick and choose people inside the area spells effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-05-2017, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T19:59:06-07:00","id":1125465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125462#post1125462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i would say that you can lower the Area Scale spell factor of that spell to cover a smaller area or lower the potency spell factor so less people get shapechanged but all subjects in the area are still covered by the spell. You cant pick and choose people inside the area spells effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use Warding Gesture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T20:11:20-07:00","id":1125466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125462#post1125462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also remember Dave saying its the second. If there are 50 people in that room then they all become frogs (after withstand checks) and anybody entering the area of the spell gets turned into frogs too. If Timmy only wanted to shapechange Alice &amp; Bob he should have used number of targets instead to target just them.<br /> <br /> Spell controls says<br /> <br /> So i would say that you can lower the Area Scale spell factor of that spell to cover a smaller area or lower the potency spell factor so less people get shapechanged but all subjects in the area are still covered by the spell. You cant pick and choose people inside the area spells effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No wonder i remember it <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bo3ekI2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T20:39:10-07:00","id":1125472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125462#post1125462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also remember Dave saying its the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, all I remember him saying and can turn up from searching is that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943564#post943564\">the area covered by Area Scale can have its outer bound be anywhere within your determined range</a> and that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933427#post933427\">blanket-targeting allowing a greater effective headcount than specified targets is a feature</a>. Do either of you have a link?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there are 50 people in that room then they all become frogs (after withstand checks) and anybody entering the area of the spell gets turned into frogs too. If Timmy only wanted to shapechange Alice &amp; Bob he should have used number of targets instead to target just them. </div> </div> </div>My issue with this is threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. This negates the point of the above-stated feature of Area Scale.<br /> 2. If the Frog Room is the correct interpretation then we lose dramatic event-type magical accidents as a narrative device in favor of location-type magical phenomena that aren't really supported elsewhere in the setting \u2014 there's plenty of precedent for &quot;everyone in this room turned into a frog on the night of the last full moon,&quot; but &quot;anyone who goes into this room turns into a frog until they get out&quot; is a lot more unusual than should be the default as a genre-emulation tool.<br /> 3. This makes applying Area Scale effectively a minor Dynamics effect that doesn't work like either version of long-Duration spells do; adding Area Scale to a spell shouldn't change its subject to <i>the area</i> just because it's affecting a more indiscriminate set of targets, and affecting more targets than you initially constructed the spell for is one of those things that prompts Masters to Seek the Threshold.<br /> <br /> I'm just not seeing how it's supposed to be the intended reading of Area Scale in the face of everything else the setting has to say about magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T21:59:33-07:00","id":1125484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125472#post1125472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, all I remember him saying and can turn up from searching is that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943564#post943564\">the area covered by Area Scale can have its outer bound be anywhere within your determined range</a> and that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933427#post933427\">blanket-targeting allowing a greater effective headcount than specified targets is a feature</a>. Do either of you have a link?<br /> <br /> My issue with this is threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. This negates the point of the above-stated feature of Area Scale.<br /> 2. If the Frog Room is the correct interpretation then we lose dramatic event-type magical accidents as a narrative device in favor of location-type magical phenomena that aren't really supported elsewhere in the setting \u2014 there's plenty of precedent for &quot;everyone in this room turned into a frog on the night of the last full moon,&quot; but &quot;anyone who goes into this room turns into a frog until they get out&quot; is a lot more unusual than should be the default as a genre-emulation tool.<br /> 3. This makes applying Area Scale effectively a minor Dynamics effect that doesn't work like either version of long-Duration spells do; adding Area Scale to a spell shouldn't change its subject to <i>the area</i> just because it's affecting a more indiscriminate set of targets, and affecting more targets than you initially constructed the spell for is one of those things that prompts Masters to Seek the Threshold.<br /> <br /> I'm just not seeing how it's supposed to be the intended reading of Area Scale in the face of everything else the setting has to say about magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That quote from dave in from rpg net. Its saying if you cloak an area then people are cloaked within that area, if they leave they arnt cloaked. Change cloaked with Turned into a frog and go from there.<br /> <br /> I dont know what the above stated feature of Area Scale you mean? Effecting more targets without being able to pick and choose? This is exactly what the frog room is doing?<br /> <br /> What is an spell effecting an entire area if not a location-type magical phenomena and how does that cause any lose of dramatic event type magical accidents?<br /> <br /> An area effect applies the spells effect to everything in the area as written in RAW. Therefore if you leave the area the spell no longer effects you, this only matters with long duration spells, a instant cast damage spell made into an area effect spell will do damage to all targets in the area then stop. If did use a long duration then it'd do that same damage every gnosis cast interval though hurting everything inside the area at that time.<br /> <br /> Care to explain what &quot;everything else the setting has to say about magic&quot;? Use as many colourful words as needed please..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-06-2017, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T22:26:39-07:00","id":1125489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125484#post1125484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know what the above stated feature of Area Scale you mean? Effecting more targets without being able to pick and choose? This is exactly what the frog room is doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The solution to getting someone who turned into a frog via a Frog Room to stop being a frog becomes &quot;remove them from the Frog Room&quot; rather than &quot;deal with the fact that there has been a spell-based explosion of Make People Frogs.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is an spell effecting an entire area if not a location-type magical phenomena and how does that cause any lose of dramatic event type magical accidents? </div> </div> </div>Again, if cursing an entire small neighborhood to involuntary anuranthropy ceases to be a concern for any resident who escapes the field, the story hook of &quot;somebody a cabal member knows was turned into a frog as collateral damage \u2014 go investigate it&quot; is replaced with &quot;this area cannot be entered without high Withstand and/or supernatural protection until it's dispelled or enough Sleepers disintegrate it \u2014 armor up or get ready for some weird shit to arrive,&quot; as-written the game seems to suggest that's more in line with spells that actually create or modify locations with their base effects rather than any spell that picks targets by area (and Warding Gesture is specifically needed to whitelist a target as an exception to an area effect).<br /> <br /> It makes Area Scale impossible to use for The Incident At Frogway Park without forcing the location to be treated with the same precautions as a Demesne while also removing any utility the factor presents for preparing spells affecting large amounts of equipment or groups of people in a secure location like a Sanctum or a Demesne (which already does the job of incentivizing mages to operate primarily out of their Sancta).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An area effect applies the spells effect to everything in the area as written in RAW. Therefore if you leave the area the spell no longer effects you. </div> </div> </div>Area Scale as-written is a wider and more indiscriminate targeting mechanism, not a geographically-specific version of Conditional Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T23:12:30-07:00","id":1125494,"title":"","content":"Ok so what you are saying is that Timmy casts an area effect spell on Alice and Bob in the other room, They get turned into frogs for the duration of the spell and because they are the only people in that room at that time its only them that get effected but if other people were in that room they would also get turned into frogs. Alicefrog and Bobfrog can then bounce away in different directions and leave that room but stay frogs until the spell expires? But nobody else entering that room after the spell was first cast gets turned into frogs?<br /> <br /> Which Daves example clearly proves doesnt happen? Because if Alicefrog and Bobfrog seperate and leave the area then the spell is no longer an area spell. Its a area wide number of targets spell which isnt an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-06-2017, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T23:38:00-07:00","id":1125500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125494#post1125494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if Alicefrog and Bobfrog seperate and leave the area then the spell is no longer an area spell. Its a area wide number of targets spell which isnt an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Frog A and Frog B leave the area and retain their enchantment then the spell is a splashy version of a targeted spell, which is generally what the intuitive reading of &quot;make a personally-targeted effect affect everyone in an area&quot; is \u2014 it doesn't necessitate changing the basic description of the spell's effect from &quot;turn the target into a frog&quot; to &quot;turn the target area into a space where people are frogs.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's already established that mages maintain sympathetic connections to both their spells and the subjects of their spells, so it's not as though there's a need for anything more involved than &quot;if you want to dispel an area-cast spell you're going to need to find the place where the spell went off&quot; to account for targets leaving the initial zone of influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T01:09:25-07:00","id":1125513,"title":"","content":"Do you want an area spell that continues after somebody leaves the area? Yes? Is this possible? No.<br /> Simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines<br /> how large the area <u><i><b>covered</b></i></u> by the spell is</span></span> </div> </div> </div>If you leave the area you are no longer covered by the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T06:30:11-07:00","id":1125576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for unintended splashy magic you use Paradox and switch the area scale from area to individual targets. Although, frankly, I think that a magical location is more likely to have unintended effects as people blunder into them depending on what you want the magic to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:43:56-07:00","id":1125594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125576#post1125576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, frankly, I think that a magical location is more likely to have unintended effects as people blunder into them depending on what you want the magic to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>My contention is that this is a more abnormal-looking outcome of wide-scale magic than makes intuitive sense \u2014 the only spell effects for which Frog Zone doesn't seem weird Duration-wise are Lasting spells (which re-cast themselves at intervals throughout the Duration anyway) and spells at least partially designed to keep their subjects within the area like your archetypal put-this-castle-to-sleep enchantment (which narratives generally frame as having to do with the enchantment rather than the castle), and meanwhile it makes Area Scale useless for giving a group of targets a benefit or malady that you don't also want your enemies or your allies to gain later as well (a spell on your Sanctum that gives anyone inside it Body Control's accelerated healing is a terrible thing to have going if someone breaks in, for example).<br /> <br /> Modeling splashy magic as changing from Area to Targets through Paradox also doesn't really work all that well when Aimed spells need to use Area Scale, which effectively turns the cost of that change to at least two Reach, results in the reduced impact of going from &quot;tried to hit everyone in this room&quot; to &quot;hit two or four people&quot; at non-Advanced Scale, and, pending statement that Paradox removes a spell from the reach of your spell control, can more unambiguously be dealt with by just dynamically reducing the amount of Scale the spell actually uses after the fact.<br /> <br /> It just feels too tidy for what &quot;make a spell hit valid target in an area&quot; seems to imply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T09:25:33-07:00","id":1125613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125594#post1125594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and meanwhile it makes Area Scale useless for giving a group of targets a benefit or malady that you don't also want your enemies or your allies to gain later as well (a spell on your Sanctum that gives anyone inside it Body Control's accelerated healing is a terrible thing to have going if someone breaks in, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not simply make a reverse version of Warding gesture, then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thing is, all I remember him saying and can turn up from searching is that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943564#post943564\">the area covered by Area Scale can have its outer bound be anywhere within your determined range</a> and that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=933427#post933427\">blanket-targeting allowing a greater effective headcount than specified targets is a feature</a>. Do either of you have a link? </div> </div> </div>Neither of those things make any difference for the current discussion. Blanket-targeting does allow a higher headcount, but nobody says that means it otherwise functions the same as just targetting multiple people, so I don't see your hang up there. What area is covered by an area spell likewise makes no difference.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest is you just saying &quot;But, if it works like this then [thing I like to play out in Y way] does not actually [play out in Y way].&quot; Yes... ok? That's not an argument for how it is, only for how you want it to be. There's house rules for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, if cursing an entire small neighborhood to involuntary anuranthropy ceases to be a concern for any resident who escapes the field, the story hook of &quot;somebody a cabal member knows was turned into a frog as collateral damage \u2014 go investigate it&quot; is replaced </div> </div> </div>Why? It'll only become more Mysterious, because you know that's not how it is <i>supposed</i> to work. The mystery! The intrigue! The excitement!<br /> <br /> Or it could just be &quot;some mage cast an area spell I guess&quot;, but I don't see that as a particularly involved story hook, so why mourn the fact that you actually have to add a bit of mystery and strangeness in there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T16:08:34-07:00","id":1125723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125613#post1125613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not simply make a reverse version of Warding gesture, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that is, in practice, just casting Warding Gesture on the area in the Frog Room interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither of those things make any difference for the current discussion. </div> </div> </div>Yes. It was all I could find. I shared those because I could not find anything else and wondered if there had been some confusion of those statements, as often happens in discussions of this sort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the rest is you just saying &quot;But, if it works like this then [thing I like to play out in Y way] does not actually [play out in Y way].&quot; Yes... ok? That's not an argument for how it is, only for how you want it to be. There's house rules for that. </div> </div> </div>That there are house rules for that does not change the fact that I'm pretty sure most people aren't going to think Area Scale works like the reverse of Ghost Gate's Reach effect for every spell without being told that's how it works. Awakened magic as presented sticks to its subjects in a way that connects back to the mage through their Nimbus, and Area Scale automatically applies to the default Range factor of a spell cast on anything you're not directly touching \u2014 it's far from unintuitive to conceive of the effects of such a spell as being more like shrapnel or a paint balloon than like a gas grenade or an umbrella given all of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? It'll only become more Mysterious, because you know that's not how it is <i>supposed</i> to work. The mystery! The intrigue! The excitement! </div> </div> </div>The <i>needless complication of a normal baseline quality of spellcasting!</i> This is a basic facet of gameplay that does not benefit from lacking a clear reason for it to work the way it does.<br /> <br /> A spell landing in a discrete location and affecting a less limited but still finite number of targets for a set length of time is more generally applicable for spell effects than a spell landing in a discrete location and affecting a notionally unlimited number of targets for as long as they stay in that discrete location; targeting a room that holds a maximum of eighty-five people should not let you affect more than eighty-five people with a spell made to put people to sleep just because you changed one spell factor \u2014 that sounds more in line with a Reach effect or a different spell.<br /> <br /> It makes Area Scale both less expedient and less dangerous, which does not seem to jive with &quot;the possibility of hitting people you didn't intend to by using a less strictly limited number of subjects is a feature, not a bug&quot; outside of a very weird application that doesn't suggest long-term Area spells are ever used outside of traps or Sanctums by any but the supremely unWise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or it could just be &quot;some mage cast an area spell I guess&quot;, but I don't see that as a particularly involved story hook, so why mourn the fact that you actually have to add a bit of mystery and strangeness in there? </div> </div> </div>Because the consequence is both louder and shorter-term than would normally be implied by &quot;so hey we altered the nature of an entire location to have an always-on application of mystical pressure throughout its area&quot; \u2014 pretty much nothing else in the setting has area-based powers that work as constant exertions rather than spaces in which the user has options they can exercise, which at the very least suggests that it shouldn't be the default function of area-based powers in Mage converted from non-area-based powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-06-2017, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T19:20:33-07:00","id":1125761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125723#post1125723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and Area Scale automatically applies to the default Range factor of a spell cast on anything you're not directly touching</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong, its probably more likely people default to 1 target for scale.<br /> <br /> You talk a lot about awakened magic as presented but its more like &quot;awakened magic has i think its like&quot;.<br /> <br /> You say its a needless complication of a baseline quality of spell casting yet its how its written in the book. A spell covers an area, if it has a duration it must be somewhere for that duration, hence its still in the area it was originally cast, no where does it that area moves or read like you cast an area spell on 40 people and then they all split up and become 40 individual spells, thats what 40 target scale is for.<br /> <br /> Something no jiving with your headcanon isnt wrong. Just do as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a> says and say you are house ruling it in your games and spare us essays on your interpretation of awakened magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T21:12:19-07:00","id":1125783,"title":"","content":"It's not interpretation when he's right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T21:16:07-07:00","id":1125785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125761#post1125761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong, its probably more likely people default to 1 target for scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using an Aimed spell \u2014 which is <i>literally what I am talking about </i>\u2014 explicitly requires you to use Area Scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> read like you cast an area spell on 40 people and then they all split up and become 40 individual spells </div> </div> </div>If I swing a bucketful of paint at a crowd of people, those people do not stop being covered in paint if they leave the area I swung the bucket at, nor does their being covered in paint become the effect of forty different buckets of paint if they leave the area and remain painted.<br /> <br /> My specific issue with the Frog Zone interpretation concerns spells that operate in a way that's analogous to covering the targets in paint - a spell that has an ongoing effect of its own doesn't have the explicit note of recurrence that instantaneous effects does, and much has already been made of how the books are written in natural rather than technical language; spells targeting an individual don't slide off them if Withstand reduces their effective Potency below 1, spells targeting multiple discrete individuals can't be cast as aimed projections, and spell control specifically doesn't let you increase a spell's spell factors without re-casting it \u2014 &quot;the spell can affect more targets than were present at the time of its casting&quot; seems to violate the spirit of that third thing, &quot;the spell has no more hold on you outside of the initial blast zone&quot; doesn't seem to jive with the first thing, and there are already spells to make hazards or alter a region of space that can specifically be used without concern for the second thing.<br /> <br /> If adding Area Scale to a spell not naturally based on altering an area changes the functional duration of the effect and the validity of targets the spell can stick to and the essential function of the spell, that's a rather more involved outcome than is implied by &quot;you can choose to have this spell affect an area&quot; in a context where, normally, if you're hit with a spell then you're hit with a spell and being hit with a spell doesn't make touching you a vector for hitting other targets with that spell. It's a fundamental alteration to how a given spell works instead of just a change to what it hits at the point of casting and that kind of merits any concrete reference at all rather than pointing to &quot;an area effect applies its effect to everything in the area&quot; and expecting anyone to extrapolate that to &quot;and it stops applying it to anything that leaves that area&quot; for all spells that could conceivably have that Scale factor added to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> spare us essays on your interpretation of awakened magic. </div> </div> </div>The Ignore List is a useful option in your Profile settings if you don't want to look at my posts, but I'm not going to stop <i>trying to piece together a coherent explanation of how the rules are intended to work as a whole and what they're intended to model</i> when people<i> keep complaining that the rules don't make sense</i> just because my using big words supposedly makes your head hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T01:55:10-07:00","id":1125825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125783#post1125783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not interpretation when he's right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read DaveBs comment on it? The one saying that a cloaking spell over an area drops off if you leave the area and reapplies if you enter? And that if you want multiple targets that can split up you need to use multiple targets scale?<br /> <br /> That proves how it works definitely and yet satchel continues to argue that he knows how the rules are intended to work as a whole. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T01:55:58-07:00","id":1125826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125785#post1125785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but I'm not going to stop <i>trying to piece together a coherent explanation of how the rules are intended to work as a whole and what they're intended to model</i> when people<i> keep complaining that the rules don't make sense</i> just because my using big words supposedly makes your head hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Im not complaining that the rules dont make sense here, you are the only one complaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T02:09:54-07:00","id":1125830,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> ts and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Satchel you both think its entirely possible to cram 40 people into a small room, take a -2 penalty and give them all one +5 strength then allow them to split up and go all over the place. <br /> <br /> And that either you have to go find where the spell was originally cast (its not there though) or dispel each of the 40 people one at a time?<br /> <br /> Why then would anybody take a -6 penalty for 40 people? (oh because if there is enemies there they will get it too blah blah, but lets assume a safe place) If the people split up you are getting 40 strength spells for a -2 penalty instead of -6?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T08:54:33-07:00","id":1125918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125825#post1125825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That proves how it works definitely and yet satchel continues to argue that he knows how the rules are intended to work as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has given contradictory answers before, the fiction has not provided much in the way of examples of it working as he describes it, and &quot;it works this way as a trade-off for advanced play&quot; is not a satisfactory explanation of <i>why</i> the factor should work this way.<br /> <br /> I have not been arguing that I know how the rules are intended to work as a whole \u2014 I am saying <i>that is what I am <b>attempting</b> to do</i>, and that a mechanical application that doesn't seem to gel with the rest of the setting and mechanics frustrates that attempt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125826#post1125826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not complaining that the rules dont make sense here, you are the only one complaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do communicate with people besides you on this subject, Git. There's been a few of them, but you're the first so far to claim that I ought to shut up entirely just so you don't have to look at large numbers of words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125830#post1125830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that either you have to go find where the spell was originally cast (its not there though)</div> </div> </div> </div>Things you use as a Yantra have a sympathetic connection to you, as do the subjects of your spells. It is no great stretch to think that the site of an area-based spell would retain its status as &quot;the place where this mage cast this spell&quot; with or without the spell being constantly and exclusively activating within those grounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why then would anybody take a -6 penalty for 40 people? (oh because if there is enemies there they will get it too blah blah, but lets assume a safe place) If the people split up you are getting 40 strength spells for a -2 penalty instead of -6? </div> </div> </div>Because precision is a thing, because you can target subjects in different places with Advanced or Sympathetic Range, because the Long-Term Nimbus makes getting your magic on something more likely to have consequences later regardless of what the spell does, because the thing you're trying to accomplish has nothing to do with whether people are in an area, because getting forty people into a small room is actually kind of hard to do outside the context of a densely-packed classroom full of students or a waiting line at a small and busy office even without accounting for room you might need to make use of Yantras, because maintaining a separate safe place from your Sanctum is something that takes effort and/or resources that you might not have available to spare and bringing a bunch of people into your Sanctum is a comparatively large risk, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T09:21:13-07:00","id":1125928,"title":"","content":"If you target an area, you have targeted everything in that area. Anyone effected by the spell because they're in the area stops being affected by it once they leave, and anyone walking into it becomes affected.<br /> <br /> Like I said in the quoted post, this is why you <i>want</i> to do things like push Number of Subjects to 10 rather than just targeting the room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:22:22-07:00","id":1126040,"title":"","content":"I've got to agree with Satchel that it's pretty unintuitive for area as the scale factor to change the effect of a spell from &quot;change the subject into a frog&quot; to &quot;make the subject change people into frogs&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:30:05-07:00","id":1126044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125928#post1125928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you target an area, you have targeted everything in that area. Anyone effected by the spell because they're in the area stops being affected by it once they leave, and anyone walking into it becomes affected.<br /> <br /> Like I said in the quoted post, this is why you <i>want</i> to do things like push Number of Subjects to 10 rather than just targeting the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that if i cast &quot;turn into frogs&quot; spell then the people and the structure will become frogs? What happens when the frog towers collapse when the spell end, does the building becomes rubble or return intact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:38:37-07:00","id":1126049,"title":"","content":"Presumably you choose what you're targeting to begin with when you cast the spell, if it's objects, people, or anything in the area of effect. That's what the Imago is for.<br /> <br /> If the frog towers collapsed the building would be rubble. But I think that would have to involve turning things into many frogs, as opposed to a single frog for the object. Like are you turning a person into a frog, a human-sized frog, or a human-shaped pile of frogs? All things that would be determined by the Imago and, as Terrorforge points out, the Arcana used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-07-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:43:31-07:00","id":1126054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126044#post1126044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean that if i cast &quot;turn into frogs&quot; spell then the people and the structure will become frogs? What happens when the frog towers collapse when the spell end, does the building becomes rubble or return intact?</div> </div> </div> </div>The structure only becomes frogs if you cast is as a Matter 4 + Life 4 Creative Thaumaturgy spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:09:57-07:00","id":1126110,"title":"","content":"I think the intuitive bit depends on where a person comes at it from. Vancian magic has a completely different outlook than the magic system in Mage. If a person familiar with a specific spell-centric magic system deals with variable spell parameters then they keep the basic spell and the parameters' affects change based on the spell. The Mage system is centered on an effect and all the spell parameters/rules are absolute. Keeping the correct mindset for the system helps.<br /> <br /> It is intuitive to consider a &quot;turn into a frog&quot; spell to be based on subject rather than area. However, aimed spells are always area, so then you can't have a ranged frog spell, it would be a zone of frog. A zone of frog is already counter-intuitive, so switch to something that is intuitively going to work with an area and back translate.<br /> <br /> A spell that sets the temperature of a room would intuitively have an area scale. If a thermometer was in the area for the spell's duration and removed, the thermometer would adjust to the ambient temperature. At least, that would be the intuitive result. A thermometer brought into the area would quick as it could read the temperature of the room set by the spell. The spell effect is not lasting so intuitively this is how it works.<br /> <br /> If we then switch this to a spell that turns people into frogs within the area, a person substitutes for a thermometer in the above example. Inside they are a frog, outside they are not. Lasting effects are permanent. A spell duration is only relevant as long as the magic is in effect and the magic is on the area rather than spread like some contagion onto things within the area.<br /> <br /> Without familiarity with free-form effect-based power systems, this may not be intuitive, but that is a lack of understanding of how the system works. Mechanically, you can't take a spell that turns a person into a frog and have it affect an area, a person is not an area. Instead you make an area where people turn into frogs. If the area is what is affected then it doesn't matter if it is temperature control, complete silence, or people turning into frogs, you will always be limited to the magic only works within the area.<br /> <br /> There are limits to the magic system. Attainments and archmastery are necessary to overcome the limits. The system doesn't support tossing a spell into a room that turns everyone into a frog for a month whether they stay in the room or not in the basic form of the system. This is good because free-form systems are complicated enough.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I found it incredibly difficult to follow the supposedly intuitive way of looking at the magic because it didn't seem to fit the free-form power model. Going from subject to area means losing subjects as a focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:50:06-07:00","id":1126119,"title":"","content":"The shorter answer would be to create Satchel's spell requires a turn to frog spell using a subject scale that is combined with a hung spell that has a condition of entering the specific area or some other method to create a contingency. There are two magic effects anyway you look at it. The first casts a spell on people within the room and upon entering the room for a duration. The second is the frog spell cast on a person with its own duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:57:57-07:00","id":1126125,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I never looked at it like that. I always assumed area spells inflicted their duration on the targets in the casting range rather than the <i>area</i> unless the subject to be affected was the area itself to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T18:00:18-07:00","id":1126126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126119#post1126119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shorter answer would be to create Satchel's spell requires a turn to frog spell using a subject scale that is combined with a hung spell that has a condition of entering the specific area or some other method to create a contingency. There are two magic effects anyway you look at it. The first casts a spell on people within the room and upon entering the room for a duration. The second is the frog spell cast on a person with its own duration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> any lose of dramatic event type magical accidents? </div> </div> </div>I hope <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> can see that is gone if you just think about it for a little bit. I admit though it would have taken me a bit of time to come up with that solution but i hope id have managed it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-07-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T21:25:45-07:00","id":1126169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126110#post1126110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we then switch this to a spell that turns people into frogs within the area, a person substitutes for a thermometer in the above example. Inside they are a frog, outside they are not. Lasting effects are permanent. A spell duration is only relevant as long as the magic is in effect and the magic is on the area rather than spread like some contagion onto things within the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing \u2014 my reading was that the spell goes off in the area and sticks to anyone that was within that area when it went off, but did not otherwise continue to propagate in the case of effects that do not specifically mess with a location, because sticking to people is what a person-affecting spell effect cast at every other Range except Aimed does. It does not follow intuitively that a spell to affect an individual target can only not affect an individual target at one specific point on the range axis \u2014 as-written, an Aimed spell that hits a person affects them only as long as they remain within arm's reach of the space they occupied when you hit them unless there's another hidden exception that lets Aimed spells without any extra Scale factors ignore the stipulation that Aimed spells must use Area Scale.<br /> <br /> There are spells for which people obviously substitute for thermometers in the above analogy, but they're spells whose effects are already things like &quot;gravity works differently in this space&quot; or &quot;there's a wall of fire here&quot; or &quot;this place is actually another place.&quot; I can conceive of plenty of visual metaphors for personally-targeted effects that pick up and cease when a person enters and leaves a given location, but the lack of anything like one of them in the book \u2014 the lack of some sort of &quot;here's how spells work in the fiction as extensions of a mage's will in the world of three spatial dimensions and linear time&quot; \u2014 means none of them come to mind as readily as &quot;making this spell into a projectile affected by Defense and cover means boosting its number of potential targets works by making it splash outward on impact.&quot;<br /> <br /> The fact that you have to find the disjunction and reverse-engineer an entirely different paradigm of effect-placement when the most obvious thing to indicate the splash-based reading isn't how it works is the bit where it's dramatically easier to use Area Scale than Number of Subjects to affect large numbers of people is, I think, self-explanatory as a demonstration that this could have been made clearer than it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are limits to the magic system. Attainments and archmastery are necessary to overcome the limits. The system doesn't support tossing a spell into a room that turns everyone into a frog for a month whether they stay in the room or not in the basic form of the system. This is good because free-form systems are complicated enough. </div> </div> </div>There are limits to the magic system, yes. One of the established, specifically-stated limits that I had based my opposition to &quot;the spell can pick up new targets and drop old ones&quot; on was the fact that that's a lower-key version of the qualities particular to Dynamics spells. A spell that can theoretically apply a normally targeted effect to an entire neighborhood full of people (but no more than that over the course of its Duration) seems substantially more precedented than a spell that can theoretically target <i>many times the population of</i> an entire neighborhood full of people over the course of its Duration before the level of Arcanum competence at which you can make viral memetic spells.<br /> <br /> It saves bookkeeping on figuring who's still affected, gives another clear reason to bother with number-based Scale, and adds another tick to the box of Excuses For Mages To Work In Isolated Locales, but the questions it raises in turn are <i>also</i> not answered or alluded to by the book \u2014 Can the area be moved, like a lantern or a sunshade or a shroud, to allow characters to maintain an effect while moving from place to place? Do characters subjected to the spell within the area gain the same sympathy to the mage that a direct target would, or is this type of Scale a viable means of targeting a subject without making them a mobile link back to you or subjecting them to your Long-Term Nimbus? Does any other normal spell modification have this same slipperiness that allows a subject to shed the effect without ending the spell or reducing its effective Potency to nil, or is Area Scale unique in this regard? Does any partial-effect weirdness happen at the thresholds of the area, or does the spell only affect a target that's fully inside the target area? Can dynamic spell control shape holes into the area of a spell's effect that either bisect the space or have no connection to an exterior edge, or does the blanketed area have to be a single contiguous filled region? \u2014 and the fact that the system defaults to &quot;a spell affects the thing it works on until it ends&quot; rather than &quot;a spell affects viable subjects in the space it occupies at the start of its Duration, which may be mobile and fragmentary if that space is one or more discrete objects, and if a viable subject is in that space it is under the effects of the spell until it leaves or the spell ends&quot; is one of those vital framing mechanisms akin to &quot;all spells default to ritual casting time unless effort and insight are leveraged to make it take effect sooner&quot; for the purposes of understanding How Magic Works.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to get clarification, but I'd prefer if that clarification came with actionable adjustments to my understanding of how it all hangs together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Rogue line-break. 08-08-2017, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T22:05:06-07:00","id":1126178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126110#post1126110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system doesn't support tossing a spell into a room that turns everyone into a frog for a month whether they stay in the room or not in the basic form of the system. This is good because free-form systems are complicated enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you can cast a spell like that, you just can't do it with an Aimed spell, which is what I'm guessing you mean by 'tossing a spell.' Presumably because you can't throw things at multiple people at once without some sort of special trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-08-2017, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T22:19:06-07:00","id":1126181,"title":"","content":"I'm glad learning about Mutants and Masterminds was of some use. The system probably isn't the most intuitive. I'm not a mage expert so there could easily be a better way to create the contingency effect.<br /> <br /> An aimed spell being called out like it is justifies having the effect on the target (person). It is a special case. I think that actually does stick with the person. Maybe I shouldn't have brought that up.<br /> <br /> In the end, a spell that (arbitrarily setting factors) turns all the people inside a room into frogs for one month has two target types with two durations (possibly more) or is a spell that uses number of subjects and the room is irrelevant. Since a spell can't have two types of targets and multiple durations, that obviously would be wrong. A combined spell or a spell with some attainment or something is required to overcome the multiple effect. When you target an area by using the area of effect column, you must effect the area, but that does not limit affecting things within the area while they remain in the area.<br /> <br /> The system probably doesn't make sense in character. It is a frame of reference issue that I wrote about before. The system is mathematical and breaks immersion, so within that frame of reference it is possible to intuit how things work easily enough. Intuition will be false if one keeps a less formulaic mindset that can seriously diminish fun.<br /> <br /> I do understand how the opposite view on the spell is reasonable. Unfortunately, reasonable is not always right in mathematics. I don't know how else to say how it works other than when a spell uses the area of effect column the target is the area and the effect can only affect something within the area as long as it remains in the area. If the effect was filling an area with water then everything in the area should be wet even if it leaves the area because that would be a lasting effect, but a cup removed from the area would be empty of water.<br /> <br /> Simple systems like this aren't necessarily easy. M&amp;M is even more simple, and difficult to grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T22:23:15-07:00","id":1126184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126178#post1126178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you can cast a spell like that, you just can't do it with an Aimed spell, which is what I'm guessing you mean by 'tossing a spell.' Presumably because you can't throw things at multiple people at once without some sort of special trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I shouldn't have mentioned aimed spells because that would be the logical interpretation. I meant targeting the room. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T23:39:46-07:00","id":1126202,"title":"","content":"Ok, maybe someone can walk me through where my parsing of the book's text is going wrong. Let's say I want to cast Without a Trace on a room (maybe it's a crime scene and I don't want anyone to find out my cabalmates and I were there, whatever.) The book says, &quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within.&quot; Ok, so far so good. So, if my three cabalmates and I are in the area of effect, they and I will have the effect placed on us that, &quot;For the Duration of the spell, the subject leaves no fingerprints, footprints, traces of blood, or any other forensic type evidence of herself behind. Using Death Mage Sight to search for such signs provokes a Clash of Wills.&quot; I don't see how the interaction of these two quotes would lead to me leaving footprints during the duration of the spell if I leave the room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-08-2017, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T00:21:06-07:00","id":1126209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126202#post1126202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe someone can walk me through where my parsing of the book's text is going wrong. Let's say I want to cast Without a Trace on a room (maybe it's a crime scene and I don't want anyone to find out my cabalmates and I were there, whatever.) The book says, &quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within.&quot; Ok, so far so good. So, if my three cabalmates and I are in the area of effect, they and I will have the effect placed on us that, &quot;For the Duration of the spell, the subject leaves no fingerprints, footprints, traces of blood, or any other forensic type evidence of herself behind. Using Death Mage Sight to search for such signs provokes a Clash of Wills.&quot; I don't see how the interaction of these two quotes would lead to me leaving footprints during the duration of the spell if I leave the room.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without a trace's text is badly written, it should say &quot;while under the effects of this spell the characters fingerprints, footprints, traces of blood or any other forensic type of evidence of herself cannot be detected.&quot; Its only a veiling spell which reveals fingerprints etc when clashed so its not stopping the targets leaving evidence just cloaking it for the duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> So while in the area all forensic evidence is cloaked with a magical veil no matter who leaves it and when you leave the area people can see your footprints, fingerprints again that you leave outside the area.<br /> <br /> Example inside the area you hands are covered in blood, but appear to leave no marks on anything, you leave the area and your bloody hands start leaving prints on the walls etc. The spell area spell ends and you look back inside the area and suddenly all your bloody hand marks are now visible that previously you couldnt see because they were veiled..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-08-2017, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T04:14:25-07:00","id":1126251,"title":"","content":"Casting Without a Trace on the room using area of effect would change the description to &quot;For the Duration of the spell, <b>all</b> subjects leave no fingerprints, footprints, traces of blood, or any other forensic type evidence of herself behind <b>while in the area</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the subjects could leave the room and still wouldn't leave any trace then what would happen to new people entering the room during the duration? If the spell doesn't affect the new people then it wasn't actually cast on an area. It would be the same as using number of subjects which means redundancy. If new people are affecting then what duration do they have? There should only be the one duration. That would make it the same as Without a Trace cast on anyone inside the room for full duration and the remaining duration for anyone entering later based on the time one enters. Or a big complicated mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T05:35:34-07:00","id":1126267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126251#post1126251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting Without a Trace on the room using area of effect would change the description to &quot;For the Duration of the spell, <b>all</b> subjects <i><b>appear to</b> </i>leave no fingerprints, footprints, traces of blood, or any other forensic type evidence of herself behind <b>while in the area</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but fixed it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:15:41-07:00","id":1126293,"title":"","content":"So the answer to &quot;where is my parsing of the text going wrong?&quot; is &quot;in the writing of the text itself&quot;, right? You see why this is not an intuitive interpretation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T08:51:37-07:00","id":1126318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126251#post1126251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If new people are affecting then what duration do they have? There should only be the one duration. That would make it the same as Without a Trace cast on anyone inside the room for full duration and the remaining duration for anyone entering later based on the time one enters. Or a big complicated mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, again, &quot;spells cannot increase their factors without being re-cast&quot; is one of those things that seems directly contradicted by allowing the spell to affect more people than were present when it was cast \u2014 to a casual reading, the effect of Pocket Dimension is &quot;there is a Pocket Dimension of this scale,&quot; not &quot;anyone who enters the area covered by this scale is in a Pocket Dimension,&quot; and likewise for similar spells that normally affect an area, and the top billing and less stringent requirements of Target Scale combined with the language of a spell &quot;hitting&quot; a region bias the natural reading towards &quot;spells that normally affect targets act the same without explicit changes represented by Reach effects et al.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;there should only be the one duration&quot; as a reading <i>relies on the predicate that the spell's effect must remain in the area</i> to be arrived at as a conclusion \u2014 when &quot;the spell remains in the area and anyone who enters it later gains the effect as well&quot; is, as far as I've seen, a view seriously advanced by <i>nobody in this discussion</i>.<br /> <br /> The sticky-effect reading assumes that there is <i>one</i> Duration, which applies to anyone who the spell hits when it initially goes off and nobody else, which is how spells that apply to people normally operate. Again, the only significant clues that this isn't how it works are a notional redundancy that can still be justified by preparation and safety being important to the Wise and the fact that naturally Area-based spells that affect locations still affect people in those locations. Otherwise you're fighting the instinct that giving a spell Area Scale \u2014 a thing that takes no special resources on its own and must be applied on any spell cast outside of Touch Range without Sensory Range \u2014 fundamentally changes the description of what the spell does in a fashion whose reverse is literally a Reach effect for some published core spells, lets a long-Duration spell affect dramatically more subjects over time than just the ones that can fit inside that space, and removes an aspect of target-based spells that does not obviously owe itself to the spell being target-based by letting the effect slide off subjects who leave the area and still regain it later.<br /> <br /> There's room to get to the spell-shadow interpretation \u2014 the above observation re: Pocket Dimension, the fact that a ball of fire burns people inside of it and not outside of it, the large number of media examples of sudden bolts of magic being vectors for damage or immobilization over more involved effects \u2014 but it would be a lot easier to arrive at that conclusion if &quot;spells last for their Duration and affect anyone who lingers in their area of effect&quot; was earlier in the description of how spellcraft worked rather than sandwiched in between &quot;spells affect a chosen target and last for their Duration&quot; and the rest of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Missing quotation mark. 08-08-2017, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:22:24-07:00","id":1126352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126040#post1126040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got to agree with Satchel that it's pretty unintuitive for area as the scale factor to change the effect of a spell from &quot;change the subject into a frog&quot; to &quot;make the subject change people into frogs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The room is not the subject, it is just the area where the spell resides. The subjects are &quot;people inside this room&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is also where your parsing of the Without a Trace goes wrong. As the Area spell says, it applies the effect to people in the room. Ergo, people outside the room are not having the effect applied to them. Note how it also does not call out the area as the subject. People inside are the subjects.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find this way of dealing with Area spells much more interesting. This way you can make radically different things happen by picking Area instead of Multiple targets, and vice versa. Making both work the same way except for &quot;this one targets indiscriminately, this one does not&quot; makes for less possibilities, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-08-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:44:55-07:00","id":1126363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126318#post1126318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;there should only be the one duration&quot; as a reading <i>relies on the predicate that the spell's effect must remain in the area</i> to be arrived at as a conclusion \u2014 when &quot;the spell remains in the area and anyone who enters it later gains the effect as well&quot; is, as far as I've seen, a view seriously advanced by <i>nobody in this discussion</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what Dave said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:59:59-07:00","id":1126376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126363#post1126363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that what Dave said?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Satchel is saying is that nobody in the &quot;sticky spells&quot; camp has suggested that duration would count down on the area as well as the individuals it sticks to, so &quot;there should only be one duration&quot; is a rebuttal to an argument no one has made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:29:54-07:00","id":1126388,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> <br /> Two questions.<br /> <br /> Prelacy forms a black iron portal in the Oneiros of a Seer Mage. I take it this is the equivalent of a Supernal verge keyed to the Exarch that you get with a demesne and later dots of Prelacy?<br /> <br /> And the Patron tool yantra can be formed by connections with Exarchs and, sometimes Scelesti bargain for them as well. Is this a Supernal and Abyssal entity thing only, or could a mage who swore allegiance to some great spirit or other thing use that as a patron tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:52:19-07:00","id":1126397,"title":"","content":"My rhetorical questions were designed to point out the logical flaws in all the positions that I could think up not suggesting that anyone had or should take that view. My view is the changed quoted text I provided, and I agree that it seems to be suggesting Lasting effects without justification, but sometimes writers fudge things, so I didn't touch that. It doesn't affect the difference between number of subjects or area of effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a><br /> &quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within (while within the area).&quot; I added the part in parenthesis to help you. It should be understood because there is a clear choice between number of subjects and area of effect, but obviously not everyone can see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a><br /> I'm not sure how Pocket Dimension comes into play. The factor is a choice between number of subjects and area is irrelevant or area of effect where number of subjects is irrelevant. After choosing area of effect, I think a &quot;reading that relies on the predicate that the spell's effect must remain in the area&quot; is natural. Choose number of subjects otherwise. The redundancy issue is not a minor thing. It is a system breaking thing. They should have wrote that spells are either subject or area oriented and use the appropriate column if that is what was wanted. A clear choice counter to that was made when the text says &quot;the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want to create an area that simulates the effects of a spell on a subject for everyone within the area, subject to discriminating subjects using Fate, you are covered. You are also covered if you want to apply the spell to multiple subjects by choosing number of subjects as a factor to increase by Reach and taking penalties. The &quot;sticky effect&quot; reading prevents spell effect on an area to create a choice between discriminating subjects or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think an area of effect spell that affects the area rather than subjects that happen to be in the area at the time is pretty intuitive. The nature of the spell then dictates whether the spell's effect is on the area or subjects within the area. Obviously, Without a Trace has no effect on an area directly as areas leave no traces by default. The nature of some spells require the effect work on subjects so you choose between simply casting the spell on multiple subjects instead of multiple times on each subject or cast on an area so subjects within the area are affected by the spell effect with the limitation that the magic works only within the area.<br /> <br /> *Maybe create a thread to discuss the &quot;why it works&quot; because I think the question of &quot;how it works&quot; already has an official answer. The same scenario is going to get the same answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-08-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:13:19-07:00","id":1126404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126397#post1126397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within (while within the area).&quot; I added the part in parenthesis to help you. It should be understood because there is a clear choice between number of subjects and area of effect, but obviously not everyone can see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your parenthetical doesn't need to be added for there to be a clear choice between number of subjects and area of effect, though. Number of subjects can exclude subjects without the use of Warding Gesture. Area of Effect can include subjects of any size. The tradeoff is between precision and scope. So no, it should not be understood because it is neither explicitly mentioned nor implied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:20:00-07:00","id":1126406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126404#post1126404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your parenthetical doesn't need to be added for there to be a clear choice between number of subjects and area of effect, though. Number of subjects can exclude subjects without the use of Warding Gesture. Area of Effect can include subjects of any size. The tradeoff is between precision and scope. So no, it should not be understood because it is neither explicitly mentioned nor implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can all agree that it could have been worded more clearly. Author's intent has been made clear, however, so I'm not sure what more we can achieve by repeating that point. I doubt we'll get errata out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:32:10-07:00","id":1126410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126406#post1126406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can all agree that it could have been worded more clearly. Author's intent has been made clear, however, so I'm not sure what more we can achieve by repeating that point. I doubt we'll get errata out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, author's intent doesn't fit well within the rest of the system in this case. Especially when you consider how it interacts with aimed spells. If I throw Dispel Magic at an opponent to suppress their Environmental Shield, all they have to do is take a step to the side and it doesn't affect them any more? But then they have to avoid that particular 3-foot patch of floor? That seems like a significantly more &quot;system breaking&quot; issue to me than the partial overlap between Area of Effect Scale and Number of Targets spell. Shouldn't Scale change a spell's Scale, not what the spell <i>does</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:45:13-07:00","id":1126416,"title":"","content":"I say just rule zero it for your setting and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:30:54-07:00","id":1126431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126410#post1126410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, author's intent doesn't fit well within the rest of the system in this case. Especially when you consider how it interacts with aimed spells. If I throw Dispel Magic at an opponent to suppress their Environmental Shield, all they have to do is take a step to the side and it doesn't affect them any more? But then they have to avoid that particular 3-foot patch of floor? That seems like a significantly more &quot;system breaking&quot; issue to me than the partial overlap between Area of Effect Scale and Number of Targets spell. Shouldn't Scale change a spell's Scale, not what the spell <i>does</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>So don't use that particular spell as an aimed spell when you're not prepared to boost Area? Honestly I see no issue here.<br /> <br /> If that is the &quot;especially when you consider&quot; scenario then I think you're wording things a bit strongly.<br /> <br /> The flip side of the coin is that you can quite simply set up Dispel Magic zones in advance as traps or neutral meeting zones. That is pretty cool to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-08-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:04:41-07:00","id":1126441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126404#post1126404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your parenthetical doesn't need to be added for there to be a clear choice between number of subjects and area of effect, though. Number of subjects can exclude subjects without the use of Warding Gesture. Area of Effect can include subjects of any size. The tradeoff is between precision and scope. So no, it should not be understood because it is neither explicitly mentioned nor implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the choice is clear then why are you getting it wrong? A distinctive between two things is irrelevant when there is no choice between them. The choice you want to exist is nothing more than min/max while limiting options. The system is designed for utility rather than min/max options like when it doesn't allow a spell to have its primary factor changed.<br /> <br /> My fault for bringing up aimed spells, but they don't create an area of effect so there is no issue. I must have missed the part where you can't cast aimed spells on multiple targets if your spell has an increased number of subjects. I guess if that isn't allowed then you just get stuck casting the spell at range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:56:06-07:00","id":1126461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126441#post1126441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the choice is clear then why are you getting it wrong? A distinctive between two things is irrelevant when there is no choice between them. The choice you want to exist is nothing more than min/max while limiting options. The system is designed for utility rather than min/max options like when it doesn't allow a spell to have its primary factor changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wh... What? I'm &quot;getting it wrong&quot; because the text does not state or imply the (apparently) intended interpretation. Your argument for &quot;zone of frog&quot; interpretation relies on a nonexistent parenthetical statement that you claim should be understood due to the lack of distinction between Area of Effect Scale and Number of Subjects scale. But such a distinction does exist.<br /> <br /> The choice between Area of Effect and Number of Subjects in the &quot;sticky spells&quot; interpretation is a choice between greater scope and more precision. Neither changes the effect of the spell (which they shouldn't because the factor in question is SCALE, not EFFECT), and both change the scale of the spell in different ways. One allows you to select a number of specific targets within sensory range, the other indiscriminately affects all targets within a specified range. That's a choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126441#post1126441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My fault for bringing up aimed spells, but they don't create an area of effect so there is no issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do. Page 114, &quot;Aimed spells (see below) must use area of effect, centered on wherever the mage aims.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126441#post1126441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed the part where you can't cast aimed spells on multiple targets if your spell has an increased number of subjects. I guess if that isn't allowed then you just get stuck casting the spell at range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, aimed spells <i>have to be cast as area of effect</i> which makes a decent number of spells effectively useless when aimed under the &quot;zone of frog&quot; interpretation. For example a spell that turns someone into a frog, if aimed, only turns the subject into a frog as long as they remain within arms reach of where they were standing when you hit them with it. This, to me, is as mentioned in my previous post, a significantly more system breaking issue than there being partial (but not total) overlap between Area of Effect Scale and Number of Targets Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T17:42:44-07:00","id":1126517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126461#post1126461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, aimed spells <i>have to be cast as area of effect</i> which makes a decent number of spells effectively useless when aimed under the &quot;zone of frog&quot; interpretation. For example a spell that turns someone into a frog, if aimed, only turns the subject into a frog as long as they remain within arms reach of where they were standing when you hit them with it. This, to me, is as mentioned in my previous post, a significantly more system breaking issue than there being partial (but not total) overlap between Area of Effect Scale and Number of Targets Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've obviously not read the past two pages but considering everyone keeps talking about sticky spells, I suppose the question remains can the area of effect move. An aimed spell is going to hit one target, regardless of whether it's a spot in a room, a person, or an object. From there, does the area of effect move with a target, providing the target is capable of it?<br /> <br /> Lets go with a less silly spell than frog or without a trace. Windstrike. Everyone in this area takes bashing damage. If I use the aimed spell at the room, I can fill the room with it, but people can leave. If I use the aimed spell at John, if John leaves, does the area of effect go with him. It's come up for me, I've run it so that it does, even if that means John runs into a crowded place and then can damage more people than the caster planned. If this is not the intent, and that's clarified elsewhere, you can fix that with a Merit that allows for 'sticky' spells, or 'ricochet' spells, if you want to target a bunch of individual subjects with an aimed spell.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that everyone has different and, apparently, really strong views about how and why magic works, but if you look at the topic thread, you can see that this is not the place for them. Boil these problems down to the necessary 'simple question' and hopefully get, or give, a simple answer. Charlaquin's the mod, but it would be cool if you need to debate your treatises on magic you did it in an appropriate thread for it so people can get back to asking simple questions and getting simple answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T17:50:48-07:00","id":1126520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126461#post1126461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wh... What? I'm &quot;getting it wrong&quot; because the text does not state or imply the (apparently) intended interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're getting it wrong because the developer said your interpretation was wrong. I simply said it must not be clear if you're getting it wrong. Maybe I'm mistaken and you are purposefully interpreting something incorrectly. Whatever.<br /> <br /> I didn't see that about aimed spells because I forgot to get an updated copy. I'm not sure what the point of an aimed spell would be anymore. Nevermind, wrong page. The system works fine without aimed spells so I'm not sure how they can break the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-08-2017, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:07:46-07:00","id":1126527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126520#post1126520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're getting it wrong because the developer said your interpretation was wrong. I simply said it must not be clear if you're getting it wrong. Maybe I'm mistaken and you are purposefully interpreting something incorrectly. Whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This conversation is not following through logically.<br /> You: &quot;[while within the area] should be understood because there is a clear choice between number of subjects and area of effect.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Actually, that shouldn't be understood because the choice is already clear without it.&quot;<br /> You: &quot;If the choice is clear, why are you coming to the wrong interpretation?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Huh? Because the choice is already clear without your parenthetical, making it not understood? Isn't that what we were just talking about?&quot;<br /> You: &quot;Nu-uh! You're getting it wrong because Dave said so!&quot;<br /> <br /> There is no consistency between what you are saying from one post to the next.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126520#post1126520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't see that about aimed spells because I forgot to get an updated copy. I'm not sure what the point of an aimed spell would be anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I am arguing that Dave's answer seems inconsistent with the rest of the system. It creates more problems than it solves (and I'm still not convinced the problems it supposedly solves are indeed problems.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126517#post1126517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate that everyone has different and, apparently, really strong views about how and why magic works, but if you look at the topic thread, you can see that this is not the place for them. Boil these problems down to the necessary 'simple question' and hopefully get, or give, a simple answer. Charlaquin's the mod, but it would be cool if you need to debate your treatises on magic you did it in an appropriate thread for it so people can get back to asking simple questions and getting simple answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right. Sorry for the derail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:08:25-07:00","id":1126528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126520#post1126520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're getting it wrong because the developer said your interpretation was wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get that from, though? He was explaining how area of effect works. It focuses on an area. Walk in it, the spell gets you, walk out of it, the spell doesn't get you anymore.<br /> <br /> But when you choose the Scale of a spell, you make a choice between Area of Effect or Number of Subjects. 'Mages must decide when casting whether they are targeting specific subjects or a blanket area of effect.' If you choose Number of Subjects, you specifically target however many people. That's the point of Dave's mentioning pushing the scale up so you can get more individuals there, so you don't have a problem where John and Jack run far away from each other, or the room, and the spell stops working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T20:41:46-07:00","id":1126572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126527#post1126527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence why I am arguing that Dave's answer seems inconsistent with the rest of the system. It creates more problems than it solves (and I'm still not convinced the problems it supposedly solves are indeed problems.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, at least, consistent with how other Area Scale effects work, and if the framing of the spellcasting system is adjusted so that Area Scale is on the front end (it is, after all, already the finite column of the Scale chart) then we get the understandable outcomes of\u2026<br /> <br /> &quot;If you want to apply a persistent effect to a mobile subject you want to stay mobile but cannot touch, you're going to have to spend the Reach for Sensory Range.&quot;<br /> <br /> And\u2026<br /> <br /> &quot;A successfully-cast spell always does something, even if that something is just standing by waiting to affect a viable target.&quot;<br /> <br /> And\u2026<br /> <br /> &quot;Getting a spell to continuously affect a target no matter where they go requires the spell focus on that target to the degree that, if successfully cast and left alone, the spell is inescapable for its Duration.&quot;<br /> <br /> A huge portion of what's making this weird is that expressing the mechanics as a set of continuums presently makes the effects of Area Scale on targeted spells look like a strange blip in the middle of the arc rather than a branch at the starting point. The name and nature of the Nimbus helps a bit with conceptualizing it after that, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:34:18-07:00","id":1126585,"title":"","content":"Is this still going on? Wow.<br /> <br /> I think its come to the stage now where some people had the wrong interpretation, either from misreading the books or misunderstanding the magic rules and that they either need to decide to house rule it or play as intended. What is going to come of any more discussion/arguments on the matter? <br /> <br /> If your mind isnt changed then play it however you like, nobody will give a crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-09-2017, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:57:57-07:00","id":1126595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126585#post1126585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this still going on? Wow.<br /> <br /> I think its come to the stage now where some people had the wrong interpretation, either from misreading the books or misunderstanding the magic rules and that they either need to decide to house rule it or play as intended. What is going to come of any more discussion/arguments on the matter? <br /> <br /> If your mind isnt changed then play it however you like, nobody will give a crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I apologized in my previous post for derailing the thread. It's clearly a pointless thing to argue over, I just get weirdly passionate about a few particular things in Mage for some reason and can't easily let them go. Maybe because I percieve them as inconsistencies that complicate an otherwise beautifully elegant system. Anyway, I'm leaving it here, hopefully we can get back to simple questions and simple answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-09-2017, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:28:07-07:00","id":1126739,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> Can I cast Exceptional Luck as Area of Effect on a Small Room, use the luck, move uot of the room (which would short circuit the luck I was given if it wasn't used up by now), and then move in again to have the effect applied to me again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:48:12-07:00","id":1126744,"title":"","content":"It probably shouldn't recharge used up boons/curses. So if you give yourself +4 dice on 4 rolls, use up two, leave and then reenter it should be reapplied but only with two instances remaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:50:28-07:00","id":1126746,"title":"","content":"I would rule that the luck used inside the room would have a universal counter, when a number of rolls were used, no matter who used them, it would tick off the number allowed and then end when they were exhausted. But that is how i would have it work in my games this is not to imply that this is how it should work or that it must work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:00:08-07:00","id":1126775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1126739#post1126739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...<br /> Can I cast Exceptional Luck as Area of Effect on a Small Room, use the luck, move uot of the room (which would short circuit the luck I was given if it wasn't used up by now), and then move in again to have the effect applied to me again?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say as long as your in the area you gain whatever the exceptional luck is giving you, anybody using it uses up one &quot;charge&quot;. If you leave you no longer get whatever it gave you but would regain it when you reentered the area with it still at whatever number of rolls or whatever was left. What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T05:54:10-07:00","id":1127073,"title":"","content":"Does anything actually say an area of effect spell has to be anchored to the Earth and not a vehicle or a person?<br /> <br /> Like, say I'm on a moving train, and I want to cast an AoE spell on the carriage I'm in. That would work, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-10-2017, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:38:55-07:00","id":1127146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127073#post1127073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anything actually say an area of effect spell has to be anchored to the Earth and not a vehicle or a person?<br /> <br /> Like, say I'm on a moving train, and I want to cast an AoE spell on the carriage I'm in. That would work, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the train would work yes, but not attaching it to something else like a person. I think the Area is static relative to the caster (otherwise even the earth wouldn't work). So if you are on a train and your Imago forms with the idea that 'where' you are is on the train then it would move with you. Same with a plane, ship or bus. Not sure how I feel about a car since the feeling of you still being 'on' the road is pretty present there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:04:12-07:00","id":1127155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127073#post1127073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anything actually say an area of effect spell has to be anchored to the Earth and not a vehicle or a person?<br /> <br /> Like, say I'm on a moving train, and I want to cast an AoE spell on the carriage I'm in. That would work, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It will work, you just define the area as the carriage and the spell affects things in it. Is it in the carriage yes, spell affects it, if not then it doesnt..Same with other movable areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:36:56-07:00","id":1127219,"title":"","content":"The spell &quot;Clear Thoughts&quot; that says &quot;The subject regains a point of Willpower&quot;. But since that's a direct effect of the spell, not a side effect of it, there's no reason why that'd be Lasting, is there?<br /> <br /> The spell does have a +2 Reach effect to make it lasting, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T16:14:12-07:00","id":1127390,"title":"","content":"Willpower should probably be treated like health. Keeping track of one granted by a spell for its duration would be a pain in the arse. What if they spend it and get another one? Do they still lose a willpower when the spell expires? <br /> <br /> No. They just get a willpower back, permanently. All other roads lead to madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T17:29:22-07:00","id":1127409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127219#post1127219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell &quot;Clear Thoughts&quot; that says &quot;The subject regains a point of Willpower&quot;. But since that's a direct effect of the spell, not a side effect of it, there's no reason why that'd be Lasting, is there?<br /> <br /> The spell does have a +2 Reach effect to make it lasting, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the lasting part to be vs the removing of conditions. So yeh what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> said too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:18:56-07:00","id":1127817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127390#post1127390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower should probably be treated like health. Keeping track of one granted by a spell for its duration would be a pain in the arse. What if they spend it and get another one? Do they still lose a willpower when the spell expires?<br /> <br /> No. They just get a willpower back, permanently. All other roads lead to madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand it, most healing is Lasting because it uses a loophole like speeding up natural regeneration, so once the spell ends the regen stops being sped up, but that doesn't reopen the wounds. Or it gives the mage the ability to sew together flesh, once the spell ends they lose that ability, but the flesh is still neatly sewn back together. I don't really see regaining willpower as &quot;healing&quot;, anyway.<br /> <br /> And there is no madness at all, it's perfectly trackable. Let's assume a starting willpower of 4 with a maximum of 5:<br /> <br /> With spell: 4 +1 (spell) = 5 -&gt; Use 1 = 4 -&gt; Regain one = 5 -&gt; spell ends, lose one = 4<br /> Without: 4 + 0 = 4 -&gt; Use 1 = 3 -&gt; Regain one = 4<br /> <br /> I don't see any conflict here? Maybe if you use the spell to regain a wp and then later indulge your virtue or something which should restore &quot;all&quot; your WP, and then you'll lose 1 when the spell ends, you might feel like you gained that one for nothing. Though luck, if you indugle in your vice and then get an opportunity to follow your virtue next scene, you'll also have done it for nothing. That's how it goes. I don't see a problem nor do I see any madness. It's not even hard to keep track of.<br /> <br /> It talks about the removing of the conditions in the Lasting part because the willpower bit is a reach effect, so it's not always there.<br /> <br /> They honestly should have devoted an entire page to just examples on what is and isn't Lasting. I feel like I can never get an actual understanding of it, and whenever people explain how they think it works inevitably it leads to &quot;Oh yes, well... except in THAT situation. There is is/isn't lasting, because... reasons...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-11-2017, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:39:38-07:00","id":1127850,"title":"","content":"What if you run out and then end the spell? What happens then? <br /> <br /> If you create a point temporary willpower that only exists as long as the spell does, then you need to keep track of that <i>particular </i>point of willpower. And then you wind up asking questions like &quot;do you spend willpower from the bottom of the stack or the top?&quot; <br /> <br /> Also regaining willpower is just as natural a process as healing. You can apply any loopholes to that here as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T20:21:42-07:00","id":1127901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127817#post1127817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I understand it, most healing is Lasting because it uses a loophole like speeding up natural regeneration, so once the spell ends the regen stops being sped up, but that doesn't reopen the wounds. Or it gives the mage the ability to sew together flesh, once the spell ends they lose that ability, but the flesh is still neatly sewn back together. I don't really see regaining willpower as &quot;healing&quot;, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Healing and damage spells can have a duration in which case they reoccur every gnosis spell interval. The effects of these spells have a lasting consequence however, either damage sticking around or wounds staying healed. I think you are confusing lasting effects created by a spell with an actual lasting spell.<br /> <br /> Control fire on a lighter to start a huge forest fire that rages on for weeks is still just a instant cast spell but it caused a lasting effect. <br /> <br /> You can think of gaining willpower to be like using control water to fill a glass, you use a spell to move the water into the glass and the water stays there when the spell has ended, same with willpower, you use magic to regain willpower and it remains in you when the spell ends.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T21:32:04-07:00","id":1127910,"title":"","content":"What practice of Mind would it be to bring people with you on an Astral Journey even if those individuals lack any astral travel powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T23:05:15-07:00","id":1127934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127910#post1127910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practice of Mind would it be to bring people with you on an Astral Journey even if those individuals lack any astral travel powers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> by people do you mean sleepers? Or a supernatural splat?<br /> <br /> But i would say Patterning (4) because that allows you to change things completely with a purview. Maybe seems a bit high and might be covered in astral realms book which i would have to check. I would allow lesser dots to allow a sleeper to enter his own oneiros though since they have that already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-12-2017, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T23:22:03-07:00","id":1127942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127934#post1127934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> by people do you mean sleepers? Or a supernatural splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Splats in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:02:56-07:00","id":1127964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127910#post1127910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practice of Mind would it be to bring people with you on an Astral Journey even if those individuals lack any astral travel powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely going to have to agree with Totalgit on this one - Patterning is where you are looking for. I also don't think that's high at all for the effect, either; Especially when you consider that that wasn't even an option in first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:06:48-07:00","id":1127965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127942#post1127942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splats in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ive not really checked the details of astral travel in 2e but in 1e each person needed to pay 1 mana to cross the threshold, if thats still a thing then you need to account for that too, 1e has a spell that allows the mage to pay the cost for others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:06:59-07:00","id":1127966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1127901#post1127901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Healing and damage spells can have a duration in which case they reoccur every gnosis spell interval. The effects of these spells have a lasting consequence however, either damage sticking around or wounds staying healed. I think you are confusing lasting effects created by a spell with an actual lasting spell.<br /> <br /> Control fire on a lighter to start a huge forest fire that rages on for weeks is still just a instant cast spell but it caused a lasting effect.<br /> <br /> You can think of gaining willpower to be like using control water to fill a glass, you use a spell to move the water into the glass and the water stays there when the spell has ended, same with willpower, you use magic to regain willpower and it remains in you when the spell ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, the water glass analogy actually works for me. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:48:28-07:00","id":1128228,"title":"","content":"Can someone please clarify or explain how exactly the Adamant Hand merit works, preferably using examples? In particular, I'm confused on what it would look like with Athletics but an example using Brawl or Weaponry would be helpful too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:31:36-07:00","id":1128247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1128228#post1128228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please clarify or explain how exactly the Adamant Hand merit works, preferably using examples? In particular, I'm confused on what it would look like with Athletics but an example using Brawl or Weaponry would be helpful too.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're running in a foot chase, the ST has you roll Dex+Athletics to gain distance between yourself and those pursuing you, that roll now counts as a +1 Order Tool Yantra reflexively applied to a spell you cast to create a portal to get out of there. Or, if that +1 isn't going to be enough, you can keep making Dex+Athletics rolls, prolonging the foot chase, until you've used up all your Yantra slots between 2 and 6 depending on your Gnosis and use those rolls as an excuse to keep adding +1 as an Order Tool Yantra until you feel you're set to cast the spell.<br /> <br /> It essentially allows you to use mundane Brawl, Weaponry, or Athletics rolls to power your spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:39:37-07:00","id":1128250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1128247#post1128247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're running in a foot chase, the ST has you roll Dex+Athletics to gain distance between yourself and those pursuing you, that roll now counts as a +1 Order Tool Yantra reflexively applied to a spell you cast to create a portal to get out of there. Or, if that +1 isn't going to be enough, you can keep making Dex+Athletics rolls, prolonging the foot chase, until you've used up all your Yantra slots between 2 and 6 depending on your Gnosis and use those rolls as an excuse to keep adding +1 as an Order Tool Yantra until you feel you're set to cast the spell.<br /> <br /> It essentially allows you to use mundane Brawl, Weaponry, or Athletics rolls to power your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant hand allows you specifically to &quot;use combat techniques as Yantras&quot; and applies only to &quot;use of that Skill in combat&quot;. Athletics covers attacks with thrown weapons and bows, and I'm pretty sure that's the intent of including it as a skill for Adamant Hand.<br /> <br /> By a selective reading of the RAW you could argue it also applies to e.g. Athletics rolls to dive into cover, but to me that seems contrary to the spirit of the Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:02:46-07:00","id":1128256,"title":"","content":"So each individual combat action can count as a distinct Yantra? Are you just able to save them until some point later in that combat until you're ready, or does it have to be immediately used on a spell right after the most recent combat action?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:06:04-07:00","id":1128258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1128256#post1128256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So each individual combat action can count as a distinct Yantra? Are you just able to save them until some point later in that combat until you're ready, or does it have to be immediately used on a spell right after the most recent combat action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like using regular Yantras they have to be used in consecutive turns that will end in a spell being cast. If combat ends you can cast a spell in the turn after combat from the bonuses you've accrued, but the bonuses will vanish after that final opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:15:30-07:00","id":1128261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1128258#post1128258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like using regular Yantras they have to be used in consecutive turns that will end in a spell being cast. If combat ends you can cast a spell in the turn after combat from the bonuses you've accrued, but the bonuses will vanish after that final opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, gotcha. So I could make 2 Brawl attacks in a row, then on my third turn cast a spell using two +1 Yantras for a total of +2 bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:32:21-07:00","id":1128264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1128261#post1128261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, gotcha. So I could make 2 Brawl attacks in a row, then on my third turn cast a spell using two +1 Yantras for a total of +2 bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>You got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:08:47-07:00","id":1129305,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'm reading the spell Constant Presence (Time 2) correct. Could anyone explain that spell for me as if I where five ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:12:13-07:00","id":1129306,"title":"","content":"When you use a time travel spell, the changes you make alter reality so that everyone but you remembers the new timeline but forgets the old one, and if you kill someone they'll suddenly be dead or whatever.<br /> <br /> Constant presence makes you ignore the changes to yourself caused by other people time travelling. So if they go back and kill you you won't die. But everyone might suddenly think you're dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:09:44-07:00","id":1129594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1129305#post1129305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'm reading the spell Constant Presence (Time 2) correct. Could anyone explain that spell for me as if I where five ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeh so Bob the Bad is older than you, he goes back and kills your mother before you were born. You better have cast constant presence. Its a shielding practice so basically it shields (provokes a clash) you from anything other people do to change you via time travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:15:27-07:00","id":1129650,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hi guys, I have a whole bunch of mage questions. It\u2019s my first mage game and it\u2019s a really dense book so I\u2019m just trying to figure this all out and it\u2019s way more challenging than I thought. There are a bunch so sorry in advance. Didn't want to make a whole thread about it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>I have a couple questions on familiars.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can one communicate telepathically with a familiar? Do you have to talk out loud to it? That seems very inconvenient and conspicuous, but I don\u2019t see anything in either the merit or the condition that suggests otherwise. Can you have a familiar without possessing its respective rank 2 attainment? Mind\u2019s Eye for Goetia, Eyes of the Dead for ghosts, etc.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If you can\u2019t communicate with a familiar telepathically without a spell, would said spell need to be a combined spell, using Telepathy (Mind 2) with Speak with the Dead (Death 1) for example? Or could one use Creative Thaumaturgy with just the corresponding Arcana? (Needing only spirit for a spirit familiar, etc.) And with what Practice, Ruling?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>I have a couple questions on Path/Order tools. </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The book says each path has 5 path tools. Do these tools have to be from the materials listed in the sidebar below as well as one of the items listed? Can it be one or the other? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And what counts as a rod? Could a measuring ruler count as a rod? A pen? A stick? An instrument vaguely shaped like one, like a chisel or a ice pick? Could I use a lead pipe as a Moros to count as either a weapon or a rod as the need suits me?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second. Is the bonus from Perfected Metals (from the </span></span><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9RnlfTkJnY2NyMjQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">perfected metallurgy preview</span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) in </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>addition</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> to the bonus from being a regular tool? For example, let\u2019s say I have a chalice made of silver, and I perfect the silver into lunargent using the Hone the Perfected form spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>According to the book: </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: Each item used as a Yantra adds +1 die to the spellcasting pool. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cups or other drinking vessels can invoke healing, intuition, perceptual magic, and gathering together. Drinking from a shared cup is a common way to spread a spell among a group.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>And according to the preview:</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lunargent offers a +2 tool Yantra for spells associated with seeing such as other places, other times, and across the Gauntlet. Additionally, it reflects things in Twilight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So if I\u2019m casting Exorcist\u2019s Eye, a Spirit spell with increased scale so that myself and my whole cabal can peer across the Gauntlet, do I get the higher of the two bonuses (+2 from lunargent), the combined bonuses of the item (+1 from Cup, +2 from Lunargent for a total of +3) or would I need to count them each as a separate yantra for a +1 and +2, separately?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can you use different parts of the same item (A knife with a gem encrusted handle, for example?) to count toward the same tool?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Last one on Twilight</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is a Death spell that allows you to pull items from twilight, and then one that allows you to shape ephemera, can you combine those to shape say\u2026. A key for the door? (provided you already know what the key needs to look like because of that one matter spell). What are you pulling from? Is there just a twilight version of everything in the real world and you can just pull a desk from twilight and shape it into a key? I know what the shadow looks like, but what do Mind and Death attuned twilight look like? What\u2019s there? I know it\u2019s a state and not a place, but I\u2019m not sure I understand what I see when I peer into Twilight when I look, aside from Ghosts and Goetia. Does it just look like black space? Is it just ghosts superimposed over the room I'm in? <i>Does Shape Ephemera refer specifically to ghosts, what other ephemera is there?</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m also not sure I understand Artifacts, Imbued items (especially) or Enhanced items (or the different purposes for each), but I probably won\u2019t be using them so I\u2019m not going to even bother.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thanks for your help, guys. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:46:36-07:00","id":1129663,"title":"","content":"Are 2e rules for the Tremere floating around somewhere I haven't seen? Someone elsewhere was acting like we had official ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:52:37-07:00","id":1129667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1129663#post1129663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are 2e rules for the Tremere floating around somewhere I haven't seen? Someone elsewhere was acting like we had official ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave B has mentioned a few things about how the Tremere differ from the standard Mage template, but I'm not sure exactly which thread that's in. I'll try and dig it up. No official mechanics though. I think they were in a post where he was talking about a modified Integrity Trait for Scelesti as well. Joining, I think it was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:02:04-07:00","id":1129674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1129667#post1129667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave B has mentioned a few things about how the Tremere differ from the standard Mage template, but I'm not sure exactly which thread that's in. I'll try and dig it up. No official mechanics though. I think they were in a post where he was talking about a modified Integrity Trait for Scelesti as well. Joining, I think it was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know what you find for either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:17:37-07:00","id":1129682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1129674#post1129674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me know what you find for either.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1094970-what-have-you-done-with-the-new-tremere?p=1095933#post1095933\">RBAWintrow did a neat little compilation post back in May</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:20:39-07:00","id":1129685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1129682#post1129682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1094970-what-have-you-done-with-the-new-tremere?p=1095933#post1095933&amp;quot;]RBAWintrow</a> did a neat little compilation post back in May[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you kindly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:25:17-07:00","id":1129686,"title":"","content":"Yup, that's the compilation post I was trying to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:25:27-07:00","id":1129727,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5279\" data-vbnamecard=\"5279\">Amravanti</a><br /> <br /> Familiars: You can telepathically communicate with your familiar, share senses with them, and they're solid/visible to you all as a default part of the benefit of having one. This comes from the fact that they share a Connected Sympathetic bond with you which makes them metaphysically a part of you.<br /> <br /> Path/Order Tools: In my games we assume that a rod is a thing you can point with that's made out of the appropriate Path material. So yeah, a lead pipe would work just fine, and I'd probably let it double as a mace as well.<br /> <br /> When presented with the Yantra bonus of perfected materials you take the higher value, so with your lunargent example you'd take just the +2.<br /> <br /> Twilight: Can be cluttered with whatever you want, or the lack thereof. Things that are suddenly destroyed often also leave &quot;ghosts&quot; behind, non-sentient ephemeral versions of their former selves. If an Avernian gate opens in the same area as them I assume they'd be sucked into the Underworld, but I don't know. From inside Twilight the regular world looks pretty much unchanged, but blurry and out of focus, so from outside Twilight looking in I would assume that the world looks pretty much unchanged but with an overlay of ghosts or goetia.<br /> <br /> You can in fact pull ephemera (If it's available, from ghosts or other sources) from Twilight and shape it into useful objects like a key. I'm personally not sure if you're supposed to be able to do that with ectoplasm though, which is basically ghost snot slathered on shit so they can Manifest.<br /> <br /> Artifacts/Imbued Items: I'm not sure anyone knows how these are actually supposed to work, the rules appear to be incomplete. They'll probably get back to them in SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:55:55-07:00","id":1129751,"title":"","content":"See, I thought you could telepathically communicate with a familiar too, but that's not actually mentioned anywhere. Just sharing senses, which isn't quite the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T06:33:03-07:00","id":1129763,"title":"","content":"Different types of Twilight are cluttered with different things. Death has ghosts and ghostly representations of ruined objects and buildings. Spirit contains the odd spirits that've managed to breach the Gauntlet. Mind doesn't naturally contain anything. Only summoned Goetia and psychic projections end up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T22:30:00-07:00","id":1130149,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> Thanks, everyone.<br /> <br /> Bummer about familiars, but you did help me understand Death twilight better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:46:11-07:00","id":1130188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1130149#post1130149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> <br /> Thanks, everyone.<br /> <br /> Bummer about familiars, but you did help me understand Death twilight better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just communicate subvocally, or establish a code that literally only works for someone who can share your senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:56:16-07:00","id":1130192,"title":"","content":"Even if you can't see a familiar by yourself, they can probably still manifest. <br /> <br /> Plus, if you can use their senses but can't see their frequency by yourself they provide a neat shortcut to doing so. <i>They</i> can see spirits/ghosts, so using their senses, so can you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T03:49:03-07:00","id":1131176,"title":"","content":"What does the word &quot;th\u00e9arch&quot; mean? Where does it come from, is it a shortening? I can't figure out the meaning of it. Is it a meaning behind it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T03:56:04-07:00","id":1131177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1131176#post1131176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the word &quot;th\u00e9arch&quot; mean? Where does it come from, is it a shortening? I can't figure out the meaning of it. Is it a meaning behind it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thearchs are mages of the Silver Ladder. I don't think there's any stated meaning above and beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T04:34:07-07:00","id":1131181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1131176#post1131176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the word &quot;th\u00e9arch&quot; mean? Where does it come from, is it a shortening? I can't figure out the meaning of it. Is it a meaning behind it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means &quot;person who rules as part of a thearchy&quot;, so basically a politician who rules because the system is one where gods are the ones in power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:44:55-07:00","id":1131448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1131181#post1131181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means &quot;person who rules as part of a thearchy&quot;, so basically a politician who rules because the system is one where gods are the ones in power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course! It's so clear now when you say it. Thanks! been freezing my mind by trying to find an answer here in the middle of summer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:28:58-07:00","id":1131474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1131181#post1131181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means &quot;person who rules as part of a thearchy&quot;, so basically a politician who rules because the system is one where gods are the ones in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also have a double meaning. Aside from being a synonym for theocracy, 'Thearchy' can also refer to a pantheon of gods with the thearch being the king of the gods. Given the Silver Ladder's beliefs about Humanity, calling the Awakened, Gods by implication makes a lot of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T11:47:10-07:00","id":1132320,"title":"","content":"Is the Essence generated by Essence Fountain Lasting?<br /> <br /> On one hand, most of these sorts of spells (those that grant willpower, or heal you) seem to be. On the other hand, I don't actually see any reason it should be, following the framework for Lasting spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T14:48:31-07:00","id":1132400,"title":"","content":"I don't know about anyone else, but I'm not going to keep track of 5+ individual points of essence. They could end up anywhere. <br /> <br /> It seems a lot more intuitive for the advanced duration to generate so much essence every so often. That would make it more like a fountain, rather than a single burst of energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T03:05:02-07:00","id":1132542,"title":"","content":"What exactly is a &quot;complex device&quot; for the purposes of +2 reach of Platonic Form? A bike? A car? A laptop? A hand grenade? A submarine? A tank? A nuclear warhead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T03:10:30-07:00","id":1132545,"title":"","content":"Examples from Matter: A car or a smartphone. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T03:12:18-07:00","id":1132546,"title":"","content":"What would be the upper limit of complexity, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T03:17:34-07:00","id":1132548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1132546#post1132546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the upper limit of complexity, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>ST Fiat. The Matter spell in question's only stated restriction is that it must be something that operates according to known physical principles (no teleporters or Warp drives). Whether or not Platonic Form is that broad is up to your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T06:08:30-07:00","id":1132575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1132546#post1132546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the upper limit of complexity, though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Off the top of my head and to avoid stupid &quot;Lets make a platonic nuke&quot; situations i'd say anything more complex than you could find on you tube to fix is out of reach. So take a car for example, i know nothing about cars, but i can go on you tube and probably fudge my way to fixing one if i had the tools etc (maybe) but you wont find &quot;how to fix a nuke&quot; video on you tube....or i hope not.<br /> <br /> If i did say that to my players, i just know it'd turn into a challenge of what can we find on you tube...<br /> <br /> Maybe i mean something is to complex is a normal person couldnt follow a intruction manual to repair it? That rules out making Ikea stuff though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-22-2017, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T06:19:16-07:00","id":1132576,"title":"","content":"The problem with having the platonic form of an explosive is that the defining property of an explosive is it's ability to violently cease to exist. I'm not sure how that would work with a mana construct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:03:49-07:00","id":1132610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1132576#post1132576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with having the platonic form of an explosive is that the defining property of an explosive is it's ability to violently cease to exist. I'm not sure how that would work with a mana construct.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is important to note that bullets and combustion engines work via explosive power, so for consistency if you can't make explosives you may make a gun or a car but not bullets or fuel that make such items useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:46:03-07:00","id":1132632,"title":"","content":"For personal use I will probably go with &quot;you need to know how to make this thing or it needs to be simple enough that you can 'picture' it in its entirety, including its insides&quot; , so the complextiy of the platonizable items will scale with the skill dots of the character...but that's for my personal use, because we like having a direct connection between mundane abilities and magical capabilities (mostly first enhancing the second). So if you can't form an imago that &quot;grokks&quot; how the thing works, you will get a pretty but empty inside model case of a, eh, let's say nuke.<br /> <br /> But I'm also interested in how the &quot;vanilla&quot; platonic ideal should work, so without making a personal table ruling for it. One of things that actually was asked about is Platonic Form of a...book. &quot;I want to form a platonic ideal of a specialized work about bugs!&quot;, for example. Would it work? My guts say &quot;yes, but the book will evaporate after X uses due to mana limits and how good it is is based on equipment bonus&quot;. How do you people think it should work by vanilla reading, and how would you handle it on your table?<br /> I'm actually more interested/scared about things like that than actually conjuring tanks out of thin air, to be honest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> This question is sponsored by Grimoire Spoiler and which resulted in interest in playing a Prime based Obrimos with a thing for books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:05:26-07:00","id":1132757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1125204#post1125204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCan informed actually be used with spell casting? It specifically says skill roll? Steadfast however just mentions a roll? Maybe giving yourself &quot;an arcane&quot; condition you give yourself a informed like condition that does the same for spell casting?<br /> <br /> Anyway brief napkin maths i can only really squeeze +8 potency out of a first time casting of Exceptional Luck then +12 and it quickly gets diminishing returns after that:<br /> <br /> Dicepool 13 from Gnosis, Arcana, Mudra, High Speech and Willpower.<br /> Base potency 3, duration 1 turn<br /> 1 reach for instant, 1 for advanced duration, 2 for bonus to spell casting<br /> +8 potency for -16<br /> Informed condition for -2<br /> 13-18 = -5, 1 mana, 1 willpower, auto succeed because of informed lasting a scene<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the necro, but why the -2 for Informed Condition? Why is there a dice penalty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:47:09-07:00","id":1132784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1132757#post1132757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the necro, but why the -2 for Informed Condition? Why is there a dice penalty?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Granting the &quot;Informed&quot; Condition is done by Reaching the Spell, I would presume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-22-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:04:03-07:00","id":1132792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1132784#post1132784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Granting the &amp;quot;Informed&amp;quot; Condition is done by Reaching the Spell, I would presume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reach doesn't impose dice penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:06:27-07:00","id":1132869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1132757#post1132757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the necro, but why the -2 for Informed Condition? Why is there a dice penalty?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to &quot;spend&quot; 1 potency for a condition so its -2? So the spell is technically +1 potency its just that potency wasnt used for a dice bonus, it was tablemaths and just easier to keep track off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-22-2017, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T11:17:01-07:00","id":1133092,"title":"","content":"Ok. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:58:46-07:00","id":1133124,"title":"","content":"Can you make an amalgam of two perfected alloys? <br /> Eg. combining Thaumium and Sophis to make an object that scavanges Mana and uses that to fuel the protective abilities of Thaumium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T13:12:04-07:00","id":1133133,"title":"","content":"Personally doubt it as Sophis and Thaumium are allready alloys. That's like asking wether you can make a mixture of two mixtures. Sure you can, but that doesn't mean their stats will stack in a linear fashion. Far more likely it'd create the magical alloy x with the completly new effect y which is entirely unrelated to Thaumium and Sophis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T13:19:58-07:00","id":1133139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133133#post1133133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you can, but that doesn't mean their stats will stack in a linear fashion. Far more likely it'd create the magical alloy x with the completly new effect y which is entirely unrelated to Thaumium and Sophis.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of amalgams is that they retain and stack the properties of their components. What would happen if you <i>could</i> do it is indisputable (it would work like I described) I'm just wondering if it's doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:44:21-07:00","id":1133171,"title":"","content":"Amalgams are just mercury alloys. Among the perfected materials only hermium can form them naturally. Regardless I believe a process as you propose would be possible using some spellcraft. Matter weaving meshes two perfected alloys together, Prime weaving lets mana flow from one into the other every ritual interval. Two spells total. For an easier solution you could just build an item (pendant for example) wherein one side is Sophis and the other is Thaumium, fused together mundanely somehow (glue?) and then the Prime weaving spell cast on the two of them. As a matter of fact you don't have to fuse them at all for this to work.<br /> <br /> The issue is more that you can't make an amalgam naturally without spells (except for hermium), same for the automatic mana exchange, that will require a spell, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:10:38-07:00","id":1133182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133171#post1133171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amalgams are just mercury alloys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...using a strict technical definition of alloys, sure. But the SOS material treats amalgams (natural hermium 'alloys') and what it calls alloys (those forged via magic) very differently. The former retains and stacks the properties of its component materials, while the latter loses the original properties and then replaces them with new ones.<br /> <br /> Your proposed solution is interesting, but not needed at all if magically forged alloys can be added to a natural hermium amalgam. I'm just wondering if that specifically is possible. The writeup says that hermium only reacts to other perfected metals, and I'm not sure if that's inclusive of magically forged alloys (which are a combination of perfected metals) or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:16:46-07:00","id":1133183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133182#post1133182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just wondering if that specifically is possible. The writeup says that hermium only reacts to other perfected metals, and I'm not sure if that's inclusive of magically forged alloys (which are a combination of perfected metals) or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Hermium essentially solves a magical alloy as it solves a perfected metal it would destroy the alloy doing so, I'd think. Either way it wouldn't facilitate the Mana transport from Sophis to Thaumium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:41:36-07:00","id":1133193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133183#post1133183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Hermium essentially solves a magical alloy as it solves a perfected metal it would destroy the alloy doing so, I'd think. Either way it wouldn't facilitate the Mana transport from Sophis to Thaumium.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the attempted assist, and some of your proposed solutions have been thought provoking, but I'm just not following you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Amalgams</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Hermium is capable of forming an amalgam with any of the other perfected metals. The resulting amalgams retain the Supernal properties of both of the combined metals.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of hermium amalgams is that one retains all special effects of the other metals included in the amalgam. Nothing loses its special properties or abilities when added to one. That is one of the two primary distinctions between amalgams and magically forged alloys. If you make an amalgam of metal x,y,z you get a new object that has all of the effects of x,y,z. If you make a spell-forged alloy, you get a new object that loses effects x,y,z and gains effect 123.<br /> <br /> If it <i>doesn't</i> work with alloys, that's one thing, but it does not follow that the material that explicitly combines metals while preserving their effects would combine magically fused alloys and destroy their effects. The special effect of Thaumium is the warding, the special effect of Sophis is the scavenging.<br /> <br /> If they can be added to an amalgam, those effects would necessarily be preserved in the resulting amalgam because that is what an amalgam does.<br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr</b> Mostly I just want to know the arguments for or against adding an alloy to an amalgam, as I don't believe conversation around what the effects would be if one were to succeed is going to be productive.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 08-23-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:14:08-07:00","id":1133327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133193#post1133193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>tl;dr</b> Mostly I just want to know the arguments for or against adding an alloy to an amalgam, as I don't believe conversation around what the effects would be if one were to succeed is going to be productive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Had to reread the doc but amalgam specifically says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with any of the other perfected metals </div> </div> </div> and does not mention alloys?<br /> <br /> So i would assume no Thaum/Sophis mix, and its prob for the best tbh..<br /> <br /> Im correct in thinking that an alloy is: A + B = C and an amalgam is: A + B + H = ABH?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-24-2017, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:42:25-07:00","id":1133350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133327#post1133327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im correct in thinking that an alloy is: A + B = C and an amalgam is: A + B + H = ABH?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep that's correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:22:41-07:00","id":1133875,"title":"","content":"This is probably a dumb question, but what dice pool does an ephemeral entity use for contested rolls, in particular against others' numina? If a Numen calls for a contested roll (or when using or creating a Numen for which a contested roll is appropriate), do you use Power + Resistance? Finesse + Resistance? Something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T12:12:34-07:00","id":1133905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133875#post1133875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a dumb question, but what dice pool does an ephemeral entity use for contested rolls, in particular against others' numina? If a Numen calls for a contested roll (or when using or creating a Numen for which a contested roll is appropriate), do you use Power + Resistance? Finesse + Resistance? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The power calling for a contested roll should specifiy what is used normally. If something calls for Strength, Intelligence, or Presence then you use Power instead; same goes for the other sets of three.<br /> <br /> If you mean a Clash of Wills then it is Rank + Influence if applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T21:03:39-07:00","id":1134037,"title":"","content":"Hi there. I am working on creating a new character for a Mage 2<sup>nd</sup> edition game who will specialize in the Death arcana. I have a few questions related to that.<br /> <br /> 1. Are praxes considered a form of improvised spellcasting, or are they a third category of casting separate from improvised spells and rotes?<br /> <br /> 2. Can praxes be made from combined spells if your gnosis is three or greater?<br /> <br /> 3. Regarding the Death 5 spell, Create Ghost: The spell description mentions that you can fashion a ghost after a living person. If you were to do so, would the newly created ghost have access to the memories and personality of the person in whose image the ghost was created, or would the resemblence be only skin (ephemera) deep?<br /> <br /> 4. Regarding Souls: I get the impression from reading the book that Souls are interchangable rather than being unique to an individual. So, if person A is suffering from the souless condition, that condition can be resolved using the soul of person B or any other soul you can get your hands on without any changes to person A\u2019s personality, memories, stats, etc? Am I understanding this correctly?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance to anyone who answers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T22:26:28-07:00","id":1134055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134037#post1134037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are praxes considered a form of improvised spellcasting, or are they a third category of casting separate from improvised spells and rotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Improvised casting is explicitly differentiated from Praxes and Rotes, so yes, they're a third category.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can praxes be made from combined spells if your gnosis is three or greater? </div> </div> </div>Presumably not, seeing as a requirement of combining Praxes is that you have every component spell as a Praxis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Regarding Souls: I get the impression from reading the book that Souls are interchangable rather than being unique to an individual. So, if person A is suffering from the souless condition, that condition can be resolved using the soul of person B or any other soul you can get your hands on without any changes to person A\u2019s personality, memories, stats, etc? Am I understanding this correctly? </div> </div> </div>The Reach-intensive nature of binding a soul to a person as a Lasting effect makes Paradox-based complications a real concern for anyone who hasn't got Death Mastery or a Rote of Soul Jar, and the nature of the things Soul Marks reveals is such that it's not hard to see peculiar side-effects arising early on, but yes, the basic problems of soullessness are generally solved with the attachment of any soul at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-26-2017, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T02:06:30-07:00","id":1134086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134037#post1134037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there. I am working on creating a new character for a Mage 2<sup>nd</sup> edition game who will specialize in the Death arcana. I have a few questions related to that.<br /> <br /> 1. Are praxes considered a form of improvised spellcasting, or are they a third category of casting separate from improvised spells and rotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Praxis are spells that are so intimate to you that you cast them with greater efficiency, need only 3 successes to be considered an Exceptional Success. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134037#post1134037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Can praxes be made from combined spells if your gnosis is three or greater?</div> </div> </div> </div>Praxis are made from Improvised spells and not combined spells. (My opinion as the book doesn't elaborate on this topic)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134037#post1134037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Regarding the Death 5 spell, Create Ghost: The spell description mentions that you can fashion a ghost after a living person. If you were to do so, would the newly created ghost have access to the memories and personality of the person in whose image the ghost was created, or would the resemblence be only skin (ephemera) deep?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just skin deep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134037#post1134037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Regarding Souls: I get the impression from reading the book that Souls are interchangable rather than being unique to an individual. So, if person A is suffering from the souless condition, that condition can be resolved using the soul of person B or any other soul you can get your hands on without any changes to person A\u2019s personality, memories, stats, etc? Am I understanding this correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>A soul, any soul, can be put into a body that is souless and it will stop the souless condition, any <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">additional effects of the soul swap is entirely left to the discretion of the ST</span>. Mechanically nothing else happens Story wise the world could change for the individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T03:47:18-07:00","id":1134103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134037#post1134037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. Regarding the Death 5 spell, Create Ghost: The spell description mentions that you can fashion a ghost after a living person. If you were to do so, would the newly created ghost have access to the memories and personality of the person in whose image the ghost was created, or would the resemblence be only skin (ephemera) deep?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it would have the memories and personality of the person, as you create a superficial echo of the person just as if he had died right now. Aka just like his normal ghost would be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T03:47:29-07:00","id":1134105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1133905#post1133905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The power calling for a contested roll should specifiy what is used normally. If something calls for Strength, Intelligence, or Presence then you use Power instead; same goes for the other sets of three.<br /> <br /> If you mean a Clash of Wills then it is Rank + Influence if applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here is an easy example: In the core book, the Drain Numen uses a contested roll of Stamina + Resolve + Gnosis. What does a spirit use to contest against that? Or Emotional Aura, which uses a contested Resolve + Composure + Gnosis roll?<br /> <br /> Also, do you have a reference for the Rank + Influence rule for Clash of Wills? I have been trying to find rules about Clashes for ephemeral beings and I have not heard that. It makes sense but was unsure where I can read about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T04:10:40-07:00","id":1134107,"title":"","content":"It'll be Resistance + Rank. Spirits compensate for the single attribute by probably having that attribute at higher values than a human can manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T04:13:50-07:00","id":1134109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134105#post1134105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here is an easy example: In the core book, the Drain Numen uses a contested roll of Stamina + Resolve + Gnosis. What does a spirit use to contest against that? Or Emotional Aura, which uses a contested Resolve + Composure + Gnosis roll?<br /> <br /> Also, do you have a reference for the Rank + Influence rule for Clash of Wills? I have been trying to find rules about Clashes for ephemeral beings and I have not heard that. It makes sense but was unsure where I can read about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drain specifically only works on a material being, but if an ephemeral entity were to roll against it they would use Resistance+Rank. The same formula goes for Emotional Aura.<br /> <br /> I don't have a reference for the Rank+Influence on a CoW, but can confirm that's how I understand it to work for spirits as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T04:25:47-07:00","id":1134112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134105#post1134105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do you have a reference for the Rank + Influence rule for Clash of Wills? I have been trying to find rules about Clashes for ephemeral beings and I have not heard that. It makes sense but was unsure where I can read about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because Mage didn't actually include any rules for clashing with ephemerals.<br /> <br /> This is from page 115 in Werewolf: The Forsaken 2e:<br /> &quot;A spirit in a Clash of Wills uses its Rank as its dice pool.<br /> If the Clash comes from the spirit using an Influence, it adds<br /> its dots in that Influence to the dice pool.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T04:53:01-07:00","id":1134113,"title":"","content":"Ok, that makes a lot more sense. Thanks for the Werewolf reference, I didn't think to look there. <br /> <br /> So for Hallucination, which calls for a Wits + Composure + Gnosis contested roll, it would be Finesse + Resistance + Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T05:43:29-07:00","id":1134118,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell ephemerals doesn't have generic rules for contested rolls. All I see are specific examples such as rolling pure Finesse when attempting to sense Rank from someone who hides it, and Power + Resistance to defend from someone trying to steal their Essence. Also, both examples are against other ephemerals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T08:17:06-07:00","id":1134145,"title":"","content":"Ephemerals must've been a pain to work with as devs since both their Supernatural Tolerance trait and their Attributes have completely different scales, and they straight up lack Skills. It's pretty obvious when they Withstand by Rank, which is pitiful, and doesn't use Rank to contest werewolf Gifts despite the rules saying that Rank is their equivalent of Supernatural Tolerance. Numina are also contested by an additional Attribute just to compensate for the ephemeral's dice pool.<br /> <br /> When it comes to contesting Numina it seems logical that ephemerals either use their corresponding Attributes without Rank (Wits + Composure + Gnosis becomes Finesse + Resistance) or use just one Attribute plus Rank (Wits + Composure + Gnosis becomes Resistance + Rank). That way the defending entity won't use more traits than the aggressor. I personally prefer the latter since all opposed power activation rolls (that I can think of right now) is stacked in the favour of the user rather than the defender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-26-2017, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:43:47-07:00","id":1134180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Regarding the Death 5 spell, Create Ghost: The spell description mentions that you can fashion a ghost after a living person. If you were to do so, would the newly created ghost have access to the memories and personality of the person in whose image the ghost was created, or would the resemblence be only skin (ephemera) deep? </div> </div> </div>It would be just as if the person would naturally created the ghost at the moment of death, so yes, a carbon copy of his personality, memories and, of course, appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:30:32-07:00","id":1134239,"title":"","content":"Is there a difference between resolving and destroying Anchors for Ghosts (as there is in owod)?<br /> <br /> When all of a Ghosts Anchors are gone, does it cease to exist or does it get drawn into the underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:51:15-07:00","id":1134245,"title":"","content":"If resolved, they move on. Where? No one can tell. If destroyed they go down to the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:54:33-07:00","id":1134246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134180#post1134180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be just as if the person would naturally created the ghost at the moment of death, so yes, a carbon copy of his personality, memories and, of course, appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">She can fashion the ghost as an echo of another person, either alive or dead, though the ghost is not the actual person.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Says its not the actual person, so no i dont think they get the memories, just appearance. I cant imagine you can just go around creating ghosts of living people then interrogating said ghost for info. To copy memories from somebody would at least require mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:57:18-07:00","id":1134249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134239#post1134239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference between resolving and destroying Anchors for Ghosts (as there is in owod)?<br /> <br /> When all of a Ghosts Anchors are gone, does it cease to exist or does it get drawn into the underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Geist: The Sin-Eaters handled what happens when you resolve a ghost's Anchors, but Geist hasn't been updated yet and the other updated gamelines doesn't even mention the possibility of resolving Anchors.<br /> What we know in second edition: Anchors protects ghosts from bleeding Essence, and serve as a &quot;respawn&quot; point if they ever run out of Essence. Should a ghost run out of Essence without having any Anchors they're immediately drawn through the nearest Avernian Gate down to the Underworld. But that's only when the ghost also has lost all its Essence. It's difficult but possible to gain Essence without Anchors, and any ghost that succeeds will just continue to linger in the Material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:01:40-07:00","id":1134251,"title":"","content":"So how was it handled in first edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:33:58-07:00","id":1134257,"title":"","content":"GtSE page 44:<br /> &quot;Passing On<br /> One of the most hotly contested aspects of interacting with ghosts is the poorly understood phenomenon<br /> of \u201cpassing on.\u201d When a ghost has resolved all of its anchors, sometimes it simply vanishes from both the<br /> mortal world and the Underworld. Its fate remains completely unknown, perhaps unknowable. Religious<br /> Sin-Eaters suggest that the ghost has passed on to some sort of afterlife, or perhaps has reincarnated<br /> into its next life. Others believe the ghost has simply dissipated and that there is no difference between<br /> what happens when a ghost \u201cpasses on\u201d and what happens when a Sin-Eater destroys a ghost \u2014 only<br /> the experiences of its last moments.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T02:11:30-07:00","id":1134401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134246#post1134246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Says its not the actual person, so no i dont think they get the memories, just appearance. I cant imagine you can just go around creating ghosts of living people then interrogating said ghost for info. To copy memories from somebody would at least require mind?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They get as much memory of the original person as a regular ghost does (that is, full of holes and prone to one-track-mindism). A ghost is, in detailed metaphysical terms, more of a negative image in ghost-Twilight of a person's psychic presence than a clone of their body, anyway. The mind's just as much part of them as their physical/ephemeral appearance is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T08:34:43-07:00","id":1134478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134401#post1134401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They get as much memory of the original person as a regular ghost does (that is, full of holes and prone to one-track-mindism). A ghost is, in detailed metaphysical terms, more of a negative image in ghost-Twilight of a person's psychic presence than a clone of their body, anyway. The mind's just as much part of them as their physical/ephemeral appearance is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, yeh im ok with that, it leaves space for interesting stuff but you might not be 100% able to get the info you want from your ghost copy. Does this mean that in your rules for playing playable ghosts, they will probably be rank 3+.<br /> <br /> I imagine rank 1 and 2 to be not really able to be a playable entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:07:47-07:00","id":1134851,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to pull a spell from your Oneiros into the normal world? Or is it already active? For example say you cast &quot;Body Control&quot; at high reach and potency for a month long duration within your own soul.<br /> <br /> When you wake up is the spell still running?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:26:01-07:00","id":1134857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134851#post1134851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to pull a spell from your Oneiros into the normal world? Or is it already active? For example say you cast &quot;Body Control&quot; at high reach and potency for a month long duration within your own soul.<br /> <br /> When you wake up is the spell still running?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells cast on yourself in the astral are cast on your dream form, so they wont effect you when you awaken, they might even end because your dream form vanishes. If cast on another goetia or other dream form then they will stay active when you are awake and stay until dispelled or ended by yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-28-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:19:24-07:00","id":1134914,"title":"","content":"How many casinos world wide are owned by Awakened keeping an eye out for Time / Fate / Space / Mind gamblers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:40:57-07:00","id":1134926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134914#post1134914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many casinos world wide are owned by Awakened keeping an eye out for Time / Fate / Space / Mind gamblers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a few, I would imagine - but they'll mostly be Seers. I'm sure the Guardians operate a few as part of the Labyrinth, but almost everything about casinos just screams &quot;Seers of the Throne&quot; - I mean come on, using the promise of material wealth to trick people into staring at a screen and pulling a lever over and over? Deliberately removing clocks and windows from the premises so they won't notice the hours slipping away? That's got the Exarchs written all over it.<br /> <br /> Plus it gives them an excellent opportunity to intercept all those fresh-faced apprentices who think they're geniuses for figuring out they could make bank by cheating at slot machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:39:02-07:00","id":1134954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134857#post1134857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells cast on yourself in the astral are cast on your dream form, so they wont effect you when you awaken, they might even end because your dream form vanishes. If cast on another goetia or other dream form then they will stay active when you are awake and stay until dispelled or ended by yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shame I was hoping there was some way to pull a spell out of nowhere and surprise the player party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T16:07:30-07:00","id":1134987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134954#post1134954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a shame I was hoping there was some way to pull a spell out of nowhere and surprise the player party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Hung Spell? Alternatively, use Two Minds, One Thought and cast the spell in the Astral with Sympathy to hit the physical world. Analysis of the spell might reveal that you're the cause of it though unless you take steps to obfuscate that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T17:34:32-07:00","id":1135002,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have two more questions if you don't mind<br /> <br /> 1. Regarding Create Ghost: Can you create a ghost from scratch, or do you need to use a human target as the template? Whether you create a ghost from scratch or using a human target, how much influence does the Wizard have over the 'one track mind-ism' of the created ghost?<br /> <br /> 2. When throwing or firing an aimed damage spell, do extra successes cause extra damage the way a thrown knife might? If you use the rules for targeting specific body parts, can you cause tilts such as arm wrack with aimed spells?<br /> <br /> Thanks again for your time and answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:03:18-07:00","id":1135006,"title":"","content":"The answer to the second question is no. No matter where you hit the subject the spell will affect the entire subject as if you cast it at touch or sensory range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T23:40:48-07:00","id":1135079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135002#post1135002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have two more questions if you don't mind<br /> <br /> 1. Regarding Create Ghost: Can you create a ghost from scratch, or do you need to use a human target as the template? Whether you create a ghost from scratch or using a human target, how much influence does the Wizard have over the 'one track mind-ism' of the created ghost?<br /> <br /> 2. When throwing or firing an aimed damage spell, do extra successes cause extra damage the way a thrown knife might? If you use the rules for targeting specific body parts, can you cause tilts such as arm wrack with aimed spells?<br /> <br /> Thanks again for your time and answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The way the spell is worded i presume you can create one from scratch or use a echo of a human alive or dead. I think you can probably set what its motives are, how it &quot;died&quot; etc. Its loyal to the mage though so its always going to have that as one of its &quot;tracks&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Aimed spells must use the area of effect scale centered on where the mage aims, so when thrown your really throwing a small/large sized spell effect at something.<br /> <br /> What is odd is allowing defense vs this though, if you have upped the scale to an entire room and throw a aimed spell at somebody in another room, they shouldnt be able to get defense vs it. This either means that a) if the spell misses its intended target it doesnt get cast or b) if it misses the target it still hits something and the spell is still cast inside the room and catches your target anyway? c) why bother targeting something with a defense, just target the center of the room and throw your spell at that point, locations dont get any defense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-29-2017, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:42:29-07:00","id":1135108,"title":"","content":"Complexity in ephemeral entities is generally expressed by Rank. They still tend to be very goal oriented in spite of Rank though. You're not really going to find a ghost of any Rank whose terribly interested in taking it easy and smelling the roses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:57:56-07:00","id":1135109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135079#post1135079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why bother targeting something with a defense, just target the center of the room and throw your spell at that point, locations dont get any defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>If collateral damage isn't a concern, nor is spending the extra reach or spell factors for scale, this is valid, sure.<br /> <br /> If either of those are a concern, you're better off targeting your actual target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T03:52:38-07:00","id":1135118,"title":"","content":"Also, and this might be bending the rules just a little, you could say that if the aimed spell hits the target the area of effect gets anchored to them, not the earth, so they can't escape it by running away or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T19:24:38-07:00","id":1135658,"title":"","content":"Once again thank you to those who have been answering my questions. Your assistance is appreciated. Please allow me to impose on you once again.<br /> <br /> Regarding combined spells: A mage with gnosis 3+ can combine multiple spells into a single casting. The book is pretty clear on most aspects of combined spells, but there are few points on which I need clarification.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If the two spells in a combined casting have different primary spell factors, which parts get the free steps up the spell factor chart? Do you have to pick one and buy up the other with dice penalties? Do they just both get the steps? Is it different if the combined spell is composed of spells from different arcana vs from just one?</li> </ol>Example 1: A mage with death 4 and gnosis 3 casts a combined spell at their enemy. The spell consists of Cold Snap (primary Factor: Duration) and Rotting Flesh (Primary Factor: Potency.) The mage uses 2 free reach to instant cast at sensory range and rolls 5 dice (gnosis +death -2.) Assuming the roll succeeds, what is the result?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The mage\u2019s dots in death provide free steps in both the potency and duration charts. The target takes 4 damage and is affected by the Ice Tilt for 5 turns.</li> <li>The mage\u2019s dots in death provide free steps in either duration or potency, but not both.</li> <li>The mage must divide their dots in death between potency for the damage effect and duration for the ice effect in any combination they choose.</li> </ol>Example 2: The mage casts a similar combined spell, but the component spells are from different arcana. In this case, does the arcana for the spell with primary factor of potency give free steps in potency and the arcana for the spell with primary factor duration give duration? Or would the mage have to choose one and then buy factors for the other with dice penalties? Perhaps instead free steps on the spell factor chart are granted using only the lesser of the two arcana?<br /> <br /> In the case of a mage casting a combined spell using 2 arcana, would they get free reach from both spells and pool them? For example, a mage with death 3 mind 3 casting a death 3 mind 2 spell would get 3 free reach? (one from death and 2 from mind?) Or am I misunderstanding?<br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR How are Primary Spell Factors adjudicated in combined spells?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for reading this and thanks in advance to anyone who answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 08-30-2017, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T19:41:53-07:00","id":1135661,"title":"","content":"They both get free steps up. Combined spells are treated as separate spells for the most part except in terms of spell control, Reach spent on Advanced Factors, and number of dice available to bump spell factors by taking dice penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T06:39:08-07:00","id":1135750,"title":"","content":"Can Proximi pattern scour? I don't see any reference to them being able to do so.<br /> <br /> Assuming the answer to this is indeed &quot;no&quot;, what happens if they have Devouring the Slain as a blessing? How many times per day can they use it without spending reach?<br /> <br /> Similarly, what if the spell were imbued in an item and used by a sleepwalker?<br /> <br /> Or an Artifact? (assuming they had the Relic Attuned merit) Would you use the Artifact's gnosis to determine how often it could scour?<br /> <br /> In the latter two cases, would the mana end up in the artifact/imbued item's pool?<br /> <br /> If said artifact/imbued item was a knife or sword set to trigger the spell when it did lethal damage to someone, would it happen immediately or would you need to leave it in for a turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:41:25-07:00","id":1135786,"title":"","content":"Just starting to play with Awakening first edition (with a group that's been playing for a lot longer). I'm a little confused about how spirits build their dice pools.<br /> <br /> In the initial rules, it says that each of the spirit's three attributes contributes toward three of the attributes. I.e., whenever you would make a roll for &quot;Intelligence + Whatever,&quot; just roll with your power pool. So far so good, and it makes spirit's high dice pools make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> But then, when it talks about how unskilled penalties are not applied to a spirit acting within its Influence, it says that a spirit using a computer would roll Power+Finesse. <br /> <br /> I totally get that a spirit could be rolling either Intelligence+Computers (Power) or Wits+Computers (Finesse). But why does it roll both? Where is it stated that you add the two most relevant attributes together? How does this allow PCs to even remotely interact with Rank 4 or 5 spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:51:18-07:00","id":1135794,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by &quot;interact&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T09:15:10-07:00","id":1135804,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd just use the 2E version. Attribute + Rank for anything directly related to their influences, Attribute on it's own for anything tangentially related that you'd expect that sort of spirit to be able to do, and Attribute - skill penalty for anything unrelated. <br /> <br /> I'm not even sure if that was actually a rule change or just how it was always supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T11:08:13-07:00","id":1135844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135794#post1135794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by &quot;interact&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I mean is to actually use the social system to cut deals and bargains with spirits, rather than just commanding them and binding them with the Spirit Arcanum. However, even if I got my manipulation+persuasion dice pool to 5+5+specialty (fat chance), a Rank 5 spirit is rolling something like 24 dice with two attribute pools. No matter how high my spirit rank is, that ain't happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135804#post1135804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd just use the 2E version. Attribute + Rank for anything directly related to their influences, Attribute on it's own for anything tangentially related that you'd expect that sort of spirit to be able to do, and Attribute - skill penalty for anything unrelated.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure if that was actually a rule change or just how it was always supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice! Interesting to know that the system got refined later. Unfortunately, this group has been playing 1e spirits for close to a decade now. I think I'm just gonna have to suck it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T11:19:05-07:00","id":1135847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135844#post1135844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean is to actually use the social system to cut deals and bargains with spirits, rather than just commanding them and binding them with the Spirit Arcanum. However, even if I got my manipulation+persuasion dice pool to 5+5+specialty (fat chance), a Rank 5 spirit is rolling something like 24 dice with two attribute pools. No matter how high my spirit rank is, that ain't happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only gets the Attribute+Attribute dice pool if interacting socially is part of its wheel house, a typical fire spirit is only going to get one attribute depending on what it's doing in the social situation.<br /> <br /> In the event a spirit does get to add two Attributes to get its dice pool though you can use magic to match it by boosting your own Attributes and Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T11:48:08-07:00","id":1135857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135847#post1135847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It only gets the Attribute+Attribute dice pool if interacting socially is part of its wheel house, a typical fire spirit is only going to get one attribute depending on what it's doing in the social situation.<br /> <br /> In the event a spirit does get to add two Attributes to get its dice pool though you can use magic to match it by boosting your own Attributes and Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you help me figure out where it says this in the book? I looked in the ghost section and the spirit section, and the only thing I could find out about how a spirit gets help for working in its wheel house, as you say, is when it says it ignores the Unskilled penalty. This is also where the two-attribute example comes from, but the way the rules are written it seems like that's its normal way of calculating its dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T12:08:17-07:00","id":1135863,"title":"","content":"It was a computer spirit interacting with a computer. If anything that actually sounds like a control influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T12:20:38-07:00","id":1135867,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that example is a spirit using its Influence: Computers power, which is activated via a Power+Finesse roll. It has nothing to do with untrained skill penalties except that spirits don't suffer from them so they don't apply to an Influence roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T13:50:56-07:00","id":1135915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1135847#post1135847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It only gets the Attribute+Attribute dice pool if interacting socially is part of its wheel house, a typical fire spirit is only going to get one attribute depending on what it's doing in the social situation.<br /> <br /> In the event a spirit does get to add two Attributes to get its dice pool though you can use magic to match it by boosting your own Attributes and Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, if it's part of its wheelhouse it get Attribute + <i>Rank</i>. Attribute + Attribute is for powers like Influence and innate abilities like perception that would be Attribute + Attribute for a human. Also combat, for some reason. From the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.255</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral beings don\u2019t possess skills, but don\u2019t suffer unskilled<br /> penalties as long as the actions they\u2019re attempting are appropriate<br /> to their natures. They roll the appropriate Attribute + Rank for<br /> actions relating directly to their concepts, or Attribute + Attribute<br /> for actions like surprise and perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>But yes, high-rank spirits do have ludicrous dice pools that put them far beyond the reach of a PCs mundane abilities. They're <i>supposed</i> to. A rank 5 spirit is an entity with powers almost beyond human comprehension, of course Jimmy the Grifter can't just walk up and roll dice at it to make it do what he wants. You're not talking an acquaintance into doing you a favor here, you're negotiating with a <i>god</i>. You interact with it on the basis of an RP encounter where you figure out a clever way to get it to do what you want, or you bring your own godlike powers to bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:07:21-07:00","id":1135921,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13628_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13628\" data-vbnamecard=\"13628\">Terrorforge</a> the question was about 1e, so you're comment is related to the wrong edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T00:55:53-07:00","id":1136111,"title":"","content":"Stupid question for a stoopid morning. What are the Reach requisites i'd need in order to make a Legacy Attainment Spell last indefinitely? (Sorry if it has been answered already, i just realized i did not know the RAW guideline, only what <b><i>i </i></b>would say about it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T01:23:16-07:00","id":1136114,"title":"","content":"Same as a spell, I think, which means it'll need to be at least the fourth attainment (to get you up to the indefinite tier) and at that level could be at most a 3 dot spell for a duration-primary effect or a 2 dot potency-primary effect (because the two/three reach minimum means you have to knock it up a slot, and there's no way of getting up to the indefinite level without duration as the primary factor).<br /> <br /> As a 5th attainment you get a bit more flexibility (you'll have scale factors free to spend on something other than duration, for one) but are still capped at 4 or 3 dots, primary factor dependent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T01:25:27-07:00","id":1136115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136111#post1136111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid question for a stoopid morning. What are the Reach requisites i'd need in order to make a Legacy Attainment Spell last indefinitely? (Sorry if it has been answered already, i just realized i did not know the RAW guideline, only what <b><i>i </i></b>would say about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, you would need 2 Reach, so you can only make Lasting effects of Adept level and below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T01:32:59-07:00","id":1136116,"title":"","content":"So, all in all, the same rules apply as in an average spell. Thank you very much Prometheus!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T01:42:32-07:00","id":1136119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136116#post1136116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, all in all, the same rules apply as in an average spell. Thank you very much Prometheus!</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't many effects that are worth it though, most attainments with a long Duration work just as well and have a relatively hassle free activation cost compared to the length of time they remain running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T04:39:22-07:00","id":1136139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136116#post1136116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, all in all, the same rules apply as in an average spell. Thank you very much Prometheus!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, you could also make a distinction between Attainments, that are based on spells with +2 Reach option and spells without it. Going purely by the numbers, the second kind would make it more difficult, as you would have to account for the dice bonuses necessary for Indefinite Duration (with Arcanum at four or five dots, you would still need to rise up one degree (two dice necessary for that)). You could accomodate the Fate 2 Attainment to impose a Condition under which the effect ceases to exist, but otherwise is Indefinite, and you could even cheat a little: &quot;I create a sword that has an Indefinite Duration except for when it is broken.&quot; You get Duration increase at no real cost. You would still need Fate 2 though, and likewise spells with Potency primary would require either Condition that is more likely to come to pass, or an additional Reach to switch Primary Potency to be Primary Duration.<br /> <br /> But really, one of the advantages of a Legacy is that Attainments can be Atypical: You can slightly limit or expand their influence. What I would do is to permit an Indefinite effect in case when you have a long lasting effect that you need to only spend a few seconds/hour per month/year or so to renew at no real cost (for example an effect on yourself, you don't even have to go anywhere to activate the Attainment). If your Attainment would affect a house for a year, I would be more cautious, because the fact that you can affect houses left and right indefinitely and never return to them to reaply the effect would make the Attainment that much more powerful.<br /> <br /> That said, you still always have an option of using the +2 Reach effect from Creative Thaumaturgy, or an Unusual Attainment, or even an Attainment based on specific Making/Unmaking spell, that has Lasing effect by default without Reach (like healing spells), after designing it with Storyteller approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":".  Brainfart, wrote Fate 4 instead of 2. 09-01-2017, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T05:51:36-07:00","id":1136149,"title":"","content":"Conditional Duration is Fate's 2 dot attainment. The 4 dot one protects you against oaths and supernatural compulsions and shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:06:04-07:00","id":1136150,"title":"","content":"What is the point of Postcognition (Time 1) if the caster can only view Unchanged subjects? The way I read it, I find it hard to imagine any kind of useful information can be gleaned by using the spell, but maybe I'm just not creative enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1577-maledicta","name":"Maledicta","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:13:10-07:00","id":1136152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maledicta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136150#post1136150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point of Postcognition (Time 1) if the caster can only view Unchanged subjects? The way I read it, I find it hard to imagine any kind of useful information can be gleaned by using the spell, but maybe I'm just not creative enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not reading closely enough, if you have Time 2 you can employ Temporal Sympathy and see further back. Even without that though it's safe to say you can pick up on anything in probably the last 24 hours, maybe further depending on how long it's been since anything significantly changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:17:28-07:00","id":1136156,"title":"","content":"Even for a dabbler with only Time 1, you could look into the past of, say, a ring and see what the wearer was doing basically any time they were wearing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:27:57-07:00","id":1136159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136156#post1136156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for a dabbler with only Time 1, you could look into the past of, say, a ring and see what the wearer was doing basically any time they were wearing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it only counts as Unchanged, for instance you wouldn't be able to see the past of the ring from before its current owner, or when it lost one of its diamonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:32:09-07:00","id":1136162,"title":"","content":"You can probably use a knowing spell to tell how far back a given subject's &quot;unchanged&quot; goes, now I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:18:31-07:00","id":1136179,"title":"","content":"I've certainly mentioned that possibility before, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T12:54:30-07:00","id":1136691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136162#post1136162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can probably use a knowing spell to tell how far back a given subject's &quot;unchanged&quot; goes, now I think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a house rule, but in the interest of game flow, I'd probably just roll that in with Postcognition itself, or anything else dependent on Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <br /> As part of casting the spell, you know how far back it can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T13:12:48-07:00","id":1136697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136691#post1136691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a house rule, but in the interest of game flow, I'd probably just roll that in with Postcognition itself, or anything else dependent on Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <br /> As part of casting the spell, you know how far back it can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e you had to target a specific time with Postcognition in order to be able to view it, it's not exactly clear whether or not that's still the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T14:45:31-07:00","id":1136719,"title":"","content":"&quot;The mage views the subject in \u201creal time\u201d <b>from a moment declared when casting</b> until the Duration of Postcognition expires.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds clear enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:04:18-07:00","id":1136725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136719#post1136719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The mage views the subject in \u201creal time\u201d <b>from a moment declared when casting</b> until the Duration of Postcognition expires.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds clear enough to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch, yup, you're right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T05:26:23-07:00","id":1136898,"title":"","content":"Page 87 makes it clear that any act of Blood Sacrifice (killing a person or animal for Mana) is an Act of Hubris, however the section on Wisdom doesn't bring it up. My question is, what level of AoH is an animal sacrifice? My first thought is that it could be a sin against Enlightened Wisdom, after all, for most people devouring the essence of a dead animal for sustenance is about as mundane as getting dressed or brushing your teeth. However that would imply some very interesting things about the setting, as it would mean that most mages could gain mana this way with very little penalty. &quot;Don't bother scrapping with your neighbours about who gets to keep that Hallow, we can just swing by the pet shop instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there an official ruling somewhere that I am missing? Or do most folk think it should be a crime against Understanding wisdom? <br /> <br /> P.S: This only came up because I just had a PC roleplay through the Mysterium Arche ritual (check there order book) which incorporates an animal sacrifice, and only now days later do I recall I should have probably asked for some kind of wisdom check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T05:58:42-07:00","id":1136905,"title":"","content":"Yeah, personally I'd put animal sacrifice and understanding and human sacrifice at falling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T07:41:52-07:00","id":1136929,"title":"","content":"Hard to place. I'd place animal sacrifice at enlightened wisdom and human sacrifice at understanding wisdom. The only reason for human wisdom being understanding wisdom is that killing a human in a planned fashion coincides with it. If you would force a roll for both the kill and drawing mana from the sacrifice, I'd make the sacrifice enlightened wisdom. Destroying a specifically awakened soul is falling wisdom, implying that destroying the soul of a sleeper is probably just understanding wisdom, just drawing mana from the life energy itself seems way less severe than destroying a soul to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T09:00:40-07:00","id":1136945,"title":"","content":"There's a huge psychological difference between using animal products and personally killing an animal. I think a lot of people in the wod (at least the city-dwellers we tend to play) could eat a hamburger without flinching but would suffer a Breaking Point if they had to personally slaughter a cow - though a butcher of course wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Wisdom, like Integrity, is a flexible, personal scale. For many mages, animal sacrifice is probably an Act of Hubris against Understanding wisdom, like the cow/hamburger situation. But for others (presumably the same sort of people who would already be comfortable slaughtering an animal for food) it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Making a habit of going down to the pet store for your weekend mana binge probably still would be, though. Carelessly burning though mana because &quot;there's always more where that came from&quot; is kind of dangerous and arrogant in itself, and habitually sacrificing droves of animals shows a callous disrespect for both life an magic that cannot be described as anything other than Hubristic.<br /> <br /> Plus it's a hassle just from a practical standpoint. You can't really go down to Petsmart and just buy five dogs without getting questions, especially if you already came in and bought five dogs two weeks ago. If you want that much life, you're gonna have to throw in with puppy mills, factory farms or other shady folks or straight up steal animals, both of which are potentially Acts of Hubris unto themselves. And once you're done, you have to dispose of all that meat somehow. And the spirits! Just imagine what the Shadow would be like around the Sanctum of a mage who routinely slaughters large quantities of animals for magical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T11:08:54-07:00","id":1136969,"title":"","content":"Create Life doesn't cost mana, so technically...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T12:25:18-07:00","id":1136988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1136969#post1136969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Create Life doesn't cost mana, so technically...</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone was wondering where the horror lies in Mage, it's right here in the fact that abusing an ethically mindboggling rules loophole like building an artificial Hallow powered by the deaths of artificial life forms created for the express purpose of ritual sacrifice is not lolrandom peasant railgun silliness as it would be in any other game, but 100% something a mage could and would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T12:53:43-07:00","id":1136999,"title":"","content":"The really scary thing is that it's possibly the simplest use of the spell imaginable. It's 5 dots and duration primary, so the animal you create will last 30 seconds with no additional spell factors. Use your free reach for instant casting and you could just rig up an assembly line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:10:47-07:00","id":1137003,"title":"","content":"So questions about mage armor. Do the MAs that actually give Armor stack with normal armor? Personally see no reason why not, but it easily can get rather ridiculously high I suppose.<br /> <br /> Some MAs add to defense (Fate, Space, Time) and allow to apply defense to attacks from firearms. Two questions here.<br /> <br /> A) Why does Mind armors defense not apply to attacks with firearms? From the description I don't see why it should any less than the others that do.<br /> <br /> B) Does that mean that defense gained from MA is applied to firearms attack (ala celerity) or all of the subjects defense? If the latter, why? Space twisting bullets out of my way I get helping, but I don't see how my natural dodging abilities would help on top under these conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:24:26-07:00","id":1137008,"title":"","content":"Space can do stuff like expand to slow stuff down, remember?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 09-03-2017, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T14:25:37-07:00","id":1137042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1137008#post1137008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space can do stuff like expand to slow stuff down, remember?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. And that effect is the Defense bonus from mage armor, I don't see why your usual defense would be enhanced along side of that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T14:43:28-07:00","id":1137048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1137042#post1137042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. And that effect is the Defense bonus from mage armor, I don't see why your usual defense would be enhanced along side of that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? One narrative effect doesn't have to correspond exactly to one and only one mechanical effect. Look at something like The Outward and Inward Eye (Space 1). The narrative effect that has is allow you to perceive in all directions, which is represented mechanically as allowing you to cast at sensory range outside what would normally be your sensory range, making you practically immune to ambush <i>and</i> reducing penalties due to range, cover or concealment by Potency.<br /> <br /> In the same way, applying Space Mage Armor distorts space around you to slow down and deflect attacks, which is mechanically represented as getting a bonus to your Defense <i>and</i> letting you use Defense against firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 09-03-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T06:58:19-07:00","id":1137663,"title":"","content":"So, here's a question: Can Proximi use conjunctional effects?<br /> <br /> Say I've got an exorcist-type proximus whose path is Thyrsus + Death, and they have Gossamer Touch as a blessing. Can they cast that so it affects ghosts?<br /> <br /> I figured they were limited enough in their magic to let them have that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T12:12:33-07:00","id":1138069,"title":"","content":"Ive personally ruled that they can if the arcana needed are among the dynasty's arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T16:04:13-07:00","id":1139030,"title":"","content":"So, primary factors other than Potency. What's the deafult for them? I know that when the primary factor is potency, it's equal to the caster's Arcanum rating, but what about Duration or Scale? Do they also jump [Arcanum] positions on the factor table by deafult when they're the primary factor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T16:12:59-07:00","id":1139035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1139030#post1139030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, primary factors other than Potency. What's the deafult for them? I know that when the primary factor is potency, it's equal to the caster's Arcanum rating, but what about Duration or Scale? Do they also jump [Arcanum] positions on the factor table by deafult when they're the primary factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the way it works is that all factors start at the first rung of the table, and then primary goes up by (Arcanum-1) steps - but the net result is that the primary factor starts at at a level equal to Arcanum. So if you have a Arcanum 4 and cast a spell with Duration primary it lasts for 5 turns, as that is the fourth step on the Standard Duration table.<br /> <br /> However, the primary factor can only be Potency or Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T16:14:51-07:00","id":1139036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1139030#post1139030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, primary factors other than Potency. What's the deafult for them? I know that when the primary factor is potency, it's equal to the caster's Arcanum rating, but what about Duration or Scale? Do they also jump [Arcanum] positions on the factor table by deafult when they're the primary factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scale is never a primary spell factor \u2014 it's always Potency or Duration \u2014 and the free steps are Arcanum dots - 1 rather than straight Arcanum dots, but yes, Duration gets free steps on the chart just like Potency does, with what that means changing accordingly if you Reach for Advanced Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T16:51:15-07:00","id":1139046,"title":"","content":"By the way, since spells require a minimum of Potency 1, Duration 1 and Scale 1 to exist (But only Potency and Duration are primary factors), and that's achieved simply by successfully casting the spell, this explains why the free steps are Arcana-1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T19:00:48-07:00","id":1139069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1139046#post1139046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, since spells require a minimum of Potency 1, Duration 1 and Scale 1 to exist (But only Potency and Duration are primary factors), and that's achieved simply by successfully casting the spell, this explains why the free steps are Arcana-1.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could have been worded differently or not even be -1 but i remember a statement from Dave saying it's for a unyet written widget","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T00:14:38-07:00","id":1139119,"title":"","content":"Do beings other than humans have souls? Like, does a cat have a soul? <br /> <br /> If I use Life magic to turn the cat into a human, does the resulting person start suffering from soul loss?<br /> <br /> What if I just use Mind to increase the cat's intelligence? Does that cause the same soul issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T01:42:40-07:00","id":1139131,"title":"","content":"Souls are a weird human-only thing that we seem to have instead of a spiritual reflection. <br /> <br /> Essentially, a cat's soul is the cat spirit associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T03:00:15-07:00","id":1139137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1139119#post1139119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I use Life magic to turn the cat into a human, does the resulting person start suffering from soul loss?<br /> <br /> What if I just use Mind to increase the cat's intelligence? Does that cause the same soul issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be surprised if it did. Even if you modify the cat's Life and Mind Patterns, there's still Spirit, Death and maybe others. These untouched Patterns remain those of a cat and work differently from those of a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T03:05:25-07:00","id":1139138,"title":"","content":"Just raising it's intelligence wouldn't do anything. There are plenty of intelligent things without souls running around. <br /> <br /> Life, I'm not so sure. Creating a human from scratch does result in a soul loss problem, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T15:49:35-07:00","id":1140025,"title":"","content":"If someone takes resistant bashing damage from containing Paradox in their rightmost health box, and that bashing damage causes them to fall unconscious, do they still get to roll for spellcasting? Or do they fall unconscious before they are able to attempt to cast the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T15:53:12-07:00","id":1140028,"title":"","content":"I'd say that, despite the roll for paradox occurring first, both events actually happen simultaneously. So they don't actually get the damage until the spells been cast. <br /> <br /> That aside I also don't think you have to roll for unconsciousness until the start of your <i>next</i> turn by RAW, so it's not actually an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:13:38-07:00","id":1140971,"title":"","content":"Has anyone come up with any new Paradox Conditions that might be interesting to employ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T10:48:21-07:00","id":1141124,"title":"","content":"As I'm currently writing up a legacy a question popped up: Can mages become ghouls? I personally don't see why not, but who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:13:18-07:00","id":1141132,"title":"","content":"Nope. Can't have two power stats, and ghouls are technically blood potency 0 now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:26:29-07:00","id":1141167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1141132#post1141132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Can't have two power stats, and ghouls are technically blood potency 0 now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a Wolf-Blood Tell that grants Primal Urge, and Wolf-Blooded explicitly retains Tells if they for whatever reason turn into a non-Werewolf major splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:20:58-07:00","id":1141183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1141132#post1141132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Can't have two power stats, and ghouls are technically blood potency 0 now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a bit weak to me. Mages are otherwise being called out in Blood and Smoke to be treated as normal mortals. What would the metaphysical reason be for mages being unghoulable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:26:38-07:00","id":1141185,"title":"","content":"Does Samuel Haight count as a metaphysical reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T18:53:25-07:00","id":1141277,"title":"","content":"1. If a mage contains a Paradox from a spell they cast in Astral Space, do they lose Dream Health or take Resistant Bashing on their real body as normal, or both? If they suffer a physical Paradox Condition, does it also manifest on their dream form?<br /> <br /> 2. If a mage releases a Paradox from a spell they cast in Astral Space, does the fallout manifest in the material or Astral, or both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T01:20:52-07:00","id":1141343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1141277#post1141277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If a mage contains a Paradox from a spell they cast in Astral Space, do they lose Dream Health or take Resistant Bashing on their real body as normal, or both? If they suffer a physical Paradox Condition, does it also manifest on their dream form?<br /> <br /> 2. If a mage releases a Paradox from a spell they cast in Astral Space, does the fallout manifest in the material or Astral, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>To 1: I\u00b4d make the physical paradoc condition what it is: physical but as long as they are in the dream form, they also suffer from it.<br /> To 2: If your Paradox makes a sting let them have the fallout manifest in both planes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T20:28:04-07:00","id":1143131,"title":"","content":"What the deuce are &quot;buried materials&quot; for Moros Mages as a Path Tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T22:15:43-07:00","id":1143145,"title":"","content":"Stuff that was once used as a grave good or more esoterically stuff that was taken from a watery grave after it was sunk for some time etc. (only my personal interpretation, but it seems to make sense)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T22:29:49-07:00","id":1143149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1143131#post1143131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the deuce are &quot;buried materials&quot; for Moros Mages as a Path Tool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lead, bone, and gems are all examples, so notionally if it's something you'd find underground or in the walls or at the core of a body or otherwise hidden beneath layers of physical covering it's probably fair game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T05:12:21-07:00","id":1143202,"title":"","content":"I dunno, if that's the case you might as well say Moros can use almost every material that the other Paths can use, especially the metals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T05:15:50-07:00","id":1143203,"title":"","content":"While I personally don't agree with that interpretation either (though I would probably let the gemstones fly in addition to what I said before), there is some evidence is may aswell be true. It's certainly not much more open than the Mastigos material &quot;worked materials&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T05:56:35-07:00","id":1143206,"title":"","content":"I would probably be open to that interpretation as long as players are inventive/interesting with it. I totally wouldn't want to deny a Moros from using the gold coin he found in some pirates long lost buried treasure or some such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T09:23:42-07:00","id":1143248,"title":"","content":"Question about the Duel Arcane.<br /> The description of the attack action seems to encourage the player to come up with some kind of cool sounding effect, then roll Attribute+Arcana. On a success a door opens, additional successes don't open more doors, they just add to your dicepool on the next round. Sounds simple, but could be fun as players enjoy describing increasingly unusual/inventive effects.<br /> <br /> however in the latter half of the paragraph it starts talking about Reach, Yantras and says we must still account for spell factors and resistances, as if we were casting conventional spells? What am I not understanding? Considering we arent even rolling Gnosis+Arcana I thought we were leaving standard spellcasting rules behind in the duel, much like in 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T10:01:03-07:00","id":1143259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1143202#post1143202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, if that's the case you might as well say Moros can use almost every material that the other Paths can use, especially the metals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same logic applies to the categories of the Thyrsus and the Acanthus. It's not an exact science, but &quot;stuff that would be appropriate to the symbolic portfolio of Alchemists and Necromancers&quot; lends a different tone to a cauldron carved from the bedrock of a quarry than &quot;stuff that would be appropriate to the symbolic portfolio of Enchanters and Witches&quot; does to a polished chunk of sea glass washed up on the beach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T16:03:27-07:00","id":1143616,"title":"","content":"Can you have more than one Dedicated Magical Tool? If so, can you stack them for their Paradox reducing effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T16:05:22-07:00","id":1143617,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can have more than one regular DMT, but you can use your soul stones as one. <br /> <br /> And yeah, in that case I'd let it stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T18:11:00-07:00","id":1143631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1143616#post1143616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have more than one Dedicated Magical Tool? If so, can you stack them for their Paradox reducing effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in certain instances, like using a Soul Stone or having 4 dots in Egregore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T20:45:19-07:00","id":1143654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1143631#post1143631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only in certain instances, like using a Soul Stone or having 4 dots in Egregore.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I figured. I allow multiple DMT, but only for their general Yantra bonus. Wasn't sure to allow stackable Paradox reduction with just them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T01:50:41-07:00","id":1143998,"title":"","content":"Remember Artifacts also act as a DMT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:33:01-07:00","id":1144963,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been asked already, but can you spend a Willpower to bolster spellcasting? Like, when I'm determining Gnosis+ Arcana+Yantras etc,etc, can Willpower be spent to increase your chances of succeeding in casting that spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:39:26-07:00","id":1144987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1144963#post1144963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been asked already, but can you spend a Willpower to bolster spellcasting? Like, when I'm determining Gnosis+ Arcana+Yantras etc,etc, can Willpower be spent to increase your chances of succeeding in casting that spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it certainly can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T20:09:05-07:00","id":1146227,"title":"","content":"If souls are part of Death's purview, why can't you just create them with Death 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T20:30:27-07:00","id":1146229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146227#post1146227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If souls are part of Death's purview, why can't you just create them with Death 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason you can't just create a Specter out of whole cloth at Death 5 \u2014 some things are outside the purview of Travelers' Arcana regardless of semantics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T20:40:28-07:00","id":1146231,"title":"","content":"Specters aren't part of Death's purview though. Souls are. Find me one purview in the book that can't be created, other than realms and souls. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 10-02-2017, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T21:15:09-07:00","id":1146243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146231#post1146231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specters aren't part of Death's purview though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arcanum is literally used to summon them in their capacity as symbols of Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Souls are. </div> </div> </div>They're also a finite resource that stops mortal Integrity from falling out, provides benefits to half the Arcana including Death, and makes Awakened magic work without constant Paradox. If anything was going to provide an exception to the soft rules for what magic can and can't do, souls would be fairly high on the list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Find me one purview in the book that can't be created, other than realms and souls. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I can find several, as a matter of fact, and while I recognize that the spirit of your request means &quot;evolution, crafting, conjuration, etc&quot; isn't what you meant, skating past &quot;regardless of semantics&quot; in the name of making it clear your original question was not remotely sincere means it's hard for me to care less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T21:51:52-07:00","id":1146253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146227#post1146227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If souls are part of Death's purview, why can't you just create them with Death 5?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Slighty more helpful that Satchel:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bEtxgTD.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Some discussion about needing all 5 subtle Arcana and then this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/a5chGy1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-03-2017, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T01:38:06-07:00","id":1146278,"title":"","content":"Another example for something that would need the practice of Entities (Arcanum 7) instead of a simple making spell would be directly awakening another person. Even masters of Prime can't do it, doesn't matter that Magic and the Supernal Realms are in the purview of the Prime Arcanum. Prime 7 on the other side can slap an awakening onto someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T05:19:22-07:00","id":1146301,"title":"","content":"Souls can't be created with magic because the developers want them to be a limited and morally complicated resource. Whether or not there's precedent for that is irrelevant, because it is a deliberate and explicit departure from usual way of things. It is a decision made on mechanical and storytelling grounds, where the worldbuilding justification basically amounts to &quot;it is a mystery&quot;.<br /> <br /> Asking why you can't make souls with Death 5 is like asking why you can't alter existing spells - the answer is &quot;because that's how magic works in this setting&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T05:46:42-07:00","id":1146309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146253#post1146253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Slighty more helpful that Satchel:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bEtxgTD.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Some discussion about needing all 5 subtle Arcana and then this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/a5chGy1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the helpful answer. That makes sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T10:23:06-07:00","id":1146372,"title":"","content":"&quot;System: Counterspell is a Clash of Wills (see p. 117), pitting the <b>acting mage\u2019s Gnosis + Arcanum</b> against the countering mage\u2019s Gnosis + Arcanum. A mage can attempt to counter any spell that uses the Arcanum, even if it uses other Arcana as well, but always counters the highest Arcanum of a target spell. The comparative ratings of the two mages\u2019 Arcana are irrelevant; an Initiate can, in theory, counter the spell of a Master. Countering the spell of a mage with a higher rating in the target Arcanum, however, requires that the player spend a point of Mana. Counterspell requires an instant action. If the mage is employing Active Mage Sight (see p. 90), she can attempt to counter a spell of the appropriate Arcanum in combat, regardless of her position in the Initiative order, provided she has not used her action yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Question, for this. Looking at it, it felt as if this highlighted portion here meant the Arcanum of the spell.<br /> <br /> IE: A Master of Mind using a Mind 1 spell with a Gnosis of 5 would roll 5+1, not 5+5 vs the attempt to counter it. That kinda makes sense, because no matter how well done, a 'Knowing' spell is a Knowing spell. But I just want to check that I'm not barking up the wrong tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T10:39:47-07:00","id":1146378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146372#post1146372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IE: A Master of Mind using a Mind 1 spell with a Gnosis of 5 would roll 5+1, not 5+5 vs the attempt to counter it. That kinda makes sense, because no matter how well done, a 'Knowing' spell is a Knowing spell. But I just want to check that I'm not barking up the wrong tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the acting mage's Gnosis + Arcanum would be his Gnosis + his rating in the Arcanum he uses for the spell. So a Master of Mind would add 5 for the Arcanum, wether he casts a Knowing, Fraying or Making spell. At least that's how I understand it. Knowing spells are not inherently easier to counter than Making spells. Iirc when you use counterspell you mess up the imago as it is forming, not the spell itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T10:44:17-07:00","id":1146380,"title":"","content":"Clashes of Wills always use the characters' ratings, not the spells'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T20:36:48-07:00","id":1146549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146372#post1146372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;System: Counterspell is a Clash of Wills (see p. 117), pitting the <b>acting mage\u2019s Gnosis + Arcanum</b> against the countering mage\u2019s Gnosis + Arcanum. A mage can attempt to counter any spell that uses the Arcanum, even if it uses other Arcana as well, but always counters the highest Arcanum of a target spell. The comparative ratings of the two mages\u2019 Arcana are irrelevant; an Initiate can, in theory, counter the spell of a Master. Countering the spell of a mage with a higher rating in the target Arcanum, however, requires that the player spend a point of Mana. Counterspell requires an instant action. If the mage is employing Active Mage Sight (see p. 90), she can attempt to counter a spell of the appropriate Arcanum in combat, regardless of her position in the Initiative order, provided she has not used her action yet.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesnt mention it under counterspell but does the spell being countered gain bonus dice from advanced duration + potency? I assume it does since it refers to the clash of wills rules and that they are just not repeating text to save space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T21:25:42-07:00","id":1146563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146549#post1146549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesnt mention it under counterspell but does the spell being countered gain bonus dice from advanced duration + potency? I assume it does since it refers to the clash of wills rules and that they are just not repeating text to save space?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does the Withstand bonus from Advanced Potency apply to Dissonance checks? The rating otherwise has no way of getting better due to being keyed off of the spell's Arcanum rating rather than the caster's, which makes me inclined to guess that it does, but Advanced Potency isn't directly mentioned in the section on Dissonance at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T01:18:58-07:00","id":1146588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1146549#post1146549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It doesnt mention it under counterspell but does the spell being countered gain bonus dice from advanced duration + potency? I assume it does since it refers to the clash of wills rules and that they are just not repeating text to save space?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally rule no for the simple reason that duration and advanced potency are properties of the spell. Counterspelling messes with the imago before it is finalized, preventing the spell from coming into existence in the first place. The imago itself does have neither advanced potency nor a duration beyond instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T06:25:03-07:00","id":1146645,"title":"","content":"Counterspelling isn't dispellation. You're not fighting the spell, you're fighting the mage. I don't see any reason that any of the methods of bolstering the spell would affect it.<br /> <br /> One more reason to prep stuff in private. I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T08:40:59-07:00","id":1147441,"title":"","content":"A question on spell damage and potency. Is the potency of the spell added to the number of successes similar to weapon damage? A mage with gnosis 2 forces 3 casts a ephemeral fireball that does bashing damage. So the base damage is 3 for potency if the mage rolls one success than it's 4 bashing or 3? and if that's the case the max potency that can be done is 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T08:44:30-07:00","id":1147443,"title":"","content":"No. Spells are all or nothing. Damage spells will only do damage equal to the levels of potency you give them. There's no limit to how high this can go though, as long as you have enough dice to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T08:46:12-07:00","id":1147445,"title":"","content":"5 would be the max for<i> free</i> potency, not the max for <i>total</i> potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T09:21:04-07:00","id":1147459,"title":"","content":"got it thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T17:40:50-07:00","id":1148479,"title":"","content":"What's the practical limit?<br /> <br /> I figure Gnosis 5 + Arcana 5 + 5 Mudra + 3 Willpower - 14 (+7 Potency) = 4 dice to roll. 12 Aggravated for a one turn instant spell is quite a bit of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T17:49:55-07:00","id":1148481,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T18:06:22-07:00","id":1148483,"title":"","content":"So that's probably enough to kill something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T00:39:33-07:00","id":1148539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1148483#post1148483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that's probably enough to kill something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For something that costs Mana and Willpower, risks Paradox, and requires borderline superhuman Skill and Gnosis, sure. At the same level a Master can very likely just instantly kill the average mortal without even bothering with damage numbers. Where is the question here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T03:02:45-07:00","id":1148548,"title":"","content":"Yeah, an unmaking spell with half that much potency is going to get past the withstand of most things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T09:47:08-07:00","id":1148610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1148539#post1148539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For something that costs Mana and Willpower, risks Paradox, and requires borderline superhuman Skill and Gnosis, sure. At the same level a Master can very likely just instantly kill the average mortal without even bothering with damage numbers. Where is the question here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a question. It was an observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T10:44:42-07:00","id":1148625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1148610#post1148610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't a question. It was an observation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You started out by asking what the practical limit was, and then followed it with what in hindsight with further elaboration is your observation of a possible damage output equation, which isn\u2019t tied to your question.<br /> <br /> Basically, you managed to create some communication confusion by asking a rhetorical question in a non-rhetorical question thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T12:30:14-07:00","id":1148653,"title":"","content":"*Enters the thread*<br /> &quot;This seems like a job for Distraction-Man!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1470_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1470\" data-vbnamecard=\"1470\">Johnny Awesome</a>, did your game reach the Acamoth yet? I'm as curious as I am needy for feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T16:57:42-07:00","id":1148706,"title":"","content":"That game is on hiatus. Thanks for asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T15:14:56-07:00","id":1149777,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked before, i looked at couldn't find it<br /> <br /> what effect do the rote skills given to you by your order have on casting rote spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:20:06-07:00","id":1149784,"title":"","content":"If the skill encoded in your rote is a rote skill conferred by your order, the mudra bonus increases by one (to a maximum of five), as if you had a specialty regarding rotes in that skill.<br /> <br /> Example: Phil is an Obrimos in the Adamantine Arrow. He has Athletics 3, Forces 3 and the rote &quot;Telekinetic Strike&quot; with Athletics as the encoded skill. When casting his rote and using the rote mudra as a Yantra, Phil adds his Athletics skill as a Yantra bonus to the spellcasting roll. Since Athletics is one of the rote skills of the order, Phil adds 4 instead of merely 3 dice to his roll. If Phil had Athletics 5 (or even higher), he would still only get 5 dice from the mudra, as the mudra yantra caps out at 5 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:37:35-07:00","id":1149789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1149784#post1149784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the skill encoded in your rote is a rote skill conferred by your order, the mudra bonus increases by one (to a maximum of five), as if you had a specialty regarding rotes in that skill.<br /> <br /> Example: Phil is an Obrimos in the Adamantine Arrow. He has Athletics 3, Forces 3 and the rote &quot;Telekinetic Strike&quot; with Athletics as the encoded skill. When casting his rote and using the rote mudra as a Yantra, Phil adds his Athletics skill as a Yantra bonus to the spellcasting roll. Since Athletics is one of the rote skills of the order, Phil adds 4 instead of merely 3 dice to his roll. If Phil had Athletics 5 (or even higher), he would still only get 5 dice from the mudra, as the mudra yantra caps out at 5 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way its worded is sounds like the max bonus is from the actual skill is +5 plus if its a order skill you get +1 for total +6 (ie the skill being +6 wont make it +7 etc) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Using a Rote\u2019s mudra adds the user\u2019s rating in the Rote\u2019s encoded Skill to her dice pool up to +5. If the Skill is one of her Order\u2019s specialized Rote Skills, she adds an extra die.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Different sentences. Skill up to +5 then if order skill +1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T17:08:53-07:00","id":1149800,"title":"","content":"It was clarified in the mechanical errata for 2e, Mudras cap out at +5, wether it's a rote skill or not, you can never get more than 5 dice from a Mudra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T17:31:59-07:00","id":1149805,"title":"","content":"I'm not in a position to double check, but I believe all Yantras are limited to +5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T07:13:52-07:00","id":1149912,"title":"","content":"Order rote skills -- am I missing more information in the book somewhere? I can't seem to find how these work in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T07:46:33-07:00","id":1149920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1149912#post1149912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order rote skills -- am I missing more information in the book somewhere? I can't seem to find how these work in 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>They apply +1 to a Rote Mudra that uses a skill taught by your Order as Rote Mudras. They're at the bottom of the quick reference character creation sheet on page 82.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T07:50:01-07:00","id":1149921,"title":"","content":"Although IIRC the limit for dice from a rote is still 5, so if you have 5 or more dots in the skill they don't do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T10:38:07-07:00","id":1149949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1149921#post1149921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although IIRC the limit for dice from a rote is still 5, so if you have 5 or more dots in the skill they don't do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's not how that works. All yantra bonuses are capped at 5 dice bonus after taking into account penalties. As Mrmdubois mentioned, no single yantra can provide more than 5 dice, regardless of whether or not they will be deducted to increase spell factors.<br /> <br /> None of that prevents the mudra yantra used in rotes from being implemented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T11:34:23-07:00","id":1149959,"title":"","content":"That's exactly what I just said. I didn't scroll up so I didn't see that Mrmdubois said the same thing earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T02:19:02-07:00","id":1150102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1149949#post1149949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. That's not how that works. All yantra bonuses are capped at 5 dice bonus after taking into account penalties. As Mrmdubois mentioned, no single yantra can provide more than 5 dice, regardless of whether or not they will be deducted to increase spell factors.<br /> <br /> None of that prevents the mudra yantra used in rotes from being implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While there is evidence of the mudra yantras cap of 5 and no other examples of any other yantra over +5, there isnt actually any text that states no single non mudra yantra can be over +5 is there? It doesnt bother be either way but we might yet get a yantra over 5 somewhere down the line unless somebody can actually find the text that says otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T07:05:42-07:00","id":1150131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1150102#post1150102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While there is evidence of the mudra yantras cap of 5 and no other examples of any other yantra over +5, there isnt actually any text that states no single non mudra yantra can be over +5 is there? It doesnt bother be either way but we might yet get a yantra over 5 somewhere down the line unless somebody can actually find the text that says otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specific text? I can't find any (granted I didn't look very hard). However, given the fact that acquiring even a +3 yantra is supposed to be difficult (e.g. the requirement of spending 3 xp to acquire the shadow name merit after character creation), I would personally rule that no yantra is capable of giving more than 5 dice. Anything more than that and you're looking at arch magic. Also, given the existence of exploding dice via 9 and 8 again as well as rote mechanics I would also say that just trying to get a very large dice pool is a bit narrow focused.<br /> <br /> If I reached the point where I felt I might need such a yantra I would start looking for an alternative solution to whatever problem I'm facing in the game. There's almost always more than one way to accomplish something, and the vast majority of the time there's actually several ways, not just two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T07:14:52-07:00","id":1150133,"title":"","content":"8 and 9 again don't actually help that much in spellcasting, because no matter how big your dice pool gets you're only gonna be rolling a small part of it, and you only need one success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T07:25:46-07:00","id":1150134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1150133#post1150133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8 and 9 again don't actually help that much in spellcasting, because no matter how big your dice pool gets you're only gonna be rolling a small part of it, and you only need one success.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does help if you\u2019re fishing for an Exceptional Success, but yeah it doesn\u2019t help achieve that initial success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T09:34:58-07:00","id":1150164,"title":"","content":"Hence the value of becoming a master of an arcanum and creating your own rotes. But honestly, you don't need more than 5-7 dice to be regularly succeeding on your spell casting rolls. Any dice above that can be used towards powering the spell, which comes back to the point of looking for an alternative solution to your problem if you can't get enough power into your spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T01:11:11-07:00","id":1150281,"title":"","content":"I feel bad for asking this. <br /> <br /> If a spell\u2019s duration is measured in turns (let\u2019s say, 3), does it take effect the turn is is cast then last for 3 *more* turns? Or 3 turns total including the turn it is cast?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming the latter, I just wanted to be certain. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T01:37:11-07:00","id":1150282,"title":"","content":"Three turns starting with, and including, the one in which it was cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T06:57:36-07:00","id":1150627,"title":"","content":"The Space spell &quot;Create Sympathy&quot; has been bugging my mind for a little while. The spell is still subject to casting range, right? Like, if I were a master of Space I would not be able to just create a connection between a famous person and a place without having both subjects of the spell (or both ends) to be within range, right? Or is it based off of the fact that I'm targeting a sympathetic connection that doesn't yet exist, thus distance doesn't matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T07:07:23-07:00","id":1150629,"title":"","content":"I think you need one of them in range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T07:11:39-07:00","id":1150632,"title":"","content":"You can't target something that doesn't exist, both targets to be connected via sympathy have to be targeted, which includes range (though this can be sympathetic range using an allready existing sympathy) and scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T16:11:25-07:00","id":1150820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1150627#post1150627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Space spell &quot;Create Sympathy&quot; has been bugging my mind for a little while. The spell is still subject to casting range, right? Like, if I were a master of Space I would not be able to just create a connection between a famous person and a place without having both subjects of the spell (or both ends) to be within range, right? Or is it based off of the fact that I'm targeting a sympathetic connection that doesn't yet exist, thus distance doesn't matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You need both of them in range. This can mean that you cast it by seeing or touching the unknown &quot;end&quot; and use sympathetic range to target someone you know without their presence being necessary. You can't cast it on your friend and make a connection to a person you've never met and who isn't there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:00:35-07:00","id":1150969,"title":"","content":"Since Rewrite History allows you to temporarily remove a template from a character then couldn\u2019t you also use it to change or add a template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:41:20-07:00","id":1150979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1150969#post1150969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Rewrite History allows you to temporarily remove a template from a character then couldn\u2019t you also use it to change or add a template?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont see why not assuming having the temportal sympathy for the point of divergence then for the duration of the spell the targets entire history has been to be that other template if possible.<br /> <br /> I would keep the &quot;cannot change the if born/made as the template&quot; part and only allow templates one can become/transform to during their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-19-2017, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:41:14-07:00","id":1151024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1150969#post1150969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Rewrite History allows you to temporarily remove a template from a character then couldn\u2019t you also use it to change or add a template?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't say &quot;no,&quot; I'd almost certainly have that be another/more expensive Reach effect, given that even without a limitation of &quot;only for templates the character is personally and intimately familiar with&quot; we're talking about altering the history of a monster than may be part of one of the many secretive stretches of the cosmology \u2014 making it so that a changeling never encountered their Keeper is one thing, but contriving the presence of a Stranger you've never met is a whole different bag of chips that may get into multiple targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:48:42-07:00","id":1151061,"title":"","content":"This is something I could see being one of those things that should work but doesn't, like soul creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T00:20:05-07:00","id":1151231,"title":"","content":"Wow, 1E legacies were <i>really weird!</i> Between Blank Badges using Occultation instead of arcana, Legions sheer weirdness, and some other stuff, I don't know how to think about a 2E rendition of Scions of God.<br /> <br /> So here's a question, Scions of God seem to flipflop on the use of optional effects on attainments, and flipflop on using space or prime for additional bonuses to the main attainments. What do you all think about that? Does it make sense for a legacy to use multiple or different arcana for their optional effects if the legacy accepts comers from all paths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T02:50:28-07:00","id":1151252,"title":"","content":"Nah, Scions of God was a mess.<br /> <br /> It seems like it'd be a fairly straightforward Spirit/Space legacy, Prime doesn't actually do anything for it except allow you to use Essence and Mana interchangeably, and you might be able to get away with that as a 4th or 5th attainment if you really felt that you had to have that as a power (I wouldn't).<br /> <br /> Pretty much all legacies accept comers from all Paths if they want in, usually by belonging to an Order the Legacy associates with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-20-2017, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T05:16:59-07:00","id":1151272,"title":"","content":"Legacy attainments can explicitly be weird, so asking whether or not something &quot;makes sense&quot; for legacy attainments would depend entirely on the individual legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T10:23:30-07:00","id":1151377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151252#post1151252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, Scions of God was a mess.<br /> <br /> It seems like it'd be a fairly straightforward Spirit/Space legacy, Prime doesn't actually do anything for it except allow you to use Essence and Mana interchangeably, and you might be able to get away with that as a 4th or 5th attainment if you really felt that you had to have that as a power (I wouldn't).<br /> <br /> Pretty much all legacies accept comers from all Paths if they want in, usually by belonging to an Order the Legacy associates with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I meant more that Scions are more open about it. I'm glad you agree that it was a bit of a mess. It went from no optional effect, to a space optional, to suddenly a prime optional. It's just weird. I wanted to narrow it down and think about it because if it were allowed, then a 2E homebrew might, within the internal logic of &quot;becoming a holy angel&quot;, include a scary-good words-and-signs optional effect, and a co-location optional effect geared toward <i>being summoned, </i>as in its limited to only allowing you to co-locate if someone wants your presence, but once they summon you, you can co-locate paradox-free (which sounds really good). It could get even weirder by possibly making it a projection instead of an actual teleport, sort of like sending a royal avatar to whoever summoned you.<br /> <br /> And when I thought about that stuff I realized it could make other legacies, especially small uncanon ones, or self-made ones for antagonists or player characters, ridiculously flexible and strong. So even though examples like that of a 2E Scions with swapping space/prime optional effects could make a cool-looking legacy about approaching the powers of the Celestines/<i>ilusahim</i> , and were allowed for <i>that</i> legacy, I can't help but think about what other npc's would think about the legacy, what they'd cook up.<br /> <br /> I could kind of see it better if the optional effects at least stayed on the same path, but for Scions it does not.<br /> <br /> Mrmdubois thanks again for your reply, because I was stuck between picking space or prime for their secondary effects, and this helps me narrow it down if it seems that Scions prefer space over prime. I personally couldn't tell, prime fits the holy theme, but space seemed to be more conducive to being &quot;more than human&quot;. And my aforementioned co-location as a form of being summoned, not unlike another spirit, just sounds so useful and so-in-theme for the Scions. Having trouble? Call on your archangel!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151272#post1151272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacy attainments can explicitly be weird, so asking whether or not something &quot;makes sense&quot; for legacy attainments would depend entirely on the individual legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose but, I do like consistency with legacies because it helps paint the idea that soul-shaping is a known process that calls on specific talents to allow it to happen. If the optional effects for a legacy can be whatever, and that was known to magic-at-large, then any mad-genius who wanted to make their own legacy and pushed themselves to do it could make incredibly potent attainments. I feel that creates a conundrum for world-building, for npc's and for player characters. I like weird if it involved weird extremes, like how Legion's Ruling Arcanum is Life, but that doesnt' affect the powers the attainment gives, it just allows the body to harbor a gulmoth that acts as the actual power.<br /> <br /> The weirdness of Scions felt a bit arbitrary to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T10:46:20-07:00","id":1151386,"title":"","content":"I think what you are ignoring in your fears about legacies becoming too flexible/powerful is that attainments and their optional effects cannot simply be &quot;whatever&quot;. They allways follow a theme. You can't just make a legacy that gives you a bunch of neat and handy effects, all these effects must be bound to a single overarching theme of the legacy. Within that theme a legacy can (and really SHOULD) be strong, but it's hardly flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T20:19:43-07:00","id":1151543,"title":"","content":"With example spells like Possession, Animal Minion, and Familiar it appears that Patterning can braid together two subjects such that one is basically, or very nearly the other. Could then Space 4 create a Connected level of Sympathy between two subjects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T20:36:19-07:00","id":1151548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151386#post1151386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what you are ignoring in your fears about legacies becoming too flexible/powerful is that attainments and their optional effects cannot simply be &quot;whatever&quot;. They allways follow a theme. You can't just make a legacy that gives you a bunch of neat and handy effects, all these effects must be bound to a single overarching theme of the legacy. Within that theme a legacy can (and really SHOULD) be strong, but it's hardly flexible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am perfectly aware of that. I just don't think that theming alone isolates the possibilities down far enough if the optional effect <i>could</i> have been from multiple arcana, but since I think we have a concensus that mages can't do that, its no longer that big of a problem to me. I find a theme to be less restrictive than a single arcana. (and having both is what makes a legacy balanced, which the 1E Scions doesn't quite seem to have.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151543#post1151543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With example spells like Possession, Animal Minion, and Familiar it appears that Patterning can braid together two subjects such that one is basically, or very nearly the other. Could then Space 4 create a Connected level of Sympathy between two subjects?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't it outright stated that Space 5 is needed for the Making practice? Well it says it can only be severed with Unmaking, but I think that means that making is what you need to get Connected sympathy. I don't have any further proof, but if it is actually up in the air even a little bit then I guess it depends on if an ST thinks that Connected sympathies existing has less &quot;weight&quot; than the ability to destroy them. I would think that is at least <i>possible </i>, so perhaps Space 4 could do it even though space 5 is needed to destroy it. But I'd personally think it needs space 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T21:32:13-07:00","id":1151563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151548#post1151548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it outright stated that Space 5 is needed for the Making practice? Well it says it can only be severed with Unmaking, but I think that means that making is what you need to get Connected sympathy. I don't have any further proof, but if it is actually up in the air even a little bit then I guess it depends on if an ST thinks that Connected sympathies existing has less &quot;weight&quot; than the ability to destroy them. I would think that is at least <i>possible </i>, so perhaps Space 4 could do it even though space 5 is needed to destroy it. But I'd personally think it needs space 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to pull source for me because I only see Space 5 as necessary for creating a Sympathetic Connection out of nothing. What I'm talking about is essentially an advanced version of Web Weaver which caps out at a Strong Sympathetic Connection, which makes sense given that it appears to take Patterning to create a Connected Sympathetic Connection, as indicated by the Familiar spells, and possibly by Possession and Animal Minion.<br /> <br /> In other words, you're not creating a Sympathetic Connection out of nothing, you're simply buffing an existing connection to the point that as far as Space is concerned you're Connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T22:06:23-07:00","id":1151573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151543#post1151543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With example spells like Possession, Animal Minion, and Familiar it appears that Patterning can braid together two subjects such that one is basically, or very nearly the other. Could then Space 4 create a Connected level of Sympathy between two subjects?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since web-weavers max is only strong, id say it falls into the category of something that probably should work with patterning but doesnt. The strongest you can braid/improve sympathy is a Strong connection. Connected either has to be natural or created using space 5. Fate technically creates the familiar condition and that leads to a connected connection naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-21-2017, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T22:07:29-07:00","id":1151574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151563#post1151563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're going to have to pull source for me because I only see Space 5 as necessary for creating a Sympathetic Connection out of nothing. What I'm talking about is essentially an advanced version of Web Weaver which caps out at a Strong Sympathetic Connection, which makes sense given that it appears to take Patterning to create a Connected Sympathetic Connection, as indicated by the Familiar spells, and possibly by Possession and Animal Minion.<br /> <br /> In other words, you're not creating a Sympathetic Connection out of nothing, you're simply buffing an existing connection to the point that as far as Space is concerned you're Connected.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for sympathy on page 173. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * \u201cConnected\u201d sympathy may only be removed with Unmaking spells. </div> </div> </div> and <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Connected The two subjects are metaphysically one e.g. a mage and her familiar or<br /> soul stone. The connection is unassailable without Unmaking magic and<br /> casting using the connection is not Withstood. </div> </div> </div>the weird thing is it only says Unmaking, nothing about Making, but none of the other spells mention making or reaching Connected, only how to move it down from that, which needs Unmaking apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T22:15:57-07:00","id":1151576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1151574#post1151574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules for sympathy on page 173. and<br /> <br /> the weird thing is it only says Unmaking, nothing about Making, but none of the other spells mention making or reaching Connected, only how to move it down from that, which needs Unmaking apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess from other spells would be then that it doesn't take Making to create a Connected level of Sympathy, just Patterning based off other spells. Heck, if we go with soul stones it doesn't even take a spell, but that's an outlier anyway so feel free to disregard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T17:00:50-07:00","id":1152062,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it. It's interesting that after you transform it into Connected Sympathy you can't unmake it without Space 5 and you're stuck with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T17:31:03-07:00","id":1152068,"title":"","content":"I don't think a spell to increase Sympathy to Connected would be Lasting. The connection would only last as long as the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T23:12:06-07:00","id":1152120,"title":"","content":"A Tremere NPC of mine was killed unexpectedly after my PCs cornered him. His angry Ghost has returned to haunt them. In life he was Gnosis 4 Adept of Death, Disciple of Matter, with a few dots in mind and space thrown in. <br /> <br /> The chapter on Liches makes clear that Ghost Mages retain their powers, but I am wondering what Rank a newborn Ghost Mage would have. Should it be high (3-4?), to represent how powerful he was in life, or low (Say 2) because he is such a new ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T03:23:55-07:00","id":1152148,"title":"","content":"For Mages turned ghosts/spirits/goetia, a good rule of thumb is to make Rank = Gnosis/2. Still, I would give any Mage at least Rank 2 as a ghost so it is self-aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T05:48:07-07:00","id":1152169,"title":"","content":"One way of determining Rank could be to derive it from the mage's new Attributes. Calculate Power, Finesse and Resistance as in dream form, and take the lowest Rank that is capable of having that number of dots. Gnosis 6-7, 8-9 and 10 would also have a minimum Rank of 2, 3 and 4 respectively if you also match trait limits.<br /> That makes it unlikely that a mage gains Rank 1 (but a possibility if they have shit Attributes) and difficult to attain actually good Rank ratings. Someone who wants to be a good ephemeral lich needs to put some work into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:00:37-07:00","id":1152418,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked and answered somewhere else but I am pretty new to the Mage Rules. <br /> <br /> The Adamantine Arrow has the three Rote Skills of Athletics, Intimidation and Medicine.<br /> <br /> Most of the Rotes I want to make for my character do not have any of these three as examples. In order to take these spells as rotes and receive the Mudra skill bonus as a Yantra do I have to fluff the way I do use these skills for those spells or can I use any skill for any rote if in my backstory I learned those rotes from a member of another Order?<br /> <br /> The reason I ask for clarification on these rules is that I have created a very non-physical and non-violent member of the Arrow who does not have Intimidation and has low Athletics. He &quot;fights&quot; in a spiritual way as he is an Astral Adept with Prime 3. While I do have high Medicine using the skill for every Rote feels stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:49:11-07:00","id":1152426,"title":"","content":"You get the yantra bonus just by having the skill required. The order rote bonus also provides a +1 if it is also one of an orders rote skills.<br /> <br /> So you can have crafts at 4 as a rote skill and gain a yantra bonus of +4 and if you were a member of the free council you would gain an additional +1 because its a order rote skill.<br /> <br /> Also since any master can create rotes with any skill the suggested rote skills for the spells are just that suggestions, if some mage can think of a reason why athletics could be used as a yantra for viewing the future then theres nothing stopping him from making a rote with athletics as a rote skill for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-24-2017, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:07:51-07:00","id":1152429,"title":"","content":"Thank you totalgit, that makes it far clearer than other posts I found. I understand now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T18:44:11-07:00","id":1153849,"title":"","content":"So, the book says Mages know when their spells Clash; do they inherently know when attainments or mage sight clash, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T19:57:30-07:00","id":1153860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1153849#post1153849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the book says Mages know when their spells Clash; do they inherently know when attainments or mage sight clash, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume yes, since on the meta level the players certainly know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T10:36:47-07:00","id":1153941,"title":"","content":"A dissenting opinion: I wouldn't assume they know, no. A Mage knows when their spells are tampered with because something interferes with the spell itself. Mage Sight is not interfered with; it simply is seeing what's there. Attainments that mimic spells, meanwhile, probably do ping for the Mage.<br /> <br /> You can also roll Clashes privately without announcing it to the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T07:47:24-07:00","id":1154117,"title":"","content":"I noticed in 2E that prime no longer covers illusions is that correct or did I miss that somewhere? There are some things from the 1E order books I was going to convert but I'm sure of a way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T07:52:41-07:00","id":1154119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154117#post1154117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed in 2E that prime no longer covers illusions is that correct or did I miss that somewhere? There are some things from the 1E order books I was going to convert but I'm sure of a way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The practice of Veiling typically covers illusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T08:47:41-07:00","id":1154128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154117#post1154117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed in 2E that prime no longer covers illusions is that correct or did I miss that somewhere? There are some things from the 1E order books I was going to convert but I'm sure of a way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1e Prime's phantasm-type illusions were replaced with 2e Primes' Green Lantern-style Platonic Form and Eidolon spells; you can still summon things, but they're not &quot;illusions&quot; so much as the Prime pattern of an object without the actual object.<br /> <br /> If you make one with conjunctional Forces, you can still make it look &quot;natural&quot;, filling the illusionist niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T09:37:33-07:00","id":1154145,"title":"","content":"Veiling covers a specific subset of illusions rather than Illusilons in general. With Veiling you can make a thing to appear as a thing of the same type that it is not. A human can be made to look like a different human of roughly the same size. Past events can be made to look different to the postcognition of another mage. More elaborate changes usually require reaches.<br /> <br /> That said classical illusions, that create something that is not there in the first place may be a bit more elaborate in their construction. Mind 4 has the Spell &quot;Hallucination&quot;, Forces could certainly do something similar. A very liberal ST may allow phantasms with a reach on a Forces veiling spell, but he could also call for this to need the weaving or pattering practice, depending on what the illusion does. Changing the color of an object probably is a simple veiling spell, creating moving illusions under your control probably requires weaving (and backing it up with control sound produces the necessary sound effects!) and lastly creating illusions that are audible, visual and even posess kinetic force of their own probably requires you to pattern several forces together, giving acess to a sort of Forces equivalent to the Golem spell from the Matter Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:28:41-07:00","id":1154182,"title":"","content":"Would Death Ruling be enough to give a person's soul a haymaker and inflict the Soul Shocked condition,<br /> or is that still a better fit for Death Weaving due to being a supernatural condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:49:14-07:00","id":1154191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154182#post1154182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Death Ruling be enough to give a person's soul a haymaker and inflict the Soul Shocked condition,<br /> or is that still a better fit for Death Weaving due to being a supernatural condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019d still be Weaving, or more likely Fraying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T21:57:40-07:00","id":1154294,"title":"","content":"Aside from their more versatile powerset, nothing keeps a Death mage from enslaving ghost mages the way they might regular ghosts, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T02:50:33-07:00","id":1154319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154294#post1154294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from their more versatile powerset, nothing keeps a Death mage from enslaving ghost mages the way they might regular ghosts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it\u2019s just more dangerous as they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T08:37:29-07:00","id":1154386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154294#post1154294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from their more versatile powerset, nothing keeps a Death mage from enslaving ghost mages the way they might regular ghosts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Notionally no, but if it's a bona fide lich rather than just a ghost who happened to be a mage in life then the retention of their Arcana puts strong odds on their ability to counter or dispel attempts at subverting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T09:00:13-07:00","id":1154400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154386#post1154386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notionally no, but if it's a bona fide lich rather than just a ghost who happened to be a mage in life then the retention of their Arcana puts strong odds on their ability to counter or dispel attempts at subverting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost mages retain their Arcana in full aswell in 2E, if I remember correctly. So the Lich/Ghost Mage divide isn't that big anymore, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T20:27:23-07:00","id":1154593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154400#post1154400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost mages retain their Arcana in full aswell in 2E, if I remember correctly. So the Lich/Ghost Mage divide isn't that big anymore, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I distinctly remember but for some reason cannot find a post by Dave stating that ghost mages of the ghosts-that-used-to-be-mages variety have Numina based on their former Praxes. Will edit in the link if/when I find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T20:30:56-07:00","id":1154595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154593#post1154593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly remember but for some reason cannot find a post by Dave stating that ghost mages of the ghosts-that-used-to-be-mages variety have Numina based on their former Praxes. Will edit in the link if/when I find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe from the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sympathy-for-the-sinister/\" target=\"_blank\">open development</a>.<br /> <br /> 'Most Pentacle Convocations even go so far as to class ghost mages as liches \u2013 most ghost mages are simply ghosts, like any other beyond a tendency to high Rank and Influences that sometimes resemble the Praxes and Attainments of the mage they\u2019re formed from. A minority, though, are free-willed, clear-minded and retain all their powers, the mages\u2019 mind and soul somehow staying attached to the ghost instead of vanishing upon death.'<br /> <br /> They've come up a few times in my game. Originally as an antagonist before the players had the power to really do much about it. Then back in time when a specific ghost mage was more of an apprentice and unable to do much about its position, which was alright for the story as it wasn't a lasting condition. But now the necromancer is seeking a secret language from a pseudo-human race and is tasking ghosts to find members of it in the Underworld. Considering the situation of what they are and who would be protecting them, a ghost mage is likely to pop up again and this time the mage, significantly powerful now, is likely to put a leash on it more than anything else.<br /> <br /> So I just wanted to make sure the rules jibed with the way I was running things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-31-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:40:09-07:00","id":1154764,"title":"","content":"If you really wanted to,<br /> couldn't you use Matter to change the density of the air to effectively redirect sounds to a specific location?<br /> My mind has it essentially acting like Control Sound, but acting with three dots of Matter instead of two dots of Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:50:48-07:00","id":1154769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1154764#post1154764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really wanted to,<br /> couldn't you use Matter to change the density of the air to effectively redirect sounds to a specific location?<br /> My mind has it essentially acting like Control Sound, but acting with three dots of Matter instead of two dots of Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:55:10-07:00","id":1154771,"title":"","content":"I'd personally throw in Forces 1 in aswell or an extended action to study the sound properties of a particular location first. You can change how matter interacts with sound with Matter alone, yes, but how the sound will be reflected is a rather difficult scientific problem to which Matter alone does not give you the awnser.<br /> <br /> Basically creating a soundproof zone, dim/enhance sound or horribly garbling it in general would be easily accomplished, but carrying the whisper of another character over to your ears specifically... boy you better have Forces 1 or a loooooooooooot of free time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:55:50-07:00","id":1154813,"title":"","content":"I'd think you could just say Matter 3 to do it with distortion and Reach to make it sound clear. You don't need to solve it scientifically, just symbolically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:29:08-07:00","id":1154877,"title":"","content":"As I said it'd depend on the degree. General rough sound alterations would be possible with Matter 3, but very precise manipulations of sound via matter (such as carrying a whisper across a room to you and nobody else) probably needs a precise knowledge of how forces and matter interact, symbolically and scientifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:59:24-07:00","id":1154973,"title":"","content":"What if you just had Matter 3 allow you to do it, and then you use a skill roll to do it <i>well?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T05:11:17-07:00","id":1155021,"title":"","content":"You could probably manage it by making a sort of pipe of vacuum. Like, a thin, cylindrical wall of low density that sound can't get through surrounding a tube of higher density for your words to go down. Bit complex, might take a reach, but definitely doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T05:40:47-07:00","id":1155024,"title":"","content":"The Mage version of cups on string. I\u2019d say Forces need not apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:24:21-07:00","id":1155270,"title":"","content":"A question about Ban.<br /> <br /> Can you use Ban + Mind 2 to stop anything with a Mind from entering the area? If so, do you have to have the lack of air and light effects associated with the usual Ban?<br /> <br /> Can you get more specific and Ban minds with &quot;hostile intent&quot;?<br /> <br /> PS: Ban seemed better in 1e when you could just use it as a force field essentially, but could still see through it without Forces 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T21:39:10-07:00","id":1155284,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1470_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1470\" data-vbnamecard=\"1470\">Johnny Awesome</a> As per the text in the Ban spell,<br /> <br /> &quot;...or create a Ban that only prohibits phenomena under that Arcanum\u2019s purview.&quot;<br /> So a Ban that prohibits solely anything with a mind getting through is possible.<br /> Seems possible without all that other stuff getting excluded.<br /> <br /> As for intent, Mind has the tools for mental stuff, so maybe.<br /> Might depend on the ST. I'd personally allow it.<br /> Like Banning anything that has thoughts of harming others in its mind or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 11-03-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T02:03:20-07:00","id":1155329,"title":"","content":"Intent is actually under Fate.<br /> <br /> Yes I think Ban can be used to make a very specific kind of Ban when using the add arcana option since it says \u201cone or more phenomena under the Arcanum\u2019s purview...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T03:51:49-07:00","id":1155338,"title":"","content":"How does Fabricate Fortune (Fate 2) interact with Space Keys? Does it allow you to bypass them completely, assuming you pass the Clash of Wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T04:22:10-07:00","id":1155344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1155338#post1155338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Fabricate Fortune (Fate 2) interact with Space Keys? Does it allow you to bypass them completely, assuming you pass the Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d rule yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:10:09-07:00","id":1155494,"title":"","content":"What do you STs out there generally figure is a good amount of XP per session or per story?<br /> <br /> My players are tracking at about 16 beats and 14 A-beats over 6 sessions. Does that seem reasonable?<br /> <br /> They're probably on track for 6 XP and 5 AXP by the end of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:13:40-07:00","id":1155499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1155494#post1155494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you STs out there generally figure is a good amount of XP per session or per story?<br /> <br /> My players are tracking at about 16 beats and 14 A-beats over 6 sessions. Does that seem reasonable?<br /> <br /> They're probably on track for 6 XP and 5 AXP by the end of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book recommends 3-5 Beats a session as a minimum so you\u2019re basically on track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T18:37:05-08:00","id":1156214,"title":"","content":"Can't a Thyrsus just keep healing a summoned Supernal entity and keep it in the Fallen World almost indefinitely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T19:12:41-08:00","id":1156220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1156214#post1156214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't a Thyrsus just keep healing a summoned Supernal entity and keep it in the Fallen World almost indefinitely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the fact that a Supernal entity with Life can't even heal themselves to get past their time limit...no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T20:51:14-08:00","id":1156231,"title":"","content":"The Supernal Summoning rules don't say anything about that unfortunately. Not only that but the Materialize manifestation implies that they suffer Mana bleed instead of Corpus bleed. On top of that the summoning rules say that they disappear when their corpus is full, which even means Bashing damage if you take it literally, which doesn't really make sense given everything else. Also, do they have to be filled with Aggravated or will being filled with Lethal kill them as well?<br /> <br /> No wonder this thread has over 4000 posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T04:38:24-08:00","id":1156283,"title":"","content":"They take damage from being in the Fallen, and also lose mana. The fact that they\u2019re material by default in the Fallen (And thus have the Materialize manifestation) doesn\u2019t protect them from this mana bleed the way being material protects other ephemeral entities from Essence bleed.<br /> <br /> You could inflict Bashing on them, but the damage they default to taking in the Fallen due to exposure is Corpus damage meaning their actual health boxes are being permanently reduced in number. They only worry about B/L/A damage in the sense that their remaining boxes could fill up and take them out quicker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:33:39-08:00","id":1156294,"title":"","content":"Identifying imbued,enhanced and artifacts -- so let let see if I am understanding this correctly. Say I have a walking cane as an imbued item that has the spell Death 3 Rotting Flesh in it. A mage with prime can use Supernal Vision and know what arcanum, what level how much mana and the nimbus. But wouldn't get the exact effect. In order to get that they would have to scrutinize is that correct?<br /> In addition a mage that doesn't have prime would only get that above info through scrutiny?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:10:28-08:00","id":1156314,"title":"","content":"Pretty much, but also Scrutiny would only work if the Mage had Prime or Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:45:06-08:00","id":1156323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1156283#post1156283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They take damage from being in the Fallen, and also lose mana. The fact that they\u2019re material by default in the Fallen (And thus have the Materialize manifestation) doesn\u2019t protect them from this mana bleed the way being material protects other ephemeral entities from Essence bleed.<br /> <br /> You could inflict Bashing on them, but the damage they default to taking in the Fallen due to exposure is Corpus damage meaning their actual health boxes are being permanently reduced in number. They only worry about B/L/A damage in the sense that their remaining boxes could fill up and take them out quicker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that they bleed Mana?<br /> <br /> As far as the Corpus vs. B/L/A: Hasn't this been cleared up by now? Aren't there just different levels of Corpus damage just like Health boxes? So what you're saying is that they literally lose the Corpus boxes over time and that otherwise they just use regular damage?<br /> <br /> Btw, I'm still not finding any reference to them not being able to heal themselves or be healed, but if they literally lose their Corpus boxes then this makes more sense.<br /> <br /> The rules should say that they lose Corpus &quot;rating&quot; or &quot;boxes&quot; if that's the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:24:13-08:00","id":1156335,"title":"","content":"It says they bleed Mana right under the Materialize Condition for ephemeral entities. The fact that there isn\u2019t a specification of what kind of damage they take (B/L/A), but instead it\u2019s just Corpus damage in the Lifespan section of summoning Supernal Entities tells me they just start losing Corpus when their time runs out. Especially considering that Lethal damage is specifically called out as occurring under other circumstances. It also mentions in the top of one paragraph that a Supernal entity can run out of Corpus, implying its being reduced as a whole. So Supernal entities risk death in two ways, by having Health boxes filled with damage, or by running out of Corpus.<br /> <br /> That damage also triggers possible losses in Power, Resistance, and Finesse. Though that can also be triggered by any form of damage taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:57:29-08:00","id":1156362,"title":"","content":"It's not clear at all from the text, but thanks to your help it is now.<br /> <br /> I guess I agree that there is a Mana bleed given what's written in the Materialize Condition, but it really should have been stated in the section where they talk about Spirits and Ghosts bleeding Essence. Pretty sloppy editing IMO.<br /> <br /> I assume you think they should lose 1 Mana per hour then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:49:58-08:00","id":1156378,"title":"","content":"I think they should start bleeding mana after their safe time limit has elapsed. That\u2019s just my opinion though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T16:26:15-08:00","id":1157657,"title":"","content":"Do you think a mage with mind and matter could use perfect recall to remember somebody and matter to form the image of that person from Ink on a page with patterning thereby creating a representational sympathetic yantra of that person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:15:36-08:00","id":1157676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1157657#post1157657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think a mage with mind and matter could use perfect recall to remember somebody and matter to form the image of that person from Ink on a page with patterning thereby creating a representational sympathetic yantra of that person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because Representational Sympathetic Yantras are dirt cheap. Also, if you had ink it would only take the Shaping spell, not Patterning to create such an image. Heck, with Shaping you could just turn a random rock into a bust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T20:38:32-08:00","id":1157688,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. What do you mean by dirt cheap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T21:15:58-08:00","id":1157693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1157688#post1157688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense. What do you mean by dirt cheap?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually got mixed up and forgot about Symbolic Yantras where you could just scribble a name down. The bar is still pretty low though considering most of the examples are the kind of thing that naturally accumulate as a person goes on living unless they're very, very careful. To me, a memory is a tangible thing and as good as a photograph as far as anyone with Mind is concerned, (especially if imprinted into a more permanent form such as an ink drawing) so it's not particularly difficult to collect Representational Yantras of people you've at least seen before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T22:53:03-08:00","id":1157701,"title":"","content":"If a mage casts the Life 4 Spell Regeneration on a Sleeper with brain damage, say returning him from coma to cognizance; does the sleeper count as 'witnessing the unbelievable&quot; and therefore enforce Quiescence; or will there be a point where the recovery strains credibility and create dissonance?<br /> <br /> Assume for the sake of convenience that the mage healer is &quot;playing doctor&quot; pretending to route the spells through machine Yantra and practices that mimic medical technology.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T00:24:34-08:00","id":1157709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1157701#post1157701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage casts the Life 4 Spell Regeneration on a Sleeper with brain damage, say returning him from coma to cognizance; does the sleeper count as 'witnessing the unbelievable&quot; and therefore enforce Quiescence; or will there be a point where the recovery strains credibility and create dissonance?<br /> <br /> Assume for the sake of convenience that the mage healer is &quot;playing doctor&quot; pretending to route the spells through machine Yantra and practices that mimic medical technology.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it obvious magic? I would say no but the spell might suffer from dissonance later via <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#004E6D\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Book\">Spells that are not obvious at the moment they are cast escape the Paradox die bonus, but may be subject to Dissonance if they are obvious when a Sleeper later encounters them.</span></span> </div> </div> </div> if a Dr knows the impossibility of the person regaining cognizance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T08:37:01-08:00","id":1157760,"title":"","content":"When using Sympathetic Scrying do you need to Reach for Sensory range? I'm assuming so.<br /> <br /> Say a Gnosis 2 Mage w/Space 3 has a dice pool of 5.<br /> <br /> Imagine he wants to Scry on a target that he has Weak Sympathy with and doesn't know their full name. So this should be Withstand 4.<br /> <br /> So Reach: +1 for sensory, +1 instant, + 1 change primary to potency, +1 advanced duration (scene) = 4 reach so 2 paradox dice<br /> <br /> Yantras: Symbolic sympathy +0 (assuming a drawing), +2 High Speech bringing his dice pool to 7.<br /> <br /> Then he would need to increase potency from 3 to 5 so that would bring his dice pool back down to 3.<br /> <br /> Does this seem correct?<br /> <br /> PS: Although it's not listed under Mana costs, am I correct that Sympathetic spells require 1 Mana to cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-11-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T09:00:44-08:00","id":1157764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1157760#post1157760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Sympathetic Scrying do you need to Reach for Sensory range? I'm assuming so.<br /> <br /> Say a Gnosis 2 Mage w/Space 3 has a dice pool of 5.<br /> <br /> Imagine he wants to Scry on a target that he has Weak Sympathy with and doesn't know their full name. So this should be Withstand 4.<br /> <br /> So Reach: +1 for sensory, +1 instant, + 1 change primary to potency, +1 advanced duration (scene) = 4 reach so 2 paradox dice<br /> <br /> Yantras: Symbolic sympathy +0 (assuming a drawing), +2 High Speech bringing his dice pool to 7.<br /> <br /> Then he would need to increase potency from 3 to 5 so that would bring his dice pool back down to 3.<br /> <br /> Does this seem correct?<br /> <br /> PS: Although it's not listed under Mana costs, am I correct that Sympathetic spells require 1 Mana to cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sympathetic attainment has the requirements (p193) as the yantra, sensory range and 1 mana so yes its 1 mana plus whatever the spell might cost.<br /> <br /> It looks right, remember he can also spend willpower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-11-2017, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T09:02:26-08:00","id":1157766,"title":"","content":"Sensory Range is a prerequisite for casting using Sympathetic Range. So, yes. You'd need that Reach for casting Scry using Sympathetic Range, as well as any other spell cast sympathetically.<br /> <br /> The actual rules for casting sympathetic magic (both spatial and temporal) is listed in their respective Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:39:35-08:00","id":1157797,"title":"","content":"Can sympathetic range be used to affect things across the gauntlet without having access to spirit yourself? So if you have a sympathetic link to a spirit in the shadow could you scry on it with just Space 2? Could you Co-Locate into the Shadow and thus cross the Gauntlet with just space?<br /> <br /> Also: The Reaching spell implies that you need it to affect stuff across the Gauntlet at all (or in other spells a specific reach). Is this the case?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:52:52-08:00","id":1157799,"title":"","content":"&quot;Any spell cast on a subject on the other side of the Gauntlet or on the Gauntlet itself is Withstood by the Gauntlet Strength. If the Gauntlet Strength at the caster\u2019s location and the Gauntlet Strength at the subject\u2019s location are different, apply the lower value (the mage can either direct the Supernal energies to cross the Gauntlet and then seek out the subject, or vice versa).&quot;<br /> Page 179.<br /> <br /> Edit. No Spirit is needed. The Reaching spell makes it possible to use magic at touch or sensory range across the Gauntlet rather than having to cast sympathetically or through remote viewing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-11-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T12:50:28-08:00","id":1157807,"title":"","content":"Once the Scrying window is open, I take it that the Mage can cast spells using remote casting (2 Reach) without further need for Sympathetic Yantras or Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T14:19:25-08:00","id":1157816,"title":"","content":"&quot;Casting spells on subjects the mage can see through the window counts as viewing them remotely&quot;<br /> Page 175, in the text about the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T05:41:25-08:00","id":1157913,"title":"","content":"Quarantine's Time 5 effect states that any influence the area, or anyone inside had on the world is either undone or is caused by somebody else and normal history reapplies itself when the spell ends.<br /> <br /> Surely it also reapplies when anybody inside also leaves right? Its not stated as such but what if:<br /> <br /> You place murderer A into a Quarantine Time prison, time is altered and the murder he commited is now committed by Murderer B instead. As written if you let Murderer A out time doesnt revert and B has still committed the murder, it only reverts when the spell ends. Wondering if this is intended? I can see some very weird scenarios happening if it is intended, which isnt a bad thing im just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-12-2017, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T07:08:40-08:00","id":1157927,"title":"","content":"I assume that letting Murderer A out is effectively ending the spell for that individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:01:24-08:00","id":1158011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1157927#post1157927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that letting Murderer A out is effectively ending the spell for that individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ofc, once you leave the area you are no longer under its effects. So yeh turn to frog spell ends when you leave so the same would happen with quarantine.<br /> <br /> Saying that, what if you put murderer A in the area, the murder was then done by murderer B, A then leaves so the original time line returns, if A reenters the area does it revert back to B having done the murder again or might it now be person C or no murder at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:02:44-08:00","id":1158023,"title":"","content":"It would probably be B again. What made B fit as a murderer happened in the past. Unless someone casts a spell to alter the past relating to the murder while murderer A is outside the spell, murderer B would still be the best fit as the murderer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T07:28:33-08:00","id":1158163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1157709#post1157709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Is it obvious magic? I would say no but the spell might suffer from dissonance later via if a Dr knows the impossibility of the person regaining cognizance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't... think so. According to the Doc it's not impossible, just highly unlikely. <br /> <br /> I supppse the only thing I'm really worried about is hanging a lasting relinquished spell off a mortal sleeper for the rest of his life. Best case scenario the spell is going to light up his pattern to any passerby Mage, if they happen to be a Banisher or a Seer looking to take advantage or even just another in the Consili with a score to settle... it's kind of paonting a big vulnerable target on him, and my Mage by extension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T07:56:32-08:00","id":1158167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1158163#post1158163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't... think so. According to the Doc it's not impossible, just highly unlikely. <br /> <br /> I supppse the only thing I'm really worried about is hanging a lasting relinquished spell off a mortal sleeper for the rest of his life. Best case scenario the spell is going to light up his pattern to any passerby Mage, if they happen to be a Banisher or a Seer looking to take advantage or even just another in the Consili with a score to settle... it's kind of paonting a big vulnerable target on him, and my Mage by extension.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that\u2019s the only spell you put on him. You can devise some Veiling spells to lower the chances of your work being noticed without closer scrutiny. Disassociating from your beneficiary will also lower the chances of their being targeted, or you via them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T17:06:04-08:00","id":1158298,"title":"","content":"I forget, and I haven't been able to find it.<br /> <br /> Is Stealing Fire subject to dissonance or paradox, as a matter of course? It makes a Sleeper into a Sleepwalker, but does the spell itself risk paradox prior to taking effect at all times, or would it depend on the context of the casting?<br /> <br /> I realized that casting spells on sleepers that are overt might be harrowingly powerful if you combine the Stealing Fire spell with the spell you're actually trying to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T17:29:00-08:00","id":1158301,"title":"","content":"Dont think there is anything obvious that happens when you actually cast Stealing Fire so outside observers and the target wont notice any obvious magic so no paradox. In what way powerful? Turning sleepers into sleepwalkers to avoid paradox is cool but then Stealing Fire has to beat withstand and is min Gnosis + 3 ( if stealing fire is lowest spell) - 2 dicepool so it has its own problems. I can see it being good vs a small number of sleepers but probably harder to use in larger crowds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T11:57:55-08:00","id":1158578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1158301#post1158301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont think there is anything obvious that happens when you actually cast Stealing Fire so outside observers and the target wont notice any obvious magic so no paradox. In what way powerful? Turning sleepers into sleepwalkers to avoid paradox is cool but then Stealing Fire has to beat withstand and is min Gnosis + 3 ( if stealing fire is lowest spell) - 2 dicepool so it has its own problems. I can see it being good vs a small number of sleepers but probably harder to use in larger crowds.</div> </div> </div> </div>well I would hope so. I'm still not sure about how many people who ST for this game and think that &quot;the number of people who can actually pull this off is slim to none&quot; is a reasonable balance for any combinations of stuff that sounds scary. I generally assume that mages who have 4 gnosis or higher are extremely rare, extremely rare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:24:37-08:00","id":1158638,"title":"","content":"I think for setting implications it's good to make certain Rotes rare as well. Like a Stealing Fire Rote won't be looked on too favorably by Guardians as it would promote abuse with all the extra Reach.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Lethal damage spells. I don't think those Rotes should be getting traded around like candy IMO. You can wipe out a whole cabal with one of these spells pretty easily if you get a large enough dice pool. I'm sure it happens, but the setting doesn't make sense if this stuff is too easy to get. You should probably have to work for it.<br /> <br /> Different tables might have different opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T16:04:51-08:00","id":1158685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1158638#post1158638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for setting implications it's good to make certain Rotes rare as well. Like a Stealing Fire Rote won't be looked on too favorably by Guardians as it would promote abuse with all the extra Reach.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Lethal damage spells. I don't think those Rotes should be getting traded around like candy IMO. You can wipe out a whole cabal with one of these spells pretty easily if you get a large enough dice pool. I'm sure it happens, but the setting doesn't make sense if this stuff is too easy to get. You should probably have to work for it.<br /> <br /> Different tables might have different opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is par for the course because neophytes are never taught 4 dot spells (for obvious logistical reasons but it does nip this one in the bud).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:40:42-08:00","id":1158998,"title":"","content":"Its worth noting that using Stealing Fire on Sleepers might be a neat way to get around Paradox in the moment, you are still going to have Wisdom problems when the spell elapses and the poor sods sanity crumbles away under the weight of the Supernal Secrets they have witnessed. Hmmm, I imagine its a spell frequently inured for this reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T15:21:57-08:00","id":1159223,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> <br /> <br /> You could call in the Guardians once it's all done.<br /> Have them scrub the memories away and all that before Stealing Fire wears off.<br /> That way they can shoulder the brunt of it if you don't have it inured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T15:36:55-08:00","id":1159229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1159223#post1159223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a><br /> <br /> You could call in the Guardians once it's all done.<br /> Have them scrub the memories away and all that before Stealing Fire wears off.<br /> That way they can shoulder the brunt of it if you don't have it inured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of Guardian philosophy is that you should clean up your own messes, if something bad happens (Especially to you) you deserve it. They act when it's beyond the control of basically anyone else including the responsible party. If they do have to clean it up for you, then they'll make it very harsh for you indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:35:50-08:00","id":1159864,"title":"","content":"Simple question, I think. Does using a Rote automatically make a spell obviously a spell? For example, if my character is casting Clear Thoughts as a Rote on a Sleeper and tells them &quot;it's a part of the therapy&quot; can that track, or is a Rote automatically a whole lot of glossia (I assume not without a High Speech Yantra) and gesticulating (reading the Core Book I'm thinking... probably not, but Mudra requirements have me guessing)?<br /> <br /> My assumption (for the example) is that if you can get the Sleeper one on one and convince them that what you're doing is a natural but unconventional form of therapy, and build it in, then it's possible to cast without triggering The Curse, but my own bias towards character goals have me wondering...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:53:45-08:00","id":1159877,"title":"","content":"Rotes aren\u2019t necessarily obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T11:25:28-08:00","id":1159930,"title":"","content":"You can cast Rotes without using the Mudra (and, in fact, cannot use the Mudra if you're casting from a Grimoire) so there's no reason for it to be more obvious than any other spells. Mudras are likely obvious to other mages, but normal people will probably just find them to be weird gestures or poses. Most people would not assume that it's something magical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T03:05:21-08:00","id":1160156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1159223#post1159223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a><br /> <br /> You could call in the Guardians once it's all done.<br /> Have them scrub the memories away and all that before Stealing Fire wears off.<br /> That way they can shoulder the brunt of it if you don't have it inured.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think most pentacle mages would think three times before drawing the Guardians attention to their flagrant use of magic on and around Sleepers. Obviously interpretations of the Orders varies from table to table OOC and Consillia to Consillia IC, but I generally wouldnt be portraying the Guardians as something like the 'clean up teams' from Men In Black who are never more than a phone call away.<br /> <br /> That leads nicely to my question. Am I correct in understanding that 'memory scrubbing' of Sleepers is a pretty difficult feat for Mind Mages below the rank of Master? Would the use of either Memory Hole or Psychic Reprogramming on a Sleeper be subject to either Paradox or Dissonance, punishing the caster, and ensuring the spell will eventually fail.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: On the question about the obviousness of Rote Mudra's the 1e Order books had lots of examples that varied between quite obvious spellcasting gestures, to very negligible and subtle ones. I imagine that a trained eye could pick them out though, you might offer your PCs dice-rolls to ID npcs using more subtle gestures, perhaps with a bonus if they share an Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","user":"Katana1515","date":". 11-18-2017, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T05:36:30-08:00","id":1160178,"title":"","content":"Paradox Risk requires that something beyond explanation occurs, or that something \u201cnatural\u201d have a clearly unnatural source in the actions of the Mage.<br /> <br /> Dissonance is always a risk, but may never happen depending on how subtley the Mage buries the lede.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T21:32:02-08:00","id":1160417,"title":"","content":"Vampires have Strix. Werewolves have idigam. Changelings have the Huntsman. Do Mages have this kind of highlighted antagonist in 2ed? If yes who is it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T22:40:07-08:00","id":1160431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1160417#post1160417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have Strix. Werewolves have idigam. Changelings have the Huntsman. Do Mages have this kind of highlighted antagonist in 2ed? If yes who is it</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Explanation is <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/falling-down/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T10:02:48-08:00","id":1160542,"title":"","content":"Nofather is dead on, but I reckon another reason why this is the case is that Mages are literally drowning in high end antagonists. The Mage splats unparalleled ability to hop between planes and tendancy to meddle means that your PC's can find themselves contending with Bound Gods, Astral representatives of abstract concepts, potent lords of shadow choirs, impossible gulmoths born of their own hubris, Cthonic monsters from the depths of the Underworld etc etc. The appearance of Exarch sent Ochemata or fickle Supernal entities is just the icing on the horror-cake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:36:46-08:00","id":1161019,"title":"","content":"So one of my players has gotten the idea to build himself a magical combat exosuit which would allow him to octo-wield (as in 8) .50 caliber heavy machine guns.<br /> <br /> Should I allow it or would it break the action economy too much?<br /> <br /> If I do allow it how should I model it? e.g. just multiple any attack roll by 8?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:44:36-08:00","id":1161021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1161019#post1161019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of my players has gotten the idea to build himself a magical combat exosuit which would allow him to octo-wield (as in 8) .50 caliber heavy machine guns.<br /> <br /> Should I allow it or would it break the action economy too much?<br /> <br /> If I do allow it how should I model it? e.g. just multiple any attack roll by 8?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Autofire rules are pretty well suited to this. What kind of investment are we looking at here vis-a-vis Arcana, spell-count, and mechanical expectations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:45:36-08:00","id":1161022,"title":"","content":"There are rules for spray or automatic fire, I'd use that and add to the existing Lethal rating a bit. His whole action would still be spent firing though, the number of guns makes little difference., just the damage output.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T19:03:03-08:00","id":1161041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1161021#post1161021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Autofire rules are pretty well suited to this. What kind of investment are we looking at here vis-a-vis Arcana, spell-count, and mechanical expectations?</div> </div> </div> </div>The players character concept is 'reckless wizard Cave Johnson' so he's always coming up with hijinks of some sort and butting heads with the Guardians. His latest project is legitimate within the scope of our game it's just that I'm worried about opening a can of worms when it comes to combat escalation. Which I'll admit is kind of silly considering the nature of M:tAw.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <br /> <br /> How does +5L with the rote quality to hit a target within range (to represent the sheer volume of fire) sound?<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Can we not multi quote? It doesn't seem to work on my browser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T19:33:42-08:00","id":1161049,"title":"","content":"On second thought, I don't think I'd add straight Lethal, but instead an equipment bonus, probably something like +1 per Potency for whatever spell is getting these guns to work in sync. In the end the beefed up dice pool will also increase the damage output on a successful hit, but the guns will still only function as one gun being fired. Not sure, but I think I'd also increase the initiative penalty. Naturally, you could mitigate that with another spell. Imo, a lot of Mage should come down to opportunity cost, and I think that'd be a fair one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T10:44:58-08:00","id":1161204,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to cast and how would you go about setting up a spell that alerts you to when your name is used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:13:25-08:00","id":1161219,"title":"","content":"i had a think about it then asked my mage GM he said<br /> &quot;a Knowing (1-dot) spell could probably pull it off. Prime would tell you if anyone speaks your Sympathetic (True) Name (because it's a Yantra tied to you), while Fate would ping if anyone speaks of you (because their intention is to refer to you). It'd be Duration primary&quot;<br /> of course you would also need to reach to set the area that the spell effects<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T16:39:45-08:00","id":1161651,"title":"","content":"Question: Can a mage with 3 matter, 3 Death use death gate to enter the twilight state but use matter on the stuff outside of twilight? For instance, while in twilight, could the mage cause the matter there hamper his enemy from the safety of twilight? If so, maybe a page number for 2nd edition to read up on why or why it isn't possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T16:47:05-08:00","id":1161655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1161651#post1161651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Can a mage with 3 matter, 3 Death use death gate to enter the twilight state but use matter on the stuff outside of twilight? For instance, while in twilight, could the mage cause the matter there hamper his enemy from the safety of twilight? If so, maybe a page number for 2nd edition to read up on why or why it isn't possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s possible. You can\u2019t typically touch things in Twilight though so you\u2019d have to use a Reach on Sensory Range it another spell (Touch of the Grave for example) to target something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T16:48:56-08:00","id":1161657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1161655#post1161655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s possible. You can\u2019t typically touch things in Twilight though so you\u2019d have to use a Reach on Sensory Range it another spell (Touch of the Grave for example) to target something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So if I am in twilight, I could say use remote control from the twilight to cause a door to move and lock, or shaping to push a face out of a wall kinda deal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T17:20:14-08:00","id":1161663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1161657#post1161657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So if I am in twilight, I could say use remote control from the twilight to cause a door to move and lock, or shaping to push a face out of a wall kinda deal</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As long as you have sensory range then yes. Shaping doesnt mention needing to physically mold the target item so one assumes its molded via thought? If it does require physical molding then you;d need touch of the grave or gossamer touch.<br /> <br /> Its odd that Gossamer touch has a reach to allow all items on a person to interact with twilight but touch of the graves doesnt when they basically are doing the same thing with different states of twilight.<br /> <br /> Note that the reverse is true, while being in twilight negates mundane obstacles like guns etc, you can still be targeted by spells (esp area ones) in twilight and or items with touch of the grave etc cast on them also. Along with being susceptable to the shape Ephemera spell too..<br /> <br /> Twilight is powerful but everybody able to enter twilight will also be doing so and have the means to counter it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-22-2017, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T06:36:21-08:00","id":1162160,"title":"","content":"The book says: &quot;The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sense her subject&quot; sounds a little loose to me. Can you cast Web of Life and target people beyond a wall, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T07:42:35-08:00","id":1162174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1162160#post1162160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says: &amp;quot;The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Sense her subject&amp;quot; sounds a little loose to me. Can you cast Web of Life and target people beyond a wall, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes, but there are limitations. You know a person is there, and you can assume they\u2019re wearing clothes, but since you\u2019re not sensing the clothes you can\u2019t target their duds. You can only act on as much information as you actually have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T10:47:24-08:00","id":1162216,"title":"","content":"But if you used a Matter spell to sense their clothes, then you probably could....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T11:53:49-08:00","id":1162231,"title":"","content":"I would say this case would require an additional reach for viewing remotely though as you don't perceive them with your own mundane senses but see them &quot;through&quot; a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T14:04:27-08:00","id":1162252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1162160#post1162160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says: &quot;The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sense her subject&quot; sounds a little loose to me. Can you cast Web of Life and target people beyond a wall, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you can hear or smell somebody on the other side of the wall then you can target them, you wont know if its friend or foe but you can zap them easily enough.<br /> <br /> Using matter to &quot;know&quot; where their clothes are wouldnt work, but if you somehow used unveiling to sense them or enhanced your munadne senses to be able to detect clothes then sure, it'd work as normal.<br /> <br /> Since web of life is a knowing spell you arnt actually sensing anything, you just know they are there without sensing them. Its like knowing somebody is in a room because you just left it but you cant see, hear or smell them anymore theres a difference between knowing and sensing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 11-24-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T19:56:37-08:00","id":1162329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1162252#post1162252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you can hear or smell somebody on the other side of the wall then you can target them, you wont know if its friend or foe but you can zap them easily enough.<br /> <br /> Using matter to &quot;know&quot; where their clothes are wouldnt work, but if you somehow used unveiling to sense them or enhanced your munadne senses to be able to detect clothes then sure, it'd work as normal.<br /> <br /> Since web of life is a knowing spell you arnt actually sensing anything, you just know they are there without sensing them. Its like knowing somebody is in a room because you just left it but you cant see, hear or smell them anymore theres a difference between knowing and sensing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea, but the Web of Life spell is pretty descriptive in its use of &quot;sensing&quot;.<br /> <br /> By tapping into the pulse of the living world, the mage becomes<br /> keenly aware of any living things nearby. She feels their<br /> presence by the weight they exert upon the Tapestry, a gravity of<br /> the life-force that connects all creatures to the same great cycle.<br /> Because the unfiltered sensing of all life might provide a sensory<br /> overload, most mages specify certain types of life to detect, such<br /> as \u201chumans, insects, and birds\u201d or \u201conly dogs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now, if you do not accept this, I think combining this with a Space 1 conjunction would allow you to actually sense the location of those living things, so with life 1 space 1 you could cast a version that specifically pinpoints them so that you could cast on them using sensory range without having to see them. If not, then a combined spell that is both knowing and unveiling could probably do the trick, which would then require a fairly strong mage to cast it, which then justifies the strength of the spell itself--a strong spell for a strong mage! I also see no reason why casting one spell that &quot;combos&quot; into the next spell should be discouraged. So this sounds pretty fair to me personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T22:05:19-08:00","id":1162360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1162329#post1162329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this idea, but the Web of Life spell is pretty descriptive in its use of &quot;sensing&quot;.<br /> snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that fluff is pretty bad tbh. The practice of knowing specifically mentions that the info is a direct awareness and a mage doesnt have to interpret it via senses whereas unveiling exposes hidden things to the mages senses.<br /> <br /> But yeh Space 1's Outward and inward eye basically does what you mention, it spreads the persons senses out over the entire area so you can just use space 1 to &quot;sense&quot; something, note its also unveiling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T22:30:51-08:00","id":1162908,"title":"","content":"So in the end does the community think you should be able to use Web of Life to sense people and then target them with sensory spells?<br /> <br /> Follow up question: Can you use Telekinesis to unlock a door handle from the outside even if you can't see it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T01:38:21-08:00","id":1162933,"title":"","content":"Web of Life still gets to be Knowing because it doesn\u2019t actually expand your sensory capabilities. In fact, I imagine Web of Life giving you sensory overload is exactly because the information it gives force-fed, ie. through Knowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T07:17:14-08:00","id":1162993,"title":"","content":"I'm ok wit considering things like Web of Life remote sensing, as was suggested earlier in the thread, as long as the spell is still active during the casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T07:31:52-08:00","id":1162995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1162908#post1162908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow up question: Can you use Telekinesis to unlock a door handle from the outside even if you can't see it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what you mean by \u2018see it,\u2019 if the player can see the locking mechanism though, he could probably shape the telekinesis to fit a keyhole or pull the credit card trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T07:48:57-08:00","id":1162999,"title":"","content":"Ok. I think I'll allow Web of Life to allow targeting if it is left active and TK would be fine because of the credit card trick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:57:12-08:00","id":1163552,"title":"","content":"Why didn't they allow Scale to be a Primary factor? I don't see how it breaks the game or anything like that and some spells seem to make sense with Scale as Primary, like Bans or Wards etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T08:28:45-08:00","id":1163561,"title":"","content":"Because the ability to cover more area or targets isn\u2019t as useful as making something last longer or be more powerful. Scale also has no effect on CoW or Withstand, while Duration and Potency can/do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:36:57-08:00","id":1163579,"title":"","content":"But why ban it as a Primary factor? You're answer seems to boil down to: &quot;Because you can't power game with it&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:58:57-08:00","id":1163593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163579#post1163579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why ban it as a Primary factor? You're answer seems to boil down to: &amp;quot;Because you can't power game with it&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it\u2019s because it has less of an impact than Potency or Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:06:07-08:00","id":1163666,"title":"","content":"But why ban it if it makes sense as being the most important factor of the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:19:09-08:00","id":1163673,"title":"","content":"Would any of the direct applications of Chaos Mastery, such as imposing the Blind Condition, or cursing their next action, require you beat a Withstand score? The spell doesn't list a Withstand, despite citing those as examples of how it can be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:31:39-08:00","id":1163680,"title":"","content":"Is a Demesne a Paradox free zone, even if it isn't appropriate to give a Yantra bonus?<br /> <br /> For instance, would you still be able to cast Life spells with no Paradox in a Stygian Demesne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:36:46-08:00","id":1163682,"title":"","content":"I always understood it that way. Was I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:40:18-08:00","id":1163683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163666#post1163666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why ban it if it makes sense as being the most important factor of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I can\u2019t think of an instance in which it would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:44:01-08:00","id":1163685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163673#post1163673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would any of the direct applications of Chaos Mastery, such as imposing the Blind Condition, or cursing their next action, require you beat a Withstand score? The spell doesn't list a Withstand, despite citing those as examples of how it can be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that yes, it would have to beat Withstand just like any other application of deleterious magic. Many of the Fate spells that can bless or curse specifically mention Withstand only applying to the part that delivers a curse, and I\u2019m not sure why Chaos Mastery failed to mention it.<br /> <br /> On a side note, it\u2019s interesting that it doesn\u2019t have any obviously positive effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:48:53-08:00","id":1163688,"title":"","content":"I assume you could use its 'narrative control' to create positive effects, for example insuring that your own vehicle emerged unscathed from a massive 10 car pile up (while presumably the Seers chasing you are hit by a lorry or some such.) But yeah, it looked a little like it might be a deliberate omission, perhaps intended to make those functions of the spell more appealing than its Fate 2 cousin Exceptional Luck, which can also inflict such conditions. Not that it needs the help, Chaos Mastery is crazy enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:18:32-08:00","id":1163952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163683#post1163683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because I can\u2019t think of an instance in which it would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? You don't think a more powerful protection spell could be a larger protection? It comes up in my game a fair amount where someone would like to protect a place and wishes that Scale could be the Primary factor. I don't buy that there's never an instance where it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:25:32-08:00","id":1163954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163952#post1163952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? You don't think a more powerful protection spell could be a larger protection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as the <i>core fundamental spine of the spell</i>, no. A protection spell that fizzles out early is going to be useless no matter how wide an area it targets. Primary Factor isn't just extra steps on the chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:44:02-08:00","id":1163959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163952#post1163952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? You don't think a more powerful protection spell could be a larger protection? It comes up in my game a fair amount where someone would like to protect a place and wishes that Scale could be the Primary factor. I don't buy that there's never an instance where it makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said. A spell that covers a larger area isn\u2019t more effective at protecting an area unless it has the Duration or Potency factors to improve its chances in a CoW or to give it a higher Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:24:39-08:00","id":1163973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1163952#post1163952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? You don't think a more powerful protection spell could be a larger protection? It comes up in my game a fair amount where someone would like to protect a place and wishes that Scale could be the Primary factor. I don't buy that there's never an instance where it makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How is actually being able to resist an effect (potency) less important than covering a big area? More efficient meta use of casting pool is not the same as more powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T18:28:56-08:00","id":1164128,"title":"","content":"Well consider the Ward spell. I'd much rather have Scale as Primary given that Potency doesn't even matter at all for this spell and Duration is easy to get with Reach.<br /> <br /> What about Co-location on a large area? Or Secret Room? Surely people have to agree that a more powerful Secret Room spell is a larger secret room...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T18:49:10-08:00","id":1164134,"title":"","content":"So, this, a Mind 2 spell, does the following:<br /> <br /> Incognito Presence (Mind \u2022\u2022) Practice: Veiling Primary Factor: Duration Withstand: Resolve Cost: 1 Mana Suggested Rote Skills: Empathy, Stealth, Subterfuge The mage hides the subject\u2019s psychic presence, causing onlookers to ignore her. When people look at her, they want to avert their eyes, or barely notice her. People cannot remember seeing her when they are no longer looking her way. Beings using supernatural abilities to concentrate on her, including Active Mage Sight, provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> What would be the rating of a Spell that didn't just make people &quot;barely notice&quot; someone, or &quot;Ignore them&quot; but not notice them at all. Like, it made it so that the mind wouldn't pick up the data that the eyes were telling them, etc, etc. You've seen it done all the time in fiction, but I was wondering, would a stronger version of something like that be three dots? That'd be my assumption, honestly, but I didn't want to make it something too easy (or too hard) to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T19:35:43-08:00","id":1164151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164134#post1164134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this, a Mind 2 spell, does the following:<br /> <br /> Incognito Presence (Mind \u2022\u2022) Practice: Veiling Primary Factor: Duration Withstand: Resolve Cost: 1 Mana Suggested Rote Skills: Empathy, Stealth, Subterfuge The mage hides the subject\u2019s psychic presence, causing onlookers to ignore her. When people look at her, they want to avert their eyes, or barely notice her. People cannot remember seeing her when they are no longer looking her way. Beings using supernatural abilities to concentrate on her, including Active Mage Sight, provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> What would be the rating of a Spell that didn't just make people &amp;quot;barely notice&amp;quot; someone, or &amp;quot;Ignore them&amp;quot; but not notice them at all. Like, it made it so that the mind wouldn't pick up the data that the eyes were telling them, etc, etc. You've seen it done all the time in fiction, but I was wondering, would a stronger version of something like that be three dots? That'd be my assumption, honestly, but I didn't want to make it something too easy (or too hard) to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Reach or two on Incognito Presence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T20:21:19-08:00","id":1164164,"title":"","content":"Incognito with a Reach I would say.<br /> <br /> Here's a question: What should Steel Windows be from 1e? Likely Weaving like Alter Conductivity is now if you are altering the opaqueness of the matter, but it could also be Veiling to make a wall invisible. What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-01-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T21:06:04-08:00","id":1164171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164128#post1164128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well consider the Ward spell. I'd much rather have Scale as Primary given that Potency doesn't even matter at all for this spell and Duration is easy to get with Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: <i>core fundamental spine of the spell</i>. A no-frills-no-effort Ward that lasts for one turn when cast by a Master of Space without further investment is a shitty Ward by any metric.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about Co-location on a large area? </div> </div> </div>By your own argument, a single Reach is enough to give a spell more Area than a -8 penalty on Standard Scale would, to say nothing of how Potency matters a lot more to a spell whose number of overlapped locations is set by Potency and whose best uses are generally going to require contending with Sympathetic Withstand, even if a spell whose main base effect is limited in how quickly it can be used by an individual wasn't best served by Duration. &quot;Reach is cheap&quot; is not the basis for determining what a spell's Primary Factor is.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or Secret Room? Surely people have to agree that a more powerful Secret Room spell is a larger secret room... </div> </div> </div>One turn of expanded or compressed space whose degree of spell-induced size alteration is set by Potency? Premature termination from Dissonance if any Sleeper happens to do the TARDIS-boggle thing due to Duration not having the insulation of the other features holding it fast? No. Fundamentally useless. Potency Primary would at least let you make your personal space the size of a house, which is less of a niche situation than being able to make a house take up as much space as one of its floors.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T23:15:07-08:00","id":1164186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164164#post1164164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: What should Steel Windows be from 1e? Likely Weaving like Alter Conductivity is now if you are altering the opaqueness of the matter, but it could also be Veiling to make a wall invisible. What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember having homebrewed it in my Legacies thread. I did it as an Unveiling spell that grants its subject the ability to see through objects.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found it in my own files<br /> <b>Steel Windows (Matter \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Science, Subterfuge, Larceny<br /> Even the thickest wall of steel cannot hinder the sight of an alchemist. For the spell's Duration, its subject may see through a solid object within his range of vision as if it were transparent by focusing his sight upon it. If the object is multi-layered, like a matryoshka doll or a building with many walls and rooms, the subject can only see through the outermost layer on his end. Trying to see through layers of particularly intricate objects, as some machines are, may require a Wits + relevant Skill roll. As the spell does not increase its subject's visual field, sufficiently large obstacles such as a mountain may only appear transparent up to a certain point.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject may see through multiple layers, each layer beyond the first requiring a turn of concentration. This still does not allow her to see entirely past huge obstacles beyond his normal sight.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Life \u2022</b>: The spell can be used to see through living creatures, revealing their insides. He may adjust how much he can see through, choosing to examine someone's muscles or analyze her organs. Understanding what he is seeing may require an Intelligence + Medicine roll, while searching for specific organs or tissues may require a Wits + Medicine roll.<br /> <br /> It looks kinda wonky, now that I look at it at the moment. As of now, Potency is quite useless. I should revise my homebrew stuff when I get the time...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 12-01-2017, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T07:56:22-08:00","id":1164267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164134#post1164134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this, a Mind 2 spell, does the following:<br /> <br /> Incognito Presence (Mind \u2022\u2022) Practice: Veiling Primary Factor: Duration Withstand: Resolve Cost: 1 Mana Suggested Rote Skills: Empathy, Stealth, Subterfuge The mage hides the subject\u2019s psychic presence, causing onlookers to ignore her. When people look at her, they want to avert their eyes, or barely notice her. People cannot remember seeing her when they are no longer looking her way. Beings using supernatural abilities to concentrate on her, including Active Mage Sight, provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> What would be the rating of a Spell that didn't just make people &amp;quot;barely notice&amp;quot; someone, or &amp;quot;Ignore them&amp;quot; but not notice them at all. Like, it made it so that the mind wouldn't pick up the data that the eyes were telling them, etc, etc. You've seen it done all the time in fiction, but I was wondering, would a stronger version of something like that be three dots? That'd be my assumption, honestly, but I didn't want to make it something too easy (or too hard) to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you\u2019re doing it, Empty Presence for instance is Death 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:00:37-08:00","id":1164270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164171#post1164171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: <i>core fundamental spine of the spell</i>. A no-frills-no-effort Ward that lasts for one turn when cast by a Master of Space without further investment is a shitty Ward by any metric.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">By your own argument, a single Reach is enough to give a spell more Area than a -8 penalty on Standard Scale would, to say nothing of how Potency matters a lot more to a spell whose number of overlapped locations is set by Potency and whose best uses are generally going to require contending with Sympathetic Withstand, even if a spell whose main base effect is limited in how quickly it can be used by an individual wasn't best served by Duration. &quot;Reach is cheap&quot; is not the basis for determining what a spell's Primary Factor is.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">One turn of expanded or compressed space whose degree of spell-induced size alteration is set by Potency? Premature termination from Dissonance if any Sleeper happens to do the TARDIS-boggle thing due to Duration not having the insulation of the other features holding it fast? No. Fundamentally useless. Potency Primary would at least let you make your personal space the size of a house, which is less of a niche situation than being able to make a house take up as much space as one of its floors.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I suppose if you look at functionality you have a point, but that isn't the criteria in the book which says that it is about what immediately comes to mind as a more powerful version of the spell. To me, a more powerful space expanding spell is one that expands more space, but I suppose it's useless if it only lasts for a turn. I think the criteria should be worded differently, but in the end I agree that Scale is less helpful as Primary than Duration in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:05:28-08:00","id":1164275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164186#post1164186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember having homebrewed it in my Legacies thread. I did it as an Unveiling spell that grants its subject the ability to see through objects.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found it in my own files<br /> <b>Steel Windows (Matter \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Science, Subterfuge, Larceny<br /> Even the thickest wall of steel cannot hinder the sight of an alchemist. For the spell's Duration, its subject may see through a solid object within his range of vision as if it were transparent by focusing his sight upon it. If the object is multi-layered, like a matryoshka doll or a building with many walls and rooms, the subject can only see through the outermost layer on his end. Trying to see through layers of particularly intricate objects, as some machines are, may require a Wits + relevant Skill roll. As the spell does not increase its subject's visual field, sufficiently large obstacles such as a mountain may only appear transparent up to a certain point.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject may see through multiple layers, each layer beyond the first requiring a turn of concentration. This still does not allow her to see entirely past huge obstacles beyond his normal sight.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Life \u2022</b>: The spell can be used to see through living creatures, revealing their insides. He may adjust how much he can see through, choosing to examine someone's muscles or analyze her organs. Understanding what he is seeing may require an Intelligence + Medicine roll, while searching for specific organs or tissues may require a Wits + Medicine roll.<br /> <br /> It looks kinda wonky, now that I look at it at the moment. As of now, Potency is quite useless. I should revise my homebrew stuff when I get the time...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your ideas, but don't you think that Veiling the wall itself is more in keeping with the original spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:18:18-08:00","id":1164282,"title":"","content":"Counterspell: Is the Clash of Wills affected by things like longer duration etc...? It seems weird to me that longer duration spells have Imagos that are harder to disrupt, but according to the rules this seems to be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:32:01-08:00","id":1164285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164282#post1164282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterspell: Is the Clash of Wills affected by things like longer duration etc...? It seems weird to me that longer duration spells have Imagos that are harder to disrupt, but according to the rules this seems to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, reason being they are spells that are literally made to last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T10:33:21-08:00","id":1164318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164285#post1164285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, reason being they are spells that are literally made to last.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it ever say that?<br /> <br /> I personally rule that no, spell factors or reaches do not add bonusses in Counterspell CoWs as you are disrupting the imago itself, not the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T10:52:49-08:00","id":1164324,"title":"","content":"I agree, Counterspelling should be easier than simply overcoming to spell with your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T11:50:00-08:00","id":1164347,"title":"","content":"I always thought the bonus from duration to clashes only applies when a spells effects clash vs a opposite effect but doesnt apply vs counterspell? Counterbeing a clash but not all clashes get the duration bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T12:56:13-08:00","id":1164362,"title":"","content":"It's not how it's written. A common problem with the book, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Counterspell just says: Use the Clash rules. And the Clash rules say that higher advanced duration levels make spells harder to Clash against, and therefore Counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:08:28-08:00","id":1164366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164362#post1164362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not how it's written. A common problem with the book, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Counterspell just says: Use the Clash rules. And the Clash rules say that higher advanced duration levels make spells harder to Clash against, and therefore Counter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the spell doesn't exist yet. You clash with the mage forming the imago (an action that doesn't last longer than an instant I may add). Spellfactors and Reaches such as Advanced Potency do no apply to imagos, they apply to spells. The Imago itself should not get any boni to the Clash roll (just as the Counterspell dicepool does not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:37:33-08:00","id":1164374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164275#post1164275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your ideas, but don't you think that Veiling the wall itself is more in keeping with the original spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably yes. Back then I wasn\u2019t thinking much about keeping my homebrew stuff closer to their original 1e versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:45:05-08:00","id":1164376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164366#post1164366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the spell doesn't exist yet. You clash with the mage forming the imago (an action that doesn't last longer than an instant I may add). Spellfactors and Reaches such as Advanced Potency do no apply to imagos, they apply to spells. The Imago itself should not get any boni to the Clash roll (just as the Counterspell dicepool does not).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it this way: Increased spell factors do represent a stronger spell, yes, but they also mean that the mage puts more effort in the spell\u2019s Imago when they form it. That effort is what gives the dice bonus to Counterspells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T16:30:32-08:00","id":1164420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164366#post1164366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the spell doesn't exist yet. You clash with the mage forming the imago (an action that doesn't last longer than an instant I may add). Spellfactors and Reaches such as Advanced Potency do no apply to imagos, they apply to spells. The Imago itself should not get any boni to the Clash roll (just as the Counterspell dicepool does not).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The spell does not, the Imago does however exist. And it's a more complicated Imago to find a weak point to counter quickly. Like a simple spells imago you could glance over pretty quickly and make a qualified guess in split second where the weak point to attack, eg counter. A stronger and more complex Imago is harder to glance quickly enough to counter with the same ease, and duration on the spells imago greatly increases the complexity of the Imago, therefore finding a weak spot to counter more difficult in the same split second. Ergo the extra dice from longer duration should apply for the CoW in Counterspelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T01:44:23-08:00","id":1164482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164376#post1164376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see it this way: Increased spell factors do represent a stronger spell, yes, but they also mean that the mage puts more effort in the spell\u2019s Imago when they form it. That effort is what gives the dice bonus to Counterspells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that you take dicepenalties for increasing spellfactors, it seems to me that a &quot;stronger&quot; imago is inherently harder to form and keep together.<br /> <br /> In the end there are multiple ways to see this issue and resolve it, none of them wrong or explicitly canon, leaving it kind of up to the ST to decide. Personally it makes more sense to me that Imagos are easier to disrupt than the finished spell, just like a house would be easier to collapse while it is still being built. In addition the other arguments I allready brought up.<br /> <br /> Speaking from a purely meta perspective it also makes sense to give counterspelling this &quot;edge&quot; because counterspelling allready sucks. It's purely reactive. You spend your whole action trying to negate what someone else is doing. So if you succeed you both do nothing and may play the same game again the next turn, if you loose you wasted your entire action. And there is no way for a counterspeller to get bonus dice on his CoW except for spending wp. Being reactive is worse enough of a downside anyway, no need to also make it exceedingly unlikely the counterspell will succeed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T04:02:48-08:00","id":1164497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164482#post1164482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that you take dicepenalties for increasing spellfactors, it seems to me that a &quot;stronger&quot; imago is inherently harder to form and keep together.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ferocious dog on a leash is harder to control, but it's going to be good at threatening other dogs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end there are multiple ways to see this issue and resolve it, none of them wrong or explicitly canon, leaving it kind of up to the ST to decide. Personally it makes more sense to me that Imagos are easier to disrupt than the finished spell, just like a house would be easier to collapse while it is still being built. In addition the other arguments I allready brought up.<br /> <br /> Speaking from a purely meta perspective it also makes sense to give counterspelling this &quot;edge&quot; because counterspelling allready sucks. It's purely reactive. You spend your whole action trying to negate what someone else is doing. So if you succeed you both do nothing and may play the same game again the next turn, if you loose you wasted your entire action. And there is no way for a counterspeller to get bonus dice on his CoW except for spending wp. Being reactive is worse enough of a downside anyway, no need to also make it exceedingly unlikely the counterspell will succeed </div> </div> </div>Fair point there. Then again, I'd argue that stopping a spell from being conjured in the first place itself is a boon enough, since in many cases a spell's effects aren't so easy to undo or act against after it's been cast. (Unless you're good at Prime so you can dispel them, but then you'd be also good at Countering anyway.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T04:46:27-08:00","id":1164506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164497#post1164497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fair point there. Then again, I'd argue that stopping a spell from being conjured in the first place itself is a boon enough, since in many cases a spell's effects aren't so easy to undo or act against after it's been cast. (Unless you're good at Prime so you can dispel them, but then you'd be also good at Countering anyway.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Being good at Prime doesn't make you good at countering, it merely enables you to do it to every spell instead of just your own nieche. And honestly dispelling spells is laughably easy since you don't even need to beat the spell in a CoW, you merely need to overcome the Arcanum rating as a withstand. And withstand is at best a speedbump, never really an unsurmountable obstacle. (Especially if you just pick up Dispellation as a rote or praxis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:30:44-08:00","id":1164637,"title":"","content":"Do spells cast from an imbued item follow the standard rules for spells? IE: time, free reach (determined by item or user?), yantras, factors etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:29:37-08:00","id":1164662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164637#post1164637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do spells cast from an imbued item follow the standard rules for spells? IE: time, free reach (determined by item or user?), yantras, factors etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells cast from a imbued item dont get access to yantras (actually doesnt say either way much like most of the imbued item text) but can use spell factors and there is also no mention of what they use for reach (since sleepers without gnosis can use them i assume they get one free reach like artifacts but that users can over reach freely).<br /> <br /> No access to yantras or extra ritual casting means imbued items have a really low dicepool (esp for sleeper use) and having many spell factors means a terrible casting dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-02-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:40:50-08:00","id":1164665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164662#post1164662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells cast from a imbued item dont get access to yantras (actually doesnt say either way much like most of the imbued item text) but can use spell factors and there is also no mention of what they use for reach (since sleepers without gnosis can use them i assume they get one free reach like artifacts but that users can over reach freely).<br /> <br /> No access to yantras or extra ritual casting means imbued items have a really low dicepool (esp for sleeper use) and having many spell factors means a terrible casting dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? It says you cast the spell but doesn't give exceptions to the standard rules. It says paradox are incured by sleepers as a gnosis 1 mage for over reaching so it seems to be more likely to follow standard rule except you use the item's arcanum rating not your own and you can use it without gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:45:19-08:00","id":1164690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164665#post1164665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure? It says you cast the spell but doesn't give exceptions to the standard rules. It says paradox are incured by sleepers as a gnosis 1 mage for over reaching so it seems to be more likely to follow standard rule except you use the item's arcanum rating not your own and you can use it without gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tbh, nobody is exactly sure (except DaveB). How would a item be able to use high speech, or a mudra on its own exactly. If the intention was that the user can use any yantra's they know while using the imbued item then it isnt mentioned, perhaps it was one of those things that seem obvious. <br /> <br /> The imbued item stuff needs a FAQ and/or Signs and Sigils, till then you are going to have to just wing it. The intention might be that having the imbued item means the user gets access to everything a mage able to cast the spell himself has access too, which brings in yantra's, extra ritual time and stuff, with non mages assumed to have gnosis 1 for number of yantra bonuses..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:47:57-08:00","id":1164692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164506#post1164506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being good at Prime doesn't make you good at countering, it merely enables you to do it to every spell instead of just your own nieche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, that *is* what I meant by better. We really do have different ideas on what constitutes \u2018better\u2019 and \u2018stronger,\u2019 don\u2019t we?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And honestly dispelling spells is laughably easy since you don't even need to beat the spell in a CoW, you merely need to overcome the Arcanum rating as a withstand. And withstand is at best a speedbump, never really an unsurmountable obstacle. (Especially if you just pick up Dispellation as a rote or praxis). </div> </div> </div>That I won\u2019t deny... but honestly, it\u2019s not like every mage invests in Prime. If Counterspell\u2019s all you\u2019ve got, well, better to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T13:54:32-08:00","id":1164882,"title":"","content":"Are &quot;Imperial Mysteries&quot; compatible with the new edition? Is some sourcebook covering Arcana 6+ still planned to be published in some distant future for the second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T14:17:24-08:00","id":1164892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1164882#post1164882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are &amp;quot;Imperial Mysteries&amp;quot; compatible with the new edition? Is some sourcebook covering Arcana 6+ still planned to be published in some distant future for the second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s compatible in terms of the general ideas in IM, but out of date in terms of specific mechanics. I don\u2019t think there\u2019s any plans to add any more books on archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T15:38:06-08:00","id":1164912,"title":"","content":"according to the current projects page:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>: This book covers the physical, tangible expressions of magic: Sacraments, Magical Tools, Grimoires, and more, <b>as well as the creations of archmage</b>s. <i>120 pages. PDF/PoD</i>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T17:46:59-08:00","id":1164933,"title":"","content":"That's specifically going to be archmaster stuff as plot fuel though, rather than focusing on clarifying how archmastery works in 2e. I know Dave has expressed that he wishes to move archmastery back to the realm of plot related stuff for Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:44:51-08:00","id":1165289,"title":"","content":"when first creating a mage character, what books are required to understand the character creation process? the main concept for him is that he's a young wannabe magician that ends up becoming awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:14:42-08:00","id":1165297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165289#post1165289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when first creating a mage character, what books are required to understand the character creation process? the main concept for him is that he's a young wannabe magician that ends up becoming awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need the corebook: Mage the Awakening Fallen World Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-05-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:02:06-08:00","id":1165308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165297#post1165297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You only need the corebook: Mage the Awakening Fallen World Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>like the 2nd edtion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:02:48-08:00","id":1165309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165308#post1165308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">like the 2nd edtion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book by that name is 2e, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:18:36-08:00","id":1165314,"title":"","content":"The book is only named Mage the Awakening Second Edition, and it's the only book needed for playing Mage second edition.<br /> Fallen World Chronicles would be the subtitle if Mage 2e was released before the 2e rebranding. Now it's only referred to in the title of the associated fiction collection The Fallen World Chronicle Anthology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522