 class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165358#post1165358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> does performing spells in front of supernatural beings cause paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, only real Sleepers (regular human beings who are untouched by the supernatural) cause that problem. Anyone with a touch of the supernatural about them (including members of other World of Darkness 'races' like Vampires or there ghouls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:26:20-08:00","id":1165372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165351#post1165351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which arcana and practice though?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends.<br /> <br /> For general purpose misdirection though Veiling at 2 dots in any arcana will have some use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:08:00-08:00","id":1165608,"title":"","content":"Btw, why doesn't Teleportation just Fray the distance like Co-location and be a 3-dot effect instead of 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:41:23-08:00","id":1165619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165608#post1165608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, why doesn't Teleportation just Fray the distance like Co-location and be a 3-dot effect instead of 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>It rewrites your spatial Pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:56:42-08:00","id":1165637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165608#post1165608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, why doesn't Teleportation just Fray the distance like Co-location and be a 3-dot effect instead of 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the lines between Weaving and Patterning are clear, like when you deal with physical things, but with the more abstract stuff it mostly boils down to balance calls. And as to why it doesn't &quot;Fray/Unravel the distance&quot;, it's because distance is a Lie, and Space effects usually just ignore it. The only distance that matters is Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T13:25:19-08:00","id":1165655,"title":"","content":"Co-location frays the distance between two spaces, making them metaphysically adjacent. However in order to get from a to b one still has to move in order to get there, even if it is just a very miniscule effort. Teleportation rewrites the space a thing occupies completly, exchanging it for another, thus making it throughly pattering.<br /> <br /> Fraying can reduce the distance between two points to allmost nothing, but pattering can directly change &quot;here&quot; into &quot;there&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T18:25:37-08:00","id":1165726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165358#post1165358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> does performing spells in front of supernatural beings cause paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, Only <b><u><i>obvious</i></u></b> magic in front of sleepers causes additional paradox. Note that unobious spells that dont suffer paradox when cast may suffer dissonance if obvious when encountered later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T02:52:23-08:00","id":1165800,"title":"","content":"When a Ghost/Spirit/Geotia spends Essence to increase its stats as described on page 254, is this a reflexive or instant action? At the moment i am assuming it takes their action, which makes it a rather less interesting option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T03:45:51-08:00","id":1165808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165800#post1165800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Ghost/Spirit/Geotia spends Essence to increase its stats as described on page 254, is this a reflexive or instant action? At the moment i am assuming it takes their action, which makes it a rather less interesting option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says in the text <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">boosting takes a turn and they can only boost a single Attribute in a turn.</span></span> </div> </div> </div> so yep its a instant action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:27:04-08:00","id":1165845,"title":"","content":"i don't know if this is a simple question but what aspirations and obsessions make sense for a young stage magcians? so far, his obessesion is finding the inner workings of space but it could make sense for it to a aspiration instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:47:38-08:00","id":1165850,"title":"","content":"Are Zombie bites -1 Bashing like human bites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:11:44-08:00","id":1165860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165845#post1165845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't know if this is a simple question but what aspirations and obsessions make sense for a young stage magcians? so far, his obessesion is finding the inner workings of space but it could make sense for it to a aspiration instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspirations and Obsessions are pretty open ended by design. Aspirations will typically be mundane though it can be related to magic. For instance gaining status in the Silver Ladder is a mundane objective with a magical connection. Obsessions are typically magical in nature, like finding the soul stone of Xanaphos the founder of the Legacy of the Cornucopia for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:43:03-08:00","id":1165889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165850#post1165850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Zombie bites -1 Bashing like human bites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weapons/Attacks: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_NormalTable\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_tr\"><td width=\"54\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Type</td> <td width=\"69\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Damage</td> <td width=\"54\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Range</td> <td width=\"85\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Dice Pool</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_tr\"><td width=\"54\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Grapple</td> <td width=\"69\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">0B</td> <td width=\"54\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Melee</td> <td width=\"85\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">7 (in group), 1<br /> (alone)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_tr\"><td width=\"54\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Bite</td> <td width=\"69\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">2L</td> <td width=\"54\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">Melee</td> <td width=\"85\" class=\"text_table_NormalTable_td\">7 (in group), 1<br /> (alone)</td> </tr> </table></div> If you mean The Horde from CofD, that is. That's the only zombies I can think of.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: The damage modifier comes from the Dread Power Natural Weapons \u2022\u2022, meaning they don't have to initiate grappling before biting, and have armor piercing 2 on their bites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T11:38:48-08:00","id":1165904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165889#post1165889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weapons/Attacks: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Type</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Damage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Range</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Dice Pool</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Grapple</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">0B</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">7 (in group), 1<br /> (alone)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Bite</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2L</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">7 (in group), 1<br /> (alone)</td> </tr> </table></div> If you mean The Horde from CofD, that is. That's the only zombies I can think of.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: The damage modifier comes from the Dread Power Natural Weapons \u2022\u2022, meaning they don't have to initiate grappling before biting, and have armor piercing 2 on their bites.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are probably referring to the death arcana created &quot;zombie&quot; or animated corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T12:34:02-08:00","id":1165913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165850#post1165850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Zombie bites -1 Bashing like human bites?</div> </div> </div> </div>If created from human corpses via death magic then yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:14:01-08:00","id":1165920,"title":"","content":"My bad. I've subscribed to all forums I'm interested in so I won't have to individually go through them for updates. That has the side effect of me not paying attention to what forum I might be posting in. Especially when the thread title isn't a context clue or easy to mistake for another like all these simple question threads.<br /> <br /> The only published Death spell to create zombie like creatures is Revenant (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) which, like the name implies, can be used to make revenants. But revenants are just ghosts possessing corpses which brings no physical change to the corpse. The teeth would be the same as for a human; i.e. -1B as stated.<br /> <br /> However, the same spell should be able to let a ghost Claim its own corpse, and WtF has revealed to us that Claimed beings are able to learn Dread Powers such as Natural Weapons. <br /> Unfortunately Claim was consciously omitted from MtA's ephemeral rules so it might be that we're not supposed to be able to apply that Manifestation through Revenant/Bind Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:52:58-08:00","id":1165941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165920#post1165920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only published Death spell to create zombie like creatures is Revenant (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) which, like the name implies, can be used to make revenants. But revenants are just ghosts possessing corpses which brings no physical change to the corpse. The teeth would be the same as for a human; i.e. -1B as stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death 3 also has a zombie-raising spell. Although I can\u2019t remember at hand whether it has a damage-enhancing option. Even if it doesn\u2019t, homebrewing one into it should be trivial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the same spell should be able to let a ghost Claim its own corpse, and WtF has revealed to us that Claimed beings are able to learn Dread Powers such as Natural Weapons. <br /> Unfortunately Claim was consciously omitted from MtA's ephemeral rules so it might be that we're not supposed to be able to apply that Manifestation through Revenant/Bind Spirit. </div> </div> </div>The Possessed Condition (or was it Controlled?) printed in Mage, if I remember, is actually fused with Claimed. Wordcount is the enemy here, it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:20:29-08:00","id":1165945,"title":"","content":"I also think you should be able to make them 0 L with a Perfecting Matter spell to sharpen their teeth, wouldn't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:27:44-08:00","id":1165947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165941#post1165941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death 3 also has a zombie-raising spell. Although I can\u2019t remember at hand whether it has a damage-enhancing option. Even if it doesn\u2019t, homebrewing one into it should be trivial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, fuck me. You're right. The name of the spell is Quicken Corpse and the text actually calls the subject a zombie, but any combat enhancing options only increases the stats of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165941#post1165941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Possessed Condition (or was it Controlled?) printed in Mage, if I remember, is actually fused with Claimed. Wordcount is the enemy here, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>MtA's version of Possessed is the same text as in CofD (only change was a few cut sentences), and since Claim was removed there was no reason to have Controlled since its only purpose was being a prerequisite for Claim. Skimming through the rest of them I think you're mistaken about Claim being fused with another Manifestation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:46:14-08:00","id":1165950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165947#post1165947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MtA's version of Possessed is the same text as in CofD (only change was a few cut sentences), and since Claim was removed there was no reason to have Controlled since its only purpose was being a prerequisite for Claim. Skimming through the rest of them I think you're mistaken about Claim being fused with another Manifestation</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t have the book with me right now. Strange, where could I have gotten that idea from... Regardless, I don\u2019t think the Mage writers intended Claiming to be non-existent in Mage. Just not getting the spotlight this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:29:53-08:00","id":1165981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1165950#post1165950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t have the book with me right now. Strange, where could I have gotten that idea from... Regardless, I don\u2019t think the Mage writers intended Claiming to be non-existent in Mage. Just not getting the spotlight this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of it is that as a specifically Weird Extreme Phenomenon relative to more temporary or gradual manifestations, Claiming is at least not meant to be built into the toolkit of Awakened magic on the &quot;everyone knows how to do it&quot; level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T22:22:19-08:00","id":1166021,"title":"","content":"Just idle speculation, but I wouldn't be surprised to learn that Mages lump Claimed in with Cryptids, or mistake one for the other considering the way Cryptids were portrayed in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T22:26:42-08:00","id":1166022,"title":"","content":"If a Mage uses Time 4 to travel back in time to a point before their Awakening. Will they be able to use magic in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T22:54:51-08:00","id":1166024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1166022#post1166022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Mage uses Time 4 to travel back in time to a point before their Awakening. Will they be able to use magic in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, that would be a use of Time 5 Corridors of Time, but the answer is yes, they'd still be able to use magic. Unless they take steps to ensure that they never Awaken, which is something you could do with Rewrite History which is Time 4, but doesn't include time travel. The effects will only stick if you do use time travel though, so Rewrite History has the potential to wear off either because of Duration lapse or other possible effects that might end the spell. Mages with Time can totally pull off the Time Lord watch though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T05:28:10-08:00","id":1166062,"title":"","content":"is it normal to craft a character throughout a chronicle? i shared a wip character sheet with a few and ended up having someone complain about it being made in a vacuum. how can i avoid this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T07:21:43-08:00","id":1166089,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on your tastes.<br /> <br /> When my groups sit down to make characters I usually get everything done as a group except maybe Nimbus, Praxis and Rotes. Then I allow my players to change their character in small ways throughout the 1st story as long as they don't change the broad strokes of what the character is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T07:34:57-08:00","id":1166278,"title":"","content":"How did Reach on combined spells work again? I do know that Reach on spell factors get shared by the spells, with optional effects having to be bought separately, but the amount of free Reach I get for the combined spell in the first place boggles me.<br /> <br /> Specifically, suppose I have Matter 4 and am combining Find the Balance (Matter 2) and Crucible (Matter 3). The errata says I get one set of free Reach. So do I get +2 Reach by counting the highest-rated spell (Matter 3 Crucible), or +3 Reach for the lowest-rated spell (Matter 2 Find the Balance)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T09:53:41-08:00","id":1166296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1166278#post1166278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did Reach on combined spells work again? I do know that Reach on spell factors get shared by the spells, with optional effects having to be bought separately, but the amount of free Reach I get for the combined spell in the first place boggles me.<br /> <br /> Specifically, suppose I have Matter 4 and am combining Find the Balance (Matter 2) and Crucible (Matter 3). The errata says I get one set of free Reach. So do I get +2 Reach by counting the highest-rated spell (Matter 3 Crucible), or +3 Reach for the lowest-rated spell (Matter 2 Find the Balance)?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Highest-rated Arcanum that meets or exceeds the spell's requirements&quot; combined with the Quick Reference chart's wording of &quot;Highest Arcanum dot used in spell&quot; suggests to me that it's +2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T14:13:06-08:00","id":1166336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1166296#post1166296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Highest-rated Arcanum that meets or exceeds the spell's requirements&amp;quot; combined with the Quick Reference chart's wording of &amp;quot;Highest Arcanum dot used in spell&amp;quot; suggests to me that it's +2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, must have missed that. Much thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T14:28:07-08:00","id":1166339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1166278#post1166278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did Reach on combined spells work again? I do know that Reach on spell factors get shared by the spells, with optional effects having to be bought separately, but the amount of free Reach I get for the combined spell in the first place boggles me.<br /> <br /> Specifically, suppose I have Matter 4 and am combining Find the Balance (Matter 2) and Crucible (Matter 3). The errata says I get one set of free Reach. So do I get +2 Reach by counting the highest-rated spell (Matter 3 Crucible), or +3 Reach for the lowest-rated spell (Matter 2 Find the Balance)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody knows for sure, this was one of the things a FAQ would be good to clear up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T14:39:17-08:00","id":1166341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1166339#post1166339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody knows for sure, this was one of the things a FAQ would be good to clear up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. But for now Satchel\u2019s reading will have to suffice. It also fits with how combined spells are limited and constrained in exchange for benefits; dice pool using the lowest Arcanum, Reach using the highest Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T18:44:44-08:00","id":1168453,"title":"","content":"Command Spirit says: &quot;This spell allows the mage to command a spirit to undertake a number of actions equal to the spell\u2019s Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should this read &quot;This spell allows the mage to issue a number of commands to a spirit equal to the spell\u2019s Potency.&quot; ?<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that an &quot;action&quot; is something like &quot;protect me&quot;, not an actual instant action for one turn in combat. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T18:48:59-08:00","id":1168454,"title":"","content":"The other question I had:<br /> <br /> Is there any reason why you couldn't unsafely relinquish a Command Spirit spell for 1 WP if it only lasts for a scene and you've already given the spirit the one command you planned on giving it? This would save a precious spell control slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T18:51:43-08:00","id":1168455,"title":"","content":"It's the spirit equivalent of Psychic Domination so it can include taking a course of action rather than just a single instant action for the Duration. <br /> <br /> Also, yes, there's no reason you can't spend a WP point to relinquish the spell, spells that are unsafely relinquished only check once a day so spending a WP point to relinquish spells that last 24 hours or less is a pretty common option for Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T19:00:37-08:00","id":1168457,"title":"","content":"Also it doesn't seem like there's a 1 WP per turn limit in Chronicles of Darkness like there was in WoD 2.0. Is this right? It only states 1 WP limit &quot;per action&quot;.<br /> <br /> So you could theoretically spend 1 WP to ignore the Stun Tilt and another to negate the -3 penalty on your next action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T20:30:08-08:00","id":1168469,"title":"","content":"You can only spend WP once per turn as far as I'm aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T20:43:58-08:00","id":1168470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168457#post1168457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it doesn't seem like there's a 1 WP per turn limit in Chronicles of Darkness like there was in WoD 2.0. Is this right? It only states 1 WP limit &quot;per action&quot;.<br /> <br /> So you could theoretically spend 1 WP to ignore the Stun Tilt and another to negate the -3 penalty on your next action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. I'd say losing two points out of a resource that caps at ten points to be able to immediately act normally is within spec for a stun effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T02:08:36-08:00","id":1168493,"title":"","content":"WP only caps for ephemerals nowadays. So the practical cap becomes the higher of 10 or double the Supernatural Tolerance trait. Except for Mind mages that are limited by the amount of Potency they can get on Augment Mind since it's only one Reach to increase beyond the trait maximums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T03:28:59-08:00","id":1168496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168493#post1168493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WP only caps for ephemerals nowadays. So the practical cap becomes the higher of 10 or double the Supernatural Tolerance trait. Except for Mind mages that are limited by the amount of Potency they can get on Augment Mind since it's only one Reach to increase beyond the trait maximums.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The chrod core book under dots says willpower is 1-10 does this get ignored or confirmed in other book/post?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Most traits range from 1 to 5 dots, but some (such as Willpower) range from 1 to 10, and others (Health) can go higher.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Under RAW it is 1 willpower per action so you could spend 1 on a reflexive action and other on a normal action. Though it mentions once per turn for spending willpower on rolls or resistance increasing, i assume this is just to clarify that you cant spend 2 willpower to get +6 to rolls or +4 to resistance. Is spending willpower to increase a diceroll or resistance a reflexive action...ill have to check.<br /> <br /> Its also telling that willpower only has 10 dots/boxes on the char sheet, even in mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-18-2017, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T04:45:22-08:00","id":1168502,"title":"","content":"Yeesh. It's defined in the fucking lexicon? I don't think any of the other 2e core books contains that passage since they have splat specific lexicons.<br /> It reminds me of the other day when I read through the VtR core book and couldn't for the life of me find any explicit limits of Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T09:45:14-08:00","id":1168543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168502#post1168502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeesh. It's defined in the fucking lexicon? I don't think any of the other 2e core books contains that passage since they have splat specific lexicons.<br /> It reminds me of the other day when I read through the VtR core book and couldn't for the life of me find any explicit limits of Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral entities have text that says willpower cap is 10 this is because they can have stats that would normally allow more than 10, I see no reason that it's a simple oversight that the same text wasn't also given for any other splats capable of getting a potential willpower over 10. <br /> <br /> Unless there is some reason that caps just ephemeral things and not other.<br /> <br /> Just saying there's no concrete proof that willpower is or isn't capped at 10 for anybody else <br /> since the lack of a ruling doesn't make one exist either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T09:50:56-08:00","id":1168545,"title":"","content":"The editing in these books is terrible. That's why we're on post #4295 though. LOL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T10:52:24-08:00","id":1168561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168545#post1168545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The editing in these books is terrible. That's why we're on post #4295 though. LOL</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I\u2019m sure you\u2019d have done a much better job of managing to pack an answer to every question that can be thought of into the book if you\u2019d been in charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T11:17:26-08:00","id":1168569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168493#post1168493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WP only caps for ephemerals nowadays. So the practical cap becomes the higher of 10 or double the Supernatural Tolerance trait. Except for Mind mages that are limited by the amount of Potency they can get on Augment Mind since it's only one Reach to increase beyond the trait maximums.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has next to zero impact on the fact that the vast majority of characters aren't going to recoup two points of Willpower in a span of time that makes ending a turn-sapping Tilt early without drawbacks a trivial expenditure.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you've invested an absurd amount of resources into being probably one of the strongest player character monsters in your locality then you might have a Willpower capacity equal to the Mana Capacity of a non-starting character&quot; literally never undoes the problem of only having so much Willpower to spend and only being able to recover it so quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T11:48:27-08:00","id":1168579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168502#post1168502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeesh. It's defined in the fucking lexicon? I don't think any of the other 2e core books contains that passage since they have splat specific lexicons.<br /> It reminds me of the other day when I read through the VtR core book and couldn't for the life of me find any explicit limits of Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The action aspect of it is defined across the board. The limitation is something that isn't as likely to come up. There hasn't been that much in regards to specific rules for high level entities (breaking the Power Attribute past 5) and what it means. There should be, but it's understandable not to get much into that in a corebook which will likely focus on characters never getting past 5 dots in Attributes and Skills beyond arguments on the forum.<br /> <br /> Incidentally. On p155, 'Coils, like Disciplines, are on a ladder from one to five dots.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-18-2017, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:24:49-08:00","id":1168592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168561#post1168561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I\u2019m sure you\u2019d have done a much better job of managing to pack an answer to every question that can be thought of into the book if you\u2019d been in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's less questions about D&amp;D 5e and there are 3 core books and over a million players. LOL<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they could afford better editing, just that it's bad, because it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:29:25-08:00","id":1168599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168592#post1168592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's less questions about D&amp;D 5e and there are 3 core books and over a million players. LOL</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a factually false statement which inclines me to believe you have no idea what you\u2019re talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-18-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:34:51-08:00","id":1168601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168592#post1168592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's less questions about D&amp;D 5e and there are 3 core books and over a million players. LOL</div> </div> </div> </div>They shut down their forum a year after publication so there isn't a centralized location for questions to be asked, but they do have a constantly-updated 'Sage Advice' book that collects answers for some FAQs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying they could afford better editing, just that it's bad, because it is. </div> </div> </div>Every question you ask seems solely so you can fixate on an error or perceived flaw and LOL at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T13:20:46-08:00","id":1168618,"title":"","content":"Not really. I love the game. I love what Dave brought (and brings) to the game. I love 2e. I hate how poorly edited it is. It's clearly a money issue.<br /> <br /> I'll try to let it go, as I seem to be annoying some people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T14:20:11-08:00","id":1168636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168618#post1168618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. I love the game. I love what Dave brought (and brings) to the game. I love 2e. I hate how poorly edited it is. It's clearly a money issue.<br /> <br /> I'll try to let it go, as I seem to be annoying some people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It might help you to remember that there\u2019s no such thing as a perfectly edited game regardless of money spent. There\u2019s also no such thing as a game that answers every possible question someone might have about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T22:15:34-08:00","id":1168720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168636#post1168636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might help you to remember that there\u2019s no such thing as a perfectly edited game regardless of money spent. There\u2019s also no such thing as a game that answers every possible question someone might have about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> However there is usually such as thing as a FAQ that can answer questions and clear things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:06:42-08:00","id":1168757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168720#post1168720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However there is usually such as thing as a FAQ that can answer questions and clear things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still wouldn\u2019t answer every question, and most questions derive from not thoroughly reading the text in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:15:56-08:00","id":1168773,"title":"","content":"Yet it would answer many questions that are dubiously explained, or not even explained at all. Besides, nothing wrong with making things clearer even if it's just the reader who's misunderstood something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T07:46:46-08:00","id":1168794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1168773#post1168773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet it would answer many questions that are dubiously explained, or not even explained at all. Besides, nothing wrong with making things clearer even if it's just the reader who's misunderstood something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it can\u2019t hurt, but I think there are some unrealistic expectations for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T01:33:55-08:00","id":1170628,"title":"","content":"How obvious is &quot;obvious&quot; when doing magic in front of Sleepers, and does context matter? Or, to put it differently, how much real magic could a stage magician get away with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T04:44:22-08:00","id":1170651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1170628#post1170628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How obvious is &amp;quot;obvious&amp;quot; when doing magic in front of Sleepers, and does context matter? Or, to put it differently, how much real magic could a stage magician get away with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T08:32:58-08:00","id":1170686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1170628#post1170628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How obvious is &quot;obvious&quot; when doing magic in front of Sleepers, and does context matter? Or, to put it differently, how much real magic could a stage magician get away with?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is obvious stage magic and then theres obvious supernal magic. You could teleport your assistant hidden behind a curtain and folk would consider that just stage magic but if you did it right in front of people without a curtain then its obvious its supernal.<br /> <br /> I think its probably as very thin line to start walking, you only need one person to properly doubt your stage magic and paradox comes a calling. Whats obvious magic may differ depending on the context and person so its probably quite risky. Even in a crown of a hundred, one doubter could give you that paradox dice instead of the 8 again paradox dice you'd get if all 100 people were doubters?<br /> <br /> Im not really sure how it works, do all sleepers need to think its obvious or only afew in a group? What sort of stage magic are you thinking supernal magic could cover? Mind could easily pull of psychic type acts etc..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T09:37:01-08:00","id":1170706,"title":"","content":"Maybe if another stage magician or any one acquainted with the &quot;craft&quot; were in the audience I'd made them roll to notice that none of the usual tricks would work and what he saw was the real deal, and thus create Paradox. Otherwise, I think you would be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T09:40:40-08:00","id":1170709,"title":"","content":"I suggest Manipulation + Expression and similar rolls (with appropriate modifiers depending on the size of the crowd, improbability of the act, and tools of distraction) to avoid Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T11:34:34-08:00","id":1171003,"title":"","content":"This is an awesome question, as one of my players just made a stage magician character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:14:23-08:00","id":1171588,"title":"","content":"Postcognition: Do you think it's a valid Time 1 Knowing spell to ask &quot;When precisely did this subject's Temporal Sympathy change?<br /> <br /> For instance, the car was parked on the street and you want to know what time it left so that you can Postcog to see it leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:52:25-08:00","id":1171600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1171588#post1171588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Postcognition: Do you think it's a valid Time 1 Knowing spell to ask &amp;quot;When precisely did this subject's Temporal Sympathy change?<br /> <br /> For instance, the car was parked on the street and you want to know what time it left so that you can Postcog to see it leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is yes to the question, no to the example as the car isn\u2019t there to be cast upon. <br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, the presence of a car on a street is likely insignificant enough to the street that the car arriving and leaving is likely in its Unchanged Past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:59:44-08:00","id":1171605,"title":"","content":"Ok. But I meant casting with the street as the subject really.<br /> <br /> If the car leaving is insignificant then how would you cast the spell to find out when the car left?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T18:43:35-08:00","id":1171689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1171605#post1171605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. But I meant casting with the street as the subject really.<br /> <br /> If the car leaving is insignificant then how would you cast the spell to find out when the car left?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'd need to watch the street via postcognition and have enough duration to see the car leave? For a knowing spell spell if your targeting the streets sympathy and asking &quot;when did X car leave&quot; the likely reply/answer vis knowing is &quot;Didnt notice&quot; as cars entering/leaving dont change its temporal sympathy.<br /> <br /> But yes, you should be able to just know when a car left by being at the location the car was at, however trying to gain knowledge via magic and asking when a car left you might get given the answer when all cars left that spot back to the sympathy changed? You'd need to maybe narrow down the time and if you are doing that anyway its easier just to postcog it anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-29-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T21:15:42-08:00","id":1171722,"title":"","content":"Not asking whether it's a good idea, or whether it'd be something a PC would ever meet.<br /> <br /> But if Ghost Mages exist? In theory could a Ghost Archmage or something freaky like that exist? I mean, obviously if it existed it'd be bad news.<br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, I'm speaking in a metaphysical sense, not in some, &quot;Is it balanced/sane&quot; sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T21:25:31-08:00","id":1171725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1171722#post1171722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not asking whether it's a good idea, or whether it'd be something a PC would ever meet.<br /> <br /> But if Ghost Mages exist? In theory could a Ghost Archmage or something freaky like that exist? I mean, obviously if it existed it'd be bad news.<br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, I'm speaking in a metaphysical sense, not in some, &quot;Is it balanced/sane&quot; sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that could exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T10:09:46-08:00","id":1172021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1171722#post1171722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not asking whether it's a good idea, or whether it'd be something a PC would ever meet.<br /> <br /> But if Ghost Mages exist? In theory could a Ghost Archmage or something freaky like that exist? I mean, obviously if it existed it'd be bad news.<br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, I'm speaking in a metaphysical sense, not in some, &quot;Is it balanced/sane&quot; sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's tricky. The Archmage would have to: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Die</li> <li>Have unfinished business</li> <li>Not be utterly annihilated without a trace</li> </ol><br /> While 2) is completely trivial, iirc Archmasters have pretty good protection from 1), and any entity capable of 1) is likely to prevent 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T10:23:44-08:00","id":1172024,"title":"","content":"When I ran an Imperial Mysteries game, one of my players wanted to be a ghost archmage. I vetoed on the logic that being a ghost is an anchored and lessened state that didn't really make sense for Crossing the Threshold. Having said that, I could see a Death Archmage voluntarily becoming a ghost lich and using imperial magic to evade the downsides, or maybe even pursuing some secret ritual to become a ghost as part of becoming an archmaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:49:07-08:00","id":1172076,"title":"","content":"If I have the Informed Condition on a subject would it be more worthwhile to resolve it in order to answer a specific question, or to save it and ask specific questions using Divination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T19:15:09-08:00","id":1172129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172076#post1172076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have the Informed Condition on a subject would it be more worthwhile to resolve it in order to answer a specific question, or to save it and ask specific questions using Divination?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you got Informed from a source that allows it to provide a Beat, that spending the Condition first is probably best, since it also helps avoid Condition pile-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T19:31:42-08:00","id":1172131,"title":"","content":"What are some things that would normally be considered morally good that would still typically be considered Acts of Hubris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T21:14:40-08:00","id":1172165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172131#post1172131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some things that would normally be considered morally good that would still typically be considered Acts of Hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom is not morality, but rather more about &quot;ends justify the means&quot; and losing control of yourself (with magic or otherwise). So of course it is possible to have something that serves the &quot;Greater Good&quot; that is also an Act of Hubris. Murdering the Seer oppressing Sleepers might serve the greater good, but it's still an Act of Hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:12:39-08:00","id":1172178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172129#post1172129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you got Informed from a source that allows it to provide a Beat, that spending the Condition first is probably best, since it also helps avoid Condition pile-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if it doesn't allow a Beat because it's from an attainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:13:21-08:00","id":1172179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172165#post1172165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wisdom is not morality, but rather more about &quot;ends justify the means&quot; and losing control of yourself (with magic or otherwise). So of course it is possible to have something that serves the &quot;Greater Good&quot; that is also an Act of Hubris. Murdering the Seer oppressing Sleepers might serve the greater good, but it's still an Act of Hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I hear people say that it isn't morality, which is why I'm asking to see if there are things that are morally good that would be considered acts of hubris. And I'm not talking about obviously evil acts done for 'The Greater Good'. I'm talking about acts that would be considered morally good that would also be unWise. So far, the only real things that are considered to go against Wisdom are things that are considered morally wrong, I figure there has to be <i>something</i> that is considered a good thing to do morally that also goes against Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-01-2018, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:19:51-08:00","id":1172180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172179#post1172179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I hear people say that it isn't morality, which is why I'm asking to see if there are things that are morally good that would be considered acts of hubris. And I'm not talking about obviously evil acts done for 'The Greater Good'. I'm talking about acts that would be considered morally good that would also be unWise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Binding a powerful and dangerous spirit to seal it away comes to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:34:26-08:00","id":1172188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172180#post1172180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Binding a powerful and dangerous spirit to seal it away comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good start. Is there any situation in which something like healing would be an act of hubris barring the risk of exposing magic/triggering Dissonance? Stopping someone from dying maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T00:09:22-08:00","id":1172206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172188#post1172188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good start. Is there any situation in which something like healing would be an act of hubris barring the risk of exposing magic/triggering Dissonance? Stopping someone from dying maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>'When innocent bystanders are affected by your character\u2019s spells or actions, she is at risk as well.' Is under High Wisdom. Altering a sapient being's nature long-term is under Medium.<br /> <br /> The Act of Hubris section is less than a page long they aren't exactly hiding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T01:00:38-08:00","id":1172210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172206#post1172206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'When innocent bystanders are affected by your character\u2019s spells or actions, she is at risk as well.' Is under High Wisdom. Altering a sapient being's nature long-term is under Medium.<br /> <br /> The Act of Hubris section is less than a page long they aren't exactly hiding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I really need to be more specific here. I was talking more mid range and lower when it comes to Wisdom, where 99% of characters are going to fall. I'm looking for ideas for non-immoral acts (that don't outright rely on negligence) that might count as acts of hubris and situations to see them applied that would commonly affect more than a small subset of PCs. Sealing dangerous entities was a pretty good example, though I'm looking for more like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-01-2018, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T01:45:15-08:00","id":1172212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172210#post1172210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I really need to be more specific here. I was talking more mid range and lower when it comes to Wisdom, where 99% of characters are going to fall. I'm looking for ideas for non-immoral acts (that don't outright rely on negligence) that might count as acts of hubris and situations to see them applied that would commonly affect more than a small subset of PCs. Sealing dangerous entities was a pretty good example, though I'm looking for more like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Posting the relevant section for my point. You got me as my sleeping pills kicked in and I'm feeling chatty.<br /> <br /> This is the last section under Medium/Understanding Wisdom, ranging from 7-4. 'Forcing a sapient being (whether a Sleeper, spirit, or anything else) to act counter to its interests, altering its nature long-term, or binding it to a task all risk degeneration, as does deliberate and premeditated murder and violence that leaves its victim with long-term injury.'<br /> <br /> Long term injury. If you go around removing peoples limbs in such a way that they will have to deal with it long-term. In werewolf we have a fetish that lets you lop off a limb, bam. Spend Essence or Negotiate to Activate it. Hit someone, bam, they've lost an arm or a leg. So some mage decides he likes that, and he makes his own item that does it. It just chops off peoples legs, maybe from a distance, he doesn't even have to hit them and their legs just plop off. Sooner or later, you'll get to Wisdom 3. I think it's sort of fair, that's not the kind of action an 'understanding' person might take. I'm building up, we can probably agree that's not the 'non-immoral act' you were looking for.<br /> <br /> But it also says 'altering its nature long-term.' So finding Matt Murdock, the young child from the news who was publicly blinded by a toxic waste spill, and healing his eyes, would be an Act of Hubris. For some reason I want to trot out the depressives, and alcoholics and other people with addiction. You go over there to them, find the addicts, maybe hit them at a methadone clinic or something, but you cast a spell, and bam, their Addiction Condition is gone. You tie it off, give it an indefinite duration, and these people are free to live their lives without this deadly urge. They can go out and change everything because you've magically erased their addiction. This is a good deed, if Superman could do it he could. I grant, not every character is going to be out there blasting the fallen world's problems away, but any mage who has a loved one would probably try it. Just like they might try to cure addicts of heroin, or Vitae. These two acts, healing the sick and wounded to the point of changing their nature, and lopping off legs. They'll take you to the same place.<br /> <br /> Then you don't even scroll down because it's in the next paragraph and you see that Low Wisdom is in a special place. Medium is where most PCs would end up providing they're playing the game as portrayed and aren't being goaded too much. At Wisdom 1-3, 'A mage at this precipice could be lost to his magic at any time. Only the darkest, most selfishly destructive acts risk degeneration at this point.' The specific acts? Killing someone in a fit of rage (but what if they're a monster?), destroying an Awakened soul (again, monster), allowing a Supernal being to be consumed by the Fallen World (supernal entities aren't exactly nice, though I think this is more oriented towards ones you've summoned) , or dealing with the Abyss (Theumiel has a good intention).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-01-2018, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T04:45:39-08:00","id":1172228,"title":"","content":"Reprogramming a serial killer to be a functional member of society would be one. Healing a long-term disability. As Satchel mentioned, binding a Spirit or some other entity to seal it away. All of these are under Medium.<br /> <br /> For Low, the only thing that immediately jumps to mind is dealing with the Abyss so you can accomplish something 'good' but 'impossible'. The Abyss is the realm of impossibility, not evil, so there are certainly things there that could help you accomplish a great good while simultaneously eating away at Fallen reality. Nofather's example of killing a monster in a fit of rage is another good example, same with destroying an Awakened Soul (this is actually an official punishment for the worst of the worst in some Consiliums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T08:33:52-08:00","id":1172269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172212#post1172212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it also says 'altering its nature long-term.' So finding Matt Murdock, the young child from the news who was publicly blinded by a toxic waste spill, and healing his eyes, would be an Act of Hubris. For some reason I want to trot out the depressives, and alcoholics and other people with addiction. You go over there to them, find the addicts, maybe hit them at a methadone clinic or something, but you cast a spell, and bam, their Addiction Condition is gone. You tie it off, give it an indefinite duration, and these people are free to live their lives without this deadly urge. They can go out and change everything because you've magically erased their addiction. This is a good deed, if Superman could do it he could. I grant, not every character is going to be out there blasting the fallen world's problems away, but any mage who has a loved one would probably try it. Just like they might try to cure addicts of heroin, or Vitae. These two acts, healing the sick and wounded to the point of changing their nature, and lopping off legs. They'll take you to the same place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now <i>this</i> is the sort of thing I'm looking for. Killing things in a rage and destroying souls is something that's going to <i>at best </i>fall into the necessary evil category imo, but curing addictions, restoring sight/limbs and what not, that's what I'm trying to find more of. Initially I'd lumped letting a Supernal Entity be consumed by the Fallen World as being something deliberately immoral or at best recklessly negligent, though you do bring up a fine point that they aren't necessarily going to be nice, or doing good things. I'm not sure whether I'd still consider it a necessary evil at that point or not but it at least makes me consider other possibilities so I'll run with it. Alas, I don't know who/what Theumiel is to make any judgments based on whether dealing with him would count in this situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172228#post1172228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reprogramming a serial killer to be a functional member of society would be one. Healing a long-term disability. As Satchel mentioned, binding a Spirit or some other entity to seal it away. All of these are under Medium.<br /> <br /> For Low, the only thing that immediately jumps to mind is dealing with the Abyss so you can accomplish something 'good' but 'impossible'. The Abyss is the realm of impossibility, not evil, so there are certainly things there that could help you accomplish a great good while simultaneously eating away at Fallen reality. Nofather's example of killing a monster in a fit of rage is another good example, same with destroying an Awakened Soul (this is actually an official punishment for the worst of the worst in some Consiliums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reprogramming, again, even when doing it for the greater good, is still pretty morally dubious. You're stripping them of their free will and permanently changing them into essentially a different person. That said, it does now make me consider how Reprogramming a serial killer who <i>wants</i> to change for the better might <i>still</i> be an act of hubris. Is it still an act of hubris if you have their full informed consent? <br /> <br /> Also, does anyone else not find it strange that destroying a persons soul is the punishment that mage society falls back on as a final punishment? It seems wholly unnecessary except in extremely specific cases in which it might matter. I mean I remember reading that that's what they do but I've yet to figure out a reason <i>why</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:05:12-08:00","id":1172294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172269#post1172269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it does now make me consider how Reprogramming a serial killer who <i>wants</i> to change for the better might <i>still</i> be an act of hubris. Is it still an act of hubris if you have their full informed consent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say so - you're still altering their nature long-term. It's healing of the mind, compared to healing someone's body by regenerating eyes that have been defective since birth. In both cases, you're changing something fundamental about the person with magic, and even if they want you to, the AoH as-written doesn't make any allowances for consent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:08:06-08:00","id":1172539,"title":"","content":"Can you make a spell that looks for the nearest example of something, or does it have to be something located within the Area of Effect?<br /> <br /> Like a compass that points towards the nearest Verge, even if it's miles away. But not an actual compass which works off of an omnipresent magnetic field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:54:24-08:00","id":1172549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172539#post1172539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you make a spell that looks for the nearest example of something, or does it have to be something located within the Area of Effect?<br /> <br /> Like a compass that points towards the nearest Verge, even if it's miles away. But not an actual compass which works off of an omnipresent magnetic field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds abit like the locate object spell changed to locate X. Locate object allows you to continue tracking something outside the initial area of effect. (not quite sure how, it must have something to do with a sympathetic connection though as that is the only way to cast on things outside of a spells range ie the area spells gives the object a medium connection cos its detected by one of your spells and can track that or sommat)<br /> <br /> So it seems its possible to track something outside of a initial area effect but i would say its using sympathy ties, so unless you have a sypathetic connection to something then no. however if locate object being able to track things that leave an area is different then that would imply yes but without sympathetic stuff i have no idea how it tracks something. I mean you need a sympathy connection to scry/find/loot at something, why would tracking something be any different and not require that sympathy if its outside a spells range?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:58:10-08:00","id":1172550,"title":"","content":"Ah, Space, of course. Thanks.<br /> <br /> If you didn't have Space you could just put a 'sense whatever' spell on large AoE and wander around until it pinged near you, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T23:01:14-08:00","id":1172551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172550#post1172550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, Space, of course. Thanks.<br /> <br /> If you didn't have Space you could just put a 'sense whatever' spell on large AoE and wander around until it pinged near you, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. (characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T02:26:49-08:00","id":1172580,"title":"","content":"Although AoE spells aren't centered around yourself and keeps moving about when you move about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T02:42:50-08:00","id":1172581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172580#post1172580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although AoE spells aren't centered around yourself and keeps moving about when you move about</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that conversation has been had once already, but I don\u2019t remember that you can\u2019t do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T03:12:21-08:00","id":1172584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172581#post1172581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that conversation has been had once already, but I don\u2019t remember that you can\u2019t do that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well considering that the spell factor Scale ; Area of Effect, targets an area and not a particular subject with the spell but all subjects (of a particular kind) within the area, I'd say it's pretty clear it's not supposed to work like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T04:12:41-08:00","id":1172601,"title":"","content":"AOE spells are stuck on the point that you specify, right? They don't follow you around as you move. The best you could do is argue for the &quot;Gnosis-based ticking over time&quot; rules, where any effect that is meant to be instantaneous periodically fires at an interval based on your Gnosis when you give it a longer Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T04:36:13-08:00","id":1172604,"title":"","content":"Nothing says that the point specified can't itself be mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T04:53:11-08:00","id":1172608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172584#post1172584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well considering that the spell factor Scale ; Area of Effect, targets an area and not a particular subject with the spell but all subjects (of a particular kind) within the area, I'd say it's pretty clear it's not supposed to work like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren\u2019t targeting an individual, you\u2019re targeting an area around an individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T05:19:09-08:00","id":1172610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172608#post1172608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You aren\u2019t targeting an individual, you\u2019re targeting an area around an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are targeting a area that happens to have that individual you want to effect in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T05:21:38-08:00","id":1172611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172551#post1172551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yep. (characters)</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh seems i misunderstood what he was asking. I thought me meant you can cast a Area spell and then walk around inside it to find the thing..<br /> <br /> So yeh the area wont move around with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T06:49:54-08:00","id":1172627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172604#post1172604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says that the point specified can't itself be mobile.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Frames of reference are fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:00:26-08:00","id":1172629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172604#post1172604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says that the point specified can't itself be mobile.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. If you cast an AOE spell while on a moving train, for example, I would say that the AOE stays relative to the train. Of course this might motivate &quot;clever&quot; players who know a tiny too much about physics to abuse this. But usually I deny too-crazy things, just to keep balance in check.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:11:13-08:00","id":1172630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172629#post1172629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. If you cast an AOE spell while on a moving train, for example, I would say that the AOE stays relative to the train. Of course this might motivate &quot;clever&quot; players who know a tiny too much about physics to abuse this. But usually I deny too-crazy things, just to keep balance in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience &quot;clever&quot; players who know enough physics and try to use that knowledge to abuse magic end up feeling sad when you explain magic != physics.<br /> <br /> As long as the area is can be defined easily then moving areas are fine. Inside cars, vans, trains, boxes etc all fine and you can move the thing and still be able to say X is in the area inside Y.<br /> <br /> So you can target the area inside something or you can target the area something is in. The former means stuff inside the car and if the car moves off the spell continues to be inside the car, the latter is the space the car occupies (and anything inside it) but if the car moves away it leaves the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:15:34-08:00","id":1172632,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd split the difference and say that an AoE imago relies on something that you can conceptualise as an &quot;area&quot; but the AoE of aimed spells centre on whatever the spell hit and if that's a person they can drag it around with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:29:38-08:00","id":1172633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172632#post1172632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd split the difference and say that an AoE imago relies on something that you can conceptualise as an &quot;area&quot; but the AoE of aimed spells centre on whatever the spell hit and if that's a person they can drag it around with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>People being able to walk about with an area ban spell will cause all sorts of headaches/trouble. I dont think mobile non-contained area spells are supposed to work like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:34:30-08:00","id":1172635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172608#post1172608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You aren\u2019t targeting an individual, you\u2019re targeting an area around an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that was what I said. Excuse any confusion. <br /> <br /> Edit: or maybe not. Probably not. You're meaning it in a literal sense whereas I mean the area itself is the subject.<br /> So sorry for adding yet more confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 01-02-2018, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T07:55:26-08:00","id":1172639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172633#post1172633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People being able to walk about with an area ban spell will cause all sorts of headaches/trouble. I dont think mobile non-contained area spells are supposed to work like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how it\u2019s a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T08:33:49-08:00","id":1172645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1172630#post1172630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience &quot;clever&quot; players who know enough physics and try to use that knowledge to abuse magic end up feeling sad when you explain magic != physics.<br /> <br /> As long as the area is can be defined easily then moving areas are fine. Inside cars, vans, trains, boxes etc all fine and you can move the thing and still be able to say X is in the area inside Y.<br /> <br /> So you can target the area inside something or you can target the area something is in. The former means stuff inside the car and if the car moves off the spell continues to be inside the car, the latter is the space the car occupies (and anything inside it) but if the car moves away it leaves the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a pretty consistent way to apply the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T08:41:26-08:00","id":1172648,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s just one way to rule it though, the game doesn\u2019t preclude the idea of a mobile AoE effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T08:55:58-08:00","id":1172653,"title":"","content":"I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>. I get that opinions might differ, and mine is firmly in the mobile AoE camp. I think it's simply more fun, despite any headaches it might cause in fringe cases. It's Mage, after all.<br /> But the most important part is being consistent during play, however you prefer to run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T07:17:28-08:00","id":1173209,"title":"","content":"Can a mage cast a spell which grants Withstand against directly damaging magical effects which are not coming from awakened magic? The shielding effects from Forces, Mind, and Fate explicitly allow for this, while Wards and Signs talks only about &quot;spells.&quot; Is it intentional?<br /> <br /> It seems that protection against directly harmful magical effects is Prime's purview, and I would be inclined to houserule Wards and Signs to work against any kind of direct damage supernatural effects. What would you say about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T07:41:25-08:00","id":1173214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173209#post1173209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage cast a spell which grants Withstand against directly damaging magical effects which are not coming from awakened magic? The shielding effects from Forces, Mind, and Fate explicitly allow for this, while Wards and Signs talks only about &quot;spells.&quot; Is it intentional?<br /> <br /> It seems that protection against directly harmful magical effects is Prime's purview, and I would be inclined to houserule Wards and Signs to work against any kind of direct damage supernatural effects. What would you say about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The shielding effects from Forces, Mind, and Fate attempt to exert immunity, not Withstanding, to effects within the purview of those Arcana. I'm not familiar with mechanics that apply Withstand to non-spell effects (Withstand is pretty beefy, arguably moreso than forcing a Clash of Wills), and the purview of Prime doesn't include all supernatural phenomena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T07:48:46-08:00","id":1173215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173209#post1173209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage cast a spell which grants Withstand against directly damaging magical effects which are not coming from awakened magic? The shielding effects from Forces, Mind, and Fate explicitly allow for this, while Wards and Signs talks only about &quot;spells.&quot; Is it intentional?<br /> <br /> It seems that protection against directly harmful magical effects is Prime's purview, and I would be inclined to houserule Wards and Signs to work against any kind of direct damage supernatural effects. What would you say about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effects that don\u2019t stem from Awakened magic don\u2019t use or worry about Withstand. If a Demon uses a time manipulation effect against you then having a higher Withstand won\u2019t help you. You\u2019ll be better served having some form of protection that invokes a CoW. In the specific example of a Demon with a time manipulation effect you would need to use some form of Time Shielding. Prime doesn\u2019t typically directly affect the powers of other entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T07:53:04-08:00","id":1173217,"title":"","content":"My mistake. It's indeed the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> So my question would now be: would you allow for spells granting the Clash of Wills against directly harming magic effects with no clear &quot;damage source&quot;?<br /> <br /> Specifically, I was thinking about Changeling Summer Court power which essentially allows to cause damage by ranting someone. It doesn't seem to fit clearly into any of Arcana's purviews What kind of protection would you allow against such an effect? Or is it just plainly bettter than attacking someone with, e.g., supernatural fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-04-2018, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:15:58-08:00","id":1173221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173217#post1173217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mistake. It's indeed the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> So my question would now be: would you allow for spells granting the Clash of Wills against directly harming magic effects with no clear &quot;damage source&quot;?<br /> <br /> Specifically, I was thinking about Changeling Summer Court power which essentially allows to cause damage by ranting someone. It doesn't seem to fit clearly into any of Arcana's purviews What kind of protection would you allow against such an effect? Or is it just plainly bettter than attacking someone with, e.g., supernatural fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>How does the fluff characterize it? That should be a good clue. Going by what little I know of Changeling it could be protected against by Fate or Mind. From your brief description it\u2019s actually not that different from Psychic Assault so I\u2019d probably go with a Mind Shielding granting a CoW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:18:36-08:00","id":1173222,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to use Remote Control (Matter 1) with Death added in to be able to work a corpse like a puppet? Have some ideas using death to make a copy of my character using death mask on a corpse, but with space I'd scry my double so I could direct it about? May end up using matter 4 for the Golem.. but same question; can I animate a golem and use remote control on it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:22:59-08:00","id":1173223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173222#post1173222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use Remote Control (Matter 1) with Death added in to be able to work a corpse like a puppet? Have some ideas using death to make a copy of my character using death mask on a corpse, but with space I'd scry my double so I could direct it about? May end up using matter 4 for the Golem.. but same question; can I animate a golem and use remote control on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first you could use just Death, but you couldn\u2019t animate a corpse like that, at most you could cause it to do corpse things, like decompose, stiffen, bloat with gas, bodily fluids pooling, etc. To actually animate a corpse you need Death 3 using a spell like Quicken Corpse.<br /> <br /> Once you create a Golem though it just does what you tell it to, and I\u2019d allow a casting of Remote Control to be the vehicle by which you give those orders. You\u2019d just have to cast Remote Control once while touching the Golem or via Sensory Range and you\u2019d then be able to direct it for the duration of the Remote Control spell from anywhere.<br /> <br /> A similar Death spell could be devised to give orders to your zombies from anywhere once it\u2019s cast upon the zombie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-04-2018, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:31:12-08:00","id":1173224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173223#post1173223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first you could use just Death, but you couldn\u2019t animate a corpse like that, at most you could cause it to do corpse things, like decompose, stiffen, bloat with gas, bodily fluids pooling, etc. To actually animate a corpse you need Death 3 using a spell like Quicken Corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, quicken corpse. This makes a different type of thing. It makes a zombie that requires verbal commands. A corpse made mobile via remote control is a corpse puppet that does what I wish it to do, via a long duration remote control with the extra reach to allow complex stuff. If it was fresh or made fresh via corpse mask, it could talk and walk and dress up, etc. A far stretch from a mindless zombie.<br /> <br /> At least, thats the idea, same with a golem. I mean you could make a robotic skeleton via matter as an example, remote control spell on it, and you have a humanoid golem that does as you say but if you need, you could take direct control.<br /> <br /> I kinda am looking at building my moro's a workshop with tools and extra hands using this combo.. such as mixing dead flesh and mechanics to make some gnarly keebler elves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:37:42-08:00","id":1173225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173221#post1173221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the fluff characterize it? That should be a good clue. Going by what little I know of Changeling it could be protected against by Fate or Mind. From your brief description it\u2019s actually not that different from Psychic Assault so I\u2019d probably go with a Mind Shielding granting a CoW.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description indicates that it is the act of dismissal itself that causes damage. The mechanism, however, is not specified.<br /> <br /> The problem is, I believe, that many effects in Changeling are far less systematised than in Mage, since by its very nature, the game defers to &quot;narrative&quot; logic rather than to some quasi-physics.<br /> <br /> My resoning was, that there is no real &quot;source&quot; of harm that can be reasonably isolated, It doesn't really seem to be mind-specific assault. It somehow seems to be purely supernatural. Given the general narrative bend of Changeling I could also guess that it could be Fate?<br /> <br /> If I understand correctly, though, the consensus is that it shouldn't be shielded by Prime, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-04-2018, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:38:15-08:00","id":1173226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173222#post1173222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use Remote Control (Matter 1) with Death added in to be able to work a corpse like a puppet? Have some ideas using death to make a copy of my character using death mask on a corpse, but with space I'd scry my double so I could direct it about? May end up using matter 4 for the Golem.. but same question; can I animate a golem and use remote control on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no one-dot practices that do what you want. Compelling is limited to making an object do what it might do anyway.<br /> <br /> I made a Ruling spell that works similarly to how you describe - Corpse Marionette a few pages back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:52:02-08:00","id":1173228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173226#post1173226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no one-dot practices that do what you want. Compelling is limited to making an object do what it might do anyway.<br /> <br /> I made a Ruling spell that works similarly to how you describe - Corpse Marionette a few pages back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see where you mean the compelling practice doesn't do what I need, but the actual rote of Remote Control allows it, if the object has a function then this spell lets you work it, with the extra reach you can do extended actions and maintain control for the duration. <br /> <br /> How is working a corpse any less complex than driving a car remotely with this spell? The Death bit I figured would allow it to work on a corpse, if not, creative casting allows it but I couldn't find your spell.<br /> <br /> I guess Im asking for why this won't work with some rules or page #'s I could read up on for me and my group's understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:56:32-08:00","id":1173229,"title":"","content":"Remote Control lets you cause an object to do something it is intended to do on a symbolic level. This is parallel to 'what it might do anyway'.<br /> <br /> Corposes are not intended to move and do things on any level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:02:54-08:00","id":1173233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see where you mean the compelling practice doesn't do what I need, but the actual rote of Remote Control allows it, if the object has a function then this spell lets you work it, with the extra reach you can do extended actions and maintain control for the duration. </div> </div> </div>I can see the confusion, but I believe this might work with certain conditions.<br /> <br /> #1. The Remote Control functionality works because it is manipulating matter in a way that is natural and possible, so animating a corpse when rigor mortis has set in may be a bit difficult. However a freshly dead corpse could be animated in such a way.<br /> #2. The actions are restricted to purely mechanical operations that you can see from your own perspective since controlling a human to perform actions requires some visual aid since the corpse is no longer capable of processing actions without a mind and does not have a &quot;track&quot; so to speak to work. So, basically, a Weekend at Bernie's? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> #3. If you want the body to not tear itself apart as rigor mortis has set in then I would say using perhaps a Death 2 Ruling Spell would suffice.<br /> <br /> Hopefully this helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:09:15-08:00","id":1173236,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1614\" data-vbnamecard=\"1614\">Berdryn</a> Regardless of whether or not you can create a corpse puppet with Death, you don\u2019t need the specific spell Remote Control and you don\u2019t need Matter at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T21:12:19-08:00","id":1173932,"title":"","content":"Here are a few questions. Survival based questions. Say my group of magi are in a post apocalyptic setting and food is tight.. we have some meager supplies, 2 lbs of bacon specifically. Now, this is fresh, but its dead meat.. well within a Moros' ability to manipulate.<br /> <br /> Say I was to cut this 2lb's in half.. can I regenerate or repair said chunk to produce more bacon?<br /> <br /> Same question but with matter at 4, can I simply turn air into fresh dead meat, have the duration last so we can cook it and so on down the road?<br /> <br /> Would this sorta thing hurt a human that ate it when the spell goes away?<br /> <br /> Same deal but with water made from air or changed from ambient moisture then ingested?<br /> <br /> What fresh hell would making something like metal into a liquid, then that into water.. ingest and... what happens after the duration ends?? <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance on any advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","user":"Berdryn","date":". 01-07-2018, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T21:52:32-08:00","id":1173943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173932#post1173932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are a few questions. Survival based questions. Say my group of magi are in a post apocalyptic setting and food is tight.. we have some meager supplies, 2 lbs of bacon specifically. Now, this is fresh, but its dead meat.. well within a Moros' ability to manipulate.<br /> <br /> Say I was to cut this 2lb's in half.. can I regenerate or repair said chunk to produce more bacon?<br /> <br /> Same question but with matter at 4, can I simply turn air into fresh dead meat, have the duration last so we can cook it and so on down the road?<br /> <br /> Would this sorta thing hurt a human that ate it when the spell goes away?<br /> <br /> Same deal but with water made from air or changed from ambient moisture then ingested?<br /> <br /> What fresh hell would making something like metal into a liquid, then that into water.. ingest and... what happens after the duration ends??<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance on any advice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> #1. Bacon at least that would sustain you requires Life, but you could produce more Bacon that has no sustenance with Matter 5 if you didn't want to transmute something or Matter 4 to transmute some material into meat. There was a Matter 3 Repair Object spell in 1E, but I imagine it would not allow you to replicate the bacon but rather it would combine the two pieces restoring it back to the original 2lb. of Bacon. I would say this would require a Life 3 effect to make it edible if created with Matter 5.<br /> #2. You can turn it into dead meat, but again without Life it would not have any sustenance.<br /> #3. It would probably have no effect on the human other than eating a bland piece of meat.<br /> #4. This would be fine, a simple Matter 3 effect.<br /> #5. Matter 3 can transform solid metal into a liquid, but changing it to water would require Matter 4. If this was ingested, if water, then the character would be hydrated. Spells that change something to an edible/consumable form typically have a lasting effect when consumed since the body digests the matter and there is nothing for the spell to unravel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-07-2018, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T22:26:20-08:00","id":1173956,"title":"","content":"I disagree, bacon transmuted from Matter would give you sustenance. The problem is that if the spell doesn't last long enough for you to derive sustenance from it as it works through your system and out of it you may end up poisoning yourself as the &quot;bacon&quot; reverts back to its original state of whatever Matter it was derived from.<br /> <br /> If food is scarce, you're better off finding a Thyrsus and getting them to help you out than you are relying on the Moros with Matter transmutations. Which is a pretty good story hook honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T22:44:45-08:00","id":1173963,"title":"","content":"When summoning Supernal Entities, can you roll more than (Gnosis + Arcana) times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T06:35:14-08:00","id":1174006,"title":"","content":"You can, but it increases the Abyssal chance, it is actually not Gnosis + Arcanum but rather Resolve + Composure + any successes dedicated to protecting from abyssal intrusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The player can make a number of rolls equal to the character\u2019s Resolve + Composure + any successes allocated to avoid Abyssal intrusion. After that point, the Storyteller rolls the character\u2019s unmodified Gnosis for every roll that the character makes. If the Storyteller accrues a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s Gnosis + the primary Arcanum in the summoning, the Abyss breaks into the Fallen World, and the creature that arrives is not a Supernal being but an Abyssal one. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-07-2018, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T06:43:08-08:00","id":1174008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173956#post1173956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, bacon transmuted from Matter would give you sustenance. The problem is that if the spell doesn't last long enough for you to derive sustenance from it as it works through your system and out of it you may end up poisoning yourself as the &quot;bacon&quot; reverts back to its original state of whatever Matter it was derived from.<br /> <br /> If food is scarce, you're better off finding a Thyrsus and getting them to help you out than you are relying on the Moros with Matter transmutations. Which is a pretty good story hook honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say you are right Mrmdubois on the meat transformation, it appears that I didn't closely read Transubstantiation, it does appear capable of transforming things with multiple compounds so I suppose it would be sustaining. However, the after effects I believe are up to ST Fiat since the rules are not clear on what happens when you consume the transformed material, but I imagine a +2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana option for making this effect Lasting is not out of the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-07-2018, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T06:44:52-08:00","id":1174009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1173963#post1173963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When summoning Supernal Entities, can you roll more than (Gnosis + Arcana) times?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. The maximum number is actually (Resolve + Composure + any successes allocated to avoid Abyssal intrusion). The Patient Merit can add 2 to this number. If you have a relevant Specialty, you can add its bonus as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","user":"Enmai","date":". 01-07-2018, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T06:49:02-08:00","id":1174010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enmai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174009#post1174009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, if you have a relevant Specialty or the Patient Merit (page 46 of the Chronicles of Darkness corebook). Summoning Supernal Entities is an extended action, so the maximum number of times you can roll is equal to (Gnosis + Arcanum + Specialty bonus). The Patient Merit can add 2 to this number.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually wrong, DaveB stated that the Patient Merit did not affect spell casting or summoning, it only affects mundane actions. As to where you are getting this Specialty Bonus, I am not sure, there may be a merit is Summoners that might give you a bonus if that is what you are referring to.<br /> <br /> Also, as stated from the Core Rulebook, the number of times is not Gnosis + Arcanum times, it is Resolve + Composure + successes allocated to prevent Abyssal intrusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T11:46:47-08:00","id":1174323,"title":"","content":"Given the ability of Death and Spirit to create gateways into their respective other realms, do you think that Prime 5 could be used to create some kind of gateway to the Supernal World? Obviously, I wouldn\u2019t recommend going through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T11:52:47-08:00","id":1174324,"title":"","content":"No, but I can't really explain the metaphysical parts since I'm not as well read on the subject as I'd like to be. The Supernal is not a realm in any way close to the realms in the Fallen World, such as the Shadow, Underworld, Astral and Hedge. If I'm not mistaken reaching the Supernal is part of mages' Ascensions, so definitely not something that can be done before accessing the Imperial practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:03:23-08:00","id":1174327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174324#post1174324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but I can't really explain the metaphysical parts since I'm not as well read on the subject as I'd like to be. The Supernal is not a realm in any way close to the realms in the Fallen World, such as the Shadow, Underworld, Astral and Hedge. If I'm not mistaken reaching the Supernal is part of mages' Ascensions, so definitely not something that can be done before accessing the Imperial practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know it\u2019s not a literal place, my reasoning though was that a Mage can create a semi-Verge with a demesne and Seers can create Verges vis their prelacy so it seemed likely to me that you could produce similar results with Prime 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:07:02-08:00","id":1174330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174323#post1174323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the ability of Death and Spirit to create gateways into their respective other realms, do you think that Prime 5 could be used to create some kind of gateway to the Supernal World? Obviously, I wouldn\u2019t recommend going through it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is this not what a Hallow is? It seems like it to me. You also get the benefit of gaining mana from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:20:04-08:00","id":1174333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174330#post1174330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this not what a Hallow is? It seems like it to me. You also get the benefit of gaining mana from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a Hallow and a Verge are two different things, they can be right on top of each other though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:29:22-08:00","id":1174337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174333#post1174333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, a Hallow and a Verge are two different things, they can be right on top of each other though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean a Demesne is typically attuned to a Path and is kind of a pseudo realm of the Supernal Realm. However, there are Verges that seem to occur that are based on one type of Arcanum, but this is more of a symbolic manifestation of the concept of that Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I view a Hallow as basically the Raw Supernal that is not indicative of a Path or Arcanum, which is why I believe Prime 5 creating a portal to the Supernal would be a Hallow. That is just my interpretation anyway and how I make sense of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:33:08-08:00","id":1174339,"title":"","content":"I always viewed Hallows like a leaky faucet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T13:28:48-08:00","id":1174351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174337#post1174337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean a Demesne is typically attuned to a Path and is kind of a pseudo realm of the Supernal Realm. However, there are Verges that seem to occur that are based on one type of Arcanum, but this is more of a symbolic manifestation of the concept of that Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I view a Hallow as basically the Raw Supernal that is not indicative of a Path or Arcanum, which is why I believe Prime 5 creating a portal to the Supernal would be a Hallow. That is just my interpretation anyway and how I make sense of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the problem with this, is that Mana is the only thing that comes out of a Hallow, an actual Verge however typically has more Supernal weirdness than that going on. It\u2019s not really a gateway since you can\u2019t actually be obliterated by approaching one because raw, unfiltered Supernal stuff is coming out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T20:51:36-08:00","id":1174456,"title":"","content":"You are more than welcome to interpret that way, i just view Verges &amp; Demesnes as the Supernal filtered. I view mana as the Supernal unfiltered. I think the description in Imperial Mysteries also hints on this as the Supernal is mana/Supernal Truth, it is the archmage's will that makes something of the world or the watchtowers. If you are not powerful enough, you are turned into mana and absorbed forever not existing as a concept. I could be way off base, but it is not strictly said what the Supernal is unfiltered since even the Watchtowers filter the Supernal into concrete concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T17:57:09-08:00","id":1174716,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to write on surfaces with Matter?<br /> <br /> I know stuff like embossing and raising letters out of stuff can work, but could my mage use his magic to write lasting words in a personal journal?<br /> <br /> Mimic graffiti in a rival neighborhood with a wave of his hand?<br /> <br /> What practice would this be you think?<br /> <br /> Can you also erase writing then, like say you touch a book and wipe out the text within?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T18:03:23-08:00","id":1174718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174716#post1174716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to write on surfaces with Matter?<br /> <br /> I know stuff like embossing and raising letters out of stuff can work, but could my mage use his magic to write lasting words in a personal journal?<br /> <br /> Mimic graffiti in a rival neighborhood with a wave of his hand?<br /> <br /> What practice would this be you think?<br /> <br /> Can you also erase writing then, like say you touch a book and wipe out the text within?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's supposed to be graffiti that's visible to Sleepers (Usually) then yes. You just need the ink on hand to smear it into the symbols you want to mark a territory as yours, if you want to erase their graffiti then it's as simple as Shaping to turn their graffiti into an indecipherable mess.<br /> <br /> Mimicing graffiti could easily be a Veiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T00:01:21-08:00","id":1174796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174718#post1174718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's supposed to be graffiti that's visible to Sleepers (Usually) then yes. You just need the ink on hand to smear it into the symbols you want to mark a territory as yours, if you want to erase their graffiti then it's as simple as Shaping to turn their graffiti into an indecipherable mess.<br /> <br /> Mimicing graffiti could easily be a Veiling spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say mimicing graffiti is probably weaving. You are altering the wall to appear differently. Why would it be veiling? What are you hiding and from whom? Its not ruling as your not controling the wall in any way etc<br /> <br /> You could erase graffitti or have it appear to vanish with veiling though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T03:12:08-08:00","id":1174815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174796#post1174796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say mimicing graffiti is probably weaving. You are altering the wall to appear differently. Why would it be veiling? What are you hiding and from whom? Its not ruling as your not controling the wall in any way etc<br /> <br /> You could erase graffitti or have it appear to vanish with veiling though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Causing a wall to look like a different kind of wall is well within Veiling\u2019s power, and I think you could decide that you want it to look like a graffiti covered wall, and there\u2019s nothing stopping you from having that faux-graffiti mimicking someone else\u2019s.<br /> <br /> You only need Weaving if you\u2019re changing actual properties of the wall, Veiling is all you ever need for cosmetic changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-10-2018, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:10:54-08:00","id":1174840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1174815#post1174815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Causing a wall to look like a different kind of wall is well within Veiling\u2019s power, and I think you could decide that you want it to look like a graffiti covered wall, and there\u2019s nothing stopping you from having that faux-graffiti mimicking someone else\u2019s.<br /> <br /> You only need Weaving if you\u2019re changing actual properties of the wall, Veiling is all you ever need for cosmetic changes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think your right, i was taking veilings conceal from or conceal things under to literally. Considering Life's &quot;Mutable mask&quot; can change features and is veiling then yeh, should be easily enough to have a matter version that changes paint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T22:39:14-08:00","id":1175381,"title":"","content":"How much [other Arcanum] would you need to add to Teleport to teleport to the Hedge/Underworld/Shadow/wherever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T01:07:49-08:00","id":1175389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1175381#post1175381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much [other Arcanum] would you need to add to Teleport to teleport to the Hedge/Underworld/Shadow/wherever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good news: this is already in the spell description. &quot;<b>Add Death \u2022\u2022, Sprit \u2022\u2022, etc</b>: By adding \u2022\u2022 in an Arcanum whose purview includes another realm of existence (e.g. the Underworld or the Shadow), the mage may move things from that realm into the physical world, or vice versa.&quot; So you would need to add 2 dots of the relevant Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T17:39:23-08:00","id":1175874,"title":"","content":"When using Ban, Space 3, are you banning the supernal symbol of something or the very detailed type of thing? Say for example, using matter, I'd like to set up a basic personal ban around my body to prevent bullets from entering beyond the ban. Do I need every known caliber of bullet in mind? can I just say 'bullet' and have that be it? <br /> <br /> Could you use ban and time to create a space where time is accelerated? Like a training dojo where you could train yourselves up a few months at a time in exchange for a week in the area? <br /> <br /> Can I use death and ban to say ban a warehouse sized field from any zombies or undead by simply saying undead or the like? Would vampires be restricted or get a clash of wills? Free to walk in as they aren't truely either? Some help with what ban is really capable of.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T18:08:49-08:00","id":1175879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1175874#post1175874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to set up a basic personal ban around my body to prevent bullets from entering beyond the ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dubious usage. This depends entirely on whether your table allows aoe spells to be centered on mobile subjects that aren't themselves 'areas'. If they do allow that, 'bullets' should be fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1175874#post1175874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use ban and time to create a space where time is accelerated? Like a training dojo where you could train yourselves up a few months at a time in exchange for a week in the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think banning Time would work more like Veil of Moments, but there has been other discussion of this further back in the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1175874#post1175874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use death and ban to say ban a warehouse sized field from any zombies or undead by simply saying undead or the like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1175874#post1175874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would vampires be restricted or get a clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>What on earth would they Clash with? Unless they have an specific ability that allows them entry into that explicit area, there's no grounds for a CoW. You don't roll Clash just because another splat is involved, it's a means to resolve conflict between supernatural powers with directly opposing effects when the direct mechanics of each don't resolve on their own (or if the powers specifically call for one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T21:39:01-08:00","id":1175911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1175874#post1175874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Ban, Space 3, are you banning the supernal symbol of something or the very detailed type of thing? Say for example, using matter, I'd like to set up a basic personal ban around my body to prevent bullets from entering beyond the ban. Do I need every known caliber of bullet in mind? can I just say 'bullet' and have that be it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullet is fine, even a simpleton would know what you mean by that. Though you might get a shock when a rocket propelled shell passes through your ban though. You might want to Ban &quot;projectiles&quot;? Personally im not in the camp that believes area spells can be moved once cast on a area so no body suit bans for mages in my games.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you use ban and time to create a space where time is accelerated? Like a training dojo where you could train yourselves up a few months at a time in exchange for a week in the area? </div> </div> </div>Why would banning time within a zone make it accelerate exactly? The ban would still have time inside it that is still moving at the same speed as time outside the ban, you just stopped time entering/leaving the banned area. Which frankly probably does nothing. Its not like banning air stops air being inside the ban area (until you use it all up etc) so same with time. You'll need Time to speed up/slowdown time im afraid.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I use death and ban to say ban a warehouse sized field from any zombies or undead by simply saying undead or the like? Would vampires be restricted or get a clash of wills? Free to walk in as they aren't truely either? Some help with what ban is really capable of. </div> </div> </div>As Inodiv has said this is fine, and its true about clashes. The only way a vampire would get a clash is from some teleport power, or somehow manipulates space. Otherwise they are just using mundane means to try entering the banned area.<br /> <br /> I think you are overthinking it. You can Ban vs &quot;Snakes&quot; to allow only snakes to enter/leave or have it so everything but snakes can enter/leave. You then just ask &quot;Is it a snake?&quot;. You seem to consider vampires to not be undead though which is slightly odd which might explain why you are confused.<br /> <br /> While ban for some odd reason doesnt mention Keys its then up to the ST how specific one can get and if you are allowed to only ban Slippy the Snake. Personally i would love to be keyed to my own Ban thanks, but alas nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-14-2018, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T17:24:10-08:00","id":1176120,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers guys, really helps as my friend and I learn how mage works.<br /> <br /> Had another question come up as well with some related questions to it as we have adept magic available now and I am wondering;<br /> <br /> Creating golems; Is there a limit on size of the object being made? Say I went to a junkyard and built a size 12 iron giant, do you just animate it if it qualifies as an object? <br /> <br /> If the iron giant is animate, I want to be able to use a scrying window to see out of its eyes and allow it to hear me for directions through said window. <br /> <br /> An extension of the above, could my mage pick up a drone and animate it via golem or direct control with remote control, but allow scrying vision through the camera of the drone? Say I upped the sympathy on the inner lens of the camera so I can see what it sees, use the control magic to move the camera/scry view, etc.<br /> <br /> We are in a situation where we can't really go scouting on foot as we are sorta in hiding in an ancestral demense out in the woods. Space 3 was recently achieved so portals aren't being widely used just yet, hence the need for mechanical cannon fodder.<br /> <br /> I know the danger of it mostly, but could you also make a soul stone object, shape it and such then animate it? A 12&quot; GI Joe with real gear the moros made with the above ideas, so the young moros has basically created a magical video game as he uses it to gather intel, work as a yantra maybe. Just exploring ideas before my next game. <br /> <br /> Thanks again for advice and answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T17:42:40-08:00","id":1176125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176120#post1176120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers guys, really helps as my friend and I learn how mage works.<br /> <br /> Had another question come up as well with some related questions to it as we have adept magic available now and I am wondering;<br /> <br /> Creating golems; Is there a limit on size of the object being made? Say I went to a junkyard and built a size 12 iron giant, do you just animate it if it qualifies as an object?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells typically only work on a Size 5 object by default, creating a golem of a larger size would require increasing your Scale factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">An extension of the above, could my mage pick up a drone and animate it via golem or direct control with remote control, but allow scrying vision through the camera of the drone? Say I upped the sympathy on the inner lens of the camera so I can see what it sees, use the control magic to move the camera/scry view, etc.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Is there a reason you're not just using video data sent from the camera to your phone or other appropriate device? Because that would be simpler. Scrying on the drone though would only give you a close up view of the drone, it wouldn't let you see through the drone's eyes, same for a more conventional golem. I could see a custom Reach clause for Scrying though that would justify being able to use their senses, although it would probably be more appropriate to form the weird kind of sympathetic bond that Mages share with their familiars that allow them to share senses, that would be Space Patterning though which isn't available to you yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I know the danger of it mostly, but could you also make a soul stone object, shape it and such then animate it? A 12&quot; GI Joe with real gear the moros made with the above ideas, so the young moros has basically created a magical video game as he uses it to gather intel, work as a yantra maybe. Just exploring ideas before my next game. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You could animate a soulstone, sure. Upshot is there's no Sympathetic Withstand for affecting it since it's effectively the same as if you're there as far as Space is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:42:00-08:00","id":1176180,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason you're not just using video data sent from the camera to your phone or other appropriate device? Because that would be simpler. Scrying on the drone though would only give you a close up view of the drone, it wouldn't let you see through the drone's eyes, same for a more conventional golem. I could see a custom Reach clause for Scrying though that would justify being able to use their senses, although it would probably be more appropriate to form the weird kind of sympathetic bond that Mages share with their familiars that allow them to share senses, that would be Space Patterning though which isn't available to you yet.<br /> <br /> ** We are in the early days of a zombie apoc game. We are basically living in the woods on some land a character owns, we have power from a ley node and a pair of generators powered by magic. I kinda envision my mage having a few scry windows up as sort of a console at his workstation, we don't really have any tech beyond what the character had at a trailer. I was hoping that a more detailed use of scrying on the part of the camera that actually has the image. It would then in turn just require Perfect Sympathy or the like to make the connection well enough, the window would already be a close up of that. I guess I'm just asking why it would require patterning to make it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T03:05:35-08:00","id":1176230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176180#post1176180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">** We are in the early days of a zombie apoc game. We are basically living in the woods on some land a character owns, we have power from a ley node and a pair of generators powered by magic. I kinda envision my mage having a few scry windows up as sort of a console at his workstation, we don't really have any tech beyond what the character had at a trailer. I was hoping that a more detailed use of scrying on the part of the camera that actually has the image. It would then in turn just require Perfect Sympathy or the like to make the connection well enough, the window would already be a close up of that. I guess I'm just asking why it would require patterning to make it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not about having a strong enough connection, it\u2019s about what Scrying actually does and doesn\u2019t do and what it doesn\u2019t do is let you see through the eye-like equivalent of your subject. Patterning can be used to actually braid two subjects together so tightly that on the metaphysical level they\u2019re one thing which is why they can share senses.<br /> <br /> Anyway, an easier method if you\u2019re camped out in just one spot would be to open a Scrying window on the area you\u2019re in with as big a Scale as you can get. Skip the drone entirely.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, and even better than Scrying, use Inward and Outward eye. It becomes nearly impossible for your group to be ambushed then as well as wide angle surveillance giving you more bang for your buck and continuing to avoid the drone problem.<br /> <br /> Both those alternatives also require only one spell control slot, and I don\u2019t know what your Gnosis is, but running multiple Scrying windows when you could use one spell is a little sloppy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-15-2018, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T06:53:51-08:00","id":1176267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176230#post1176230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not about having a strong enough connection, it\u2019s about what Scrying actually does and doesn\u2019t do and what it doesn\u2019t do is let you see through the eye-like equivalent of your subject. Patterning can be used to actually braid two subjects together so tightly that on the metaphysical level they\u2019re one thing which is why they can share senses.<br /> <br /> Anyway, an easier method if you\u2019re camped out in just one spot would be to open a Scrying window on the area you\u2019re in with as big a Scale as you can get. Skip the drone entirely.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, and even better than Scrying, use Inward and Outward eye. It becomes nearly impossible for your group to be ambushed then as well as wide angle surveillance giving you more bang for your buck and continuing to avoid the drone problem.<br /> <br /> Both those alternatives also require only one spell control slot, and I don\u2019t know what your Gnosis is, but running multiple Scrying windows when you could use one spell is a little sloppy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a great workaround. Thank you for explaining, been trying to figure out whats possible with what we have. We are about equal in power, gnosis 4. my guy has matter 4, death 3, forces 3, space 3 at this time.<br /> <br /> I was wondering on the in-outward eye, but what would this massive scale scry window appear? Is it for example a 2x3 magic window I can pan and zoom within the area or is the inward/outward eye spell what lets you see that whole scrying area at once so you don't need to 'pan/zoom' with it?<br /> <br /> This current scenario is my first play using the above arcana levels in 2e, space, time and fate so far are the most confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T09:38:19-08:00","id":1176303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176267#post1176267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great workaround. Thank you for explaining, been trying to figure out whats possible with what we have. We are about equal in power, gnosis 4. my guy has matter 4, death 3, forces 3, space 3 at this time.<br /> <br /> I was wondering on the in-outward eye, but what would this massive scale scry window appear? Is it for example a 2x3 magic window I can pan and zoom within the area or is the inward/outward eye spell what lets you see that whole scrying area at once so you don't need to 'pan/zoom' with it?<br /> <br /> This current scenario is my first play using the above arcana levels in 2e, space, time and fate so far are the most confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scrying doesn\u2019t allow panning and zooming.<br /> <br /> Since you also have Forces though what I\u2019d do if I were you is to combine cast Inward and Outward Eye (Pg. 174), with Zoom In (Pg. 144) and you\u2019ll be able to see anything happening within 3 miles of your location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T03:01:27-08:00","id":1176733,"title":"","content":"Can matter 4 create a lifelike copy of someone, say we go to the effort of gathering 'parts' or the like as a moros. Could one make a flesh-golem?<br /> <br /> We are asking as a powerful banisher is hunting for us *we think*. Anyway, I want to make a copy of a cabal mate we can animate.<br /> <br /> Consider instead a proper marionette, with crafts and science, and things like fake hair, fake skin, bone and the like on hand as we make it.. could we just animate a size 5 golem out of clay and use shaping to 'morph' it into someone's likeness?<br /> <br /> Would matter 4 be able to account for colors, scents, etc? Or would it just look like a clay statue of someone, clothes and all.<br /> <br /> There was also talk of taking the clay and forming it into like a suit that shaping and other magic could be on it so when needed, he could say, shape the clay bit around a forearm into a blade or something akin to a weapon. Imagine Clayface from Batman, but in either a suit or golem form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T04:00:23-08:00","id":1176742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176733#post1176733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can matter 4 create a lifelike copy of someone, say we go to the effort of gathering 'parts' or the like as a moros. Could one make a flesh-golem?<br /> <br /> We are asking as a powerful banisher is hunting for us *we think*. Anyway, I want to make a copy of a cabal mate we can animate.<br /> <br /> Consider instead a proper marionette, with crafts and science, and things like fake hair, fake skin, bone and the like on hand as we make it.. could we just animate a size 5 golem out of clay and use shaping to 'morph' it into someone's likeness?<br /> <br /> Would matter 4 be able to account for colors, scents, etc? Or would it just look like a clay statue of someone, clothes and all.<br /> <br /> There was also talk of taking the clay and forming it into like a suit that shaping and other magic could be on it so when needed, he could say, shape the clay bit around a forearm into a blade or something akin to a weapon. Imagine Clayface from Batman, but in either a suit or golem form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tricky. I\u2019d allow the flesh-puppet, maybe even just a Reach or two on existing spells (like Shaping), accompanied by Medicine and/or Crafts rolls... but then again, Life and Matter were always the stingiest when it comes to cross-Arcana application. I can see a strong case being made for such life-like imitation requiring equal dots in Life. Like how Wonderful Machine has an \u201cAdd Life\u201d option. But I\u2019m more in favor of allowing pure Matter to do the job.<br /> <br /> Oh, maybe without adding Life, the puppet seems noticeably off? Like how Platonic Forms require Forces to look natural. <br /> <br /> The clay suit-armor I\u2019m wary of, since I think every instance of shapeshifting would require a separate spell. A single spell creating such a protean tool seems tough. Maybe a stretch with Making (Matter 5)? That\u2019s the level we get creation of complex patterns. <br /> <br /> Maybe an Artifact? Direct Supernal intrusion is a good excuse to ignore some of the rules of standard Awakened magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T04:44:55-08:00","id":1176746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176742#post1176742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tricky. I\u2019d allow the flesh-puppet, maybe even just a Reach or two on existing spells (like Shaping), accompanied by Medicine and/or Crafts rolls... but then again, Life and Matter were always the stingiest when it comes to cross-Arcana application. I can see a strong case being made for such life-like imitation requiring equal dots in Life. Like how Wonderful Machine has an \u201cAdd Life\u201d option. But I\u2019m more in favor of allowing pure Matter to do the job.<br /> <br /> Oh, maybe without adding Life, the puppet seems noticeably off? Like how Platonic Forms require Forces to look natural.<br /> <br /> The clay suit-armor I\u2019m wary of, since I think every instance of shapeshifting would require a separate spell. A single spell creating such a protean tool seems tough. Maybe a stretch with Making (Matter 5)? That\u2019s the level we get creation of complex patterns.<br /> <br /> Maybe an Artifact? Direct Supernal intrusion is a good excuse to ignore some of the rules of standard Awakened magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally i would say its just death if you want to create a real corpse. Matter you could animate some form of clay or whatever and disguise it as a real corpse/living person via mundane or magical means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T16:44:02-08:00","id":1176856,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, new player here just want to clear some questions on character creation:<br /> <br /> 1) What are rote skills? I can't find the page that talks about them in more detail.<br /> 2) What is a Praxis, which page can I read more about them?<br /> 3) How many Dedicated Magical Tools can a starting mage have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T16:59:42-08:00","id":1176858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176856#post1176856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, new player here just want to clear some questions on character creation:<br /> <br /> 1) What are rote skills? I can't find the page that talks about them in more detail.<br /> 2) What is a Praxis, which page can I read more about them?<br /> 3) How many Dedicated Magical Tools can a starting mage have?</div> </div> </div> </div>1: Rote skills are a holdover from 1e, they grant a +1 dice bonus to the Mudra Yantra when the Rote you're casting uses one of your Orders Rote Skills. So say you're Mysterium, and you have a Rote that has the Rote Skill of Occult, then when you use the Mudra Yantra for that Rote which grants you a number of dice equal to your dots in Rote you can add one more die because of your Order's Rote Skill.<br /> <br /> 2: A Praxis is a personal spell that you tend to cast a lot. You get one for free everytime you purchase a dot of Gnosis, and you can purchase additional Praxis for 1 XP each. A Praxis is basically like any other spell, except that when you cast it you get an Exceptional Success on 3 Successes instead of 5. I'm sorry that I can't remember specific page numbers. There's a sidebar that details your options when you get an Exceptional Success on a spell. I can't remember where exactly that is either, but it's things like bypassing Withstand, gaining a Condition that can result in an Arcane Beat or replenishing Mana spent on a spell +1, etc.<br /> <br /> 3: Any Mage can only have 1 Dedicated Magical Tool. Although, when Signs of Sorcery comes out there will apparently be rules for trying to have more than one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-17-2018, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T17:02:58-08:00","id":1176861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176856#post1176856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, new player here just want to clear some questions on character creation:<br /> <br /> 1) What are rote skills? I can't find the page that talks about them in more detail.<br /> 2) What is a Praxis, which page can I read more about them?<br /> 3) How many Dedicated Magical Tools can a starting mage have?</div> </div> </div> </div>p82 has the order rote skill list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T17:18:26-08:00","id":1176866,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T17:52:09-08:00","id":1176867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176858#post1176858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: A Praxis is a personal spell that you tend to cast a lot. You get one for free everytime you purchase a dot of Gnosis, and you can purchase additional Praxis for 1 XP each. A Praxis is basically like any other spell, except that when you cast it you get an Exceptional Success on 3 Successes instead of 5. I'm sorry that I can't remember specific page numbers. There's a sidebar that details your options when you get an Exceptional Success on a spell. I can't remember where exactly that is either, but it's things like bypassing Withstand, gaining a Condition that can result in an Arcane Beat or replenishing Mana spent on a spell +1, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let's say that at character creation my mage has Fate 3, can he have Grave Misfortune (Fate 3) as a Praxis?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: Any Mage can only have 1 Dedicated Magical Tool. Although, when Signs of Sorcery comes out there will apparently be rules for trying to have more than one. </div> </div> </div>Ah gotcha.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T18:15:40-08:00","id":1176870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176867#post1176867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's say that at character creation my mage has Fate 3, can he have Grave Misfortune (Fate 3) as a Praxis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T18:20:32-08:00","id":1176872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176870#post1176870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, he can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T19:38:42-08:00","id":1176877,"title":"","content":"Does supernal veil hide magic from sleepers? Do I need to cast it combo'ed with the spell I want to hide?<br /> <br /> Could I use forces and space to create a ban area which essentially is a construction zone for magic casting? Say, in this area, no sleeper can see into or enter the area while we are inside casting magic? This would be over our dead mentor's demense with a camp of survivor sleepers around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T23:52:13-08:00","id":1176905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1176877#post1176877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does supernal veil hide magic from sleepers? Do I need to cast it combo'ed with the spell I want to hide?<br /> <br /> Could I use forces and space to create a ban area which essentially is a construction zone for magic casting? Say, in this area, no sleeper can see into or enter the area while we are inside casting magic? This would be over our dead mentor's demense with a camp of survivor sleepers around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like how machine invis can hide matter from sleepers then yes. If cast on the ban below then yes it'll be invis to sleepers.<br /> <br /> A ban on its own will create an area where sleepers cant enter or see inside alreay without forces. (You could add it to let light through though) Just remember to not stay inside the ban for long unless you have let air inside via matter or you will suffocate in your own ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-18-2018, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:01:47-08:00","id":1177043,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's a question: how do you keep Lucky Number (fate 2) from breaking the setting? I just ran a Mage game where one of my players had it as a praxis. It started with him wanting to use it to call the phone nearest to their quarry and use his hacking skills to find the phone's location (the spell itself doesn't tell you the location of the phone, but he had really high computer skills). Of course, then he realized he didn't need to call the bad-guy's phone, he could just open google-earth, cast the spell, and randomly punch in coordinates that &quot;just so happened&quot; to be the bad-guy's exact location. Once you realize that this sort of shenanigans is perfectly valid within the spells limits, you realize all sorts of crap is possible. Like randomly punching on a key board until you've typed out all of the weaknesses of the spirit you're hunting. Luckily, I realized the implications and ruled that the spell <i>did, </i>in fact, run off of some sort of sympathy, but neither he nor I were happy with nerfing one of his signature spells, and it was still up to me to ad-hoc whether &quot;yes this incredibly unlikely thing is a thing you can do&quot; or not.<br /> For reference, the odds of &quot;just happening&quot; to punch in the correct, 12-character password on the first try is of the same order of magnitude as &quot;just happening&quot; to be struck by lighting on any given second (which, incidentally, isn't possible without Fate 5 and +2 reach).<br /> Sorry if that was a little rant-y. Does anyone have any better ideas for how to deal with this spell? Did the two of us just read it completely wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:25:47-08:00","id":1177050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177043#post1177043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's a question: how do you keep Lucky Number (fate 2) from breaking the setting? I just ran a Mage game where one of my players had it as a praxis. It started with him wanting to use it to call the phone nearest to their quarry and use his hacking skills to find the phone's location (the spell itself doesn't tell you the location of the phone, but he had really high computer skills). Of course, then he realized he didn't need to call the bad-guy's phone, he could just open google-earth, cast the spell, and randomly punch in coordinates that &quot;just so happened&quot; to be the bad-guy's exact location. Once you realize that this sort of shenanigans is perfectly valid within the spells limits, you realize all sorts of crap is possible. Like randomly punching on a key board until you've typed out all of the weaknesses of the spirit you're hunting. Luckily, I realized the implications and ruled that the spell <i>did, </i>in fact, run off of some sort of sympathy, but neither he nor I were happy with nerfing one of his signature spells, and it was still up to me to ad-hoc whether &quot;yes this incredibly unlikely thing is a thing you can do&quot; or not.<br /> For reference, the odds of &quot;just happening&quot; to punch in the correct, 12-character password on the first try is of the same order of magnitude as &quot;just happening&quot; to be struck by lighting on any given second (which, incidentally, isn't possible without Fate 5 and +2 reach).<br /> Sorry if that was a little rant-y. Does anyone have any better ideas for how to deal with this spell? Did the two of us just read it completely wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Veiling spells. Especially if word gets around that he's using Fate spells to find people a lot. Lucky Number is not an Unveiling spell, so any Veiling magic that hides the subject will simply cause Lucky Number to report wrong information. Space would probably be able to do it, as well as maybe a creative thaumaturgy Fate Veiling spell (Warding Gesture itself doesn't really seem to deal with probabilities). Also, I run my games with the idea that the players specifically need to be Unveiling something or be using magic that <i>very directly</i> clashes in order for Clashes of Wills to trigger against Veiling magic. Some people may interpret Lucky Number as Clashing against relevant Veiling magic, but I would not allow that in my games.<br /> <br /> While I would probably allow the GPS thing, I think that randomly punching the keyboard to find Spirit weakness is outside the limits of what this spell can do. It's more about entering small pieces of data such as phone numbers and passwords, not entire paragraphs with detailed pieces of information regarding things under the purview of another Arcanum. The spell works on probability, so while you could argue that randomly typing out spirit weaknesses should be possible, I would counter with the argument that such a manipulation of probability is beyond the boundaries of the Practice of Ruling. Ruling is about minor alterations, not sweeping changes. Finding information about a spirit through random chance is either a Weaving or Patterning of Fate, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:39:50-08:00","id":1177053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177050#post1177050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Veiling spells. Especially if word gets around that he's using Fate spells to find people a lot. Lucky Number is not an Unveiling spell, so any Veiling magic that hides the subject will simply cause Lucky Number to report wrong information. Space would probably be able to do it, as well as maybe a creative thaumaturgy Fate Veiling spell (Warding Gesture itself doesn't really seem to deal with probabilities). Also, I run my games with the idea that the players specifically need to be Unveiling something or be using magic that <i>very directly</i> clashes in order for Clashes of Wills to trigger against Veiling magic. Some people may interpret Lucky Number as Clashing against relevant Veiling magic, but I would not allow that in my games.<br /> <br /> While I would probably allow the GPS thing, I think that randomly punching the keyboard to find Spirit weakness is outside the limits of what this spell can do. It's more about entering small pieces of data such as phone numbers and passwords, not entire paragraphs with detailed pieces of information regarding things under the purview of another Arcanum. The spell works on probability, so while you could argue that randomly typing out spirit weaknesses should be possible, I would counter with the argument that such a manipulation of probability is beyond the boundaries of the Practice of Ruling. Ruling is about minor alterations, not sweeping changes. Finding information about a spirit through random chance is either a Weaving or Patterning of Fate, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say you are entirely correct on every point...which is why it's so annoying that the spell seems to go out of it's way to try and bypass these restrictions. &quot;This spell uses the input device as its subject....It does not require sympathy...the magic applies to the probabilities of random input, rather than locating a target.&quot; Theoretically, no matter what kind of veiling you use, the spell doesn't care because it doesn't actually target you. I guess the problem is that they didn't want to involve Sympathy rules in a Fate spell. *deep breath* Okay, I gonna move on now. Thanks for the suggestions, I just hate making &quot;dirty&quot; edits to the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:58:08-08:00","id":1177059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177053#post1177053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say you are entirely correct on every point...which is why it's so annoying that the spell seems to go out of it's way to try and bypass these restrictions. &amp;quot;This spell uses the input device as its subject....It does not require sympathy...the magic applies to the probabilities of random input, rather than locating a target.&amp;quot; Theoretically, no matter what kind of veiling you use, the spell doesn't care because it doesn't actually target you. I guess the problem is that they didn't want to involve Sympathy rules in a Fate spell. *deep breath* Okay, I gonna move on now. Thanks for the suggestions, I just hate making &amp;quot;dirty&amp;quot; edits to the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading all it can do is gain access to a person or thing by using random input when using a device.<br /> <br /> So, the GPS trick, or figuring out the weakness of a spirit wouldn\u2019t work as that\u2019s information, not access. There is a secondary effect of gaining some information of course, which is that you can look at your past calls or whatever you punched in and remember that information (And gain the Informed Condition as a result), but that\u2019s incidental to the intent of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T15:00:30-08:00","id":1177060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177053#post1177053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say you are entirely correct on every point...which is why it's so annoying that the spell seems to go out of it's way to try and bypass these restrictions. &quot;This spell uses the input device as its subject....It does not require sympathy...the magic applies to the probabilities of random input, rather than locating a target.&quot; Theoretically, no matter what kind of veiling you use, the spell doesn't care because it doesn't actually target you. I guess the problem is that they didn't want to involve Sympathy rules in a Fate spell. *deep breath* Okay, I gonna move on now. Thanks for the suggestions, I just hate making &quot;dirty&quot; edits to the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the part where it's a bit up to interpretation. It could <i>technically </i>be argued that Lucky Number bypasses things like Space Veiling spells since it's not targeting you directly. Personally I would probably go with the interpretation that Veiling spells can confuse Lucky Number. But even if you don't go with that interpretation, you may have another thing to fall back on: the Imago. Mages can do basically anything with magic. The key is: they have to <i>know how to do it</i>. A mage can create Vitae with magic. 99% of mages don't know what Vitae is, much less have studied in-depth enough to form a proper Imago that creates proper Vitae. A mage with casual knowledge about Vitae could probably create an imitation, but it wouldn't work like actual Vitae.<br /> <br /> The Imago for using Lucky Number to find someone needs to incorporate, at minimum, a decent amount of information about the person being sought. &quot;Guy with black hair that shot a fireball at me last week&quot; is probably not enough. You would need things like Shadow Name, maybe even associates, or last known location. One thing that trips mages up a lot is completely mundane solutions. Most mage players are completely gung-ho about using magic to solve everything that they often forget simple mundane techniques for hiding or spying work very well! Can't form an Imago to &quot;randomly&quot; locate someone if you barely know anything about them.<br /> <br /> Of course, maybe your players already know a lot about the bad guy. And if they know a decent amount of information, let Lucky Number find the bad guy. Mages are very good at finding information and blowing through most puzzles in a couple of turns. Just because they can find someone, though, doesn't mean it's not dangerous as hell for them to approach (especially if they're unprepared).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T15:01:30-08:00","id":1177061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177059#post1177059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my reading all it can do is gain access to a person or thing by using random input when using a device.<br /> <br /> So, the GPS trick, or figuring out the weakness of a spirit wouldn\u2019t work as that\u2019s information, not access. There is a secondary effect of gaining some information of course, which is that you can look at your past calls or whatever you punched in and remember that information (And gain the Informed Condition as a result), but that\u2019s incidental to the intent of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a good interpretation... and much simpler to use as a justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T11:49:37-08:00","id":1177376,"title":"","content":"One should also keep in mind that Mage doesn't lend itself well to plots that require hiding information from your players. <br /> <br /> I've had much more success with plots that basically assume players will nearly immediately uncover all relevant information (they'll usually find a way) and then design scenarios in such a way that &quot;Now, what do we <b>do</b> with this information?&quot; is the far more important question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T11:48:35-08:00","id":1177903,"title":"","content":"Here's my take on why Lucky Number can't do that:<br /> <br /> Guessing a password/phone number/etc. is a straightforward probabilistic event. The thing you're guessing is (in theory) at least pseudorandom, lies within a well-defined sample space, and the act of guessing it has an immediate outcome (you're in or not, you reach the right phone or not, etc.). Conceptually it's not all that different from pouring a bucket of dice on the floor and hoping to get all sixes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Guessing&quot; a location or a bane is none of those things. The thing you're trying to guess is not random, the sample space is ill-defined beyond (e.g.-) &quot;probably somewhere on Earth,&quot; and the result must be verified by other means. Altogether you're talking about something much closer to divination than to rigging an RNG. Not that divination methods based on supposedly-random processes aren't very much a thing, but you need a higher practice (probably Weaving?) for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T14:59:39-08:00","id":1177945,"title":"","content":"And if someone still wants to use Lucky Number that way, making it a +1 or +2 Reach option could work, assuming everyone at the table agrees. Maybe even have Add Space as an added requirement for pinpointing coordinates like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:01:47-08:00","id":1178064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177903#post1177903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my take on why Lucky Number can't do that:<br /> <br /> Guessing a password/phone number/etc. is a straightforward probabilistic event. The thing you're guessing is (in theory) at least pseudorandom, lies within a well-defined sample space, and the act of guessing it has an immediate outcome (you're in or not, you reach the right phone or not, etc.). Conceptually it's not all that different from pouring a bucket of dice on the floor and hoping to get all sixes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Guessing&quot; a location or a bane is none of those things. The thing you're trying to guess is not random, the sample space is ill-defined beyond (e.g.-) &quot;probably somewhere on Earth,&quot; and the result must be verified by other means. Altogether you're talking about something much closer to divination than to rigging an RNG. Not that divination methods based on supposedly-random processes aren't very much a thing, but you need a higher practice (probably Weaving?) for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well put. To often i see fate being used for stupid things that dont make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:03:27-08:00","id":1178065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1177945#post1177945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if someone still wants to use Lucky Number that way, making it a +1 or +2 Reach option could work, assuming everyone at the table agrees. Maybe even have Add Space as an added requirement for pinpointing coordinates like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugg, slapping on extra reach to existing spells just to make them &quot;work&quot; isnt the right way to go about things. Just use creative thaum and make an entire different spell that does what you want which doesnt require adding reach to existing spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:29:21-08:00","id":1178070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178065#post1178065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugg, slapping on extra reach to existing spells just to make them &amp;quot;work&amp;quot; isnt the right way to go about things. Just use creative thaum and make an entire different spell that does what you want which doesnt require adding reach to existing spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the effect is similar to what the original spell could accomplish, but more complex, then creating a Reach option is entirely appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:07:05-08:00","id":1178094,"title":"","content":"I know how I\u2019d answer this, but what are your thoughts on the fact that Postcognition or Perfect Recall being used to review a grimoire that you\u2019ve only read once, and using those visions to cast or learn a spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:39:00-08:00","id":1178102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178094#post1178094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know how I\u2019d answer this, but what are your thoughts on the fact that Postcognition or Perfect Recall being used to review a grimoire that you\u2019ve only read once, and using those visions to cast or learn a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not married to this opinion, but despite having <i>very</i> permissive games, I don't think I'd allow this. Allowing it would imply that the only thing there really <i>is</i> to a Grimoire is writing down instructions, symbols, etc, so if you can perfectly recall them, you can follow it.<br /> <br /> My counter to that implied assumption would be that, if that were the case, you wouldn't need Prime 1 to create a Grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:46:52-08:00","id":1178128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178070#post1178070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the effect is similar to what the original spell could accomplish, but more complex, then creating a Reach option is entirely appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but allowing Lucky Number to accomplish such things is at the very least Weaving in my opinion, if not Patterning. Things like punching in the GPS location of a target start to approach the Strings of Fate spell, where you specify an event and Fate conspires to make it happen as soon as possible. If you want to know the exact GPS coordinates of someone, couldn't a Space Knowing spell that is cast sympathetically at the target tell you? That's a different path to the same result.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T12:20:24-08:00","id":1178143,"title":"","content":"It doesn\u2019t at all seem to me like Strings of Fate unless you use Strings of Fate with the goal of finding out where X is, but this is a discussion about what you can accomplish with random information input which is a function that\u2019s covered by Lucky Numbers.<br /> <br /> Obviously a Sympathetic use of Space can find where someone is, that\u2019s a pretty clear cut use of Locate Object. I\u2019m not sure how it\u2019s relevant though since it\u2019s long been established that one arcana can often accomplish the same thing as another arcana with the right application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T13:05:04-08:00","id":1178168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178065#post1178065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ugg, slapping on extra reach to existing spells just to make them &amp;quot;work&amp;quot; isnt the right way to go about things. Just use creative thaum and make an entire different spell that does what you want which doesnt require adding reach to existing spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, this wouldn\u2019t be the optimal way, and I agree with Sith_Happens on how Lucky Number is supposed to work, but at the same time I don\u2019t see why adding Reach options wouldn\u2019t work, especially if it could help close distracting discussions at the table. (Then again, I\u2019m pretty lenient with Reach anyway)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T14:28:14-08:00","id":1178197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178102#post1178102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not married to this opinion, but despite having <i>very</i> permissive games, I don't think I'd allow this. Allowing it would imply that the only thing there really <i>is</i> to a Grimoire is writing down instructions, symbols, etc, so if you can perfectly recall them, you can follow it.<br /> <br /> My counter to that implied assumption would be that, if that were the case, you wouldn't need Prime 1 to create a Grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this, The fact you need prime 1 to create a grimiore and not just a pen and some paper. Saying that though, i would probably let them spend exp to learn the rote from a memory they just wouldnt be able to use the mechanical effects from a memory until they spent exp on it or got a proper grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-22-2018, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:32:30-08:00","id":1178257,"title":"","content":"Is there a page reference for Inferior Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:42:43-08:00","id":1178266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178257#post1178257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a page reference for Inferior Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>P82 (characters) -Above the order skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:49:06-08:00","id":1178269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178102#post1178102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My counter to that implied assumption would be that, if that were the case, you wouldn't need Prime 1 to create a Grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even a counter as it is a continuation of the question, but to create a grimoire requires Prime 1 for sure, but I'm not sure that a vision/memory of one actually counts as a grimoire even if it functions as one for the person viewing the vision/memory. You certainly can't have the vision/memory without a real grimoire existing to base it on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T22:52:30-08:00","id":1178371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178266#post1178266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P82 (characters) -Above the order skills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I noticed in Page 84, that talks about limits of untrained Arcana dot raising, is there other penalties for the Inferior Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T02:42:02-08:00","id":1178391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178371#post1178371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed in Page 84, that talks about limits of untrained Arcana dot raising, is there other penalties for the Inferior Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can\u2019t use the Yantra bonus a Verge of your Path provides as an Environment on a spell from your Inferior Arcana.<br /> <br /> Also, any improvised spell from a common or inferior arcana costs a point of mana to cast.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an Index in the back of the book with every relevant page reference by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:00:27-08:00","id":1178627,"title":"","content":"So. Acamoth are sleeping Abyssal entities trapped in the Fallen World, who make deals with mages to ride their Gnostic dreams back to the Astral so they can commune with the Abyss. Represented in 2E with the Goetia rules. <br /> <br /> Wait, Goetia rules? Does that mean they\u2019re not actually in the physical world? So when books talk about them being hidden in the remote and desolate places of the world, those places are actually Astral domains, or possible Synesi? (I was reviewing my previous Legacy conversions, came across the Fangs of Mara, and noticed something doesn\u2019t click right. I may have to do them over...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:08:47-08:00","id":1178631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178627#post1178627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Acamoth are sleeping Abyssal entities trapped in the Fallen World, who make deals with mages to ride their Gnostic dreams back to the Astral so they can commune with the Abyss. Represented in 2E with the Goetia rules.<br /> <br /> Wait, Goetia rules? Does that mean they\u2019re not actually in the physical world? So when books talk about them being hidden in the remote and desolate places of the world, those places are actually Astral domains, or possible Synesi? (I was reviewing my previous Legacy conversions, came across the Fangs of Mara, and noticed something doesn\u2019t click right. I may have to do them over...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Acamoth are trapped in the Astral, not the Fallen. Gulmoth are the ones trapped in the Fallen. Acamoth aren't necessarily asleep either, many of them are pretty active.<br /> <br /> I think Fangs of Mara typically interact with and fight against Acamoth, as opposed to Legion which primarily pact with Gulmoth, because they have to get those spare Abyssal body parts from physical entities.<br /> <br /> For reference, if you've read any of the Dresden Files stuff, there's a particular type of monster that replaces parts of its psyche with Outsiders. That would be a person that's dealing with Acamoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-23-2018, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:11:12-08:00","id":1178632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178631#post1178631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Acamoth are trapped in the Astral, not the Fallen. Gulmoth are the ones trapped in the Fallen. Acamoth aren't necessarily asleep either, many of them are pretty active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought Acamoth were the trapped and sleeping ones, and Gulmoth the summoned and rampaging ones. Faulty categorization, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:15:41-08:00","id":1178635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178632#post1178632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I thought Acamoth were the trapped and sleeping ones, and Gulmoth the summoned and rampaging ones. Faulty categorization, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason I can think of that Abyssal creatures fall asleep at all is because they're beaten into hibernation, in much the same way a discorporated spirit is (Though given the tendency of the Abyss to subvert the rules, there are probably those that don't hibernate even when discorporated or depowered when you'd expect them to be). The Fangs probably prey on the dreams of the ones that do qualify for hibernation though, and then they use those &quot;dreams&quot; to wreak havoc on the rest of them and anyone else that stands in their way.<br /> <br /> Acamoths are very capable of rampaging, it's just that they're limited in their rampages to the Astral, or, you know, the tortured dreams of any Scelesti that decides it's worth the risk to pact with them.<br /> <br /> In a weird way, Acamoths are more approachable, imo, you can make your deal, suffer your horrible consequences and more or less leave them where you found them (Barring future Astral trips). A Gulmoth might follow you home in a more literal sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-23-2018, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:32:58-08:00","id":1178641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178635#post1178635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only reason I can think of that Abyssal creatures fall asleep at all is because they're beaten into hibernation, in much the same way a discorporated spirit is (Though given the tendency of the Abyss to subvert the rules, there are probably those that don't hibernate even when discorporated or depowered when you'd expect them to be). The Fangs probably prey on the dreams of the ones that do qualify for hibernation though, and then they use those &amp;quot;dreams&amp;quot; to wreak havoc on the rest of them and anyone else that stands in their way.<br /> <br /> Acamoths are very capable of rampaging, it's just that they're limited in their rampages to the Astral, or, you know, the tortured dreams of any Scelesti that decides it's worth the risk to pact with them.<br /> <br /> In a weird way, Acamoths are more approachable, imo, you can make your deal, suffer your horrible consequences and more or less leave them where you found them (Barring future Astral trips). A Gulmoth might follow you home in a more literal sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. (And in hindsight, I shouldn\u2019t have expected the Abyss of all things to follow clean rules)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T03:37:07-08:00","id":1178715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178627#post1178627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Acamoth are sleeping Abyssal entities trapped in the Fallen World, who make deals with mages to ride their Gnostic dreams back to the Astral so they can commune with the Abyss. Represented in 2E with the Goetia rules.<br /> <br /> Wait, Goetia rules? Does that mean they\u2019re not actually in the physical world? So when books talk about them being hidden in the remote and desolate places of the world, those places are actually Astral domains, or possible Synesi? (I was reviewing my previous Legacy conversions, came across the Fangs of Mara, and noticed something doesn\u2019t click right. I may have to do them over...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Acamoth were abyss entities in the astral, and Gulmoth were physical? At least in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T04:38:10-08:00","id":1178722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178715#post1178715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Acamoth were abyss entities in the astral, and Gulmoth were physical? At least in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still are, already talked about it, read previous posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:28:29-08:00","id":1178733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178722#post1178722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still are, already talked about it, read previous posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, didnt see them when i replied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:17:53-08:00","id":1178772,"title":"","content":"What's possible in terms of Illusions via Forces? Could you tie in Matter to give them a solid feel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:19:37-08:00","id":1178773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178772#post1178772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's possible in terms of Illusions via Forces? Could you tie in Matter to give them a solid feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by illusions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:26:10-08:00","id":1178775,"title":"","content":"I imagine something like a mirage or an hollogram could be done by manipulating light. If you add Matter at 4 and have Forces at 4 too, you could indeed make it solid. Note that all &quot;living&quot; creatures or people would actually be just moving objects unless you use Life instead of, or in addition to, Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:31:00-08:00","id":1178776,"title":"","content":"I mean Veiling is pretty much nothing but illusions, just saying illusions is incredibly vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T11:18:31-08:00","id":1178873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178776#post1178776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Veiling is pretty much nothing but illusions, just saying illusions is incredibly vague.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah sorry, I meant to be vague as I couldn't recall anything to do with 'illusion' in WoD. Im looking at stuff akin to D&amp;D, for example the traditional car chase where the hero makes a quick right and an illusion drops behind him, making the alley entrance another market stall front.<br /> <br /> I think the question has been answered already, tho my exact situation is that my mage is planning a large feast for a wary band of survivors of a post apoc world, paradox and such aside, I had hoped to do something entertaining with light and sound, heat, etc.. a warm druid grove with bountiful treats within.<br /> <br /> I figure if I have forces (at 3) and matter (at 4), could I not make a solid hologram butler for example? I figure I need mind to give any creation free will, at 5 I suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T11:46:14-08:00","id":1178885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1178873#post1178873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah sorry, I meant to be vague as I couldn't recall anything to do with 'illusion' in WoD. Im looking at stuff akin to D&amp;D, for example the traditional car chase where the hero makes a quick right and an illusion drops behind him, making the alley entrance another market stall front.<br /> <br /> I think the question has been answered already, tho my exact situation is that my mage is planning a large feast for a wary band of survivors of a post apoc world, paradox and such aside, I had hoped to do something entertaining with light and sound, heat, etc.. a warm druid grove with bountiful treats within.<br /> <br /> I figure if I have forces (at 3) and matter (at 4), could I not make a solid hologram butler for example? I figure I need mind to give any creation free will, at 5 I suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that\u2019s because illusions are pretty vague in general being things that appear to be one thing, but are actually another.<br /> <br /> That specific example could be a Space, Matter, or Mind Veiling effect at least.<br /> <br /> As for a holographic butler, first it\u2019s not an illusion unless you\u2019re trying to trick people into believing it\u2019s something it isn\u2019t. I think your best bet is to make a Golem with Matter and then do a graphic overlay with Forces using light to get whatever appearance you want. Maybe a Reach on Golem could allow you to create a Golem out of thin air instead of a statue if the intangibility is that important to you. Yup, no free will though unless you stick some kind of guiding intelligence into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T12:49:52-08:00","id":1178905,"title":"","content":"Plus you can use Mind to create sensory input, that's closer to D&amp;D Ilusion magic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T18:22:47-08:00","id":1179037,"title":"","content":"How much butterfly effect is there supposed to be in this game? The whole &quot;past is written&quot; thing feels like it's <i>trying</i> to answer that but at least to me it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T18:58:34-08:00","id":1179048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179037#post1179037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much butterfly effect is there supposed to be in this game? The whole &amp;quot;past is written&amp;quot; thing feels like it's <i>trying</i> to answer that but at least to me it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Case by case, I think. Depends on how far back to the past you travel, and thus how much of the timeline you unravel and then potentially remake. It\u2019s safe to assume that what the time-travelling mage doesn\u2019t directly mess with will be left alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T02:42:40-08:00","id":1179144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179037#post1179037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much butterfly effect is there supposed to be in this game? The whole &quot;past is written&quot; thing feels like it's <i>trying</i> to answer that but at least to me it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only things directly altered by a Mage who goes back pick up an aura visible to Mage Sight. Since this aura effect doesn\u2019t spread to other things interacted with by those things that do have an aura I think it\u2019s safe to assume that as little as possible changes. This is also backed up by the fact that the further in the past you go the more resistance you get in the form of Temporal Sympathy Withstand. History hates change.<br /> <br /> This has some advantages, one it means the ST doesn\u2019t have to work very hard to figure out the effects of the time travel. Two, it\u2019s much less likely to turn into an ST screw job the way Wish was encouraged to be used in dnd. and that can help maintain trust at the table. Three, this can be used to keep from obviating the actions of your other non-time traveling PCs in most cases, as unless the Mage directly interferes with them they still went and did whatever it was they did in the past as far as it\u2019s possible for them to have done so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T02:27:11-08:00","id":1179466,"title":"","content":"How accurate does a symbolic yantra have to be? Would a stick figure work? Is there any way to disguise your appearance to the level that you cannot be sympathetic yantra'd to death, or would, say, a svelte female who is wearing a disguise that makes her look like a man of 500 lbs be able to targeted via a sketch of her apparent disguise?<br /> <br /> Would a guy who once wore an otherwise indistinguishable Mickey Mouse costume during a bank robbery be able to be targeted via a picture of Mickey Mouse everafter, or would the person drawing an otherwise indistinguishable copy of Mickey Mouse have to envision that particular (otherwise unknown) bank robber as to count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":".  added further example 01-26-2018, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T02:36:17-08:00","id":1179467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179466#post1179466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How accurate does a symbolic yantra have to be? Would a stick figure work? Is there any way to disguise your appearance to the level that you cannot be sympathetic yantra'd to death, or would, say, a svelte female who is wearing a disguise that makes her look like a man of 500 lbs be able to targeted via a sketch of her apparent disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">includes<u><i><b> indirect representations</b></i></u> of the subject drawings, caricatures, or posed and costumed photographs.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I would say a picture of a person in disguise counts as a costumed photograph. It is the person in a costume/disguise after all. Sympathy works on representation so if it represents the target however it looks then it counts. Consider this if the target can say &quot;Yeh this photo/drawing is me in a chicken outfit&quot; then that is a representation of him isnt it?<br /> <br /> Since symbolic sympathetic yantras arnt close enough to the target to gain any bonus when used as a normal yantra this implies they really can be quite crude and are more commonly used as part of sympathetic casting. The actual sympathetic link (the withstand rating) though does the heavy lifting though, the yantra just helps define the target in the imago, it really doesnt matter what the person looks like for the actual withstand rating link part.<br /> <br /> If you have the other half of what is required for a sympathetic casting, ie a sympathetic link to the target (either copied from something or gained normally) then you must already have some idea of who you are casting on, sketching a stick drawming of a fat 500lb man for use as a yantra seems fair enough as its a still representing/focusing them, if somebody else could say when show the picture &quot;Thats a picture of a 500lb guy&quot; (even writing the weight on some scales the fat strawman is standing on) then it'd count. The spell then uses the sympathetic link you have gained and casts the spell through the link on that person whoever she is disguised as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-26-2018, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T02:37:45-08:00","id":1179468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179466#post1179466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How accurate does a symbolic yantra have to be? Would a stick figure work? Is there any way to disguise your appearance to the level that you cannot be sympathetic yantra'd to death, or would, say, a svelte female who is wearing a disguise that makes her look like a man of 500 lbs be able to targeted via a sketch of her apparent disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn\u2019t any real protection from a Symbolic Yantra if the Mage actually knows who they\u2019re targeting. So a disguise will only work for as long as a Mage not knowing who they should actually target.<br /> <br /> The upside of Symbolic Yantras is that they provide no Sympathy to the target and the target cannot be targeted if the Mage has no personal Sympathy to the would be target so if a Symbolic Yantra is all the Mage has then they don\u2019t actually have anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T02:58:08-08:00","id":1179471,"title":"","content":"I would say yes to all of them. As long as it has a mind, it can be affected by Mind.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean a mage can use Mind magic on an intelligent brick the same way they use mind magic on a human. Mages learn to improvise spells and must form an Imago relating to it. They'd have to research intelligent bricks and figure out how the brick became intelligent before working magic on it. This is why obscure rotes and grimoires are valuable. If someone invented a rote that allows Psychic Domination on a brick, then that rote would become very valuable to all mages interested in intelligent brick domination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T02:59:54-08:00","id":1179472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179471#post1179471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say yes to all of them. As long as it has a mind, it can be affected by Mind.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean a mage can use Mind magic on an intelligent brick the same way they use mind magic on a human. Mages learn to improvise spells and must form an Imago relating to it. They'd have to research intelligent bricks and figure out how the brick became intelligent before working magic on it. This is why obscure rotes and grimoires are valuable. If someone invented a rote that allows Psychic Domination on a brick, then that rote would become very valuable to all mages interested in intelligent brick domination.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ???????????","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:05:24-08:00","id":1179473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179471#post1179471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say yes to all of them. As long as it has a mind, it can be affected by Mind.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean a mage can use Mind magic on an intelligent brick the same way they use mind magic on a human. Mages learn to improvise spells and must form an Imago relating to it. They'd have to research intelligent bricks and figure out how the brick became intelligent before working magic on it. This is why obscure rotes and grimoires are valuable. If someone invented a rote that allows Psychic Domination on a brick, then that rote would become very valuable to all mages interested in intelligent brick domination.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn\u2019t appear to relate to anything at all.<br /> <br /> That said though, it\u2019s also wrong, if a brick had a mind, then Mind would work just fine on it. Psychic Domination doesn\u2019t distinguish between intelligences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:18:18-08:00","id":1179475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179473#post1179473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn\u2019t appear to relate to anything at all.<br /> <br /> That said though, it\u2019s also wrong, if a brick had a mind, then Mind would work just fine on it. Psychic Domination doesn\u2019t distinguish between intelligences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would appear that I was answering a question from page 28 of this thread. Must have made a typo when I was typing in the page number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:51:47-08:00","id":1179481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179466#post1179466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a guy who once wore an otherwise indistinguishable Mickey Mouse costume during a bank robbery be able to be targeted via a picture of Mickey Mouse everafter, or would the person drawing an otherwise indistinguishable copy of Mickey Mouse have to envision that particular (otherwise unknown) bank robber as to count?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would need to be a picture of the bank robber in a Mickey Mouse costume, or a drawing of a bank robber in a mickey mouse costume. (mickey mouse holding a gun and drawn in a bank would work). (If a person asked &quot;what does this drawing/picture represent?&quot; and somebody is able to answer &quot;a bank robber dressed in a mickey mouse costume&quot; then thats enough for the yantra to work). As said before its a representation of him. The other part of sympathetic casting (ie the link/withstand rating) does all the actual work. Any random picture of mickey mouse is not a represention of the robber but a picture of the robber in the costume is.<br /> <br /> Owning a picture of the bank robber in a mickey mouse costume on its own wont allow you to sympathetically cast on the robber. You'd need to somehow gain a actual link to him. You could probably borrow a weak link from the photo though as its got a link to the robber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-26-2018, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:48:41-08:00","id":1179766,"title":"","content":"Could you use a design sketch, blueprint or technical drawing of some sort as a Yantra to create the design within the yantra? For example, with Matter 4, I'd like to draw out a small floorplan to be dug out of a stone wall within an old quarry, using state change and shaping, simply making the whole cavity of the floorplan become a gas and shape/guide the stuff elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Could I include Space with Matter to locate all the ferrous metal in a range within a mine, state change into gas and co-locoation it out of the ground and into the caster's immediate area? Pure ore shaped into ingots? Maybe include forces 3 to process the ore directly via magic? Smelting it without a smelter? <br /> <br /> Same kind of deal I guess, could a yantra design of a car or theoretical proto-type nail shotgun be simply created from existing air with a reach from Matter 4?<br /> <br /> Touching on a past question on Matter and Food creation, could a character with matter 4 use a fast food menu or some other representation of a food item to create said food item? Would it actually taste like the item or just be what the caster's idea of it is. If its the actual symbol of the item? Id have to vote that it does taste like the thing it is, via the example of water into wine and how wine is a strong symbol. Though I think the symbol should be the human average idea of the item.. or perhaps it tastes like the best example of itself? Maybe if you had mind, you could infuse a memory into it like how they already include additives, allegedly, into food nowadays. This is more of a role-play question as we are hoping that it has a morale boost for an important npc meeting in a world where luxuries like that are ultra rare.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you all who answer my random weirdness. I really appreciate the straight forward answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T05:04:55-08:00","id":1179795,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1614\" data-vbnamecard=\"1614\">Berdryn</a> design sketches and using menus are fine, but they\u2019re not Yantras. Bright side, even though they provide no dice bonus they\u2019re flavorful.<br /> <br /> If you want to locate all the ferrous metal in a mine you only need Matter. You could co-locate it, or you could just use Shaping to take it out of the ground. You don\u2019t need Forces at all, Matter by itself could process, refine and shape ore. I\u2019ve noticed you have a tendency to over complicate by assuming you need more than one arcana for a task by the way. Typically, you don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> The last question is really something only your ST could answer in terms of what it\u2019s specifically like, but it should certainly be within your power to make good tasting food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T05:23:57-08:00","id":1179797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179795#post1179795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1614\" data-vbnamecard=\"1614\">Berdryn</a> I\u2019ve noticed you have a tendency to over complicate by assuming you need more than one arcana for a task by the way. Typically, you don\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call this 'how to spot someone most familiar with first edition'.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the spells I've looked over for 1E are terribly reliant on conjunctional magic, it's a wonder that anyone was ever actually able to do anything enjoyable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T10:55:50-08:00","id":1179879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1179795#post1179795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1614\" data-vbnamecard=\"1614\">Berdryn</a> design sketches and using menus are fine, but they\u2019re not Yantras. Bright side, even though they provide no dice bonus they\u2019re flavorful.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you could use it as a sacramental Yantra if you destroyed it while casting the spell, which is even more colorful if you do it in the appropriately ritual fashion. There may be a legacy (up to your story teller, there isn't one in RAW) of some sort that uses blueprints etc. as specific Yantra. Or if this sort of floorplan creating behavior isn't a one off for your character, you could be on the way to making one yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:06:17-08:00","id":1179915,"title":"","content":"Thanks again guys. Yeah my knowledge is based on 1e as we learn 2nd, sadly its been more of an annoyance having to relearn stuff. <br /> <br /> Specifically, we are co - STing a game so in part, I am the ST. Though, as for my idea of needing Forces or other arcana just to do something seemed legit as for example, I want to create a hot meal. Would you not need Forces to provide that heat to the transmuted matter or does the transmutation create the heat as it is part of that item's symbol. <br /> <br /> I figured I'd need forces if I wanted something to glow during an Imago, like runes etched into the asphalt around me as I cast something defensive, as another example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T22:57:53-08:00","id":1180352,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've clogged up the Werewolf forum enough with questions about how to make my stupid wolf-blooded mage character work, so here's a question for the mage perspective: <br /> <br /> When a werewolf is doing their &quot;unstoppable killing machine&quot; frenzy thing, attempts to &quot;influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty.&quot; This is obviously intended for when a power involves a contested roll (stat+tolerance vs stat+tolerance+raging bonus) but no Awakened magic uses contested rolls (except for clash of wills, but the werewolf forum already decided that a clash isn't appropriate since it's not &quot;two powers clashing&quot; as much as &quot;calming down a rampaging werewolf is storming hard). So how would this actually work for the mage? A direct die penalty on the casting roll seems equally out of place. Increasing the werewolf's Withstand somehow is clunky. Or does the mage just ignore it can cast like normal because &quot;Magic&quot;? Is Clash of Wills the only thing that makes sense? Clash of Wills is the only thing that makes sense, isn't it...<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T23:35:08-08:00","id":1180355,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if summoned Supernal Entities can return to the Supernal World prior to the ending of the summoning?<br /> <br /> e.g. if they're in real trouble and need to leave otherwise they risk destruction, or if the summoner is completely and totally unwilling or unable to complete their Trial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T00:10:41-08:00","id":1180358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180352#post1180352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've clogged up the Werewolf forum enough with questions about how to make my stupid wolf-blooded mage character work, so here's a question for the mage perspective:<br /> <br /> When a werewolf is doing their &quot;unstoppable killing machine&quot; frenzy thing, attempts to &quot;influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty.&quot; This is obviously intended for when a power involves a contested roll (stat+tolerance vs stat+tolerance+raging bonus) but no Awakened magic uses contested rolls (except for clash of wills, but the werewolf forum already decided that a clash isn't appropriate since it's not &quot;two powers clashing&quot; as much as &quot;calming down a rampaging werewolf is storming hard). So how would this actually work for the mage? A direct die penalty on the casting roll seems equally out of place. Increasing the werewolf's Withstand somehow is clunky. Or does the mage just ignore it can cast like normal because &quot;Magic&quot;? Is Clash of Wills the only thing that makes sense? Clash of Wills is the only thing that makes sense, isn't it...<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it's not contested, the attempt is penalized thusly. At least the mage is rolling. It'd take a -4 to target the pattern of something in size 7, coupled with the primal urge penalties. So yes, it'd be pretty hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T00:12:16-08:00","id":1180359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180352#post1180352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've clogged up the Werewolf forum enough with questions about how to make my stupid wolf-blooded mage character work, so here's a question for the mage perspective: <br /> <br /> When a werewolf is doing their &quot;unstoppable killing machine&quot; frenzy thing, attempts to &quot;influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty.&quot; This is obviously intended for when a power involves a contested roll (stat+tolerance vs stat+tolerance+raging bonus) but no Awakened magic uses contested rolls (except for clash of wills, but the werewolf forum already decided that a clash isn't appropriate since it's not &quot;two powers clashing&quot; as much as &quot;calming down a rampaging werewolf is storming hard). So how would this actually work for the mage? A direct die penalty on the casting roll seems equally out of place. Increasing the werewolf's Withstand somehow is clunky. Or does the mage just ignore it can cast like normal because &quot;Magic&quot;? Is Clash of Wills the only thing that makes sense? Clash of Wills is the only thing that makes sense, isn't it...<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a Clash? Strange. I love Clashes. <br /> <br /> Anyway, in that case the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge won\u2019t have an effect on the mage\u2019s Mind spells to calm them down, unless you employ a house rule to make it so. \u201cUse the Supernatural Tolerance trait if it is higher than the standard Withstand rating\u201d seems popular. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the raging werewolf is in Gauru form... Gauru increases Size beyond 5. IIRC, that means the mage needs to spend a Reach for Advanced Scale. And did Gauru increase Resolve and/or Composure? My Werewolf lore is fuzzy at the moment. If those two are increased, depending on the intent of the spell, the mage may face an increased Withstand rating. <br /> <br /> Lastly, I highly doubt an average mage will survive long enough to cast a calming spell in front of a raging werewolf anyway. Or that a given mage will have enough Mind magic in the first place. So making the calming spell bypass Primal Urge if the mage manages to cast it doesn\u2019t seem too unfair.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reading Malus\u2019 reply and the exact wording of the Werewolf rule again, I see there\u2019s a strong case for Primal Urge penalizing spellcasting after all, despite spellcasting rolls usually being unaffected by penalties originating from the subject\u2019s natural properties. ST call territory, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-29-2018, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T00:13:46-08:00","id":1180360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180355#post1180355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if summoned Supernal Entities can return to the Supernal World prior to the ending of the summoning?<br /> <br /> e.g. if they're in real trouble and need to leave otherwise they risk destruction, or if the summoner is completely and totally unwilling or unable to complete their Trial?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don\u2019t remember if they can explicitly do so, them being unable to is stranger. I\u2019d at least allow leaving early if the Trial is botched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T00:27:27-08:00","id":1180362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180358#post1180358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if it's not contested, the attempt is penalized thusly. At least the mage is rolling. It'd take a -4 to target the pattern of something in size 7, coupled with the primal urge penalties. So yes, it'd be pretty hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I always forget about how increased size gives you a defacto Withstand bonus...Although now I'm have a fridge logic moment as to why that works if it's targeting the mind and not the body...Whatever. Thanks for the responses!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T03:39:12-08:00","id":1180374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180355#post1180355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if summoned Supernal Entities can return to the Supernal World prior to the ending of the summoning?<br /> <br /> e.g. if they're in real trouble and need to leave otherwise they risk destruction, or if the summoner is completely and totally unwilling or unable to complete their Trial?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as they\u2019re in the summoning circle and aren\u2019t being forced to stay they can leave again at any time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:41:39-08:00","id":1180493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180362#post1180362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I always forget about how increased size gives you a defacto Withstand bonus...Although now I'm have a fridge logic moment as to why that works if it's targeting the mind and not the body...Whatever. Thanks for the responses!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Withstand bonus; that\u2019d come from the Resolve/Stamina/Composure bonus that the form would give. The mage is forced to use Advanced Scale and probably sacrifice a few dice to affect things of Size 6 and above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T14:52:45-08:00","id":1180510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180493#post1180493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not Withstand bonus; that\u2019d come from the Resolve/Stamina/Composure bonus that the form would give. The mage is forced to use Advanced Scale and probably sacrifice a few dice to affect things of Size 6 and above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware, hence &quot;defacto&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Affecting something size 7 is -4 dice, just as if you took -4 to increase potency by 2. So, assuming you (the mage) remember to account for it, size 7 is mechanically equivalent to their (the werewolf's) Withstand being 2 higher (unless you Reach for Advanced Scale, in which case it's 1 higher). Probably good to clarify this for anyone who didn't know what I was referring to though. Also, for reference, a werewolf in war form gets +2 Stamina but no bonuses to Resolve/Composure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T18:24:43-08:00","id":1180564,"title":"","content":"A much-delayed read on a thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1094104#post1094104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books section on Mage Sight contains the following example, which i am struggling to understand, was hoping you guys could help.<br /> <br /> <i>Concealment magic, of whatever type, can hide a target from Active Mage Sight, but only if the concealment would logically mask the target from the purview of the Arcanum in question. Even then, if the concealment power uses the same magical principles as the detecting Arcanum, the mage still has a chance to see through it. <b>For example, a light-based invisibility spell would conceal a target from Mind Sight, but Life Sight could still detect the living being, with or without the assistance of photons. </b></i><br /> <br /> If Life Sight could detect an invisible mage by picking up on his lifesigns, why on earth does Mind Sight not have a chance to pick up on the presence of a sentient mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Follow along logically from the Periphery's &quot;any supernatural attempt at concealment hides the effect from the mage&quot; and recall the specification that &quot;the mage can only determine the symbols related to phenomena within her senses&quot; \u2014 if Mind Sight can't let you see an unmanifested Goetia without the benefit of the Attainment, it's certainly not going to tell you that there's a mind occupying the space where you can't see a person, but Life Sight deals with an entire class of phenomena for which camouflage is a natural ability and which exists as part of a wider ecosystem; breathing and having a temperature are both things that Life Sight can pick up on that have no bearing on light-based occlusion or the question of whether or not you're a thinking being.<br /> <br /> Active Sight lets you take something you can perceive and extrapolate a bit more out of it, but it's not a universal revelatory lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T01:11:16-08:00","id":1180637,"title":"","content":"Wow thats a blast from the past, thanks for digging that out and coming up with an answer. Personally that logic doesn't appeal to me. To me if I have a supernatural power that detects sentient minds and another supernatural power is hiding one from me, a Clash of Wills is the correct and simplest answer. My solution at my table is that I will broadly allow just about any Active Mage Sight to clash a veiling spell, as a clever player can make an argument for just about any combination of Sight vs Veil (assuming its a person being concealed at least). It also helps stop veiling spells like Supernal Veil, Incognito Presence etc being the solution to everything without making them worthless. <br /> <br /> Thats just my personal take of course, but its been working for me so far. Thanks again for answering!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T20:53:37-08:00","id":1180997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1180352#post1180352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've clogged up the Werewolf forum enough with questions about how to make my stupid wolf-blooded mage character work, so here's a question for the mage perspective:<br /> <br /> When a werewolf is doing their &quot;unstoppable killing machine&quot; frenzy thing, attempts to &quot;influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty.&quot; This is obviously intended for when a power involves a contested roll (stat+tolerance vs stat+tolerance+raging bonus) but no Awakened magic uses contested rolls (except for clash of wills, but the werewolf forum already decided that a clash isn't appropriate since it's not &quot;two powers clashing&quot; as much as &quot;calming down a rampaging werewolf is storming hard). So how would this actually work for the mage? A direct die penalty on the casting roll seems equally out of place. Increasing the werewolf's Withstand somehow is clunky. Or does the mage just ignore it can cast like normal because &quot;Magic&quot;? Is Clash of Wills the only thing that makes sense? Clash of Wills is the only thing that makes sense, isn't it...<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd rule Gauru form adds twice the Primal Urge to the normal Withstand rating for resisting such things rather than penalizing the dice. That fits the model of Withstand perfectly, after all. It's not magically contested, but they <i>are</i> a deadly rage monster so it isn't easy to be sufficiently comprehensive. Bonus: That way, the spell might snap into effect the moment they shift forms rather than prevent it from taking place. <br /> <br /> I think they probably intended a penalty to activation die pools, but the Withstand notion is a better fit here.<br /> <br /> (Ed.: Well, hmm. I reread the rules and that's not technically what it says. I could have sworn there was a detail about a reduction of Withstand un-penalizing the Potency of the effect. Huh. Well, still, in p114, Withstand: section: &quot;If a spell must overcome some aspect of its subject to take full effect, it will list a Withstand rating in its description...&quot; That's absolutely what the werewolf trait describes, so I stand by that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 01-31-2018, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T22:28:21-08:00","id":1181020,"title":"","content":"I may have overlooked this in the book but how hard is it to become a master in an arcanum?<br /> <br /> What is a reasonable amount of time, on average, for mage to take a common arcanum like Space from 3 to 5? <br /> <br /> Would it make sense to go from 0 to 3 Forces in 3 months time, if the xp was available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:09:45-08:00","id":1181048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181020#post1181020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have overlooked this in the book but how hard is it to become a master in an arcanum?<br /> <br /> What is a reasonable amount of time, on average, for mage to take a common arcanum like Space from 3 to 5? <br /> <br /> Would it make sense to go from 0 to 3 Forces in 3 months time, if the xp was available?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s as fast as the XP is available. Taking a common arcana past the 4th dot requires a Mentor to train you, same goes for Inferior past the 3rd dot.\u2019","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T03:10:58-08:00","id":1181062,"title":"","content":"Regarding werewolf, why are you changing the rule instead of using it as is? It does not increase Withstand, it just applies a penalty to the spellcasting roll same as with any other power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:03:55-08:00","id":1181081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181062#post1181062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding werewolf, why are you changing the rule instead of using it as is? It does not increase Withstand, it just applies a penalty to the spellcasting roll same as with any other power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not thenate, but IIRC the RAI behind Withstand mechanics was that it makes no sense for a subject's natural qualities to penalize spellcasting rolls, because spellcasting is all in the mage's head. Dice penalties to spellcasting thus only represent something that disrupts that inner focus required to build an Imago.<br /> <br /> But Primal Urge is a supernatural quality, not a natural one, so I'd say it's a grey area. I wouldn't mind Primal Urge times two being added to Withstand, even if it makes even only moderately powerful werewolves in Kuruth practically impossible to mind-control. That way mages will have to wait until Kuruth runs out, just like everybody else who has to deal with raging werewolves.<br /> <br /> Of course, all this hangs on the assumption that Kuruth vs. mind-control magic doesn't use Clash of Wills, in which case the penalty becomes much smoother to apply. For me, this trumps the above ruling.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait. We\u2019re talking about Withstand, not spellcasting roll penalties. How did I manage to confuse the two?? Please ignore what I just said and move along.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aaaand we got word of god while I was typing that edit. Nice to see something confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-31-2018, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:14:25-08:00","id":1181083,"title":"","content":"If you insist on using a penalty as a Withstand level - and in most cases you shouldn't, so this is a judgement call, halve the dice penalty rounding up. A withstand level effectively eats a raise in a spell's Potency, which is -2 dice.<br /> <br /> *Doubling* a penalty is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:24:28-08:00","id":1181402,"title":"","content":"I ask forgiveness should this question have already been asked, but what do Proximi use for Clash of Wills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:37:29-08:00","id":1181406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181402#post1181402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask forgiveness should this question have already been asked, but what do Proximi use for Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they just get Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:46:19-08:00","id":1181410,"title":"","content":"I considered this too, but it felt wrong... I mean, with less XP a Proximi can have a CoW equal to a Master Mage. Seems kind of... unfair to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T11:25:29-08:00","id":1181446,"title":"","content":"Pure Willpower? Absolutely not, I think. Clash of Wills doesn't automatically use the activation dice pool. It's just a coincidence that mages use the same dice pool as their unmodified casting dice pool. A CoW dice pool is supposed to be Power Rating (Arcanum for mages) + Supernatural Advantage (Gnosis for mages). If the power has no rating a fitting Attribute is used instead. Proximi does have ratings on their powers, so the first part would be the dot rating of the Blessing they've cast.<br /> As for the second part; that would be up to the individual table. I'm personally in the camp that they simply don't have anything standing in for Supernatural Advantage (as that would make the maximal dice pool 9, including WP expenditure and a Reach for Advanced Potency), but there exists one other precedent in the VtR book Half-Damned. Dhampir substitute Supernatural Advantage with their Resolve.<br /> <br /> Related to all of this we really, really need official rules or guidelines on handling CoW when not playing a major splat. This has been lacking since GMC Rules Update was first released several years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-01-2018, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T11:45:32-08:00","id":1181454,"title":"","content":"Hey Tessie,<br /> <br /> I considered that as well, but like you, I struggled with coming up for the SA. I would guess maybe Resolve would work here, but I agree, we really need much more clarification on these things and with more Minor Templates being created/used it would be very nice to have some type of &quot;This is what you do&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T20:19:28-08:00","id":1181555,"title":"","content":"I don't understand dedicated magical tools.<br /> <br /> Suppose my tool is a glass bauble, I want to cast incognito presence where it can represent transparency and so not being seen when using it as a yantra does it<br /> <br /> 1. Occupy 1 slot to reduce paradox by 2 and give a +1 bonus<br /> 2. One slot for paradox reduction and another yantra slot for the +1?<br /> <br /> If I instead want to cast levitate for which my dedicated tool is not representative at all does it<br /> 1. Only do paradox reduction<br /> 2. Paradox reduction and yantra bonus<br /> 3. Not do anything due to not being representative of levitation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T20:50:10-08:00","id":1181558,"title":"","content":"Another question, is it possible to dismiss a spell warped by the abyss?<br /> <br /> For example if a mage casts a spell to strike her enemies blind, gets a paradox which uses its reach to also strike her friends blind would she simply be able to take an action to reduce the target back to only her enemies, dismiss the spell entirely or would she have to dispel it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T22:26:30-08:00","id":1181576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181555#post1181555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand dedicated magical tools.<br /> <br /> Suppose my tool is a glass bauble, I want to cast incognito presence where it can represent transparency and so not being seen when using it as a yantra does it<br /> <br /> 1. Occupy 1 slot to reduce paradox by 2 and give a +1 bonus<br /> 2. One slot for paradox reduction and another yantra slot for the +1?<br /> <br /> If I instead want to cast levitate for which my dedicated tool is not representative at all does it<br /> 1. Only do paradox reduction<br /> 2. Paradox reduction and yantra bonus<br /> 3. Not do anything due to not being representative of levitation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure devs have clarified that &quot;using&quot; your dedicated tool always gives you paradox reduction without any additional requirements (does not take a slot or require symbolic appropriateness). <br /> <br /> As an addition, you can use it as a yantra with the same restrictions as an order or path tool (takes one slot and probably requires some symbolic connection to the spell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T22:34:48-08:00","id":1181578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181558#post1181558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, is it possible to dismiss a spell warped by the abyss?<br /> <br /> For example if a mage casts a spell to strike her enemies blind, gets a paradox which uses its reach to also strike her friends blind would she simply be able to take an action to reduce the target back to only her enemies, dismiss the spell entirely or would she have to dispel it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. RAW wouldn't seem to indicate a loss of spell control. The caster definitely wouldn't be able to dismiss anomalies not directly tied to the spell, though. At the very least, the ST could spend a reach or two to remove the spell completely from the caster' control. <br /> <br /> It is, however, very easy to argue that, RAI the spell is tainted, so the mage couldn't reduce the target factor to no longer include their friends without dismissing it entirely. <br /> <br /> Good question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T22:46:48-08:00","id":1181579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181578#post1181578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. RAW wouldn't seem to indicate a loss of spell control. The caster definitely wouldn't be able to dismiss anomalies not directly tied to the spell, though. At the very least, the ST could spend a reach or two to remove the spell completely from the caster' control.<br /> <br /> It is, however, very easy to argue that, RAI the spell is tainted, so the mage couldn't reduce the target factor to no longer include their friends without dismissing it entirely.<br /> <br /> Good question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that all viable options that keep the spell active on the intended targets take an instant action suggests to me that 2e's equivalent of a Havoc Paradox is not in itself meant to be an ongoing threat so much as a somewhat-common minor thing that can snowball in the wrong circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:13:25-08:00","id":1181647,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Paradox, I have a question concerning this topic as well.<br /> <br /> What is the Wisdom score used to determine the Paradox anomalies from those invoked by Imbued Item? Sure, it is simple enough for a Mage using it, but what about a Sleeper/Sleepwalker/Werewolf/Vampire? Should Integrity/Harmony/Humanity be substituted for Wisdom to determine duration? Should it be treated as Wisdom 0 since they lack Wisdom?<br /> <br /> I know it is 1 die, thus a 33% chance of happening, but it can happen yet there are no rules on the duration of the anomaly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T09:29:51-08:00","id":1181684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181647#post1181647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Paradox, I have a question concerning this topic as well.<br /> <br /> What is the Wisdom score used to determine the Paradox anomalies from those invoked by Imbued Item? Sure, it is simple enough for a Mage using it, but what about a Sleeper/Sleepwalker/Werewolf/Vampire? Should Integrity/Harmony/Humanity be substituted for Wisdom to determine duration? Should it be treated as Wisdom 0 since they lack Wisdom?<br /> <br /> I know it is 1 die, thus a 33% chance of happening, but it can happen yet there are no rules on the duration of the anomaly.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gut reaction is to use the Wisdom of the creator from the moment the item was created (for anyone using the item, including other mages). Don't go accepting candy from Mad wizards kids!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T11:23:02-08:00","id":1182027,"title":"","content":"Do Proximi get any free spell factor steps based on the level of the Blessing? I.e getting +2 Potency for a Potency-primary 3 dot blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T11:43:49-08:00","id":1182034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182027#post1182027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Proximi get any free spell factor steps based on the level of the Blessing? I.e getting +2 Potency for a Potency-primary 3 dot blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T12:45:52-08:00","id":1182050,"title":"","content":"Yeah I didn't think so, but wanted to be sure I was inferring properly (since they lack Arcana).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T23:32:25-08:00","id":1182190,"title":"","content":"Did we have any details on Abyssal Environmental Tilts? They're mentioned as possible outcomes of Anomalies in Mage 2E core, but that's just it. No examples or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T07:06:53-08:00","id":1182251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182190#post1182190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we have any details on Abyssal Environmental Tilts? They're mentioned as possible outcomes of Anomalies in Mage 2E core, but that's just it. No examples or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far not yet. I imagine it\u2019s stuff like a Wisdom disabler, or that forces Paradox on spells or increases the hazard of them, as well as other totally unnatural, corrosive effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T08:23:59-08:00","id":1182270,"title":"","content":"Is Potency a fixed determined result (damage, duration, etc ) of a spell ?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> A mage is casting a spell Rotting Flesh with Gnosis 1 and Death 3. The mage spents a point of willpower to add 3 dices to the roll. A mage takes a -4 penalty to increase it's potency by 2 points. She also increases the potency of a spell by 3 points (mages are allowed to increase the primary factor up to Highest arcana rating used in the spell).<br /> <br /> This makes a spell of 5 potency and a pool of 3 dices.<br /> <br /> The dice results in 8,9,9. <br /> <br /> Does this mean that the mage deals 5 damage and the bonus success are always making it all or nothing roll ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T08:42:35-08:00","id":1182277,"title":"","content":"You're right. Bonus successes doesn't do anything unless you manage to achieve an Exceptional Success, and then only the effects described. Potency, just like all other factors, is determined before the roll is made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T08:47:35-08:00","id":1182278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182270#post1182270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Potency a fixed determined result (damage, duration, etc ) of a spell ?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> A mage is casting a spell Rotting Flesh with Gnosis 1 and Death 3. The mage spents a point of willpower to add 3 dices to the roll. A mage takes a -4 penalty to increase it's potency by 2 points. She also increases the potency of a spell by 3 points (mages are allowed to increase the primary factor up to Highest arcana rating used in the spell).<br /> <br /> This makes a spell of 5 potency and a pool of 3 dices.<br /> <br /> The dice results in 8,9,9.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the mage deals 5 damage and the bonus success are always making it all or nothing roll ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Already answered but note that free primary spell factors are highest Arcana - (minus) 1. Its just Potency starts at 1 but its important for the other spell factors.<br /> Also remember yantras, you get 1 yantra reflexively so you should always try and use one even if its just your path tool.<br /> <br /> Also note that if the spell had been a praxis it would have been a Exceptional success...(3 instead of 5 successes needed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-04-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T08:59:55-08:00","id":1182281,"title":"","content":"Is there a benefit of getting an Exceptional Success on a spell ? I can't find a single spell that has an exceptional success description in the spell section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T09:14:37-08:00","id":1182284,"title":"","content":"That's because it's on page 115 in the spell casting system section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T09:28:57-08:00","id":1182286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182281#post1182281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a benefit of getting an Exceptional Success on a spell ? I can't find a single spell that has an exceptional success description in the spell section.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most useful are: Ignoring withstand ratings, gaining a condition (steadfast is always good) &amp; regaining mana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T09:29:14-08:00","id":1182287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182278#post1182278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already answered but note that free primary spell factors are highest Arcana - (minus) 1. Its just Potency starts at 1 but its important for the other spell factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duration ansd Scale also start at 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:09:31-08:00","id":1182402,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is a simple question, but is there anything about the nature of Awakening that prevents a Mage who never meets any other Mages or other folks who can see their magic for what it is from just assuming he's schizophrenic? I mean, everyone else seems to have logical explanations for any magic he says he's done.<br /> <br /> Also, does making prophecies in the presence of Sleepers cause Paradox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:26:38-08:00","id":1182410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182402#post1182402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is a simple question, but is there anything about the nature of Awakening that prevents a Mage who never meets any other Mages or other folks who can see their magic for what it is from just assuming he's schizophrenic? I mean, everyone else seems to have logical explanations for any magic he says he's done.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to conceptualize what you want to do inside your head, and will it to happen to cast a spell, so... unlikely?<br /> <br /> I suppose Banishers, the type that retains Integrity instead of Wisdom, certainly think so. <br /> <br /> EDIT: And wouldn\u2019t it be less \u201ceveryone has alternate logical explanations\u201d and more \u201ceveryone is apparently amnesiac or in need of therapy?\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, does making prophecies in the presence of Sleepers cause Paradox? </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say it depends on how it\u2019s delivered. Phrasing it as intuitive leaps of logic, secret sources of information, big data analyses, and deduction from advanced theories will hide it. Going all Oracle of Delphi, booming with divine voice and halo will not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:40:26-08:00","id":1182417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182410#post1182410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And wouldn\u2019t it be less \u201ceveryone has alternate logical explanations\u201d and more \u201ceveryone is apparently amnesiac or in need of therapy?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how good they are at rationalizing it probably, which would be likely dependent on how high their Integrity is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T16:03:13-08:00","id":1182421,"title":"","content":"Depends on whether the prophecy itself is Supernal, and whether delivering the prophecy is part of the spell rather than the spell imparts the prophecy and you just recite it.<br /> <br /> If you have a specific situation in mind you'd have to describe it in order to get a proper answer instead of &quot;depends on X, Y and/or Z&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T18:52:49-08:00","id":1182468,"title":"","content":"For space mage armor &quot;if the character successfully dodges an attack the player can spend one point of mana to redirect the attack to another applicable target. The attack hits with successes equal to the mages space arcanum rating&quot;<br /> <br /> 1) Does dodging an attack require to take the dodge action IE forgoing ones turn?<br /> <br /> 2) Can this be done for multiple attacks per turn?<br /> <br /> 3) What is an applicable target? Someone whom the shooter could have shoot or someone whom the mage could potentially fire a weapon at?<br /> <br /> 4) So Mr untouchable with a defense of 10 that applies against firearms would not even get a chance to resist when the mages ally shot the mage in order to allow the mage to redirect the shoot thus circumventing the defense?<br /> <br /> 5) In the case of some fisticuffs someone tries to attack the mage are they a valid target for having their fist redirected back to themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T23:35:55-08:00","id":1182511,"title":"","content":"1. Well, yes. How do you expect to dodge without dodging?<br /> <br /> 2. Not unless you're capable of dodging multiple attacks each turn, with every redirected attack costing one Mana so you're also subject to your Mana per turn limits.<br /> <br /> 3. The former, I'm pretty sure.<br /> <br /> 4. That would require the mage also being able to dodge the attack, with the risk of failing and getting shot by their ally. I would not allow the use of this attainment on attacks without any successes (before comparing successes).<br /> <br /> 5. I wouldn't say so, but others might run it differently. I can very much see the appeal of such a humorous incident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T09:41:43-08:00","id":1182632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182468#post1182468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For space mage armor &quot;if the character successfully dodges an attack the player can spend one point of mana to redirect the attack to another applicable target. The attack hits with successes equal to the mages space arcanum rating&quot;<br /> <br /> 1) Does dodging an attack require to take the dodge action IE forgoing ones turn?<br /> <br /> 2) Can this be done for multiple attacks per turn?<br /> <br /> 3) What is an applicable target? Someone whom the shooter could have shoot or someone whom the mage could potentially fire a weapon at?<br /> <br /> 4) So Mr untouchable with a defense of 10 that applies against firearms would not even get a chance to resist when the mages ally shot the mage in order to allow the mage to redirect the shoot thus circumventing the defense?<br /> <br /> 5) In the case of some fisticuffs someone tries to attack the mage are they a valid target for having their fist redirected back to themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie has a pretty good grasp on how I would rule it, but I thought I would lend my opinion on some of the questions you asked.<br /> <br /> #2. Yes, this should be possible since dodging is applicable against multiple attacks, but as Tessie pointed out you need to have the mana per turn limit to handle this.<br /> <br /> #3. I would say anyone within a Space Rating yard radius of you would be an applicable target. That is just how I would rule it anyway.<br /> <br /> #4. This one is a tricky one and I agree with Tessie's interpretation on this as well, but I think the intent would be use the Mage's Space Rating as a die pool to make an attack rather than it just being automatic successes since that seems way overpowered to begin with.<br /> <br /> #5. I agree with Tessie here as well, but you can also change the direction of a bullet from a gun to &quot;straight to the attacker&quot;, so this would be possible in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T10:05:29-08:00","id":1182640,"title":"","content":"#3 I would rule an applicable target is anybody in los of the mage that the mage could attack him/herself. Since the attack is redirected from him viable targets should be from him. It doesnt mention range though, one assumes you cant just pick a target a mile off but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4720\" data-vbnamecard=\"4720\">Taldorblackfire</a>'s space rating in yards sounds way to short esp if you are shot from further than that. Perhaps reduce the attack successes by range from the mage as if he was the shooter..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T21:01:38-08:00","id":1182797,"title":"","content":"Are supernatural beings (e.g.- vampires) Sleepwalkers? There are a few parts of the appendix that seem to contradict each other on that even if they obviously aren't Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T22:22:14-08:00","id":1182816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182797#post1182797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are supernatural beings (e.g.- vampires) Sleepwalkers? There are a few parts of the appendix that seem to contradict each other on that even if they obviously aren't Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Anything with a supernatural merit is also considered a sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:14:32-08:00","id":1182852,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, what did you read that seemed to contradict that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:19:32-08:00","id":1182854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182632#post1182632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2. Yes, this should be possible since dodging is applicable against multiple attacks, but as Tessie pointed out you need to have the mana per turn limit to handle this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the wording of the rules does allow the dodging of multiple opponents normally, but it completely disregards the usual turn order where each attack is both declared and resolved before the next attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-06-2018, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T06:11:34-08:00","id":1182888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182854#post1182854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the wording of the rules does allow the dodging of multiple opponents normally, but it completely disregards the usual turn order where each attack is both declared and resolved before the next attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wont each attack still be declared and resolved before the next still? The person dodging is just giving up their action by dodging before his init turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T07:11:00-08:00","id":1182899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182852#post1182852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, what did you read that seemed to contradict that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The part saying that &quot;Any character possessing <b>Integrity</b> and a Supernatural Merit that reflects an internal talent or inborn ability is immune to the Curse.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T07:18:58-08:00","id":1182902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182888#post1182888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wont each attack still be declared and resolved before the next still? The person dodging is just giving up their action by dodging before his init turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I figured it out. It's both a bit inelegant and not actually written in the rule, but i guess you roll your Dodge dice pool multiple times with a cumulative penalty for each attacker. I assumed you only roll once as is how actions usually are resolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T07:23:10-08:00","id":1182906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182899#post1182899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part saying that &amp;quot;Any character possessing <b>Integrity</b> and a Supernatural Merit that reflects an internal talent or inborn ability is immune to the Curse.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Sleepwalker is a mortal specific state, other supernatural splats not suffering from Quiescence doesn\u2019t indicate that they\u2019re Sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:09:31-08:00","id":1182972,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras Companion does say that Mummies are treated as Sleepwalkers at least for quiescence and such. I've always taken the 'any supernatural template' bit to be separate from the integrity + merit bit, so any supernatural counts as a Sleepwalker for the sake of spell holding and merits. I mean, even Sleepers can technically hold spells (it's just a terribad idea).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T11:30:46-08:00","id":1182994,"title":"","content":"If there is an old picture or video recording of something being concealed with magic how would that interact with Mage sight? It should cause a clash when viewed with active mage sight right? But, is there anyway it could trigger peripheral mage sight? I'm trying to lay some breadcrumbs for my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T12:01:14-08:00","id":1183009,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it'd depend on the nature of the concealment, and perhaps what was being concealed. If it was pure physical invisibility, such that the camera simply couldn't record the phenomenon, I'd say no. If it has to purely physical concealment, you could have an Investigation roll to reveal something like &quot;this looks photoshoped&quot;. But if the photo/recording itself is warded, or it's some kind of active effect keeping people from seeing it, that would definitely Clash. And if it's Abyssal in origin, make their Mage Sight go crazy.<br /> <br /> Edit: hang on, just realized you were asking about peripheral sight specifically...hm normally concealment effects don't trigger peripheral, otherwise they wouldn't be very good at concealment. But if it wasn't really meant for concealment, and just so happens to work to keep people seeing it, that could trigger it. Again, it partially depends on how the concealment works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 02-06-2018, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T12:04:44-08:00","id":1183011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182994#post1182994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is an old picture or video recording of something being concealed with magic how would that interact with Mage sight? It should cause a clash when viewed with active mage sight right? But, is there anyway it could trigger peripheral mage sight? I'm trying to lay some breadcrumbs for my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't reveal anything actually, it might reveal something if it was recorded via that Prime spell in the SoS spoilers. The exception would probably be if there was a Veiling spell cast on the medium that portrayed a supernatural event itself, if the proper Mage Sight was applied.<br /> <br /> So, I think you'll either have to make the supernal event more obvious (Hidden only by Quiesence from Sleepers), or under the direct influence of a spell of some sort.<br /> <br /> In either case, unless there's an actual supernatural event happening via viewing the medium, I don't think PMS would trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T12:09:34-08:00","id":1183013,"title":"","content":"Another thought. You could say the photograph/recording itself picked up some residual mojo from what-ever-it-was, and that's what's pining their Sight. Like, if the picture is of a ghost, the camera happened to get some ectoplasm or whatever smudged on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T15:03:15-08:00","id":1183052,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this counts as a simple question, but. . .<br /> <br /> I have this fragment of a memory of living spells: essentially spells that had taken on a life and even sentience of their own, and like float around and affect hapless passers-by with whatever piece of magic they represent. Does anyone know what book that's from? Or did I just completely make it up just think it's part of the Mage setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T15:39:40-08:00","id":1183068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1183052#post1183052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this counts as a simple question, but. . .<br /> <br /> I have this fragment of a memory of living spells: essentially spells that had taken on a life and even sentience of their own, and like float around and affect hapless passers-by with whatever piece of magic they represent. Does anyone know what book that's from? Or did I just completely make it up just think it's part of the Mage setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a synthesis of self-sustaining spells from Dynamics and the Tulpas of Mad Ones, but otherwise I don't recall anything in that vein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T16:20:31-08:00","id":1183083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1183068#post1183068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a synthesis of self-sustaining spells from Dynamics and the Tulpas of Mad Ones, but otherwise I don't recall anything in that vein.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I did a bit of research, and I think what I was actually thinking of was <a href=\"http://eberron.wikia.com/wiki/Living_Spell\" target=\"_blank\">something from D&amp;D</a>. Ah well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T09:47:57-08:00","id":1183287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1182468#post1182468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For space mage armor &quot;if the character successfully dodges an attack the player can spend one point of mana to redirect the attack to another applicable target. The attack hits with successes equal to the mages space arcanum rating&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) In the case of some fisticuffs someone tries to attack the mage are they a valid target for having their fist redirected back to themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is plausible <i>without</i> magic, so why not when bending space?<br /> <br /> (ed. note: The <i>damage</i> inflicted is mostly conserved if you simply dodge unexpectedly. This doesn't lead to a punch landing a <i>punch</i>, necessarily, but it does deliver a similar jolt to the body due to momentum and impulse. Generally, jabs and crosses won't redirect to jabs and crosses, but uppercuts and roundhouses might by simply extending the arcs. Stabs and slashes more frequently result in stabs and slashes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  clarity 02-07-2018, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:38:30-08:00","id":1183330,"title":"","content":"Well, here's a couple questions that will make it obvious which supplement I just read:<br /> <br /> 1) Do Pangeans trigger Paradox normaly when they use their Arcana?<br /> <br /> 2) And/or do they get unlimited reach like a Supernal entity?<br /> <br /> 3) Also, is there any particular reason why a Pangean's casting pool is Rank + Arcana? That's going to be a much smaller pool than an equivalent Supernal entity's Power+Finesse. *confused face*<br /> <br /> 4) Would this post be better if I let my computer auto-correct &quot;Pangeans&quot; to &quot;Penguins&quot;?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T12:56:20-08:00","id":1183357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1183330#post1183330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here's a couple questions that will make it obvious which supplement I just read:<br /> <br /> 1) Do Pangeans trigger Paradox normaly when they use their Arcana?<br /> <br /> 2) And/or do they get unlimited reach like a Supernal entity?<br /> <br /> 3) Also, is there any particular reason why a Pangean's casting pool is Rank + Arcana? That's going to be a much smaller pool than an equivalent Supernal entity's Power+Finesse. *confused face*<br /> <br /> 4) Would this post be better if I let my computer auto-correct &quot;Pangeans&quot; to &quot;Penguins&quot;?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 &amp; 2 are directly related concepts. There is no mention of a different system for Pangean Arcana use and they are not supernal entities, so the normal casting rules seem to apply. (At absurd ranks, they might start to use the same sort of crazy rules that spirits do.)<br /> <br /> 3: They still get their full dose of Numina and Influence. Pangeans aren't hurting for power.<br /> 4: Yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T14:03:46-08:00","id":1183373,"title":"","content":"I know that any Major Template doesn't play well with any other supernatural source of power, but is it possible to stack Minor Templates? For instance, is it possible for someone to simultaneously be a Proximus, a Wolf-Blooded and a Stigmatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23822-zinay","name":"zinay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T15:04:09-08:00","id":1183398,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything officially ruling it out. Personally, I'd Rule of Cool it. If the character concept and backstory worked, I'd let a player stack minor templates. That said, I know from personal experience that crossing gamelines in play can be tricky (corruption of themes and all that). Also, more than two templates does seem to be getting a little silly.<br /> <br /> Concerning Proximus and Wolf-blooded specifically, an idea crossed my mind for a Proximus Dynasty that was also an entire family of wolf-bloods. Mechanically, I'd roll their Tell into the family curse for simplicity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T15:18:36-08:00","id":1183407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zinay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1183373#post1183373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that any Major Template doesn't play well with any other supernatural source of power, but is it possible to stack Minor Templates? For instance, is it possible for someone to simultaneously be a Proximus, a Wolf-Blooded and a Stigmatic?</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers expressed that templates aren\u2019t an in-universe thing. Just something for convenience of writing and playing the games. Which means there\u2019s no real ban on template stacking. <br /> <br /> But the trick lies in making the stacking look at least plausible, which is where I believe most ideas get sunk. If you can get past that, then great. <br /> <br /> Oh, and a lot of the semi-official template stacking seems to spawn things that are markedly different from both \u2018ingredients,\u2019 or add one\u2019s elements to the another, instead of straight-up combining them. Like the infamous Admonitoria, or possibly the Tremere Liches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T23:01:43-08:00","id":1183484,"title":"","content":"It all depends on the purpose of stacking templates. If a ST wants to throw a curve ball at some PC's who think they know it all then sure i can see a hybrid template doing that. But if its a PC just wanting to stack templates for power sthen that is for me is a huge red flag and i probably shouldnt allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T03:41:12-08:00","id":1183538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zinay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1183373#post1183373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that any Major Template doesn't play well with any other supernatural source of power</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly not the case any longer in 2E per Word of God","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T07:25:42-08:00","id":1184392,"title":"","content":"If someone uses Sever Oath to alter (but not destroy) a magical oath that another person has taken, does this trigger a Clash of Wills against the original caster of Sworn Oaths? Further, does the mage who originally cast Sworn Oaths know that the oath was altered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T08:23:56-08:00","id":1184406,"title":"","content":"Yes and Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T11:31:59-08:00","id":1184455,"title":"","content":"1. For what can mages use ectoplasm created by death arcana ?<br /> 2. In a combat situation how can a mage defend against a Forces 4 Thunderbolt spell with potency 7 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T15:20:39-08:00","id":1184528,"title":"","content":"For question 2:<br /> <br /> Alter Conductivity (Matter 3) can make a mage resistant to electric damage up to Potency (maybe Potency 7?). Forces Mage Armor would do the same. There are a million spells to make one intangible (Death 3, Ghost Gate), or to jump to another realm (Spirit), or to create a Space separate from the chaos outside world (Space, Ban, etc.) or to allow mages to pre-empt or reverse other actions (Time). Counter Spell would also work, as would any spells to remove Clouds from the sky by altering the weather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T17:17:12-08:00","id":1184563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1184455#post1184455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. For what can mages use ectoplasm created by death arcana ?<br /> 2. In a combat situation how can a mage defend against a Forces 4 Thunderbolt spell with potency 7 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) It can be used for what the Ectoplasmic shaping spell uses it for. A mirror to see ghosts/twilight things and create the open condition for ghosts on. He can create it himself with the ectoplasm spell (before this he needs to find it another way) and then he can also then use shape epherera to make it into a rating 2 weapon or 2 points or armor, only useful vs twilight things though but still handy sometimes.<br /> <br /> 2) <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5279\" data-vbnamecard=\"5279\">Amravanti</a> Thunderbolt channels ambient energies and doesnt require a cloud or to be outside to work.(your thinking of the call lightning spell), Alter Conductivity reduces electrical damage by 2 per potency, so 4 should be enough to reduce thunderbolt, however the spell is only called thunderbolt but describes it as ambient energy so might not be electrical, however the reach for AC makes it include all energy so i think that would definitely work.<br /> <br /> <br /> I find the best way to avoid everything is colocate with the +2 reach for 2 reflexive moves, also keyed to only yourself or allies. Its alot of extra reach but being able to reflexively pop up, smack somebody then reflexively pop away and your opponent not being able to do anything is highly frustrating,bonus points if you make yourself visible from either location so your opponents can see their attacks pass right through you. This requires being prepped beforehand though..<br /> <br /> Counterspell will also potentially work, either with prime or forces. Here the potency of the spell doesnt matter its just a gnosis + arcana vs gnosis + arcana.<br /> <br /> The problem with being in twilight/ jumping into the spirit realm etc is that you'd have to win init and do it before he gets his spell off.<br /> <br /> He cant cast on you if he cant see/sense you (barring space 2 etc), so anything that can create a opaque barrier between you and him would also potentually work,Ban, creating/shaping/moving a wall/object with matter? Making it dark, blinding him (though he can prob still use other senses maybe) but again these all require acting before him and setting stuff up again.<br /> <br /> Really the best chance if not able to have things prepared before he casts is counterspell. Its here that N+1 obv becomes useful. Counterspell uses your action too, but if you have another mage with you then one can counter and the other can cast offensive things and obv 2 v 1 its highly likely the 2 will win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-10-2018, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T17:27:36-08:00","id":1184569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1184392#post1184392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone uses Sever Oath to alter (but not destroy) a magical oath that another person has taken, does this trigger a Clash of Wills against the original caster of Sworn Oaths? Further, does the mage who originally cast Sworn Oaths know that the oath was altered?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1184406#post1184406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly negating the oath via Sever Oath wouldnt trigger a CoW's though right, the only reason it triggers one when you try to change it is because of two effects trying to do the same thing and only one can be in place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-10-2018, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T18:11:43-08:00","id":1184575,"title":"","content":"That was my reasoning, and given that a mage always knows when their spells are being Clashed with, they would know something is up. Good point on the negation thing, I really didn't consider it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T18:14:54-08:00","id":1184577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1184575#post1184575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my reasoning, and given that a mage always knows when their spells are being Clashed with, they would know something is up. Good point on the negation thing, I really didn't consider it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably better to negate it then put your own on after then rather than alter somebody elses. Though A mage can detect when one of his spells is dispelled right so probably can sense when its severed. His spell control will return at least so i assume mages at least sense that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-10-2018, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T23:55:39-08:00","id":1184650,"title":"","content":"My mistake. You're right, I thought he was referring to Call Lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 02-11-2018, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T04:26:34-08:00","id":1184693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1184577#post1184577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably better to negate it then put your own on after then rather than alter somebody elses. Though A mage can detect when one of his spells is dispelled right so probably can sense when its severed. His spell control will return at least so i assume mages at least sense that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they had relinquished it, yeah, you are right. I can't remember if is actually stated as plainly as the thing about the spells clashing, but I assume a mage does have an instinctual knowledge of their Spell Control limits, so they know when they are going to push past its limits or when they are no longer sustaining a spell that's been dispelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T12:20:04-08:00","id":1185302,"title":"","content":"How does healing magic interact with sleepers in regards to paradox? I assume you might be able to skirt around it with a clever 2 or 1 dot effect, but I'm assuming all 3 dot or greater practices will probably cause it.<br /> <br /> Similarly curing something dramatic like cancer or ebola with magic might be very likely to cause paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T12:49:38-08:00","id":1185309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185302#post1185302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does healing magic interact with sleepers in regards to paradox? I assume you might be able to skirt around it with a clever 2 or 1 dot effect, but I'm assuming all 3 dot or greater practices will probably cause it.<br /> <br /> Similarly curing something dramatic like cancer or ebola with magic might be very likely to cause paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might risk (not cause) Paradox, but once the cure is in there\u2019s nothing there for Dissonance to unravel unless you\u2019ve done something like Regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T13:05:00-08:00","id":1185315,"title":"","content":"If the spell introduces a mundane cure it won't cause paradox. If the spell itself is a cure that works over time you might encounter some Quiescence IF you can't pass it of as mundane medication or treatment. If the cure is instantaneous you'll encounter Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T13:44:31-08:00","id":1185329,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, most healing effects of the &quot;no, you didn't take three lethal&quot; variety are lasting, so Dissonance won't undo them. But you will roll Paradox, and the Sleeper you healed will experience a Breaking Point and Quiescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T13:56:10-08:00","id":1185335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185329#post1185329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, most healing effects of the &quot;no, you didn't take three lethal&quot; variety are lasting, so Dissonance won't undo them. But you will roll Paradox, and the Sleeper you healed will experience a Breaking Point and Quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, this gives me an idea for a future story arc. Stories will come filtering in of a 'miracle worker' going around healing the blind and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","user":"Enlightened_Milkman","date":".  Grammar is hard. 02-12-2018, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T19:43:32-08:00","id":1185460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185335#post1185335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, this gives me an idea for a future story arc. Stories will come filtering in of a 'miracle worker' going around healing the blind and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, If its obvious magic and quiescence is involved then all sleeper parties will forget and not be able to spread stories? Sleepwalkers are gossips!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T20:09:42-08:00","id":1185469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185460#post1185460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, If its obvious magic and quiescence is involved then all sleeper parties will forget and not be able to spread stories? Sleepwalkers are gossips!!!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pentacle Magicians are always afraid of those who speak of &quot;creating&quot; Sleepwalkers, because you never really know what will drive them over the edge of Sleeperdom, of or sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T04:59:27-08:00","id":1185546,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked before, but I cannot find it anywhere.<br /> <br /> How do AOE spells interact with touch/self range? I've always played it such that the origin point for the AOE must be yourself or somewhere within arm's reach (which will probably still include you in the area of the spell anyway). But could you, for example, originate the edge of your area at your fingertip, thus excluding yourself from the area of the spell?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T05:35:36-08:00","id":1185549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185546#post1185546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been asked before, but I cannot find it anywhere.<br /> <br /> How do AOE spells interact with touch/self range? I've always played it such that the origin point for the AOE must be yourself or somewhere within arm's reach (which will probably still include you in the area of the spell anyway). But could you, for example, originate the edge of your area at your fingertip, thus excluding yourself from the area of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T05:55:54-08:00","id":1185552,"title":"","content":"Are a Mage's attempts to teleport a target rendered ineffective if the target exists in multiple planes simultaneously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T06:04:16-08:00","id":1185553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185552#post1185552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are a Mage's attempts to teleport a target rendered ineffective if the target exists in multiple planes simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, though depending on how that works you might only move one part of their existence. For instance if a Mage is in the Astral and you teleport their body it won\u2019t move their dream form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T07:09:08-08:00","id":1185569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185552#post1185552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are a Mage's attempts to teleport a target rendered ineffective if the target exists in multiple planes simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way do you mean &quot;exist in multiple planes simultaneously&quot;? An example would both be useful and interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T07:27:48-08:00","id":1185572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185546#post1185546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been asked before, but I cannot find it anywhere.<br /> <br /> How do AOE spells interact with touch/self range? I've always played it such that the origin point for the AOE must be yourself or somewhere within arm's reach (which will probably still include you in the area of the spell anyway). But could you, for example, originate the edge of your area at your fingertip, thus excluding yourself from the area of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Covered way back in the day:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=943564#post943564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any part of the area has to be within touch / sensory range, not all of it. You can make D&amp;D like cones if you want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T08:30:58-08:00","id":1185588,"title":"","content":"I figured it had been addressed somewhere, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T08:49:06-08:00","id":1185597,"title":"","content":"Question: What type of Demesne is formed when Mages from multiple different paths work together to make a larger Demesne? Which Supernal Realm should it be symbolically linked to, if any? If the Demesne is big enough, could they in theory deck out individual rooms to their tastes in order to make them semiotically suitable for all the different types of spell they would want to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T17:32:53-08:00","id":1185783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185569#post1185569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what way do you mean &quot;exist in multiple planes simultaneously&quot;? An example would both be useful and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something or someone that is bleeding through or traveling from one realm to another. Or someone in their dream realm while their body is in the physical realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T18:05:00-08:00","id":1185789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185783#post1185783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something or someone that is bleeding through or traveling from one realm to another. Or someone in their dream realm while their body is in the physical realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I answered the question of a dream body, results might differ depending on the state of the subject and other realm interactions though or the arcana of the Mage attempting the transportation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T18:07:27-08:00","id":1185790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185597#post1185597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: What type of Demesne is formed when Mages from multiple different paths work together to make a larger Demesne? Which Supernal Realm should it be symbolically linked to, if any? If the Demesne is big enough, could they in theory deck out individual rooms to their tastes in order to make them semiotically suitable for all the different types of spell they would want to cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s kind of up to the ST. Presumably, though you could create a Demesne with varying areas amenable to Mages of multiple Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T09:07:43-08:00","id":1185969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TriCitiesLodge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185783#post1185783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something or someone that is bleeding through or traveling from one realm to another. Or someone in their dream realm while their body is in the physical realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fun part about mage is that I still have three different answers depending on the way this travelling works. I'm assuming that it can't <br /> If it's through a portal (or through two geographically connected locations) then it depends on whether the teleport spell would be able to affect both sides of the portal. If a spirit is partway through the gauntlet it should be no problem teleporting the entire spirit to your target location. However, a Supernal entity that's in the process of being summoned is partway in a realm (or &quot;realm&quot;) that can't normally be affected or reached by non-Imperial magic, and probably can't be teleported since you shouldn't be able to teleport Supernal entities directly from the Supernal Realms.<br /> But there could also be a fringe cases where you can't affect one end of the entity but the other is not geographically tied to any location. Perhaps an entity from a Lower Depth that is in the process of clawing its way through to the Fallen at a random location. In that case you could rule that a teleport spell would teleport the part of the entity that's already in the Fallen, but doing so wouldn't literally or metaphysically bisect the entity so it would just resume its efforts at the new location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:43:21-08:00","id":1186006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1185969#post1185969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case you could rule that a teleport spell would teleport the part of the entity that's already in the Fallen, but doing so wouldn't literally or metaphysically bisect the entity so it would just resume its efforts at the new location.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it did literally or metaphysically bisect an entity, teleport would be so nerfworthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T02:19:01-08:00","id":1186589,"title":"","content":"The answers I come up with for interpreting the multiple locations is essentially this: (Sorry if it's off. I'm sleepy)<br /> <br /> A. Anything not covered by the cope of the spell cast isn't affected. You'd need Mind and Reach, at least, to move an astral entity as part of a teleport spell. (probably better as a Combined Spell) Similarly, if the mage can't reach past the Gauntlet, grabbing any pieces out there shouldn't work very well. It might, though, move them if physical location is meaningful to both the state that they are in and the spell as cast.<br /> <br /> B. Related to scope: You'd need to target each piece. If you can, since they are one entity, that would mostly mean that you'd normally need Sympathy to target all the parts. If you did, you should be able to define their location in the singular, pulling them back together. <br /> <br /> C. If you don't target multiple parts, the targeted part is the only part moved. If you do, the penalty should build from the most difficult and build from there.<br /> <br /> That's how I'd handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T13:07:58-08:00","id":1187339,"title":"","content":"Does Withstanding a spell require a roll or the Withstanding rating acts as a constant ?<br /> <br /> For example if spell with withstand composure is cast with Potency 3 and the target has Composure 2. Does the target roll his composure or just removes 2 potency from the spell ?<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Do all spells start at standard spell casting (ritual) ? Meaning if you want to cast a spell as instant you always have to spend reach ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1013,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","user":"Stralos","date":". 02-18-2018, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T13:17:59-08:00","id":1187341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187339#post1187339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Withstanding a spell require a roll or the Withstanding rating acts as a constant ? <br /> <br /> For example if spell with withstand composure is cast with Potency 3 and the target has Composure 2. Does the target roll his composure or just removes 2 potency from the spell ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T13:30:15-08:00","id":1187344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187339#post1187339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Withstanding a spell require a roll or the Withstanding rating acts as a constant ?<br /> <br /> For example if spell with withstand composure is cast with Potency 3 and the target has Composure 2. Does the target roll his composure or just removes 2 potency from the spell ?<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Do all spells start at standard spell casting (ritual) ? Meaning if you want to cast a spell as instant you always have to spend reach ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) The later, meaning final Potency of the spell is just 1. If the Composure had been 3, reducing Potency to 0, it would have no effect.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, fortunately you always have at least 1 Free Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-18-2018, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T22:53:51-08:00","id":1187465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187339#post1187339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Withstanding a spell require a roll or the Withstanding rating acts as a constant ?<br /> <br /> For example if spell with withstand composure is cast with Potency 3 and the target has Composure 2. Does the target roll his composure or just removes 2 potency from the spell ?<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Do all spells start at standard spell casting (ritual) ? Meaning if you want to cast a spell as instant you always have to spend reach ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Note that this also means that if the targets composure/withstand trait is later raised (via willpower or another spell for example) then that might reduce the potency of the spell to 0 and it no longer affects that target. Another note is that you need to actually be aware a spell is being cast on you before you can use willpower to increase a resistant trait, which depending on the spell may or may not let folk do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T09:05:19-08:00","id":1187571,"title":"","content":"Since a Mage and their familiar share a Connected Sympathy (I.e. if the familiar is there then so is the Mage for all intents and purposes when casting except Reach must be spent as if remote viewing), is the reverse true? For instance could a distant familiar use the Sign Numina to send a message to their Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T09:52:34-08:00","id":1187584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187571#post1187571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since a Mage and their familiar share a Connected Sympathy (I.e. if the familiar is there then so is the Mage for all intents and purposes when casting except Reach must be spent as if remote viewing), is the reverse true? For instance could a distant familiar use the Sign Numina to send a message to their Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregard this post.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\">That's not how Connected Sympathy works. You still need to cast Sympathetically meaning you need to spend a Mana and use a sympathetic Yantra. Unless the familiar has a way to use Numina sympathetically (which would be rare but certainly not out of the question for ephemerals with Space or Sympathy as an Influence) they wouldn't be able to use them on the Connected mage unless they're actually present.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-19-2018, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T10:02:58-08:00","id":1187585,"title":"","content":"From the book: &quot;The entity and its bonded mage have a Connected Sympathetic link to one another, may use one another\u2019s senses with a reflexive action (casting magic through a Familiar requires a Reach for remote viewing, but does not require the Sympathetic Range Attainment)&quot;<br /> <br /> I agree that it is only one way though, unless the Familiar has a long range Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 02-19-2018, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T10:08:12-08:00","id":1187590,"title":"","content":"Right. I forgot that part of the Familiar Condition and focused on Connected. In that case it would be if the familiar has a way of using Numina through remote viewing, which oddly enough seems less likely than being able to use Numina/Influences sympathetically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:13:45-08:00","id":1187706,"title":"","content":"Does the &quot;treat Awakened Status like Resources&quot; note in Consilium/Order Status interact with the &quot;raise Availability by one to procure a service within a day instead of a week&quot; specification on the page that section references?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:36:47-08:00","id":1187711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187706#post1187706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the &quot;treat Awakened Status like Resources&quot; note in Consilium/Order Status interact with the &quot;raise Availability by one to procure a service within a day instead of a week&quot; specification on the page that section references?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been treating it as though it does in my game. My logic being that scarcity in mage society is less about logistics or access to material and more about placating the egos of people that can summon stuff from the other side of the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T12:05:59-08:00","id":1187930,"title":"","content":"What would be needed to call a lightning bolt down from a storm, solidify it and use a portion of it as a whip or another form of weapon? <br /> <br /> Im guessing alchemist's touch essentially to keep the energy from killing the mage. What discipline though to shape and harness it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Question 2: Is there a way to channel the power of a lightning bolt into mana? Maybe like some mix of forces and prime? It was mentioned that this would be used to make some sort of mana battery for casting on the go lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T12:20:04-08:00","id":1187935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187930#post1187930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be needed to call a lightning bolt down from a storm, solidify it and use a portion of it as a whip or another form of weapon?<br /> <br /> Im guessing alchemist's touch essentially to keep the energy from killing the mage. What discipline though to shape and harness it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Question 2: Is there a way to channel the power of a lightning bolt into mana? Maybe like some mix of forces and prime? It was mentioned that this would be used to make some sort of mana battery for casting on the go lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Shaping and using it as a weapon would probably be a forces 3 weaving spell, altering the property of the electricity to become &quot;stable&quot; and keep a shape. You'd need some other spell to protect you from it though like alchemists touch or another creative forces shielding spell.<br /> <br /> As for lightning into mana, i would say no. Mundane lightning has no mana/magical power so i wouldnt allow it. If it were possible then it would be used to turn power sockets into mana chargers..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T13:14:22-08:00","id":1187949,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there an old Prime spell in 1e that allowed you to turn Structure into Mana from an object? If so, couldn't the same principle be used to turn energy (ie. lightning) into Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T13:17:05-08:00","id":1187951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187930#post1187930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 2: Is there a way to channel the power of a lightning bolt into mana? Maybe like some mix of forces and prime? It was mentioned that this would be used to make some sort of mana battery for casting on the go lol</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> is right about the first part, but wrong on the second. You could Pattern lightning into mana with a Forces+Prime 4 spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T13:25:31-08:00","id":1187956,"title":"","content":"That makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T13:36:36-08:00","id":1187959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187949#post1187949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there an old Prime spell in 1e that allowed you to turn Structure into Mana from an object? If so, couldn't the same principle be used to turn energy (ie. lightning) into Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was. The fact it got removed and wasnt replaced suggests that gaining mana from mundane stuff is harder or not possible in 2e anymore. Mana is reasonably harder to get in 2e over 1e. (artifacts dont regain 1 per day etc etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:07:52-08:00","id":1189129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1187959#post1187959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was. The fact it got removed and wasnt replaced suggests that gaining mana from mundane stuff is harder or not possible in 2e anymore. Mana is reasonably harder to get in 2e over 1e. (artifacts dont regain 1 per day etc etc)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, yeah I was thinking something similar as the next question was a combo imbued spell.. though I am not quite sure how that works, we haven't done it.. but could you make the imbued item that had call lightning / prime 4, the idea here would be to pump the mana storage and the item would simply call lightning to itself to take that charge in as mana. I don't think it should be a 1:1 conversion.. but maybe, its mage so why couldn't it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T04:54:48-08:00","id":1189195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189129#post1189129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, yeah I was thinking something similar as the next question was a combo imbued spell.. though I am not quite sure how that works, we haven't done it.. but could you make the imbued item that had call lightning / prime 4, the idea here would be to pump the mana storage and the item would simply call lightning to itself to take that charge in as mana. I don't think it should be a 1:1 conversion.. but maybe, its mage so why couldn't it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, an item imbued to do this would need to be imbued with (at least) two spells. The first spell would be Call Lightning, the second spell would be Forces 4+Prime 4 to convert the lightning to mana, you would get 1 point of mana per point of Potency in that spell. That conversion spell also needs Duration though or the mana will convert back to lightning before you can use it. Also don\u2019t forget there\u2019s an upper limit on how much mana you can store in an imbued item dependent on the number of extra successes you roll during the imbuing.<br /> <br /> You know though, this plan requires double adepthood, and you have to get lucky with storms. I suppose you could blast your container with Thunderbolt though.<br /> <br /> What I have to wonder though is, why aren\u2019t you just concentrating on Hallows? They already generate stored mana in the form of Tass which saves you from a significant amount of effort, and with Prime 4 you could go around finding dormant Hallows and getting mana out of them by waking them back up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T11:13:31-08:00","id":1189269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imbued items are granted a single spell. </div> </div> </div>Do combined spells only count as one spell for spell control purposes OR one spell in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T09:04:28-08:00","id":1189414,"title":"","content":"Does mage armour stack with regular armour ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T10:13:18-08:00","id":1189426,"title":"","content":"Yes. Explicitly so, I believe.<br /> <br /> Edit: Most types of Mage Armor doesn't even grant Armor rating. Can't find anything about stacking those that grant actual armor, but I still think they stack since they grant both magical and mundane armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-25-2018, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T10:48:05-08:00","id":1189431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189414#post1189414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does mage armour stack with regular armour ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. (characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:16:31-08:00","id":1189439,"title":"","content":"I'm been thinking about Combined Spells recently. They seem cool in theory, but the downsides seem to often outweigh the benefits. <br /> <br /> Can someone please give me an example of a genuinely useful Combined Spell? Something beyond mere utility would be nice; less along the lines of &quot;I combined Read Thoughts with Detect Emotions&quot; and more along the lines of &quot;Walking with the Sun&quot; (mass Clone spell)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T14:05:39-08:00","id":1189462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189439#post1189439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm been thinking about Combined Spells recently. They seem cool in theory, but the downsides seem to often outweigh the benefits.<br /> <br /> Can someone please give me an example of a genuinely useful Combined Spell? Something beyond mere utility would be nice; less along the lines of &quot;I combined Read Thoughts with Detect Emotions&quot; and more along the lines of &quot;Walking with the Sun&quot; (mass Clone spell)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I frequently employ Shielding Practices of different types together: Wards &amp; Signs w/ Mental Shield is a classic morning ritual to keep safe. Or, I combine different Unveiling to enhance my Sleepwalker's sight with Interconnections and Supernal Vision, in order to be a better second set of eyes for me. Though, I've yet to use it in some way such as your other example. Maybe Accelerate Growth on a tree, with Shadow Crafting to also make its much larger shadow a weapon as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T14:15:01-08:00","id":1189463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189439#post1189439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm been thinking about Combined Spells recently. They seem cool in theory, but the downsides seem to often outweigh the benefits. <br /> <br /> Can someone please give me an example of a genuinely useful Combined Spell? Something beyond mere utility would be nice; less along the lines of &amp;quot;I combined Read Thoughts with Detect Emotions&amp;quot; and more along the lines of &amp;quot;Walking with the Sun&amp;quot; (mass Clone spell)</div> </div> </div> </div>Utility *is* what Combined Spells are for... maybe you\u2019d be better off looking for conjunctional spells? Like a Forces 4 + Life 4 spell that turns you digital, allowing you to hack someone\u2019s computer with your barehands. I dunno what Walking with the Sun is, but a Mass Cloning spell sounds like a Life + Mind or Space spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T16:20:45-08:00","id":1189489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189414#post1189414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does mage armour stack with regular armour ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A decent potency Aegis spell + Matter mage armor is very nice, and can make even a starting Moros a literal tank. (partly because you only need to focus on general armor, the mage armor gives you AP immunity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-25-2018, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T18:27:14-08:00","id":1189505,"title":"","content":"Walking with the Sun was a rote in Mage 1e<br /> <br /> It was more along the lines of a Devotion (opposed to Discipline) for Mages: a &quot;conjunctional&quot; spell, I guess, that required Life 5, Mind 5, Space 4, Optional Matter 3 or 5 (I think that was it, not 100% sure)<br /> <br /> It cloned the Mage per success, teleporting the clones anywhere in the world. Virtual 1-man army, with the ability to flip between clones for the purpose of casting spells (your soul could inhabit any of the clones, but only 1 at a time. switching was reflexive), shared mana pool. With optional matter, you could copy existing equipment with 3, or create new equipment per clone with 5.<br /> <br /> It was pretty insane for a Master spell, but the requirements were sky high. Closest thing to an Archmaster spell outside being an Archmage, imo... we need more spells like this in 2e, which is why I asked for some cool examples. I'm probably thinking &quot;conjunction&quot; spells, though...<br /> <br /> It was pretty hilarious in a 1v1 situation: all the sudden the Big Bad is staring down 6 dudes instead of the lone Mage, and gets bum-rushed by 5 clones + you, with &quot;you&quot; being any of the 6. Sure, they couldn't cast except for 1, but an AoE strength buff was enough to have these Legacy-attainment, brawl 5 clones to grapple and beat down pretty much anyone in a normal game (the only real threat besides a &quot;Greater Being&quot; was another Multi-Master Mage). <br /> <br /> But yeah, if you've made it that far along as a Mage, you deserve that kind of power. That same Mage casting WwtS was once upon a time someone who couldn't even outheal the DPT of his Werewolf and Vampire teammates. But the smallest minnows often grow to be the biggest fish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 02-25-2018, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T18:44:11-08:00","id":1189507,"title":"","content":"That would definitely be a conjunctional spell. Not a combined spell. Combined spells are not one spell using effects from multiple Arcana. Combined spells are literally just two different spells that you cast simultaneously.<br /> The benefits are: less casting time, simultaneous effects, less spell control needed, less Mana spent on Spell Factors, and less Willpower spent if relinquishing the combined spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T19:36:06-08:00","id":1189514,"title":"","content":"So at 8 hours for a solid night's rest and a repeating activation of 3 hours for gnosis 1, a disciple of life could theoretically fit 88 hours of rest into 24 with the knit spell. At that rate one would have a week of rest in slightly less than 2 days. Would this count for healing aggravated damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T02:36:03-08:00","id":1189564,"title":"","content":"Probably down to ST fiat. It says you get the equivalent of a good night's sleep and regain a point of Willpower. I think the point of the effect is to regain Willpower. Healing Aggravated damage is a Patterning effect. Of course, Time could do something like this much more obviously at Time 3... so probably up to the ST. Personally I would not allow it since the main intent of the Knit Reach effect is Willpower regain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T04:54:44-08:00","id":1189575,"title":"","content":"There is no way increasing healing times would be the intent of that Reach. In that case you'd heal up to 12 bashing using that Reach in addition to what you heal using Potency. If you want to increase healing times, use a spell that increases actual healing times instead of a Reach that's most likely intended to just shunt out stress and tiredness.<br /> <br /> Edit: 48 bashing, actually. I'm just used to our house rule of healing one bashing per hour instead of 15 minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-27-2018, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T05:08:41-08:00","id":1189577,"title":"","content":"What happens when a Sleeper witnesses magic in 2nd edition? I know a paradox manifests but I didn't find any rules about it in the 2nd edition book pertaining a Sleeper actually witnessing magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T05:16:53-08:00","id":1189579,"title":"","content":"Everything about that is written in the section about Sleepers starting on page 298 in the Supporting Cast appendix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T10:00:51-08:00","id":1189620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189577#post1189577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a Sleeper witnesses magic in 2nd edition? I know a paradox manifests but I didn't find any rules about it in the 2nd edition book pertaining a Sleeper actually witnessing magic</div> </div> </div> </div>When a sleeper witnesses obvious magic, they add 1 dice to the mages paradox pool. (as per the table on page 115). Then depending on the number of people this then gains a dice trick, 8,9 or rote action for &quot;a few&quot;, &quot;a large group&quot; and &quot;full crowd&quot; (I really hate the non definate woolly descriptions in 2e, arguing over what a campus' size is stupid)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T12:15:23-08:00","id":1189653,"title":"","content":"So, Granny Weatherwax has a neat trick that allowed her to act as if she was invincible by displacing wounds through time. It seems like a simple Temporal Stutter, but is it? Also, how would you set it up so that the spell to shunt damage into the future is already active before you take the damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T12:42:40-08:00","id":1189663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189653#post1189653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Granny Weatherwax has a neat trick that allowed her to act as if she was invincible by displacing wounds through time. It seems like a simple Temporal Stutter, but is it? Also, how would you set it up so that the spell to shunt damage into the future is already active before you take the damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cast it as a combined spell with Hung Spell using the Fate Lesser Utility Attainment to add a Conditional Duration is how I'd do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T13:23:05-08:00","id":1189676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189663#post1189663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cast it as a combined spell with Hung Spell using the Fate Lesser Utility Attainment to add a Conditional Duration is how I'd do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesnt need to be combined with hung spell, you can cast hung spell first then put the &quot;ignore damage till later&quot; spell into it, but yep conditional duration will work, but only the first time.<br /> <br /> It could just be a effect of the spell that &quot;while under the effects of this spell all damage taken is ignored until the spell ends&quot; which is very powerful, maybe add some other drawbacks like cant gain willpower, or mana etc, make it an advanced/weaving version of veil of moments, sorta maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T14:55:39-08:00","id":1189704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189676#post1189676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Doesnt need to be combined with hung spell, you can cast hung spell first then put the &quot;ignore damage till later&quot; spell into it, but yep conditional duration will work, but only the first time.<br /> <br /> It could just be a effect of the spell that &quot;while under the effects of this spell all damage taken is ignored until the spell ends&quot; which is very powerful, maybe add some other drawbacks like cant gain willpower, or mana etc, make it an advanced/weaving version of veil of moments, sorta maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking on it some more, i would also maybe add a &quot;for a number of attacks equal to potency the subject of this spell can ignore all damage. Once the spell ends the subject will take all ignored damage&quot; to limit it abit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T15:14:57-08:00","id":1189707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189704#post1189704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it some more, i would also maybe add a &amp;quot;for a number of attacks equal to potency the subject of this spell can ignore all damage. Once the spell ends the subject will take all ignored damage&amp;quot; to limit it abit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The limit of it from my view is that the damage is only postponed until the spell is over, so you\u2019re pretty susceptible to dispellation, or being forced to end the spell earlier.<br /> <br /> I mostly just wanted to know what Practice to use though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T18:51:35-08:00","id":1189743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189575#post1189575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no way increasing healing times would be the intent of that Reach. In that case you'd heal up to 12 bashing using that Reach in addition to what you heal using Potency. If you want to increase healing times, use a spell that increases actual healing times instead of a Reach that's most likely intended to just shunt out stress and tiredness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually brings up an interesting question. Must the intent of a particular reach effect (or even spell) prevent possible unintended side consequences? Because that kinda seems more interesting in terms of story than making everything strictly just so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T10:51:57-08:00","id":1189927,"title":"","content":"<b>New Q: </b>First edition query, someone is claiming that mages are immune to the possession numen and is getting backing by one other person. Neither has references and I can find no such mention in the books. Have I been missing something for all these years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:05:53-08:00","id":1189938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189743#post1189743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually brings up an interesting question. Must the intent of a particular reach effect (or even spell) prevent possible unintended side consequences? Because that kinda seems more interesting in terms of story than making everything strictly just so.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case it's more about common sense than unintended side effects. Since the main use of the spell is to heal damage, you'd think that a Reach that would instantly heal 32-48 bashing (depending on how long a full night is) would mention that. Hence we can deduce that there is no way the resting Reach affects healing times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-27-2018, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:08:19-08:00","id":1189939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189927#post1189927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>New Q: </b>First edition query, someone is claiming that mages are immune to the possession numen and is getting backing by one other person. Neither has references and I can find no such mention in the books. Have I been missing something for all these years?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they\u2019re definitely wrong.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mages can use a Shielding spell to make themselves immune or highly resistant to Possession though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-27-2018, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:11:17-08:00","id":1190004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189938#post1189938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case it's more about common sense than unintended side effects. Since the main use of the spell is to heal damage, you'd think that a Reach that would instantly heal 32-48 bashing (depending on how long a full night is) would mention that. Hence we can deduce that there is no way the resting Reach affects healing times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the possesion numen in the nwod blue book and book of spirits fail to mention mages being immune. Now ive not looked at 1e in awhile so there might be some obscure reference hidden somewhere in all the 1e books but in the 2+ years i ran a 1e game with a spirit master character in it, it was never established that mages are immune to possession.<br /> <br /> The persons lack of any references is indeed telling..<br /> <br /> oooops wrong quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-27-2018, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:22:07-08:00","id":1190009,"title":"","content":"Good day to you too, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T20:24:56-08:00","id":1190115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1189927#post1189927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>New Q: </b>First edition query, someone is claiming that mages are immune to the possession numen and is getting backing by one other person. Neither has references and I can find no such mention in the books. Have I been missing something for all these years?</div> </div> </div> </div>As said before, they are definitely wrong. Mages are perhaps the least susceptible to it, due to a myriad of spells and attainments that can assist in shielding or shrugging off it's effects, but definitely not immune. I am assuming you're referring to 2nd Edition. It's <i>possible</i> that was 1st Edition thing (but even then I think that was not the case).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T22:14:27-08:00","id":1190149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1190115#post1190115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <i>possible</i> that was 1st Edition thing (but even then I think that was not the case).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's\u2026 <i>possible</i> that they confused &quot;an entity possessing a mage normally gains no access to their powers&quot; from Summoners for a broader immunity? Admittedly that's a bit of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T02:29:51-08:00","id":1190182,"title":"","content":"Or confusing possession with claiming. In 1st great templates like Mage were immune to Claiming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T04:18:51-08:00","id":1190196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1190182#post1190182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or confusing possession with claiming. In 1st great templates like Mage were immune to Claiming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the most plausible. I've made that mistake myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:28:34-08:00","id":1190213,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone is immune to Claiming either in second edition (unless the spalt is explicitly immune to Manifestations; I have a hard time believing Bound from GtSE could be targeted by a second Manifestation). In fact, with current design philosophy I'd suspect a major splat being Claimed would lose the host's supernatural abilities, but develop Dread Powers in line with both the spirit's concept and the host's previous powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T10:25:31-08:00","id":1190330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1190182#post1190182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or confusing possession with claiming. In 1st great templates like Mage were immune to Claiming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, missed that? I read claiming to see too. Where was this stated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T12:35:35-08:00","id":1190387,"title":"","content":"In first ed Claimed was a major template and those couldn't stack. The fluff explanation was that while humans were like soft clay ready to be molded, major templates (Werewolf, Vampire, Mage) were like finished pottery out of the oven, they could not be shaped again, only broken.<br /> <br /> EDIT : of course that's no longer the case as template stacking is not flat out prohibited and Claimed is a Condition anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:52:25-08:00","id":1190450,"title":"","content":"Conditional Trigger + Hung Spell + X: if the condition is met (I get punched in the face), I can trigger X spell to release from Hung Spell, correct? <br /> And if so, does that mean I can also actively cast a spell that turn, because X spell was simply released. not cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T08:09:33-08:00","id":1190672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1190450#post1190450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conditional Trigger + Hung Spell + X: if the condition is met (I get punched in the face), I can trigger X spell to release from Hung Spell, correct?<br /> And if so, does that mean I can also actively cast a spell that turn, because X spell was simply released. not cast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much yes. You can have conditional trigger like &quot;when i take damage&quot;, hung spell and teleport, and teleport away whenever you take damage. I would watch with the trigger get punched in the face though, its rather specific and what if you get punched but arnt hurt?<br /> <br /> &quot;when i take damage&quot;, &quot;when i fall unconsious&quot;, &quot;when i take full bashing or wound penalties?&quot; might be better?<br /> <br /> Note that the conditional trigger will end the hung spell which releases ALL spells held within it.<br /> <br /> Hung spell holding more than 1 spell and releasing them sorta breaks the action economy but it hasnt been much of a problem so far. (mainly due to spell control limits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-01-2018, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T07:38:42-08:00","id":1191341,"title":"","content":"I remember there was a ritual of sorts you had to complete in 1st edition when reaching a 4 or 5 dot in an arcana. How was it called and in what book is it mentioned ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T07:43:42-08:00","id":1191342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1191341#post1191341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember there was a ritual of sorts you had to complete in 1st edition when reaching a 4 or 5 dot in an arcana. How was it called and in what book is it mentioned ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing, nor has there been.<br /> <br /> You might be referring to the fact that you need a mentor to teach you the fifth dot of your common arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T17:30:16-08:00","id":1191486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1191341#post1191341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember there was a ritual of sorts you had to complete in 1st edition when reaching a 4 or 5 dot in an arcana. How was it called and in what book is it mentioned ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be referring to a mage may have to prove he can do X to be called a Adept or Master. Like there is probably tests/trials mages have to go through to prove they are masters etc. But its not really a ritual. And isnt required to actually learn 4-5th dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T01:43:57-08:00","id":1191577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1191486#post1191486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may be referring to a mage may have to prove he can do X to be called a Adept or Master. Like there is probably tests/trials mages have to go through to prove they are masters etc. But its not really a ritual. And isnt required to actually learn 4-5th dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be the thing I am referring to. My memory is vague on this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:24:45-08:00","id":1193617,"title":"","content":"Did the new attainment rules effectively remove always active attainments or can you spend 2 reach (advanced duration + indefinite duration) to make an always active attainment?<br /> <br /> (Without being a very high level attainment at least)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","user":"Bomaz","date":". 03-09-2018, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:28:04-08:00","id":1193619,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly it was too impractical to use Indefinite Duration because of the number of steps on the Duration table to reach Indefinite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:06:24-08:00","id":1193632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1193617#post1193617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the new attainment rules effectively remove always active attainments or can you spend 2 reach (advanced duration + indefinite duration) to make an always active attainment?<br /> <br /> (Without being a very high level attainment at least)</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re better off with Attainments that have Advanced Duration, by the time you become a Master they only need to be renewed once a year which even with a scene long activation is a pretty tiny time sink.<br /> <br /> You could do Indefinite, but you have to account for Reach, and a -10 dice penalty meaning the Potency or Scale would be 1 at best and it wouldn\u2019t really be Indefinite until you became a Master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T02:00:30-08:00","id":1193850,"title":"","content":"If a mage drains ghost of essence (or reduces its essence to 0 in no matter what way) and burns it's whole corpus (e.g. using death 3 spell) is that enough to get rid of the ghost permanently or will be it back next time someone mentions it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","user":"qendi","date":". 03-10-2018, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T05:47:02-08:00","id":1193890,"title":"","content":"What you described is the <i>normal </i>way of killing ghosts. And other ephemerals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:00:31-08:00","id":1194158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1193890#post1193890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you described is the <i>normal </i>way of killing ghosts. And other ephemerals.</div> </div> </div> </div>for me nor al was getti g rid of anchors / exorcising the motherf***** out to Underworld <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> thanks for claryfing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T04:21:40-07:00","id":1194203,"title":"","content":"You're not killing it that way. You're just banishing it to another realm from where it's so difficult to return most ghosts never do.<br /> <br /> Edit: Is returning when mentioned a 1e thing? In this edition if they are discorporated (losing all Corpus but not Essence) they slowly reform at one of their Anchors, with being remembered only slowly reducing the duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-11-2018, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:30:24-07:00","id":1194343,"title":"","content":"The Destiny merit (page 100) drawback mentions Doom. Is this a condition or is it just a fun way of saying, your character has a prophesy/curse on him and it's up for you and a storyteller to figure it out (something similar like the 1st edition did)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T16:16:55-07:00","id":1194387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194343#post1194343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Destiny merit (page 100) drawback mentions Doom. Is this a condition or is it just a fun way of saying, your character has a prophesy/curse on him and it's up for you and a storyteller to figure it out (something similar like the 1st edition did)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little like having a Ban for a spirit, it's an activity that's designed by your ST to be something that you're drawn to do but which will also risk your well being for engaging in it. You're drawn to engage in it because if you fail you get an automatic refresh of all your WP, but your WP is less useful when your Doom is present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T17:14:55-07:00","id":1194399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194343#post1194343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Destiny merit (page 100) drawback mentions Doom. Is this a condition or is it just a fun way of saying, your character has a prophesy/curse on him and it's up for you and a storyteller to figure it out (something similar like the 1st edition did)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chronicles of Darkness presentation of a similar rule likens a Doom to a negative Aspiration. As the Merit goes on to explain, your Doom is a particular tragic outcome their Destiny makes them likely to suffer. Mechanically the Doom becomes more likely because of how it modifies the use of Willpower to add dice when the Doom is in play. So, for example, if your Doom is to burn to death saving another, and you're in a house on fire with someone you care about, spending Willpower wouldn't be as effective on rolls to keep yourself from burning to death, but you could spend it more safely on rolls to get the other person to safety at your own expense. (These rolls don't refresh all Willpower when you fail them, only the point you spent on them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T02:01:36-07:00","id":1194465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194399#post1194399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Chronicles of Darkness presentation of a similar rule likens a Doom to a negative Aspiration. As the Merit goes on to explain, your Doom is a particular tragic outcome their Destiny makes them likely to suffer. Mechanically the Doom becomes more likely because of how it modifies the use of Willpower to add dice when the Doom is in play. So, for example, if your Doom is to burn to death saving another, and you're in a house on fire with someone you care about, spending Willpower wouldn't be as effective on rolls to keep yourself from burning to death, but you could spend it more safely on rolls to get the other person to safety at your own expense. (These rolls don't refresh all Willpower when you fail them, only the point you spent on them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just curious about the scaling of Doom. Since Destiny is a 1 to 5 dot merit, it seems fitting the the more dots you have in it the stronger your Doom gets. Mrmdubois explanation (down bellow) makes perfect sense in this case. It's a bit hard for me to grasp your example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194387#post1194387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a little like having a Ban for a spirit, it's an activity that's designed by your ST to be something that you're drawn to do but which will also risk your well being for engaging in it. You're drawn to engage in it because if you fail you get an automatic refresh of all your WP, but your WP is less useful when your Doom is present.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T05:33:51-07:00","id":1194498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194343#post1194343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Destiny merit (page 100) drawback mentions Doom. Is this a condition or is it just a fun way of saying, your character has a prophesy/curse on him and it's up for you and a storyteller to figure it out (something similar like the 1st edition did)</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T10:31:31-07:00","id":1194570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194465#post1194465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just curious about the scaling of Doom. Since Destiny is a 1 to 5 dot merit, it seems fitting the the more dots you have in it the stronger your Doom gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Doom doesn't &quot;get stronger&quot; the more dots you have in Destiny, because your Destiny does not &quot;get stronger&quot; the more dots you have in it \u2014 Destiny gives you a pool of points to spend on making rerolls or applying the rote quality, neither of which can stack. What Doom does is let you guarantee a number of rolls (up to your Destiny dots per chapter) will only cost you Willpower to enhance them them if they succeed \u2014 in other words, characters with more Destiny dots are encouraged to lean harder into their Dooms because the price of failure is less concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T00:22:33-07:00","id":1194755,"title":"","content":"What practice is it to directly turn a Resonant (X) Condition into Resonant (Y)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T01:57:26-07:00","id":1194767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194755#post1194755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practice is it to directly turn a Resonant (X) Condition into Resonant (Y)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Directly? Sounds like Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T04:10:22-07:00","id":1194787,"title":"","content":"Does the base (non-Reach) effect of the Reaching spell actually do anything when casting at sensory range across the Gauntlet? I kind of feel like it's supposed to let you bypass the Gauntlet Strength Withstand on your other spells but it doesn't actually say that and I can't think of what it would be good for otherwise besides touching things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T05:19:06-07:00","id":1194799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194787#post1194787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the base (non-Reach) effect of the Reaching spell actually do anything when casting at sensory range across the Gauntlet? I kind of feel like it's supposed to let you bypass the Gauntlet Strength Withstand on your other spells but it doesn't actually say that and I can't think of what it would be good for otherwise besides touching things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re poking a hole in the Gauntlet so whatever follows logically from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:13:18-07:00","id":1194825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194787#post1194787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the base (non-Reach) effect of the Reaching spell actually do anything when casting at sensory range across the Gauntlet? I kind of feel like it's supposed to let you bypass the Gauntlet Strength Withstand on your other spells but it doesn't actually say that and I can't think of what it would be good for otherwise besides touching things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirit Summons spell is easier if you have a portal to the shadow nearby. Am i right in thinking that spirits using a iris/portal to cross from the shadowlands to the material arrive in twilight though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:26:06-07:00","id":1194827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194767#post1194767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Directly? Sounds like Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say weaving - it's not a total transformation, it's still Resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:44:39-07:00","id":1194834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194825#post1194825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i right in thinking that spirits using a iris/portal to cross from the shadowlands to the material arrive in twilight though?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:59:35-07:00","id":1194838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194827#post1194827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say weaving - it's not a total transformation, it's still Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I felt \u2018directly\u2019 was the important word there. <br /> <br /> But anyways, indirect change via Weaving is much more sensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T08:59:42-07:00","id":1194858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194825#post1194825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit Summons spell is easier if you have a portal to the shadow nearby. Am i right in thinking that spirits using a iris/portal to cross from the shadowlands to the material arrive in twilight though?</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how they cross from the Shadow into the material they end up in Twilight, except if they're also granted a Manifestation at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T11:24:11-07:00","id":1194908,"title":"","content":"Related question: Is it possible for a material being to end up in the Shadow without transforming into ephemera? If so, what effect does that have?<br /> <br /> And what happens if a non-spirit ephemeral entity like a ghost ends up in the shadow? Afaik the Shadow doesn't have a &quot;twilight&quot; state so I guess it would have to be solid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T11:40:58-07:00","id":1194914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194908#post1194908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question: Is it possible for a material being to end up in the Shadow without transforming into ephemera? If so, what effect does that have?<br /> <br /> And what happens if a non-spirit ephemeral entity like a ghost ends up in the shadow? Afaik the Shadow doesn't have a &amp;quot;twilight&amp;quot; state so I guess it would have to be solid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of situations devised by the ST, no, the normal method of operation is to become ephemeral. Presumably though remaining a physical being in the Shadow wouldn\u2019t be that different. It\u2019s not like the translation into a dream body when entering the Astral.<br /> <br /> A ghost would probably be forced to manifest, it might be reasonable to have it start suffering essence bleed. Goetia would probably continue to appear as images only able to interact via powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:25:24-07:00","id":1194927,"title":"","content":"Ephemeral entities in realms where there is no Twilight will automatically become solid as if they were Materialized (but without actually using that Manifestation).<br /> <br /> Edit: And unless the ghost for some reason has an Anchor in the Shadow, it will start bleeding Essence. The Shadow is not its &quot;home&quot; realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-13-2018, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:06:32-07:00","id":1195228,"title":"","content":"I have a question, What level of Forces would it take to create Light Constructs (Green Lantern Style constructs)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:24:45-07:00","id":1195235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1195228#post1195228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question, What level of Forces would it take to create Light Constructs (Green Lantern Style constructs)?</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, Solid light sounds very much like the practice of weaving so maybe 3? Pretty similar to solid mana which is platonic form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:51:58-07:00","id":1195244,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it\u2019s Weaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:22:26-07:00","id":1195254,"title":"","content":"I dunno, turning electromagnetic radiation solid sounds like &quot;transforming it into something completely different&quot; to me. There's an argument that it isn't even within the purview of Forces alone, but if it is it's at least Patterning, maybe even Making an otherwise nonexistant form of energy.<br /> <br /> Then again, smacking someone with a giant green fist is arguably just a lime-flavored Telekinetic Strike. Which is the thing, I guess; what Green Lantern calls &quot;hard light constructs&quot; would probably be considered &quot;kinetic constructs&quot; in Mage. Creating an &quot;object&quot; that consists of a shaped area where kinetic force is redirected is Weaving, but at a level of control beyond what's normally possible at that level so... Weaving, but with a Reach or two?<br /> <br /> The cosmetic effect of the object being visible as a glowing thing I guess is technically Patterning the kinetic energy into visible light, but it <i>is</i> cosmetic so I wouldn't get bent out of shape about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:41:06-07:00","id":1195267,"title":"","content":"Thanks all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:35:47-07:00","id":1195365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1195267#post1195267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think Dave said that Green Lantern style constructs are the purview of Prime. It's how Platonic Forms can be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:57:08-07:00","id":1195432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1195365#post1195365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think Dave said that Green Lantern style constructs are the purview of Prime. It's how Platonic Forms can be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t be done with other arcana as well. Obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T13:34:26-07:00","id":1196582,"title":"","content":"What is the best resource at this moment if I wish to read more about the Supernal realms ? (Pandemonium, Arcadia, Aethe, Primal Wild &amp; Stygia). Would 'The Astral realms' and 'Tome of the Watchtowers' fit ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T14:03:17-07:00","id":1196593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1196582#post1196582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the best resource at this moment if I wish to read more about the Supernal realms ? (Pandemonium, Arcadia, Aethe, Primal Wild &amp; Stygia). Would 'The Astral realms' and 'Tome of the Watchtowers' fit ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the core for 2e has the best info really, and Summoners can give you an idea about the denizens at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T15:20:50-07:00","id":1196623,"title":"","content":"Summoners can provide great advice and direction on what a specific Supernal entity will seem like, based on their secondary Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T12:42:44-07:00","id":1198074,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible for a Mage to summon a Goetic Demon of their Vice, cut the links between them and the demon, then use magic to keep the vice from regrowing, basically keeping themselves free from Pride, Envy or Wrath which has its own problems? What levels of Mind and Space would it take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:01:50-07:00","id":1198082,"title":"","content":"Supressing your Vice should probably as easy as a ruling practice. Taking the concept of a vice away from your mind should in my mind be an unamking spell. An Excision spell could make such effects lasting in my mind, but unamking should be able to do it with a duration attached.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:44:53-07:00","id":1198100,"title":"","content":"Quarantine by itself would effectively banish a goetia for its duration without allowing it the chance to start reforming in the Oneiros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:51:48-07:00","id":1198102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1198074#post1198074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible for a Mage to summon a Goetic Demon of their Vice, cut the links between them and the demon, then use magic to keep the vice from regrowing, basically keeping themselves free from Pride, Envy or Wrath which has its own problems? What levels of Mind and Space would it take?</div> </div> </div> </div>Goetic Summons (Mind 3) to summon the Goetia, and then Mind 2 to just order the Goetia to do what you want. No Space required unless you want to create a more physical prison specifically for Goetia with Ban (Space 3). As long as the Goetia still exists I don't think it'll regrow. If it does it'd be a simple Shielding spell to prevent that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1198082#post1198082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supressing your Vice should probably as easy as a ruling practice. Taking the concept of a vice away from your mind should in my mind be an unamking spell. An Excision spell could make such effects lasting in my mind, but unamking should be able to do it with a duration attached.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell is named Amorality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:23:51-07:00","id":1198116,"title":"","content":"Thanks I thought you needed Space 4 to cut the threads of sympathy between the Goetic Demon and yourself and not be open to its influence anymore. Still that means if the character is a Mastigos he could free himself of unwanted desires at character creation.<br /> <br /> Mages are weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:29:21-07:00","id":1198119,"title":"","content":"It's stated directly in Goetic Summons that simply summoning a Goetia from someone's Oneiros removes that part of their personality as long as the Goetia stays in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T16:35:56-07:00","id":1198162,"title":"","content":"I think the downside is that a new goetia doesn't step up to become your new Vice or whatever, that part of you is simply excised and so you can't get WP or XP for acting on whatever it might have represented while it's gone.<br /> <br /> It can also, obviously, go disastrously wrong as in the case of the Gloria Mundi SAS which ended up introducing these interesting kinds of edge cases of what happens when a goetia gets loose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T13:28:43-07:00","id":1198393,"title":"","content":"How many Masques would you guys estimate that the 'average' Guardian keeps in their back pocket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:38:04-07:00","id":1198409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1198393#post1198393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Masques would you guys estimate that the 'average' Guardian keeps in their back pocket?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one, but always willing to add more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:20:00-07:00","id":1199041,"title":"","content":"Does regular armor protect agains direct damage dealing magic effects like: Thunderbolt, Rotting flesh, Piercing Earth ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:33:51-07:00","id":1199049,"title":"","content":"I'd have it protect against Thunderbolt and Piercing Earth, with have a direct physical attack vector. Rotting Flesh attacks your life pattern (to borrow the term from Ascension) directly and no amount of mundane armor would protect against it. Likewise I'd personally have Rotting Flesh circumvent Forces of Matter mage armor aswell, but I guess that's up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:36:21-07:00","id":1199050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199041#post1199041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does regular armor protect agains direct damage dealing magic effects like: Thunderbolt, Rotting flesh, Piercing Earth ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spells, but those particular examples sound like they would. Armor won\u2019t do much against Life-Force Assault, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:27:08-07:00","id":1199220,"title":"","content":"If I would cast Rotting flesh (page 132) with potency 5 and a standard duration 3 does it mean I would have this spell linger for 3 turns and deal 5 damage each turn ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:33:40-07:00","id":1199221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199220#post1199220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I would cast Rotting flesh (page 132) with potency 5 and a standard duration 3 does it mean I would have this spell linger for 3 turns and deal 5 damage each turn ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Instantaneous spells cast at Durations longer than a turn repeat themselves at set intervals dependent on Gnosis. And I\u2019m sure no level of Gnosis has One Turn as that interval... so no, you\u2019d only deal 5 damage one time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:40:36-07:00","id":1199227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199221#post1199221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Instantaneous spells cast at Durations longer than a turn repeat themselves at set intervals dependent on Gnosis. And I\u2019m sure no level of Gnosis has One Turn as that interval... so no, you\u2019d only deal 5 damage one time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is interesting, perhaps you remember the page in the core-book where this is mentioned ?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <b>FOUND IT. Page 113 <i>Duration</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T18:19:15-07:00","id":1199272,"title":"","content":"So in the astral realm there a realm that\u2019s warhammer 40k and my husbundo Konrad Curze is there \ud83d\udc9c\ud83d\udc9c\ud83d\udc9c\u2764\ufe0f\u2764\ufe0f\ud83d\ude0d\ud83d\ude0d\ud83d\ude0d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T18:32:40-07:00","id":1199275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199272#post1199272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the astral realm there a realm that\u2019s warhammer 40k and my husbundo Konrad Curze is there \ud83d\udc9c\ud83d\udc9c\ud83d\udc9c\u2764\ufe0f\u2764\ufe0f\ud83d\ude0d\ud83d\ude0d\ud83d\ude0d</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Astral there's a realm that is nothing but Steamed Hams fighting Gru's Plan and more long-lived memes for prominence in the collective soul of mankind.<br /> <br /> There's a realm where Cyberpunk and Post-Cyberpunk fight a war for continued relevance in the SciFi genre.<br /> <br /> There's a series of interconnected realms/areas where all the different perspectives on Starbucks reside.<br /> <br /> The Astral contains every single collectively held thought of mankind that exists, as well as every collectively held thought that used to exist (if you know where to look).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T19:56:02-07:00","id":1199286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199220#post1199220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I would cast Rotting flesh (page 132) with potency 5 and a standard duration 3 does it mean I would have this spell linger for 3 turns and deal 5 damage each turn ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Spells which logically have a immediate effect but are cast with a duration , recur every multiple of the mages gnosis ritual time. p113<br /> <br /> Heh stupid forum didnt show me all the replies already again!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T08:29:04-07:00","id":1199721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199275#post1199275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Astral there's a realm that is nothing but Steamed Hams</div> </div> </div> </div>Aurora Borealis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T10:33:33-07:00","id":1200114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1199721#post1199721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aurora Borealis?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Verge?!<br /> <br /> At this time of year?!<br /> <br /> At this time of day?!<br /> <br /> In this part of the city, localized ENTIRELY within your Sanctum?!<br /> <br /> \u201cYes!\u201d<br /> <br /> ... May I see it?<br /> <br /> \u201cNnnno\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:00:05-07:00","id":1200166,"title":"","content":"I have a question regarding mechanics when changing spells primary factor using reach.<br /> <br /> Lets take a fate spell Chaos Mastery (page 138). Spells primary factor is Duration and it can cause a number of effects equal to Potency. Because mages gain free primary spell factors equal to highest arcanum dot - 1 used in a spell is it possible to change the spells primary factor from duration to potency, increase potency using free potency points and then increase duration taking -2 dice penalty ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:13:13-07:00","id":1200176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200166#post1200166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question regarding mechanics when changing spells primary factor using reach.<br /> <br /> Lets take a fate spell Chaos Mastery (page 138). Spells primary factor is Duration and it can cause a number of effects equal to Potency. Because mages gain free primary spell factors equal to highest arcanum dot - 1 used in a spell is it possible to change the spells primary factor from duration to potency, increase potency using free potency points and then increase duration taking -2 dice penalty ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That's part of the point of being able to change the primary factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:56:12-07:00","id":1200195,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to cast teleportation (page 178) to teleport your self behind an enemy in such a way that an item you're crying would impale him ? Effectively this is combining 2 spells Teleportation (page 178) and Collapse (page 177). In my personal opinion this is either a spell combination or requires additional reach (+2 maybe?) and maybe mana ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:30:34-07:00","id":1200208,"title":"","content":"Combined spell for sure, you teleport and something get stuck in something else: dealing damage.<br /> (or if it's within your speed and don't want to become over-fanatic about the rules and such, just a collapse-spell with narrative effect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T15:03:34-07:00","id":1200233,"title":"","content":"You actually by RAW cannot combine spells like that, since the two spells have different targets (your opponent for the damage spell and the space behind him for the teleport). Personally I'd let it fly as a combined spell though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T16:20:16-07:00","id":1200255,"title":"","content":"That's true, add fate 2 &quot;whatever the spell is called&quot; (the ones that lets you choose whichever spells effect what) as well and it would work (I think). That one becomes extremely difficult to pull of though. I'd just allow it or as said, maybe use narrative terms to allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T16:25:23-07:00","id":1200256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200255#post1200255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, add fate 2 &amp;quot;whatever the spell is called&amp;quot; (the ones that lets you choose whichever spells effect what) as well and it would work (I think). That one becomes extremely difficult to pull of though. I'd just allow it or as said, maybe use narrative terms to allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warding Gestures!<br /> <br /> That said, I can also see this just being a Reach clause on Collapse, for less headache-y handwaving purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T21:04:57-07:00","id":1200338,"title":"","content":"Here's something I've become confused over. With speaking with Hermit, I found out that rotes and praxes are only one experience point a pop. Does this mean that when character creation mentions six dots worth of rotes, a starting mage should have six spells under their belts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T21:11:02-07:00","id":1200339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200338#post1200338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something I've become confused over. With speaking with Hermit, I found out that rotes and praxes are only one experience point a pop. Does this mean that when character creation mentions six dots worth of rotes, a starting mage should have six spells under their belts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just three rotes, period. You start with six dots <i>in the Arcana</i>, subject to the requirements of your Path, but the character creation process doesn't mention starting rotes in terms of total dots in the post-errata copy of the PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T22:08:59-07:00","id":1200353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200233#post1200233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You actually by RAW cannot combine spells like that, since the two spells have different targets (your opponent for the damage spell and the space behind him for the teleport). Personally I'd let it fly as a combined spell though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say combined spells have to have the same target? Both spells can even have different scales as long as you spend reach to separate the effects. A combined spell is two spells cast as one, its not two spells cast AT one.<br /> <br /> I could combine a shielding spell on myself with a targeted fireball spell at an enemy. Both spells are using the same scale (ie 1 target) so dont need extra reach to separate either.<br /> <br /> If you are/do combine teleport/collapse then both spells have the 1 target scale factor (one being you for the teleport, the other being the enemy for the collapse spell) so wouldnt need to be separated with an extra reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Spell stacking still applies <b><i><u>IF</u></i></b> the constituent spells affect the same thing.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Highlight my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-28-2018, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T22:34:49-07:00","id":1200355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200353#post1200353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Highlight my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;same thing&quot; that excerpt is referring to is the fact that the rules for spell stacking do not have an exception in combined casting \u2014 &quot;you can't double-cast Degrading the Form to get a discount on Potency&quot; has pretty much nothing to do with whether simultaneously warding your house and setting an observer across the street on fire is as valid for combined casting as establishing an area where people are turned into frogs and their pocket change rolls into your collection box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T00:28:29-07:00","id":1200362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200355#post1200355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;same thing&quot; that excerpt is referring to is the fact that the rules for spell stacking do not have an exception in combined casting \u2014 &quot;you can't double-cast Degrading the Form to get a discount on Potency&quot; has pretty much nothing to do with whether simultaneously warding your house and setting an observer across the street on fire is as valid for combined casting as establishing an area where people are turned into frogs and their pocket change rolls into your collection box.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but the fact you can spend 1 reach to separate each spells scale factor means one spell can have an area scale and the other could have indiv targets or some spell can be a small room area and the other could be a campus sized area (that if cast via sensory range need not be the same area as the previous spell.) Means both spells can have a different target as long as the scale is or with reach not the same.<br /> <br /> A mage might want to combine knit on himself with bruise flesh on a enemy for example, without stating up a example etc im not sure how effective it'd end up and its probably better to do one or the other but combining spells would allow it.<br /> <br /> So for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1013_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1013\" data-vbnamecard=\"1013\">Stralos</a> example i would class that is what a combined teleport/collapse spell looks like cast within sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:10:04-07:00","id":1200389,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is a simple question, but what can a Master of, say, Life do with a reasonable chance of success without spending any Mana or Reach? Or at least no more reach than whatever free reach they get from their Arcana Level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:12:47-07:00","id":1200391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200389#post1200389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is a simple question, but what can a Master of, say, Life do with a reasonable chance of success without spending any Mana or Reach? Or at least no more reach than whatever free reach they get from their Arcana Level?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:14:29-07:00","id":1200392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200391#post1200391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can do a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, how about with no Reach at all, and no Attainments that cost Mana, and no Yantras. Just envisioning the Imago in their mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-28-2018, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:47:33-07:00","id":1200399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200392#post1200392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, how about with no Reach at all, and no Attainments that cost Mana, and no Yantras. Just envisioning the Imago in their mind</div> </div> </div> </div>They can still do a lot, but less than what they can do in the previous question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:54:04-07:00","id":1200400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200339#post1200339\"