l=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Subjects can always choose not to Withstand spells. It's not explicitly written, but I think all spells are Withstood. Only negative spells have the rating written out since those are the spells you want to Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all.<br /> <br /> (characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:29:03-07:00","id":1200931,"title":"","content":"Ooh. As long as you're here, this question of mine never got an answer (both people who tried answering seemed to think I was asking about the Iris option when I specifically wasn't):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1194787#post1194787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the base (non-Reach) effect of the Reaching spell actually do anything when casting at sensory range across the Gauntlet? I kind of feel like it's supposed to let you bypass the Gauntlet Strength Withstand on your other spells but it doesn't actually say that and I can't think of what it would be good for otherwise besides touching things.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T13:20:41-07:00","id":1200951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200908#post1200908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all.<br /> <br /> (characters)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The subject of a spell can always choose not to Withstand a spell, but she must consciously choose to do so as a reflexive action.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it mentioned in those spells' description that the subject can't choose to not Withstand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T13:33:15-07:00","id":1200956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200951#post1200951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The subject of a spell can always choose not to Withstand a spell, but she must consciously choose to do so as a reflexive action.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it mentioned in those spells' description that the subject can't choose to not Withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Dave is saying not all spells are Withstood. Direct Damage spells for example are never Withstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T13:41:11-07:00","id":1200964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200956#post1200956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Dave is saying not all spells are Withstood. Direct Damage spells for example are never Withstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. That's true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:03:11-07:00","id":1200975,"title":"","content":"Could you explain to me what spells count as aimed spells ? From my understanding this is an open ended question (there is no strict rule), and all spells that send a flying projectile are aimed. If this is the case, then would a spell like Thunderbolt be inferior to a spell Mind Flay as one would be penalised by defence while the other not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:05:31-07:00","id":1200978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200975#post1200975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain to me what spells count as aimed spells ? From my understanding this is an open ended question (there is no strict rule), and all spells that send a flying projectile are aimed. If this is the case, then would a spell like Thunderbolt be inferior to a spell Mind Flay as one would be penalised by defence while the other not.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Aimed Spell is a spell cast at Self/Touch Range but used against a target that is not yourself or something you are touching. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:14:07-07:00","id":1200980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200975#post1200975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain to me what spells count as aimed spells ? From my understanding this is an open ended question (there is no strict rule), and all spells that send a flying projectile are aimed. If this is the case, then would a spell like Thunderbolt be inferior to a spell Mind Flay as one would be penalised by defence while the other not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not specific spells that are aimed. Aiming a spell is an option you could do for absolutely any spell. As Satchel explained you cast the spell at Self/Touch Range but instead of having yourself or someone next to you be the subject you throw that spell as a projectile against whoever you want to be the subject.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, the spell itself is not penalised by Defense. Gnosis + Athletics/Firearms is a separate roll to see if the spell hits or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:20:28-07:00","id":1200985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200975#post1200975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain to me what spells count as aimed spells ? From my understanding this is an open ended question (there is no strict rule), and all spells that send a flying projectile are aimed. If this is the case, then would a spell like Thunderbolt be inferior to a spell Mind Flay as one would be penalised by defence while the other not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bTo elaborate on what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, all spells CAN be aimed. Aiming a spell is a style of casting it not a description of the particular spell. Your two examples spells are not different in that regard, they either require touch, Sensory, or Aiming to hit the target.<br /> <br /> Esit: Ninja'ed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:22:23-07:00","id":1200988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200980#post1200980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not specific spells that are aimed. Aiming a spell is an option you could do for absolutely any spell. As Satchel explained you cast the spell at Self/Touch Range but instead of having yourself or someone next to you be the subject you throw that spell as a projectile against whoever you want to be the subject.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, the spell itself is not penalised by Defense. Gnosis + Athletics/Firearms is a separate roll to see if the spell hits or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I should have been more clear, as I was interested about the Spell hitting part, that requires me to roll Gnosis + Athletics/Firearms - defence. Does that mean that all spells require this roll to hit an unwilling target ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:27:52-07:00","id":1200991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200988#post1200988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I should have been more clear, as I was interested about the Spell hitting part, that requires me to roll Gnosis + Athletics/Firearms - defence. Does that mean that all spells require this roll to hit an unwilling target ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you are Aiming then yes, if you touch them then no. Or if you spend a Reach to cast at Sensory Range then no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:28:25-07:00","id":1200992,"title":"","content":"My bad again. I rushed to asking before taking my time to fully read the book.<br /> <br /> Page 114:<br /> The standard Range factor for all spells is touch/self, meaning that the mage can cast the spell on herself or a subject she touches without any penalties. A mage can target an individual she cannot touch with a self/touch spell by succeeding on an Aimed Spell roll. The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the mage must be able to directly see her subject. A spell cast with sensory range cannot be dodged and does not require an Aimed Spell roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:29:39-07:00","id":1200994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1200988#post1200988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I should have been more clear, as I was interested about the Spell hitting part, that requires me to roll Gnosis + Athletics/Firearms - defence. Does that mean that all spells require this roll to hit an unwilling target ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any spell not using some form of Advanced Range (i.e. anything below Sensory Range) requires that the spell make contact with the subject, whether through touch or an Aimed projection, either of which generally requires that you overcome their Defense or otherwise have it immobilized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T14:47:30-07:00","id":1201000,"title":"","content":"(As a side note, one of those ways to <i>mostly</i> ignore Defense is the two-dot &quot;Fast Spells&quot; Merit (core book, p. 101) that treats your Aimed spells as Firearms attacks for the purposes of whether or not Defense applies. Not a universal fix since some mages and certain other supernatural creatures <i>can</i> still use part or all of their Defense against Firearms with the right Spooky Powers, but if you're targeting unwilling creatures a lot it's a good way to save a Reach in most cases. It does require a little investment in Time in order to get it, though.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it seems like everything else has been covered.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T23:41:50-07:00","id":1201165,"title":"","content":"Quick question, i was reading the rule for creating a familiar and the effect of their ranks, supposed i want my mage to have a rank 2 familiar with the four dot merit, the Rank chart says that it will have between 9 to 14 attributes dot to spend and between 3 to 5 numina. Does my familiar begin play with the lowest number of dots ? Can those dots be increased without supernal magic ? Can i choose how many dots my spirit familiar gets ?<br /> <br /> Also, does a spirit being linked to a mage could began to better understand the human mindset ? Or maybe only spirit more close to humanity accept the familiar bond ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 03-30-2018, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T01:13:56-07:00","id":1201183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1201165#post1201165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, i was reading the rule for creating a familiar and the effect of their ranks, supposed i want my mage to have a rank 2 familiar with the four dot merit, the Rank chart says that it will have between 9 to 14 attributes dot to spend and between 3 to 5 numina. Does my familiar begin play with the lowest number of dots ? Can those dots be increased without supernal magic ? Can i choose how many dots my spirit familiar gets ?<br /> <br /> Also, does a spirit being linked to a mage could began to better understand the human mindset ? Or maybe only spirit more close to humanity accept the familiar bond ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should discuss it with your ST and come up with appropriate stats/numina. Every player gaining a familiar would obviously want 14 attribute points and 5 numina for a familar but its up to you and your ST to decide if its possible in your current game. Personally the more effort you did as a player in describing the familiar etc the more i would give you, if the PC just said &quot;yeh i get a rank 2 familiar, i dont care which&quot; then that PC is getting one with 9 dots and 3 numina, if she even gets one at all. (ie i let her spend exp on the merit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:13:06-07:00","id":1201699,"title":"","content":"&lt;double post&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","user":"Bomaz","date":".  double post 03-31-2018, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:36:52-07:00","id":1201708,"title":"","content":"I believe so, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:19:20-07:00","id":1201750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1201708#post1201708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe so, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say not, considering that otherwise the Rank chart allows for spirits with literally impossible spreads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:37:30-07:00","id":1201760,"title":"","content":"The rules for creating an Ephemeral Entity don't state that they start off with a single dot in each Attribute, so in the absence of further direction it's more reasonable to assume that they do not.<br /> <br /> Also as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, that could result in Rank 3-5 entities having more dots to put into Attributes than they could actually spend (e.g. the Trait limit for Rank 5 is 15, which means that if provided the maximum of 45 dots to spend, they could not expend them all before reaching the Trait limit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T21:53:13-07:00","id":1201850,"title":"","content":"With Fate, Destiny seems to be a kind of signal of importance that typically only Mages pick up on, particularly those with Fate. Is it really that far fetched to suppose that Fate 2 could then Veil your importance to others such that you're generally overlooked? It's probably not quite the non-descriptness of Incognito Presence, others could remember you if they were pressed, but that in the moment they will typically overlook you as being beneath their notice, does that sound reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T22:16:40-07:00","id":1201853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1201850#post1201850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Fate, Destiny seems to be a kind of signal of importance that typically only Mages pick up on, particularly those with Fate. Is it really that far fetched to suppose that Fate 2 could then Veil your importance to others such that you're generally overlooked? It's probably not quite the non-descriptness of Incognito Presence, others could remember you if they were pressed, but that in the moment they will typically overlook you as being beneath their notice, does that sound reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Disguising yourself as a Background Character, not Plot-Important Character? Sounds legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T16:52:39-07:00","id":1202055,"title":"","content":"Can Mages be Claimed normally (assuming they don't have Spirit dots) or, just like it's far harder to steal Awakened souls than Sleeper Souls, does it require a lot more power to affect their soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:05:55-07:00","id":1202060,"title":"","content":"I see nothing in claim for werewolf 2e that says mages cant be claimed normally (even with dots in spirit) though they would also get their gnosis as ww's get primal urge to resist. Dots in spirit wont automatically help resist but if they had a spirit shield (&quot;Ephemeral shield&quot; for example) spell up for them to gain a clash. If however the claim or urged condition counts as a mental condition the mage can pattern restore and spend 3 mana to get rid of it.<br /> <br /> I dont think claimed will have access to the mages arcana though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-01-2018, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:12:57-07:00","id":1202062,"title":"","content":"I more meant that any mage with Spirit Dots could probably whip up a bunch of ways to get rid of at least lower-ranked spirits, or at least keep them out of their head/soul. Which, actually, is what I see you just said. Yeah, spirits would definitely go for easier targets.<br /> <br /> I also agree that Possessed and Claimed mages would not give the spirit control over their Mage powers, as they are mediated through the body's original guiding intelligence and its current soul.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think Claimed is just a Mental condition, considering all the physical changes attached to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:31:52-07:00","id":1202068,"title":"","content":"I think that a Claimed mage will develop Dread Powers mimicking the mage\u2019s Praxes and Attainments. Or maybe become a pseudo-Legacy of some sort, if the Claim was consensual/ engineered by the mage himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:38:18-07:00","id":1202069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202062#post1202062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I more meant that any mage with Spirit Dots could probably whip up a bunch of ways to get rid of at least lower-ranked spirits, or at least keep them out of their head/soul. Which, actually, is what I see you just said. Yeah, spirits would definitely go for easier targets.<br /> <br /> I also agree that Possessed and Claimed mages would not give the spirit control over their Mage powers, as they are mediated through the body's original guiding intelligence and its current soul.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think Claimed is just a Mental condition, considering all the physical changes attached to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the spirit can somehow detect if a mage has a shield up or not then it probably only finds out the mage is harder to claim when it tries it? But yeh since spirits clash with rank (+ influence if apt which i dont think manifestations count as) its probable that low ranked spirits will fail vs a spirit shield clash.<br /> <br /> Is there an actual list of what is and isnt considered mental/physical or environmental conditions/tilts? Since pattern restore mentions them i assumed that they would mention what type they are but seems not and it seems like its left up to each ST to decide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:41:45-07:00","id":1202070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202068#post1202068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a Claimed mage will develop Dread Powers mimicking the mage\u2019s Praxes and Attainments. Or maybe become a pseudo-Legacy of some sort, if the Claim was consensual/ engineered by the mage himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. even none consensual claiming will probably result in a mage claimed gaining odd dread powers that mimic them. I cant imagine the depths/trouble a mage would have to be in to willingly agree to get claimed though or what getting claimed would solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:39:17-07:00","id":1202647,"title":"","content":"This is less a rules question but more just trying to understand the development team and writers. <br /> <br /> So you get magic from connecting with the Watchtowers, but you need to follow the Watchtowers\u2019 path to get that connection, right? So why go with the word \u201cwatchtower\u201d, since that relies more on someone at that structure being able to see others. Why not call them \u201clighthouses\u201d or something that depends more on the observer\u2019s noticing the thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T12:04:29-07:00","id":1202666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202647#post1202647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is less a rules question but more just trying to understand the development team and writers. <br /> <br /> So you get magic from connecting with the Watchtowers, but you need to follow the Watchtowers\u2019 path to get that connection, right? So why go with the word \u201cwatchtower\u201d, since that relies more on someone at that structure being able to see others. Why not call them \u201clighthouses\u201d or something that depends more on the observer\u2019s noticing the thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Watchtowers and their surrounding realm also serve as a sort of Supernal outhold, a fortified storehouse of a Mage\u2019s connection to the Supernal. There\u2019s also the fact that watchtowers frequently served as long distance line of sight communications with signal fires.<br /> <br /> The Supernal and its associated lexicon changes over time though. For instance in To The Strongest the realms and towers were nothing like they are now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T12:04:34-07:00","id":1202667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202647#post1202647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is less a rules question but more just trying to understand the development team and writers.<br /> <br /> So you get magic from connecting with the Watchtowers, but you need to follow the Watchtowers\u2019 path to get that connection, right? So why go with the word \u201cwatchtower\u201d, since that relies more on someone at that structure being able to see others. Why not call them \u201clighthouses\u201d or something that depends more on the observer\u2019s noticing the thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Watchtower is a term used in actual occult practices at the turn of 20th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:02:18-07:00","id":1202724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202667#post1202667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watchtower is a term used in actual occult practices at the turn of 20th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that explains it perfectly as far as I'm concerned. Though ever since thinking of the Lighthouses idea, I've just been thinking of a pirate setting for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:41:33-07:00","id":1202742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202724#post1202724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that explains it perfectly as far as I'm concerned. Though ever since thinking of the Lighthouses idea, I've just been thinking of a pirate setting for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new Dark Eras coming out has a Golden Age of Piracy era for mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:58:24-07:00","id":1202750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202647#post1202647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is less a rules question but more just trying to understand the development team and writers. <br /> <br /> So you get magic from connecting with the Watchtowers, but you need to follow the Watchtowers\u2019 path to get that connection, right? So why go with the word \u201cwatchtower\u201d, since that relies more on someone at that structure being able to see others. Why not call them \u201clighthouses\u201d or something that depends more on the observer\u2019s noticing the thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, tidbits dropped by Dave (the developer) seem to indicate that the Watchtowers do in fact have a choosing mechanism on whom Awakens. Which would mean that a Watchtower does observe the Fallen World on some level. <br /> <br /> But as others said, the Supernal manifests differently at different times and places. Who knows what future mages will refer to their Paths/Watchtowers/Realms as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:13:29-07:00","id":1202757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202750#post1202750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, tidbits dropped by Dave (the developer) seem to indicate that the Watchtowers do in fact have a choosing mechanism on whom Awakens. Which would mean that a Watchtower does observe the Fallen World on some level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, once you've surmounted the Watchtower, you have a vantage there for the rest of your life barring specific supernatural interference \u2014 the term is most commonly used in the context of the Awakening itself, after which it serves as the point of reference for the mage's Path.<br /> <br /> (It seems to lend a curious visual to the assumption and dismissal of a Shadow Name persona \u2014 Calvin White may be able to live a mundane life among the Sleepers, but Caladrius Snowbird is <i>always</i> in the Watchtower of the Golden Key.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:58:03-07:00","id":1202806,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason why Transubstantiation (Matter 4) doesn't have a Lasting option? Would it break things to add it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:08:00-07:00","id":1202808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202806#post1202806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it break things to add it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The economy and the very concept of scarcity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:00:14-07:00","id":1202820,"title":"","content":"As Inodiv says. You can still spend reach to get the advanced duration options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T22:28:38-07:00","id":1202870,"title":"","content":"Why can Devouring the Slain (Death 3, Fraying) deal lethal damage? I thought you needed an Unraveling Practice for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T22:47:17-07:00","id":1202876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202870#post1202870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can Devouring the Slain (Death 3, Fraying) deal lethal damage? I thought you needed an Unraveling Practice for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Death spell that works by Scouring an injured subject's Pattern. Casting Withering, for contrast, doesn't take two extra Reach to affect multiple fresh targets in a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T02:26:32-07:00","id":1202919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202806#post1202806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason why Transubstantiation (Matter 4) doesn't have a Lasting option? Would it break things to add it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost all 4 dots spells lack a lasting option. Once you reach the 4th and 5th dots the changes you introduce by casting a spell are so large and dramatic they start to require an upkeep even if the result isn't necessarily supernatural in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T15:17:44-07:00","id":1203154,"title":"","content":"So for a Mystery in where multiple Arcana is used, say Prime and Forces for instance, but the mage using focused mage sight only got Prime, it seems like just the Opacity is higher or is there something else? It seems like it's just harder without understanding the pieces, but still allows for the mage with only Prime to fill out the Forces gaps and still get Deep information and such when he solves it? Or?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T15:23:23-07:00","id":1203160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203154#post1203154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for a Mystery in where multiple Arcana is used, say Prime and Forces for instance, but the mage using focused mage sight only got Prime, it seems like just the Opacity is higher or is there something else? It seems like it's just harder without understanding the pieces, but still allows for the mage with only Prime to fill out the Forces gaps and still get Deep information and such when he solves it? Or?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure there's a mechanic to clue a Mage into what arcana he's missing to be able to use Scrutiny, but other than that the Mage will be stumped. Alternatively, you could decide what the Mystery has more of, Prime or Forces, and then let him Scrutinize the Prime part and give incomplete information and not allow them to reduce Opacity to 0, I'd probably go with the second route personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T21:16:01-07:00","id":1203287,"title":"","content":"You always know if you're about to risk a paradox. Do other mages sense if you risked paradox when you cast a spell? If not, can they with Mage Sight? And if not, can they with a Prime spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T02:03:38-07:00","id":1203329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203287#post1203287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You always know if you're about to risk a paradox. Do other mages sense if you risked paradox when you cast a spell? If not, can they with Mage Sight? And if not, can they with a Prime spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Prime Knowing spell could reveal they\u2019re putting together something more complicated than they can handle. Mage Sight would only be useful to study the aftermath, it\u2019s not predictive it\u2019s analytical and Paradox or risk thereof doesn\u2019t actually exist until just before the spell is cast and occurs faster or as fast as Reflexive actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T02:20:02-07:00","id":1203333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203287#post1203287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You always know if you're about to risk a paradox. Do other mages sense if you risked paradox when you cast a spell? If not, can they with Mage Sight? And if not, can they with a Prime spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maaaybe the Display of Power spell could, since it reveals the Imago as it is being formed, and over-Reaching could show up there. Even if it does, however, I doubt that Paradox from Sleeper presence, inuring, etc will show up. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the Scelesti know a thing or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T16:28:04-07:00","id":1203562,"title":"","content":"So all yantras need semiotic symbolism, that far is pretty clear.<br /> The orders have different tools they teach their members to use as Yantras, ergo Order Tools. These must be linked to their understanding as well to the spell in use.<br /> The description says the following for the Diamond Orders:<br /> &quot;The formal magical<br /> style of the Diamond Orders and the Seers of the Throne all<br /> resonate through the same tools \u2014 the Arrow uses martial Tools<br /> as symbols of conflict; the Guardians use cloaks, masks, and<br /> veils as symbols of things hidden and revealed; the Mysterium<br /> teaches books, writing, and language as Tools of knowledge and<br /> communication; and the Silver Ladder uses signs of authority to<br /> as Tools of status and persuasion.&quot;<br /> <br /> So far so good, a Silver Ladder mage can use a police badge for a spell to grant him access somewhere or a Arrow may use a literal shield to ward against incoming attacks or a Guardian may use a surgeon mask to give him self incognito presence in the hospital and so forth...<br /> <br /> What are the symbolism for the free council?<br /> It says:<br /> &quot;The Free Council are an oddity among all the other Orders.<br /> While every Libertine may use complex mechanisms and systems<br /> as Order Tools&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure i get what &quot;complex mechanisms and systems&quot; means but what are they symbols of, can they use an appropriate system for any spell as long as they can find meaning behind it?<br /> Like can all Libertines use for say for instance, bureaucratic forms as an Order Tool for use in a spell that makes their subject confused or a wifi-router to make a telepathy spell toward someone on the other side of the globe (with sympathy and such ofc) as bureaucracy is strongly symbolic with confusion and wifi-routers are symbolic means of communication?<br /> Or what are the Libertines Order Tools supposed to do?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Also, why is Techn\u00e9 actually worth 2 exp? I can't seem to get that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 04-05-2018, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T16:43:34-07:00","id":1203566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203562#post1203562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure i get what &quot;complex mechanisms and systems&quot; means but what are they symbols of, can they use an appropriate system for any spell as long as they can find meaning behind it?<br /> Like can all Libertines use for say for instance, bureaucratic forms as an Order Tool for use in a spell that makes their subject confused or a wifi-router to make a telepathy spell toward someone on the other side of the globe (with sympathy and such ofc) as bureaucracy is strongly symbolic with confusion and wifi-routers are symbolic means of communication?<br /> Or what are the Libertines Order Tools supposed to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>See the Order's Magical Symbolism writeup on page 51.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit:<br /> Also, why is Techn\u00e9 actually worth 2 exp? I can't seem to get that one. </div> </div> </div>It gives you an extra pair of Order Tools that you can choose with relative freedom, as well as the ability to get 8-Again on spellcasting without relying on the aid of discrete spells. That's three different effects \u2014 what's confusing about that costing more than one dot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:07:02-07:00","id":1203599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203566#post1203566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the Order's Magical Symbolism writeup on page 51.<br /> <br /> It gives you an extra pair of Order Tools that you can choose with relative freedom, as well as the ability to get 8-Again on spellcasting without relying on the aid of discrete spells. That's three different effects \u2014 what's confusing about that costing more than one dot?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So: &quot;tool of wonder, humanity\u2019s reach exceeding its imagination&quot; is that what their yantras can be used for? Or am I missing the point?<br /> <br /> Yeah it's an order tool or actually two if you include some sleepers, so for two yantra slots you get two dice, if you use the focus as well as sleepers, as long as the spell ain't obvious and if you get more mages with both the merit and the same focus the leader get 8 again.<br /> <br /> It just seems expensive and of very limited use. Why not just buy a fitting shadow name and use the focus as part of it for the same experience and you get two dice on almost all spells that falls into the theme of the name and you don't need some overly complex situation to fix the spell. And you get an free yantra slot you could use as well, giving at least one die on the roll and maybe more. Sure you miss the few times the 8 again on teamwork could be applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:22:45-07:00","id":1203698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203599#post1203599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: &quot;tool of wonder, humanity\u2019s reach exceeding its imagination&quot; is that what their yantras can be used for? Or am I missing the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire deal with Tool Yantras is that they help spells whose effects are associated with what those tools do, and a generalist Libertine has the benefit of treating things like <i>computers and astrology</i> as specialist tools without needing particular investment. Their Instruments can be used for <i>the things they can be used for,</i> and the draw of techn\u00e9 is that <i>that is a lot of different things,</i> depending on the specific tool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah it's an order tool or actually two if you include some sleepers, so for two yantra slots you get two dice, if you use the focus as well as sleepers, as long as the spell ain't obvious and if you get more mages with both the merit and the same focus the leader get 8 again. </div> </div> </div>Yantras worth more than one die without a limitation or cost are thin on the ground and being able to use your hobbyist cliques to manage low-key magic better is inherently geared toward having the spaces where those specialties are relevant be important to the character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just seems expensive and of very limited use. </div> </div> </div>It's two dots.<br /> <br /> For the same price Adamant Hand gives you the ability to spend three turns punching people and cast on the fourth turn as though you had spent those turns gesturing with a knife and stave in a magic system where this doesn't help the inbuilt drawbacks of casting on a timescale measured in seconds.<br /> <br /> For the same price a Guardian can get as little back as another extra Virtue and Vice that they have to become a different person to benefit from.<br /> <br /> For the same price a th\u00e9arch can get a set of benefits that only help them in the particular field of &quot;being part of the magical legal apparatus that arbitrates between local mages.&quot;<br /> <br /> Two dots is the <i>standard cost</i> for most core Order Merits that aren't Egregore or Prelacy or the spine of all the Masques a Guardian has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not just buy a fitting shadow name and use the focus as part of it for the same experience and you get two dice on almost all spells that falls into the theme of the name and you don't need some overly complex situation to fix the spell. </div> </div> </div>You can't buy <i>an arbitrarily large number of separate Shadow Names</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you get an free yantra slot you could use as well, giving at least one die on the roll and maybe more. Sure you miss the few times the 8 again on teamwork could be applicable. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183342-what-am-i-missing-about-the-sanctum-merit?p=1183828#post1183828\">Raw mechanical utility is not the purpose of most Awakened Merits</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-06-2018, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:58:26-07:00","id":1203709,"title":"","content":"You totally can buy an arbitrarily large number of Shadow Names, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:08:44-07:00","id":1203713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203709#post1203709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You totally can buy an arbitrarily large number of Shadow Names, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;One&quot; is not a number of <i>separate</i> Shadow Names, and if you were meant to be able to get more than one then it would have the same rider clause that Alternate Identity includes \u2014 and Mage's copy of Alternate Identity specifically differentiates an Alternate Identity from a Shadow Name, so it's clearly not just a matter of the text being duplicated from a non-Mage book and so not including considerations for its use in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:18:04-07:00","id":1203717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203713#post1203713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;One&quot; is not a number of <i>separate</i> Shadow Names, and if you were meant to be able to get more than one then it would have the same rider clause that Alternate Identity includes \u2014 and Mage's copy of Alternate Identity specifically differentiates an Alternate Identity from a Shadow Name, so it's clearly not just a matter of the text being duplicated from a non-Mage book and so not including considerations for its use in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>3/3/2017, on 4chan's /tg/ board, DaveB answered a couple of questions on Shadow Names<br /> <br /> &quot;&gt;DaveB, if you're still around, would it be possible for a mage to have 2 shadow names?<br /> Yeah, just buy the Merit multiple times<br /> <br /> &gt; How much Space would it be required to alter a Shadow Name and/or confer an additional one? Making? Dominions? Entities?<br /> Wouldn't say Space. A Shadow Name's just something you call yourself - the Merit represents it starting to resonante Supernally over time, such that you can use it as a Yantra. I would say Prime. Possibly archmaster-y.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, you can totally have 4, 3-dot merits for<br /> &quot;The Angel of Destruction&quot;, &quot;The Wise Old Witch&quot;, &quot;She who waits in Shadows&quot;, and &quot;The Mystic Leader of Mankind&quot;<br /> It's having at least one Shadow Name which grants your normal life protection from your Nimbus.<br /> Nothing says you can't cultivate multiple separate personas.<br /> I imagine many Guardians do, given the 5-dot Masque benefit can grant a Shadow Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:55:41-07:00","id":1203727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203717#post1203717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3/3/2017, on 4chan's /tg/ board, DaveB answered a couple of questions on Shadow Names</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the sort of thing you want to<i> <b>actually state outright first</b></i>, given that the /tg/ archive-dump is not the primary reference and lack of text-tone makes it otherwise easy to read your response as a joke on the meaning of &quot;arbitrary.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, you can totally have 4, 3-dot merits for<br /> &quot;The Angel of Destruction&quot;, &quot;The Wise Old Witch&quot;, &quot;She who waits in Shadows&quot;, and &quot;The Mystic Leader of Mankind&quot;<br /> It's having at least one Shadow Name which grants your normal life protection from your Nimbus.<br /> Nothing says you can't cultivate multiple separate personas.<br /> I imagine many Guardians do, given the 5-dot Masque benefit can grant a Shadow Name. </div> </div> </div>The larger point stands: &quot;developing an affinity for using multiple different Sleeper practices as magical aids&quot; means a dramatically different thing than &quot;investing to a moderately high degree in multiple different magical personas,&quot; particularly as a trick particular to the Sect that prefers Assemblies to Consilia and aligns itself with a variety of traditions that might otherwise sprout the odd Nameless Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T01:16:25-07:00","id":1203752,"title":"","content":"Can you use Dream Reaching to tag along on someone else's Astral journey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T01:45:23-07:00","id":1203757,"title":"","content":"no. the astral isn't a dream","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T05:23:23-07:00","id":1203794,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203698#post1203698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire deal with Tool Yantras is that they help spells whose effects are associated with what those tools do, and a generalist Libertine has the benefit of treating things like <i>computers and astrology</i> as specialist tools without needing particular investment. Their Instruments can be used for <i>the things they can be used for,</i> and the draw of techn\u00e9 is that <i>that is a lot of different things,</i> depending on the specific tool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the question is more: Can Order Tools be used for <i>any</i> kind of spell as long as the player can give some form of semiotic justification or just spells relating to their teachings and symbolism?<br /> Can the Arrows use weapons and armour for things not realting to conflict? Can the Gaurdians use masks to give them selves a shit-ton of extra Prensence to give a speech infront of hundreds of people on the principles of tax-law... I don't think they can, they need to find some spell that resonates with the symbolism that the Order preaches, right?<br /> I just don't seem to find what the free council yantra symbolism is? I get <b><i>what </i></b>they can use but it's not that clear for what purpose.<br /> <br /> Okey now it's pretty clear, the Libertine symbolism is Culture. I didn't realize that every order has their symbolism in the heading in the &quot;Magical Symbolism: &lt;insert&gt;&quot; heading. Was looking over that and in the texts and it wasn't super clear exactly what was supposed to be their symbolism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yantras worth more than one die without a limitation or cost are thin on the ground and being able to use your hobbyist cliques to manage low-key magic better is inherently geared toward having the spaces where those specialties are relevant be important to the character. </div> </div> </div>Yeah they are sparse but the Techn\u00e9 merit takes up slots that you could fill most of the time anyway without it. Many times you can use a Enviroment yantra to get the same bonus. You need to be at Gnosis 3 before you could even take use of the whole merit as well as your order tool. It still takes up 3 slots to use the full effect if you want to incorporate your order tool as well, as it would be likely, already appropriate. Im just saying it seems like for most mages, it's just better to invest in the Shadow Name merit, even if you could only get one (which was pointed out, you can get more or change it). The Techn\u00e9 ain't any more universal as a yantra then the Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's two dots. </div> </div> </div>Still experience, about two sessions wasted<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the same price/.../ </div> </div> </div>Yeah but we're not talking about the other Order merits, which some of them are clearly better and more useful then others.<br /> But over all, it's only Masque, Prelacy and Epopt that's actually worth putting exp into, might be because they're styles.<br /> So 2 dots happens to be the common thing for the poor suckers that didn't get a style merit, but Lex Magica and Adamant Hand are arguably more useful even though the AH merit is pretty circumstantial. <br /> But yeah I'm aware that it's meant to be some extra spice for the characters, but why not make it one dot, or give every one styles that do something useful. If it ain't useful it ain't going to be bought. Sure mileage vary but i can't see why someone would choose Techn\u00e9 over a appropriate shadow name or such.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T05:25:04-07:00","id":1203795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203757#post1203757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no. the astral isn't a dream</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but surely you could use a Weaving or Patterning Mind spell to do just that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:43:03-07:00","id":1203869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203795#post1203795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but surely you could use a Weaving or Patterning Mind spell to do just that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didnt the astral realms book have something similar, just port over the spells. Somebody would have to pay the mana cost for entering the astral though, Im sure one of the 1e spells let the caster spend for people he brought along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:52:05-07:00","id":1203872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203794#post1203794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okey now it's pretty clear, the Libertine symbolism is Culture. I didn't realize that every order has their symbolism in the heading in the &quot;Magical Symbolism: &lt;insert&gt;&quot; heading. Was looking over that and in the texts and it wasn't super clear exactly what was supposed to be their symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was why I pointed to that section, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah they are sparse but the Techn\u00e9 merit takes up slots that you could fill most of the time anyway without it. Many times you can use a Enviroment yantra to get the same bonus. </div> </div> </div>By this selfsame logic you might as well never bother with common Sacraments. A place doesn't need to be resonant with gematria or ornithology for a character with the appropriate Techn\u00e9 to use the active presence of its practitioners anywhere to benefit spells that take less than a scene to cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You need to be at Gnosis 3 before you could even take use of the whole merit as well as your order tool. It still takes up 3 slots to use the full effect if you want to incorporate your order tool as well, as it would be likely, already appropriate. </div> </div> </div>You can make use of &quot;the whole Merit&quot; at Gnosis <i>1</i>. The bonuses Techn\u00e9 opens up are not meant to be the same as the singular bonus Shadow Name opens up. Most Yantras give less than two dice \u2014 this does not make them worthless to everyone with less than four &quot;slots.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Im just saying it seems like for most mages, it's just better to invest in the Shadow Name merit, even if you could only get one (which was pointed out, you can get more or change it). The Techn\u00e9 ain't any more universal as a yantra then the Shadow Name. </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> more universal than Shadow Name, because <i>what the Shadow Name Merit represents is more specific than Techn\u00e9</i>. Three dots in a Shadow Name built on the symbolism of a binder of demons won't let a Libertine use religious trappings and practices for things that don't fit with that persona.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still experience, about two sessions wasted </div> </div> </div>If your approach to a Merit is to call the cost of getting it a waste compared to picking up largely-redundant dots in another instance of a different Merit you already have, then it's just possible your approach to character advancement is askew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah I'm aware that it's meant to be some extra spice for the characters, but why not make it one dot, or give every one styles that do something useful. If it ain't useful it ain't going to be bought. Sure mileage vary but i can't see why someone would choose Techn\u00e9 over a appropriate shadow name or such. </div> </div> </div>Literally the same reasons a character would take Hobbyist Clique instead of/on top of Professional Training. It's not just about the dice bonuses and approaching the game in that manner is going to result in you asking a lot of fruitless variants on this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:51:35-07:00","id":1204305,"title":"","content":"Death Spell Devouring the Slain (Page 130) allows a mage to harvest willpower or mana (dealing damage in a ratio 1:1) for each potency from his target. With 1 reach a mage is allowed to cast this spell on a target that has not received damage. From what is written this seems like a superior version of a spell Rotting Flesh (page 132) or a Rank 4 spell Withering (page 133) allowing the mage to deal lethal damage with a 3 dot arcanum. Is this the intent of a design ? Personally I would rule that the target has to be stationary as the intent of the spell is not to deal damage, but to replenish the mages resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1013,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","user":"Stralos","date":". 04-07-2018, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:25:26-07:00","id":1204345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204305#post1204305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Spell Devouring the Slain (Page 130) allows a mage to harvest willpower or mana (dealing damage in a ratio 1:1) for each potency from his target. With 1 reach a mage is allowed to cast this spell on a target that has not received damage. From what is written this seems like a superior version of a spell Rotting Flesh (page 132) or a Rank 4 spell Withering (page 133) allowing the mage to deal lethal damage with a 3 dot arcanum. Is this the intent of a design ? Personally I would rule that the target has to be stationary as the intent of the spell is not to deal damage, but to replenish the mages resources.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without another Reach it counts towards the limit of times you can Scour, even if you harvest Willpower instead of Mana, so that might be a balancing element. And reading the spell's description again it seems that harvesting Willpower doesn't inflict damage, though it still counts towards the Scouring limit. And Rotting Flesh has a Reach option that inflicts Social penalties, while Withering can inflict aggravated damage, so they have their niches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:25:40-07:00","id":1204346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204305#post1204305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Spell Devouring the Slain (Page 130) allows a mage to harvest willpower or mana (dealing damage in a ratio 1:1) for each potency from his target. With 1 reach a mage is allowed to cast this spell on a target that has not received damage. From what is written this seems like a superior version of a spell Rotting Flesh (page 132) or a Rank 4 spell Withering (page 133) allowing the mage to deal lethal damage with a 3 dot arcanum. Is this the intent of a design ? Personally I would rule that the target has to be stationary as the intent of the spell is not to deal damage, but to replenish the mages resources.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1202876#post1202876\">We literally just did this one</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:44:36-07:00","id":1204355,"title":"","content":"In Legacies, it mentions that a spell that normally costs more than one Mana has the cost reduced to one Mana. However, since it seems like the spells are no longer improvised, what sort of spell costs more than one Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:19:45-07:00","id":1204365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204355#post1204355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Legacies, it mentions that a spell that normally costs more than one Mana has the cost reduced to one Mana. However, since it seems like the spells are no longer improvised, what sort of spell costs more than one Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found the most exploitative spell to turn into an Attainment is Platonic Form.<br /> Make yourself a construct with your Potency in Mana, get a discount down to 1 with the Attainment.<br /> Then drain all that Mana back out using Channel Mana.<br /> <br /> Boom, free Mana.<br /> <br /> But also Eidolon and Create Truth.<br /> <br /> Create Truth can also be rather ludicrous as a fifth Attainment (at Gnosis 8 though, so meh).<br /> Scene-long ritual, creates a 3-dot Hallow with a duration of a year, for a single point of Mana.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*<br /> But to concisely answer your question:<br /> Not very many, and those those do are usually quite ludicrous when they only cost 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 04-07-2018, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:40:36-07:00","id":1204377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204365#post1204365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make yourself a construct with your Potency in Mana, get a discount down to 1 with the Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potency increases the object's Mana <i>capacity</i>, which isn't filled for free by the fact of casting \u2014 the extra Mana &quot;cost&quot; is not so much <i>spent</i> as <i>transferred</i>. This is not just exploitative but conceptually shaky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Create Truth can also be rather ludicrous as a fifth Attainment (at Gnosis 8 though, so meh).<br /> Scene-long ritual, creates a 3-dot Hallow with a duration of a year, for a single point of Mana. </div> </div> </div>Create Truth is Withstood by the Potency of its own target effect \u2014 a 3-dot Hallow would require an effective Potency of 6 to produce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:43:48-07:00","id":1204379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204377#post1204377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potency increases the object's Mana <i>capacity</i>, which isn't filled for free by the fact of casting \u2014 the extra Mana &quot;cost&quot; is not so much <i>spent</i> as <i>transferred</i>. This is not just exploitative but conceptually shaky.<br /> <br /> Create Truth is Withstood by the Potency of its own target effect \u2014 a 3-dot Hallow would require an effective Potency of 6 to produce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely correct with regards to Create Truth, can't believe I missed that.<br /> However Platonic From states its cost is 1+<br /> Which implies that the cost is a part of the spell, and viable for the reduction.<br /> <br /> Either way you can just do what I do with my Legacy updates, and have that single point be 'stretched' across multiple uses.<br /> <br /> Despite my fondness, the books are far from perfect and require some sensible adjudication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T11:25:45-07:00","id":1204633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204305#post1204305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Spell Devouring the Slain (Page 130) allows a mage to harvest willpower or mana (dealing damage in a ratio 1:1) for each potency from his target. With 1 reach a mage is allowed to cast this spell on a target that has not received damage. From what is written this seems like a superior version of a spell Rotting Flesh (page 132) or a Rank 4 spell Withering (page 133) allowing the mage to deal lethal damage with a 3 dot arcanum. Is this the intent of a design ? Personally I would rule that the target has to be stationary as the intent of the spell is not to deal damage, but to replenish the mages resources.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Satchel's prior answers are on point, but its also worth noting that Devouring the Slain is Withstood, while Withering/Rotting Flesh is not. That puts a pretty significant dent in the spells impact damage wise. Its a powerful spell, but I think it compares pretty well to plenty of the other crazy stuff that opens up at Disciple level.<br /> <br /> PS Obviously, don't forget to point out to your players that using it frequently is likely to lose them a lot of Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T21:55:15-07:00","id":1205093,"title":"","content":"Ward's RAW primary is Potency, but it uses Clash of Wills, so it doesn't benefit from increased Potency. Should its primary be Duration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T22:19:22-07:00","id":1205097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1205093#post1205093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ward's RAW primary is Potency, but it uses Clash of Wills, so it doesn't benefit from increased Potency. Should its primary be Duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a old copy, The errata'd copy has wards primary as duration. Go update it on drivethrurpg..which really should have given you the errata copy by now though? Odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T23:02:52-07:00","id":1205106,"title":"","content":"Oh, you are correct. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:42:01-07:00","id":1205396,"title":"","content":"Would a Mortal attempting to use a merit based Supernatural power against a Mage automatically fail any Clash of Wills that might result or would they use their dots in the merit as their Clash dice? E.g. a Mortal has Telepathy and uses it against a Mage with Mental Shield active. My assumption is that they'd simply fail.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:58:30-07:00","id":1205408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1205396#post1205396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Mortal attempting to use a merit based Supernatural power against a Mage automatically fail any Clash of Wills that might result or would they use their dots in the merit as their Clash dice? E.g. a Mortal has Telepathy and uses it against a Mage with Mental Shield active. My assumption is that they'd simply fail.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d let them Clash, though I have no idea what their dice pools would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:09:12-07:00","id":1205411,"title":"","content":"Mortals have never had rules for Clashes of Wills. To say it bugs me is an understatement.<br /> The closest you could do to how it works for supers is to roll the Attribute most relevant to the used Supernatural Merit (which would be the Attribute in the activation dice pool if there is one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:45:15-07:00","id":1205418,"title":"","content":"Usually Mortals activate a power by spending and then rolling WP, don't they? If so that would be the CoW dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T17:22:52-07:00","id":1205425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1205418#post1205418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually Mortals activate a power by spending and then rolling WP, don't they? If so that would be the CoW dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any power I've seen. Most use Attribute+skill and some (or most) costs a point of WP.<br /> But CoW for mortals has been discussed a few times on the forums, but no clear answer i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T18:39:55-07:00","id":1205430,"title":"","content":"I default to a single Attribute for mortals (since not all supernatural merits scale).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T00:47:50-07:00","id":1205486,"title":"","content":"So if I'm reading this correctly, *every* spell a mage casts in the same scene after they've triggered a paradox roll has a paradox roll. Yes no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:28:01-07:00","id":1205499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1205486#post1205486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm reading this correctly, *every* spell a mage casts in the same scene after they've triggered a paradox roll has a paradox roll. Yes no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, every paradox roll a mage makes after the first in a scene gets a cumulative paradox modifier of +1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:52:10-07:00","id":1205505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taralx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1205486#post1205486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm reading this correctly, *every* spell a mage casts in the same scene after they've triggered a paradox roll has a paradox roll. Yes no?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only on the other spells that risk Paradox. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:48:15-07:00","id":1205573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1205505#post1205505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, only on the other spells that risk Paradox. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeh, i missed the *every* part. It should read: Not every spell but every paradox roll made..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:02:01-07:00","id":1206025,"title":"","content":"It seems likely, but could Making spells create Temenotic Realms or Underworld Dominions? Should these be modeled on Spirit Manse? Are there any particular details that might differ from that spell that should be paid attention to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:04:58-07:00","id":1206059,"title":"","content":"I think that requires the Imperial Practice Domains, but could be wrong. For example, you can create a pocket dimension with Space Making instead of Domains. So creating a Dead Dominion might be possible with Death 5 + Space 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:21:28-07:00","id":1206064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206059#post1206059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that requires the Imperial Practice Domains, but could be wrong. For example, you can create a pocket dimension with Space Making instead of Domains. So creating a Dead Dominion might be possible with Death 5 + Space 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit Manse creates an area in the Shadow, why would this be different and why would it require Space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:35:52-07:00","id":1206073,"title":"","content":"Creating dead dominions specifically with all related mechanics sounds like dominions. Creating a little pocket in the underworld that either uses autch depths rules or just resides in another domain and uses their rules would be Making, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:24:54-07:00","id":1206097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206064#post1206064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit Manse creates an area in the Shadow, why would this be different</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason you don't need Spirit 5 to cross into the Shadow outside an established Iris \u2014 the way the Shadow works is not quite like the other otherworlds, particularly not the Temenos. (Pending the next dev blog from Geist we also have no idea how the Underworld's functioning may have changed from 1e.) Outside of semantics and arbitrary symmetry there's no reason to automatically assume Spirit Manse has identical equivalents in the other Subtle Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:48:44-07:00","id":1206134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206097#post1206097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same reason you don't need Spirit 5 to cross into the Shadow outside an established Iris \u2014 the way the Shadow works is not quite like the other otherworlds, particularly not the Temenos. (Pending the next dev blog from Geist we also have no idea how the Underworld's functioning may have changed from 1e.) Outside of semantics and arbitrary symmetry there's no reason to automatically assume Spirit Manse has identical equivalents in the other Subtle Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div> There\u2019s also no reason to assume there isn\u2019t. It can go either way depending on ST leniency. Assuming it\u2019s possible what needs to be taken into consideration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T13:05:24-07:00","id":1206141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206134#post1206134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There\u2019s also no reason to assume there isn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you assume Life 4 has the same capacity to evaporate people as Matter 4 has to evaporate rocks? Would you assume Prime 5 has the same capacity to create Mana wholesale as Spirit 5 has for making Essence? Would you assume Time 4 gave you the ability to teleport in the same manner as Space 4? The setting metaphysics are not Calvinball.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming it\u2019s possible what needs to be taken into consideration? </div> </div> </div><i>How space works in those other realms</i>. Spirit Manse creates a new instance of a known phenomenon in a dimension where the parameters of a territory are plastic due in part to a variable degree of reference to the neighboring portions of the physical world. The Temenos is fashioned from powerful shared ideas that are never quite truly forgotten and the Underworld is a sealed-off hostile environment by simple virtue of what it is; neither of them operate in the same way as the Shadow does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T13:56:16-07:00","id":1206155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206141#post1206141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you assume Life 4 has the same capacity to evaporate people as Matter 4 has to evaporate rocks? Would you assume Prime 5 has the same capacity to create Mana wholesale as Spirit 5 has for making Essence? Would you assume Time 4 gave you the ability to teleport in the same manner as Space 4? The setting metaphysics are not Calvinball.<br /> <br /> <i>How space works in those other realms</i>. Spirit Manse creates a new instance of a known phenomenon in a dimension where the parameters of a territory are plastic due in part to a variable degree of reference to the neighboring portions of the physical world. The Temenos is fashioned from powerful shared ideas that are never quite truly forgotten and the Underworld is a sealed-off hostile environment by simple virtue of what it is; neither of them operate in the same way as the Shadow does.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order, yes with enough Potency, yes, no because time and space aren\u2019t the same in Mage and only one controls your location in space.<br /> <br /> The Temenos is also flexible though in that any group thought no matter how small or uninfluential creates a realm associated with it.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is admittedly more of a question mark for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T14:08:16-07:00","id":1206157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206155#post1206155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Temenos is also flexible though in that <b>any group thought no matter how small or uninfluential creates a realm associated with it.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> &quot;If an author or other type of artist creates a new narrative, but never shares this work with anyone else, then his ideas naturally remain part of his own Oneiros and have no effect on the Temenos. The same thing happens when artists share their work with others, only to find that everyone exposed to the work is completely uninterested. <b>In such cases, the work lacks the power to become part of the Temenos. Also, if a work is too similar to some existing narrative that is better known and that has a more powerful effect on viewers, then this new narrative is effectively subsumed into the realm of the Temenos occupied by the other, more well-known and powerful work. </b>In such cases, the few distinctive features of the new narrative are either eliminated or become another minor element in the realm associated with the more popular narrative.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T14:18:34-07:00","id":1206162,"title":"","content":"Okay, that\u2019s not a direct refutation of my point, first it means that the realm you create only needs a group that\u2019s influenced to create it in the first place. Second minor elements can eventually end up dominating a bigger thing as people turn their attention to it.<br /> <br /> Granted though, you\u2019re more likely to find success generating new Oneiros realms than Temenos ones via a Making spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T14:49:48-07:00","id":1206170,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a><br /> <br /> Time &quot;Teleporting&quot; would really be essentially a Temporal Pocket - you don't <i>teleport</i> per se, you simply move there in what seems like an instantaneous amount of time to everyone but you. At least I think that's what they had in mind when they wrote that post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T15:40:27-07:00","id":1206179,"title":"","content":"The short answer seems to be that the Shadow is more mutable than the other Invisible Realms, hence Spirit Manse.<br /> <br /> From what we\u2019ve seen in 2E tidbits, Dead Dominions seem to be tied too closely to its kerberos for normal mages to replicate. And the part Satchel quoted seems to imply that a mage will have better luck temporarily gating off an existing Temenotic realm, \u2018creating\u2019 a new Astral realm in the same way idigam can \u2018create\u2019 new Deep Shadow realms by taking a chunk out of the existing Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:22:21-07:00","id":1206958,"title":"","content":"Can a master of time go back in time, kill the parents of an ennemy mage before this mage is ever born thus effectively erase him from history and killing him in the process ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:48:20-07:00","id":1206970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206958#post1206958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a master of time go back in time, kill the parents of an ennemy mage before this mage is ever born thus effectively erase him from history and killing him in the process ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, unless that Mage has Constant Presence active (which would give them a Clash to survive, but people would still act as if they don't know them since they don't exist in the timeline anymore)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:51:00-07:00","id":1206971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206970#post1206970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, unless that Mage has Constant Presence active (which would give them a Clash to survive, but people would still act as if they don't know them since they don't exist in the timeline anymore)</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, if he'd cast Constant Presence on his parents via Temporal Sympathy, which may avoid the latter issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:16:04-07:00","id":1206978,"title":"","content":"Wow, i tought erasing an Awakened timeline was Archemastery level","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:40:24-07:00","id":1206986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206978#post1206978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, i tought erasing an Awakened timeline was Archemastery level</div> </div> </div> </div>Safely erasing it without unintended side effects and not changing anything else in the process is Archmastery. Or if the other mage is older than you, you'd need Archmastery as time 5 can only go back as far as your own (the subject's) lifetime (though you could instead send someone else even older back to do it for you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:47:09-07:00","id":1206989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206971#post1206971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, if he'd cast Constant Presence on his parents via Temporal Sympathy, which may avoid the latter issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Temporal Sympathy works \u2014 eligibility for that Attainment post-errata works as a whitelist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:58:54-07:00","id":1206993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206986#post1206986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safely erasing it without unintended side effects and not changing anything else in the process is Archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Events in Time will hue as closely to the original timeline as possible in spite of changes. This is what prevents causal temporal paradox in Mage and saves the ST a headache. The butterfly effect is minimal, you\u2019re actually more likely to get it with Archmasters if they end up generating Aponoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T13:03:09-07:00","id":1206994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206989#post1206989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how Temporal Sympathy works \u2014 eligibility for that Attainment post-errata works as a whitelist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't actually played as or with an Acanthus that bothered with TS since before the errata - but I thought you could use combined spells to work around that, to a point?<br /> <br /> Alternatively...could he just put Constant Presence on his parents in the present? I suppose it wouldn't actually have to placed on their past selves to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 04-14-2018, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T13:16:17-07:00","id":1206999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206993#post1206993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Events in Time will hue as closely to the original timeline as possible in spite of changes. This is what prevents causal temporal paradox in Mage and saves the ST a headache. The butterfly effect is minimal, you\u2019re actually more likely to get it with Archmasters if they end up generating Aponoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where'd you read that? I don't see anything like that in the section on Time magic in the book (It just talks about there not being temporal paradoxes because of undoing your reason for traveling, etc), and what I recall from the Developers is that archmastery is the 'safe' way to make changes to the past as it's the only way to account for all of the potential changes and oddities.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Found the quote I was thinking of<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/827072-how-does-time-work-in-mage?p=828106#post828106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's a time gap, it gets filled in &quot;naturally&quot; by whatever's most likely to have happened following the altered events.<br /> <br /> Which means that <b>the further back you go, the more you're leaving to chance.</b><br /> <br /> A Dynamic Time Travel spell would use Time 6 and work backward - archmages stipulate what they want the <i>outcome</i> of their shenanigans to be, and the Imperial spell then traces back and adjusts history appropriately by itself, without the archmage's input. <b>It's much, much safer, but that's why archmasters are feared and respected.</b><br /> <br /> The Imperial Practices do still exist in 2e; the progression of Dynamics, Excision, Entities, Dominions, and Transfiguration is still there, just like it was in 1e before we wrote Imperial Mysteries. &quot;Archmages can make self-adjusting spells at six dots, templates at seven, subsouls and pocket worlds at eight, and anything at nine&quot; has always been in the gameline's underlying assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/827072-how-does-time-work-in-mage?p=828166#post828166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a Time Master could, say, go back a month, ensure his spell has a Duration longer than that, spend that month's do-over micromanaging everything he wanted to change, and then when he caught back up to the present his spell would end and the new history become &quot;set&quot;. If he wanted to alter something that happened ten years ago but couldn't manage anything beyond the month Duration, though... Well, that's much riskier, as he doesn't know what will have happened in the intervening 9 years and 11 months. Once his spell ends, history fills itself in, with no regard for what he may have wanted.<br /> <br /> Which I feel is an appropriate level of &quot;we want to allow Masters more time travel than they had in first edition, but we don't want to just give them the same capability as archmasters&quot; balance. You have to be very careful when meddling with the past beyond the immediately preceding events, and many Masters of Time just plain don't think it's worth the risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":".  Dave quotes 04-14-2018, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:36:07-07:00","id":1207036,"title":"","content":"Hum i'm still very confused, time is messing with my head","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:37:28-07:00","id":1207037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1206994#post1206994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't actually played as or with an Acanthus that bothered with TS since before the errata - but I thought you could use combined spells to work around that, to a point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Sympathy only extends the timeframe of spells that target the past, like Postcognition, instead of allowing mages to cast spells before they actually cast the spell. So no fireballs from the future. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively...could he just put Constant Presence on his parents in the present? I suppose it wouldn't actually have to placed on their past selves to begin with. </div> </div> </div>Hmm... then maybe this saves those parents, but the world will already have changed so that they were always murdered. Not sure on this, unlike Temporal Sympathy - been awhile since I read Constance Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:23:17-07:00","id":1207050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207037#post1207037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporal Sympathy only extends the timeframe of spells that target the past, like Postcognition, instead of allowing mages to cast spells before they actually cast the spell. So no fireballs from the future.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Sympathy points out you could Combine Spells to do just that. Combine a Fireball spell with Postcognition and you could hurl a fireball into the room the enemy stood in yesterday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:28:22-07:00","id":1207053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207050#post1207050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporal Sympathy points out you could Combine Spells to do just that. Combine a Fireball spell with Postcognition and you could hurl a fireball into the room the enemy stood in yesterday.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sure the combined spells had to actually make sense with the Time spell being combined. Like Postcognition with Detect Substance. But I\u2019ll double-check the pdf when I get home. <br /> <br /> That fireball trick might work if it\u2019s being combined with Shifting Sands... but then it\u2019s less fireball from the future and more fireballing mage from the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:39:16-07:00","id":1207060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207053#post1207053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m sure the combined spells had to actually make sense with the Time spell being combined. Like Postcognition with Detect Substance. But I\u2019ll double-check the pdf when I get home.<br /> <br /> That fireball trick might work if it\u2019s being combined with Shifting Sands... but then it\u2019s less fireball from the future and more fireballing mage from the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing about making sense exists in the write up:<br /> &quot;but unlike Sympathetic Range,<br /> Temporal Sympathy can only be used on Time spells that call<br /> for it and other spells Combined with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> But even if it did, you could Combine some more fitting spells to wack someone from the future.<br /> As well, Shifting Sands don't use Temporal Sympathy, you time travel yourself (or the subject) back a few turns/scenes and redo stuff while the duration is active.<br /> So you can't combine the fireball with that spell to throw a fireball from the future. You get yourself back in time, throw a fireball and go back to the present as two different spells, not a Combined one.<br /> <br /> And listed how few spells actually call for Temporal Sympathy, Postcognition combined with another spell is probably the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:01:47-07:00","id":1207064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207060#post1207060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can't combine the fireball with that spell to throw a fireball from the future. You get yourself back in time, throw a fireball and go back to the present as two different spells, not a Combined one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because, as falco's quotation points out, it leaves <i>a massive amount to chance</i>, to say nothing of how Shifting Sands is still subject to the standard rules of time travel and there's reason to believe traveling back in time doesn't put you in a different place than you were back then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And listed how few spells actually call for Temporal Sympathy, Postcognition combined with another spell is probably the way to go. </div> </div> </div>Not really, no, because the thing that Postcognition does and the thing that a different spell piggybacking on what Postcognition does are unlikely to be close enough to share Yantra semiotics unless the latter is another sensory spell.<br /> <br /> &quot;Probably the way to go&quot; is to not assume that retroactive casting is part of the intended design space \u2014 Temporal Sympathy prevents spells from beginning before they were cast without actually moving their point of origin to the same point in the timeline, a la &quot;go back in time and cast a fireball, don't cast a fireball back in time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:07:38-07:00","id":1207067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207060#post1207060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nothing about making sense exists in the write up:<br /> &quot;but unlike Sympathetic Range,<br /> Temporal Sympathy can only be used on Time spells that call<br /> for it and other spells Combined with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> But even if it did, you could Combine some more fitting spells to wack someone from the future.<br /> As well, Shifting Sands don't use Temporal Sympathy, you time travel yourself (or the subject) back a few turns/scenes and redo stuff while the duration is active.<br /> So you can't combine the fireball with that spell to throw a fireball from the future. You get yourself back in time, throw a fireball and go back to the present as two different spells, not a Combined one.<br /> <br /> And listed how few spells actually call for Temporal Sympathy, Postcognition combined with another spell is probably the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-Archmastery Time magic that sends something to the past work by destroying the timeline up to the desired point of effect. That is, sending a subject to the past (without Archmastery) requires the mage to select a point in the subject\u2019s past. Now consider that spells don\u2019t exist until you actually cast them. There is no past history of the spell that you can send the spell back to. That is why spells can\u2019t be cast from the present into the past, short of Archmastery which can create Irises to the past, circumventing everything I said above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:29:22-07:00","id":1207078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207064#post1207064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because, as falco's quotation points out, it leaves <i>a massive amount to chance</i>, to say nothing of how Shifting Sands is still subject to the standard rules of time travel and there's reason to believe traveling back in time doesn't put you in a different place than you were back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just pointing out that Shifting Sands ain't compatible with Temporal sympathy, and because it ain't you can't &quot;throw fireballs back in time&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really, no, because the thing that Postcognition does and the thing that a different spell piggybacking on what Postcognition does are unlikely to be close enough to share Yantra semiotics unless the latter is another sensory spell.<br /> <br /> &quot;Probably the way to go&quot; is to not assume that retroactive casting is part of the intended design space &quot; </div> </div> </div>How is yantra semiotics even relevant to this? You don't even need a Yantra except for an old photo or such for Temporal Sympathy, which would have a semiotic connection to the past subject. <br /> <br /> How is not assuming &quot;other spells Combined with them.&quot; not intended design? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Temporal Sympathy prevents spells from beginning before they were cast without actually moving their point of origin to the same point in the timeline, a la &quot;go back in time and cast a fireball, don't cast a fireball back in time. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if i follow what you mean here. Would you mind giving some explanation, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:42:44-07:00","id":1207082,"title":"","content":"About Shifting Sands; I was using that as an example of how to cast a spell into the past, not what can be Combined with past-affecting spells and be extended via Temporal Sympathy. Sorry if I was misleading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:43:01-07:00","id":1207083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207067#post1207067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pre-Archmastery Time magic that sends something to the past work by destroying the timeline up to the desired point of effect. That is, sending a subject to the past (without Archmastery) requires the mage to select a point in the subject\u2019s past. Now consider that spells don\u2019t exist until you actually cast them. There is no past history of the spell that you can send the spell back to. That is why spells can\u2019t be cast from the present into the past, short of Archmastery which can create Irises to the past, circumventing everything I said above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well this logic does not apply with either Shifting Sands or Corridors of Time, the later being able of using Temporal Sympathy. It's a circle argument and paradoxical to that.<br /> If the Present sends something into the Past and by that action the time after the Past is destroyed and a new Present created, nothing was ever Sent to the Past. If this was true, then temporal sympathy wouldn't work at all with Corridors of Time. The Present would 'catch up' and 'act' like it has always been. A &quot;fireball to the past&quot; would have the same impact on the Present as a Shifting Sand spell, in where the new Present 'acts' like the fireball was always cast.<br /> <br /> Time magic works around the causal loop paradox by acting as if time always was as before it was changed. <br /> <br /> Pre-Archmastery Time magic that sends something to the past work by destroying the timeline <i>after</i> the desired point of effect, ergo where the spell duration starts in the past.<br /> <br /> If I send someone back in time for one minute to the first of June 2017: 23:45, everything after the arrival on 23:45 that date is destroyed, the time traveler has one minute to make changes to history, in which after time fills back to cover what happened between now and 23:46 of June 1st 2017, and the time traveler is back to this date, everything between is filled by ST fiat, butterfly effect and whatever logic would follow the actions, small or large is up to the ST.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:07:31-07:00","id":1207092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207078#post1207078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is yantra semiotics even relevant to this?[\u2026]<br /> How is not assuming &quot;other spells Combined with them.&quot; not intended design?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apply a common-sense reading here: Yantra bonuses apply to every component of a Combined spell and there are multiple spells whose combined effects would be nonsensical to parse out as a thing you were conducting as a singular describable act of magic. Given the constraints of Combined spells, that means a very small dicepool if the effect is allowed at all.<br /> <br /> Postcognition combined with a spell results in Postcognition and the other spell's effects becoming active at the same time \u2014 it doesn't track at all as the vector for an offensive spell, since all of the things you would have to do to be able to cast on them with Temporal Sympathy already puts their vulnerability at your disposal and there is zero delay between &quot;perceive past version of target&quot; and &quot;harm past version of target.&quot; Sensory spells, meanwhile, scan perfectly to that combination, because what Postcognition gives you is a view of the record, not a probe in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure if i follow what you mean here. Would you mind giving some explanation, please? </div> </div> </div>Spells begin when they're cast and end when they end; they do not exist before or after that span, and Time magic largely works around that by creating effects that either reference the history of an object from the present as sensory information or temporarily propel the user along their or history in the volatile state of a time-traveler.<br /> <br /> It is the latter state that allows a character anything like retroactive influence, and only then through displacing the origin point of that influence to within the normal flow of causality \u2014 if there's a fireball that's been cast into the past, it's because there was someone or something put into the past to cast it from a starting point in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:45:08-07:00","id":1207109,"title":"","content":"Yours and others arguments has given me somethings to think about. And it seems like you're all quite right. Thanks for straightening the temporal sympathy thing out a bit.<br /> <br /> But then comes another question: Besides getting some saved word count on a few time spells, what good is the Time 2 attainment for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You really can't use it for anything besides a few Reach effects,costing mana and sensory range for like a handful of spells.<br /> All Temporal sympathy comes down to is word count if it really can't be used for anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T20:27:38-07:00","id":1207140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207109#post1207109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then comes another question: Besides getting some saved word count on a few time spells, what good is the Time 2 attainment for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a question of &quot;good for.&quot; It's an ability that modifies your spellcasting options and becomes available at a specific degree of mastery in a particular Arcanum \u2014 the word for that is &quot;Attainment.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T20:36:02-07:00","id":1207143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207140#post1207140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a question of &quot;good for.&quot; It's an ability that modifies your spellcasting options and becomes available at a specific degree of mastery in a particular Arcanum \u2014 the word for that is &quot;Attainment.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was a rhetorical question though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T22:42:52-07:00","id":1207169,"title":"","content":"I mean, a permissive Storyteller could still certainly allow the Postcognition Fireball (I probably would) while abiding with a reasonable interpretation of the RAW.<br /> <br /> But your DP is going to be lower in general, as Satchel points out, as well it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T06:34:34-07:00","id":1207240,"title":"","content":"What is this Parametric Language the Secret Order of the Gate is said to use? The word &quot;parametric,&quot; at a glance, seems to have many different meanings, and I can't figure out which one the Order is supposed to be referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:24:01-07:00","id":1207257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207240#post1207240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this Parametric Language the Secret Order of the Gate is said to use? The word &amp;quot;parametric,&amp;quot; at a glance, seems to have many different meanings, and I can't figure out which one the Order is supposed to be referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Parametric Language is the Gate's occult tongue. The Secret Order believes the Lonely Exarch used it to command the Abyss to open, and tame the newly-Fallen World -- and to banish it, so that the fallen World would survive. It is a language that gives comprehensible structures to the Abyss' anti-entities. It's a tongue of negatives, that defines things based on what they are not, providing a general conceptual shape -- even a prison -- for Abyssal entities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Found on a wikia so not necessarily 100% correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:16:26-07:00","id":1207340,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Choose the Thread have Duration as a primary factor? Potency doesn't really do anything but make it harder to dispel vs other spells that actually use potency (ie for bonuses, penalties, or other effects) This is simply the next roll within a duration that can be rolled twice, no bonuses or penalties or anything that's really affected by Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:38:46-07:00","id":1207348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207340#post1207340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Choose the Thread have Duration as a primary factor? Potency doesn't really do anything but make it harder to dispel vs other spells that actually use potency (ie for bonuses, penalties, or other effects) This is simply the next roll within a duration that can be rolled twice, no bonuses or penalties or anything that's really affected by Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells that contend with Withstand are Potency primary, you can cast Choose the Thread on someone else and make them take the worse of the two rolls for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T12:55:37-07:00","id":1207381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207240#post1207240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this Parametric Language the Secret Order of the Gate is said to use? The word &quot;parametric,&quot; at a glance, seems to have many different meanings, and I can't figure out which one the Order is supposed to be referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda thought it might mean something like defining. If the Abyss makes no sense, then the language gives it definition so the Mage can work with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:40:11-07:00","id":1207458,"title":"","content":"New question ! Does a mage with spirit can inflict damage to other ephemeral being liek ghost and goetia or angel without adding another arcana ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:44:25-07:00","id":1207459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207458#post1207458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question ! Does a mage with spirit can inflict damage to other ephemeral being liek ghost and goetia or angel without adding another arcana ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without some means of affecting that entity like its being Materialized or both of you being in a space where its form of Twilight doesn't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:51:52-07:00","id":1207462,"title":"","content":"Well with the Howl From Beyond it says it can affect physical being and spirit in the twilight, but does other entity in the twilight get hurt too if i'm aware of their presence ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:56:45-07:00","id":1207465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207462#post1207462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well with the Howl From Beyond it says it can affect physical being and spirit in the twilight, but does other entity in the twilight get hurt too if i'm aware of their presence ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without other Arcana, because that's how Twilight works. Ghosts don't interact with spirits in Twilight, and Howl From Beyond is a means of interacting with the form of Twilight used by spirits in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T19:36:04-07:00","id":1207488,"title":"","content":"A question involving Primary Factors and their minimum level when boosted through Advanced Potency/Duration: Let's say Adam Acanthus wants to cast Oaths Fulfilled to see how a deal he just made will go down in the future. He's a Disciple of Fate, so Primary factor is 3, or 3 turns. He casts it, and selects Advanced Duration for one of his Reaches. Does his spell's duration heighten up to 1 scene/hour, or to a higher amount?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:22:49-07:00","id":1207511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207488#post1207488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question involving Primary Factors and their minimum level when boosted through Advanced Potency/Duration: Let's say Adam Acanthus wants to cast Oaths Fulfilled to see how a deal he just made will go down in the future. He's a Disciple of Fate, so Primary factor is 3, or 3 turns. He casts it, and selects Advanced Duration for one of his Reaches. Does his spell's duration heighten up to 1 scene/hour, or to a higher amount?</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of extra steps transfers directly in the switch from the Standard to Advanced version of a spell factor. That's one of the main things Duration-primary spells are written to benefit from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:41:42-07:00","id":1207521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207511#post1207511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The number of extra steps transfers directly in the switch from the Standard to Advanced version of a spell factor. That's one of the main things Duration-primary spells are written to benefit from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which means the spell in the example would last for a day, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:49:30-07:00","id":1207523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207521#post1207521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which means the spell in the example would last for a day, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>A week; two extra steps is two extra steps on the Advanced table as well as the Standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T21:13:43-07:00","id":1207526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207523#post1207523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A week; two extra steps is two extra steps on the Advanced table as well as the Standard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wasn't sure about all this. Thanks for clarifying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:39:01-07:00","id":1207730,"title":"","content":"For a Time based healing spell, should I allow the health restored to be a Lasting effect by default or should I allow any Lasting healing only as a reach option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:48:39-07:00","id":1207732,"title":"","content":"You increase the timeflow of healing. The healing itself is just a side effect and therefor Lasting. (It should also increase the rate for other biological processes like the menstrual cycle and ageing and such.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T13:40:45-07:00","id":1207745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207732#post1207732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You increase the timeflow of healing. The healing itself is just a side effect and therefor Lasting. (It should also increase the rate for other biological processes like the menstrual cycle and ageing and such.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have it advance hunger, thirst, and fatigue too, personally, with a Reach option to bypass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:21:21-07:00","id":1207771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207745#post1207745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have it advance hunger, thirst, and fatigue too, personally, with a Reach option to bypass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 2, Body Control does all this and what's more it's all positive effects lol.<br /> As for time, it'd likely be just easy to cut yourself out of time (ie veil of moments but with indefinite duration or however long you need) and just &quot;fast forward&quot; the present needle rest of the party has some time to act while you essentially heal in a hyperbolic chamber lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:48:12-07:00","id":1207784,"title":"","content":"Are the Secondary spell factors of a spell 1, or half the Highest Arcanum used in the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:57:58-07:00","id":1207785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207784#post1207784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Secondary spell factors of a spell 1, or half the Highest Arcanum used in the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The primary factor goes up by arcanum dots, there rest stay at the top of their respective charts (unless you take -2 and so on)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T16:22:37-07:00","id":1207795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207784#post1207784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Secondary spell factors of a spell 1, or half the Highest Arcanum used in the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Secondary spell factors are 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T17:09:19-07:00","id":1207806,"title":"","content":"Dont know if this question is within the purview of the thread but...<br /> <br /> What would be the consequences of having Wisdom start at 3 instead of 7 at character creation?<br /> <br /> From what i remember from the book starting at 3 wisdom would affect the duration of the paradox anomaly (longer than at 7 wisdom), the roll to contain the paradox and the duration of the paradox condition (shorter than at 7 wisdom).<br /> <br /> Am i missing anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T17:37:57-07:00","id":1207811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207806#post1207806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont know if this question is within the purview of the thread but...<br /> <br /> What would be the consequences of having Wisdom start at 3 instead of 7 at character creation?<br /> <br /> From what i remember from the book starting at 3 wisdom would affect the duration of the paradox anomaly (longer than at 7 wisdom), the roll to contain the paradox and the duration of the paradox condition (shorter than at 7 wisdom).<br /> <br /> Am i missing anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>It will take you at least four stories of concentrated effort to get up to Wisdom 7 and everything you ever cast a spell on or use as a Yantra will be a valid subject for your Long-Term Nimbus until you raise your Wisdom to 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T18:02:23-07:00","id":1207816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207811#post1207811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will take you at least four stories of concentrated effort to get up to Wisdom 7 and everything you ever cast a spell on or use as a Yantra will be a valid subject for your Long-Term Nimbus until you raise your Wisdom to 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh i hadnt thought of the nimbus. Good catch thanks, i'll go reread that.<br /> I'm not overly concerned about reaching back to wisdom 7. If a player is interested in uping theyre wisdom i'll look into allowing them to buy more starting wisdom with merit points (like maybe 3 point for 1 more wisdom or something).<br /> Tho it might be better to make the starting wisdom 4 instead of 3 with the nimbus things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T10:20:11-07:00","id":1208935,"title":"","content":"Would a practice of unravelling in Prime +Forces or Matter be enough to transmute raw energies or matter into mana ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T11:29:43-07:00","id":1208957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1208935#post1208935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a practice of unravelling in Prime +Forces or Matter be enough to transmute raw energies or matter into mana ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that\u2019s actually Patterning. The mana will revert when the spell expires though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-19-2018, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:21:01-07:00","id":1208975,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it be lasting ? Since you destroyed something to his base component and absorbed it in your pattern ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:37:17-07:00","id":1208979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1208975#post1208975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it be lasting ? Since you destroyed something to his base component and absorbed it in your pattern ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because mana isn\u2019t a base component of everything in existence anymore as far as I can tell. That was a 1e concept that was a holdover from Ascension. Mana now is more like Supernal radiation. So you can\u2019t destroy something down to mana, but you can transform it into mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:08:04-07:00","id":1208990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1208979#post1208979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because mana isn\u2019t a base component of everything in existence anymore as far as I can tell. That was a 1e concept that was a holdover from Ascension. Mana now is more like Supernal radiation. So you can\u2019t destroy something down to mana, but you can transform it into mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum but if you use the mana for spellcasting or if you spend it on something else like pattern restauration, what would happen once the duration of the spell is over ? And furthermore, since a mage with a familiar can transfer mana and essence between them, would you say that transforming essence from a resonant condition to mana would be lasting ? Since they both are &quot;spiritual&quot; non material &quot;fuel&quot; ?<br /> <br /> (My character is a stigmatic who awekened so i had this idea of a Prime based legacy for him, his brand acting like another mana reservoir and maybe letting him gorge himself on essence that would converted to mana once per day from a resonant condition as spirit would)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:13:09-07:00","id":1208991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1208990#post1208990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And furthermore, since a mage with a familiar can transfer mana and essence between them, would you say that transforming essence from a resonant condition to mana would be lasting ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's lasting because it's done through the Familiar Manifestation. The spell only grants that Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:16:04-07:00","id":1208992,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the transformation of essence to mana from a Familiar is Lasting for the same reason most spell effects are Lasting, it\u2019s a secondary effect rather than the point of the spell.<br /> <br /> As for energy or Matter converted to mana that\u2019s subsequently consumed, I\u2019d say that\u2019s gone for simplicity\u2019s sake, but it could slowly lead to molecular build ups or fevers or something after the spell would have expired. Probably nothing immediately harmful, but requiring monitoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-19-2018, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T14:11:18-07:00","id":1209007,"title":"","content":"Alright, that makes sense ! Thanks for the help ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:32:27-07:00","id":1209424,"title":"","content":"Why does a mage with death only need a practice of weaving to open a portal to twilight and turn to ephemera but spirit mage need at least 4 to be able to enter twilight as per the spells Ghost gate and Twilight body ? Also i assume a mage can shape spirit ephemera or essence into object at the same level death mage can shape ectoplasm and death attuned ephemera ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:40:07-07:00","id":1209425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209424#post1209424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does a mage with death only need a practice of weaving to open a portal to twilight and turn to ephemera but spirit mage need at least 4 to be able to enter twilight as per the spells Ghost gate and Twilight body ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In-universe reasoning may be that the Arcanum of transitions has relatively easier access to its relevant liminal state of being, compared to the Arcanum of repercussions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also i assume a mage can shape spirit ephemera or essence into object at the same level death mage can shape ectoplasm and death attuned ephemera ? </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I\u2019d rule so for spirit ephemera, but not for Essence since it doesn\u2019t look like something that can be shaped by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Grammar 04-20-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:55:20-07:00","id":1209430,"title":"","content":"I guess that most things in the material could get a reflection into death twilight when it dies and become ghosts but doesn't have the same connection toward the shadow and that's why it's a patterning spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:05:40-07:00","id":1209438,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm... I\u2019d rule so for spirit ephemera, but not for Essence since it doesn\u2019t look like something that can be shaped by itself. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> That sounds fair, wondering if a patterning spell could use essence to fuel and create object into the material world like mana can do with prime tough<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209430#post1209430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that most things in the material could get a reflection into death twilight when it dies and become ghosts but doesn't have the same connection toward the shadow and that's why it's a patterning spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaving a portal to the spirit attuned twilight doesn't really seems hard, nearly all things material have a spirit equivalent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 04-20-2018, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:07:38-07:00","id":1209441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209424#post1209424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does a mage with death only need a practice of weaving to open a portal to twilight and turn to ephemera but spirit mage need at least 4 to be able to enter twilight as per the spells Ghost gate and Twilight body ? Also i assume a mage can shape spirit ephemera or essence into object at the same level death mage can shape ectoplasm and death attuned ephemera ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Imo, you only need Spirit 3 to enter Spirit attuned Twilight via an Iris. The highest possible cost would be a Reach option on Reaching. Twilit Body simply bypasses the need for an Iris to translate you into ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:10:59-07:00","id":1209445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209441#post1209441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imo, you only need Spirit 3 to enter Spirit attuned Twilight via an Iris. The highest possible cost would be a Reach option on Reaching. Twilit Body simply bypasses the need for an Iris to translate you into ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hum that makes sense, they could have included a note at the end of the Death spell indicating that you could do it with spirit, like it does in some spirit spell to summon or command (you know the : use mind or death for goetia and ghost)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:31:41-07:00","id":1209449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209438#post1209438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving a portal to the spirit attuned twilight doesn't really seems hard, nearly all things material have a spirit equivalent</div> </div> </div> </div>And they're living their lives in another dimension, where you can pop open an Iris with Spirit 3 and some Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:57:37-07:00","id":1209456,"title":"","content":"Regarding Twilight... we know that, despite poetic langauge used to describe it, Twilight is a state of being (or more exactly, states of being) in the material/living/waking world and not an otherworld overlaid on top of it.<br /> <br /> However... it could be that ghostly Twilight muddies up the distinctions, from what we\u2019ve seen of how Cenotes in 2E are described and how Neter-Khertet is perceived. Of course, I suspect the relationship between ghostly Twilight and the Underworld is like that between dreams and the Astral (ie. interconnected but separated), but still it gives us something to muse about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Clarity 04-20-2018, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T23:57:58-07:00","id":1209533,"title":"","content":"Are there any magic eaters in the books? Things that devour or destroy Mana in an area, beyond mages taking it out of a hallow or eating it in tass form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T00:46:13-07:00","id":1209542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209533#post1209533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any magic eaters in the books? Things that devour or destroy Mana in an area, beyond mages taking it out of a hallow or eating it in tass form?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one character in Night Horrors: the Unbidden. Madame T-something (forgot the name).<br /> <br /> Also question: any one got a 2nd ed write up for the Dreamspeakers? I need one for my current chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 04-21-2018, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T01:22:18-07:00","id":1209550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1209533#post1209533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any magic eaters in the books? Things that devour or destroy Mana in an area, beyond mages taking it out of a hallow or eating it in tass form?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bound devour Mana, and Mana-sources. Including Mages.<br /> Some can even eat Sleepwalkers and Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T04:31:30-07:00","id":1209574,"title":"","content":"Anything from the Abyss is also a potential manavore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:08:26-07:00","id":1210266,"title":"","content":"Not a simple question but. What would happen if a Mage tries to replicate a lair? Or claim chambers in the primordial dream with Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:41:52-07:00","id":1210278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1210266#post1210266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a simple question but. What would happen if a Mage tries to replicate a lair? Or claim chambers in the primordial dream with Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anywhere from new Attainments to a new Legacy to a new template (Tremere, anyone?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:37:44-07:00","id":1210810,"title":"","content":"Not nearly a simple question, but why is it that the Orders all have a section in the 2E book labeled Hubris, but the actions described don't count as Acts of Hubris for members of said orders? Wouldn't it be more interesting to say that acting in your Order's Hubris has real, significant weight to it, besides just the social aspect? Like if such actions were considered Hubris against Falling Wisdom, it would really bring up a lot more thought into going Nameless, instead of just going with the free rote skills, High Speech, Occult dot, and possible proprietary Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T23:17:21-07:00","id":1210834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1210810#post1210810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not nearly a simple question, but why is it that the Orders all have a section in the 2E book labeled Hubris, but the actions described don't count as Acts of Hubris for members of said orders? Wouldn't it be more interesting to say that acting in your Order's Hubris has real, significant weight to it, besides just the social aspect? Like if such actions were considered Hubris against Falling Wisdom, it would really bring up a lot more thought into going Nameless, instead of just going with the free rote skills, High Speech, Occult dot, and possible proprietary Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intention seems to be that things like this are where Wisdom is personalized, becoming expanded beyond the base Acts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:23:42-07:00","id":1210924,"title":"","content":"Fair, but it would be slightly easier to codify if &quot;engage in your Order's hubris&quot; was stuck somewhere into the Acts of Hubris section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:12:10-07:00","id":1211247,"title":"","content":"Would it be feasible to produce a heatless light using solely Prime magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:59:40-07:00","id":1211259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1211247#post1211247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be feasible to produce a heatless light using solely Prime magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with Prime 3 Platonic Form or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:01:51-07:00","id":1211261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1211259#post1211259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, with Prime 3 Platonic Form or similar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my first thought. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T04:39:41-07:00","id":1211358,"title":"","content":"Forces could do it too, just take any ol' existing light (or any object, that provides <i>any</i> sort of force even gravity since it has <i>mass</i> presumably) and just transform and amplify whatever into light (heatless by the very nature of the magic) Not sure why the focus on Prime but Platonic Form definitely comes to mind as pretty much the only spell to do it with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T08:39:50-07:00","id":1211434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1211247#post1211247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be feasible to produce a heatless light using solely Prime magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of depends on what you understand under heatless. The heat of a lot of light sources is just a byproduct, the visible light is usually not felt as warm. White light in reasonable intensities is not felt, because you don't absorb much of the radiation. So an LED flashlight is already pretty close to what you want and you could mimic the effect with either Forces or Platonic Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:27:30-07:00","id":1212020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1207240#post1207240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this Parametric Language the Secret Order of the Gate is said to use? The word &quot;parametric,&quot; at a glance, seems to have many different meanings, and I can't figure out which one the Order is supposed to be referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie's answer was what I remember from that section as well, in case you haven't had a chance to look into the matter more. Basic premise is that the language will say what something is not, instead of what it is. It doesn't sound like a very easy langauge to work with, so I imagine it has some sort of inconceivable trick that allows it to actually function, something a human mind could not cook up, but something a superintelligence like the lonely exarch could.<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with the greek philosopher Parmenides, think of the parametic language as Parmenides' worst nightmare. Parmenides said something to the effect of &quot;you can't describe something by what it is not&quot; and the Lonely Exarch is all &quot;hold my beer&quot; and made a language that is purely that.<br /> <br /> I guess a working example, if I'm not mistaken, would be like... somewhere on the forum someone said something like a &quot;bird that isn't a bird knocking on your door&quot;, so the parametic language might work by defining the bird-not-bird by saying, well, you're not a bird, you're not a raptor, you're not a mammal, and you're not a spirit, and entrapping and commanding the abyssal by using the definitions of what it isn't as a sort of lattice to trap or compel it? Especially if used as a yantra?<br /> <br /> Not a whole lot to go off of as the parametic language was literally only described in a paragraph, but, its a fun thought experiment irregardless to have a language that works in the complete opposite fashion of all other languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:36:16-07:00","id":1212022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1210924#post1210924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, but it would be slightly easier to codify if &quot;engage in your Order's hubris&quot; was stuck somewhere into the Acts of Hubris section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it would also make character creation harder and complicate the metaphysics of using the Inuring mechanic. Hubris is about downfalls though, so the Acts of Hubris are so significant that they limit the net-capacity of a Mage to be wise with their magic, and the Order's hubris is lesser, more sociological down-falls instead of existential. However, another way to look at it is that the hubris of an Order is a clear path to Acts of Hubris, so perhaps its actually redundant to classify them mechanically when the Order's hubris is an in-story way for you to reach an act of hubris that follows from the faults of the Order you've joined.<br /> <br /> I think it is important to separate the two because the Order's varying perspectives allow them to cloud Acts of Hubris. A Silver Ladder mage does not consider mind-controlling or commanding spirits to be an Act of Hubris--the power to do this is humanity's birthright, in their view. Never the less, it is an Act of Hubris to do this.<br /> <br /> If the Acts of Hubris are what will mechanically cause Wisdom to lower? Then the Hubris section in the Orders write-ups are the road-maps the players and ST can follow to get to those Acts of Hubris. Which is handy! It helps the ST make the npc's interesting, and it helps players have excellent and believable ways to cause logical but compelling drama, and get that sweet sweet arcane xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:12:18-07:00","id":1212030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212020#post1212020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tessie's answer was what I remember from that section as well, in case you haven't had a chance to look into the matter more. Basic premise is that the language will say what something is not, instead of what it is. It doesn't sound like a very easy langauge to work with, so I imagine it has some sort of inconceivable trick that allows it to actually function, something a human mind could not cook up, but something a superintelligence like the lonely exarch could.<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with the greek philosopher Parmenides, think of the parametic language as Parmenides' worst nightmare. Parmenides said something to the effect of &amp;quot;you can't describe something by what it is not&amp;quot; and the Lonely Exarch is all &amp;quot;hold my beer&amp;quot; and made a language that is purely that.<br /> <br /> I guess a working example, if I'm not mistaken, would be like... somewhere on the forum someone said something like a &amp;quot;bird that isn't a bird knocking on your door&amp;quot;, so the parametic language might work by defining the bird-not-bird by saying, well, you're not a bird, you're not a raptor, you're not a mammal, and you're not a spirit, and entrapping and commanding the abyssal by using the definitions of what it isn't as a sort of lattice to trap or compel it? Especially if used as a yantra?<br /> <br /> Not a whole lot to go off of as the parametic language was literally only described in a paragraph, but, its a fun thought experiment irregardless to have a language that works in the complete opposite fashion of all other languages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thought so. So maybe making my homebrew Merit (in the respective thread) for it require High Speech isn\u2019t a good idea afterall, hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:33:05-07:00","id":1212607,"title":"","content":"Dispel Magic (Prime \u2022)<br /> Practice: Compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Arcanum rating of the subject spell\u2019s caster<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athletics, Intimidation, Occult<br /> All Awakened magic contains the capacity to end, to allow<br /> the Fallen World\u2019s laws to reassert themselves. By Compelling<br /> these flaws in an extant spell, the mage may temporarily suppress<br /> it \u2014 or even destroy it entirely. This spell is not potent enough<br /> to dispel an archmage\u2019s spells, and only works against Awakened<br /> magic. In addition, the mage must include all Arcana involved<br /> in the casting of the subject spell at one dot.<br /> A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of<br /> Dispel Magic.<br /> Add Fate \u2022: The mage may suppress the subject spell selective-<br /> ly, for a number of subjects equal to Dispel Magic\u2019s Scale factor.<br /> +2 Reach: For one point of Mana, the effect is Lasting. If the<br /> spell\u2019s original caster is still alive and has not relinquished the<br /> spell, she knows one of her spells was destroyed.<br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Unraveling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Arcanum rating of the subject spell\u2019s caster<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athletics, Intimidation, Occult<br /> Supernal truths can never truly be unmade, but with this spell<br /> the mage may cast them back across the Abyss, effectively erasing<br /> any spell she comes across. This spell is not potent enough to<br /> dispel archmages\u2019 spells.<br /> A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of<br /> Supernal Dispellation.<br /> Add Fate \u2022: The mage may suppress the subject spell selec-<br /> tively, for a number of subjects equal to the Dispel\u2019s Scale factor.<br /> +2 Reach: For one point of Mana, the effect is Lasting. If the<br /> spell\u2019s original caster is still alive and has not relinquished the<br /> spell, she knows one of her spells was destroyed.<br /> <br /> Would anyone mind telling me what the difference is here, mechanically? These spells mechanically look identical but one is 1 dot the other 4. Are their any real reasons to use one practice over the other (aside from limitations of your progress in the arcanum)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:43:05-07:00","id":1212610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212607#post1212607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dispel Magic (Prime \u2022)<br /> [..]<br /> In addition, the mage must include all Arcana involved<br /> in the casting of the subject spell at one dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the difference.<br /> <br /> Edit: Both spells also talk about dispelling Supernal magic, but only Dispel Magic mentions that it only works on Awakened magic. I'm pretty sure Supernal Dispellation isn't supposed to be able to dispell a vampire's Disciplines or werewolf's Gifts, but I think it's weird that both doesn't reiterate the same limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-28-2018, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:28:39-07:00","id":1212627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212610#post1212610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the difference.<br /> <br /> Edit: Both spells also talk about dispelling Supernal magic, but only Dispel Magic mentions that it only works on Awakened magic. I'm pretty sure Supernal Dispellation isn't supposed to be able to dispell a vampire's Disciplines or werewolf's Gifts, but I think it's weird that both doesn't reiterate the same limits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Supernal Dispellation probably isn't meant to dispel other supernaturals' powers.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Word of Command has an &quot;Add Any Other Arcanum&quot; add-on that lets it affect non-Supernal magical items, so it wouldn't be too out of place for Supernal Dispellation to have similar a similar add-on. 4 dots seem nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T09:03:57-07:00","id":1212688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212627#post1212627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, Supernal Dispellation probably isn't meant to dispel other supernaturals' powers.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Word of Command has an &quot;Add Any Other Arcanum&quot; add-on that lets it affect non-Supernal magical items, so it wouldn't be too out of place for Supernal Dispellation to have similar a similar add-on. 4 dots seem nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an appropriate effect for a 4 dot spell, being able to counter disciplines by including a dot of death or contracts with a dot of fate, or whatever. You're 1 dot away from being a master of &quot;truth&quot; among other things and Prime armour protects against wholly supernatural attacks - it's in theme to be able to affect other supernatural effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T09:07:59-07:00","id":1212690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212688#post1212688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like an appropriate effect for a 4 dot spell, being able to counter disciplines by including a dot of death or contracts with a dot of fate, or whatever. You're 1 dot away from being a master of &amp;quot;truth&amp;quot; among other things and Prime armour protects against wholly supernatural attacks - it's in theme to be able to affect other supernatural effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant each Arcana added also being at 4 dots, like Supernal Dispellation + Death or Mind 4 to unravel a Dominate command. But hey, 1 dot could work I guess, depending on how one spins the rationale and whether others at the table are on board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T09:27:07-07:00","id":1212696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212690#post1212690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant each Arcana added also being at 4 dots, like Supernal Dispellation + Death or Mind 4 to unravel a Dominate command. But hey, 1 dot could work I guess, depending on how one spins the rationale and whether others at the table are on board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Few mages are going to have 4 dots in several arcana, at least in your typical campaign. That being said, 2 dots would be more in-line with other &quot;Add dot&quot; effects to affect realms/states of beings represented by other arcana. (ie teleporting from the hedge is 2 fate, teleporting bodily into the shadow or twilight is 2 of death or spirit, or perhaps even the underworld or other strange places.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:35:05-07:00","id":1212876,"title":"","content":"We don't have a thread for a collection of magical items (Imbued Items, Enhanced Items, Artifacts) in Mage, do we? Or did I miss one?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and did we ever get a published example of such magical items under 2E rules? I don\u2019t remember such, but I may have missed one or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-28-2018, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T19:03:56-07:00","id":1212889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212876#post1212876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have a thread for a collection of magical items (Imbued Items, Enhanced Items, Artifacts) in Mage, do we? Or did I miss one?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and did we ever get a published example of such magical items under 2E rules? I don\u2019t remember such, but I may have missed one or two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that im aware off. Would love to see any examples of them that arnt rubbish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T19:08:51-07:00","id":1212890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212889#post1212889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that im aware off. Would love to see any examples of them that arnt rubbish.</div> </div> </div> </div>None official nor homebrewed? Hmm...<br /> <br /> Any qualities you (or anybody else reading this) find important for designing magical items?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T19:26:18-07:00","id":1212894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212890#post1212890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None official nor homebrewed? Hmm...<br /> <br /> Any qualities you (or anybody else reading this) find important for designing magical items?</div> </div> </div> </div>That they work? Without having a chance dice for activation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T19:31:49-07:00","id":1212896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212894#post1212894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That they work? Without having a chance dice for activation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chance die? How so? Imbued Items roll its spell\u2019s Arcanum rating + its user\u2019s Gnosis if any, and Artifacts have their own Gnosis &amp; Arcana ratings that its user can substitute their own for, don\u2019t they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:47:05-07:00","id":1212915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212896#post1212896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chance die? How so? Imbued Items roll its spell\u2019s Arcanum rating + its user\u2019s Gnosis if any, and Artifacts have their own Gnosis &amp; Arcana ratings that its user can substitute their own for, don\u2019t they?</div> </div> </div> </div>They still have to take spell factors into account so for anything not lasting 1 turn, 1 target or potency one each UserGnosis + SpellArcana dicepool is going to take serious penalties that cant be offset by yantra's or extra ritual time. A simple persistent imbued object alone requires -10 for indefinite duration for example. Any amount of withstand that requires overcome will be a huge problem also.<br /> <br /> Its also unclear or doesnt state that imbued items get the free step bonuses that normal casters the Arcana-1 step upgrades to primary spellfactor. Making them subpar to a normal casting.<br /> <br /> There is also the problem about how does reach work? Do you get one free reach for the spells arcana level equalling the spell (so need to pick a higher arcana spell just to give a lower one more free reaches?) In which case if that one reach isnt be put to instant cast all imbued items cast in ritual time? Ritual time of the User? (Whats that for a sleeper?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-29-2018, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:53:01-07:00","id":1212919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212915#post1212915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They still have to take spell factors into account so for anything not lasting 1 turn, 1 target or potency one each UserGnosis + SpellArcana dicepool is going to take serious penalties that cant be offset by yantra's or extra ritual time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reach and Primary factor bonuses are still a thing, whereupon the larger concern for successful spellcasting is inability to contain Paradox \u2014 the system is entirely capable of supporting dicepools in the single digits without this being a failure state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:24:53-07:00","id":1212927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212915#post1212915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They still have to take spell factors into account so for anything not lasting 1 turn, 1 target or potency one each UserGnosis + SpellArcana dicepool is going to take serious penalties that cant be offset by yantra's or extra ritual time. A simple persistent imbued object alone requires -10 for indefinite duration for example. Any amount of withstand that requires overcome will be a huge problem also.<br /> <br /> Its also unclear or doesnt state that imbued items get the free step bonuses that normal casters the Arcana-1 step upgrades to primary spellfactor. Making them subpar to a normal casting.<br /> <br /> There is also the problem about how does reach work? Do you get one free reach for the spells arcana level equalling the spell (so need to pick a higher arcana spell just to give a lower one more free reaches?) In which case if that one reach isnt be put to instant cast all imbued items cast in ritual time? Ritual time of the User? (Whats that for a sleeper?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The imbuement itself is persistent without its imbued spell needing to be Indefinite, so I\u2019d not worry about that. <br /> <br /> On the other points, I see and now agree that Spell Factors leave the dice rather low, but Satchel gives us their reassurance as usual. (In exchange for raising another question about Paradox, though!) <br /> <br /> Ah well, I\u2019ll try to write up a sample Doomsday Clock from the 1E Legacy writeup that has them as its namesake, and see where I can go with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:37:20-07:00","id":1212928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212919#post1212919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reach and Primary factor bonuses are still a thing, whereupon the larger concern for successful spellcasting is inability to contain Paradox \u2014 the system is entirely capable of supporting dicepools in the single digits without this being a failure state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Big assumptions not actually stated in either the attainment or the merit. We can assume that the extra steps are based on the spellArcana level of the spell imbued but that is still an assumption/extrapolation that an imbued items use is basically normal spell casting just without the user having access to the arcana/spell imbued or gnosis. Noticing that imbued items can only contain one triggered spell means i was confusing them with Artifacts and that we can again only assume (its not mentioned unlike in the artifact merit) they get only one free reach.<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that single digit dicepools are failure states, in fact i imagine most spells end up around that number but have considerably higher potency, duration, scale than anything put out by a imbued item. I have tried converting many of the cool 1e imbued items to 2e and its just a effort in futility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:44:00-07:00","id":1212932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212927#post1212927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The imbuement itself is persistent without its imbued spell needing to be Indefinite, so I\u2019d not worry about that.<br /> <br /> On the other points, I see and now agree that Spell Factors leave the dice rather low, but Satchel gives us their reassurance as usual. (In exchange for raising another question about Paradox, though!)<br /> <br /> Ah well, I\u2019ll try to write up a sample Doomsday Clock from the 1E Legacy writeup that has them as its namesake, and see where I can go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The attainment imprints the item with a spell, which can then go on to cast it multiple times. Each time its triggered it casts another copy of that imprinted spell which can have different spell factors. You could make two rings of strength via the attainment: One that is triggered upon being worn that casts the honing the form spell each time its worn for X duration. Meaning that you'd need to rewear it once the duration expired, or you can make it a persistant effect (ie always active) that always gives you the strength while worn. This is the different from a persistent or contingent effect mentioned in the creation attainment.<br /> <br /> The fact the imprinting of the spell on the item is also persistent is not the same as a persistent spell effect provided by the spell that was imprinted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:58:41-07:00","id":1212936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212932#post1212932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The attainment imprints the item with a spell, which can then go on to cast it multiple times. Each time its triggered it casts another copy of that imprinted spell which can have different spell factors. You could make two rings of strength via the attainment: One that is triggered upon being worn that casts the honing the form spell each time its worn for X duration. Meaning that you'd need to rewear it once the duration expired, or you can make it a persistant effect (ie always active) that always gives you the strength while worn. This is the different from a persistent or contingent effect mentioned in the creation attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may sound like exploiting loopholes, but couldn\u2019t the contingent trigger for that Ring of Strength could be \u201cbeing worn right now\u201d rather than \u201cwearing\u201d? This would mean that the ring spams Honing the Form every time the Duration runs out, as long as it\u2019s kept worn. Instead of having a ring that casts long-Duration spells every time it\u2019s worn, or a ring that has to be constantly taken off and re-worn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T00:17:59-07:00","id":1212970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212936#post1212936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may sound like exploiting loopholes, but couldn\u2019t the contingent trigger for that Ring of Strength could be \u201cbeing worn right now\u201d rather than \u201cwearing\u201d? This would mean that the ring spams Honing the Form every time the Duration runs out, as long as it\u2019s kept worn. Instead of having a ring that casts long-Duration spells every time it\u2019s worn, or a ring that has to be constantly taken off and re-worn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could as it says you can have conditions as triggers and one condition can be &quot;being worn&quot;. You'd still just need to roll the activation and spend the mana each time though. So it might get expensive mana wise over a persistent effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T00:26:06-07:00","id":1212973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1212970#post1212970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose you could as it says you can have conditions as triggers and one condition can be &amp;quot;being worn&amp;quot;. You'd still just need to roll the activation and spend the mana each time though. So it might get expensive mana wise over a persistent effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, forgot the Mana cost for a moment. Man, the magical items rules are confusing in Mage 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:13:28-07:00","id":1213029,"title":"","content":"Say, wasn't there a Death 1 + Time 1 spell that Dave posted sometime, one people wondered why it was a Time + Death spell because it sounded like just a Death spell? (Or was it Time?) Anybody remember what was its name, or where it was posted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:28:37-07:00","id":1213035,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/txfNtja.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1213029#post1213029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, wasn't there a Death 1 + Time 1 spell that Dave posted sometime, one people wondered why it was a Time + Death spell because it sounded like just a Death spell? (Or was it Time?) Anybody remember what was its name, or where it was posted?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:32:26-07:00","id":1213036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1213035#post1213035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. Thanks!<br /> <br /> So it was an alternate Forensic Gaze. Ah well. Back to the drawing board for the Cult of the Doomsday Clock's 1st Attainment...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T12:53:17-07:00","id":1213508,"title":"","content":"Isn't the real issue with imbued items the problem that lower dot spells are always weaker as imbued items? It isn't written, but, like, if you want a tarot deck that really does predict the future as an imbued item, it will be limited to 1 dot and 1 reach. It isn't really stated that you can take a 1 dot spell as a higher dot imbued item so that you can get the dice and reach you need to use the tarot deck easier.<br /> <br /> That was always my issue. If I were to ST for something, I'd allow imbued items with weaker spells to be taken at higher merit costs to make the spell more versatile, but I don't see anything in the rules that guarantees this is valid?<br /> <br /> In-game, however, I always viewed imbued items most important value being pseudo-grimoires that help train a magic user unskilled in a certain arcanum, by practicing and studying a particular spell they care about, but that's sort of a soft advantage if anything compared to griomoires (unless the setting assumes Grimoires are more valuable and in need of guarding, but the books always make magical items seem more valuable than grimoires so I dunno?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:30:21-07:00","id":1213573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1213508#post1213508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the real issue with imbued items the problem that lower dot spells are always weaker as imbued items? It isn't written, but, like, if you want a tarot deck that really does predict the future as an imbued item, it will be limited to 1 dot and 1 reach. It isn't really stated that you can take a 1 dot spell as a higher dot imbued item so that you can get the dice and reach you need to use the tarot deck easier.<br /> <br /> That was always my issue. If I were to ST for something, I'd allow imbued items with weaker spells to be taken at higher merit costs to make the spell more versatile, but I don't see anything in the rules that guarantees this is valid?<br /> <br /> In-game, however, I always viewed imbued items most important value being pseudo-grimoires that help train a magic user unskilled in a certain arcanum, by practicing and studying a particular spell they care about, but that's sort of a soft advantage if anything compared to griomoires (unless the setting assumes Grimoires are more valuable and in need of guarding, but the books always make magical items seem more valuable than grimoires so I dunno?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If we take the lenient approach of \u201cfollow the normal rules for spellcasting unless explicitly mentioned otherwise,\u201d we still get Primary factor bonuses and extra Reach. But because this is of course not actually written in the rules, I can\u2019t decide if that would mean the user\u2019s abilities or the imbuer\u2019s. I\u2019d go with the latter, making a 1-dot spell Imbued by a Master have higher spell factors and Reach than one imbued by an Apprentice or something. But this is houserule territory. <br /> <br /> Valuable magical items seem more focused on Grimoires and Artifacts, which I believe also have more immediate mechanical benefits than Imbued Items. <br /> <br /> I do hope Signs And Sorcery (or any other future Mage supplements) expands upon magical items in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T21:32:17-07:00","id":1213670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1213573#post1213573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we take the lenient approach of \u201cfollow the normal rules for spellcasting unless explicitly mentioned otherwise,\u201d we still get Primary factor bonuses and extra Reach. But because this is of course not actually written in the rules, I can\u2019t decide if that would mean the user\u2019s abilities or the imbuer\u2019s. I\u2019d go with the latter, making a 1-dot spell Imbued by a Master have higher spell factors and Reach than one imbued by an Apprentice or something. But this is houserule territory.<br /> <br /> Valuable magical items seem more focused on Grimoires and Artifacts, which I believe also have more immediate mechanical benefits than Imbued Items.<br /> <br /> I do hope Signs And Sorcery (or any other future Mage supplements) expands upon magical items in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered that as well! But then I ran into a problem in which there was no easy way to determine the attributes of the mage who created the Imbued Item, assuming you bought it instead of made it yourself. All of this is stuff I like to think a lot about anyway cuz I kind of like crafting in games, even here in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T01:52:36-07:00","id":1213703,"title":"","content":"Ok everyone I would like a little help understanding the Nimbus Tilt. I have a good understanding of it with the exception of how long it lasts. It lasts &quot;Reach in Turns&quot; does that mean that it lasts for a number of turns equal to the Free Reaches you have? Does it last for a number of reaches you used? Or does it mean something else.<br /> <br /> This seems to work backwards to how I would think it would work. The higher the spell the less time it will stick around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:59:09-07:00","id":1213728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1213703#post1213703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok everyone I would like a little help understanding the Nimbus Tilt. I have a good understanding of it with the exception of how long it lasts. It lasts &quot;Reach in Turns&quot; does that mean that it lasts for a number of turns equal to the Free Reaches you have? Does it last for a number of reaches you used? Or does it mean something else.<br /> <br /> This seems to work backwards to how I would think it would work. The higher the spell the less time it will stick around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lasts for as many turns as there were reach in the spell, doesn't matter if they're free or invoked paradox. It had a strength equal to potency so the higher the spell odds are your potency is higher too.<br /> Pretty sure it always lasts at least one turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:38:54-07:00","id":1213927,"title":"","content":"What are the benefits of the nimbus tilt? I think I understand the mechanic but its usefulness is kind of questionable. I know that has been talked a bit but maybe someone can help me figure out its uses. This is not a criticism against the developers either, cuz I'm sure its usefulness is simply not apparent, niche.<br /> <br /> Here are the ones I can think of, did I miss any?<br /> The nimbus has weak effects that don't last long. The big problem with it is that it adds extra math that bogs down the flow of combat, which is already very slow for how fast combat goes in narrative. IF this hinderance is not a problem for a table, then we have these uses?<br /> <br /> Possibility to min-max allies you want to affect, but, not great. I don't think you can use the tilt to buff yourself either, but not positive.<br /> <br /> Briefly compound effects on victims of spells. Not sure how useful this is. If a tilt lowers a victim's Withstand long enough for you to hit them with a powerful spell, it could change the flow of combat? I don't have experience with how useful that is though. An example is hitting someone with a fraying spell, and if your tilt lowers resolve, then once tilted, you can transition into mind control magic? Just as an example, but, I am not sure if the Withstand returns to normal after the tilt ends will affect the mind control spell, and if it does, the few turns the mind control does work for might be <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> The last thing I thought of is that, <i>I think</i>, the nimbus is not subject to paradox? It would be to quiescence I'm sure, but I think you could use it on sleepers without risk of abyssal intrusion? I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:01:31-07:00","id":1213938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1213927#post1213927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What are the benefits of the nimbus tilt? I think I understand the mechanic but its usefulness is kind of questionable. I know that has been talked a bit but maybe someone can help me figure out its uses. This is not a criticism against the developers either, cuz I'm sure its usefulness is simply not apparent, niche.<br /> <br /> Here are the ones I can think of, did I miss any?<br /> The nimbus has weak effects that don't last long. The big problem with it is that it adds extra math that bogs down the flow of combat, which is already very slow for how fast combat goes in narrative. IF this hinderance is not a problem for a table, then we have these uses?<br /> <br /> Possibility to min-max allies you want to affect, but, not great. I don't think you can use the tilt to buff yourself either, but not positive.<br /> <br /> Briefly compound effects on victims of spells. Not sure how useful this is. If a tilt lowers a victim's Withstand long enough for you to hit them with a powerful spell, it could change the flow of combat? I don't have experience with how useful that is though. An example is hitting someone with a fraying spell, and if your tilt lowers resolve, then once tilted, you can transition into mind control magic? Just as an example, but, I am not sure if the Withstand returns to normal after the tilt ends will affect the mind control spell, and if it does, the few turns the mind control does work for might be <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> The last thing I thought of is that, <i>I think</i>, the nimbus is not subject to paradox? It would be to quiescence I'm sure, but I think you could use it on sleepers without risk of abyssal intrusion? I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, using Nimbus always felt like making lemonades out of lemons. It\u2019s magic leaking into reality using the mage as a conduit, sorta like supernatural radiation. <br /> <br /> That said, your last and second-to-last points are ones I\u2019d go with. A quick and relatively safe display of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:04:21-07:00","id":1214248,"title":"","content":"The Nimbus is not recommended for newbs. It's cool unnecessary fluff that slows combat down. That being said I usually start asking players about their signature nimbus after a few sessions, their long term after a few more and then their immediate and tilt in Session 7 or so. The tilt isn't going to come up much at low Gnosis anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T18:50:58-07:00","id":1214869,"title":"","content":"Reading the spell casting section, p 122 in second edition, I can see no reason why anyone casting a spell on someone or something immediately present would ever not use the material sympathy Tool Yantra. Am I missing something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T18:56:48-07:00","id":1214872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1214869#post1214869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the spell casting section, p 122 in second edition, I can see no reason why anyone casting a spell on someone or something immediately present would ever not use the material sympathy Tool Yantra. Am I missing something here?</div> </div> </div> </div>A subject does not count as its own material sympathy Yantra, IIRC. Away from my pdf now, so can\u2019t confirm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T19:24:52-07:00","id":1214878,"title":"","content":"Nope, cut off a piece of hair and get yourself a material sympathy yantra.<br /> <br /> Some might forget, or not trust the other to not secretly hide a bit to use against you later, but by and large a material sympathy yantra from a willing subject is an excellent and easy to acquire yantra if you have the time. Even that can be simple though.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of interpretation, but I think you still need to &quot;separate&quot; something from them though. You can't just touch them and use them themselves, you need a piece of hair, a drop of blood, a strip of skin or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:13:44-07:00","id":1214890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1214869#post1214869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the spell casting section, p 122 in second edition, I can see no reason why anyone casting a spell on someone or something immediately present would ever not use the material sympathy Tool Yantra. Am I missing something here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The semiotics of the spell or not wanting to damage the subject to get an appropriate piece of it \u2014 remember that spellcasting is not an abstract exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:05:36-07:00","id":1216188,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to gain Reach other than Arcana mastery and (effectively) the use of a dedicated tool? Technically, the tool only reduces Paradox pools, but in effective terms, this is equivalent to two extra Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:19:25-07:00","id":1216191,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to gain Reach other than Arcana mastery and (effectively) the use of a dedicated tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:27:52-07:00","id":1216196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216188#post1216188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to gain Reach other than Arcana mastery and (effectively) the use of a dedicated tool? Technically, the tool only reduces Paradox pools, but in effective terms, this is equivalent to two extra Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting in a Demesne (or naturally occurring Verge) does not risk Paradox, and thus effectively affords you infinite Reach.<br /> <br /> With dedicated tools it's worth noting that reducing a two-dice Paradox pool to zero is not the same thing as not risking Paradox - there's still a chance die to roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:36:40-07:00","id":1216203,"title":"","content":"You can also spend Mana to decrease Paradox pools (to a minimum of Chance Die, as noted). Just remember that increasing your Gnosis also increases how many Paradox Dice you get per Reach above maximum.<br /> <br /> As for actually gaining extra Reaches, no, I don't think so. Overreaching is how a mage digs their own grave, and in my experience the most important limit on spellcasting in stressed situations. Any way of gaining additional free Reaches would be extremely powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:52:26-07:00","id":1216214,"title":"","content":"On that note, probably the most important tool you have for gaining &quot;extra&quot; Reach is planning and preparation. Creating or borrowing a Demesne is the most extreme example, but even if you don't have that option most of your free Reach usually goes to the &quot;tax&quot; of casting the spell instantly and/or at range. So arrange a situation where you can spend three hours (or less, depending on Gnosis) within touching distance of your target, and you've gotten yourself two free Reach, my friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:49:41-07:00","id":1216350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216191#post1216191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to gain Reach other than Arcana mastery and (effectively) the use of a dedicated tool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotes give you extra reach as if you were a master which is technically other than Arcana mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T18:19:40-07:00","id":1216405,"title":"","content":"Being a Scelestus with high Gnosis. It requires good luck, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2018, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T19:32:20-07:00","id":1216437,"title":"","content":"How exactly does imbuing items work? Seems a bit silly to have my bow only cast honing the form at its most basic level, for a single turn, for a point of mana after being instant cast. They say any spell you could cast, so shouldn't that include whatever reach you could apply and so on. Similar to crafting a legacy attainment, imo. I'm looking at things like a contingency ring that heals the wearer for 8L once the user suffers wound penalties from lethal or a bracer that grants a boon to dex after a certain gesture along a bow string. Things that should be noticeable and have some duration would be nice.<br /> <br /> If that isn't the case I'll stick to straight forward simple things like rote on a few rolls at a time or stuff that isn't really reliant on primary factors when cast at yourself like momentary flux or shifting sands.<br /> <br /> The imbued rules aren't particularly clear, but if any spell I could cast is used I could cast a ritual heal with yantras and stuff, copying the effect on the item and having it just &quot;copy&quot; that spell when it's spending mana and rolling the trigger. That'd obviously be ideal compared to casting without any benefits at all just be factor spells<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-07-2018, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T20:42:55-07:00","id":1216463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216437#post1216437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does imbuing items work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do it this way: once an item is relinquished any spell factors (and thus dice pools) and reach (and thus non-witness based paradox) are locked in and can't be changed; otherwise the ability to change spell factors if you retain control of the item is pointless.<br /> <br /> Items with a persistent effect either have to target the item itself or the bearer, these function as passive buffs and effectively have an indefinite duration (this makes Imbuing useful as you can bypass the large dice penalty). E.g. a <i>Ring of Mind Shielding </i>would be the <i>Mental Shield</i> spell with a persistent effect tied to the ring, with maybe a reach spent to give it Advanced Potency (+2 to the Clash of Wills roll).<br /> <br /> Items that cast the spell would function more like D&amp;D style wands, a ring with <i>Mental Shield</i> of this type would not take effect merely by being worn, but <i>could</i> cast copies of the <i>Mental Shield</i> spell on multiple targets for a mana each. Reach and spellfactors would have been pre-determined by the person creating it and couldn't be changed, but would be useful for a group of Mages where no one had any dots in Mind.<br /> <br /> When buying the Imbued item merit you can pay more for a higher effective rating, giving you extra free reach for the imbued spell, better default spell factors, and a larger activation dicepool. It also would increase the dicepool used on Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-08-2018, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T20:54:13-07:00","id":1216471,"title":"","content":"[oops, double post]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-08-2018, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T21:59:35-07:00","id":1216491,"title":"","content":"You folks think introducing Spirits of Mana &amp; Magic would be a bad idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:18:36-07:00","id":1216496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216491#post1216491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You folks think introducing Spirits of Mana &amp; Magic would be a bad idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Less \u201cbad\u201d and more \u201chow the heck do I justify this?!\u201d for me.<br /> <br /> Having a spirit of Mana would be like having a spirit of Essence, and not just because they\u2019re both \u201cfuel\u201d stuff. Essence/Mana is the medium and/or byproduct of Resonance, rather than something that Resonates. If a spirit of Mana exists, it\u2019ll probably look like an idigam. <br /> <br /> Magic looks like too broad of a concept. It\u2019ll be like having a spirit of (all) Emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:35:46-07:00","id":1216498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216496#post1216496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019ll be like having a spirit of (all) Emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair that's how spirit hierarchy works. While spirits of anger and sadness and happiness may battle it out in the streets, above them there's higher ranked conceptuals that feed from all of them, then above them, however many rungs, you get a grand conceptual god of emotions. But that's getting way high up.<br /> <br /> So smaller and more focused spirits of magic (curses, protection, destruction, divination) probably make sense at a lower-tier game, then broader ones at the higher tiers. I'd probably avoid Mana spirits, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-08-2018, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:52:34-07:00","id":1216505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216498#post1216498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair that's how spirit hierarchy works. While spirits of anger and sadness and happiness may battle it out in the streets, above them there's higher ranked conceptuals that feed from all of them, then above them, however many rungs, you get a grand conceptual god of emotions. But that's getting way high up.<br /> <br /> So smaller and more focused spirits of magic (curses, protection, destruction, divination) probably make sense at a lower-tier game, then broader ones at the higher tiers. I'd probably avoid Mana spirits, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I was using the wrong example - I imagined a spirit of \u201cMagic\u201d would be more like a spirit of all Conceptuals, Elementals, etc. Very broad in scope<br /> <br /> However, the possibilities of a magic spirit are too fun to just dismiss. Hmm... well I suppose a spirit-Lich can be said to be a spirit of magic from a certain perspective...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:46:39-07:00","id":1216753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216496#post1216496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less \u201cbad\u201d and more \u201chow the heck do I justify this?!\u201d for me.<br /> <br /> Having a spirit of Mana would be like having a spirit of Essence, and not just because they\u2019re both \u201cfuel\u201d stuff. Essence/Mana is the medium and/or byproduct of Resonance, rather than something that Resonates. If a spirit of Mana exists, it\u2019ll probably look like an idigam.<br /> <br /> Magic looks like too broad of a concept. It\u2019ll be like having a spirit of (all) Emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH, I think of Supernal entities as &quot;spirits&quot; of Mana. The Platonic Ideal of Essence as Mana, and thus the platonic ideal of Essence-based beings (Ghosts, Goeta, Spirits, etc.) as Supernal beings.<br /> <br /> As to the original question, though, I could easily see spirits of non-supernal magic existing as well if the proper resonance gathers enough. A long-lived mystery cult or similar, doing rituals in a place for decades or centuries seems very likely to create a properly magic-themed resonance in that area, and thus possibly spawn spirits based on that resonance, which then in turn act to strengthen that resonant condition to keep the meal ticket churning out delicious essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24114-hyperluminary","name":"Hyperluminary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24114_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:30:27-07:00","id":1216849,"title":"","content":"Acnthus wagons are listed as rapier, bow, precision weapons. So what constitutes a precision weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:58:35-07:00","id":1216856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216849#post1216849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acnthus wagons are listed as rapier, bow, precision weapons. So what constitutes a precision weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably weapons that deal pinpoint damage or require a particular level of finesse to be most effective. A sniper rifle is probably a precision weapon, a grenade isn't. Weapons that pierce or elude defenses are probably what we're looking at rather than those that can (With skill) simply brute force defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T18:29:08-07:00","id":1216875,"title":"","content":"Starting a fire is clearly an application of Forces. To simplify very slightly, a fire is the transformation of chemical potential energy into thermal energy in the presence an oxidizing agent. So starting a fire seems to fit nicely under Forces 1 or Forces 2. A fire-starting spell is inherently transitory, and the fire is Lasting (you start a fire, it keeps burning, no more magic needed). But would thin be a Compelling (Forces 1) or a Ruling (Forces 2) spell? I can easily see either being a Praxis of Rote in a low-tech era because it's so incredibly useful not having to mess around with flint and steel and tinder, or worse, a firedrill or firebow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T19:45:02-07:00","id":1216882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216875#post1216875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting a fire is clearly an application of Forces. To simplify very slightly, a fire is the transformation of chemical potential energy into thermal energy in the presence an oxidizing agent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Ruling to me. Forcing a chemical reaction which while possible, isn't likely at all to happen on its own.<br /> If you get it to a point where the reaction is not out of the ordinary of the current situation, such as by using a firebow, then you could probably move it down to Compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T01:03:55-07:00","id":1216927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1216875#post1216875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting a fire is clearly an application of Forces. To simplify very slightly, a fire is the transformation of chemical potential energy into thermal energy in the presence an oxidizing agent. So starting a fire seems to fit nicely under Forces 1 or Forces 2. A fire-starting spell is inherently transitory, and the fire is Lasting (you start a fire, it keeps burning, no more magic needed). But would thin be a Compelling (Forces 1) or a Ruling (Forces 2) spell? I can easily see either being a Praxis of Rote in a low-tech era because it's so incredibly useful not having to mess around with flint and steel and tinder, or worse, a firedrill or firebow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way to make it a Ruling spell that I can think of would be to use a variant of Control Heat in an object in an attempt to make it spontaneously combust.<br /> <br /> Transformation is typically the province of Weaving or Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T02:08:34-07:00","id":1216932,"title":"","content":"A firestarting spell wouldn't by itself transform anything. It would just start the process of a naturally occuring transformation. I think Ruling make sense, with additional Reach required if the fuel is difficult to ignite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:37:17-07:00","id":1216977,"title":"","content":"Or just a higher Potency; Reach isn't always the way to go for greater effectiveness. Potency 1 would be good for tinder, or for a candle's wick or a gas lamp, Potency 2 for most woods or other liquid or solid fuels, Potency 3 for particularly hard-to-light fuels, such as avgas or ash wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-09-2018, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T19:14:56-07:00","id":1217238,"title":"","content":"Ok I\u2019m making a campaign with the main bad guy is like the Joker. Matter/Life/Prime and for henchmen I\u2019m going to use manikins that are being animated using magic. I\u2019m thinking normal thug rules for henchmen. I don\u2019t want them to be alive. More or less mindless manikins. Thoughts? Do I need Life? I\u2019m using Mage: Ascension 2E. What Archtype should I use for him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24169-bac946","name":"bac946","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T22:10:16-07:00","id":1217270,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised you went with Prime instead of Mind.<br /> <br /> But if you look at Matter 4 you have the Golem spell. While the name suggests (to me) a hulking brute they can be smaller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T01:44:51-07:00","id":1217294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bac946</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1217238#post1217238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019m using Mage: Ascension 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a typo? If not then you need to define what you mean by archetype or switch to the Ascension forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:29:24-07:00","id":1217330,"title":"","content":"Founding a Legacy means all attainments all require 1 higher Gnosis because their Novel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:42:00-07:00","id":1217333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1217330#post1217330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Founding a Legacy means all attainments all require 1 higher Gnosis because their Novel?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Attainments require 1 higher Gnosis because there's no tutor. You could consider the Attainments novel if you're the Legacy's founder, but it's the no tutor part that is important.<br /> <br /> Edit: Unless you found a Legacy, induct someone in it, and let them develop the Attainments for you. That person would then be able to tutor you, but you're really not much of a founder if you let someone else lead the development of the Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-10-2018, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:30:25-07:00","id":1217343,"title":"","content":"Thanks, just making sure I had everything done right seeing as I spent the experience. So I have to wait until Gnosis 7 for my next attainment then, and 9 after that. This is surely the work of the highest mages lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T10:41:07-07:00","id":1217442,"title":"","content":"Reading Regeneration, I find it extremely irritating that the regeneration is strictly transitory. Would it cause any significant problems to allow Regeneration to be Lasting for, let's say, +2 Reach, then spend of Mana, or both? I can't see any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-10-2018, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T10:56:45-07:00","id":1217446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1217442#post1217442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading Regeneration, I find it extremely irritating that the regeneration is strictly transitory. Would it cause any significant problems to allow Regeneration to be permanent for, let's say, +2 Reach, then spend of Mana, or both? I can't see any.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's your game, you do whatever you want with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> But i can see this from two perspectives right on hand. The first would be story possibilities, in where you'd actually need to get on an adventure of sorts to heal that brain tumor for good or fix your severed legs. The other one is with dissonence and quiesence from sleepers when it comes to obvious magic. &quot;Hey John, didn't you loose both your hands in that accident last week?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T11:05:01-07:00","id":1217452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1217442#post1217442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading Regeneration, I find it extremely irritating that the regeneration is strictly transitory. Would it cause any significant problems to allow Regeneration to be permanent for, let's say, +2 Reach, then spend of Mana, or both? I can't see any.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you want is magic that leaves Lasting results as a side effect instead of as an intended effect. You could permanently regenerate a hand if you gave a subject the regenerative properties of something else, maybe a starfish, and tweaked it to allow for reproduction of human body parts. The spell isn't intended to regenerate a limb, it's intended to give you the ability to regenerate limbs, any limbs that result are merely Lasting byproducts of the spell, not subject to the existence of the spell itself.<br /> <br /> Another alternative is to harvest some stem cells from the subject and force them to grow into a replacement limb that can then be surgically grafted onto the body. It's not that much different from using Matter to bend steel into a shape that it stays in when you're done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-10-2018, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T12:06:13-07:00","id":1217469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1217294#post1217294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a typo? If not then you need to define what you mean by archetype or switch to the Ascension forum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry your right. I meant Tradition or Technocratic ranks. I\u2019m not real familiar with the Technocratic to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24169-bac946","name":"bac946","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T12:49:55-07:00","id":1217479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bac946</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1217469#post1217469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry your right. I meant Tradition or Technocratic ranks. I\u2019m not real familiar with the Technocratic to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still the wrong forum. This is the mage awakening forum, not the mage ascension forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T13:11:43-07:00","id":1218047,"title":"","content":"If I have Time 4 and an attainment that allows me to use say, Chronos' Curse. The additional factors are at a -2 per? (ie at Time 5, the most potency the attainment will ever each is 7, at -4 of the 5 dots in the arcanum) Meaning many supernaturals will be immune to it either via things like Resilience, Honing the Form, or other means, and it can never exceptionally succeed to bypass withstand like a spell.<br /> <br /> I'd have to use Degrading the Form or similar means of reducing their stamina before using the attainment, but without combining a spell with the attainment. Hm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-12-2018, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T17:10:05-07:00","id":1218101,"title":"","content":"Attainments encounter major issues when brushing up against Withstand. That is intentional. They're supposed to be less flexible, and less powerful than a version of their effect performed through spellcasting with sufficient effort.<br /> <br /> If you want to get past some subject's crazy high Resolve/Stamina/Composure, then gather some Yantras, spend Willpower, and cast a normal spell with enhanced spell factors.<br /> Attainments do their best work when they're self-enhancements, or don't directly affect other people in a way that involves Withstand.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T03:50:29-07:00","id":1218166,"title":"","content":"Edit: Sigh, please ignore this post. I was wrong again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 05-13-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T04:23:26-07:00","id":1218170,"title":"","content":"Can an attribute be lowered below 0? (ie start applying penalties due to extreme frailness, whatever) Things like Befuddle and Degrading the Form do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T05:01:22-07:00","id":1218174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218170#post1218170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an attribute be lowered below 0? (ie start applying penalties due to extreme frailness, whatever) Things like Befuddle and Degrading the Form do this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure you could lower an attribute to 0 in most instances, maybe there is some powers that allows that, but non I can think of. Like it's pretty obvious that with 0 in an attribute, that attribute would be &quot;gone&quot;. In mage terms, i guess you might be able to do that with an Unmaking spell, but degrading the form is limited to a minimum of 1. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T05:24:21-07:00","id":1218176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218166#post1218166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While cumbersome in use, Nimbus Tilts can be used to further reduce Resistance Attributes to let some Spells through. Granted, it works best for Spells without a Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nimbus Tilts penalize rolls, not derived Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T05:47:10-07:00","id":1218182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218170#post1218170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an attribute be lowered below 0? (ie start applying penalties due to extreme frailness, whatever) Things like Befuddle and Degrading the Form do this.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218174#post1218174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you could lower an attribute to 0 in most instances, maybe there is some powers that allows that, but non I can think of. Like it's pretty obvious that with 0 in an attribute, that attribute would be &quot;gone&quot;. In mage terms, i guess you might be able to do that with an Unmaking spell, but degrading the form is limited to a minimum of 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if there's a ruling on this in 2e, but in 1e if an attribute is reduced to 0, you don't get to roll at all. The idea being that e.g. no amount of Firearms skill will make up for the fact that having zero Dexterity means you have completely lost the ability to coordinate your movements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:55:36-07:00","id":1218410,"title":"","content":"If a Lancea et Sanctum Vampire with Sorcerous Eunuch had a spell cast on them by a Mage, would they penalize the casting dice pool by their Resolve, or does a Mage's power not count as 'Magical' ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T23:25:40-07:00","id":1218422,"title":"","content":"So the text says &quot;sorcery&quot; and then later references &quot;theban sorcery, cruac and other blood sorceries&quot;. So one could argue it only applies vs blood magic/sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T23:26:08-07:00","id":1218423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218410#post1218410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Lancea et Sanctum Vampire with Sorcerous Eunuch had a spell cast on them by a Mage, would they penalize the casting dice pool by their Resolve, or does a Mage's power not count as 'Magical' ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a trickier question, and would probably require ST adjudication.<br /> From what I remember of dev commentary for Mage, the system is built on the assumption that nobody else's mystic powers will impose a negative penalty on your spellcasting roll, which is you constructing the Imago in your head, and then attempting to translate that into reality. It's a yes/no determination, which can get another boost if it's well made (Exceptional Success).<br /> <br /> Where resistance does come into play, it takes the form of Withstand, or if there's an opposing and incompatible power, a Clash of Wills. Which is why unlike most other splats, Mage spells don't give a hoot about other character's power stats.<br /> <br /> If I was feeling particuarly generous, I might say that Sorcerous Eunuch is sufficiently anti-Magic to take the role of a power that grants a Clash of Wills, and given it's persistent in effect, granting it the dice pool bonus in that clash for being a persistent power.<br /> <br /> Beyond that though, unless you're playing a Vampire game and want to offer some power to counteract a NPC Mage, I'd say the power likely wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* of course, I haven't read the merit in a while, and it might just work on Vampire Magic, in which case, no dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T01:15:23-07:00","id":1218438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218422#post1218422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the text says &quot;sorcery&quot; and then later references &quot;theban sorcery, cruac and other blood sorceries&quot;. So one could argue it only applies vs blood magic/sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure that's a fair reading of the implications of that reference, which just refers to sorceries the vampire can never learn (meaning, sorceries the vampire could previously learn).<br /> <br /> I'd let it interact in some way with Awakened magic for fun. That would mean probably an increased withstand (either a flat number, or make withstand higher of Resolve/Withstand, or something like that) or Clash of Wills. By my reading, it should work on Awakened magic RAW, though, just from a narrative standpoint, it seems unlikely that the methods described would interact with Awakened magic in any real way. Still, blood magic works in mysterious ways. I think it's a fun tool to add to throw Mages for a loop, so I'd use it, but sparingly for vampire NPCs.<br /> <br /> In a vampire game with a few mage NPCs I also don't think it's really a problem to have it work as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 05-14-2018, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T04:10:09-07:00","id":1218466,"title":"","content":"by RAW it sounds like it wouldn't have an effect, but I'd probably call for a Clash of Wills or something just because i don't like the idea of various splats bypassing each others' powers because there's no explicit attention paid to it in the write-up. For example, it sounds unfair that a demon fresh off the Fall could just roll up to a centuries-old master of Dominate and use The Word on him, and he'd have no more defense against it than a particularly stubborn mall cop would.<br /> <br /> Unless that's the point, of course. I might do that if I wanted to introduce Demons as something so weird and alien to the ordinary night crawlers of the world that their powers don't even work on the same axes and can't be defended against by mere blood magic. Which is something you may want to do with Awakened magic, but it depends on what sort of story you're telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:33:06-07:00","id":1218556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218466#post1218466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by RAW it sounds like it wouldn't have an effect, but I'd probably call for a Clash of Wills or something just because i don't like the idea of various splats bypassing each others' powers because there's no explicit attention paid to it in the write-up. For example, it sounds unfair that a demon fresh off the Fall could just roll up to a centuries-old master of Dominate and use The Word on him, and he'd have no more defense against it than a particularly stubborn mall cop would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would a vampire with Dominate get to Clash against The Word? Dominate doesn't provide any defence against similar effects; vampiric, demonic, or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:54:39-07:00","id":1218571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218556#post1218556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would a vampire with Dominate get to Clash against The Word? Dominate doesn't provide any defence against similar effects; vampiric, demonic, or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because even when we're talking in-splat power measuring contests, it's always struck me as weird that Mindbender the Dominating Methuselah doesn't have any more resistance to Vinny Ventrue's attempts to go digging around in his skull than his rent-a-cop ghoul.<br /> <br /> I've learned this is not so much a thing in 2e Dominate specifically since there's a Blood Potency component to the requisite use of Mesmerize, but e.g. Demon is full of powers (like The Word) that supernaturals (including other demons and many angels, excepting those higher-ranked ones with silly Resistance scores) are effectively defenseless against.<br /> <br /> From a purely mechanical standpoint, you could argue that since if a vampire tried to Dominate a target a demon had used The Word on or vice versa it would reasonably trigger a Clash of Wills, a vampire might be allowed to &quot;Dominate&quot; herself and trigger a Clash. Or at least a demon might be able to use The Word on herself if you want to be stickler about eye contact and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 05-14-2018, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:57:22-07:00","id":1218572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218438#post1218438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's a fair reading of the implications of that reference, which just refers to sorceries the vampire can never learn (meaning, sorceries the vampire could previously learn).<br /> <br /> I think depending on the game, I'd let it interact in some way with Awakened magic for fun. That would mean probably an increased withstand (either a flat number, or make withstand higher of Resolve/Withstand) or Clash of Wills. Truthfully though, just from a narrative standpoint, it seems unlikely that the methods described would interact with Awakened magic in any real way. But then, blood magic works in mysterious ways. I still think it's a fun tool to add to throw Mages for a loop, so I'd use it sparingly.<br /> <br /> In a vampire game with a few mage NPCs I also don't think it's really a problem to have it work as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>So i mainly meant that when it stated Sorcery it later sort of defined what it meant by sorcery (ie not supernal magic). Crossovers are always going to cause some friction as the developers dont always have access to other systems or even consider (they dont need to) other splats. Personally if you are going to rule it works on supernal magic reducing the dicepool is far to good esp since mages have pretty small dicepools already. Instead i would allow it to Clash vs supernal magic and work as written vs blood sorcery. (Tbh it probably should have just been a clash vs blood sorcery too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T09:02:49-07:00","id":1218574,"title":"","content":"Then your problem seems to be with resisted rolls rather than balance between major templates. Vinny the Ventrue is just as susceptible to Noel the Nosferatu's use of Mortal Terror (Nightmare 5).<br /> The reason The Word doesn't use Supernatural Tolerance is because one of the uses counts the number of successes, and the devs have decided that such rolls are resisted rather than contested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T09:17:09-07:00","id":1218584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1218423#post1218423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a trickier question, and would probably require ST adjudication.<br /> From what I remember of dev commentary for Mage, the system is built on the assumption that nobody else's mystic powers will impose a negative penalty on your spellcasting roll, which is you constructing the Imago in your head, and then attempting to translate that into reality. It's a yes/no determination, which can get another boost if it's well made (Exceptional Success).<br /> <br /> Where resistance does come into play, it takes the form of Withstand, or if there's an opposing and incompatible power, a Clash of Wills. Which is why unlike most other splats, Mage spells don't give a hoot about other character's power stats.<br /> <br /> If I was feeling particuarly generous, I might say that Sorcerous Eunuch is sufficiently anti-Magic to take the role of a power that grants a Clash of Wills, and given it's persistent in effect, granting it the dice pool bonus in that clash for being a persistent power.<br /> <br /> Beyond that though, unless you're playing a Vampire game and want to offer some power to counteract a NPC Mage, I'd say the power likely wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* of course, I haven't read the merit in a while, and it might just work on Vampire Magic, in which case, no dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Sorcerous Eunuch applies to Awakened magic (which I personally think it should since the mention of blood sorcery concerns another part of the power) I'd take a page from Dave Brookshaw who posted earlier in this thread about a similar situation concerning werewolves and how they penalise supernatural effects that would mind control them while in Kuruth:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1181083#post1181083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you insist on using a penalty as a Withstand level - and in most cases you shouldn't, so this is a judgement call, halve the dice penalty rounding up. A withstand level effectively eats a raise in a spell's Potency, which is -2 dice.<br /> <br /> *Doubling* a penalty is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either straight up penalise the roll by the vampire's Resolve, or add half of it as a Withstand rating. If spending WP for the second effect, just remove successes from the casting roll. Withstand and resisted rolls are analogous in Mage so you could just choose your preference, but there's nothing similar to removing successes so I'd just keep it exactly that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:41:22-07:00","id":1219392,"title":"","content":"It typically takes more gusto to affect spellcasting rules in general right? Like being drunk might affect it, but for the most part unless something specifically affects spellcasting rolls it doesn't? Or is it arguable that a creature could say, give you -10 to <i>all rolls</i> and that's going to include spellcasting. Likewise with anything that affects any supernatural effects/rolls, which makes a bit more sense. Abjuration (the discipline) for example would remove <i>every</i> spell within a radius, but not attainments, but other sources that simply say penalize all actions by X shouldn't apply to spellcasting imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T18:23:41-07:00","id":1219501,"title":"","content":"I feel like Supernal Magic is rather blatantly meant to be something that Sorcerous Eunuch can affect. There's a lot of 'do not suffer a witch' vibes in some of the Lance stuff. As it is, I'd say that the process they undergo could certainly make it more difficult to form an Imago against them (per the rules for when a spell is resisted/contested), akin to a sort of passive countermagic; the Eunuch just sort of inherently disrupts the formation of it by their existence, or perhaps their antimagical nature is such that the Imago reflecting them becomes more complex or hard to focus on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T10:11:50-07:00","id":1219690,"title":"","content":"Simple enough question: Which Arcana are required for the now-classic &quot;fireball&quot; spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:07:49-07:00","id":1219715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1219690#post1219690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple enough question: Which Arcana are required for the now-classic &amp;quot;fireball&amp;quot; spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you want to do it, but the most straightforward would be Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:14:29-07:00","id":1219718,"title":"","content":"I should have asked &quot;Which Arcana and at what level?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:27:06-07:00","id":1219722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1219718#post1219718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have asked &amp;quot;Which Arcana and at what level?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how you do it, you can control fire right from Forces 1, for instance, so existing fire Influenced into a path that covers a large enough area over one turn is enough like a fireball to make most of the differences between that and flinging fire from your hands neglible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:59:13-07:00","id":1219739,"title":"","content":"Straight up creating a fireball from nothing would be making (5). Using existing fire to create a fireball would propably be rulling (2 dots), You could use Patterning to collect the ambient heat/sound/whatever in a area and tranform it into a fireball (4 dots, maybe with a Reach). In general Forces makes it much easier to work on something existing, sorta like Pyro from the X-men movies, turning a Zippo into a fireball thrower is 3 dots at most.<br /> <br /> Other Arcana that could do something like a fireball could be Prime, Matter and maybe some others but it would be pretty roundabound and might exactly not fit &quot;make a fireball&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 05-17-2018, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T13:28:00-07:00","id":1219769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a> Now that I'm back to my books and computer. The most straightforward way to create a fireball is going to be with Forces, the most obvious example is to take Thunderbolt and simply make it fire instead of lightning. The classic version of Fireball isn't a single target attack so you'd want to spend a Reach on making it Advanced Scale, or take a dice penalty hit big enough to make it the size of a small room.<br /> <br /> There are other ways to create AoE flash fire effects though other arcana, at varying Practice levels though. Fate 5 for instance can cause almost anything to happen, it's just slightly less good than having Wish in DnD.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I was terse earlier, my allergies are kicking my ass today and I didn't have much energy to put into being polite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T14:52:31-07:00","id":1219798,"title":"","content":"Also note if it is the classic fireball spell that starts at you and flies to your target then its also going to be a thrown spell. Non thrown spells originate at the target after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-17-2018, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T16:47:18-07:00","id":1219822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1219718#post1219718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have asked &quot;Which Arcana and at what level?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A fireball out of &quot;thin air&quot; would be Forces 4 (Patterning) to convert ambient energy into an explosion of fire. A truly <i>ex nihilo </i>fireball would be Forces 5 (Making). A fireball from an existing source of fire would be a combined casting of Influence Fire (Forces 1 (Compelling)) and Control Fire (Forces 2 (Ruling)).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:35:54-07:00","id":1220034,"title":"","content":"Can Channel Mana be used to create tass? That is, if a mage has a suitable target (such as water in a sports bottle) could mana be channeled into to create tass? I'm thinking Prime 3 would be right for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:59:25-07:00","id":1220042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220034#post1220034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Channel Mana be used to create tass? That is, if a mage has a suitable target (such as water in a sports bottle) could mana be channeled into to create tass? I'm thinking Prime 3 would be right for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book could be clearer, but I think tass transform into a physical form rather than flowing into a preexisting object so you wouldn't need water in the bottle.<br /> As for creating tass, I think it would require Patterning. Compare the spells Channel Mana and Destroy Tass. The former sucks out the Mana until the tass collapses by itself while the latter directly destroys the physical form of the tass. If tass can contain more than one Mana (something the book never mentions) then you could potentially recharge it with Channel Mana, but to create new tass should require Patterning.<br /> <br /> Edit: You could probably create tass with Channel Mana by pumping Mana into a Hallow until it naturally congeals into tass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-18-2018, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T13:45:54-07:00","id":1220082,"title":"","content":"Tass is just stored mana, Platonic Form as a holder for mana is Tass, mana in a physical object is Tass. I'd argue that a Hallow congealing mana into Tass is actually the cause of an ambient Channel Mana effect that a Hallow simply has a natural consequence of its existence. So I don't see a reason why you couldn't use Channel Mana to pump something full of mana and get Tass as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T14:22:28-07:00","id":1220088,"title":"","content":"Your reasoning is sound. If anything, Platonic Form should be more difficult to create than tass. But it begs the question, why the fuck is Destroy Tass Unraveling instead of Fraying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T14:27:32-07:00","id":1220090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220082#post1220082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass is just stored mana, Platonic Form as a holder for mana is Tass, mana in a physical object is Tass. I'd argue that a Hallow congealing mana into Tass is actually the cause of an ambient Channel Mana effect that a Hallow simply has a natural consequence of its existence. So I don't see a reason why you couldn't use Channel Mana to pump something full of mana and get Tass as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually argue that a hallow is more of an ambient Platonic Form, as Tessie did above. Hallows don't channel mana, they are just where mana leaks into the world. If that mana goes otherwise uncollected, it pools in a form that resonates with the Hallow, thus creating Tass. Mana isn't being pumped into a pre-existing physical object that happens to be there, it is merely taking up a pattern appropriate to the resonance and symbology of the Hallow that it passes through between the Supernal and Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24114-hyperluminary","name":"Hyperluminary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24114_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T15:27:37-07:00","id":1220109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220088#post1220088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your reasoning is sound. If anything, Platonic Form should be more difficult to create than tass. But it begs the question, why the fuck is Destroy Tass Unraveling instead of Fraying?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure, the only thing that I can think of is that it\u2019s like half an Unmaking spell in that the object is destroyed, but the mana isn\u2019t so the creator may have thought that too strong for Fraying, but not strong enough for Unmaking which could destroy the object and mana both in one go.<br /> <br /> It might also have something to do with the fact that mimicking metaphysically \u201cnatural\u201d traits seems to be part of the 3rd dot Practices, but outright supernatural, couldn\u2019t be done without a lower Practice stuff seems to be reserved for dots 4&amp;5. Completely annihilating a vessel for mana seems to fit those parameters. That\u2019s entirely conjecture on my part though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-18-2018, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T15:30:43-07:00","id":1220112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyperluminary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220090#post1220090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would actually argue that a hallow is more of an ambient Platonic Form, as Tessie did above. Hallows don't channel mana, they are just where mana leaks into the world. If that mana goes otherwise uncollected, it pools in a form that resonates with the Hallow, thus creating Tass. Mana isn't being pumped into a pre-existing physical object that happens to be there, it is merely taking up a pattern appropriate to the resonance and symbology of the Hallow that it passes through between the Supernal and Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>While your opinion isn\u2019t wrong in describing how mama leaks into reality, the fact remains that the way in which the mana is channeled from the Hallow to its Tass is irrelevant to the fact that that\u2019s what is happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T00:48:37-07:00","id":1220458,"title":"","content":"Does a prime 2 &quot;Control supernal entity&quot; spell roughly equivalent to the &quot;control spirit/ghost&quot; spells sound reasonable?<br /> <br /> Also has the official mage stand on ghosts changed in 2nd ed? Cause in 1st ed the party line was roughly &quot;ghosts are objects&quot;, while the 2nd ed core book doesn't spend much wordcount on ghosts but it reads:<br /> &quot;Mages know that ghosts aren\u2019t really dead souls, but reflections generated by passions that persist after souls pass to unknown kingdoms. Some believe that a ghost <br /> is part of the original soul, separated by traumatic death, and others hold that it contains the person\u2019s actual personality: everything that can be defined as \u201cthem.\u201d Therefore, ghosts <br /> must be laid to rest. The dead should be honored.&quot;<br /> So it seems that general perspective is somewhat different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T00:56:06-07:00","id":1220459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220458#post1220458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a prime 2 &amp;quot;Control supernal entity&amp;quot; spell roughly equivalent to the &amp;quot;control spirit/ghost&amp;quot; spells sound reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gut reaction was no.<br /> <br /> A more sound response is that Supernal entities are made up of multiple Arcana, and so controlling them would require all of them instead of just Prime alone (unless, of course, the entity is made up of only Prime for some reason)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also has the official mage stand on ghosts changed in 2nd ed? Cause in 1st ed the party line was roughly &amp;quot;ghosts are objects&amp;quot;, while the 2nd ed core book doesn't spend much wordcount on ghosts but it reads:<br /> &amp;quot;Mages know that ghosts aren\u2019t really dead souls, but reflections generated by passions that persist after souls pass to unknown kingdoms. Some believe that a ghost <br /> is part of the original soul, separated by traumatic death, and others hold that it contains the person\u2019s actual personality: everything that can be defined as \u201cthem.\u201d Therefore, ghosts <br /> must be laid to rest. The dead should be honored.&amp;quot;<br /> So it seems that general perspective is somewhat different? </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are not the people they remember themselves as, but they are still people. <br /> <br /> Those who focus on the former part will tend to have an easier time justifying their exploitation. Those who focus on the latter part disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T01:13:21-07:00","id":1220461,"title":"","content":"That's how I treated ghosts even in 1ed. Was recently rereading the book because I might be running a new game and restarting my old one and the ghost thing piqued my interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 05-20-2018, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T01:31:38-07:00","id":1220464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220459#post1220459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts are not the people they remember themselves as, but they are still people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Said the Sin-Eater. But what do <i>they</i> know about ghosts, am I right fellow mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T02:38:27-07:00","id":1220477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220464#post1220464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said the Sin-Eater. But what do <i>they</i> know about ghosts, am I right fellow mages?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Bokor over there disagrees. And in case you disagree with him, his zombie minion(s) next to him make him very persuasive!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T08:04:11-07:00","id":1220540,"title":"","content":"If I have a time based legacy, can I use time in a bottle to instantly use an attainment? Likewise with Space *Everywhere&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:28:28-07:00","id":1220559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220540#post1220540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a time based legacy, can I use time in a bottle to instantly use an attainment? Likewise with Space *Everywhere&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the example of the 11Q in the book, it seems to not be intended, but I can't see that it would really hurt anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:28:28-07:00","id":1220560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220540#post1220540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a time based legacy, can I use time in a bottle to instantly use an attainment? Likewise with Space *Everywhere&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the example of the 11Q in the book, it seems to not be intended, but I can't see that it would really hurt anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T19:34:24-07:00","id":1220688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220540#post1220540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a time based legacy, can I use time in a bottle to instantly use an attainment? Likewise with Space *Everywhere&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say &quot;no&quot;. Time in a Bottle replaces you spending a reach with you spending a point of mana, Legacies do not allow you to spend reach on attainments as the reach is &quot;built in&quot;.<br /> <br /> IMO, anything that reads &quot;when X occurs you may do Y instead&quot; still requires you to be able to do X.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T19:40:55-07:00","id":1220689,"title":"","content":"In D&amp;D, there's a marvellously useful spell called Leomund's Secret Chest. The effect is pretty simple: the caster first makes or has made a pair of wood chests, one normal sized, one miniature. The large one can be sent away (in D&amp;D, into to Ethereal Plane) and called back by use of the miniature. In Awakening this would clear be a Space spell, with the miniature chest acting as a sympathetic Yantra. I'm just wondering if it should be Space 4 or Space 5. And I'm not regrading the miniature as &quot;you absolutely must have this!&quot; It might well be optional or entirely needless under Awakening rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T19:52:38-07:00","id":1220692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220689#post1220689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In D&amp;D, there's a marvellously useful spell called Leomund's Secret Chest. The effect is pretty simple: the caster first makes or has made a pair of wood chests, one normal sized, one miniature. The large one can be sent away (in D&amp;D, into to Ethereal Plane) and called back by use of the miniature. In Awakening this would clear be a Space spell, with the miniature chest acting as a sympathetic Yantra. I'm just wondering if it should be Space 4 or Space 5. And I'm not regrading the miniature as &amp;quot;you absolutely must have this!&amp;quot; It might well be optional or entirely needless under Awakening rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Space 4 Teleportation, used with Sympathetic Range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:15:42-07:00","id":1220697,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T01:11:43-07:00","id":1220755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220692#post1220692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like Space 4 Teleportation, used with Sympathetic Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space 4 if the larger chest is teleported somewhere else in the material plane. Space 5 if the chest is teleported into a pocket dimension. But by space 5 you can just created a pocket realm and teleport stuff into/out of it whenever without the need for a chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T01:15:09-07:00","id":1220757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220755#post1220755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Space 4 if the larger chest is teleported somewhere else in the material plane. Space 5 if the chest is teleported into a pocket dimension. But by space 5 you can just created a pocket realm and teleport stuff into/out of it whenever without the need for a chest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops. I forgot the \u201cEthereal Plane\u201d part, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a>. Recreating that part by reimagining DnD\u2019s Ethereal Plane as a Pocket Dimension is going to take Space 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:54:58-07:00","id":1220835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220755#post1220755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Space 4 if the larger chest is teleported somewhere else in the material plane. Space 5 if the chest is teleported into a pocket dimension. But by space 5 you can just created a pocket realm and teleport stuff into/out of it whenever without the need for a chest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chest can still be convenient, for moving collections of objects like clothes, books or tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T12:18:31-07:00","id":1220901,"title":"","content":"When founding a Legacy, it mentions that the Gnosis requirement is increased from 2 to 3. Is the requirement for the Ruling Arcanum also increased?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24149-the-third-king","name":"The Third King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:38:06-07:00","id":1220928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Third King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220901#post1220901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When founding a Legacy, it mentions that the Gnosis requirement is increased from 2 to 3. Is the requirement for the Ruling Arcanum also increased?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You can join an established legacy at gnosis 2 but to found one requires 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:55:15-07:00","id":1220932,"title":"","content":"I meant do you need [Ruling Arcanum] 3 to found a Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24149-the-third-king","name":"The Third King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:57:25-07:00","id":1220933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Third King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220932#post1220932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant do you need [Ruling Arcanum] 3 to found a Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don\u2019t, the only thing that changes are Gnosis requirements. If it did require increased knowledge of arcana you\u2019d never have a fifth attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-21-2018, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:57:52-07:00","id":1220934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Third King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1220932#post1220932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant do you need [Ruling Arcanum] 3 to found a Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything that indicates you wouldn't only need to follow the chart for the first Attainment?<br /> It's got to be extremely rare for someone not with 3+ in a legacy's Ruling Arcanum to found that legacy, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:47:20-07:00","id":1221501,"title":"","content":"Question: Can the Prime effect As Above, So Below be used on a Rote Mudra Skill? RAW it requires a specific example of the Yantra per the book, but is a specific Rote skill acceptable for that or too vague? I tend to think it is both too vague and too cheesy, but I want to get some additional opinions on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24114-hyperluminary","name":"Hyperluminary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24114_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T12:03:38-07:00","id":1221516,"title":"","content":"The Yantra has to be the subject for the spell. Since a mudra is not a discrete entity it's probably impossible to target it directly with As Above, So Below. However, if you choose to assign one Potency to that mudra, you could probably cast As Above, So Below as an AoE spell and be able to perform the mudra in that area with the dice trick.<br /> <br /> Edit: If it does work, it would only affect a specific mudra for a specific Rote per Potency. You can't cast it on a Skill and have all mudras using that Skill gain the dice trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-23-2018, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T12:03:50-07:00","id":1221517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyperluminary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221501#post1221501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Can the Prime effect As Above, So Below be used on a Rote Mudra Skill? RAW it requires a specific example of the Yantra per the book, but is a specific Rote skill acceptable for that or too vague? I tend to think it is both too vague and too cheesy, but I want to get some additional opinions on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the only Yantra in the Actions subset that I'd allow AASB to apply to is Runes; the spell feels like it's intended to be used on phenomena that continue to concretely exist rather than the abstract category of &quot;a Yantra.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:45:17-07:00","id":1221704,"title":"","content":"So, imbued items seem pretty weak; My question is, do they benefit from the single free reach and potency of their given spell?<br /> <br /> ie: Mend is a 4 dot spell you roll 4 dice as a sleep(walker) would you benefit from 4 potency to start with and a reach to make it instant or prolonged or whatever? The rules don't really go into detail other than &quot;you roll the spells Arcanum rating + Gnosis if any have fun&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no point in making an item that casts Mend at 1 potency (2L) for a mana and handing it to my proximus friend only for them to heal 2L for a point of mana - not when I can effortlessly heal then for 10L even sympathetically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:56:20-07:00","id":1221709,"title":"","content":"The books don't specify but as you use the spells Arcanum rating for determining the size of the dice pool it would make sense to use that value to determine the primary spellfactor. So a Mending would have 4 potency base,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:25:53-07:00","id":1221795,"title":"","content":"Could a Forces mage chill something by pulling heat out of it? Or would it require Death? Death would be easier, of course, but that's not what I'm wondering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:40:40-07:00","id":1221800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221795#post1221795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Forces mage chill something by pulling heat out of it? Or would it require Death? Death would be easier, of course, but that's not what I'm wondering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. And it doesn't require pulling heat out (implying moving the energy to something else). Just lowering it is enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T14:27:40-07:00","id":1221839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221704#post1221704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, imbued items seem pretty weak; My question is, do they benefit from the single free reach and potency of their given spell?<br /> <br /> ie: Mend is a 4 dot spell you roll 4 dice as a sleep(walker) would you benefit from 4 potency to start with and a reach to make it instant or prolonged or whatever? The rules don't really go into detail other than &amp;quot;you roll the spells Arcanum rating + Gnosis if any have fun&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There's no point in making an item that casts Mend at 1 potency (2L) for a mana and handing it to my proximus friend only for them to heal 2L for a point of mana - not when I can effortlessly heal then for 10L even sympathetically.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, and rereading the rules for the Imbue Item Attainment (which talks about the imbuer being able to lower spell factors or cancel the spell), is making me interpret the Arcanum (+ Gnosis) roll to \u201ccast\u201d the spell isn\u2019t the actual spellcasting dice pool (from which spell factors are derived), but simply a dice pool used to trigger the Imbued spell, with its spell factors and Reach all pre-assigned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T15:16:44-07:00","id":1221856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221704#post1221704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, imbued items seem pretty weak; My question is, do they benefit from the single free reach and potency of their given spell?<br /> <br /> ie: Mend is a 4 dot spell you roll 4 dice as a sleep(walker) would you benefit from 4 potency to start with and a reach to make it instant or prolonged or whatever? The rules don't really go into detail other than &quot;you roll the spells Arcanum rating + Gnosis if any have fun&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no point in making an item that casts Mend at 1 potency (2L) for a mana and handing it to my proximus friend only for them to heal 2L for a point of mana - not when I can effortlessly heal then for 10L even sympathetically.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, from my reading (and this could very well have some head-cannon intruding), Imbuing basically imprints a copy of &quot;casting the spell&quot; upon an item with a few adjustable parameters. The Mage who Imbued the spell, if they retain Spell Control over it, can adjust the Spell Factors whenever the item is used. By implication, I <i>think</i> that Imbuements that are Relinquished have their spells treated as if they were Relinquished (no modifying Spell Factors).<br /> <br /> Now, how this factors into your question is that the Imbued Item <i>should</i> cast the spell exactly as if you were casting it - each time it is activated. So, since you need Life 4 to cast it, it should have at least 1 Reach and a base 4 Potency. Whether it can be Imbued with higher Potency and Reach if you have Life 5 is unclear. You <i>can</i> explicitly over-Reach using it, though.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Also what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T17:57:15-07:00","id":1221892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221839#post1221839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, and rereading the rules for the Imbue Item Attainment (which talks about the imbuer being able to lower spell factors or cancel the spell), is making me interpret the Arcanum (+ Gnosis) roll to \u201ccast\u201d the spell isn\u2019t the actual spellcasting dice pool (from which spell factors are derived), but simply a dice pool used to trigger the Imbued spell, with its spell factors and Reach all pre-assigned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is something I can get behind. Thanks. Imbuing an item with &quot;any spell you could cast&quot; gives this a little meat too. So I should be able to ritually cast something pretty nice for my Proximus, and &quot;copy&quot; that specific spell (since the Imago would include the potency, and so on and so on) and then you simply try to activate it with that roll mentioned - possibly over-reaching above anything that's set to say, cast at sensory range (in the case of a self/touch heal imbuement) or so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T18:36:01-07:00","id":1221902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221839#post1221839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, and rereading the rules for the Imbue Item Attainment (which talks about the imbuer being able to lower spell factors or cancel the spell), is making me interpret the Arcanum (+ Gnosis) roll to \u201ccast\u201d the spell isn\u2019t the actual spellcasting dice pool (from which spell factors are derived), but simply a dice pool used to trigger the Imbued spell, with its spell factors and Reach all pre-assigned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to disagree; the section about the makers of unrelinquished imbued items retaining spell control shares a paragraph with the text that explains how keeping that connection also lets them remotely destroy them, which suggests that's more about not needing to worry so much about your creations being used against your interests.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the roll isn't substantially worse than a Retainer uses, Reach and Primary spell factors can do a lot of heavy lifting, and there's little to suggest that Willpower isn't as viable to use on it as it is on regular casting. Mage as a gameline has historically been less concerned with outfitting non-mage minions with magical items than, say, Changeling or Demon; it's within spec for imbued items to be less viable than tokens or gadgets, particularly in an edition where Artifacts are no longer exclusively usable by mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T18:41:25-07:00","id":1221905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221902#post1221902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to disagree; the section about the makers of unrelinquished imbued items retaining spell control shares a paragraph with the text that explains how keeping that connection also lets them remotely destroy them, which suggests that's more about not needing to worry so much about your creations being used against your interests.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the roll isn't substantially worse than a Retainer uses, Reach and Primary spell factors can do a lot of heavy lifting, and there's little to suggest that Willpower isn't as viable to use on it as it is on regular casting. Mage as a gameline has historically been less concerned with outfitting non-mage minions with magical items than, say, Changeling or Demon; it's within spec for imbued items to be less viable than tokens or gadgets, particularly in an edition where Artifacts are no longer exclusively usable by mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken about Retainer and Willpower. <br /> <br /> By Reach and primary spell factors, which are you indicating that the item\u2019s activation uses - the imbuer\u2019s, or the user\u2019s? Or either in the case of Awakened users, like Artifacts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T20:44:54-07:00","id":1221929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1221905#post1221905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Reach and primary spell factors, which are you indicating that the item\u2019s activation uses - the imbuer\u2019s, or the user\u2019s? Or either in the case of Awakened users, like Artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precedent would suggest the item's. The actual breadth of &quot;Touch Range&quot; being what it is and the effects of releasing Paradox being what they are, instant casting and Advanced Duration will carry most effects a good chunk of the way with minimal risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:24:51-07:00","id":1222242,"title":"","content":"Any purchased dots beyond the fifth count as a half-dot worth of spells when calculating an Enhanced Item's costs. But what happens if the Merit is combined with the Imbued Item Merit, such that the dot costs for the Imbued spells and/or increased Mana capacity hit 5+ even before calculating the Enhancements? I'd like to say the increased marginal cost of Enhanced Item only counts the Enhanced Item's own functions, but what does everybody else think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:36:05-07:00","id":1222244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1222242#post1222242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any purchased dots beyond the fifth count as a half-dot worth of spells when calculating an Enhanced Item's costs. But what happens if the Merit is combined with the Imbued Item Merit, such that the dot costs for the Imbued spells and/or increased Mana capacity hit 5+ even before calculating the Enhancements? I'd like to say the increased marginal cost of Enhanced Item only counts the Enhanced Item's own functions, but what does everybody else think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to treat &quot;these Merits can be combined&quot; as &quot;these Merits can be used jointly to represent an item with both of their effects&quot; \u2014 they still have separate ratings for the purposes of their own mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:44:28-07:00","id":1222247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1222244#post1222244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to treat &quot;these Merits can be combined&quot; as &quot;these Merits can be used jointly to represent an item with both of their effects&quot; \u2014 they still have separate ratings for the purposes of their own mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So would it be possible to have one such combined item/Merit go over 10 dots in theory, yes? Because I'm writing one now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:55:56-07:00","id":1222250,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to say yes. Calculate the &quot;Imbued&quot; Merit cost by itself, calculate the &quot;Enhanced&quot; Merit cost by itself, then add them. That's your total cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-26-2018, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T16:31:52-07:00","id":1222323,"title":"","content":"Is there a theoretical limit to the amount of Durability that can be added to an object via Alter Integrity? The practical limit on how high an object's Durability can become is clearly (maximum dice pool/2)+2. But with an arbitrarily large pool, there seems no theoretical upper limit. I don't actually have a problem with that, I just want to know if it's correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T17:02:51-07:00","id":1222328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1222323#post1222323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a theoretical limit to the amount of Durability that can be added to an object via Alter Integrity? The practical limit on how high an object's Durability can become is clearly (maximum dice pool/2)+2. But with an arbitrarily large pool, there seems no theoretical upper limit. I don't actually have a problem with that, I just want to know if it's correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>The effect increases Durability, can be Lasting, and has no in-built restriction other than Withstand.<br /> So if you take it as a Praxis or Rote, and want to go fishing for Exceptionals with which to ignore that Withstand, you can theoretically create an object with Durability 20+ by layering one spell on top of another.<br /> e.g. Durability 2 base + Potency 3 Alter Integrity spell = Withstand/Durability 5. Get an Exceptional on a Potency 3 Alter Integrity spell, that's Withstand/Durability 8, keep going from there.<br /> <br /> Make a feather than can scratch diamonds.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure cumulative Lasting effects don't override previous effects.<br /> Otherwise repeated healing would have some... Atypical side effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T17:48:20-07:00","id":1222329,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:45:52-07:00","id":1223204,"title":"","content":"Can Matter 5 alone create recognizable food like steak, bacon or tofu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:51:44-07:00","id":1223211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223204#post1223204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Matter 5 alone create recognizable food like steak, bacon or tofu?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:53:33-07:00","id":1223213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223211#post1223211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure it can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could Matter 4 transmute them from existing matter? Or is 5 already doing that b/c Conservation of Mass/Energy is not part of the Lie?<br /> <br /> Would you need Forces to make sure the food was the right temperature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:32:34-07:00","id":1223231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223213#post1223213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could Matter 4 transmute them from existing matter? Or is 5 already doing that b/c Conservation of Mass/Energy is not part of the Lie?<br /> <br /> Would you need Forces to make sure the food was the right temperature?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use Transubstantuation to convert one form of matter to something edible, and yes you\u2019d need Forces 2 for it to be heated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:19:18-07:00","id":1223288,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, you can't create lifeforms with Matter so any food you create will be free from diseases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:30:43-07:00","id":1223584,"title":"","content":"When it comes to relinquishing spells, is it common practice to use a mind spell to temporarily buff an attribute and spend that extra willpower? 3 dots of mind permanently waiving the experience cost of relinquishing spells is something worth asking about I figured. They mention rules for temporary health, I thought maybe that'd apply to willpower to prevent such a glaring loop hole.<br /> <br /> Mind mages are straight up better than the others who have to spend their hard earned XP on maintaining buff or defensive spells - even just the casual advantages of essentially ignoring your spell control limit (and benefits to clash of wills besides for long term spells you're now free to cast and let go)<br /> <br /> Do the rules actually support this? If so, I guess I'll be getting 3 dots of mind asap lest I get left behind in experience and prepared defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-31-2018, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:57:57-07:00","id":1223591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223584#post1223584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to relinquishing spells, is it common practice to use a mind spell to temporarily buff an attribute and spend that extra willpower? 3 dots of mind permanently waiving the experience cost of relinquishing spells is something worth asking about though, I figured. They mention rules for temporary health, I thought maybe that'd apply to willpower to prevent such a glaring loop hole that makes mind mages straight up better than the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you spend/loose a point of willpower from safely relinquishing a spell, then its lost until you pay the xp to regain it. So you'll still have lost it when whatever spell you used to increase your willpower ends. Using magic to gain temp willpower points is still a spell control slot and is still subject to dispelling etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-31-2018, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:28:24-07:00","id":1223602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223591#post1223591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you spend/loose a point of willpower from safely relinquishing a spell, then its lost until you pay the xp to regain it. So you'll still have lost it when whatever spell you used to increase your willpower ends. Using magic to gain temp willpower points is still a spell control slot and is still subject to dispelling etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So similar to temporary health, if it's spent it doesn't matter if your &quot;cap&quot; changes it still counts as a spent dot. I don't suppose you have a source?<br /> <br /> The way it's been ruled in most of the games I've played is you grant yourself extra willpower, spend those dots, dismiss the spell; the extra willpower is spent instead of your main pool. Thanks for clearing that up though I kinda figured that was pretty strong lol, even among mages which are typically considered The best when prepared among the supernaturals.<br /> <br /> So when the extra willpower expires, does all spent willpower (points and dots) remain spent? (Ie, I have 8 willpower, grant myself 4, spend 6. Once the spell expires I have 2/8 willpower left, not 6/8 likewise with dots.) When I've spent more than my normal capacity it'd just all be spent then afaik, but then how would spending more dots than you have work? You'd still essentially have free relinquished spells..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-31-2018, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:44:33-07:00","id":1223606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223602#post1223602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So similar to temporary health, if it's spent it doesn't matter if your &amp;quot;cap&amp;quot; changes it still counts as a spent dot. I don't suppose you have a source?<br /> <br /> The way it's been ruled in most of the games I've played is you grant yourself extra willpower, spend it, dismiss the spell; the extra willpower is spent instead of your main pool. Thanks for clearing that up though I kinda figured that was pretty strong lol, even among mages which are typically considered The best when prepared among the supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... chances are, if one one ruling leads to exploiting rules for minmaxing, and another ruling leads to less powergaming but more adherence to the setting and lore, chances are RAI is the latter. Especially in these games, and especially in Mage!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:50:29-07:00","id":1223608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223602#post1223602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So similar to temporary health, if it's spent it doesn't matter if your &quot;cap&quot; changes it still counts as a spent dot. I don't suppose you have a source?<br /> <br /> The way it's been ruled in most of the games I've played is you grant yourself extra willpower, spend those dots, dismiss the spell; the extra willpower is spent instead of your main pool. Thanks for clearing that up though I kinda figured that was pretty strong lol, even among mages which are typically considered The best when prepared among the supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you have Resolve 2 + Composure 2 for a normal willpower of 4. Use a mind spell to increase your Resolve by 2 which also raises your <i>dots in </i>willpower by 2 to 6. When you spend a <i>dot </i>relinquishing a spell you would then have 5 and when the spell ends you loose 2 points of Resolve and also 2 points of willpower so you are left with 3 when the spell ends. Spending points of willpower with temp points gained from an increase in resolve/composure is fine since its pretty each to regain willpower points. There is no other way to gain willpower other than raising resolve or composure, you cant raise willpower directly.<br /> <br /> It works the same with temp health, if you have a spell that has increased your stamina by 3 giving you 3 extra health levels for a total of 10. If you take 10 points of bashing and have a full health bar and loose those 3 points of stamina, you take 3 lethal damage as it wraps round. Those 8th,9th and 10th health levels of bashing damage dont just vanish and leave you with 7 health levels of bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-31-2018, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:53:10-07:00","id":1223610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223608#post1223608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you have Resolve 2 + Composure 2 for a normal willpower of 4. Use a mind spell to increase your Resolve by 2 which also raises your <i>dots in </i>willpower by 2 to 6. When you spend a <i>dot </i>relinquishing a spell you would then have 5 and when the spell ends you loose 2 points of Resolve and also 2 points of willpower so you are left with 3 when the spell ends. Spending points of willpower with temp dots gained from an increase in resolve/composure is fine since its pretty each to regain willpower anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it should be that willpower points/dots remain spent, the temporary increase is just that - temporary and those dots are gone along with the spell granting them. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T07:26:54-07:00","id":1223612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223610#post1223610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it should be that willpower points/dots remain spent, the temporary increase is just that - temporary and those dots are gone along with the spell granting them. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically you could have a base willpower of 4, increase your resolve/willpower by 6 gaining 6 willpower dots and use those dots to relinquish 6 spells. However when the spell ends you are either willpower -2 or 0 however and personally as a ST i would do really bad things to you. Either way your rebuying 6 willpower dots before your back to normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T07:42:33-07:00","id":1223617,"title":"","content":"However, I'd say that yes, it's legitimate to raise your Resolve or Composure, increase your Willpower, and spend those extra points (points, not dots) without losing normal willpower points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T08:16:13-07:00","id":1223627,"title":"","content":"Talking to a fellow player they made a strong argument for the latter case of &quot;I grant WP, it's spent, spell takes those spent dots away&quot; saying that a spell only takes what's granted.<br /> <br /> The example given is a sword or life form shaped or created, what have you. If someone destroys the item/creature the spell is still under spell control until dismissed. Once dismissed, it doesn't then destroy another item or creature in place of the old one it was maintaining. Likewise with willpower which is tracked from right to left, anything spent would vanish alongside anything not spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-31-2018, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T09:08:55-07:00","id":1223642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223627#post1223627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking to a fellow player they made a strong argument for the latter case of &quot;I grant WP, it's spent, spell takes those spent dots away&quot; saying that a spell only takes what's granted.<br /> <br /> The example given is a sword or life form shaped or created, what have you. If someone destroys the item/creature the spell is still under spell control until dismissed. Once dismissed, it doesn't then destroy another item or creature in place of the old one it was maintaining. Likewise with willpower which is tracked from right to left, anything spent would vanish alongside anything not spent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You dont colour temp willpower points red and then spend/loose them and only remove the red ones when the temp willpower ends. The fact damage done to health levels doesnt vanish when the health levels vanish means you cant escape your fate. Spent willpower is claimed/done even if you have lost it in the mean time. Its zerosum, You gain 2 willpower via magic. Spend/loose 1 to relinquish then loose 2 via magic ending means you have lost 3 you cant claim to have lost one twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T11:14:03-07:00","id":1223672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223642#post1223642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You dont colour temp willpower points red and then spend/loose them and only remove the red ones when the temp willpower ends. The fact damage done to health levels doesnt vanish when the health levels vanish means you cant escape your fate. Spent willpower is claimed/done even if you have lost it in the mean time. Its zerosum, You gain 2 willpower via magic. Spend/loose 1 to relinquish then loose 2 via magic ending means you have lost 3 you cant claim to have lost one twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first argument in response; the retort was that willpower dots are tracked from the right, besides that - you're not gaining/losing willpower so much as recalculating the new max based on changing attributes. I agree with you, I'm simply posting the opposition in this argument for completeness sake and also for other opinions. However re-calculating the new max (ie like health when your stamina changes) is a bit of a moot point imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-31-2018, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T16:19:40-07:00","id":1223753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223672#post1223672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my first argument in response; the retort was that willpower dots are tracked from the right, besides that - you're not gaining/losing willpower so much as recalculating the new max based on changing attributes. I agree with you, I'm simply posting the opposition in this argument for completeness sake and also for other opinions. However re-calculating the new max (ie like health when your stamina changes) is a bit of a moot point imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly dont see how tracking them from the right makes any difference since when you gain or loose willpower you colour/rub out the most right willpower dot on the character sheet. Gain x willpower, pencil x more dots on the character sheet to the right of whatever you had originally, loose x willpower rub out x dots. The fact you rubbed another one out relinquishing a spell in between makes no difference, you still rub out the x you gained from the spell when it ends. If you fill in 2 extra willpower dots, rub one out when relinquishing a spell then later lose those extra 2 willpower points why would anybody think they only rub out 1 willpower dot when they need to remove 2 willpower dots? Even recalculating new maxes would be base max 4 which becomes max 6 (with +2) that becomes max 5 (relinquish a spell) which slides to become a max of 3 when you remove the +2.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T16:26:51-07:00","id":1223754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223753#post1223753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly dont see how tracking them from the right makes any difference since when you gain or loose willpower you colour/rub out the most right willpower dot on the character sheet. Gain x willpower, pencil x more dots on the character sheet to the right of whatever you had originally, loose x willpower rub out x dots. The fact you rubbed another one out relinquishing a spell in between makes no difference, you still rub out the x you gained from the spell when it ends. If you fill in 2 extra willpower dots, rub one out when relinquishing a spell then later lose those extra 2 willpower points why would anybody think they only rub out 1 willpower dot when they need to remove 2 willpower dots? Even recalculating new maxes would be base max 4 which becomes max 6 (with +2) that becomes max 5 (relinquish a spell) which slides to become a max of 3 when you remove the +2.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I get that. I think it's more &quot;Your new max is is 6 instead of 4, you spent 1 dot, and so you lose the 2 granted dots, one of which was spent so you go back down to 4 instead of 3.&quot; I can see why someone would argue that (basically, I make 2 dots appear out of thin air, I spent one of the dots that was &quot;made&quot; and when the spell is gone I lose the one I didn't spend, and one of the dots was &quot;spent&quot; and is therefore gone either way. I don't agree with that methodology though.<br /> <br /> They're treating the dots as a &quot;product of the spell&quot; that can be spent, as if it were gold or some physical thing where you're just gaining and spending the gained sum, then letting the spell expire since it's &quot;product&quot; has been used/destroyed - similar to if you had a life form you created and killed, and then dismissed the spell as far as the logic is concerned.<br /> <br /> At any rate this is all academic, the ST. in our group will likely come to her own conclusion which is fine either way I guess but I'm glad I don't sound like a crazy person for suggesting it not be so easy to circumvent basically every limit of mage. (free relinquishes means spell control/duration and a few other things are largely irrelevant to that mage.)<br /> <br /> That being said, a relinquished spell can still be dispelled, the willpower point still lost and that 1 xp amounting to nothing, unlike imbued items which take a 5 dot prime spell to destroy (but still can be) or other items represented by merits and therefore falling under Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-31-2018, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T22:02:23-07:00","id":1223834,"title":"","content":"I'm not too clear on shadow names. Shadow names are for use in magical circles, period. Birth names make you more vulnerable to sympathetic magic (and these days, they're laughably easy to discover)). So do we normally have situation like this: Frank Chandler Awakens, adopts the shadow name Chandu, and starts to create a new everyday identity as Tom Collins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T22:33:06-07:00","id":1223837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223834#post1223834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too clear on shadow names. Shadow names are for use in magical circles, period. Birth names make you more vulnerable to sympathetic magic (and these days, they're laughably easy to discover)). So do we normally have situation like this: Frank Chandler Awakens, adopts the shadow name Chandu, and starts to create a new everyday identity as Tom Collins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frank Chandler Awakens, adopts the Shadow Name Chandu, and takes pains to separate the persona of Chandu from Chandler's life as much as he can. If his social attachments permit it, he may adopt an Alternate Identity as Tom Collins to further insulate his sympathetic name from discovery, possibly going so far as to abandon his old life entirely and set up shop in a new region altogether, but many mages get by just fine with drama-club supplies, careful scheduling, and judicious use of magic ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T23:05:50-07:00","id":1223839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223834#post1223834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too clear on shadow names. Shadow names are for use in magical circles, period. Birth names make you more vulnerable to sympathetic magic (and these days, they're laughably easy to discover)). So do we normally have situation like this: Frank Chandler Awakens, adopts the shadow name Chandu, and starts to create a new everyday identity as Tom Collins?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Satchel said, and IIRC Order Status has Alternate Identity as one of the Merits a mage can \u201cborrow\u201d from them precisely because of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T02:17:14-07:00","id":1223859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1223834#post1223834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too clear on shadow names. Shadow names are for use in magical circles, period. Birth names make you more vulnerable to sympathetic magic (and these days, they're laughably easy to discover)). So do we normally have situation like this: Frank Chandler Awakens, adopts the shadow name Chandu, and starts to create a new everyday identity as Tom Collins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not knowing a sympathetic name is basically a -2 dice penalty and hardly a massive barrier to somebody determined to sympathetically cast at you. Some mages might go to all that trouble others might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T10:16:22-07:00","id":1224191,"title":"","content":"Does the Adamant Hand merit allow you to cast <i>any</i> spell reflexively the same turn as a combat action? Or is it still specifically spells like Exceptional Luck that have the +2 reach option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T11:05:40-07:00","id":1224201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224191#post1224191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Adamant Hand merit allow you to cast <i>any</i> spell reflexively the same turn as a combat action? Or is it still specifically spells like Exceptional Luck that have the +2 reach option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant Hand doesn't make casting a spell reflexively possible at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T11:42:54-07:00","id":1224205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224201#post1224201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adamant Hand doesn't make casting a spell reflexively possible at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Effect: Your character has studied extensively in the Ada-<br /> mantine Arrow martial arts. This allows her to use combat<br /> techniques as Yantras for instant spells. When taking this Merit,<br /> choose Athletics, Weaponry, or Brawl, which your character<br /> must have three or more dots in. This Merit allows use of that<br /> Skill in combat as a reflexive Order tool Yantra, adding dice<br /> to a spell cast on subsequent turns, or to a spell cast reflexively<br /> in the same turn as the combat action. You may purchase this<br /> Merit multiple times to reflect the other styles.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;To a spell cast reflexively&quot; makes sense that it doesn't actually grant the ability to cast reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T11:58:31-07:00","id":1224207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224205#post1224205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;To a spell cast reflexively&quot; makes sense that it doesn't actually grant the ability to cast reflexively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, it doesn't grant the ability to cast a spell reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T00:47:17-07:00","id":1224293,"title":"","content":"Addamant Hand affects spells that already can be cast reflexively, like Turn Momentum for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T06:17:45-07:00","id":1224336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224293#post1224293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addamant Hand affects spells that already can be cast reflexively, like Turn Momentum for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant Hand can be used with any spell regardless of whether it\u2019s reflexive.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re both missing the point of what Adamant Hand does, it allows you to use an action to accomplish a thing with Athletics, Brawl, or Weaponry to serve as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-03-2018, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T06:29:10-07:00","id":1224339,"title":"","content":"I know what it does. I only wanted to clarify that the way the description mentions reflexive casting in the description means that it can effect spells that are cast reflexively as opposed to allowing you to cast spells reflexively.<br /> <br /> The wording is slightly confusing in that manner, so i tried to clarify that. Seems I failied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 06-03-2018, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T12:22:26-07:00","id":1224416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224339#post1224339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what it does. I only wanted to clarify that the way the description mentions reflexive casting in the description means that it can effect spells that are cast reflexively as opposed to allowing you to cast spells reflexively.<br /> <br /> The wording is slightly confusing in that manner, so i tried to clarify that. Seems I failied.</div> </div> </div> </div>It simply makes it possible to use combat actions with a specific skill to count as reflexive Yantras. Simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> 'Nother question - Shield of Chronos. If someone views the past of someone I was with, would it still clash? ie, I shield myself and use shifting sands - someone postcognition's someone else that was involved in the unwritten (shield) time. Would they see the past with me cut out (clash aside) or would they clash to see the past I was involved with period?<br /> Likewise, if I just indefinitely cast Shield of Chronos, anyone I interacted with would have some safety as I'm essentially veiled from their history? Or would it be a clash to look at the time regardless of who is present &quot;at that time in the past&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T14:49:00-07:00","id":1224445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224416#post1224416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It simply makes it possible to use combat actions with a specific skill to count as reflexive Yantras. Simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> 'Nother question - Shield of Chronos. If someone views the past of someone I was with, would it still clash? ie, I shield myself and use shifting sands - someone postcognition's someone else that was involved in the unwritten (shield) time. Would they see the past with me cut out (clash aside) or would they clash to see the past I was involved with period?<br /> Likewise, if I just indefinitely cast Shield of Chronos, anyone I interacted with would have some safety as I'm essentially veiled from their history? Or would it be a clash to look at the time regardless of who is present &quot;at that time in the past&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd fail to see you unless they have something that would allow them to CoW, the past isn't obstructed wholesale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T15:07:15-07:00","id":1224452,"title":"","content":"Questions on potency and withstand:<br /> A mage has prime armor (3 dots) and Wards and Signs (potency 4) active and is the target of an attack spell with potency 8. How much damage does the mage take?<br /> <br /> Similarly with a resolve of 3 and Wards and Signs (potency 4) the mage is the target of a mind spell Psychic Domination with potency 5. What is the potency of Psychic Domination after withstand?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T15:57:53-07:00","id":1224466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224452#post1224452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions on potency and withstand:<br /> A mage has prime armor (3 dots) and Wards and Signs (potency 4) active and is the target of an attack spell with potency 8. How much damage does the mage take?<br /> <br /> Similarly with a resolve of 3 and Wards and Signs (potency 4) the mage is the target of a mind spell Psychic Domination with potency 5. What is the potency of Psychic Domination after withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wards and Signs grants a Withstand of 4. Potency (8) - Withstand (4) = 4 effective Potency, meaning 4 damage. Prime Armor removes 3 damage and the mage takes 1 damage.<br /> <br /> When a spell is Withstood multiple times you count the highest Withstand rating (4 from Wards and Signs) and add one to that per additional Withstand (+1 from Resolve) for a total of 5 Withstand. Potency (5) - Withstand (5) = 0 effective Potency. The spell has no effect, unless the Withstand rating is lowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T16:12:16-07:00","id":1224471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224466#post1224466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wards and Signs grants a Withstand of 4. Potency (8) - Withstand (4) = 4 effective Potency, meaning 4 damage. Prime Armor removes 3 damage and the mage takes 1 damage.<br /> <br /> When a spell is Withstood multiple times you count the highest Withstand rating (4 from Wards and Signs) and add one to that per additional Withstand (+1 from Resolve) for a total of 5 Withstand. Potency (5) - Withstand (5) = 0 effective Potency. The spell has no effect, unless the Withstand rating is lowered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Damage spells aren't withstood normally - the stamina is already accounted for in health. Also, it says if there are multiple withstand ratings, add +1 to the highest. Not <i>per</i> extra withstand rating afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T17:46:22-07:00","id":1224498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224471#post1224471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damage spells aren't withstood normally - the stamina is already accounted for in health. Also, it says if there are multiple withstand ratings, add +1 to the highest. Not <i>per</i> extra withstand rating afaik.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings (for example, a Withstood spell cast with the Sympathetic Range Attainment) it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wards and Signs does not exclude spells that aren't normally Withstood. In fact, it's probably primarily used to deal with damage spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T22:21:36-07:00","id":1224567,"title":"","content":"Could a mage create a contagious zombie plague? Death 5 would be pretty well a necessity, I think, but that assumes it's even possible, which assumption I'm not entirely prepared to make. It's the &quot;contagious&quot; part that gives me pause; creating a great many zombies is just Quicken Corpse with a high Scale factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T22:37:42-07:00","id":1224571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224567#post1224567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a mage create a contagious zombie plague? Death 5 would be pretty well a necessity, I think, but that assumes it's even possible, which assumption I'm not entirely prepared to make. It's the &quot;contagious&quot; part that gives me pause; creating a great many zombies is just Quicken Corpse with a high Scale factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short of archmastery, I'm pretty sure contagious spells are firmly in the realm of severe Paradox effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T22:52:44-07:00","id":1224576,"title":"","content":"Why use Death when you can use Life? There are zombie viruses in real life that can take over simpler organisms. You\u2019d also have the advantage of it not being a spell doing the heavy lifting, the spell would create the virus but what the virus does after that isn\u2019t very magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T01:12:55-07:00","id":1224604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224567#post1224567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a mage create a contagious zombie plague?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he knew what he was doing, and such a thing was possible under Fallen science? Sure. Life 5 to create the plague which would infect Patient 0.<br /> Everyone he then infects has a Lasting copy of that 'naturally possible' virus.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if such a thing is not possible under fallen science you'd need a spell which constantly updates its parameters to allow for 'infection'.<br /> Which is Death 6, Dynamics to kill and raise any infected individual as a Zombie.<br /> <br /> An alternative route for Archmasters is Death/Life 7 Entities, to turn a normal 'scientific' Plague into a Supernatural Zombie-Plague, either making the infected individuals classic 'walking corpse' zombies, or new-fangled 'altered living' zombies respectively.<br /> <br /> Both of which likely being breaches of the Pax Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T06:02:48-07:00","id":1224652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224604#post1224604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he knew what he was doing, and such a thing was possible under Fallen science? Sure. Life 5 to create the plague which would infect Patient 0.<br /> Everyone he then infects has a Lasting copy of that 'naturally possible' virus.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if such a thing is not possible under fallen science you'd need a spell which constantly updates its parameters to allow for 'infection'.<br /> Which is Death 6, Dynamics to kill and raise any infected individual as a Zombie.<br /> <br /> An alternative route for Archmasters is Death/Life 7 Entities, to turn a normal 'scientific' Plague into a Supernatural Zombie-Plague, either making the infected individuals classic 'walking corpse' zombies, or new-fangled 'altered living' zombies respectively.<br /> <br /> Both of which likely being breaches of the Pax Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other alternatives are self-propagating Spirits/Ghosts/Goetia (which is cheating), or a Imbued Item (the &quot;item&quot; here being a corpse, and the Imbued spell being <i>Quicken Corpse</i>)... that could make other Imbued Items. Which breaks the rules, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T06:18:34-07:00","id":1224659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224604#post1224604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he knew what he was doing, and such a thing was possible under Fallen science? Sure. Life 5 to create the plague which would infect Patient 0.<br /> Everyone he then infects has a Lasting copy of that 'naturally possible' virus.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if such a thing is not possible under fallen science you'd need a spell which constantly updates its parameters to allow for 'infection'.<br /> Which is Death 6, Dynamics to kill and raise any infected individual as a Zombie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basing what you can and cant do with magic on Fallen Science is a slippely slope and wrong. Fallen science says people cant instantly travel from one place to another, but magic says otherwise. Dont use Fallen science saying X is or is not possible to decide if something is possible with magic or not instead use the supernal practices as written.<br /> <br /> Personally i would say contagious spells fall onto realm of dynamics. Altering/improving existing plagues to causes effects similar in its victims so they act like zombies (but arnt magically undead/dead) would be just Life weaving but the effects would end whenthe spell ended as the plague returns to its normal mundane version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T06:26:56-07:00","id":1224664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224659#post1224659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i would say contagious spells fall onto realm of dynamics. Altering/improving existing plagues to causes effects similar in its victims so they act like zombies (but arnt magically undead/dead) would be just Life weaving but the effects would end whenthe spell ended as the plague returns to its normal mundane version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use the +2 Reach option to give them Lasting heritable traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T06:50:48-07:00","id":1224669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224659#post1224659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basing what you can and cant do with magic on Fallen Science is a slippely slope and wrong. Fallen science says people cant instantly travel from one place to another, but magic says otherwise. Dont use Fallen science saying X is or is not possible to decide if something is possible with magic or not instead use the supernal practices as written.<br /> <br /> Personally i would say contagious spells fall onto realm of dynamics. Altering/improving existing plagues to causes effects similar in its victims so they act like zombies (but arnt magically undead/dead) would be just Life weaving but the effects would end whenthe spell ended as the plague returns to its normal mundane version.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand if fallen science says that something IS possible then you should be able to do it with magic. Some sickness have the abillity to influence behavior in a way that makes spreading easier (like rabies for instance). Not quite zombie plague but in some cases close enough if you pump the effect with magic and make it heritable.<br /> <br /> For something more direct I think there was a spell in 1E that allowed to imbue a living being supernatural abillities mimicking spells. Afaik it was a Prime+Life+X Patterning spell. Perhaps go from that and use Reach to make it heritable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T08:37:54-07:00","id":1224707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1224659#post1224659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basing what you can and cant do with magic on Fallen Science is a slippely slope and wrong. Fallen science says people cant instantly travel from one place to another, but magic says otherwise. Dont use Fallen science saying X is or is not possible to decide if something is possible with magic or not instead use the supernal practices as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life already has effects that can only be made Lasting (if the affected lifeform procreates) if the effects can be physically possible. If not physically possible, you can't spread those qualities along to any progeny. This is by the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T13:33:27-07:00","id":1225066,"title":"","content":"I find the mage sight system somewhat opaque.<br /> <br /> Anyone who know where I can find some fairly detailed examples for various mysteries and mage sights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T14:13:45-07:00","id":1225078,"title":"","content":"I think Signs of Sorcery is supposed to get into it, there was a <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\">peek</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T00:25:23-07:00","id":1225183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1225078#post1225078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Signs of Sorcery is supposed to get into it, there was a <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\">peek</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Still some examples would be very helpful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T00:55:45-07:00","id":1225187,"title":"","content":"Ok, from how I'm reading any sort of supernatural effect can be a Mystery when it comes to mage sight. This includes spells. So anything weird is a potential mystery that mages can investigate with Mage sight, whether it's a door leading to 1942, someone being posessed or a cursed painting. It would be easier to help if you mentioned what in particular are you struggling with.<br /> <br /> Though I have to admit I started to delve into the mage sight rules recently so my understanding might be off:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T06:15:11-07:00","id":1225556,"title":"","content":"Are Rampant and Megalomaniacal Mental Conditions which can be Pattern Restored away?<br /> I would assume so, they're both Conditions without a physical element, which affect the mind and decision-making.<br /> <br /> Or are they more like Spiritual ailments that can't be so simply cleansed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T06:43:49-07:00","id":1225557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1225556#post1225556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are they more like Spiritual ailments that can't be so simply cleansed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they alter your Obsessions and share this quality with the likes of Mystery Commands, I wouldn't put them in the same class of Condition as Shaken, Spooked, or Guilty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T16:53:02-07:00","id":1225769,"title":"","content":"Does Supernal Dispellation (Prime 4) alert the caster if you don\u2019t make the effect Lasting? For instance, if a mage\u2019s Ban (Space 3) were supressed for a turn or two while the Prime caster makes an escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18145-goatmanofcoffee","user":"Goatmanofcoffee","date":".  Added Arcanum for Ban for better clarification 06-07-2018, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18145-goatmanofcoffee","name":"Goatmanofcoffee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T05:35:27-07:00","id":1225851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goatmanofcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1225769#post1225769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Supernal Dispellation (Prime 4) alert the caster if you don\u2019t make the effect Lasting? For instance, if a mage\u2019s Ban (Space 3) were supressed for a turn or two while the Prime caster makes an escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>+2 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, the effect is Lasting. If the spell\u2019s original caster is still alive and has not relinquished the spell, she knows one of her spells was destroyed.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bIf it's specified, it's probably to contrast it to the non-Lasting effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T12:51:59-07:00","id":1226555,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would agree with Tessie, this is most likely how a lot of shenanigans can ensue in the Mage Frat House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T14:42:21-07:00","id":1226574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1225066#post1225066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the mage sight system somewhat opaque.<br /> <br /> Anyone who know where I can find some fairly detailed examples for various mysteries and mage sights?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886930-sample-mysteries\">Sample Mysteries</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T21:30:22-07:00","id":1227589,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this a simple question, but this seems the best to ask it first. Is a flying carpet an Imbued Item or an Enhanced Item? We all know what a flying carpet is: an ornate rug upon which a person stands, and which then flies, normally under the user's control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T21:59:06-07:00","id":1227594,"title":"","content":"Depends whether it's an inanimate rug until your use the command phrase, putting it innately under the user's mental/spell-control at per a spell, or it's a perpetually active preprogrammed item that moves when you pull the tassels or something to provide external stimulus/input. <br /> <br /> Former is an imbued item, latter an enhanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 06-15-2018, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T13:11:17-07:00","id":1228362,"title":"","content":"Distance is irrelevant to most Space spells. This means that <i>distance is irrelevant.</i> So I have to wonder, what, if anything, would keep a mage from use a high resolution photo of an extraterrestrial body to teleport to that body? I know there are environmental concerns (air, temperature, etc.), but those are secondary to my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T13:32:20-07:00","id":1228367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1227594#post1227594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends whether it's an inanimate rug until your use the command phrase, <u>putting it innately under the user's mental/spell-control at per a spell</u>, or it's a perpetually active preprogrammed item that moves when you pull the tassels or something to provide external stimulus/input.<br /> <br /> Former is an imbued item, latter an enhanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception that the effect still would not be under the activator's Spell Control. Imbued Items don't have/track Spell Control for their effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T13:35:39-07:00","id":1228369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228362#post1228362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distance is irrelevant to most Space spells. This means that <i>distance is irrelevant.</i> So I have to wonder, what, if anything, would keep a mage from use a high resolution photo of an extraterrestrial body to teleport to that body? I know there are environmental concerns (air, temperature, etc.), but those are secondary to my question.</div> </div> </div> </div>A photo is a <i>really bad</i> Sympathetic Connection. There <i>may</i> also be Temporal Sympathy concerns? The photo is a <i>really old</i> image of the subject, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T13:39:08-07:00","id":1228370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228362#post1228362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distance is irrelevant to most Space spells. This means that <i>distance is irrelevant.</i> So I have to wonder, what, if anything, would keep a mage from use a high resolution photo of an extraterrestrial body to teleport to that body? I know there are environmental concerns (air, temperature, etc.), but those are secondary to my question.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a photo is a great Sympathetic Yantra, it doesn't actually share Sympathy with its subject unless they've interacted in meaningful ways beyond just being a photo. But mages can definitely go explore space if they want to in other ways (either find samples of the moon or Mars and use that Sympathy, or build your own spaceship). It's just that most Mysteries are found on Earth (or in other realms) and the environmental challenges requires various levels of proficiency with several Arcana, so it requires a lot of work (meaning a lot that can go wrong) for no guaranteed payoff. And most mages reaching enough proficiency in the right Arcana to be useful on such an expedition have probably already stumbled upon a Mystery to obsess about right here on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-18-2018, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T15:37:23-07:00","id":1228398,"title":"","content":"<b>A)</b> Is there any mechanism for trading Reach for bonus spell casting Dice?<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Is there any way to reabsorb a Released spell back into Spell Control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T17:21:47-07:00","id":1228419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228369#post1228369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A photo is a <i>really bad</i> Sympathetic Connection. There <i>may</i> also be Temporal Sympathy concerns? The photo is a <i>really old</i> image of the subject, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if your idea of &quot;really old&quot; is extremely strict. The furthest object in the Solar System of which we have images is the Pluto-Charon system; those images were only about six or seven hours old when they arrived, and now they're only five years out of date. Mars is vastly closer in temporal terms, to the point NASA has had livestreams from Mars' surface. I can find hi-res video from last year, or get a recent photo (recent as in &quot;about two hours ago&quot;) online. And according to page 122, a recent photo counts as &quot;Material sympathy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T17:22:26-07:00","id":1228420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228398#post1228398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A)</b> Is there any mechanism for trading Reach for bonus spell casting Dice?<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Is there any way to reabsorb a Released spell back into Spell Control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T17:56:45-07:00","id":1228428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228419#post1228419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And according to page 122, a recent photo counts as &quot;Material sympathy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A sympathetic Yantra is not a sympathetic connection. The literal map is not the literal territory and has no inherent mystical link to it just for being a high-res representation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T18:04:03-07:00","id":1228431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228398#post1228398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A)</b> Is there any mechanism for trading Reach for bonus spell casting Dice?<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Is there any way to reabsorb a Released spell back into Spell Control?</div> </div> </div> </div>For now, no to both questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T18:37:31-07:00","id":1228443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228419#post1228419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if your idea of &amp;quot;really old&amp;quot; is extremely strict. The furthest object in the Solar System of which we have images is the Pluto-Charon system; those images were only about six or seven hours old when they arrived, and now they're only five years out of date. Mars is vastly closer in temporal terms, to the point NASA has had livestreams from Mars' surface. I can find hi-res video from last year, or get a recent photo (recent as in &amp;quot;about two hours ago&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> online. And according to page 122, a recent photo counts as &amp;quot;Material sympathy.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, intra-solar? I was thinking distant stars. Some of which might already be dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T19:53:27-07:00","id":1228471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228443#post1228443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, intra-solar? I was thinking distant stars. Some of which might already be dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be be decidedly challenging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T20:02:53-07:00","id":1228480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228428#post1228428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sympathetic Yantra is not a sympathetic connection. The literal map is not the literal territory and has no inherent mystical link to it just for being a high-res representation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the rules as presented, Co-Location has no Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 06-18-2018, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T20:20:00-07:00","id":1228484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228480#post1228480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the rules as presented, the Withstand would be 3. Challenging, yes, but opening a portal to another planet (or the space near another planet) ought to be challenging. I have no difficulty with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is though, sympathetic Yantra =/ sympathetic connections. For sympathetic spells, you need both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T20:28:48-07:00","id":1228487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228480#post1228480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the rules as presented, Co-Location has no Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the rules as presented, Co-Location <i>needs Sympathetic Range to affect distant locations.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T21:32:42-07:00","id":1228496,"title":"","content":"Yes. And that in turn requires a Sympathetic Yantra, such as a recent photograph. A recent photograph is a valid Yantra, you yourself admit that. So, casting at Sympathetic Range with Sympathetic Yantra is not enough ho actually perform Co-Location. You must *also* have a Sympathetic Connection, and according to you, this is not possible.<br /> <br /> Casting a spell on a target location is the only listed example of a connection between a mage and anything which is not a prized and irreplaceable possession, which renders Sympathy all but useless for basically any purpose. Simply going across town with Space requires physically going across town, choosing your destination, casting a spell on it to get a connection, going back, then casting the Space spell, probably before the spell you cast to create a connection fades. It's literally easier to go to the Moon than to the mall, because you can see the Moon, in great detail with a decent home telescope, on almost any night (and quite a few days) not completely overcast, and so it's a Sensory Range target. Is this actually how you want Sympathy to work? Because that's the logical consequence of your position: Sympathetic casting goes from reasonably useful to extremely niche, bordering on useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T21:54:43-07:00","id":1228500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228496#post1228496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You must *also* have a Sympathetic Connection, and according to you, this is not possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from <i>a photograph</i>, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because that's the logical consequence of your position: Sympathetic casting goes from reasonably useful to extremely niche, bordering on useless. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The logical consequence of my position&quot; is that mages who want to make use of sympathetic connections develop them themselves, acquire access to things and people that have those connections to borrow them, or otherwise maneuver themselves to be able to exploit the physical shortcuts available through mystical proximity.<br /> <br /> Miss me with this &quot;Sympathetic casting is borderline useless if I can't use a postcard as a doorway to Paris on its own&quot; line of argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T22:25:39-07:00","id":1228503,"title":"","content":"So, sympathetic casting on one's opponents is now largely pointless. To cast a spell on an opponent by sympathy, you need to commit burglary or kidnapping or both, which against any worthwhile opponent would be in all likelihood vastly more difficult that normal spying, then you can actually cast the spell with the family member or body sample or prized possession. So why do it? Under what circumstances is sympathetic range of greater utility that sensory, given that sensory range is vastly easier to arrange?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T22:48:47-07:00","id":1228504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228503#post1228503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, sympathetic casting on one's opponents is now largely pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic casting exists for more than long-distant wizard-sniping against &quot;opponents,&quot; but yeah, it's generally not the best idea to jump to sympathetic shenanigans to mess with another mage if you aren't in it for the long haul or aiming for a decisive blow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To cast a spell on an opponent by sympathy, you need to commit burglary or kidnapping or both, which against any worthwhile opponent would be in all likelihood vastly more difficult that normal spying, then you can actually cast the spell with the family member or body sample or prized possession. So why do it? </div> </div> </div>Is this a joke or have you forgotten both how mages tend to operate <i>and</i> what having enough competence in Space to manage sympathetic casting entails?<br /> <br /> This is the stuff of at least a little detective work for anyone you're not already intimately familiar with, borrowing a connection is the work of a single extra spell, and if your goal is just being able to target the spell at all then a drawing of the subject is all you need. This is a big part of why mages do the whole &quot;secrecy&quot; thing and keep up Shadow Names and Sancta and have societies whose common rules tend to include some variation on &quot;don't fuck around on other mages' turf.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Under what circumstances is sympathetic range of greater utility that sensory, given that sensory range is vastly easier to arrange? </div> </div> </div>Sensory range doesn't have a terminate clause built into using it on a target in case they notice something's up. Sensory range can't help you get at a mage who's gone to ground in an unfamiliar neck of the woods. Sensory range doesn't save you a Reach to affect a target that's even as close as several rooms away.<br /> <br /> Sensory range requires your presence in a way that sympathetic range does not and this matters to the process of affecting distant targets because &quot;distance is a lie&quot; doesn't mean shit for your ability to navigate the world in which the Lie operates beyond your immediate perspective, your personal shortcuts, and any loose threads you can get your hands on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-19-2018, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T01:49:55-07:00","id":1228530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228503#post1228503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [...] given that sensory range is vastly easier to arrange?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is simply a very wrong statement. In quite a lot of times it will be far easier to aquire something or someone with a sympathatic connection to your target, that to actually find your target. But yes in the case that your target is right in front of you, sympathetic casting is largely useless. Working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T02:32:46-07:00","id":1228535,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a>: Look at the spell Borrow Threads. That's how you get a Sympathetic Connection to your intended subject without even needing to see the intended subject in the first place because you can cast Borrow Threads on something or someone who themselves has a Sympathetic Connection with the intended subject.<br /> Casting at Sympathetic Range is useful when you must have distance between yourself and your subject for whatever reason (such as not being able to find the subject), and it's not possible to cast a spell with a longer duration on beforehand. A good use for someone who might get into a fight would be to use another Space spell to gain Sympathy with a location otherwise unrelated to you, and cast Co-Location with Sympathetic Range on that location to get an escape route with no ties to you when you cancel the spells. Casting Sympathetically is definitely not common, but it really has its uses at times. As a Lesser Utility Attainment it's not supposed to replace Sensory Range. It's supposed to complement Sensory Range, and I think it does a good job at that.<br /> <br /> As for casting with Sensory Range to the moon, it's generally assumed you need to be able to distinguish the area you're targetting which is not the case with most telescopes.<br /> &quot;Live&quot; feeds of other celestial bodies also come with a time delay that might prohibit casting at Remote Range. The moon is close enough, but there's a distinct lack of video cameras there right now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>: You don't save a Reach because you need to increase range to Sensory in order to apply Sympathetic Range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Apparently the mobile version of the site doesn't allow the use of @name to bring attention to the post. I'm sorry if you've already read my post and it shows up in your notifications again. Not sure 06-19-2018, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:11:34-07:00","id":1228555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228535#post1228535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>: You don't save a Reach because you need to increase range to Sensory in order to apply Sympathetic Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you need another Reach to do remote casting on a target you can't directly sense without Sympathetic Range. That was what &quot;several rooms away&quot; was about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:46:30-07:00","id":1228568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228535#post1228535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[A good use for someone who might get into a fight would be to use another Space spell to gain Sympathy with a location otherwise unrelated to you</div> </div> </div> </div>How does one establish a link to a location? Asking seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:50:34-07:00","id":1228569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228568#post1228568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one establish a link to a location? Asking seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the example Medium connections and then take a look at the first couple paragraphs of page 90, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:54:21-07:00","id":1228570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228568#post1228568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one establish a link to a location? Asking seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>You cast Web-Weaver on something you touch at that moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T09:18:03-07:00","id":1228600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228568#post1228568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one establish a link to a location? Asking seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>The slow way of building Sympathy is always a physical connection. Be there. Visit the place to the point where you've built up a sense of belonging, like a home or a personal work space. You could probably get Weak sympathy by carrying out emotionally significant actions there, like proposing to your partner. Such a connection would fade faster.<br /> <br /> The fast way to do it is with spells. There are three spells that can grant you sympathy to place (or an object or a person; works just as well):<br /> Borrow Threads (Space 2) to borrow another person's or object's sympathy with the place. Correspondence (Space 1) can be used to figure out who to cast Borrow Threads on.<br /> Web-Weaver (Space 3) can be used to step up the marginal sympathy of standing in the location to a Weak connection.<br /> Create Sympathy (Space 5) can straight up create a sympathetic connection between two subjects.<br /> You could also just cast any spell that has the location as a subject (probably through AoE due to Size limitations) since any subject under a spell has a Weak connection to the mage who cast the spell.<br /> <br /> For Sympathetic Yantra you could just take a photo of the location with your phone. That's why my Mastigos did in preparation of freeing Sleepwalker prisoners in the cellar of a Seer Pylon's headquarters. He cast Co-Location and moved the prisoners and the other Cabal mates in one part of the building to the designated escape spot while the priest themed Obrimos of the Cabal was stalling for time by literally preaching towards the two highly shocked Seers about trying to steal away the Sleepwalkers that were under our protection. We also got away with a Grimoire that wasn't ours, but who's keeping count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T21:17:58-07:00","id":1230737,"title":"","content":"The chicago book had an example of the tribune tower with its collection of building parts. Mages in 2e would be able to borrow sympathy from those parts to cast sympathic spells. Borrow a link from the part of Giza and you could teleport to the pyramids or many other places from borrowed sympathy links.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-28-2018, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:11:25-07:00","id":1230805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1228503#post1228503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To cast a spell on an opponent by sympathy, you need to commit burglary or kidnapping or both</div> </div> </div> </div>No. This is what Borrow Threads, Web-Weaver, and Correspondence are for. Literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:57:54-07:00","id":1231172,"title":"","content":"I only wanted to say that while a &quot;Symphaty yantra&quot; doesn't always have a symphathetic connection to what it represents, it might have on. A blood sample will propably have symphaty to the donor for instance. So having an appropriate yantra might also mean having a proper target for Borrow Threads and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T08:15:28-07:00","id":1231362,"title":"","content":"If I'm innured to a spell what does that mean?<br /> <br /> The book says &quot;any future<br /> uses will not incur Wisdom loss no matter the action. &quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that if I use psychic domination to have a person commit murder it is<br /> 1. Giving them a breaking point<br /> 2. Obvious magic on sleeper<br /> 3. Murder<br /> <br /> Which are all acts of hybris. Is all that wiped away?<br /> <br /> But murder using physic reformatting to make someone want to murder is still an act of hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23764-bomaz","name":"Bomaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T08:21:26-07:00","id":1231364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1231362#post1231362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm innured to a spell what does that mean?<br /> <br /> The book says &quot;any future<br /> uses will not incur Wisdom loss no matter the action. &quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that if I use psychic domination to have a person commit murder it is<br /> 1. Giving them a breaking point<br /> 2. Obvious magic on sleeper<br /> 3. Murder<br /> <br /> Which are all acts of hybris. Is all that wiped away?<br /> <br /> But murder using physic reformatting to make someone want to murder is still an act of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If Psychic Domination is Innuered, no use of that spell will be an Act of Hybris, no matter what you do with that spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T08:44:07-07:00","id":1231375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bomaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1231362#post1231362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which are all acts of hybris. Is all that wiped away?<br /> <br /> But murder using physic reformatting to make someone want to murder is still an act of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"523\" data-vbnamecard=\"523\">Poseur</a> said. The specific spell that incurred Wisdom loss can be inured and will no longer be a Wisdom risk to use no matter how you use it. However, it will always risk Paradox, and if you use a different spell that effectively does the same thing like in your example there it's still an Act of Hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T18:02:28-07:00","id":1232003,"title":"","content":"Craftsman's Eye allows the mage to use the studied object, including gaining the 8-Again quality on rolls to do so. But what's the base pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T18:09:16-07:00","id":1232005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232003#post1232003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craftsman's Eye allows the mage to use the studied object, including gaining the 8-Again quality on rolls to do so. But what's the base pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>The base pool depends on the appropriate attribute plus skill for using the tool, plus whatever equipment bonus the tool provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T18:20:04-07:00","id":1232008,"title":"","content":"Depends on what the object is used for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T19:59:22-07:00","id":1232030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232005#post1232005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The base pool depends on the appropriate attribute plus skill for using the tool, plus whatever equipment bonus the tool provides.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the spell allows the use of the object at zero skill (meaning no untrained penalty)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T20:19:01-07:00","id":1232031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232030#post1232030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the spell allows the use of the object at zero skill (meaning no untrained penalty)?</div> </div> </div> </div>...no. Its effects are clearly listed, and that isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> It gives 8-Again and, if the object has a non-obvious purpose or means of use (like the examples listed - a safe, puzzle box, etc) it reveals the information required for use. If it's broken, or otherwise obstructed from use, the spell reveals how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T20:19:35-07:00","id":1232032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232030#post1232030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the spell allows the use of the object at zero skill (meaning no untrained penalty)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell applies the 8-Again quality to rolls using the tool in question. That is all it does. Negating the unSkilled penalty is a different effect entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:16:34-07:00","id":1232130,"title":"","content":"What are perfected materials and how does one get them? The core mentions them several times but offers no explanation, beyond their being closer to supernal ideals, or spells to get or create said perfection. Is this something 1e explained more clearly in a book you can point me at? Does perfected iron hurt Fae, given normally conjured iron would not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:18:56-07:00","id":1232131,"title":"","content":"Talked about in this Blog post: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfect...n-development/</a><br /> <br /> The upcoming Signs of Sorcery book has a whole section on perfected materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:25:02-07:00","id":1232133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232130#post1232130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does perfected iron hurt Fae, given normally conjured iron would not?</div> </div> </div> </div>ElvesofZion provided the complete text we have so far, but to address this, specifically: yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T15:51:16-07:00","id":1232494,"title":"","content":"This might be a question better suited to Demon, but...<br /> How would you handle the interaction a Demon using Cover to Spoof a Mage's 'Pierce Deception'?<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills as normal for PD, or should the Spoofing win outright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T16:28:44-07:00","id":1232500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232494#post1232494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a question better suited to Demon, but...<br /> How would you handle the interaction a Demon using Cover to Spoof a Mage's 'Pierce Deception'?<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills as normal for PD, or should the Spoofing win outright?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoof's mechanical tradeoff is that it's an unresisted and uncontested straight roll of no more than ten dice to beat individual effects for a scene if you don't swing an exceptional success. Dice math being what it is, I'd lean in favor of having a successful spoof be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T16:41:49-07:00","id":1232503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232494#post1232494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a question better suited to Demon, but...<br /> How would you handle the interaction a Demon using Cover to Spoof a Mage's 'Pierce Deception'?<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills as normal for PD, or should the Spoofing win outright?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoofing does exactly what spoofing says it does. A successful roll will make the demon register as their Cover rather than as a demon. This explicitly includes supernatural powers of revelation, and there is no reason for Pierce Deception to be an exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T16:49:34-07:00","id":1232505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232494#post1232494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a question better suited to Demon, but...<br /> How would you handle the interaction a Demon using Cover to Spoof a Mage's 'Pierce Deception'?<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills as normal for PD, or should the Spoofing win outright?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, the wording on Spoof indicates that it supersedes the Clash of Wills roll. If the Spoof roll failed and the Demon had an additional supernatural ability masking it, then there would be a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <s>What's also important to note is that Spoof would only stop the Mage from knowing that the Demon wasn't a normal Mortal, Spoof would have no effect on <i>Pierce Deception</i>'s ability to see through mundane lies.</s> This is stopped by Liar's Tongue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-04-2018, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T17:09:47-07:00","id":1232508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232505#post1232505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's also important to note is that Spoof would only stop the Mage from knowing that the Demon wasn't a normal Mortal, Spoof would have no effect on <i>Pierce Deception</i>'s ability to see through mundane lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume Liar's Tongue would cover this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T17:17:10-07:00","id":1232511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232508#post1232508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume Liar's Tongue would cover this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I had forgotten about that ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T14:38:59-07:00","id":1232707,"title":"","content":"When putting a spell together, do you know how much Withstand the target has, or do you have to guess and hope your chosen Potency is good enough to affect them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T14:42:47-07:00","id":1232708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232707#post1232707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When putting a spell together, do you know how much Withstand the target has, or do you have to guess and hope your chosen Potency is good enough to affect them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T15:10:50-07:00","id":1232720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232707#post1232707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When putting a spell together, do you know how much Withstand the target has, or do you have to guess and hope your chosen Potency is good enough to affect them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s the latter as was said, however if you were smart you would have previously cast a Knowing spell to determine what the Withstand was before just guessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T16:24:02-07:00","id":1232739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232720#post1232720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s the latter as was said, however if you were smart you would have previously cast a Knowing spell to determine what the Withstand was before just guessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing so however, if recognized, might be equivalent to pointed a gun at someone (or at least showing it). Sure, the &quot;quick draw&quot; can go wrong, but scanning someone's Withstand beforehand can give away the surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T18:04:40-07:00","id":1232762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232739#post1232739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing so however, if recognized, might be equivalent to pointed a gun at someone (or at least showing it). Sure, the &amp;quot;quick draw&amp;quot; can go wrong, but scanning someone's Withstand beforehand can give away the surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why if you were smart you would have taken steps to avoid being detected and have a quick getaway set up in the event of being noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T19:00:45-07:00","id":1232770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232762#post1232762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence why if you were smart you would have taken steps to avoid being detected and have a quick getaway set up in the event of being noticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking about the hypothetical attacker or defender here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T21:04:40-07:00","id":1232794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232770#post1232770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking about the hypothetical attacker or defender here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T12:37:19-07:00","id":1232907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1190387#post1190387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first ed Claimed was a major template and those couldn't stack. The fluff explanation was that while humans were like soft clay ready to be molded, major templates (Werewolf, Vampire, Mage) were like finished pottery out of the oven, they could not be shaped again, only broken.<br /> <br /> EDIT : of course that's no longer the case as template stacking is not flat out prohibited and Claimed is a Condition anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah woah I am way behind it seems! Other than archmages and even then I thought people were against it... since when was template stacking tolerated/allowed? Whats the sources on this?<br /> <br /> Sorry for quoting an old post but this is very valuable to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T13:01:19-07:00","id":1232913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232907#post1232907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah woah I am way behind it seems! Other than archmages and even then I thought people were against it... since when was template stacking tolerated/allowed? Whats the sources on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's apparently not been as big a deal as people have made it out to be. Like, there's clearly people who have wanted to do it, and haven't let posters who didn't like Sam Haight rule how they were going to have fun. But it's like Thorbes said, it's just a matter of seeing Claimed being a Condition now. Wolf-Blooded, too, are handled with Tells in second edition, rather than their own template, and you keep the Tells if you turn into something else. It's not a big thing, we still do have templates and some of them can't be overlapped, Hurt Locker outright says not to let the 'micro templates' be used by supernatural characters.<br /> <br /> Rose expanded on her outlook on templates as a developer, when some people were talking about the perceived importance of templates, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/208267-lesser-greater-templates-what-does-it-even-mean-what-can-stack-what-can-t?p=208448#post208448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the extent that it's something we use internally, it was originally intended to clean up crossover, by not allowing mages to be ghouled. And there's definitely a general principle that a lot of supernatural powers can't be combined. But greater and lesser templates have never really been a major design principle. Mostly, it's all just templates (or, as we usually call them, character types), and most of them can't be combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T13:45:39-07:00","id":1232921,"title":"","content":"Okay so stacking *is* prohibited then. Short of archmastery its not doable.<br /> <br /> So mages cannot be ghouled? Thats a damper... unless they can still become obsessed with a vampire? I like my options open on how an Elder can achieve control over mages to keep interesting stories open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T13:58:06-07:00","id":1232926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232921#post1232921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so stacking *is* prohibited then. Short of archmastery its not doable.<br /> <br /> So mages cannot be ghouled? Thats a damper... unless they can still become obsessed with a vampire? I like my options open on how an Elder can achieve control over mages to keep interesting stories open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every supernatural can be blood bonded, but not ghouled. Obviously some have workarounds like some mages and werewolves being able to cure it, or Demons being able to become someone who isn't blood bonded. Dhampir did get a second edition makeover (in Half-Damned) and they're less inherently antagonistic to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-06-2018, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T14:21:12-07:00","id":1232930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1232907#post1232907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Woah woah I am way behind it seems! Other than archmages and even then I thought people were against it... since when was template stacking tolerated/allowed? Whats the sources on this?<br /> <br /> Sorry for quoting an old post but this is very valuable to me</div> </div> </div> </div>The source is that there is no explicit rule against template stacking in most cases, but all major templates are still intended to be unstackable afaik. Mostly it's just minor templates that can be stacked, such as Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Edit: Turns out this was an old tab I had opened almost two hours ago, so I'm a bit late to the party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T23:59:01-07:00","id":1233005,"title":"","content":"How do you determine the strength of a Paradox Condition when paradox is released? Is it just how many successes were rolled by the paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T00:15:49-07:00","id":1233006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233005#post1233005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you determine the strength of a Paradox Condition when paradox is released? Is it just how many successes were rolled by the paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not generate a Paradox Condition when a Paradox is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T00:26:43-07:00","id":1233007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233006#post1233006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do not generate a Paradox Condition when a Paradox is released.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The paradox reach options allow you put a Condition on the subject of the spell.<br /> I assumed it would be a Paradox Condition, though I may be mistaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T00:41:42-07:00","id":1233009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233007#post1233007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The paradox reach options allow you put a Condition on the subject of the spell.<br /> I assumed it would be a Paradox Condition, though I may be mistaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t say it\u2019s a Paradox Condition, just a Condition. You could use a Paradox Condition I suppose, but I wouldn\u2019t unless it was being inflicted by a Scelesti or was good for the story. Most subjects of a Mage\u2019s spell won\u2019t be able to resolve a Paradox Condition, or be adversely affected by it being there or allowing it to lapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T00:46:40-07:00","id":1233011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233007#post1233007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The paradox reach options allow you put a Condition on the subject of the spell.<br /> I assumed it would be a Paradox Condition, though I may be mistaken?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The likely intent is any suitable Condition, as long as it represents how badly the Paradox'ed spell is screwing around with the subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:18:13-07:00","id":1233263,"title":"","content":"Would a spell to manipulate currents and waves be Matter (as with Shaping) or Forces (as with Control Weather)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T15:44:26-07:00","id":1233295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233263#post1233263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a spell to manipulate currents and waves be Matter (as with Shaping) or Forces (as with Control Weather)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either could work. Matter would just move the water itself, Forces would manipulate Gravity, which would move the water (and everything else) as it does. Time might even be able to adjust the &quot;now&quot; to high or low tide (though not much else).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T22:11:12-07:00","id":1233904,"title":"","content":"Can you stick a ghost in a Soul Jar? <br /> <br /> My first instinct would be &quot;no&quot;, because 1. ghosts aren't actually souls, 2. what's to keep a mage with only Death 2 from ending all ghost fights in one Clash of Wills -- Command Ghost, &quot;get your dead ass in this here jar?&quot; <br /> <br /> But the Gaolers of Ialdabaoth in Grimoire of Grimoires are explicitly called out as using their first attainment to prepare a vessel to bind a ghost or spirit &quot;as through the use of a 'Soul Jar' spell&quot;, implying that you *can* trap a ghost in a Soul Jar.<br /> <br /> (That, and if Soul Jar isn't the spell for trapping a ghost or spirit so it won't cause any trouble, what *is*? Bind Spirit and Transfer Anchor let you trap an entity in a given place, but they're still free to make trouble as much as their new lodging allows, you can't just stick then in a box and have done. Create Fetish is overkill -- I'm just looking for a way to *trap* ghosts and spirits in convenient objects, not gain access to their Numina.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7058-kerredai","name":"Kerredai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T22:44:28-07:00","id":1233906,"title":"","content":"Strictly, Soul Jar can't trap a ghost. However, a &quot;Trap Ghost&quot; spell would, in all likelihood, be mechanically identical to Soul Jar. And yes, this means that a mage can end a ghost fight with a Clash of Wills. I do not see a problem with this; I loathe the idea that it's somehow fundamentally wrong for a magician to be able to solve a problem with magic, especially if it's a problem that in fiction and folklore is best solved with magic. For a specific example, banishing spells in Exalted are supposed to be off-limits because they &quot;limit the story potential of demons,&quot; which results in the world's greatest experts on demonology, masters of all magics, who wield the powers of the unknown, the unseen, the occult and the ghostly, having exactly no options for dealing with demons that anybody else can't employ, and probably better. If you want to create an effective demon hunter in that game, the list of useful abilities doesn't even include Occult. I wish I were joking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T23:16:15-07:00","id":1233910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerredai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233904#post1233904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you stick a ghost in a Soul Jar?<br /> <br /> My first instinct would be &quot;no&quot;, because 1. ghosts aren't actually souls, 2. what's to keep a mage with only Death 2 from ending all ghost fights in one Clash of Wills -- Command Ghost, &quot;get your dead ass in this here jar?&quot;<br /> <br /> But the Gaolers of Ialdabaoth in Grimoire of Grimoires are explicitly called out as using their first attainment to prepare a vessel to bind a ghost or spirit &quot;as through the use of a 'Soul Jar' spell&quot;, implying that you *can* trap a ghost in a Soul Jar.<br /> <br /> (That, and if Soul Jar isn't the spell for trapping a ghost or spirit so it won't cause any trouble, what *is*? Bind Spirit and Transfer Anchor let you trap an entity in a given place, but they're still free to make trouble as much as their new lodging allows, you can't just stick then in a box and have done. Create Fetish is overkill -- I'm just looking for a way to *trap* ghosts and spirits in convenient objects, not gain access to their Numina.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaolers of Ialdabaoth is 1e, and so in 2e, no Soul Jar isn't sufficient to trap a ghost. You could use Command Ghost to tell a ghost to get into a jar, but it would suffer Essence bleed if you moved it too far from its Anchor. Your best solution with just Command Ghost to trap a ghost it to simply command it to stay where it is, and to not use its powers.<br /> <br /> Gaolers of Ialdabaoth in 2e, may have a unique attainment that allows them to bottle ghosts, but it's going to have to be at least their 2nd attainment, and to justify that level of power will probably have to have restrictions that justify it being able to work.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a> said there's nothing wrong with a Mage winning a fight simply by winning a CoW. Speaking from personal experience too, you are not guaranteed to win in a CoW. I rolled off against a goetia that had one die less than me and sure, they got lucky, but they tore right through my defense which was enough for a K.O.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T02:05:29-07:00","id":1233928,"title":"","content":"It's very easy to bottle a ghost - you use Death to force them into the Fetter Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T08:03:04-07:00","id":1233999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233928#post1233928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very easy to bottle a ghost - you use Death to force them into the Fetter Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the same as trapping it inside the bottle, though. The ghost will still be free to exit the bottle and otherwise act freely in Twilight so long as it stays within 5 yards of the bottle.<br /> <br /> The Gaolers' first attainment is already not clear on its own mechanics. It could be read as to imply that the trapped beings are dormant while within, but that's far from explicit. Maybe the attainment's effect can be reproduced by a +1 (+2?) Reach ability on the regular Soul Jar spell? Or would it be better to have it be a totally different spell instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T08:48:58-07:00","id":1234015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233999#post1233999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the same as trapping it inside the bottle, though. The ghost will still be free to exit the bottle and otherwise act freely in Twilight so long as it stays within 5 yards of the bottle.<br /> <br /> The Gaolers' first attainment is already not clear on its own mechanics. It could be read as to imply that the trapped beings are dormant while within, but that's far from explicit. Maybe the attainment's effect can be reproduced by a +1 (+2?) Reach ability on the regular Soul Jar spell? Or would it be better to have it be a totally different spell instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave is pretty much right though, one, the entity has a very limited amount of freedom of movement, and two the entity isn't allowed to use any of its powers except on the Fetter which is probably the bigger concern. The real problem is that not every ghost is going to have the Fetter Manifestation, and for those exceptions you'd need to rewrite them with Death 4.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow Soul Jar to capture ghosts though, souls and ghosts are explicitly different so a spell designed to affect one probably shouldn't be able to affect the other. In fact, Soul Jar only works because souls are supposed to be inside a container in the first place and the magic is being used to confuse that naturally occurring mechanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T09:03:07-07:00","id":1234020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234015#post1234015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real problem is that not every ghost is going to have the Fetter Manifestation, and for those exceptions you'd need to rewrite them with Death 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you even activate an ephemeral entity's own Manifestations? The normal way of making ephemeral entities Manifest through spells is by applying Manifestation Conditions on them regardless of what Manifestations they have access to. For this specific example it would be the Revenant spell, with 3 Potency to apply Anchor and Open on the intended &quot;ghost jar&quot; and Fettered on the ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T09:06:03-07:00","id":1234021,"title":"","content":"Forgot Fettered entities can only use Influences and Numina on their Fetter. The point still stands, though: they're not &quot;trapped&quot; inside the Fetter.<br /> <br /> On another note, I can't find the FAQ sheet with the answers to all the questions in the 2e FAQ thread. I'm specifically trying to find out why the Ghost/Goetia/Spirit Summons spells are 3-dot effects, and this is supposedly answered there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T09:54:11-07:00","id":1234032,"title":"","content":"I don't think there has ever been a completed FAQ sheet. Dave isn't getting paid to do it, and is also busy with other projects he is getting paid for. So priorities.<br /> <br /> My guess though is that it's because the spell can accomplish things with one spell that you would otherwise require multiple 2 dot spells for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T10:00:30-07:00","id":1234033,"title":"","content":"At the point you are using Bind Ghost you can also strip away Numina (and Attributes). Craft Fetish is also at 4 dots, and a similar 'You stay in there until I say otherwise,' can probably be done with ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-11-2018, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T12:24:27-07:00","id":1234068,"title":"","content":"Are there separate rules for identifying an active spell, or is that just a Mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8721-taralx","name":"taralx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T12:54:45-07:00","id":1234076,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that if you are watching a spell being cast you can identify what it does just by watching it with Mage sight. I don't have the book on me to look into it and verify though. If it's an active spell that is just sitting around for whatever reason, then yes it would be a Mystery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T10:53:34-07:00","id":1234330,"title":"","content":"A classic D&amp;D Spell is <i>feather fall</i>. It's pretty simple: the subject falls very slowly for the duration. Clearly this would be Forces, but would it be 1 or 2? The idea is to create a &quot;slow fall&quot; spell at the lowest dot level it can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:09:49-07:00","id":1234334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234330#post1234330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A classic D&amp;D Spell is <i>feather fall</i>. It's pretty simple: the subject falls very slowly for the duration. Clearly this would be Forces, but would it be 1 or 2? The idea is to create a &quot;slow fall&quot; spell at the lowest dot level it can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put it as Shielding, so 2 dots, as it protects you from the deleterious effects of gravity.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Shielding, Here is the purview of Fate: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blessings, hexes, probability, fortune, oaths, promises, intentions, destiny. </div> </div> </div> Does anyone have any interesting ideas for Shielding against these and how it would work out in their games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T17:16:43-07:00","id":1234453,"title":"","content":"My Mage casts Invisibility, or some sort of Live Veiling effect on herself.<br /> Can she see herself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T17:45:26-07:00","id":1234463,"title":"","content":"If it's a mental invisibility, or some other effect on others, then yes. If she's created a cloaking field, Star Trek style, I'd say no. Indeed, she'd be blind without using some other means to see (night vision spell or gear, for the most obvious example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T19:44:55-07:00","id":1234497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234463#post1234463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a mental invisibility, or some other effect on others, then yes. If she's created a cloaking field, Star Trek style, I'd say no. Indeed, she'd be blind without using some other means to see (night vision spell or gear, for the most obvious example).</div> </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t run the risk of being blinded by your own spells unless it\u2019s specifically mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234453#post1234453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Mage casts Invisibility, or some sort of Live Veiling effect on herself.<br /> Can she see herself?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say no, but if she really has to she can flip on her Mage Sight, beat herself in a CoW, and then be able to see herself as her Mage Sight pierces the Veiling effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:08:55-07:00","id":1234570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234334#post1234334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Shielding, Here is the purview of Fate: Does anyone have any interesting ideas for Shielding against these and how it would work out in their games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Shielding from Oaths would prevent any Oath-based magic from forming. Same for Blessings/Hexes. For probability/fortune, I'd treat it like Shield of Chronos and block perception of the character's fate or choices - they become unpredictable, a wild card in destiny's game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T04:52:13-07:00","id":1234588,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Dulling the Spindle (Fate \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> This shield provokes a Clash of Wills against any supernaturally binding oaths, attempts to change the subjects Destiny, any Fate spells, and other fate-related supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Knock on Wood (Fate \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Stealth, Subterfuge, Survival<br /> This spell makes the subject immune to mundane accidents. She won't slip and fall in the stairs, or pull out right in front of the car she didn't see. Attempts to avoid traps or crossing dangerous terrain gains the spell's Potency as bonus dice, as fate draws her eyes to the faint glimmer of the tripwire or places her foot on the most stable rock.<br /> Direct attacks and supernatural powers are not affected by this spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject gains the Charmed Condition for the duration of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:48:01-07:00","id":1234703,"title":"","content":"That second spell is exceptionally good <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:00:58-07:00","id":1234729,"title":"","content":"This is gonna be controversial but is the whole fluff of the Hegemonic Ministry dying kinda of wrong seeing the rise of nationalism and xenophobia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:31:56-07:00","id":1234741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234729#post1234729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is gonna be controversial but is the whole fluff of the Hegemonic Ministry dying kinda of wrong seeing the rise of nationalism and xenophobia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a conflict of global (cosmic) proportions on which of the ministries are the hegemonic (no pun) ones. The rise and fall of a progenitor ministry could take centuries. Global mercantilism, trade and the idea of globalisation and the capitalist system has had hundreds of years in the making, but it is still not enough to topple the Hegemonic ministry. The rise of nationalism once again seen in the world is probably a strong kick back from the Hegemonic ministry to defend it's position as progenitor.<br /> <br /> But no, it probably ain't true that it's wrong. Nationalism is still trending down compared to earlier, and the believes in the global market and capitalism is surely on the rise still. However, if the current political climate is more then a hic-up in our western democracies is impossible to say for sure, I hope it's just a hic-up but I might be completely wrong. But from an In-game perspective once again, it's clear it's an ongoing war of tyranny of whom's gonna be top dog over whom in the Iron Pyramid.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of the progenitors, it's fairly interesting to see whom has been strong before in history and whom is weaker now etc. The General might have had power for the longest, but is surely weaker today then before. And the Father surely is still strong, but not as before.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 07-13-2018, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:36:52-07:00","id":1234743,"title":"","content":"in the western world , go to say Afghanistan and those two whould have way more influence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:38:54-07:00","id":1234744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234741#post1234741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's a conflict of global (cosmic) proportions on which of the ministries are the hegemonic (no pun) ones. The rise and fall of a progenitor ministry could take centuries. Global mercantilism, trade and the idea of globalisation and the capitalist system has had hundreds of years in the making, but it is still not enough to topple the Hegemonic ministry. The rise of nationalism once again seen in the world is probably a strong kick back from the Hegemonic ministry to defend it's position as progenitor.<br /> <br /> But no, it probably ain't true that it's wrong. Nationalism is still trending down compared to earlier, and the believes in the global market and capitalism is surely on the rise still. However, if the current political climate is more then a hic-up in our western democracies is impossible to say for sure, I hope it's just a hic-up but I might be completely wrong. But from an In-game perspective once again, it's clear it's an ongoing war of tyranny of whom's gonna be top dog over whom in the Iron Pyramid.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of the progenitors, it's fairly interesting to see whom has been strong before in history and whom is weaker now etc. The General might have had power for the longest, but is surely weaker today then before. And the Father surely is still strong, but not as before.</div> </div> </div> </div>. Yeah some people have the unflinching belief that Lord Mammon can solve all our problems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:07:34-07:00","id":1234755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234744#post1234744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> in the western world , go to say Afghanistan and those two whould have way more influence<br /> <br /> Yeah some people have the unflinching belief that Lord Mammon can solve all our problems</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, locally much stronger in some places then others for sure, but in the global position things are changing over the years. The world isn't as deadly with it's unnecessary conflicts as it used to be, and religion has not a strong grip on humanity as a whole as it had earlier, and nation states, borders and nationality and race is not as much a thing as earlier. Change takes time, and in the case of whom among the exarchs who wield the most powers, those struggles can take millennia. Or a revolution can come suddenly, like in the case of the Eye. It can't have taken many years for it to topple the previous holder of that position, whomever that was. So on the global scale, some tyranny is winning and some failing, but it takes time. Father wasn't progenitor before the High middle ages if I'm not mistaken.<br /> <br /> The exarch of matter constitutes that everything has a price, not many in the west that would argue differently about most things.The fact is, our consumption and capitalistic society is strengthening Mammon, and fast. If this is good or bad I leave to an OOC discussion not suitable here, just pointing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:20:16-07:00","id":1234758,"title":"","content":"The. Exarch\u201ds are BAD ,strengthning them is suppose To be BAD! Somethings should not be bought and sold like a new shirt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T04:03:01-07:00","id":1234906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1234729#post1234729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is gonna be controversial but is the whole fluff of the Hegemonic Ministry dying kinda of wrong seeing the rise of nationalism and xenophobia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Predicting the future is hard. Remember the Seer book was written in 2009. It was one year out from the financial crash. It fit a lot more with the times.<br /> <br /> That said, the Ministries aren't abstract entities, they're functioning organisations. It doesn't really matter how their abstract niche is doing if their organisation is doing badly. I mean Mammon are showing up very very late to the party. There's some indication that the Hegemony were the Ministry that attempted to pull in the Free Council, so they were the worst damaged by the blowback.<br /> <br /> Also, the other ministries can more or less move into Hegemony's space. Xenophobia and nationalism speak as much to Praetorian, Paternoster and Panopticon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T07:35:57-07:00","id":1234948,"title":"","content":"Yeah I mean Panopticon is probably as strong as ever , SOTT was out before the whole Snowden leak right? The probly had A Huuge party after that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T08:23:13-07:00","id":1234963,"title":"","content":"does anyone have a good source for real world arcane sigils, or flashier spells... things that would help with imagery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:48:55-07:00","id":1236547,"title":"","content":"What arcana(s) could make Aether? I'm leaning towards Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T14:09:24-07:00","id":1236553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1236547#post1236547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What arcana(s) could make Aether? I'm leaning towards Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Humans understand part of Aether as akin to the principle of entropy, but it is also a waste product from Essence of a sort, so I'd call for Forces and Spirit. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T14:34:40-07:00","id":1236562,"title":"","content":"Question(s): when crafting and using imbued items, can the action of casting a particular spell be encoded as the trigger for an imbued item? Also, can multiple imbued items have the same trigger and be triggered simultaneously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12771-revanreborn","name":"RevanReborn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T14:37:46-07:00","id":1236563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1236547#post1236547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What arcana(s) could make Aether? I'm leaning towards Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d create some sort of conversion mechanism made of Prime and Fate (Arcana associated with angels, IIRC) and use Spirit to input Essence through it, gaining Aether as output. No idea how the first part would look like, though. An enchanted engine of some sort, or even a faux occult matrix made up of people and events and actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T14:42:18-07:00","id":1236565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RevanReborn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1236562#post1236562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question(s): when crafting and using imbued items, can the action of casting a particular spell be encoded as the trigger for an imbued item? Also, can multiple imbued items have the same trigger and be triggered simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Action of spellcasting? As in, forming an Imago? Likely not since it\u2019s in your head. If some other action, then no difference from, well, just setting that action as the trigger. <br /> <br /> For triggering multiple items... I think yes? But the turn economy, so to speak, is always a concern here, so I can\u2019t say for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T07:58:58-07:00","id":1238229,"title":"","content":"So, I was rereading the portion of the book on page 93 about focused mage sight and I once again read that mages can use more than one arcana at a time if they wish when scrutinizing a mystery. As per the stated rules this lowers how many rolls a player can have their mage make before they risk spilling their nimbus into the mystery. So, I was trying to figure out the purpose of doing this and my natural conclusion was that you get to add the dice of the second arcanum to the die rolls for scrutinizing the mystery so long as the second arcanum is appropriately linked to the mystery at hand. This thus gives a reason as to why you would do it in the first place, because otherwise you would just use the most appropriate arcanum that you have the most skill in. Am I correct in thinking that that is how this works? If not, what am I missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:13:59-07:00","id":1238232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238229#post1238229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was rereading the portion of the book on page 93 about focused mage sight and I once again read that mages can use more than one arcana at a time if they wish when scrutinizing a mystery. As per the stated rules this lowers how many rolls a player can have their mage make before they risk spilling their nimbus into the mystery. So, I was trying to figure out the purpose of doing this and my natural conclusion was that you get to add the dice of the second arcanum to the die rolls for scrutinizing the mystery so long as the second arcanum is appropriately linked to the mystery at hand. This thus gives a reason as to why you would do it in the first place, because otherwise you would just use the most appropriate arcanum that you have the most skill in. Am I correct in thinking that that is how this works? If not, what am I missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's how it works. The benefit of using multiple Arcana is that specific Arcana may reveal specific Deep Information, as per the last example of the list of possible Deep Information. Using Death on a ghoul reveals more about the Vitae and Disciplines the ghoul has access to. Other Arcana would not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:53:02-07:00","id":1238245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238232#post1238232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's how it works. The benefit of using multiple Arcana is that specific Arcana may reveal specific Deep Information, as per the last example of the list of possible Deep Information. Using Death on a ghoul reveals more about the Vitae and Disciplines the ghoul has access to. Other Arcana would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting....I see. The way I've been going about it so far is that any mixed mystery allows for full revelation no matter the arcana used to scrutinize it so long as the opacity is reduced to 0. After thinking about it, I think I would keep it the way I have been doing it with the exception that mixed mysteries require the other arcana in order to unlock the ability to continue scrutinizing it as per the suggestions in the mage sight write spoilers of SoS.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, mystery x has 4 opacity and is related to both Death and Mind. The Moros player reduces the opacity to 2 with Death but has no Mind and must use Mind to finish scrutinizing mystery x after he has acquired knowledge and skill within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:33:46-07:00","id":1238302,"title":"","content":"The spell concept is pretty simple: Mage is here, destination is there. Space Knowing or Unveiling to get a path from here to there. But do you need Sympathetic Range if &quot;there&quot; isn't in line of sight? Like, you're lost downtown and your home is in a suburb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:58:19-07:00","id":1238312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238302#post1238302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell concept is pretty simple: Mage is here, destination is there. Space Knowing or Unveiling to get a path from here to there. But do you need Sympathetic Range if &amp;quot;there&amp;quot; isn't in line of sight? Like, you're lost downtown and your home is in a suburb?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what the subject of your spell is. I think in this case you would be the subject of the spell so no you wouldn\u2019t need Sympathy, and it would be Knowing, but you would need to know the place exists. It\u2019s not too dissimilar to Dial the Lucky Number in Fate 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:24:17-07:00","id":1238322,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming that most of the time, the destination will be at least approximately known to the caster. &quot;My home&quot; or &quot;the Royal Museum&quot; or &quot;that particular store whose name I can't recall.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T13:03:53-07:00","id":1238335,"title":"","content":"Going by Locate Object (I mean it basically does the same thing) here and there both need to be within the area of the spell. If they are not sympathetic connection would indeed be required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T15:11:16-07:00","id":1238382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238335#post1238335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by Locate Object (I mean it basically does the same thing) here and there both need to be within the area of the spell. If they are not sympathetic connection would indeed be required.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s to find a thing in (or out of) a place, not to find a place itself, and I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s a good idea to conflate the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T16:54:18-07:00","id":1238414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238245#post1238245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or in other words, mystery x has 4 opacity and is related to both Death and Mind. The Moros player reduces the opacity to 2 with Death but has no Mind and must use Mind to finish scrutinizing mystery x after he has acquired knowledge and skill within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additional Arcana increases Opacity by one. Maybe you should make it so that you would unlock the secrets of Death when reducing Opacity to 1, and Mind to finish it off? Otherwise an equivalent Mystery with effects relating to a single Arcanum (i.e. Opacity 3) would require reducing Opacity by three instead of two to get to the Arcanum specific information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T19:06:08-07:00","id":1238471,"title":"","content":"With <i>Changeling: the Lost 2e</i> being released (to backers), does anyone know if Mages still have their Gnosis damaged by the Hedge?<br /> <br /> I assume not as it's not mentioned anywhere and the effects of the Thorns has dramatically changed, but I don't know if DaveB or anyone else has expressed an opinion on the matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T01:36:41-07:00","id":1238531,"title":"","content":"If a Master of Life makes two humans,<br /> and those two artificial humans were made to procreate...<br /> Would the resulting child have a mind and soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T06:22:50-07:00","id":1238570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238531#post1238531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Master of Life makes two humans,<br /> and those two artificial humans were made to procreate...<br /> Would the resulting child have a mind and soul?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There\u2019s no reason it wouldn\u2019t, but it\u2019s up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T14:02:49-07:00","id":1238685,"title":"","content":"So I've been going back and forth with my players over the use of Life/Mind magic for 'overclocking' their attributes and skills (I know there are examples in the corebook but I was rather generous back when we were all still learning the system and now I'm kind of bound by precedent). I know that the arcana have more overlap by design in 2e but I still want to maintain some distinction between arcana.<br /> <br /> Currently, the compromise we have going is that they may use either Mind or Life to enhance skills, Life to enhance social/physical attributes, and Mind to enhance mental/social attributes.<br /> <br /> Should I bring the hammer down and go with exactly how the example spells work or do you folks think our compromise is reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T14:31:38-07:00","id":1238696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238685#post1238685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been going back and forth with my players over the use of Life/Mind magic for 'overclocking' their attributes and skills (I know there are examples in the corebook but I was rather generous back when we were all still learning the system and now I'm kind of bound by precedent). I know that the arcana have more overlap by design in 2e but I still want to maintain some distinction between arcana.<br /> <br /> Currently, the compromise we have going is that they may use either Mind or Life to enhance skills, Life to enhance social/physical attributes, and Mind to enhance mental/social attributes.<br /> <br /> Should I bring the hammer down and go with exactly how the example spells work or do you folks think our compromise is reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do they justify things like raising Academics or Manipulation via Life, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T17:47:30-07:00","id":1238732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1238685#post1238685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been going back and forth with my players over the use of Life/Mind magic for 'overclocking' their attributes and skills (I know there are examples in the corebook but I was rather generous back when we were all still learning the system and now I'm kind of bound by precedent). I know that the arcana have more overlap by design in 2e but I still want to maintain some distinction between arcana.<br /> <br /> Currently, the compromise we have going is that they may use either Mind or Life to enhance skills, Life to enhance social/physical attributes, and Mind to enhance mental/social attributes.<br /> <br /> Should I bring the hammer down and go with exactly how the example spells work or do you folks think our compromise is reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Skills represent <i>knowledge</i> of how to do something, I don't see a way of imparting that with Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T20:43:23-07:00","id":1238773,"title":"","content":"You could certainly impart muscle memory. But that would probably be best represented with equipment bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T15:54:42-07:00","id":1239066,"title":"","content":"So far they've never given themselves dots ex nihilo. They usually enhance whatever rating they already possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T21:00:37-07:00","id":1239184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1239066#post1239066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far they've never given themselves dots ex nihilo. They usually enhance whatever rating they already possessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just rule it on a case by case basis, like Life could make you give you dots in Stealth by fine tuning your senses to pick up on cues you're giving off that may make you easier to detect, and subtly shifting your weight so you step more quietly. Like, narratively if the magic fits then it makes sense it can probably create the mechanical benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T00:44:50-07:00","id":1239218,"title":"","content":"For attributes I don't see that much of a problem. You could for example make a life spell to emit pheromones to make you more attractive and boost presence and or manipulation with it. For skills I would also rule on a case basis. If they get a good explanation, go with it. But raising academics with life e.g. would be difficult. Also, keep in mind, that it basically makes no difference if you raise the attribute or the skill for a roll. So just raising the fitting attribute with life might in most cases be more justifiable and easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T03:35:19-07:00","id":1239243,"title":"","content":"Muscle memory is actually imparting knowledge. Those are learned reflexes based on experiences; not just instinctive reflexes like pulling away from pain, perceiving potential dangers, and dodging. At most Life could increase Physical Skills since most of them could theoretically benefit from enhanced instinctive reflexes, but I'd personally represent enhanced reflexes with bonuses, dice tricks and/or changes to Perception, Defense (specifically using the higher of Wits and Dex) and Initiative.<br /> <br /> As for pheromones, I think that should be considered an equipment bonus (applicable to social maneuvering where the other party is susceptible) instead of actually Attribute increases. Attributes should be universally applicable, while pheromones would only work against a few related species at a time (which ones decided at the casting of the spell), and only at close range. You shouldn't have to ignore Attribute dots because you're talking over the phone or using Animal Ken to calm the guard dog you're trying to pass.<br /> Similarly, using Life to become more attractive (or other appearances which could help you) would instead grant Striking Looks rather than Pre/Man.<br /> <br /> That's one way of introducing any change you make to the players while maintaining in-game consistency. &quot;We could just retroactively say it was bonuses applicable in those situations rather than actual Attribute increases.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T06:56:22-07:00","id":1239287,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, I was wondering by re-reading the spell from Mtaw 2nd edition ... what would be considered a tool for the spell crucible ( page 157) .. could a gun fit the bill? Similary, would you allow Find the balance (p155) to be used on a gun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:38:15-07:00","id":1239321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elggur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1239287#post1239287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I was wondering by re-reading the spell from Mtaw 2nd edition ... what would be considered a tool for the spell crucible ( page 157) .. could a gun fit the bill? Similary, would you allow Find the balance (p155) to be used on a gun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it made by humans? It\u2019s probably a tool, art, shelter or food. A gun is just a tool for killing. Guns rely on balance and heft and the owner\u2019s familiarity or inherent comfort with that to operate at a higher level of accuracy. So I don\u2019t see why it wouldn\u2019t be valid for both spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T08:49:33-07:00","id":1241852,"title":"","content":"How do you calculate Reach in a Combined Spell?. Do you just calculate it deifferently for each spell (e.g. A Mage with Space 5 and Spirit 3, combining Co-Location and Howl From Beyond, gets 3 Reach on the first spell and 1 on the other) or calculate with the lowest Arcanum Rating? (so in the example, both spells get one Reach each).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 08-02-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:03:46-07:00","id":1241858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elggur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1239287#post1239287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I was wondering by re-reading the spell from Mtaw 2nd edition ... what would be considered a tool for the spell crucible ( page 157) .. could a gun fit the bill? Similary, would you allow Find the balance (p155) to be used on a gun?</div> </div> </div> </div>The tool is a symbol for the spell. As long as you can justify the tool in question for the spell in question, it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T10:08:15-07:00","id":1241893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1241852#post1241852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you calculate Reach in a Combined Spell?. Do you just calculate it deifferently for each spell (e.g. A Mage with Space 5 and Spirit 3, combining Co-Location and Howl From Beyond, gets 3 Reach on the first spell and 1 on the other) or calculate with the lowest Arcanum Rating? (so in the example, both spells get one Reach each).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's unclear because all we know is that Free Reach is determined as normal. I'm inclined to think that this means that since they are two separate spells being cast as one they each have their separate Free Reach to spend on effects independently with the exception that if you spend a Reach on Factors from either spell it ends up affecting both spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T12:25:53-07:00","id":1241985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1241893#post1241893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's unclear because all we know is that Free Reach is determined as normal. I'm inclined to think that this means that since they are two separate spells being cast as one they each have their separate Free Reach to spend on effects independently with the exception that if you spend a Reach on Factors from either spell it ends up affecting both spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds preferable to the way I've been doing it, my way was a little stingier. I've been just using the worst dice pool and worst reach pool possible of the two spells--which ends up not mattering if the two spells are from the same arcanum/level. It seemed sensible to me that the &quot;reach&quot; you have is only as good as the most difficult spell you were splicing, only so much power you could channel simultaneously.<br /> <br /> Mechanically I like your method though, gives a little more freedom to make combining spells worth it, but that also makes combined rituals <i>reaaally</i> good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T16:13:30-07:00","id":1242114,"title":"","content":"What do you guys feel about a Death greater utility arcana attainment based on 'Honorary Rank'? And by based I mean a flat copy-paste. The Geist kickstarter has made me want to do more story-arcs in and around the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T17:44:09-07:00","id":1242153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1241852#post1241852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you calculate Reach in a Combined Spell?. Do you just calculate it deifferently for each spell (e.g. A Mage with Space 5 and Spirit 3, combining Co-Location and Howl From Beyond, gets 3 Reach on the first spell and 1 on the other) or calculate with the lowest Arcanum Rating? (so in the example, both spells get one Reach each).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1166296#post1166296\">Prior discussion may be helpful here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T12:27:43-07:00","id":1242451,"title":"","content":"A mage with sufficient Space has a house on a large lot. The house includes a stairway that leads to a teeny little basement room... with an Indefinite spell on it to make it an elaborate underground base. High ceilings, indoor swimming pool, all that. So, would this trigger Dissonance if a Sleeper saw it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:35:18-07:00","id":1242492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1242451#post1242451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage with sufficient Space has a house on a large lot. The house includes a stairway that leads to a teeny little basement room... with an Indefinite spell on it to make it an elaborate underground base. High ceilings, indoor swimming pool, all that. So, would this trigger Dissonance if a Sleeper saw it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose if the stairs go deep enough it may be plausible, but even then not everyone has an underground base under their house.<br /> It's underground, so you can't view it from the outside and walk in followed by an &quot;It's bigger on the inside...&quot; moment.<br /> Play it off correctly and have a long stairwell, or maybe an elevator, and then I suppose it won't trigger the sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:43:12-07:00","id":1242498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1242451#post1242451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage with sufficient Space has a house on a large lot. The house includes a stairway that leads to a teeny little basement room... with an Indefinite spell on it to make it an elaborate underground base. High ceilings, indoor swimming pool, all that. So, would this trigger Dissonance if a Sleeper saw it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11641_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11641\" data-vbnamecard=\"11641\">Yelesom</a> said. Sleepers don\u2019t automatically trigger Dissonance just by seeing the product of magic. It has to be obvious that what they\u2019re looking at could only be done via magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T05:23:58-07:00","id":1242920,"title":"","content":"Pardon if this specific question was answered before, but what exactly happens with an Unsafely Relinquished Imbued Item?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T09:23:18-07:00","id":1242962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1242920#post1242920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon if this specific question was answered before, but what exactly happens with an Unsafely Relinquished Imbued Item?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing as with s spell, eventually corruption leaks in, and thus you probably end up with a \u201ccursed\u201d item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T09:33:47-07:00","id":1242966,"title":"","content":"I forget are alternate methods to safely relinquish spells going to be in Signs of Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T12:00:48-07:00","id":1242989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1242962#post1242962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same thing as with s spell, eventually corruption leaks in, and thus you probably end up with a \u201ccursed\u201d item.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, apply the Spell Factor degradation to all future uses of the Item, then? As well as tracking individual instances of generated spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T19:11:04-07:00","id":1244017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1242989#post1242989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, apply the Spell Factor degradation to all future uses of the Item, then? As well as tracking individual instances of generated spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, it's just like all unsafely relinquished magic it's going to start slowly accumulating paradox reaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T19:33:30-07:00","id":1244024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244017#post1244017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly, it's just like all unsafely relinquished magic it's going to start slowly accumulating paradox reaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the Imbuement isn't itself a spell. So the only possible consequence for Paradox Reaches is it affecting the resulting spells as if <i>they</i> incurred Paradox, separate of whether they actually incurred Paradox upon activation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T20:37:51-07:00","id":1244039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244024#post1244024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but the Imbuement isn't itself a spell. So the only possible consequence for Paradox Reaches is it affecting the resulting spells as if <i>they</i> incurred Paradox, separate of whether they actually incurred Paradox upon activation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell you imbue is the one that would be corrrupted, so all spells subsequently cast via the item would have the same corruption as their \u201ctemplate\u201d spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T07:23:34-07:00","id":1244131,"title":"","content":"A spell/blessing/invocation for Trial by Ordeal would involve an appropriate protective spell and conditional duration, the condition being &quot;the subject makes a statement he knows to be false.&quot; So the accused would say &quot;I am not guilty,&quot; lay his handing on the hot metal plate, and Alchemist's Touch prevents burns if he's being truthful. Is this a valid construction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T07:58:47-07:00","id":1244142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244131#post1244131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell/blessing/invocation for Trial by Ordeal would involve an appropriate protective spell and conditional duration, the condition being &amp;quot;the subject makes a statement he knows to be false.&amp;quot; So the accused would say &amp;quot;I am not guilty,&amp;quot; lay his handing on the hot metal plate, and Alchemist's Touch prevents burns if he's being truthful. Is this a valid construction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could the trigger conditions for Conditional Duration \u201cread minds\u201d like that? Gut instinct says no, but I\u2019m away from the text right now so I can\u2019t check better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:11:27-07:00","id":1244149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244142#post1244142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the trigger conditions for Conditional Duration \u201cread minds\u201d like that? Gut instinct says no, but I\u2019m away from the text right now so I can\u2019t check better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate has to do with intentions so if the intent to lie was there it could probably pick up on that. On the other hand it wouldn\u2019t pick up a person attempting to be honest who unknowingly only has false info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:19:23-07:00","id":1244153,"title":"","content":"That is true, but it's very rare that a person will believe sincerely that he has committed an offence he did not. It can happen, but the person needs to be severely psychotic to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:58:25-07:00","id":1244166,"title":"","content":"If one would want to try out the Second Edition of Mage, how useful would supplements from the first edition be in terms of rules and crunch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T09:06:41-07:00","id":1244168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244153#post1244153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true, but it's very rare that a person will believe sincerely that he has committed an offence he did not. It can happen, but the person needs to be severely psychotic to start with.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's what you believe then the answer to your original question is no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T09:07:39-07:00","id":1244169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244166#post1244166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one would want to try out the Second Edition of Mage, how useful would supplements from the first edition be in terms of rules and crunch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not very useful at all, but almost all of the setting material from those same supplements are still relevant and valuable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:20:54-07:00","id":1244213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1244153#post1244153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true, but it's very rare that a person will believe sincerely that he has committed an offence he did not. It can happen, but the person needs to be severely psychotic to start with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that as you formulated it, you aren't asking if they committed a crime, you're asking if they're 'guilty'. That's probably fine for most cases like theft or what have you, but for more emotive cases like if a mage has died it may well not be enough.<br /> <br /> The fiction in the core book is a good example of the problem. The mage being questioned believes she's guilty even after the conspiracy is revealed and she's cleared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:26:52-07:00","id":1245202,"title":"","content":"Can you folks please help me remember how to correctly apply the rules for legacy attainment dice pools? I'm getting back into Mage and having to reparse these rules.<br /> <br /> I guess please just check and correct my examples; hopefully these are comprehensive.<br /> <br /> <b>Example 1: Telekinetic Strike (Forces) as a third-tier attainment requiring Forces 3</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assume the casting mage has Forces 4.</li> <li>The free reach goes to instant casting.</li> <li>Range<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Casting the spell at touch range uses the normal Dexterity + Brawl or Weaponry; no special alternative roll just because it's a legacy attainment.</li> <li>It's possible to activate the attainment as an Aimed Spell and the attack roll is the normal Gnosis + MAX(Athletics, Firearms) - Defense -- it doesn't have a special Aimed Spell roll just because it's a legacy attainment.</li> <li>Whether the attainment must be cast via touch or aiming is not built into the definition of the attainment; the mage can choose which method to use at the time of casting.</li> <li>Casting the spell automatically succeeds if the above rolls succeed.</li> </ol></li> <li>Spell factors (<b>Note of confusion: I can't remember if &quot;additional spells factors&quot; uses the mage's dots in the relevant arcanum or the attainment's prerequisite dots in the arcanum)</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Duration is inapplicable.</li> <li>The maximum possible effective Potency of the spell is 1+2+3 = 6.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>One because the casting succeeds automatically (every successful spell gets one free Potency rating)</li> <li>Two from &quot;additional spell factors that would incur a penalty...&quot; The mage has Forces 4. Each additional level of Potency applies a -2 penalty to the die roll.</li> <li>Three from the the mage's Forces rating of 4, minus 1, since Potency is the primary spell factor.</li> </ol></li> <li>Alternatively, the attainment could have Potency 4 and Scale of a large room by applying the permitted additional spell factors to Scale rather than Potency. Or it could have Potency 5 and Scale of a small room. These Scale factors only matter for Aimed Casting.</li> <li>The allocation of additional spell factors is not part of the definition of the attainment and can be varied between castings according the mage's choice.</li> </ol></li> </ol><b>Example 2: Mental Shield (Mind) as a third-tier attainment requiring Mind 3</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assume the casting mage has Mind 3 and Gnosis 4.</li> <li>Rather than instant casting, use the free reach for Advanced Duration. This spell takes one scene to cast.</li> <li>Since this is a third-tier attainment mimicking a Mind 2 spell, it gets another reach. Say it's spent to make the Duration as Indefinite.</li> <li>Touch/Aimed range</li> <li>Spell factors<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Potency is meaningless for this spell.</li> <li>Duration is Indefinite via reach.</li> <li>Scale can be 1 + 1 = 2 ranks to affect via Aimed Casting everyone within a small room, which could include the casting mage.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>One Scale rank is a freebie for the (automatically) successful casting of the spell.</li> <li>One additional spell rank that would incur a -2 penalty since casting mage has 3 dots of Mind.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li>Clash of Wills: Affected subjects get to roll 4 + 3 + 4 = 11 dice<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Four for casting mage's Gnosis.</li> <li>Three for the casting mage's Mind dots.</li> <li>Four because the spell's Duration is Indefinite.</li> <li>Subjects still have the option to spend a Willpower point to further bolster the roll.</li> <li><b>Or maybe this is wrong and subjects simply get an automatic 3 successes on the clash roll per the &quot;If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes&quot; bit. Not sure whether they can use Willpower in that case.</b></li> </ol></li> <li>The mage can have multiple instances of this spell in effect simultaneously, each effecting different subjects. Each casting counts against his maximum number of active spells (in this case 4 max).</li> </ol>Finally, a mage cannot take advantage of Teamwork when casting legacy attainments<br /> <br /> Please point out where I got something wrong or left something out. Thanks to anyone who puts the effort into checking me on this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T16:48:02-07:00","id":1245232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1245202#post1245202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you folks please help me remember how to correctly apply the rules for legacy attainment dice pools? I'm getting back into Mage and having to reparse these rules.<br /> <br /> I guess please just check and correct my examples; hopefully these are comprehensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so here's how I've understood the rules. Take it with a grain of salt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Example 1: Telekinetic Strike (Forces) as a third-tier attainment requiring Forces 3</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assume the casting mage has Forces 4.</li> <li>The free reach goes to instant casting.</li> <li>Range<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Casting the spell at touch range uses the normal Dexterity + Brawl or Weaponry; no special alternative roll just because it's a legacy attainment.</li> <li>It's possible to activate the attainment as an Aimed Spell and the attack roll is the normal Gnosis + MAX(Athletics, Firearms) - Defense -- it doesn't have a special Aimed Spell roll just because it's a legacy attainment.</li> <li>Whether the attainment must be cast via touch or aiming is not built into the definition of the attainment; the mage can choose which method to use at the time of casting.</li> <li>Casting the spell automatically succeeds if the above rolls succeed.</li> </ol><br /> </li> </ol> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I assume that Touch and Aimed can be chosen, and that all those rolls benefit from auto successes as per Automatic Activation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div></li> <li>Spell factors (<b>Note of confusion: I can't remember if &quot;additional spells factors&quot; uses the mage's dots in the relevant arcanum or the attainment's prerequisite dots in the arcanum)</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T17:55:01-07:00","id":1245249,"title":"","content":"Attainments explicitly don\u2019t count against spell control.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m CoW, I assume that the attainment receives automatic successes in the way 21C Hermit describes going by the fact that in 11Q this seems to be the case when Matter MS is in effect. You can probably restrict it to when engaging in a particular activity at a particular time though, in the 11Q example it only appears to work right as you arrive at the scenery begin an investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T20:10:51-07:00","id":1245298,"title":"","content":"Thanks very much to both of you; I think that covers everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T00:51:46-07:00","id":1245354,"title":"","content":"CoW doesn't receive any automatic successes. Roll Arcanum+Gnosis as usual. The automatic successes refers to the activation of the Attainment. I'd look up a quote from DaveB confirming this if I weren't on my phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T02:10:57-07:00","id":1245367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1245354#post1245354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CoW doesn't receive any automatic successes. Roll Arcanum+Gnosis as usual. The automatic successes refers to the activation of the Attainment. I'd look up a quote from DaveB confirming this if I weren't on my phone.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a> posted a quote and link to it in my homebrew thread, second from the last page. <br /> <br /> I interpreted that as the mage who is challenging the Attainment is the one who rolls Gnosis + Arcanum, rather than the Attainment user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T03:26:50-07:00","id":1245382,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/881992-mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-errata-thread/page14\">The CoW link in question.</a><br /> <br /> CoW is rolled normally for both the Attainment user and the person clashing, no automatic successes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T03:52:07-07:00","id":1245387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1245382#post1245382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/881992-mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-errata-thread/page14&amp;quot;]The</a> CoW link in question.[/URL]<br /> <br /> CoW is rolled normally for both the Attainment user and the person clashing, no automatic successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>By chance, did Dave or anybody else confirm elsewhere that it\u2019s both parties and not just the one who\u2019s challenging the Attainment user? His answer there feels kinda vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T04:28:37-07:00","id":1245396,"title":"","content":"I don't suppose any book has commented on the coincidence that the current Greater Ministries owe their loyalty to the Exarchs who draw/provide their Arcana from/to Path Mastigos and Path Obrimos?<br /> <br /> I mean, odds are it's a complete coincidence, but it might be possible to argue that these Paths (and other Legacies promoting their use) would be more common in the Seers as Mages of those Paths find more to associate with, and more natural aptitude for the principles and powers of the Ministries?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T04:32:24-07:00","id":1245398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1245387#post1245387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By chance, did Dave or anybody else confirm elsewhere that it\u2019s both parties and not just the one who\u2019s challenging the Attainment user? His answer there feels kinda vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it vague? It works exactly like every other Mage clash, including those that the normal Arcana attainments can provoke, i.e. Gnosis + Arcana vs Gnosis + Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 08-13-2018, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T04:43:10-07:00","id":1245401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1245396#post1245396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose any book has commented on the coincidence that the current Greater Ministries owe their loyalty to the Exarchs who draw/provide their Arcana from/to Path Mastigos and Path Obrimos?<br /> <br /> I mean, odds are it's a complete coincidence, but it might be possible to argue that these Paths (and other Legacies promoting their use) would be more common in the Seers as Mages of those Paths find more to associate with, and more natural aptitude for the principles and powers of the Ministries?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know either, but if any book mentions this it\u2019ll the 1E Seers book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T04:48:03-07:00","id":1245402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1245398#post1245398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it vague? It works exactly like every other Mage clash, including those that the normal Arcana attainments can provoke, i.e. Gnosis + Arcana vs Gnosis + Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there are two parties and two dice pools, and one of them has a clause that suggest they may not roll normally while still engaging in the Clash? Special laws and general laws and all that.<br /> <br /> (Okay, maybe I need to rest a bit from cramming in my law studies, seei