long indeed. So the more you invest into your golem army, the better. Add <i>Alter Integrity</i> at Matter 5 to make them juggernauts, stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:25:35-08:00","id":1280724,"title":"","content":"Mind 1 Knowing would be the correct Practice to determine if a particular being is or is not sapient, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:40:21-08:00","id":1280727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1280724#post1280724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 1 Knowing would be the correct Practice to determine if a particular being is or is not sapient, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say, yes... if casted upon the subject.<br /> Sensory Spell are Unveiling as practice, and the subject is herself. Knowing Spell are casted UPON a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T01:18:10-08:00","id":1280854,"title":"","content":"Misread something, redundant post. Please delete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 01-15-2019, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T15:15:35-08:00","id":1280990,"title":"","content":"If I make a Human with create life is it a sleeper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T15:35:32-08:00","id":1280993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1280990#post1280990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I make a Human with create life is it a sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if you make a Human with just Life then it is not a Sleeper, but basically a Human shell. It would probably only have the basic of physical stimuli since no Mind is incorporated.<br /> <br /> If you included a Mind with Mind 5, this would mean you have a Human Shell with a Mind. So, this would also technically not be a Human, but pretty close. So it would not be a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> A Sleeper is essentially a &quot;human&quot; in that they have a shell, mind, and soul.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T16:16:23-08:00","id":1281001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1280724#post1280724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 1 Knowing would be the correct Practice to determine if a particular being is or is not sapient, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically yes, but its the harder way. Active Mind Sight allows you to detect at a glance if something is a thinking being, as well as if someone is asleep, comatose, awake, meditating or astral projecting. You are also aware when anyone you can perceive spends or gains Willpower.<br /> <br /> If Mind is your Ruling Arcana, entering it is a reflexive action, otherwise its instant. Regardless of that, it requires no dice rolls and provides a much more comprehensive analysis than a Knowing spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-15-2019, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T16:25:50-08:00","id":1281004,"title":"","content":"Creating a soul requires mastery of all 5 subtle Arcana. <br /> <br /> But psychic genesis can create a Sleepwalker goetia, which is only relevant for yantras, as goetia suffer no Quiescence.<br /> <br /> But if you meant your golem army, you could just bind an emphemeral entity to it. Moros are very well equipped for this. They can make the item an Anchor. Or they can bind or persuade the ghost to do it. Which means not only making golems with a huge variety of gadgets, but advanced &quot;AI&quot; for turrets, security systems, cars (the MIB one has nothing on a dedicated Moros), smartphones and much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T18:10:42-08:00","id":1281018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1281004#post1281004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating a soul requires mastery of all 5 subtle Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>It requires more than that, Mages cannot create souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T19:17:16-08:00","id":1281029,"title":"","content":"I thought it was subtler than that! Something like &quot;some peeps think that you need 5 fold mastery, and as vanishingly rare as that is no one has proven success.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it might be up to the ST if it works.<br /> <br /> However I feel it implied that only archmages can do it. Alternatively it IS possible with 5fold mastery but without archmaster support you'll be assassinated?? My vote is on archmastery but I feel that tidbit from the book kept the door open for funsies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T01:35:10-08:00","id":1281060,"title":"","content":"Its one of those things no one has managed to pull off, but a lot of lore suggesting it. Most of it comes from the Tremere, so your mileage might vary (depending on what the ST wants to go with).<br /> <br /> I think this historical expression fits the question well: Here Be Dragons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-16-2019, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T14:37:30-08:00","id":1281184,"title":"","content":"What determines a Demesne ruling arcanum? Are its ruling arcanums just the arcanums of the mages soulstone? The first soulstone used on it? Or the Symbols that fill the Demesne determine its Ruling acanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:51:12-08:00","id":1281223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1281184#post1281184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What determines a Demesne ruling arcanum? Are its ruling arcanums just the arcanums of the mages soulstone? The first soulstone used on it? Or the Symbols that fill the Demesne determine its Ruling acanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>The the Mage's Soul Stone. You can combine multiple, thus making a Demesne that is attuned to all Five Paths and thus has all arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T22:26:10-08:00","id":1281257,"title":"","content":"is control fire affected by scale of the spell? If i make my bics flame into a forest fire how big is the fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T22:34:55-08:00","id":1281258,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the scale of Control Fire would determine how large of an initial fire you can affect. Contrary to popular belief, forest fires are rarely single fires, but are far more often many smaller fires, fairly well-delineated, which could be brought under control or even extinguished with Control Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T23:38:56-08:00","id":1281261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1281223#post1281223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The the Mage's Soul Stone. You can combine multiple, thus making a Demesne that is attuned to all Five Paths and thus has all arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where i can find reference for this?<br /> My tought is that the ruling arcana of the mage who opens the Demesne are ruling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T06:06:58-08:00","id":1281284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Excerpt pg. 99 - A mage can create a Demesne using one or more soul stones. The mage doesn\u2019t have to use her own soul stone. </div> </div> </div>So, there is the part about containing more than one soul stone involved and it doesn't have to be the mage's own so you can have all Paths attuned at the Demesne. Take into consideration this is pretty rare though as not every cabal has all Paths and not all cabal members will always contribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Formatting error when posting. 01-17-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T00:23:56-08:00","id":1281471,"title":"","content":"I am sorry if I am asking to much but how do things in fate magic manifest? When I hex someone with blindness does dust or debris fly into their eye or do they have a blood vessels burst or either ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T04:23:26-08:00","id":1281482,"title":"","content":"However you want to represent it. Those sound like good ways to explain them within a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T18:31:36-08:00","id":1282935,"title":"","content":"If a mage uses a Pattering of Mind to Astral Project as a goetia (how would that even work stat wise ?), could they be able to take lethal damage to empower a Talen (or whatever the name is for the astral version) with one of their Influences? If so, would their real body take damage to reflect that ? Or would only their Corpus be affected, allowing them to heal with Mind only ? <br /> <br /> Since one becomes ephemera when crossing into a Realm Invisible, Pattering should allow them to assume another form (similar logic to Shapechanging). <br /> <br /> I imagine it could be possible, because a Death version of this could create Mementos. One way to look at it is that, since ghost don't normally don't know how or want to weave their ephemera into something, Mementos are created naturally via strong exposure to death resonances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-26-2019, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T21:07:52-08:00","id":1282956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1282935#post1282935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage uses a Pattering of Mind to Astral Project as a goetia (how would that even work stat wise ?), could they be able to take lethal damage to empower a Talen (or whatever the name is for the astral version) with one of their Influences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, between &quot;take lethal damage to form a talen&quot; not being a thing that non-spirits are able to do by the books and translating a living mage into an ephemeral being wholesale generally coming across as a very permanent change on account of it being a more secure form of lichdom than plain spellwork.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine it could be possible, because a Death version of this could create Mementos. </div> </div> </div>That\u2026 sounds like the opposite of a solid rationale for cross-applying a principle of how things from the Shadow work to other entities just because they share baseline mechanics.<br /> <br /> &quot;These things form under nebulous circumstances and are related to the baleful energies of death in the broken system presently represented by the Underworld&quot; doesn't sound like the kind of thing that should be manageable by normal Awakened spellcasting outside of the more complete and temporary setup implied by Ghost Binding as a Ceremony and the way the products of Craft Fetish differ from the products of the Fetish Wolf Rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T01:33:09-08:00","id":1282985,"title":"","content":"The train of thought was &quot;these are both beings made of Essence, if one is able to tear apart its power to temporarily infuse an item with it, is it not possible that another being composed of Essence can utilize its Corpus in a similar manner? Or is it specifically something only spirit ephemeral beings are able to do ?&quot;<br /> <br /> The spirit transformation wasn't meant to be permanent, rather the idea was to use Patterning to temporarily alter a mage's ephemeral form in order to utilize spirit like abilities, such as Influence. In which case, could that be extended to talen crafting ? Although Mementos were not the best parallel, I mean more along the line of &quot;single use Death resonant items, like an alternate version of alchemy crafting, but with a more necromantic feel to it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-27-2019, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T14:06:22-08:00","id":1283116,"title":"","content":"Can a mage release a spell without losing a willpower dot in their own Oneiros without consequence since there is no risk of Paradox there ever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:13:49-08:00","id":1283127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283116#post1283116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage release a spell without losing a willpower dot in their own Oneiros without consequence since there is no risk of Paradox there ever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately not, because Will is the fuel, not the program. <br /> <br /> So even if you run your reality bending program in a highly controlled environment, it still needs resources to function. Normally your Gnosis supercomputer does that for you, by very efficiently using your Awakened Will. <br /> <br /> But if you cut it off from it, you need to provide some infrastructure for it to run. <br /> <br /> So you have two options. First one is to allocate the resources and permanently dedicate a senior programmer from HQ to keep it bug free (relinquishing with a WP dot). <br /> <br /> Second option is to just allocate resources, let it run unsupervised forever and see what happens (relinquishing with a WP point).<br /> <br /> Either way, you still need something to execute the program. The big advantage is that your Oneiros guarantees it will be bug free forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-27-2019, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:36:40-08:00","id":1283128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283127#post1283127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately not, because Will is the fuel, not the program.<br /> <br /> So even if you run your reality bending program in a highly controlled environment, it still needs resources to function. Normally your Gnosis supercomputer does that for you, by very efficiently using your Awakened Will.<br /> <br /> But if you cut it off from it, you need to provide some infrastructure for it to run.<br /> <br /> So you have two options. First one is to allocate the resources and permanently dedicate a senior programmer from HQ to keep it bug free (relinquishing with a WP dot).<br /> <br /> Second option is to just allocate resources, let it run unsupervised forever and see what happens (relinquishing with a WP point).<br /> <br /> Either way, you still need something to execute the program. The big advantage is that your Oneiros guarantees it will be bug free forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since my Oneiros presumably is destroyed after my mind stops working what mechanical effects would relinquishing with a point of WP do to risk any danger? Will the Paradox roll happen still?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:36:46-08:00","id":1283129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283127#post1283127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big advantage is that your Oneiros guarantees it will be bug free forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the case.<br /> <br /> Although it utilizes the same systems, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/888577-2e-can-you-cancel-a-spell-you-have-relinquished?p=890749#post890749\">it has been clarified by the Dev</a> that relinquished spells going haywire is not Paradox, and therefore the protection from Paradox afforded by the Oneiros would not apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283116#post1283116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage release a spell without losing a willpower dot in their own Oneiros without consequence since there is no risk of Paradox there ever?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, for the above mentioned reason: haywire spells aren't actually suffering from Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-27-2019, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:43:30-08:00","id":1283133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283129#post1283129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not the case.<br /> <br /> Although it utilizes the same systems, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/888577-2e-can-you-cancel-a-spell-you-have-relinquished?p=890749#post890749\">it has been clarified by the Dev</a> that relinquished spells going haywire is not Paradox, and therefore the protection from Paradox afforded by the Oneiros would not apply.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, for the above mentioned reason: haywire spells aren't actually suffering from Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">10char</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:18:06-08:00","id":1283138,"title":"","content":"Interesting, so it just a mechanical abstraction for a poorly maintained Imago.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated question, lets say an Acanthus wants to use Shared Fate to connect a room and a symbolic representation. So for example, if the Seer meeting room is connected to a scaled model the mage has. So if the mage's cabal destroy the model with a ton of Moros enhanced dynamite, something comparatively bad happens to the room and everyone within it.<br /> <br /> How could you accomplish that ? Affecting the room and its contents needs an AoE but the model is a small item that will be outside of it. Even using advanced scale boosted to to room size targets, it would not affect the Seers inside. Maybe AoE with the scaled model as a Sympathy yantra ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:05:14-08:00","id":1283152,"title":"","content":"If an explosion goes off in the model which causes an explosion to occur in the room, I fail to see how that wouldn't affect the Seers in the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T19:07:40-08:00","id":1283168,"title":"","content":"In theory it should, or they could be called away before it happens because they weren't fated to be hit by it, but perhaps I am overthinking the what ifs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T19:27:13-08:00","id":1283170,"title":"","content":"is the Seers of the Throne book outdated or still very much worth the read","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T20:16:52-08:00","id":1283179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283170#post1283170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the Seers of the Throne book outdated or still very much worth the read</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the mechanical stuff might be outdated, but all the fluff is still relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T18:27:24-08:00","id":1283406,"title":"","content":"Was thinking about a situation where a mage with access to Mind was sleeping but would desire to make themselves either conscious or lucid in the dream. So:<br /> 1. Are those possible dry or would you have to have prepared before hand?<br /> 2. If possible, what practice would most fit such spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T04:23:31-08:00","id":1283480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283406#post1283406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was thinking about a situation where a mage with access to Mind was sleeping but would desire to make themselves either conscious or lucid in the dream. So:<br /> 1. Are those possible dry or would you have to have prepared before hand?<br /> 2. If possible, what practice would most fit such spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Practice is easy: Compelling. Waking up from sleep is both extremely basic and quite easy to trigger.<br /> <br /> As for how, you could do it both ways. Either it's a precast spell that triggers upon certain conditions (requires some Fate in addition to Mind 1), or you choose to do it during sleep. The latter requires that the mage is lucidly dreaming, which is something all mages are capable of doing innately. If they don't want to spend time meditating beforehand they could cast Dream Reaching (Mind 2) with a Reach on themselves to automatically dream lucidly. Once lucidly dreaming they can just choose to wake up without even casting a spell for it. This means it's possible for all mages to do what you want even if they don't have access to Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T08:28:37-08:00","id":1283515,"title":"","content":"Are there matter spells that can enhance weapons? For instance would Finding the Balance work on a gun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T08:52:21-08:00","id":1283520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283515#post1283515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there matter spells that can enhance weapons? For instance would Finding the Balance work on a gun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weapons are a specialized form of equipment, so yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T17:22:31-08:00","id":1283600,"title":"","content":"final question about book relevancy. are the faction books still good or outdated and talk too much about Atlantis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T18:09:22-08:00","id":1283606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283600#post1283600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">final question about book relevancy. are the faction books still good or outdated and talk too much about Atlantis</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean the Order books. They\u2019re still good. Just keep in mind the Atlantis bits are them buying into a shared mythology, not something they take as literally true. A lot of it isn\u2019t Atlantis bits and are excellent windows into how the Orders work, how they are alike and differ from other Orders, and have lots of fodder for creating characters with unique philosophies, pursuits and interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T01:44:56-08:00","id":1283668,"title":"","content":"What does the add fate1 option do on the Dispel spell?<br /> If i understand it correctly it let you choose which spell suppress on a target with more than one on.<br /> In this case if i cast it without the fate1 it suppress one random spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T02:58:56-08:00","id":1283674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283668#post1283668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the add fate1 option do on the Dispel spell?<br /> If i understand it correctly it let you choose which spell suppress on a target with more than one on.<br /> In this case if i cast it without the fate1 it suppress one random spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. You target one specific spell with &quot;Dispel Magic&quot;, only that spell is affected. If you add in Fate 1 you can however determine for which subjects (if there are multiple people affected) are dispelled. Say a Thyrsus turns Mike, Sabrina and Tyler into rodents. Now Examplus, an Obrimos, comes by and decides to Dispel the spell. He doesn't like Tyler very much however and is fine with him being a rodent, so he uses Fate 1 to only dispel the transformation on Mike and Sabrina, leaving Tyler affected by the spell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T03:34:25-08:00","id":1283677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1283674#post1283674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite. You target one specific spell with &amp;quot;Dispel Magic&amp;quot;, only that spell is affected. If you add in Fate 1 you can however determine for which subjects (if there are multiple people affected) are dispelled. Say a Thyrsus turns Mike, Sabrina and Tyler into rodents. Now Examplus, an Obrimos, comes by and decides to Dispel the spell. He doesn't like Tyler very much however and is fine with him being a rodent, so he uses Fate 1 to only dispel the transformation on Mike and Sabrina, leaving Tyler affected by the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thanks \ud83d\udc4d<br /> This makes a lot more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T07:53:11-08:00","id":1284496,"title":"","content":"Should active death mage sight beat a vampire's obfuscate automatically? The guy who wants to run Mage for our group says yes, I say that should clearly be a clash of wills. Please help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13524-ruadni","name":"Ruadni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T10:02:21-08:00","id":1284527,"title":"","content":"As I wrote in your other thread: Mind Sight would get to Clash while Death Sight would probably get to Clash. Death has no reason to just bypass Obfuscate without even a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T10:13:19-08:00","id":1284534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284527#post1284527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I wrote in your other thread: Mind Sight would get to Clash while Death Sight would probably get to Clash. Death has no reason to just bypass Obfuscate without even a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. The page hung when I tried to post that thread so I didn't think it had gone through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13524-ruadni","name":"Ruadni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T05:42:53-08:00","id":1284695,"title":"","content":"Quick reminder: why is it that using adamantine hand as a yantra allows a person to keep their defense while casting in combat? I can't remember the reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T07:41:17-08:00","id":1284707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284695#post1284695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick reminder: why is it that using adamantine hand as a yantra allows a person to keep their defense while casting in combat? I can't remember the reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've misread. You always get to keep your Defense when casting spells. What Adamant Hand does is allow you to <i>attack</i> during a turn you're casting a spell","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T13:38:52-08:00","id":1284796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284707#post1284707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've misread. You always get to keep your Defense when casting spells. What Adamant Hand does is allow you to <i>attack</i> during a turn you're casting a spell</div> </div> </div> </div>You are also wrong.<br /> <br /> Adamant Hand allows you to reflexively add <s>successes on an attack</s> the attack as an order tool to a spell you cast on a <i>subsequent</i> turn. If the spell is reflexive you can use the merit for that spell as well, but reflexive spells can always be cast the same turn you make an attack.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 02-04-2019, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T14:41:09-08:00","id":1284805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284796#post1284796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are also wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages taking multiple turns to cast a spell (usually because<br /> they are utilizing Yantras or spending more Mana than their<br /> Gnosis allows) still apply Defense against attacks but may not<br /> make combat actions unless another rule such as the Adamant<br /> Hand Merit allows it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am correct even if I didn't go into the particulars of Adamant Hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284796#post1284796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adamant Hand allows you to reflexively add successes on an attack to a spell you cast on a <i>subsequent</i> turn. If the spell is reflexive you can use the merit for that spell as well, but reflexive spells can always be cast the same turn you make an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant Hand serves as an Order tool Yantra that is used reflexively <i>the same turn</i> you use the chosen Skill to attack. That means the attack does happen during the casting time of the spell (as turns spent adding Yantras are part of the spell casting action) regardless of whether the spell casting <i>roll</i> is made during that or subsequent turns.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the text for Adamant Hand is often misunderstood due to how vague it is, but generally people misread it to mean it grants the chosen Skill dot rating as a bonus. The actual bonus is the +1 that all Tool Yantras add (unless stated otherwise in their specific rules).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T15:12:03-08:00","id":1284813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284805#post1284805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Mages taking multiple turns to cast a spell (usually because<br /> they are utilizing Yantras or spending more Mana than their<br /> Gnosis allows) still apply Defense against attacks but may not<br /> make combat actions unless another rule such as the Adamant<br /> Hand Merit allows it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am correct even if I didn't go into the particulars of Adamant Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you are wrong, that section specifically deals with spells that are cast over multiple turns. So if I'm casting a spell over four turns (because I'm incorporating multiple yantras) and have Adamant Hand I can spend one of those turns attacking to <i>subsequently</i> add the bonus to the spell casting roll if the spell being cast is an instant action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adamant Hand serves as an Order tool Yantra that is used reflexively <i>the same turn</i> you use the chosen Skill to attack. That means the attack does happen during the casting time of the spell (as turns spent adding Yantras are part of the spell casting action) regardless of whether the spell casting <i>roll</i> is made during that or subsequent turns.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the text for Adamant Hand is often misunderstood due to how vague it is, but generally people misread it to mean it grants the chosen Skill dot rating as a bonus. The actual bonus is the +1 that all Tool Yantras add (unless stated otherwise in their specific rules). </div> </div> </div><br /> Actual text of the merit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adamant Hand</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">character has studied extensively in the Adamantine<br /> Arrow martial arts. This allows her to use combat<br /> techniques as Yantras for instant spells. When taking this Merit,<br /> choose Athletics, Weaponry, or Brawl, which your character<br /> must have three or more dots in. This Merit allows use of that<br /> Skill in combat as a reflexive Order tool Yantra, adding dice<br /> to a spell cast on <b>subsequent turns</b>, or to a spell cast reflexively<br /> in the same turn as the combat action. You may purchase this<br /> Merit multiple times to reflect the other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know what you think subsequent means, but it does not mean the same turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought I edited out the &quot;add successes&quot; bit, I typed that before rereading the merit and meant to delete it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T15:46:51-08:00","id":1284820,"title":"","content":"It's talking about the final spellcasting action where you roll the dice pool. It's saying subsequent turn because an instant spell can't be cast the same turn you attack because you're not allowed to take more than one instant action each turn. It even specifies that reflexive spellcasting can be done during the very same turn.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about, which should be abundantly clear if you read the text I originally quoted from the book, is the larger spellcasting action (of which the final spellcasting action is only a part) that incorporates all turns you spend incorporating Yantras. Yantras can only be applied while they exist/are being carried out, and the attack is reflexively used as a Yantra when you perform the attack. That means the attack is carried out during the first turn of the spell casting, <i>just like it says in the text I quoted directly from the book</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T16:47:55-08:00","id":1284844,"title":"","content":"Can Adamant Hand accumulate ? So if you spent 4 turns dodging a rampaging werewolf while the party prepares some spells, can you then add +4 to an instant spell as a reflexive yantra or does it always stay as +1 ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T17:00:24-08:00","id":1284851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1284844#post1284844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Adamant Hand accumulate ? So if you spent 4 turns dodging a rampaging werewolf while the party prepares some spells, can you then add +4 to an instant spell as a reflexive yantra or does it always stay as +1 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Subsequent turns,&quot; plural, suggests you could, space permitting, put four +1 Yantras toward an appropriate spell, bearing in mind that semiotics still apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T17:23:16-08:00","id":1284856,"title":"","content":"Fascinating, that is a pretty nice bonus indeed, wish there was a Firearms version, but I imagine that a sharpshooting Arrow can make up for it with a very mobile combat approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T04:27:49-08:00","id":1285200,"title":"","content":"Last game I had an NPC want to refer to another mage's day-to-day non-mage identity but I couldn't really think of what terminology they'd use? Like a mage has their persona and their... I couldn't think of a good term for it.<br /> <br /> Is there a term I've missed, or does anyone have any good ideas for a term?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:28:54-08:00","id":1285212,"title":"","content":"There doesn't exist a term for it as far as I know so I would just go with &quot;mundane persona&quot; or something similar, depending on context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:57:14-08:00","id":1285220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1285212#post1285212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn't exist a term for it as far as I know so I would just go with &quot;mundane persona&quot; or something similar, depending on context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. That's more or less where I was going. I dunno, it just came up in a way that made it feel as if there should be some kind of regularised terminology.<br /> <br /> Maybe Mundane Persona and Supernal Persona? That could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:03:24-08:00","id":1288404,"title":"","content":"A heard that the Fluff of Awakening changed in 2 Edtion. Who did it change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:41:09-08:00","id":1288464,"title":"","content":"Atlantis is mostly just an accepted theory versus being a pretty concrete thing. Most mages have a combined belief that things were better sometime in the past with their own background. Meaning it is much more open for the ST to do whatever they feel fits best. I personally always considered it a theory myself and just used it to make some cool moments where the characters found relics that might have been from the fabled city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:42:53-08:00","id":1288466,"title":"","content":"Not a theory, a myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:51:07-08:00","id":1288470,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Either way, it is less concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T02:30:55-08:00","id":1288551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1288404#post1288404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A heard that the Fluff of Awakening changed in 2 Edtion. Who did it change?</div> </div> </div> </div>That not a remotely simple question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T18:44:04-08:00","id":1288799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1288470#post1288470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* Either way, it is less concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an important distinction, though. In 1E, it was a theory - there were Mages (possibly even a majority of them) that believed that Atlantis was a semi-literal origin story.<br /> <br /> In 2E, it's a myth and a metaphor, and any Mages that genuinely believe that the events described in that myth took place even remotely literally are liable to be fairly...touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:48:29-08:00","id":1289103,"title":"","content":"When your Nimbus goes off, you're at the epicenter. Do you think you could craft a spell to have it go off somewhere else? How would you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:14:16-08:00","id":1289111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1289103#post1289103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When your Nimbus goes off, you're at the epicenter. Do you think you could craft a spell to have it go off somewhere else? How would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>A prime weaving spell i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:43:47-08:00","id":1289524,"title":"","content":"So tass and mana can have resonance, right? And when a Mage &quot;consumes&quot; the mana/tass it's in his pattern, right? So:<br /> 1. Is that particular bit of mana separate from the rest of his pool?<br /> 2. If so, does the resonance &quot;degrade&quot; over time if he doesn't use that bit of mana?<br /> 3. If not, does the resonance &quot;infect&quot; the rest of his pool?<br /> 4. Is it possible that there are combinations that I haven't considered?<br /> 5. What does resonance actually mean?<br /> <br /> And yes, I have recognized that this could be a Mystery, just wondering if there's an official understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:02:42-08:00","id":1289548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1289524#post1289524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is that particular bit of mana separate from the rest of his pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes up the same amount of &quot;space&quot; in the pool as Mana he got from oblations or Obsessions, but I'd say it's probably worth keeping track of how much Resonant Mana of which types a character has.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. If so, does the resonance &quot;degrade&quot; over time if he doesn't use that bit of mana? </div> </div> </div>Probably not, at least in a direct mechanical sense.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. If not, does the resonance &quot;infect&quot; the rest of his pool? </div> </div> </div>Likewise probably not, although retaining/cycling Mana with the same Resonance/from the same external source may have narrative effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Is it possible that there are combinations that I haven't considered? </div> </div> </div>I don't know what this means.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. What does resonance actually mean? </div> </div> </div>The metaphysical energies that precipitate emotions, images, or themes in their vessels and surroundings, propagated along ley lines and fed upon by spirits and goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:34:04-08:00","id":1289562,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Satchel!<br /> <br /> Eh, #4 was like if you could say yes to numbers 2 or 3 but not require the &quot;if&quot; portion. Like, resonance &quot;degrading&quot; but also &quot;infecting&quot; the rest of your mana, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Which basically means that you can ignore it, given the answers to the rest of the questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:48:40-08:00","id":1289568,"title":"","content":"Hello, I\u2019m currently playing an acanthus in a home game. Was having a light debate with our ST over Fate and direct damage spells with Only dots in fate<br /> <br /> It appears that all other spheres of magic have a way of applying direct damage at 3 4 and 5 dots. Fate on the other hand seems to be alone in that it does not have an explicit rote in 2e spelled out that does direct damage. I was suggesting that it makes sense that I could use my third dot in fate to inflict bashing damage by using fraying effects to effect their fate, perhaps causing misfortune and damaging them indirectly (such as tripping and twisting an ankle, or a cutting of their destiny which hurts their lifeline). My ST suggested that while these are feasible things to do with Fate they require other spheres, such as forces for convenient physics shenanigans, or to damaging their destiny and indirectly hurting them it would require death spheres. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not perfectly rules savvy, so please forgive my ignorance. I think they are correct in the examples I listed, but is it possible to do direct damage with fate alone? And what does that magic look like?<br /> <br /> Thanks <br /> <br /> Brassfist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:26:38-08:00","id":1289580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brassfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1289568#post1289568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I\u2019m currently playing an acanthus in a home game. Was having a light debate with our ST over Fate and direct damage spells with Only dots in fate<br /> <br /> It appears that all other spheres of magic have a way of applying direct damage at 3 4 and 5 dots. Fate on the other hand seems to be alone in that it does not have an explicit rote in 2e spelled out that does direct damage. I was suggesting that it makes sense that I could use my third dot in fate to inflict bashing damage by using fraying effects to effect their fate, perhaps causing misfortune and damaging them indirectly (such as tripping and twisting an ankle, or a cutting of their destiny which hurts their lifeline). My ST suggested that while these are feasible things to do with Fate they require other spheres, such as forces for convenient physics shenanigans, or to damaging their destiny and indirectly hurting them it would require death spheres.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not perfectly rules savvy, so please forgive my ignorance. I think they are correct in the examples I listed, but is it possible to do direct damage with fate alone? And what does that magic look like?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> <br /> Brassfist</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate is kind of unique in that it is, almost by definition, intangible and at the periphery. I don't know what a direct-damage fate spell would look like. I think Fate operates on a pretty unique level with the hexes and boons and it's probably appropriate that it can't be used to directly damage someone.<br /> <br /> I would rule it this way: a spell with instant cast time is meant, mostly, to resolve in a turn (3 seconds). If someone is actively doing something that has a meaningful risk of hurting them within the next three seconds, I'd say it falls in the purview of fate to cause that catastrophe. If someone is running, you could make them stumble and trip, for example (maybe roll Dexterity + Athletics to resist, as they normally would). But if someone is not actively participating in an activity that could actually cause them physical harm in the next turn, I'd say it's probably outside the purview of Fate to make that happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:58:38-08:00","id":1289608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brassfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1289568#post1289568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I\u2019m currently playing an acanthus in a home game. Was having a light debate with our ST over Fate and direct damage spells with Only dots in fate<br /> <br /> It appears that all other spheres of magic have a way of applying direct damage at 3 4 and 5 dots. Fate on the other hand seems to be alone in that it does not have an explicit rote in 2e spelled out that does direct damage. I was suggesting that it makes sense that I could use my third dot in fate to inflict bashing damage by using fraying effects to effect their fate, perhaps causing misfortune and damaging them indirectly (such as tripping and twisting an ankle, or a cutting of their destiny which hurts their lifeline). My ST suggested that while these are feasible things to do with Fate they require other spheres, such as forces for convenient physics shenanigans, or to damaging their destiny and indirectly hurting them it would require death spheres.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not perfectly rules savvy, so please forgive my ignorance. I think they are correct in the examples I listed, but is it possible to do direct damage with fate alone? And what does that magic look like?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> <br /> Brassfist</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first of all the fact that you use the terminology of sphere's indicates that you (or the ST) may have some hold overs from Ascension, which is a completely different game. Awakening, especially 2e, requires far, far fewer conjunctional Arcana to achieve what it wants to do and we use the proper term of Arcana (plural) or Arcanum (singular).<br /> <br /> That being said, Fate is the one Arcana that does seem to have a problem with dealing direct damage. Now, some people have said that you can just use Fraying and Unraveling to do direct damage using any of the Arcana (Unmaking doesn't do damage, it destroys entirely), but the problem is that you'll notice that not all the other arcana's direct damage spells work off of Fraying and Unraveling. Forces is probably the prime example where Weaving and Patterning are typically used instead.<br /> <br /> Now, I think you can and ought to be able to hurt someone with Fate, just not directly. That's the thing about Fate, it's practically entirely about indirect causes and effects. So I would still allow Fate to hurt someone in the heat of battle, you'd just have to have the ST fluff it differently with the possibility that the damage isn't immediate. For instance, you cast a Fate Unraveling spell on an enemy and when their buddy next fires their auto rifle, one of the bullets ricochets into him, dealing potency lethal damage. Or you cast a Fate Fraying spell with a duration longer than one turn and the next time your enemy tries to attack you they end up tripping and hurting themselves, dealing potency bashing damage. That sort of thing. If nothing is happening in the scene and absolutely nothing in the environment could hurt the person under any circumstance whatsoever, then....yeah, I'd say Fate can't do direct damage there. But in that instance you're probably the one attacking first, so...eh, better to curse them instead. Now you'll want to notice that I said &quot;absolutely nothing in the environment could hurt the person under any circumstances whatsoever...&quot; The reason I said that is that Fate can cause just about anything to happen given enough time, so if there is a potential hazard in the area but it isn't currently dangerous, then Fate could make it both dangerous and more specifically to the person you've cursed. You just have to fluff it so that the hazard seems random. So yeah, creativity is your ST's friend in the instance of Fate damage spells.<br /> <br /> Realistically speaking, thought, direct damage spells are not the way you want to fight anyways. Beyond some Storytellers saying that you can only risk Wisdom loss due to spellcasting, magic is far more useful in hampering your enemies and giving you a (or several) advantages such that your opponents won't want to commit violence against you, will flee, will throw down their weapons and beg for mercy, or some other end to the fighting. So an example of using a spell to give yourself an advantage would be to grant yourself the 8 again on firearms/brawl/weaponry rolls while also having Mage armor up. Your enemies will find it hard to hurt you while you end up just blowing their brains out/choking them out/cutting them to pieces so quickly their heads spin (sometimes in more than one way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 02-19-2019, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:38:32-08:00","id":1290783,"title":"","content":"How is the Mind 2 effect Incognito Presence intended to work? Does it really prevent you from being noticed in any situation? If a Vampire walks in on you in their Haven are they not going to pay attention to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:59:13-08:00","id":1290831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1290783#post1290783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the Mind 2 effect Incognito Presence intended to work? Does it really prevent you from being noticed in any situation? If a Vampire walks in on you in their Haven are they not going to pay attention to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much unless they have a power that could counter it, like Auspex probably. If you've ever seen the Silence from Dr. Who I imagine it's a lot like that, but more aggressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:39:10-08:00","id":1290852,"title":"","content":"Which should not be a new, terrifying concept to vampires, as it's how Obfuscate works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:43:13-08:00","id":1290877,"title":"","content":"If I have a situation where a mage can cast a conditional trigger hung spell sympathetically, lets say a healing spell, meant to heal someone who is going into a fight the mage cannot be present for and is using a proxy instead... what sort of magic will show up to an obrimos opponent trying to scrutinize the proxy?<br /> <br /> I am unsure if the hung spell is already sympathetically linked to the proxy and visible to the scrutinizer, or if the spell being hung means its still back where it was cast and ready to hop across space using sympathy (assuming the sympathy doesnt change after the trigger goes off?)<br /> <br /> Basically, are hung sympathetic spells a good way to hide your back up magic or are they still visible on the subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T15:57:01-08:00","id":1290922,"title":"","content":"One more question that came up in game last night: can a sleepwalker just hold one or two spells total or is it per Mage they have a connection with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:23:00-08:00","id":1290965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1290877#post1290877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a situation where a mage can cast a conditional trigger hung spell sympathetically, lets say a healing spell, meant to heal someone who is going into a fight the mage cannot be present for and is using a proxy instead... what sort of magic will show up to an obrimos opponent trying to scrutinize the proxy?<br /> <br /> I am unsure if the hung spell is already sympathetically linked to the proxy and visible to the scrutinizer, or if the spell being hung means its still back where it was cast and ready to hop across space using sympathy (assuming the sympathy doesn't change after the trigger goes off?)<br /> <br /> Basically, are hung sympathetic spells a good way to hide your back up magic or are they still visible on the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the hung spell is already on the subject when it is cast. Just because you had to use Spatial sympathy doesn't prevent it from being visible to Prime. I could be wrong, but that's my take on it. If you don't want a spell to be visible to Active Mage Sight you need to veil it. If you can't be monitering the conflict at the time then that's just the risk you will have to take. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T23:22:48-08:00","id":1292950,"title":"","content":"A question about Demenses. Does a demenses prevent paradox for all magic or just magic that has the right semiotic associations. Can magic not have the Yantra bonus but still not cause paradox in a demense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:45:19-08:00","id":1293028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1292950#post1292950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about Demenses. Does a demenses prevent paradox for all magic or just magic that has the right semiotic associations. Can magic not have the Yantra bonus but still not cause paradox in a demense?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, and no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T08:34:46-08:00","id":1293045,"title":"","content":"The Paradox mitigation is automatic as long as the spell qualifies for the Yantra bonus, so you don't have to use the Demesne/Verge as a Yantra if you don't want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T20:29:17-08:00","id":1293947,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's a stupid question. Can I use a Matter Weaving practice to transform water into wine? Or making water be alcoholic. Or even turn steel into lead or making steel flammable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24409-jclepf","name":"jclepf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T21:21:47-08:00","id":1293954,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately not, that is transforming one thing within the Arcanum's purview into something else entirely, which required the Practice of Pattering, specifically the <i>Transmutation </i>spell. Weaving can allow the water to cause drunkenness, or make it flammable, give it a lower freezing point or make it corrosive. Weaving can only alter properties without changing the nature of the object, such as a Weaving of Life giving you dragon wings without transforming you into one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-05-2019, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T06:17:11-08:00","id":1294020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1293947#post1293947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's a stupid question. Can I use a Matter Weaving practice to transform water into wine? Or making water be alcoholic. Or even turn steel into lead or making steel flammable</div> </div> </div> </div>No, yes, no, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:06:17-08:00","id":1294057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1293947#post1293947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or making water be alcoholic.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1294020#post1294020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarification: Give alcoholic properties to water, not having the water contain alcohol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:24:53-08:00","id":1294066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1290831#post1290831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much unless they have a power that could counter it, like Auspex probably. If you've ever seen the Silence from Dr. Who I imagine it's a lot like that, but more aggressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this post is over a week old now but I just caught it. This does not seem right to me, as I did not think incognito presence worked in a situation where-in the observer would reasonably expect to recognize everyone he saw. Incognito presence would not let you walk into a private home and be ignored by the family that lived there and it wouldn't let you walk into a private Haven and be ignored by the vampire, unless said family or said vampire maintained a very large staff that was regularly in the house or Haven. unless I am very mistaken about how incognito presence works. and I thought the first level of obfuscate worked the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:52:54-08:00","id":1294074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1294066#post1294066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this post is over a week old now but I just caught it. This does not seem right to me, as I did not think incognito presence worked in a situation where-in the observer would reasonably expect to recognize everyone he saw. Incognito presence would not let you walk into a private home and be ignored by the family that lived there and it wouldn't let you walk into a private Haven and be ignored by the vampire, unless said family or said vampire maintained a very large staff that was regularly in the house or Haven. unless I am very mistaken about how incognito presence works. and I thought the first level of obfuscate worked the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the spell again, it makes no mention of people having a chance of reacting in a way that doesn't lead to them pretty much ignoring the subject of the spell. Others don't want to acknowledge that the subject is there at all, and when forced to will immediately forget the subject is there when they look away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T09:00:02-08:00","id":1294078,"title":"","content":"Like Mrmdubois says, Incognito does not have a built in failure condition. Unlike Obfuscate you <i>need</i> to have a supernatural power (Knowing/Unveiling spells, Active Mage Sight, or a vampire's Auspex, for example) and win a Clash of Wills in order to pierce Incognito Presence.<br /> Unlike the Silence from Doctor Who, people who look directly at the subject will still ignore their presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T11:40:21-08:00","id":1294117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1294057#post1294057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clarification: Give alcoholic properties to water, not having the water contain alcohol.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok... so, I can make water become corrosive to corrode some kind of steel or attack someone? And can I make it with sweat? Is it Matter or Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24409-jclepf","name":"jclepf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T11:56:40-08:00","id":1294122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1294078#post1294078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Mrmdubois says, Incognito does not have a built in failure condition. Unlike Obfuscate you <i>need</i> to have a supernatural power (Knowing/Unveiling spells, Active Mage Sight, or a vampire's Auspex, for example) and win a Clash of Wills in order to pierce Incognito Presence.<br /> Unlike the Silence from Doctor Who, people who look directly at the subject will still ignore their presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading the spell, I must have been confusing the descriptions of Incognito presence with level one Obfuscate. It actually works more like level three obfuscate. It seems over powered, but then it is a mage ability, and it is in line with the standard level 2 arcana abilities in that it is basically hiding the person from other conscious minds. Oh well. Live and learn what you should have known since 2015.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:55:26-08:00","id":1294324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1294117#post1294117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok... so, I can make water become corrosive to corrode some kind of steel or attack someone? And can I make it with sweat? Is it Matter or Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fresh sweat I'd say is Life, bottled is Matter. Most organic materials have a tendency to shift from Life to Matter given time not being, y'know, alive. How much time depends on your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:05:45-08:00","id":1294700,"title":"","content":"Good day! Please tell me, are there any reference to artifact creation in corebook? Or should i homebrew it?<br /> I ask not about corresponding merit, but process itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-07-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:22:14-08:00","id":1294706,"title":"","content":"The Merit itself should provide you with the guidelines to design it as an ST. If you're asking about how to create them in-character, well, you can't. Artefacts aren't designed and created by mages. That would be Imbued Items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T04:43:12-07:00","id":1295763,"title":"","content":"Thenks for ansver.<br /> But i have another question. Should i consider sarcasm (and another means for awoiding to tell the lies) as a lie (for spell Pierce Deception)?<br /> In sort of way:<br /> Mage with the Pierce Deception active spell:<br /> - Was it you who stole hexed cross?<br /> Thief (who truly are stole damn cross) sarcasticaly:<br /> variant a)<br /> - No shit negro, it's was me! Naturally, if I am a thief, then you need to blame me! //thief means lie, but literaly it's truth<br /> variant b)<br /> - No, of cose no! Haw could you think! //thief means truth, but literaly it's lie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-11-2019, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:12:10-07:00","id":1295825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295763#post1295763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thenks for ansver.<br /> But i have another question. Should i consider sarcasm (and another means for awoiding to tell the lies) as a lie (for spell Pierce Deception)?<br /> In sort of way:<br /> Mage with the Pierce Deception active spell:<br /> - Was it you who stole hexed cross?<br /> Thief (who truly are stole damn cross) sarcasticaly:<br /> variant a)<br /> - No shit negro, it's was me! Naturally, if I am a thief, then you need to blame me! //thief means lie, but literaly it's truth<br /> variant b)<br /> - No, of cose no! Haw could you think! //thief means truth, but literaly it's lie</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime doesn't care about sarcasm, and sarcasm doesn't actually avoid lying anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:44:00-07:00","id":1295834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295825#post1295825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime doesn't care about sarcasm, and sarcasm doesn't actually avoid lying anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>this is understandable. If it's Words of Truth then target compelled to tell the truth. But if it's Pierce Deception what mage feel? That target lie when she literaly lie or when she mean to lie? What shoul i say to my players? &quot;She defenetly lie!&quot;? Becose target lie in both variants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:38:00-07:00","id":1295851,"title":"","content":"So define how you are using sarcasm, are you meaning someone says something along the line of \u201cOh really. I imagine you could see me killing this guy right?\u201d That would not register as truthful or a lie since that is more like asking a question. Or you mean someone saying, \u201cI totally killed that guy\u201d in a scarcastic way, this would ring true if they killed the guy because from my understanding the words are what the spell focuses on not the actual intent. As Mrmdubois stated, Prime doesn\u2019t care what context you are using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:19:15-07:00","id":1295968,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked, but I can't find an answer:<br /> <br /> For the spell Crucible, the base spell gives 8-again, the first reach option gives rote quality. Do those effects stack? Like you get rote on the first roll as well as 8 again on the whole dice pool? I'm just not sure if it's in addition to the 8 again, or a replacement for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:56:00-07:00","id":1295993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295763#post1295763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Was it you who stole hexed cross?<br /> Thief (who truly are stole damn cross) sarcasticaly:<br /> variant a)<br /> - No shit negro, it's was me! Naturally, if I am a thief, then you need to blame me! //thief means lie, but literaly it's truth<br /> variant b)<br /> - No, of cose no! Haw could you think! //thief means truth, but literaly it's lie</div> </div> </div> </div>In the first instance, there are two statements. To me that would result in two responses. &quot;No shit it was me&quot; *True* &quot;If I am a thief, then you need to blame me!&quot; *false* <br /> In the second instance, it is clearly a *false* response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T18:23:33-07:00","id":1295999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295968#post1295968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been asked, but I can't find an answer:<br /> <br /> For the spell Crucible, the base spell gives 8-again, the first reach option gives rote quality. Do those effects stack? Like you get rote on the first roll as well as 8 again on the whole dice pool? I'm just not sure if it's in addition to the 8 again, or a replacement for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They stack. Reach options don't modify base effects unless they say that they modify base effects, and contrary to what some people think Rote Action can stack with 8/9-Again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:04:31-07:00","id":1296153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295999#post1295999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They stack. Reach options don't modify base effects unless they say that they modify base effects, and contrary to what some people think Rote Action can stack with 8/9-Again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, but thanks for confirming it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T11:11:27-07:00","id":1296181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295834#post1295834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is understandable. If it's Words of Truth then target compelled to tell the truth. But if it's Pierce Deception what mage feel? That target lie when she literaly lie or when she mean to lie? What shoul i say to my players? &quot;She defenetly lie!&quot;? Becose target lie in both variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Words of Truth doesn't actually compel honesty, it simply makes it so that if you do speak truth to the subject they know it's true and understand the truth you're speaking<br /> <br /> As for Pierce Deception, it will do that, pierce deceptions, if the subject says something misleading the spell will notify the Mage..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T10:01:57-07:00","id":1296439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1295999#post1295999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They stack. Reach options don't modify base effects unless they say that they modify base effects, and contrary to what some people think Rote Action can stack with 8/9-Again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can i ask for some reference about rote action + 8/9 Again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:07:04-07:00","id":1296472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296439#post1296439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i ask for some reference about rote action + 8/9 Again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this. I won't be able to reference the CofD corebook but I could have sworn 8-again and Rote were discouraged from stacking, and it was for-sure discouraged in 1e Mage as &quot;similar effects&quot;, stating these don't stack.<br /> <br /> If they can then great?? But I actually need to know evidence for this, it would be crazy helpful~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:37:10-07:00","id":1296476,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there is no explicit rule that states this allowed. I think I recall a developer stating that you could do so, but it is expressed nowhere in any book that you can get the Rote Action plus 8/9-again. In fact, Rote now removes the default 10 again stating you can only re-roll failures once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:45:13-07:00","id":1296477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296439#post1296439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i ask for some reference about rote action + 8/9 Again?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296472#post1296472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I second this. I won't be able to reference the CofD corebook but I could have sworn 8-again and Rote were discouraged from stacking, and it was for-sure discouraged in 1e Mage as &quot;similar effects&quot;, stating these don't stack.<br /> <br /> If they can then great?? But I actually need to know evidence for this, it would be crazy helpful~</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe evidence is that there is absolutely no evidence to the contrary. Rote Action and 8/9-Again are two separate things that doesn't interfere with each other. The house rule would be saying that they are mutually exclusive, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Some people point towards a particular wording in the Rote Action text, but it's merely an odd wording.<br /> &quot;When you make a roll, you can reroll any dice that do not show an 8, 9, or 10.&quot;<br /> That does not mean you do not reroll 8s, 9, and 10s. It only means that the Rote Action quality doesn't apply to successes.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the official Onyx Path dice app does reroll all X-Again dice when Rote Action is applied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296476#post1296476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there is no explicit rule that states this allowed. I think I recall a developer stating that you could do so, but it is expressed nowhere in any book that you can get the Rote Action plus 8/9-again. In fact, Rote now removes the default 10 again stating you can only re-roll failures once.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's expressed absolutely nowhere that you can't, either (see my above point about the text for Rote Action), and it's absolutely backwards assuming that they can't over assuming that they can when presented with an absence of rules.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's like saying you can't spend both Mana and Willpower on Scrutiny rolls. There doesn't have to be a rule explicitly allowing you to do so. You're already allowed to do so by virtue of there not being a rule against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-13-2019, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:49:17-07:00","id":1296479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296477#post1296477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bThe evidence is that there is absolutely no evidence to the contrary. Rote Action and 8/9-Again are two separate things that doesn't interfere with each other. The house rule would be saying that they are mutually exclusive, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Some people point towards a particular wording in the Rote Action text, but it's merely an odd wording.<br /> &quot;When you make a roll, you can reroll any dice that do not show an 8, 9, or 10.&quot;<br /> That does not mean you do not reroll 8s, 9, and 10s. It only means that the Rote Action quality doesn't apply to successes.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the official Onyx Path dice app does reroll all X-Again dice when Rote Action is applied.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's expressed absolutely nowhere that you can't, either (see my above point about the text for Rote Action), and it's absolutely backwards assuming that they can't over assuming that they can when presented with an absence or rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, it is extremely weird wording. Very interesting they chose to say it that way. I stand corrected and the Onyx Path Die App does do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:52:52-07:00","id":1296481,"title":"","content":"Along the die rolling questions, do two 9-agains stack to an 8-again? I was asked this once and I thought you could have 6 9-again stacking powers and they still result in 1 9-again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:54:57-07:00","id":1296482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296481#post1296481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Along the die rolling questions, do two 9-agains stack to an 8-again? I was asked this once and I thought you could have 6 9-again stacking powers and they still result in 1 9-again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some effects will state that if you already have 9-Again you instead get 8-Again, but if that's not stated you only end up with 9-Again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:57:34-07:00","id":1296483,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that is how I phrased it as well, unless &quot;stated&quot; you never get 8-again from 9-again regarding an ability. There are a few examples I recall reading stating that and I assumed that was a good general rule of thumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T13:50:04-07:00","id":1296501,"title":"","content":"Thanks for previous answers - as i understand Prime work only on literally (in)correct sentences. And i have another question (&gt;_&lt; i have very curious player, who only start playing in CofD and in particular MtAw). Question popup when we discouse cability of 3 and 4 dots of Metter.<br /> Can &quot;you&quot; use Advanced Scale factor for dirrect damage spell? And if yes, can &quot;you&quot; use Advanced Scale factor for object's shrinking?<br /> As if &quot;you&quot; want put in pocket SUV you only need take 1 Reach for Scale Size 5 and -6 for 3 Potency.<br /> Or if &quot;you&quot; want destroy SUV you only need take 1 Reach and -4 for Scale Size 15 factor and roll only 1 sucsess, becose that succses will aply on full volume of veachel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-13-2019, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T14:28:58-07:00","id":1296511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296501#post1296501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can &quot;you&quot; use Advanced Scale factor for dirrect damage spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Not sure why you have doubts about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296501#post1296501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And if yes, can &quot;you&quot; use Advanced Scale factor for object's shrinking?<br /> As if &quot;you&quot; want put in pocket SUV you only need take 1 Reach for Scale Size 5 and -6 for 3 Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need to have enough Scale Factor steps to be able to affect the SUV in the first place. You need to take a -4 penalty to reach Size 15 on the Advanced Scale (assuming a SUV has Size 15; any Size above 6 is extremely nebulous).<br /> <br /> The other problem is that you change the subject's Size by Potency, which is not the same thing as steps along the Scale Factor. Potency 3 will only subtract 3 from Size, making it a Size 12 SUV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296501#post1296501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if &quot;you&quot; want destroy SUV you only need take 1 Reach and -4 for Scale Size 15 factor and roll only 1 sucsess, becose that succses will aply on full volume of veachel.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need one success to have the spell go off as intended. Not sure what you mean by destroy, though. If you're still talking about changing its Size, it'll just turn back to normal when the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:07:18-07:00","id":1296557,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind if you move to Area of Effect for a spell you're going to want to make extra sure you're not in it, or take yourself out via another spell (I think it's in the Fate arcana?). Presumably some mages have died trying to blanket an area with a killing spell unwisely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:06:08-07:00","id":1296577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296477#post1296477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bThe evidence is that there is absolutely no evidence to the contrary. Rote Action and 8/9-Again are two separate things that doesn't interfere with each other. The house rule would be saying that they are mutually exclusive, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Some people point towards a particular wording in the Rote Action text, but it's merely an odd wording.<br /> &amp;quot;When you make a roll, you can reroll any dice that do not show an 8, 9, or 10.&amp;quot;<br /> That does not mean you do not reroll 8s, 9, and 10s. It only means that the Rote Action quality doesn't apply to successes.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the official Onyx Path dice app does reroll all X-Again dice when Rote Action is applied.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's expressed absolutely nowhere that you can't, either (see my above point about the text for Rote Action), and it's absolutely backwards assuming that they can't over assuming that they can when presented with an absence of rules.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's like saying you can't spend both Mana and Willpower on Scrutiny rolls. There doesn't have to be a rule explicitly allowing you to do so. You're already allowed to do so by virtue of there not being a rule against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your help! I am going to look if that rule was in 1E or if I was mislead by someone. Im very excited by this news, I wasn't going off the wording for those descriptors but rather that Mage spells that do the same effect don't stack and was always told that dice tricks are the same effect and can't stack on that principle. If this case is not the same, great.<br /> <br /> Related question though. Is the rule on non-stacking effects purely mechanical? Example, doubling your Speed using Forces and also Time, they have the same effect but very different reasons... Can you stack those or should we *not* stack those because both affect Speed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T23:31:04-07:00","id":1296616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296511#post1296511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only need one success to have the spell go off as intended. Not sure what you mean by destroy, though. If you're still talking about changing its Size, it'll just turn back to normal when the spell ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Main idia about it, when you use <b>targeted </b>spell you need -30 Potency factor or 15 sucsses for full destraction (on 4 dot) of SUV or its shrinking (on 3 dot). But if there three targets you can use Advanced Scale factor to attack/shrinking them. Asume, each target have size 5 and health/structure 7 (i diliberetly leave out durability). For threir transformation/destraction you need take 1 reach for Advanced Scale factor and -10 penalty or 5 sucsses for Potency. In total, you get the same 15 successes (beacose there three targets was affected by spell).<br /> Is it possible to consider each separate volume of size 5 from an SUV as a separate target? Or even each separate volume of size 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:49:34-07:00","id":1296649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296616#post1296616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Main idia about it, when you use <b>targeted </b>spell you need -30 Potency factor or 15 sucsses for full destraction (on 4 dot) of SUV or its shrinking (on 3 dot). But if there three targets you can use Advanced Scale factor to attack/shrinking them. Asume, each target have size 5 and health/structure 7 (i diliberetly leave out durability). For threir transformation/destraction you need take 1 reach for Advanced Scale factor and -10 penalty or 5 sucsses for Potency. In total, you get the same 15 successes (beacose there three targets was affected by spell).<br /> Is it possible to consider each separate volume of size 5 from an SUV as a separate target? Or even each separate volume of size 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean 15 Potency, not 15 successes. Successes are rolled, while Potency is what determines the strength of a spell's effect.<br /> <br /> For transformation you need Potency equal to how much Size you wish to add or remove to the subject (plus extra for Withstand).<br /> <br /> To fill a Health or Structure track with a direct damage spell you need Potency equal to the amount of Health/Structure boxes. If you want complete destruction you'll have to use three times as much Potency for a third dot spell to cause the bashing damage to wrap around to full aggravated damage. Four dot spells generally have a Reach option to deal aggravated damage. If not using that option you need twice as much Potency to make enough lethal damage to wrap around to full aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The SUV is one subject. All spells cast on the SUV must have enough Scale Factor steps to account for its Size. You cannot count it like three separate subjects just like you can't count a human as three separate subjects.<br /> <br /> You also can't divide Size like that. It's an abstract and non-linear measurement. One third of an SUV is still much larger than one human. Similarly, if you take a Size 5 human and chop them up you might end up with 10-15 different Size 1 parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T05:32:47-07:00","id":1296661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296649#post1296649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SUV is one subject. All spells cast on the SUV must have enough Scale Factor steps to account for its Size. You cannot count it like three separate subjects just like you can't count a human as three separate subjects.<br /> <br /> You also can't divide Size like that. It's an abstract and non-linear measurement. One third of an SUV is still much larger than one human. Similarly, if you take a Size 5 human and chop them up you might end up with 10-15 different Size 1 parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>As expected. Thank you. As a whole, the question is settled, further just thinking out loud.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Destroying a skyscraper will be much harder... Just all the discussion came from the question &quot;What degree of power do you need to destroy mega structure&quot;. And then it resulted in optimization.<br /> Then, can i assume, that's mage CAN create 4 degree environmental tilt what can destroy buildings in a fairly short time (scenes? Dozen of rounds?)?<br /> And, as i undestend, mage CAN NOT repeat thing from Ant-m*n 2, where whole laborotory building shrink to suitcase. It's seems slightle imposible even on extendet roll. 75 dices for mana + 30 all yantras (what prohibited as it is) + 10 Gnosis + 5 Arcane + 18 Willpower (each casting round, whats also prohibited) + 5 for extendet casting and we get (if i not forget somethin) only 143 dices. The probability of this effect tends to zero.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-14-2019, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T09:52:53-07:00","id":1296731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296661#post1296661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As expected. Thank you. As a whole, the question is settled, further just thinking out loud.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Destroying a skyscraper will be much harder... Just all the discussion came from the question &quot;What degree of power do you need to destroy mega structure&quot;. And then it resulted in optimization.<br /> Then, can i assume, that's mage CAN create 4 degree environmental tilt what can destroy buildings in a fairly short time (scenes? Dozen of rounds?)?<br /> And, as i undestend, mage CAN NOT repeat thing from Ant-m*n 2, where whole laborotory building shrink to suitcase. It's seems slightle imposible even on extendet roll. 75 dices for mana + 30 all yantras (what prohibited as it is) + 10 Gnosis + 5 Arcane + 18 Willpower (each casting round, whats also prohibited) + 5 for extendet casting and we get (if i not forget somethin) only 143 dices. The probability of this effect tends to zero.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Advanced Scale at default can affect a large house or building, it's beyond the size of a singular object, but there's no reason it can't be shrunk down to the size of a suitcase if you use the AoE rules. You won't be moving the building if you do that, but you can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T09:54:17-07:00","id":1296732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296577#post1296577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question though. Is the rule on non-stacking effects purely mechanical? Example, doubling your Speed using Forces and also Time, they have the same effect but very different reasons... Can you stack those or should we *not* stack those because both affect Speed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hazard to say it's purely mechanical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T16:55:16-07:00","id":1296826,"title":"","content":"When casting Sever Oaths to negate a supernatural agreement, who is the target of the spell? For instance, if a mage wanted to undo a statement Sealed by a changeling, would they cast it on the person whose words were Sealed, or the changeling who made the Sealing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T17:02:14-07:00","id":1296827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1296826#post1296826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When casting Sever Oaths to negate a supernatural agreement, who is the target of the spell? For instance, if a mage wanted to undo a statement Sealed by a changeling, would they cast it on the person whose words were Sealed, or the changeling who made the Sealing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking I'd say whoever the supernatural agreement primarily interacts with. If it would be a spell, who would be the subject to that spell? That's the person who has the effect of the supernatural agreement on themselves and thus the person on whom you need to cast Sever Oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T00:20:30-07:00","id":1296928,"title":"","content":"Either.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019d say a Changeling-sealed oath or a demon Pact is \u201con\u201d both the supernatural being and the oathmaker, so like a Sympaathetic Link it can be ripped off at either end)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T11:04:41-07:00","id":1297033,"title":"","content":"Good day! It's again me. &gt;_&lt;<br /> Now he (player) ask about copy of lie (he's persistent). I try to explayen, that's Pierce Deseption will only triger when charcter know that's he is lying. But there are also material carriers of information AND their copies. Do I understand correctly that the copy will retain the properties of the original?<br /> And if the copy is a script written by the scribe, the information has passed through the scribe and will inherit his idea of the truth. But if through a copier, the copy will have the properties of the original","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-15-2019, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:47:50-07:00","id":1297074,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to understand the rules for summoning a Supernal Entity. But I'm not getting very far.<br /> There is a lot written about summoning in the Mage the Awakening Second Edition book, but I haven't found much about it on the forums.<br /> <br /> Let's make a fairly weak Mage that wants to summon a very powerful Specter.<br /> <br /> The target is a Specter of Stygia called &quot;Utnapishtim&quot;, a Master of Death and Mind.<br /> Am I correct in assuming this must therefor be a Rank 5 Supernal Entity?<br /> <br /> The summoner is a mage who specializes in summoning.<br /> <br /> Relevant stats:<br /> Gil (Gilgamesh)<br /> Path Moros<br /> Gnosis 2, Death 3, Mind 3, Matter 1<br /> Mana 11/2 (total/turn)<br /> <br /> Health 6, Speed 10, Will 10, Wisdom 7, Init 9, Def 6<br /> <br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> <br /> Int 2, Wits 2, Resolve 5<br /> Pres 1, Mani 1, Comp 5<br /> Str 1, Dex 4, Stam 1<br /> <br /> He doesn't scare easily and with his high Initiative and speed he can run away really fast if it comes to that.<br /> When on the job he'll use Mind 2 &quot;Augment Mind&quot; to boost his Intelligence to 5 for however long this is going to take.<br /> <br /> I think for Skills only Occult is relevant and I don't need to stat out the rest.<br /> Occult 5, Skill Specialty Summoning, Asset skill.<br /> <br /> Also lets give him Athletics 4, Skill Specialty Running.<br /> He may end up needing to outrun a Gulmoth after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Arcana<br /> Matter 1, Death 3, Mind 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> High Speech, Order status (SL), Sanctum 1, Safe Place 1, Demesne 3<br /> Professional Training 5 page 106<br /> Profession: Summoner<br /> Networking<br /> Contacts<br /> (his teacher)<br /> Contacts<br /> (another Summoner)<br /> Continuing Education<br /> (9-Again for Asset Skills)<br /> Breath of Knowledge<br /> (Not relevant here)<br /> On the Job Training<br /> (Not relevant here)<br /> The Routine<br /> (Spend Willpower to reroll all failed dice on the first roll)<br /> <br /> <br /> Gil is in his Sanctum in his summoning room. He has no helpers because this is confusing enough as it is.<br /> The room lies in a Demesne.<br /> <br /> Calling up Utnapishtim requires that Gil kows how. Fortunatly another summoner told him all about this powerful Specter.<br /> Gil is a Moros and a Disciple in all paths Utnapishtim has, a requirement for summoning an Entity of Stygia.<br /> <br /> Summoning a Supernal entity is an extended action. Each roll takes an hour.<br /> Starting the ritual costs 2 Mana because Gil has specified that this summon must have Mind as a second Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Gil needs a base of 10 successes to bring the entity across the Abyss and into the Fallen World.<br /> As this is a Rank 5 Entity, we add five successes per Rank of the entity past 1.<br /> The needed total is now 30!<br /> <br /> He wants the Entity to talk to him regarding what tasks it wants in exchange for helping Gil, and on later summonings Gil may ask Utnapishtim to cast a spell for him.<br /> Supernal Entities having infinite Reach can be quite useful. We add 2 needed successes so Utnapishtim can stick around for a hour without taking damage.<br /> 32 successes needed...<br /> <br /> We subtract a whole 3 needed successes because Gil is in a Demesne oriented to the Realm Stygia.<br /> 29 successes needed.<br /> <br /> Gil has his summoning circle in a specially prepared room, themed after Stygia. Wallpaper with ghosts on them, paper skeletons, scented candles (lavender), even a plastic skull he can wave around and brood cryptically over while performing his ritual. That's how you know he's a Professional!<br /> This enviroment lets us roll Intelligence + Occult. Every two successes on this roll removes one success from the target number of the summoning spell. His (boosted) intelligence is 5, his effective occult is 6 because he has a Skill Specialty. He re-rolls the failures because he has the Professional Training Merit.<br /> Lets say he gets 8 successes. We subtract 4 from the summoning total.<br /> 25 successes needed, it seems impossible.<br /> <br /> Here's where I start to get fuzzy on what to do.<br /> <br /> To get the needed successes we need to roll some dice.<br /> The number of rolls we can make is fixed to our Gnosis + Arcana. So 5. This is how it's written in the segment on Extended Actions (page 214).<br /> Our dicepool is also 5.<br /> <br /> If we could keep making rolls after 10 rolls (and 10 hours!) we start risking Abyssal intrusion (page 95).<br /> We get this number from the character's Resolve + Composure + any successes allocated to avoid Abyssal intrusion.<br /> We didn't assign any, would that have been wise? I don't see that being usefull unless you're, say, Gnosis 10, Death 5 and so get 15 rolls.<br /> Even then, you only get an Annunaki poking a tentacle through if you are extremely unlucky.<br /> <br /> Gil gets only 5 rolls anyway. He's at zero risk, barring a Dramatic Failure.<br /> <br /> We are likely to get around 10-12 successes after 5 hours of chanting, dancing and brooding ominously.<br /> I don't see how he could summon this being. Is there no way to get more rolls? Or subtract more from the needed total?<br /> <br /> Gil might just manage a Rank 1 Specter for a hour (12 successes needed). But even at a higher Gnosis, he won't be able to do much more.<br /> Would Teamwork, (page 214) make a diference? Get some more Moros to help? Would they need at least a dot in Mind as well?<br /> Even one of the helpers getting a bad roll is so punishing it seems you might als well start over with the ritual.<br /> <br /> I must be missing something, or misunderstanding something. English is my 2nd language.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Ps; reading posts on the forum is a lot of fun, but making a post takes a lot of effort!<br /> <br /> Pps; More Gnosis, while expensive to get, seems to help al lot. You get 1 extra roll with 1 extra dice per roll for each Gnosis after all.<br /> At Gnosis 5 you average about 24 successes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 03-15-2019, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T14:20:47-07:00","id":1297083,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is difficult. It's supposed to be difficult. You're trying to summon the most powerful type of Supernal entity possible (something that should be difficult/risky for even a Master) with a mage that is barely able to do Supernal summons in the first place. I think you need to check your expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T15:23:38-07:00","id":1297096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297033#post1297033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good day! It's again me. &gt;_&lt;<br /> Now he (player) ask about copy of lie (he's persistent). I try to explayen, that's Pierce Deseption will only triger when charcter know that's he is lying. But there are also material carriers of information AND their copies. Do I understand correctly that the copy will retain the properties of the original?<br /> And if the copy is a script written by the scribe, the information has passed through the scribe and will inherit his idea of the truth. But if through a copier, the copy will have the properties of the original</div> </div> </div> </div>Pierce Deception doesn\u2019t rely on a subject knowing they\u2019re lying, just the presence of a lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T16:22:58-07:00","id":1297109,"title":"","content":"If they don't know it's a lie, then it isn't. The messenger arrives to tell the Lord vampire with his mage adviser that his loyal servent Sandro's is dead. <br /> <br /> Little do they know Sandro's faked his death and hired a street urchin to pass the information to the messenger. Now Sandros was fairly unimportant, the player did not delve further and let it be. The key factor was the vampire no longer used his summon discipline on Sandros. Had he used it, made the roll, the &quot;dead&quot; Sandros would have come a running. <br /> <br /> So this is a real game event setup by one player against another player in league with Sandros. <br /> <br /> At the end of the day the messenger was not lying or providing falsehood. All of his information was second hand. <br /> <br /> Just thought I would share. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:33:20-07:00","id":1297267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297109#post1297109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't know it's a lie, then it isn't. The messenger arrives to tell the Lord vampire with his mage adviser that his loyal servent Sandro's is dead.<br /> <br /> Little do they know Sandro's faked his death and hired a street urchin to pass the information to the messenger. Now Sandros was fairly unimportant, the player did not delve further and let it be. The key factor was the vampire no longer used his summon discipline on Sandros. Had he used it, made the roll, the &quot;dead&quot; Sandros would have come a running.<br /> <br /> So this is a real game event setup by one player against another player in league with Sandros.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the messenger was not lying or providing falsehood. All of his information was second hand.<br /> <br /> Just thought I would share.<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that the spell doesn't necessarily work off of objective truth (this would break the setting and I actually had a whole thing written up about that before realizing it's not the point), I believe, in your example, the spell would still work.<br /> <br /> Unknowingly propagating a lie doesn't change the fact that the scenario in question is an active deception and one that should ping Pierce Deception. The fact that it's being borne by an unknowing pawn doesn't change that fact. What matters, in my opinion, is whether or not the scenario in question is born by an intent to deceive, regardless of where, specifically, that intent originated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:03:35-07:00","id":1297280,"title":"","content":"About that Summoning question, in the mage fictions, a being even less powerful was depicted being summoned by a *group* and the whole city felt it enter our world.<br /> <br /> This 5th rank Spectre is no joke. You're summoning a demi-god, a being worthy of being a true gods avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:17:17-07:00","id":1297285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297280#post1297280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About that Summoning question, in the mage fictions, a being even less powerful was depicted being summoned by a *group* and the whole city felt it enter our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is neat. Where can I read it specifically? Chapter opening fiction or in one of the anthologies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:58:59-07:00","id":1297295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297285#post1297285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is neat. Where can I read it specifically? Chapter opening fiction or in one of the anthologies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Scarlet Witch is referring to the piece of fiction on pg. 74/5 of Summoners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:31:40-07:00","id":1297343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297295#post1297295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Scarlet Witch is referring to the piece of fiction on pg. 74/5 of Summoners.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I'll be sure to read that!<br /> <br /> Do I get a random Supernal Entity every Summon or is it possible to specify which one you get? <br /> <br /> I think lower Rank Entities, and a higher Gnosis will be safer options for the time being. My character will most likely be a Thyrsus if I can convince the ST to work with spirits. That might work if another player takes Spirit as an Arcana to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:15:54-07:00","id":1297366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297343#post1297343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I'll be sure to read that!<br /> <br /> Do I get a random Supernal Entity every Summon or is it possible to specify which one you get?<br /> <br /> I think lower Rank Entities, and a higher Gnosis will be safer options for the time being. My character will most likely be a Thyrsus if I can convince the ST to work with spirits. That might work if another player takes Spirit as an Arcana to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that unless you have worked out or learned of a specific ritual that can summon a specific entity then the results will be somewhat random though will still have the arcana you're allowed to specify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:31:57-07:00","id":1297370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297267#post1297267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that the spell doesn't necessarily work off of objective truth (this would break the setting and I actually had a whole thing written up about that before realizing it's not the point), I believe, in your example, the spell would still work.<br /> <br /> Unknowingly propagating a lie doesn't change the fact that the scenario in question is an active deception and one that should ping Pierce Deception. The fact that it's being borne by an unknowing pawn doesn't change that fact. What matters, in my opinion, is whether or not the scenario in question is born by an intent to deceive, regardless of where, specifically, that intent originated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what your saying, keep in mind I am going from memory (books in another state). I think there are considerations. Maybe with Fate, sympathetic link to the street urchin, sympathetic link to Sandros who are both out of sensory range (let's get some extra reach involved) or maybe extra Arcana. For me it's like looking through a keyhole there no immediate falsehood and I accept that I added the word immediate. If the mage opens the doors views more of the scene, components, links them the falsehoods become apparent. <br /> <br /> It may just be me massaging and interpreting as I want. Was it rank 1 or 2? Can you post the guts of the spell as a paste, you've got me wondering? Is that a forum violation, I'm new to the forums. <br /> <br /> Another thought is it would be difficult to use on the majority of people. Because most pass on details and information thinking they heard the conversation right, but they are wrong or missing information. I feel like the fasehood ometer would always be on. Constant false positives? What do you think. Coworker just told me about a new policy where I work, I was like that makes no sense, I asked the boss and he was like no that is for a different store. Would that be a falsehood?<br /> <br /> Anyway great discussion, you are making me have second thoughts. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:45:25-07:00","id":1297375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297370#post1297370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe with Fate, sympathetic link to the street urchin, sympathetic link to Sandros who are both out of sensory range (let's get some extra reach involved)</div> </div> </div> </div>It really has nothing to do with Sympathy. Fate rules over 'intentions', but if that was necessary the spell as-written would require it already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297370#post1297370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or maybe extra Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much less common in 2E than 1E. This also isn't adding an extra effect or anything, this is how the spell works out of the box.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297370#post1297370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's like looking through a keyhole there no immediate falsehood and I accept that I added the word immediate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's totally reasonable to view it that way, it's just not the interpretation I believe was intended (but I could be wrong, and I could <i>really</i> see it going either way)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297370#post1297370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may just be me massaging and interpreting as I want. Was it rank 1 or 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Knowing (or maybe Unveiling) so it's 1 dot. Note that there's not exactly a direct correlation between dot level and power level/usefulness, it's just based on Practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297370#post1297370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the fasehood ometer would always be on.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the examples is knowing when someone has dyed their hair, so yeah. This sounds about right to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297370#post1297370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coworker just told me about a new policy where I work, I was like that makes no sense, I asked the boss and he was like no that is for a different store. Would that be a falsehood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if there was any intent to deceive along the way. Being mistaken isn't the same thing, but if she was spreading an intentional lie that someone else told her with intent to deceive, and not just spreading misinformation/coming to incorrect conclusions, I'd say so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T16:52:04-07:00","id":1297386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297375#post1297375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>You have given me much too ponder, wish I had my books here. Great discussion. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:42:22-07:00","id":1297399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297343#post1297343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I get a random Supernal Entity every Summon or is it possible to specify which one you get?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's the way it's written. But personally I'd follow Mrmdubois on this as that seems more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T19:05:27-07:00","id":1297418,"title":"","content":"Supernal Summoming has great fluff in 1st Edition!!<br /> <br /> Here's how it works. You roll to get your target successes and if your ST is willing to let you get a named entity, and likely will if your shooting for Supernal Familiar, then you'll get that specific entity. No reason not to if the ST wants to play ball.<br /> <br /> IN GAME, though, Mages have *no idea* what they're going to get, and you can ABSOLUTELY do specific rituals like Mrmboyo said, but, the Mages STILL have no guarantee what will show up.<br /> <br /> The reason is fascinating. Your Summoning is almost analogous to creating a soft-verge or a... Supernal Locus in which Entities might come through, and you attract them like baiting an animal to come out of its hovel. The Summoners book described it as if you attract Supernal entities sense of curiosity about you, and then the first one to take the bait is what shows up.<br /> <br /> So while your rolling dice and accumulating successes you can guess how long you still have to go...<br /> <br /> But the Mage has *no idea* because to them, they're just opening up a resonance to bait something through and hoping it shows up sooner rather than later, it could soon, or *hooouuurs* , with no way of knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T05:26:28-07:00","id":1298565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1297418#post1297418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal Summoming has great fluff in 1st Edition!!<br /> <br /> Here's how it works. You roll to get your target successes and if your ST is willing to let you get a named entity, and likely will if your shooting for Supernal Familiar, then you'll get that specific entity. No reason not to if the ST wants to play ball.<br /> <br /> IN GAME, though, Mages have *no idea* what they're going to get, and you can ABSOLUTELY do specific rituals like Mrmboyo said, but, the Mages STILL have no guarantee what will show up.<br /> <br /> The reason is fascinating. Your Summoning is almost analogous to creating a soft-verge or a... Supernal Locus in which Entities might come through, and you attract them like baiting an animal to come out of its hovel. The Summoners book described it as if you attract Supernal entities sense of curiosity about you, and then the first one to take the bait is what shows up.<br /> <br /> So while your rolling dice and accumulating successes you can guess how long you still have to go...<br /> <br /> But the Mage has *no idea* because to them, they're just opening up a resonance to bait something through and hoping it shows up sooner rather than later, it could soon, or *hooouuurs* , with no way of knowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scarlet Witch is correct, I believe it has been stated that some of the fluff is still usable from 1E Supplemental Books but the mechanical aspects of favors and so forth have changed considerably in 2E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage the Awakening: Summoners pg. 70<br /> Optionally, if the character is aware of a particular being, the Storyteller might allow her to add successes to the summoning spell \u2014 see p. 73 \u2014 to call it.) </div> </div> </div>So, I think it is feasible to summon a specific being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Formatting from copy/pasta. 03-22-2019, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T07:54:49-07:00","id":1298587,"title":"","content":"Also, for anyone curious here are your chances of risking abyssal intrusion when summoning entities of different ranks for a starting Mage based on 5 million simulations:<br /> The following conditions in play: <br /> Gnosis 1, Demesne Bonus, No Paradox, Base Duration, No Sleepers, 3 Occult Bonus (6 successes on Occult Roll), No Abyssal Protection, Resolve and Composure 3<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 0%<br /> Rank 3: 8%<br /> Rank 4: 14%<br /> Rank 5: 32%<br /> <br /> The length of time is probably a good amount requiring some Stamina + Resolve checks I am sure. Based on the percentages, your biggest worry is passing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:14:14-07:00","id":1298672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298587#post1298587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for anyone curious here are your chances of risking abyssal intrusion when summoning entities of different ranks for a starting Mage based on 5 million simulations:<br /> The following conditions in play:<br /> Gnosis 1, Demesne Bonus, No Paradox, Base Duration, No Sleepers, 3 Occult Bonus (6 successes on Occult Roll), No Abyssal Protection, Resolve and Composure 3<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 0%<br /> Rank 3: 8%<br /> Rank 4: 14%<br /> Rank 5: 32%<br /> <br /> The length of time is probably a good amount requiring some Stamina + Resolve checks I am sure. Based on the percentages, your biggest worry is passing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking, you don't get enough rolls with those stats that the ST even gets to roll for Abyssal incursions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:39:21-07:00","id":1298685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298672#post1298672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically speaking, you don't get enough rolls with those stats that the ST even gets to roll for Abyssal incursions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the inverse happens I am afraid because you have more die to roll and get more successes and since the successes are static this only decreases your chance of the abyss. Let's look at high-game (Gnosis 4) then, same conditions as before except you now have Gnosis 4.<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 0%<br /> Rank 3: 4%<br /> Rank 4: 6%<br /> Rank 5: 15%<br /> <br /> Noticeably smaller chance of risking abyssal incursions, my guess is the larger die pool offsets the build up of the dreaded abyssal incursions. It seems the chance of the abyss creeping in gets smaller each gnosis upgrade. Not to mention arcana upgrade, I am still assuming you stayed at Arcana 3. Had you went to Arcana 4, these chances would have dropped even more.<br /> <br /> For giggles, I simulated a Gnosis 8 mage assuming you are a master at that point with your arcana. Aside from Gnosis 8 and Arcana 5, no differences in parameters.<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 0%<br /> Rank 3: 0%<br /> Rank 4: 0%<br /> Rank 5: 0%<br /> <br /> So, essentially you eliminate the abyss from the equation around Gnosis 8, I don't want to run every possible Gnosis but can. The problem is with the abyssal incursion is you have to get as many successes as Gnosis + Arcana with fewer rolls each Gnosis and Arcana upgrade, that is why it levels out at 0% at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Added 8 Gnosis rating. 03-22-2019, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:48:31-07:00","id":1298707,"title":"","content":"No, I mean that with Gnosis 1 and Arcanum 3 (the stats in your initial post) you only have 4 in your base dice pool. That means four rolls total in the summoning action but the combined Resolve + Composure is 6, meaning the ST don't have a chance to roll for Abyssal incursion before the character has run out of rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:06:04-07:00","id":1298717,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see. Fair enough, let's assume subpar stats then. Most Mages will have Resolve and Composure 3, but let's assume they spent their points on other pretty attributes leaving them with Resolve and Composure 2. They use their free Resistance Attribute on Stamina so they can fight good.<br /> <br /> The following conditions in play with 5 million simulations:<br /> Gnosis 1, Demesne Bonus, No Paradox, Base Duration, No Sleepers, 2 Occult Bonus (4 successes on Occult Roll, thus only 2 point reduction), No Abyssal Protection, Resolve and Composure 2, No Willpower Spent<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 7%<br /> Rank 3: 13%<br /> Rank 4: 37%<br /> Rank 5: 56%<br /> <br /> You are correct, at that point summoning a Rank 4-5 supernal being gets dicey at best with a good chance of incurring abyssal incursions. Assuming you don't pass out before then when you get to the 4-5 range anyway.<br /> <br /> If you really want to test some limits, let's say the Mage spends Willpower on each roll until they are out, which should be equal to their Resolve + Composure. Assuming that happens and let's add a 1 Duration Bonus since we don't want the good ol' Supernal Being getting hurt instantly upon landing:<br /> Gnosis 1, Demesne Bonus, No Paradox, 30 Min. Duration, No Sleepers, 2 Occult Bonus, No Abyssal Protection, Resolve &amp; Composure 2, Using All Willpower<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 1%<br /> Rank 3: 6%<br /> Rank 4: 26%<br /> Rank 5: 40%<br /> <br /> With all those factors, it is pretty safe at Rank 4, and a moderate chance at Rank 5. It is looking much better than before.<br /> <br /> Let's say you have fairly decent Willpower, Resolve 2 &amp; Composure 3. Given the same conditions the following is your chance of letting the abyss into your summoning:<br /> Gnosis 1, Demesne Bonus, 2 Occult Bonus, 30 Min. Duration, No Paradox, No Abyssal Protection, Resolve 2, Composure 3, Using all Willpower<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 0%<br /> Rank 3: 5%<br /> Rank 4: 14%<br /> Rank 5: 27%<br /> <br /> Let's say you went extreme and have an exceptional willpower, Resolve 3 &amp; Composure 4. Given the same conditions the following is your chance of letting the abyss into your summoning:<br /> Gnosis 1, Demesne Bonus, 2 Occult Bonus, 30 Min. Duration, No Paradox, No Abyssal Protection, Resolve 3, Composure 4, Using all Willpower<br /> Rank 1: 0%<br /> Rank 2: 0%<br /> Rank 3: 2%<br /> Rank 4: 5%<br /> Rank 5: 15%<br /> <br /> All in all, summoning Supernal Beings is a pretty safe bet for even the weakest of mages and a sure thing for moderately willed mages. With an exceptionally willed mage it is nothing to summon an extremely powerful supernal being.<br /> <br /> Based on my calculations, Abyssal Protection changes your odds by about 2% for every 1 success dedicated. This is pretty laughable given how rare it is for a moderately powered mage to summon a powerful supernal being and let the abyss slip in. You might use it in the event you want to have a long duration for the supernal being to be safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Added additional parameters. 03-22-2019, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T16:54:30-07:00","id":1298784,"title":"","content":"Ah, but how likely is it that a Gnosis 1 mage will succeed on the summoning? Even though the chance of an abyssal intrusion is 0%, you still need to get enough successes to actually summon something.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Arcana 3 gives you 4 rolls of 4 dice.<br /> Summoning a Rank 1 Supernal Entity takes 10 successes.<br /> A Rank 5 takes 10+(5x4)=30.<br /> Your only options to reduce this a bit are -3 for a Demesne and half the successes of rolling Intelligence+Occult.<br /> <br /> To really have a chance I think you need Gnosis + Arcana to come to 9 or 10 at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 03-22-2019, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:10:41-07:00","id":1298787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298784#post1298784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but how likely is it that a Gnosis 1 mage will succeed on the summoning? Even though the chance of an abyssal intrusion is 0%, you still need to get enough successes to actually summon something.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Arcana 3 gives you 4 rolls of 4 dice.<br /> Summoning a Rank 1 Supernal Entity takes 10 successes.<br /> A Rank 5 takes 10+(5x4)=30.<br /> Your only options to reduce this a bit are -3 for a Demesne and half the successes of rolling Intelligence+Occult.<br /> <br /> To really have a chance I think you need Gnosis + Arcana to come to 9 or 10 at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, as long as you don't risk Abyssal Intrusion you succeed. So, subtract the abyssal intrusion from 100% and that is your chance of summoning a Supernal Being of the specified rank successfully. You have no limit on the rolls you can make, you just have a Safe Limit, which is equal to Resolve + Composure + successes allocated for Abyssal Intrusion Protection. Your main goal is to remove as much required successes as possible and increasing your die pool as much as you can.<br /> <br /> Based on a Starting Mage with Gnosis 1, Arcana 3, Resolve 3, Composure 2, No Paradox for the week, a Demesne assigned to the path, no duration bonus, 4 successes on their occult roll, no other mage involved, no sleepers, and spending all willpower will summon a Rank 1 Supernal Being in 2 turns with 0% abyssal intrusion chance.<br /> The same mage with the same parameters would summon a Rank 2 Supernal Being in 4 turns with a 1% abyssal intrusion chance (basically meaning 1% of the time required more than the 5 Safe Turns) This means 99% chance of success<br /> The same mage with the same parameters would summon a Rank 3 Supernal Being in 6 turns with a 5% abyssal intrusion chance. 95% chance of success<br /> The same mage with the same parameters would summon a Rank 4 Supernal Being in 8 turns with a 13% abyssal intrusion chance. 87% chance of success<br /> The same mage with the same parameters would summon a Rank 5 Supernal Being in 11 turns with a 25% abyssal intrusion chance. 75% chance of success","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Spelling error. 03-22-2019, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:17:50-07:00","id":1298790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298787#post1298787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have no limit on the rolls you can make</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Systems: Summoning a Supernal entity is an extended action,<br /> and is subject to the same rules as other such actions <span style=\"color:#004E6D\">(see p. 214)</span>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Make a note of your<br /> Attribute + Skill + Specialty (if any); that\u2019s the maximum number<br /> of times you can roll before the action fails.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most books just says to use the base dice pool as the limit, which would be Gnosis+Arcanum in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:21:24-07:00","id":1298792,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I guess I misunderstood Abyssal Intrusions assuming you had no limit. Then they really want this to be a group event, but even then to summon a Rank 3-5 supernal being requires a considerable number of mages, perhaps a consilium's worth. I thought summoning was meant to be a solo act based on the 1E Summoners.<br /> <br /> Edit: I checked, in 1E Summoners you had no limit. So, that added to my confusion. You can safely summon 1-2 Rank beings no problem, but I would say a Rank 5 would require at least a cabal worth of similar Mages. Really is odd to me they made such a change when summoning was meant to be a personal thing. *shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 03-22-2019, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:43:30-07:00","id":1298826,"title":"","content":"So, based on 10 million simulations, and a cabal of 6 very similar mages in Gnosis &amp; Arcana Rating all with the same Path. All of these mages are going all out spending willpower and we shall assume the same conditions mentioned in the previous instances. They will have the following chance to summon a supernal being of the particular rank as indicated below:<br /> Rank 1: ~93% within 1 turn (seen variations of up to +2%)<br /> Rank 2: 89% within 1 turn<br /> Rank 3: ~78% within 2 turns (seen variations of up to +2%)<br /> Rank 4: ~69% within 3 turns (seen variations of up to -1%)<br /> Rank 5: ~49% within 3 turns (seen variations of up to -2%)<br /> <br /> This assumes the Teamwork where each success from a Mage adds 1 die to the lead Mage's die pool.<br /> <br /> 0% Abyssal Intrusion for all of these.<br /> <br /> This is my problem with Abyssal Intrusion if Summoning works like other Teamwork and Extended Actions, it is 0% always. The only way you could have any chance of this happening is you literally have 1 Resolve &amp; 1 Composure. Even then it is highly highly unlikely that you will ever invite the abyss into your summoning. This makes me think that something is wrong here and they intended to add the clause &quot;You can spend as many rounds possible summoning and unlike other Extended Actions, Summoning works on the interval of the lead Mage's gnosis.&quot; This would make sense and actually have some bearing on some sort of consequences.<br /> <br /> I personally would use 1E's Summoning Rules found in Summoners. That makes more sense because there is a risk of Abyssal Intrusion, you can summon any Rank Entity assuming you are awake when you succeed, and it can be solo'd but is much easier with a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 03-22-2019, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T20:45:09-07:00","id":1298836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298826#post1298826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we shall assume the same conditions mentioned in the previous instances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those conditions include rolling four successes on an Attribute + Skill roll.<br /> <br /> That's something that has roughly sixty percent odds of happening on a roll of ten dice with 8-Again.<br /> <br /> It therefore should <i>probably</i> not be taken for granted in these simulations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T22:46:59-07:00","id":1298852,"title":"","content":"Either i fuck in my eyes or i don't understand, why summoning of more ranked spirit should be more paradoxical? As far as I understand, this imposes a larger penalty (especially if there is not a single sympathetic link with the spirit). But this does not require additional reaches.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Systems: Summoning a Supernal entity is an extended action,<br /> and is subject to the same rules as other such actions <span style=\"color:#004E6D\">(see p. 214)</span>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Make a note of your<br /> Attribute + Skill + Specialty (if any); that\u2019s the maximum number<br /> of times you can roll before the action fails.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most books just says to use the base dice pool as the limit, which would be Gnosis+Arcanum in this case. </div> </div> </div>As i read when you cast as extended action, you do not roll as many times as you have a basic dicepool, but simply add +5 at maximum (+1 per &quot;round&quot;, &quot;Casting Time&quot; p. 114).<br /> <br /> ....... Or it's all about first edition?<br /> Summoning entities less paradoxical in 2ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-23-2019, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T00:21:01-07:00","id":1298873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298852#post1298852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either i fuck in my eyes or i don't understand, why summoning of more ranked spirit should be more paradoxical? As far as I understand, this imposes a larger penalty (especially if there is not a single sympathetic link with the spirit). But this does not require additional reaches.<br /> <br /> As i read when you cast as extended action, you do not roll as many times as you have a basic dicepool, but simply add +5 at maximum (+1 per &quot;round&quot;, &quot;Casting Time&quot; p. 114).<br /> <br /> ....... Or it's all about first edition?<br /> Summoning entities less paradoxical in 2ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The conversation is about summoning Supernal entities, not about spirits. Totally different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T03:01:44-07:00","id":1298888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298836#post1298836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those conditions include rolling four successes on an Attribute + Skill roll.<br /> <br /> That's something that has roughly sixty percent odds of happening on a roll of ten dice with 8-Again.<br /> <br /> It therefore should <i>probably</i> not be taken for granted in these simulations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not include die tricks for this scenario because not every Path has access to one. Does not change the argument about Abyssal Intrusion though. You just don't have enough dice to roll to make it happen, ever. If you are referencing Abyssal Intrusion it doesn't get 8-again ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 03-23-2019, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T03:12:58-07:00","id":1298895,"title":"","content":"Let's make a Mage that wants to summon a very powerfull Specter.<br /> <br /> The target is a Specter of Stygia called &quot;Utnapishtim&quot;, a Master of Death and Mind.<br /> A Supernal Entity can cast spells up to its Rank.<br /> <br /> Relevant stats:<br /> Gil (Gilgamesh)<br /> Path Moros<br /> Gnosis 5, Death 3, Mind 3, Matter 1<br /> Mana 15/5 (total/turn)<br /> Will 10<br /> Int 5, Resolve 5, Comp 5<br /> Occult 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Preparations:<br /> <br /> He'll use Mind 2 &quot;Augment Mind&quot; to boost his Intelligence, Resolve and Composure to 5 for a week.<br /> <br /> He is using a Demesne from a Cabal member or his Order, he has spent some time preparing it for this summoning so he can improve his chances.<br /> <br /> Gil has no helpers because this is complicated enough as it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Calling up Utnapishtim requires that Gil knows how. Fortunatly another summoner told him all about this powerful Specter.<br /> Gil is a Moros and a Disciple in all paths Utnapishtim has, a requirement for summoning an Entity of Stygia.<br /> <br /> Summoning a Supernal entity is an extended action. Each roll takes an hour.<br /> Starting the ritual costs 2 Mana because Gil has specified that this summon must have Mind as a second Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Gil needs a base of 10 successes to bring the entity across the Abyss and into the Fallen World.<br /> As this is a Rank 5 Entity, we add five successes per Rank of the entity past 1.<br /> The needed total is now 30!<br /> <br /> He wants the Entity to talk to him regarding what tasks it wants in exchange for helping Gil, and on later summonings Gil may ask Utnapishtim to cast a spell for him.<br /> Supernal Entities having infinite Reach can be quite useful. We add 1 needed successes so Utnapishtim can stick around for a half-hour without taking damage.<br /> 31 successes needed...<br /> <br /> Gil does not assign any successes to reduce the chance of an Abyssal Intrusion.<br /> <br /> We subtract a whole 3 needed successes because Gil is in a Demesne oriented to the Realm Stygia.<br /> 28 successes needed.<br /> <br /> Gil has his summoning circle in a specially prepared room, themed after Stygia. Wallpaper with ghosts on them, paper skeletons, scented candles (lavender), even a plastic skull he can wave around and brood cryptically over while performing his ritual. <br /> This enviroment lets us roll Intelligence + Occult. Every two successes on this roll removes one success from the target number of the summoning spell. His (boosted) intelligence is 5, his Skill in Occult is 5.<br /> So 10 dice.<br /> He spends 1 Willpower point on the roll for +3 dice.<br /> Lets say he gets 4 successes (1 success per 3 dice). We subtract half, so 2 from the summoning total.<br /> <br /> 26 successes needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Summoning:<br /> <br /> To get the needed successes for the summon, we need to roll some dice.<br /> The number of rolls we can make is fixed to our Gnosis (5) + Arcana (3). So 8. This is how it's written in the segment on Extended Actions (page 214).<br /> Our dicepool is also Gnosis + Arcana, so 8.<br /> <br /> Gil spends 8 of his remaining 9 Willpower on these rolls for +3 dice per roll.<br /> <br /> 8 rolls of 11 dice.<br /> We are likely to get around 32 successes after 8 hours of chanting, dancing and brooding ominously.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Abyss:<br /> <br /> We start risking Abyssal intrusion (page 95) after 10 rolls (Resolve + Composure + any successes allocated to avoid Abyssal intrusion).<br /> <br /> On every subsequent roll, the Storyteller rolls the character\u2019s unmodified Gnosis (5). If the Storyteller accrues a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s Gnosis + the primary Arcanum in the summoning (8), then the Abyss breaks into the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Gil gets 8 summoning rolls. He's at no risk. He gets 0 &quot;Intrusion&quot; rolls of 5 dice. On 8 successes he gets an Intruder.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T03:51:37-07:00","id":1298901,"title":"","content":"Here is your chance of summoning Utnapishtim without any aid from a friendly mage to boost your die rolls: ~60% in 7 turns<br /> If Gil was a Master without 8-again: ~88% in 7 turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Read your post wrong and I apologize, I did not see you had already account for no intrusion. 03-23-2019, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T04:59:34-07:00","id":1298916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298873#post1298873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversation is about summoning Supernal entities, not about spirits. Totally different things.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\uff20_\uff20) </span></span>I am nearly lost... What's the bloody difference (in terms of mechanism)? Specters and ghosts (kerberois as well) can be summoned on third dot of Death. Goetia - on third dot of Mind... Abyssal creature can be summoned on five successes on Paradox Roll (what can be made delibiraitly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T05:03:31-07:00","id":1298917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298916#post1298916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\uff20_\uff20) </span></span>I am nearly lost... What's the bloody difference (in terms of mechanism)? Specters and ghosts (kerberois as well) can be summoned on third dot of Death. Goetia - on third dot of Mind... Abyssal creature can be summoned on five successes on Paradox Roll (what can be made delibiraitly).</div> </div> </div> </div>OsuNeko, well, the big difference is summoning those entities are spells with Reach Options and have spell casting rules. Summoning Supernal Beings is not really a spell, but rather a ritual using extended actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T05:18:15-07:00","id":1298919,"title":"","content":"Link very please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T05:22:02-07:00","id":1298921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298919#post1298919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Link very please!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I am unaware if there is an online resource containing this data. I know it is on page 94 of the Mage 2E Core Rulebook near the bottom right corner of the page is where it starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:02:43-07:00","id":1298928,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> But for what bloody means you need summon some <s>unknown fucking shit</s> <s>abyssal</s> supernal entities through ritual when you can summone suitable entities through common means with more chances on successes and lesser chances on paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-23-2019, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:09:25-07:00","id":1298930,"title":"","content":"Supernal Beings can perform feats that other entities can't do like bring artifacts down or give you knowledge about the Arcana to help you advance faster. They are also less likely to hold a grudge against you since they go back to the Supernal and I assume forget about you, but who knows, maybe they will hold grudges if you deal with them wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:10:18-07:00","id":1298931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298928#post1298928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> But for what bloody means you need summon some <s>unknown fucking shit</s> [s]abyssal[/] supernal entities through rutual when you can summone suitable entities through common means with more chances on successes and lesser chances on paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal entities generally have information that is very useful in one way or another that most ephemeral entities really couldn't know. Supernal entities can also, rarely, bring an Artefact with them. They're also capable of casting spells, meaning a mage at three dot in any Arcanum may be able to summon a spellcaster with up to five dots in the same Arcanum on top of Supernal entities having infinite Reaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:10:30-07:00","id":1298932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298928#post1298928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> But for what bloody means you need summon some <s>unknown fucking shit</s> [s]abyssal[/] supernal entities through rutual when you can summone suitable entities through common means with more chances on successes and lesser chances on paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try reading the section. The reasons why are in literally the first paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:52:43-07:00","id":1298937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298901#post1298901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is your chance of summoning Utnapishtim without any aid from a friendly mage to boost your die rolls: ~60% in 7 turns<br /> If Gil was a Master without 8-again: ~88% in 7 turns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! Do those numbers change if I take my time summoning? The rules claim it can take hours, not turns.<br /> <br /> Mage The Awakening 2nd Edition, Page 95:<br /> Systems: Summoning a Supernal entity is an extended action,<br /> and is subject to the same rules as other such actions (see p. 214).<br /> Dice Pool: Gnosis + Arcanum<br /> Action: Extended (see below for required successes;<b> each roll<br /> is one hour)</b><br /> Cost: 1 Mana, 2 if specifying a second Arcanum<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298928#post1298928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> But for what bloody means you need summon some <s>unknown fucking shit</s> <s>abyssal</s> supernal entities through ritual when you can summone suitable entities through common means with more chances on successes and lesser chances on paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but using Spirit to summon spirits, or Death to summon ghosts, or Mind to summon Goetia, gives you an entity from the Fallen world.<br /> Summoning a Supernal Entity from the Supernal Realms give you a being that can cast supernal magic. Like a mage but without the limitations.<br /> <br /> For example,<br /> If you want to travel back in time to before you where born, the Time Arcanum cannot do that for you. But a Supernal Entity of Rank 3 can cast the spell for you, with infinite free Reach and almost no limits!<br /> <br /> If you need an Adept or Master level spell cast for you and you are not an Adept or Master, and you can't trust any Master mages to do it for you, a Supernal Entity of Rank 5 can do it for you.<br /> <br /> Do you need a spell to cover more area than you can Reach? Instead of blowing yourself up with Paradox trying to increase the area of effect, summon an Entity with infinite free Reach!<br /> <br /> It will want a favor of you. And summoning it will be difficult (but not very risky). But summoning Supernal Entities can be very useful.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of summoning from a Supernal Realm are a bit different than just casting spells to call ghosts or goetia or spirits from the Shadow.<br /> See page 94 of Mage The Awakening 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 03-23-2019, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:24:57-07:00","id":1298948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298888#post1298888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not include die tricks for this scenario because not every Path has access to one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I'm saying that it's a bad idea to assume four successes on a roll that isn't going to average four successes even with the deck stacked heavily in its favor.<br /> <br /> Your conditions present an absurdly optimized scenario where you assume the character always succeeds at a coin toss, only ever uses prime magical real estate, can enlist the aid of five other mages with identical capabilities to their own, burns through their Willpower and gets their allies to do the same, and has minimal to zero concern about their summoned entity <i>immediately getting weaker</i>.<br /> <br /> As an extended action, summoning takes an hour per roll and every time you fail a roll you have to take a Condition or start over from the beginning. Without spending Willpower on every single roll in the process, most characters have a chance ranging from one-in-ten to one-in-twenty of failing any given roll in that process. You don't think the results of failure in a delicate process like Supernal summoning might have an impact on the chances of something going wrong?<br /> <br /> This is a process for summoning a time-limited entity with a prerequisite for its support. Most mages performing a Supernal summoning are not doing so just to get the guest of honor to show up, and Abyssal intrusion represents a rare disastrous outcome in the first place. The outside possibility that your attempt to evoke an intermediate forge-god instead draws down an alien thing with bones of molten glass is there to make the attempt a tense process, not to deter you from attempting it at all, and using almost literally the best possible scenario for checking the likelihood of it happening is bad math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:30:50-07:00","id":1298951,"title":"","content":"mnnnn ... it seems I became a victim of my own habit to pervert with the metaplot: I could hardly see the difference between entities (The Influence is comparable to Arcanes, as if the slippers spirit had the Slippers Arcane). I should take this into concideration.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298937#post1298937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will want a favor of you. And summoning it will be difficult (but not very risky). But summoning Supernal Entities can be very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can hardly imagine that True Fay or Demon or Angel do any thing for mage \u200bexcept if it is necessary to themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-23-2019, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:46:13-07:00","id":1298952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298948#post1298948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip<br /> Your conditions present an absurdly optimized scenario<br /> snip<br /> using almost literally the best possible scenario for checking the likelihood of it happening is bad math.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying. But if you're planning to something so risky, and have time to prepare, would a mage not stack the deck as much as possible? Mind spells to boost stats, Demesne and a prepared summoning circle, you would want to mitigate the risks of failure or intrusion as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Things get really interesting when you have to improvise and can't get an optimal situation. But considering the risks, would a player (not character) really risk it? At some point using Order Status, Mentor or trading favors for help becomes a better solution for the characters. But that becomes less interesting to the players.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12029\" data-vbnamecard=\"12029\">OsuNeko</a>, Entities that are not interested will refuse to be summoned.<br /> So if a being shows up when summoned, it must be interested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bribe it with Tass or other gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 03-23-2019, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:51:33-07:00","id":1298953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298952#post1298952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But considering the risks, would a player (not character) really risk it? At some point using Order Status, Mentor or trading favors for help becomes a better solution for the characters. But that becomes less interesting to the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>At some point you have to recognize the issues of time crunch and limited resources. Do you imagine the Storyteller is going to put upcoming events on hold for a week so your character can time out that Paradox they racked up or wait for five other Moros to clear their schedules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:58:29-07:00","id":1298954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298951#post1298951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can hardly imagine that True Fay or Demon or Angel do any thing for mage \u200bexcept if it is necessary to themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily you're not summoning True Fae, demons and angels from other games or as they're described in IRL mythology. You're summoning Fae, Demons and Angels, the Supernal entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T08:26:52-07:00","id":1298959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298951#post1298951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mnnnn ... it seems I became a victim of my own habit to pervert with the metaplot: I could hardly see the difference between entities (The Influence is comparable to Arcanes, as if the slippers spirit had the Slippers Arcane). I should take this into concideration.<br /> <br /> Can hardly imagine that True Fay or Demon or Angel do any thing for mage \u200bexcept if it is necessary to themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal entities have a Trial, a test they put to Mages, it can be as simple as being polite, or unafraid, or as hard as never acting without compassion or always speaking the truth. If you pass the Trial they give you their boon. The Trial shows that a Mage understands the Supernal entity\u2019s symbolism, if you can do that they make pretty free with the magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T08:39:53-07:00","id":1298965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298948#post1298948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. I'm saying that it's a bad idea to assume four successes on a roll that isn't going to average four successes even with the deck stacked heavily in its favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never really said this was the case, don't know where you are getting this from. I have no idea what the average # of successes are for the 50 million simulations I ran. Would be a headache if I do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your conditions present an absurdly optimized scenario where you assume the character always succeeds at a coin toss, only ever uses prime magical real estate, can enlist the aid of five other mages with identical capabilities to their own, burns through their Willpower and gets their allies to do the same, and has minimal to zero concern about their summoned entity <i>immediately getting weaker</i>. </div> </div> </div>This was before the condition thing, so I see where you are coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an extended action, summoning takes an hour per roll and every time you fail a roll you have to take a Condition or start over from the beginning. Without spending Willpower on every single roll in the process, most characters have a chance ranging from one-in-ten to one-in-twenty of failing any given roll in that process. You don't think the results of failure in a delicate process like Supernal summoning might have an impact on the chances of something going wrong?<br /> <br /> This is a process for summoning a time-limited entity with a prerequisite for its support. Most mages performing a Supernal summoning are not doing so just to get the guest of honor to show up, and Abyssal intrusion represents a rare disastrous outcome in the first place. The outside possibility that your attempt to evoke an intermediate forge-god instead draws down an alien thing with bones of molten glass is there to make the attempt a tense process, not to deter you from attempting it at all, and using almost literally the best possible scenario for checking the likelihood of it happening is bad math. </div> </div> </div>Ah, I had not considered gaining a Condition, you are correct. So, you can take a Condition or give up then and there. Interesting potentials, thanks for this Satchel. I imagine the Condition is Supernal in nature, maybe it subtracts 1-2 from your die rolling if you continue. Perhaps it increases in penalty each time, I see where you are going with this. Perhaps your safe rolls decreases by 1 each round giving a greater chance to your abyssal incursion, that could work as well.<br /> <br /> In that case, Summoning Supernal Beings could be dangerous if you failed 1 round. With a die pool of 4 that is probably going to be somewhere in the neighborhood of 24% based on probability. So, literally 1/4 rolls you will get a Condition. However, spending Willpower each round will net you a set of 7 die pool making this chance to 1 in 10. However, since this is an extended action and not spell casting you could get the Rote Quality on the die pool. This would reduce your chance of getting a failure to less 1 in 100. Those odds are looking pretty good. If we assumed Rote Condition plus 8-again quality even with 4 die you are going to do a pretty good job of never risking an abyssal intrusion and this is all possible with starting characters.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, team up with an Acanthus to give you some buffs or get yourself an imbued item that does the very best.<br /> <br /> So, let's do a non-optimized scenario. Let's take 1 Mage with Resolve 2, Composure 2, Gnosis 1, Arcana Rating 3 and knows a buddy Acanthus. He doesn't want to waste the willpower dot on a demesne bonus, but he hasn't invoked a Paradox within the last week so he doesn't take that penalty. He gets Rote Quality plus 8-again on his rolls and decides to take a crack at summoning a Supernal Being. They decide an hour long chat should be enough and plan to increase the duration by 2, they also get an Occult Bonus luckily with 1 reducing their successes by 1 to counter one point of duration. For the purposes a Condition Chance is ST Fiat, you may decide to invite Abyssal Intrusion or basically cause the summoning to essentially fail since there are no RAW mechanics on how this should work when summoning a Supernal Being.<br /> <br /> Here are the results given all the above, and let's just say for this instance they don't use willpower, his chance of success is the following:<br /> Rank 1: 33% Summon Success, 35% Condition Chance* (maybe multiple), 0% default Abyssal Intrusion<br /> <br /> *Condition chance considers at least 1 failure happening during all the die rolls<br /> <br /> So, yeah a novice probably should not try summoning a Supernal Being for sure, unless they plan on going all out as the success is determined down below.<br /> <br /> If they spent willpower this is the result they would have:<br /> Rank 1: 82% Summon Success, 3% Condition Chance, 0% default Abyssal Intrusion<br /> <br /> If they used a Demesne associated with the correct path and don't spend willpower this is the results:<br /> Rank 1: 71% Summon Success, 29% Condition Chance, 0% default Abyssal Intrusion<br /> <br /> If they used a Demesne associated with the correct path and spend willpower this is the results:<br /> Rank 1: 95% Summon Success, 2% Condition Chance, 0% default Abyssal Intrusion<br /> <br /> So, get a Demesne, get some willpower, and some die tricks if you are low powered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T08:56:35-07:00","id":1298971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1298965#post1298965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never really said this was the case, don't know where you are getting this from. I have no idea what the average # of successes are for the 50 million simulations I ran. Would be a headache if I do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel is talking about the Int+Occult roll that you've stated grants +2 to the summoning roll. For that you need four or five successes. You need at least twelve dice in order to get four successes on average (if not including any dice tricks). It's possible for a starting mage that has maxed those two traits, used one Specialty on Supernal summoning/entities, and one Merit dot on Area of Expertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T09:02:38-07:00","id":1298972,"title":"","content":"Ah ok, my bad. Yeah, I reduced the Occult Roll to just 2 successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T23:48:48-07:00","id":1299143,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I'm hoping you can tell me a bit more about Goetia, because what's in the core book seems to be lacking. Specifically, how do you run them as supporting NPCs and antagonists? What would you expect from an encounter with one in someone's Oneiros versus the Tenemos versus the real world? What do they want from people? I want to understand what makes them interesting and engaging to players, more than just another type of ephemera that can be bent to the player's will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:39:58-07:00","id":1299221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299143#post1299143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, I'm hoping you can tell me a bit more about Goetia, because what's in the core book seems to be lacking. Specifically, how do you run them as supporting NPCs and antagonists? What would you expect from an encounter with one in someone's Oneiros versus the Tenemos versus the real world? What do they want from people? I want to understand what makes them interesting and engaging to players, more than just another type of ephemera that can be bent to the player's will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Astral book from 1e? That covers a lot of it. Summoners has some more info.<br /> <br /> One of the key features is that if you pull a goetia from an Oneiros the person stops being affected by it completely. Like say you yank out their goetia of anger, they\u2019ll not be angry again until it\u2019s put back, if you kill it they won\u2019t be angry until it has a chance to regrow. <br /> <br /> They\u2019re not as overtly predatory as spirits are. Typically you just don\u2019t see them in the Fallen because they don\u2019t normally have a means of leaving the Astral and don\u2019t have Manifestations when they do, though exceptions exist like in the L.A. setting.<br /> <br /> In the Oneiros the weaker ones aren\u2019t very well established characters, they\u2019re actors that grab roles relevant to the scene being played out in the Oneiros at the moment and their role is indistinguishable from themselves. There are more established and stable goetic like Virtue or Vice, etc. Typically what any goetia wants is to expand its influence, they can be similar to spirits like that, but their Influences are really the only way to directly influence a person most of the time.<br /> <br /> Goetia in the Temenos tend to be more stable like the greater goetia in the Oneiros. They\u2019re more nuanced too because they\u2019re fed by the ideas of more than just one person. They are living repositories of information and symbolism, and they want to get that information out on an instinctive level. Since they\u2019re not spirit\u2019s starved for Essence they\u2019ll typically do this for free, whether or not you want them too. They\u2019ll do what\u2019s appropriate for their character to disseminate it which may or may not be in a friendly way. Some particularly powerful goetia can induce permanent shifts in the ideology of people who happen across them.<br /> <br /> In the Anima Mundi things get more intense and primal, but it can be an even greater resource for information that doesn\u2019t fall under the domain of human knowledge. A tiger goetia may want to spread understanding of tigers, not humanity\u2019s conception of tigers, but the shit tigers know about themselves. It might eat you to do this, but you might be able to avoid that by becoming or demonstrating acceptable levels of tiger-ness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-24-2019, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:26:16-07:00","id":1299287,"title":"","content":"I have a question: when character take rote spell with weaponry/brawl skill AND take Adamantin Hand, that character can benefit twice from skill or only once when casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:35:26-07:00","id":1299292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299287#post1299287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question: when character take rote spell with weaponry/brawl skill AND take Adamantin Hand, that character can benefit twice from skill or only once when casting?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re misreading how Adamant Hand works. It doesn\u2019t apply the skill to a spell as a Yantra. It allows you to take an action with one of the listed skills and then count that as a Reflexive +1 Order Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:36:24-07:00","id":1299293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299287#post1299287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question: when character take rote spell with weaponry/brawl skill AND take Adamantin Hand, that character can benefit twice from skill or only once when casting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the intention is That Adamant Hand only gives you +1 as if it were an Order Tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T20:43:17-07:00","id":1299836,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked before, but:<br /> Casting at sympathetic range: Does it need 1 reach or 2? It looks like it's one reach to go from touch to sensory, and then another reach to go from sensory to sympathetic. Is that correct?<br /> <br /> The book says, &quot;<br /> \u2022 Move the spell from touch/self to sensory range<br /> \u2022If at sensory range, allow the mage to cast on a subject she is viewing remotely&quot;<br /> <br /> But maybe viewing remotely is different? The bit on sympathetic range just says &quot;To use this Attainment, the mage must be casting a spell at sensory range, use a sympathy Yantra, and spend one Mana&quot;. No extra reach. Is that correct, instead? I think that's correct but I'm not 100%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13524-ruadni","name":"Ruadni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:13:28-07:00","id":1299847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299836#post1299836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But maybe viewing remotely is different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Viewing remotely is for looking through a live video feed, scrying window, etc.<br /> <br /> <s>It takes 2 Reach to use sympathetic range. One for sensory, and one for the Attainment itself.</s><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  This is wrong, see below 03-26-2019, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:15:23-07:00","id":1299848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299836#post1299836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been asked before, but:<br /> Casting at sympathetic range: Does it need 1 reach or 2? It looks like it's one reach to go from touch to sensory, and then another reach to go from sensory to sympathetic. Is that correct?<br /> <br /> The book says, &quot;<br /> \u2022 Move the spell from touch/self to sensory range<br /> \u2022If at sensory range, allow the mage to cast on a subject she is viewing remotely&quot;<br /> <br /> But maybe viewing remotely is different? The bit on sympathetic range just says &quot;To use this Attainment, the mage must be casting a spell at sensory range, use a sympathy Yantra, and spend one Mana&quot;. No extra reach. Is that correct, instead? I think that's correct but I'm not 100%.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, there are two ways to cast a spell on a target that's outside of sensory range. One way is to cast remotely, this requires spending a Reach to make the spell sensory range and another Reach to cast the spell through whatever is allowing you to remotely view your subject in real time, be it a security camera or a scrying window. The other way to cast outside of sensory range is via Sympathy. This requires that you have Sympathy with your target, and that you employ a sympathetic yantra. Once you have those you spend 1 Reach to move the spell to sensory range, and then you pay one point of mana to activate the Sympathetic Casting attainment you get when you have Space 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:16:12-07:00","id":1299849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299847#post1299847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. Viewing remotely is for looking through a live video feed, scrying window, etc.<br /> <br /> It takes 2 Reach to use sympathetic range. One for sensory, and one for the Attainment itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only requires 1 Reach and a point of mana to cast at Sympathetic Range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:23:20-07:00","id":1299851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299849#post1299849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It only requires 1 Reach and a point of mana to cast at Sympathetic Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind, I was wrong. I thought the Attainment itself required a Reach but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T04:04:57-07:00","id":1299899,"title":"","content":"I understand that this is most likely a question of permission from the StoryTeller, but the question arose: can character assemble gears from processed (by Platonic Form spell) tass pieces which gave the shape of the corresponding simplest parts of the mechanism (screw, gears, springs etc). Each tass is created by a separate spell. If permited What properties will the final mechanism have? I do not think that the gadget will work for a long time, since its use is tied to mana invested in tass. And not a few important question, is it possible to create substances using the Platonic Form? For example, the perfect gunpowder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-26-2019, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T06:00:30-07:00","id":1299930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299899#post1299899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that this is most likely a question of permission from the StoryTeller, but the question arose: can character assemble gears from processed (by Platonic Form spell) tass pieces which gave the shape of the corresponding simplest parts of the mechanism (screw, gears, springs etc). Each tass is created by a separate spell. If permited What properties will the final mechanism have? I do not think that the gadget will work for a long time, since its use is tied to mana invested in tass. And not a few important question, is it possible to create substances using the Platonic Form? For example, the perfect gunpowder.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tass machine you put together from individual gears made via Platonic Form won't have any special properties you don't create with additional magic. It probably would run out of mana at a rate of 1 per time you turned it on or used it from all its parts. As for gunpowder I'd be inclined to say no, but that's because in 1e constructs of tass were chemically inert, and I wouldn't want to let Prime run completely rough shod over Matter, your ST might decide differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T11:37:18-07:00","id":1300017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299930#post1299930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your ST might decide differently</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem there is that ST is me, and players tend to ask difficult questions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299930#post1299930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and I wouldn't want to let Prime run completely rough shod over Matter</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think so: such method will be very mana consuming: 1 mana per shell AND 1 mana for each created gear which is needed to assemble a gun <b>per shot</b>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1299930#post1299930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but that's because in 1e constructs of tass were chemically inert</div> </div> </div> </div>One more difficult question: the \u201cperfect gunpowder\u201d must have tremendous explosive power... but is it possible, in principle, to ignite?..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 03-26-2019, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T12:12:20-07:00","id":1300027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1300017#post1300017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem there is that ST is me, and players tend to ask difficult questions.<br /> <br /> I dont think so: such method will be very mana consuming: 1 mana per shell AND 1 mana for each created gear which is needed to assemble a gun <b>per shot</b>.<br /> <br /> One more difficult question: the \u201cperfect gunpowder\u201d must have tremendous explosive power... but is it possible, in principle, to ignite?..</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use just straight Platonic Form to create a gun, it\u2019s a fairly \u201csimple\u201d mechanical device, one mana per shot.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I\u2019d rule that if you use Platonic Form to make gunpowder it would be inert, so no combustion, ignition, explosions, etc. You can let it if you want though, I\u2019d make it cost the same Reach that creating a complex object like a gun does which is +2 Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T23:30:38-07:00","id":1301816,"title":"","content":"Page 91 of the core book, when talking about active mage sight, reads &quot;It automatically uses the mage's two Path Ruling Arcana, has no cost to add any third Ruling Arcanumn, and costs one point of Mana per scene to include a Common or Inferior Arcanum.&quot; <br /> <br /> My confusion here is that this is the only place in the book I've been able to find that implies there is any way to gain a 3rd Ruling Arcana. I was under the impression your Ruling Arcana is decided by your Path, and that's it. So, is there a way to gain more Ruling Arcanum, and where is that explained? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T23:40:52-07:00","id":1301819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluespade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1301816#post1301816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 91 of the core book, when talking about active mage sight, reads &quot;It automatically uses the mage's two Path Ruling Arcana, has no cost to add any third Ruling Arcanumn, and costs one point of Mana per scene to include a Common or Inferior Arcanum.&quot;<br /> <br /> My confusion here is that this is the only place in the book I've been able to find that implies there is any way to gain a 3rd Ruling Arcana. I was under the impression your Ruling Arcana is decided by your Path, and that's it. So, is there a way to gain more Ruling Arcanum, and where is that explained? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the Legacies section starting on page 197.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:58:38-07:00","id":1301965,"title":"","content":"Some questions regarding (god-machine) angels, specifically exiles if the distinction matters.<br /> <br /> 1. What Arcana do they fall under? I seem to remember reading Prime+Fate somewhere, but my google-fu fails me.<br /> 2. How far do the no mind-control thing go? Is it flat no, or can\u2019t go against the mission, or just can\u2019t order them to fall?<br /> 3. Do angelic Covers unravel under scrutiny like demonic ones? I\u2018m assuming they can do the same spoofing that demons can.<br /> 4. Regarding the previous, how much can a mage mess with covers? What level would suppressing/removing glitches be(assuming angels get glitches)? Making new cover whole clot seem like a little much, but could they alter an existing one?<br /> 5. Is there a thematic/balance reason against taking an exile as a familiar in as a way to exchange essence for services rendered?<br /> 6. Regarding familiars(not necessarily angelic ones), what happens if a spell like Bolster Spirit makes the familiar Rank 3, and thus ineligible for familiar condition? Do the Bond reasserts itself after the spell ends, or does it needs to be recast?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:35:20-07:00","id":1301972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsarnok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1301965#post1301965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. How far do the no mind-control thing go? Is it flat no, or can\u2019t go against the mission, or just can\u2019t order them to fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>The second one for the reasons of the third one. You can command an angel to do something it can do, but if that something clashes with its orders then its orders win out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Do angelic Covers unravel under scrutiny like demonic ones? I\u2018m assuming they can do the same spoofing that demons can. </div> </div> </div>Angelic cover identities are not subject to the needs of regular maintenance like demonic Covers do, because the Infrastructure that contains them is still connected to the Machine.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Regarding familiars(not necessarily angelic ones), what happens if a spell like Bolster Spirit makes the familiar Rank 3, and thus ineligible for familiar condition? Do the Bond reasserts itself after the spell ends, or does it needs to be recast? </div> </div> </div>The spell remains, but is ineffective until the entity's Rank returns to a level that allows the Familiar Manifestation to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:37:28-07:00","id":1302094,"title":"","content":"Q: Ghost Gate destroys the material form of all objects taken into the Twilight. Is there any way to retrieve them back besides Touch of the Grave (where they are only ephemera and fall apart after the duration)? Notably I ask since (though not released yet) the Signs of Sorcery book suggests Perfected Materials can be passed back and forth through the Twilight to perfect them. Just want to make sure I'm not missing something!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20870-lonrem","name":"Lonrem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T20:34:55-07:00","id":1302103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lonrem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1302094#post1302094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: Ghost Gate destroys the material form of all objects taken into the Twilight. Is there any way to retrieve them back besides Touch of the Grave (where they are only ephemera and fall apart after the duration)? Notably I ask since (though not released yet) the Signs of Sorcery book suggests Perfected Materials can be passed back and forth through the Twilight to perfect them. Just want to make sure I'm not missing something!</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably the Reach option on Ghost Gate probably doesn't lead to permanent destruction of objects since it's a temporary transition by design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T21:30:14-07:00","id":1302112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1302103#post1302103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably the Reach option on Ghost Gate probably doesn't lead to permanent destruction of objects since it's a temporary transition by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about that, except they specifically mention that the clothes and personal possessions turn into ephemera, which nearly duplicates the core spell's wording. Though if the items being ephemera is only temporary, it does balance it out from being a useful 'combat' spell to strip someone of all their equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20870-lonrem","name":"Lonrem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:01:07-07:00","id":1302189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lonrem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1302112#post1302112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about that, except they specifically mention that the clothes and personal possessions turn into ephemera, which nearly duplicates the core spell's wording. Though if the items being ephemera is only temporary, it does balance it out from being a useful 'combat' spell to strip someone of all their equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, why is a fairly simple weaving spell the +1 reach option on a spell that creates a gateway that does the simple weaving spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:28:32-07:00","id":1302198,"title":"","content":"The Reach effect does something a bit more complex than the base spell presumably. It doesn't potentially leave a gate to be exploited, it doesn't destroy your stuff, you have a guaranteed exit strategy from Twilight that can be Reflexively activated if you've cast it on yourself, those are just the benefits I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:52:46-07:00","id":1302212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1302198#post1302198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Reach effect does something a bit more complex than the base spell presumably. It doesn't potentially leave a gate to be exploited, it doesn't destroy your stuff, you have a guaranteed exit strategy from Twilight that can be Reflexively activated if you've cast it on yourself, those are just the benefits I can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, I am right in thinking that the spell duration is on the portal, not the transition into Twilight? That seems like a potentially really handy thing.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm wondering is why is the spell written to include a gateway in the first place. Like, Transubstantiation doesn't create a gateway that alters matter, it just alters matter. Is the implication that ghost gates are a phenomena that the spell merely activates?<br /> <br /> Looking for comparison, there's Twilit Body for transforming into Spirit Ephemera in Twilight at 4 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T12:06:30-07:00","id":1302293,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure the Duration is for the gate effect, unless you\u2019re using the Reach effect in which case it\u2019s on the translation of the subject into ephemera.<br /> <br /> I assume that Death Twilight is qualitatively different than Spirit Twilight which is why these kinds of differences exist between transitions into those respective modes of Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T09:46:39-07:00","id":1303548,"title":"","content":"This is not a question, but rather a test of one\u2019s own understanding. In general, the company is developing in the manner in which I expect it. Players have fun, and I'm interested in telling them stories. But sometimes they roll out a pile of dies, which periodically surprises me. Do I understand correctly that a player can collect the next hand?<br /> Gnosis (1 - 10 dies) + Arcane (1 - 5) + prolonged cast (1 - 5) + mana (if prolonged, 6 x Gnosis) + Yantras and Factors (number x power (2 - 6) x (1 - 5) - Factors) + 3 for Will.<br /> Do i forgot something?<br /> And is Withstand factor only Resist Attribute + Gnosis + Some Merits?<br /> For that matter, Gnosis and Supernatural Resistance merit add up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 04-08-2019, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:11:18-07:00","id":1303552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1303548#post1303548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not a question, but rather a test of one\u2019s own understanding. In general, the company is developing in the manner in which I expect it. Players have fun, and I'm interested in telling them stories. But sometimes they roll out a pile of dies, which periodically surprises me. Do I understand correctly that a player can collect the next hand?<br /> Gnosis (1 - 10 dies) + Arcane (1 - 5) + prolonged cast (1 - 5) + mana (if prolonged, 6 x Gnosis) + Yantras and Factors (number x power (2 - 6) x (1 - 5) - Factors) + 3 for Will.<br /> Do i forgot something?<br /> And is Withstand factor only Resist Attribute + Gnosis + Some Merits?<br /> For that matter, Gnosis and Supernatural Resistance merit add up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana don't give you dice, no idea what the 6xGnosis means. Factors are not multiplied. Adding a factor that doesn't come for free by being a primary factor is -2 dice to get +1 factor. Factors aren't dice though.<br /> <br /> Withstand is whatever the resistance attribute is, and that's it, Gnosis isn't a part of Withstand. If they have another source of Withstand it adds +1 to the Withstand score. So for instance if you target something that is Withstood by Composure and they have Composure 3, then their Withstand is 3. If they have Composure 3, and they have Wards and Signs cast on them, then they get the Potency of Wards and Signs as their Withstand and they add +1 from their Composure. If the spell is being cast Sympathetically then they get the Potency from Wards and Signs +1 from Composure and +1 from it coming at them via Sympathy if the caster is using anything less than a Connected Sympathy to target them. Some Merits may grant a Withstand, but it's either going to be the value that the Merit says, or it's going to add +1 as it's an additional Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:26:54-07:00","id":1303556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1303552#post1303552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana don't give you dice, no idea what the 6xGnosis means. Factors are not multiplied. Adding a factor that doesn't come for free by being a primary factor is -2 dice to get +1 factor. Factors aren't dice though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmn, the high Gnosis becomes useless. It's hard for me to imagine what you can spend mana more than 3-5 per round, if not for boosting cast.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1303552#post1303552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Withstand is whatever the resistance attribute is, and that's it, Gnosis isn't a part of Withstand. If they have another source of Withstand it adds +1 to the Withstand score. So for instance if you target something that is Withstood by Composure and they have Composure 3, then their Withstand is 3. If they have Composure 3, and they have Wards and Signs cast on them, then they get the Potency of Wards and Signs as their Withstand and they add +1 from their Composure. If the spell is being cast Sympathetically then they get the Potency from Wards and Signs +1 from Composure and +1 from it coming at them via Sympathy if the caster is using anything less than a Connected Sympathy to target them. Some Merits may grant a Withstand, but it's either going to be the value that the Merit says, or it's going to add +1 as it's an additional Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it not so that supernatural beings can use their core power (Gnosis/Primal Urge/Blood Potency) for protecting themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:32:36-07:00","id":1303559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1303556#post1303556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not so that supernatural beings can use their core power (Gnosis/Primal Urge/Blood Potency) for protecting themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Against normal contests, yes, but they decided to use Withstand so you could cast against higher Gnosis Mages and other supernaturals easier. If you had to cast against a Power Stat 7 whatever, you would need to have Potency 8 in addition to whatever the rest of your factors were. So it's an Attribute, which usually remains lower, but also is meant to encourage research of spell targets.<br /> <br /> Using Supernatural Tolerance for Withstand is a common houserule in crossover games, though. And things like Beast have stealth bonuses to trick mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-08-2019, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:52:57-07:00","id":1303563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1303556#post1303556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmn, the high Gnosis becomes useless. It's hard for me to imagine what you can spend mana more than 3-5 per round, if not for boosting cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reducing Paradox dice from Reaching beyond your safe limits is the big one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T11:00:14-07:00","id":1303566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1303563#post1303563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reducing Paradox dice from Reaching beyond your safe limits is the big one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Five is a nice point to aim for, since you need it if you want any Arcana at 5. But at that point your Paradox dice for Reach are 3 a pop. And going higher can be nice for big dicepools, for spellcasting and Withstand, not to mention getting your other arcana to 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:17:02-07:00","id":1304215,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the previous answers, but I as always have a question. Can you dispel/counterspell any kind of Mage Sight? Or Veiling practice (of corresponded arcane) is only method to withstand mage Sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:14:03-07:00","id":1304231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1304215#post1304215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the previous answers, but I as always have a question. Can you dispel/counterspell any kind of Mage Sight? Or Veiling practice (of corresponded arcane) is only method to withstand mage Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot turn off a Mage's Mage Sight. If you mean can you fool it, then yeah Veiling is pretty much the only way, but they get a Clash of Wills. They are not aware however if they lose that Clash of Wills while using their Mage Sight because Mages only automatically know they are in a Clash of Wills if it involves their spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T00:59:45-07:00","id":1307169,"title":"","content":"Do prime spells that veil magic veil themselves automatically or do you have to have the spell target itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T01:26:36-07:00","id":1307175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1307169#post1307169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do prime spells that veil magic veil themselves automatically or do you have to have the spell target itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Veiling spells in general don't ping PMS is the key thing. AMS will invoke a CoW regardless if the right arcana are in use. So, use a Veiling spell so no one bothers to use AMS and you're fine. If a Mage uses AMS and gets into a CoW and loses they don't know they had a CoW by the way, but the Mage with the Veil up knows they were in a CoW and won. Obviously if the Mage with a Veil up loses, then both parties in the CoW knows they lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T15:07:33-07:00","id":1307593,"title":"","content":"Can spirits feel sympathy or empathy? I know they're single-minded and ultimately only care about essence, but I am specifically thinking of 1E's &quot;Umbragos&quot; from... uhh was it Intruders or was it Night Horrors?<br /> <br /> Anyway Umbragos is a gulmoth that in text uses a sob story to earn followers and some are spirits... but like how or why? I don't think it was covered that well.<br /> <br /> Should I chalk that up to a difference in portrayal from the more cohesive Werewolf-centric take on Spirits more prevalent in 2E books? Or is there a way for spirits to feel emotions unrelated to their Natures as long as theyre not *contrary* to their Natures/Influences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T15:45:23-07:00","id":1307603,"title":"","content":"Umbragos being an Abyssal probably broke the rules. It could very well have relied on an ability to get sympathy or empathy from<br /> spirits that spirits aren\u2019t supposed to have because it exists as the sole exception due to its Abyssal nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:13:35-07:00","id":1307607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1307593#post1307593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway Umbragos is a gulmoth that in text uses a sob story to earn followers and some are spirits... but like how or why? I don't think it was covered that well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a bit odd. Like, why would another Spirit care what Umbragos was originally a spirit of? That said, Spirits are clearly able to hold grudges and might go for a spirit offering free essence.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure how coherent the general description is. Like, there's mention of Abyssal tainted spirits going into the Material to 'steal' essence... which is what Spirits do anyway. It seems to imply that Spirits are normally 'bound' to specific reflections in the Material, which isn't really right.<br /> <br /> I think if you wanted Umbragos to work you'd need to have it actually alter spirits to not need essence anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is there a way for spirits to feel emotions unrelated to their Natures as long as theyre not *contrary* to their Natures/Influences? </div> </div> </div>I think that's right, but 'Emotions' is different to empathy. Like, Spirits seem pretty good at anger and vengeful no matter their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:52:44-07:00","id":1307639,"title":"","content":"Thats what I thought too. Getting into someone else's perspective is an out-of-context problem for Spirits or even outright impossible. So I doubt Umbragos or anyone else could use nostalgia for a Time Before to sway spirits. I think the smartest and oldest could maybe emulate empathy on an intellectual scale but not really &quot;live&quot; it. And thats optimistic.<br /> <br /> Thank you all!<br /> <br /> And yes the time I used Umbragos I skipped it manipilating people with words and it instead used a spined tail to inject mind-twisting essence to build its court, and used empty promises to lure in prey. I also gave it the personality of Hexxus from Ferngully cuz it was a very wacky game at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T08:02:57-07:00","id":1308683,"title":"","content":"I have some questions on the various summoning (ghost, spirit, goetia) spells<br /> <br /> The sensory restriction applies also on known entities summoned?<br /> How doea the scale and range factor interacts with the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T11:52:30-07:00","id":1308982,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m sure this has been asked many times in the past, but some of the answers are quite old, like 2014. So forgive me.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking of getting into Mage: Awakening 2nd ed. I have the core book and I see Signs of Sorcery is close to being finished (for real). How compatible and/or relevant are the older sourcebooks? Is it the mechanics that have mostly changed? Do we anticipate more 2nd edition product support? Any guidance appreciated,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T12:07:47-07:00","id":1308984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1308982#post1308982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m sure this has been asked many times in the past, but some of the answers are quite old, like 2014. So forgive me.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking of getting into Mage: Awakening 2nd ed. I have the core book and I see Signs of Sorcery is close to being finished (for real). How compatible and/or relevant are the older sourcebooks? Is it the mechanics that have mostly changed? Do we anticipate more 2nd edition product support? Any guidance appreciated,</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the fluff is still applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T15:01:31-07:00","id":1309020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1308683#post1308683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some questions on the various summoning (ghost, spirit, goetia) spells<br /> <br /> The sensory restriction applies also on known entities summoned?<br /> How doea the scale and range factor interacts with the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no answer to this, you have to homerule it. Sensory range is bigger than some of the Advanced Range spellfactors. Solve that how you wish but I personally feel you should just bump the spellfactors a bit. Like pretend the arms-length range or basic factor was now sensory range (roughly 200 yards) and then expand accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1308982#post1308982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m sure this has been asked many times in the past, but some of the answers are quite old, like 2014. So forgive me.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking of getting into Mage: Awakening 2nd ed. I have the core book and I see Signs of Sorcery is close to being finished (for real). How compatible and/or relevant are the older sourcebooks? Is it the mechanics that have mostly changed? Do we anticipate more 2nd edition product support? Any guidance appreciated,</div> </div> </div> </div>Your biggest fluff concern is that Atlantis is much less important and most mages think of it as analogy, and that the Supernal is &quot;closer&quot; than before. The Supernal is a little less &quot;above&quot; and &quot;a place&quot; than before (it never was truly a place but it was discussed as such before), the supernal is more of a way of seeing and interacting with the Fallen World than before. The Supernal is still *real* of course, waaaaay more real than Atlantis, but the atmosphere is ah... more &quot;casual&quot; than before? Less Mages pining to return to their Watchtower for a second look now that Mages have easier access to partial glimpses of the Supernal whenever they carelessly want to.<br /> <br /> My other advice is about the invisible worlds. The Underworld is now worse than 1e Mage showed, the Shadow is much more Silent Hillish than 1e mage displayed, and the Astral is easier to interact with and feels way less like a &quot;human focused Shadow&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T15:32:16-07:00","id":1309026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309020#post1309020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your biggest fluff concern is that Atlantis is much less important and most mages think of it as analogy, and that the Supernal is &amp;quot;closer&amp;quot; than before. The Supernal is a little less &amp;quot;above&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;a place&amp;quot; than before (it never was truly a place but it was discussed as such before), the supernal is more of a way of seeing and interacting with the Fallen World than before. The Supernal is still *real* of course, waaaaay more real than Atlantis, but the atmosphere is ah... more &amp;quot;casual&amp;quot; than before? Less Mages pining to return to their Watchtower for a second look now that Mages have easier access to partial glimpses of the Supernal whenever they carelessly want to.<br /> <br /> My other advice is about the invisible worlds. The Underworld is now worse than 1e Mage showed, the Shadow is much more Silent Hillish than 1e mage displayed, and the Astral is easier to interact with and feels way less like a &amp;quot;human focused Shadow&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this, very kind.<br /> <br /> I only have a very casual understanding of this version of Mage (I know Ascension a little bit better). May I repeat this back in my own words to make sure I understand?<br /> <br /> 1.) Atlantis is something like folklore or metaphor than a literal truth. It suggests there was something of a golden age when the Supernal and Fallen Worlds weren\u2019t divided. Those primordial details are not particularly important.<br /> <br /> 2.) 1st edition treated the Supernal Realms like another dimension or plane, suggestive of alternate place that was somewhat divine (because it was \u201cup\u201d). Second Edition treats the Supernal Realms more like a different frequency that exists alongside the Fallen World, separated from one another by the Lie.<br /> <br /> 3.) The concept of interacting with the Supernal Realms is less daunting (or is just easier), because you don\u2019t have to return to a Watchtower. You can see the Supernal Realm with Mage Sight..? Which brings the Supernal Realms into play more often..?<br /> <br /> 4.) These invisible worlds are also sort of like the Supernal Realms, in that they\u2019re frequencies of the material world. The Underworld and Shadow are nastier, and the Astral is easier to interact with, while being less human-centric. <br /> <br /> Does that sound about right? (I went and looked up terms on the book\u2019s Lexicon. Ten minutes ago I wouldn\u2019t have known the proper terms)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:23:35-07:00","id":1309033,"title":"","content":"Im sure others have better answers, but<br /> <br /> 1) Yes, Atlantis is a teaching tool and philosophical goal. Silver Ladder is more interested in it now but its not the prevailing myth Mages adhere to. Most mages use their *own* cultures to see the Supernal now and the Time Before. The Time Before is not locked to Atlantis either, it can manifest as all kinda things in the Ruins<br /> <br /> 2)Mostly yeah. Supernal Realms are symbols so human Mages do the best they can, and with Aedes and Emanation Realms coming in Signs of Sorcery, the Supernal is a veil away and not universes.<br /> <br /> 3)Yep, and more to come, Aedes etc<br /> <br /> 4)No, but you're not off the table either. The Supernal Realms and the Invisible Realms similarities should be seen as coincidences. The Primal Wilds are not an influence on the Shadow (except for maybe the Exarchs cuz theyre control freaks). Instead, think of the Supernal Realms as language dialects that help you &quot;read&quot; the supernatural. Death sight &quot;reads&quot; vampires but vampires arent *made* of death arcana, theyre just susceptible to it. Same with the realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T18:02:14-07:00","id":1309055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309033#post1309033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im sure others have better answers, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re the answers I got. \ud83d\ude01<br /> <br /> Seriously thanks, I\u2019ll hit this Core book again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T00:11:15-07:00","id":1309122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309020#post1309020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no answer to this, you have to homerule it. Sensory range is bigger than some of the Advanced Range spellfactors. Solve that how you wish but I personally feel you should just bump the spellfactors a bit. Like pretend the arms-length range or basic factor was now sensory range (roughly 200 yards) and then expand accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Your biggest fluff concern is that Atlantis is much less important and most mages think of it as analogy, and that the Supernal is &amp;quot;closer&amp;quot; than before. The Supernal is a little less &amp;quot;above&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;a place&amp;quot; than before (it never was truly a place but it was discussed as such before), the supernal is more of a way of seeing and interacting with the Fallen World than before. The Supernal is still *real* of course, waaaaay more real than Atlantis, but the atmosphere is ah... more &amp;quot;casual&amp;quot; than before? Less Mages pining to return to their Watchtower for a second look now that Mages have easier access to partial glimpses of the Supernal whenever they carelessly want to.<br /> <br /> My other advice is about the invisible worlds. The Underworld is now worse than 1e Mage showed, the Shadow is much more Silent Hillish than 1e mage displayed, and the Astral is easier to interact with and feels way less like a &amp;quot;human focused Shadow&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, i ll try this way, thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T03:12:18-07:00","id":1309143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309026#post1309026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) 1st edition treated the Supernal Realms like another dimension or plane, suggestive of alternate place that was somewhat divine (because it was \u201cup\u201d). Second Edition treats the Supernal Realms more like a different frequency that exists alongside the Fallen World, separated from one another by the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a heavily fictionalised version of the Realm of Forms from Plato, if that's any help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T08:40:07-07:00","id":1309186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309143#post1309143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a heavily fictionalised version of the Realm of Forms from Plato, if that's any help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it does, Michael. At first I nodded my head, but then I decided I wanted to make sure I understood. I\u2019d been briefly introduced to Plato\u2019s concept of perfect forms, but not the Realm of Forms, per se.<br /> <br /> I found some slides online from a college course that speaks to the Realm of Forms. It states the Realm of Forms is Eternal and Unchanging, does that hold true for the Supernal Reams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T08:53:23-07:00","id":1309190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309186#post1309186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it does, Michael. At first I nodded my head, but then I decided I wanted to make sure I understood. I\u2019d been briefly introduced to Plato\u2019s concept of perfect forms, but not the Realm of Forms, per se.<br /> <br /> I found some slides online from a college course that speaks to the Realm of Forms. It states the Realm of Forms is Eternal and Unchanging, does that hold true for the Supernal Reams?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Archmages are so strong because they have discovered adaptive, evolving truth-symbols. So its true for regular Mages but not true overall, and the epiphany and sight of these complex maleable forms lets Archmages rework the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:24:48-07:00","id":1309201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309186#post1309186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d been briefly introduced to Plato\u2019s concept of perfect forms, but not the Realm of Forms, per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, the capitalisation wasn't needed. It just means the platonic forms considered as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I found some slides online from a college course that speaks to the Realm of Forms. It states the Realm of Forms is Eternal and Unchanging, does that hold true for the Supernal Reams? </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> said, not really. It only really takes the basic concept of a world of forms and then does it's own thing from there.<br /> <br /> It's worth mentioning that whilst Plato introduced (maybe) the basic idea of forms, Mage actually takes it's cues more from Neoplatonism and it's descendants which tended to be more mystical and magical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T11:30:35-07:00","id":1309235,"title":"","content":"You guys have been great. Gonna hush up for a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:03:38-07:00","id":1309688,"title":"","content":"Does peripheral mage sight pick up on ongoing effects like an active spell, or only when a spell is being cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T14:21:20-07:00","id":1309760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309688#post1309688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does peripheral mage sight pick up on ongoing effects like an active spell, or only when a spell is being cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only when something happens. Ongoing effects will not be noticed until you use active mage sight. The peripheral is very powerful but like some animals, &quot;if it aint moving you dont see it&quot; so to speak.<br /> (can you guess my path?)<br /> <br /> edit: woops I was wrong!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 08-09-2019, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T15:03:42-07:00","id":1309779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309688#post1309688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does peripheral mage sight pick up on ongoing effects like an active spell, or only when a spell is being cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless this has been clarified in a devquote elsewhere, Peripheral Sight picks up active supernatural effects that are not concealed or are not concealing in nature. So the halo of spells you've got hanging around you will probably ping, If you have Supernal Veil up on those spells, though, you'll be fine (this is, in fact, one of the purposes of the spell). If you've cast Invisibility on yourself, that won't ping either, since its whole point is to not be noticed (outside of weird ST things).<br /> <br /> There's been some argument over whether casting a concealing spell itself can trigger Peripheral Sight. I fall on the side of it would, but that's presently a table consideration unless there's been a statement I've not read.<br /> <br /> Edit: There's also an entire line of debate which could be had on whether casting Invisibility on your Flaming Sword of Fire would render it undetectable to Peripheral Sight. Go with what is best for your game on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 05-03-2019, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T16:14:26-07:00","id":1309788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309688#post1309688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does peripheral mage sight pick up on ongoing effects like an active spell, or only when a spell is being cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any active supernatural effect, whether instantaneous or ongoing, that is not a concealment effect, pings peripheral mage sight. It is not limited to spells.<br /> <br /> A Vampire just chilling would not trigger peripheral mage sight, a Vampire using Dominate would, an extant Lord of the Land (Animalism 5) effect would, Obfuscate would not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T17:05:15-07:00","id":1309799,"title":"","content":"A simple way to check is to ask:<br /> <br /> 1- Are they actively using their powers ?<br /> <br /> 2- Whether its a mage power or not, does it fall under the general Practice of Veiling ?<br /> <br /> If the answer to 1 is yes and the answer of 2 is no, the Peripheral Mage Sight triggers if the source is within sensory range. So this means using Active Mage Sight and most Legacy Achievements make it ping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T17:05:19-07:00","id":1309800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309688#post1309688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does peripheral mage sight pick up on ongoing effects like an active spell, or only when a spell is being cast?</div> </div> </div> </div>A question for the ages. As you can see above there's no consensus, and afaik there hasn't been any dev clarification on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T17:55:35-07:00","id":1309816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309800#post1309800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A question for the ages. As you can see above there's no consensus, and afaik there hasn't been any dev clarification on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The base is clear enough. It specifies it notices <i>active supernatural effects</i>, and Supernal Veil clearly states it exists for covering those up to avoid detection. And it's been clarified further on these forums that active supernatural concealing effects don't show up to Peripheral Sight.<br /> <br /> Where it hangs up is in the small details; do concealing effects, at the moment of casting, ping it? Do all Veiling spells impart this benefit, like casting Invisibility on a magic sword? These are the bits you're going to have to decide what works best for your game and the circumstances you want to evoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T19:03:42-07:00","id":1309966,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s a weird one: Turn Momentum is fairly clear about how it works but why it works like that is a little hard for me to wrap my head around based on most other spells. A player was trying to cast it on the whole cabal but it basically says the subject of the spell are the objects moving. But then it seems like it can only be objects moving towards the mage casting the spell. Does anyone have a good explanation of what this spell is actually doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T19:42:19-07:00","id":1309968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309966#post1309966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here\u2019s a weird one: Turn Momentum is fairly clear about how it works but why it works like that is a little hard for me to wrap my head around based on most other spells. A player was trying to cast it on the whole cabal but it basically says the subject of the spell are the objects moving. But then it seems like it can only be objects moving towards the mage casting the spell. Does anyone have a good explanation of what this spell is actually doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>OH! See the spell uses the words &quot;targets&quot; and &quot;objects&quot; to refer to the things you want to have turned, but, not the word &quot;subject&quot; which is the important part.<br /> Its like how red light green light affects traffic lights and other timing based events but the *subject* only needs to be the *mage* or her *cabal*<br /> <br /> the subject CAN be the target, OR, you can have the subject generate a ... we'll call it a Mass Effect field that turns momentum on objects traveling too fast.<br /> <br /> If the object is HUGE you'll need to use it as the subject though, like a car. But if theyre small like bullets, then your the subject, and the potency will equal the number of bullets rocks spells darts etc you can turn.<br /> <br /> EDIT: tl dr the bullets *arent* the subject afterall, is the point. The benefactor of the spell is the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T22:06:53-07:00","id":1309978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309968#post1309968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OH! See the spell uses the words &quot;targets&quot; and &quot;objects&quot; to refer to the things you want to have turned, but, not the word &quot;subject&quot; which is the important part.<br /> Its like how red light green light affects traffic lights and other timing based events but the *subject* only needs to be the *mage* or her *cabal*<br /> <br /> the subject CAN be the target, OR, you can have the subject generate a ... we'll call it a Mass Effect field that turns momentum on objects traveling too fast.<br /> <br /> If the object is HUGE you'll need to use it as the subject though, like a car. But if theyre small like bullets, then your the subject, and the potency will equal the number of bullets rocks spells darts etc you can turn.<br /> <br /> EDIT: tl dr the bullets *arent* the subject afterall, is the point. The benefactor of the spell is the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is it always tied to defense? And does the fact that Time is necessary for really fast objects mean something about the control? And the scale effects the object as well as the amount of subjects you can give the ability to? I guess I\u2019m still a little puzzled. I wish the actual term subject was in there instead of mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T22:34:53-07:00","id":1309982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1309978#post1309978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So is it always tied to defense? And does the fact that Time is necessary for really fast objects mean something about the control? And the scale effects the object as well as the amount of subjects you can give the ability to? I guess I\u2019m still a little puzzled. I wish the actual term subject was in there instead of mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can discuss it with you with a pm sometime if no one else answers your question.<br /> <br /> I have a hotfix for you that might help though. This is a perfect example of a &quot;word-limit&quot; spell. I got into the habit of solving my own issues with some spells by reminding myself of Daves very resteicted word count, as even a few more pages would have a deceptive impact on the cost to make the book.<br /> <br /> Spells like these, do what makes sense by imagining if you were the writer and knew you had to take a spell that could be its own page and HAVE to squish it down to a paragraph, and look for keywords that look like they're trying to cover for all the scrapped text. Like how they assume the subject will be a Mage (cuz it saves space than to elaborate).<br /> <br /> They accomplished a lot with so few words but some spells definitely feel like they were condensed haaard and used to be a lot longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:15:58-07:00","id":1310068,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Withstanding Magic&quot; subsection on page 114 reads: &quot;Before dice are rolled for spellcasting, the caster must consider if her subject can Withstand her magic, as it could affect the dice pool and outcome of the casting.&quot; The section then goes on to explain that Withstand reduces Potency... and does not explain mechanics for anything else related. So, does Withstand affect the spellcasting dice pool, as it implies in the header, or not? How so? This seems like one of the most important mechanics in the entire book but it's just kind of vaguely implied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:25:10-07:00","id":1310069,"title":"","content":"Only indirectly: you will want to increase Potency if you know your spell will be Withstood, which involves a dice penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:25:47-07:00","id":1310070,"title":"","content":"Involves a dice penalty how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:34:35-07:00","id":1310074,"title":"","content":"Go back a page.<br /> <br /> EDIT - not a page here, a page in the book. Potency is <i>the page before</i> the bit you quoted saying the book was vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 05-05-2019, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:39:02-07:00","id":1310077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluespade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1310070#post1310070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Involves a dice penalty how?</div> </div> </div> </div>After you cast the spell at the target, the potency of the spell is automatically reduced by the withstand. So if your spell has only 1 in potency, then a withstand of 2 means the spell gets dropped to -1 potency (ie. it doesn't do anything anymore).<br /> <br /> Therefore, you have to guess beforehand at what the targets withstand will be and adjust the potency of the spell accordingly. So in my example, if you think someone will have a withstand of 2, you'll need a potency of 3 (ie. you give your spell two extra potency, taking a penalty of -4)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:59:37-07:00","id":1310082,"title":"","content":"Right. So, Withstand never actually affects the dicepool of the spell. Only the caster's decision to increase Potency affects the dicepool. Correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T18:19:27-07:00","id":1310159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluespade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1310082#post1310082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. So, Withstand never actually affects the dicepool of the spell. Only the caster's decision to increase Potency affects the dicepool. Correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically? In 1E there were penalties for profusely complicated imagos, and sometimes I still use that, or other times I'll have a character roll a skill-check of some kind to see if they can even formulate the imago. Most of the time your knowledge of the arcana fills in gaps in scientific knowledge on a subject, and only the first time. Example, a player of mind wanted to use Matter to make a jetpack but he has no Forces, so I asked him to have a science+intelligence-3 check to see if he could come up with the imago for the jetpack, he succeeded, and we skipped that check on future uses since we knew now he *could* envision such a complex thing.<br /> <br /> However, outside of Mage there may be powers that will affect your dice pool. I think Angels have an Incept that does something like decrease a supernatural power's initial dice pool. But yeah, the dice pool for a normal, common spell should only be affected by yantras and the complexity (potency duration scale) of your imago.<br /> <br /> The only other thing I can think of is *raw distraction*, like being grappled---mages lose -3 dice when being grappled, so, depending on your ST, distraction can factor too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T00:38:13-07:00","id":1310236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluespade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1310082#post1310082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. So, Withstand never actually affects the dicepool of the spell. Only the caster's decision to increase Potency affects the dicepool. Correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T12:12:58-07:00","id":1311261,"title":"","content":"The spell Sybil's Sight is covered in 2ed by active Fate sight, correct ? Or do you need an Unveiling spell ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T00:57:50-07:00","id":1311725,"title":"","content":"at what wisdom level is a blood sacrifice of a chicken an act of hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T01:37:33-07:00","id":1311727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311725#post1311725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at what wisdom level is a blood sacrifice of a chicken an act of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question!<br /> <br /> So, sacrificing a human or other sapient being is <i>at least</i> Hubris at Understanding Wisdom (it is, at a minimum, premeditated and deliberate murder). However, the Blood Sacrifice blurb seems to imply that such an act is itself inherently hubristic on top of the premeditated murder, so sacrificing a human for Mana is something I would peg as Hubristic even for a Mage at Falling Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Killing a chicken for mana is definitely not as bad as murdering a human for mana, but the question then becomes: is it as bad as the regular premeditated murder of a human?<br /> <br /> If you want to discourage wanton sacrificing of animals for mana I'd make it an act of hubris against Understanding Wisdom. Otherwise, it's probably an Act of Hubris against Enlightened Wisdom; most mages could probably do it if they were desperate for mana, but most probably don't want to bother because 1) ew and 2) there are easier ways to go about it. But a group of rural mages running a poultry farm might find it a very easy way to harvest lots of mana, you're killing the chickens anyway, so why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T13:49:00-07:00","id":1311864,"title":"","content":"It is possible to give the anchor condition to a ghost using the Revenant spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T15:18:16-07:00","id":1311878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311864#post1311864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is possible to give the anchor condition to a ghost using the Revenant spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the Anchor Condition is a Manifestation then it appears to be yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T15:44:30-07:00","id":1311883,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a Manifestation Condition. It's the base Manifestation Condition for ghosts and is thus required before applying any other Manifestation Conditions as per the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:56:10-07:00","id":1311942,"title":"","content":"Can you have a praxis and a rote for the same spell and get the benefits of both simultaneously? For example, psychic domination as both a rote and praxis, and use all the extra dice you get from using your rote skill to more frequently get exceptional successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:20:01-07:00","id":1311951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NitroXanax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311942#post1311942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have a praxis and a rote for the same spell and get the benefits of both simultaneously? For example, psychic domination as both a rote and praxis, and use all the extra dice you get from using your rote skill to more frequently get exceptional successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you gotta pick one. Says so specifically on 112 under the description for how Rotes work.<br /> <br /> You have to choose to cast one of them, you can't have both, and, sometimes, you'll want neither.<br /> <br /> Typically go with Rotes--they're way stronger and more versatile. The exception is when you want to fish for an exceptional success because you *need* one of those effects, the prime example is negating Withstand. Praxes also become more appealing as your arcana gets closer to Mastery because the benefits of the rote drifts away from free reach (the high point) to extra dice (really nice but, early game rotes are way better). Almost always prefer rotes, but you want praxes when you specifically need an advantage the exceptional success offers that raw power simply does not. This is rare, but it does come up. As such, an Unmaking praxis is *waaay* scarier than an unmaking rote.<br /> <br /> I figured a break-down on the pros and cons of both would be a good transition after that simple &quot;nope&quot; cuz that's not very helpful to an otherwise easy question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:22:20-07:00","id":1311952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311951#post1311951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, you gotta pick one. Says so specifically on 112 under the description for how Rotes work.<br /> <br /> You have to choose to cast one of them, you can't have both, and, sometimes, you'll want neither.<br /> <br /> Typically go with Rotes--they're way stronger and more versatile. The exception is when you want to fish for an exceptional success because you *need* one of those effects, the prime example is negating Withstand. Praxes also become more appealing as your arcana gets closer to Mastery because the benefits of the rote drifts away from free reach (the high point) to extra dice (really nice but, early game rotes are way better). Almost always prefer rotes, but you want praxes when you specifically need an advantage the exceptional success offers that raw power simply does not. This is rare, but it does come up. As such, an Unmaking praxis is *waaay* scarier than an unmaking rote.<br /> <br /> I figured a break-down on the pros and cons of both would be a good transition after that simple &quot;nope&quot; cuz that's not very helpful to an otherwise easy question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your help! And yeah, the explanation was useful to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T21:09:38-07:00","id":1311973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311951#post1311951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praxes also become more appealing as your arcana gets closer to Mastery because the benefits of the rote drifts away from free reach (the high point) to extra dice (really nice but, early game rotes are way better).</div> </div> </div> </div>The other notable benefit Masters get from rotes, of course, is that they gate the discovery of their Signature Nimbus on an effect behind Scrutiny (when most Masters are going to have Signature Nimbuses that stick around a fairly long time) \u2014 a Master-level Praxis leaves mystical residue that one lucky Revelation roll identifies as their handiwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T22:12:32-07:00","id":1311986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311973#post1311973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other notable benefit Masters get from rotes, of course, is that they gate the discovery of their Signature Nimbus on an effect behind Scrutiny (when most Masters are going to have Signature Nimbuses that stick around a fairly long time) \u2014 a Master-level Praxis leaves mystical residue that one lucky Revelation roll identifies as their handiwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> That brings up another important point. Once you are a Master, your rotes become essentially much weaker--all they give you is a dice bonus. HOWEVER, if you will turn your attention to the Attainments section, you will find that Masters can also MAKE their own rotes. When they do this, the rote gains the ability to reroll failed dice given constraints. This is SUPER powerful and revitalizes rotes to prominent usefulness, BUT, I think I forgot to mention that because *it costs xp to do this*, and time.<br /> <br /> When I said what I said I had been thinking about rotes the mage *learns* as opposed to *creates* but, when a mage casts a rote *they* created, the roll gains a dice trick called &quot;rote-quality&quot; and its REALLY good. Like, stupid good. But it costs xp.<br /> <br /> But, Satchel brought up one of the REALLY EASY TO MISS AND IGNORE benefits of rotes. The Nimbus of a rote is changed to the person who made it, with the person who *cast* it buried underneath the nimbus of the creator. Investigating mages sort of has to do a magical equivalent to a Fourier Transform (I'm actually talking about Scrutiny from Mage Sight) to discover the true identity of the Mage who cast the spell, otherwise the rote obscures the rote.<br /> <br /> Example, (A)be casts a rote that (B)elle needs to investigate cuz it was a crime. Let's say Abe had a Praxis that, for Withstand purposes, would have been better cuz the Exceptional Success would have been SO SWEET, but, he went with a Rote PURELY because it wasn't *his* rote so it wouldn't be *his* nimbus attached to it. As Satchel noted, if Abe used a praxis, Belle could do a lucky Revelation and say &quot;ah ha that's Abe's nimbus, he's the culprit!&quot;<br /> But Abe used a rote, an OLD AS BALLS rote from 400 years ago by a long dead Mage. So when Belle Revelates it, she discovers a nimbus she doesn't remotely recognize, and when she asks around, no one has any idea what that nimbus is either. Through some detective work, she realizes that the spell is a rote, probably from a dead mage.<br /> She has no choice but to Scrutinize Abe's spell one more time, if she still has time to do it, but the opacity is too high for her to complete it before she runs out of rolls to throw. She's clever though and realizes what kind of power she's dealing with from the opacity alone, but, the best she can deduce is that Abe is one possible perpetrator, but there's three other Masters who could have done it, and Masters being what they are... she can't really investigate anyone without a reason because they can easily kill her and have way more political clout than she does. She needs solid proof before she can even investigate, cuz horror game.<br /> <br /> ((Let's ignore for a moment that mana-spammers eat scrutiny like cheez-its))<br /> <br /> This game is so complicated but the story possibilities the weird mechanics supplies is staggering. Its like each mechanical &quot;what the fuck&quot; is easily twistable INTO A STORY HOOK. its great!<br /> <br /> So, after all of that, that would be my next advice. Anytime you find an issue with Mage, consider how it can be turned into a storyhook, cuz with a heavily restricted page-count, I think Dave Brookshaw's team kinda-sorta left a lot of questions unanswered so that storytellers can go &quot;OOOOOOO!!&quot;, but most of the people who wanna play are just like &quot;uhhh can I get an answer for this please?&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile some of us just put on our most sadistic grins and are like &quot;If this question has no definitive answer... I have such a good excuse to be... <i><b>Eviiiiiillll</b></i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T03:14:15-07:00","id":1312030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1311986#post1311986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That brings up another important point. Once you are a Master, your rotes become essentially much weaker--all they give you is a dice bonus. HOWEVER, if you will turn your attention to the Attainments section, you will find that Masters can also MAKE their own rotes. When they do this, the rote gains the ability to reroll failed dice given constraints. This is SUPER powerful and revitalizes rotes to prominent usefulness, BUT, I think I forgot to mention that because *it costs xp to do this*, and time.<br /> <br /> When I said what I said I had been thinking about rotes the mage *learns* as opposed to *creates* but, when a mage casts a rote *they* created, the roll gains a dice trick called &amp;quot;rote-quality&amp;quot; and its REALLY good. Like, stupid good. But it costs xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't created Rotes cost as much as learned Rotes? Whether it's worth it for a Rote you've already learned (thus netting you with a duplicate Rote without refunding your original XP unless your group house rules such stuff) can definitely be something players would rethink, but any new Rotes for Mastered Arcana should definitely be created rather than learned.<br /> <br /> The benefits of Rote Action on a roll is 0.2333 extra successes per die in the dice pool (given no extra X-Again modifiers), or 70% more successes on average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T07:07:10-07:00","id":1312080,"title":"","content":"Would Life 3 (Weavings) 'Many Faces' be sufficient to change someone's sex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":". 05-14-2019, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T07:33:56-07:00","id":1312090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312080#post1312080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Life 3 (Weavings) 'Many Faces' be sufficient to change someone's sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T07:33:57-07:00","id":1312091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312080#post1312080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Life 3 (Weavings) 'Many Faces' be sufficient to change someone's sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T17:20:53-07:00","id":1312185,"title":"","content":"What would the Spiritual Implication of using the name of one of the Exarchs as a Shadow name it\u201ds Mammon by the way and the Character is a Ancho-communist that wants to bring Fully Automated space Communism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T17:35:26-07:00","id":1312188,"title":"","content":"I mean, the Exarchs don't have names, they have titles, Mammon is the name of a Ministry in service to The Chancellor, and much like you don't name yourself Odin if you like both your eyes, it's probably a bad idea (and is definitely in bad taste).<br /> <br /> Though it's not as bad an idea as using Exarchial Yantras without being a Prelate.<br /> <br /> Arguably, though, it's also a vague enough title that it doesn't actually manifest in any meaningful way, though it's still in bad taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T17:42:05-07:00","id":1312189,"title":"","content":"So what would happen then? <br /> She\u2019s doing this almost Entirely to piss Authority figures off. She loves doing that and Booze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T17:45:22-07:00","id":1312191,"title":"","content":"Either a) She would steadily become more and more like the Chancellor, or b) nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T21:32:37-07:00","id":1312233,"title":"","content":"Mammon has meaning beyond its connection to the Chancellor. The character would start to exhibit signs of greed and would likely have ill-gotten or somehow tainted wealth gather to them.<br /> <br /> It's a terrible name for an anarcho-communist, because ironic Shadow Names don't really work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T02:22:39-07:00","id":1312262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312189#post1312189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would happen then?<br /> She\u2019s doing this almost Entirely to piss Authority figures off. She loves doing that and Booze.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way to make it work would be to actually craft a deliberate Persona around it with the Shadow Name merit. Just using it casually leaves you open to what other people think it means.<br /> <br /> I could actually see Mammon working for them well. Like, &quot;you cannot serve God and Mammon&quot;, is usually taken to mean that there's an inherent opposition between the pursuit of material goods and religious spirituality. A communist perspective might affirm that phrase but reverse the importance. People's material wants are fine, they're merely perverted by the systems they exist within, and spirituality is a way for people to come to terms with that state.<br /> <br /> That said, it doesn't sound like that's what the character wants to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T08:58:49-07:00","id":1312303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312189#post1312189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would happen then? <br /> She\u2019s doing this almost Entirely to piss Authority figures off. She loves doing that and Booze.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might I recommend Scrooge for irony?<br /> Or perhaps Dionysus or Bacchus if you want booze and rebellious attitude.<br /> <br /> Using the name of the enemy more explicitely miiight be better reserved for a character meant for tragedy and failure. Such as &quot;fights Exarch but accidentally becomes their best servant if they even survive&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: I meant these suggestions with Shadow Merit cuz Michaels right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T18:42:07-07:00","id":1312469,"title":"","content":"If a mage goes into twilight and goes underground can they float or climb back to the surface or are they stuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T21:20:57-07:00","id":1312483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallarah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312469#post1312469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage goes into twilight and goes underground can they float or climb back to the surface or are they stuck?</div> </div> </div> </div>Floating tends to only be for aesthetic purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T02:33:41-07:00","id":1312516,"title":"","content":"How do they go underground in the first place? That ghosts and spirits can walk around implies that what they're walking on is solid even in Twilight. Not sure it's possible to just sink into the Earth while in Twilight (unless, similar to flight, it's related to the entity's nature; like a mole spirit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T16:03:29-07:00","id":1312665,"title":"","content":"Is Destroying an abyssal entity like a Acamoth and Gulmoth an act of hubris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T17:00:32-07:00","id":1312677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312665#post1312665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Destroying an abyssal entity like a Acamoth and Gulmoth an act of hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say generally &quot;no,&quot; so maybe we should rather consider ways in which it would be.<br /> <br /> Obvious one is a character becoming power-hungry or dangerous for the attempt, successful or not. Doing so indiscrimently without regard for collateral damage. Compare with a heroic defeat of a gulmoth that hunted innocent people. How an Arrow might do this compared to a Seer if you will.<br /> <br /> It might also depend on what the character knows. Abyssals are even more indestructable than Supernals. Killing Supernals doesn't sometimes make them cease existing but causes them to slip into the Abyss. Only way I know to permanelty do them in is IN the Abyss. They're not really here in our world, they sort of press themselves in. I think it was in Summoners this was explained, its kind of like the Who quote &quot;a footprint doesn't look like a boot&quot;, the gulmoth's full antisymbology doesnt ever truly enter our world, hence why paradoxes summon them---no matter how they get here theyre technically paradoxes, so the full &quot;is not&quot; is never here.<br /> <br /> A character who knows killing the gulmoth is rationally pointless may be fine, but a mage who doesn't know this and gets a power trip or feels motivated by endless revenge might still face hubris when killing gulmoths as often as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T22:56:38-07:00","id":1312719,"title":"","content":"How does the Outward and Inward eye +2 Reach effect interact with Scrying magic? Would a mage be able to see back into a one way Scrying window?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T00:32:59-07:00","id":1312726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312719#post1312719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Outward and Inward eye +2 Reach effect interact with Scrying magic? Would a mage be able to see back into a one way Scrying window?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but only if they knew it were there. It might also require a CoW at the ST's discretion. Probably does imo since it's the intent of the 1-way viewer not to be seen, and the intent of the OaIE user to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T17:30:14-07:00","id":1312849,"title":"","content":"Are there any examples of diseases and their severity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T06:22:58-07:00","id":1312928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312849#post1312849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any examples of diseases and their severity?</div> </div> </div> </div>In dark eras companion it is showed the black death and it seems to be a severity 2 disease","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T08:51:33-07:00","id":1312948,"title":"","content":"Lets say a ghost still looks like it did when alive (hasn't been warped by the Underworld or similarly unfortunate circumstances), could you create a lesser type of manifestation by using an Unveiling to make them visible in the material and Touch of the Grave to let them interact with physical objects within an area ? Basically something to give the impression they are still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-18-2019, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T12:00:13-07:00","id":1312989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1312948#post1312948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a ghost still looks like it did when alive (hasn't been warped by the Underworld or similarly unfortunate circumstances), could you create a lesser type of manifestation by using an Unveiling to make them visible in the material and Touch of the Grave to let them interact with physical objects within an area ? Basically something to give the impression they are still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Death Veiling could hide their dead nature, and yes you could use spells other than their Manifestation mechanics to make them both visible and solid. It requires a bit more investment of spells than just exploiting their natural mechanics, but other than that there's no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T14:40:04-07:00","id":1313019,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> One more question: a mage needs Gnosis 3 to become a founder of a Legacy, but do they use the minimum Gnosis chart for the orthodox ones (because they are creating the Legacy's orthodoxy) or the novel Attainment one (because they are coming up with something new as they develop each new one) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T15:21:16-07:00","id":1313024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1313019#post1313019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> One more question: a mage needs Gnosis 3 to become a founder of a Legacy, but do they use the minimum Gnosis chart for the orthodox ones (because they are creating the Legacy's orthodoxy) or the novel Attainment one (because they are coming up with something new as they develop each new one) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Novel, because they are coming up with a new attainment each time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T17:03:12-07:00","id":1313042,"title":"","content":"Got it, thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T14:28:52-07:00","id":1313741,"title":"","content":"Have the purview and capabilities of the Fate arcanum changed much between editions? Specifically Fate and not magic or casting in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T15:34:45-07:00","id":1313749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1313741#post1313741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have the purview and capabilities of the Fate arcanum changed much between editions? Specifically Fate and not magic or casting in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T17:39:56-07:00","id":1313948,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hey guys I have a doubt about supernal summoning. So, if I summon a Rank 5 entity that means it has its main arcana level 5, right? Level 5 Arcana means that it has access to the making and unmaking practices so, if a rank 5 supernal entity has the power to create things, can it create the summoning circle that keeps it safe from essence bleeding in another location? My team group is about to summon a Moirae, it uses Fate. And I'm in doubt if it's possible to unsummon it when finished or we need to wait it to bleed Corpus until disappear? </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24409-jclepf","name":"jclepf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T18:21:08-07:00","id":1313959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1313948#post1313948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys I have a doubt about supernal summoning. So, if I summon a Rank 5 entity that means it has its main arcana level 5, right? Level 5 Arcana means that it has access to the making and unmaking practices so, if a rank 5 supernal entity has the power to create things, can it create the summoning circle that keeps it safe from essence bleeding in another location? My team group is about to summon a Moirae, it uses Fate. And I'm in doubt if it's possible to unsummon it when finished or we need to wait it to bleed Corpus until disappear?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a summoned Supernal entity could do that, then a Master would not need to engage with the system of Supernal Summoning, which should be as clear an indicator as anything that a Supernal entity below the level of pure plot-device can't circumvent the systems required to bring a Supernal entity into reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T20:24:02-07:00","id":1313974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1313948#post1313948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hey guys I have a doubt about supernal summoning. So, if I summon a Rank 5 entity that means it has its main arcana level 5, right? Level 5 Arcana means that it has access to the making and unmaking practices so, if a rank 5 supernal entity has the power to create things, can it create the summoning circle that keeps it safe from essence bleeding in another location? My team group is about to summon a Moirae, it uses Fate. And I'm in doubt if it's possible to unsummon it when finished or we need to wait it to bleed Corpus until disappear? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The entity will leave on its own when it\u2019s done unless you\u2019ve gotten it so far away from the summoning circle that it can\u2019t make it back in time before being taken by the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T20:39:25-07:00","id":1313977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1313948#post1313948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#4B4B4B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hey guys I have a doubt about supernal summoning. So, if I summon a Rank 5 entity that means it has its main arcana level 5, right? Level 5 Arcana means that it has access to the making and unmaking practices so, if a rank 5 supernal entity has the power to create things, can it create the summoning circle that keeps it safe from essence bleeding in another location? My team group is about to summon a Moirae, it uses Fate. And I'm in doubt if it's possible to unsummon it when finished or we need to wait it to bleed Corpus until disappear? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>but they also lack attainments, which you need for them to summon. So, not in and of themselves. An ST COULD just make up a numina or an Influence that can swing it, but Rank 5 Supernals aren't going tp have such things so lightly. Also, my suggestion cuts heavily into the entities numins count so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T04:05:51-07:00","id":1314033,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Supernals even have Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T05:49:22-07:00","id":1314043,"title":"","content":"They do not have Influences, Manifestations or Numina. It's all replaced by having two Arcana equal to Rank dots and sometimes additional Arcana at lower dot levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T09:05:47-07:00","id":1314096,"title":"","content":"Really? Thats a shocker... dang, I thought they did in 1e, was at least that true?<br /> <br /> I figured they still did because the book doesn't go out of its way to say they don't, it instead just doesn't list them as having them. I can see clearly where it verifies they lack manifestations so I guess it checks out... mmm.<br /> It would make sense though for them to lack numina after the sentence saying theyre not actually ephemera...<br /> <br /> But Im still disappointed.<br /> <br /> So yeah they can't summon themselves outside a verge I guess! They lack attainments or numina. No go...<br /> <br /> ((but Imma gonna homerule numina for player whee!))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T10:16:48-07:00","id":1314117,"title":"","content":"The fact that they have arcana kind of obviates the need for Numina. They do have their Boons though, which are about as close to Numina as they get I guess, but they can only use them under certain conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T10:56:57-07:00","id":1314121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1314117#post1314117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that they have arcana kind of obviates the need for Numina. They do have their Boons though, which are about as close to Numina as they get I guess, but they can only use them under certain conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no its a plot hole for my game now. A supernal was summoned with painstaking research who would have a particular (and homeruled) numina.<br /> <br /> My player also really really likes his aether familiar who has(had) Awe. So its more of a personal problem. Definitely arcana are way better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T15:27:52-07:00","id":1315026,"title":"","content":"I have 3 simple but important questions about the relationship between Arcana and Legacy Attainments:<br /> <br /> 1. Can you use Arcana Attainments, if you possess them, while using your Legacy Attainments? For example, you use Matter Ruling to shape matter and instead of spending Reach to increase the duration, you spend Mana to do the same by activating the Matter 2 Lesser Utility Attainment.<br /> <br /> 2. If you can, does the Mana spent count as Mana used in the Legacy Attainment and so is the subject to the 'Mana Break' rule of Legacies? The Mana Break rule states that if you would spend more than one Mana point on activating the Legacy Attainment, you only really spend one.<br /> <br /> 3. Likewise if you can, can you gain the Arcanum Attainment after you learn the Legacy Attainment and still be able to use it in the Legacy Attainment? For example, you activate a Legacy Attainment after one scene of effort, but later learn Time 4 and can use the Time in a Bottle Greater Utility Attainment to activate the Legacy Attainment as an instant action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T16:04:31-07:00","id":1315037,"title":"","content":"I second all those questions!!<br /> <br /> My guess is the maker needs the arcana attainment and programs it into the legacy attainment permanently so that using the legacy attainment always invokes the arcana attainment too. Because of this, the arcana attainment will need to be either the primary arcana or the additional-effect arcana. Like, no Time in a Bottle if Time isnt either of the legacies theme-arcana.<br /> <br /> THATS A GUESS and it supposes that adding attainents to attainments is even kosher. I don't know for sure, and I assume so because there is some extra wiggle room the Eleventh Question got. Its THE most obvious section of the book where that word limit hit haaard. A lot of nuance has to be grasped out of looking at the rules and the Eleventh Question and deciding if some of the contradictions are actually features.<br /> <br /> So theres my guesses but I am very invested in these questions please halp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T16:04:57-07:00","id":1315038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315026#post1315026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have 3 simple but important questions about the relationship between Arcana and Legacy Attainments:<br /> <br /> 1. Can you use Arcana Attainments, if you possess them, while using your Legacy Attainments? For example, you use Matter Ruling to shape matter and instead of spending Reach to increase the duration, you spend Mana to do the same by activating the Matter 2 Lesser Utility Attainment.<br /> <br /> 2. If you can, does the Mana spent count as Mana used in the Legacy Attainment and so is the subject to the 'Mana Break' rule of Legacies? The Mana Break rule states that if you would spend more than one Mana point on activating the Legacy Attainment, you only really spend one.<br /> <br /> 3. Likewise if you can, can you gain the Arcanum Attainment after you learn the Legacy Attainment and still be able to use it in the Legacy Attainment? For example, you activate a Legacy Attainment after one scene of effort, but later learn Time 4 and can use the Time in a Bottle Greater Utility Attainment to activate the Legacy Attainment as an instant action.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to all of these questions is &quot;no.&quot; Legacy Attainments are intentionally inflexible and, once learned, cannot be modified. When designing a Legacy that has a particular Arcana as a prerequisite it <i>could</i> be appropriate to incorporate an Arcana Attainment into the Legacy Attainment (especially in the case of Spatial and Temporal Sympathy), but I wouldn't do it for Legacies that do not include the Arcana from which the Arcane Attainment comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T07:41:23-07:00","id":1315166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315038#post1315038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The answer to all of these questions is &quot;no.&quot; Legacy Attainments are intentionally inflexible and, once learned, cannot be modified. When designing a Legacy that has a particular Arcana as a prerequisite it <i>could</i> be appropriate to incorporate an Arcana Attainment into the Legacy Attainment (especially in the case of Spatial and Temporal Sympathy), but I wouldn't do it for Legacies that do not include the Arcana from which the Arcane Attainment comes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense, although I would still like to have some sort of an official ruling. I originally thought that you can't use Attainments at all, but if you *could* that would be potentially a huge deal for some Legacies.<br /> <br /> On a different note, the primary and secondary spell factors in Legacy Attainments should be possible to use not at full strength, correct? That's because the strength of Attainments is not fixed, but increases with your knowledge of the relevant Arcana. So you shouldn't have to get, say, 5 automatic succeses as a Master, but could instead opt to just get 3, or to use the Attainment at Potency 2 instead of 5 (or 2 instead of 3 if it's a secondary spell factor). Increased knowledge of the Arcana should not prevent you from using Attainments as when your Arcana rating was lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T19:44:14-07:00","id":1315352,"title":"","content":"What kinda of magic would it take to force open an Iris? I think I\u2019ve read it somewhere but not sure. In this case I\u2019m mainly thinking of an existing Avernian gateway but also wondering about Iris in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T20:43:53-07:00","id":1315369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315352#post1315352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kinda of magic would it take to force open an Iris? I think I\u2019ve read it somewhere but not sure. In this case I\u2019m mainly thinking of an existing Avernian gateway but also wondering about Iris in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Weaving spell of the appropriate Arcanum, in this case Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T23:14:18-07:00","id":1315384,"title":"","content":"Another question, how do Goetia sustain themselves? It seem as though without having any Manifestations naturally they are limited to their Essence In hours to be about, but what does that mean to Mages that have summoned them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T23:17:31-07:00","id":1315386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315352#post1315352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kinda of magic would it take to force open an Iris? I think I\u2019ve read it somewhere but not sure. In this case I\u2019m mainly thinking of an existing Avernian gateway but also wondering about Iris in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also the space spell correspondence let you know the iris key","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T23:18:50-07:00","id":1315387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315369#post1315369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Weaving spell of the appropriate Arcanum, in this case Death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What makes you say it\u2019s a weaving spell? Not disagreeing, just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T23:55:28-07:00","id":1315392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315387#post1315387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you say it\u2019s a weaving spell? Not disagreeing, just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Circa 2016:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=873580#post873580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic rule of thumb is that Mage lumps any form of existing gateway together as an &quot;Iris&quot;; many require some specific means of opening them called a &quot;key&quot; in Mage-Lexicon, and opening one without the proper key is always a Weaving spell of the appropriate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Head to your nearest graveyard and pop open the Avernian gate? Death 3. Open a hole in the Gauntlet that only opens under a bood moon? Spirit 3. Make that alley that leads from New York to Chicago without having to circle the block three times clockwise? Space 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T00:20:52-07:00","id":1315394,"title":"","content":"So when we concluded that Supernals lack certain advantages, it was because they were omitted from lists of beings who say, have numina.<br /> <br /> With that, does this means our mage-book's coverage of spirits specifically can gorge on resonance means that other ephemeral entities *cannot* gorge themselves on resonance, like say, a goetia?<br /> <br /> If so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315384#post1315384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, how do Goetia sustain themselves? It seem as though without having any Manifestations naturally they are limited to their Essence In hours to be about, but what does that mean to Mages that have summoned them?</div> </div> </div> </div>[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> From my reading of the rules, I kinda hate saying it but it looks like goetia cannot remain active in the physical world for long. The only manifestation they'll be able to get is Familiar, so that's about it I guess.<br /> <br /> Without the power to gorge on resonance like a spirit, the goetia is pretty much boned. Even hanging out at a resonant location apparently doesn't work. I used to think the resonant-tag alone stopped essence bleed but apparently you *need* fetter to stop the bleed. Oof.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315166#post1315166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would make sense, although I would still like to have some sort of an official ruling. I originally thought that you can't use Attainments at all, but if you *could* that would be potentially a huge deal for some Legacies.<br /> <br /> On a different note, the primary and secondary spell factors in Legacy Attainments should be possible to use not at full strength, correct? That's because the strength of Attainments is not fixed, but increases with your knowledge of the relevant Arcana. So you shouldn't have to get, say, 5 automatic succeses as a Master, but could instead opt to just get 3, or to use the Attainment at Potency 2 instead of 5 (or 2 instead of 3 if it's a secondary spell factor). Increased knowledge of the Arcana should not prevent you from using Attainments as when your Arcana rating was lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is but only because the 5th Attainment for the Eleventh Question has some mechanics that don't make sense to me without one additional reach to throw around, and since the legacy involves time, having time in a bottle would make sense. But we won't get an official ruling I don't think. Its been asked enough times that, I'm sure, if Dave wanted to comment on it, he probably would have, so we either have to hope clarification is coming in Signs or that most people have the general jist down that it isn't that important?<br /> <br /> What me and my small group of, sadly, non-related friends do is that an arcana attainment can be part of a legacy attainment but, as mentioned by @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\">proindrakenzol </a></b>if we assume we can do it at all, it makes sense that it should become mandetory and is no longer optional. This would mean that Time in a Bottle can be part of a legacy, but if it is, it is mandetory to have it, and you cannot use the legacy attainment without Time in a Bottle's effect and cost being applied to (good thing for mana break, another hint that attainments can be mixed).<br /> So I'd imagine the result is that, a legacy that uses time magic could have Time in a Bottle encoded into the 4th and 5th Legacy Attainments (but not the others), as these are the Attainments that specifically require (and guarantee) that you'll even HAVE Time in a Bottle. In exchange, the effect of Time in a Bottle *will* occur when using these legacy attainments.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think this is how Eleventh Question's Penultimate Answer gets its mileage. It confused me a lot. &quot;Why does the Optional Matter effect get instant use and other stuff too? Oh wait, its cuz its not instant. But how long does the object last for, and how come they get sensory range?&quot;<br /> Combining sensible arcana attainments seems like a good work-around without handwaving it. At least to me.<br /> <br /> I love legacies.<br /> <br /> As for the strength of attainments, they're &quot;fixed&quot;, at least, they're put on variables that, while your arcana change, how they'll affect the attainment does not change. This is a really lame way to describe it but, the primary factor *will* match your Arcana (unless you waste a pre-determined reach on switching factors but why would the creator do this... ...), and the secondary (or scale) will add up to *baaasically* 1/2 your arcana. Not really but, close enough.<br /> So I don't think you can opt in for decreasing the primary factor at will, and I do not think you can spread the values around for a better haul. Although since there's only one 2E official updated legacy I guess there's little to stop us from homeruling at our tables, after all, if people are having fun, what's the problem...?<br /> I hope this is helping but legacies really suffered to that word-count limit.<br /> So yeah, it would appear that a legacy creator can't cut-and-paste some of the primary spellfactor's power and put it onto, say, scale and let duration do the &quot;penalty to lowest prerequisite arcanum&quot; thingy. And gosh have I wanted to do juuust thaat same thing.<br /> <br /> Lore wise it also would be reasonable to assume that a legacy's user can't opt-in for decreasing the attainment's power when used, as it has become a part of your soul and being to use the power this way, and very completely. It's not quite like a muscle that was trained and can be controlled, like with the mind and imagination and arcana. Kind of like how mage armor cannot be decreased, or how pattern restoration cannot be modulated. It would be cool if we could but, compared to other attainments. Legacy attainments seem very strict about the &quot;push button receive effect&quot; feel.<br /> <br /> Welp I hope I didn't make too much of a fool out of myself &gt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T00:29:40-07:00","id":1315398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> From my reading of the rules, I kinda hate saying it but it looks like goetia cannot remain active in the physical world for long. The only manifestation they'll be able to get is Familiar, so that's about it I guess.<br /> <br /> Without the power to gorge on resonance like a spirit, the goetia is pretty much boned. Even hanging out at a resonant location apparently doesn't work. I used to think the resonant-tag alone stopped essence bleed but apparently you *need* fetter to stop the bleed. Oof.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>But you can use a Mind 4 spell similar to revenant to give goetia a long lasting manifestation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 05-30-2019, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T01:38:00-07:00","id":1315400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315398#post1315398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you can use a Mind 4 spell similar to revenant to give goetia a long lasting manifestation</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, but, the problem is that the Prometheus wanted to know how a goetia can get by without a mage's help I thought... I didn't know we were letting magic factor in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T02:59:16-07:00","id":1315413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315384#post1315384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, how do Goetia sustain themselves? It seem as though without having any Manifestations naturally they are limited to their Essence In hours to be about, but what does that mean to Mages that have summoned them?</div> </div> </div> </div>To summarise what others have said:<br /> <br /> Goetia can't naturally remain in the material. They can gain Essence from Resonant Conditions, but loses it faster due to Essence bleed than they can gain it.<br /> Goetia simply aren't equipped to be in the material, and have no natural ways of exiting the Astral anyway. There needs to be shenanigans going on for them to reach the material, and where there's such shenanigans you can always throw on some more shenanigans like Manifestations \u00e0 la the LA setting where Temenotic Goetia of famous people possess those people despite not having any natural abilities to do so.<br /> <br /> Mages who summon Goetia needs to grant them Manifestations to keep Essence bleed at bay. Either Mind 4 for Familiar (if the Goetia consents to it) or conjunctional Death or Spirit 4 for other Manifestation Conditions like Fettered, Possessed, or Claimed. Alternatively, the Mage could just procure enough Essence through other means and feed the Goetia to keep it from discorporating and returning back to the Astral. It might also be possible with a Shielding spell to shield a Goetia from Essence bleed, but they'd still require one Essence each day to keep going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T09:42:02-07:00","id":1315473,"title":"","content":"A few questions about Dissonance.<br /> <br /> 1. What happens if the same spell has been witnessed by Sleepers multiple times in a Scene, like for example a Shielding spell affording its protection in multiple instances during that Scene? Is there still only one roll? One roll per instance? One roll with a bonus?<br /> <br /> 2. What if multiple spells were witnessed? Do you only roll once for all (possible since Dissonance uses Withstand which could be used to make one roll apply to multiple different Withstands)? Once for each spell?<br /> <br /> 3. Since Dissonance is rolled at the end of a Scene, could the roll be prevented by murdering the witnessing Sleepers before the end of the Scene? Or could it at least be made easier by mind-breaking their Integrity before the end of the Scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T12:24:34-07:00","id":1315539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315413#post1315413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To summarise what others have said:<br /> <br /> Goetia can't naturally remain in the material. They can gain Essence from Resonant Conditions, but loses it faster due to Essence bleed than they can gain it.<br /> Goetia simply aren't equipped to be in the material, and have no natural ways of exiting the Astral anyway. There needs to be shenanigans going on for them to reach the material, and where there's such shenanigans you can always throw on some more shenanigans like Manifestations \u00e0 la the LA setting where Temenotic Goetia of famous people possess those people despite not having any natural abilities to do so.<br /> <br /> Mages who summon Goetia needs to grant them Manifestations to keep Essence bleed at bay. Either Mind 4 for Familiar (if the Goetia consents to it) or conjunctional Death or Spirit 4 for other Manifestation Conditions like Fettered, Possessed, or Claimed. Alternatively, the Mage could just procure enough Essence through other means and feed the Goetia to keep it from discorporating and returning back to the Astral. It might also be possible with a Shielding spell to shield a Goetia from Essence bleed, but they'd still require one Essence each day to keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So how do we think this works with Grigori? Are they an exception to essence bleed? Doesn't seem like they have a home realm to go back to because they are just Resonant with their bodies. Actually while I'm on the subject what could you do with Influence: Watching? Looking through the table I couldn't think of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T12:42:08-07:00","id":1315545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315539#post1315539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do we think this works with Grigori? Are they an exception to essence bleed? Doesn't seem like they have a home realm to go back to because they are just Resonant with their bodies. Actually while I'm on the subject what could you do with Influence: Watching? Looking through the table I couldn't think of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since they aren't Goetia or Spirits, and are from this realm, they likely wouldn't have Essence Bleed. It's basically a form of astral projection, with costs handled by the Shroud of Observation, including any bleed if it is a thing. Some idigam do a similar thing when ripping souls out of humans (though the Grigori are said to be their pilots mind and soul).<br /> <br /> Influence would likely be Observation. Strengthen would allow you to bolster one's ability to observe, say, seeing 20+ miles away. Manipulate and Control would let you get around things like barriers, or through things like walls or safes, potentially even into seeing things that couldn't 'normally' be seen, like intent or thought, thats not getting into the possibility of altering the abilities of others (say, making your observations look past them even if you would normally see an entity in Twilight). Create or Mass Create would basically let you multiply your sources of observation, like dropping a ward in a MOBA game, used on others could create hallucinations or visions or outright lies, though the Grigori didn't seem like they were mean to get to those levels of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-30-2019, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T09:00:03-07:00","id":1315703,"title":"","content":"It makes a lot of sense symbolically speaking. It takes more than an idea/goetia for them to be realized. It also means there is mechanically more of an incentive for the use of Numina and Influences, tending towards giving more of a psychic phenomena vibe. I wonder if Veil of Moments could be used to prevent the Essence expenditure, in the same train of thought as preventing a person from becoming more tired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-31-2019, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T15:44:36-07:00","id":1315763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315703#post1315703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes a lot of sense symbolically speaking. It takes more than an idea/goetia for them to be realized. It also means there is mechanically more of an incentive for the use of Numina and Influences, tending towards giving more of a psychic phenomena vibe. I wonder if Veil of Moments could be used to prevent the Essence expenditure, in the same train of thought as preventing a person from becoming more tired.</div> </div> </div> </div>makes enough sense that imma steal your idea<br /> <br /> *yoink*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T17:41:36-07:00","id":1315777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315394#post1315394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my reading of the rules, I kinda hate saying it but it looks like goetia cannot remain active in the physical world for long. The only manifestation they'll be able to get is Familiar, so that's about it I guess.<br /> <br /> Without the power to gorge on resonance like a spirit, the goetia is pretty much boned. Even hanging out at a resonant location apparently doesn't work. I used to think the resonant-tag alone stopped essence bleed but apparently you *need* fetter to stop the bleed. Oof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth remembering that Mage's copy of the ephemeral being mechanics isn't completely flush with the instances in other games; the ability of ghosts to recover Essence from being remembered isn't listed, either, and the Beast Player's Guide's treatment on Dreamborn uses the systems for spirits as a baseline with their explicit exceptions listed, which both do not include &quot;they can't harvest Resonance&quot; and specifically say that they suffer Essence bleed <i>if not in the presence of suitable resonance</i>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1241532-unpacking-manifestation-conditions-redux?p=1258503#post1258503\">It's possible, in other words,</a> that &quot;Anchor specifies a range limit to its effects&quot; is a thing that exists to make normal ghosts limited actors rather than to make Werewolf's <i>nanutari</i> and Demon's unembodied loyalists functionally toothless as antagonists for stories lasting more than a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T19:44:29-07:00","id":1315791,"title":"","content":"It might also be possible that a mage could use a Perfecting of Mind to optimize the goetia into not losing Essence passively. Perhaps a shielding to protect them from the bleeding effect of Twilight on their Essence pool. Third option is a Weaving to change &quot;can only absorb Essence passively from a Resonant area&quot; to &quot;can also actively gorge on Resonant essence up to [Potency] times a day&quot;.<br /> <br /> So hopefully the mage would have the Gnosis to conjunctionally cast one of those when doing a goetic summon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T21:29:29-07:00","id":1315797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315539#post1315539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually while I'm on the subject what could you do with Influence: Watching? Looking through the table I couldn't think of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna go out on a limb and guess that the servitors of the Greater Ministry of the Exarch of People Act Differently When They Know They're Being Watched can heighten the sense of being watched, brute-force their way through the sensory fog of Twilight to pick up more detail, redirect the attention of surveillance around themselves, and make use of the basic ephemeral being mechanics to always know where their bodies and their targets are within at least a mile of their ephemeral forms.<br /> <br /> The important thing about &quot;Grigori are treated as Rank 2 goetia&quot; is that they're largely invisible to people who aren't a moderately specific subset of mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315791#post1315791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might also be possible that a mage could use a Perfecting of Mind to optimize the goetia into not losing Essence passively. Perhaps a shielding to protect them from the bleeding effect of Twilight on their Essence pool. Third option is a Weaving to change &quot;can only absorb Essence passively from a Resonant area&quot; to &quot;can also actively gorge on Resonant essence up to [Potency] times a day&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shape Spirit being our only precedent to work from suggests that these are Patterning effects if they're doable at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T12:31:38-07:00","id":1315911,"title":"","content":"If I inure an Unraveling direct damage spell can I kill a person with it and not suffer wisdom lose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T14:15:12-07:00","id":1315939,"title":"","content":"Yes, but you already lost Wisdom once to be able to do it and you still need to deal with the rapidly escalating Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T14:50:38-07:00","id":1315944,"title":"","content":"Does the force 4 environmental immunity attainment<br /> Protect the mage from the damage of an house on fire or a storm's lightning ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T16:21:05-07:00","id":1315967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1315944#post1315944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the force 4 environmental immunity attainment<br /> Protect the mage from the damage of an house on fire or a storm's lightning ?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about vacuum? The mage in question needs to get air somewhere to breathe. I don't think this Attainment would protect him in such a situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T10:21:36-07:00","id":1316104,"title":"","content":"if i inure myself to a spell that makes a sword of mana can i just cut peoples heads off in rage with it without wisdom risked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T17:04:28-07:00","id":1316167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316104#post1316104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if i inure myself to a spell that makes a sword of mana can i just cut peoples heads off in rage with it without wisdom risked?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think so but only because of the &quot;rage&quot; part. Being under control is what makes wisdom. Paradoxically (fitting given inuring invokes it), lopping off heads with calculation and a stone-cold plan would not, after inuring. Thats my interpretation at least.<br /> <br /> See the wisdom system is meant to fascilitate engaging characters, but people usually treat it as a pure punishment system.<br /> <br /> I think its fun to try and maintain a wisdom score that makes sense for how you play. For me thats Wisdom 5, not a very wise mage but eager to help people, just incautious and stubborn.<br /> <br /> But yeah if your a scelesti hunter or guardian who inured a primeal fire sword it would let you kill with it, but a blind rage is still a blind rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T18:46:59-07:00","id":1316180,"title":"","content":"For what you want to do, I suggest an Artifact akin to Sikanda from The Neverending Story or Suiguutou from The Twelve Kingdoms. A powerful sword with mysterious properties, drawing it symbolizes bending their mind to killing the target (Sikanda), not necessarily in self defense. Failing to discipline their mind means its spirit will try to lead them astray (Suiguutou), much in the same way as a Daimon, its suggested course of action will make them powerful, it will be looking out for the wielder's best interests, but it won't make them a better person. <br /> <br /> Now you can ask things like &quot;when is it right to wield this sword ?&quot; or &quot;do I really need a scabbard to sheath my mind ?&quot;. <br /> <br /> Acting in accordance with its wishes gives +1 dice on the Wisdom check (so it neutralizes Obsession / Vice penalties but enhances Virtue bonuses).<br /> <br /> But if your character grows rather than being entrapped by it, its shape and function may change to reflect that. Now your fluctuating relationship with Wisdom creates a plot hook for character growth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-02-2019, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T10:14:36-07:00","id":1316271,"title":"","content":"For the purposes of Warding Gesture (p. 136) and Unbound Fate (p. 195), what counts as a non-Fate mystical compulsion? Obviously, having your mind and body directly subverted with Psychic Domination (p. 161) or a Ruling of Life should count. But what about more subtle manipulation including emotion-affecting spells, like Emotional Urging (p. 160) or a fear-causing spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T11:06:28-07:00","id":1316280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316271#post1316271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purposes of Warding Gesture (p. 136) and Unbound Fate (p. 195), what counts as a non-Fate mystical compulsion? Obviously, having your mind and body directly subverted with Psychic Domination (p. 161) or a Ruling of Life should count. But what about more subtle manipulation including emotion-affecting spells, like Emotional Urging (p. 160) or a fear-causing spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say those count as also being protected against by the spell. Those spells are there to give you some insurance that you will do what you set out to do, and will not to anything you don't want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T12:36:37-07:00","id":1316683,"title":"","content":"can a sleeper be a shield bearer for a legacy attainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T13:56:05-07:00","id":1316696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316683#post1316683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can a sleeper be a shield bearer for a legacy attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please give more details? Did you mean like taking an oath to make it work ? Tying its availability to the sleeper (&quot;if you die, I lose its use until I find another shield brother and he proves worthy by the trial&quot;) ? Having them join the Legacy's mystery cult and perform tasks and rituals ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are 