sleeper be a shield bearer for a legacy attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think Attainments USE spellslots! They do??<br /> <br /> EDIT: I cant find anything on the matter but my gut says that you'd never need a shield-bearer for an Attainment because they dont use up spellslots so a sleepwalker would never need to *hold* the attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 06-05-2019, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T14:19:51-07:00","id":1316702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316698#post1316698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't think Attainments USE spellslots! They do??<br /> <br /> EDIT: I cant find anything on the matter but my gut says that you'd never need a shield-bearer for an Attainment because they dont use up spellslots so a sleepwalker would never need to *hold* the attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, so you can use them as often as you want. Its why a Bokor with lots of time and &quot;resources&quot; becomes too vital for the Free Council to label as left handed. A tireless amount of laborers which double as a simple soldiers or test subjects come in very handy...provided their master is not pointing them against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-05-2019, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T15:27:17-07:00","id":1316715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316698#post1316698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't think Attainments USE spellslots! They do??<br /> <br /> EDIT: I cant find anything on the matter but my gut says that you'd never need a shield-bearer for an Attainment because they dont use up spellslots so a sleepwalker would never need to *hold* the attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316702#post1316702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't, so you can use them as often as you want. Its why a Bokor with lots of time and &quot;resources&quot; becomes too vital for the Free Council to label as left handed. A tireless amount of laborers which double as a simple soldiers or test subjects come in very handy...provided their master is not pointing them against you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I never saw them mentioned as using spell slots or not so I Just assumed they still did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T20:17:14-07:00","id":1316757,"title":"","content":"Yeah...they never did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T15:41:41-07:00","id":1316899,"title":"","content":"How does Proximi spell control work? It seems like it would be too powerful if it was based off their Willpower, but if its only based on Gnosis they'd have to always use their free reach to cast any spell. Am I missing something that spells it out somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T16:33:05-07:00","id":1316906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316899#post1316899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Proximi spell control work? It seems like it would be too powerful if it was based off their Willpower, but if its only based on Gnosis they'd have to always use their free reach to cast any spell. Am I missing something that spells it out somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Proximi Blessings (similar to most Legacy Attainments) are based on spells, but they aren't actually spells. They only use the spell rules that are directly referenced in their own rules. Spell control is not referenced and hence isn't a factor for neither Legacy Attainments nor Proximi Blessings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T05:46:37-07:00","id":1316967,"title":"","content":"Well here's something else that came up with Proximi. Myrmidons have Dispel Magic as a Blessing, Dispel Magic says you have to include any dots in spells you want to dispel. How does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T05:56:39-07:00","id":1316972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316967#post1316967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well here's something else that came up with Proximi. Myrmidons have Dispel Magic as a Blessing, Dispel Magic says you have to include any dots in spells you want to dispel. How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an oversight. If you still want to include Dispel Magic, I'd consider the Myrmidon to have the required dot in all Arcana they have a Blessing from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T06:08:54-07:00","id":1316973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316967#post1316967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well here's something else that came up with Proximi. Myrmidons have Dispel Magic as a Blessing, Dispel Magic says you have to include any dots in spells you want to dispel. How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently encountered the selfsame question. The way how I handled it in my games is assuming Myrmidons have 1 dot each in Forces, Mind and Prime for the purposes of Dispel Magic (in other words, 1 dot in each Blessing Arcanum available to that Proximus).<br /> A more liberal interpretation could be that they can dispel any magic, regardless of Arcanum, but I would then require an extra Reach. This still would not be all too powerful as Proximi are heavily limited by the Potency they can achieve anyway.<br /> <br /> Of course the most strict and RAW interpretation is that they are entirely limited to dispelling Prime spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T06:52:33-07:00","id":1316980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316973#post1316973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the most strict and RAW interpretation is that they are entirely limited to dispelling Prime spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even that since they don't have any Prime dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T09:05:09-07:00","id":1316995,"title":"","content":"Oh, god-damnit.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that must have been an oversight. Treat them as having Forces 1, Mind 1, and Prime 1 for that Blessing's purposes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T12:51:15-07:00","id":1317042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1316980#post1316980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not even that since they don't have any Prime dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I misremembered the exact text of the spell. My bad.<br /> <br /> Regardless, we now have Word of God anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T02:12:43-07:00","id":1317140,"title":"","content":"How do the Supernal Beings living in Emanations work? Do they always have one Arcanum corresponding to the Emanation's Arcanum + one other Arcanum at the same level (both equal to their Rank) and possibly other Arcana at lower levels? They don't seem to be Path-based, unlike in Verges, as the Emanations don't appear to be connected to any specific Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T15:44:29-07:00","id":1317431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1317140#post1317140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Supernal Beings living in Emanations work? Do they always have one Arcanum corresponding to the Emanation's Arcanum + one other Arcanum at the same level (both equal to their Rank) and possibly other Arcana at lower levels? They don't seem to be Path-based, unlike in Verges, as the Emanations don't appear to be connected to any specific Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine whatever is symbolically resonant with the Emanation's theme. For example, in an old western ghost town you would have the huxler that swindles mortals and ghosts out of free will (Exarchial entity of Death &amp; Fate), the undertaker trying to get all the dead residents to move on (Prime and Death), the blacksmith who tries to forge it into a full Verge (Prime and Matter), the crazy old prospector that is ominously aware of where all the secrets are (Space &amp; Time), etc. The Emanation's true nature might not necessarily be evident until the mages have an Eureka moment. I think your rule sounds pretty sensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T07:45:34-07:00","id":1318677,"title":"","content":"So regarding indefinite spells. I see that you can spend a reach and a point of mana to increase duration from advanced to indefinite. But looking at the advanced duration table it also shows that you can reach indefinite with a dice penalty; then in parenthesis on that table it also lists the reach and mana cost. So is that trying to say you pay the dice penalty <b>or </b>the reach/mana? Or do you pay both?<br /> <br /> Also regarding relinquishing indefinite spells. It indicates in one paragraph that you roll each chapter to see if the spell goes awry regardless of the spell's duration. But then in the next paragraph it indicates that most mages only relinquish indefinite spells, as relinquishing safely is very taxing. This seems to hint that there is some sort of mechanical benefit to relinquishing indefinite spells over spells of other durations. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 06-15-2019, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T07:50:20-07:00","id":1318678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318677#post1318677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So regarding indefinite spells. I see that you can spend a reach and a point of mana to increase duration from advanced to indefinite. But looking at the advanced duration table it also shows that you can reach indefinite with a dice penalty; then in parenthesis on that table it also lists the reach and mana cost. So is that trying to say you pay the dice penalty <b>or </b>the reach/mana? Or do you pay both?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to spend the Mana and the extra Reach in addition to taking dice penalties sufficient to offset the number of steps between Indefinite and whatever stage of Advanced Duration the spell gets (if any) from its primary spell factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also regarding relinquishing indefinite spells. It indicates in one paragraph that you roll each chapter to see if the spell goes awry. But then in the next paragraph it indicates that most mages only relinquish indefinite spells, as relinquishing safely is very taxing. This seems to hint that there is some sort of mechanical benefit to relinquishing indefinite spells over spells of other durations. Am I missing something? Or was that little sentence pointless flavor? </div> </div> </div>The mechanical benefit to relinquishing indefinite spells is that you're not spending a resource that costs an Experience to recover on an effect that's going to end after a set amount of time anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T08:03:36-07:00","id":1318681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318678#post1318678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanical benefit to relinquishing indefinite spells is that you're not spending a resource that costs an Experience to recover on an effect that's going to end after a set amount of time anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>But see, the book says, &quot;<i>Most mages only relinquish indefinite spells, as relinquishing safely is extremely taxing.</i>&quot; Exact wording. Indicating that they're not spending a Willpower Dot to do it and seemingly implying that there is some benefit to relinquishing indefinite spells unsafely over spells of other duration.<br /> <br /> It's a confusing statement because there is no benefit to that in the rules as stated. It's safer to relinquish limited duration spells, as there is only a limited time such spells could go awry. An indefinite spell literally has the entire rest of the Chronicle to roll over and over until something goes wrong. I assume it was some sort of oversight, and I'm not missing anything in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T08:26:47-07:00","id":1318689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318681#post1318681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But see, the book says, &amp;quot;<i>Most mages only relinquish indefinite spells, as relinquishing safely is extremely taxing.</i>&amp;quot; Exact wording. Indicating that they're not spending a Willpower Dot to do it and seemingly implying that there is some benefit to relinquishing indefinite spells unsafely over spells of other duration.<br /> <br /> It's a confusing statement because there is no benefit to that in the rules as stated. It's safer to relinquish limited duration spells, as there is only a limited time such spells could go awry. An indefinite spell literally has the entire rest of the Chronicle to roll over and over until something goes wrong. I assume it was some sort of oversight, and I'm not missing anything in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of risking the spell going wrong, the player may spend a Willpower dot to relinquish the spell safely. In this case, the spell continues until its Duration runs down or it is dispelled.<br /> <br /> That means that a safely relinquished spell would never go awry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T08:35:00-07:00","id":1318692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318689#post1318689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Instead of risking the spell going wrong, the player may spend a Willpower dot to relinquish the spell safely. In this case, the spell continues until its Duration runs down or it is dispelled.<br /> <br /> That means that a safely relinquished spell would never go awry</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understood that. What I'm referring to is that the book, with its wording, is hinting that relinquishing an indefinite spell <i>unsafely </i>is somehow more viable or safer than a spell of a lower duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 06-15-2019, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T09:17:41-07:00","id":1318700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318692#post1318692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understood that. What I'm referring to is that the book, with its wording, is hinting that relinquishing an indefinite spell <i>unsafely </i>is somehow more viable or safer than a spell of a lower duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Mages only safely relinquish a spell of Indefinite Duration is what\u2019s being said. Spells of shorter Duration are relinquished unsafely more often because they run out of Duration before they can go \u201coff message\u201d from unsafe relinquishment.<br /> <br /> It isn\u2019t at all hinting that relinquishing a spell of Indefinite Duration unsafely is somehow more viable.or safer than a spell of lower Duration. Your reading there is simply incorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T11:01:25-07:00","id":1318713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318700#post1318700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most Mages only safely relinquish a spell of Indefinite Duration is what\u2019s being said. Spells of shorter Duration are relinquished unsafely more often because they run out of Duration before they can go \u201coff message\u201d from unsafe relinquishment.<br /> <br /> It isn\u2019t at all hinting that relinquishing a spell of Indefinite Duration unsafely is somehow more viable.or safer than a spell of lower Duration. Your reading there is simply incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm beginning you see what you mean. My misunderstanding was thinking in game terms. I was thinking:<br /> <br /> Relinquish = Relinquish Unsafely<br /> Relinguish Safely = Relinquish Safely<br /> <br /> In that sentence they were just using the word normally, where I was instead thinking in game terms where specific ways of phrasing or saying something is a reference to a mechanic or rule. I apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 06-15-2019, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T14:16:57-07:00","id":1318751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318713#post1318713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm beginning you see what you mean. My misunderstanding was thinking in game terms. I was thinking:<br /> <br /> Relinquish = Relinquish Unsafely<br /> Relinguish Safely = Relinquish Safely<br /> <br /> In that sentence they were just using the word normally, where I was instead thinking in game terms where specific ways of phrasing or saying something is a reference to a mechanic or rule. I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically if you spend a willpower <b>dot</b> the spell will never go wild, because you quite literally sever a chunk of your will to manage it.<br /> <br /> Utilizing a willpower <b>point</b> means you placed a brick on the gas pedal and left the car. Driving it now doesn't tax you, so that's good. Hopefully it won't crash or run someone over. You can add conditional duration to prevent this, but now you used another resource on it.<br /> <br /> So normally you only unsafely relinquish without over Reaching and for short durations. Its clean, efficient and causes no fallout (unless you need to cancel it right there, better hope you have an Obrimos friend nearby).<br /> <br /> Regardless of this, any relinquished spell can be dispelled. So the optimal move is to cast something indefinitely, make it as powerful as possible and relinquish with a willpower dot to get a cost benefit worth the risk.<br /> <br /> Lastly, don't forget every spell a mage had on his spell control is relinquished unsafely upon their demise. One mage's horrific death can create other mages' Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-15-2019, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T22:32:43-07:00","id":1318803,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","user":"WalkingEye","date":". 06-16-2019, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T22:53:36-07:00","id":1318805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318803#post1318803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a mage dies, all of her spells are immediately relinquished as though the player spent a Willpower point. pg118<br /> <br /> so when you die its a safe relinquish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spending a Willpower <i>point</i> is an unsafe relinquish, spending a <i>dot</i> is how you safely relinquish. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T07:14:24-07:00","id":1318854,"title":"","content":"When casting a spell, is a mage aware of the withstand rating of their subject? If not, are they told what it is after attempting a cast or is that something that's kept more or less secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T07:41:35-07:00","id":1318857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318854#post1318854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When casting a spell, is a mage aware of the withstand rating of their subject? If not, are they told what it is after attempting a cast or is that something that's kept more or less secret?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they aren't, but a Knowing spell can inform that, if they are not in a hurry. Subtle cues also help, a prominent politician will probably have high composure, a marathon runner will have high stamina and a stubborn person probably has high resolve. In general this is a fair assumption about base stats and skill dots:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Substandard, weaker at it than most people<br /> \u2022\u2022 Average, everyday level<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Eminent expert level, a very strong athlete, a gifted diplomat, an intelligent researcher<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Respected master, a standard of excellence in this skill or stat, a world class talent<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Peak human level<br /> <br /> So unless its a main antagonist or a powerful supernatural, those help make a fair estimation, since being extremely powerful outside their specialties will be rarer.<br /> <br /> I think the final Potency is kept vague as a general rule and the GM gives you a narrative baseline to work with. But you can always houserule it otherwise, if it suits your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-16-2019, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T08:50:30-07:00","id":1318868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318854#post1318854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When casting a spell, is a mage aware of the withstand rating of their subject? If not, are they told what it is after attempting a cast or is that something that's kept more or less secret?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're aware that the spell is still active, but if the subject isn't affected they can infer that it's been Withstood. They *don't* know the Withstand rating (and you shouldn't tell your players, strictly speaking - just &quot;it doesn't seem to affect him,&quot; etc)<br /> <br /> Of course, spells like Know Nature and Analyse Life can tell the player how many dots in a particular attribute their character's subject has, but that takes time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T12:38:19-07:00","id":1318923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1318854#post1318854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When casting a spell, is a mage aware of the withstand rating of their subject? If not, are they told what it is after attempting a cast or is that something that's kept more or less secret?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the others explained, after casting the ST will probably keep the Withstand a secret. The player can guess the Withstand by observing how well the spell is working but it is a guess.<br /> <br /> One time a player of mine knew how Withstand works (a spell withstood continues to exist but doesn't appear to do anything) and when he was cast on by a mastigos hoping to control him, the spell wasn't strong enough. But his character acted like he was under control and fooled the mastigos with a subterfuge roll and successfully stole a thing he needed.<br /> <br /> I feel examples help with things like these. It is easier to remember rules when you know how to use them in unusual ways.<br /> <br /> Theres one more reason withstand is kept secret other than to create paranoia--withstand ratings can change. By spending 1 wp a turn, a subject boosts their Withstand by 2. This is only for a turn but, if a mastigos is ordering to kill yourself, you can spend a point of willpower, resist the spell for a turn, and shoot the mastigos (unfortunately the mastigos's spell keeps living without the caster, next turn you kill yourself without dispellation or more wp to spend)<br /> <br /> Rules like this can create weird scenarios and mysteries. Imagine discovering that murder scene as a mage and trying to piece what happened together.<br /> <br /> With the WP boosting Withstand rule, this means a player has to guess the Withstand and exceed it with potency. If they wanna be sure the victim cannot will their way through it, they need to exceed the Withstand not by 1, but by 3. If the Composure of a victim of a Fate spell is 3, their Withstand is 3, and 5 with wp spent. The Acanthus needs Potency 4 for the spell to work, but needs 6 to be sure.<br /> Assume here the acanthus is guessing the composure is 3. Its not common but its a safe assumption. When I cast I assume Withstand will be at least 3.<br /> Spells that do something a number of times equal to potency like a hex, are also a good way to find out someone's Withstand just on math. If Potency is 5 and you use the hex twice, you know their Conposure is 3. Again, wp spending can trick this.<br /> <br /> And, if guessing the Withstand and exceeding it is too risky for a Mage, they can always try ignoring it with a Praxis, as exceptional successes negate Withstand!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T09:55:12-07:00","id":1319958,"title":"","content":"About Possession (Mind 4)<br /> <br /> Am I right to assume you can possess objects by using this spell? It doesn't specify you can't, and the Possessed Condition expects this.<br /> <br /> Another question maybe is, shouldn't Possession talk about multiple subjects instead of allowing only the caster to possess others? The explanation given in the Possessed Condition (superimposition of an ethereal form onto a physical target) seems to indicate it would not be that weird for a Mage to force a subject other them themself to possess another, as a Mage is perfectly capable of Astral Projecting others. There are a few of these spells which seem to work on the Mage alone and I always find that they don't mesh well with the rest of 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T11:34:27-07:00","id":1319972,"title":"","content":"I have a question about interaction with Angels and Demons (God-machine), the brother of a character apparently is now the Cover of a Demon (via pact), I would like to know if there is any place that explains how mages deal with this type of supernatural creature, how does Mage Sight interact with Covers and everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24409-jclepf","name":"jclepf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T12:45:32-07:00","id":1319994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jclepf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1319972#post1319972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about interaction with Angels and Demons (God-machine), the brother of a character apparently is now the Cover of a Demon (via pact), I would like to know if there is any place that explains how mages deal with this type of supernatural creature, how does Mage Sight interact with Covers and everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Demons have an ability called Spoof.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent, page 112</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spoof</b><br /> Whenever a demon is subjected to an effect that might reveal her to be a supernatural being, she may attempt to \u201cspoof\u201d the effect, fooling it into thinking she\u2019s an ordinary human. A demon cannot spoof in demonic form, for obvious reasons. The demon does not have to be aware of the effect to spoof it; spoofing happens reflexively. The demon does not necessarily know where the incoming detection attempt is coming from.<br /> Spoofing doesn\u2019t affect any power or effect that doesn\u2019t explicitly detect whether a target is human or supernatural, nor does it inhibit any effects other than that detection. It also doesn\u2019t replace a demon\u2019s ability to contest the effect. For example, if a human psychic tries to read a demon\u2019s aura, the demon can spoof the psychic\u2019s ability to detect that she isn\u2019t human, but not his ability to read her emotional state. She might, however, get a contested roll against the power.<br /> Spoofing does work against effects that would detect the demon as supernatural by implication. For example, if a mage cast a spell that lets him detect every human mind in a 20-yard radius, a demon could spoof the effect since not registering as a human is a dead giveaway that she\u2019s a supernatural entity.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Cover<br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Not only does the demon fail to spoof the effect, anyone observing becomes aware that she\u2019s not human even if the effect would only impart that information to one person. Knowing that she\u2019s not human does not specifically tell an observer that she is a demon unless they would have another way of knowing or recognizing that information.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The effect functions normally.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The effect is spoofed. It registers the demon as an ordinary human. Further readings by the same effect during the same scene continue to read the demon as a normal human.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As a normal success, but any uses of the same effect by the same character for the rest of the story register the demon as human.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the differences might be visible under mage sight and specific spells (Prime 1's Pierce Deception being the most direct way), but the Demon can always try to spoof it into making the mage see them as a normal human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","user":"Andrew Kaninchen","date":". 06-21-2019, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T21:22:54-07:00","id":1320199,"title":"","content":"Pacts should show up to Fate or Space analysis unless they got some more of their &quot;we just win&quot; BS for those.. (Due to the agreement to the doom and the relationship, respectively.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T23:00:22-07:00","id":1320206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1319958#post1319958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Possession (Mind 4)<br /> <br /> Am I right to assume you can possess objects by using this spell? It doesn't specify you can't, and the Possessed Condition expects this.<br /> <br /> Another question maybe is, shouldn't Possession talk about multiple subjects instead of allowing only the caster to possess others? The explanation given in the Possessed Condition (superimposition of an ethereal form onto a physical target) seems to indicate it would not be that weird for a Mage to force a subject other them themself to possess another, as a Mage is perfectly capable of Astral Projecting others. There are a few of these spells which seem to work on the Mage alone and I always find that they don't mesh well with the rest of 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason you couldn't possess an object.<br /> <br /> There are spells in the game that specify the Mage as the subject by default, but there's no reason to assume that the Mage -must- be the subject. So yes, you can cast Possession on someone else. Just make sure your Scale factors are set up accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T16:13:38-07:00","id":1320353,"title":"","content":"Do memories have sympathetic ties to their subjects?<br /> Like if a guy had a memory of a small town in Connecticut,<br /> or a chick had a fond memory of a music box their friend once owned.<br /> Do these memories hold ties to their subjects, or is it just the owners of these memories that have the ties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T17:34:35-07:00","id":1320363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320353#post1320353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do memories have sympathetic ties to their subjects?<br /> Like if a guy had a memory of a small town in Connecticut,<br /> or a chick had a fond memory of a music box their friend once owned.<br /> Do these memories hold ties to their subjects, or is it just the owners of these memories that have the ties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Memories would have Sympathy to the person that created them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T19:01:00-07:00","id":1320372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320363#post1320363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Memories would have Sympathy to the person that created them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T19:45:28-07:00","id":1320381,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11641_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11641\" data-vbnamecard=\"11641\">Yelesom</a> I would argue the existance of a strong connection with the creator of the memory and a number of &quot;fainter&quot; secondary to otjer things (entities, places, moments, concepts) that the memory evokes. <br /> <br /> If Joe has a memory of his ex, Anna, then the memory would be connected primarily to Joe (he created the memory) and with a lesser degree to Anna (it is not her memory, but she was instrumental and present in the memory's creation)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, memories of Joe with things that were not instrumental in the memory's creation will have only Joe as a sympathetic connection. Ex Joe's memory of a random taxi ride<br /> <br /> In game terms I would assign &quot;secondary&quot; sympathy connecting the contents of the memory with the memory itself with strength equal to how much sympathy the contents of the memory had to the memory's creator at the time of creation.<br /> <br /> I hope it helped more than it confused you \ud83d\ude1b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 06-23-2019, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T20:05:35-07:00","id":1320383,"title":"","content":"Memories granting sympathetic connections to anyone but the person that created them would have setting-changing effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T20:14:49-07:00","id":1320385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320372#post1320372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing more?</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be able to turn them into a Sympathetic Representation Yantra, but you'd need to have them out of your head to do so, and you would still need Sympathy to the subject you want to effect. Other than that, no, because those are the memories of the person who created them, no one else's, and under normal circumstances no one else even has access to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T20:17:25-07:00","id":1320387,"title":"","content":"Is there a page spread write up of either the Mammon or Pantechicon ministries anywhere? I vaguely recall something like that in 1st ed but can't remember where. I'll be sad if it was just a dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T23:05:16-07:00","id":1320416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320383#post1320383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Memories granting sympathetic connections to anyone but the person that created them would have setting-changing effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320385#post1320385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be able to turn them into a Sympathetic Representation Yantra, but you'd need to have them out of your head to do so, and you would still need Sympathy to the subject you want to effect. Other than that, no, because those are the memories of the person who created them, no one else's, and under normal circumstances no one else even has access to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. The memories are someone else's.<br /> Couldn't a Mastigos steal their memories though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T23:26:55-07:00","id":1320419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320416#post1320416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic connections have a subtle impact on the way events unfold in the world and are generally founded on circumstances more concrete than the purely mental dimension. Unless you're dealing with the residents of a Temenotic neighborhood, no amount of brainwashing is going to cause a transplanted vacation in Paris to actually make it easier for someone to get to Paris again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T23:46:14-07:00","id":1320420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320419#post1320419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathetic connections have a subtle impact on the way events unfold in the world and are generally founded on circumstances more concrete than the purely mental dimension. Unless you're dealing with the residents of a Temenotic neighborhood, no amount of brainwashing is going to cause a transplanted vacation in Paris to actually make it easier for someone to get to Paris again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Alrighty.<br /> Seems I'll have to think of a different way to go Ramona Flowers with someone's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T00:52:23-07:00","id":1320426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320387#post1320387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a page spread write up of either the Mammon or Pantechicon ministries anywhere? I vaguely recall something like that in 1st ed but can't remember where. I'll be sad if it was just a dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mammon gets a fair amount of space in Reign of the Exarchs. That's the closest thing I can think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T02:46:38-07:00","id":1320439,"title":"","content":"I also want to add that sympathetic connections are built from (meaningful) interactions. A memory doesn't actually interact with anyone other than the memory's creator, its dream actors (if accessed through the Oneiros) and anyone who'd visit the memory. Dream actors are part of the memory (should be connected sympathy) but also reset whenever the memory is done playing so they're not really relevant, while visitors <i>usually</i> don't have any meaningful enough interactions with the memory to form more than the lowest and most fleeting of sympathetic connections; possibly also reset the next time the memory resets since the memory would shed any changes imposed on it with its reset unless additional magic is used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T03:45:21-07:00","id":1320445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320416#post1320416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. The memories are someone else's.<br /> Couldn't a Mastigos steal their memories though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well if you\u2019re stealing someone else\u2019s memories then yes, they\u2019d have Sympathy to their originator. I imagine it would fade fast though as the person who used to have them and the memory itself would quickly disassociate. Though if the subject knew they\u2019d lost memories that might be enough to make the Sympathy last longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T01:14:19-07:00","id":1320681,"title":"","content":"Hi, i m a little confused by the Hung spell rules.<br /> The target of it must be a mage who then cast the other spells, but what about the target of the suspended spells?<br /> Must be the same mage?<br /> Touch only?<br /> Could they be sensory ranged if the target is present while i cast hung spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T07:24:01-07:00","id":1320738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320681#post1320681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, i m a little confused by the Hung spell rules.<br /> The target of it must be a mage who then cast the other spells, but what about the target of the suspended spells?<br /> Must be the same mage?<br /> Touch only?<br /> Could they be sensory ranged if the target is present while i cast hung spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be inclined to have a liberal interpretation of what can be Hung and not give myself a headache over any of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T08:56:56-07:00","id":1320761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320681#post1320681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, i m a little confused by the Hung spell rules.<br /> The target of it must be a mage who then cast the other spells, but what about the target of the suspended spells?<br /> Must be the same mage?<br /> Touch only?<br /> Could they be sensory ranged if the target is present while i cast hung spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't provide any logical holes in the fluff or the crunch side of things. Is there a reason you're thinking you should limit the forms?<br /> <br /> A sympathetic spell would target whatever it targeted when cast, just delayed.<br /> Touch or Sensory could be aimed after the delay as reasonably as before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T09:43:33-07:00","id":1320772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320761#post1320761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't provide any logical holes in the fluff or the crunch side of things. Is there a reason you're thinking you should limit the forms?<br /> <br /> A sympathetic spell would target whatever it targeted when cast, just delayed.<br /> Touch or Sensory could be aimed after the delay as reasonably as before.</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason to limit it, but a player asked me questions like &quot;can i hung a spell with sensory range and specify a target when the hunged spell is released or the target must be selected before?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T12:08:17-07:00","id":1320807,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see why not. I suppose it means they could basically have a big spell ready to go off on the next person that irritates them enough, but eh, so what? It\u2019s going to take up 2 spell control slots, and people are going to wonder about the spells on them, so it\u2019s got plot potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T02:52:42-07:00","id":1320922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320807#post1320807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t see why not. I suppose it means they could basically have a big spell ready to go off on the next person that irritates them enough, but eh, so what? It\u2019s going to take up 2 spell control slots, and people are going to wonder about the spells on them, so it\u2019s got plot potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the end i ruled that as the imago of the spell must be whole when it is casted the sensory option is possible only if the target is present at the hung spell casting, else you must use sympathy or touch/aimed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T02:56:28-07:00","id":1320923,"title":"","content":"About dedicated tools, i understand that if i use both the bonuses (+1 tool and -2 paredox) they count as two yantra for the maximum usable limit.<br /> But how many action are required? One or two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T08:33:21-07:00","id":1320962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320923#post1320923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About dedicated tools, i understand that if i use both the bonuses (+1 tool and -2 paredox) they count as two yantra for the maximum usable limit.<br /> But how many action are required? One or two?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that if you use your Dedicated Tool for a spell it can act as a tool yantra for you get both benefits and it's still one yantra, if you incorporate it into a spell for which it does not work as a tool yantra you only get the Paradox reduction benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T09:55:48-07:00","id":1320979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320923#post1320923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About dedicated tools, i understand that if i use both the bonuses (+1 tool and -2 paredox) they count as two yantra for the maximum usable limit.<br /> But how many action are required? One or two?</div> </div> </div> </div>What proindrakenzol said, you get both benefits if they both apply for only one Yantra slot. And depending where on the cast you incorporate the DT it's either Reflexive or one Instant Action as usual for other Yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T10:28:50-07:00","id":1320984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320979#post1320979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What proindrakenzol said, you get both benefits if they both apply for only one Yantra slot. And depending where on the cast you incorporate the DT it's either Reflexive or one Instant Action as usual for other Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok but then the phrase &quot;If she uses one ritual item in many ways, each individual use counts as one Yantra for this limit.&quot; In wich cases applies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T10:53:08-07:00","id":1320989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320984#post1320984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ok but then the phrase &quot;If she uses one ritual item in many ways, each individual use counts as one Yantra for this limit.&quot; In wich cases applies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say Anne the Mastigos is casting a universal language spell on Bob the Obrimos. Anne decides to use a radio antenna as one of her yantras. An antenna is both a <b>wand</b> and a <b>symbol of communication</b>, since both symbols would apply (Anne is targeting someone {wand} and casting a spell involving communication) she could incorporate both meanings into her casting, but each meaning would count as a separate yantra despite being the same physical object.<br /> <br /> The -2 paradox is a rider, not an independent use of an object's symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T10:59:10-07:00","id":1320991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1320989#post1320989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say Anne the Mastigos is casting a universal language spell on Bob the Obrimos. Anne decides to use a radio antenna as one of her yantras. An antenna is both a <b>wand</b> and a <b>symbol of communication</b>, since both symbols would apply (Anne is targeting someone {wand} and casting a spell involving communication) she could incorporate both meanings into her casting, but each meaning would count as a separate yantra despite being the same physical object.<br /> <br /> The -2 paradox is a rider, not an independent use of an object's symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems reasonable and this way the fourth merit of the Egregore style would be more useful.<br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T16:19:06-07:00","id":1321056,"title":"","content":"Unless there's an errata that addressed this, I think both interpretations are valid, but I also prefer this reading.<br /> <br /> (And re. ruling more narrowly on hung sensory spells: It's not a big deal as long as you're <i>consistent</i> about it. I'd rule to allow any as an ST, but as a <i>player</i> it wouldn't bug me to have the game so limited. I'd only cry foul if an NPC did it without some appropriate special sauce.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T02:51:16-07:00","id":1321366,"title":"","content":"For the Soul Marks spell, does the third Attainment, if Novel, count as a Gnosis 5 or Gnosis 4 spell? As i understand it, it should be Gnosis 4, as you need higher understanding to develop a Novel Attainment, but the power of the Attainment (and therefore the ability of the spell to detect it) remains the same...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T03:41:13-07:00","id":1321371,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if I understand your question correctly, but the Gnosis requirement for creating a new Legacy Attainment has nothing to do with the design specs of said Attainment, nor its level. My interpretation of the spell is that any 5+ Gnosis attainment simply refers to any 4th or 5th-level attainments. I can see the alternate interpretation valid as well, but I think the RAI is to see the power itself, not its origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T04:41:41-07:00","id":1321374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321371#post1321371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if I understand your question correctly, but the Gnosis requirement for creating a new Legacy Attainment has nothing to do with the design specs of said Attainment, nor its level. My interpretation of the spell is that any 5+ Gnosis attainment simply refers to any 4th or 5th-level attainments. I can see the alternate interpretation valid as well, but I think the RAI is to see the power itself, not its origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, my question could be rephrased as: Do you need tho use the Reach effect to see the third Attainment if you designed it yourself or not? My default presumption was &quot;you need to use Reach even if the third Attainment is a Novel one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T08:30:30-07:00","id":1321399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321374#post1321374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, my question could be rephrased as: Do you need tho use the Reach effect to see the third Attainment if you designed it yourself or not? My default presumption was &amp;quot;you need to use Reach even if the third Attainment is a Novel one.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Well then, I would err on the side of &quot;you really need to rip this person's soul in order to look deeper&quot;. The Rule of Fun is the no. 1 rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T08:59:14-07:00","id":1321400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321374#post1321374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, my question could be rephrased as: Do you need tho use the Reach effect to see the third Attainment if you designed it yourself or not? My default presumption was &amp;quot;you need to use Reach even if the third Attainment is a Novel one.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rule that a novel third attainment leaves a strong enough mark on the soul that you can see it without the reach option. Otherwise there would be no Gnosis 5 Legacy Attainments, just 6 and 8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T09:08:02-07:00","id":1321402,"title":"","content":"I agree. A novel Attainment isn't stronger compared to anyone who is taught the very same Attainment from its creator, but developing it yourself should put a bigger impact on your soul than just learning a preexisting Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T14:10:46-07:00","id":1321429,"title":"","content":"If, instead of using a spell to just give someone a new limb, you gave a person the ability to &quot;naturally&quot; regrow a body part like a lizard or the like, would the regrown body part remain after the spell is dismissed/dispelled? I am inclined to say yes, since the limb was not created by the spell itself, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T14:17:38-07:00","id":1321430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321429#post1321429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, instead of using a spell to just give someone a new limb, you gave a person the ability to &quot;naturally&quot; regrow a body part like a lizard or the like, would the regrown body part remain after the spell is dismissed/dispelled? I am inclined to say yes, since the limb was not created by the spell itself, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if you were to grant the subject of the spell the ability to regrow a limb it would remain after the spell's duration expired. However, if the spell's duration ended before the limb regrowth was complete that would cause issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T14:24:25-07:00","id":1321431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321429#post1321429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, instead of using a spell to just give someone a new limb, you gave a person the ability to &quot;naturally&quot; regrow a body part like a lizard or the like, would the regrown body part remain after the spell is dismissed/dispelled? I am inclined to say yes, since the limb was not created by the spell itself, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done something similar. I'd say yes but you have to keep the limb secret until its done, and it will take *awhiiiile*<br /> I am hesitant to say what might happen if the spell is dissonanced-out before the limb is finished.<br /> <br /> edit: whoops I type too slow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T15:23:09-07:00","id":1321434,"title":"","content":"While I support that ruling be aware it also potentially opens the door to making other modifications that are \u201cnon-magical.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T15:35:22-07:00","id":1321436,"title":"","content":"You could use Time to speed things up. And I think that the &quot;non-magical&quot; modifications are a feature, not a bug. If you are creative, why not be rewarded for that? There are things like the +2 Reach option for Transform Life that already point in that direction, not to mention you could also go begging some Supernal Entity for a Boon anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T15:40:58-07:00","id":1321438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321434#post1321434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I support that ruling be aware it also potentially opens the door to making other modifications that are \u201cnon-magical.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine getting too crazy with it would require other rolls that verify the character can engineer the changes right? Or do you think Arcana would cover some of that? Perhaps the balance could be in unwanted side effects too like an improper imago for a kind of life-spell for genetically engineering someone to digest cellulose resulting in cancer or the loss of the ability to digest meat? (this example assumes that it takes a few months for the spell to finish converting the patient's system)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T16:07:55-07:00","id":1321440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321438#post1321438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd imagine getting too crazy with it would require other rolls that verify the character can engineer the changes right? Or do you think Arcana would cover some of that? Perhaps the balance could be in unwanted side effects too like an improper imago for a kind of life-spell for genetically engineering someone to digest cellulose resulting in cancer or the loss of the ability to digest meat? (this example assumes that it takes a few months for the spell to finish converting the patient's system)</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you haven't asked me, but I always imagined it as a combination of some magic and attribute + skill rolls that represent the raw knowledge about what you want to achieve and how you do it. You could also substitute or support some of the skill checks with the right additional Arcana, like using Fate to guide the process to a convenient outcome etc.<br /> <br /> So, for example, you could use Life 2 (or Fate Chaos Mastery or something similar) to make CRISPR-Cas9 always align perfectly, and Attribute + Skill checks and/or Fate 2(3?,4?) to assure a particular biological function actually results from the process (Fate or your knowledge would allow you to select the proper sequence for CRISPR).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 06-28-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T16:24:35-07:00","id":1321441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321438#post1321438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd imagine getting too crazy with it would require other rolls that verify the character can engineer the changes right? Or do you think Arcana would cover some of that? Perhaps the balance could be in unwanted side effects too like an improper imago for a kind of life-spell for genetically engineering someone to digest cellulose resulting in cancer or the loss of the ability to digest meat? (this example assumes that it takes a few months for the spell to finish converting the patient's system)</div> </div> </div> </div>The arcana cover all the knowledge necessary as they represent your knowledge of the symbols(ism) needed to get a desired effect. If you\u2019re going to allow arm regrowth I don\u2019t think you should put traps in the other ideas players will come up with. They\u2019ll get themselves into enough hot water in other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T16:42:55-07:00","id":1321442,"title":"","content":"Supernal magic runs on symbolism and doesn't really care about such details. If you genetically engineer a life form that can't exist without magic, then it can't be made lasting. If you engineer a life form that could physically exist without the upkeep of a spell, then that spell could possibly be made lasting if such an option fits the spell effect and Practice. Spells that can create physically impossible creations are generally Patterning and Making anyway, two Practices that only rarely have lasting options at all.<br /> <br /> If you design an imago for granting the ability to regrow a limb, then the subject will be able to regrow limbs. You don't need to know anything at all about DNA, cell division or anything else biological since the spell will simply take the Supernal symbols of regeneration and apply it to the subject for the duration of the spell. Spells might have unintended consequences (like all piercings holes regrowing if the piercings are taken out) but never unintended side effects that the spell weren't designed to do.<br /> Quick edit: The mage could simply just limit the regen spell to only apply to the missing arm, but if the subject gains a general regenerative quality then it'll apply to the whole subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-28-2019, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T18:27:28-07:00","id":1321445,"title":"","content":"@Tessie<br /> I agree but I didn't wanna assume. My other reason for questioning was that using mundane skills for knowledge checks would facilitate making Lasting options possible by knowing what the Imago should look like to create an effect the Fallen World understands easier. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5973_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5973\" data-vbnamecard=\"5973\">Prometheus</a> 's example which might be able to kiiinda sorta stand up to dissonance if anyone studying your miracle subject was deemed a mutant instead of magical. Plausible deniability spells in other words. &quot;Nope no magic here, just nature being weird as always&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T04:55:15-07:00","id":1321498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321445#post1321445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other reason for questioning was that using mundane skills for knowledge checks would facilitate making Lasting options possible by knowing what the Imago should look like to create an effect the Fallen World understands easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really an issue anyway. If you use a spell that can engineer a life form that can't physically exist without magic, then meticulously making sure the life form could exist without supernatural properties wouldn't make a difference because a spell that imposes such a major transformation or creation (i.e. Patterning or Making) can't generally be made lasting. The spell is the upkeep of the result whether or not the result could mundanely exist.<br /> If you instead use a spell to merely sculpt a life form into a new form by having the changes be gradual and natural (e.g. the regen spell for lost limbs) then you can't impose changes that cannot physically exist anyway because you have limited yourself to what's physically possible (in terms of results; you can always boost the effectiveness of natural processes to supernatural levels).<br /> And your Arcana dots should provide you with the relevant information about which Practice you would require for what effect. That's what your Arcana dots are supposed to do (other than allowing you to cast spells), granting you knowledge about the symbols and Practices behind the Arcana. Biological knowledge only matters in that you'll have an easier time coming up with ideas for your Life spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like Prometheus's example which might be able to kiiinda sorta stand up to dissonance if anyone studying your miracle subject was deemed a mutant instead of magical. Plausible deniability spells in other words. &quot;Nope no magic here, just nature being weird as always&quot; </div> </div> </div>Quiescence is mostly about whether a Sleeper thinks what they're perceiving is impossible or supernatural, or not. If you have a creature that is impossible but withstand visual inspection, then further tests will sooner or later have the testers realise (before they unrealise) that what they're looking at is impossible, but it should take time and as a mage you should really not let your mutant dog with active spells on it be discovered, captured and tested on by Sleepers for an extended period of time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I do have a question of my own to this thread:<br /> Let's say someone is regrowing an arm through use of the above mentioned Weaving regeneration spell; the arm itself is mundane but the fact that it's growing is not. As far as I understand, anyone who knows the character has lost an arm should trigger Quiescence when they see the half-formed arm (and, honestly, other people should also freak out at it depending on how it regrows) which can Dissonance away the spell, right?<br /> When the spell ends (either because it was prematurely cancelled or the arm regrew completely), will people (who know the subject was missing an arm and it couldn't be reattached) still trigger Quiescence because they're seeing an impossibility caused by Supernal magic, or will they just take regular breaking points (until it stops being as traumatic, so probably only one breaking point each) because there's no longer any Supernal magic involved in it?<br /> As far as I know it should be the latter, but I'd like some confirmation because it's a bit weird to me that someone would stop experiencing Quiescence (when the spell goes away) even though nothing has changed in their perception (since the impossible arm remains).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-29-2019, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T08:16:07-07:00","id":1321511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321498#post1321498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I do have a question of my own to this thread</div> </div> </div> </div>Without an active spell to worry about the impact of Dissonance, what are the differences between Quiescence breaking points and normal, supernatural ones?<br /> Off the top of my head, the only thing I could think of would be that the Quiescence ones keep happening? eg. you can't become desensitized to them.<br /> <br /> I would probably run it as the latter, personally. Though, as a counterpoint, I suppose it's not that different from looking at a photograph of Supernal phenomena - both are evidence of supernal magic left after the fact. And I believe that looking at photos/videos of Supernal magic causes Quiescence, though I might be mixing that up with photos of werewolves causing Lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T09:51:14-07:00","id":1321517,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, if there are no Supernal phenomena involved, the Sleeper won't Disbelieve/have Quiescence/Cause Paradox. They may get a ton of ordinary breaking points from seeing their friend's arm regrown (or even their own if they had it healed while unconscious), but it is the Abyssal shard in Sleeper's soul that interferes with a Supernal phenomenom which is the problem. Anything currently working within the boundaries of natural laws will not be a problem, whether originally created by magic or not. Likewise, Sleepers can see a Vampire use a Discipline and disbelieve all they want, but they won't <i>D</i>isbelieve (or suffer Quiescence), as there is nothing Supernal involved, only &quot;low&quot; magic.<br /> <br /> Also, the photograph may actually contain a supernatural phenomenom and be its image at the same time, likely by the way of Sympathy. Mages have their Sight ping when they look at the photograph as well, despite the photograph technically being mundane, and the Sight pings only to show a supernatural Mystery. If the photograph shows non-Supernal magic, Awakened will still get a ping as it is still a supernatural phenomenom, and Sleepers will not Disbelieve generic magic, only the Supernal, so they will remember it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T14:00:25-07:00","id":1321540,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> I am sorry for the miscommunication but your point was my point too--I was talking about alterations that CAN exist on their own but currently do not. So the arm thing is what I'm thinking of.<br /> Ehh I didn't wanna use my example because it's embarrassing but the idea was for a private short game between me and my SO and they let me have a spell that grants Striking Looks as a permanent Lasting effect *if* I can keep the metabolism altering spell in-effect for a year. Irl and in-game, my character was homeless and living in her car and basically had to eat out all the time.<br /> <br /> So like the arm thing, I was thinking of skill checks used ONLY because the Mage desires outcomes that are *side-effects* of a spell, instead of what the spell does explicitely. Like if you want to throw matchsticks in the air and make them fall in a specific pattern, fate or matter might have you covered but if you want to do it with forces do you need a crafts roll because the forces spell isnt enough?<br /> <br /> Stuff like that occassionally came up in 1e so maybe its just an old dead 1e thing. But yeah I was thinking less &quot;dragon dog that breathes fire&quot; and more &quot;how can you maintain your weight with such a shitty diet&quot;<br /> <br /> and okay maaybe I also like the idea of being a cryptid chick in the woods with an undispellable tail and accept pariahness in favor of my preferred ideal aesthetics... ... YEEES there are easier less permanent solutions but, being &quot;true&quot; is why I love this game, of discovering uncovering and becoming truths even when your fellows say its still a lie is really fun to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T20:08:35-07:00","id":1321686,"title":"","content":"I have been thinking of the true limb regrow problem and how to make a spell about it. Here is what I have so far: it would be of the practice of Weaving, duration primary. Each thing you want to regrow requires a point of Potency and the effect will require the same time to restore one as the heal time for resistant aggravated damage. You queue multiple regrows, each one starts as the previous one finishes, but if it is dispelled or ended prematurely (for example, by Dissonance), then the raw pain will cause a one turn penalty of [Potency]. With an extra Reach you can cancel the penalty. But otherwise you can pick up where it stopped.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-30-2019, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T00:41:48-07:00","id":1321697,"title":"","content":"The merit supernal watcher(sign of sorcery)<br /> gives you a supernal entity as a sort of ally.<br /> It states that the entity often appears in your active mage sight.<br /> Do you think it is a special case or other supernal entities can appear in active mage sight outside of aedes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T04:09:15-07:00","id":1321704,"title":"","content":"The Black Angels have a *looot* of arcana dots... is there a mechanical thing I missed or do they just sorta have extra arcana outside of the core rules? Please let me know if I missed something. They also lack a bane or boons, is that because they're not summoned? They're Supernals right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T13:23:36-07:00","id":1321766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321704#post1321704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Angels have a *looot* of arcana dots... is there a mechanical thing I missed or do they just sorta have extra arcana outside of the core rules? Please let me know if I missed something. They also lack a bane or boons, is that because they're not summoned? They're Supernals right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for Supernal Entities and their Arcana only limit the maximum dots they can have in their two primary Arcana, and impose no limits on the number of secondary, lower-rated Arcana they may possess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T05:43:51-07:00","id":1321869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321704#post1321704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Angels have a *looot* of arcana dots... is there a mechanical thing I missed or do they just sorta have extra arcana outside of the core rules? Please let me know if I missed something. They also lack a bane or boons, is that because they're not summoned? They're Supernals right?</div> </div> </div> </div>They should have both Bane and Boons. You should put it into errata (it's on Discord).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T08:19:45-07:00","id":1321880,"title":"","content":"Just to make sure I\u2019ve got this right, a Mage can reveal and scrutinize a mystery if any of the Arcanum involved are in their Mage sight? The advantage of using multiple ones is just increasing their dice pool? So if a Mystery is primarily Time magic but has a Space effect, a Mage could do everything they needed to do with Space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T09:04:15-07:00","id":1321882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321880#post1321880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make sure I\u2019ve got this right, a Mage can reveal and scrutinize a mystery if any of the Arcanum involved are in their Mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to be using Active Mage Sight to be able to enter Focused Mage Sight, and you can only use Focused Mage Sight with Arcana that you're using Active Mage Sight with; since adding Arcana beyond your Ruling set to your Active Mage Sight costs Mana, Scrutinizing a Mystery relating to something outside the field of your Path or Legacy is more expensive.<br /> <br /> Any Arcanum can provide you with the basic surface information of what Arcana the Mystery falls under, but if it's not the one you're using then that's all you're getting apart from a little extra on an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The advantage of using multiple ones is just increasing their dice pool? So if a Mystery is primarily Time magic but has a Space effect, a Mage could do everything they needed to do with Space? </div> </div> </div>The advantages are that you count more than one Arcanum in the pool and get the information about that Mystery that pertains to the additional Arcana at the cost of failed rolls raising the Opacity sooner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T10:26:33-07:00","id":1321889,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE<br /> The advantages are that you count more than one Arcanum in the pool and get the information about that Mystery that pertains to the additional Arcana at the cost of failed rolls raising the Opacity sooner.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> So are you saying you would not be able to get all the deep information from a Mystery unless you're using all the Arcanum in your Mage Sight that are involved in the Mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T11:17:25-07:00","id":1321896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321889#post1321889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The advantages are that you count more than one Arcanum in the pool and get the information about that Mystery that pertains to the additional Arcana at the cost of failed rolls raising the Opacity sooner. </div> </div> </div><br /> So are you saying you would not be able to get all the deep information from a Mystery unless you're using all the Arcanum in your Mage Sight that are involved in the Mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got some wires crossed; Both the corebook and Signs are consistent that Deep Information concerns the Arcana you're using Focused Sight on, and Deep Information is provided when you Reveal a Mystery that you've lowered the Opacity on, so the only benefit to including multiple Arcana in the process of Scrutiny is the extra dice. The benefit of the step <i>before</i> that \u2014 including multiple Arcana in your Active Sight \u2014 is that you can Reveal the Deep Information pertaining to other Arcana in a single sitting, since Revelation doesn't have any associated extra costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T11:36:18-07:00","id":1321903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1321889#post1321889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The advantages are that you count more than one Arcanum in the pool and get the information about that Mystery that pertains to the additional Arcana at the cost of failed rolls raising the Opacity sooner. </div> </div> </div><br /> So are you saying you would not be able to get all the deep information from a Mystery unless you're using all the Arcanum in your Mage Sight that are involved in the Mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>After (Gnosis+ Arcanum) rolls, every failed Scrutiny roll increases Opacity by (Gnosis/2), rounded up. This increase affects everyone. For every arcanum added after the first, this happens one turn sooner. Opacity becomes exponentially more difficult to reduce at each level. <br /> <br /> So if you had 1 dot in every arcana, it would cost you 1 WP point to activate Revelation, plus consume up to 7 mana (3 free Ruling Arcana plus the cost of the other 7 for normal Active Sight, but I doubt a Mystery would involve all 10) and would make you have to worry about Opacity increases up to 9 turns sooner than normal when Scrutinizing. So you would have to use Miracle, or thow a ton of mana at it (1 mana used equals one more success counted, but only counts if you got 1 natural success) or use some other ace up your sleeve to avoid it backfiring.<br /> <br /> So what is optimal ? First figure out the key Arcana via any of the sights. Then you can analyze it under each individual lens, which is easier the better you are at it. If you have multiple mages, the WP cost is spread between them.<br /> <br /> So can you use raw power to punch through it in one go ? Yes, but it requires quite a bit of it. As Opacity rises, this becomes increasingly impractical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-02-2019, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T12:49:53-07:00","id":1322085,"title":"","content":"Are you able to get information from your memories in Astral space that there is no way you could have known at the time? For instance let's say there was an Artifact that was destroyed but you had held it when you were still a sleeper. Could you go into your memory of that moment and use Mage Sight on it even though that would give you information that you never actually learned at the time? I ask because its really a trip into the Soul as I understand it and perhaps it wouldn't work the way a recreation based only on memory would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T16:35:36-07:00","id":1322119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322085#post1322085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you able to get information from your memories in Astral space that there is no way you could have known at the time? For instance let's say there was an Artifact that was destroyed but you had held it when you were still a sleeper. Could you go into your memory of that moment and use Mage Sight on it even though that would give you information that you never actually learned at the time? I ask because its really a trip into the Soul as I understand it and perhaps it wouldn't work the way a recreation based only on memory would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it depends on if the artifact did anything to cause the character a breaking point. Getting the truth probably requires a simple Time spell, but for a memory, you probably do need something more to go off of. If I had to throw someone a bone, I might do a thing where it registers as magical from a pms ting, but not enough for active mage sight to tell much, but enough to signal &quot;Okay, onto something, now I just need a Time spell to help me go see what truly was there.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T18:27:06-07:00","id":1322134,"title":"","content":"I would have it ping on PMS but only activate any effect the mage remembers seeing. Active and focused sight would probably point them to a part of the Temenos that contains more history on it.<br /> <br /> However, if they had used a Knowing of Time &amp; Mind to photograph a scene as a memory and the Artifact was on it, then I would have mage sight function as if they were dealing with the real one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-04-2019, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T11:09:29-07:00","id":1322253,"title":"","content":"Okay, so on the subject of aiming spells.<br /> <br /> Let's say that I'm feeling flippant and decide to hurl a fireball at someone. This is a mage with relevant mage armor, which basically makes hitting them a crapshoot. I'm aiming the spell for some reason instead of manifesting it on top of them like a sane person.<br /> <br /> What happens to the spell if it misses when thrown? Does the spell fail because the subject of the spell\u2014the other mage\u2014was a critical part of the imago? Or did I just potentially ruin some other distant unfortunate's day?<br /> <br /> If the spell simply fails then what if the spell is fashioned in the way of a grenade and you're lobbing it at them to explode where it hits? Obviously, it will still likely miss, but how do you determine if it lands nearby and still damages them? As far as I could tell, neither the CoD or Mage books rule on how grenades or explosives work beyond, &quot;Everyone in the area has a really bad day.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T11:42:10-07:00","id":1322260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322253#post1322253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so on the subject of aiming spells.<br /> <br /> Let's say that I'm feeling flippant and decide to hurl a fireball at someone. This is a mage with relevant mage armor, which basically makes hitting them a crapshoot. I'm aiming the spell for some reason instead of manifesting it on top of them like a sane person.<br /> <br /> What happens to the spell if it misses when thrown? Does the spell fail because the subject of the spell\u2014the other mage\u2014was a critical part of the imago? Or did I just potentially ruin some other distant unfortunate's day?<br /> <br /> If the spell simply fails then what if the spell is fashioned in the way of a grenade and you're lobbing it at them to explode where it hits? Obviously, it will still likely miss, but how do you determine if it lands nearby and still damages them? As far as I could tell, neither the CoD or Mage books rule on how grenades or explosives work beyond, &quot;Everyone in the area has a really bad day.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a fireball is not particularly picky between targets. So you would probably hit a bystander on a dramatic fail or just set something on fire on a fail, probably starting an all consuming blaze if something is not done about it. But if the scale is above default, EVERYTHING inside it gets hit, including allies and the structure nearby. This is why the AoE effect of Warding Gesture is an amazing failsafe, its the only way to restrict all your AoE/aimed spells to only damage a given target. Those in danger still get to roll to dodge it if they have some kind of thing that allows them to roll defense against firearms (that is a key point, only some Mage Armors grant that and other splats have abilities that also do).<br /> <br /> But aiming spells means no over Reaching for sensory range, which means less problems with Paradox dice accumulating in a domino of doom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-04-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T13:00:17-07:00","id":1322269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322253#post1322253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so on the subject of aiming spells.<br /> <br /> Let's say that I'm feeling flippant and decide to hurl a fireball at someone. This is a mage with relevant mage armor, which basically makes hitting them a crapshoot. I'm aiming the spell for some reason instead of manifesting it on top of them like a sane person.<br /> <br /> What happens to the spell if it misses when thrown? Does the spell fail because the subject of the spell\u2014the other mage\u2014was a critical part of the imago? Or did I just potentially ruin some other distant unfortunate's day?<br /> <br /> If the spell simply fails then what if the spell is fashioned in the way of a grenade and you're lobbing it at them to explode where it hits? Obviously, it will still likely miss, but how do you determine if it lands nearby and still damages them? As far as I could tell, neither the CoD or Mage books rule on how grenades or explosives work beyond, &quot;Everyone in the area has a really bad day.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When you use an Aimed Spell it's an AoE spell. So a fireball is going to set the area it lands in on fire. If it was a spell that turns any people into it into frogs and there's no people where it lands, it'll do nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T13:37:44-07:00","id":1322273,"title":"","content":"@RobinCoyote: you can reflexively cancel any spell you cast, if your aimed spell misses you can end it before it strikes a bystander.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T22:23:07-07:00","id":1322336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322273#post1322273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@RobinCoyote: you can reflexively cancel any spell you cast, if your aimed spell misses you can end it before it strikes a bystander.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it is a paradox right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T23:31:21-07:00","id":1322346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322273#post1322273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@RobinCoyote: you can reflexively cancel any spell you cast, if your aimed spell misses you can end it before it strikes a bystander.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cancelling a spell is reflexive but it must happen before or after the instant action of hurling the aimed spell, unless you are able to make two action at the same time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T01:26:12-07:00","id":1322366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322346#post1322346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cancelling a spell is reflexive but it must happen before or after the instant action of hurling the aimed spell, unless you are able to make two action at the same time</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no timing restrictions on reflexive actions, they can be done at any time. Also, throwing the spell is itself a reflexive action, not an instant action (page 115, <b>Aimed Spells</b>).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> as far as I can tell there is nothing stopping you from cancelling a paradox tainted aimed spell before you actually throw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T01:44:42-07:00","id":1322369,"title":"","content":"are Goetia sapient?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T02:00:58-07:00","id":1322370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322369#post1322369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are Goetia sapient?</div> </div> </div> </div>Goetia of rank 1 and higher are capable of acting with judgement (they can make decisions, such as becoming a familiar, that are not purely instinctual) so they are sapient.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T06:09:16-07:00","id":1322398,"title":"","content":"It s possible to cast instantly scribe grimoire?<br /> The way i understand it the mage must write by hand several pages so i would say no, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T07:52:44-07:00","id":1322414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322398#post1322398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It s possible to cast instantly scribe grimoire?<br /> The way i understand it the mage must write by hand several pages so i would say no, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you can. If you cast it ritually, you'll presumably scribe it by hand during the full ritual interval. If you cast it with instant casting you'll only be limited to how fast it takes to actually scribe down the Rote. With additional Arcana or spells you could just transfer the contents immediately. Some uses of Astral Grimoire and Living Grimoire (from Signs of Sorcery) couldn't be possible if the spell didn't scribe the Rote for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T08:42:37-07:00","id":1322427,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm wondering if forces damage spells that pull from, say, a source of fire or electricity use up the source? Or do forces damage spells allow you to amplify and increase the &quot;volume&quot; of the force while hurling it at someone's face, leaving the source at its origin? I'm aware that electrical wiring or appliances are likely to short out and fry, but what about fire?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-05-2019, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T10:32:12-07:00","id":1322450,"title":"","content":"Don't have the book here, but it should be either Weaving/Perfecting or Patterning (depending on bashing or lethal/aggravated) so I'd say amplification is the most likely. Especially since it scales with Potency and has no upper limit, iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:10:19-07:00","id":1322457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322427#post1322427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm wondering if forces damage spells that pull from, say, a source of fire or electricity use up the source? Or do forces damage spells allow you to amplify and increase the &quot;volume&quot; of the force while hurling it at someone's face, leaving the source at its origin? I'm aware that electrical wiring or appliances are likely to short out and fry, but what about fire?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Direct damage spells, to which you seem to be referring, do not pull from any source, they simply magically manifest damage.<br /> <br /> Forces, especially, is capable of causing damage by utilizing other sources of harm (e.g. directing an extant fire), and such a spell would potentially deplete its source, but such a spell is not a &quot;direct damage spell&quot; per the book.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not a fan of the direct damage spells. As written only the Forces, Life, and Prime ones make sense in the context of the practices (and Forces has much better and more efficient damaging options than <i>Thunderbolt</i> most of the time).<br /> <br /> <i>Withering</i>, Death 4, should be Patterning; you are not Unravelling Death, you're enhancing it considerably.<br /> <br /> <i>Piercing Earth</i>'s (Matter 4) description is achievable with <i>Shaping</i> (Matter 2), the effect described is clearly ruling and it causing agg damage makes no sense.<br /> <br /> &amp;c.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T12:46:02-07:00","id":1322476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322427#post1322427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm wondering if forces damage spells that pull from, say, a source of fire or electricity use up the source? Or do forces damage spells allow you to amplify and increase the &amp;quot;volume&amp;quot; of the force while hurling it at someone's face, leaving the source at its origin? I'm aware that electrical wiring or appliances are likely to short out and fry, but what about fire?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I debated this too. By practices, Ruling seems to cause fires by, I'd imagine, redistributing kinetic energy from molecules, moving heat from one source to another, even concentrating it.<br /> This would mean that using Ruling to cause fires removes heat from other sources, which the spell doesnt mention but... that'd fit the practice for it to do that. Or burn fuel more quickly. <br /> At Perfecting you literally just turn up the heat.<br /> <br /> For electricity it probably is moot. The flow of electricity is constant. I presume that in the Supernal Aether, electricity flowing in wires won't need to interact with Matter by necessity so Im not positive you'd short out anything either. I like unintended logical consequences but, magic sometimes bypasses physical limitations so not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T14:29:30-07:00","id":1322497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322457#post1322457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Direct damage spells, to which you seem to be referring, do not pull from any source, they simply magically manifest damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telekinetic Strike (Forces 3), Windstrike (Matter 3), Piercing Earth (Matter 4), Howl From Beyond (Spirit 3) and Shadow Scream (Spirit 4) are all described as using something in the environment against the victim. Most of the others simply don't impose damage as much as they impose an effect that deals damage. Tying damage directly to Potency is a simplification of the effects rather than having the writer or the player come up with something new each time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322457#post1322457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces, especially, is capable of causing damage by utilizing other sources of harm (e.g. directing an extant fire), and such a spell would potentially deplete its source, but such a spell is not a &quot;direct damage spell&quot; per the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The five spells I mentioned above does fit that description, except that the source is likely not something that can run out anytime soon as they redistribute elements that are highly abundant. But all except Telekinetic Force (at least one of the two ways it can be used) should logically be impossible to use in certain environments, though. Piercing Earth ain't gonna do much if there's no ground or other solids nearby to pull from, and Shadow Scream can't pull from any source if you're in a pocket dimension or other place without an adjacent Shadow to pull from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322457#post1322457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Withering</i>, Death 4, should be Patterning; you are not Unravelling Death, you're enhancing it considerably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this has been called out as a mistake. Compare with the similar spell Rotting Flesh which is Perfecting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322457#post1322457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Piercing Earth</i>'s (Matter 4) description is achievable with <i>Shaping</i> (Matter 2), the effect described is clearly ruling and it causing agg damage makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It causing aggravated damage (with a Reach) makes total sense if you think about the fact that Shaping has no reason to have any significant amount of force behind it. You can reform any shape into any other shape, but I'd imagine having a spike of earth rise up from the ground to hit your victim would result in a relatively slow moving spike that is also prone to break on contact with anything. I would personally rule that you can't create a shape that would require displacing any reasonably solid materials, meaning you might push someone away if they don't push back. You can still cause a <i>lot</i> of damage with creative uses, but the same can be said for at least one of the two dot spells for every single Arcanum.<br /> If Shaping is the artist creating his art by hand, then Piercing Earth is the industrial press; get your hand stuck in the former and you'll get a nick depending on what tools are used, but get your hand stuck in the latter and you no longer have a hand.<br /> Piercing Earth being Patterning is a bit weird on its own, but the effects are certainly not Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-05-2019, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T15:01:42-07:00","id":1322508,"title":"","content":"How would a Bound/Sin Eater from Geist be brought along with Mages on a trip to the Astral Realms? Would it even be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T15:25:36-07:00","id":1322514,"title":"","content":"Aside from just physically bringing them into the Astral with conjunctional Space, I'd say that Mind Patterning should be enough to create a psychic projection and bringing it with the mage through regular meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T18:01:38-07:00","id":1322539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322497#post1322497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Telekinetic Strike (Forces 3), Windstrike (Matter 3), Piercing Earth (Matter 4), Howl From Beyond (Spirit 3) and Shadow Scream (Spirit 4) are all described as using something in the environment against the victim. Most of the others simply don't impose damage as much as they impose an effect that deals damage. Tying damage directly to Potency is a simplification of the effects rather than having the writer or the player come up with something new each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all of those descriptions are of <i>indirect </i>damage, just like using Forces 2 to toss fire or electricity at someone is indirect. That is the crux of my problem with the majority of the &quot;direct&quot; damage spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The five spells I mentioned above does fit that description, except that the source is likely not something that can run out anytime soon as they redistribute elements that are highly abundant. But all except Telekinetic Force (at least one of the two ways it can be used) should logically be impossible to use in certain environments, though. Piercing Earth ain't gonna do much if there's no ground or other solids nearby to pull from, and Shadow Scream can't pull from any source if you're in a pocket dimension or other place without an adjacent Shadow to pull from. </div> </div> </div>Again, this simply highlights the inherently indirect nature of the spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe this has been called out as a mistake. Compare with the similar spell Rotting Flesh which is Perfecting. </div> </div> </div>Obviously it's a mistake, that's what I was pointing out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It causing aggravated damage (with a Reach) makes total sense if you think about the fact that Shaping has no reason to have any significant amount of force behind it. </div> </div> </div>The second statement, &quot;Shaping has no reason to have any significant amount of force behind it,&quot; in no way supports the premise that <i>Piercing Earth</i> should be able to do aggravated damage; they are entirely unrelated, logically.<br /> <br /> I also do not believe the second statement to be well founded. Why do you believe <i>Shaping</i> cannot have &quot;any significant amount of force&quot;? There is nothing in the description that precludes it, and the ability to shape large amounts of matter into something else seems to be doable in a single turn, it's a single <i>reflexive</i> Wits + Crafts roll with nothing defining how long it takes, this seems to at least allow for the possibility of it being very fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can reform any shape into any other shape, but I'd imagine having a spike of earth rise up from the ground to hit your victim would result in a relatively slow moving spike that is also prone to break on contact with anything. </div> </div> </div>Why? Nothing in the spell implies it makes what you're shaping especially brittle, nor is there an implication that the process is slow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would personally rule that you can't create a shape that would require displacing any reasonably solid materials, meaning you might push someone away if they don't push back. </div> </div> </div>Why? Nothing implies such a restriction beyond your own assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can still cause a <i>lot</i> of damage with creative uses, but the same can be said for at least one of the two dot spells for every single Arcanum.<br /> If Shaping is the artist creating his art by hand, then Piercing Earth is the industrial press; get your hand stuck in the former and you'll get a nick depending on what tools are used, but get your hand stuck in the latter and you no longer have a hand.<br /> Piercing Earth being Patterning is a bit weird on its own, but the effects are certainly not Ruling. </div> </div> </div>The effects are exactly Ruling because it is the same effect as <i>Shaping</i>. The only thing you're hanging your hat on is your belief that <i>Shaping</i> is slow (not supported by the text) and what is being shaped is brittle during the shaping (also not supported by the text).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-06-2019, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T02:55:19-07:00","id":1322581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322539#post1322539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all of those descriptions are of <i>indirect </i>damage, just like using Forces 2 to toss fire or electricity at someone is indirect. That is the crux of my problem with the majority of the &quot;direct&quot; damage spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I argued against. I provided examples of direct damage spells (some of which explicitly states that they are direct damage spells) that does pull from a source because you said the following:<br /> &quot;Direct damage spells, to which you seem to be referring, do not pull from any source, they simply magically manifest damage.&quot;<br /> That statement is simply false regardless of what you think direct damage spells should be like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this simply highlights the inherently indirect nature of the spells. </div> </div> </div>I think you have the wrong idea of direct damage spells. Only a few of the direct damage spells actually cause direct damage (Life-Force Assault, for example) while the majority imposes an effect that does damage. The direct damage spell format is just that, a format for spells that are specifically designed to deal damage even if it's through relatively indirect means. They follow a mold to simplify it for the players. If you can find other ways of damaging people with other spells, you do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously it's a mistake, that's what I was pointing out. </div> </div> </div>And <i>my</i> point is that it's already been adressed as a mistake, unless I'm misremembering details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second statement, &quot;Shaping has no reason to have any significant amount of force behind it,&quot; in no way supports the premise that <i>Piercing Earth</i> should be able to do aggravated damage; they are entirely unrelated, logically. </div> </div> </div>Bad phrasing from my side. See further down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also do not believe the second statement to be well founded. Why do you believe <i>Shaping</i> cannot have &quot;any significant amount of force&quot;? There is nothing in the description that precludes it, and the ability to shape large amounts of matter into something else seems to be doable in a single turn, it's a single <i>reflexive</i> Wits + Crafts roll with nothing defining how long it takes, this seems to at least allow for the possibility of it being very fast. </div> </div> </div>Because it's not what Shaping is supposed to do. While I don't have any proof that Shaping can't have any force behind it, there's really nothing supporting your position either. So I'm defaulting to the guidelines that say that damaging spells start at three dots, and providing an explanation for how that can be so that fits the given facts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? Nothing in the spell implies it makes what you're shaping especially brittle, nor is there an implication that the process is slow. </div> </div> </div><i>Earth</i> is brittle when not compacted into a smooth surface. Stone is less brittle, but read the next paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? Nothing implies such a restriction beyond your own assumptions. </div> </div> </div>Let me restate and readjust my reasoning: Ruling does not allow you to do things that are naturally impossible. A shape that takes up more space than is available is impossible, hence Shaping can't create such shapes. Now you have another reason as for why Shaping wouldn't be able to do what you think it could do, and it doesn't even have to slow down the process at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The effects are exactly Ruling because it is the same effect as <i>Shaping</i>. The only thing you're hanging your hat on is your belief that <i>Shaping</i> is slow (not supported by the text) and what is being shaped is brittle during the shaping (also not supported by the text). </div> </div> </div>The effects are only the same as Shaping because you've assumed that the two spells work identically. I'm trying to figure out how they can be different by looking at what the two spells could do differently. Trying to work with the book instead of getting caught up on a single interpretation. I've even changed my mind about how they might differ one or two times in just two posts.<br /> <br /> I did have some misgivings about Patterning as a Practice for Piercing Earth, but now that I've thought more about it, I'm inclined to think about Piercing Earth as transforming from one shape to another, which, unlike Shaping's redistributing of material in ways that are limited by the usual constrains of Ruling, doesn't really care much about what's in the way. It's not Collapse (Space 4) that overlaps things within the same space, it's instead violently pushing away what's in the way (thus the description of earth lashing against the victim). That way it makes sense to me that the spell can cause lethal or even aggravated damage with a Reach. The Reach makes the already violent transformation more violent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Grammar 07-06-2019, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T08:33:28-07:00","id":1322598,"title":"","content":"Wow, I almost feel bad for asking my previous question. ._.<br /> <br /> And yet, I have <i>more</i>~<br /> <br /> So I'm looking at the Practices and as they become more powerful, what they do seems to be more clear. It's the Initiate practices that have been the hardest to grasp. I think I've got Unveiling and Knowing figured out, but Compelling is particularly hard to grasp mostly because of the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Groundeater. That's what's confusing me. &quot;Compelling spells nudge a preferred but possible outcome into reality.&quot; Groundeater is literally pinching or contracting space in such a way that the subject moves in an alarming way. Shouldn't that fall under the purview of Ruling?<br /> <br /> In general, Space seems like a hard one to come up with Compelling spells for since space honestly for the most part just...is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T13:22:40-07:00","id":1322636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322598#post1322598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I almost feel bad for asking my previous question. ._.<br /> <br /> And yet, I have <i>more</i>~<br /> <br /> So I'm looking at the Practices and as they become more powerful, what they do seems to be more clear. It's the Initiate practices that have been the hardest to grasp. I think I've got Unveiling and Knowing figured out, but Compelling is particularly hard to grasp mostly because of the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Groundeater. That's what's confusing me. &amp;quot;Compelling spells nudge a preferred but possible outcome into reality.&amp;quot; Groundeater is literally pinching or contracting space in such a way that the subject moves in an alarming way. Shouldn't that fall under the purview of Ruling?<br /> <br /> In general, Space seems like a hard one to come up with Compelling spells for since space honestly for the most part just...is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever been scared of something and it felt like you couldn't get away? Or so anxious the room felt bigger or smaller? Almost like a nightmare but you were awake? That spell posits that the phenomenon is real but Sleepers will rationalize it away. To me the spell is more about putting a little bit of that nightmarishness of chase-dreams and Pandemonium into full effect. Its super rare for space (in game) to twist so subtly from the resonance of anxious scared people, but what can happen will happen to the Compelling practice. Some of these things, I've found, are easier if you remember that the premise of the game says that us as players are baaaasically sleepers? So some of our objections are *because* we are sleepers.<br /> <br /> So compelling space to shrink... my initial reaction was &quot;but thats not something that could happen on its own&quot; and then I asked myself &quot;but what if it could?&quot;<br /> And then THATS a scary thought! We can apply this to quite a few Mage spell-questions, but, its not always satisfactory. Like, I can explain why the control fire spell works as it does and is Ruling, but it feels like it should still be perfecting. Ah well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T00:35:04-07:00","id":1322714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322598#post1322598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I almost feel bad for asking my previous question. ._.<br /> <br /> And yet, I have <i>more</i>~<br /> <br /> So I'm looking at the Practices and as they become more powerful, what they do seems to be more clear. It's the Initiate practices that have been the hardest to grasp. I think I've got Unveiling and Knowing figured out, but Compelling is particularly hard to grasp mostly because of the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Groundeater. That's what's confusing me. &amp;quot;Compelling spells nudge a preferred but possible outcome into reality.&amp;quot; Groundeater is literally pinching or contracting space in such a way that the subject moves in an alarming way. Shouldn't that fall under the purview of Ruling?<br /> <br /> In general, Space seems like a hard one to come up with Compelling spells for since space honestly for the most part just...is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that in mage space is a lie, based of perception of sympathetic distance.<br /> You feel more &quot;close&quot; to someone you love for example.<br /> In this case have you ever been outside of your house at night after you ve seen an horror movie?<br /> Space bends, scary figures seems bigger and closer, the road to the house door seem so far...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T05:01:28-07:00","id":1322747,"title":"","content":"Compelling is a bit undefined as to what can it do. In general I tend to assume that if it's something that can happen on it's own then it's compelling but the printed spells don't always follow that plus it doesn'twork for some of the more esoteric arcana. For instance space and time don't particulary do things on their own. So in those cases I go &quot;Is the effect subtle enough to not be overtly supernatural&quot; and &quot;Do i want my PCs use that kind of effect and 1 dot&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally I think compelling is mostly there to have characters be able to actually DO something at 1 dot, not just enhance their perceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T07:53:14-07:00","id":1322967,"title":"","content":"So I have a question regarding the phrases &quot;rote quality&quot;, &quot;rote action quality&quot;, and &quot;rote action&quot;. Are these all the same thing?<br /> <br /> My original assumption was that &quot;rote quality&quot; was talking about the spell type, and &quot;rote action quality&quot; was talking about a &quot;rote action.&quot;<br /> <br /> But then in the middle of the text block for Rotes, the spell type, it says, &quot;Casting a Rote from a Grimoire rather than from memory, or casting a Rote she designed herself, gives the mage\u2019s spellcasting dice pool the rote quality.&quot;<br /> <br /> So obviously, unless I'm mistaken, they're using &quot;rote quality&quot; and &quot;rote action quality&quot; interchangeably to refer to &quot;rote actions&quot; right? Unless there is an actual rote quality I completely breezed over? I'm asking because there are 500-some instances of the word &quot;rote&quot; in the book, so ctrl+F is useless for this, and the index lists something like several dozen page numbers for the word &quot;rote&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-08-2019, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T08:16:04-07:00","id":1322970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1322967#post1322967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a question regarding the phrases &quot;rote quality&quot;, &quot;rote action quality&quot;, and &quot;rote action&quot;. Are these all the same thing?<br /> <br /> My original assumption was that &quot;rote quality&quot; was talking about the spell type, and &quot;rote action quality&quot; was talking about a &quot;rote action.&quot;<br /> <br /> But then in the middle of the text block for Rotes, the spell type, it says, &quot;Casting a Rote from a Grimoire rather than from memory, or casting a Rote she designed herself, gives the mage\u2019s spellcasting dice pool the rote quality.&quot;<br /> <br /> So obviously, unless I'm mistaken, they're using &quot;rote quality&quot; and &quot;rote action quality&quot; interchangeably to refer to &quot;rote actions&quot; right? Unless there is an actual rote quality I completely breezed over? I'm asking because there are 500-some instances of the word &quot;rote&quot; in the book, so ctrl+F is useless for this, and the index lists something like several dozen page numbers for the word &quot;rote&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rote quality = rote action quality = rote action. Reroll all failed dice once.<br /> <br /> The spell type is only termed &quot;Rote&quot;. When casting a Rote from a Grimoire you gain the rote quality on your spell casting roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:02:31-07:00","id":1323834,"title":"","content":"I know this has been asked before but its such a huge topic by this point and finding the precise answer among tangential questions is kinda hard.<br /> <br /> Sorry for asking. I know sometimes people say &quot;yes&quot; and sometimes &quot;no&quot; but, about using fate magic to power up other supernatural powers...<br /> <br /> Can you get rote quality and 8-again to stack simultaneously on a single spell? Yes I know this means rituals if yes.<br /> Can you apply rote8-again to other supernatural instant actions like buffing a werewolf Gift or a Numina, or to use in Clash of Wills? <br /> <br /> Can you get Miracle to work on Supernatural powers? I thought it was yes but, I am unclear if thats from the Hex-Bless section or not cuz I think Miracle omits that possibility? Also would that be something you can use on clashes of wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T00:32:24-07:00","id":1323882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1323834#post1323834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this has been asked before but its such a huge topic by this point and finding the precise answer among tangential questions is kinda hard.<br /> <br /> Sorry for asking. I know sometimes people say &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot; and sometimes &amp;quot;no&amp;quot; but, about using fate magic to power up other supernatural powers...<br /> <br /> Can you get rote quality and 8-again to stack simultaneously on a single spell? Yes I know this means rituals if yes.<br /> Can you apply rote8-again to other supernatural instant actions like buffing a werewolf Gift or a Numina, or to use in Clash of Wills? <br /> <br /> Can you get Miracle to work on Supernatural powers? I thought it was yes but, I am unclear if thats from the Hex-Bless section or not cuz I think Miracle omits that possibility? Also would that be something you can use on clashes of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that to get rote quality and 8-again to stack simultaneously on a single spell you need to use the rule of combined spells.<br /> To affect supernatural powers with hex/boon and miracle i would suggest to add the arcana whose purview includes the power to target","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T00:55:37-07:00","id":1323885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1323834#post1323834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you get rote quality and 8-again to stack simultaneously on a single spell? Yes I know this means rituals if yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, applying two buffs that affect the same thing don't stack, but 8-again and rote quality are different so can stack.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming you mean a single spell will have both 8-again and rote action quality, not that a single spell grants both effects to a different spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you apply rote8-again to other supernatural instant actions like buffing a werewolf Gift or a Numina, or to use in Clash of Wills? </div> </div> </div>8-again definitely for supernatural instant actions, rote action quality I would personally limit to ritual powers such as Theban Sorcery or Werewolf Rites.<br /> <br /> I would be loath to allow dice tricks to apply to Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you get Miracle to work on Supernatural powers? I thought it was yes but, I am unclear if thats from the Hex-Bless section or not cuz I think Miracle omits that possibility? Also would that be something you can use on clashes of wills? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say it can't affect supernatural powers, and it's not a Boon or a Hex, so I'd say it's &quot;fair game.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Prime spell that provoked a Clash from <i>Miracle</i> would provoke a Clash if you tried to usean intercession against the resultant clash, so you'd get a weird stack of clashing to affect clashes. I, personally, would exempt Clash of Wills rolls from the effects because of how I view the mechanic, but I can't think of any rules reason why it wouldn't be allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-12-2019, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T03:14:15-07:00","id":1323897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1323834#post1323834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you get rote quality and 8-again to stack simultaneously on a single spell? Yes I know this means rituals if yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why ritual only? Are you thinking that you'd only get Rote action from casting from a Grimoire? You also get Rote action if you created that Rote in the first place, in which case it's still possible to cast it with a Reach for instant casting. There could possibly be other ways you could get Rote action, but none that I can recall right now. Theoretically speaking, the boon from a Supernal entity should easily be able to grant Rote action on a limited amount of spells.<br /> <br /> 8 Again can be granted by Exceptional Luck or As Above, So Below. They have to be cast first, though. Combining them, as suggested above, doesn't work because the effects of those spells only take place after you've rolled to see if you've successfully cast those spells.<br /> <br /> <s>As for supporting other supernatural powers, I believe it's suggested in the core book that you might grant extra dice.</s> I'm not opposed to extending it to dice tricks, but I would be careful about how easy they can be granted.<br /> I wholeheartedly agree that CoW dice pools should be completely off limits (mages can't even apply dice tricks to their own CoW pools, only bonus dice by playing into the CoW duration system and +1 from Advanced Potency).<br /> Similarly, I like the idea of Rote action only being applicable on ritual actions. I'd come up with a Spirit+Prime Scribe Pack/Wolf Rite spell that grants Rote action on a single Pack or Wolf Rite if the rite leader uses the grimoire as a tool during the ritual. Probably also requiring Arcana that are relevant to the specific rite, such as Forces for a rite that manipulates the weather, or Space for a rite that establishes and enforces a boundary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-12-2019, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T07:03:25-07:00","id":1323947,"title":"","content":"The core book doesn't at all say that it's possible to boost other supernatural creatures' power activation dice pools. I was probably just misremembering the explicit rule that you can't raise or decrease supernatural traits, which does leave the possibility of boosting dice pools open but it's far from being suggested as I previously claimed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:31:45-07:00","id":1323972,"title":"","content":"@Tessie:<br /> <br /> Scarlet Witch is specifically asking about the limits of the Fate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Under Boons it says &quot;{t}he boon may also affect spellcasting rolls <b>and other powers</b> at the cost of +2 Reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for rote quality only applying to rituals read the Fate 3 spell <i>Superlative Luck</i>, the reach option to affect spellcasting is limited to ritual casting and doubles the interval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T03:13:38-07:00","id":1324922,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Create Sympathy (Space 5). Let's say I want to create a connection between two persons. The spell says &quot;the mage creates a new sympathetic connection on the subject&quot;. So is it sufficient that only one of those persons is within sensory range? Or do I need to have at least 2 subjects for this spell to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T03:57:57-07:00","id":1324928,"title":"","content":"As phrased it only seems to require a single subject, but that makes little sense, imo. I would rule it as requiring at least two subjects, creating one between both. Adding additional subjects would either create connections between all of them or between one of the and the others, the mage decides when casting the spell.<br /> Not RAW, but what makes most sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T08:54:44-07:00","id":1324975,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a spell that should, like Familiar, require two subjects imo. You don't actually have to have both subjects present since you can employ Sympathy to make your Sympathy, but you'll still be taking dice penalties to deal with Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T10:12:51-07:00","id":1324994,"title":"","content":"Can you buy the Hallow Merit at rating 5 plus whatever positive features it might have, or is the rating limited to 5 dots max?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T12:00:29-07:00","id":1325028,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T02:25:47-07:00","id":1325185,"title":"","content":"I m not sure about the Amalgams (from signs of sorcery) mechanics.<br /> For example can i join orichalcum and siderite throwing them in a batch of hermium?<br /> Or all the amalgam are meant to be one metal joined with hermium?<br /> In the first case the output material would keep the hermium proprieties or only that of the other two metals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:53:48-07:00","id":1325596,"title":"","content":"The Exarchal Dreams Condition mentions only two ways to get rid of it: Supernal harrowing and reaching Notice 0. It also says that Seers and those with Tyrannical Awakening have the minimum of Notice 1, so I presume they can never be completely rid of the Condition, which makes sense. Unless you betray the Seers, you are a servant of the Exarchs and cannot be completely beneath their notice. And those who had Tyrannical Awakening have Exarch influence written into their very Soul, so they cannot ever get completely rid of it either (nor the dot in Seer Status and potentially the maximum of three dots in Status with the other Orders, as the Seer admiration and other Orders' suspicion will never really go away either).<br /> <br /> I'm bringing this up, because one of the two options when gaining the Full Understanding of an Iron Seal is to remove the Condition. This makes sense for non-Seers who didn't have a Tyrannical Awakening, as one can simply presume that Full Understanding decreases Notice to 0, thus resolving the Condition. But what about those with Tyrannical Awakening? It seems that the resolution requirement of Notice 0 doesn't apply to these mages, as they can never have it. My default presupposition here is that they can never fully remove Exarchal Dreams, even with an Iron Seal - the Condition, dot in Seer Status they have even if they hate the Order, and the potential suspicion of other Orders is a package that comes with Tyrannical Awakening.<br /> <br /> At least that's my interpretation. Frankly, I prefer this approach, as it makes Tyrannical Awakenings more unique and creates interesting story elements beyond trying to reach Full Understanding of an Iron Seal. Besides, it makes both Exarchal Dreams and Iron Seal compatible with each other in their effect's descriptions.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T01:44:05-07:00","id":1325910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1325596#post1325596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exarchal Dreams Condition mentions only two ways to get rid of it: Supernal harrowing and reaching Notice 0. It also says that Seers and those with Tyrannical Awakening have the minimum of Notice 1, so I presume they can never be completely rid of the Condition, which makes sense. Unless you betray the Seers, you are a servant of the Exarchs and cannot be completely beneath their notice. And those who had Tyrannical Awakening have Exarch influence written into their very Soul, so they cannot ever get completely rid of it either (nor the dot in Seer Status and potentially the maximum of three dots in Status with the other Orders, as the Seer admiration and other Orders' suspicion will never really go away either).<br /> <br /> I'm bringing this up, because one of the two options when gaining the Full Understanding of an Iron Seal is to remove the Condition. This makes sense for non-Seers who didn't have a Tyrannical Awakening, as one can simply presume that Full Understanding decreases Notice to 0, thus resolving the Condition. But what about those with Tyrannical Awakening? It seems that the resolution requirement of Notice 0 doesn't apply to these mages, as they can never have it. My default presupposition here is that they can never fully remove Exarchal Dreams, even with an Iron Seal - the Condition, dot in Seer Status they have even if they hate the Order, and the potential suspicion of other Orders is a package that comes with Tyrannical Awakening.<br /> <br /> At least that's my interpretation. Frankly, I prefer this approach, as it makes Tyrannical Awakenings more unique and creates interesting story elements beyond trying to reach Full Understanding of an Iron Seal. Besides, it makes both Exarchal Dreams and Iron Seal compatible with each other in their effect's descriptions.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe full understanding an iron seal is the ONLY way a tyrannical awakened can get rid of the condition.<br /> By interacting with exarcal symbols he could cause an Aponoia to rewrite his awakening","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T02:04:05-07:00","id":1325912,"title":"","content":"Core book says that sleepers witnessing obvious supernal phenomenon cause dissonance in spells, entities and demesne.<br /> It also says that a supernal verge cause spontaneus supernal phenomenon but demesne doesn t.<br /> So what kind of feature has a demesne that could activate dissonance in sleepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T02:42:17-07:00","id":1325917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1325912#post1325912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core book says that sleepers witnessing obvious supernal phenomenon cause dissonance in spells, entities and demesne.<br /> It also says that a supernal verge cause spontaneus supernal phenomenon but demesne doesn t.<br /> So what kind of feature has a demesne that could activate dissonance in sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mage casting an obvious spell inside of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T02:52:03-07:00","id":1325918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1325917#post1325917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Mage casting an obvious spell inside of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think that the dissonance would target both the spell and the demesne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T04:33:02-07:00","id":1325933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1325912#post1325912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what kind of feature has a demesne that could activate dissonance in sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume it simply means mages casting magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:59:29-07:00","id":1327425,"title":"","content":"I already asked something similar but i m still confused by imbued items in Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Persistent Items are always active until their spell\u2019s duration expires, unless dispelled<br /> (pag 67)<br /> <br /> Persistent spell ef-fects imbued into an item lend credence to the Memias school of thought. The spell\u2019s effect is permanently on and needs no additional Imago or trigger from the user<br /> (pag 68)<br /> <br /> I don t understand if persistent spells are by default indefinite duration or not, and if not what criteria are used to determine it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T17:17:44-07:00","id":1327505,"title":"","content":"Can i use Exceptional Luck/Superlative Luck or So Above so Below , for Imbue Item?<br /> Or make a new one for apply Dice Trick on Imbue Item's roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T21:53:37-07:00","id":1327536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1327505#post1327505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i use Exceptional Luck/Superlative Luck or So Above so Below , for Imbue Item?<br /> Or make a new one for apply Dice Trick on Imbue Item's roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i would say that Exeptional and superlative luck can modify the roll, as they can modify magical powers rolls.<br /> But so above so below targets only Yantras, so i would say no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T22:44:39-07:00","id":1327538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1327536#post1327536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, i would say that Exeptional and superlative luck can modify the roll, as they can modify magical powers rolls.<br /> But so above so below targets only Yantras, so i would say no</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks You! Right, So Above So Below cant do &quot;the magic&quot; (this time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T00:12:00-07:00","id":1327542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1327425#post1327425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already asked something similar but i m still confused by imbued items in Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Persistent Items are always active until their spell\u2019s duration expires, unless dispelled<br /> (pag 67)<br /> <br /> Persistent spell ef-fects imbued into an item lend credence to the Memias school of thought. The spell\u2019s effect is permanently on and needs no additional Imago or trigger from the user<br /> (pag 68)<br /> <br /> I don t understand if persistent spells are by default indefinite duration or not, and if not what criteria are used to determine it</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, i don t know how to calculate ALL the spell factors of a persistent spell.<br /> Maybe you must cast the spell before imbuing it ?<br /> Or when the user take the item it activates automatically, with spell factors decided by users and an activation roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 07-26-2019, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T03:14:39-07:00","id":1327553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1327542#post1327542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinking about it, i don t know how to calculate ALL the spell factors of a persistent spell.<br /> Maybe you must cast the spell before imbuing it ?<br /> Or when the user take the item it activates automatically, with spell factors decided by users and an activation roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My interpretation is : a Persistent spell is &quot;Indefinite&quot; OR with a set duration at your choice. You choose the Reach, and can craft it so that Primary Factor is always Potency.<br /> When duration elapsed or the spell is destroyed by dispelletion, you can reactivate the spell without cast it again, but you, user, must use word of power.<br /> <br /> This is usefull for make a kinda &quot;on/off&quot; based on duration of the effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T16:47:10-07:00","id":1329533,"title":"","content":"If I cast a spell Like Heightened Senses is it limited to +5 and going beyond that with a mana presumably or is it just a straight bonus without being held back by a trait limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T17:19:07-07:00","id":1329540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1329533#post1329533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I cast a spell Like Heightened Senses is it limited to +5 and going beyond that with a mana presumably or is it just a straight bonus without being held back by a trait limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good question, but I believe thinking of it as an equipment bonus is ok, and mundane equipment is capped at +5, so I think the extra mana and maybe a reach (like with Honing the Form) can be justified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T20:44:25-07:00","id":1329566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1329533#post1329533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I cast a spell Like Heightened Senses is it limited to +5 and going beyond that with a mana presumably or is it just a straight bonus without being held back by a trait limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moving beyond +5 is almost universally (it could be universal, I'm just not interested in checking all the spells that might do it) done, when it is done, by adding a reach and a point of mana. Both, together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-06T07:41:40-07:00","id":1329607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1329533#post1329533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I cast a spell Like Heightened Senses is it limited to +5 and going beyond that with a mana presumably or is it just a straight bonus without being held back by a trait limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Traits always have a cap (which is usually 5 if no other number is given) while bonuses have no cap. To increase a Trait beyond its cap you need both a Mana and a Reach.<br /> <br /> Heightened Senses grants a bonus to perception (Wits+Composure) rolls so it has no cap.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: Note that equipment modifiers are traits that are applied as bonuses when used, hence they too are capped at +5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-06-2019, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T15:30:52-07:00","id":1329980,"title":"","content":"Do you cast Constant Presence when you think someone\u2019s going to go to the past or when you see that someone\u2019s from the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T16:19:38-07:00","id":1329988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1329980#post1329980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you cast Constant Presence when you think someone\u2019s going to go to the past or when you see that someone\u2019s from the future?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding of Time, it's the latter, because the spell isn't going to extend backwards in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T19:20:56-07:00","id":1330015,"title":"","content":"From my understanding -<br /> <br /> The spell would need to be active in the objective present to prevent changes from 'sticking' when the traveler returns. Duration allowing. it doesn't matter if it was cast in the past (when you saw someone that was from the 'future') or because you believe someone in the present is about to go to the past, as long the spell is active on their return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T00:03:40-07:00","id":1330033,"title":"","content":"To check my understanding of the two different forms of entropic unreality in simplified terms:<br /> <br /> While both the Abyss and the Lower Depths may both subject ordered reality to various forms of breakdown and corruption by their presence or activities, the two interact poorly with each other and usually have a different class of agenda.<br /> <br /> Is it fair to say that, while Depths creatures seek to take something from reality to sustain their signature hungers and the knock-on effects of their doing so are corruptive or destructive, Abyssal entities more often have strange hungers but serve the anti-universes they hail from by corrupting and destroying parts of the Tapestry around them?<br /> <br /> tl;dr Is &quot;virus versus parasite&quot; a reasonable metaphor to describe the main difference between Abyssal and Infernal &quot;demons&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T00:58:44-07:00","id":1330043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1330033#post1330033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To check my understanding of the two different forms of entropic unreality in simplified terms:<br /> <br /> While both the Abyss and the Lower Depths may both subject ordered reality to various forms of breakdown and corruption by their presence or activities, the two interact poorly with each other and usually have a different class of agenda.<br /> <br /> Is it fair to say that, while Depths creatures seek to take something from reality to sustain their signature hungers and the knock-on effects of their doing so are corruptive or destructive, Abyssal entities more often have strange hungers but serve the anti-universes they hail from by corrupting and destroying parts of the Tapestry around them?<br /> <br /> tl;dr Is &amp;quot;virus versus parasite&amp;quot; a reasonable metaphor to describe the main difference between Abyssal and Infernal &amp;quot;demons&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding yes, abyssals are like viruses, who try to enter reality, expand and transform it to make it more like the abyss.<br /> Akarthoi (if i remember their name correctly) try to steal something from reality and bring it back to lower depths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T07:59:07-07:00","id":1330065,"title":"","content":"How work, exactly, the permutation of Arcana in Focused sight? <br /> You add a second, or third, Arcana as bonus dice, or only change Arcana for roll from one to another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T09:36:37-07:00","id":1330070,"title":"","content":"It's honestly kind of confusing, and Signs of Sorcery didn't really clear it up for me. The way I handle it is if you add extra Arcana I give you extra information regarding those Arcana, but I mostly eye-ball it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T10:58:22-07:00","id":1330084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1330070#post1330070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly kind of confusing, and Signs of Sorcery didn't really clear it up for me. The way I handle it is if you add extra Arcana I give you extra information regarding those Arcana, but I mostly eye-ball it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My vote is for bonus dice, based upon<br /> &quot; While Active Mage Sight allows a mage to observe the effects of multiple Arcana at once, Focused Mage Sight requires the mage give all her attention to one Arcanum.<br /> System: The Mage may use Focused Mage Sight to study Mysteries under the purview of any Arcanum she has as part of her Active Mage Sight.<b> See Mage, p. 93 for information on including multiple Arcana in Focused Mage Sight\u2019s dice pool&quot; </b>Signs of Sorcery pg 27<br /> Bold mine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:06:12-07:00","id":1330086,"title":"","content":"Using multiple arcana in FMS seems to provide no bonus, except for the extra information, and it reduces the number of safe rolls you can make by 1 per additional arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T11:15:48-07:00","id":1330094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1330086#post1330086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using multiple arcana in FMS seems to provide no bonus, except for the extra information, and it reduces the number of safe rolls you can make by 1 per additional arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhh Dave, say anything about this? Thanks for your post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:47:33-07:00","id":1330108,"title":"","content":"The reduction in the number of safe rolls is in pg. 93 with all the other rules for Scrutiny, and in the part about Deep Information it mentions the info must be related to the Arcanum being used, but that's all. From that I gather you can examine a mystery with any of it's component Arcana but only get information related to the ones you included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:14:37-07:00","id":1330112,"title":"","content":"Mhhh but... if i erase opacity...i can made again revelation with another Arcana, too?<br /> Example: Examine a spell of Life and Space. My Tyrsus had only Life Spirit and Fate.<br /> Next week he learn is first dot on Space Arcana.<br /> Can he study again the spell with Life And Space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:25:42-07:00","id":1330118,"title":"","content":"That's the part where it gets unclear. I would allow the mage to try a Revelation roll to get any extra info. The way I understand it, you should use the same Opacity as the last time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:36:38-07:00","id":1330121,"title":"","content":"On Discord Server, this is the idea that talked about.<br /> I found this neat too!<br /> Erase Opacity, and than you can RE roll for Revelation with another arcana. Some mystery need 2+ Arcana for be scrutinized/reveleaded.<br /> <br /> Permutation make this information gathering process more fast, when this is not mandatory from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-09-2019, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:29:10-07:00","id":1330147,"title":"","content":"Should Area of Effect spells behave like continuous effects in the area, or bursts that affect everyone at the moment of casting, or can they be both?<br /> <br /> Some effects have an area as a subject, so them being continuous seems obvious. But what about a Shielding spell intended to affect subjects in the area and not the area itself? To me that seems to be ok, but then I'm asking myself what if I just want it to be like a burst, like Shielding allies before heading into danger, is that ok too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:49:07-07:00","id":1330152,"title":"","content":"AoE effects affect only those in the area, if the subjects leave the area they are no longer valid subjects for an AoE spell.<br /> <br /> Your example of a Shielding Spell is a spell that has multiple subjects and is not actually cast on the area at all, as you pointed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:53:32-07:00","id":1330155,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess that makes sense. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T06:33:01-07:00","id":1330377,"title":"","content":"Good day,<br /> I understand the rules of inuring a spell from wisdom roll, but i don t understand how it is possible.<br /> You make a bargain with the abyss or something similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T07:58:16-07:00","id":1330381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885489-whats-the-logic-behind-inured-spells\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885489-whats-the-logic-behind-inured-spells\"> Whats the logic behind 'Inured' spells - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885489-whats-the-logic-behind-inured-spells\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885489-whats-the-logic-behind-inured-spells </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I am vastly enjoying my first read through of 2nd edition so far, but I am still struggling to get my head around a few things. I understand that Wisdom is to an extent divorced from plain old Morality or the Integrity system that Mortals use. My read is that its meant to represent the Magi's ability to use his powers responsibly and seems intended to encourage a more calculated and precise mentality (hence things like premeditated murder being a lesser sin than manslaughter.) I am really struggling to understand how 'inuring spells' fits into this. PG 89 gives us the mechanical effects, but I cant </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I had similar questions a while back and created this thread. It might help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T09:22:27-07:00","id":1330395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1330381#post1330381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885489-whats-the-logic-behind-inured-spells\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-inured-spells</a><br /> <br /> I had similar questions a while back and created this thread. It might help!</div> </div> </div> </div>It cleared my toughts, thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T17:52:38-07:00","id":1330653,"title":"","content":"How common are Imbued Items in mage society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T19:10:35-07:00","id":1330664,"title":"","content":"I think there should be a fair number of them kicking around, or at least stashed in the Orders' vaults. My reasoning is that even if you think there should be few people able to create them, you have millennia of Diamond history to pass them from Master to Apprentice and to accumulate in Order Archives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T23:52:28-07:00","id":1331030,"title":"","content":"What happens to your oneiros when you die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T02:13:11-07:00","id":1331045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331030#post1331030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to your oneiros when you die?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that probably it s slowly absorbed by temenos, the memories in common with other people at last, while the others fade away","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T04:03:20-07:00","id":1331049,"title":"","content":"The Oneiros is both your soul and your mind (in a way) but when you die the mind dies and the soul disappears into the unknown. As such I think that the Oneiros becomes cut off from the rest of the Astral, or at least changed in a way that makes it impossible to visit. What happens after that is pretty difficult to observe in-setting since you can't observe an Oneiros from the outside and scrying inside it might not reveal anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T08:35:31-07:00","id":1331069,"title":"","content":"The best way to find out is to be in the Oneiros when the person generating it kicks the bucket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T08:43:47-07:00","id":1331072,"title":"","content":"Relatedly, what happens to visitors in an Oneiros of someone who gets their soul taken? What happens to the inside of the Oneiros when it disconnects from the person it's representing? Also, why is removing parts of an Oneiros capable of instantly making huge changes to a individual's personality while the total loss of an Oneiros confers much more gradual changes and starts out extremely subtle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T09:24:11-07:00","id":1331079,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been implied that the Oneiros is in the soul. There\u2019s also no indication that I can recall that souls require bodies to maintain their state. Though I\u2019d speculate that that they enter a stasis without a body providing new input. So, a visitor would probably notice that the Oneiros they\u2019re in is still capable of being interacted with, but making changes in it is frustrating and more difficult (Or maybe not since the visitor would now be the Oneiros\u2019 only source of new stimulus).<br /> <br /> Define big and subtle changes though, like if a goetia is yoinked that change is only as big as the goetia itself was, andcif you yoink the whole soul I don\u2019t really consider the flipping of Virtue and Vice followed by a slippery slope into complete apathy really that subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T10:41:16-07:00","id":1331087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331069#post1331069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way to find out is to be in the Oneiros when the person generating it kicks the bucket.</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201cbest way.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T10:48:54-07:00","id":1331089,"title":"","content":"I never said that it is subtle. I said that it <i>starts out</i> extremely subtle because no one might even notice the change other than &quot;he's been a bit perky these last few days&quot;. Yank basically any Goetia from an Oneiros and that person immediately loses that aspect of their personality. Depending on what that is, it might also be subtle but it can also be extremely jarring.<br /> <br /> Consider this: Removing some fuel rods or control rods from a nuclear reactor will immediately start affecting its performance, just like removing parts of your Oneiros will affect your personality. Removing all of the rods will lead to a complete shutdown, and the same seem to hold true for an Oneiros if you remove all aspects of that person's personality. (It's just not feasible since an Oneiros contains multitudes that can't easily be handled even with Advance Scale factors.)<br /> If you instead directly remove the entire reactor, you obviously lose your entire output. But if you remove the entire Oneiros of a person (as the soul or with the soul, doesn't really matter since it's removed either way), you don't have them entering a catatonic state. It's as if there's still a reactor there, with a little weird performance, sure, but fully functional. It's only over time that the major consequences of soul loss will take effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:09:27-07:00","id":1331111,"title":"","content":"I personally think of the Soul as the fuel of a person's being. The Oneiros is highly personalized, it's in essence the unconscious Mind, full with each individuals memories, fears, and other personality traits. Souls on the other hand are mostly interchangeable. As I understand it, and I think the book uses this same language, when you take out someone's Soul they start &quot;running on fumes&quot;. They can prolong that state for a bit, but inevitable they shut down. But if you put the Soul back, any Soul, they will slowly rev up once again.<br /> <br /> A possible theory for what happens when you die is that a part of your Oneiros becomes your ghost's Memories, Anchors, their Virtue and Vice and maybe forming part of their Bans, while the rest just ceasing to be at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T16:34:42-07:00","id":1331134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331111#post1331111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A possible theory for what happens when you die is that a part of your Oneiros becomes your ghost's Memories, Anchors, their Virtue and Vice and maybe forming part of their Bans, while the rest just ceasing to be at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not fit with ghosts formed from near-death experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T08:09:51-07:00","id":1331210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331134#post1331134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does not fit with ghosts formed from near-death experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or ghosts of animals or inanimate objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T08:19:28-07:00","id":1331211,"title":"","content":"I don't think Inanimate object's ghosts even have Memories or Anchors or anything like that. Animals DO have minds, even if humans can't Astral travel to them. In Astral Realms it mentions some Mages debate whether the Oneiros exists if there isn't a traveler there. The way I understand it is that the Oneiros is the form a traveler makes sense of the unconscious mind. Just because we can't Astral travel to animals or other beings' minds doesn't mean they don't exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T09:30:52-07:00","id":1331343,"title":"","content":"Do all the mages in a teamwork casting of a spell use a spell control slot while all the primary caster maintains spell control? Do they all need to spend a willpower to release spell control safely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T11:02:45-07:00","id":1331361,"title":"","content":"Simply put I don't think so, it wouldn't be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T13:37:07-07:00","id":1331379,"title":"","content":"Just the primary caster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-18T10:48:45-07:00","id":1331484,"title":"","content":"If you open a target's Doors with magic, does they count as willing/convinced to swear an oath or does it also count as forcing them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-18T14:00:51-07:00","id":1331508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331484#post1331484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you open a target's Doors with magic, does they count as willing/convinced to swear an oath or does it also count as forcing them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say that\u2019s going to be dependent on the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-18T14:20:10-07:00","id":1331511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331508#post1331508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d say that\u2019s going to be dependent on the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>For example, you find a capable gunslinger, he is very drunk. You want him to swear to &quot;defend and assist [given person] to the best of your abilities and may old guilts come due if you don't&quot;. If the gunslinger doesn't hate the person and you use magic to open the last Doors, to give that last push towards a yes, is he a valid target for Sworn Oaths ? I consider forcing him would be more along the lines of psychic domination, possession, etc. But Emotional Urging could count as manipulation, but I am not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-18T18:04:36-07:00","id":1331528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1331511#post1331511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, you find a capable gunslinger, he is very drunk. You want him to swear to &quot;defend and assist [given person] to the best of your abilities and may old guilts come due if you don't&quot;. If the gunslinger doesn't hate the person and you use magic to open the last Doors, to give that last push towards a yes, is he a valid target for Sworn Oaths ? I consider forcing him would be more along the lines of psychic domination, possession, etc. But Emotional Urging could count as manipulation, but I am not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is, does the person feel like they're being forced or that they're making a choice of their own free will?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-18T18:30:58-07:00","id":1331530,"title":"","content":"Its basically me wondering if you could use a Ruling of Fate to make sure a target would be intoxicated, delirious or otherwise medicated to a degree that it lowers their Doors by [Potency]. <br /> <br /> The idea is inspired by Prisioner of Azkaban, when Harry drinks a luck potion and manages to convince Slughorn to give up key evidence. He managed to get talk to him after he was drunk and nostalgic about the past, so I thought it could be a cool Acanthus persuasion and oath binding trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T01:39:35-07:00","id":1331552,"title":"","content":"I think that's better represented through bonus dice on social rolls from Exceptional Luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T03:59:40-07:00","id":1331564,"title":"","content":"Thought it over a bit (and reread the original question). What I meant is that the way Harry convinced Slughorn seems to be a combination of Charmed, for nudging the two into the path that leads to Slughorn drinking and reminiscing thus removing one Door, and bonus dice and/or dice tricks on Socialise and Persuasion rolls during their conversation, just like how Exceptional Luck works.<br /> <br /> Applying Charmed in that way removed a Door by making Harry put them into the best situation possible for what Harry wanted, and as such it did not actually affect Slughorn personally and it shouldn't count towards supernatural coercion.<br /> Your other suggestion, casting on a subject to make them end up in a more receptive state of mind, is more of a grey area. That is a much more direct manipulation of your target, and if the spell would <i>force</i> the target into becoming intoxicated (which I think would be Fate Weaving at the least) regardless of whether they wanted to imbibe or not then I'd definitely say it's forced.<br /> <br /> What I think a Fate mage should do in order to lower Doors (without it being supernatural coercion) is to use a spell that's kinda like Shifting the Odds and the Charmed Condition in that it makes the subject of the spell (possibly the mage) come across the target in a more receptive context. I don't think it should remove more than one Door, and might also end up failing if it's not possible for the target to end up in such a context (just like Shifting the Odds can fail if what you're looking for literally can't be reached). After that, Exceptional Luck on your own rolls to make you more persuasive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T08:23:12-07:00","id":1331603,"title":"","content":"Yeah, exceptional luck was my first approach, but I wanted to compress all that into a single Door opening spell. <br /> <br /> The lucky stumble into a situation where the person is highly suggestible state seemed like a suitable trope for a lucky character.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it was meant to be a variation of Shifting The Odds mixed with Ruling's ability to apply Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:22:41-07:00","id":1332022,"title":"","content":"Question about Lunargent: Since it is a perfected version of silver, shouldn't it be even more damaging to werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:41:33-07:00","id":1332026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332022#post1332022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Lunargent: Since it is a perfected version of silver, shouldn't it be even more damaging to werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T15:56:40-07:00","id":1332033,"title":"","content":"No, definitely not.<br /> <br /> Giving Perfected material banes a damage boost would involve somehow predicting the effects of all material banes - does Perfected Fire do extra damage to vampires? Should Perfected Gold do extra damage to a spirit that has gold as its bane? What about material weaknesses that aren't straight damage?<br /> <br /> Simply too much bother, which is why we went for &quot;removes all other specifications, then acts like X&quot;. So Siderite counts as cold iron, meteroic iron, flame-forged iron, stainless steel, cast iron - whatever adjectives the supernatural being of choice bolts onto &quot;iron&quot;, Siderite counts as it. As Lunargent counts for Silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T16:10:44-07:00","id":1332036,"title":"","content":"No. It'd be their bane still, but no. Signs of Sorcery explicitly states this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T16:18:31-07:00","id":1332038,"title":"","content":"On top of being much simpler, I also prefer that perfected materials won't cause more damage. Werewolves' Bane is silver, so silver is already the purest form of their Bane. Lunargent is the perfected version of silver, but it shouldn't count as better or more pure than regular silver for the purposes of werewolves because regular silver is already the epitome or ideal version of their Bane.<br /> There might still be other ways of increasing the damage of silver, but I think they should actively interact with the property of being a Bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T17:34:26-07:00","id":1332044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332038#post1332038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of being much simpler, I also prefer that perfected materials won't cause more damage. Werewolves' Bane is silver, so silver is already the purest form of their Bane. Lunargent is the perfected version of silver, but it shouldn't count as better or more pure than regular silver for the purposes of werewolves because regular silver is already the epitome or ideal version of their Bane.<br /> There might still be other ways of increasing the damage of silver, but I think they should actively interact with the property of being a Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is always the option of letting them &quot;engineer&quot; harmful Essence. For example, take a fang of a werewolf or wolf blooded, for they remember how to fell the great wolf. Next take iron, for it has tasted the blood of humans through the ages. Put them into a pool/bowl/spring of water that reflects the full moon, that they may soak in the moons tears and fury. Channel this into a weapon of silver, that it may bite deeper into the Uratha. At least good for a few charges.<br /> <br /> At least that a very Thrysus solution. <br /> <br /> But a Moros might just make a wasp knife or a custom bullet, then have it fragment after it does damage or dissolve into a fine powder and flood the unfortunate victim's organism. Naturally, the silver was Weaved with the properties of tetradotoxin, after the alloy with Hermium was finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-21-2019, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:27:16-07:00","id":1332104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332033#post1332033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, definitely not.<br /> <br /> Giving Perfected material banes a damage boost would involve somehow predicting the effects of all material banes - does Perfected Fire do extra damage to vampires? Should Perfected Gold do extra damage to a spirit that has gold as its bane? What about material weaknesses that aren't straight damage?<br /> <br /> Simply too much bother, which is why we went for &quot;removes all other specifications, then acts like X&quot;. So Siderite counts as cold iron, meteroic iron, flame-forged iron, stainless steel, cast iron - whatever adjectives the supernatural being of choice bolts onto &quot;iron&quot;, Siderite counts as it. As Lunargent counts for Silver.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332038#post1332038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of being much simpler, I also prefer that perfected materials won't cause more damage. Werewolves' Bane is silver, so silver is already the purest form of their Bane. Lunargent is the perfected version of silver, but it shouldn't count as better or more pure than regular silver for the purposes of werewolves because regular silver is already the epitome or ideal version of their Bane.<br /> There might still be other ways of increasing the damage of silver, but I think they should actively interact with the property of being a Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, makes sense, thanks. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another question: On signs of sorcery I've read about &quot;spontaneous casting&quot; and &quot;spontaneous spell&quot;, but I'm highly unsure about what it means. Can you give me a definition of those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:34:13-07:00","id":1332106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332104#post1332104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: On signs of sorcery I've read about &quot;spontaneous casting&quot; and &quot;spontaneous spell&quot;, but I'm highly unsure about what it means. Can you give me a definition of those?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the context I'd say non-Rote spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T06:14:26-07:00","id":1332113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332104#post1332104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, makes sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another question: On signs of sorcery I've read about &quot;spontaneous casting&quot; and &quot;spontaneous spell&quot;, but I'm highly unsure about what it means. Can you give me a definition of those?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a typo for improvised spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T06:27:14-07:00","id":1332115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332113#post1332113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a typo for improvised spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, ok, thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T09:05:35-07:00","id":1332297,"title":"","content":"Hello (again), i have a doubt regarding the possibility of 8-Again and rote action active at the same time on an object.<br /> Is it possible that both effects take place or rote action overwrites 8-Again (or vice versa)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T09:37:34-07:00","id":1332303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332297#post1332297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello (again), i have a doubt regarding the possibility of 8-Again and rote action active at the same time on an object.<br /> Is it possible that both effects take place or rote action overwrites 8-Again (or vice versa)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of an ST call, but there's no reason I can think of to make one overwrite the other except that the chances of Exceptional Success continue to go up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T09:56:52-07:00","id":1332311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332297#post1332297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello (again), i have a doubt regarding the possibility of 8-Again and rote action active at the same time on an object.<br /> Is it possible that both effects take place or rote action overwrites 8-Again (or vice versa)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can find no reason both would not be able to apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T10:13:58-07:00","id":1332318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332311#post1332311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can find no reason both would not be able to apply.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, thanks. I read what seemed to me as an &quot;ascending&quot; order (can't remember precisely where) and the thought stuck ^_^'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T10:21:58-07:00","id":1332321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332297#post1332297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello (again), i have a doubt regarding the possibility of 8-Again and rote action active at the same time on an object.<br /> Is it possible that both effects take place or rote action overwrites 8-Again (or vice versa)?</div> </div> </div> </div>On my guess this is a case of spell stacking. Two Dice Trick, from spells, at the same time, at my table is a case of stacking.<br /> &quot; Spell Stacking<br /> When multiple spells affect the same aspect of a character the<br /> effects of the spells do not stack, and instead the spell with the<br /> highest Potency takes effect.&quot; (Mage Awakening pp 118)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T11:03:53-07:00","id":1332331,"title":"","content":"That is good ruling, although there are many other sources of dice tricks. Last week a player used a spell to get rote action on an asset skill from professional training, and I didn't even think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T11:59:28-07:00","id":1332349,"title":"","content":"I concur it's good ruling, thinking about it, good point of view","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T14:44:26-07:00","id":1332369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1330377#post1330377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good day,<br /> I understand the rules of inuring a spell from wisdom roll, but i don t understand how it is possible.<br /> You make a bargain with the abyss or something similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>To avoid necro\u2019ing that thread, my take is that no, inuring does not make a single lick of sense and probably shouldn\u2019t be possible, and that\u2019s precisely why Paradox is the consequence of doing it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T15:00:47-07:00","id":1332477,"title":"","content":"do legacy attainments trigger peripheral mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T16:42:40-07:00","id":1332483,"title":"","content":"Yes. Unless they deal with a concealment power of some kind.<br /> <br /> Mages\u2019 peripheries are source-agnostic. They\u2019re triggered by any supernatural event, so a Legacy Attainment using the wielder\u2019s Gnosis instead of the Supernal World? Doesn\u2019t matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T04:52:06-07:00","id":1332521,"title":"","content":"Does Tipping the Hourglass affect Initiative order or Initiative score?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T10:19:37-07:00","id":1332553,"title":"","content":"It seems fairly implied that it is the initiative score that changes for the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T10:56:13-07:00","id":1332674,"title":"","content":"Something that popped up. We are up against a vampire with the swarm form merit. The ST says that the first mages spell will fail since he has only 1 person as a target, and the he needs to either change it to an area of effect spell, or do something else.<br /> <br /> The player, a Mastigos, argues that it shouldn't matter as it's still one target, the vampire, and not every crow he became.<br /> <br /> The ST counters that a size 7 bear is also one target, but you need to account for the fact that it is size 7 in the imago. The same applies to the swarm.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where I fall on this as it is such a grey area I have never encountered. What is the general consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25600-redtooth-redtooth","name":"Redtooth-Redtooth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:56:39-07:00","id":1332702,"title":"","content":"Is swarm form reflexive or is it an instant action? I would say you need extra spellfactors to target the vampire's swarm form, but if you beat it in initiative and their merit is not reflexive, you can get the first shot in.<br /> <br /> There is more info on swarms in the life arcana section I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:56:02-07:00","id":1332722,"title":"","content":"When you use a legacy attainment do you trigger peripheral mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:59:23-07:00","id":1332723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332722#post1332722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you use a legacy attainment do you trigger peripheral mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Peripheral Mage Sight triggers on all activated supernatural effects, except those meant to hide something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T17:46:10-07:00","id":1332754,"title":"","content":"New question (I think -- I didn't see it in the last ten pages or so.)<br /> <br /> I know that this book is still undergoing the errata process, but I'm curious about Contact High, from Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> a. Clearly it's cast on the caster themselves, and doesn't seem to take extra factors for targets. But do the effects also affect the caster? i.e. can they benefit from the initiative boost? Do they take the initiative penalty as well? Is this something they opt in to, one way or another, or does it require additional spell factors?<br /> <br /> b. The reach effect immunizes living targets, but applies the drug to everything they touch. What is the point of this? If it doesn't affect living targets, why does it matter if it covers everything? Or is it +1 reach per target immunized? It seems really unclear.<br /> <br /> c. The spell doesn't list a withstand, and the primary factor in the spell is duration. So do we treat this as resisting a regular drug, then? And if so, what is the toxicity rating? Equal to the potency? Seems like you'd need to bump the potency for that to be at all useful.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25599-harvester","name":"Harvester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T07:24:51-07:00","id":1332810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332702#post1332702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is swarm form reflexive or is it an instant action? I would say you need extra spellfactors to target the vampire's swarm form, but if you beat it in initiative and their merit is not reflexive, you can get the first shot in.<br /> <br /> There is more info on swarms in the life arcana section I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vampire was already a swarm, and the swarm section in life doesn't give a definitive answer on this question. The player and ST are debating it, and I told them I would post the question here for clarification. <br /> <br /> I still don't know where I land. The ST is adamant that there is no reason a Mage wouldn't have to account for the fact that the person is suddenly multiple creatures spread out over a large area. And the player still argues that targets mean individuals, and not all the things a individual may be connected to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25600-redtooth-redtooth","name":"Redtooth-Redtooth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T10:13:45-07:00","id":1332833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redtooth-Redtooth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332674#post1332674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that popped up. We are up against a vampire with the swarm form merit. The ST says that the first mages spell will fail since he has only 1 person as a target, and the he needs to either change it to an area of effect spell, or do something else.<br /> <br /> The player, a Mastigos, argues that it shouldn't matter as it's still one target, the vampire, and not every crow he became.<br /> <br /> The ST counters that a size 7 bear is also one target, but you need to account for the fact that it is size 7 in the imago. The same applies to the swarm.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where I fall on this as it is such a grey area I have never encountered. What is the general consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on the spell.<br /> <br /> For a Mind spell, there is still only one actual <i>mind</i> controlling the swarm, thus it still only has one target (the brain is not the mind), however you still must account for the increased size of the swarm. And yes, this means a swarm could potentially defeat a spell by expanding to a larger size.<br /> <br /> Other spells might have to account for the additional physical bodies: most Life (or Death, in the case of vampires) spells would need to target each individual body in the swarm because the spells are specifically affecting the bodies, which are decidedly numerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T12:07:13-07:00","id":1332859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332833#post1332833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it depends on the spell.<br /> <br /> For a Mind spell, there is still only one actual <i>mind</i> controlling the swarm, thus it still only has one target (the brain is not the mind), however you still must account for the increased size of the swarm. And yes, this means a swarm could potentially defeat a spell by expanding to a larger size.<br /> <br /> Other spells might have to account for the additional physical bodies: most Life (or Death, in the case of vampires) spells would need to target each individual body in the swarm because the spells are specifically affecting the bodies, which are decidedly numerous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what the player, who is a Mastigos, is saying. He was attempting to control the swarms leader, and told the ST that it was only one mind.<br /> <br /> The ST is adamant in his ruling however. I believe his response was &quot;The normal sized guy, and the 7 foot guy also only have one mind, but you still have to take into account the size of the 7 foot guy. Thus you need to take into account that the mind belonging to said vampire is now in several bodies. Hence you need to reflect this in your spell's imago. AoE is your best bet&quot;<br /> <br /> I like the size idea though, maybe it will be a good compromise point for the ST and player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25600-redtooth-redtooth","name":"Redtooth-Redtooth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T14:39:06-07:00","id":1332892,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that a mind has no size stat. Still, I'd side with the ST.<br /> <br /> The scale table in MTAw 2nd Ed. core rules p. 114 details this.<br /> If you go by RAW, the swarm can either be targetted as individual subjects (size of the largest subject is below 5 and thus irrelevant in this case) or by applying the area of effect column and determining the volume of the swarm (possibly also hitting other targets swarmed over in the area).<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, that even tho the spell is targetting the mind as an abstract concept, the spell still plays out in the fallen world, where the subject is the swarm, not the mind directly that controls it. It 'affects' the mind of the swarm by affecting the swarm as its subject(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","user":"Caimbeul","date":". 08-27-2019, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T17:53:02-07:00","id":1332922,"title":"","content":"Can I take a spell like Honing the Form and then change the target scale from effecting subjects to a area scale buffing or debuffing anyone who enters the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T21:53:41-07:00","id":1332935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332922#post1332922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I take a spell like Honing the Form and then change the target scale from effecting subjects to a area scale buffing or debuffing anyone who enters the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>*affecting<br /> <br /> And yes, you can choose whether it affects an area (and all contained therein) or specific targets upon casting.<br /> <br /> However, if choosing the former, bear in mind that as soon as someone leaves the area of effect the effects of the spell end upon them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T23:32:26-07:00","id":1332937,"title":"","content":"Probably someone already asked it but i am unable to find the thread.<br /> A mage with matter 3 and prime 4 casting a spell that require matter 3 and prime 2 has 1 or 3 free reaches ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T00:06:40-07:00","id":1332941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332937#post1332937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably someone already asked it but i am unable to find the thread.<br /> A mage with matter 3 and prime 4 casting a spell that require matter 3 and prime 2 has 1 or 3 free reaches ?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Highest arcanum of the spell vs your own -&gt; matter 3 vs matter 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T03:53:17-07:00","id":1332954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caimbeul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332941#post1332941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Highest arcanum of the spell vs your own -&gt; matter 3 vs matter 3</div> </div> </div> </div>The text actually says that it's the mage's highest Arcanum (which would be Prime 4 in this case) that determines free Reaches, but I would personally rule it as you say, take the highest Arcanum required for the spell. My rationale is that the highest Arcanum of the spell is what determines the base effect of the spell; any other Arcana just add to the effect or just fulfil some prerequisite for it. That's how you determine the dice pool so it's more consistent. If multiple Arcana are tied, I'd take whichever of those that would grant fewest amount of Reaches. For example, a mage with Life 4, Matter 5 that wants to turn someone to a pillar of salt (Life 4, Matter 4) would have one free Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T09:06:36-07:00","id":1332981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1332954#post1332954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The text actually says that it's the mage's highest Arcanum (which would be Prime 4 in this case) that determines free Reaches, but I would personally rule it as you say, take the highest Arcanum required for the spell. My rationale is that the highest Arcanum of the spell is what determines the base effect of the spell; any other Arcana just add to the effect or just fulfil some prerequisite for it. That's how you determine the dice pool so it's more consistent. If multiple Arcana are tied, I'd take whichever of those that would grant fewest amount of Reaches. For example, a mage with Life 4, Matter 5 that wants to turn someone to a pillar of salt (Life 4, Matter 4) would have one free Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right, I tend to confuse that. As 'Combined Spells' states that the reach is calculated (as normal) against the highest arcanum of the mage that meets or exceeds the requirements of the spell.<br /> <b>So the correct answer by RAW is: 3 reach as it measures the involved arcana against the highest the mage posesses. In that case it would be Prime.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T06:25:28-07:00","id":1333094,"title":"","content":"Among the Arcana used in the spell, the Highest Arcanum determines the free reaches and the lowest Arcanum determines the dice pool. At least that's how I understand it. So, for instance a Mage with Gnosis 3, Prime 4 and Mind 2, casting a Prime 3 - Mind 1 spell, would have 2 free reaches and a dice pool of 3 dice (3 from Gnosis + 2 from Mind -2 per spell beyond the first)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 08-29-2019, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:54:47-07:00","id":1333103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333094#post1333094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the Arcana used in the spell, the Highest Arcanum determines the free reaches and the lowest Arcanum determines the dice pool. At least that's how I understand it. So, for instance a Mage with Gnosis 3, Prime 4 and Mind 2, casting a Prime 3 - Mind 1 spell, would have 2 free reaches and a dice pool of 3 dice (3 from Gnosis + 2 from Mind -2 per spell beyond the first)</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the rules of combined spells, not of spells that use multiple arcana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T10:26:33-07:00","id":1333123,"title":"","content":"All examples of spells that use multiple Arcana in the book (other than combined spells) are spells from one Arcanum that have an extra effect if you have a number of dots in another Arcanum. But they are still considered spells of the first Arcanum I think. For instance, the matter 4 spell &quot;Transubstantiation&quot; can do more things if you also have Life 4, but it is still a Matter spell. From what I understand, the fact that it contains a Life effect doesn't account for anything. It should be treated as a normal matter spell in regard to reaching and dice pools regardless of whether you have the Life dots or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 08-29-2019, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T11:08:03-07:00","id":1333408,"title":"","content":"Which Arcanum would be used to perceive God-Machine angels in Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T15:46:56-07:00","id":1333435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333408#post1333408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Arcanum would be used to perceive God-Machine angels in Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Dark Eras 2 preview it mentions mages being able to mess with infrastructure with Fate/Prime so presumably those would be the arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T12:31:06-07:00","id":1333580,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know if this has been covered before, but a discussion on a discord server was sparked by me spitballing spell ideas. I\u2019m fairly new to actually playing mage and trying to train up my creativity, looking at the mage armor attainments it sparked an idea in my head that if I can conceivably do what is presented as an attainment at the right arcana, I could duplicate a similar effect with a full spell<br /> <br /> What would be the point of that you may ask? It isn\u2019t reflexive and counts against my held spells if I do that. Yes, but I can also potentially up its scale and apply that \u201carmor\u201d to a group of people, sharing my ability to apply defense to firearms with space armor for example<br /> <br /> The general consensus has been \u201cno, That sounds broken and waiting for abuse\u201d, which fair... but this is Mage so that in and of itself doesn\u2019t seem like an issue.<br /> <br /> And if it isn\u2019t possible, why not? What in game reason is there for me to not be able to replicate at least the partial effect of mage armor, sans being able to cast it reflexively and have it not count against my held spells. Since as a full spell it wouldn\u2019t benefit from either of those and I think that\u2019s the balancing factor<br /> <br /> Ideally I would like something kind of official on this if possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","user":"Lord Jub-Jub","date":". 09-03-2019, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T20:35:31-07:00","id":1333633,"title":"","content":"how fast would you allow someone with perfect recall and transmission to be able to write a program/text they already experienced before to a computer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T22:24:09-07:00","id":1333640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333633#post1333633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how fast would you allow someone with perfect recall and transmission to be able to write a program/text they already experienced before to a computer?</div> </div> </div> </div>With Forces 2, and assuming they saw the underlying binaries or code and not merely the program running, you'd be able to instantaneously &quot;write&quot; the program to a disk; your limiting factor is spell casting time. If you just put the code on the disk it'd still have to compile, though.<br /> <br /> Typing it would be based on how quicklthe player could convince me they could type, but anything of complexity would take a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T23:27:53-07:00","id":1333643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333580#post1333580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know if this has been covered before, but a discussion on a discord server was sparked by me spitballing spell ideas. I\u2019m fairly new to actually playing mage and trying to train up my creativity, looking at the mage armor attainments it sparked an idea in my head that if I can conceivably do what is presented as an attainment at the right arcana, I could duplicate a similar effect with a full spell<br /> <br /> What would be the point of that you may ask? It isn\u2019t reflexive and counts against my held spells if I do that. Yes, but I can also potentially up its scale and apply that \u201carmor\u201d to a group of people, sharing my ability to apply defense to firearms with space armor for example<br /> <br /> The general consensus has been \u201cno, That sounds broken and waiting for abuse\u201d, which fair... but this is Mage so that in and of itself doesn\u2019t seem like an issue.<br /> <br /> And if it isn\u2019t possible, why not? What I\u2019m game reason is there for me to not be able to replicate at least the partial effect of mage armor, sans being able to cast it reflexively and have it not count against my held spells. Since as a full spell it wouldn\u2019t benefit from wither of those and I think that\u2019s the balancing factor<br /> <br /> Ideally I would like something kind of official on this if possible</div> </div> </div> </div>It suggested that prime 4 can give magical powers to things that have none (the spell apocalypse give mage sight, the imbue item attainment give the ability to cast a spell).<br /> So i think that a prime 4 spell could give template abilities like pattern restoration.<br /> For arcana attainment a prime 4 + the arcana level of the correspondent attainment seems reasonable, but i would add some limitation:<br /> -the spell can give only utility attainment<br /> -for balancing issue i would call for the &quot;1 extra mana cost for summoning supernal perfection&quot;<br /> -for mage armor the 1 mana cost should be payed, by the caster or by a mage target, for every subject of the spell, and probably i would allow it to last only one scene","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T22:04:31-07:00","id":1333790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333643#post1333643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It suggested that prime 4 can give magical powers to things that have none (the spell apocalypse give mage sight, the imbue item attainment give the ability to cast a spell).<br /> So i think that a prime 4 spell could give template abilities like pattern restoration.<br /> For arcana attainment a prime 4 + the arcana level of the correspondent attainment seems reasonable, but i would add some limitation:<br /> -the spell can give only utility attainment<br /> -for balancing issue i would call for the &amp;quot;1 extra mana cost for summoning supernal perfection&amp;quot;<br /> -for mage armor the 1 mana cost should be payed, by the caster or by a mage target, for every subject of the spell, and probably i would allow it to last only one scene</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but that isn\u2019t what I asked. I\u2019m not trying to give someone the power to use the attainment, I don\u2019t even care so much about the defense boost. I\u2019m asking if I can use creative thaumaturgy to replicate at least an effect one might see in a mage armor attainment, albeit not being reflexive and counting against my held spells, with the possibility of paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T01:18:19-07:00","id":1333801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333790#post1333790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay but that isn\u2019t what I asked. I\u2019m not trying to give someone the power to use the attainment, I don\u2019t even care so much about the defense boost. I\u2019m asking if I can use creative thaumaturgy to replicate at least an effect one might see in a mage armor attainment, albeit not being reflexive and counting against my held spells, with the possibility of paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, core book says &quot;Mages protect themselves from general harm through the power of their Arcana with the Mage Armor Attainment rather than Shielding spells.&quot;.<br /> I think that it a mainly for balancing issue so, in theory a prime 5 spell + ARCANA 2 could do a similar effect IF AND ONLY IF the storyteller is ok with that.<br /> The logic is that prime 5 give complete mastery over its purview (spells), so if the storyteller says it is possible beyond archmastery i would use that arcana combination","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T07:53:11-07:00","id":1333829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333801#post1333801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, core book says &amp;quot;Mages protect themselves from general harm through the power of their Arcana with the Mage Armor Attainment rather than Shielding spells.&amp;quot;.<br /> I think that it a mainly for balancing issue so, in theory a prime 5 spell + ARCANA 2 could do a similar effect IF AND ONLY IF the storyteller is ok with that.<br /> The logic is that prime 5 give complete mastery over its purview (spells), so if the storyteller says it is possible beyond archmastery i would use that arcana combination</div> </div> </div> </div>So then your answer is no. I cannot use creative thaumaturgy in order to duplicate, for example, the secondary effect of space mage armor of applying defense against firearms on its own because... the exarchs don\u2019t let me I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T09:13:38-07:00","id":1333834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333829#post1333829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So then your answer is no. I cannot use creative thaumaturgy in order to duplicate, for example, the secondary effect of space mage armor of applying defense against firearms on its own because... the exarchs don\u2019t let me I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, i would allow those secondary effect as a merit or a weird legacy attainment.<br /> Naturally all that i ve said is only my opinion and i m not a writer or administrator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T09:35:59-07:00","id":1333840,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13063_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13063\" data-vbnamecard=\"13063\">Lord Jub-Jub</a> if your goal is to provide the ability to apply defense against firearms, that is doable with things other than Mage Armor; specifically the Time 3 spell Acceleration has that as one of its effects.<br /> <br /> Applying the Spirit or Death versions would likely be Weaving effects of both Life (if targeting a living thing) and Spirit or Death as appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T04:30:57-07:00","id":1333934,"title":"","content":"I don't think the reason Mages use the Mage Armor attainments to rather than spells to protect THEMSELVES is because they can't do it with spells. I think it's just because it's easier and safer. I believe its fully possible to use a spell for protection. Spells used this way could even be much more powerful than Mage Armor. There are spells even within the sample list under each Arcanum that do just that. Here are some examples.<br /> <br /> ~Forces 3 spell &quot;Turn Momentum&quot; protects from bullets<br /> ~Space 3 spell &quot; Ban&quot; can disallow pretty much anything (with the use of an appropriate second Arcanum) to enter an area<br /> ~Time 3 spell &quot;Acceleration&quot; as mentioned by <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\">proindrakenzol</a></b>, can add potency to defense, even against firearms.<br /> ~Prime 2 spell &quot;Wards and Signs&quot; makes the target Withstand spells that target them.<br /> ~Matter 3 spell &quot;Aegis&quot; increases the armor of objects (even clothing)<br /> <br /> There are probably more, but you get my point.<br /> <br /> You can use many (if not all) of your Arcana creatively to offer a target or targets protection from many different things. Usually these spells are at a dot rating for 3 or higher, which makes sense for balance and logical reasons. At the second dot, you can easily protect yourself, but it takes something more to protect something other than your own Pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T07:11:35-07:00","id":1333948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333840#post1333840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> if your goal is to provide the ability to apply defense against firearms, that is doable with things other than Mage Armor; specifically the Time 3 spell Acceleration has that as one of its effects.<br /> <br /> Applying the Spirit or Death versions would likely be Weaving effects of both Life (if targeting a living thing) and Spirit or Death as appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn\u2019t the only goal, no, merely an example. The other part of the question was that if I couldn\u2019t duplicate this ability I apparently have at arcana 2, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T07:17:34-07:00","id":1333949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333934#post1333934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the reason Mages use the Mage Armor attainments to rather than spells to protect THEMSELVES is because they can't do it with spells. I think it's just because it's easier and safer. I believe its fully possible to use a spell for protection. Spells used this way could even be much more powerful than Mage Armor. There are spells even within the sample list under each Arcanum that do just that. Here are some examples.<br /> <br /> ~Forces 3 spell &amp;quot;Turn Momentum&amp;quot; protects from bullets<br /> ~Space 3 spell &amp;quot; Ban&amp;quot; can disallow pretty much anything (with the use of an appropriate second Arcanum) to enter an area<br /> ~Time 3 spell &amp;quot;Acceleration&amp;quot; as mentioned by <b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">proindrakenzol</a></b>, can add potency to defense, even against firearms.<br /> ~Prime 2 spell &amp;quot;Wards and Signs&amp;quot; makes the target Withstand spells that target them.<br /> ~Matter 3 spell &amp;quot;Aegis&amp;quot; increases the armor of objects (even clothing)<br /> <br /> There are probably more, but you get my point.<br /> <br /> You can use many (if not all) of your Arcana creatively to offer a target or targets protection from many different things. Usually these spells are at a dot rating for 3 or higher, which makes sense for balance and logical reasons. At the second dot, you can easily protect yourself, but it takes something more to protect something other than your own Pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they apparently cannot duplicate the effects of Mage Armor with creative thaumaturgy, is what I\u2019m asking. This isn\u2019t a question of \u201ccan I protect myself or other people with magic\u201d, I\u2019m not looking for advice on how to do that. I simply want to know, can I duplicate this ability I apparently have as an attainment at arcana 2, with a full spell, taking on all the disadvantages of using it as a spell. If I cannot do that, what is the in game, in universe reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T10:47:07-07:00","id":1333987,"title":"","content":"Mage Armor is not magic. It is an attainment and thus a meta-magic ability with its own set of rules. Think of them more in terms of &quot;strange legacy attainment effects&quot; than &quot;spells as attainments&quot;.<br /> In theory you can duplicate the effect approximately with C.Th. but it is in no way guaranteed to be as simple as &quot;Arcana 2&quot;.<br /> <br /> For a rough guideline how an attainment (arcana influenced mage sight, same arcana level as mage armor) might get applied to a subject as a spell, look at the Prime 4 Spell &quot;Apocalypse&quot;.<br /> <br /> You are asking the wrong question. Do not ask &quot;how can I apply mage armor as a spell?&quot;.<br /> Ask: &quot;How can I apply effect x as a magical practice?&quot;<br /> Derived from that you can just use the usual C.Th.-approach to meet these requirements.<br /> <br /> This is where you get hung up. The same applies to some other attainments.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at an in universe reason just look at the patterning practice. Attainments are in some way part of your pattern. You need to change the pattern in order to grant something akin to an attainment effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","user":"Caimbeul","date":". 09-04-2019, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T12:53:26-07:00","id":1334007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caimbeul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1333987#post1333987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage Armor is not magic. It is an attainment and thus a meta-magic ability with its own set of rules. Think of them more in terms of &amp;quot;strange legacy attainment effects&amp;quot; than &amp;quot;spells as attainments&amp;quot;.<br /> In theory you can duplicate the effect approximately with C.Th. but it is in no way guaranteed to be as simple as &amp;quot;Arcana 2&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> For a rough guideline how an attainment (arcana influenced mage sight, same arcana level as mage armor) might get applied to a subject as a spell, look at the Prime 4 Spell &amp;quot;Apocalypse&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> You are asking the wrong question. Do not ask &amp;quot;how can I apply mage armor as a spell?&amp;quot;.<br /> Ask: &amp;quot;How can I apply effect x as a magical practice?&amp;quot;<br /> Derived from that you can just use the usual C.Th.-approach to meet these requirements.<br /> <br /> This is where you get hung up. The same applies to some other attainments.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at an in universe reason just look at the patterning practice. Attainments are in some way part of your pattern. You need to change the pattern in order to grant something akin to an attainment effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was asking \u201chow can I apply this effect of mage armor as a spell\u201d, everyone else(including yourself) was interpreting that as casting mage armor as a spell. The logic of it is still screwy but my question got answered elsewhere with a suitable in universe answer so I\u2019ll drop it here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T13:34:59-07:00","id":1334014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334007#post1334007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was asking \u201chow can I apply this effect of mage armor as a spell\u201d, everyone else(including yourself) was interpreting that as casting mage armor as a spell. The logic of it is still screwy but my question got answered elsewhere with a suitable in universe answer so I\u2019ll drop it here</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I provided responses for both approaches. Would you mind sharing what in universe justification you got for it? Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T23:42:39-07:00","id":1334049,"title":"","content":"Just a general system question. If a weapons damage rating is lower than an objects durability do they just bounce off or can a vampire destroy a tank with a baseball bat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-05T03:05:01-07:00","id":1334059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334049#post1334049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a general system question. If a weapons damage rating is lower than an objects durability do they just bounce off or can a vampire destroy a tank with a baseball bat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just calculate damage as normal (successes + damage modifier - Durability). If the vampire score enough successes to deal damage to a tank, then they do so. By RAW improvised weapons (which I would consider anything not meant to strike a tank) also takes damage if the vampire were to use Vigor. A more realistic take is to deal that damage to the weapon regardless of whether Vigor was used or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T06:08:10-07:00","id":1334156,"title":"","content":"I have a hopefully simple question regarding Practices. Let's say I wanted to take a clump of dirt and turn it into liquid gold. Obviously this falls under the scope of two separate Practices. Patterning to turn the dirt to gold, Weaving to give it the properties of a liquid.<br /> <br /> My question is if you need two Practices to technically create the desired effect, would selecting the higher Practice of Patterning grant you the effects under Weaving simply by being a higher practice?<br /> <br /> I mean, technically Ruling is used to move something under the Arcanum's purview, yet higher Practice damage spells don't seem to really care that the description of the Practice they're using doesn't include descriptive text stating that it does anything other than what it's supposed to. Big offenders are Windstrike(Weaving) and Piercing Earth(Patterning), both of which are essentially the mage basically hurling Matter at the target in various forms but seem to have nothing to do with either Practice they fall under.<br /> <br /> It's almost as if it was intended that lower Practices be encompassed by higher ones. But then, if that's the case is it only the Practices that most align with each other that do this? Ruling, Weaving, and Patterning? Ruling, Fraying, and Unraveling? Or do all lower Practices fall under any one higher Practice? For instance, casting a Patterning spell with the properties described under Fraying included?<br /> <br /> Honestly, it feels like a lot of mechanics are simply implied and left open for interpretation. Especially Practices, which has all of a single paragraph plus a sentence or two per practice that outline how it all works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T07:11:16-07:00","id":1334164,"title":"","content":"The Matter damage spells are bad examples and you should not look to their descriptions when designing your own spells.<br /> <br /> For your example of turning solid dirt into liquid gold, you need to cast two spells. Or a combined spell. This is not because you're using two Practices (if you could cast it as a single spell both Practices would theoretically be included as if you cast a Matter 3+Matter 4 spell, simplified to be just Matter 4) but because you're facilitating two separate effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T08:01:23-07:00","id":1334169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334164#post1334164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Matter damage spells are bad examples and you should not look to their descriptions when designing your own spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they're in the book\u2014the official rule book that everyone reads to get an idea for the basis of how the system works. Is there some sort of pending retraction or errata not yet in the current copy of the book posted somewhere that supports the fact that they're poor examples? I mean, looking at errata logs I <i>can </i>find, both spells got looked at and the only thing they did was change the spells to Weaving and Patterning respectively. It feels unsatisfying to simply discard any spell and go, &quot;Ignore that, it doesn't fit the view of how I feel the system should work.&quot;<br /> <br /> It feels more productive to go, &quot;The rules apparently allow this, there's a precedent, so let's rationalize how and why,&quot; which can only serve to open and expand the possibilities.<br /> <br /> I'm consistently left wondering if the writers cut or left out a few essential clarifications in the Creative Thaumaturgy rules trying to make page/word count because it feels like most of the related answers in this thread may as well be preceded with, &quot;My best guess/interpretation is...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T09:34:57-07:00","id":1334188,"title":"","content":"If you have Constant Presence cast on you and someone Shifting Sands back and changes things, would you remember what happened in the new timeline as well the old one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T10:27:40-07:00","id":1334196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334188#post1334188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Constant Presence cast on you and someone Shifting Sands back and changes things, would you remember what happened in the new timeline as well the old one?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on who wins the CoW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T14:40:14-07:00","id":1334241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334196#post1334196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on who wins the CoW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm assuming it's successful. To clarify, if Constant Presence keeps your present state immune to changes in history, will that mean that the past you remember will be one no one else does? For instance if you are at a party and a fight breaks out and people get killed. Another Mage goes back in time and prevents the fight from ever happening. Do things all of the sudden rearrange around you and you have no idea what happened because the past you lived through was different? Or do you remember both versions of the event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":565,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","user":"Therian","date":". 09-06-2019, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T15:08:52-07:00","id":1334244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334241#post1334241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming it's successful. To clarify, if Constant Presence keeps your present state immune to changes in history, will that mean that the past you remember will be one no one else does? For instance if you are at a party and a fight breaks out and people get killed. Another Mage goes back in time and prevents the fight from ever happening. Do things all of the sudden rearrange around you and you have no idea what happened because the past you lived through was different? Or do you remember both versions of the event?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are treated as a time traveler having just arrived at the Present, so you would remember alterations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T20:55:57-07:00","id":1334294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334244#post1334244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are treated as a time traveler having just arrived at the Present, so you would remember alterations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a very solid and clear answer, well said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T10:14:17-07:00","id":1334875,"title":"","content":"Another, hopefully easier to answer question<br /> <br /> I was looking at some improvised spells I could do now that I\u2019m at Mind 3, and me and my group have run into a disagreement on what practice something counts as<br /> <br /> I was looking at clear mind as a reference example, and noticed it had the effect of restoring willpower, and I was discussing using it as a way to recharge the willpower batteries. Another player brought up I should be able to cast a spell to just restore willpower itself at Mind 3<br /> <br /> I looked into it though, looking at other examples, already knowing that inflicting bashing is usually a disciple effect while you have to wait till 4 to inflict lethal. Then there are spells like knit, which restore bashing and with a reach effect can restore lethal, then at life 4, mend life simply restores the lethal itself <br /> <br /> This suggests to me, when taking into account clear mind only restores 1 willpower with a reach effect, that it should actually be a patterning Mind 4 spell to simply restore willpower<br /> <br /> However the other player argues that restoring willpower shouldn\u2019t be as hard as healing lethal damage, so it should be able to be cast at Mind 3 as a perfecting effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T10:32:11-07:00","id":1334883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334875#post1334875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However the other player argues that restoring willpower shouldn\u2019t be as hard as healing lethal damage, so it should be able to be cast at Mind 3 as a perfecting effect</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that restoring Willpower normally requires effort to get more than once a day and has a lower lower limit than Health suggests it's probably better placed at Mind 4 to restore it in quantity than at the same level of Arcanum mastery as &quot;heal damage that normally heals four points an hour.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T10:50:17-07:00","id":1334891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334875#post1334875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another, hopefully easier to answer question<br /> <br /> I was looking at some improvised spells I could do now that I\u2019m at Mind 3, and me and my group have run into a disagreement on what practice something counts as<br /> <br /> I was looking at clear mind as a reference example, and noticed it had the effect of restoring willpower, and I was discussing using it as a way to recharge the willpower batteries. Another player brought up I should be able to cast a spell to just restore willpower itself at Mind 3<br /> <br /> I looked into it though, looking at other examples, already knowing that inflicting bashing is usually a disciple effect while you have to wait till 4 to inflict lethal. Then there are spells like knit, which restore bashing and with a reach effect can restore lethal, then at life 4, mend life simply restores the lethal itself <br /> <br /> This suggests to me, when taking into account clear mind only restores 1 willpower with a reach effect, that it should actually be a patterning Mind 4 spell to simply restore willpower<br /> <br /> However the other player argues that restoring willpower shouldn\u2019t be as hard as healing lethal damage, so it should be able to be cast at Mind 3 as a perfecting effect</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that you can create an healing effect that repeat itself every ritual interval if you set a sufficiently long duration.<br /> Clear mind could restore a lot of willpower in a few hours","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T11:17:57-07:00","id":1334897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334891#post1334891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that you can create an healing effect that repeat itself every ritual interval if you set a sufficiently long duration.<br /> Clear mind could restore a lot of willpower in a few hours</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have clarified that the question was actually \u201cIs the base effect of restoring willpower patterning or perfecting\u201d rather than adding in my observations of looking at effects, so that\u2019s on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T11:41:58-07:00","id":1334907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334897#post1334897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should have clarified that the question was actually \u201cIs the base effect of restoring willpower patterning or perfecting\u201d rather than adding in my observations of looking at effects, so that\u2019s on me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The base effect is Perfecting because it can be accomplished with a Perfecting spell. Patterning would allow you to restore multiple Willpower at once by altering the state of the Mind to a different state (i.e. without willpower to with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T15:36:13-07:00","id":1334989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334907#post1334907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The base effect is Perfecting because it can be accomplished with a Perfecting spell. Patterning would allow you to restore multiple Willpower at once by altering the state of the Mind to a different state (i.e. without willpower to with).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that.<br /> But i don t understand the in game reason for why healing willpower should be more difficult than healing health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T06:37:50-07:00","id":1335101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1334989#post1334989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with that.<br /> But i don t understand the in game reason for why healing willpower should be more difficult than healing health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly a balance call. Your ways of replenishing Willpower are usually limited and require dramatic actions or developments, or many days without spending more. Healing bashing damage is trivial and even a few lethal may not bother you at all before healing naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T01:21:21-07:00","id":1335430,"title":"","content":"How does Peripheral Mage Sight interact with demons' subtler powers, particularly Embeds and stuff like Legend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T03:32:03-07:00","id":1335452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1335430#post1335430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Peripheral Mage Sight interact with demons' subtler powers, particularly Embeds and stuff like Legend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Legend would probably be under Cover concealment, but embeds are active use of a power so i think they are detectable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T12:42:42-07:00","id":1336078,"title":"","content":"In 2e, does the number of Sleepers who witness an act of obvious magic actually increase the chance of Paradox, or is it just +1 no matter how many?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind, found the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 09-16-2019, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T12:47:24-07:00","id":1336081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336078#post1336078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, does the number of Sleepers who witness an act of obvious magic actually increase the chance of Paradox</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but not just by adding dice.<br /> <br /> P115, 'Multiple Sleeper witnesses do not add Paradox dice, but increase the chances of a Paradox occurring. If a few Sleepers witness the magic casting, the Paradox roll gains the 9-Again quality, a large group grants the Paradox roll the 8-Again quality, and a full crowd grants the Paradox roll the rote quality.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T04:13:21-07:00","id":1336817,"title":"","content":"Does a dedicated magical tool gives his paradox reduction effect if used in a spell without a semiotic meaning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T04:17:20-07:00","id":1336818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336817#post1336817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a dedicated magical tool gives his paradox reduction effect if used in a spell without a semiotic meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The paradox-reduction effect is not due to it being employed as a yantra but by virtue of being a dedicated tool. The text itself provides the example of a mage who uses their dedicated tool even without being able to profit off of the symbolism for a yantra.<br /> <br /> In other terms: It BEING the dedicated tool, the tool with which they cast magic predominantly IS a semiotic meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T05:25:46-07:00","id":1336837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caimbeul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336818#post1336818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The paradox-reduction effect is not due to it being employed as a yantra but by virtue of being a dedicated tool. The text itself provides the example of a mage who uses their dedicated tool even without being able to profit off of the symbolism for a yantra.<br /> <br /> In other terms: It BEING the dedicated tool, the tool with which they cast magic predominantly IS a semiotic meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same interpretation but the book example is not so clear to me.<br /> So the semiotic is an issue only when you try to understand if it ALSO applies the bonus as a Path/Order tool, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T06:52:34-07:00","id":1336858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336837#post1336837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the same interpretation but the book example is not so clear to me.<br /> So the semiotic is an issue only when you try to understand if it ALSO applies the bonus as a Path/Order tool, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can always use anything as a Yantra, but only gain the dice bonus if it's symbolic of the spell. Anytime you use a Dedicated Tool (even if it doesn't grant a dice bonus) you gain the Paradox reduction bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T07:20:53-07:00","id":1336861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336858#post1336858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. You can always use anything as a Yantra, but only gain the dice bonus if it's symbolic of the spell. Anytime you use a Dedicated Tool (even if it doesn't grant a dice bonus) you gain the Paradox reduction bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did not know that. This is interesting.<br /> <br /> I have a question about the Shadow Name persona yantra. Does using this yantra require actually saying your shadow name out loud or weaving it into an invocation as you're casting the spell? Or is it just the mindset that matters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T08:22:41-07:00","id":1336874,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the clarification","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T08:25:51-07:00","id":1336875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336861#post1336861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I did not know that. This is interesting.<br /> <br /> I have a question about the Shadow Name persona yantra. Does using this yantra require actually saying your shadow name out loud or weaving it into an invocation as you're casting the spell? Or is it just the mindset that matters?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game i consider it like a superhero secret identity.<br /> It s a matter of style, someone say aloud the names of his spells, others use spells that are into the character, others dress in an appropriate manner or interact with accessories while casting.<br /> I think it depends on personal taste","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T08:47:39-07:00","id":1336880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336861#post1336861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know that. This is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how you Dedicate a tool in the first place; using it as a Yantra for a month regardless of whether you gain a bonus or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336861#post1336861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the Shadow Name persona yantra. Does using this yantra require actually saying your shadow name out loud or weaving it into an invocation as you're casting the spell? Or is it just the mindset that matters?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Persona is a weird Yantra because it's something you would start doing the moment you go out to do mage stuff. When you're casting a spell you've either already adopted your Shadow Name and can use your own current behaviour as a Yantra (if it's applicable for the spell), or you're not in your mage Persona and can't use it regardless of whether it's relevant to the spell or not. You don't do anything extra to use it as a Yantra (unless you wish to style it up) because you've already been acting out the Yantra for some time before it's even time to cast the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T08:55:42-07:00","id":1336883,"title":"","content":"In my current game I told players I expect them to embody their Shadow Name to a level we all agree appropriate to their dot rating. One of my players has 3 dot Shadow Name Santa Claus, and while I don't expect him to be in costume 24/7, we agreed he should carry a hat and beard at all times to put on in case of magical emergencies, and he should be in full costume if he knows he will be among Mages. And I do the same with the NPCs. So, they don't have to say their name, although that might be a part of it for some characters, but they have to embody their Shadow Name, especially during rituals.<br /> <br /> But that's just what we agreed for this game because it sounded fun. You can be more or less demanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T10:17:31-07:00","id":1336894,"title":"","content":"My rule for Shadow Name is that the concept behind the name has to apply to the spell in question.<br /> <br /> In <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12673\" data-vbnamecard=\"12673\">EW-Matias</a>' example of &quot;Santa Clause&quot; the Shadow Name would only provide a bonus if they were doing something Santa Clause-esque, which afaik would be rather strictly limited to giving out presents.<br /> <br /> Had a Mastigos player whose Shadow Name was Jace (from Magic: the Gathering); it had rather broad applications <i>vis a vis</i> the Mind Arcanum, but he got relatively little when using Space except for scrying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T10:34:06-07:00","id":1336898,"title":"","content":"Well, that's not an interpretation, that's just how it works. We are discussing how &quot;using&quot; the yantra looks like in the fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T10:43:06-07:00","id":1336905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336898#post1336898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's not an interpretation, that's just how it works. We are discussing how &quot;using&quot; the yantra looks like in the fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake.<br /> <br /> I think the accoutrements required depend on the Shadow Name in question: for a name with an established image like &quot;Santa Clause&quot; I agree accoutrements are necessary, something more generic like &quot;Builder&quot; probably wouldn't need much beyond the spell fitting into the concept of building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T11:06:08-07:00","id":1336912,"title":"","content":"Could the Shadow name be related to the way you cast spells and not on the kind of spells you use? For instance, I was thinking of a character whose Shadow Name persona chants incantations out loud as part of creating the imago. Could that be the touch we need to allow the shadow name to work on any spell?<br /> <br /> Also, concerning the dedicated tool, I have a question. When casting spells as an instant action, the book says that you can incorporate 1 yantra reflexively and that each extra yantra takes 1 turn. If I reflexively incorporate a yantra other than the dedicated tool and cast the spell as an instant action without taking the extra turn to incorporate it in the casting (regardless of whether I would get the dice bonuses from the tool or not), do I still get the -2 to paradox rolls bonus, even though I didn't incorporate the tool in the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 09-19-2019, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T15:23:55-07:00","id":1336951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336912#post1336912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the Shadow name be related to the way you cast spells and not on the kind of spells you use? For instance, I was thinking of a character whose Shadow Name persona chants incantations out loud as part of creating the imago. Could that be the touch we need to allow the shadow name to work on any spell?<br /> <br /> Also, concerning the dedicated tool, I have a question. When casting spells as an instant action, the book says that you can incorporate 1 yantra reflexively and that each extra yantra takes 1 turn. If I reflexively incorporate a yantra other than the dedicated tool and cast the spell as an instant action without taking the extra turn to incorporate it in the casting (regardless of whether I would get the dice bonuses from the tool or not), do I still get the -2 to paradox rolls bonus, even though I didn't incorporate the tool in the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Dedicated Tool isn\u2019t used as a Yantra for either of its benefits then you don\u2019t get any of its benefits. <br /> <br /> Yantras other than the Dedicated Tool do not grant the -2 to the Paradox pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T15:26:27-07:00","id":1336952,"title":"","content":"I wanted to ask this on the Werewolf forum but, I wasn't sure if that was the right place since this is also a Mage question, and I just asked some questions over there. Forgive me if this is idiotic.<br /> <br /> So, in 1E you could get a Supernal Familiar. Signs of Sorcery makes me think they wanted to step away from that since we have Watcher now, but, I loved the Supernal Familiar idea, even if a weak Supernal denizen is pretty limited in arcana (strong otherwise though!).<br /> <br /> So my question is, if you have a Supernal Spirit-Beast Totem, and some werewolves find it, what will they make of it? If it can remain in the Fallen World, is it enough of a spirit they might consider it for a Totem if they don't already have it? Would they see it as some scary alien to be destroyed? I'm sure it comes down to the pack in question, but I also know werewolves have strong instincts and prejudices, and that angle I'm less familiar with. I really wanna know how they'd react, like, ideas on what it would smell like to them, what their own Gifts might make of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T15:38:16-07:00","id":1336954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336912#post1336912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the Shadow name be related to the way you cast spells and not on the kind of spells you use? For instance, I was thinking of a character whose Shadow Name persona chants incantations out loud as part of creating the imago. Could that be the touch we need to allow the shadow name to work on any spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see the symbolism there. That's just the High Speech Yantra. Or it could be related to a Techn\u00e9 focus. But and example of something similar I've discussed with one of my players is that since his Shadow Name is Fudo, and Fuos is sometimes depicted with a lasso, maybe he could use one as a symbol of restraining or binding in a ritual as a way of using his Shadow Name for such a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":". 09-19-2019, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T16:39:14-07:00","id":1336960,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, both <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\">Mrmdubois</a> </b>and <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\">EW-Matias</a></b><br /> <br /> My character doesn't have a shadow name at the moment, but I was considering getting one. I'll work on it and maybe come up with a more solid idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 09-19-2019, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T21:41:26-07:00","id":1337012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336952#post1336952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to ask this on the Werewolf forum but, I wasn't sure if that was the right place since this is also a Mage question, and I just asked some questions over there. Forgive me if this is idiotic.<br /> <br /> So, in 1E you could get a Supernal Familiar. Signs of Sorcery makes me think they wanted to step away from that since we have Watcher now, but, I loved the Supernal Familiar idea, even if a weak Supernal denizen is pretty limited in arcana (strong otherwise though!).<br /> <br /> So my question is, if you have a Supernal Spirit-Beast Totem, and some werewolves find it, what will they make of it? If it can remain in the Fallen World, is it enough of a spirit they might consider it for a Totem if they don't already have it? Would they see it as some scary alien to be destroyed? I'm sure it comes down to the pack in question, but I also know werewolves have strong instincts and prejudices, and that angle I'm less familiar with. I really wanna know how they'd react, like, ideas on what it would smell like to them, what their own Gifts might make of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Supernal Familiar is out.<br /> <br /> As for a Totem, they\u2019re not really very spirit like. They are Truths of ephemeral reality, not the ephemeral brings they define.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T02:46:40-07:00","id":1337050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336912#post1336912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the Shadow name be related to the way you cast spells and not on the kind of spells you use? For instance, I was thinking of a character whose Shadow Name persona chants incantations out loud as part of creating the imago. Could that be the touch we need to allow the shadow name to work on any spell</div> </div> </div> </div>It works for both. The important part is, that you can incorporate the symbolic meaning of the shadow name into the spell. Either in intention OR effect. It must be 'in character'. It's all about the symbol and thus the semiotic meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1336912#post1336912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, concerning the dedicated tool, I have a question. When casting spells as an instant action, the book says that you can incorporate 1 yantra reflexively and that each extra yantra takes 1 turn. If I reflexively incorporate a yantra other than the dedicated tool and cast the spell as an instant action without taking the extra turn to incorporate it in the casting (regardless of whether I would get the dice bonuses from the tool or not), do I still get the -2 to paradox rolls bonus, even though I didn't incorporate the tool in the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you dont use the dedicated tool, you dont get either bonus. There is a reason you can use a dedicated tool as both a path AND an order tool: If you use it AND if you can link the semiotic meaning you get both, the path/order tool yantra bonus AND the paradox dice reduction. Applying the dedicated tool as a yantra counts only as one (unless you want to apply it for both cases, path AND order AND only if you are able to derive a semiotic meaning that would be sufficiently different) use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25562-caimbeul","name":"Caimbeul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25562_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T03:30:58-07:00","id":1337053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1337012#post1337012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Supernal Familiar is out.<br /> <br /> As for a Totem, they\u2019re not really very spirit like. They are Truths of ephemeral reality, not the ephemeral brings they define.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Worlds of Flesh and Spirit hold more alien creatures than any run-of-the-mill vampires, mages, or Beasts. Can a pack include a ghost? <b>A Strix totem?</b> The answer ultimately depends on the story you want to tell, but as with the more common supernatural creatures, agency is key.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, if you want it in your game, it's quite possible to have non-ephemeral Totems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T06:30:01-07:00","id":1337077,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t say it wasn\u2019t possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T22:56:31-07:00","id":1337214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1337053#post1337053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;The Worlds of Flesh and Spirit hold more alien creatures than any run-of-the-mill vampires, mages, or Beasts. Can a pack include a ghost? <b>A Strix totem?</b> The answer ultimately depends on the story you want to tell, but as with the more common supernatural creatures, agency is key.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, if you want it in your game, it's quite possible to have non-ephemeral Totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks! The Pack, right? Yes thats what I had in mind but, how to get there? Like, could woofs be impressed by the Truth of it, or, would they only care cuz of its power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T00:52:19-07:00","id":1337223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1337214#post1337214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh thanks! The Pack, right? Yes thats what I had in mind but, how to get there? Like, could woofs be impressed by the Truth of it, or, would they only care cuz of its power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the 'wolf. Some would be interested only in its raw power, others in its nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T12:13:19-07:00","id":1337346,"title":"","content":"About the spell &quot;as above so below&quot;, on which kind of yantra do you think it works?<br /> Only environmental and tools?<br /> Could work on some or all actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T13:49:04-07:00","id":1337364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1337346#post1337346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the spell &quot;as above so below&quot;, on which kind of yantra do you think it works?<br /> Only environmental and tools?<br /> Could work on some or all actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>As all spells it's cast on a subject. It can work for environmental Yantras (if big enough to cover the relevant area) as well as any physical Tool Yantras. For actions, I'd say the spell needs to be cast on whoever performs the action, and that you decide which action style Yantra you intend to affect when casting the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T07:58:15-07:00","id":1337498,"title":"","content":"The spell Haunted Grimoire from Signs of sorcery puzzles me.<br /> The complexity of the spell seems to imply that the caster perform it to receive a boost on the primary factor of the inscribed spell.<br /> The rules work well for low level spells, but for level 3+ spells it require a spirit so powerful that it almost alway win the first clash of will and gets free.<br /> Is it supposed to work that way?<br /> Or it is an errata and the spirit should use rank+power for the clash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T02:20:10-07:00","id":1337781,"title":"","content":"When using Sympathetic Range, is the 'active' link that between the sympathetic yantra and the target, or between the mage and the target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T03:28:24-07:00","id":1337790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1337781#post1337781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Sympathetic Range, is the 'active' link that between the sympathetic yantra and the target, or between the mage and the target?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage and the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T10:26:29-07:00","id":1337824,"title":"","content":"The Mage and the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T06:46:23-07:00","id":1338984,"title":"","content":"I don t know if it has been asked before, how could you assess the integrity/wisdom score of someone?<br /> Soul mark could be useful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T15:28:15-07:00","id":1339452,"title":"","content":"Ok, so. Wisdom degeneration.<br /> In the 4-7 (Medium/Understanding) category it says that allowing a sleeper to witness obvious magic, thus risking greater paradox, can cause wisdom degeneration. If a mage allows a sleeper to witness obvious magic, but at the same time spends extra mana to nullify the extra dice from the sleeper witness and reduces the spell's paradox to a chance die, does he still need to roll for wisdom degeneration?<br /> <br /> Also, would you give bonus dice to a wisdom degeneration roll if the mage's life was in danger when casting the spell that triggered it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T16:01:43-07:00","id":1339458,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's still the standard degeneration check. Quiescence spiritually harms the observer, regardless of extra effort put in to mitigate the external effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T19:28:55-07:00","id":1339505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1338984#post1338984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don t know if it has been asked before, how could you assess the integrity/wisdom score of someone?<br /> Soul mark could be useful?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no, Integrity isn't really a measure of how healthy your soul is. Neither is Wisdom. I'd err toward not allowing a spell to check either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1339452#post1339452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so. Wisdom degeneration.<br /> In the 4-7 (Medium/Understanding) category it says that allowing a sleeper to witness obvious magic, thus risking greater paradox, can cause wisdom degeneration. If a mage allows a sleeper to witness obvious magic, but at the same time spends extra mana to nullify the extra dice from the sleeper witness and reduces the spell's paradox to a chance die, does he still need to roll for wisdom degeneration?<br /> <br /> Also, would you give bonus dice to a wisdom degeneration roll if the mage's life was in danger when casting the spell that triggered it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Inodiv said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T07:04:55-07:00","id":1339584,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the spiritual harm to the observer is more important than the paradox effects. I get that. Thus, we roll for Wisdom. Would you give any bonus dice to the roll, because of the paradox mitigation and/or the personal risk to the mage which made the spell necessary? Like for instance when the spell/action that caused the Wisdom degeneration roll was done in defense of one's Virtue, the books says you get +1 die. Would something similar be applicable for other situations as well?<br /> <br /> Edit: Another question that came to mind. Does the tass produced at a hallow have an expiration date? Or can it be harvested and kept for an indefinite amount of time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 10-05-2019, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T07:21:08-07:00","id":1339587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1339584#post1339584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so the spiritual harm to the observer is more important than the paradox effects. I get that. Thus, we roll for Wisdom. Would you give any bonus dice to the roll, because of the paradox mitigation and/or the personal risk to the mage which made the spell necessary? Like for instance when the spell/action that caused the Wisdom degeneration roll was done in defense of one's Virtue, the books says you get +1 die. Would something similar be applicable for other situations as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not give any kind of bonus to the degeneration roll; just because you take care to protect your fist before punching someone doesn't mean you didn't punch someone, likewise here: you didn't do anything for the <i>victim</i>, just yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Another question that came to mind. Does the tass produced at a hallow have an expiration date? Or can it be harvested and kept for an indefinite amount of time? </div> </div> </div>I believe if the tass is collected in a perishable substance it goes bad when the substance goes bad, but otherwise remains indefinitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T09:07:28-07:00","id":1339608,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't personally give any bonus dice. Being put in a hard situation doesn't generally result in bonus dice for Wisdom rolls by my take.<br /> <br /> If anything, it can penalize them (see impassioned murder vs premeditated). The Mage shouldn't have let themselves get into that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:03:12-07:00","id":1339694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1338984#post1338984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don t know if it has been asked before, how could you assess the integrity/wisdom score of someone?<br /> Soul mark could be useful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really but you can guess by spying on someones longterm nimbus. The more their nimbus leaks, the lower their wisdom. When I run Guardians this is how they catch low-wisdom Mages, and I have hunters call these &quot;witch-signs&quot; and similarly, find low-wisdom mages my discovering their their nimbus is leaking.<br /> <br /> However you did inspire me to think up a spell that does it. It might be a bit of a stretch but, I think 2 or 3 of Mind Prime and or Time mixed at the Knowing practice will tell you how in-control of their magic the subject is, and give Wisdom based on how much their letting their power leak through from their careless regard for their actions. The important component is Time, because if wisdom cannot be read directly, then a spell that only tells you how severe the after-effects of low wisdom have been for your target, should also tell you the wisdom itself. Id be willing to believe it wont give an accurate result though, like giving &quot;understanding wisdom&quot; as the answer instead of an exact number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T19:54:50-07:00","id":1339747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1339505#post1339505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say no, Integrity isn't really a measure of how healthy your soul is. Neither is Wisdom. I'd err toward not allowing a spell to check either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 299 literally describes Integrity as the health of the Soul. I think having particularly Low or High Integrity or Wisdom should count as a Soul Mark. I'd tell a player wether the character falls into Elightened, Understanding or Falling Wisdom, or if they get either a big or small bonus/penalty to breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T01:49:00-07:00","id":1339786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1339747#post1339747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 299 literally describes Integrity as the health of the Soul. I think having particularly Low or High Integrity or Wisdom should count as a Soul Mark. I'd tell a player wether the character falls into Elightened, Understanding or Falling Wisdom, or if they get either a big or small bonus/penalty to breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both integrity and wisdom are described as some kind of soul health, so i was confused about Soul marks not revealing any info","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T01:04:33-07:00","id":1341411,"title":"","content":"How much mana would you grant for a blood sacrifice of a horror?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T10:59:19-07:00","id":1341475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1341411#post1341411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much mana would you grant for a blood sacrifice of a horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>How I would run it:<br /> <br /> Depends on the horror, anywhere from 1 (or none) in the case of an individual member of a fairly weak swarm, to as much as you can harvest before it dissipates in the case of some sort of giant elder god thing.<br /> <br /> A single fly from a swarm of hundreds of evil flies whose buzzing causes insanity: no mana<br /> <br /> Cthulhu: as much as you can find a way to store.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-15-2019, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T16:54:01-07:00","id":1341520,"title":"","content":"I think Sundered World did it that you get something like the creatures stamina or size, once size is at least 5, (only 1 mana if size is less than 5).<br /> <br /> So I'd go with size+horror rating. Horror Potency 4 and size 7 could be 11 mana perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T14:39:50-07:00","id":1341709,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Advice. <br /> <br /> Also Another question I am not exactly 100% clear on when you try to summon a supernal being can you specify a entity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T15:00:22-07:00","id":1341714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1341709#post1341709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the Advice.<br /> <br /> Also Another question I am not exactly 100% clear on when you try to summon a supernal being can you specify a entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have three dots in the Arcana you want the Supernal entity to have as its secondary Arcana then you can specify <i>that</i>, but there are no rules for summoning, say, Samael the Seraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T15:23:34-07:00","id":1341719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1341714#post1341714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you have three dots in the Arcana you want the Supernal entity to have as its secondary Arcana then you can specify <i>that</i>, but there are no rules for summoning, say, Samael the Seraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but in signs of sorcery i found this:<br /> &quot;If a mage attempts to summon a Supernal entity that dwells within the Aedes...l<br /> &quot;When you attempt to summon your Supernal watcher, the summoning only...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T15:41:10-07:00","id":1341723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1341719#post1341719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but in signs of sorcery i found this:<br /> &quot;If a mage attempts to summon a Supernal entity that dwells within the Aedes...l<br /> &quot;When you attempt to summon your Supernal watcher, the summoning only...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1151_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1151\" data-vbnamecard=\"1151\">WalkingEye</a> <br /> <br /> I looked those up.<br /> <br /> <br /> The rules for the Supernal Watcher merit imply that you can summon your specific watcher (and that it is easier than summoning other supernal entities). However, watchers are limited to rank 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> Summoning whatever entity happens to live in the Aedes does not, to me, count as summoning a specific entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T20:34:17-07:00","id":1341769,"title":"","content":"While there\u2019s no specific rule for it, I\u2019d totally allow the summoning of a specific Supernal Entity. Give it a whole specific ritual you have to perform and so on. Cram Order libraries with records of how to summon who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T01:43:28-07:00","id":1341815,"title":"","content":"The books reference that you can research a particular supernals trial before attempting to summon them, so you likely can summon specific supernals if you have both the appropriate Targeted Arcana and are of the appropriate Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:02:31-07:00","id":1342157,"title":"","content":"Summoning specific entities is like trapping a specific wild animal, but you can't see what you caught til the trap is sprung. 1e described it as sort of *luring* Supernals to you, the Summoning creates a way to interact with our world and eventually a denizen decides, for whatever reason, to use your summons, for curiosity or some other reason.<br /> <br /> So you can never force a specific entity to come against its will, but if the ST has a denizen in mind in which it would be *glad* to show up for anyone who uses its sigils in the ritual? Then it becomes VERY possible. It would be like the Bat Signal, the denizen can choose not to come, and then you might get &quot;Robin&quot; by mistake, but its almost certain you'll get &quot;Batman&quot;, it knows you are calling and it believes it should come when called.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T22:43:34-07:00","id":1342653,"title":"","content":"Empty Presence death 5 does it resolve all conditions to the point were persistent conditions like disabled or blind in a lasting way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T01:40:29-07:00","id":1342664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1342653#post1342653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empty Presence death 5 does it resolve all conditions to the point were persistent conditions like disabled or blind in a lasting way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it, but that would be an ST call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T11:27:10-07:00","id":1342978,"title":"","content":"If your Legacy's secondary Arcanum is Time and you have a mana spending fourth primary Attainment, is it viable to say &quot;mana is spent to and, if you have Time 4, to activate Time in a Bottle, truncated to one mana due to Legacy rules&quot; ? I imagine not, but am not sure. Would it be valid for a side effect of the fourth optional Time Attainment to incorporate Time in a Bottle into the primary one ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:03:09-07:00","id":1342990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1342978#post1342978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your Legacy's secondary Arcanum is Time and you have a mana spending fourth primary Attainment, is it viable to say &quot;mana is spent to and, if you have Time 4, to activate Time in a Bottle, truncated to one mana due to Legacy rules&quot; ? I imagine not, but am not sure. Would it be valid for a side effect of the fourth optional Time Attainment to incorporate Time in a Bottle into the primary one ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd absolutely allow the second one - &quot;If you have time 4, this attainment only requires (snipping a lock of your hair / lighting a candle / praying to the goddess / some thematic Instant action) instead of a scene to activate, and...&quot;<br /> <br /> I tend to be more flexible than the book suggests on adding reach to attainments in general though, so your mileage may vary. My rule of thumb is &quot;if you add a significant restriction beyond those in the base spell, you can get +1 reach in the attainment.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:14:34-07:00","id":1342993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1342978#post1342978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your Legacy's secondary Arcanum is Time and you have a mana spending fourth primary Attainment, is it viable to say &quot;mana is spent to and, if you have Time 4, to activate Time in a Bottle, truncated to one mana due to Legacy rules&quot; ? I imagine not, but am not sure. Would it be valid for a side effect of the fourth optional Time Attainment to incorporate Time in a Bottle into the primary one ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make it part of the Fourth Optional.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 4<br /> The primary attainment can now be cast with Instant Casting as if using Time in a Bottle. In addition &lt;other attainment stuff&gt;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:16:25-07:00","id":1342994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1342990#post1342990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I'd absolutely allow the second one - &amp;quot;If you have time 4, this attainment only requires (snipping a lock of your hair / lighting a candle / praying to the goddess / some thematic Instant action) instead of a scene to activate, and...&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I tend to be more flexible than the book suggests on adding reach to attainments in general though, so your mileage may vary. My rule of thumb is &amp;quot;if you add a significant restriction beyond those in the base spell, you can get +1 reach in the attainment.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that is something I like to do as well. If I add any free Reach, I incorporate a proportional amount of thematic complications or restrictions to balance it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:20:30-07:00","id":1342996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1342993#post1342993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would make it part of the Fourth Optional.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 4<br /> The primary attainment can now be cast with Instant Casting as if using Time in a Bottle. In addition &lt;other attainment stuff&gt;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. It didn't sound too insane for an optional bonus and that is certainly the cleanest way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T06:42:43-07:00","id":1343572,"title":"","content":"If a spirit uses the Speed numen on a target and a mage casts Acceleration, do the effects stack or only the greatest one takes effect ? What about one using a Strengthen Influence to enhance a car that a mage used a Perfecting on ? In other words, do the abilities of ephemeral entities count as magic for the purposes of stacking rules ?<br /> <br /> Can the Strengthen Influence heal aggravated wounds within its domain ? If so, the big selling point of the Regenerate numen is not efficiency, bur rather that it can be used on any living being without hassle, correct ?<br /> <br /> If you have a ghost of a reporter with Influence: Journalism, then the methods to write an article on a PC without going down the possession route are by either Materializing or using the Manipulate Manifestation ? Or does detailed work (typing, programming, assembling a clock) require the Control one ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-25-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T07:21:33-07:00","id":1343578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1343572#post1343572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, do the abilities of ephemeral entities count as magic for the purposes of stacking rules ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's specifically <i>spells</i> that don't stack. Spells and Legacy Attainments also have their specific stacking rules. Everything else is simply not explained and thus probably stackable (barring the regular <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u00b15 limit or the ST ruling otherwise).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1343572#post1343572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Strengthen Influence heal aggravated wounds within its domain ? If so, the big selling point of the Regenerate numen is not efficiency, bur rather that it can be used on any living being without hassle, correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strengthen probably can't heal anything except if it's Influence: Healing or something similar (in which case it should probably only increase the rate of healing, not actually heal on its own). I say probably because we've only got the roughest of guidelines on Influence uses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1343572#post1343572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a ghost of a reporter with Influence: Journalism, then the methods to write an article on a PC without going down the possession route are by either Materializing or using the Manipulate Manifestation ? Or does detailed work (typing, programming, assembling a clock) require the Control one ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically ST fiat since the Influence rules are so underexplained. I can see it go either way (or even require Create for a literal and thus reductive reading of the rules).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T07:57:43-07:00","id":1343584,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Influences confuse me more often than not.<br /> <br /> For example, does Healing allow you to increase the target's healing rate at Strengthen and instantly heal at Create ? Or does Strengthen heal instantly and Create allow you to create a remedy (even one that previously didn't exist) or medical equipment ? The rules are so vague that I understood &quot;yes, both are doable. Depends on the thematic flavor of the being&quot;.<br /> <br /> So its deliberately open ended to give the ST a flexible toolkit, cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T08:03:23-07:00","id":1343586,"title":"","content":"I don't think Strengthen should heal instantly. It only affects the &quot;healing&quot; that is already present, i.e. the body's natural healing. Strengthening it should make it more effective and/or efficient, reducing healing times according to the entity's Rank. Something like &quot;divide all healing times by [Rank+1]&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"