iv class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/265598\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/265598 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Your one-stop online shop for new and vintage RPG products from the top publishers, delivered fresh to your desktop in electronic format. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:26:51-07:00","id":1344960,"title":"","content":"If a Fang of Mara uses Imposing Nimbus merit to inflict the Broken condition, that constitutes an Act of Hubris, correct ?<br /> <br /> What about a Steward of the Celestial Orrery causing an Obsession with the current mission in service to the Oracles ?<br /> <br /> Could a Tamer of the Cave use it to inflict Aporia, a custom Condition version of The Inescapable Question (such as when Obi-Wan when he said &quot;you don't want to sell deathsticks, you want to go home and rethink your life&quot;) ? If so, would that constitute an Act of Hubris ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:05:51-08:00","id":1345835,"title":"","content":"So a short linguistic question- when I want to talk about the Oneiros of a number of different individual, do I still use Oneiros, or there is some plural form I need to use? For some reason I remember a word in the style of &quot;Oneiri&quot;, but I'm not sure if I imagined it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:24:12-08:00","id":1345844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1345835#post1345835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a short linguistic question- when I want to talk about the Oneiros of a number of different individual, do I still use Oneiros, or there is some plural form I need to use? For some reason I remember a word in the style of &quot;Oneiri&quot;, but I'm not sure if I imagined it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, &quot;Oneiroi&quot; is (as I understand it) the proper Greek plural of the word. On the other hand, it's been stated that the plural form of e.g. the names of each Paths is the same as their singular names. Suffice it to be said that I don't think anybody's going to give you any trouble for using either one as long as you're consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:43:45-08:00","id":1345872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1345835#post1345835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a short linguistic question- when I want to talk about the Oneiros of a number of different individual, do I still use Oneiros, or there is some plural form I need to use? For some reason I remember a word in the style of &quot;Oneiri&quot;, but I'm not sure if I imagined it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oneiros\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia (source of all true knowledge) says &quot;Oneiroi,&quot;</a> but I doubt anyone would call you out for using &quot;oneiroses.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:11:57-08:00","id":1345882,"title":"","content":"Can you use the Fast Spells Merit on Attainments? Attainments are usually basically internalized Praxes, so I believe it could be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:13:04-08:00","id":1345884,"title":"","content":"On top of being the proper Greek plural, Oneiroi is used as plural in the book. (Oneiroses is by far the option that sounds the worst to me despite being the standard English pluralisation.)<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1345882#post1345882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the Fast Spells Merit on Attainments? Attainments are usually basically internalized Praxes, so I believe it could be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow it for any Aimed Legacy Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-04-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:03:10-08:00","id":1346127,"title":"","content":"It's Oneiroi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T14:41:41-08:00","id":1347104,"title":"","content":"Is is possible for a mage to have more than the 3 rote skills granted by his/her order? Like through a merit, or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T16:06:37-08:00","id":1347120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1347104#post1347104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is is possible for a mage to have more than the 3 rote skills granted by his/her order? Like through a merit, or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T23:23:44-08:00","id":1347175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1347104#post1347104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is is possible for a mage to have more than the 3 rote skills granted by his/her order? Like through a merit, or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ve read a past thread with a comment from dave, he said that it s possibile to have only a set of three","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T07:04:58-08:00","id":1347233,"title":"","content":"<i>Psychic Genesis</i> lets you, with a Reach, create a goetia that counts as a Sleepwalker for ritual casting purposes. If you just wanted to add that property to an existing one, how could it be done ? With a Reach option on the Ritual Focus Spell ? With a Weaving ? Pattering perhaps ? I think either of the furst two, but I am not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T23:27:56-08:00","id":1347413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1347233#post1347233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Psychic Genesis</i> lets you, with a Reach, create a goetia that counts as a Sleepwalker for ritual casting purposes. If you just wanted to add that property to an existing one, how could it be done ? With a Reach option on the Ritual Focus Spell ? With a Weaving ? Pattering perhaps ? I think either of the furst two, but I am not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T14:04:38-08:00","id":1347552,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you. One more question, Sleepwalkers count as a +1 environment yantra, independent of number, correct ? Or is it dependent on the number of Sleepwalkers ?<br /> <br /> In essence, I am wondering if a Thrice Great lodge could try to get enough allies to cast a Spirit conjunctional variation of ir to empower a big spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T14:47:11-08:00","id":1347557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1347552#post1347552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thank you. One more question, Sleepwalkers count as a +1 environment yantra, independent of number, correct ? Or is it dependent on the number of Sleepwalkers ?<br /> <br /> In essence, I am wondering if a Thrice Great lodge could try to get enough allies to cast a Spirit conjunctional variation of ir to empower a big spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Sleepwalkers together counts as the environment, and the environment Yantra grants a +1 bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T18:58:06-08:00","id":1347594,"title":"","content":"Ok, makes sense, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:00:34-08:00","id":1347674,"title":"","content":"Does the life spell Animal minion give you access to the subject senses?<br /> Because if you are unaware of your surroundings it can be hard to direct the puppet without other arcana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T08:34:20-08:00","id":1347691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1347674#post1347674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the life spell Animal minion give you access to the subject senses?<br /> Because if you are unaware of your surroundings it can be hard to direct the puppet without other arcana</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s basically Life based Possession, so yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:08:09-08:00","id":1347991,"title":"","content":"Hello, I have a some questions regarding Cold and the Arcanum of Death:<br /> - With Death 3, Cold Snap, you can freeze an area enough to impose the ice tilt and with 1 reach you inflict the Extreme cold condition. Does this translate in any way to an extreme environment rating? <br /> - If it does, with a potency of 4 should the spell create a level 4 hazard? Or a Patterning would be better suited?<br /> - Could Cold Snap work as a dorect attack? Having your body instantly turn from warm to frozen is surely excruciating. And paralyzing too.<br /> <br /> In general, I'm unsure on how cold works with the arcanum of Death, from a mechanical point of view.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moreover, but about acceleration (Time 3):<br /> - If a mage accelerates himself with a potency of 6, for example, if an hour elapses for those around him not under the spell shouldn't he feel the effect of 6 hours of being awake, standing still etc. etc.? Or the spell shields the caster from this possible effect?<br /> - The spell seems to me similar to Vampiric Celerity. If this is true, the caster shouldn't be seeing everything at normal speed and &quot;just&quot; react way way faster to things he is aware of?<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, about Fools Rush In (Fate 2):<br /> - &quot;Little or no knowledge about a situation&quot; is a bit unclear to me. One of my players translated it more or less in &quot;every time something unexpected happens I can use the bonus&quot;, but I'm not much convinced. Can somenone give me an example or two to understand the boundaries of this spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:42:19-08:00","id":1348000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1347991#post1347991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I have a some questions regarding Cold and the Arcanum of Death:<br /> - With Death 3, Cold Snap, you can freeze an area enough to impose the ice tilt and with 1 reach you inflict the Extreme cold condition. Does this translate in any way to an extreme environment rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it does not directly correlate to a specific Extreme Environment rating. Extreme Environment is meant to model large area effects of nature such as weather or earthquakes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - If it does, with a potency of 4 should the spell create a level 4 hazard? Or a Patterning would be better suited? </div> </div> </div>See above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Could Cold Snap work as a dorect attack? Having your body instantly turn from warm to frozen is surely excruciating. And paralyzing too. </div> </div> </div>A direct attack just deals direct damage. You could certainly have a cold-based direct attack spell with Death, its base effects would be identical to <i>Rotting Flesh</i>, but its reach option could be to inflict the Extreme Cold tilt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In general, I'm unsure on how cold works with the arcanum of Death, from a mechanical point of view. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cold&quot; is &quot;produced&quot; by slowing down molecular motion, basically you're &quot;killing&quot; energy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, but about acceleration (Time 3):<br /> - If a mage accelerates himself with a potency of 6, for example, if an hour elapses for those around him not under the spell shouldn't he feel the effect of 6 hours of being awake, standing still etc. etc.? Or the spell shields the caster from this possible effect? </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's up to the Mage casting the spell, but by default there would be no deleterious effects from the spell as they'd normally be mentioned (and probably have reach option to ignore them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The spell seems to me similar to Vampiric Celerity. If this is true, the caster shouldn't be seeing everything at normal speed and &quot;just&quot; react way way faster to things he is aware of? </div> </div> </div>Similar to, but different from. The Mage is actually controlling Time itself, which means the particulars will be different than merely fast reaction times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, about Fools Rush In (Fate 2):<br /> - &quot;Little or no knowledge about a situation&quot; is a bit unclear to me. One of my players translated it more or less in &quot;every time something unexpected happens I can use the bonus&quot;, but I'm not much convinced. Can somenone give me an example or two to understand the boundaries of this spell? </div> </div> </div>&quot;A turn or two of studying the scene before acting is acceptable, but extensive reconnaissance or a detailed briefing does not permit the necessary degree of randomness this spell requires.&quot;<br /> <br /> Any time the subject of the spell does something without having more than a round or two of preparation the bonus applies.<br /> <br /> Spend hours poring over plans for breaking into the secure compound? No bonus. Eyeball for a few seconds before Leeroy Jenkinsing the gate? Bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:34:41-08:00","id":1348018,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, i'd have some other doubts tho:<br /> - Death's Cold produces tilts and condition, at least with Cold Snap. Would it be possibile for other death spells of higher level to create Extreme Environment level or it only worsen condition and tilts?<br /> - About the mechanic of cold I meant game mechanic, my bad ^_^'<br /> - About Fools Rush In, a couple of turns after leeroy jenkinsing in a fight, for example, the spell would no more work because the caster is already in &quot;too deep&quot; in a situation or if something else unexpected happens he can use again the bonus (like another enemy popping out of nowhere or an attack from somewhere unseen)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:42:38-08:00","id":1348020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1348018#post1348018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers, i'd have some other doubts tho:<br /> - Death's Cold produces tilts and condition, at least with Cold Snap. Would it be possibile for other death spells of higher level to create Extreme Environment level or it only worsen condition and tilts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death doesn't really lend itself to causing Extreme Environment as it can't really affect weather patterns the same way Forces can; Forces can cause cascade effects in weather systems, Death would be limited to whatever the scale of the spell is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - About the mechanic of cold I meant game mechanic, my bad ^_^' </div> </div> </div>Same answer. Death has cold because of how &quot;cold&quot; is &quot;made.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - About Fools Rush In, a couple of turns after leeroy jenkinsing in a fight, for example, the spell would no more work because the caster is already in &quot;too deep&quot; in a situation or if something else unexpected happens he can use again the bonus (like another enemy popping out of nowhere or an attack from somewhere unseen)? </div> </div> </div>The bonus applies so long as the character is winging it, there's nothing that says or implies the bonus should stop working at any point barring in depth preparation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:29:12-08:00","id":1348380,"title":"","content":"What type of Mind spell would let you enter an unwilling Mage\u2019s Oneiros and what would be the advantage of that over using Mind spells to get information or change things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T19:35:18-08:00","id":1348391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1348380#post1348380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What type of Mind spell would let you enter an unwilling Mage\u2019s Oneiros and what would be the advantage of that over using Mind spells to get information or change things?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you would need a Weaving to force them into the meditative trance so you could follow them in. Weaving is enough to open the gates of the Arcanum's related phenomenons.<br /> <br /> The advantage is simple, discretion. For example, if you convince the goetia responsible for a memory that locking it up will be in the mage's best interests, they will, which leaves no trace (provided you wiped any traces of your Nimbus after casting the entrance spell). Convincing their daimon could make their Obsessions change. Empowering or humiliating certain goetia will alter their weight on the mage's mind. Better yet, alter the data for an important memory or flee into the Temenos with it. Altering the subject manually is a lot more work, but it can have very powerful and long lasting effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T20:23:08-08:00","id":1348398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1348380#post1348380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What type of Mind spell would let you enter an unwilling Mage\u2019s Oneiros and what would be the advantage of that over using Mind spells to get information or change things?</div> </div> </div> </div>To enter an Oneiros you need to work with the person to get to their Oneiros via a dream bridge, or you must have telepathic contact. Theoretically, Mental Scan with the Reach to read surface thoughts is all you need, but your ST may disagree. Telepathy is a sure bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T10:12:15-08:00","id":1349610,"title":"","content":"A few questions about Proximi:<br /> <br /> 1. Blessings are Supernal in nature, so can Proximi buy their Blessings with Arcane XP, if they gained AXP previously via Forge Purpose spell?<br /> 2. When a Proximus casts a Blessing within their Oneiros that doesn't leave its borders, do they have unlimited Reach without Paradox risk just like mages do?<br /> 3. Can Blessings be somewhat modified, similar to Legacy Attainments, for example so they can only affect the Proximus in question? For instance, if you have a Bloodline with Blessings that change the members' bodies or improve their minds, it feels weird to just arbitrarily let them be able to use these Blessings on others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:24:05-08:00","id":1349704,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say yes, yes, and no probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T16:02:24-08:00","id":1349711,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I asked about the point 3 because I believe that Blessings interpreted in the way I suggested would mean that some Proximi Bloodlines/powers would gain much more flavor thanks to that interpretation. More &quot;I am a seer who will now through my oracular powers foretell your future&quot; and less &quot;I can just cast a spell on whoever and have them do everything instead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T22:46:27-08:00","id":1349788,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s how they are now? I\u2019m a little confused.<br /> <br /> Mechanically they get no benefits from having a restriction on their Blessings, but you can certainly play them as if they have restrictions. The point of a restriction on an attainment is that it comes with a mechanical impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T06:34:58-08:00","id":1349851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1349788#post1349788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically they get no benefits from having a restriction on their Blessings, but you can certainly play them as if they have restrictions. The point of a restriction on an attainment is that it comes with a mechanical impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't see anywhere the explicit statement that you can restrict/slightly modify Blessings in this way, but if you can, than that's exactly what I wanted to hear. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T12:14:06-08:00","id":1349899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1349851#post1349851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I didn't see anywhere the explicit statement that you can restrict/slightly modify Blessings in this way, but if you can, than that's exactly what I wanted to hear. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no I was saying as far as I know that you can\u2019t do that with Blessings. They aren\u2019t the same as Attainments and receive no benefit from restrictions.<br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t stop you from pretending they have restrictions in the narrative of your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:11:02-08:00","id":1349930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1349899#post1349899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn\u2019t stop you from pretending they have restrictions in the narrative of your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually how I meant my answer, sorry for the misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> By the way, did you mean by the way you answered that Attainments receive benefits from restrictions? That's a new information for me. I only remember the section on Attainments stating that you can slightly modify their scope and that overall they shouldn't have their power level changed too much from the baseline. Do you mean that by restricting one thing, you are allowed to increase another aspect of the Attainment in power? I guess that would make sense given how the Attainments are defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:37:22-08:00","id":1349938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1349930#post1349930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually how I meant my answer, sorry for the misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> By the way, did you mean by the way you answered that Attainments receive benefits from restrictions? That's a new information for me. I only remember the section on Attainments stating that you can slightly modify their scope and that overall they shouldn't have their power level changed too much from the baseline. Do you mean that by restricting one thing, you are allowed to increase another aspect of the Attainment in power? I guess that would make sense given how the Attainments are defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granting an extra Reach in exchange for limiting a spell factor or effect is common for homebrew Attainments (because many people find the number of Reaches very underwhelming due to them being tied to the Arcanum prerequisite). I'm not saying house rule because the Attainment creation guidelines are only guidelines that can explicitly be ignored, but it's also not an option presented in the book.<br /> <br /> As for restricting Blessings; as written they are Supernal spells that the Proximus is able to cast. What you're looking for seem to be closer to internalised abilities that they're able to activate. I would design those as Supernatural Merits with the Proximus Dynasty as a prerequisite (much like how the limited Attainments are unique to a Legacy) or bake it into their Curse, somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T23:34:21-08:00","id":1349986,"title":"","content":"Tessie over here nailing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T08:16:57-08:00","id":1351288,"title":"","content":"I've got a question about exceptional successes on a spellcasting roll. <br /> <br /> One of the options the caster can select is &quot;all Mana spent on the spell is refunded...&quot; Does this include any Mana that was spent to mitigate the Paradox pool, or because that's a separate roll, is it not included?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T08:41:48-08:00","id":1351292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForgeEternal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1351288#post1351288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question about exceptional successes on a spellcasting roll. <br /> <br /> One of the options the caster can select is &amp;quot;all Mana spent on the spell is refunded...&amp;quot; Does this include any Mana that was spent to mitigate the Paradox pool, or because that's a separate roll, is it not included?</div> </div> </div> </div>I include it, otherwise the amount of mana that can be spent on a single spell is pretty limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T08:03:31-08:00","id":1352605,"title":"","content":"Good day,<br /> When using a mind spell to astral project in the material world, can a mage invoke the amnion and path tools or it is possible only in the astral realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T13:23:18-08:00","id":1352671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1352605#post1352605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good day,<br /> When using a mind spell to astral project in the material world, can a mage invoke the amnion and path tools or it is possible only in the astral realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Raising the Amnion while under the effects of the <i>Psychic Projection</i> spell seems doable, but the Path Tools section specifies &quot;in dreams or the Astral.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T23:41:41-08:00","id":1352958,"title":"","content":"Hello all, returning player from 1<sup>st</sup>. I am a bit confused on the cost of grimoires and imbued/enhanced items.<br /> <br /> When you create a grimoire I guess you have to spend one experience point for the merit. Can you have more than one grimoire? Have any of your players heavily invested in making lots of grimories because them costing exp seems a bit steep but at the same time the rote quality if pretty strong. What if they find a grimoire? Do they have to pay experience points for the things they find in play? Same thing goes for imbued/enhanced items and artifacts? I am a bit worried that would take the joy out of finding something really cool if you have to buy it with experience just to keep it. <br /> <br /> Also if you make your own imbued item and relinquish control do you pay one willpower dot &amp; exp equal to the merit, then also have to pay off the willpower dot? That seems a little unnecessarily costly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T00:03:57-08:00","id":1352959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1352958#post1352958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you create a grimoire I guess you have to spend one experience point for the merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Grimoire is mostly rated as a Merit so you can requisition it with Order/Consilium Status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you have more than one grimoire? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have any of your players heavily invested in making lots of grimories because them costing exp seems a bit steep but at the same time the rote quality if pretty strong. </div> </div> </div>Rote quality is strong, but remember that this comes at the cost of needing to cast the spell in ritual time at double the interval length.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also if you make your own imbued item and relinquish control do you pay one willpower dot &amp; exp equal to the merit, then also have to pay off the willpower dot? That seems a little unnecessarily costly. </div> </div> </div>You pay off the Willpower dot recovery at your leisure. The resources are rated as Merits for the purposes of requisitions and starting kit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T00:24:43-08:00","id":1352961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1352959#post1352959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Grimoire is mostly rated as a Merit so you can requisition it with Order/Consilium Status.<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> Rote quality is strong, but remember that this comes at the cost of needing to cast the spell in ritual time at double the interval length.<br /> <br /> You pay off the Willpower dot recovery at your leisure. The resources are rated as Merits for the purposes of requisitions and starting kit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was under the impression that you had to pay experience points for merits? These items are merits just like order status, shadow name, contacts, or any of the others which you have to buy with experience. Is there a section I am missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T02:42:18-08:00","id":1352983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1352961#post1352961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that you had to pay experience points for merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do, but your imbued item isn't a merit; it's not covered by sanctity of merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T07:40:27-08:00","id":1353017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1352961#post1352961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that you had to pay experience points for merits? These items are merits just like order status, shadow name, contacts, or any of the others which you have to buy with experience. Is there a section I am missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your mistake is thinking that the Merits are necessary for having Grimoires or imbued items, but they're not. If you buy the Grimoire Merit you gain a Grimoire, but if you gain a Grimoire through other means (creating it yourself, or pilfering it from a rival mage) you have no reason or obligation to buy the Merit.<br /> <br /> And, as noted, Merits also serve as a way to determine &quot;Availability&quot; for temporary requisitioning and such.<br /> <br /> In short, the item isn't the Merit, and gaining the item doesn't force you to buy the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T14:26:06-08:00","id":1353150,"title":"","content":"If you cast a spell that has a number of uses limited by Potency, such as <i> Superlative Luck </i>,as an AoE, what happens if the charges are used up ? Lets say it had Potency 3 and they used the charges, does the target get another 3 while remaining inside the area ? Do they get more only if they re-enter it ? Or are they simply not affected again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-06-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T20:02:46-08:00","id":1353229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1353150#post1353150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cast a spell that has a number of uses limited by Potency, such as <i> Superlative Luck </i>,as an AoE, what happens if the charges are used up ? Lets say it had Potency 3 and they used the charges, does the target get another 3 while remaining inside the area ? Do they get more only if they re-enter it ? Or are they simply not affected again?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell only has 3 charges it only has 3 charges. Making it an AoE just qualifies anyone in it to use them until they\u2019re gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T12:35:45-08:00","id":1353400,"title":"","content":"So its not the type of effect that gives 3 charges to everyone, it just gives everyone a link to a pool containing 3 charges. Interesting, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T16:29:53-08:00","id":1353444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1353400#post1353400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its not the type of effect that gives 3 charges to everyone, it just gives everyone a link to a pool containing 3 charges. Interesting, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually disagree with Mrmdubois on this ruling but I wouldn't be interested in defending my case. I debated even replying to this cuz these sorts of things can get funky real fast but, I gotta say spending dice and reach to AoE a spell that gets weaker the more people are involved in it, seems weird to me. But it would make acanthi less intense, especially for an ST. This ruling is definitely waaay easier. And it makes its own sense. I could see it being either way honestly. I'd brink it up with your ST. I could be wrong and there may be better reasons tha I am aware of but this personally looks like ST fiat territory, since its not explicit and obvious (which are loaded terms around here I guess)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T18:47:11-08:00","id":1353470,"title":"","content":"I do usually go for the easiest thing for the ST to do. They're spinning a bunch of plates already, anything to reduce the workload is usually good imo.<br /> <br /> If the player wants a bigger luck benefit that lasts, then don't use a spell that relies on charges. There are many types of Boons, take advantage of one of the other ones if you don't want the effect to go away too quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-07-2019, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:44:28-08:00","id":1353556,"title":"","content":"Has anyone codified a legacy built around an Emanation?<br /> <br /> I see a lot of story potential in the idea of niche legacies that are tightly linked to specific Emanations but I'm having trouble implementing one according to the game rules. For example, &quot;learn to travel to an Emanation without a Thura&quot; as an attainment, or summoning objects from Emanations. Maybe these are kinds of attainments are more narrative rather than actions easily mapped to Arcana dots? I'd love to see how other STs have implemented these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T09:08:55-08:00","id":1353562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1353556#post1353556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone codified a legacy built around an Emanation?<br /> <br /> I see a lot of story potential in the idea of niche legacies that are tightly linked to specific Emanations but I'm having trouble implementing one according to the game rules. For example, &amp;quot;learn to travel to an Emanation without a Thura&amp;quot; as an attainment, or summoning objects from Emanations. Maybe these are kinds of attainments are more narrative rather than actions easily mapped to Arcana dots? I'd love to see how other STs have implemented these.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, in the 2ed Legacy conversion thread. The Walkers in the Mists are able to generate a thura in any Demesne generated with their soul stone. Plus they gain a weak sympathetically connection to the Mists:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page17\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page17\"> Even more Legacies, updated to 2E - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page17\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page17 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm using this thread as both a homebrew hub, venue for receiving criticisms, and way to receive suggestions for conversions should anyone reading this be </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But as their name implies, they are attuned to one specific Emanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T09:36:26-08:00","id":1353567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1353556#post1353556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone codified a legacy built around an Emanation?<br /> <br /> I see a lot of story potential in the idea of niche legacies that are tightly linked to specific Emanations but I'm having trouble implementing one according to the game rules. For example, &amp;quot;learn to travel to an Emanation without a Thura&amp;quot; as an attainment, or summoning objects from Emanations. Maybe these are kinds of attainments are more narrative rather than actions easily mapped to Arcana dots? I'd love to see how other STs have implemented these.</div> </div> </div> </div>What they said, but don\u2019t feel like you have to use Space to make being bound to an emanation realm work. An emanation legacy can be bound so closely to the emanation they come from that they count as an extension of it and can apply some of its rules no matter where they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T12:38:02-08:00","id":1353605,"title":"","content":"Last week my players and me got into a disagreement over Exceptional Luck. I was under the impression that all spells that give Boons or Hexes must have some intended outcome that they nudge Fate towards (for example, wishing some one good luck on their test, or safe travel, or to &quot;break a leg&quot;). But as my friend's pointed out, it's only some of the spells that specify that the Boon or Hex must be related to other aspects of the spell. So, is Exceptional Luck intended to be generic &quot;good/bad luck&quot; that can apply to any and all rolls and/or situations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T15:58:25-08:00","id":1353644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1353605#post1353605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last week my players and me got into a disagreement over Exceptional Luck. I was under the impression that all spells that give Boons or Hexes must have some intended outcome that they nudge Fate towards (for example, wishing some one good luck on their test, or safe travel, or to &amp;quot;break a leg&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. But as my friend's pointed out, it's only some of the spells that specify that the Boon or Hex must be related to other aspects of the spell. So, is Exceptional Luck intended to be generic &amp;quot;good/bad luck&amp;quot; that can apply to any and all rolls and/or situations?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it can be applied following the rules for boons or Hexes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T00:24:19-08:00","id":1354532,"title":"","content":"Question about Tass and Hallows.<br /> Does Tass only form as Mana overflows beyond the Hallow dot rating?<br /> <br /> Say I have a 3-dot Hallow and wait 12 days.<br /> Is that 3 Mana and 9 Tass just sitting in the now plugged-up Hallow?<br /> Or does it all crystallize after like 9 days without use? Thus making it just 9 Tass in a dry Hallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T01:54:57-08:00","id":1354537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354532#post1354532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Tass and Hallows.<br /> Does Tass only form as Mana overflows beyond the Hallow dot rating?<br /> <br /> Say I have a 3-dot Hallow and wait 12 days.<br /> Is that 3 Mana and 9 Tass just sitting in the now plugged-up Hallow?<br /> Or does it all crystallize after like 9 days without use? Thus making it just 9 Tass in a dry Hallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way i understand it is the first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T03:06:19-08:00","id":1354542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354532#post1354532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Tass and Hallows.<br /> Does Tass only form as Mana overflows beyond the Hallow dot rating?<br /> <br /> Say I have a 3-dot Hallow and wait 12 days.<br /> Is that 3 Mana and 9 Tass just sitting in the now plugged-up Hallow?<br /> Or does it all crystallize after like 9 days without use? Thus making it just 9 Tass in a dry Hallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>9 Tass and 3 mana. Leave it for another 3 days and it will go dormant as all the mana it can produce congeals into tass. In a sense, tass is created via an overflow of mana from a Hallow, but when the tass builds up it prevents any further mana from leaking from the Hallow. Kind of like detritus in a stream naturally forming a dam over time.<br /> <br /> Also, tass can be created by Mages with spells, and this is how you essentially get mana stockpiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-12-2019, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T19:58:40-08:00","id":1354710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1353400#post1353400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its not the type of effect that gives 3 charges to everyone, it just gives everyone a link to a pool containing 3 charges. Interesting, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody in the area should get 3 charges while in the area. Consider how using Mym's interpretation would work for a area affect damage spell (with or without a duration). Also consider the other option of just using increased number of targets. If you instead gave 3 charges to 10 people using increased number of target s instead of area why is it then different when using area. Nobody is going to argue that the 3 charges are split between the 10 targets are they?. Area has its own disads such as giving the charges to ANYBODY even your enemies etc...<br /> <br /> A Honing the form area spell with potency 2 would give (+2) (Dexterity) to everybody in (area Y), Area Superlative luck with potency 3 would give (3)(rote rolls) to everybody in (area y). If you go with myrms interpretation then the x potency for the Dex spell would also have to be divided between all the people in the area....<br /> <br /> Myrms mistake is thinking the spell has 3 charges when its actually imparting 3 charges of luck to its targets just like the Dex spell is imparting 2 dex to its targets.<br /> <br /> Since the spell doesnt have charges (it has potency which the charges are based on) or end once those charges are used there is no problem with reentering the area, its the same spell so you dont get a new set of charges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-12-2019, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T22:44:02-08:00","id":1354721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354710#post1354710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you instead gave 3 charges to 10 people using increased number of target s instead of area why is it then different when using area. Nobody is going to argue that the 3 charges are split between the 10 targets are they?. Area has its own disads such as giving the charges to ANYBODY even your enemies etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>You answered the question you raised completely on your own, good job. Yes, area spells and individual subject spells operate differently.<br /> <br /> The 3 charges are distributed evenly over the entire area. The fact that they may not be used evenly is entirely irrelevant. Also, it's known that if you use a spell to create an AoE like, &quot;Everything inside this area is sluggish.&quot; Then everyone is sluggish when they enter the spell, stop being sluggish when they leave it, and then become sluggish again when they re-enter. Which makes complete nonsense of your interpretation, &quot;They already used their charges, so if they come back in they don't get them back.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd appreciate it if you learned to spell my name properly as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T22:50:45-08:00","id":1354723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354721#post1354721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You answered the question you raised completely on your own, good job. Yes, area spells and individual subject spells operate differently.<br /> <br /> The 3 charges are distributed evenly over the entire area. The fact that they may not be used evenly is entirely irrelevant. Also, it's known that if you use a spell to create an AoE like, &quot;Everything inside this area is sluggish.&quot; Then everyone is sluggish when they enter the spell, stop being sluggish when they leave it, and then become sluggish again when they re-enter. Which makes complete nonsense of your interpretation, &quot;They already used their charges, so if they come back in they don't get them back.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd appreciate it if you learned to spell my name properly as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said, 3 charges are given to each target in the area exactly the same way gaining 2 dex would work in a area Honing spell. You leave a +2 dex area you loose +2 dex, you leave a SP area you lose access to the charges that the spell gave you, you'd gain them back once you reenter the area but you would still only have what the spell gave you minus any you have already used.<br /> <br /> Spells operate the same cast either on a individual or an area, all that gets modified is the TARGETs of spell when you choose either more targets or an area.<br /> <br /> Are you also suggesting that when casting a 3 potency SP spell on 3 targets you divide the charges between the 3 targets?<br /> <br /> The wording of both Honing the form and SP say along the lines of &quot;The subject gains X&quot;. If your interpretation was correct the honing the form's area would gain +2 dex not everybody inside it. Its obvious then that if multiple people inside an area can gain dexterity from honing the form and ALL count as subjects while inside the area then there is nothing stopping all subjects inside a SP area from gaining access to x number of rote actions while inside that area. Otherwise the first person to enter the + dexterity area would be the only person to get that increased dexterity or nobody gets it since the subject in the case of an area is the area and not the things inside it..<br /> <br /> When entering an area spell you become subject to that spell, so you gain the increased dex or gain a number of rote rolls equal to its potency. Each individual person is a different subject (since withstand interferes and a spell can have a different or no effect on each subject) so each gets a set of charges or whatever.<br /> <br /> Giving a room of 100 people +2 dexterity each for 2 potency is fine but giving 100 people 3 rote rolls each isnt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-13-2019, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T22:52:31-08:00","id":1354724,"title":"","content":"And since the target is the -area- the number of charges is 3 for the area. The potential users of those charges are irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T23:56:49-08:00","id":1354729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354724#post1354724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since the target is the -area- the number of charges is 3 for the area. The potential users of those charges are irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The target might be an area, but the area is not the subject. Everything in the area is the subject. Explain then please what happens to a potency 2 honing spell for dexterity that says &quot;may improve the subjects physical attributes&quot; and gives the subject +2 dexterity. How does this work in your world if the area is the only thing gaining the +2 dexterity since the area in your interpretation is the one and only subject? Gaining +2 dexterity is exactly the same as gaining x rote rolls. The only difference is that one is a charge and hence gets used up on use.<br /> <br /> If the area is the subject with the 3 charges, how does one access those charges? Billy might be the subject of a SP spell with y charges but Bob cant go up and use Billy's charges for him even if he was under the same spell which had 2 targets as subjects. How does one use the areas charges if the area gains the charges and not each subject inside the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-13-2019, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T06:29:29-08:00","id":1354755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354542#post1354542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 9 Tass and 3 mana. Leave it for another 3 days and it will go dormant as all the mana it can produce congeals into tass. In a sense, tass is created via an overflow of mana from a Hallow, but when the tass builds up it prevents any further mana from leaking from the Hallow. Kind of like detritus in a stream naturally forming a dam over time.<br /> <br /> Also, tass can be created by Mages with spells, and this is how you essentially get mana stockpiles.</div> </div> </div> </div> Another three days? The Merit says it caps at 3-times it's dots in tass and goes dormant by RAW, which is why i chose 12 days at the begining for a 3-dot hallow. Taking into account overflow and tass limitaion.<br /> Are you saying 6 days and then +3 more before all the mana turns to tass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T06:37:14-08:00","id":1354756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354755#post1354755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another three days? The Merit says it caps at 3-times it's dots in tass and goes dormant by RAW, which is why i chose 12 days at the begining for a 3-dot hallow. Taking into account overflow and tass limitaion.<br /> Are you saying 6 days and then +3 more before all the mana turns to tass?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wont it go dormant in 3 days if no mana is used? It generates 3 mana per day and can only store 9 before becoming dormant? After 3 days all that's left is 9 Tass that needs to all be removed before it starts producing 3 mana per day again. Use 3 mana a day from the hallow and none will be left over to become Tass so it won't go dormant, use less and any unused mana will become Tass until it reaches 9 and then the hallow goes dormant.<br /> <br /> Not sure what you mean by overflow mana, it's unnspent/unused mana that conjeales into Tass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-13-2019, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T07:05:54-08:00","id":1354761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354755#post1354755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another three days? The Merit says it caps at 3-times it's dots in tass and goes dormant by RAW, which is why i chose 12 days at the begining for a 3-dot hallow. Taking into account overflow and tass limitaion.<br /> Are you saying 6 days and then +3 more before all the mana turns to tass?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the trouble is that you've misunderstood the rate of Mana generation, so here's the breakdown:<br /> A Hallow produces one Mana per dot per day, meaning your 3 dot Hallow produces 3 Mana per day. Since the tass cap is three times the dot rating, your Hallow is capped at 9. It takes 3 days, not 9 or 12, to fill up the cap.<br /> Note that the Merit states that the Hallow stops producing Mana once the tass cap is reached, meaning that once the non-tass Mana congeals into tass to the point where it's fully saturated, it does not produce any additional non-tass Mana, thus limiting it to storing a maximum of 9 Mana and only in the form of tass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-13-2019, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T08:05:06-08:00","id":1354773,"title":"","content":"Good catch Tessie, I mathed that wrong.<br /> <br /> totalgit, it\u2019s pretty simple. The area is the subject, and it works like an area, in other words it either has a property that affects everyone, or it has a limited resource that everyone in it has access to. In terms of a property you could think of it like a speed limit on the road, or being at high altitude and suffering from oxygen deprivation. In the second it\u2019s like having a forest anyone can walk into and cut down a tree whenever they want. Just because anyone can take a tree doesn\u2019t mean the distribution of tree takers will be even. You are confusing the fact that the special properties a spell bestows on the subject of the area can have an impact on those in it with the idea that those in it are the subjects. They are not the subjects, they\u2019re simply being affected by the properties of the area. If the area has no more charges to give then it just doesn\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T09:03:55-08:00","id":1354777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354773#post1354773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The area is the subject</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something the book neither supports nor refutes. Personally I'm of the opinion that everything within an AoE that is a valid subject is its own subject. For spells where the physical space can be a valid subject (Co-Location, for example) that whole area becomes a single subject that gains supernatural properties. For spells where individual creatures are valid subjects (for example, Hone the Form) then each individual creature becomes a separate subject.<br /> <br /> The whole cast on a subject area to make non-subjects in that area gain the spell effect is weird to me. It's the <i>subject</i> who's supposed to gain the stat boost from Hone the Form, not secondary targets.<br /> (Yes, you can design spells that affect secondary targets, like explosions that affect people around the exploding subject, but that's not what I'm talking about nor what spells like Hone the Form or Superlative Luck are like.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T09:13:52-08:00","id":1354779,"title":"","content":"It's why Area of Effect is differentiated from Subjects or Size imo.<br /> <br /> If the idea was to affect many subjects than you'd simply use the multiple Subjects use of Scale.<br /> <br /> Instead you're treating the area as if it has special properties, i.e. +2 Dex, or has 3 charges of luck, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-13-2019, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T10:06:45-08:00","id":1354787,"title":"","content":"There are <i>many</i> differences between AoE and subjects, and just as many reasons to use one over the other.<br /> 1.) You can affect subjects you can't see (either by being in cover or by being invisible) by covering a building or a room.<br /> 2.) You can affect multiple subjects without having to resort to sensory range (due to the impracticality of having to touch multiple targets the same turn).<br /> 3.) You tie the effect to a location, meaning it stops for subjects who leave the area where you want the spell to be active.<br /> 4.) You can affect subjects in the future without even having to see them as long as they enter the area.<br /> 5.) You don't need to know that all subjects exists within the area, but also risk affecting subjects you didn't anticipate.<br /> Et cetera.<br /> <br /> Having all targets within an area actually be subjects reduces the many differences by a marginal amount. Especially considering that, according to you, all spells that doesn't deal with charges in one way or another, would work identically.<br /> <br /> You're introducing an extra step between subject and effect, an exemption to the magic rules that is never mentioned in the book, nor accounted for in any spell descriptions that I know of. It also leads to weird situations where you're applying certain effects separately but other effects shared. And how do you factor Withstand into account? Grave Misfortune, for example, has a number of charges equal to Potency, but since it's Withstood everyone within the AoE could have different amounts of charges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T10:19:02-08:00","id":1354790,"title":"","content":"Grave Misfortune would work as I've described earlier. There's a set number of charges in the area. They get used up by whoever meets the conditions to use them until the charges are gone. Even access to the charges is granted, not even distribution of charges to all users. It's like having a vending machine. There are only so many snacks in there, and someone can purchase multiple snacks.<br /> <br /> Withstand operates normally. If their Withstand exceeds the Potency of the spell then they act as if they are not under the effects of it and under no compulsion to consume charges from it.<br /> <br /> There isn't an extra step either. This area gives +2 Dex, the area is the subject and the +2 Dex is the effect. Same goes for spells with charges: This area has 3 charges for Grave Misfortune, so that's what it's got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T11:13:06-08:00","id":1354792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354790#post1354790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grave Misfortune would work as I've described earlier. There's a set number of charges in the area. They get used up by whoever meets the conditions to use them until the charges are gone. Even access to the charges is granted, not even distribution of charges to all users. It's like having a vending machine. There are only so many snacks in there, and someone can purchase multiple snacks.<br /> <br /> Withstand operates normally. If their Withstand exceeds the Potency of the spell then they act as if they are not under the effects of it and under no compulsion to consume charges from it.<br /> <br /> There isn't an extra step either. This area gives +2 Dex, the area is the subject and the +2 Dex is the effect. Same goes for spells with charges: This area has 3 charges for Grave Misfortune, so that's what it's got.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell does not have charges the subject gets rote rolls and those have charges. Each subject gets a different set of rote rolls just like each subject takes a separate set of damage if it was a damage spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T11:17:09-08:00","id":1354793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354792#post1354792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell does not have charges the subject gets rote rolls and those have charges. Each subject gets a different set of rote rolls just like each subject takes a separate set of damage if it was a damage spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell effects everything in the area it can apply to, in this case anything that can take damage. It has charges to this effect. It doesn't change anything I've said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T11:21:09-08:00","id":1354794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354790#post1354790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grave Misfortune would work as I've described earlier. There's a set number of charges in the area. They get used up by whoever meets the conditions to use them until the charges are gone. Even access to the charges is granted, not even distribution of charges to all users. It's like having a vending machine. There are only so many snacks in there, and someone can purchase multiple snacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the number of charges varies because one of the targets has Composure 1 and the other Composure 2. For a Potency 3 Grave Misfortune they would have 2 and 1 charges, respectively. How can the spell have a varying number of charges shared across all secondary targets?<br /> The only way to resolve it simply would be to ignore Withstand for the number of charges, which would be <i>another</i> exception to the rules just to make it work your way, and another situation where Potency is treated differently depending on whether it's a charge or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354790#post1354790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't an extra step either. This area gives +2 Dex, the area is the subject and the +2 Dex is the effect. Same goes for spells with charges: This area has 3 charges for Grave Misfortune, so that's what it's got.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>the area is the subject</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The subject is defined.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>and the +2 Dex is the effect.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The spell effect is defined.<br /> <br /> The next step would be that the spell effect is applied to the subject.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>This area gives +2 Dex,</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> And now you've <i>added</i> that the subject pushes the effect forward to a secondary target. That's not what Hone the Form does. The <i>spell</i> adds two dots of Dexterity to the <i>subject</i>. What you're describing is the <i>subject</i> adding two dots of Dexterity to a <i>secondary target</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-13-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T11:23:50-08:00","id":1354795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354793#post1354793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell effects everything in the area it can apply to, in this case anything that can take damage. It has charges to this effect. It doesn't change anything I've said.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think there is a difference between a potency 2 SP with 2 targets and a area SP spell with 2 people in its area? On the one hand 2 people get 2 rote rolls each and in the area they get 2 between them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T02:32:12-08:00","id":1354868,"title":"","content":"To make things work easier i ve always stated that an area spell of the kind of honing the form simply cast the spell on all the subjects present in the area at the time of casting, and then the spell works normally, no matter where they go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T06:56:16-08:00","id":1354883,"title":"","content":"What I find strange is how the charge per area approach can affect certain cases.<br /> <br /> For example, lets say honing the form for Dex is cast on your sanctum with Potency 3 and then 10 mages are inside. Those 10 get +3 to Dex. But if you cast a Potency 3 boon for fine motor tasks, only 3 people will get the boon once. So it becomes oddly difficult to use Fate to make a lucky workspace for your cabal.<br /> <br /> So my original interpretation was:<br /> <br /> * An area of effect affects everything inside it, meaning it auto renews so long as you stay within a certain radius of the center (or re-enters once charges are expended). So a lucky zone is whan an Acanthus would make to defend their sanctum instead of, for example, the golem area that a Moros could employ.<br /> <br /> * Throwing a target out of their comfort zone or moving that zone is an interesting way around these effects, with Forces, Matter and Space providing the most obvious ways to do so.<br /> <br /> * Certain spells can become especially dangerous as an AoE effect, such as Shared Fate. But using them without setup also places the caster and their cabal mates at risk.<br /> <br /> * Additional spell work is needed to make sure only select targets are affected by the effect. Therefore Prime or Fate pose a real risk of affecting these filters.<br /> <br /> * It becomes interesting to prioritize Scale and Duration over Potency for AoE casts, but it adds the risk of easier dispelling. Balancing these factors is the drawback of a wide reaching effect, in addition to how easily it would cause Disbelief.<br /> <br /> It all came from the following though experiment: Moros and Obrimos make a tool arsenal. Mastigos can carry all they need with them or hide their caches extremely well. Thrysus have fetishes, talens, spirits, trained animals and perhaps cryptids at their disposal. But what kind of tools and sanctum defenses does an Acanthus usually make (apart from Warding Gesture, Monkey's Paw and The Right Tool enhanced personal possessions) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-14-2019, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T16:37:37-08:00","id":1355508,"title":"","content":"Ephemeral entities who lose their Corpus become dormant, disperse into ephemera, and reform in a nearby Resonant site (or similar location.) Would it be possible to trigger the latter parts of this process without pummeling a spirit into dormancy? Effectively &quot;banishing&quot; the spirit to the nearest Resonant site? What Practice would you use?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354883#post1354883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It all came from the following though experiment: Moros and Obrimos make a tool arsenal. Mastigos can carry all they need with them or hide their caches extremely well. Thrysus have fetishes, talens, spirits, trained animals and perhaps cryptids at their disposal. But what kind of tools and sanctum defenses does an Acanthus usually make (apart from Warding Gesture, Monkey's Paw and The Right Tool enhanced personal possessions) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely the Acanthus sees you coming and just happens to have the appropriate tool nearby?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:13:10-08:00","id":1355517,"title":"","content":"How many points of mana would you say a Hallow created using the Create Truth spell has upon creation? I'm inclined to say zero so that legacy attainments based on that spell cannot leverage the &quot;mana break&quot; rule to create an immediate net source of mana on demand for the cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 12-17-2019, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T18:39:41-08:00","id":1355550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355508#post1355508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral entities who lose their Corpus become dormant, disperse into ephemera, and reform in a nearby Resonant site (or similar location.) Would it be possible to trigger the latter parts of this process without pummeling a spirit into dormancy? Effectively &quot;banishing&quot; the spirit to the nearest Resonant site? What Practice would you use?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Discorporate Manifestation does this. Adding new manifestations and forcing the subject to use them are both possible, though book seems to disagree with itself on the level of expertise required. Theoretically, Weaving really should do the trick, but the closest published spell that does this (Revenant) is Patterning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355517#post1355517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say zero</div> </div> </div> </div>Same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T13:34:20-08:00","id":1355687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355517#post1355517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many points of mana would you say a Hallow created using the Create Truth spell has upon creation? I'm inclined to say zero so that legacy attainments based on that spell cannot leverage the &amp;quot;mana break&amp;quot; rule to create an immediate net source of mana on demand for the cabal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say full mana points, so they can start generating tass after a day or mana instantly. Its the capstone Attainment, it should feel powerful. At this point a Fate primary Legacy can, for example, use Miracle to give the cabal a similar mana engine (use all the mana you need, then get it all back plus one). <br /> <br /> If you are looking for some inspiration for restrictions, the Stewards of the Celestial Orrery in 1ed needed to setup with a previous Attainment to become a moving power source, then spend a willpower point to become a living Hallow. They could produce mana once a day and could not oblate to themselves.<br /> <br /> The homebrew Legacy of the House of Fire &amp; Stone produces a 2 dot Hallow that lasts a week, but requires the mage to spend a mana and spend at least one night in a place. However, it avoids the thaumic boom that Create Truth usually creates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T16:43:25-08:00","id":1355717,"title":"","content":"I would say that it spews its potency in mana into the area around the hallow causing &quot;massive ripples and aftershocks through the local network of ley lines, which almost certainly creates new Mysteries&quot;. Think of it like creating a mana volcano/tap that spews the mana into the surrounding area maybe?<br /> <br /> Sure its a huge mana break if used as an attainment (25 mana down to 1?) but hey it is a 5 point attainment needing a min of 8 gnosis to have. Been awhile since ive read attainments but isnt it like only duration 4 rounds or something? So they spend 1 mana to create a 5 point allow that lasts 4 rounds? Yes its a net gain of 4 mana but with a limited time to use it before the mana presumably fades? (it doesnt say in the spell but i would rule the mana fade/spreads out/becomes unusable once the spell ends, even if it should maybe normally hang around until it becomes tass)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-18-2019, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T21:37:07-08:00","id":1355761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355717#post1355717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that it spews its potency in mana into the area around the hallow causing &quot;massive ripples and aftershocks through the local network of ley lines, which almost certainly creates new Mysteries&quot;. Think of it like creating a mana volcano/tap that spews the mana into the surrounding area maybe?<br /> <br /> Sure its a huge mana break if used as an attainment (25 mana down to 1?) but hey it is a 5 point attainment needing a min of 8 gnosis to have. Been awhile since ive read attainments but isnt it like only duration 4 rounds or something? So they spend 1 mana to create a 5 point allow that lasts 4 rounds? Yes its a net gain of 4 mana but with a limited time to use it before the mana presumably fades? (it doesnt say in the spell but i would rule the mana fade/spreads out/becomes unusable once the spell ends, even if it should maybe normally hang around until it becomes tass)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's if the reach is spent on instant cast, for something like creating a Hallow Advanced Duration makes more sense, meaning you create a 3-dot Hallow (potency of 1 + Prime/2 rounded down) that lasts a year.<br /> <br /> [Edit] I think it'd actually be a 2-dot Hallow, since the Withstand is the rating of the Hallow to be created and you have potency 3; personally I think the rating should just be the potency of the spell, Withstand doesn't really make sense on this particular spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 12-19-2019, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:58:45-08:00","id":1355779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355761#post1355761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's if the reach is spent on instant cast, for something like creating a Hallow Advanced Duration makes more sense, meaning you create a 3-dot Hallow (potency of 1 + Prime/2 rounded down) that lasts a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>True so its spending a scene (for ritual attainments) to save 14 mana. Seems fair to me considering what it takes to actually learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:24:18-08:00","id":1355886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355508#post1355508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral entities who lose their Corpus become dormant, disperse into ephemera, and reform in a nearby Resonant site (or similar location.) Would it be possible to trigger the latter parts of this process without pummeling a spirit into dormancy? Effectively &quot;banishing&quot; the spirit to the nearest Resonant site? What Practice would you use?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would use Fraying - Spirit Banishment (Fraying) sounds like the opposite of Spirit Summons (Perfecting).<br /> <br /> &quot;Fraying spells... can weaken targetsunder the Arcanum\u2019s purview... or erode the barrier between worlds. They can also directly attack targets using the energies of the Arcanum.&quot;<br /> <br /> That definitely sounds like a practice that can banish things or send them away from whatever they were trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:29:56-08:00","id":1355889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1354794#post1354794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet the number of charges varies because one of the targets has Composure 1 and the other Composure 2. For a Potency 3 Grave Misfortune they would have 2 and 1 charges, respectively. How can the spell have a varying number of charges shared across all secondary targets?<br /> The only way to resolve it simply would be to ignore Withstand for the number of charges, which would be <i>another</i> exception to the rules just to make it work your way, and another situation where Potency is treated differently depending on whether it's a charge or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<i>the area is the subject</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The subject is defined.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>and the +2 Dex is the effect.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The spell effect is defined.<br /> <br /> The next step would be that the spell effect is applied to the subject.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>This area gives +2 Dex,</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> And now you've <i>added</i> that the subject pushes the effect forward to a secondary target. That's not what Hone the Form does. The <i>spell</i> adds two dots of Dexterity to the <i>subject</i>. What you're describing is the <i>subject</i> adding two dots of Dexterity to a <i>secondary target</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking about this the last little while, but haven't had a chance to respond til now. I'd say that the number of charges isn't variable, even if the number that can be applied to a given individual in the area isn't, and that isn't a problem since I've already said that while everyone has access to the charges they may not be evenly used among everyone before running out. In this case, Withstand protects you by limiting the number of charges that are negative to you that can be applied to you.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, I can see why you'd say that. Area works like that though, if you set the area on fire, everything in the area is on fire. If you give the area +2 Dex then naturally everything in the area also receives +2 Dex. It may be simpler to say that people or whatever inside the area, are considered part of the area until they leave it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T16:45:59-08:00","id":1355963,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the book pretty clearly define area spells as applying to the area and every valid subject within it?<br /> If not, I know Dave has clarified this before. Seems like a set and done thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T17:55:56-08:00","id":1355976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1355963#post1355963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't the book pretty clearly define area spells as applying to the area and every valid subject within it?<br /> If not, I know Dave has clarified this before. Seems like a set and done thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines<br /> how large the area covered by the spell is, <b>applying the spell<br /> effect to anyone or anything within</b>. A mage cannot single out<br /> <b>specific subjects</b> in the declared space unless she uses the spell<br /> Warding Gesture.&quot;<br /> <br /> I bolded the parts i think important. Anything within the area and NOT thee area being one. The other being the &quot;specific subjects&quot; part makes it pretty clear to me that anyone/thing in the area becomes a subject of the spell and each one is a specific subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-19-2019, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T19:43:04-08:00","id":1356221,"title":"","content":"Right, so saying it wouldn't apply Dex +2 to subjects in the area is kind of nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T22:31:00-08:00","id":1356237,"title":"","content":"That would be a weird thing to say, and I don\u2019t think anyone said that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T07:17:51-08:00","id":1356296,"title":"","content":"The argument is not whether people in the area would get +2 Dex or not; it's whether they're subjects of the spell or not. And I say they're subjects because the spell grants +2 Dex to its subjects regardless of whether you cast per subject or AoE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:31:23-08:00","id":1356324,"title":"","content":"Do Mages have any inherent ability to detect if another Mage causes a Paradox in their presence, assuming the effects aren't immediately obvious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T12:41:43-08:00","id":1356349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356324#post1356324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Mages have any inherent ability to detect if another Mage causes a Paradox in their presence, assuming the effects aren't immediately obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not aside from the general PMS for supernatural effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T16:11:18-08:00","id":1356388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356324#post1356324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Mages have any inherent ability to detect if another Mage causes a Paradox in their presence, assuming the effects aren't immediately obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>From core book, the only way are uncovering deep information using focused mage sight<br /> <br /> Signs of sorcery adds the prime 1 nimbus tuning spell, which provide additional informations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 12-21-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T15:57:38-08:00","id":1356712,"title":"","content":"Hi, a player of mine asked me about a spell that could transform a mannequin/prostethic arm in a fully functional flesh arm to workaround temporarily an amputated arm.<br /> I thought about a Matter 3 (weaving) + Life 4 (Patterning) Spell should do the trick, does it sound right?.<br /> Then i got asked about turning someone into electricity, as per transforming his whole body and being to electricity keeping mental functionality, fundamentally turning the guy in an &quot;elemental&quot; version of himself.<br /> I thought about a Force 4 + Life 4 spell (both Patterning i presume) but I'm not sure if there may be other implications, any idea in regard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T16:40:10-08:00","id":1356721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356712#post1356712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, a player of mine asked me about a spell that could transform a mannequin/prostethic arm in a fully functional flesh arm to workaround temporarily an amputated arm.<br /> I thought about a Matter 3 (weaving) + Life 4 (Patterning) Spell should do the trick, does it sound right?.<br /> Then i got asked about turning someone into electricity, as per transforming his whole body and being to electricity keeping mental functionality, fundamentally turning the guy in an &quot;elemental&quot; version of himself.<br /> I thought about a Force 4 + Life 4 spell (both Patterning i presume) but I'm not sure if there may be other implications, any idea in regard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning one thing into another is a Patterning (4 dot) spell for both the original and desired substance, so going from matter to living flesh would require Matter 4 + Life 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T17:47:56-08:00","id":1356729,"title":"","content":"At that point, they might as well just use Life 4 to regenerate it. A simpler solution is to perhaps use Life 3 Weaving to aid in transplanting a living replacement, but that depends on low their Wisdom is. But it will still look unnatural, no matter how much the arm looks like the mage's.<br /> <br /> Permanent solutions include a Weaving 3 to gain a starfish or lizard's regenerative healing, added to body control to regrow the limb the long way (unless you have a master of Time). <br /> <br /> Another option is to summon a Life Supernatural Entity to do it for them, or give instructions on a way to do it. They can also bargain with a high Ranking Healing spirit (like that of a famous hospital or medical school). Last option is to give the Life sight to a Matter mage so he can construct a perfect, custom made prosthesis. Attaching it would require an extended medicine roll and would probably be agonizing, but at least they become a Fullmetal Alchemist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-23-2019, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T19:31:15-08:00","id":1356882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356729#post1356729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it will still look unnatural, no matter how much the arm looks like the mage's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird qualifier to throw in there, I don't think that makes any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T06:37:57-08:00","id":1356921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356882#post1356882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird qualifier to throw in there, I don't think that makes any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they are low Wisdom enough to steal limbs from living people and graft them into themselves Tzimisce style, then it might be good to leave a few clues for a perceptive person to notice. Unless they take measures, mundane or supernatural, to hide it. <br /> <br /> You know, add a few interesting complications to hiding such an act of hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T06:50:02-08:00","id":1356923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356921#post1356921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if they are low Wisdom enough to steal limbs from living people and graft them into themselves Tzimisce style, then it might be good to leave a few clues for a perceptive person to notice. Unless they take measures, mundane or supernatural, to hide it. <br /> <br /> You know, add a few interesting complications to hiding such an act of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe it's grown specifically for the future user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T11:00:26-08:00","id":1356934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356729#post1356729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it will still look unnatural, no matter how much the arm looks like the mage's.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1356921#post1356921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if they are low Wisdom enough to steal limbs from living people and graft them into themselves Tzimisce style, then it might be good to leave a few clues for a perceptive person to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean the latter, you shouldn't phrase it like the former. The first reads like an absolute assertion, presumably backed by unstated sources. The latter reads like (good) storytelling advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T15:39:20-08:00","id":1356948,"title":"","content":"<br /> Then i got asked about turning someone into electricity, as per transforming his whole body and being to electricity keeping mental functionality, fundamentally turning the guy in an &quot;elemental&quot; version of himself.<br /> I thought about a Force 4 + Life 4 spell (both Patterning i presume) but I'm not sure if there may be other implications, any idea in regard?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A spell that transforms the target into something<br /> that falls within the Purview of another Arcanum, like<br /> transforming into a living pillar of fire (Life and Forces),<br /> requires a mage to know the Practice of Patterning for the<br /> destination Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>So yes forces 4 + life 4...however Deaths &quot;Shadow Flesh&quot; spell completely ignores the above rules so you know whatever....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T01:47:31-08:00","id":1357331,"title":"","content":"Life 4 + Forces 4 can turn a person into a being of living flame. Using the same requirements to turn a person into a being of living lightning isn't different enough to make me want to give myself headaches over it.<br /> <br /> As for Shadow Flesh, I mentioned that in the errata thread, and it got passed over for getting errataed, so it's probably safe to say that it's intentional. Any reasoning you come up with is going to be a rationalization, but the one I've settled for after talking about with with other folks on the forum is that everyone has the capacity to be dead. Temporarily turning yourself into a corpse with Patterning is no big deal. As such, turning yourself into a different aspect of Death, I.e. darkness instead of a ghost, is also just not a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T17:24:48-08:00","id":1357910,"title":"","content":"Is there any fan supplements that update 1e legacies to 2e? Are there any offical legacy supplements in the pipeline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T19:36:55-08:00","id":1357933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1357910#post1357910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any fan supplements that update 1e legacies to 2e? Are there any offical legacy supplements in the pipeline?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few threads right here on the forum that have done so. Only two legacies have been officially updated. Keepers of the Covenant looks like it might be getting an update with the next Dark Eras. They probably aren\u2019t going to do anymore legacy books for quite some time though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T19:38:41-08:00","id":1357934,"title":"","content":"Has there been any info that would indicate whether time travel could prevent a mage from awakening. If you prevented the circumstances that caused the awakening would it never happen? Or is it now something that would always happen? And if so, would time travel meddle with timeline of it taking place? My players are about to go back to a time where they could potentially mess with their futures enough to prevent it and I\u2019m curious of what the consequences could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T19:46:05-08:00","id":1357936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1357934#post1357934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any info that would indicate whether time travel could prevent a mage from awakening. If you prevented the circumstances that caused the awakening would it never happen? Or is it now something that would always happen? And if so, would time travel meddle with timeline of it taking place? My players are about to go back to a time where they could potentially mess with their futures enough to prevent it and I\u2019m curious of what the consequences could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening is an act of Imperium, once it happens it\u2019s very, very difficult to undo. It\u2019s pretty unlikely your players could undo their Awakening unless you decide that\u2019s where you want the story to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T19:57:54-08:00","id":1357940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1357934#post1357934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any info that would indicate whether time travel could prevent a mage from awakening. If you prevented the circumstances that caused the awakening would it never happen? Or is it now something that would always happen? And if so, would time travel meddle with timeline of it taking place? My players are about to go back to a time where they could potentially mess with their futures enough to prevent it and I\u2019m curious of what the consequences could be.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Signs of Sorcery</i> says that once someone Awakens it retroactively becomes their destiny to Awaken, so short of killing them time shenanigans shouldn't prevent an Awakening (though it could screw it up and turn someone into a Banisher).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T21:25:00-08:00","id":1358347,"title":"","content":"Less a mechanical question than a practical application question: How often do people find themselves pushing the limits of their characters' spellcasting ability?<br /> <br /> There's some clear avenues for Awakened characters to speed their development by converting failed Imagos to dramatic failures, stacking Yantras to offset &quot;insurance&quot; spell factors, casting spells beyond their safe control totals, and so on, but at the same time a lot of these things are elective and there's a pretty wide space for risk-averse play in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> What makes a risky maneuver &quot;worth it&quot; for those who don't lean into those options as much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T22:29:56-08:00","id":1358353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358347#post1358347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less a mechanical question than a practical application question: How often do people find themselves pushing the limits of their characters' spellcasting ability?<br /> <br /> There's some clear avenues for Awakened characters to speed their development by converting failed Imagos to dramatic failures, stacking Yantras to offset &quot;insurance&quot; spell factors, casting spells beyond their safe control totals, and so on, but at the same time a lot of these things are elective and there's a pretty wide space for risk-averse play in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> What makes a risky maneuver &quot;worth it&quot; for those who don't lean into those options as much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably it s an obvious thing, but i see that during battles my players are more prone to risky magic.<br /> Also, spells that helps to progress in the plot are seen as a necessary risk<br /> But in fact they rarely convert spell in dramatic failure, only when they fear no real consequence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T22:51:53-08:00","id":1358355,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, most of the times the more complicated spells came out were in combat, especially against threats that are not 'A guy standing across the room from you.' They were pulled out against things like a giant owl monster with a deafening hoot in a blizzard, an idigam resembling a slug of stone plates the size of two football fields, a trio of invisible dogs, a car full of who knows what (armed men) driving after them after they pissed off some local Seers. Two harbingers of the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for dramatic failures, my players took them when they arose but they didn't arise much in spellcasting. We had one memorable failure-to-Dramatic during some Mage scrutinizing some bodies (remnants of the idigam) and a Supernal entity hopped in and made the entire experience awful for her. The players were experienced with Chronicles stuff but only partially with mage, so they weren't dealing with any 'If I lose Wisdom my character is ruined' types. Paradox came up a decent amount through spells.<br /> <br /> Anyways the idea seems to be stressed situations. Whether the character is on edge because something is about to happen to them or someone or thing they care about and they just need it to stop, or they don't have much time, or they're in a strange place and are unaware of local enemies or allies. Let them sit in their sanctum and they'll cast the safest spells all day. Once they -need- to use a Reach to get to cast a spell fast, then you have your foot in the door. Raise the stakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-02-2020, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T23:43:05-08:00","id":1358361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358353#post1358353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably it s an obvious thing, but i see that during battles my players are more prone to risky magic.<br /> Also, spells that helps to progress in the plot are seen as a necessary risk<br /> But in fact they rarely convert spell in dramatic failure, only when they fear no real consequence</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of clarity, I'm asking less about players being forced into taking a gamble in dire circumstances and more about characters choosing to skirt the boundaries of best practices in the name of personal advancement; following through on dangerous Obsessions, experimenting with Reaching beyond their grasp to try and develop new Praxes, taking Paradox Conditions to work out the bugs in their magic, and so on all feel thematically encouraged by the nature of Arcane Beats.<br /> <br /> Like, this is ostensibly a thing that the Awakened get up to with some regularity according to the fiction, but a lot of discussion seems to treat that as going above and beyond the game's stated PC role of portraying characters with their flaws in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T08:49:39-08:00","id":1358427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1357936#post1357936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awakening is an act of Imperium, once it happens it\u2019s very, very difficult to undo. It\u2019s pretty unlikely your players could undo their Awakening unless you decide that\u2019s where you want the story to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is the Death of Magic Boon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T12:17:54-08:00","id":1358462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1357940#post1357940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> says that once someone Awakens it retroactively becomes their destiny to Awaken, so short of killing them time shenanigans shouldn't prevent an Awakening (though it could screw it up and turn someone into a Banisher).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To go a little further, the characters would actually be protected from the changes in their timeline because of Time magic. So if they meddled with the circumstances of their Awakening but we\u2019re still fated to Awaken, I guess it\u2019s possible they come back to a timeline where it occurred in a different way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T12:47:32-08:00","id":1358467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358427#post1358427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there is the Death of Magic Boon...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, but special care should be taken when procuring it. There will probably be hoops the mage will need to jump through to get the Supernal Entity to agree:<br /> <br /> &quot;So lets review, you want me to exhume the remains of five generations of the Zamkni\u0119te-Oko family, arange them inside a circle of powdered eagle bone, then place a giant lens forged from the sands of Saragarhi at its center. Is that correct ?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is so&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why exactly?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you want the Boon or not ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-02-2020, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T18:34:58-08:00","id":1358514,"title":"","content":"One thing I was wondering about. Multiple copies of spells doing the same thing do not stack. So if you have a Potency 4 boost to speed using Space and a Potency 3 using Time, only the Space one takes hold, while the Time one does nothing but consume spell control until release.<br /> <br /> But lets say you use an Enhance Skill for Occult and one for Investigation. Even if there is the Reach option to split Potency, can those two stack as independent spells ? So far I interpreted as yes, since they are not concurrently boosting the same stat, but I wanted to double check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-02-2020, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T01:14:53-08:00","id":1358569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358514#post1358514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I was wondering about. Multiple copies of spells doing the same thing do not stack. So if you have a Potency 4 boost to speed using Space and a Potency 3 using Time, only the Space one takes hold, while the Time one does nothing but consume spell control until release.<br /> <br /> But lets say you use an Enhance Skill for Occult and one for Investigation. Even if there is the Reach option to split Potency, can those two stack as independent spells ? So far I interpreted as yes, since they are not concurrently boosting the same stat, but I wanted to double check.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, they could. Advantage of the Reach option is it takes up less Spell Control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T05:30:43-08:00","id":1358596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358569#post1358569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, they could. Advantage of the Reach option is it takes up less Spell Control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, thank you. So in theory a mage could cast powerful individual sized AoE spells centered on a ring, wallet, coin, tie pin or other random item, store them away and use them as a situation demands. Like a Thrysus using certain gloves when they need to become combat juggernauts or a belt that lets a Mastigos talk their way out of anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T06:41:24-08:00","id":1358611,"title":"","content":"What are a few reasons that Pierce Deception could invoke a Clash of Wills other than attempting to pierce a magical deception or illusion? Need some possible alternative explanations for the Clash so that mere occurrence of the Clash (which the mage will always notice) does not itself give away the presence of a magical illusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T06:54:28-08:00","id":1358613,"title":"","content":"Anything that offers a blanket protection/block against some aspect of the spell, such as the Arcanum or Practice used, Awakened magic, or any supernatural effects at all. Generally such blanket effects aren't that fun so they're pretty rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T06:59:03-08:00","id":1358615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358611#post1358611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are a few reasons that Pierce Deception could invoke a Clash of Wills other than attempting to pierce a magical deception or illusion? Need some possible alternative explanations for the Clash so that mere occurrence of the Clash (which the mage will always notice) does not itself give away the presence of a magical illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Clash of Wills only occurs when two concurrent supernatural powers try to influence a target, so no mundane explanation really.<br /> <br /> You could add Fate 1 &amp; Mind 2 to some other Arcana to trigger a false Clash of Wills in response to that Arcana's scrutiny, one that &quot;always fails&quot;. That seems fine for the players to use, but may be a red herring with too simple a payoff if used by an NPC.<br /> <br /> So perhaps a pact with a Demon, Changeling, True Fae or similar being could grant the target a variation of Cover and Spoofing. It could immediately conceal the illusion from Pierce Deception, but the players would have an avenue of investigation when the payment is due.<br /> <br /> That being said, if the players somehow get an exceptional success and they choose the &quot;bypass Withstand&quot; option, could it be interpreted as punching through the illusion without a Clash of Wills ? I am not sure. In general its extremely difficult to hide information a mage is looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-03-2020, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T10:10:15-08:00","id":1358640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358611#post1358611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are a few reasons that Pierce Deception could invoke a Clash of Wills other than attempting to pierce a magical deception or illusion? Need some possible alternative explanations for the Clash so that mere occurrence of the Clash (which the mage will always notice) does not itself give away the presence of a magical illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your best bet is to have enough instances of the illusion being trivial in some way that a failed CoW doesn't immediately make them think that something untoward is occuring; maybe it's just a Life veiling spell to hide the Mage's freckles, or they're hanging out in cat shape while they talk to you, or you're meeting in a bad part of town so your contact made their nice watch look like cheap junk to avoid any issues with Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T13:13:51-08:00","id":1358684,"title":"","content":"There is any issue to grant Key for not-space magic ?<br /> I refer to :<br /> &quot; Spells that can be Keyed are called out below, usually at the cost of a Reach. The Key may have a number of requirements equal to the spell\u2019s Potency&quot;<br /> Example, make an AoE spell with a +1 Reach for exclude or limitate the effect upon a requirement(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T13:49:25-08:00","id":1358690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358684#post1358684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is any issue to grant Key for not-space magic ?<br /> I refer to :<br /> &quot; Spells that can be Keyed are called out below, usually at the cost of a Reach. The Key may have a number of requirements equal to the spell\u2019s Potency&quot;<br /> Example, make an AoE spell with a +1 Reach for exclude or limitate the effect upon a requirement(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is normally the purview of Warding Gesture, so I consider that you require it for generic AoE spells. Otherwise adding conjunctional Fate 1 during casting should allow the spell to know when someone has a certain intention or if a mundane condition is true (by adding some functionality of Oaths Fulfilled into it and considering Fate's general purview), with an additional Reach permitting conditions only detectable by Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> But its possible conjunctional Space 2 could do it, but you would need to mix some other Arcanum at 1 or a generic yantra to even detect the condition, depending on its complexity. Everyone who is dressed in green passes ? Easy, no yantra required. Only descendants from X family may pass ? Sure, within the purview of Space, but you will probably need a representational yantra. Only members members of Y club can pass ? You probably will need one here as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-03-2020, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T14:43:22-08:00","id":1358704,"title":"","content":"Use a specific Yantra, maybe without bonus dice but only for this effect? Great idea Kaiser, nice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T15:01:05-08:00","id":1358710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358704#post1358704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use a specific Yantra, maybe without bonus dice but only for this effect? Great idea Kaiser, nice!</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, if its indirect representation such as their name or a drawing of the family crest. Then yep, no bonus.<br /> <br /> But if its a picture of them, piece of DNA, family tree, painting, heirloom or similar, then you get a +1 bonus.<br /> <br /> I believe that is it, but I recommend double checking the rules of Sympathy yantras for more details. So the option is there should they choose to go through some additional steps for extra dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T09:22:36-08:00","id":1358888,"title":"","content":"Hello, one of my players is a Forge Master and has managed to become disiciple of spirit so, for the sake of forging perfected materials the slow way (shadow realm &quot;passings&quot;) she is setting up shop and she intends to put a forge spirit in the aforementioned shop hoping to maybe get a little faster tempering times, get a measure of protection for the shop and have a &quot;little&quot; helper for the forging process. I wrote &quot;little&quot; since the idea would be to have a rank 3 Forge spirit in house.<br /> <br /> Which could be the actual benefits and drawbacks of this kind of set up? (My groups always disregarded the spirit world for more flashier Arcanas and solutions -maybe wisely sometimes-, so i never not delved a lot in spirits pacts, courts and the like)<br /> <br /> Some more precise questions in regard are:<br /> - While it would be a lot easier to go for less powerful spirits, wouldn't even a rank 3 spirit jump at the idea of becoming the spirit of an actual forge? Would it put particularly taxing conditions being it of Rank 3?<br /> - Would it actually be useful as a forging assistant? Could it do some of the tempering on his own in regard to perfect materials or create some normal objects on his own?<br /> - In time the Forge should become a Loci from where the spirit should be able to gather more and more essence, becoming more and more powerful. How much time/essence should it need to get a rank? I always found spirits evolution foggy :/<br /> - The spirit would be operating on this side of the Gauntlet or anyway across the Gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T11:07:33-08:00","id":1358904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358888#post1358888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, one of my players is a Forge Master and has managed to become disiciple of spirit so, for the sake of forging perfected materials the slow way (shadow realm &quot;passings&quot;) she is setting up shop and she intends to put a forge spirit in the aforementioned shop hoping to maybe get a little faster tempering times, get a measure of protection for the shop and have a &quot;little&quot; helper for the forging process. I wrote &quot;little&quot; since the idea would be to have a rank 3 Forge spirit in house.<br /> <br /> Which could be the actual benefits and drawbacks of this kind of set up? (My groups always disregarded the spirit world for more flashier Arcanas and solutions -maybe wisely sometimes-, so i never not delved a lot in spirits pacts, courts and the like)<br /> <br /> Some more precise questions in regard are:<br /> - While it would be a lot easier to go for less powerful spirits, wouldn't even a rank 3 spirit jump at the idea of becoming the spirit of an actual forge? Would it put particularly taxing conditions being it of Rank 3?<br /> - Would it actually be useful as a forging assistant? Could it do some of the tempering on his own in regard to perfect materials or create some normal objects on his own?<br /> - In time the Forge should become a Loci from where the spirit should be able to gather more and more essence, becoming more and more powerful. How much time/essence should it need to get a rank? I always found spirits evolution foggy :/<br /> - The spirit would be operating on this side of the Gauntlet or anyway across the Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember the influence table on p256, in order for spirits to create things they need influence 4 which means rank 4. 1-3 includes strengthen, manipulate &amp; control via influences, it could however use its sudo skill to make mundane things maybe. As long as you can feed the spirit then it'll have skills equiv to its nature. So a rank 3 &quot;Forge&quot; spirit should have a decent dicepool to help out. Where it helps out depends on if you can keep an open condition around for it to manifest or whatever.<br /> The spirit progression rules are non-existant atm, but i believe giest 2e has/will have playable ghosts so you may be able to borrow similar rules for how a spirit increases its ranks, otherwise you'll have to wing it.<br /> Id have to reread perfected materials again but it its just passing it back and forth through the gauntlet then i dont think the spirit can even help with this, unless it can hold the stuff and pass back and forth itself too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T13:13:34-08:00","id":1358921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358904#post1358904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Remember the influence table on p256, in order for spirits to create things they need influence 4 which means rank 4. 1-3 includes strengthen, manipulate &amp; control via influences, it could however use its sudo skill to make mundane things maybe. As long as you can feed the spirit then it'll have skills equiv to its nature. So a rank 3 &quot;Forge&quot; spirit should have a decent dicepool to help out. Where it helps out depends on if you can keep an open condition around for it to manifest or whatever.<br /> The spirit progression rules are non-existant atm, but i believe giest 2e has/will have playable ghosts so you may be able to borrow similar rules for how a spirit increases its ranks, otherwise you'll have to wing it.<br /> Id have to reread perfected materials again but it its just passing it back and forth through the gauntlet then i dont think the spirit can even help with this, unless it can hold the stuff and pass back and forth itself too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even better if the spirit cannot help with the passings, it feels more adequate if the player does it.<br /> If it has materialize it could actually work in the forge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T20:02:20-08:00","id":1358986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1358888#post1358888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, one of my players is a Forge Master and has managed to become disiciple of spirit so, for the sake of forging perfected materials the slow way (shadow realm &amp;quot;passings&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> she is setting up shop and she intends to put a forge spirit in the aforementioned shop hoping to maybe get a little faster tempering times, get a measure of protection for the shop and have a &amp;quot;little&amp;quot; helper for the forging process. I wrote &amp;quot;little&amp;quot; since the idea would be to have a rank 3 Forge spirit in house.<br /> <br /> Which could be the actual benefits and drawbacks of this kind of set up? (My groups always disregarded the spirit world for more flashier Arcanas and solutions -maybe wisely sometimes-, so i never not delved a lot in spirits pacts, courts and the like)<br /> <br /> Some more precise questions in regard are:<br /> - While it would be a lot easier to go for less powerful spirits, wouldn't even a rank 3 spirit jump at the idea of becoming the spirit of an actual forge? Would it put particularly taxing conditions being it of Rank 3?<br /> - Would it actually be useful as a forging assistant? Could it do some of the tempering on his own in regard to perfect materials or create some normal objects on his own?<br /> - In time the Forge should become a Loci from where the spirit should be able to gather more and more essence, becoming more and more powerful. How much time/essence should it need to get a rank? I always found spirits evolution foggy :/<br /> - The spirit would be operating on this side of the Gauntlet or anyway across the Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>One approach is to make the workshop convenient for it. Start by giving it the right Resonance, then ward it from any other spirit than it from entering and use a Shielding spell to prevent Essence bleed within it. Now make the items tangible in Twilight via Gossamer Touch so it can manipulate them. <br /> <br /> The workshop now is now a safe, reliable and exclusive source of Essence in the human side of the gauntlet, a very attractive thing indeed. Because spirits are brilliant at anything within their purview, a Rank 3 one will be skilled beyond peak human level. The downside is that higher Ranked spirits are likely to receive an Essence tithe from weaker ones, so additional negotiations might be needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T03:43:18-08:00","id":1359234,"title":"","content":"2 questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can you have multiple instances of the Familiar or Supernal Watcher Merits?<br /> 2. The Legacy +1 Yantras take a turn to use. Does that mean they have to take at least a turn like the High Speech Yantra? Or can they be used reflexively if they are the first to be used like other Yantras that take a turn to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T05:16:56-08:00","id":1359245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1359234#post1359234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can you have multiple instances of the Familiar or Supernal Watcher Merits?<br /> 2. The Legacy +1 Yantras take a turn to use. Does that mean they have to take at least a turn like the High Speech Yantra? Or can they be used reflexively if they are the first to be used like other Yantras that take a turn to use?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 -&gt; Yes, there's a merit called multiple familiars (or similar). It's in 1e, in summoners if I'm not mistaken.<br /> 2 -&gt; Unless specifically stated, any first yantra used is reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T07:34:13-08:00","id":1359285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1359234#post1359234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can you have multiple instances of the Familiar or Supernal Watcher Merits?<br /> 2. The Legacy +1 Yantras take a turn to use. Does that mean they have to take at least a turn like the High Speech Yantra? Or can they be used reflexively if they are the first to be used like other Yantras that take a turn to use?</div> </div> </div> </div>1- I don't see why not. If your mage wants to deal with more ephemeral entities, then its fine. The Familiar bond can be severed anytime, so its all about how interested the being is in obeying. <br /> <br /> Are you helping a ghost tie up some loose ends, figure out why they can't move on, finish their life's work, find their last descendants to give them something ? Is being around you saving a spirit from being hunted by the Seers (like a Magath whose domain undermines them), is it simply eating very well by hanging around with your character or are they your allies in some grander plan of Shadow politics? Is the goetia mentoring you in a skill ? Is it a part of someone that showed up in your soul and you are working to figure out why ? If the context makes sense, go for it.<br /> <br /> Supernal Watcher could represent entities that teach you a unique skillset. For example, one for supernatural smithing techniques and one for alchemy, or one for Abyssal exorcism and one for tracking Scelesti. The main problem is that they will watch, judge and possibly interfere, perhaps they could have contradictory goals. But its another way to flesh out your character's themes and create plot hooks, which sounds pretty good to me.<br /> <br /> 2- Same as always, first non-mantra use of a yantra is free, subsequent ones require an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-06-2020, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T08:02:27-08:00","id":1359288,"title":"","content":"How much of sanctum and sigil is relevant in 2nd ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T14:20:57-08:00","id":1359353,"title":"","content":"Most of it seems to be, with a lot of it is setting rules (how Mages deal with issues, or don't and just gank each other, territory, etc) that's easily used in second edition. The mechanics (mostly just example mages) need some touch ups but they're easy to convert, I used the Seer mansion in our second edition game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-06-2020, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T17:54:58-08:00","id":1361823,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for two different Aedes of two different paths to exist in the same location, like coterminous alternate realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T00:06:53-08:00","id":1361861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1361823#post1361823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for two different Aedes of two different paths to exist in the same location, like coterminous alternate realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any reason why that couldn't happen. Go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T06:45:36-08:00","id":1361894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1361823#post1361823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for two different Aedes of two different paths to exist in the same location, like coterminous alternate realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very. Happens all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T03:22:27-08:00","id":1363272,"title":"","content":"Could a spirit benefit of being brought into the Underworld, or other suitable denizens that have or have not the shadow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T09:38:45-08:00","id":1363306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1363272#post1363272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a spirit benefit of being brought into the Underworld, or other suitable denizens that have or have not the shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, sure, but it would be an unusual spirit. It would need a source of Essence, probably from eating ghosts or trading for it with ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T10:40:09-08:00","id":1363315,"title":"","content":"Could someone, Explain it Like I'm Five, the differences between a Verge, Emanation, and Aedes. I don't mean mechanically, but physically and metaphysically.<br /> <br /> As an old Ars Magica player they all sound like different ways to describe a Regio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T12:10:13-08:00","id":1363332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1363315#post1363315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone, Explain it Like I'm Five, the differences between a Verge, Emanation, and Aedes. I don't mean mechanically, but physically and metaphysically.<br /> <br /> As an old Ars Magica player they all sound like different ways to describe a Regio.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what i ve understand:<br /> -aedes, supernal world is near to material, mage can see it<br /> -verge, supernal and material touches, exchanges are possible<br /> -emanation, supernal subrealm, accessible through an iris, often found in verges","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T13:49:00-08:00","id":1363342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1363272#post1363272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a spirit benefit of being brought into the Underworld, or other suitable denizens that have or have not the shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have access to its full power without having to use Manifestations, which is a very powerful advantage. It would still need to feed on compatible Resonance it finds somewhere in there.<br /> <br /> The big issue is that without consuming other spirits, it would have a difficult time gaining Rank. So can it eat ghosts ? I think so, but it would probably become a magath, a twisted amalgam of human wills, regrets and obssesive spirit behavior. Which is your signal to break open some Junji Ito books. <br /> <br /> So basically, they would need to be kept under constant watch and resupplied by a Spirit mage or equivalent to be relatively &quot;stable&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-25-2020, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T17:29:29-08:00","id":1363373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1363306#post1363306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theoretically, sure, but it would be an unusual spirit. It would need a source of Essence, probably from eating ghosts or trading for it with ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1363342#post1363342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would have access to its full power without having to use Manifestations, which is very powerful advantage. It would still need to feed on compatible Resonance it finds somewhere in there.<br /> <br /> The big issue is that without consuming other spirits, it would have a difficult time gaining Rank. So can it eat ghosts ? I think so, but it would probably become a magath, a twisted amalgam of human wills, regrets and obssesive spirit behavior. Which is your signal to break open some Junji Ito books.<br /> <br /> So basically, they would need to be kept under constant watch and resupplied by a Spirit mage or equivalent to be relatively &quot;stable&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, the Magath possibility is something I did not think about, and is quite interesting.actually. But shouldn't it be specific for Spirit eating other spirits only?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T19:42:22-08:00","id":1363387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1363373#post1363373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, the Magath possibility is something I did not think about, and is quite interesting.actually. But shouldn't it be specific for Spirit eating other spirits only?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically yes, but the Realms Invisible are weird and unusual interactions are bound to happen. One Twilight could have doors to another, one Realm leading into the other. A door in the Underworld could lead to the Astral. Does that mean you can bodily enter the collective unconscious ? Yep, maybe even take things out to the material. How that works in that instance is a Mystery.<br /> <br /> So maybe the old pier throws all active beings from Death Twilight to the Shadow during the day and to the Death one during the night. The desperate ghost of the sea captain eats the ocean spirit in a gamble to avoid the Great Below and becomes a Magath of death at sea. Now its up to the confused mages/geists/werewolves to figure this situation out.<br /> <br /> Perhaps some medicine spirits found an aisle in their Shadow hospital that lead to the Underworld of bubonic plague victims, but couldn't find their way out. Running low on Essence, they devoured the ghosts that represented the affliction, becoming Magath of parasitic healing. Now you have all you need to make your own version of the Valley of Defilement from Demons' Souls. The bosses are the highest ranking spirits and everything else is a warped and devoted ghost. Perhaps you could even make the holy weapons into famous imbued items or Artifacts that setup another plot hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-26-2020, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T19:33:10-08:00","id":1364085,"title":"","content":"Does the Spirit 4 attainment \u201cHonorary Rank\u201d apply the mage\u2019s honorary rank to all ephemera or specifically to spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T20:36:19-08:00","id":1364093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1364085#post1364085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Spirit 4 attainment \u201cHonorary Rank\u201d apply the mage\u2019s honorary rank to all ephemera or specifically to spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T08:49:53-08:00","id":1364357,"title":"","content":"Are there any resources, 1e or 2e, that denote the commonality of sleepwalkers? Specifically those that are not a supernatural splat or possessing some other internal supernatural ability.<br /> <br /> Recently got into a discussion with some other STs about this and it seems pretty divided into thinking that people who are just sleepwalkers with nothing else going on are more rare than say vampires or werewolves, whereas on my side I would think sleepwalkers would be more common than any splat by sheer virtue that mortals are just so much more numerous and there is at least some evidence that mortals exposed to supernal(or abyssal) magic can experience a fitful slumber and become a sleepwalker","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T09:30:53-08:00","id":1364365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1364357#post1364357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any resources, 1e or 2e, that denote the commonality of sleepwalkers? Specifically those that are not a supernatural splat or possessing some other internal supernatural ability.<br /> <br /> Recently got into a discussion with some other STs about this and it seems pretty divided into thinking that people who are just sleepwalkers with nothing else going on are more rare than say vampires or werewolves, whereas on my side I would think sleepwalkers would be more common than any splat by sheer virtue that mortals are just so much more numerous and there is at least some evidence that mortals exposed to supernal(or abyssal) magic can experience a fitful slumber and become a sleepwalker</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like actual Mage populations, it's going to be a table consideration. The only thing that's &quot;known&quot; is that Sleepwalkers tend to be more numerous than Mages themselves since they make up the bulk of the Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T07:45:15-08:00","id":1365725,"title":"","content":"Is this thread open for any questions? The original post for this thread does not say what this thread is for.<br /> <br /> Scouring your pattern. Are there any long term consequences for repeatedly scouring your pattern for mana? For instance, maybe you scour your stamina or health day after day. Would there be any consequences for doing this in the long run?<br /> <br /> Can you learn or develop your own Mudras? I know that your order teaches you their mudras, their rote specialties. These bestow an additional die, above and beyond the skill used for the rote. However, the orders forbid teaching them to those outside their order. Despite this, I would like to be able to learn more mudras or even develop them. I think this would be especially important if you wanted to form your own order or something. Did I mention the extra die?<br /> <br /> Life 4 - Regeneration. Can I make this effect lasting? From what I understand, I could make the spell <s>permanent</s> indefinite (with 2 reaches and a point of mana), but that leaves it open to being dispelled or be detected with mage sight.<br /> <br /> Can you learn a praxis or rote for mage sight? I want to be able to use mage sight for common and inferior arcanum without spending mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 02-07-2020, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T10:00:59-08:00","id":1365755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365725#post1365725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you learn or develop your own Mudras? I know that your order teaches you their mudras, their rote specialties. These bestow an additional die, above and beyond the skill used for the rote. However, the orders forbid teaching them to those outside their order. Despite this, I would like to be able to learn more mudras or even develop them. I think this would be especially important if you wanted to form your own order or something. Did I mention the extra die?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mudra is the Yantra that you can use for Rotes. Each Rote has its own Mudra that is connected to a specific Skill. Anyone who learns a Rote will learn to use that Mudra.<br /> <br /> When in an Order you gain a +1 bonus on Mudras that use one of the Order Rote Skills. The reason each Order has those specific Rote Skills is because of how magic is taught within that Order. You can't just simply learn additional Order Rote Skills. It's not a huge loss since it's a +1 bonus that you might not even get if you've reached 5+ dots in the Skill already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365725#post1365725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 4 - Regeneration. Can I make this effect lasting? From what I understand, I could make the spell permanent (with 2 reaches and a point of mana), but that leaves it open to being dispelled or be detected with mage sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as written, no. If you want a similar effect that is Lasting, cast a Life 3 spell to impart a regenerative property on the subject, and wait for the limb to regrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365725#post1365725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you learn a praxis or rote for mage sight? I want to be able to use mage sight for common and inferior arcanum without spending mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Mage Sight isn't a spell (anymore; it used to be a collection of spells in first edition). But you can gain one additional Ruling Arcanum (which thus also makes Mage Sight with that Arcanum free) by joining a Legacy, and there are spells for mages to share their own Mage Sights with others, which can circumvent the cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T02:53:04-08:00","id":1365975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365725#post1365725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this thread open for any questions? The original post for this thread does not say what this thread is for.<br /> <br /> Scouring your pattern. Are there any long term consequences for repeatedly scouring your pattern for mana? For instance, maybe you scour your stamina or health day after day. Would there be any consequences for doing this in the long run?<br /> <br /> Can you learn or develop your own Mudras? I know that your order teaches you their mudras, their rote specialties. These bestow an additional die, above and beyond the skill used for the rote. However, the orders forbid teaching them to those outside their order. Despite this, I would like to be able to learn more mudras or even develop them. I think this would be especially important if you wanted to form your own order or something. Did I mention the extra die?<br /> <br /> Life 4 - Regeneration. Can I make this effect lasting? From what I understand, I could make the spell permanent (with 2 reaches and a point of mana), but that leaves it open to being dispelled or be detected with mage sight.<br /> <br /> Can you learn a praxis or rote for mage sight? I want to be able to use mage sight for common and inferior arcanum without spending mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can develop your own rotes with an arcana at 5 and then choose the rote skill for it. Thats effectively developing your own mudras. Try not to use the term permanent for indefinite and relinquished too, it looks like you already know they can be dispelled and/or eroded eventually but it still the wrong term and can confuse new people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T05:40:09-08:00","id":1365987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365725#post1365725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 4 - Regeneration. Can I make this effect lasting? From what I understand, I could make the spell permanent (with 2 reaches and a point of mana), but that leaves it open to being dispelled or be detected with mage sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of interest, you can alter your pattern (usually done with weaving) to give yourself the property of regeneration so that your body will naturally grow back that which it lost. It's slow and obviously won't work if you're trying to grow back the portion of your brain that allows for consciousness (emphasis on your), but in that respect it's superior to the actual Regeneration spell since its effects ARE lasting (obviously you'll drop the spell once you've regrown whatever it is that you need).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T15:15:55-08:00","id":1366127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365975#post1365975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try not to use the term permanent for indefinite and relinquished too, it looks like you already know they can be dispelled and/or eroded eventually but it still the wrong term and can confuse new people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry. I picked the wrong word then. I should have used Indefinite. Permanent has the same meaning in DND 3.5. I'll edit my post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T16:35:51-08:00","id":1366152,"title":"","content":"So this is a doozy and I'm surprised it has not come up before:<br /> <br /> The spell stacking rules state &quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When multiple spells affect the same aspect of a character the effects of the spells do not stack, and instead the spell with the highest Potency takes effect. </div> </div> </div>Now the question is if a character had a &quot;Honing the form spell&quot; with potency 3 giving +3 to strength on them and somebody else casts a &quot;Degrading the form&quot; also on strength spell with a potency of 2 to give -2 strength. (both spells have a week duration) Will the degrading spell be suppressed due to the spell stacking rules because both spells affect the same aspect of the character. IE Strength. The fact that one is a positive modifier and one is a negative modifier is not mentioned as mattering for the purpose of the spell stacking rule. So then the &quot;degrading&quot; spell is suppressed by the &quot;honing&quot; spell. Others seem to think this is a dumb idea and that the positive and negative modifiers are different or that they both work at the same time so you would end up with a +1 strength net. Is my reading of the spell stacking rules completely wrong or am I just a subject of gaslighting?<br /> <br /> The &quot;aspect of a character&quot; part also now has me wondering if the spell stacking rules do not apply to things that are not a character, ie items. Surely it would have been worded as &quot;aspect of something/anything/everything&quot; if it were to apply across the board to characters and items?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-07-2020, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T18:48:47-08:00","id":1366203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1366152#post1366152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is a doozy and I'm surprised it has not come up before:<br /> <br /> The spell stacking rules state &quot;<br /> <br /> Now the question is if a character had a &quot;Honing the form spell&quot; with potency 3 giving +3 to strength on them and somebody else casts a &quot;Degrading the form&quot; also on strength spell with a potency of 2 to give -2 strength. (both spells have a week duration) Will the degrading spell be suppressed due to the spell stacking rules because both spells affect the same aspect of the character. IE Strength. The fact that one is a positive modifier and one is a negative modifier is not mentioned as mattering for the purpose of the spell stacking rule. So then the &quot;degrading&quot; spell is suppressed by the &quot;honing&quot; spell. Others seem to think this is a dumb idea and that the positive and negative modifiers are different or that they both work at the same time so you would end up with a +1 strength net. Is my reading of the spell stacking rules completely wrong or am I just a subject of gaslighting?<br /> <br /> The &quot;aspect of a character&quot; part also now has me wondering if the spell stacking rules do not apply to things that are not a character, ie items. Surely it would have been worded as &quot;aspect of something/anything/everything&quot; if it were to apply across the board to characters and items?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say they're not the same effects, they're opposite effects. You combine them and then keep the difference. So in your example, a +3 mod added to a -2 mod would be +1 mod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T20:33:50-08:00","id":1366229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1366203#post1366203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say they're not the same effects, they're opposite effects. You combine them and then keep the difference. So in your example, a +3 mod added to a -2 mod would be +1 mod.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could be right and they are not the same effect but then you could also say that modifying an attribute up or down is the same effect, it is only the value that is different too (positive or negative its still a modification to an attribute after all) even if they are not the same effect they DO affect the same aspect of the character (Strength). Which is all the spell stacking rules require for them to function? Does stack for this purpose means only positive modifiers? Well no since two negative modifiers would also not stack? Does it then mean only the same type of modifiers? So you cant stack multiple positive modifiers but you can also have negative modifiers that cant stack together? And have two stacks, one for positive modifiers and one for negative modifiers? It doesn't seem to make that distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-07-2020, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T21:15:38-08:00","id":1366231,"title":"","content":"The only thing I have to work with is that one paragraph you quoted. And the last sentence for combined spells (I found it while doing a pdf search for &quot;spell stacking&quot;). The book does not mention spell stacking anywhere else (except when it tries to point you to where it is). So I don't think we're going to able to solve this problem by looking at the book.<br /> <br /> Core Rulebook, p. 119<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spell stacking still applies if the<br /> constituent spells affect the same thing. </div> </div> </div>I fear I may have muddied the waters by discovering that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 02-08-2020, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T23:05:58-08:00","id":1366247,"title":"","content":"Well, no answer to the long term effects of scouring your pattern for mana daily.<br /> <br /> A follow up for mage sight.<br /> <br /> Is there anyway of knowing what kind of mage sight you need to be using? I don't want to be flipping through a bunch of different mage sights, wasting mana in the process, in order to study whatever phenomena your peripheral mage sight alerts you to.<br /> <br /> Does peripheral mage sight have the same range as active mage sight? Could it detect something happening in a building on the other side of the street? Would the said building block my active mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T23:58:42-08:00","id":1366250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1366247#post1366247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no answer to the long term effects of scouring your pattern for mana daily.</div> </div> </div> </div>The long term effects of reducing your Health and/or Stamina every day for magical power are that your Health and/or Stamina is going to be lower every day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there anyway of knowing what kind of mage sight you need to be using? I don't want to be flipping through a bunch of different mage sights, wasting mana in the process, in order to study whatever phenomena your peripheral mage sight alerts you to. </div> </div> </div>Per Signs of Sorcery, Using Focused Mage Sight on a Mystery it doesn't apply to allows you to Reveal what Arcanum it falls under and (almost) nothing else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does peripheral mage sight have the same range as active mage sight? </div> </div> </div>If the area or point of origin of an effect is within reach of your senses (including recordings or magical channels of observation), it triggers your Periphery. If you can directly observe a phenomenon with your senses, Active Mage Sight can tell you relevant information about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T02:54:33-08:00","id":1366268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1366247#post1366247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no answer to the long term effects of scouring your pattern for mana daily.<br /> <br /> A follow up for mage sight.<br /> <br /> Is there any way of knowing what kind of mage sight you need to be using? I don't want to be flipping through a bunch of different mage sights, wasting mana in the process, in order to study whatever phenomena your peripheral mage sight alerts you to.<br /> <br /> Does peripheral mage sight have the same range as active mage sight? Could it detect something happening in a building on the other side of the street? Would the said building block my active mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no written mechanical long term effects of daily scouring, that doesn't mean you can't come up with them, it might even develop into an obsession?<br /> <br /> The example from SoS about PMS is a mage casting a spell behind a closed door. It only triggers your PMS if the spell's area of effect encompasses you otherwise its blocked by the door. If you couldn't see the spell's origin in that building or if it was a room area effect and you weren't in that room in the building then no your PMS would not get triggered by a spell you cant perceive in a building across the street, if they cast it at a window (you could see) or the area was a city block then your PMS would trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-08-2020, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T11:44:00-08:00","id":1366364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1366247#post1366247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no answer to the long term effects of scouring your pattern for mana daily.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a line in Signs of Sorcery that might imply mages get most of their mana from Scourging, so I doubt it.<br /> <br /> That said, I borrowed the idea of mages often doing some kind of self-mortification to accompany scouring from 1E and made it mandatory. That's been pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T22:58:08-08:00","id":1366488,"title":"","content":"I reread some of the rules again. I found something under creative thaumaturgy p. 127. It says that making a spell lasting costs 2 reach, but it says you should think carefully before allowing it. I can think of a few reasons why allowing it might be bad. The normal way of making spells last a long time is the make the spell indefinite, which costs 2 reach, 1 mana, and maybe even a point of willpower or a willpower dot. Also it might cost a dice penalty of up to -10 to make the duration indefinite. It would be quite the advantage if you could skip all that and simply make the spell lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T04:52:20-08:00","id":1366524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1366488#post1366488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reread some of the rules again. I found something under creative thaumaturgy p. 127. It says that making a spell lasting costs 2 reach, but it says you should think carefully before allowing it. I can think of a few reasons why allowing it might be bad. The normal way of making spells last a long time is the make the spell indefinite, which costs 2 reach, 1 mana, and maybe even a point of willpower or a willpower dot. Also it might cost a dice penalty of up to -10 to make the duration indefinite. It would be quite the advantage if you could skip all that and simply make the spell lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could otherwise just boil it down to two questions:<br /> &quot;Could this spell effect persist without supernatural upkeep?&quot; If no, then it couldn't be made lasting.<br /> &quot;Could this spell effect change anything other than Conditions and certain Merits on a character sheet?&quot; If yes, then it should be disallowed for the sake of balance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T08:30:37-08:00","id":1366557,"title":"","content":"Well, thanks for the help. I still have some questions, but I think I should finish reading the core rule book first, and then read Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:40:17-08:00","id":1367609,"title":"","content":"If I had a player who wants to have a pcs imaginary friend from childhood be an ally or familiar what would be the easiest way to go about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:09:39-08:00","id":1367622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1367609#post1367609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a player who wants to have a pcs imaginary friend from childhood be an ally or familiar what would be the easiest way to go about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make it a rank 1 Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T03:47:03-08:00","id":1368020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1365725#post1365725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this thread open for any questions? The original post for this thread does not say what this thread is for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can you learn or develop your own Mudras? I know that your order teaches you their mudras, their rote specialties. These bestow an additional die, above and beyond the skill used for the rote. However, the orders forbid teaching them to those outside their order. Despite this, I would like to be able to learn more mudras or even develop them. I think this would be especially important if you wanted to form your own order or something. Did I mention the extra die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading SoS and it seems its possible to alter rotes. P82 mentions being able to change the rote skill of a rote. Which sounds like its technically developing your own Mudra for the new skill. The downside is that unlike making your own rote you do not get the rote action effect. (but you werent getting that anyways before you change the skill involved.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-15-2020, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T22:31:47-08:00","id":1368463,"title":"","content":"I'm tempted to house rule that 'order rote skills' (or whatever those things on p. 82 are called) can be purchased for 1 experience point each. They're less valuable than skills (2 xp) so that only leaves 1 xp. Skills can be used be used as skills, and as mudras in spell casting rote spells. This rote skill is like a specialty only useful for spell casting.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much time or effort it would take to develop them yet. Maybe its fine to leave it blank.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 02-17-2020, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T23:09:56-08:00","id":1368467,"title":"","content":"I thought this was in a book somewhere already. You can only have three rote skills; if you change Order, they change when you get trained. Nameless Orders have to buy them instead of a Merit at the third dot of Status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T23:16:03-08:00","id":1368468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368463#post1368463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm tempted to house rule that 'order rote skills' (or whatever those things on p. 82 are called) can be purchased for 1 experience point each. They're less valuable than skills (2 xp) so that only leaves 1 xp. Skills can be used be used as skills, and as mudras in spell casting rote spells. This rote skill is like a specialty only useful for spell casting.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much time or effort it would take to develop them yet. Maybe its fine to leave it blank.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically how Left-Hand Path says apostates develop rote specialties \u2014 essentially buying them as three one-dot Merits \u2014 so yeah, straightforward enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368467#post1368467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought this was in a book somewhere already. You can only have three rote skills; if you change Order, they change when you get trained. Nameless Orders have to buy them instead of a Merit at the third dot of Status.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, sidebar on page 80 of 2e Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:12:14-08:00","id":1368472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368468#post1368468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, sidebar on page 80 of 2e Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't mention a cap of 3 rote skills though. It's not something that is explicitly mentioned I think (maybe in SoS), but p82 of core lists the 3 rote skills of each order and to qualify for the +1 order rote bonus to mudras you only ever have a 3 skill list to choose from which would depend on your current order. So while I didn't think rote skills were capped at 3 of the top of my head when going to see what would happen if you changed order it's pretty clear that your rote skills would have changed to the 3 from your new order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-17-2020, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:01:06-08:00","id":1368557,"title":"","content":"My thoughts were that these were freebies. I'm under the impression that you start the game with 6 dots of Arcanum, 1 Order status merit dot (so you can start play as a member of one of rhe named orders), High speech (if a member of an order), 3 free rotes, 1 free praxis per dot of Gnosis, and +1 to an attribute dot (determined by path). (Did I miss anything?)<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking that the 3 rote specialties should be freebies as well, if they weren't already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:05:18-08:00","id":1368558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368557#post1368557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Order status merit dot</div> </div> </div> </div>Which grants the Order Rote Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:54:38-08:00","id":1368577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368557#post1368557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm thinking that the 3 rote specialties should be freebies as well, if they weren't already.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orders are Sects that make up the majority of organized mages in the world and have been around for hundreds of years. Left-Hand Path puts the <i>combined</i> population of Nameless Order mages on par with a single mid-sized Ministry, and even in 2e proper the collection of non-Sect mages is &quot;a relative handful.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a difference in reach here, such that Mystery Cult Initiation (Nameless Order) gives you that freebie at your third dot in effective Status along with the benefits of the preceding two dots. The Pentacle and the Seers are whole-ass institutions in the magical world; they offer as basic training what many Nameless Orders accord to their higher echelons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-17-2020, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T12:08:35-08:00","id":1368607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368557#post1368557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts were that these were freebies. I'm under the impression that you start the game with 6 dots of Arcanum, 1 Order status merit dot (so you can start play as a member of one of rhe named orders), High speech (if a member of an order), 3 free rotes, 1 free praxis per dot of Gnosis, and +1 to an attribute dot (determined by path). (Did I miss anything?)<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking that the 3 rote specialties should be freebies as well, if they weren't already.</div> </div> </div> </div>The +1 attribute in 2ed can be applied only to stamina, resolve or composure and the choice is not influenced by the path","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T12:13:41-08:00","id":1368608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368607#post1368607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The +1 attribute in 2ed can be applied only to stamina, resolve or composure and the choice is not influenced by the path</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops. I must be thinking of 1E then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T18:13:46-08:00","id":1368830,"title":"","content":"I'm assume the answer is no, but I'm asking anyways. When creating an Imbued Item (p. 195), after you succeed in imbuing an item, can you keep making rolls until you get an exceptional success? The effect I'm looking for is relinquishing a magic item without having to spend a willpower dot.<br /> <br /> Do imbued items has any resistance to being dispelled or destroyed? Would it be safer to imbue an item with a spell as a persistent power, or would casting the spell with a long duration and relinquishing it be just as good?<br /> <br /> Am I reading this right? In order to increase Wisdom, you must use arcane xp? Wisdom is the Mage's version of the morality stat. Why would it be exclusively arcane xp? I would think it should be normal xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T19:01:35-08:00","id":1368837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368830#post1368830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assume the answer is no, but I'm asking anyways. When creating an Imbued Item (p. 195), after you succeed in imbuing an item, can you keep making rolls until you get an exceptional success? The effect I'm looking for is relinquishing a magic item without having to spend a willpower dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>An extended action allows a number of rolls equal to Attribute + Skill + Specialty (in this case it's actually Gnosis + Prime).<br /> <br /> Reaching the required number of successes on an Imbued Item renders the item complete.<br /> <br /> Nothing says you can't keep working on it after it's complete to try to &quot;perfect&quot; the relinquishment process provided you still have unused rolls, so I would allow the imbuer to continue rolling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do imbued items has any resistance to being dispelled or destroyed? </div> </div> </div>The imbuement process cannot be dispelled because it is an attainment, however a persistent spell can be dispelled (and the item can be reactivated using <i>Word of Command</i>).<br /> <br /> They have no special resistance to being destroyed intrinsic to the imbuement process, but I imagine most crafters take the time to enhance the item's durability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be safer to imbue an item with a spell as a persistent power, or would casting the spell with a long duration and relinquishing it be just as good? </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you're going for, but generally the persistent item is going to be better. If a persistent item's power runs out or is dispelled then all you need to do is cast <i>Word of Command</i> and pay a mana to reactivate it, no need to relinquish again; whereas an Indefinite duration spell being dispelled requires you to recast and re-relinquish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I reading this right? In order to increase Wisdom, you must use arcane xp? Wisdom is the Mage's version of the morality stat. Why would it be exclusively arcane xp? I would think it should be normal xp. </div> </div> </div>Increasing Wisdom is an Obsession, meaning it's a Mystery that must be contemplated and unraveled, hence the need for Arcane XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T20:55:49-08:00","id":1368851,"title":"","content":"Edit: I think this has stopped being simple questions. I think I should think about this some more and if I'm still not sure, I'll write up a new thread.<br /> <br /> I've been reading and rereading the imbue item rules. I'm not sure if I fully understand it. I feel like it would be times be better to cast a spell normally instead of imbuing an item. Please bear with me.<br /> <br /> So the dice pool for an imbued item is the caster's gnosis + the minimum arcanum required? So a spell caster (life 3, gnosis 3) who uses an imbued item with a life 1 effect would roll 4 dice? The total 4 = 1 (the dot requirement of the imbued spell) + 3 (the user's gnosis). Likewise, a sleeper using the same imbued item would roll only get to roll only 1 dice?<br /> <br /> Also, would the life spell would only have 1 free reach because the imbued item's arcanum was only 1 dot?<br /> <br /> Do you have to cast the spell fresh every time? Can I cast a really strong spell and use that every time? For example, Honing the Form (Life 3) allows me raise 1 physical attribute by potency dot. Lets say I wanted to make an item using a spell that had a potency of 6 and 2 reaches with the intent to make a spell that raised all 3 physical attributes by 2. Could I imbue an item like that, or would the person with the imbued item have settle for a much weaker effect?<br /> <br /> As for the mana cost, can I assume they mean that the mana cost is equal to the sum total of all arcanum needed? So if the imbued item had 3 spells, one a life 1 effect, one a life 3 effect, and one a prime 1 effect, the total mana required would be 4 (life 3 + prime 1)? And the total rolls needed on the extended action would thus be 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 02-19-2020, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T23:47:32-08:00","id":1368865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368851#post1368851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I think this has stopped being simple questions. I think I should think about this some more and if I'm still not sure, I'll write up a new thread.<br /> <br /> I've been reading and rereading the imbue item rules. I'm not sure if I fully understand it. I feel like it would be times be better to cast a spell normally instead of imbuing an item. Please bear with me.<br /> <br /> So the dice pool for an imbued item is the caster's gnosis + the minimum arcanum required? So a spell caster (life 3, gnosis 3) who uses an imbued item with a life 1 effect would roll 4 dice? The total 4 = 1 (the dot requirement of the imbued spell) + 3 (the user's gnosis). Likewise, a sleeper using the same imbued item would roll only get to roll only 1 dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct. Personally, I house rule that you can purchase the item at a higher effective dot rating for extra dice (and primary spell factor and safe reach).<br /> <br /> Also, the Prime 1 spell <i>Word of Command</i> lets you trigger the item using that spell, meaning you can max out spell factors (have 0 or 1 die to roll from the item) and then roll Gnosis + Prime + Yantras for the item.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, would the life spell would only have 1 free reach because the imbued item's arcanum was only 1 dot? </div> </div> </div>The item has free reach equal to what the item creator would have. Also, reach is fixed at creation, so if the creator overreached the item always risks paradox and releases it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have to cast the spell fresh every time? </div> </div> </div>Depends on if it's persistent or triggered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I cast a really strong spell and use that every time? For example, Honing the Form (Life 3) allows me raise 1 physical attribute by potency dot. Lets say I wanted to make an item using a spell that had a potency of 6 and 2 reaches with the intent to make a spell that raised all 3 physical attributes by 2. Could I imbue an item like that, or would the person with the imbued item have settle for a much weaker effect? </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that you could craft an imbued item with a persistent effect that would apply to whoever wore the item, so, yes, you could theoretically create a ring of<i> All Physical Attributes +2</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the mana cost, can I assume they mean that the mana cost is equal to the sum total of all arcanum needed? So if the imbued item had 3 spells, one a life 1 effect, one a life 3 effect, and one a prime 1 effect, the total mana required would be 4 (life 3 + prime 1)? And the total rolls needed on the extended action would thus be 8. </div> </div> </div>That is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T00:37:44-08:00","id":1368868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368851#post1368851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the mana cost, can I assume they mean that the mana cost is equal to the sum total of all arcanum needed? So if the imbued item had 3 spells, one a life 1 effect, one a life 3 effect, and one a prime 1 effect, the total mana required would be 4 (life 3 + prime 1)? And the total rolls needed on the extended action would thus be 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember and I don't know if it is spelled out in the core book but SoS makes it clear that only one spell in an imbued item can be contingent (ie triggered). SoS also tries to clear up imbued items, adds flexible reach which allows the user to reduce any reach used as without this option if an item has an advanced duration, it will always use advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Not sure how or if that one contingent spell can be a combined spell. It'd give me an aneurysm if I had to try to work it out I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368851#post1368851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have to cast the spell fresh every time? Can I cast a really strong spell and use that every time? For example, Honing the Form (Life 3) allows me raise 1 physical attribute by potency dot. Lets say I wanted to make an item using a spell that had a potency of 6 and 2 reaches with the intent to make a spell that raised all 3 physical attributes by 2. Could I imbue an item like that, or would the person with the imbued item have settle for a much weaker effect?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So either you have it contingent on a trigger and the user can cast the spell over and over on different targets each activation, altering the spell factors such as potency or duration each time but not (unless flexible) the reach for multiple stats (so you would always divide whatever potency by the 3 attributes) or you can have it as a persistent effect that will give the user/wearer/holder/whatever the spell's effect until it expires (these effects are usually made indefinite though good luck with the -10 spell factors which low initial dice pools)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-19-2020, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T07:58:36-08:00","id":1368927,"title":"","content":"Is there any source for game mechanics or examples for the below passage on what Reapers can do with souls found in the section on Reapers from the core rulebook?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <i>Souls are incredibly powerful. A mage can consume a soul to access any of the Subtle Arcana that relate to her victim. She may drink deep on the Fated good fortune of one victim, and the intelligence and wits of another unwilling donor\u2019s Mind. She can also use a victim\u2019s soul to bind his ghost to her power, gaining his ghost as a slave to her will. She can even drain his soul to extend her own lifespan...<br /> <br /> ...many Reapers develop Legacies based around using those souls with a different subtle Arcanum</i>.</div> <br /> I've been working on a Death-aligned Banisher faction for a chronicle and I'd like to add some Reapers to the mix too.<br /> <br /> I've got Dark Eras and know about the Nagaraja. That write-up, to my mind, does not reflect the above. A couple of Nagaraja Mind attainments make use of a jarred soul, but they follow the general rule for atypical legacy attainments (&quot;These adjustments shouldn\u2019t make Attainments significantly more or less powerful than they otherwise would be.&quot;). Hence no &quot;incredible power&quot; is gained beyond what any mage can obtain by joining a non-Reaper legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Is there anything that better explains what amazing, powerful things Reapers do with souls that justifies all the drawbacks of being a Reaper?</b><br /> <br /> My intuition is that there is not because Reapers are generally meant to be ST characters and STs are meant to have an uncluttered landscape for deciding these effects ourselves. I'd like to be sure though before I go hog wild.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:26:04-08:00","id":1368938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368927#post1368927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any source for game mechanics or examples for the below passage on what Reapers can do with souls found in the section on Reapers from the core rulebook?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <b>Is there anything that better explains what amazing, powerful things Reapers do with souls that justifies all the drawbacks of being a Reaper?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only official thing is the preview we have from Nameless and Accursed: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/nameless-accursed-tremere-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/nameless-accu...the-awakening/</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:42:04-08:00","id":1368942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1368927#post1368927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Is there anything that better explains what amazing, powerful things Reapers do with souls that justifies all the drawbacks of being a Reaper?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What drawbacks? If you're stealthy enough you can even stay in an Order.<br /> The Tremere does have drawbacks, but that's because they're mixing being Reapers with being Liches (and also having changed their template) and will be detailed in Nameless &amp; Accursed.<br /> <br /> As for what amazing, powerful things Reapers can do, go wild. We've got precious little information about what souls are good for other than as a Sacrament Yantra and a few spells in Signs of Sorcery. Hopefully Nameless &amp; Accursed will rectify that.<br /> For Reaper Legacies specifically, don't be afraid to bump up the power a bit. Legacy Attainments are pretty underwhelming most of the time anyway (unless they're atypical in a way that can't be replicated with the prerequisite Arcana ratings).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:44:33-08:00","id":1368954,"title":"","content":"I believe the key is to make sure Reapers consume souls as part of the Attainments, that way they are constantly on the hunt. Because souls are incredibly powerful, drawing upon them justifies some extra features. <br /> <br /> A very cool example is the 2ed conversion of Cloud Infinite by 21C Hermit. Although its Prime and Mind focused, so I am not sure if its what you are looking for. <br /> <br /> Carnival Melancholy is the next one that comes to mind, but their bonuses don't seem to be that powerful. <br /> <br /> Legion (the Guardian Masque caused affliction) can be very disturbing and make for great antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-19-2020, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T09:40:52-08:00","id":1369143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is correct. Personally, I house rule that you can purchase the item at a higher effective dot rating for extra dice (and primary spell factor and safe reach). </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> The alternative is to let imbued items be difficult to use. A simple imbued items (dot 1 spell) in the hands of a rookie mage (gnosis 1) is going to have a small dice pool. And thats before you try adding more reach and spell factors. Handing a rookie mage a powerful imbued item (let say a dot 5 spell) to give a larger dice pool is going to have its own problems.<br /> <br /> I still have a problem though. I see nothing in the rules that would make creating imbued items with powerful persistent effects more difficult. It seems that a ring of strength +1 (simple), a ring of all physical attributes +2 (moderate), a ring of all physical attributes +10 (clearly over-powered) all would have the have the same difficulty to make.<br /> <br /> I feel that I might have to homebrew my own magic item crafting rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T13:55:43-08:00","id":1369197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369143#post1369143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense.<br /> <br /> The alternative is to let imbued items be difficult to use. A simple imbued items (dot 1 spell) in the hands of a rookie mage (gnosis 1) is going to have a small dice pool. And thats before you try adding more reach and spell factors. Handing a rookie mage a powerful imbued item (let say a dot 5 spell) to give a larger dice pool is going to have its own problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Letting it be more difficult for rookie mages is the default.<br /> <br /> And to clarify: imbued items have fixed reach (unless designed in a specific way and still under the control of the creator), and whether they risk paradox from overreach is based on whether the creator of the item would have overreached (the actual paradox dice per overreach is determined by the user's Gnosis, however).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still have a problem though. I see nothing in the rules that would make creating imbued items with powerful persistent effects more difficult. It seems that a ring of strength +1 (simple), a ring of all physical attributes +2 (moderate), a ring of all physical attributes +10 (clearly over-powered) all would have the have the same difficulty to make. </div> </div> </div>While it's not 100% clear, <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> implies that persistent items still have to be initially activated via <i>Word of Command,</i> which means the activator (presumably the creator) would still have to have a base activation dicepool of 2x the number of spell factor increases to activate the item with those factors.<br /> <br /> This does mean that a <i>ring of strength +1</i> is going to be something the creator intentionally made below their actual capability, but there can be story reasons for that and it does make a <i>ring of all physical attributes +10</i> impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel that I might have to homebrew my own magic item crafting rules. </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend reading through <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> if you haven't already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:48:05-08:00","id":1369244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369197#post1369197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Letting it be more difficult for rookie mages is the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is. I was agreeing with your house rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369197#post1369197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's not 100% clear, <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> implies that persistent items still have to be initially activated via <i>Word of Command,</i> which means the activator (presumably the creator) would still have to have a base activation dicepool of 2x the number of spell factor increases to activate the item with those factors.<br /> <br /> This does mean that a <i>ring of strength +1</i> is going to be something the creator intentionally made below their actual capability, but there can be story reasons for that and it does make a <i>ring of all physical attributes +10</i> impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work? You mentioned it several times, I've read it several times. The spell, word of command, activates magic items, but it says nothing about spell factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369197#post1369197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd recommend reading through <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> if you haven't already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the middle of reading it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:53:40-08:00","id":1369247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369244#post1369244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that work? You mentioned it several times, I've read it several times. The spell, word of command, activates magic items, but it says nothing about spell factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you activate an imbued item you roll your Gnosis + its rating as a dice pool. If you want to increase the spell factors of the item, then you take the normal -2 penalty per factor from that dice pool. If you use <i>Word of Command</i> then you still determine the spell factors as normal, but <i>Word of Command</i> grants a number of successes equal to the potency of <i>Word of Command</i> on the activation roll of the item. This means you can reduce your Gnosis + item rating dice pool to zero or one for spell factors and then use <i>Word of Command</i> instead of rolling your chance die or single die.<br /> <br /> That's my interpretation of the rules interaction, at least.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T00:27:58-08:00","id":1369294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369143#post1369143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense.<br /> <br /> The alternative is to let imbued items be difficult to use. A simple imbued items (dot 1 spell) in the hands of a rookie mage (gnosis 1) is going to have a small dice pool. And thats before you try adding more reach and spell factors. Handing a rookie mage a powerful imbued item (let say a dot 5 spell) to give a larger dice pool is going to have its own problems.<br /> <br /> I still have a problem though. I see nothing in the rules that would make creating imbued items with powerful persistent effects more difficult. It seems that a ring of strength +1 (simple), a ring of all physical attributes +2 (moderate), a ring of all physical attributes +10 (clearly over-powered) all would have the have the same difficulty to make.<br /> <br /> I feel that I might have to homebrew my own magic item crafting rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I houseruled that when the creator starts imbuing an item with a persistent effect, he first forms the imago of the spell, fixing spell factors and reach.<br /> Considering that you cannot use yantras on an attainment and that if you reduce the dicepool to -5 or worse you cannot cast a spell the creator has a limit on how powerful the imbued persistent spell can be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:00:51-08:00","id":1369374,"title":"","content":"The Soul Grafting Spell in Signs of Sorcery is conjuctional Death and Prime patterning.<br /> <br /> One use of that spells deals not with soul stones, but with souls: taking another soul (like from a soul jar) and grafting onto the subject's soul.<br /> <br /> Why would that require conjunctional Prime?<br /> <br /> I'm working from memory atm and don't have the book onhand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 02-21-2020, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T09:20:43-08:00","id":1369394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369374#post1369374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Soul Grafting Spell in Signs of Sorcery is conjuctional Death and Prime patterning.<br /> <br /> One use of that spells deals not with soul stones, but with souls: taking another soul (like from a soul jar) and grafting onto the subject's soul.<br /> <br /> Why would that require conjunctional Prime?<br /> <br /> I'm working from memory atm and don't have the book onhand.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell uses soul stones and mage souls (specifically mage souls) to raise your effective Gnosis for most spellcasting purposes and explicitly can only be used on a target whose own soul is integrated with them already. Pretty much all its effects are specifically to do with Awakened magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T12:31:16-08:00","id":1369423,"title":"","content":"IIRC the spell internally has two &quot;versions.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first one grafts a soul stone onto a mage's soul. I buy Prime for that as a transformation from a yantra/nimbus-imprint Prime thing into a bit of extra soul to empower the subject.<br /> <br /> The second one only deals with souls. If I had to summarize that one in English it would be &quot;I transform <i>my</i> soul to incorporate <i>this other soul right here.&quot; </i>It's just dealing with souls -- and not poetic flavor-text maybe-souls, but definitely the sort of Souls included in the purview of Death. So why does that effect require Prime too?<br /> <br /> Shouldn't these be two different spells?<br /> <br /> I mean if the reason is that they determined that spell's arcana based on the game-mechanical effects it achieves rather than what phenomena it's acting on and what it does to them then okay. I'll feel like in that respect it's inconsistent with most other spells as well as the rules for spell building though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T12:37:29-08:00","id":1369424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369423#post1369423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the spell internally has two &quot;versions.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first one grafts a soul stone onto a mage's soul. I buy Prime for that as a transformation from a yantra/nimbus-imprint Prime thing into a bit of extra soul to empower the subject.<br /> <br /> The second one only deals with souls. If I had to summarize that one in English it would be &quot;I transform <i>my</i> soul to incorporate <i>this other soul right here.&quot; </i>It's just dealing with souls -- and not poetic flavor-text maybe-souls, but definitely the sort of Souls included in the purview of Death. So why does that effect require Prime too?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, again, <i>specifically the souls of other mages</i>, to the same effect as grafting a soul stone onto your soul except moreso. Integrating another mage's soul into yourself with Death has no special effects besides recovering lost Gnosis faster, but Soul Grafting <i>increases your magical abilities</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Soul Grafting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The caster grafts an unattached mage\u2019s soul or a soul stone\u2019s fragment onto the subject\u2019s own soul, which must be integrated with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-21-2020, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:00:46-08:00","id":1369427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369424#post1369424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrating another mage's soul into yourself with Death has no special effects besides recovering lost Gnosis faster, but Soul Grafting <i>increases your magical abilities</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is either of these close to what you're trying to convey?<br /> <br /> 1) The arcana are selected for this spell based on the mechanical benefits it provides rather than in-game phenomenon that the spell manipulates; the flavor text has little relation to the game mechanics.<br /> <br /> and/or<br /> <br /> 2) The spell is transforming something under the purview of Death (mage soul, soul stone) into something under the purview of Prime (an increase to magical abilities).<br /> <br /> If #2, do you suppose mages can do the same thing with another arcanum + Prime? Transform a spirit or a ghost or a big fire into an increase in someone's magical abilities? This obviously would be a different spell entirely from Soul Grafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:28:31-08:00","id":1369434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369427#post1369427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The spell is transforming something under the purview of Death (mage soul, soul stone) into something under the purview of Prime (an increase to magical abilities).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's using Patterning to rewrite the Gnosis potential/Gnosis retention of another mage's soul/soul stone into your own effective Gnosis in the same fashion as teleportation uses Patterning to &quot;rewrite&quot; a subject's physical location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If #2, do you suppose mages can do the same thing with another arcanum + Prime? Transform a spirit or a ghost or a big fire into an increase in someone's magical abilities? This obviously would be a different spell entirely from Soul Grafting. </div> </div> </div>Given that most things that aren't soul stones and mage souls don't have any direct impact on your Gnosis, probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:33:23-08:00","id":1369436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369427#post1369427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is either of these close to what you're trying to convey?<br /> <br /> 1) The arcana are selected for this spell based on the mechanical benefits it provides rather than in-game phenomenon that the spell manipulates; the flavor text has little relation to the game mechanics.<br /> <br /> and/or<br /> <br /> 2) The spell is transforming something under the purview of Death (mage soul, soul stone) into something under the purview of Prime (an increase to magical abilities).<br /> <br /> If #2, do you suppose mages can do the same thing with another arcanum + Prime? Transform a spirit or a ghost or a big fire into an increase in someone's magical abilities? This obviously would be a different spell entirely from Soul Grafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider this: Replacing your soul with the soul of another mage doesn't grant you any direct access to anything relating to them. It's for whatever reason not a natural effect of using someone else's soul. Grafting the soul to yours instead of replacing it has no reason to be more effective in that regard. But as stated in a handful of places in the books, use of other subtle Arcana can tap into the potential of a soul. Look at it as the mage using Prime to align the Awakened/Gnosis part of a soul or soul stone to their own soul. Without Prime that part simply lies untapped.<br /> Remember that souls specifically are part of all five subtle Arcana. Death is the most relevant but it doesn't cover the whole of the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:09:37-08:00","id":1369445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369247#post1369247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you activate an imbued item you roll your Gnosis + its rating as a dice pool. If you want to increase the spell factors of the item, then you take the normal -2 penalty per factor from that dice pool. If you use <i>Word of Command</i> then you still determine the spell factors as normal, but <i>Word of Command</i> grants a number of successes equal to the potency of <i>Word of Command</i> on the activation roll of the item. This means you can reduce your Gnosis + item rating dice pool to zero or one for spell factors and then use <i>Word of Command</i> instead of rolling your chance die or single die.<br /> <br /> That's my interpretation of the rules interaction, at least.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can go all the way to -5 dicepool when spellcasting remember and then use WoC to activate the item.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369247#post1369247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's not 100% clear, <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> implies that persistent items still have to be initially activated via <i>Word of Command,</i> which means the activator (presumably the creator) would still have to have a base activation dicepool of 2x the number of spell factor increases to activate the item with those factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not sure you can use WoC on the initial creation of a imbued item. You are using an attainment to create the item and WoC works on already created items. I think for persistant effects you have to succeed on the &quot;casting&quot; roll without help from WoC. This is where other things like fates 9 again becoming 1 die instead of a chance die can come in handy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T16:35:13-08:00","id":1369924,"title":"","content":"Here's a scenario: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mage enters their Oneiros (exact method shouldn't matter)</li> <li>Mage casts Augment Mind, spending all the Reach they want because the Oneiros is Paradox-free.</li> <li>Mage returns to their body.</li> </ol><br /> Are the Mage's mental/social attributes still boosted by the spell now that they're back in the physical world?<br /> <br /> I want to say yes because the spell affects the Mage's mind, which is consistent across the astral and the physical. Something like Honing the Form obviously wouldn't work because it'd affect the mage's body, which they don't have on-hand while astral. But I could see a counter-argument that no spells would carry over from the astral to the physical because they're stuck on the mage's astral form (and because game balance).<br /> <br /> If it does work, it means you could use your Oneiros as a poor-man's Demesne to load up on paradox-free spells, so long as the spells themselves aren't physical. In particular, I'm picturing a Proximus using this, since Proximi need all the Reach they can get...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T17:04:08-08:00","id":1369931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369924#post1369924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it does work, it means you could use your Oneiros as a poor-man's Demesne to load up on paradox-free spells, so long as the spells themselves aren't physical. In particular, I'm picturing a Proximus using this, since Proximi need all the Reach they can get...</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that the Oneiros is not casually accessible without a particular Merit and that Reach has negligible impact on the success or failure of a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T17:22:01-08:00","id":1369932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369931#post1369931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the Oneiros is not casually accessible without a particular Merit and that Reach has negligible impact on the success or failure of a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the use is marginal for Mages (especially since the active spells still count against spell control when you leave), but if you're a Proximus that wants to buff-up without spending <i>5 hours</i> per spell, have a limited amount of Mana, and even one measly Paradox success ruins the spell/gift, all that free Reach would be very convenient. And a Proximus with the Astral Adept merit raises fewer questions than one with their own Demesne (even if the later sounds like it's own story-hook, hmm...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T05:22:05-08:00","id":1370038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369932#post1369932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the use is marginal for Mages (especially since the active spells still count against spell control when you leave), but if you're a Proximus that wants to buff-up without spending <i>5 hours</i> per spell, have a limited amount of Mana, and even one measly Paradox success ruins the spell/gift, all that free Reach would be very convenient. And a Proximus with the Astral Adept merit raises fewer questions than one with their own Demesne (even if the later sounds like it's own story-hook, hmm...).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The new detective is certainly an odd one, but remarkably effective and overall very sociable. Sure, she can investigate new crimes fine enough, but her greatest talent is solving cold cases. <br /> <br /> When she is stuck, she makes all sorts of scribbles in her office's white board. Runes and rats, graphs and thought bubbles. It has a sort of sideways logic to it....like I almost....get it. Don't bother talking to her while she is like that, she has a look that is half way between the thousand yard stare of someone who has seen too much and a person on the verge of inspiration. <br /> <br /> She called it a type of meditation, a dive into the unconscious mind to help parse through information more effectively that the conscious mind normally could. She says its a traditional skill in her family, which they learn in their subconscious psychology study group (Cryptopoly/Labyrinth). She says I have a knack for it and that I can give it a shot if I want, I think I just might.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-24-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:12:46-08:00","id":1370159,"title":"","content":"If a Mage creates transfers a sympathetic link between himself and a random person with a spell, how would that show up with Correspondence. The spell says the caster understands the connections the same way the subject thinks about them, but if the subject isn\u2019t really aware of the mage then how would they show up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:51:24-08:00","id":1370168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370159#post1370159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Mage creates transfers a sympathetic link between himself and a random person with a spell, how would that show up with Correspondence. The spell says the caster understands the connections the same way the subject thinks about them, but if the subject isn\u2019t really aware of the mage then how would they show up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it makes more sense to describe the nature of their relationship (through the perspective of the subject) rather than the subject's conscious thoughts on their relationship. For example, if the subject is being stalked by someone without knowing it and you look at their connection to their stalker, then I'd describe it as an observer, because being observed is the only way the subject has directly been &quot;interacting&quot; with the stalker. (The stalker as a subject would instead show &quot;target of obsession&quot; since that's the nature of their relationship to their victim.) It also sidesteps the problem with subjects that are objects not having any descriptors on any of their sympathetic connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-24-2020, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:59:48-08:00","id":1370169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370168#post1370168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it makes more sense to describe the nature of their relationship (through the perspective of the subject) rather than the subject's conscious thoughts on their relationship. For example, if the subject is being stalked by someone without knowing it and you look at their connection to their stalker, then I'd describe it as an observer, because being observed is the only way the subject has directly been &amp;quot;interacting&amp;quot; with the stalker. (The stalker as a subject would instead show &amp;quot;target of obsession&amp;quot; since that's the nature of their relationship to their victim.) It also sidesteps the problem with subjects that are objects not having any descriptors on any of their sympathetic connections.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So how do you think you would describe the mage who created the connection out of nowhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T16:09:21-08:00","id":1370170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370169#post1370169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So how do you think you would describe the mage who created the connection out of nowhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blank. The connection is artificial and there is no relationship.<br /> The exception is if the mage created a connection between himself and the subject, since mages and their spell subjects automatically gain a connection and that becomes the &quot;flavour&quot; of the connection.<br /> <br /> If the connection is transfered or copied, then it still holds the &quot;flavour&quot; of the original two linked entities.<br /> <br /> If the connection is merely strengthened, then no change in &quot;flavour&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T16:26:47-08:00","id":1370175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370170#post1370170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blank. The connection is artificial and there is no relationship.<br /> The exception is if the mage created a connection between himself and the subject, since mages and their spell subjects automatically gain a connection and that becomes the &amp;quot;flavour&amp;quot; of the connection.<br /> <br /> If the connection is transfered or copied, then it still holds the &amp;quot;flavour&amp;quot; of the original two linked entities.<br /> <br /> If the connection is merely strengthened, then no change in &amp;quot;flavour&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my question is in the case where the mage uses Create Sympathy to make it, if a player used Correspondence on the subject what would they learn about the mage on the other end of the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T16:37:27-08:00","id":1370178,"title":"","content":"How would a persistent imbued item that gave somebody a condition work after the condition is resolved? (or one that gave a certain amount of uses I suppose, what happens after those uses have been expended, is it just a useless persistent item now)<br /> <br /> Paranoid mage wants to use the <i>Exceptional Luck</i> spell from fate to make a persistent imbued item that gives him the<i> charmed </i>condition. He was wise to be paranoid as later he gets hit by a sniper without his mage armor up and would otherwise have taken a deadly shot but charmed means he survives and the condition gets resolved what then happens with the item?<br /> <br /> I seem to recall from somewhere that spells that give conditions end when the condition resolves? (can't remember where). Does the persistent spell then end but can then be reactivated using <i>Word of Command</i> and the item gives a new <i>charmed</i> condition?<br /> <br /> Or does this spell continually reapply the <i>charmed</i> condition every time its resolved, if it does reapply a condition is it at the next gnosis interval (creators, users?) or as soon as its resolved?<br /> <br /> Obviously, if the item above constantly reapplies <i>charmed </i>then its a superb item, if one needs to use <i>words of command</i> to reactivate it then it's less superb but still good (giving it to somebody without <i>WoC</i> for example) and if once the condition is resolved and <i>WoC</i> doesn't work its still a good one-off effect but then it's probably better to make a continent item so you can reactivate the item after the condition has resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-24-2020, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T16:46:09-08:00","id":1370181,"title":"","content":"Spells only reapply their effects if the effect is instantaneous, in which case it happens every period of time equal to the mage's ritual interval. A Condition isn't instantaneous, and merely just disappears when resolved. You'd need to recast the spell in order to regain the Condition. Afaik, the spell doesn't end just because the Condition resolves. The only time a spell ends because of its own effect (rather than being cancelled, running out of duration, or outside interference), it's because the spell changes the subject so that it no longer becomes a valid subject for the spell.<br /> (Alternatively, just stack up a bunch of Charmed Conditions, only one is active at a time due to the spelll stacking rules, when it resolves the next becomes active, and hope your ST lets you get away with it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T16:48:11-08:00","id":1370182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370170#post1370170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blank. The connection is artificial and there is no relationship.<br /> The exception is if the mage created a connection between himself and the subject, since mages and their spell subjects automatically gain a connection and that becomes the &quot;flavour&quot; of the connection.<br /> <br /> If the connection is transfered or copied, then it still holds the &quot;flavour&quot; of the original two linked entities.<br /> <br /> If the connection is merely strengthened, then no change in &quot;flavour&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought mages have a medium connection with their spells but not the subject of those spells? You can't just cast a spell on something to then have a medium connection to that subject as that then completely nulls the point of the borrow threads spell? Having a connection to your spells is useful for things like if you relinquish them and need to sympathetically dispel them, or being able to scry on one of your spells (which yes will let you scry on the subject of the spell too but only by proxy)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess my question is in the case where the mage uses Create Sympathy to make it if a player used Correspondence on the subject what would they learn about the mage on the other end of the connection. </div> </div> </div>If they can tell by the link being blank then all they will know is that a master of space created that link. It doesn't have to be the thing at the other end that made it either though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-24-2020, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T17:15:20-08:00","id":1370185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370181#post1370181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells only reapply their effects if the effect is instantaneous, in which case it happens every period of time equal to the mage's ritual interval. A Condition isn't instantaneous, and merely just disappears when resolved. You'd need to recast the spell in order to regain the Condition. Afaik, the spell doesn't end just because the Condition resolves. The only time a spell ends because of its own effect (rather than being cancelled, running out of duration, or outside interference), it's because the spell changes the subject so that it no longer becomes a valid subject for the spell.<br /> (Alternatively, just stack up a bunch of Charmed Conditions, only one is active at a time due to the spelll stacking rules, when it resolves the next becomes active, and hope your ST lets you get away with it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells ending when conditions resolves is p126 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conditions created with magic only last as long as the Duration factor of the spell. If the target resolves the Condition before the Duration expires, <b>the spell ends early</b> and the target gains a Beat as normal. </div> </div> </div>I considered multiple of the same conditions but the text from the boon section says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> no character can have multiple instances of a Condition unless they apply to two different and specific things. </div> </div> </div>Is there any real difference from taking x damage every gnosis interval and gaining x condition (if not already having it) every gnosis interval though? Gaining the condition is instantaneous, the fact that condition lingers onwards may not matter?<br /> <br /> I think that some effects are just not suited as persistent items and that is fine, having a contingent version that lasts X time and being able to recast it again is better. I mean it is counter-intuitive to create a persistent effect for spells that you know will end, right? Sos says persistent items are active until the spell's duration ends, resolving conditions also ends the spells too, so I think WoC could be used to reactive the item when it stops being active from the spell's duration ending, that or once a persistent items duration ends it just stops being an imbued item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-24-2020, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:14:12-08:00","id":1370301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370182#post1370182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought mages have a medium connection with their spells but not the subject of those spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Medium connection to the spell. Weak connection to the spell subject and any Yantras used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370185#post1370185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells ending when conditions resolves is p126</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. It's just weird to me because that's not normally how spells work, nor does it take into account spells that have additional/multiple effects. E.g. a mage casts Exceptional Luck to get +4 to 4 rolls and the Charmed Condition, but resolves the Condition first and loses their bonus dice because the spell automatically ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370185#post1370185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered multiple of the same conditions but the text from the boon section says</div> </div> </div> </div>I was unclear. You can't have multiple Charmed from the same spell, but you can have multiple spells that grants Charmed. Due to spell stacking, only one of these spells will grant Charmed at a time, but once one is resolved (especially if the spell ends upon resolving) then the next spell in the stack becomes active and grants Charmed. Technically, at least. I would not be surprised if this practice is banned by most groups who think of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1370185#post1370185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any real difference from taking x damage every gnosis interval and gaining x condition (if not already having it) every gnosis interval though? Gaining the condition is instantaneous, the fact that condition lingers onwards may not matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's tied to Duration then it's by definition not an instantaneous effect (even though all spells takes effect instantaneously). The only time a Condition can be reapplied every ritual time interval is if it's Lasting, but the text on page 126 assumes that's not the case for Conditions created by spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:26:31-08:00","id":1370347,"title":"","content":"Every time I try to make an imbued item another question pops up.<br /> <br /> So I assume that when creating an imbued item the creator has access to any rote spells he knows and can use those for the free reaches in that item? creators/users (with flex reach) can only remove reaches after creation so it only matters during the creation process.<br /> <br /> For my example charmed item you'd need to find somebody with Exceptional Luck as a rote and Prime 4. Let's assume they have Gnosis 3 and Fate 3.<br /> <br /> To imbue the item they need mana equal to all the arcana used and a base of 4 successes on a Gnosis + Prime extended roll. Let us give the item a mana store of 5 (base 1 + 2 per extra success) too for a total of 6 successes needed.<br /> <br /> The spell the item casts will be Exceptional Luck with 1 reach for instant cast, 1 reach for advanced duration and 1 reach to swap the primary factor to duration so that when activated the item casts a instant, base potency 1 EL spell used to give the charmed condition to 1 target at touch range with a base duration of (spells arcana -1 OR creators arcana -1?) let us assume its the imbued spells arcana rating for base factors and then it will be 1 day.<br /> <br /> I do not think the creator has to succeed in casting the spell for it to imbue into the item, he just needs to succeed in the creation Gnosis + Prime extended roll.<br /> <br /> Then a user can activate the item casting the base spell on themselves with a dice pool of 2 (spells arcana) + Gnosis (possibly with a -2 to increase the duration to a week) then recast another copy taking -2 to increase its potency to 2 (can you add an additional boon to this spell? Does the spell even need to be locked to only giving the subject charmed each time? Probably not.)<br /> The potency 2 duration day spell will suppress the potency 1 duration week spell, but provide you with a second charmed when the first gets resolved.<br /> The item uses 1 mana per casting and only causes paradox from other factors since there was no overreach involved. If rotes cant be applied to imbued item creation then this item has 1 over reach and it'd be better to find somebody with fate 4+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-25-2020, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T03:32:04-08:00","id":1372123,"title":"","content":"A question concerning Dream Health: I might just have missed it, but is it possible to heal it, presumably using Mind versions of Life's healing spells?<br /> <br /> And on a related note, does it ever say what type of damage the Ecstatic Wind does? (If not, I'm half-tempted to put it at Bashing at Weak, Lethal at Medium, and Aggravated when Strong).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24057-malus-black","name":"Malus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T05:18:06-08:00","id":1372133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372123#post1372123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question concerning Dream Health: I might just have missed it, but is it possible to heal it, presumably using Mind versions of Life's healing spells?<br /> <br /> And on a related note, does it ever say what type of damage the Ecstatic Wind does? (If not, I'm half-tempted to put it at Bashing at Weak, Lethal at Medium, and Aggravated when Strong).</div> </div> </div> </div>BtP Player's Guide says it deals lethal to beasts, and all other splats mentioned in that book use a variation of the same rules (which does comply with the rules printed in Mage).<br /> The strength of the Ecstatic Wind doesn't change the type of damage for beasts. It shouldn't for mages either because it's already accounted for in how much damage they take and how often they take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T23:15:17-08:00","id":1372226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372123#post1372123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question concerning Dream Health: I might just have missed it, but is it possible to heal it, presumably using Mind versions of Life's healing spells?<br /> <br /> And on a related note, does it ever say what type of damage the Ecstatic Wind does? (If not, I'm half-tempted to put it at Bashing at Weak, Lethal at Medium, and Aggravated when Strong).</div> </div> </div> </div>if i remember it right core book says that you still use life to heal yourself in the astral form, probably in tge chapter about astral projection","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T03:37:50-08:00","id":1372242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372226#post1372226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if i remember it right core book says that you still use life to heal yourself in the astral form, probably in tge chapter about astral projection</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a function of the Astral running on a WYSIWYG principle. If you're in your Dream Form anywhere else it should be Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T01:23:24-08:00","id":1372399,"title":"","content":"Question. If my character gains the Abyssal Nimbus condition, after failing to fully contain a paradox, is there any way to resolve that condition (or otherwise get rid of it) without waiting for it to lapse (so I can scour it) or waiting for an abyssal entity to manifest? The other two sample paradox conditions have ways to resolve them by taking action. Is this one different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T06:16:24-08:00","id":1372441,"title":"","content":"The text says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resolution: An Abyssal Entity uses the Condition to Manifest, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. </div> </div> </div>The second option is to scour it from your pattern. So just do that?<br /> <br /> Scouring after letting a condition lapse is to remove the taint it leaves behind not to remove the condition itself (since it's gone having already lapsed), you don't have to wait for the condition to lapse to scour it. So take a point of lethal damage and gain no mana from it like normal scouring to remove the condition before it lapses. You won't gain the arcane beat though since you didn't wait and let it lapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-03-2020, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T06:28:29-08:00","id":1372445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372399#post1372399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. If my character gains the Abyssal Nimbus condition, after failing to fully contain a paradox, is there any way to resolve that condition (or otherwise get rid of it) without waiting for it to lapse (so I can scour it) or waiting for an abyssal entity to manifest? The other two sample paradox conditions have ways to resolve them by taking action. Is this one different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Release more Paradoxes in the hopes of summoning a Gulmoth or seek out Abyssal entities already in the world. It may be dependent upon an outside entity for resolution, but Gulmoth are by no means encouraged to be stingy with their Manifestations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T06:37:10-08:00","id":1372449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372441#post1372441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text says<br /> <br /> The second option is to scour it from your pattern. So just do that?<br /> <br /> Scouring after letting a condition lapse is to remove the taint it leaves behind not to remove the condition itself (since it's gone having already lapsed), you don't have to wait for the condition to lapse to scour it. So take a point of lethal damage and gain no mana from it like normal scouring to remove the condition before it lapses. You won't gain the arcane beat though since you didn't wait and let it lapse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, thanks mate, I was confused. Got it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:09:29-08:00","id":1372572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372445#post1372445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Release more Paradoxes in the hopes of summoning a Gulmoth or seek out Abyssal entities already in the world. It may be dependent upon an outside entity for resolution, but Gulmoth are by no means encouraged to be stingy with their Manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, sure, that's a solution, but i was primarily looking for ways to avoid abyssal intrusion. Thanks for the reply though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:53:59-08:00","id":1372585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372572#post1372572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, sure, that's a solution, but i was primarily looking for ways to avoid abyssal intrusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the solution to that is to not cause or contain Paradoxes or to take a different Condition. The ship has kind of sailed by that point.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Nimbus relies on an outside actor for its normal resolution, but it also affects more than just you in a way that is mildly predictable and at least partially under your control \u2014 anything you use magic on, as well as at least everything you have Strong sympathy to through your Shadow Name (and, more likely, Medium ones as well), is Resonant for any Abyssal entity until any Abyssal entity uses that fact to Manifest.<br /> <br /> The way of dealing with it without waiting for it to settle and then carving it out of you (and the wait is important for Paradox Conditions, because that Duration chart does not exist for no reason at all) is to seek out an encounter with the Abyss (and, theoretically, escape or remove that manifestation thereafter). That is the story beat that the Condition's normal Resolution represents: the marks of your magic are tainted with the Abyss in a general sense and will remain so until something more concrete uses it to gain a foothold in the Tapestry or you let it blend for magical insight.<br /> <br /> Barring an exceptionally successful Paradox roll, you stand a decent chance that whatever uses your Nimbus to Manifest is either down a bit of Essence for the effort or had to settle for making an Image that spooked a Sleeper well enough to trigger Quiescence. Abyssal Nimbus is the core Paradox Condition you take for an open-ended &quot;Something Abyssal is going to fuck with my life&quot; complication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T05:21:15-08:00","id":1372678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372585#post1372585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the solution to that is to not cause or contain Paradoxes or to take a different Condition. The ship has kind of sailed by that point..</div> </div> </div> </div>Checking earlier discussions about paradox conditions it seems people think the text is wrong and that you cant just scour the condition to remove it before it lapses. There were lots of references to the text contradicting itself etc.<br /> <br /> It says each paradox condition has 2 resolution mechanics. One being to accept the negative qualities and the other is to let it lapse.<br /> <br /> For Abyssal Nimbus this is:<br /> <br /> Resolution mechanic 1: Letting the condition lapse, you gain an arcane beat and become tainted, the only way to remove the taint (not condition) is to scour it out.<br /> Resolution mechanic 2: An abyssal entity uses the condition to manifest, scour the condition from your pattern, or do nothing and let it lapse.<br /> <br /> Note just because resolution mechanic 2 has multiple options doesn't nullify or make the 2 resolutions statement wrong. One just has multiple options.<br /> <br /> The text even says &quot;Removing a Paradox Condition in this manner <i>(Scouring) </i>deals a single point of lethal damage to the mage, but she does not gain Mana from the Scouring.&quot; Which does not seem like a mistake too when combined with the resolution text of abyssal nimbus'. It's saying if you are tainted the only option is to scour it but if you scour the taint or condition you don't gain the mana etc.<br /> <br /> Saying you cant scour the condition itself because that makes the duration table pointless is silly. You don't gain arcane beats by just scouring the condition that's all. So the table is more a &quot;how long do I need to wait and suffer to get my arcane beat&quot; table. Thinking an enlightened mage has to deal with an abyssal nimbus for an entire month and can only get rid of it by letting an entity use it to manifest or let it lapse is ludicrous. No, they can scour it out before it lapses as per its resolution text but won't gain the arcane beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-04-2020, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:15:02-08:00","id":1372713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372678#post1372678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking an enlightened mage has to deal with an abyssal nimbus for an entire month and can only get rid of it by letting an entity use it to manifest or let it lapse is ludicrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enlightened mages are comparatively rare looking at the requirements for raising Wisdom, and it feels unlikely that a Paradox Condition that, for most mages, lasts <i>a day</i> can be turned off early by taking <i>one point of lethal damage</i>.<br /> <br /> A Paradox Condition prevents magic from being used to overcome its limitations while its Duration lasts \u2014 it feels inauthentic to treat &quot;cut an effect historically equated with the wrath of the gods out of your existence&quot; as both not-magic and &quot;accepting the negative consequences of your actions.&quot; It also doesn't seem like the preferable solution to a particularly Wise mage afflicted with it \u2014 this is the part of the mechanics where This Wizard Has Magical Scars From Fucking Up With Magic lives, and self-mutilation feels more adjacent to the impulsive responses characterized to low-Wisdom mages, who happens to have a shorter timetable for how soon they can/have to do so to remove the taint.<br /> <br /> The text presents lapsing as a resolution criterion, then differentiates between lapsing and resolving, then lists lapsing as a separate resolution criterion from the thing that it earlier specifies is the only way to resolve a lapsed Condition. That's a contradiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:52:22-08:00","id":1372722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372585#post1372585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the solution to that is to not cause or contain Paradoxes or to take a different Condition. The ship has kind of sailed by that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way you phrase that, implies that I can choose which paradox condition I get. Is that the case?<br /> <br /> My main problem is what I can do to avoid affecting others with my magic/paradox. The other conditions seem both easier to resolve and more harmless from a moral standpoint since they only hurt or hinder the mage who has them as long as said mage takes proper precaution until the condition resolves. Abyssal Nimbus is something beyond your control. So, having the option to just scour it is great if this is how it works. Not getting an Arcane Beat seems like a small price .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T09:27:04-08:00","id":1372726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372722#post1372722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way you phrase that, implies that I can choose which paradox condition I get. Is that the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Communicating to your Storyteller, out of character, that you are not interested in the story beat that Abyssal Nimbus represents is how you avoid dealing with a Paradox Condition you don't want to deal with. There's two others in the core and the list is explicitly not exhaustive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main problem is what I can do to avoid affecting others with my magic/paradox. </div> </div> </div>Let it lapse and then Scour it. This, at least, is unambiguously a valid means of clearing any Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other conditions seem both easier to resolve and more harmless from a moral standpoint since they only hurt or hinder the mage who has them as long as said mage takes proper precaution until the condition resolves. </div> </div> </div>The other core Paradox Conditions are &quot;Until you successfully cast a spell that doesn't risk Paradox, any spell you cast that doesn't spend extra Reach on nothing automatically fails and adds your entire spellcasting pool to the resulting Paradox roll&quot; and &quot;Until you fully contain a Paradox, your next spell that risks Paradox risks more Paradox.&quot;<br /> <br /> Part of the metaphysics of Mage is that pretty much nothing exists in isolation \u2014 magical self-mutilation is an Act of Hubris, and your Nimbus spreads across your sympathies because to a certain degree your connections are part of you. The &quot;harmless from a moral standpoint&quot; route is to be careful with your magic and know how to handle things when you screw up, but the game is not built under the assumption that you can avoid problems altogether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not getting an Arcane Beat seems like a small price . </div> </div> </div>This is exactly why I don't believe Scouring before lapsing is the way the system is supposed to work \u2014 specific costs notwithstanding, Arcane Beats are <i>less</i> useful than regular Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:06:19-08:00","id":1372734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372726#post1372726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let it lapse and then Scour it. This, at least, is unambiguously a valid means of clearing any Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> This is exactly why I don't believe Scouring before lapsing is the way the system is supposed to work \u2014 specific costs notwithstanding, Arcane Beats are <i>less</i> useful than regular Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Letting it lapse resolves the condition. You don't scour a condition if you let it lapse, you scour the taint that is left behind by it lapsing and tainting your magic. You keep the taint until your scour it as at this point the only way to remove it is by scouring which could be long after the condition has gone. Before this point, while you still have the condition, you can resolve the condition by either of its resolution options, one of which just happens to also be scouring the condition itself.<br /> <br /> The fact the resolution requirements for the three abyssal conditions have<i> &quot;the mage scours the condition from her pattern&quot;</i> (not taint) as one of the options makes the prior text <i>&quot;At this point, the only way for the mage to remove the taint from her Pattern is to Scour it out, similar to Pattern Scouring for Mana as described on <span style=\"color:#004E6D\">p. 87</span>. <b>Removing a Paradox Condition</b> in this manner deals a single point of lethal damage to the mage, but she does not gain Mana from the Scouring.&quot; </i>make sense. Surely it would say &quot;removing the taint in this matter deals...&quot; if it only meant you can scout taint or do you really believe its a mistake even when the resolution texts mention it also?. The resolution text for each condition specifically says you can scour the condition (not taint) it's just a bit odd to me that the previous text mentions what happens when you scour a condition before it shows up as an option in the resolution text.<br /> <br /> The way its worded may also mean that removing taint via scouring does give you mana since it only declares that removing a paradox condition doesn't gain the mage mana. If both scourings didn't give mana then surely it would say something like &quot;scouring both the taint or condition is similar to pattern scouring blah blah does not gain mana?<br /> <br /> Thinking Arcane beats are less useful, that 1 resistant lethal is a small price or that enlightened mages are rare is fine but as RAW it's perfectly fine to scour both conditions and taint (gaining an arcane beat when the condition lapses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-04-2020, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:45:46-08:00","id":1372751,"title":"","content":"Couple of related questions that came up:<br /> <br /> 1. If a single spell with multiple subjects is the target of another spell, do those effects just effect the one subject?<br /> <br /> 2. If you were trying to hide spells that were cast on you, could you make yourself the subject of Supernal Veil and hide them, or would you have to cast it on the individual spells that you were the subject of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T12:48:48-08:00","id":1372788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372751#post1372751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If a single spell with multiple subjects is the target of another spell, do those effects just effect the one subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>All subjects are subject to the same spell. Any changes to that spell affects all subjects. (That said, the spell could theoretically change in ways that only affects some of the subjects, depending on how much you allow spells to change other spells.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372751#post1372751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If you were trying to hide spells that were cast on you, could you make yourself the subject of Supernal Veil and hide them, or would you have to cast it on the individual spells that you were the subject of?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's the latter, but I see no problem with Supernal Veil also covering other supernatural effects on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T13:00:34-08:00","id":1372790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1372751#post1372751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of related questions that came up:<br /> <br /> 1. If a single spell with multiple subjects is the target of another spell, do those effects just effect the one subject?<br /> <br /> 2. If you were trying to hide spells that were cast on you, could you make yourself the subject of Supernal Veil and hide them, or would you have to cast it on the individual spells that you were the subject of?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) If you cast a spell with multiple subjects, then that's one spell but those subjects can then part ways if somebody then later dispelled that spell it would only dispel it on that subject and not the other subjects. If the caster chooses to lower that spells potency then all the subjects have the potency lowered and obviously if he ends the spell then all subjects lose the spells effect too.<br /> <br /> 2) Since SV says its subjects can include spells, then you'd need to add multiple targets to veil multiple spells. Casting SV with oneself as the subject would only hide yourself from detection. Though you could use multiple targets and include yourself plus 4 spells for example or yourself plus 2 spells plus your vampire friend as long as you take the spell factor penalties to cover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T21:13:24-07:00","id":1373838,"title":"","content":"What are Ways, exactly? Like I understand if a Moros is an alchemist, he focuses on Matter, Death if a Necromancer. But is that all there is to it? Is there also supernal significance, symbolism, and philosophy that goes along with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T21:37:58-07:00","id":1373839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1373838#post1373838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Ways, exactly? Like I understand if a Moros is an alchemist, he focuses on Matter, Death if a Necromancer. But is that all there is to it? Is there also supernal significance, symbolism, and philosophy that goes along with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The nicknames for Paths aren't consistently or even mostly divided by favored Ruling Arcana \u2014 the names for the Obrimos are roughly split between mystical and religious focuses, Mastigos epithets are likewise iconoclastic and exploratory, and what the Acanthus are called is pretty directly down to whether or not you mind their meddling. Moros of every stripe are Alchemists, but &quot;Necromancer&quot; is what they call the ones who <i>focus on</i> the dead; likewise, most Thyrsus are implicitly &quot;Shamans,&quot; to the average other mage, but an Ecstatic has gone beyond simply walking between worlds and become that little bit more of a weirdo cryptid-person at the boundary.<br /> <br /> Which Path nickname your character leans toward will probably affect their Shadow Name, their Nimbus, and their reputation, but that's a high-level narrative framing thing more than a concrete in-universe structural element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T02:21:05-07:00","id":1373869,"title":"","content":"Do Legacy Attainments count as spells towards Spell Control rules?<br /> <br /> Also, how does Mana Break work towards mana storing spells such as Platonic Form or Mana Battery? It looks like infinite mana being generated ridiculously fast, which sounds stupid to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T02:42:03-07:00","id":1373870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1373869#post1373869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Legacy Attainments count as spells towards Spell Control rules?<br /> <br /> Also, how does Mana Break work towards mana storing spells such as Platonic Form or Mana Battery? It looks like infinite mana being generated ridiculously fast, which sounds stupid to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since they aren't spells they don't count towards spell control.<br /> Platonic form costs 1 mana to cast plus whatever mana you put into its mana capacity. I would say filling this capacity is not part of the cost of the spell and the reach just allows the mage to fill it at the time of casting bypassing the need to use channel mana later.<br /> <br /> But then ridiculous mana generation from a mage isn't anything that OP compared to other things they can do. The reach does say &quot;by spending mana as part of the casting&quot; which would mean gaining mana from nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-10-2020, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T14:39:43-07:00","id":1374808,"title":"","content":"Can a clash of will receive more dices from other sources than willpower and spell duration?<br /> I'd say no from the description, since it takes into account only this two possibilites...<br /> <br /> Edit: And advanced potency too ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","user":"Khalendas","date":". 03-14-2020, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T01:43:12-07:00","id":1374890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1374808#post1374808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a clash of will receive more dices from other sources than willpower and spell duration?<br /> I'd say no from the description, since it takes into account only this two possibilites...<br /> <br /> Edit: And advanced potency too ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those 3 seem to be the only things that increase Clashes for mages yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T04:01:36-07:00","id":1374900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1374890#post1374890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those 3 seem to be the only things that increase Clashes for mages yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thought so, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T01:41:27-07:00","id":1375037,"title":"","content":"If a Tremere exhausts your soul all the way over time and returns it, you get soul shocked and lose a perm wp, but it solves your soullessness problem.<br /> <br /> If for whatever reason you get your soul back before it has exhausted your soul, what sort of penalties accrue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T03:52:33-07:00","id":1375054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375037#post1375037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Tremere exhausts your soul all the way over time and returns it, you get soul shocked and lose a perm wp, but it solves your soullessness problem.<br /> <br /> If for whatever reason you get your soul back before it has exhausted your soul, what sort of penalties accrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be wrong, but I believe if a soul is truly exhausted all the way it's destroyed, the soul shock and loss of a dot of WP are the results of having a soul that has been only partially devoured (Though probably almost all the way) put back in you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T04:35:23-07:00","id":1375060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375054#post1375054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be wrong, but I believe if a soul is truly exhausted all the way it's destroyed, the soul shock and loss of a dot of WP are the results of having a soul that has been only partially devoured (Though probably almost all the way) put back in you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deinos is right. An exhausted soul is only destroyed if it's released, and a transferred exhausted soul does impose those penalties. (See Devours the Years, page 133.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375037#post1375037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Tremere exhausts your soul all the way over time and returns it, you get soul shocked and lose a perm wp, but it solves your soullessness problem.<br /> <br /> If for whatever reason you get your soul back before it has exhausted your soul, what sort of penalties accrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really divide either Soul Shocked or losing a WP dot into a lesser penalty so just remove the worst penalty. I.e. the person who gets the partially exhausted soul should only get Soul Shocked. That is, if you want to house rule a penalty at all.<br /> Getting a fully exhausted soul back is remarkably lenient. No change in recovery times from Soul Loss, and no damage to either Integrity/Wisdom or Gnosis beyond what you temporarily got from soullessness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-16-2020, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T11:18:35-07:00","id":1375118,"title":"","content":"Can a Tremere refresh a soul by putting it back in their owner?<br /> <br /> I ask because reading that, the idea of a &quot;pantry&quot; of people kept by a lich that they put souls back in after they run dry, let them sleep it off, and then take their souls back in the name of limiting how many people they need to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T11:38:13-07:00","id":1375127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375118#post1375118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Tremere refresh a soul by putting it back in their owner?<br /> <br /> I ask because reading that, the idea of a &quot;pantry&quot; of people kept by a lich that they put souls back in after they run dry, let them sleep it off, and then take their souls back in the name of limiting how many people they need to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no mention of it, so technically no? But since there's also no mention of any kind of book keeping for exhausted souls and no permanent side effects for having an exhausted soul (and zero mentioned side effects for a partially exhausted soul), possibly yes?<br /> <br /> If souls &quot;recharge&quot; over time, I'd have it so they do so very slowly so it's not possible for a Tremere to have two souls and a dedicated pantry person, and use that to be able to sustain themselves indefinitely by just cycling the soul over and over. If you do it before the soul is fully exhausted, the pantry person wouldn't technically sustain any harm other than what you house rule (see my post directly above).<br /> <br /> I really wish switching out a person's soul would have any mentioned side effects at all. Anything to base more severe consequences for if continuing to switch out the soul over and over and over. Right now it's completely plug'n'play with zero problems, and I doubt that's intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T12:18:50-07:00","id":1375134,"title":"","content":"Good stuff, thank you.<br /> <br /> I expect that your typical Tremere feeds on those who are gonna die anyway, either through their actions or, if they're a real bleeding heart, through a cataclysm they have foreseen, being at death's door, etc. so that there is nothing to trace them to their work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T04:14:35-07:00","id":1375411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375118#post1375118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Tremere refresh a soul by putting it back in their owner?<br /> <br /> I ask because reading that, the idea of a &quot;pantry&quot; of people kept by a lich that they put souls back in after they run dry, let them sleep it off, and then take their souls back in the name of limiting how many people they need to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually possible, I think. Page 133, under the Devour the Years ability says: &quot;A soul that no longer provides sustenance is destroyed if the Tremere expels it into a free-floating state. If integrated into an individual in need of a personal soul, the new owner suffers the Soul Shocked Condition and loses one <i>dot</i> of Willpower.&quot; So the answer seems to be yes, but they have to recover from soul shock, and also (over time at least) willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T10:53:06-07:00","id":1375982,"title":"","content":"With Signs of Sorcery and Nameless and Accursed out now, do we have any rules beyond the tiny amount in the core about how Morpheans, Spirit-transformed mages, or Ghost Liches work?<br /> <br /> I have both books, and don't see anything about any of these topics in them, but I want to make sure I'm not missing anything here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T13:47:03-07:00","id":1376005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375982#post1375982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Signs of Sorcery and Nameless and Accursed out now, do we have any rules beyond the tiny amount in the core about how Morpheans, Spirit-transformed mages, or Ghost Liches work?<br /> <br /> I have both books, and don't see anything about any of these topics in them, but I want to make sure I'm not missing anything here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral liches (and, I think, all fleshy liches except the Tremere) were omitted from NaA. We <i>might</i> get them in Fallen Worlds, if that book is still planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T16:55:30-07:00","id":1376029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1375118#post1375118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Tremere refresh a soul by putting it back in their owner?<br /> <br /> I ask because reading that, the idea of a &quot;pantry&quot; of people kept by a lich that they put souls back in after they run dry, let them sleep it off, and then take their souls back in the name of limiting how many people they need to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on the answers of others.<br /> I think it would also go against the theme and beliefs of the Tremere of feeding the Seventh Watchtower. They want to devour souls using their Hollow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T02:06:53-07:00","id":1376493,"title":"","content":"Question: how can someone enter the shadow? Can someone just walk through a locus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:31:03-07:00","id":1376509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1376493#post1376493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: how can someone enter the shadow? Can someone just walk through a locus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a Verge or supernatural &quot;assistance&quot; it would require having some sort of ability to cross the Gauntlet. A Locus is just a place where the Gauntlet is so thin it becomes a lot easier to get through the Gauntlet there (on top of a few other effects) but without the ability to pass the Gauntlet it doesn't matter how thin the Gauntlet is.<br /> A Verge is where the Gauntlet has a hole in it. Those you could just walk through. Depending on the nature of the Verge it might be a little more complex than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T07:56:25-07:00","id":1376554,"title":"","content":"Can Nasnasi become Rapt? Or are Qliphoth meant to replace that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T09:03:04-07:00","id":1376563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1376554#post1376554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Nasnasi become Rapt? Or are Qliphoth meant to replace that?</div> </div> </div> </div>To become Rapt you need Wisdom, and Nasnasi don't have Wisdom. On the other hand, becoming a Nasnas is a very quick way to become Rapt because if a Nasnas regains Wisdom (by losing their Joining) they end up at Wisdom 1 and from there you're only one Act of Hubris away, but then you stop being a Nasnas in the process of becoming Rapt.<br /> And yes, Qliphoth is supposed to be the equivalent. Except it happens at Joining 10 instead of Wisdom 0, because Joining is kinda the inverse of Wisdom in some regards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-25-2020, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T09:47:26-07:00","id":1376569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1376493#post1376493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: how can someone enter the shadow? Can someone just walk through a locus?</div> </div> </div> </div>People who aren't werewolves are mostly going to be reliant upon spirits using Shadow Gate; a locus is just a place where passage between worlds is particularly easy.<br /> <br /> Most other methods are spells or Mysteries in themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T02:48:55-07:00","id":1376795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1376509#post1376509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without a Verge or supernatural &quot;assistance&quot; it would require having some sort of ability to cross the Gauntlet. A Locus is just a place where the Gauntlet is so thin it becomes a lot easier to get through the Gauntlet there (on top of a few other effects) but without the ability to pass the Gauntlet it doesn't matter how thin the Gauntlet is.<br /> A Verge is where the Gauntlet has a hole in it. Those you could just walk through. Depending on the nature of the Verge it might be a little more complex than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Thanks. Reliable as always Tessie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1376569#post1376569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who aren't werewolves are mostly going to be reliant upon spirits using Shadow Gate; a locus is just a place where passage between worlds is particularly easy.<br /> <br /> Most other methods are spells or Mysteries in themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's exactly why I asked. We have a werewolf in the party, and we were wondering if we could assist him in the Sacred Hunt. Seems we need to find another way to cross into the Shadow. Maybe he can make a deal with a spirit. Thanks for the reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 03-27-2020, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T09:14:52-07:00","id":1376814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1376554#post1376554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Nasnasi become Rapt? Or are Qliphoth meant to replace that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T03:30:51-07:00","id":1377144,"title":"","content":"Question: Would an item (like a ring) that would affect its wearer with a spell passively (like nightvision) be an enhanced or an imbued item?<br /> Also is anyone aware of any previous post or an external source that explains the process of imbuing an item a bit more than the core 2e book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T06:03:15-07:00","id":1377162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377144#post1377144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Would an item (like a ring) that would affect its wearer with a spell passively (like nightvision) be an enhanced or an imbued item?<br /> Also is anyone aware of any previous post or an external source that explains the process of imbuing an item a bit more than the core 2e book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's possible to create such items except through homebrew.<br /> Enhanced items have spells cast upon the item itself. You could have the spell be AoE, but then the spell would constantly be active on the ring as well as anyone (or anything) close enough to the ring regardless of whether the ring is worn or not. There's a Fate spell for exempting subjects from an AoE spell, but that would increase the dot rating and might be detrimental for other spells you might want to use this way. For example, a ring of invisibility would always be visible even when you wear it.<br /> An imbued item is much closer if you set the trigger to wearing the ring, but then you still need to cast the imbued item's spell and you can just as well cast it on anyone within range. The spell also wouldn't end when you take off the ring.<br /> Since an Artefact is way too rad for a single passive buff spell, I think the best way to handle it is either through a custom Fate and/or Prime spell, or using a homebrew Yantra type that only activates during certain conditions and on certain subjects (very much like the Basilisk Yantra in Signs of Sorcery).<br /> <br /> Imbued items are re-explained and expanded upon in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T07:05:41-07:00","id":1377170,"title":"","content":"Is Spiral the Primal Avatar from <i>Nameless and Accursed</i> the first explicitly cross-splat NPC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T07:06:26-07:00","id":1377171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377162#post1377162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's possible to create such items except through homebrew.<br /> Enhanced items have spells cast upon the item itself. You could have the spell be AoE, but then the spell would constantly be active on the ring as well as anyone (or anything) close enough to the ring regardless of whether the ring is worn or not. There's a Fate spell for exempting subjects from an AoE spell, but that would increase the dot rating and might be detrimental for other spells you might want to use this way. For example, a ring of invisibility would always be visible even when you wear it.<br /> An imbued item is much closer if you set the trigger to wearing the ring, but then you still need to cast the imbued item's spell and you can just as well cast it on anyone within range. The spell also wouldn't end when you take off the ring.<br /> Since an Artefact is way too rad for a single passive buff spell, I think the best way to handle it is either through a custom Fate and/or Prime spell, or using a homebrew Yantra type that only activates during certain conditions and on certain subjects (very much like the Basilisk Yantra in Signs of Sorcery).<br /> <br /> Imbued items are re-explained and expanded upon in Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could said item be an eyebrow earing for instance, affecting everyone within a few centimeters of it, including itself? That way, the wearer is the only one who is truly affected unless someone's face almost touches their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Actually this raises another question. Can you reduce the Area of Effect of a Spell deliberately to something smaller than what the level of the scale aspect would normally affect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 03-29-2020, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T07:13:30-07:00","id":1377172,"title":"","content":"Depends on whether the AoE needs to encompass the subject fully or if it's enough to be partly within the AoE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T07:18:12-07:00","id":1377174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377172#post1377172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on whether the AoE needs to encompass the subject fully or if it's enough to be partly within the AoE.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, didn't think of that. It probably should need to encompass the subject fully. Well, thanks for the reply Tessie. Guess I'll have to keep casting that damn nightvision for now. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T19:15:20-07:00","id":1377259,"title":"","content":"Oh dear I'm asking about Proximi again...<br /> <br /> So being eternally strapped for Reach, I assumed a Proximus would want to us Aimed spells for ranged casting. Except, rules as written, any Aimed spell they use would have a range of 0, since all of the range bands for Aimed spells are factors of the caster's Gnosis, which Proximus lack. Any chance I'm missing something? Or are Proximi just functionally not able to use Aimed spells?<br /> <br /> Edit: Unrelated question: Mages learn High Speech automatically when the Awaken, and Sleepers suffer minor Quiescence from it. But what about Sleepwalkers? Is it theoretically possible for them to learn High Speech (probably not to the same fluency as a Mage)? What effects might this have? The High Speech Merit only covers using it as a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Edit again: Apparently I'm on a roll with random questions. Is there any reason why you have to be a Mage to have a familiar? I.e. could a Spirit 4+ Mage cast the Familiar spell to link a spirit with a Sleepwalker or other splat?<br /> <br /> Better yet (this probably strays out of &quot;simple question&quot; territory), is it plausible to have a spell that creates a familiar-like bond between a Mage and some other entity that has Essence? Like, say, a werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":".  more questions 03-29-2020, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T20:05:15-07:00","id":1377269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377259#post1377259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages learn High Speech automatically when the Awaken, and Sleepers suffer minor Quiescence from it. But what about Sleepwalkers? Is it theoretically possible for them to learn High Speech</div> </div> </div> </div>High Speech is a function of Peripheral Mage Sight, so without being under an effect that grants Mage Sight, I don't think Sleepers can learn it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377259#post1377259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently I'm on a roll with random questions. Is there any reason why you have to be a Mage to have a familiar</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Mages are valid targets for the Familiar Spell, but why that is the case is never elaborated on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T21:30:59-07:00","id":1377278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377259#post1377259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better yet (this probably strays out of &quot;simple question&quot; territory), is it plausible to have a spell that creates a familiar-like bond between a Mage and some other entity that has Essence? Like, say, a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Web-Weaver and/or Forge Sympathy along with a Prime/Spirit spell for the relevant fuel-swapping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377269#post1377269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only Mages are valid targets for the Familiar Spell, but why that is the case is never elaborated on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fact that it has multiple effects that only make sense in relation to a mage is reasonably salient here; other things don't have Mana or a Signature Nimbus to interact with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T23:55:31-07:00","id":1377302,"title":"","content":"High Speech for Sleepwalkers (and other non-Mage supernatural beings) - it\u2019s a Merit in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T01:06:14-07:00","id":1377308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377259#post1377259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit again: Apparently I'm on a roll with random questions. Is there any reason why you have to be a Mage to have a familiar? I.e. could a Spirit 4+ Mage cast the Familiar spell to link a spirit with a Sleepwalker or other splat?<br /> <br /> Better yet (this probably strays out of &quot;simple question&quot; territory), is it plausible to have a spell that creates a familiar-like bond between a Mage and some other entity that has Essence? Like, say, a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a werewolf in particular it might work with a single Spirit 4 spell. Not only do they already have Essence, but they also have a natural affinity for spiritual bonds, such as to their Pack, Lodge and Tribal Totems. When designing such a spell I would probably alter some details, though, like using the other's senses.<br /> The werewolf could also use it as an opportunity to develop a Mage/Mana/Supernal style Wolf Gift.<br /> <br /> For others I would say you'd have to cast spells that emulate the individual effects, like Mind for sharing senses, Space for the Sympathetic Connection, Prime+something to exchange and convert fuel traits, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-30-2020, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T11:43:30-07:00","id":1377377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377302#post1377302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Speech for Sleepwalkers (and other non-Mage supernatural beings) - it\u2019s a Merit in Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. That was literally next on my list of things to read anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T02:41:18-07:00","id":1377910,"title":"","content":"can you use pattern restoration or clear thoughts mind 3 to remove megalomaniacal or rampant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T02:46:02-07:00","id":1377913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377910#post1377910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you use pattern restoration or clear thoughts mind 3 to remove megalomaniacal or rampant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it, but you don't get any Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T05:44:12-07:00","id":1377933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1377259#post1377259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear I'm asking about Proximi again...<br /> <br /> So being eternally strapped for Reach, I assumed a Proximus would want to us Aimed spells for ranged casting. Except, rules as written, any Aimed spell they use would have a range of 0, since all of the range bands for Aimed spells are factors of the caster's Gnosis, which Proximus lack. Any chance I'm missing something? Or are Proximi just functionally not able to use Aimed spells?<br /> <br /> Edit: Unrelated question: Mages learn High Speech automatically when the Awaken, and Sleepers suffer minor Quiescence from it. But what about Sleepwalkers? Is it theoretically possible for them to learn High Speech (probably not to the same fluency as a Mage)? What effects might this have? The High Speech Merit only covers using it as a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Edit again: Apparently I'm on a roll with random questions. Is there any reason why you have to be a Mage to have a familiar? I.e. could a Spirit 4+ Mage cast the Familiar spell to link a spirit with a Sleepwalker or other splat?<br /> <br /> Better yet (this probably strays out of &quot;simple question&quot; territory), is it plausible to have a spell that creates a familiar-like bond between a Mage and some other entity that has Essence? Like, say, a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>This article has some homebrew rules for familiars, including an Occult \u2022\u2022 based binding rite from Hunter:Witchfinders. Perhaps its more in line with what you are looking for:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/09/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-familars.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/0...ilars.html?m=1</a><br /> <br /> Reverse engineering some of the techniques in Witchfinders could be useful for a Proximus to wield non-Supernal magic or simply survive when they are targeted.<br /> <br /> High Speech Perception is the merit you are looking for. It doesn't let them write it, but they can understand it, which has all sorts of applications. For example, if a mage has Hidden High Speech and the Sleepwalker can comprehend it, then they have a communication channel that is secure from mundane scrutiny (within the limits of High Speech, but still pretty good).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-02-2020, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:49:25-07:00","id":1378294,"title":"","content":"Also, as it\u2019s a low-cost supernatural Merit directly relating to mages, I would totally allow a PC to give it out with a Prime and Mind spell under the guidelines for spells temporarily granting Merits. It\u2019d trigger a Sleeper, but for a Sleepwalker, being able to clue them in on Mage-Speak is useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T23:08:56-07:00","id":1378684,"title":"","content":"Currently designing an Artifact and need a little help.<br /> <br /> The artifact is a sword that is basically unbreakable and can be made to cut through anything.<br /> <br /> What would the merit rating and stats be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T01:46:09-07:00","id":1378699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1378684#post1378684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently designing an Artifact and need a little help.<br /> <br /> The artifact is a sword that is basically unbreakable and can be made to cut through anything.<br /> <br /> What would the merit rating and stats be?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use a Perfected item (2 points merit) to stat a sword made of Siderite.<br /> It bypass normal Durability and it s very hard (but the book don t say how much).<br /> If you need it to be an artifact you could add the 2 points to the Artifact merit, maybe with a spell to increase Durability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T21:27:32-07:00","id":1378920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1378684#post1378684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently designing an Artifact and need a little help.<br /> <br /> The artifact is a sword that is basically unbreakable and can be made to cut through anything.<br /> <br /> What would the merit rating and stats be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, &quot;Artifacts&quot; cast spells, rather than have persistent magical qualities, so an Artifact sword that can make itself indestructible could theoretically cast the spell to make any target temporarily indestructible. In mechanical terms, it sounds like you want an Enhanced Item with the dots allocated to improve Durability combined with two-dot Perfected Item merit from Signs of Sorcery to make it out of Siderite. Normal iron has 3 Durability, so I'd assume Siderite would be at least 4. If that isn't indestructible enough, you can add a point of Durability per merit point, up to 5. You can also always refluff it so that it's just magical rather than being made of Perfected Iron.<br /> <br /> Long story short, for seven dots, you get a sword that treats diamonds like tissue paper (ignores Durability) and would take some hefty magic to dent (Durability 7).<br /> <br /> <br /> Alright, I came here to ask my own question and got distracted:<br /> <br /> So because there are spirits for just about everything under the sun (and some from over the sun), theoretically, most everything is potentially Resonant because most everything falls under the purview of some spirit somewhere. However, I can't find anything that says that a spirit has to actually be present for the Resonant Condition to be in effect. Most of the time, you don't care. But with the Channel Essence spell, you can draw &quot;Essence into [your] Pattern from a Resonant Condition...&quot; So what determines when something is actually Resonant? Or can I just get Essence from my dirty socks because <i>somewhere </i>out there is a dirty-sock spirit that resonates with them? Edit: I guess the question really is: is the Resonant condition just a marker that something falls under a thematically appropriate spirit's influence, or is it the result of the spirit and thing actually resonating with each other? Is the essence just sitting there waiting for an appropriate spirit to collect it, or is the spirit actually creating the essence by it's presence, or something? (Am I going to stop second-guessing myself before I let people answer?)<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, am I correct that any given Resonant Condition could only provide you with 1 essence per day, like it would for a spirit? Edit again: No wait, spirits can gorge an appropriate condition to get more by rolling so 1 isn't necessarily the limit...what does this mean for the mage?<br /> <br /> I think this is the sixth time I've edited this post, so I'll ask one more question, then close the tab and go to bed: if a spirit spends a day in proximity to two Resonant conditions, do they regain 1 essence or 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 04-06-2020, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T22:58:55-07:00","id":1378927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1378920#post1378920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So because there are spirits for just about everything under the sun (and some from over the sun), theoretically, most everything is potentially Resonant because most everything falls under the purview of some spirit somewhere. However, I can't find anything that says that a spirit has to actually be present for the Resonant Condition to be in effect.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> \u200bEdit: I guess the question really is: is the Resonant condition just a marker that something falls under a thematically appropriate spirit's influence, or is it the result of the spirit and thing actually resonating with each other? Is the essence just sitting there waiting for an appropriate spirit to collect it, or is the spirit actually creating the essence by it's presence, or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, of course not. That would be incredibly backwards, given that the mechanical function of the Resonant Condition is primarily to say &quot;appropriate spirits can gain Essence from this and use it to Manifest.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what determines when something is actually Resonant? Or can I just get Essence from my dirty socks because <i>somewhere </i>out there is a dirty-sock spirit that resonates with them? </div> </div> </div>From a narrative perspective, are your dirty socks important? Does their being there say something about the world? Are you looking for the sort of Essence that dirty socks could be expected to have?<br /> <br /> &quot;Everything has a spirit&quot; should not be interpreted too specifically \u2014 tightly-defined invisible entities are the domain of goetia, whereas spirits tend to diffuse into broad categories that result in particularly bizarre hybrids if they feed on Essence whose ties to their concept are too abstract. The spirit of your dirty socks, if it rates attention at all, is more probably a spirit of clutter or filth or fashion rather than a Dirty Sock Spirit, and the Essence your dirty socks give off can support spirits that aren't the spirit of your dirty socks \u2014 it can, in a pinch, kind of support <i>any</i> spirit.<br /> <br /> Essence scarcity for spirits in the Shadow is a matter of feeding grounds and the need to spend it to effect change; werewolves have a different relation to it on account of their own needs and limitations, and mages largely operate outside of these constraints because Essence isn't a thing they need and making half a dozen magath because you fed house-spirits horse-Essence to see what would happen is part of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Also, am I correct that any given Resonant Condition could only provide you with 1 essence per day, like it would for a spirit? Edit again: No wait, spirits can gorge an appropriate condition to get more by rolling so 1 isn't necessarily the limit...what does this mean for the mage? </div> </div> </div>It means, assuming you're a Thyrsus or a member of a Spirit-based Legacy or have spent the time to develop Channel Essence as a Rote or Praxis, that you can draw upon as much of a fuel source you have no personal use for as you care to cast the spell for, provided you have the space in your Pattern or other vessels to move it to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this is the sixth time I've edited this post, so I'll ask one more question, then close the tab and go to bed: if a spirit spends a day in proximity to two Resonant conditions, do they regain 1 essence or 2? </div> </div> </div>One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T08:37:43-07:00","id":1378991,"title":"","content":"Question about Swarm of Locust\\Miracle or Fate Making spells in general:<br /> Could a Fate Master call down meteorites as little as a fist or as big as the one that exterminated the dinosaurs or similar kind of destruction with the afoprementioned spells or in any other fashion with Making practices?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T09:05:38-07:00","id":1378999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1378927#post1378927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, of course not. That would be incredibly backwards, given that the mechanical function of the Resonant Condition is primarily to say &quot;appropriate spirits can gain Essence from this and use it to Manifest.&quot;<br /> <br /> From a narrative perspective, are your dirty socks important? Does their being there say something about the world? Are you looking for the sort of Essence that dirty socks could be expected to have?<br /> <br /> &quot;Everything has a spirit&quot; should not be interpreted too specifically \u2014 tightly-defined invisible entities are the domain of goetia, whereas spirits tend to diffuse into broad categories that result in particularly bizarre hybrids if they feed on Essence whose ties to their concept are too abstract. The spirit of your dirty socks, if it rates attention at all, is more probably a spirit of clutter or filth or fashion rather than a Dirty Sock Spirit, and the Essence your dirty socks give off can support spirits that aren't the spirit of your dirty socks \u2014 it can, in a pinch, kind of support <i>any</i> spirit.<br /> <br /> Essence scarcity for spirits in the Shadow is a matter of feeding grounds and the need to spend it to effect change; werewolves have a different relation to it on account of their own needs and limitations, and mages largely operate outside of these constraints because Essence isn't a thing they need and making half a dozen magath because you fed house-spirits horse-Essence to see what would happen is part of the game.<br /> <br /> It means, assuming you're a Thyrsus or a member of a Spirit-based Legacy or have spent the time to develop Channel Essence as a Rote or Praxis, that you can draw upon as much of a fuel source you have no personal use for as you care to cast the spell for, provided you have the space in your Pattern or other vessels to move it to.<br /> <br /> One.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, thanks for the response. That's basically how I originally thought the whole Resonance thing worked, but I managed to get myself confused. It was actually the differential between the Mage and Werewolf Essence economies that caused my concern. I guess the trick is just to enforce some kind of narrative consequences if a spirit mage starts bankrolling his werewolf friends in dirty-sock essence. (Also, I recognize that my conception of spirits is somewhat skewed by my prior exposure to spren from the <i>Stormlight Archive, </i>which are more similar to astral entities.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T09:31:51-07:00","id":1379006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1378991#post1378991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Swarm of Locust\\Miracle or Fate Making spells in general:<br /> Could a Fate Master call down meteorites as little as a fist or as big as the one that exterminated the dinosaurs or similar kind of destruction with the afoprementioned spells or in any other fashion with Making practices?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If its within the scope of possibility, even if pretty unlikely, then its within its scope. So technically its doable.<br /> <br /> As small as a fist ? Sure, you could probably even specify what its made of (I imagine this is one of the oldest alternative ways to get perfected metals).<br /> <br /> But as big as the one that destroyed the dinosaurs? That was estimated to be 11-81 km in diameter, so you would likely need Imperial spell factors to pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-06-2020, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T09:46:46-07:00","id":1379009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1379006#post1379006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If its within the scope of possibility, even if pretty unlikely, then its within its scope. So technically its doable.<br /> <br /> As small as a fist ? Sure, you could probably even specify what its made of (I imagine this is one of the oldest alternative ways to get perfected metals).<br /> <br /> But as big as the one that destroyed the dinosaurs? That was estimated to be 11-81 km in diameter, so you would likely need Imperial spell factors to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Size spell factor matters on that kind of spells too? Because it only seemed to make something happen. Like, as example, potency would not seem to have much sense, nor area. That would solve some problems, actually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:44:30-07:00","id":1379038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1379009#post1379009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Size spell factor matters on that kind of spells too? Because it only seemed to make something happen. Like, as example, potency would not seem to have much sense, nor area. That would solve some problems, actually</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the AoE decides how big of an area is affected by such spells (same for weather control spells). The Chicxulub Crater is 150 km in diameter, which is definitely more than a campus/small neighbourhood. Since AoE is the one part of the Scale factor that can't be increased further, it should be impossible to replicate with such a spell without Imperial factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:31:53-07:00","id":1379048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1379038#post1379038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure the AoE decides how big of an area is affected by such spells (same for weather control spells). The Chicxulub Crater is 150 km in diameter, which is definitely more than a campus/small neighbourhood. Since AoE is the one part of the Scale factor that can't be increased further, it should be impossible to replicate with such a spell without Imperial factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, if I'm not mistaken ANY spell must follow the spell factor chart at cast, I don't think there are exceptions... So, for example, a Miracle at cast would have to apply the spell factors decided at cast to every intercession there after, am I right?<br /> <br /> Like, if I have a scale of a campus i could influence a target with anything i want to the max scale of a campus, e.g. throwing down a campus size meteorite but no more bigger.<br /> Does this sound correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:11:49-07:00","id":1379057,"title":"","content":"The meteor isn't the subject so its Size is irrelevant in this case. Throwing down a campus sized meteor would result in a crater that is many, many times larger than that campus. Think instead that the immediate wave of destruction resulting from a meteor impact should be contained within the AoE. Windows will still shatter far beyond that range, but buildings should still stand.<br /> Remember that the spell is about making something happen within the AoE, and the meteor is just the delivery. It would be completely different if you designed a Forces/Matter spell that directly controls the meteor (though in that case you would use the Size part of the Scale chart since the meteor is the spell's subject).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T15:19:10-07:00","id":1379073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1379057#post1379057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The meteor isn't the subject so its Size is irrelevant in this case. Throwing down a campus sized meteor would result in a crater that is many, many times larger than that campus. Think instead that the immediate wave of destruction resulting from a meteor impact should be contained within the AoE. Windows will still shatter far beyond that range, but buildings should still stand.<br /> Remember that the spell is about making something happen within the AoE, and the meteor is just the delivery. It would be completely different if you designed a Forces/Matter spell that directly controls the meteor (though in that case you would use the Size part of the Scale chart since the meteor is the spell's subject).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the thing is that the effects are limited to the target or target area, right.<br /> One last question: if a big meteorite is to crash on a single person and there's no area defined, the dude should die horiibly but nothing else should thena happen outside arm's lenght?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T23:57:25-07:00","id":1379186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1379073#post1379073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, the thing is that the effects are limited to the target or target area, right.<br /> One last question: if a big meteorite is to crash on a single person and there's no area defined, the dude should die horiibly but nothing else should thena happen outside arm's lenght?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i think that blood and organs would splash farther than an arm s lenght, as well as bone splinters that could hit someone else, but those things would be collateral &quot;damage&quot;, not under mage control like the previous example broken windows.<br /> But i think that hitting a gas tank with a spell of the same size would cause much more collateral damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T02:39:34-07:00","id":1379190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1379186#post1379186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, i think that blood and organs would splash farther than an arm s lenght, as well as bone splinters that could hit someone else, but those things would be collateral &quot;damage&quot;, not under mage control like the previous example broken windows.<br /> But i think that hitting a gas tank with a spell of the same size would cause much more collateral damage</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, only the direct effect would be limited, but everything &quot;else&quot; would be outside the direct scope of the spell and react as it should to the spell effects. An enormous meteorite would not be working for attaccking a single target in a mall, because it would logically hit and destroy/kill much more else other than the intended target, so the spell would conjure something that would be smaller at arrival at least, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:21:20-07:00","id":1380143,"title":"","content":"Can Time grant access to many-worlds style alternate timelines?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking no; it seems like in Mage there's only a single timeline. Spells like &quot;visit an alternate timeline for Duration where Potency things enumerated by the caster are different&quot; don't fly right?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, could there be emanation realms that work like alternative timelines of the fallen world? Seems like an awkward fit for that system too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:39:06-07:00","id":1380147,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain how a mage can manipulate temporal sympathy itself and what effects are possible?<br /> <br /> It's unclear to me from the rules. I'm not sure whether Space, which has purview over sympathy, is involved in manipulating temporal sympathy. I'm also wondering if any of the Space spells dealing with sympathy have temporal analogs (e.g. transferring temporal connections between subjects, bolstering/weakening temporal connections to modify temporal withstand, creating/destroying temporal connections). And I'm not really sure what practical effects would arise from transferring or creating temporal connections where none existed previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:45:51-07:00","id":1380167,"title":"","content":"Temporal sympathy isn't a mystical bond as much as it is similarity to the self. You could definitely artificially increase it, and <i>maybe</i> decrease it through magic, but you can't transfer temporal sympathy to someone else. You also can't create temporal sympathy between two subjects unless they're actually the same thing at different times in it's personal timeline (though then it would already have temporal sympathy to itself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:47:59-07:00","id":1380168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380143#post1380143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Time grant access to many-worlds style alternate timelines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as a casual thing, no, though isolated instances might be accessed through Weaving in the same way Irises to other realms are opened by appropriate Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spells like &quot;visit an alternate timeline for Duration where Potency things enumerated by the caster are different&quot; don't fly right? </div> </div> </div>Given that &quot;stipulate how things changed with Time&quot; is the realm of Imperial spells, nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise, could there be emanation realms that work like alternative timelines of the fallen world? Seems like an awkward fit for that system too. </div> </div> </div>Emanation Realms are expressions of aspects of singular Arcana, so no, probably not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380147#post1380147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain how a mage can manipulate temporal sympathy itself and what effects are possible?<br /> <br /> It's unclear to me from the rules. I'm not sure whether Space, which has purview over sympathy, is involved in manipulating temporal sympathy. I'm also wondering if any of the Space spells dealing with sympathy have temporal analogs (e.g. transferring temporal connections between subjects, bolstering/weakening temporal connections to modify temporal withstand, creating/destroying temporal connections). And I'm not really sure what practical effects would arise from transferring or creating temporal connections where none existed previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Sympathy is a Time thing that is no more manipulatable with Space than spatial sympathetic connections can be manipulated with Time. You could borrow, fabricate, or destroy a subject's temporal sympathies with its past selves, but the practical effects of that mostly boil down to making it easier to meddle with those points in the past or repeat them in the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:16:13-07:00","id":1380191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380168#post1380168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that &quot;stipulate how things changed with Time&quot; is the realm of Imperial spells, nope.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Rewrite History</i> allows the creation of alternate timelines on an <b>individual</b> basis. Viewing such changes seems like a fair expansion on the theme. Visiting them would be unusual magic. <br /> <br /> If deleting someone's timeline allows them to relive that time and catch back up to the present, Creation seems a valid path to creating a persistent alternate version of the past for the spell's subject, but the rules for which applies would need to be defined. It wouldn't be Lasting for a Master, either..<br /> <br /> Applying such magic to an area with Scale could have some interesting effects, though it's clearly in the realm of &quot;up to the Storyteller&quot; what exactly happens. Salamanca in Mage could be interpreted as something like this, too, though probably going really wrong.<br /> <br /> The G-M makes alternate timelines through Infrastructure, some times, so there's limited precedent in other gamelines, at least.<br /> <br /> It's a valid plot element if you wanted to run it, though it'd be easiest if you decided that temporal irises are created by archmasters or some esoteric phenomena. That way, you can limit the options and be able to actually plot things out. Also, it would require defining fewer games rules. Heck, you could use Aponia from riding Awakenings as the means of accessing these other worlds if you wanted it to be particularly tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:53:10-07:00","id":1380200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380191#post1380191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a valid plot element if you wanted to run it, though it'd be easiest if you decided that temporal irises are created by archmasters or some esoteric phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>has to be</i> esoteric phenomena, in Awakening's metaphysics \u2014 the many-worlds &quot;anything that can happen happens somewhere&quot; version of alternate timelines is not the default means by which Time works, and the most prominent examples of alternate timelines are maintained by Infrastructure, produced as weird currents in the Ocean of Osiris, or don't-exist as greater Abyssal entities (including the most-developed Annunaki in the setting so far).<br /> <br /> By default, if alternate timelines exist as anything more than pockets of weirdness of varying scale, they do so from different configurations of the Supernal than the one a character occupies in the present. Meddling in the Supernal may make it so that things have always been the other way, but if that configuration exists at the same time as another unfolding of events then the one is at a smaller scale than the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:58:25-07:00","id":1380284,"title":"","content":"Which makes me wonder, since Orichalcum is impossible to damage or alter by non-magical means, does it mean a Time mage carrying an item made of it will have a unchanged temporal sympathetic link to every moment it was present ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T02:24:05-07:00","id":1380340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380284#post1380284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes me wonder, since Orichalcum is impossible to damage or alter by non-magical means, does it mean a Time mage carrying an item made of it will have a unchanged temporal sympathetic link to every moment it was present ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>object</i> will have an unchanged temporal sympathy to <i>itself</i> for quite some time.<br /> Personally I might rule that enough changes in its history (like forming/changing sympathetic connections, or be subject to spells even if they don't alter it physically) might lower its temporal sympathy, but only one step and only after a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T16:36:14-07:00","id":1380515,"title":"","content":"So I have two questions about Yantras:<br /> <br /> 1. Let's say you have 3 Dedicated Yantras and use two of them when casting a spell. Can you also use the third as a normal Path/Order Tool, even if you would not be able to if it wasn't Dedicated? As rules simply say that you can use Dedicated Yantras as Path/Order Tools too, I presume that the answer is yes? Besides, you probably need to use all three in all spells for a month, so there likely isn't even another option anyway...<br /> <br /> 2. If you use something as a Shadow Name Persona Yantra, can you use the same thing as another type of Yantra, even if it builds on the same thing? To use the core book Legacy Yantra example, let's say that your Legacy allows you to use high from a drug as a Yantra. Now a mage Dionysus has getting high as a part of his Shadow Persona. Can he interpret and use the drug as both a Persona Yantra and a Legacy Yantra, despite them being based in the same mental state? I know that the rules allow for interpreting one thing as multiple Yantras, but does this apply to getting different types of Yantras you are qualified for from a thing with the same meaning/nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:25:14-07:00","id":1380519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380515#post1380515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have two questions about Yantras:<br /> <br /> 1. Let's say you have 3 Dedicated Yantras and use two of them when casting a spell. Can you also use the third as a normal Path/Order Tool, even if you would not be able to if it wasn't Dedicated? As rules simply say that you can use Dedicated Yantras as Path/Order Tools too, I presume that the answer is yes? Besides, you probably need to use all three in all spells for a month, so there likely isn't even another option anyway...<br /> <br /> 2. If you use something as a Shadow Name Persona Yantra, can you use the same thing as another type of Yantra, even if it builds on the same thing? To use the core book Legacy Yantra example, let's say that your Legacy allows you to use high from a drug as a Yantra. Now a mage Dionysus has getting high as a part of his Shadow Persona. Can he interpret and use the drug as both a Persona Yantra and a Legacy Yantra, despite them being based in the same mental state? I know that the rules allow for interpreting one thing as multiple Yantras, but does this apply to getting different types of Yantras you are qualified for from a thing with the same meaning/nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. While it's never explicitly disallowed, the language used for multiple Dedicated Tools assumes it's only two Tools. It might not be possible with more (and if it were, it'd require additional rules or clarifications).<br /> <br /> 2. The Persona Yantra is the role you act out when casting the spell, meaning you can't reuse it as any other type of Yantra because no other category can be represented through the role you play (except Techn\u00e9 based around theatre, but that's not really the same thing).<br /> \u200bBut other than practical issues, there's no limit for reusing props for different Yantras. The only limit is that you can't use the same prop as the <i>same</i> Yantra. Using an object as a Path Tool, Patron Tool, Sympathetic Yantra, and Sacrament works (but only if you use it as a Sacrament last due to practical limits) because those are four different Yantras, even if they all build on the same symbolism. You could also potentially use an object as multiple different Path Tool Yantras, but each time they <i>would</i> require different symbolism (a spear acting as both a weapon and a rod, for example) or they would be the same Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-11-2020, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:47:21-07:00","id":1380523,"title":"","content":"Is Paradox still an issue in the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:30:48-07:00","id":1380533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380523#post1380523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Paradox still an issue in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending word to the contrary in Fallen Worlds, I see no reason to assume otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:26:44-07:00","id":1380548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380340#post1380340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <i>object</i> will have an unchanged temporal sympathy to <i>itself</i> for quite some time.<br /> Personally I might rule that enough changes in its history (like forming/changing sympathetic connections, or be subject to spells even if they don't alter it physically) might lower its temporal sympathy, but only one step and only after a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, so it could still be useful for postcognition. Cool, thanks.<br /> <br /> One more question comes to mind: Ectoplasm Shaping allows the caster to mold it into anything, but would it allow it to be shaped into weapons to attack ghosts or a living being's soul ? <br /> <br /> For example, could a Left Handed mage defeat a living target by using ectoplasmic throwing daggers to wear at their souls and then Compel them into the appropriate level of soul loss symptoms ? Or could that property only be achieved by a Weaving ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T23:35:17-07:00","id":1380590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380548#post1380548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, so it could still be useful for postcognition. Cool, thanks.<br /> <br /> One more question comes to mind: Ectoplasm Shaping allows the caster to mold it into anything, but would it allow it to be shaped into weapons to attack ghosts or a living being's soul ? <br /> <br /> For example, could a Left Handed mage defeat a living target by using ectoplasmic throwing daggers to wear at their souls and then Compel them into the appropriate level of soul loss symptoms ? Or could that property only be achieved by a Weaving ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ectoplasm doesn\u2019t target the soul by default, but I don\u2019t see a reason it can\u2019t do physical harm since it\u2019s manifest ghost stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T07:17:20-07:00","id":1380937,"title":"","content":"Do Imbued Items benefit from bonus to the Primary Factor based on the creator's proficiency in the relevant Arcanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:03:56-07:00","id":1381025,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked again, but here we go.<br /> <br /> In Signs of Sorcery, there is a merit called Shadow Self, which requires you to have five dots in Shadow Name. But in the 2e book, the Shadow Name merit only goes up to three dots. What's up with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:40:36-07:00","id":1381228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1381025#post1381025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been asked again, but here we go.<br /> <br /> In Signs of Sorcery, there is a merit called Shadow Self, which requires you to have five dots in Shadow Name. But in the 2e book, the Shadow Name merit only goes up to three dots. What's up with that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figured it was a typo from your description. I consider that confirmed, as my copy has it listed as a 3 dot requirement. If you have the ebook, you might see about updating the version you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:33:21-07:00","id":1381289,"title":"","content":"Can a mage can use Shifting Sands to reveal all of the information about a mystery in one effective turn? Disregarding mysteries with Locked (and maybe Linked) Opacity, the mage just alternates between scrutiny rolls and Shifting Sands to jump back a couple of turns. The successes from scrutiny continue to accrue because they represent information the mage gained about the mystery. If she suffers a dramatic failure on revelation or scrutiny roll, just Shifting Sands back for a do-over and it's like it never happened. Does this work? It seems like it makes solving even high-opacity mysteries just an exercise in persistence for freshly-awakened Acanthus specializing in Time as long as she has the relevant mage sight(s).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, I realized the answer to my own question. It doesn't work because of the spell stacking rules. This trick is only useful for low-opacity mysteries that the mage was only near for moment before losing access, since each attempt marches time forward by one turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-14-2020, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:18:31-07:00","id":1381359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1381289#post1381289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage can use Shifting Sands to reveal all of the information about a mystery in one effective turn? Disregarding mysteries with Locked (and maybe Linked) Opacity, the mage just alternates between scrutiny rolls and Shifting Sands to jump back a couple of turns. The successes from scrutiny continue to accrue because they represent information the mage gained about the mystery. If she suffers a dramatic failure on revelation or scrutiny roll, just Shifting Sands back for a do-over and it's like it never happened. Does this work? It seems like it makes solving even high-opacity mysteries just an exercise in persistence for freshly-awakened Acanthus specializing in Time as long as she has the relevant mage sight(s).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, I realized the answer to my own question. It doesn't work because of the spell stacking rules. This trick is only useful for low-opacity mysteries that the mage was only near for moment before losing access, since each attempt marches time forward by one turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of using the Time Arcanum to help scrutinize a Mystery, if you had enough time, could Veil of Moments allow them to reveal all information ? Nimbus contamination of a Mystery is something that worsens over time, so maybe ? The caveat is that it still doesn't stop Supernal entities from taking an interest.<br /> <br /> A Weaving may allow it, by connecting the present to [Potency] turns in the future in a loop. Since the future is more malleable than the present, they could get it done in &quot;one turn&quot;. Its similar to how Dr Strange learned a lot fighting Dormammu for &quot;ages&quot;. Since the intended application doesn't require repairing damage, you can get away with a Weaving rather than Unmaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-14-2020, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T05:04:46-07:00","id":1381608,"title":"","content":"Scrutiny is an active investigation where the mage interacts with a Mystery. By resetting the mage's interference with the Mystery, you'd also reset the mage's progress because they'd have to go through all of that again.<br /> As an ST you may invoke the rule for consecutive attempts. Sooner or later all possible angles and approaches will be exhausted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:52:47-07:00","id":1381701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1380937#post1380937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Imbued Items benefit from bonus to the Primary Factor based on the creator's proficiency in the relevant Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not. And i need to keep typing because characters..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:41:21-07:00","id":1381783,"title":"","content":"Is a permanent condition inflicted by Imposing Nimbus subject to a Clash of Wills ? Or does it count as a natural effect that cannot resist dispelling ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T22:42:54-07:00","id":1382289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1381783#post1381783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a permanent condition inflicted by Imposing Nimbus subject to a Clash of Wills ? Or does it count as a natural effect that cannot resist dispelling ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s inflicted by magic, but it\u2019s not a spell so it probably shouldn\u2019t get a CoW. Since it\u2019s not a spell you can\u2019t dispel it either, though it can be removed by more magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T06:25:40-07:00","id":1382322,"title":"","content":"Interesting, so just treat it as a normal Condition. Makes sense, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T20:54:57-07:00","id":1382432,"title":"","content":"Are aimed spells automatically obvious magic to sleepers?<br /> <br /> If you use an aimed spell in the presence of a sleeper, does it automatically incur paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-19-2020, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T21:08:45-07:00","id":1382434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382432#post1382432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are aimed spells automatically obvious magic to sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that Defense applies suggests they're at least <i>visible</i>, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you use an aimed spell in the presence of a sleeper, does it automatically incur paradox? </div> </div> </div>They'd still have to recognize that something was going on, so I think &quot;in their presence&quot; is a bit of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T06:52:49-07:00","id":1382511,"title":"","content":"Here's a simple question: I remember seeing somewhere that sympathetic links were one-way, but now I can't find the reference anywhere, anybody know anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26103-alambril","name":"Alambril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T07:49:26-07:00","id":1382525,"title":"","content":"It's not stated directly, but implied by word choices the write-up on Sympathy. The book consistently uses &quot;the connection from A to B&quot; rather than &quot;the connection between A and B.&quot;<br /> <br /> It also matches up with a common sense understanding of those connections in real-world scenarios. Consider a stalker and stalkee, where the stalker has yet to reveal himself. The stalker has a connection to the stalkee, but the stalkee doesn't even know the stalker exists and so has no connection to him.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For sympathetic range spells, you're meant to use a connection from the caster to the spell's subject. Suppose the stalker above is a mage. He might have a strong connection to the target for sympathic range spells. The stalkee would have no connection back to the stalker for sympathetic range spells, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-19-2020, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:44:50-07:00","id":1382543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382525#post1382525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the stalkee doesn't even know the stalker exists and so has no connection to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not knowing who you interact with (or even that you're interacting with someone) does not prevent a sympathetic connection from being formed. A sympathetic connection does not depend on the there being an emotional connection (though strong emotions do seem to increase the strength of sympathetic connections) so a stalker victim should definitely have a sympathetic connection to their stalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:46:59-07:00","id":1382545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382543#post1382543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not knowing who you interact with (or even that you're interacting with someone) does not prevent a sympathetic connection from being formed. A sympathetic connection does not depend on the there being an emotional connection (though strong emotions do seem to increase the strength of sympathetic connections) so a stalker victim should definitely have a sympathetic connection to their stalker.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I feel like it contradicts previous discussions we've had on sympathy, but okay. I don't think my scenario described any interaction of the stalkee with the stalker unless you count something like &quot;being observed by.&quot; At the very least the connections would have different strengths and so there's justification for them being distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:59:32-07:00","id":1382547,"title":"","content":"I definitely think &quot;being observed&quot; is an interaction in this context. There is both a physical and an emotional distance, but a distinct metaphysical important. Depending on the extent of the stalking I could see it reaching a medium sympathy. (Strong would require things like living in the same home and being in physical proximity during prolonged periods of time, but that's difficult to hide without also affecting the victim with some Veiling-style supernatural effect, which would cause/increase sympathy on its own.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T10:16:08-07:00","id":1382550,"title":"","content":"If we think about sympathy as how close two subjects are the link would be of the same strength for both.<br /> But i m not sure that sympathy means closeness as it was in mage the ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T10:45:20-07:00","id":1382553,"title":"","content":"I would have to know how sympathy in Ascension works before I can say anything about that.<br /> <br /> What I'm basing my thoughts on is the description of sympathy as physical, emotional or mystical. One of the examples is a murder weapon and victim. Assuming the weapon had never been connected to the victim before the murder, then the physical connection would not have time to form, and an emotional connection straight up can't form or be sustained (since neither weapon nor body are thinking beings), which leaves a mystical connection that will last &quot;for years&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T11:12:38-07:00","id":1382557,"title":"","content":"I don't know with confidence which interpretation is correct, but I'll note that the stalkee would have no sympathetic yantra for the stalker if they've never even had an encounter, and so could not use any potential connection formed from stalkee to stalker for sympathetic range spells. Although I guess with Matter she could create one a la the 11Q attainment.<br /> <br /> In terms of gameplay I don't like Enemy Space Mage being able to peruse his sympathetic connections to find new ones formed with people who are (unbeknownst to him him) plotting against him, use those connections + Matter to make a sympathy yantra, bolster the connection, then cast against his mysterious new enemies from sympathetic range. It works for some stories but not for most I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-19-2020, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:45:09-07:00","id":1382572,"title":"","content":"On my earlier sympathy question, I actually found something after reading <i> everything</i> through more carefully: On p. 175-176, under the Veil Sympathy spell, under the +2 reach option, <b>&quot;The mage may suppress all the subject\u2019s sympathetic links. This effect applies in both directions; not only does the subject lose his links to loved ones, but those people lose their links to him. The spell is Withstood by the strongest connection the subject has&quot;. </b>This does actually quite unambiguously demonstrate that Sympathetic links are in fact only one-way, as the other person's potential link back to the subject seems to be explicitly distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26103-alambril","name":"Alambril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:50:36-07:00","id":1382573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382432#post1382432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are aimed spells automatically obvious magic to sleepers?<br /> <br /> If you use an aimed spell in the presence of a sleeper, does it automatically incur paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>On this matter the book has this to say:<b>&quot; Aimed spells appear as bolts of energy or projections coming from the casting mage, as opposed to spells cast at sensory range which materialize at the point of the subject&quot; p. 115</b>. I would rule that if a Sleeper would see this, Quiescence would inevitably have something to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26103-alambril","name":"Alambril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:22:24-07:00","id":1382629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382557#post1382557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of gameplay I don't like Enemy Space Mage being able to peruse his sympathetic connections to find new ones formed with people who are (unbeknownst to him him) plotting against him, use those connections + Matter to make a sympathy yantra, bolster the connection, then cast against his mysterious new enemies from sympathetic range. It works for some stories but not for most I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not an issue since it's practically impossible to find low level sympathetic connections without actively searching for them (and anyone who actively searches for a stalker in their own sympathetic connections without reason to suspect one is paranoid to the point where it's probably highly debilitating for them).<br /> <br /> Also, as you point out yourself, they'd not have access to any sympathetic Yantra if they don't know who it is. Can't even make a crude drawing (really don't know why you mix Matter into it) without knowing what they look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T18:19:23-07:00","id":1382649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382629#post1382629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (really don't know why you mix Matter into it).</div> </div> </div> </div>They referenced the 11Q, so that\u2019s where it\u2019s coming from because one of the Matter attainments can create a Sympathetic Yantra. Not that it matters because in that case they still have to know who they need a Sympathetic Yantra too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:13:23-07:00","id":1382729,"title":"","content":"That constraint isn't mentioned by the attainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Querent no longer requires a sympathy Yantra for a subject she wishes to affect with sympathetic spells. Time and Matter conspire to create one for her. Impressions from the past or emanations from the future shape present matter into a representational sympathy Yantra. This usually takes the form of a lucky find during an investigation. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Whatever is at the other end of this connection&quot; is sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-20-2020, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:43:50-07:00","id":1382750,"title":"","content":"It's an impressive and interesting Attainment, and like most impressive and/or interesting Attainments it can't be replicated through a spell using the same Arcana. The best mages outside that particular Legacy can hope for is to use Fate to make you stumble over what you need, though nothing guarantees that you'll find something relevant to that particular topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:05:37-07:00","id":1382871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382750#post1382750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an impressive and interesting Attainment, and like most impressive and/or interesting Attainments it can't be replicated through a spell using the same Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, why's that? I've not heard that legacy attainments in 2e can do things that are impossible for normal spells. I thought legacy attainments were meant to be based on praxes, and any adjustments to those praxes &quot;shouldn\u2019t make Attainments significantly more or less powerful than they otherwise would be.&quot; Pretty weird if the only the official 2e legacy we had for the longest time flaunted that. Although I wouldn't put it past them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T20:40:19-07:00","id":1382888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1382871#post1382871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, why's that? I've not heard that legacy attainments in 2e can do things that are impossible for normal spells. I thought legacy attainments were meant to be based on praxes, and any adjustments to those praxes &quot;shouldn\u2019t make Attainments significantly more or less powerful than they otherwise would be.&quot; Pretty weird if the only the official 2e legacy we had for the longest time flaunted that. Although I wouldn't put it past them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you looked on the very next page in the &quot;Strange Attainments&quot; sidebar you might see it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T21:05:28-07:00","id":1382892,"title":"","content":"Yeah, good point. Although I'm still skeptical that section applies to the 11Q attainment; it looks vanilla to me. Matter to reshape stuff in the environs into the representational sympathy yantra (Transubstantiation), Time to gaze into the future to see what form it needs to take (Prophecy). If they went full &quot;Strange Attainment&quot; I'm not sure why they mentioned Matter and Time at all; could have just said that they don't need sympathy yantras anymore for sympathetic range casting, full stop.<br /> <br /> Anyway, no point getting too hung up on that one attainment no one actually asked about. There are plenty of ways for a Warlock to peruse his sympathetic connections and with a bit of persistence get at the people on the other ends. I posted a couple off-the-cuff in Creative Thaumatury thread; it doesn't exactly take an archmaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-21-2020, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T03:31:15-07:00","id":1382941,"title":"","content":"It might not require much in Space (technically possible even before you get access to Sympathetic Range) but it does require <i>actively searching for certain sympathetic connections before suspecting that they exist</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, remember the fact that Correspondence (and thus probably also other Knowing/Unveiling spells cast on the self) only reveals the nature of a sympathetic connections from the perspective of the subject. By RAW this means you can't find stalkers without knowing about them in the first place, and even if you use the common house rule to provide somewhat objective information (otherwise you could literally never identify sympathetic connections from non-thinking subjects) you should still have to search for something like &quot;stalker&quot; or &quot;unseen/unknown observer&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T06:43:28-07:00","id":1382966,"title":"","content":"Totally agree. Maybe I play up the horror aspect a bit more in my game than you do in yours; in mine the head of a Seer Pylon is paranoid enough to jump through these hoops by default. I mean they commonly advance by sabotaging or killing each other.<br /> <br /> Rather than a mage regularly sieving all her sympathetic connections though, I think it's more efficient to keep up a long-Duration effect that alerts the mage to changes in sympathetic connections (assuming the caster can spare the spell control). It's like instead of regularly querying a database to poll for changes, you instead set up a trigger to execute whenever a row is updated or created. Adjust potency if desired to ignore Weak connections. I also believe it's possible design spells to help track down the entity at the other end of a sympathetic connection using the connection itself. I put a couple of spells along these lines <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1382736#post1382736\">in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread</a>. The write-up on Sympathy makes it clear that the connections themselves are viable subjects for spell casting.<br /> <br /> I'll also note that the way I run sympathy, connections have more nuance than a single meaning because you can't always boil down complex relationships into a single tag-line. Consider two Seers, one the head of a Pylon and the other her lieutenant. The connection from the lieutenant to the Pylon head might encompass &quot;my leader,&quot; &quot;my lover,&quot; and &quot;the one I&quot;m plotting to overthrow&quot; all at once, and for me any of those are viable keys for searching/identifying that connection.<br /> <br /> Of course I also don't run what you described previously, where A can form a connection to B purely because B has surveilled or plotted against A, even when A doesn't know B exists. It's like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NEAg8p0vizE\" target=\"_blank\">that scene in Endgames</a> where Scarlet Witch is like &quot;You took everything from me!&quot; and alternate-timeline Thanos is like &quot;I don't even know who you are.&quot; Sure, Scarlet Witch has a connection to Thanos as soon as she returns to existence, but I'd say Thanos has no connection to Scarlet Witch prior to fighting her. But I am considering whether your perspective is somehow better (the spells I wrote are useful primarily if you're correct on this point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-21-2020, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T02:30:14-07:00","id":1383111,"title":"","content":"So I'll be running a game, we decided that we'll use the Los Angeles setting from book and in order to flesh out the game I'm asking:<br /> <br /> What would be good source to learn general info about the city? Or maybe do you have any interesting tidbits to share? Tried browsing wiki but there's a lot of text to go through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T09:36:32-07:00","id":1383150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383111#post1383111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'll be running a game, we decided that we'll use the Los Angeles setting from book and in order to flesh out the game I'm asking:<br /> <br /> What would be good source to learn general info about the city? Or maybe do you have any interesting tidbits to share? Tried browsing wiki but there's a lot of text to go through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one, there's a <i>lot</i> more city than just Los Angeles city proper, you're in pretty continuous suburbs or city from the southern end of Orange County until you hit the farmland in Ventura County, and then there's a brief interruption before you hit Santa Barbara County.<br /> <br /> In LA city <i>only</i> downtown LA has decent public transportation, and I use &quot;decent&quot; quite loosely, you really do need a car to get around. Distance is denoted in time rather than distance (&quot;yada yada is about 20 minutes away&quot;). Anything less than a two hour drive is considered close.<br /> <br /> Freeways are called &quot;the &lt;number&gt;&quot; (e.g. &quot;the one-oh-one&quot;, &quot;the four-oh-five&quot;, &quot;the one-eighteen&quot;) except for Highway 1 which is called PCH (Pacific Coast Highway). Toll roads are super rare and are generally privately owned bypasses.<br /> <br /> Food trucks are <i>super</i> popular, places will have things like a &quot;food truck Friday&quot; where food trucks will all set up to sell food. And the food trucks sell diverse and gourmet food, everything from the classic taco truck to gourmet grilled cheese sandwiches, to sushi and dim sum.<br /> <br /> On the topic of food: the best food can be found in the weirdest places, my girlfriend and I got some super incredible authentic Indian food from a random gas station downtown.<br /> <br /> There's a super cool distillery in the Arts District call Lost Spirits, it's Willy Wonka's chocolate factory for adults (they even have a boat ride).<br /> <br /> LA has lots of cool museums. The California Science Center (with the Space Shuttle Endeavor), Natural History Museum, and African-American History Museum are all right next to each other, and are next to the coliseum for the 1984 Olympics. There's also the La Brea Tar Pits, which are real tarpits with bones and such they actually pulled out of the pits on display; and the Griffith Park Observatory, which has appeared in numerous films and even some anime.<br /> <br /> Hollywood is in LA, and that's its own entire thing to unpack. There's active movie sets and you can see very famous people walking around living their everyday lives. Sometimes streets will be blocked off for filming, or you'll see a crew set up in a park or something.<br /> <br /> Disney has the El Capitan theater which does special events after major movie releases (they built Pizza Planet and an Army Men obstacle course for <i>Toy Story</i>). In Anaheim (which is not in LA but is close) there's also Disneyland and California Adventure.<br /> <br /> LA also has quite a bit of nightlife, but I moved away before I was really old enough to enjoy it and came back after I was nightlifed out from being in the military, so I can't speak too much to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:05:24-07:00","id":1383167,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to understand how Reflexive Casting works. It only seems to come up on a few spells like Turn Momentum for +1 Reach, but not for others like Velocity Control. So let's say someone fires a gun at me. I can cast Turn Momentum with +1 Reach to use it Reflexively (do I also have to Reach for Quick Casting?) and up to Potency # bullets automatically miss, right? If I can't do this with Velocity Control, then why does the spell say I can reduce the damage of a projectile attack? Am I supposed to cast VC before the attack comes? Do either/both of these spells require Sensory Range to work on ranged attacks, or is the arm's reach bubble of the base Scale sufficient?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:16:02-07:00","id":1383172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383167#post1383167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to understand how Reflexive Casting works. It only seems to come up on a few spells like Turn Momentum for +1 Reach, but not for others like Velocity Control. So let's say someone fires a gun at me. I can cast Turn Momentum with +1 Reach to use it Reflexively (do I also have to Reach for Quick Casting?) and up to Potency # bullets automatically miss, right? If I can't do this with Velocity Control, then why does the spell say I can reduce the damage of a projectile attack? Am I supposed to cast VC before the attack comes? Do either/both of these spells require Sensory Range to work on ranged attacks, or is the arm's reach bubble of the base Scale sufficient?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflexive casting is +2 reach and a mana, you don't need to spend a reach on Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> <i>Turn Momentum</i> is a bit different, you cast the spell beforehand and get the effects of the spell for the duration. The spell effect is turning aside a number of things equal to potency, by default this requires you to hold your action, for a reach this can be done reflexively. There isn't an option to cast the spell reflexively, only to use its effect.<br /> <br /> I would allow <i>Velocity Control</i> to be cast reflexively, otherwise you'd have to hold precast it on the projectile you want to affect or hold your action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:31:34-07:00","id":1383202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383172#post1383172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reflexive casting is +2 reach and a mana, you don't need to spend a reach on Instant Casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What page is this on? I assume this works for all spells?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383172#post1383172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Turn Momentum</i> is a bit different, you cast the spell beforehand and get the effects of the spell for the duration. The spell effect is turning aside a number of things equal to potency, by default this requires you to hold your action, for a reach this can be done reflexively. There isn't an option to cast the spell reflexively, only to use its effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in order for this spell to be effective in combat I would need to cast it before I'm attacked, use 3 Reach for Quick Casting, Advanced Duration, and Reflexive, and THEN I can reflexively deflect a number of projectiles per turn equal to Potency. If I get it as a Rote it's safe to cast, but otherwise even with my Dedicated Tool it will inflict 2 Paradox dice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I imagine it looking something like Fortune from Metal Gear Solid: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/sCUY6q8i3Yw?t=22\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/sCUY6q8i3Yw?t=22</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383172#post1383172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow <i>Velocity Control</i> to be cast reflexively, otherwise you'd have to hold precast it on the projectile you want to affect or hold your action.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I wanted to use this spell to stop a bullet en route to my face, I would need 2 Reach and 1 Mana for reflexive casting. Assuming I have Forces 3 that means I'm overreaching by 1, using my Dedicated Tool reduces Paradox to a chance die (or can I not use any Yantras b/c reflexive?), and it will cost 2 Mana for Reflexive and casting outside my Ruling Arcana. If I make it a Rote, I can do the same for 1 Mana, no Paradox, and I'll have 1 extra Reach. Would applying that to Duration mean I can keep stopping bullets reflexively on subsequent turns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:14:41-07:00","id":1383214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383202#post1383202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What page is this on? I assume this works for all spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not on any specific page and it does not work for all spells, but all spells that have it as an option have it as a +2 Reach +1 Mana option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in order for this spell to be effective in combat I would need to cast it before I'm attacked, use 3 Reach for Quick Casting, Advanced Duration, and Reflexive, and THEN I can reflexively deflect a number of projectiles per turn equal to Potency. If I get it as a Rote it's safe to cast, but otherwise even with my Dedicated Tool it will inflict 2 Paradox dice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I imagine it looking something like Fortune from Metal Gear Solid: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/sCUY6q8i3Yw?t=22\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/sCUY6q8i3Yw?t=22</a> </div> </div> </div>It would be a number of projectiles equal to potency total, not per turn. And, yes, you can take it as a rote, that's why rotes exist.<br /> <br /> Or you cast it at the beginning of the day, use one reach for Advanced Duration, one for Reflexive, and take a minus two penalty to your roll to increase the Duration factor to a full day. You would then be able to deflect a number of projectiles equal to the potency of the spell reflexively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I wanted to use this spell to stop a bullet en route to my face, I would need 2 Reach and 1 Mana for reflexive casting. Assuming I have Forces 3 that means I'm overreaching by 1, using my Dedicated Tool reduces Paradox to a chance die (or can I not use any Yantras b/c reflexive?), and it will cost 2 Mana for Reflexive and casting outside my Ruling Arcana. If I make it a Rote, I can do the same for 1 Mana, no Paradox, and I'll have 1 extra Reach. Would applying that to Duration mean I can keep stopping bullets reflexively on subsequent turns? </div> </div> </div>2 reach and a mana for reflexive casting, probably another reach for sensory range, you would still be able to use a yantra as long as it wasn't High Speech.<br /> <br /> Duration would just mean the <i>Velocity Control </i>on the object lasts longer. <i>VC </i>is cast on the object, <i>TM</i> is cast on yourself and creates a momentum turning bubble around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-22-2020, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:26:54-07:00","id":1383382,"title":"","content":"Also I would like to add that you need to add Time 1 and an extra reach to stop objects too fast to gain defense against them (like bullets).<br /> I am unsure if this means that then it would count as a combined spell, or if it's just a reach you can take if you have time 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T10:14:22-07:00","id":1383388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383382#post1383382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I would like to add that you need to add Time 1 and an extra reach to stop objects too fast to gain defense against them (like bullets).<br /> I am unsure if this means that then it would count as a combined spell, or if it's just a reach you can take if you have time 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. Combined spells are multiple spells cast as a single spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T13:40:45-07:00","id":1383434,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure I know the answer to this, but I\u2019ll ask anyway just to be sure. If I were to cast First Impressions on a Sleeper, I would incur Paradox, right? If I\u2019m wearing my Dedicated Tool (pendant) I reduce this to a chance roll, but do I have to touch it and wave it around or something, or is just having it on my person enough? Btw, 1 Reach for quick cast during a hand shake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:46:15-07:00","id":1383446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383434#post1383434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure I know the answer to this, but I\u2019ll ask anyway just to be sure. If I were to cast First Impressions on a Sleeper, I would incur Paradox, right? If I\u2019m wearing my Dedicated Tool (pendant) I reduce this to a chance roll, but do I have to touch it and wave it around or something, or is just having it on my person enough? Btw, 1 Reach for quick cast during a hand shake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why it would cause Paradox by casting it on a Sleeper. It's a pretty non-obvious use of magic, unless you were bumping up like...I dunno, someone who's completely repugnant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:52:07-07:00","id":1383447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383434#post1383434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure I know the answer to this, but I\u2019ll ask anyway just to be sure. If I were to cast First Impressions on a Sleeper, I would incur Paradox, right? If I\u2019m wearing my Dedicated Tool (pendant) I reduce this to a chance roll, but do I have to touch it and wave it around or something, or is just having it on my person enough? Btw, 1 Reach for quick cast during a hand shake.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is no, if the mage is a bit smart about it. The Sleeper does not cause Paradox unless they witness something that is obvious magic, so a low Potency First Impressions spell cast subtly (i.e. no High Speech ramblings or brandishing and waving around Tool Yantras) should not cause any problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:23:55-07:00","id":1383613,"title":"","content":"Not exactly a question about the rules. But I remember a while ago that Dave Bradshaw said that the cannon New York City setting was based on someone's Chronicle. <br /> <br /> I tried searching but I couldn't find what he originally said anyone have a link to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:39:21-07:00","id":1383617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1383613#post1383613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly a question about the rules. But I remember a while ago that Dave Bradshaw said that the cannon New York City setting was based on someone's Chronicle.<br /> <br /> I tried searching but I couldn't find what he originally said anyone have a link to that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was Travis Stout's 2e playtest chronicle. And, I believe, his current house game's chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:56:08-07:00","id":1383619,"title":"","content":"Thanks Dave. Sorry I misspelled your name. Autocorrect changed it and I didn't notice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T13:40:40-07:00","id":1384010,"title":"","content":"For a game I'm running, I'm planning on including a plot with a struggle within the Seers between some who worship the Ruin and the Raptor trying to exacerbate global warming, and some in the Ministry of Mammon who don't want to preserve the status quo (I'm thinking that if they worship the Ruin and/or the Raptor then the prospect of civilization suffering an apocalypse (Ruin) that forces people to struggle to survive in a harsh environment without modern society to help them (Raptor), may appeal to them.), since one of my PCs has (End Global Warming Using Matter Magic) as an obsession and I wanted them to have an antagonist so that their best bet wouldn't just be &quot;How many advanced scale and duration CO2 to other Nitrogen and Oxygen can I fit into my spell control?&quot;<br /> <br /> But now I'm having trouble figuring out what these Seers (the Raptor[ites?] and Ruin[ists?]) could actually be doing to exacerbate global warming? <br /> <br /> Manipulating business leaders and politicians seems obvious but our game is set in a Midwestern town adjacent to a midsized Southern city, there aren't going to be any ensorcelled oil tycoons or world leaders around. <br /> <br /> So the question is, <b>if you are a mage and an asshole and you want to use your magic to make climate change worse without just telling sleeper leaders to ignore the ill-effects of fossil fuels and animal agriculture, what's your best bet?</b> Are we back to &quot;Transubstantiation all of this Nitrogen into CO2?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:40:51-07:00","id":1384027,"title":"","content":"Probably not a simple question.<br /> <br /> But really it helps a lot to do the more institutional things. Unless you're an archmage who can make changes that affect the world on a world-wide scale, you'd be severely limited if you just decided to 'make pollution via magic.' Your better bet is social stuff, amplified by Mind and whatever spells you need, to do things like encourage certain lobbys, lower regulations for certain things, make fake companies to sell environmental credits to polluting companies, encourage social media pushes attacking significant people or studies regarding climate change. Basically find existing institutions and help them (if they're adding to climate change) or hinder them (if they're fighting it).<br /> <br /> Worse comes to worse or you want to really get crazy with it then you can probably find look up the plots of the villains in Captain Planet and emulate them. It's easier to solve, is the problem. A monster that eats trees and craps coal is more fun to look at but would probably be solved sooner than something like an entire country opening themselves to dumping the world's nuclear waste, which would require a lot of fiddling around with the government and bureaucracy to fix, especially if people have no incentive to fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-26-2020, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:34:38-07:00","id":1384045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384027#post1384027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not a simple question.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I had that thought almost immediately after posting. D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But really it helps a lot to do the more institutional things. Unless you're an archmage who can make changes that affect the world on a world-wide scale, you'd be severely limited if you just decided to 'make pollution via magic.' Your better bet is social stuff, amplified by Mind and whatever spells you need, to do things like encourage certain lobbys, lower regulations for certain things, make fake companies to sell environmental credits to polluting companies, encourage social media pushes attacking significant people or studies regarding climate change. Basically find existing institutions and help them (if they're adding to climate change) or hinder them (if they're fighting it).<br /> <br /> Worse comes to worse or you want to really get crazy with it then you can probably find look up the plots of the villains in Captain Planet and emulate them. It's easier to solve, is the problem. A monster that eats trees and craps coal is more fun to look at but would probably be solved sooner than something like an entire country opening themselves to dumping the world's nuclear waste, which would require a lot of fiddling around with the government and bureaucracy to fix, especially if people have no incentive to fix it. </div> </div> </div>I figure that any Seers who want to manipulate people to this end would probably want to hang out in DC, New York, Brussels, various national capitols but the social media thing could work for a setting with less politically powerful sleepers around. Can you use a basilisk yantra on the internet?<br /> <br /> I actually may take a look at some Captain Planet plot synopses, no reason ExxarchMobil can't have multiple irons in the fire.<br /> <br /> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:42:51-07:00","id":1384055,"title":"","content":"Sould the entity created with Psychic Genesis have access to any Influence and numina that a goetia could have without limitation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T18:12:53-07:00","id":1384066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384055#post1384055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sould the entity created with Psychic Genesis have access to any Influence and numina that a goetia could have without limitation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, so long as the Influence or Numen is thematically appropriate. Keep in mind there are some balancing factors:<br /> <br /> - To make them reasonably powerful, you need to invoke Paradox by Reaching for Rank 2. The only way to avoid it is via ritual casting, but even then their lifetime is a couple of turns.<br /> <br /> - For the reason above, relinquishing unsafely is not advisable.<br /> <br /> - They only get Enhance or Manipulate, Rank 3 and Control would take an additional spell.<br /> <br /> - Without a conjunctional Mind &amp; Spirit spell, they get no Manifestations.<br /> <br /> - They still bleed Essence and cannot actively restock like spirits.<br /> <br /> So similar to creating a Hallow, getting the most out of the spell is an entire mystical logistics problem. You do get far more loyal and stable beings than spirits, which can be very useful.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the improvised version would be used to generally create sentient unseen servants with Dissonance free abilities. <br /> <br /> No matter the option chosen, casters still have to deal with an Act of Hubris from creating sentient life, plus more from any breaking point the ephemeral powers cause to Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-26-2020, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:11:51-07:00","id":1384085,"title":"","content":"Actually that created a question, that I may know the answer to.<br /> <br /> If a Seer wanted to gaslight people on social media using magic, what is the Arcana for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:19:16-07:00","id":1384237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384085#post1384085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that created a question, that I may know the answer to.<br /> <br /> If a Seer wanted to gaslight people on social media using magic, what is the Arcana for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind and/or Forces depending on strategy employed. Space, optionally.<br /> <br /> Forces alone can allow a spell cast with Scope to create a number of accounts that appear a certain way. <br /> <br /> Mind alone can simply make them think things that are not so, and one could (theoretically) set up some appropriate mundane online nonsense as an Environmental Yantra on such an attack.You'd likely want Space to do that remotely.<br /> <br /> Using Mind with Forces conjunctionally could allow casting on them through a network, presumably. Not recalling off the top of my head if 2e still has the network-as-an-independent-entity/symbol thing the Free Council used in the 1e setting. If not, you'd probably need to toss in Space for the Sympathetic attainment, but you could create a mental illusion.<br /> <br /> The Mind options could simply crack their sanity. It really wouldn't be significantly harder. I don't figure Seers gaslight much with magic except as they are feeling impish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:43:41-07:00","id":1384246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384085#post1384085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that created a question, that I may know the answer to.<br /> <br /> If a Seer wanted to gaslight people on social media using magic, what is the Arcana for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think Prime, Prime 3 would be able to make an untrue thing seem true and Prime 2 would be able to hide the falsity of a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:31:32-07:00","id":1384307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384246#post1384246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would think Prime, Prime 3 would be able to make an untrue thing seem true and Prime 2 would be able to hide the falsity of a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True.<br /> <br /> Yet another approach would be Spirit, where you pay/force a spirit of technology or social media to bedevil their interactions.<br /> <br /> Death could <i>possibly</i> pull the same thing off, but that seems more of a stretch.<br /> <br /> Fate might even be called in to serve if you wanted to make their hits tend towards things that shake their understanding. They could &quot;happen&quot; to run into those with the views that you want to suggest, etc..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:29:38-07:00","id":1384427,"title":"","content":"Probably this has been adressed in the thread &quot;What is &quot;obvious&quot; magic in 2ed?&quot; but i can t find a specific answer.<br /> Example 1: medieval times, some people witness a magical effect, but it is performed by a renowned saint and it appears as a canonical miracle.<br /> Considering that the witnesses have all a sincere faith, would they consider the event supernatural (and so obvious magic) or the way things normally work (and so no magic)?<br /> Example 2: a sleeper is raised in a society were mages secretly cast &quot;fireball&quot; everytime someone point a finger and says &quot;burn&quot;.<br /> Would the sleeper believe that everyone's ability to cast fireball in that way is normal (and so not magic)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:34:19-07:00","id":1384428,"title":"","content":"Unless things have changed in 2nd Edition (I'm not 100% up to snuff on it yet) the belief system of the sleeper doesn't factor in as if something is subtle or vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:36:50-07:00","id":1384430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384427#post1384427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably this has been adressed in the thread &quot;What is &quot;obvious&quot; magic in 2ed?&quot; but i can t find a specific answer.<br /> Example 1: medieval times, some people witness a magical effect, but it is performed by a renowned saint and it appears as a canonical miracle.<br /> Considering that the witnesses have all a sincere faith, would they consider the event supernatural (and so obvious magic) or the way things normally work (and so no magic)?<br /> Example 2: a sleeper is raised in a society were mages secretly cast &quot;fireball&quot; everytime someone point a finger and says &quot;burn&quot;.<br /> Would the sleeper believe that everyone's ability to cast fireball in that way is normal (and so not magic)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obvious magic is magic done in their presence that they can detect with their senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:39:33-07:00","id":1384432,"title":"","content":"If the Sleeper recognises that something is supernatural, it's going to cause Paradox regardless of whether the Sleeper has been conditioned to accept it or if that kind of effect has been normalised. The second example could theoretically avoid Paradox, but only if the Sleeper has a non-magical explanation for why people can cast fireballs. It's close to practically impossible, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-28-2020, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T10:02:10-07:00","id":1384434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384432#post1384432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Sleeper recognises that something is supernatural, it's going to cause Paradox regardless of whether the Sleeper has been conditioned to accept it or if that kind of effect has been normalised. The second example could theoretically avoid Paradox, but only if the Sleeper has a non-magical explanation for why people can cast fireballs. It's close to practically impossible, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That s exactly what i m trying to understand.<br /> Core book says that the sleeper must recognize the event as supernatural to qualify as obvious magic.<br /> Then all natural events are not registered as magic.<br /> A miracle is natural for a devote believer?<br /> If anyone can do a trick is that trick natural?<br /> <br /> Belief must depend on witness, a modern man seeing a mage turning on a discharged lighter with Force would not suspect a supernatural event, but a primitive man living in a forest would!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T10:50:30-07:00","id":1384443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384434#post1384434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That s exactly what i m trying to understand.<br /> Core book says that the sleeper must recognize the event as supernatural to qualify as obvious magic.<br /> Then all natural events are not registered as magic.<br /> A miracle is natural for a devote believer?<br /> If anyone can do a trick is that trick natural?<br /> <br /> Belief must depend on witness, a modern man seeing a mage turning on a discharged lighter with Force would not suspect a supernatural event, but a primitive man living in a forest would!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sleeper must recognize the event AND the event must be Supernal, the Sleeper doesn't have to recognize the event <i>as</i> Supernal.<br /> <br /> When determining if something is obvious magic ask yourself two questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is this a spell as opposed to an attainment or secondary consequence of a spell (a lasting effect)?<br /> 2) Can a Sleeper perceive it?<br /> <br /> If the answer to both is &quot;yes&quot; then it is obvious magic <i>whether or not the Sleeper believes </i><i>disbelieves in magic. </i>Ascension is the game that cares about belief, not Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:10:24-07:00","id":1384448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384434#post1384434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That s exactly what i m trying to understand.<br /> Core book says that the sleeper must recognize the event as supernatural to qualify as obvious magic.<br /> Then all natural events are not registered as magic.<br /> A miracle is natural for a devote believer?<br /> If anyone can do a trick is that trick natural?<br /> <br /> Belief must depend on witness, a modern man seeing a mage turning on a discharged lighter with Force would not suspect a supernatural event, but a primitive man living in a forest would!</div> </div> </div> </div>A miracle is by definition supernatural. (Not technically, but technically nothing can actually be supernatural so that's not a helpful perspective.) If the Sleeper believe they're witnessing a miracle, then they have recognised something as supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384443#post1384443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleeper must recognize the event AND the event must be Supernal, the Sleeper doesn't have to recognize the event <i>as</i> Supernal.<br /> <br /> When determining if something is obvious magic ask yourself two questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is this a spell as opposed to an attainment or secondary consequence of a spell (a lasting effect)?<br /> 2) Can a Sleeper perceive it?<br /> <br /> If the answer to both is &quot;yes&quot; then it is obvious magic <i>whether or not the Sleeper believes </i><i>disbelieves in magic. </i>Ascension is the game that cares about belief, not Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sleeper needs to <i>recognise it as magic</i>. It's not enough to just see it. For example, if a Sleeper watches a mage cast a spell to turn on the light without touching the switch, that spell would suffer Paradox. If the Sleeper doesn't see what the mage is doing and can justify the light suddenly turning on as the mage flicking the switch, then that spell no longer would suffer Paradox. In both cases the Sleeper would see the effects of the spell, but in only one of them would the Sleeper recognise it as supernatural. See the sidebar &quot;Obvious magic&quot; on page 298.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:54:31-07:00","id":1384465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384448#post1384448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleeper needs to <i>recognise it as magic</i>. It's not enough to just see it. For example, if a Sleeper watches a mage cast a spell to turn on the light without touching the switch, that spell would suffer Paradox. If the Sleeper doesn't see what the mage is doing and can justify the light suddenly turning on as the mage flicking the switch, then that spell no longer would suffer Paradox. In both cases the Sleeper would see the effects of the spell, but in only one of them would the Sleeper recognise it as supernatural. See the sidebar &quot;Obvious magic&quot; on page 298.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, no, the Sleeper would not see the spell or the effects of the spell (the switch flipping), they'd see the lasting consequences of the spell (the light turning on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:06:12-07:00","id":1384470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384434#post1384434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That s exactly what i m trying to understand.<br /> Core book says that the sleeper must recognize the event as supernatural to qualify as obvious magic.<br /> Then all natural events are not registered as magic.<br /> A miracle is natural for a devote believer?<br /> If anyone can do a trick is that trick natural?<br /> <br /> Belief must depend on witness, a modern man seeing a mage turning on a discharged lighter with Force would not suspect a supernatural event, but a primitive man living in a forest would!</div> </div> </div> </div>Your lighter example though is a mage trying to hide magic in a vein that would be accepted by Witnesses. I'm amazed trying to do the same thing with primitive man would try something like banging Flint against something for the example. But even so unless it was a time where lighters never existed I would say that even primitive man who's never seen a lighter isn't going to cause a paradox from the example you cited. The way I would describe it is that they're sort of inertia to the Fallen World. Anything that is possible under the rules of the Fallen world is seen as subtle no matter the case of the sleeper viewer.<br /> <br /> Looking back at your example of someone who's lived in a society that could somehow throw Fireballs with a point of their finger, now you're talking more about the concept of Sleepwalker families and that like. A concentrated effort to create someone who can view the Suprernal without the Lie coming in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:06:43-07:00","id":1384471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384443#post1384443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sleeper must recognize the event AND the event must be Supernal, the Sleeper doesn't have to recognize the event <i>as</i> Supernal.<br /> <br /> When determining if something is obvious magic ask yourself two questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is this a spell as opposed to an attainment or secondary consequence of a spell (a lasting effect)?<br /> 2) Can a Sleeper perceive it?<br /> <br /> If the answer to both is &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot; then it is obvious magic <i>whether or not the Sleeper believes </i><i>disbelieves in magic. </i>Ascension is the game that cares about belief, not Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I m aware of the differences with ascension.<br /> I m not saying &quot;this sleeper believe in magic, so he doesn t cause paradox if magic conform to his beliefs&quot;<br /> But corebook says that the sleeper must recognise the spell as something that violates a natural law, in other words supernatural.<br /> My doubt are only on the definition of supernatural, because the knowledge of natural laws are dependent on personal experience and education.<br /> Hypnosys is a good example, as it is a natural phenomenon but poorly understood by many people.<br /> A mage using mind to put someone to sleep IN FACT violates a natural law but a man who know how hypnosys work broadly would not consider it impossible.<br /> But a psychologist who know EXACTLY how hypnosys works would recognise that a man cannot hypnotise someone just imposing a hand and talking softly, and think how could it be?<br /> <br /> So, returning to Example 1, if the society in which a man is raised teaches that miracles are an expression of divine law, and then normal, how this affect obvious magic recognition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:17:06-07:00","id":1384473,"title":"","content":"I think you're overthinking at to be honest. And confusing a few ideas.<br /> <br /> For example just because to a person Divine Law is normal, doesn't make the event not a supernatural event. If that were the case a mage could walk into an Evangelical Church and do all sorts of types of spellcrafting and be considered just miracles of god. I think that's breaking the system a little bit.<br /> <br /> Like many of said it's not belief that shapes whether something is subtle or vulgar it's the Fallen World, the Abyss, and the Lie.<br /> <br /> While I'll say some unique options to hide vulgar magic can be used in those cases. A mage for example praying for divine intervention and having it heal someone within the confines of a church group might actually work.<br /> <br /> But if you did find some primitive man who's never seen a lighter before and you use forces to create flame of a lighter I wouldn't say that would count as vulgar. The Fallen world as a whole has already accepted that lighter create fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","user":"DeimosMasque","date":".  Fixed some things to make clearer what I mean. 04-28-2020, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:35:12-07:00","id":1384475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384473#post1384473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're overthinking at to be honest. And confusing a few ideas.<br /> <br /> For example just because to a person Divine Law is normal, doesn't make the event not a supernatural event. If that were the case a mage could walk into an Evangelical Church and do all sorts of types of spellcrafting and be considered just miracles of god. I think that's breaking the system a little bit.<br /> <br /> Like many of said it's not belief that shapes whether something is subtle or vulgar it's the Fallen World, the Abyss, and the Lie.<br /> <br /> While I'll say some unique options to hide vulgar magic can be used in those cases. A mage for example praying for divine intervention and having it heal someone within the confines of a church group might actually work.<br /> <br /> But if you did find some primitive man who's never seen a lighter before and you use forces to create flame of a lighter I wouldn't say that would count as vulgar. The Fallen world as a whole has already accepted that lighter create fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>What seems like overthinking is in fact caused by two player of mine arguing about it.<br /> One uses Force magic to cause explosions, masking it as throwing gunpowder in a fire (but it s just sand).<br /> Another one is widely recognized as a saint and says that as the church states that saints can heal the sick, this is not magic.<br /> The first says that technology is based on natural laws, so it can t be recognised as supernatural.<br /> The second responds that in medieval times theology was more recognised as natural than science (because Paternoster ministry heavily integrated it in the Lie), so miraclez are natural and science is magic for superstitious people.<br /> What can i answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 04-28-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:54:40-07:00","id":1384479,"title":"","content":"That belief doesn't determine Vulgarity, the Fallen World does. Things that mimic things actually possible in the Real World can be used to hide magic. Things that are actually impossible (such as miraculously healing the sick with not even a placebo to hide the act) are Vulgar.<br /> <br /> Also the Paternoster didn't integrate religious dogma and law into the Lie to make their magic easier, they did it to keep people asleep.<br /> <br /> Edit: To put it another way the Fallen World doesn't give a crap if you believe it's possible, it just cares about the fact that it is actually impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:56:17-07:00","id":1384481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384473#post1384473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're overthinking at to be honest. And confusing a few ideas.<br /> <br /> For example just because to a person Divine Law is normal, doesn't make the event not a supernatural event. If that were the case a mage could walk into an Evangelical Church and do all sorts of types of spellcrafting and be considered just miracles of god. I think that's breaking the system a little bit.<br /> <br /> Like many of said it's not belief that shapes whether something is subtle or vulgar it's the Fallen World, the Abyss, and the Lie.<br /> <br /> While I'll say some unique options to hide vulgar magic can be used in those cases. A mage for example praying for divine intervention and having it heal someone within the confines of a church group might actually work.<br /> <br /> But if you did find some primitive man who's never seen a lighter before and you use forces to create flame of a lighter I wouldn't say that would count as vulgar. The Fallen world as a whole has already accepted that lighter create fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, i don t understand why do you think that the primitive man would not cause paradox.<br /> The book says that the act must be a spell and that the witness must recognize it as impossible.<br /> If you think that the Fallen world as a whole decide if something is impossibile, doesn t it contradict this rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:58:20-07:00","id":1384483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384475#post1384475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What seems like overthinking is in fact caused by two player of mine arguing about it.<br /> One uses Force magic to cause explosions, masking it as throwing gunpowder in a fire (but it s just sand).<br /> Another one is widely recognized as a saint and says that as the church states that saints can heal the sick, this is not magic.<br /> The first says that technology is based on natural laws, so it can t be recognised as supernatural.<br /> The second responds that in medieval times theology was more recognised as natural than science (because Paternoster ministry heavily integrated it in the Lie), so miraclez are natural and science is magic for superstitious people.<br /> What can i answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>The one using Forces magic to cause explosions but covering it up with fake gunpowder is distracting Sleepers via sleight of hand, causing them to miss the actual cause of the magic and thus its supernatural nature.<br /> <br /> The would-be saint is banking on people recognizing their works as supernatural.<br /> <br /> The first would not suffer paradox in front of anyone inclined to associate the explosion with the powder into the fire, this would be almost anyone (including those not familiar with gunpowder) because human brains are pretty good at connecting immediate cause and effect (even when they shouldn't). The only time it would fail is if the Sleeper had reason to believe the powder wouldn't cause an explosion and therefor perceive that there was magic.<br /> <br /> The latter would always risk Paradox and cause Quiescence, because the witnesses would know they are witnessing the Supernatural, even if they believe in the supernatural (and miracles are, by definition, supernatural).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:02:23-07:00","id":1384484,"title":"","content":"Like I said partly I'm not entirely up to snuff on 2nd Edition rules yet. So I may be letting 1st edition concepts sneak in here.<br /> <br /> But the way I interpret the impossible rule, is that you are already doing something blatant. IE I snap my fingers and make fire, I lay hands on someone and heal there wounds, I wave my hand and your knife rusts. <br /> <br /> If you are making a plausible attempt to hide your magic then it's already subtle. <br /> <br /> Now if we were talking different time periods and time travel and such I'd make a different argument because in my mind the Fallen World has an inertia to it. A time traveling mage in a different time, I might not allow the lighter trick because they don't exist. <br /> <br /> But I think that's more me than hard rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:20:35-07:00","id":1384488,"title":"","content":"Wait, if i m understanding it righty everyone is saying that in Awakening setting there is only one objective truth at a time, and that it is contained as a symbol in the Supernal realm and that other interpretation are objectively false, even if humanity doesn t know it?<br /> Then the primitive man would not summon paradox because even if he think it is impossible in fact it isn t, right?<br /> And the only way to alter this truth is with Imperial working, so the only way for Example 1 to work would be if in medieval times Paternoster was more powerful and the rule &quot;miracles are normal because the pope say so and the pope is always right&quot; were fully integrated in the Lie and in the Supernal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 04-28-2020, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:40:03-07:00","id":1384522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384488#post1384488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, if i m understanding it righty everyone is saying that in Awakening setting there is only one objective truth at a time, and that it is contained as a symbol in the Supernal realm and that other interpretation are objectively false, even if humanity doesn t know it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. When a Mage performs a spell they are drawing down the Supernal into the Fallen, the <i>Abysss </i>is what prevents that perfect Truth from manifesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then the primitive man would not summon paradox because even if he think it is impossible in fact it isn t, right? </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. If the primitive man were distracted by the show you put on such that he did not notice the actual <i>magic</i>, then there would be no Paradox, even if he didn't understand the scientific principles behind why the distraction is a good one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the only way to alter this truth is with Imperial working, so the only way for Example 1 to work would be if in medieval times Paternoster was more powerful and the rule &quot;miracles are normal because the pope say so and the pope is always right&quot; were fully integrated in the Lie and in the Supernal? </div> </div> </div>Nope. One, it's the way Supernal Truths get filtered through the Abyss into the Fallen that matters <i>vis a vis </i>the Sleeping curse. Two, rewriting the Supernal does not cause a short change in time, it rewrites the entire timeline. If the Paternoster were to rewrite the Supernal the way you describe then the Fallen world and all its denizens would always have worked that way and will always work that way, and history will be completely different to accommodate this now Truth that retroactively always was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T16:35:17-07:00","id":1384530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384475#post1384475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What seems like overthinking is in fact caused by two player of mine arguing about it.<br /> One uses Force magic to cause explosions, masking it as throwing gunpowder in a fire (but it s just sand).<br /> Another one is widely recognized as a saint and says that as the church states that saints can heal the sick, this is not magic.<br /> The first says that technology is based on natural laws, so it can t be recognised as supernatural.<br /> The second responds that in medieval times theology was more recognised as natural than science (because Paternoster ministry heavily integrated it in the Lie), so miraclez are natural and science is magic for superstitious people.<br /> What can i answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who doesn't know about explosives would cause Paradox in the first place, because for them it's obvious magic they can't rationalise.<br /> The thaumaturge would also cause Paradox because miracles aren't natural no matter how much people might believe them to be so. The Sundered World gives us a clear example of a similar situation: Sleepers know that magic exists, and thus it's &quot;natural&quot; to them, but mages still need to work their magic in private because Sleeper onlookers still cause Paradox for obvious magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384465#post1384465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, no, the Sleeper would not see the spell or the effects of the spell (the switch flipping), they'd see the lasting consequences of the spell (the light turning on).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not lasting. The light switch is still off, and the light will turn off once the spell ends. Regardless, the immediate consequences of magic should still cause Paradox even if the spell is just &quot;electricity flows through this wire&quot; and the light is a natural consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-28-2020, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T19:40:43-07:00","id":1384544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384530#post1384530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not lasting. The light switch is still off, and the light will turn off once the spell ends. Regardless, the immediate consequences of magic should still cause Paradox even if the spell is just &quot;electricity flows through this wire&quot; and the light is a natural consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you meant telekinetically throwing the switch. If the switch is off and the Sleeper notices after the fact it will still suffer dissonance and cause quiescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:33:56-07:00","id":1384568,"title":"","content":"Shadows deny visual information to a certain degree, but Death should be able to make this effect stronger. What practice would be required for a target to become invisible in half light or only when covered in shadows ? Compelling ? Ruling ? Veiling perhaps ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:56:24-07:00","id":1384573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384568#post1384568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadows deny visual information to a certain degree, but Death should be able to make this effect stronger. What practice would be required for a target to become invisible in half light or only when covered in shadows ? Compelling ? Ruling ? Veiling perhaps ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think veiling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T22:57:23-07:00","id":1384577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384522#post1384522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. When a Mage performs a spell they are drawing down the Supernal into the Fallen, the <i>Abysss </i>is what prevents that perfect Truth from manifesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not exactly. If the primitive man were distracted by the show you put on such that he did not notice the actual <i>magic</i>, then there would be no Paradox, even if he didn't understand the scientific principles behind why the distraction is a good one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nope. One, it's the way Supernal Truths get filtered through the Abyss into the Fallen that matters <i>vis a vis </i>the Sleeping curse. Two, rewriting the Supernal does not cause a short change in time, it rewrites the entire timeline. If the Paternoster were to rewrite the Supernal the way you describe then the Fallen world and all its denizens would always have worked that way and will always work that way, and history will be completely different to accommodate this now Truth that retroactively always was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I m confused by your words &quot;distract him from the actual magic&quot;.<br /> The primitive man sees a man creating fire pushing the lighter button, for him if another mages points a wand and says FIRE it s the same, he would think &quot;those men are creating fire with their magic sticks&quot;.<br /> <br /> But i get what you are saying about the Abyss filtering supernal truth.<br /> It is still not clear to me how the Lie works.<br /> What/who defines the truth filtered by the Abyss at a given time?<br /> The Lie is constant and don t variate in time or it is influenced by technology and phylosopical variations (integrated in the society by Exarchs and their cults)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T23:08:29-07:00","id":1384580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384530#post1384530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone who doesn't know about explosives would cause Paradox in the first place, because for them it's obvious magic they can't rationalise.<br /> The thaumaturge would also cause Paradox because miracles aren't natural no matter how much people might believe them to be so. The Sundered World gives us a clear example of a similar situation: Sleepers know that magic exists, and thus it's &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; to them, but mages still need to work their magic in private because Sleeper onlookers still cause Paradox for obvious magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not lasting. The light switch is still off, and the light will turn off once the spell ends. Regardless, the immediate consequences of magic should still cause Paradox even if the spell is just &amp;quot;electricity flows through this wire&amp;quot; and the light is a natural consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is a contradiction.<br /> In the case of explosive paradox is defined by what people Belief is possible, in the case of miracles it is not important what people Belief?<br /> In both cases i m using magic, not a natural law (i m throwing sand in fire, not gunpowder), but in the first i persuade people that i m using a natural law, then why i can t do the same in the second case (for this people theology is the way the world function, it is their &quot;science&quot;)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T03:51:08-07:00","id":1384612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384580#post1384580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is a contradiction.<br /> In the case of explosive paradox is defined by what people Belief is possible, in the case of miracles it is not important what people Belief?<br /> In both cases i m using magic, not a natural law (i m throwing sand in fire, not gunpowder), but in the first i persuade people that i m using a natural law, then why i can t do the same in the second case (for this people theology is the way the world function, it is their &quot;science&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're trying to explain away the magic by saying it's magic. That still makes it magic in the eyes of the Sleepers regardless of whether they've internalised it as natural law or not (see my comment about the Sundered World). You need to explain away the magic with an actual natural law.<br /> <br /> In both cases anyone who recognises a spell as impossible (regardless of whether or not it actually is) would cause Paradox.<br /> In both cases anyone who recognises a spell as magic (regardless of whether or not they've internalised that magic as a natural law) would cause Paradox.<br /> In both cases anyone who assumes the spell follows an actual natural law would not cause Paradox because they have not recognised it as supernatural.<br /> Belief alone does not factor into it; it's about perception and recognition (although belief, as well as education, can and does change the circumstances under which people recognises magic).<br /> <br /> Do note that just because an explosion can be explained away through mundane explosives doesn't mean all explosions are Paradox free. If a Sleeper has no reason to suspect explosives in an area, any explosions there would still be unexplained by them, and the belief of placed explosives will instead be the natural justification after the fact. Throwing sand into the fire is a great way to provide the explanation for any Sleepers who can extrapolate from that, but only if the force of the explosion corresponds to the &quot;explosives&quot; used. So not an actual explosion; more like a fireball from deflagration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T04:11:33-07:00","id":1384615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384612#post1384612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're trying to explain away the magic by saying it's magic. That still makes it magic in the eyes of the Sleepers regardless of whether they've internalised it as natural law or not (see my comment about the Sundered World). You need to explain away the magic with an actual natural law.<br /> <br /> In both cases anyone who recognises a spell as impossible (regardless of whether or not it actually is) would cause Paradox.<br /> In both cases anyone who recognises a spell as magic (regardless of whether or not they've internalised that magic as a natural law) would cause Paradox.<br /> In both cases anyone who assumes the spell follows an actual natural law would not cause Paradox because they have not recognised it as supernatural.<br /> Belief alone does not factor into it; it's about perception and recognition (although belief, as well as education, can and does change the circumstances under which people recognises magic).<br /> <br /> Do note that just because an explosion can be explained away through mundane explosives doesn't mean all explosions are Paradox free. If a Sleeper has no reason to suspect explosives in an area, any explosions there would still be unexplained by them, and the belief of placed explosives will instead be the natural justification after the fact. Throwing sand into the fire is a great way to provide the explanation for any Sleepers who can extrapolate from that, but only if the force of the explosion corresponds to the &amp;quot;explosives&amp;quot; used. So not an actual explosion; more like a fireball from deflagration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you in all points but the definition of magic.<br /> In the example of Vinca culture paradox occours because even if people believe in magic they recognize it as supernatural, because only special people can do it and it defy the rules of the world as they know it.<br /> In the case of miracles in medieval time it appears that you think that people saw God and its rules as a magical thing, am i right?<br /> I don t think that theologians of that time approached divine law under a mystical tone, they genuinely considered divine intervention on the same guise as modern thermodynamic.<br /> I think that my confusion derive by a lack of understanding on how the Lie actually works, and i really need to clarify it to define correctly what &quot;obvious magic&quot; is.<br /> But i understand that it would no more be a simple question, so i think i will create a new thread to discuss it with whoever is not bored by this discussion ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T08:11:49-07:00","id":1384652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384615#post1384615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you in all points but the definition of magic.<br /> In the example of Vinca culture paradox occours because even if people believe in magic they recognize it as supernatural, because only special people can do it and it defy the rules of the world as they know it.<br /> In the case of miracles in medieval time it appears that you think that people saw God and its rules as a magical thing, am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>In both cases there are special people who can work wonders. In both examples Sleepers would consider it natural because they &quot;know&quot; that's how the world works. In both cases the special people do things that breaks the rules of the world. It's basically the same thing, except the medieval example adds a step of belief in a different power behind the thaumaturge, but that step doesn't change anything relevant.<br /> You're getting caught up on whether the Sleeper believes their explanation is natural or not, rather than whether it actually <i>is</i> natural or not. The Vinca example proves that the belief that a mage's magic is natural does not matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384615#post1384615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of miracles in medieval time it appears that you think that people saw God and its rules as a magical thing, am i right?<br /> <br /> I don t think that theologians of that time approached divine law under a mystical tone, they genuinely considered divine intervention on the same guise as modern thermodynamic.<br /> I think that my confusion derive by a lack of understanding on how the Lie actually works, and i really need to clarify it to define correctly what &quot;obvious magic&quot; is.<br /> But i understand that it would no more be a simple question, so i think i will create a new thread to discuss it with whoever is not bored by this discussion ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not have used the word &quot;magical&quot; since magic is witchcraft and witchcraft is evil, but I absolutely do think people had a concept about what's mundane and what's not. What's not mundane would be supernatural because that's the general meaning of the word. (I ignore the literal meaning because it's an oxymoron and not helpful in any discussion.)<br /> If it helps, replace every instance of &quot;natural&quot; with &quot;mundane&quot; and every instance of &quot;supernatural&quot; and &quot;magical&quot; with &quot;extra-mundane&quot; in my posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T08:32:24-07:00","id":1384653,"title":"","content":"How close do you need to be to a phenomenon to use focused mage sight to study it?<br /> <br /> If an effect is impacting a wide enough area that you can see it from say, half a mile a way, can you used FMS from that distance to learn what is going on, or do you have to actually approach it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T09:29:34-07:00","id":1384657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSV_FOtNMC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384653#post1384653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How close do you need to be to a phenomenon to use focused mage sight to study it?<br /> <br /> If an effect is impacting a wide enough area that you can see it from say, half a mile a way, can you used FMS from that distance to learn what is going on, or do you have to actually approach it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can sense it you can use FMS on it. If I wanted a pc to get closer to my massive Mystery that they can safely analyze with FMS from a half a mile away then I'd lock the Opacity to the distance I want them to actually be at from it. So, say I have a Mystery they can see from a half a mile away. I'll let them get through a level of Opacity, give them some info, and also tell them, you can find out more if you get closer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:36:48-07:00","id":1384664,"title":"","content":"Can a mage use hand and body movements as a yantra? Stuff like, using one's fingers to &quot;draw&quot; high speech runes in the air or physically &quot;pushing&quot; when trying to use telekinesis, or dancing. If yes, what kind of yantra would it be, and how would you use it rules-wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:43:44-07:00","id":1384665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384664#post1384664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage use hand and body movements as a yantra? Stuff like, using one's fingers to &quot;draw&quot; high speech runes in the air or physically &quot;pushing&quot; when trying to use telekinesis, or dancing. If yes, what kind of yantra would it be, and how would you use it rules-wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mudra<br /> <br /> Quick edit: Dancing could also fit under Techn\u00e9 with that focus.<br /> No drawing High Speech runes in the air, though. You could either speak High Speech (Mantra) or draw them properly (Runes). The point is for High Speech to actually be expressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:47:24-07:00","id":1384668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384665#post1384665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mudra<br /> <br /> Quick edit: Dancing could also fit under Techn\u00e9 with that focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Tessie<br /> <br /> Can a mudra yantra exist outside of a rote? If yes, how would it function? Could it just give a normal +1 die bonus?<br /> If not, could it just be considered an Action Yantra, like High Speech and Concentration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:48:44-07:00","id":1384669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384668#post1384668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks Tessie<br /> <br /> Can a mudra yantra exist outside of a rote?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's something about that in SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:49:07-07:00","id":1384670,"title":"","content":"The Mudra draws from memorisation. There can be no memorisation of spells that haven't been studied and learnt, and spells that are studied and learnt are Rotes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mrmdubois is right. Signs of Sorcery does have something similar based on transferring memorised techniques from one spell to another, but with a drop in effectiveness since you're basically creating two imagos at once. The improvised spell needs to be of the same Arcanum and Practice, and the spell you draw from is still a Rote that you have learnt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:55:39-07:00","id":1384672,"title":"","content":"When I said &quot;drawing&quot; High Speech runes, I didn't mean using High Speech or Runes as a yantra, just mentally drawing them as part of forming an Imago, and maybe using your hands as an aid to do that. I'm looking to sort of use these movements as a &quot;tool&quot; through the Broad Dedication Merit in SoS, I'm not actually trying to benefit from the die bonuses by using this thing as a mudra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T12:24:00-07:00","id":1384682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384573#post1384573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would think veiling</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, its an unnatural effect focused on hiding. Cool, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:19:35-07:00","id":1384687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384672#post1384672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said &quot;drawing&quot; High Speech runes, I didn't mean using High Speech or Runes as a yantra, just mentally drawing them as part of forming an Imago, and maybe using your hands as an aid to do that. I'm looking to sort of use these movements as a &quot;tool&quot; through the Broad Dedication Merit in SoS, I'm not actually trying to benefit from the die bonuses by using this thing as a mudra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you don't need to talk to use High Speech. Any form of communication, even body language can convey it. So yeah, hand gestures and stuff works, you don't even need the Broad Dedication Merit to use High Speech in that way for your spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:46:24-07:00","id":1384692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384687#post1384687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, you don't need to talk to use High Speech. Any form of communication, even body language can convey it. So yeah, hand gestures and stuff works, you don't even need the Broad Dedication Merit to use High Speech in that way for your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think only spoken and written High Speech is described in the books. Regardless, it's only those two forms that can be used as Yantras (Mantra and Runes). If you could convey High Speech through body language, you'd get no bonus for attempting to use it as a Yantra. It's simply worthless unless you've taken Broad Dedication and can convey High Speech through body language (which I'm not convinced of) as a Dedicated Tool that you'd actually gain anything from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:19:36-07:00","id":1384702,"title":"","content":"Regardless of High Speech though, I think there should be some way to incorporate actual body movement of some kind (as opposed to the mnemonic techniques of a rote) as a yantra in a spell, considering that so many other things can serve as yantra.<br /> <br /> Both Mantras and Concentration are under the Actions category, so I'm guessing that other types of Actions could find their way into the yantra family. My idea, based on my interpretation of the book and the things said in this conversation so far, is that it could be another type of Action yantra. Thoughts on that?<br /> <br /> (The whole idea of &quot;drawing&quot; glyphs and runes in the air was just an attempt to give body movement some extra symbolism relevant to a particular character. There is no attempt to somehow tie it to High Speech or Runes mechanically.)<br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the Broad Dedication Merit is irrelevant in regards to whether body movement can be a yantra or not, its only function is to turn it into a dedicated &quot;tool&quot; IF it can first be a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 04-29-2020, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:39:52-07:00","id":1384705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of High Speech though, I think there should be some way to incorporate actual body movement of some kind (as opposed to the mnemonic techniques of a rote) as a yantra in a spell, considering that so many other things can serve as yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way mudras are described in the fiction often doesn't seem very much like how Rotes are described. There are a few instances that describe it as a sort of sign-language version of High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:47:32-07:00","id":1384708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of High Speech though, I think there should be some way to incorporate actual body movement of some kind (as opposed to the mnemonic techniques of a rote) as a yantra in a spell, considering that so many other things can serve as yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned before, that's Techn\u00e9 (and, to a less versatile extent, Adamant Hand) \u2014 turning the use of a particular form of action into an Order Tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:02:13-07:00","id":1384713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of High Speech though, I think there should be some way to incorporate actual body movement of some kind (as opposed to the mnemonic techniques of a rote) as a yantra in a spell, considering that so many other things can serve as yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mudra, certain forms of Techn\u00e9, and baking it into a fitting Persona. In the latter case the movements would only be a part of the actual Yantra and not have any meaning on their own (and you'd probably be forced to incorporate those movements anytime you want to cast with your Persona Yantra).<br /> Stretching it even further would be certain Path Tools that are interacted with through dance (though dancing around a pole as a rod type Path Yantra is the only thing that comes to mind, and I'm not sure it's compatible with the given wand/rod symbolism).<br /> <br /> Other than that is starting to come up with homebrew Yantras. Dance could be an Order Tool for a Nameless Order (either one that is a basic benefit, or a more involved Yantra that requires an additional Merit like Adamant Hand) or a minor Legacy Yantra. You could also come up with a Merit that does allow you to express High Speech through body language (with the same benefits and drawbacks of the Mantra). The High Speech Merit would certainly be a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Mantras and Concentration are under the Actions category, so I'm guessing that other types of Actions could find their way into the yantra family. My idea, based on my interpretation of the book and the things said in this conversation so far, is that it could be another type of Action yantra. Thoughts on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately we don't really have many good examples of Action Yantras when it comes to extrapolating new Action Yantras. They're all unique in some way with non-standard benefits and/or drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I believe that the Broad Dedication Merit is irrelevant in regards to whether body movement can be a yantra or not, its only function is to turn it into a dedicated &quot;tool&quot; IF it can first be a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything can be used as a Yantra. The question is whether it grants dice or not. If it doesn't, the Yantra is simply worthless rather than invalid. That allows you to Dedicate any object you want, including objects that are normally never used as Tool Yantras. Broad Dedication would allow the same thing for non-Tool Yantras, which would grant an actual benefit to dancing if it'd otherwise be a worthless Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T16:23:06-07:00","id":1384735,"title":"","content":"Talking about using hand signs for High Speech makes me think of this: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5nNeZIw1vI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5nNeZIw1vI</a><br /> IRL Mage in action: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dz0yEIf7H5g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dz0yEIf7H5g</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T22:24:54-07:00","id":1384774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of High Speech though, I think there should be some way to incorporate actual body movement of some kind (as opposed to the mnemonic techniques of a rote) as a yantra in a spell, considering that so many other things can serve as yantra.<br /> <br /> Both Mantras and Concentration are under the Actions category, so I'm guessing that other types of Actions could find their way into the yantra family. My idea, based on my interpretation of the book and the things said in this conversation so far, is that it could be another type of Action yantra. Thoughts on that?<br /> <br /> (The whole idea of &quot;drawing&quot; glyphs and runes in the air was just an attempt to give body movement some extra symbolism relevant to a particular character. There is no attempt to somehow tie it to High Speech or Runes mechanically.)<br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the Broad Dedication Merit is irrelevant in regards to whether body movement can be a yantra or not, its only function is to turn it into a dedicated &quot;tool&quot; IF it can first be a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are actions you can take that also work as Yantras, yeah, there are examples in the 11Q section and where such info has been provided for other legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T22:27:48-07:00","id":1384777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384692#post1384692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think only spoken and written High Speech is described in the books. Regardless, it's only those two forms that can be used as Yantras (Mantra and Runes). If you could convey High Speech through body language, you'd get no bonus for attempting to use it as a Yantra. It's simply worthless unless you've taken Broad Dedication and can convey High Speech through body language (which I'm not convinced of) as a Dedicated Tool that you'd actually gain anything from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why that would be the case, you couldn't be subtle about it, but if you're using High Speech then you're using High Speech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T05:02:29-07:00","id":1384823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384777#post1384777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why that would be the case, you couldn't be subtle about it, but if you're using High Speech then you're using High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still needs to be spoken vocably and loudly for the Mantra.<br /> Reading through the books again it's pretty clear to me that High Speech is a spoken &quot;language&quot; with the written &quot;script&quot; being a specific permutation. High Speech conveyed through body language or sign language would be a different permutation and most likely require a homebrewed Merit to be used at all. Body/sign language High Speech as a Yantra could be baked into that Merit or be an additional Merit with the first one as a prerequisite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:46:00-07:00","id":1384896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384702#post1384702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of High Speech though, I think there should be some way to incorporate actual body movement of some kind (as opposed to the mnemonic techniques of a rote) as a yantra in a spell, considering that so many other things can serve as yantra.<br /> <br /> Both Mantras and Concentration are under the Actions category, so I'm guessing that other types of Actions could find their way into the yantra family. My idea, based on my interpretation of the book and the things said in this conversation so far, is that it could be another type of Action yantra. Thoughts on that?<br /> <br /> (The whole idea of &quot;drawing&quot; glyphs and runes in the air was just an attempt to give body movement some extra symbolism relevant to a particular character. There is no attempt to somehow tie it to High Speech or Runes mechanically.)<br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the Broad Dedication Merit is irrelevant in regards to whether body movement can be a yantra or not, its only function is to turn it into a dedicated &quot;tool&quot; IF it can first be a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once played a mage who was deaf, and who used what was essentially a sign language variant of High Speech. I made it clear though that to Sleeper witnesses, his gestures looked particularly bizarre, and that to anyone who actually knew sign language, what he was signing came off as gibberish. Unfortunately, the game ended up not lasting long enough to ever see this in action, but maybe that could be something that could work for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:58:27-07:00","id":1384901,"title":"","content":"Lets say two different mages cast Transform Life upon a target and the changes are non-conflicting. For example, mage A adds the ability to breathe underwater and retractable claws, mage B adds kangaroo legs and spider eyes. Would one spell overwrite the other, or are they considered as not affecting the same trait and therefore stack ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-30-2020, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T14:25:51-07:00","id":1384921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384901#post1384901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say two different mages cast Transform Life upon a target and the changes are non-conflicting. For example, mage A adds the ability to breathe underwater and retractable claws, mage B adds kangaroo legs and spider eyes. Would one spell overwrite the other, or are they considered as not affecting the same trait and therefore stack ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow both to be in effect, with a Clash of Wills determining which one takes precedence if any of the alterations are mutually condratictary.<br /> <br /> Trading spell control for versatility is fine, imo, the issue is trading spell control for even more dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:31:58-07:00","id":1384953,"title":"","content":"How obvious does magic have to be to induce Paradox? I brought this up in my First Mage thread, and I know this will be up to my Storyteller but I'm curious to get other opinions. Say a Forces Mage is doing a fire spinning performance (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NG8EEWNevpw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NG8EEWNevpw</a>) and casts Influence Fire with 1 reach for Quick Cast and 1 to increase the size, would this sort of subtle(?) magic in front of Sleepers cause Paradox? If the spell fails, would it just not go off or would it run the risk of going out of control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:46:28-07:00","id":1384956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384921#post1384921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would allow both to be in effect, with a Clash of Wills determining which one takes precedence if any of the alterations are mutually condratictary.<br /> <br /> Trading spell control for versatility is fine, imo, the issue is trading spell control for even more dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:54:15-07:00","id":1384958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384953#post1384953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How obvious does magic have to be to induce Paradox? I brought this up in my First Mage thread, and I know this will be up to my Storyteller but I'm curious to get other opinions. Say a Forces Mage is doing a fire spinning performance (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NG8EEWNevpw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NG8EEWNevpw</a>) and casts Influence Fire with 1 reach for Quick Cast and 1 to increase the size, would this sort of subtle(?) magic in front of Sleepers cause Paradox? If the spell fails, would it just not go off or would it run the risk of going out of control?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it shatters a Sleeper's notion of &quot;the supernatural isn't real&quot;, then it causes Paradox.<br /> <br /> If you use your cellphone to cast Remote Control at sensory range, they may think &quot;its just an app&quot;. If you chant or point a wand at the device and it happens, Paradox.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you get 5 Strength from magic its fine. But if you develop them beyond that, Paradox.<br /> <br /> Luck and emotions are harder to gauge, but yes that one conman could have said just the right thing to sway your friend. That person can just be plain lucky. In those cases, the degree and frequency of these outliers may be the accuser that causes Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-30-2020, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:50:01-07:00","id":1385033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384958#post1384958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, if you get 5 Strength from magic its fine. But if you develop them beyond that, Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually more likely to run into Dissonance than Paradox since magical strength doesn\u2019t have to noticeably alter your body to be applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:56:19-07:00","id":1385035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384953#post1384953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How obvious does magic have to be to induce Paradox? I brought this up in my First Mage thread, and I know this will be up to my Storyteller but I'm curious to get other opinions. Say a Forces Mage is doing a fire spinning performance (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NG8EEWNevpw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NG8EEWNevpw</a>) and casts Influence Fire with 1 reach for Quick Cast and 1 to increase the size, would this sort of subtle(?) magic in front of Sleepers cause Paradox? If the spell fails, would it just not go off or would it run the risk of going out of control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically it\u2019s if you perform magic in front of them and it\u2019s obvious that it\u2019s magic. You could read a dude\u2019s mind Right on front of them and then tell them what they were thinking, the spell if done without Yantras or other giveaways never registers as occurring to them until after it\u2019s come into effect.<br /> <br /> Or for another example you could tell a Sleeper you will cast a spell to create a rainstorm out of nowhere at 8 PM, if you cast the spell behind closed doors it doesn\u2019t risk Paradox from the Sleeper.<br /> <br /> If you look back over this thread just a few pages you\u2019ll see an in depth discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:03:08-07:00","id":1385037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384823#post1384823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still needs to be spoken vocably and loudly for the Mantra.<br /> Reading through the books again it's pretty clear to me that High Speech is a spoken &amp;quot;language&amp;quot; with the written &amp;quot;script&amp;quot; being a specific permutation. High Speech conveyed through body language or sign language would be a different permutation and most likely require a homebrewed Merit to be used at all. Body/sign language High Speech as a Yantra could be baked into that Merit or be an additional Merit with the first one as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>High Speech is the idea of language or communication, it\u2019s a meta concept that Mages naturally interact with, and this level of being \u201cover\u201d language allows you to convey it via any means of communication. The sounds you make when speaking it don\u2019t matter for conveying its meaning. So there\u2019s no reason why you cannot convey your meaning via other methods of communication as well. Making gestures is communicative, and High Speech can be conveyed by it. If you\u2019ve been trained by an Order to use High Speech as a Yantra then any means of producing High Speech will do the job. The restrictions of doing so still apply, you cannot be subtle, your hands and body will jerk and move in odd ways if you gesture in High Speech, but it\u2019s a valid use of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:51:45-07:00","id":1385049,"title":"","content":"The Mantra is explicitly and specifically <i>vocal</i> and <i>loud</i>. If you can express High Speech through different means, it would either have to be a different Yantra or an alteration of the Mantra.<br /> <br /> All language surrounding High Speech in 2e core and SoS exclusively refers to it as a spoken language, except when it refers to runes which are extrapolated from the visual patters that Mana takes when sublimating freely. The fact that written High Speech has an explanation that is more involved than &quot;it can be conveyed through any means of communication&quot; highly implies that's not the case.<br /> I'm not saying High Speech can't be expressed through other means (as you said, it already rides on one form of communication) but it's clear to me that, unlike spoken High Speech, mages have no innate ability to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T03:47:47-07:00","id":1385054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384901#post1384901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say two different mages cast Transform Life upon a target and the changes are non-conflicting. For example, mage A adds the ability to breathe underwater and retractable claws, mage B adds kangaroo legs and spider eyes. Would one spell overwrite the other, or are they considered as not affecting the same trait and therefore stack ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is not permitted.<br /> By rule you cannot cast multple spell for cumulative effect: only the one with more Potency take priority.<br /> You can not benefit from two Honing the Form , for example, at the same time: your tapestry can hold the spells, but only one may be active at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T04:17:35-07:00","id":1385055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385054#post1385054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that is not permitted.<br /> By rule you cannot cast multple spell for cumulative effect: only the one with more Potency take priority.<br /> You can not benefit from two Honing the Form , for example, at the same time: your tapestry can hold the spells, but only one may be active at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When multiple spells affect the same <i>aspect</i> of a character the effects of the spells do not stack, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean you can have multiple Honing the Form if they just increase different Attributes? If not, does that mean you <i>can't</i> have both Honing the Form and Augment Mind (the Mind version that increases Mental and/or Social Attributes) because both increase Attributes? If each Attribute category is considered a single &quot;aspect&quot; for the purposes of spell stacking, could you have two versions of Augment Mind cast on you as long as one only increase Mental Attributes and the other Social Attributes?<br /> <br /> &quot;[..] and instead the spell with the highest Potency takes effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you can't cast Honing the Form twice to raise two different Attributes, can you suppress your increased Strength by increasing your Stamina even further?<br /> If you <i>can</i> increase different Attributes with two castings, what about split Potency? If one spell would increase both Strength and Dexterity by 2, and the second spell would increase Strength by 5, does that mean you lose out on the Dexterity increase? What if the character already had Strength 3 and the second spell didn't include the Reach for increasing about the trait maximum; would the character lose their increased Dexterity without gaining any additional Strength just because the second spell have a higher Potency?<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is that the spell stacking rules are so extremely bare bones that any edge cases (And you don't have to go far to find them: Are two different Attributes different &quot;aspects&quot; of the same character?) can result in multiple rulings and no one could say they go against RAW.<br /> <br /> So on the question &quot;Can you cast Transform Life multiple times on the same subject as long as the added traits doesn't interfere with each other?&quot; I have to answer: No one really knows. I think the best way to handle it is to pick an option and be consistent about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T05:52:41-07:00","id":1385063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385037#post1385037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High Speech is the idea of language or communication, it\u2019s a meta concept that Mages naturally interact with, and this level of being \u201cover\u201d language allows you to convey it via any means of communication. The sounds you make when speaking it don\u2019t matter for conveying its meaning. So there\u2019s no reason why you cannot convey your meaning via other methods of communication as well. Making gestures is communicative, and High Speech can be conveyed by it. If you\u2019ve been trained by an Order to use High Speech as a Yantra then any means of producing High Speech will do the job. The restrictions of doing so still apply, you cannot be subtle, your hands and body will jerk and move in odd ways if you gesture in High Speech, but it\u2019s a valid use of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385049#post1385049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mantra is explicitly and specifically <i>vocal</i> and <i>loud</i>. If you can express High Speech through different means, it would either have to be a different Yantra or an alteration of the Mantra.<br /> <br /> All language surrounding High Speech in 2e core and SoS exclusively refers to it as a spoken language, except when it refers to runes which are extrapolated from the visual patters that Mana takes when sublimating freely. The fact that written High Speech has an explanation that is more involved than &quot;it can be conveyed through any means of communication&quot; highly implies that's not the case.<br /> I'm not saying High Speech can't be expressed through other means (as you said, it already rides on one form of communication) but it's clear to me that, unlike spoken High Speech, mages have no innate ability to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A </span></span></span><b>mantra</b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is a sacred utterance, a numinous</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> sound, a syllable, word or phonemes</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, or group of words in Sanskrit believed by practitioners to have psychological and/or spiritual powers. (Copied from Wikipedia, so take this with a grain of salt)<br /> <br /> So using High Speech as a Mantra specifically asks for the mage to speak the words out loud. However, I would argue that there could be other ways to incorporate the High Language as a yantra, only it would not be High SPEECH. Runes are one of those ways. Transmitting the High Language through body language could be a variation of High Speech with different complications. You would have to perform strange and possibly &quot;unnatural&quot; looking gestures (to a Sleeper's eyes anyway), but it is still a bit more subtle that speaking gibberish out loud. So maybe it could be a Merit that requires you to already possess the High Speech Merit, that would allow a mage to do that. You would possibly still have to spend an extra turn to perform the gestures because of the time limitations of the fallen world, and then it could function in a similar manner as High Speech. I would probably not allow a spell to benefit from both of those uses of High Speech concerning die bonuses, because the idea is that you are still using High Speech, but you have found a different way to express it, other than a Mantra.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1384901#post1384901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say two different mages cast Transform Life upon a target and the changes are non-conflicting. For example, mage A adds the ability to breathe underwater and retractable claws, mage B adds kangaroo legs and spider eyes. Would one spell overwrite the other, or are they considered as not affecting the same trait and therefore stack ?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I would allow that, as long as they affect entirely different traits. For instance, if spell A gives the target claws and spell B gives the target spider legs, that is ok, but if spell A gives the target claws and spell B gives the target's hand membranes that would help them swim better, that might constitute a conflict.<br /> <br /> Similarly with a spell like Hone the form (which was mentioned earlier), I would consider if the changes made by the 2 spells, affect the same parts of the target's body. For instance, if spell A grants increased strength by enhancing the muscles, and spell B grants increased stamina, that might be a conflict, because both spells affect the target's muscles in some way.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 05-01-2020, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:13:03-07:00","id":1385199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385055#post1385055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;When multiple spells affect the same <i>aspect</i> of a character the effects of the spells do not stack, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean you can have multiple Honing the Form if they just increase different Attributes? If not, does that mean you <i>can't</i> have both Honing the Form and Augment Mind (the Mind version that increases Mental and/or Social Attributes) because both increase Attributes? If each Attribute category is considered a single &quot;aspect&quot; for the purposes of spell stacking, could you have two versions of Augment Mind cast on you as long as one only increase Mental Attributes and the other Social Attributes?<br /> <br /> &quot;[..] and instead the spell with the highest Potency takes effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you can't cast Honing the Form twice to raise two different Attributes, can you suppress your increased Strength by increasing your Stamina even further?<br /> If you <i>can</i> increase different Attributes with two castings, what about split Potency? If one spell would increase both Strength and Dexterity by 2, and the second spell would increase Strength by 5, does that mean you lose out on the Dexterity increase? What if the character already had Strength 3 and the second spell didn't include the Reach for increasing about the trait maximum; would the character lose their increased Dexterity without gaining any additional Strength just because the second spell have a higher Potency?<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is that the spell stacking rules are so extremely bare bones that any edge cases (And you don't have to go far to find them: Are two different Attributes different &quot;aspects&quot; of the same character?) can result in multiple rulings and no one could say they go against RAW.<br /> <br /> So on the question &quot;Can you cast Transform Life multiple times on the same subject as long as the added traits doesn't interfere with each other?&quot; I have to answer: No one really knows. I think the best way to handle it is to pick an option and be consistent about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember Dave mentioning that its possible to cast 3 different honing spells, one for each physical attribute without spell stacking and he also mentioned why you would spend reach to improve all 3 with 1 spell because you want to save spell control slots.<br /> <br /> There was a massive argument on discord about if a bonus/penalty counts towards spell stacking though. Does a spell giving +3 strength stack with a spell giving -2 strength or does the +3 strength spell suppress the -2 spell? Personally I think each stat is a separate aspect of a character and +ve or -ve effects count towards spell stacking. Some people think that a bonus is a separate aspect than a penalty though so two bonus's/penalty wont stack, but a bonus and a penalty will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-02-2020, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:31:28-07:00","id":1385203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385063#post1385063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would possibly still have to spend an extra turn to perform the gestures because of the time limitations of the fallen world, and then it could function in a similar manner as High Speech. I would probably not allow a spell to benefit from both of those uses of High Speech concerning die bonuses, because the idea is that you are still using High Speech, but you have found a different way to express it, other than a Mantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would still cost the time delay that High Speech already does, and wouldn't be able to be combined with speaking High Speech. Though it does create a kind of cool image in my head of like...y'know those monks that can make it sound almost like they're multiple people at once using throat singing? Cool aesthetically, but no extra mechanical benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T04:58:54-07:00","id":1385235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385063#post1385063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A <b>mantra</b> is a sacred utterance, a numinous sound, a syllable, word or phonemes, or group of words in Sanskrit believed by practitioners to have psychological and/or spiritual powers. (Copied from Wikipedia, so take this with a grain of salt)<br /> <br /> So using High Speech as a Mantra specifically asks for the mage to speak the words out loud. However, I would argue that there could be other ways to incorporate the High Language as a yantra, only it would not be High SPEECH. Runes are one of those ways. Transmitting the High Language through body language could be a variation of High Speech with different complications. You would have to perform strange and possibly &quot;unnatural&quot; looking gestures (to a Sleeper's eyes anyway), but it is still a bit more subtle that speaking gibberish out loud. So maybe it could be a Merit that requires you to already possess the High Speech Merit, that would allow a mage to do that. You would possibly still have to spend an extra turn to perform the gestures because of the time limitations of the fallen world, and then it could function in a similar manner as High Speech. I would probably not allow a spell to benefit from both of those uses of High Speech concerning die bonuses, because the idea is that you are still using High Speech, but you have found a different way to express it, other than a Mantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is basically what I've already said.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Protip: You can use ctrl+shift+v to paste text without keeping formatting from the source.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T07:55:00-07:00","id":1385242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385235#post1385235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is basically what I've already said.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Protip: You can use ctrl+shift+v to paste text without keeping formatting from the source.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I know, I was supporting that opinion. Just wanted to sum up what was said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 05-02-2020, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T11:30:55-07:00","id":1385276,"title":"","content":"Do you need to spend a reach for each of the advanced factors you want, or one reach affects all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T11:34:26-07:00","id":1385277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385276#post1385276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to spend a reach for each of the advanced factors you want, or one reach affects all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each different Advanced spell factor. Advanced Duration is one Reach, Advanced Potency is another, Advanced Scale is a third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T18:33:57-07:00","id":1385335,"title":"","content":"Another mage sight related question.<br /> <br /> If a mage nonmagically remotely views a supernatural phenomenon will it trigger peripheral mage sight?<br /> <br /> If a mage uses active mage sight in the same situation, will it let them learn more about the phenomenon? I'm assuming focused is right out since you aren't there to force mana through the phenomenon's pattern.<br /> <br /> Example: A bank gets robbed by a man who was under the supernatural influence of and/or being abetted by a greed spirit. The news shows security footage of the man, directly being manipulated by a supernatural force (obviously they don't know this). Does a mage watching this news story have their PMS ping? If they have spirit and mind dots and use spirit and mind mage sight will they be able to see what's going on through the footage? Does it change anything if it's live footage vs a recording or even a photo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T06:18:51-07:00","id":1385397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSV_FOtNMC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385335#post1385335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another mage sight related question.<br /> <br /> If a mage nonmagically remotely views a supernatural phenomenon will it trigger peripheral mage sight?<br /> <br /> If a mage uses active mage sight in the same situation, will it let them learn more about the phenomenon? I'm assuming focused is right out since you aren't there to force mana through the phenomenon's pattern.<br /> <br /> Example: A bank gets robbed by a man who was under the supernatural influence of and/or being abetted by a greed spirit. The news shows security footage of the man, directly being manipulated by a supernatural force (obviously they don't know this). Does a mage watching this news story have their PMS ping? If they have spirit and mind dots and use spirit and mind mage sight will they be able to see what's going on through the footage? Does it change anything if it's live footage vs a recording or even a photo?</div> </div> </div> </div>SoS has this to say about PMS <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage can even see the presence of a Mystery in a<br /> photograph or a video, or through a scrying window or reconstruction of the past via Postcognition or the like. </div> </div> </div>So yes to PMS through a video.<br /> <br /> And this to say about Active Mage sight <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlike Peripheral Mage Sight, Active Mage Sight requires<br /> direct observation of the phenomena in question: it doesn\u2019t<br /> work on recordings or a live television feed. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T14:03:07-07:00","id":1385454,"title":"","content":"What are the 1ed books that can still be used for 2ed Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T20:14:15-07:00","id":1385525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385397#post1385397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SoS has this to say about PMS <br /> <br /> So yes to PMS through a video.<br /> <br /> And this to say about Active Mage sight</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that directly answers the question, thank you!<br /> <br /> It's also interesting that only PMS works. &quot;Some kind of magical BS is happening in this security footage but I have no idea what kind.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T23:21:07-07:00","id":1385548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385454#post1385454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the 1ed books that can still be used for 2ed Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like an answer to this too.<br /> <br /> They're obvious ones like obviously the Tremere do not work the same way anymore.<br /> <br /> Obviously the orders have the same history as they do in their books.<br /> <br /> But what of the mechanics of those books.<br /> <br /> Are Free Council members able to learn the Save Point rote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T12:17:24-07:00","id":1385635,"title":"","content":"I've just read Imperial Mysteries and I'm pretty sure the vast majority could still be used","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26103-alambril","name":"Alambril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T21:46:03-07:00","id":1385999,"title":"","content":"But Imperial Mysteries shows rule sets that don't exist in either base rule set so it's easy to just add it on top.<br /> <br /> But what about the merits and rotes that are in the other books. We have some updated merits, and we know the Legacies need updating. But how easy is it to just grab the merits and rotes from those old books and just use them no changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:03:00-07:00","id":1386003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385548#post1385548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Free Council members able to learn the Save Point rote?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the explicit rules of time travel in 2e? Nah.<br /> <br /> You could rig up a Hung Spell with Conditional Duration and dump a Corridors of Time into that, which produces much the same effect, but that's two spells with an explicit cost of at least 2 Mana each time and it's contingent on keeping track of temporal sympathy on top of being subject to dispellation like any other time travel spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1385999#post1385999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about the merits and rotes that are in the other books. We have some updated merits, and we know the Legacies need updating. But how easy is it to just grab the merits and rotes from those old books and just use them no changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotes don't work the same anymore anyway. Generally speaking when we talk about 1e books still being useful for 2e it's in terms of their utility in understanding the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T23:27:28-07:00","id":1386016,"title":"","content":"That answers my question then. <br /> <br /> Fluff yes.<br /> Crunch no.<br /> <br /> Edit: I actually remember when the Free Council book came out and that Save Point Rote was first read. <br /> <br /> It was a deeply controversial Rote. At that point Time Travel didn't even remotely work that way. And was considered a game breaking Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","user":"DeimosMasque","date":". 05-06-2020, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:49:15-07:00","id":1386092,"title":"","content":"Would a Compelling of Life and Death be sufficient so that, when the caster succeeded in an Intimidation roll, it intensified the fear they created so they could apply a related condition such as Cowed, Spooked, Frightened, Madness or Nightmares ? I am not sure if it would be enough and if it could be applied at the mage rather than the target.<br /> <br /> More specifically, I am trying to see if it could be a viable first Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-06-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:43:26-07:00","id":1386117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1386092#post1386092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Compelling of Life and Death be sufficient so that, when the caster succeeded in an Intimidation roll, it intensified the fear they created so they could apply a related condition such as Cowed, Spooked, Frightened, Madness or Nightmares ? I am not sure if it would be enough and if it could be applied at the mage rather than the target.<br /> <br /> More specifically, I am trying to see if it could be a viable first Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you get an Exceptional Success you either get a Condition or you apply a Condition to someone else. Compelling might reduce the threshold for Exceptional Success to three successes. At least, that's how I'd design a Compelling spell around that idea.<br /> For an Attainment I would instead have it that an intimidating social interaction against a subject would apply a fitting Condition to that subject as long as the Potency (Arcanum dots) exceed the subject's Withstand (in this case Composure). Advanced Duration as a secondary spell factor, after which the Condition fades if not resolved yet. It also fades if the mage applies the Attainment on another subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T11:10:50-07:00","id":1386127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1386117#post1386117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you get an Exceptional Success you either get a Condition or you apply a Condition to someone else. Compelling might reduce the threshold for Exceptional Success to three successes. At least, that's how I'd design a Compelling spell around that idea.<br /> For an Attainment I would instead have it that an intimidating social interaction against a subject would apply a fitting Condition to that subject as long as the Potency (Arcanum dots) exceed the subject's Withstand (in this case Composure). Advanced Duration as a secondary spell factor, after which the Condition fades if not resolved yet. It also fades if the mage applies the Attainment on another subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be more focused on a diplomatic approach. I was thinking more along the lines of the encounter with the Nazgul in Weathertop, something that could be applied in combat to amplify their unnerving presence. Didn't creative thaumaturgy say that Compelling make a nervous person Spooked or a drowsy person asleep ? This would be a specialization of that, perhaps Potency primary, as an AoE with advanced duration and scale. Maybe being restricted to only intensify fear could make up for the extra Reach ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-06-2020, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T09:39:13-07:00","id":1387289,"title":"","content":"It's time for the silly question of the day!<br /> <br /> The rote of Platonic Form can make weapons as well? And a weapon with durability 1, can be used to fight?<br /> <br /> Also how an object made of mana may look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T10:56:42-07:00","id":1387297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387289#post1387289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's time for the silly question of the day!<br /> <br /> The rote of Platonic Form can make weapons as well? And a weapon with durability 1, can be used to fight?<br /> <br /> Also how an object made of mana may look?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it can, but anything more complex, such as a gun, is out of its reach. The weapon will be perfectly usable, just not very durable and it still uses mana per attack, so its not the most cost efficient.<br /> <br /> Without Supernal Veil, its clearly supernatural. This may manifest in different ways depending on the mage. For example, it may appear as its made of pure Aethereal light when used by an Obrimos. But to a Moros it may manifest as a translucent object, like an illusion, but with substance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T12:41:33-07:00","id":1387311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387297#post1387297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed it can, but anything more complex, such as a gun, is out of its reach. The weapon will be perfectly usable, just not very durable and it still uses mana per attack, so its not the most cost efficient.<br /> <br /> Without Supernal Veil, its clearly supernatural. This may manifest in different ways depending on the mage. For example, it may appear as its made of pure Aethereal light when used by an Obrimos. But to a Moros it may manifest as a translucent object, like an illusion, but with substance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this rote but since my english is poor, I still don't understand how attacks an damage works. I assume the standard rules don't apply to it, I'm right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T13:14:37-07:00","id":1387315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387311#post1387311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this rote but since my english is poor, I still don't understand how attacks an damage works. I assume the standard rules don't apply to it, I'm right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potency is allocated to increase the durability, equipment bonus or mana capacity of the item. <br /> <br /> The tool or weapon can be used normally, but each use/attack consumes one mana from its battery. Once either the battery is without mana or the duration ends, then the object vanishes.<br /> <br /> So the challenge is figuring out the right balance for your current needs and how much mana you want to commit to the weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T13:21:48-07:00","id":1387317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387311#post1387311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this rote but since my english is poor, I still don't understand how attacks an damage works. I assume the standard rules don't apply to it, I'm right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Italian?<br /> Il tiro attacco funziona normalmente a seconda della tipologia di arma, per i danni il bonus dell arma parte da +0 letali e puo essere aumentato di 1 per ogni Potency allocato li.<br /> Nota che \u00e8 l unico incantesimo che crea oggetti senza settare come bonus massimo il +5.<br /> Inoltre uno dei reach applicabili fa in modo che tu possa applicare sempre il ritira gli 8 con quell arma.<br /> <br /> I hope i had guessed right with the language","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:07:15-07:00","id":1387339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387317#post1387317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Italian?<br /> Il tiro attacco funziona normalmente a seconda della tipologia di arma, per i danni il bonus dell arma parte da +0 letali e puo essere aumentato di 1 per ogni Potency allocato li.<br /> Nota che \u00e8 l unico incantesimo che crea oggetti senza settare come bonus massimo il +5.<br /> Inoltre uno dei reach applicabili fa in modo che tu possa applicare sempre il ritira gli 8 con quell arma.<br /> <br /> I hope i had guessed right with the language</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I'm italian!<br /> <br /> Se non erro queste armi hanno anche una riserva di mana, ma non sono riuscito a capire a quanto essa ammonti.<br /> <br /> Sorry guys, forgive me for writing in my native language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:03:43-07:00","id":1387363,"title":"","content":"With Imperial Rites, Imperial spells, Imperial practices, etc... What empire are we talking about? Who's the emperor/empress?<br /> <br /> Why is this particular word used for these things?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I wondered if it were bastardized Latin like a number of other Mage terms, but &quot;imperium&quot; seems to be Latin for &quot;government&quot;. Seems like a weird connotation to throw in for archmasters, who are specifically forbidden by the Pax from holding official power in the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 05-10-2020, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:20:30-07:00","id":1387367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387363#post1387363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Imperial Rites, Imperial spells, Imperial practices, etc... What empire are we talking about? Who's the emperor/empress?<br /> <br /> Why is this particular word used for these things?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I wondered if it were bastardized Latin like a number of other Mage terms, but &quot;imperium&quot; seems to be Latin for &quot;government&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its imperium in the sense of command, like in imperative verbs. You aren't just ruling phenomena, recreating or altering them. An archmage is literally commanding essential building blocks of the Tapestry to be redefined to their standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-11-2020, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T18:07:01-07:00","id":1387377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387363#post1387363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Imperial Rites, Imperial spells, Imperial practices, etc... What empire are we talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Recall that the symbol-tyrants with an iron grip on reality are widely rumored to have originally been mages from a retroactively-erased culture (painted in broad strokes that nevertheless discuss its outside in terms where outposts and barbarians come up a lot in the narrative) and are collectively named with a term that means &quot;rule from outside.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Empire that acts of Imperium commands is reality as it is known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T00:55:43-07:00","id":1387659,"title":"","content":"What is the origin Path of the Illumined Path Legacy? 1E had it be Thyrsus. So had 2E core. The example mage in Nameless and Accursed is also Thyrsus and it grants him Prime Ruling, but here it is listed as Obrimos Legacy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T05:47:51-07:00","id":1387691,"title":"","content":"Since the Arrow get a +1 yantra from symbols of attack &amp; defense, would it make sense for one of their combat Legacies to get a +2 for customized weapons or a +3 for those that bear some kind of identifying emblem of the caster (rune on the pommel, coat of arms, the blade has an image of their shadow name, etc) ? The extra difficulty would come from doing the customizing or procuring someone who could do it for them. One key detail is that they are not Matter or Prime focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:14:34-07:00","id":1387705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387691#post1387691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Arrow get a +1 yantra from symbols of attack &amp; defense, would it make sense for one of their combat Legacies to get a +2 for customized weapons or a +3 for those that bear some kind of identifying emblem of the caster (rune on the pommel, coat of arms, the blade has an image of their shadow name, etc) ? The extra difficulty would come from doing the customizing or procuring someone who could do it for them. One key detail is that they are not Matter or Prime focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>If, once procured, the weapons are both reusable and as easy to incorporate as their regular Order Tool, they couldn't be more than +1 Yantras, imo. The difficulty of having to procure them is a negligent drawback if it's not something you have to do for each spell (like Sacraments). Compare to Path Tools that are always +1 despite listing precious metals, gems and even perfected materials as possible materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T08:15:44-07:00","id":1387726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387705#post1387705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If, once procured, the weapons are both reusable and as easy to incorporate as their regular Order Tool, they couldn't be more than +1 Yantras, imo. The difficulty of having to procure them is a negligent drawback if it's not something you have to do for each spell (like Sacraments). Compare to Path Tools that are always +1 despite listing precious metals, gems and even perfected materials as possible materials.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but that would create an overlap with Order tools that would render the yantra useless. If bonuses requiring more than a +1 impose disadvantageous condition, require rare materials or special care, perhaps a +2 could be conferred to one that is both customized and bears their emblem, with a +3 in case its ritually maintained. In essence, I want to incentivize the use of personalized weapons. Similar to how Highlander characters have their own distinctive blades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:26:52-07:00","id":1387795,"title":"","content":"Consider that out of the two regular +3 Yantras, one is having a part of the person you're casting a spell on, and the other requires a non-reusable thing so rare you might want to spend a session obtaining it. I think having such a weapon <i>and</i> spending time to maintain its symbolism (even if it's not part of the spell casting) might turn it to a +2 Yantra. Personally I would rather have the ritual for preparing/maintaining your chosen weapon be a +2 Yantra for the time it takes to perform it.<br /> If the Legacy has Prime, one Attainment could be that the chosen weapon grants 8-Again on spell casting rolls like As Above, So Below (or other Attainments that only work on a specifically prepared weapon). Alternatively, you could have some non-standard requirement/restriction for the Legacy like not being able to dedicate non-weapon Yantras, forcing members to care for a single weapon unless they're okay losing out on not having a Dedicated Tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:49:10-07:00","id":1387813,"title":"","content":"I think I will go with the one about maintaining the symbolism, even though the other ones are also intriguing. Thanks for the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T04:34:19-07:00","id":1387978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387726#post1387726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that would create an overlap with Order tools that would render the yantra useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it might not be a yantra for that legacy. Like, I've been puzzled why the Perfected Adepts don't have any weapon or offensive yantra, but you might have the answer there. An Arrow legacy might not teach those yantras because they're assumed to already know how to wield them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T04:53:05-07:00","id":1387985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387978#post1387978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it might not be a yantra for that legacy. Like, I've been puzzled why the Perfected Adepts don't have any weapon or offensive yantra, but you might have the answer there. An Arrow legacy might not teach those yantras because they're assumed to already know how to wield them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for example, being able to dodge all attacks perfectly would make a cool +2 yantra for the Legacy I am working on (who are very focused on survival and endurance) or to give the Perfected Adepts a reward for Matrix like dodging. But then I thought, &quot;hold on, that overlaps with the Adamantine Hand, doesn't it ?&quot;. I think adding an extra requirement (not taking any damage in this case) might allow it to work. Perhaps coating a weapon in the blood of a wound that caused lethal damage might also work.<br /> <br /> They know how to wield the Order's yantras, but now elevate the practice using their Legacy's focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-13-2020, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:42:02-07:00","id":1388044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1387985#post1387985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps coating a weapon in the blood of a wound that caused lethal damage might also work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the blood qualifies as a +2 sacrament yantra if you qualify that the wound has to come from the mage himself or from a worthy opponent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:38:45-07:00","id":1388056,"title":"","content":"Some questions I've been struggling with:<br /> <br /> The matter 3 spell &quot;Alter Integrity&quot; allows you to make an object more durable than it &quot;naturally&quot; could be. But. It also allows this effect to be made &quot;Lasting&quot;, implying you're giving it a new natural state (despite the state being seemingly unnatural).<br /> <br /> Would this not create a permanent &quot;magic item&quot;? Like, a gold dagger durable enough to scratch a diamond, that doesn't cause paradox and cannot be degraded like most magic effects?<br /> <br /> How does this reconcile with Fallen reality without being in conflict with the &quot;Lasting&quot; rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> How would a sleeper explain coming across bullet proof sheets of paper, without it becoming a scientific mystery showcased with live rounds on the 12 o'clock news?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26162-justaman","name":"Justaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T09:48:36-07:00","id":1388068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388056#post1388056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this reconcile with Fallen reality without being in conflict with the &quot;Lasting&quot; rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane means of reducing Durability exist and more Durable stuff is harder to use Alter Integrity on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would a sleeper explain coming across bullet proof sheets of paper, without it becoming a scientific mystery showcased with live rounds on the 12 o'clock news? </div> </div> </div>By not being in that contrived situation or by shrugging it off and going about their day.<br /> <br /> Weird stuff happens in the Chronicles of Darkness. Most people have fearfully made their peace with it or look to exploit it in secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T15:55:53-07:00","id":1388171,"title":"","content":"The ST and the players must not to let stuff happen in the game that breaks the setting even in cases where the rules would seem to allow it. This is part of roleplaying and it's particularly important in Mage. I recommend against trying to solve all such problems using the rules alone. That way lies madness. &quot;Don't break the setting&quot; is the rule that trumps all other rules.<br /> <br /> The published rotes have no shortage of problematic edge cases and inconsistencies with the rules. Don't worry about it until and unless it causes a problem for a story. Even then, try to follow the Rule of Cool so everyone has a good time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 05-13-2020, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T20:18:01-07:00","id":1388219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388056#post1388056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions I've been struggling with:<br /> <br /> The matter 3 spell &quot;Alter Integrity&quot; allows you to make an object more durable than it &quot;naturally&quot; could be. But. It also allows this effect to be made &quot;Lasting&quot;, implying you're giving it a new natural state (despite the state being seemingly unnatural).<br /> <br /> Would this not create a permanent &quot;magic item&quot;? Like, a gold dagger durable enough to scratch a diamond, that doesn't cause paradox and cannot be degraded like most magic effects?<br /> <br /> How does this reconcile with Fallen reality without being in conflict with the &quot;Lasting&quot; rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> How would a sleeper explain coming across bullet proof sheets of paper, without it becoming a scientific mystery showcased with live rounds on the 12 o'clock news?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there are many more bizarre things out there than almost indestructible sheets of paper. Like Claimed, Mementos, Hedgeway and Gadgets. Probably anyone who drew too much attention on this would end up being stolen, disappeared or killed (by a Mage, angel or secret society). It is part of the cruelty and apathy of the Fallen World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T03:21:05-07:00","id":1388284,"title":"","content":"Question: For a 2nd ed Mage, is it possible to combine the advantages of a Rote and Praxis when casting a spell, or is it a case of &quot;choose one&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T03:58:02-07:00","id":1388293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388284#post1388284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: For a 2nd ed Mage, is it possible to combine the advantages of a Rote and Praxis when casting a spell, or is it a case of &quot;choose one&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>One or the other. It says that explicitly on page 112:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The benefits of Rotes do not stack with the benefits of Praxes. If a mage has the same spell as both a Rote and a Praxis, she must decide at casting which she uses. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T11:50:45-07:00","id":1388377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388293#post1388293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One or the other. It says that explicitly on page 112:</div> </div> </div> </div>Managed to miss that one somehow. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T15:40:05-07:00","id":1388777,"title":"","content":"How do you guys rule on the case where a mage transformed something via magic, and then there was an additional Fallen World mechanics transformation applied to it, and then the duration of the spell expires?<br /> <br /> Example: You transform an elephant into an apple. A guy eats the apple. Awhile later the spell expires. The chewed-up, partially-digested apple turns into an elephant-Scale volume of chewed-up, partially-digest elephant and explodes the guy from the inside out? Or the chewing and digesting effectively made the original transformation Lasting? Or maybe it turns back into the elephant in the original state it had prior to the casting of the spell?<br /> <br /> My default answer is &quot;whatever is most horrific&quot; (i.e. the guy explodes and everything nearby gets covered in masticated elephant) but I'd like to avoid causing myself a headache if there's some unforeseen consequences to how I rule on this kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T17:34:34-07:00","id":1388798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388777#post1388777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you guys rule on the case where a mage transformed something via magic, and then there was an additional Fallen World mechanics transformation applied to it, and then the duration of the spell expires?<br /> <br /> Example: You transform an elephant into an apple. A guy eats the apple. Awhile later the spell expires. The chewed-up, partially-digested apple turns into an elephant-Scale volume of chewed-up, partially-digest elephant and explodes the guy from the inside out? Or the chewing and digesting effectively made the original transformation Lasting? Or maybe it turns back into the elephant in the original state it had prior to the casting of the spell?<br /> <br /> My default answer is &amp;quot;whatever is most horrific&amp;quot; (i.e. the guy explodes and everything nearby gets covered in masticated elephant) but I'd like to avoid causing myself a headache if there's some unforeseen consequences to how I rule on this kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another puzzling example, what happens if a mage transforms into blood mist, to move unimpeded in gaseous form, and is then consumed by a vampire. Is the vitae nourishing ? What happens to their mana ? What happens after it is processed and incorporated into its pattern ? Do they become two wills in one body ? Can the vampire bleed him from his system ? Does the merge create an automatic restoration of certain advantages of the living so long as the last point of &quot;Vitae&quot; is not used up ? Can the mage become bigger if he reforms after stealing more vitae than he originally was ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:06:56-07:00","id":1388806,"title":"","content":"My head just exploded as if it were full of elephant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T21:45:28-07:00","id":1388842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388806#post1388806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My head just exploded as if it were full of elephant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d tend to err towards what will be better for the game rather than looking for consistency of mechanics for edge cases like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:20:39-07:00","id":1388931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1388798#post1388798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another puzzling example, what happens if a mage transforms into blood mist, to move unimpeded in gaseous form, and is then consumed by a vampire. Is the vitae nourishing ? What happens to their mana ? What happens after it is processed and incorporated into its pattern ? Do they become two wills in one body ? Can the vampire bleed him from his system ? Does the merge create an automatic restoration of certain advantages of the living so long as the last point of &quot;Vitae&quot; is not used up ? Can the mage become bigger if he reforms after stealing more vitae than he originally was ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all of those actually can be answered.<ul><li>Vampire's don't get Vitae <i>from</i> blood; they get it <i>through</i> blood. Unless the mage designed the spell that the blood mist would be the mage's own blood, the vampire would gain no Vitae from drinking it. (And the vast majority of vampires wouldn't be able to drink it in the first place.)</li> <li>If the vampire could drink the mage and process them into Vitae, the mage would continually take damage during the feeding process because dealing damage is just as important to feeding as the medium being blood. If fully consumed, the mage would definitely die.</li> <li>I don't recall if it has been included in any supplements yet, but Dave Brookshaw has stated that mage Vitae should cause hallucinations (similar to Mage Sight) in vampires, and I think it's because of the Mana. Otherwise the Mana would just do what it usually does when not in a proper container; dissipate.</li> <li>If the mage dies, their will isn't there to do anything. If the mage is ingested without harm, there's no meaningful interaction to merge their wills.</li> <li>Vampires can bleed in two ways: Willingly expressing Vitae, and involuntarily bleeding according to natural processes when using Blush of Health. The vampire could definitely bleed the remains of the mage if processed into Vitae (though there are no general rules for &quot;tagged&quot; Vitae, afaik, so they might not be able to choose which Vitae to bleed). Ingested blood doesn't naturally appear at wounds (unless, say, the stomach was pierced).</li> <li>There are no advantages gained from drinking blood from non-humans in second edition.</li> <li>The mage can never become larger by the spell ending. Only the blood that the mage transformed into would change back. If Vitae was mixed up in the mist of blood, then that Vitae would remain where it was when the spell ends (which is quite possibly in the space the mage's old body now occupies.</li> </ul>With a huge caveat for the fact that anything can happen if the ST thinks it would be more interesting and fun than what I just described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-16-2020, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T07:20:01-07:00","id":1389300,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. Thank you. Taking the opportunity, I would like to ask about the difference between Supernal Veil and Cloak Nimbus.<br /> <br /> Cloak Nimbus means your Nimbus does not flare when you cast. Supernal Veil wards a target from all active magical detection. <br /> <br /> So in other words, if a mage casts while under Cloak Nimbus, the spell will still trigger the Peripheral Sight ? So anyone who looks in that general direction and sees them in touch range, or traces an aimed spell's trajectory can connect the dots, correct? In other words, Cloak Nimbus only hides the culprit, but everyone nearby still knows something supernatural happened within sensory range, is that about right ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:22:02-07:00","id":1389335,"title":"","content":"Experienced Seers of Understanding Wisdom are very unlikely right? Forcing people do things counter to their interests and premeditated murder are basically the Seer M.O. Experienced Seers should generally be of Falling Wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:42:41-07:00","id":1389343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389300#post1389300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. Thank you. Taking the opportunity, I would like to ask about the difference between Supernal Veil and Cloak Nimbus.<br /> <br /> Cloak Nimbus means your Nimbus does not flare when you cast. Supernal Veil wards a target from all active magical detection.<br /> <br /> So in other words, if a mage casts while under Cloak Nimbus, the spell will still trigger the Peripheral Sight ? So anyone who looks in that general direction and sees them in touch range, or traces an aimed spell's trajectory can connect the dots, correct? In other words, Cloak Nimbus only hides the culprit, but everyone nearby still knows something supernatural happened within sensory range, is that about right ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems like your main point of point of interest is about concealing the act of spellcasting from PMS. I think the best way to do that is with a Prime spell analogous to Hung Spell which enables Potency subsequent spells not to ping PMS and costs 1 mana. The reason that neither Cloak Nimbus nor Supernal Veil can accomplish this is that the spell pings PMS upon casting, and it can't be Veiled by either of those two spells until after it has been cast.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if a mage wants to conceal a long-lasting spell from being detected by someone who arrives on the scene later, Supernal Veil serves for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 05-17-2020, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:44:20-07:00","id":1389344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389343#post1389343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It seems like your main point of point of interest is about concealing the act of spellcasting from PMS. I think the best way to do that is with a Prime spell analogous to Hung Spell which enables Potency subsequent spells not to ping PMS and costs 1 mana. The reason that neither Cloak Nimbus nor Supernal Veil can accomplish this is that the spell pings PMS upon casting, and it can't be Veiled by either of those two spells until after it has been cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you cast both with a combination spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T10:15:20-07:00","id":1389351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389335#post1389335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Experienced Seers of Understanding Wisdom are very unlikely right? Forcing people do things counter to their interests and premeditated murder are basically the Seer M.O. Experienced Seers should generally be of Falling Wisdom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they've Inured the primary spells they use to that end and taken a practical approach to becoming Wiser; I wouldn't put the proportion significantly higher than Pentacle mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T10:27:22-07:00","id":1389355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389344#post1389344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you cast both with a combination spell</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think a Combined Spell will accomplish that. The Supernal Veil portion of the Combined Spell would have no subject, as the spell you want to Veil does not exist until the Combined Spell is cast. This is the reason that Hung Spell is itself not formulated as a Combined Spell.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think this comes down to how the ST resolves the ambiguity in how PMS works and multiple interpretations are valid. If the ST rules that the <b>mage</b> triggers PMS when casting a spell, Veiling the mage ahead of time prevents the PMS ping. If the ST rules that the <b>spell</b> triggers PMS when it's cast, then Supernal Veil doesn't help. If the ST rules that the <b>subject</b> triggers PMS when effected by a spell, then Veiling the subject prevents the PMS ping. I don't think the rules about PMS are specific enough to say which is the correct interpretation conclusively.<br /> <br /> Like, here's the text from Signs of Sorcery:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> As described on p. 90 of Mage, Peripheral Mage Sight automatically detects the presence of any active, unconcealed supernatural effects: the <b>casting </b>of a spell, <b>activation </b>of a vampire\u2019s Discipline...</div>Since a &quot;casting&quot; or an &quot;activation&quot; are not things a Veiling spell can target, it's up to the ST exactly what needs to be Veiled to prevent a PMS ping. I personally rule that it's the magical effect itself since Supernal Veiling specifically mentions that it can target spells.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Eh, maybe this bit of text lends credence to the idea that it's the spell itself that needs to be veiled:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Likewise, if a ghost in the same room uses a Numen, the mage knows that something supernatural happened, but without a spell or Attainment to let her see things in Twilight, the effect would seem to originate from empty space.</div> <br /> Substitute &quot;Veiled mage casting a spell&quot; for &quot;ghost in Twilight using a Numen&quot; and it seems like the intention is that the spell will still ping PMS even if the mage is Veiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 05-17-2020, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T10:59:34-07:00","id":1389361,"title":"","content":"So while I was looking into this, I noticed that Supernal Veil RAW conceals supernatural subjects from detection, period -- as if being concealed from supernatural means of detection is a subset of the concealment it provides. We're meant to interpret that as &quot;Veils from detection via Magic&quot; rather than &quot;Veils Magic Thing from detection&quot; right? RAW it seems like it can make mages, vampires, etc... concealed from all mundane means of detection in addition to supernatural means of detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T11:38:26-07:00","id":1389380,"title":"","content":"A couple of questions about ephemeral beings:<br /> <br /> How does a materialized spirit or ghost appear if examined either physically or by Life magic. Does a materialized cat spirit that looks like a cat also feel like a cat and read as a cat to life magic, or does it feel like a bag of goo and read strangely / not register to Life magic? What about supernal creatures (who to my understanding are solid by default in the phenomenal world)?<br /> <br /> Do Supernal entities have numina, or is their power bound up in their influence arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T11:54:00-07:00","id":1389387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389380#post1389380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a materialized spirit or ghost appear if examined either physically or by Life magic. Does a materialized cat spirit that looks like a cat also feel like a cat and read as a cat to life magic, or does it feel like a bag of goo and read strangely / not register to Life magic? What about supernal creatures (who to my understanding are solid by default in the phenomenal world)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits have stylised appearances related to their natures. A cat spirit will have a lot of cat traits, but will generally not be confused for an ordinary cat. How it feels, sounds, smells, etc, will also be related to its cat nature (with the exception of the fact that it can talk). Being materialised does not change how it appears to Life Sight. It still has the same body as it did when in a Twilight state as well as when in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389380#post1389380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Supernal entities have numina, or is their power bound up in their influence arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the table on page 254 only ephemeral entities get Numina. So no. Also, they straight up have Arcana instead of Influences, rather than Influences that map to the Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:01:59-07:00","id":1389391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389387#post1389387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirits have stylised appearances related to their natures. A cat spirit will have a lot of cat traits, but will generally not be confused for an ordinary cat. How it feels, sounds, smells, etc, will also be related to its cat nature (with the exception of the fact that it can talk). Being materialised does not change how it appears to Life Sight. It still has the same body as it did when in a Twilight state as well as when in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> According to the table on page 254 only ephemeral entities get Numina. So no. Also, they straight up have Arcana instead of Influences, rather than Influences that map to the Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. I had forgotten that supernal beings don't fall under the umbrella of ephemeral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:13:04-07:00","id":1389432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1389391#post1389391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answer. I had forgotten that supernal beings don't fall under the umbrella of ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to think about ephemera as a substance (which it happens to be in the setting). That's why all ephemeral beings share so many similarities, most notably being in Twilight when in the material world.<br /> Supernal entities, on the other hand, are made up of Supernal symbols and thus have no substance. Ironically, that makes them fully physical when they enter the Fallen world, because they have nothing that forces them into Twilight upon arrival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T03:59:29-07:00","id":1392474,"title":"","content":"Do you think that a sleepwalker subject of the apocalypse spell could use focused mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:00:39-07:00","id":1392503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1392474#post1392474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that a sleepwalker subject of the apocalypse spell could use focused mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While Awakened subjects may control the new Sight as though it were<br /> their own, focusing it and pushing it back to the Periphery<br /> like their own, other subjects gain Active Mage Sight and<br /> cannot shut the Sight off \u2014 it lasts until the spell\u2019s Duration<br /> expires, but still applies dice pool penalties and Willpower<br /> costs as per Mage Sight </div> </div> </div>As per the text above I would say they only gain Active Mage sight and Awakened subjects can focus it as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T02:46:58-07:00","id":1394001,"title":"","content":"If I want to use the reflexive casting option on a spell like Exceptional Luck, do I need to pay the +1 Reach for Instant Casting in addition to the +2 Reach for the reflexive casting or should I assume that cost is built in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T04:17:16-07:00","id":1394015,"title":"","content":"Okay so... Mage may be the next CoD game translated in french (my native language) and I musr confess it's the one I'm the least int\u00e9rested by... Can someone give me a bullet point for why Mage : The Awakening is the best game for you ? Or even just a great game, compared to the other splat (knowing that Vampire and Demon have already been translated and that I like them both a lot, and that Werewolf, Changeling and Beasts are the one which would interest me most, from the very little I know about it) ?<br /> <br /> Basically, why is Mage more than a game about arrogant humans playing God ? Which isn't exactly attractive to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T04:50:46-07:00","id":1394019,"title":"","content":"I will give you my reasons why Mage the awakening is my favourite game.<br /> <br /> This game is about playing humans, sure humans with a lot of powerbut you are not a monster (at least not yet).<br /> The game is about curiosity, finding out the truth of reality.<br /> The game is about freeing humanity from god-tyrants.<br /> The game is about seeing that the world is aweful and being given the opportunity to change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T07:31:05-07:00","id":1394026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1394015#post1394015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so... Mage may be the next CoD game translated in french (my native language) and I musr confess it's the one I'm the least int\u00e9rested by... Can someone give me a bullet point for why Mage : The Awakening is the best game for you ? Or even just a great game, compared to the other splat (knowing that Vampire and Demon have already been translated and that I like them both a lot, and that Werewolf, Changeling and Beasts are the one which would interest me most, from the very little I know about it) ?<br /> <br /> Basically, why is Mage more than a game about arrogant humans playing God ? Which isn't exactly attractive to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>While some mages takes the easiest path playing god, this choice has consequences.<br /> Mage for me is about people who gain powers, great powers, and try their best to wield them with responsability, sometimes they fail and sometimes it is hard to define what is right or wrong.<br /> Your opponents instead don t even try to contain their hubris, an this choice gives them power, more power than you, but slowly they turn into monsters, constant reminders of what you can easily become if you don t pay attention.<br /> Temptation, curiosity, ethics, hubris, mystery are all great themes for a story.<br /> As a narrator i must say that on the other side it is difficult for me to create challenging stories for such powerful characters.<br /> Overall i think that it is one of my favourite game line","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:05:21-07:00","id":1394032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1394015#post1394015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so... Mage may be the next CoD game translated in french (my native language) and I musr confess it's the one I'm the least int\u00e9rested by... Can someone give me a bullet point for why Mage : The Awakening is the best game for you ? Or even just a great game, compared to the other splat (knowing that Vampire and Demon have already been translated and that I like them both a lot, and that Werewolf, Changeling and Beasts are the one which would interest me most, from the very little I know about it) ?<br /> <br /> Basically, why is Mage more than a game about arrogant humans playing God ? Which isn't exactly attractive to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2022 Its about exploring and trying to understand the secret world that once lay just beyond your mundane senses <br /> \u2022 Its about testing the limits of your creativity and perceptiveness, using magic to bypass or sidestep problems<br /> \u2022 Its about what humans do when given great power. Where do hope and altruism end ? Where do selfishness and hubris begin ? Its not always simple to draw those lines <br /> \u2022 Its about uncovering the secrets of the past and using them to forge the future<br /> \u2022 Its about characters that, for all their power, are ultimately all too human, with all the good and ill that comes with it <br /> <br /> Its about all that and so much more. Its overall a terrific game line and I cannot recommend it enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-04-2020, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:31:35-07:00","id":1394040,"title":"","content":"Thanks for those answers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7463_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7463\" data-vbnamecard=\"7463\">Toine</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24346_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24346\" data-vbnamecard=\"24346\">Neos01</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> !<br /> <br /> Not gonne lie, I'm still not feeling it. It's strange because a lot of the CoD game I like conceptually seems to have a &quot;hidden world&quot; (the GM, the Hedge and beyond, the Shadow, etc.) but the one of Mage really doesn't appeal to me so far. Perhaps because it looks a little too much like how most people imagined magic and all that in the XIXth Century and all that, which never truly appealed to me ? Then again, the Ordo Dracul is also based on that idea but calls to me more...<br /> <br /> I really can't pinpoint why I don't feel Mage like the other games and it frustrates me to no end...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:42:48-07:00","id":1394047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1394040#post1394040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for those answers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7463_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7463\" data-vbnamecard=\"7463\">Toine</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24346_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24346\" data-vbnamecard=\"24346\">Neos01</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> !<br /> <br /> Not gonne lie, I'm still not feeling it. It's strange because a lot of the CoD game I like conceptually seems to have a &quot;hidden world&quot; (the GM, the Hedge and beyond, the Shadow, etc.) but the one of Mage really doesn't appeal to me so far. Perhaps because it looks a little too much like how most people imagined magic and all that in the XIXth Century and all that, which never truly appealed to me ? Then again, the Ordo Dracul is also based on that idea but calls to me more...<br /> <br /> I really can't pinpoint why I don't feel Mage like the other games and it frustrates me to no end...</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I recommend this thread:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088486-mage-booklist\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-mage-booklist</a><br /> <br /> At the bottom of the first post is an AP list, they are amazing to get the feel of Mage. The start of the Broken Diamond one has the GM explaining the themes and feeling of the setting in a very compelling way. Plus they are all very good reads. <br /> <br /> The start of Broken Diamond for the feel and themes, plus Bleak House for a one-shot that puts them in action. Those are the best recommendations I have for an introduction into the setting.<br /> <br /> Mage felt very weird for me at first, those APs are what made the setting click for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br />