mple-question-awakened-edition?p=1394202#post1394202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Coaxing the Spirits be used in the same way as Words of Command to reliably activate a Fetish ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:53:33-07:00","id":1394426,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:55:43-07:00","id":1394563,"title":"","content":"Does Step 1 of the Duel Arcane mean that the loser suffers an agreed-upon Condition based on the stakes in addition to the Defeated Condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:38:59-07:00","id":1394620,"title":"","content":"Yes, although I allow that the stakes may be represented by multiple distinct Conditions that the loser acquires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-06-2020, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:40:05-07:00","id":1395405,"title":"","content":"This is a question about enhancing items at Scale, and in particular how to interpret Duration for that case.<br /> <br /> I've got a closet full of daggers -- dozens of them. Monkey's Paw at Area of Effect Scale &quot;small room.&quot;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The single casting enhances all of those daggers.</li> <li>The daggers retain the enhancement when carried away from the closet.</li> <li>If I relinquish the spell, I pay one willpower dot to to relinquish and it covers all the daggers.</li> <li>If the enhancement is dispelled from a single dagger, it's dispelled from all of them.</li> </ol>Are all of the above true?<br /> <br /> Now suppose the spell had high Duration. Does the closet continue to serve as sort of an enhanced dagger factory for the Duration of the spell? Throw a dagger (or whatever) in the closet and it gets enhanced as long as the spell is still going? Does the Duration apply to the enhancement spell's operation on the area of effect, or on the application of the enhancement to the items in that area, or to both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T12:29:19-07:00","id":1395428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1394001#post1394001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to use the reflexive casting option on a spell like Exceptional Luck, do I need to pay the +1 Reach for Instant Casting in addition to the +2 Reach for the reflexive casting or should I assume that cost is built in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule that such an option replaces rather than upgrades casting time so Reach would be +2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T12:52:14-07:00","id":1395436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395405#post1395405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question about enhancing items at Scale, and in particular how to interpret Duration for that case.<br /> <br /> I've got a closet full of daggers -- dozens of them. Monkey's Paw at Area of Effect Scale &quot;small room.&quot;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The single casting enhances all of those daggers.</li> <li>The daggers retain the enhancement when carried away from the closet.</li> <li>If I relinquish the spell, I pay one willpower dot to to relinquish and it covers all the daggers.</li> <li>If the enhancement is dispelled from a single dagger, it's dispelled from all of them.</li> </ol>Are all of the above true?<br /> <br /> Now suppose the spell had high Duration. Does the closet continue to serve as sort of an enhanced dagger factory for the Duration of the spell? Throw a dagger (or whatever) in the closet and it gets enhanced as long as the spell is still going? Does the Duration apply to the enhancement spell's operation on the area of effect, or on the application of the enhancement to the items in that area, or to both?</div> </div> </div> </div>All subjects in an area of effect are targeted, barring shielding effects, so 1 is true. The recasting thing is only for spells that have some impulsive effect: &quot;...would <b><i>logically have an immediate effect</i></b> but is cast with Advanced Duration, the effect recurs at every multiple of the character\u2019s Gnosis-based ritual casting time, until the Duration runs out.&quot; (emph. mine) <i>Monkey's Paw</i> uses Duration as normal, so, no: Upgrading to Advanced Duration doesn't create a <i>Monkey's Paw</i> dispenser.<br /> <br /> Yes, the daggers would retain the effect for the Duration and relinquishing is a single effect. Enjoy AoE.<br /> (ed. Limitation being: Leaving the area would leave the effect behind, too. Casting on each individual knife as a distinct subject would be handled via Number of Subjects. THAT would retain the effect for the duration, wherever they went.)<br /> <br /> Aesthetically, I'd prefer dispelling one manifestation only dispelling <i>that one</i>. As it's a single spell being targeted, though, it logically <i>should </i>go poof as a single thing like you suggest. (If you retain spell control, you could drop some and not all, though)<br /> <br /> (I'd love to hear arguments from the rules why that isn't so because I'd prefer it otherwise. Best I'm coming up with is that the scale of the Dispel effect limits the scope of what is dispelled, but that's weak.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 06-09-2020, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T13:10:10-07:00","id":1395445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395405#post1395405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are all of the above true?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 is wrong. The spell affects valid targets within the scope of its effect, and Area Scale makes the scope of its effect the area instead of attaching it to specific individual targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T13:22:09-07:00","id":1395450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395405#post1395405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question about enhancing items at Scale, and in particular how to interpret Duration for that case.<br /> <br /> I've got a closet full of daggers -- dozens of them. Monkey's Paw at Area of Effect Scale &quot;small room.&quot;[*]The single casting enhances all of those daggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The single casting enhances everything in the room/closet or that enters the closet, not just the daggers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]The daggers retain the enhancement when carried away from the closet. </div> </div> </div>Once they leave the area of effect the enhancement ends. If you want it to persist use Advanced Scale: Targets instead of Advanced Scale: Area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]If I relinquish the spell, I pay one willpower dot to to relinquish and it covers all the daggers. </div> </div> </div>It covers everything in the closet or that enters the closet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]If the enhancement is dispelled from a single dagger, it's dispelled from all of them. </div> </div> </div>The enhancement isn't really on the dagger, per se, it's on the area of the closet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are all of the above true? </div> </div> </div>None of the above are true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now suppose the spell had high Duration. Does the closet continue to serve as sort of an enhanced dagger factory for the Duration of the spell? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Throw a dagger (or whatever) in the closet and it gets enhanced as long as the spell is still going? </div> </div> </div>Only as long as it remains in the closet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Duration apply to the enhancement spell's operation on the area of effect, or on the application of the enhancement to the items in that area, or to both? </div> </div> </div>It applies to the area of effect, and anything leaving that area loses the benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-09-2020, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T13:41:24-07:00","id":1395453,"title":"","content":"There seem to be some differences of opinion on the details, but it looks like the bottom line is that a newly-minted Acanthus cannot in fact create an entire closet full of portable disposable Boons by casting and relinquishing a single spell so I'm satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T21:24:04-07:00","id":1395523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395453#post1395453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There seem to be some differences of opinion on the details, but it looks like the bottom line is that a newly-minted Acanthus cannot in fact create an entire closet full of portable disposable Boons by casting and relinquishing a single spell so I'm satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it could be done, it would require a Fate conjunctional variation of Endless Bounty (copy the item and its luck). But that seems out of reach for a newly minted Acanthus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-10-2020, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T04:52:32-07:00","id":1395811,"title":"","content":"Can you use the Sympathetic Range Attainment multiple times on a single spell in order to affect multiple subjects the mage cannot see? If that is the case, what would be the Withstand rating of the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T07:05:42-07:00","id":1395834,"title":"","content":"You can - you can even, for example, increase your Scale factor to cast a spell on three people and use Sympathetic Range for only one of them, be viewing a second through a scrying window and be touching the third.<br /> <br /> However, the Attainment says *a* subject. You have to waste a yantra slot on a sympathetic yantra, have a sympathetic link, and pay a Mana for each individual subject. The Withstand ratings follow the standard rules for Withstand stacking - the highest individual rating plus one for each additional rating that applies. (Remember that not knowing their name adds one *to that individual rating* when doing this math). Because of this, you'll find that you will only be confident of multiple-sympathy spells where the spells themselves aren't Withstood but have Potency as the primary factor. Having the spell as a Praxis helps, as you might gamble on an exceptional success cancelling Withstand.<br /> <br /> So - yeah. But you only really see it in high-Gnosis, high-Arcana mages that have the dice pools to burn on the complexities involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T07:48:26-07:00","id":1395842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enmai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395811#post1395811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that is the case, what would be the Withstand rating of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Withstand rating is <i>per subject</i>, not per spell. Just pointing it out so you don't get into a mental pitfall regarding that part.<br /> Each subject calculates their own Withstand rating which in this case would probably invoke the multiple Withstand rule: Use the highest Withstand rating plus one for each additional Withstand rating that applies. In your example it would be the higher of their relevant Resistance Attribute and their Sympathetic Withstand rating according to the strength of the Sympathetic Connection (plus potential increase for not knowing their Sympathetic Name), and then add one to that. If the spell is not normally Withstood, it's just their Sympathetic Withstand rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T15:23:37-07:00","id":1395920,"title":"","content":"Really basic concept question: Are things in the Abyss still described by some combination of Supernal symbols?<br /> <br /> Various tidbits suggest to me that the answer is probably yes, but I wanted to get other people's reads on it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T15:53:25-07:00","id":1395924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395920#post1395920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really basic concept question: Are things in the Abyss still described by some combination of Supernal symbols?<br /> <br /> Various tidbits suggest to me that the answer is probably yes, but I wanted to get other people's reads on it as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say &quot;no,&quot; actually. The Abyss would be described by its own, Abyssal symbols, the filtering of the Supernal Symbols' Truth through the Abyssal Symbols' Anti-truth is what creates the Lie of the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T16:08:09-07:00","id":1395926,"title":"","content":"I don't think so.<br /> <br /> I think that N&amp;A implies that Abyssal realities are defined by anti-symbols. While Supernal symbols express what <b>is</b>, Abyssal anti-symbols express what <b>is not</b>. That's why Abyssal realities are described as &quot;empty&quot; -- they lack affirmative truths. Anything not expressly disallowed by an Abyssal reality's anti-symbols exists within that reality. It's like if you described the rules of a game only by saying what things the players <i>can't</i> do, so that any wild-ass thing not disallowed by those rules is allowed. The players could go wild with an unbounded amount of nonsense and the game wouldn't be fun for long.<br /> <br /> Abyssal intruders desire affirmative truths and invade &quot;our&quot; reality to experience them.<br /> <br /> Scelesti are seduced by the infinite possibilities available in realities where only a finite number of things are impossible. The example Scelesti by Path from N&amp;A describe mages who essentially apply a Boolean NOT operator to the fundaments of their Paths (e.g. Acanthus who hold that there is no destiny and choices do not determine consequences).<br /> <br /> &quot;Every choice has its consequences&quot; is the sort of thing a Supernal symbol would capture.<br /> <br /> &quot;Outcomes cannot be predicted from actions&quot; is the sort of thing an Abyssal anti-symbol would capture. Outcomes could depend on random chance, or the phase of the moon, or how many freckles John has on his nose, so long as they can't be predicted from someone's actions. Such realities are incomprehensible to humans and difficult to describe as a ST, so &quot;mind-shattering unreality&quot; is a good place to leave off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-11-2020, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T16:46:20-07:00","id":1395932,"title":"","content":"The idea that mages had to learn their Arcana in a certain order (because the order you obtain the first dot effected the absolute maximum you could attain, with your tenth Arcana capped at 4 even with Gnosis 10) from 1st edition seems to have been dropped in 2e. Is this the case?<br /> <br /> If my bracketed explanation is unclear, I am talking about the Arcana Mastery table on page 78 of the first edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T17:47:07-07:00","id":1395939,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is dropped. Though you still need to raise your Gnosis to get arcana limits up to a point. It's all in the Gnosis table, underneath the Gnosis subsection.l<br /> <br /> The only difficulty with learning assorted Arcana comes with problem with needing teachers outside of your Ruling Arcana, and having to spend normal, not Arcane, Experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T18:34:27-07:00","id":1395945,"title":"","content":"Brilliant. To be honest, I'm glad. It never really resonated with me and just felt like an excessive restriction. I'm aware of the Gnosis limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T19:03:42-07:00","id":1395950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395924#post1395924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say &quot;no,&quot; actually. The Abyss would be described by its own, Abyssal symbols, the filtering of the Supernal Symbols' Truth through the Abyssal Symbols' Anti-truth is what creates the Lie of the Fallen World.</div> </div> </div> </div>My arguments:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gate is an Exarch, or at least near enough to one that her Secret Order can be a Legacy; further, one that has access to an Abyssally-tainted Emanation Realm, i.e. a place where an Arcanum (Space, if memory serves) is strongly manifested is used by a heretical Ministry to command Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> 2. Mages can be drawn from Abyssal worlds (Awakened doppelgangers are one of the oldest described forms of Paradox in the game across both editions, as a core example, the basis for a Legacy, and the backstory of a signature character) and their magic is not significantly different from their truly-extant counterparts.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Abyssal Symbols&quot; have never, to my knowledge, been described in any terms firmer than &quot;things can be found in the Abyss that present false or antithetical symbolism to those found in Supernal Mystery Plays&quot;; the Annunaki are the closest concretely-described such phenomena, but they're more defined ludonarratively by their opposition to Form and/or their desire to subsume what exists than to their component entities being anything so visually indistinct as &quot;not-a-cat&quot; or &quot;un-fire.&quot; Reality is out to lunch in the Abyss, but the vast stretch of corrupted imagination being visible there doesn't mean a person trapped within it stops being a person \u2014 we've <i>seen</i> people experience its contents within the fiction.<br /> <br /> 4. &quot;The Abyss&quot; and &quot;Abyssal entities&quot; are, as the Nemean firmly reminds us in The Unmurdered Man, not to be confused with each other; there are multiple mentions of things being consigned to the Abyss because they are impossible or because they so offended the gods and/or the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> 5. Abyssal entities are modeled with the systems that use Essence and Resonance rather than Mana and Arcana, and are arguably the best-adapted among invisible entities to the material world; when present in the world, they are firmly (sometimes upsettingly) on the &quot;concrete&quot; side of the Supernal World's point &quot;where concrete and the abstract mix.&quot; We have basically zero evidence that the Arcana do not work on Abyssal entities small enough to interact with, and the Arcana are the descriptive lens through which the Awakened gather occult information.<br /> <br /> 6. Befouling a spell draws upon the Abyss and never happens by accident, but mages who simply Reach beyond their grasp aren't invoking anybody's Abyssal shard, and the general bent of phenomena presented by known Annunaki is not incompatible with their components being real things assembled in nonsensical fashions. &quot;Things that can't exist&quot; require reference to things that <i>can</i> exist to be engaged with in a descriptive context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T19:48:03-07:00","id":1395958,"title":"","content":"Maybe each Abyssal reality (Annunaki) consists of a mix of Supernal symbols and anti-symbols:<ul><li>Supernal symbols for 9 Arcana and anti-symbols for the 10th, or</li> <li>Supernal symbols for 4 of the 5 Paths and anti-symbols for the 5th</li> </ul>This is the &quot;why not both&quot; option that results in Abyssal phenomenon that obey many of the rules of &quot;our&quot; reality but utterly defy others.<br /> <br /> The second option aligns with the idea of Abyssal watchtowers.<br /> <br /> This may fit better with more of the clues peppered throughout the published material; I just don't understand how an Annunaki accesses or has Supernal symbols when the Abyss is meant to be separate from and in opposition to the Supernal. Maybe as stillborn realities they have their own &quot;copies,&quot; symbols identical to those from the Supernal but native to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> I prefer the explanation that Abyssal intruders become &quot;sheathed&quot; in a hodgepodge of Supernal truths upon entering the Fallen World, like a virus's RNA sheathed in bits of the membrane of the cell that birthed it. Which I made up myself and is not supported by anything published.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Befouling a spell draws upon the Abyss and never happens by accident, but mages who simply Reach beyond their grasp aren't invoking anybody's Abyssal shard </div> </div> </div>Overreaching replays in miniature the circumstances of the Fall, where mages' hubris allowed the Abyss to sunder the Material from the Supernal. That symbolism allows the Abyss to invade the overreaching Mage's spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-11-2020, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T20:11:30-07:00","id":1395961,"title":"","content":"Also not-a-cat is not an anti-symbol. An anti-symbol would negate the possibility of cats -- nothing more and nothing less. With that anti-symbol in play you could have something like a cat-octopus-futon chimera, but not a straight-up cat.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't see why Abyssal entities must be described by Supernal symbols in order to be effected by those symbols via magic. Wood doesn't have to be made of little fires in order to burn. The 2E core rulebook says &quot;Even in a Verge, ordered reality repels Annunaki.&quot; I doubt that they're intrinsically described by the thing that repels them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-11-2020, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T22:57:21-07:00","id":1395974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1395961#post1395961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I don't see why Abyssal entities must be described by Supernal symbols in order to be effected by those symbols via magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that is how the Supernal relates to the Phenomenal and why Aponoia happens (and strengthens the Abyss as contradictions proliferate) when you mess with it.<br /> <br /> Five-thousand-year-old airplanes powered by blood sacrifice sharing history with the Wright brothers' invention is an inconsistency that paves the way for the great dreamers to enter reality, and messing up your Imago so that your spell does more or less than it should accomplishes the same thing on a smaller scale with or without the direct attribution of your fumble to an Abyssal gestalt consciousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 2E core rulebook says &quot;Even in a Verge, ordered reality repels Annunaki.&quot; I doubt that they're intrinsically described by the thing that repels them. </div> </div> </div>This is where you are running into problems: I am literally asking about any Abyssal being smaller than an Annunaki, as encountered outside of the whole-world context of an Annunaki.<br /> <br /> Magic doesn't affect Abyssal beings very well in the Abyss because stillborn gods are much bigger fish than you and Paradox runs rampant there (and can constrain your magic besides), but the un-world's ability to change the rules on a dime doesn't make its pieces naturally immune to basic WYSIWYG interference when encountered in a Phenomenal context where space and time exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T05:32:15-07:00","id":1395998,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all, I don't think this turned out to be a simple question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll try and restate it to see whether I'm following you:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> It's obvious from many examples that Abyssal entities on the level of Gulmoth and Acamoth are vulnerable to Supernal magic. Are they so vulnerable because they're actually defined in part or in whole by Supernal symbols, or merely as a concession to their role as Mage antagonists? If the latter, what are they <i>really </i>defined by?</div>I feel like I've given the range of <i>opinions</i> on this that I can based on what I remember from Intruders and N&amp;A, but AFAIK this has never been answered definitively, and I'm almost certain it's not been addressed in the 2E era.<br /> <br /> I think the most important idea to explore in this conversation is that of anti-symbols, which show up repeatedly in the context of the Abyss. Like this snippet from Intruders:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Around Anumerus, each integer from zero through nine gains significance and meaning. Some mystagogues familiar with the power of numbers believe that Anumerus\u2019s \u201canti-numbers\u201d directly oppose the mystic attributes of numbers in the Supernal Realm, and assign the following meanings to his creations. </div> </div> </div>And then if you read each number's description, they're associated with the negations of (or assertions of the opposites of) particular Supernal truths.<br /> <br /> Regarding Anumerus himself (who I assume is not an Annunaki based on his description***, but it's not stated by the source):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Practitioners of Left-Handed Legacies sometimes look to stories of Anumerus and assume that his intelligence, his human-like manifestation and his orderly nature mean that he can be contacted, bargained with or controlled. But Anumerus is no more than the sum of his parts. He is the components of whatever never-been concept of numbers exists in the Abyss </div> </div> </div>This, to me, reads like this non-Annunaki Abyssal entity is composed of non-Supernal symbols of the Abyss rather than Supernal symbols. So how do mages counter him with Supernal magic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, there is the possibility of ritual banishment. Exiling Anumerus magically would require a Supernal counter for each of his anti-numbers \u2014 a spell or Artifact empowered by the same principle and Arcanum that Anumerus twists. A Prime spell of creation could counter the anti-zero </div> </div> </div>By overcoming his anti-symbols with the corresponding Supernal symbols. What implications this has for the broader metaphysics I don't know.<br /> <br /> I feel like if you need to find some deeper truth than this kind of example illustrates you might have to PM one of the two or three people in the world who could provide that.<br /> <br /> <br /> *** Anumerus may be a <i>manifestation </i>of an Annunaki, like an avatar. It's up to you whether a being presented as a Rank 4 entity manifested in Twilight counts as &quot;small&quot; in the context of your question.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, in 2E Anumerus is actually <i>the</i> example Gulmoth referenced in the core rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, the Gulmoth Anumerus, which twists mathematics into insane anti-numbers, may draw Essence from the Resonance of \u201cnumbers.\u201d </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-12-2020, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:48:22-07:00","id":1396167,"title":"","content":"Can Bolster Spirit be used on Werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:54:10-07:00","id":1396170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396167#post1396167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Bolster Spirit be used on Werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since they're not spirits, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T08:02:54-07:00","id":1396172,"title":"","content":"Aren't they? They are either fully Spirit and fully Human hybrids or half of each. Hence Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":"hence 6666. 06-13-2020, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T09:10:47-07:00","id":1396181,"title":"","content":"They're partly spirit, but they are very far from being spirits themselves. Spirit can be used to mess around some with werewolves, but you definitely can't use Bolster Spirit (or any other Spirit spell that would alter their bodies) on a werewolf because their bodies are physical flesh and blood. Bolster Spirit also explicitly messes around with traits that werewolves simply doesn't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T09:12:12-07:00","id":1396182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396172#post1396172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't they? They are either fully Spirit and fully Human hybrids or half of each. Hence Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean they should be affected by Spirit at high harmony, Life at low harmony, and both in the middle? I had assumed a werewolf on the material side of the gauntlet was ultimately a living thing subject to Life, on the other side of the gauntlet effectively a spirit subject to Spirit magic, regardless of harmony ranking. I can't point out any RAW reference spelling that out however. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:09:27-07:00","id":1396186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396182#post1396182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean they should be affected by Spirit at high harmony, Life at low harmony, and both in the middle? I had assumed a werewolf on the material side of the gauntlet was ultimately a living thing subject to Life, on the other side of the gauntlet effectively a spirit subject to Spirit magic, regardless of harmony ranking. I can't point out any RAW reference spelling that out however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever their Harmony is at they're always part spirit and part flesh. But it would be the other way around, with Spirit at Low Harmony.<br /> <br /> The only werewolves that go completely spirit are some rare zi'ir (a sort of equivalent to the Rapt).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:26:18-07:00","id":1396221,"title":"","content":"For interacting with dead materials such as natural plant fibers, wood, bone, and other materials that used to be alive that people use to make objects, can Death manipulate them in the same way that Matter manipulates metals, stone, and so forth?<br /> <br /> For example could there be a Death version of Aegis that raises the armor of a wooden shield?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:55:35-07:00","id":1396246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396221#post1396221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For interacting with dead materials such as natural plant fibers, wood, bone, and other materials that used to be alive that people use to make objects, can Death manipulate them in the same way that Matter manipulates metals, stone, and so forth?<br /> <br /> For example could there be a Death version of Aegis that raises the armor of a wooden shield?</div> </div> </div> </div>A wooden shield would just be Aegis, it's Matter, not Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:20:56-07:00","id":1396250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396246#post1396246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A wooden shield would just be Aegis, it's Matter, not Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>So &quot;wood is to tree as corpse is to person&quot; is false? Where's the dividing line between Death and Matter when it comes to materials that once lived?<br /> <br /> Like, h<a href=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcSyx3PXkK-VwFcTJAvF4SL1GrNKHeK7PDjMFlBsgvbDUfBrfJk3&amp;usqp=CAU\" target=\"_blank\">ere's a Native American breastplate made of coyote bones</a>. That thing can only be enhanced through Matter, not Death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-13-2020, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:31:51-07:00","id":1396256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396246#post1396246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wooden shield would just be Aegis, it's Matter, not Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bArcana are not mutually exclusive. Just because Aegis would work on a wooden shield doesn't mean Death wouldn't work on a wooden shield.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396250#post1396250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &quot;wood is to tree as corpse is to person&quot; is false? Where's the dividing line between Death and Matter when it comes to materials that once lived?<br /> <br /> Like, h<a href=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcSyx3PXkK-VwFcTJAvF4SL1GrNKHeK7PDjMFlBsgvbDUfBrfJk3&amp;usqp=CAU\" target=\"_blank\">ere's a Native American breastplate made of coyote bones</a>. That thing can only be enhanced through Matter, not Death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would not consider worked materials count as a corpse (but that's a personal judgement call because the line between Death and Matter is not explained in the game). However, even if it did, you couldn't necessarily cast a Death version of Aegis on it anyway. Aegis works by changing a material property, which falls under Matter regardless of the nature of the subject. That's the reason you can't just cast a Life version of Aegis on a living person, turning their skin virtually indestructible. No, you need to actually grant them biological armour (such as tougher hide or a carapace) if you intend to replicate the effect using Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:35:34-07:00","id":1396257,"title":"","content":"I have searched for answers to these questions but wasn't able to find them, my apologies if they are floating around somewhere.<br /> <br /> In regards to imbued items, I still have to questions I'm not sure on even after reading SoS.<br /> <br /> -First, do the spells in imbued items benefit from free steps along the primary spell factor? If so, who's Arcana is it derived from, the Creator's? User's? Arcanum rating of the spell in question?<br /> <br /> -Second, if the creator of the item doesn't use a reach for instant casting, can imbued items be used to cast ritual spells? If so, who's Gnosis is it based on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24738-the-dunkening","name":"THE DUNKENING","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:42:54-07:00","id":1396261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396256#post1396256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I would not consider worked materials count as a corpse (but that's a personal judgement call because the line between Death and Matter is not explained in the game). However, even if it did, you couldn't necessarily cast a Death version of Aegis on it anyway. Aegis works by changing a material property, which falls under Matter regardless of the nature of the subject. That's the reason you can't just cast a Life version of Aegis on a living person, turning their skin virtually indestructible. No, you need to actually grant them biological armour (such as tougher hide or a carapace) if you intend to replicate the effect using Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, how does that reconcile with the death spell &quot;Shadow Crafting&quot;? According to that spell, Death by itself seems fully capable of granting material properties to shadows, which ordinarily do not have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24738-the-dunkening","name":"THE DUNKENING","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:44:50-07:00","id":1396262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>THE DUNKENING</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396261#post1396261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, how does that reconcile with the death spell &quot;Shadow Crafting&quot;? According to that spell, Death by itself seems fully capable of granting material properties to shadows, which ordinarily do not have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The combination of Death and shadows is notorious for breaking the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:57:57-07:00","id":1396265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396262#post1396262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The combination of Death and shadows is notorious for breaking the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but it's not only death that does it. Even something like the direct damage Matter spells seem to spill over into other arcana. Windstrike doesn't deal damage because of any base property of air, it deals damage because of the force put behind the air, and that force is directly under the purview of Forces. Yet, conjunctional Forces isn't required for that spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24738-the-dunkening","name":"THE DUNKENING","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:02:24-07:00","id":1396272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>THE DUNKENING</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396265#post1396265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but it's not only death that does it. Even something like the direct damage Matter spells seem to spill over into other arcana. Windstrike doesn't deal damage because of any base property of air, it deals damage because of the force put behind the air, and that force is directly under the purview of Forces. Yet, conjunctional Forces isn't required for that spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct damage spells are notorious for breaking the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:16:02-07:00","id":1396402,"title":"","content":"Question created by the recent brief exchange about werewolves and Spirit:<br /> How do werewolves perceive a mage with 4 or more dots in Spirit, since said mage now has spirit rank? Would they treat the mage like a spirit, be confused, or (due to technically being not spirits even if they deal with spirits as part of their normal existence) would they not notice change made by the Spirit 4 attainment at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:55:00-07:00","id":1396418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396402#post1396402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question created by the recent brief exchange about werewolves and Spirit:<br /> How do werewolves perceive a mage with 4 or more dots in Spirit, since said mage now has spirit rank? Would they treat the mage like a spirit, be confused, or (due to technically being not spirits even if they deal with spirits as part of their normal existence) would they not notice change made by the Spirit 4 attainment at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have no innate way of knowing whether someone has Rank or not. They can't even tell what honorary Rank other werewolves have unless they can perceive another's Renown and know how Renown correlates to honorary Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:56:44-07:00","id":1396419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396402#post1396402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question created by the recent brief exchange about werewolves and Spirit:<br /> How do werewolves perceive a mage with 4 or more dots in Spirit, since said mage now has spirit rank? Would they treat the mage like a spirit, be confused, or (due to technically being not spirits even if they deal with spirits as part of their normal existence) would they not notice change made by the Spirit 4 attainment at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i dont know if werewolf can perceive ranks, but the mage acquire an honorary rank the same way as a werewolf does, so i think that there would be no confusion on the nature of the mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:27:35-07:00","id":1396552,"title":"","content":"Psychic Domination (Mind 2) uses Potency for its primary spell factor. This makes me believe that if I cast it, give the command jump on the spot for 1 hour, and succeed, the person will do just that for one hour.<br /> <br /> 1) Is that the case?<br /> <br /> 2) If that is the case, does that mean reaching for advanced duration will allow me to give new orders for the rest of the scene?<br /> <br /> 3) If that is not the case, why is the spell's primary factor potency instead of duration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:01:02-07:00","id":1396559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396552#post1396552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) If that is not the case, why is the spell's primary factor potency instead of duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Withstood spell whose effect is not inherently dependent upon lasting a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:14:17-07:00","id":1396563,"title":"","content":"Does that mean my initial interpretation is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:53:47-07:00","id":1396591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396563#post1396563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean my initial interpretation is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The ideas form urges and desires within the subject that he is compelled to act upon even against his will <u>as long as the spell remains active.</u>&quot; You need Advanced Duration to make any command hold for longer than the timeframe represented by Transitory Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T21:12:15-07:00","id":1396602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396563#post1396563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean my initial interpretation is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the duration of the spell, you can give the target simple one-word commands that aren't against their will. (not sure how this is worked out, I think 99% of commands not using the extra reach options will probably count as against the targets will, hell if it's not why are you needing to mind control them?) If you use the reach version to give them commands against their will it specifically says only one task and it can not be suicidal, the +2 reach options sort that.<br /> <br /> It seems odd that without any reach options, commanding somebody to &quot;Jump&quot; for an hour isn't against their will? Can anybody think of some examples for nonreach uses that don't seem dumb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-15-2020, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T21:37:14-07:00","id":1396608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396602#post1396602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems odd that without any reach options, commanding somebody to &quot;Jump&quot; for an hour isn't against their will? Can anybody think of some examples for nonreach uses that don't seem dumb?</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-Reach <i>also</i> operates even against the target's will. The distinction is that without Reach you're limited to simple instructions that the target carries out in line with your intent, while Reach allows you the complexity of instruction to send the target to specific locations and/or carry out specific tasks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T22:20:41-07:00","id":1396613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396608#post1396608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Reach <i>also</i> operates even against the target's will. The distinction is that without Reach you're limited to simple instructions that the target carries out in line with your intent, while Reach allows you the complexity of instruction to send the target to specific locations and/or carry out specific tasks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overcoming the withstand rating is basically overpowering their will and that's why its withstood, I just derped. The no reach option is like you say simple one-word commands. Being able to give multiple one-word commands esp with a long duration can still accomplish a lot i think. &quot;Follow&quot; (maybe a bit ambiguous), &quot;Stop&quot;/&quot;Stay&quot; etc..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-15-2020, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:27:11-07:00","id":1396808,"title":"","content":"Crossover question: Does a Beast with Advanced Fame gain an increased sympathetic Withstand floor relative to their regular Fame dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:31:00-07:00","id":1396943,"title":"","content":"Question about mage sight<br /> <br /> So from my understanding from Signs Of Sorcery, every mage sees the symbols of her path. Acanthus see the thorns and the mists, Thrysus feel Ecstacy and hear the singing paths, and so on.<br /> <br /> So how does this color individual mages' perceptions? From what I understand, they all experience it in their own unique ways, but they still have the mainstays of they Realm of Arcana.<br /> <br /> I geuss as an example, one of the Thrysus examples in the corebook experiences the Primal Wild through the lens of imperial Britain. Does she still feel ecstasy and hear the singing paths? How does her mage sight look like in addition to those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T08:54:17-07:00","id":1397301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396808#post1396808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover question: Does a Beast with Advanced Fame gain an increased sympathetic Withstand floor relative to their regular Fame dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s how I\u2019d do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T08:55:58-07:00","id":1397302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396943#post1396943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about mage sight<br /> <br /> So from my understanding from Signs Of Sorcery, every mage sees the symbols of her path. Acanthus see the thorns and the mists, Thrysus feel Ecstacy and hear the singing paths, and so on.<br /> <br /> So how does this color individual mages' perceptions? From what I understand, they all experience it in their own unique ways, but they still have the mainstays of they Realm of Arcana.<br /> <br /> I geuss as an example, one of the Thrysus examples in the corebook experiences the Primal Wild through the lens of imperial Britain. Does she still feel ecstasy and hear the singing paths? How does her mage sight look like in addition to those?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages of the same Path experience similar themes through their Sight, but the details are individualized. You can make them whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T01:08:42-07:00","id":1397912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1396182#post1396182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean they should be affected by Spirit at high harmony, Life at low harmony, and both in the middle? I had assumed a werewolf on the material side of the gauntlet was ultimately a living thing subject to Life, on the other side of the gauntlet effectively a spirit subject to Spirit magic, regardless of harmony ranking. I can't point out any RAW reference spelling that out however.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a really cool idea, irregardless if it is accurate or not. That's a cool idea!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T17:54:24-07:00","id":1398265,"title":"","content":"How much of the crossover advice in Tome of Mysteries can be safely left in 1E? It seems that 2E changes a lot of the advice Tome of Mysteries has on crossover, particularly because we now have clash of wills, which typically gives every side a fair shot with supernatural potency + thingy vs ditto. Or does a lot of it still stack up?<br /> <br /> Example, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:LinotypeZapfino-Three\">Vitae, Essence and Mana<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyT-Regu\">While mages can make use of spirit Essence, they cannot<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyT-Regu\">directly steal it from a werewolf. (In theory, in the highly<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyT-Regu\">improbable event that a willworker and an Uratha were<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyT-Regu\">to work together on such a project, it might be possible to<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyT-Regu\">allow such an exchange to occur between two willing parties.)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So, life+spirit cannot take essence from a werewolf still or would this fly nowadays? I'd imagine it could come down to a clash of wills but I'd also happily accept clashing against Luna and auto-losing like what is commonly tossed around with affecting G-M Angels and clashing against the God-Machine and losing.<br /> <br /> I was rereading parts of Tome of Mysteries and Left-Hand Path to compare Tremere lore with Nameless and Accursed, and while I know 1E is 1E, I still find a lot of the lore helpful! But I also feel a little in over my head with it sometimes, since Tome of Mysteries compares 1e vamp with 1e mage and such, and 1e vamp and 2e vamp are pretty different, much less 1e vamp and 2e <i>mage</i></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T06:54:36-07:00","id":1398348,"title":"","content":"Stealing Essence from a Werewolf would work if they have no means of protecting themselves from its loss. You only lose against the GM when trying to make its angels go off mission which would force them to Fall because Mages shouldn't be out there creating splats. Though apparently they're sometimes the origins of Deviants, so...eh.<br /> <br /> When comparing 1e to 2e usually it's safest to keep the lore and chuck or update the mechanics. Then if the lore in 2e specifically disagrees with a bit of lore in 1e, the 2e lore is more up to date and should be what you work with unless you have specific reasons for not wanting to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T07:05:33-07:00","id":1398350,"title":"","content":"Spirit alone should do it just fine. After all, you don't need Life+Prime to channel Mana from a mage. (And if you can steal the fuel trait of mages, why not from other splats; especially those with fuel traits you can hold in your own pattern?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T07:45:01-07:00","id":1398358,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say it's Spirit to steal Essence, Spirit+Prime to convert Essence to Mana. I'd also make it a combat roll, so Aiming rules and Withstanding apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/518-alieron","name":"Alieron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T07:51:55-07:00","id":1398359,"title":"","content":"What was the ruling on spells that use potency as a kind of ammunition, especially fate spells, when using multiple subjects? Do they all share the same potency or do they each get uses of the fate spells per potency? Like lets have 4 subjects and 10 potency. Do they all take from the proverbial cookie jar, or do they each have 10 uses each, like their own private ammo cache of fate to draw upon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:35:56-07:00","id":1398494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1398359#post1398359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the ruling on spells that use potency as a kind of ammunition, especially fate spells, when using multiple subjects? Do they all share the same potency or do they each get uses of the fate spells per potency? Like let's have 4 subjects and 10 potency. Do they all take from the proverbial cookie jar, or do they each have 10 uses each, like their own private ammo cache of fate to draw upon?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same way, if you give +3 strength to 5 people, they each get 1 instance of a +3 strength spell, each person would get 10 uses. There was a huge argument over what happens when you use it over an area at one point that never got resolved though. My interpretation was while in the area a person receives an instance of the spell and has access to his own 10 uses, he can use them in the area but once he uses them up that's it, he can't leave and return and get a new 10 uses. Other peoples think that the area has 10 uses and people in the area spend from that common pool of only 10 uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T19:41:33-07:00","id":1398505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alieron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1398358#post1398358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would say it's Spirit to steal Essence, Spirit+Prime to convert Essence to Mana. I'd also make it a combat roll, so Aiming rules and Withstanding apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need to worry about Aiming if you are not using the Reach for Sensory Range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T19:45:44-07:00","id":1398507,"title":"","content":"As the person pushing the latter argument for AoE spells I'll admit after giving it some time to mellow and ruminate on it I've backed down from that take. I had that stance because it felt like it was a way of gaming spell factors. Since then I've realized that there are other spells that similarly game factors, for instance the Reach on Transform Life lets you get Subjects beyond the original amount set by your spell. So let that be the end of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T10:36:16-07:00","id":1400134,"title":"","content":"do I need to use a reach to gain sensory range on spells like Words of Truth? My reading of it seems conflicted on whether it\u2019s a spell the mage is casting on themselves to make their words ring with truth or if it\u2019s something you\u2019re casting on the target to make them hear the truth of your words. It\u2019s a withstood spell, but it\u2019s base description is that \u201call subjects of this spell can hear her and understand her clearly, regardless of distance, noise, or language barriers.\u201d Which suggests you\u2019re casting on a subject rather than yourself. So if I were to cast this without sensory range, I would have to touch the subject and then after that (provided what I\u2019m saying is within the duration of the spell) they would have that effect on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T10:56:02-07:00","id":1400137,"title":"","content":"<br /> [Edit] I remembered the spell incorrectly, Tessie is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-30-2020, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T13:03:51-07:00","id":1400163,"title":"","content":"You cast it on the people you wish to hear and understand you. The spell explicitly says they are the subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T22:42:24-07:00","id":1400458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1400134#post1400134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do I need to use a reach to gain sensory range on spells like Words of Truth? My reading of it seems conflicted on whether it\u2019s a spell the mage is casting on themselves to make their words ring with truth or if it\u2019s something you\u2019re casting on the target to make them hear the truth of your words. It\u2019s a withstood spell, but it\u2019s base description is that \u201call subjects of this spell can hear her and understand her clearly, regardless of distance, noise, or language barriers.\u201d Which suggests you\u2019re casting on a subject rather than yourself. So if I were to cast this without sensory range, I would have to touch the subject and then after that (provided what I\u2019m saying is within the duration of the spell) they would have that effect on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell, as intended, will target people the Mage wants to speak to and be believed by, and is Withstood. So if you want to convince someone you are telling the truth, you have to touch them, or, use sensory range. O\u0335r\u0335,\u0335 \u0335c\u0335a\u0335s\u0335t\u0335 \u0335a\u0335s\u0335 \u0335a\u0335n\u0335 \u0335a\u0335r\u0335e\u0335a\u0335 \u0335o\u0335f\u0335 \u0335e\u0335f\u0335f\u0335e\u0335c\u0335t\u0335 \u0335a\u0335n\u0335d\u0335 \u0335t\u0335h\u0335e\u0335 \u0335s\u0335p\u0335e\u0335l\u0335l\u0335 \u0335w\u0335i\u0335l\u0335l\u0335 \u0335b\u0335e\u0335 \u0335w\u0335i\u0335t\u0335h\u0335s\u0335t\u0335o\u0335o\u0335d\u0335 \u0335b\u0335y\u0335 \u0335t\u0335h\u0335e\u0335 \u0335h\u0335i\u0335g\u0335h\u0335e\u0335s\u0335t\u0335 \u0335c\u0335o\u0335m\u0335p\u0335o\u0335s\u0335u\u0335r\u0335e\u0335 \u0335w\u0335i\u0335t\u0335h\u0335i\u0335n\u0335 \u0335r\u0335a\u0335n\u0335g\u0335e\u0335,\u0335 \u0335a\u0335n\u0335d\u0335 \u0335t\u0335h\u0335e\u0335n\u0335 \u0335*\u0335e\u0335v\u0335e\u0335r\u0335y\u0335o\u0335n\u0335e\u0335*\u0335 \u0335w\u0335i\u0335l\u0335l\u0335 \u0335b\u0335e\u0335 \u0335s\u0335u\u0335s\u0335c\u0335e\u0335p\u0335t\u0335i\u0335b\u0335l\u0335e\u0335 \u0335t\u0335o\u0335 \u0335t\u0335h\u0335e\u0335 \u0335c\u0335a\u0335s\u0335t\u0335e\u0335r\u0335'\u0335s\u0335 \u0335w\u0335o\u0335r\u0335d\u0335s\u0335 \u0335o\u0335f\u0335 \u0335t\u0335r\u0335u\u0335t\u0335h\u0335.\u0335<br /> <br /> However, given Creative Thaumaturgy, if you want to design spells where anyone can benefit from words of truth, but only within a defined area, or other permutations, that's definitely doable. The spell as described shouldn't rule out other possibilities with creative thaumaturgy, provided it is still within the theme and scope of Prime and the Practice you are looking at. It should be possible to cast a version of the spell where the person you are speaking to is giving a testimony, and the mage herself is the &quot;subject&quot; who will receive the words of truth.<br /> <br /> Or at least I hope so, but this seems like a good look at it to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 07-02-2020, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T01:19:34-07:00","id":1400472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1400458#post1400458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, cast as an area of effect and the spell will be withstood by the highest composure within range, and then *everyone* will be susceptible to the caster's words of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. An AoE means that everyone within the area is a subject and each subject applies Withstand separately. If you cast it at Potency 3 over an area, everyone with Composure 3 or higher will be unaffected while everyone with Composure 1 or 2 (or who chooses not to apply Composure as their Withstand rating) are affected while they remain within the area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T01:56:55-07:00","id":1400476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1400472#post1400472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. An AoE means that everyone within the area is a subject and each subject applies Withstand separately. If you cast it at Potency 3 over an area, everyone with Composure 3 or higher will be unaffected while everyone with Composure 1 or 2 (or who chooses not to apply Composure as their Withstand rating) are affected while they remain within the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez so blunt, but thanks, I was wrong. I must have been doing the above as a short-hand for large groups.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> I'd love an opinion from anyone, though, about how or why Tremere can steal souls from werewolves, unless that's an errata. I seem to remember a lot of how Mages and other stuff can't normally do that since a werewolf is a fusion of flesh and spirit? Or if it is a logical justification. What happens to the werewolf though? Would they just get soul loss conditions or does this make an empty wolf? It has been awhile since I read about what the Idigam do to them and would love a comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 07-02-2020, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T02:48:56-07:00","id":1400484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1400476#post1400476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez so blunt, but thanks, I was wrong. I must have been doing the above as a short-hand for large groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies. I do like the concept. I'd use it either as a universal Reach option for AoE spells, or having a Merit (with Space or Mind as prerequisite) grant it as a free option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1400476#post1400476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit:<br /> I'd love an opinion from anyone, though, about how or why Tremere can steal souls from werewolves, unless that's an errata. I seem to remember a lot of how Mages and other stuff can't normally do that since a werewolf is a fusion of flesh and spirit? Or if it is a logical justification. What happens to the werewolf though? Would they just get soul loss conditions or does this make an empty wolf? It has been awhile since I read about what the Idigam do to them and would love a comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there's nothing that says that mages can't do it with werewolves. It's just that the two published spells only works on Sleepers and mages, respectively.<br /> Werewolves being a fusion of flesh and ephemera doesn't factor into it; they still have souls (or something that is close enough) as evident by idigam being able to rip them out. If mages can't do it with spells, it's because their souls are considered part of the template and can't be messed around with.<br /> <br /> Tremere does it through their own special traits (that honestly should be called Hollow Attainments or even Dread Powers; not just &quot;Other Traits&quot;) so them being able to do it doesn't imply anything about the possibility of doing it through spells. (And in a reversal, they can't do it on Beasts because they have Horrors instead of souls, but Horrors can explicitly be separated from Beasts using spells. This kills the Beast.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T07:10:50-07:00","id":1400515,"title":"","content":"I would say you can sever a werewolf's soul, but it would require conjunctional Spirit and it would be a Patterning of both Arcana (I am assuming supernaturals have a stronger connection to their souls). The idea is that their souls is differently integrated into them than standard humans and so require an extra level of specialization to separate them from their vessel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T07:45:09-07:00","id":1400521,"title":"","content":"Actually, when reading through Dave Brookshaw's spoiler for Tremere and souls in N&amp;A, I found that Death 5 works on vampires, werewolves and changelings. It certainly makes sense that vampires and changelings don't have proper souls (since the former dies before becoming a vampire, meaning the soul passes on, and the latter has their soul ripped to shreds (unless that was another edition/version of the game)).<br /> It's interesting to note that werewolves either lose their souls or have them dramatically transformed (more so than the souls of mages and possibly deviants since the latter explicitly has souls; they're just horribly broken) as part of the First Change. I doubt it just ejects because it's not needed, so I'm quite curious about what'd happen if it was removed before (or during) the First Change.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/pePHGAc.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"at