:[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T13:44:32-07:00","id":1401185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1401181#post1401181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Compelling of Forces be enough to harness ambient static energy to create a Van Der Waals grip, allowing the mage to cling to surfaces like a gecko ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you do it normally/naturally? If no, then Compelling is not the way to go. Ruling, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T15:08:59-07:00","id":1401198,"title":"","content":"Geckos can, so I was hoping to enable it in the same way Nightvision enables bat echolocation or a shark's bioelectric vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T04:20:50-07:00","id":1401316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1401198#post1401198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geckos can, so I was hoping to enable it in the same way Nightvision enables bat echolocation or a shark's bioelectric vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightvision is an Unveiling spell. It lets you take in more information, which is exactly what Unveiling is supposed to do.<br /> You also can't compare animal features because &quot;gaining/emulating an animal feature&quot; is not a Forces effect. It's a coincidental side effect of that particular spell. If anything, it'd imply you'd require a Weaving spell because that's the practice of Transform Life (which grants animal features).<br /> <br /> Compelling spells are supposed to &quot;nudge a preferred but possible outcome into reality.&quot; While what's &quot;possible&quot; is stretched really thin with many spells, the spirit of the rule is that it shouldn't require much force/energy. Moving around things with little to no mass, shaping things with little to no substance, activating pre-existing processes and systems, etc, are the most common effects.<br /> <br /> Also, if you look to the three Influence spells that are Compelling you'll see that they all only direct existing forces and are explicitly incapable of increasing them.<br /> <br /> To emulate a gecko you need to significantly increase the electrostatic interaction to support a huge amount of weight. That goes far beyond the description of Compelling as well as the Forces Compelling precedents we have in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:58:50-07:00","id":1401973,"title":"","content":"How unlikely is it to see a Guardian of the Veil as a Hierarch? I haven't read their book, and am not clear on the subtleties of their idea that all thrones are false in juxtaposition to their own political authority within and without the Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T17:50:33-07:00","id":1401996,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the above, are the 1st edition Order books good reads or are they fairly outdated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T19:23:03-07:00","id":1402005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1401973#post1401973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How unlikely is it to see a Guardian of the Veil as a Hierarch? I haven't read their book, and am not clear on the subtleties of their idea that all thrones are false in juxtaposition to their own political authority within and without the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an excerpt from the book, p123, '\u200bHierarch: One can travel the seven seas and the like number of continents, and she will seldom \ufb01nd a Hierarch who belongs to the Guardians of the Veil. The Guardians are so disliked and distrusted that achieving the popular support necessary for ascendance to the position would be a true political miracle.'<br /> <br /> It gets more into what those situations are like, usually being about the consilium needing what the Guardians offer and are good at (namely secrecy) but also occasionally the Guardians taking control in a consilium by force. It's implied that even when there is a Guardian Hierarch, it doesn't last long..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1401996#post1401996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the above, are the 1st edition Order books good reads or are they fairly outdated?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still relevant, though they are dense reads, and the mechanics are pretty much all outdated, practices and Arcana having shifted around a bit and Merits I think having more impact in second edition. They get into that a bit <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, but to quote &quot;That\u2019s a significant portion of the edition\u2019s wordcount devoted to developing the Orders described in the first edition core, and we have no desire to throw it away, so the first thing I can tell you about the Orders in second edition is\u2026 You\u2019ll recognize them. If you\u2019ve read Left Hand Path or Mage Noir, both written after all the Order books were out, you\u2019ve seen roughly how we think of the Orders. Our Guardians of the Veil are clearly the Guardians from their book. That\u2019s not to say we\u2019re not placing emphasis in slightly different places, or tweaking here and there, but if you own the Order books rest assured that they\u2019re still very much relevant in the new edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the Free Council have changed the most? They went over it more when the book came out, the question came up a lot (you can probably find the developer and writers talking about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-09-2020, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T20:12:29-07:00","id":1402008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1402005#post1402005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an excerpt from the book, p123, '\u200bHierarch: One can travel the seven seas and the like number of continents, and she will seldom \ufb01nd a Hierarch who belongs to the Guardians of the Veil. The Guardians are so disliked and distrusted that achieving the popular support necessary for ascendance to the position would be a true political miracle.'<br /> <br /> It gets more into what those situations are like, usually being about the consilium needing what the Guardians offer and are good at (namely secrecy) but also occasionally the Guardians taking control in a consilium by force. It's implied that even when there is a Guardian Hierarch, it doesn't last long..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're still relevant, though they are dense reads, and the mechanics are pretty much all outdated, practices and Arcana having shifted around a bit and Merits I think having more impact in second edition. They get into that a bit <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, but to quote &amp;quot;That\u2019s a significant portion of the edition\u2019s wordcount devoted to developing the Orders described in the first edition core, and we have no desire to throw it away, so the first thing I can tell you about the Orders in second edition is\u2026 You\u2019ll recognize them. If you\u2019ve read Left Hand Path or Mage Noir, both written after all the Order books were out, you\u2019ve seen roughly how we think of the Orders. Our Guardians of the Veil are clearly the Guardians from their book. That\u2019s not to say we\u2019re not placing emphasis in slightly different places, or tweaking here and there, but if you own the Order books rest assured that they\u2019re still very much relevant in the new edition.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I think the Free Council have changed the most? They went over it more when the book came out, the question came up a lot (you can probably find the developer and writers talking about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you nofather. It's great to hear they wrote the orders in 2nd edition with that in mind.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, you mean the Free Council changed the most from its book to 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T20:29:37-07:00","id":1402009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1401973#post1401973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How unlikely is it to see a Guardian of the Veil as a Hierarch? I haven't read their book, and am not clear on the subtleties of their idea that all thrones are false in juxtaposition to their own political authority within and without the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, how desperate are they ? The Guardians are the secret police of the Awakened, so the level of transparency required of a hierarch position would not come easily to them. Because of this, putting an Eleventh Question as Hierarch could work, because they are committed to the truth and can make good liasons, or intimidate with how much they know.<br /> <br /> Another option is Bearer of the Eternal Voice, but they would need to be very discrete as to not let people know they are one or using their gifts.<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of need. If there is a crisis so serious that only the Guardians can deal with, then having them take the lead is natural. But that also means they may fabricate the incident that tilts the scales to this outcome.<br /> <br /> Another option is if there is too much political infighting and only the Guardians can mediate to keep everyone in line. Lets say there are few Ladders in a Consilium, the Mysterium and Free Council constantly bicker about research and access to information. In that case, an Arrow and Guardian alliance may keep the order, since Arrow philosophy is against taking a permanent role of power, the Guardians may be the only ones for for the job.<br /> <br /> In summary, it all comes down to whether circumstances are grave enough that you would agree to be lead by spies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-10-2020, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T20:29:38-07:00","id":1402010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1402008#post1402008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you nofather. It's great to hear they wrote the orders in 2nd edition with that in mind.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, you mean the Free Council changed the most from its book to 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: nevermind, just read up on that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T13:10:44-07:00","id":1402108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1402009#post1402009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends, how desperate are they ? The Guardians are the secret police of the Awakened, so the level of transparency required of a hierarch position would not come easily to them. Because of this, putting an Eleventh Question as Hierarch could work, because they are committed to the truth and can make good liasons, or intimidate with how much they know.<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>don't saaay?</i> Omigosh that's amazing!! He's already an Eleventh Question so that's perfect! Yay that makes me so excited!<br /> <br /> And thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> too! That was the info I felt was why I should ask this question before I proceeded. My Guardian Hierarch is kind of in a strange situation too--in a sign of cooperation, the position is only of a &quot;Dual-Hierarch&quot;, one for domestic issues, the other for the Mystery that seems determined to blow the lid off the Veil and to support the local Arrows who took a <i>huuuge </i>hit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T13:14:42-07:00","id":1402109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1402108#post1402108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You <i>don't saaay?</i> Omigosh that's amazing!! He's already an Eleventh Question so that's perfect! Yay that makes me so excited!<br /> <br /> And thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> too! That was the info I felt was why I should ask this question before I proceeded. My Guardian Hierarch is kind of in a strange situation too--in a sign of cooperation, the position is only of a &quot;Dual-Hierarch&quot;, one for domestic issues, the other for the Mystery that seems determined to blow the lid off the Veil and to support the local Arrows who took a <i>huuuge </i>hit!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is an old post by Dave that I think captures the feel well on how the Questions fit into Guardian politics (its from RPG.net, so I wasn't sure how else to post the quote here):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Yeah. I like the tension between the Question and the rest of the order - in a magical society of liars, having people dedicated to uncovering the truth is unsettling.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In my house game, the local 11Q is one step removed from local Guardian leadership thanks to that, despite being a Master. He's not a particularly easy man to get along with. He uses the second attainment almost as reflex now, and having been mildly discriminated against because of his Legacy his whole career he's long since stopped even pretending to be sorry about it - if someone is going to be freaked out anyway, he may as well cultivate that image. Naturally, the local Guardians made him Emissary (the Guardian in charge of inter-order relations) because that discourages the other orders from interfering with them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Anyways - he, finding no suitable apprentices in his own order and with a mid-high but pretty unshakable order status, has decided to take a Free Councillor (one of the PCS) as an apprentice, and is teaching him Time ready to induct him into the Legacy despite the fallout that will result - in his opinion, the Epopt can </span></span></span><i>try</i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> to punish him for breaking the order restriction on his Legacy, but he gave her several years to steer Guardian apprentices his way and he has more dirt on her than anyone else could even suspect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This gives the Guardian PC in the cabal the screaming heebie jeebees. He already regards the 11Q as being nearly heretical, and sees the Master's social troubles and seeming inability to not use his attainments on everyone he talks to as being a result of the Legacy; the 11Q, to a young Messianistic-leaning Guardian who takes the order-as-a-religion very seriously, are </span></span></span><i>broken</i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. They've given up their ability to function as proper Guardians in order to fulfil their niche role perfectly. Whenever the 11Q is around, the Guardian tolerates all his eccentricities because he thinks the 11Q is a holy man. Like a mad hermit kind of a holy man. As for what he thinks about the Libertine PC being steered Question-wards, it's like a trainee priest finding out one of his friends is being recruited by a hardcore monastary, despite not believing in God.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">All of this, naturally, is lost on the Libertine who just sees a Master taking an interest in him.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(And you're right - the Attainments are only one element in a whole suite of powers. But Questions have all those Mage Sight spells available as per normal. The Attainments are the deductive cherry on top. Other mages will eventually get to the same conclusion, but a Question does it faster)&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T23:12:26-07:00","id":1404531,"title":"","content":"Do the effects of <i>Zoom In</i> compound with those of <i>The Outward and Inward Eye</i> ? For example, if <i>Zoom In</i> lets them see for two miles, would that combine to let the caster see everything within the two miles radius in every direction ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T14:00:00-07:00","id":1404636,"title":"","content":"I've ruled that a &quot;yes&quot; in the past, but required perception rolls to see things of interest due to the enormous breadth of perspective. The reason is that bit in Outward and Inward Eye about the subject still being able to be surprised by dent of a distraction. Clearly it requires some mental effort and focus on the subject's part to understand what she's seeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T14:18:38-07:00","id":1404641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1404636#post1404636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've ruled that a &quot;yes&quot; in the past, but required perception rolls to see things of interest due to the enormous breadth of perspective. The reason is that bit in Outward and Inward Eye about the subject still being able to be surprised by dent of a distraction. Clearly it requires some mental effort and focus on the subject's part to understand what she's seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent, thank you. It doesn't completely rule out the possibility. But it allows and archeomancer to explore from relative safety and anticipate ambushes consistently well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T22:39:38-07:00","id":1405472,"title":"","content":"2 questions<br /> <br /> 1) Are the spell factors of an imbued item set and unable to be changed?<br /> 2) Are there any ways a sleepwalker could boost the casting roll besides willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T23:10:48-07:00","id":1405477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1405472#post1405472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions<br /> <br /> 1) Are the spell factors of an imbued item set and unable to be changed?<br /> 2) Are there any ways a sleepwalker could boost the casting roll besides willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 i think that only always on items have fixed factors<br /> <br /> 2 increasing the ritual time if not using istant casting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T05:05:07-07:00","id":1405546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1405472#post1405472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions<br /> <br /> 1) Are the spell factors of an imbued item set and unable to be changed?<br /> 2) Are there any ways a sleepwalker could boost the casting roll besides willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find someone to cast AoE Fate boons centered on the imbued item, which can only be used to activate it. 8-again, rote property, dice bonuses, you can make the activation roll a lot more reliable. While that doesn't depend on only the Sleepwalker, maybe they know a Fate mage who owes them a favor or they can even hire one in a Lorehouse.<br /> <br /> A Veiling of Fate should probably be used as well, so the increased improbability of all these lucky coincidences is hidden from Sleepers, preventing Breaking Points and Quiescence (at least from the casting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-31-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T03:59:03-07:00","id":1406934,"title":"","content":"Not sure in which thread it would be better to post this...<br /> In dark eras 2 there is a Mage spell (fate 4, mind 1, + optional death 4) that allows a changeling to learn Goblin contract from the target creature as if it was a hobgoblin.<br /> Assuming that Strix are possible targets, i m wondering if there is a way to create a similar effect with a Cruac ritual.<br /> What themes should it use if possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:57:07-07:00","id":1408382,"title":"","content":"I know that goetia do not &quot;naturally&quot; have manifestations, so no free ones from rank but would it be absurd to allow them to spend a numina on a manifestation as other ephemeral beings can as this is more &quot;learnt&quot; than natural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T12:53:27-07:00","id":1408398,"title":"","content":"Is it according to the rules? No. Is it absurd? Also no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:18:12-07:00","id":1408447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1408382#post1408382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that goetia do not &quot;naturally&quot; have manifestations, so no free ones from rank but would it be absurd to allow them to spend a numina on a manifestation as other ephemeral beings can as this is more &quot;learnt&quot; than natural?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from the BPG's more focused discussion of Dreamborn, the framing of &quot;they <u>don't have</u> Manifestations&quot; combines with goetia being NPCs who don't go through an onscreen advancement process to suggest to me that they can't &quot;spend&quot; Numina slots on Manifestation, particularly given that the BPG's take mostly makes explicit things that are inferred by absence in Mage 2e Core's writeup \u2014 the Invisible Entities section accords the ability to buy more Manifestations to spirits and ghosts and specifically says that goetia don't naturally have Manifestations but can be given them by magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T20:39:00-07:00","id":1410442,"title":"","content":"The spell Create Sympathy says &quot;To a Master of Space, powerful connections are forged as easily as snapping one\u2019s fingers. With this spell, the mage creates a new sympathetic connection on the subject. These new connections are Lasting, but can fade with time as described on p. 172.&quot;. Does that require the spell to target both the subject receiving the sympathetic link and the object/place/person it's being linked to or does it only have to target the subject receiving the link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25869-jesterthemad","user":"JesterTheMad","date":". 08-25-2020, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25869-jesterthemad","name":"JesterTheMad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T13:36:50-07:00","id":1410878,"title":"","content":"Have the Lords of Mars been detailed anywhere ? As far as Signs of Sorcery suggested, they seem like a Prime focused Moros Legacy. The Mars that could have been has a very Stygian sound to it, but the writeup for the Emanation mentions &quot;electric storms&quot; (Forces) and demons (Mind). But it says they summon the power of the red planet, its artifacts and entombed servants. So it sounds like a blend of ghost and platonic manipulation.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to ask, do Path tools elevate a tool to a +2 or make them usable twice (Arcadian aspect added on top of the standard one) ? For example, a silver mirror could be effective in any spell that targets the self, uses the Arcadian Arcanum or play on the Fae themes, correct ? So a boon on a person reflected in it would be able to add +1 in two separate instances, once for being a mirror and again for being a Path tool ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-28-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T14:11:19-07:00","id":1410883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1410878#post1410878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wanted to ask, do Path tools elevate a tool to a +2 or make them usable twice (Arcadian aspect added on top of the standard one) ? For example, a silver mirror could be effective in any spell that targets the self, uses the Arcadian Arcanum or play on the Fae themes, correct ? So a boon on a person reflected in it would be able to add +1 in two separate instances, once for being a mirror and again for being a Path tool ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Path Tool is one way to make tools actually grant dice as Yantras. A silver mirror is a +1 Yantra for any Acanthus who uses it in any spell (regardless of Arcanum) that fits the symbolism. It is not a valid Tool Yantra for any other Path unless there is a specific reason for it (like a Legacy Yantra).<br /> <br /> To rephrase it: The five Path Tool categories are only valid Yantras if they are Path Tools. Coins, cups, mirrors, etc, are not general Tool Yantras that can always be applicable. They need to be tied to the Path by using the right materials (or shapes, in the case of weapons) in order to become usable as Yantras.<br /> Additionally, if something is valid as two separate Yantras (a switchblade being both a Rod and a Weapon) you'd need to add it as two separate Yantras in order to gain +1 and +1 dice from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-28-2020, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T15:26:12-07:00","id":1410892,"title":"","content":"1. Since nothing seems to prevent a Soul-Shocked character from re-entering the Astral before the condition is resolved, is there anything official on what might happen if an already soul-shocked character re-enters the Astral and &quot;dies&quot; again? I'm planning an Astral-heavy game, and I'd like it if the players were risking more than a few points of willpower if they die repeatedly.<br /> <br /> 2. Generally speaking, a Mage does not have to worry about witnesses causing Paradox while in the Tenemos, correct? They can still over-Reach, but, barring truly exceptional circumstances, there's no actual Sleepers around, just Goetia.<br /> <br /> 3. A bit off-the-wall, but a Harrowed Banisher would still be able to use magic in his Oneiros without fear of Paradox like a normal Mage, correct? Presumably he'd still suffer the normal Harrowed problems, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T17:20:32-07:00","id":1410906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1410892#post1410892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Since nothing seems to prevent a Soul-Shocked character from re-entering the Astral before the condition is resolved, is there anything official on what might happen if an already soul-shocked character re-enters the Astral and &quot;dies&quot; again? I'm planning an Astral-heavy game, and I'd like it if the players were risking more than a few points of willpower if they die repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The consequences of being &quot;killed&quot; in your own Oneiros by its own contents suggest that &quot;dying&quot; in the Astral otherwise still exhausts your Dream Health, which needs time and/or magic to recover as normal.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think 1e's hazards stopped being risks of Astral travel in the edition change; the Ecstatic Wind will still warp your soul, things from the Temenos can still warp your mind, and self-destructive behavior still has a reasonable chance of being an Act of Hubris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Generally speaking, a Mage does not have to worry about witnesses causing Paradox while in the Tenemos, correct? They can still over-Reach, but, barring truly exceptional circumstances, there's no actual Sleepers around, just Goetia. </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. A bit off-the-wall, but a Harrowed Banisher would still be able to use magic in his Oneiros without fear of Paradox like a normal Mage, correct? Presumably he'd still suffer the normal Harrowed problems, regardless. </div> </div> </div>1e's mechanics for Paradox in the Astral specified that a Banisher's Oneiros had mostly the same effects on Paradox as a Sleeper's, with possible exceptions based on their own Path or Arcana. Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T19:38:00-07:00","id":1410923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1410892#post1410892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Since nothing seems to prevent a Soul-Shocked character from re-entering the Astral before the condition is resolved, is there anything official on what might happen if an already soul-shocked character re-enters the Astral and &amp;quot;dies&amp;quot; again? I'm planning an Astral-heavy game, and I'd like it if the players were risking more than a few points of willpower if they die repeatedly.<br /> <br /> 2. Generally speaking, a Mage does not have to worry about witnesses causing Paradox while in the Tenemos, correct? They can still over-Reach, but, barring truly exceptional circumstances, there's no actual Sleepers around, just Goetia.<br /> <br /> 3. A bit off-the-wall, but a Harrowed Banisher would still be able to use magic in his Oneiros without fear of Paradox like a normal Mage, correct? Presumably he'd still suffer the normal Harrowed problems, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul Shocked means a diminished sense of self. So what happens when you are shocked again ? A couple of things come to mind:<br /> <br /> 1- Your lost sense of self connected you to another mage's Oneiros. You probably saw the Iron Door and regretted becoming an Egregore. Then again, that is the least of your problems, your Daimons seems.... off...somehow (you swapped a Virtue/Vice/Aspiration/Obsession).<br /> <br /> 2- Rather than returning to the real world, you fell into an Astral Emanation and need to exit it to return to your physical body, better hurry before it starves.<br /> <br /> 3- Something was invited into your mind. Perhaps a drone of the Morphean Continuity, The Unforgotten or even the mythos of your Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> 4- You're fine, what were you worried about? You also found a hidden operation of the Praetorian, too bad you have no idea who is the Seer whose body you inhabited. You should probably worry about where their mind went.<br /> <br /> 5- Your lesser sense of self makes you sensible to others, too sensible. Whenever you fall asleep, your mind is projected to a being talking or thinking about you, forcing you to share their senses for a scene. These beings gain a Strong sympathetic connection to the mage until the next time they dream of someone else or their sense of self is restored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T03:07:26-07:00","id":1410978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1410906#post1410906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The consequences of being &amp;quot;killed&amp;quot; in your own Oneiros by its own contents suggest that &amp;quot;dying&amp;quot; in the Astral otherwise still exhausts your Dream Health, which needs time and/or magic to recover as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the dream form is consistent between multiple journeys. There's no rules for how to regain Dream Health (unlike Corpus, another permutation of Health), and by its nature the dream form is very ephemeral and fleeting. Unlike your regular body it's not something that persists when you're not using it; you manifest it the moment you enter the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T09:43:03-07:00","id":1414220,"title":"","content":"A quick clarifications regarding Order requisitioning. Is it assumed that an Order in a Caucus always has the ability to provide its specialty resources ? For example, lets say an Arrow asks for a lunargent bullet magazine to protect their cabal on werewolf territory. If no one invested in Order Archive, does it mean the Availability rating is base price because the Order's specialty cancels out the penalty of it not being a Caucus resource ? Or does it mean that the Availability is reduced by one because its always considered a resource available to Order members ?<br /> <br /> One more question please. The main point of investing in the Order Archive merit is not to have a discount on requisitioning, but to cancel out the &quot;untrained penalty&quot; of an item outside its purview ? For example, if an Arrow from the Council of Dragons wants to make information more widely available to incentivize strategic thinking amongst Talons, adding Library to the Archives simply allows them to requisition them at base availability rather than cheaper (because that is the Mysterium's specialty), correct ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T10:32:00-07:00","id":1414227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414220#post1414220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick clarifications regarding Order requisitioning. Is it assumed that an Order in a Caucus always has the ability to provide its specialty resources ? For example, lets say an Arrow asks for a lunargent bullet magazine to protect their cabal on werewolf territory. If no one invested in Order Archive, does it mean the Availability rating is base price because the Order's specialty cancels out the penalty of it not being a Caucus resource ? Or does it mean that the Availability is reduced by one because its always considered a resource available to Order members ?<br /> <br /> One more question please. The main point of investing in the Order Archive merit is not to have a discount on requisitioning, but to cancel out the &quot;untrained penalty&quot; of an item outside its purview ? For example, if an Arrow from the Council of Dragons wants to make information more widely available to incentivize strategic thinking amongst Talons, adding Library to the Archives simply allows them to requisition them at base availability rather than cheaper (because that is the Mysterium's specialty), correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Orders aren't &quot;in&quot; a Caucus, a Caucus is a the local political organization for a particular Order. So you might have the Adamantine Arrow Caucus of the Pacific Northwest that includes Arrows that are members of all Consillia and/or Assemblies in the PNW region.<br /> <br /> If you meant &quot;Consillia&quot; then they're just separate things. Order Status lets you requisition from your Caucus, or other Caucus of the same Order at a penalty. Consillium Status lets you requisition from the Consillium. Consillium requisitions should be broader, but shallower: you have a bit of everything available to every Order represented in the Consillium, but only what the members can/will provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T11:17:54-07:00","id":1414233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414227#post1414227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Orders aren't &quot;in&quot; a Caucus, a Caucus is a the local political organization for a particular Order. So you might have the Adamantine Arrow Caucus of the Pacific Northwest that includes Arrows that are members of all Consillia and/or Assemblies in the PNW region.<br /> <br /> If you meant &quot;Consillia&quot; then they're just separate things. Order Status lets you requisition from your Caucus, or other Caucus of the same Order at a penalty. Consillium Status lets you requisition from the Consillium. Consillium requisitions should be broader, but shallower: you have a bit of everything available to every Order represented in the Consillium, but only what the members can/will provide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see. But <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> seems to imply members of the same Concilia can be under the influence of more than one Caucus, but a Caucus seems like they would have very big areas of influence. So they can overlap ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T11:50:42-07:00","id":1414240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414233#post1414233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see. But <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> seems to imply members of the same Concilia can be under the influence of more than one Caucus, but a Caucus seems like they would have very big areas of influence. So they can overlap ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A single Caucus covers a large region, but each Caucus is Order specific. So while the Arrow might have a single Caucus covering the entire PNW, the Free Council might have three Caucuses in that same area, the Guardians might have one for the entire North American West Coast, and so on. So a single Consillium, say Seattle and its environs, would be under five different Caucuses (one for each Order), but a different Consillium; San Francisco might be under the same Caucus as Seattle for the Free Council, the Mysterium, and the Silver Ladder, but a different one for the Adamantine Arrow and the Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> <br /> A single Consillium is &quot;part&quot; of every Order Caucus for which it has members of the Order and falls under their region of influence. A single Caucus will usually cover multiple Consillia. Each Order has its own set of Caucuses, and each Order's Caucuses do not necessarily have the same regions of influence as another Order's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T15:22:31-07:00","id":1414275,"title":"","content":"Question on Teleport (Space 4): The text says &quot;by default the subject's current location and destination must both be within sensory range...&quot; the implication being that you don't actually need a Reach to teleport yourself (or a subject within touch range) to a point within sensory range. This could make sense metaphysically, because unlike Co-location, you are not actually affecting the target location, you are just overwriting the subject's position. Am I reading this right?<br /> <br /> Assuming the above is correct, the question of Teleporting at Sympathetic Range gets a little weird, because the Attainment requires you to have already Reached to get Sensory Range, but for the base spell, using sensory range doesn't make sense (unless it's required to target the actual subject). So what's the intent here? Do you have to spend a total of two Reach to teleport to a destination at Sympathetic Range, even though the destination is not actually the subject of the spell, or just one Reach because the range was already &quot;sensory&quot;?<br /> <br /> My instinct is to just treat the destination as a subject for the purposes of Range, thus requiring Sensory Range to teleport farther than arms-length, but the text does not make that clear if this is the intended function of the spell. It would also make it extremely similar in function to Co-location.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T15:43:38-07:00","id":1414278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414275#post1414275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on Teleport (Space 4): The text says &quot;by default the subject's current location and destination must both be within sensory range...&quot; the implication being that you don't actually need a Reach to teleport yourself (or a subject within touch range) to a point within sensory range. This could make sense metaphysically, because unlike Co-location, you are not actually affecting the target location, you are just overwriting the subject's position. Am I reading this right?<br /> <br /> Assuming the above is correct, the question of Teleporting at Sympathetic Range gets a little weird, because the Attainment requires you to have already Reached to get Sensory Range, but for the base spell, using sensory range doesn't make sense (unless it's required to target the actual subject). So what's the intent here? Do you have to spend a total of two Reach to teleport to a destination at Sympathetic Range, even though the destination is not actually the subject of the spell, or just one Reach because the range was already &quot;sensory&quot;?<br /> <br /> My instinct is to just treat the destination as a subject for the purposes of Range, thus requiring Sensory Range to teleport farther than arms-length, but the text does not make that clear if this is the intended function of the spell. It would also make it extremely similar in function to Co-location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sensory range means that the subject you will teleport can be anywhere within your sensory range. By default you need to touch them or can only teleport yourself.<br /> <br /> The destinations can be anywhere within sensory range.<br /> <br /> A sympathetic cast can be used to teleport the subject to a location outside of sensory range. So you could send them to Mars if you had a picture from the NASA rover.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the sympathetic cast can be used to affect a subject outside of sensory range and teleport them to any point within the caster's sensory range. In this way, you could pull an imbued item from your Sanctum.<br /> <br /> You could use sympathy to cast on a subject outside of sensory range and move them somewhere outside sensory range. But you would need the one mana for the Attainment, commit two yantra slots and deal with a Withstand of the weakest connection +1, plus any other wards they may have used. So its doable, but would probably need preparations.<br /> <br /> In most mundane situations, Co-Location is sufficient. But without expending Reach on a Key, anyone with the most basic notion of Space magic or granted Space Mage Sight can use it. Even with a Key, it can be followed back for scrying, remote casting, etc. <br /> <br /> Teleportation is a lot cleaner, no magical doorway required, just a quick rewrite of the location from A to B. Well, hopefully, if they don't follow any other Nimbus impressions left by the caster.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-17-2020, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T15:50:44-07:00","id":1414279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414240#post1414240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A single Caucus covers a large region, but each Caucus is Order specific. So while the Arrow might have a single Caucus covering the entire PNW, the Free Council might have three Caucuses in that same area, the Guardians might have one for the entire North American West Coast, and so on. So a single Consillium, say Seattle and its environs, would be under five different Caucuses (one for each Order), but a different Consillium; San Francisco might be under the same Caucus as Seattle for the Free Council, the Mysterium, and the Silver Ladder, but a different one for the Adamantine Arrow and the Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> <br /> A single Consillium is &amp;quot;part&amp;quot; of every Order Caucus for which it has members of the Order and falls under their region of influence. A single Caucus will usually cover multiple Consillia. Each Order has its own set of Caucuses, and each Order's Caucuses do not necessarily have the same regions of influence as another Order's.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes it a lot clearer, thank you. <br /> <br /> Regarding requisition, how exactly does the Order Archive merit behave in those scenarios?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T16:28:49-07:00","id":1414289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414279#post1414279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes it a lot clearer, thank you.<br /> <br /> Regarding requisition, how exactly does the Order Archive merit behave in those scenarios?</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to the Order Archive Merit's extended action roll and security benefits, it helps the ST determine what is most readily available to the Caucus.<br /> <br /> A 3-dot Lorehouse might have Imbued Items, Grimoires, and Mentor as its Assets.<br /> A Libertine wishing to requisition a Familiar would add one to the availability rating, as Familiars are not one of the Assets of the Lorehouse.<br /> If instead they sought the benefits of the Library Merit (not an Asset, so +1 availability) for research into the burial rites of the Chumash peoples (-1 availability because it pertains to Sleeper culture) they would simply requisition it at the dot rating of the Library.<br /> And if they were seeking an Imbued (an Asset) cell phone (Sleeper technology) they'd be able to grab it at -1 availability from its actual rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's not clear, but I think:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The character treats her Status Merit as one dot lower if<br /> she requisitions the resource from a Caucus not her own<br /> but within her home Consilium or Assembly, two dots<br /> lower if from a Caucus within the same Convocation,<br /> and three dots lower if from a Caucus unrelated to her<br /> home one. </div> </div> </div>is combining Consillium/Assembly requisitions and Caucus requisitions. So an Arrow using their <b>Consillium</b> Status to requisition an item from an Athenaeum (Mysterium) would treat their <b>Consillium</b> status as one lower; the same Arrow using their <b>Order</b> status to requisition an item from an Armory of a different Arrow Caucus whose members are part of the same Convocation treats their <b>Order</b> status as two lower; and if the Armory is completely unrelated their <b>Order</b> status is three lower.<br /> <br /> But that's just my interpretation, and could be wrong; my game's Consillia and Assemblies are more akin to Convocations already, covering large geographical areas (all of the French speaking regions of Europe share one Consillium, likewise the German speaking regions, &amp;c; the PNW, South Western US, &amp;c. have single Consillia or Assemblies; &amp;c.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:35:58-07:00","id":1414301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414289#post1414289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In addition to the Order Archive Merit's extended action roll and security benefits, it helps the ST determine what is most readily available to the Caucus.<br /> <br /> A 3-dot Lorehouse might have Imbued Items, Grimoires, and Mentor as its Assets.<br /> A Libertine wishing to requisition a Familiar would add one to the availability rating, as Familiars are not one of the Assets of the Lorehouse.<br /> If instead they sought the benefits of the Library Merit (not an Asset, so +1 availability) for research into the burial rites of the Chumash peoples (-1 availability because it pertains to Sleeper culture) they would simply requisition it at the dot rating of the Library.<br /> And if they were seeking an Imbued (an Asset) cell phone (Sleeper technology) they'd be able to grab it at -1 availability from its actual rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's not clear, but I think:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> is combining Consillium/Assembly requisitions and Caucus requisitions. So an Arrow using their <b>Consillium</b> Status to requisition an item from an Athenaeum (Mysterium) would treat their <b>Consillium</b> status as one lower; the same Arrow using their <b>Order</b> status to requisition an item from an Armory of a different Arrow Caucus whose members are part of the same Convocation treats their <b>Order</b> status as two lower; and if the Armory is completely unrelated their <b>Order</b> status is three lower.<br /> <br /> But that's just my interpretation, and could be wrong; my game's Consillia and Assemblies are more akin to Convocations already, covering large geographical areas (all of the French speaking regions of Europe share one Consillium, likewise the German speaking regions, &amp;c; the PNW, South Western US, &amp;c. have single Consillia or Assemblies; &amp;c.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So either you don't invest in the Order specialties and are able to requisition them at no extra difficulty than other specialties or you double down on them and access them at -1 of the actual availability. <br /> <br /> That is a lot clearer, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T00:37:11-07:00","id":1414515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414278#post1414278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sensory range means that the subject you will teleport can be anywhere within your sensory range. By default you need to touch them or can only teleport yourself.<br /> <br /> The destinations can be anywhere within sensory range.<br /> <br /> A sympathetic cast can be used to teleport the subject to a location outside of sensory range. So you could send them to Mars if you had a picture from the NASA rover.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the sympathetic cast can be used to affect a subject outside of sensory range and teleport them to any point within the caster's sensory range. In this way, you could pull an imbued item from your Sanctum.<br /> <br /> You could use sympathy to cast on a subject outside of sensory range and move them somewhere outside sensory range. But you would need the one mana for the Attainment, commit two yantra slots and deal with a Withstand of the weakest connection +1, plus any other wards they may have used. So its doable, but would probably need preparations.<br /> <br /> In most mundane situations, Co-Location is sufficient. But without expending Reach on a Key, anyone with the most basic notion of Space magic or granted Space Mage Sight can use it. Even with a Key, it can be followed back for scrying, remote casting, etc. <br /> <br /> Teleportation is a lot cleaner, no magical doorway required, just a quick rewrite of the location from A to B. Well, hopefully, if they don't follow any other Nimbus impressions left by the caster.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit more involved sending somebody to mars than just having a picture of mars. The picture is a good yantra but since it's never been to mars itself its not a good link to mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T16:20:05-07:00","id":1414667,"title":"","content":"Does <i>One Mind, Two Thoughts</i> allow a user to maintain concentration on a spell as one of their mental actions ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T20:32:31-07:00","id":1417984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1414667#post1414667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does <i>One Mind, Two Thoughts</i> allow a user to maintain concentration on a spell as one of their mental actions ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use the Reach option that allows for Instant Mental tasks, I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> Question: ordinarily, Active Mage Sight doesn't work on recordings. What about memories enhanced by Perfect Recall (Mind 1)? For reference, the spell's text give the example of a memory retrieved: &quot;She can recall the exact details of a conversation, including bits that she wasn\u2019t consciously concentrating on, such as what kind of suit someone was wearing, or the smell of his cologne.&quot; Maybe with a Reach effect?<br /> <br /> Follow-up question: With the right Mind (possibly with added Prime) spell, could a Mage use Focused Mage Sight on an otherwise ordinary memory? Or is a Prime Weaving effect (like Camera Obscura) going to be required in order to &quot;record&quot; the Supernal information in the moment the memory is formed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T20:55:29-07:00","id":1417987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1417984#post1417984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you use the Reach option that allows for Instant Mental tasks, I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> Question: ordinarily, Active Mage Sight doesn't work on recordings. What about memories enhanced by Perfect Recall (Mind 1)? For reference, the spell's text give the example of a memory retrieved: &quot;She can recall the exact details of a conversation, including bits that she wasn\u2019t consciously concentrating on, such as what kind of suit someone was wearing, or the smell of his cologne.&quot; Maybe with a Reach effect?<br /> <br /> Follow-up question: With the right Mind (possibly with added Prime) spell, could a Mage use Focused Mage Sight on an otherwise ordinary memory? Or is a Prime Weaving effect (like Camera Obscura) going to be required in order to &quot;record&quot; the Supernal information in the moment the memory is formed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is Perfect Recall only includes what you could perceive at the time. You remember you felt your peripheral sight ping, but you never used Time sight to see the fracture in the timeline. Therefore, it doesn't register anything if you use it on the memory.<br /> <br /> You would need Prime 1 to recall the supernatural details of the scene. Alternatively, just add Time 1. You get a perfect mental reference to the moment and use that perfect link to follow the Postcognition threat back to the appointed time. The advantage is that, unlike Camera Obscura, the scene doesn't degrade.<br /> <br /> A third option is to use Spirit 1 to find an echo of the events as perceived by the quasi sentient ephemera of the scene. It would be a blurry mess, probably with a penalty to Opacity, but it would still be a place to start.<br /> <br /> There are many ways to go about it, all you need is a lens that is good enough to provide a lead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-13-2020, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T15:56:56-07:00","id":1418109,"title":"","content":"Greetings!<br /> <br /> I have two questions about Awakening &quot;metaplot&quot; (or backstory?) that I don't think merit their own thread so I am posting them here.<br /> <br /> 1 - The tale of Merlin, who Ascended apparently by ruining Camelot... Where is it told? I've seen lots of references to this at these boards, but I can't find anything on the 2nd edition Sourcebooks that I own... Is it in Dark Eras? Or just... Backstage info from the Devs?<br /> <br /> 2 - Is there any information on the... Origin... Of the Abyss? I saw someone claiming that it used to be &quot;around&quot; the whole Tapestry instead of &quot;between&quot; the Phenomenal and Supernal Worlds, and what the Gate did was to forcibly change its &quot;placement&quot;, but I can't say if that is canonical, implied, or a fanciful bit from a personal chronicle that was presented as fact. I would guess the third option, but the question I worded in 1 makes me wonder if it isn't something that slipped by me as well.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1578-patricl_gleason","name":"Patricl_Gleason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1578_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T16:18:10-07:00","id":1418115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Patricl_Gleason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418109#post1418109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - The tale of Merlin, who Ascended apparently by ruining Camelot... Where is it told? I've seen lots of references to this at these boards, but I can't find anything on the 2nd edition Sourcebooks that I own... Is it in Dark Eras? Or just... Backstage info from the Devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dug up the salient quotes pointing to the relevant books <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1413594-confused-about-aeons?p=1415818#post1415818\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - Is there any information on the... Origin... Of the Abyss? I saw someone claiming that it used to be &quot;around&quot; the whole Tapestry instead of &quot;between&quot; the Phenomenal and Supernal Worlds, and what the Gate did was to forcibly change its &quot;placement&quot;, but I can't say if that is canonical, implied, or a fanciful bit from a personal chronicle that was presented as fact. I would guess the third option, but the question I worded in 1 makes me wonder if it isn't something that slipped by me as well. </div> </div> </div>Historical looks in very early Dark Eras suggest 1e's forwarded mythology about the Exarchs creating the Abyss are just that.<br /> <br /> Mummy's perspective on the cosmology in Dreams of Avarice provides a very probable equivalent in the formless waters-that-are-not-waters of Nu and the stillborn children of Atum and Khepera who slid into those waters in the frenzy of creation that the great gods began to thwart the Devourer; in this model, the location predates material existence, but its denizens were made soon after reality kicked into gear.<br /> <br /> Changeling's resonant not-quite-equivalent in the Hedge, meanwhile, tends to suggest that the borderland was created after the Fae took Arcadia (in 2e) or only became significant after whatever change led the Fae to start taking human captives (in 1e). The lines are blurred here, as the dream-level view of the Aeon of the Abyss explicitly stands in opposition to the Fae, but the Huntsmen (who predate the Fae as residents of Arcadia) move with more speed and more of their own intent within the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: There's theories to be found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T02:43:45-07:00","id":1418325,"title":"","content":"It has been said that mastery over an arcana allow the creation of an iris to the appropriate realm (underworld for death, ecc).<br /> Do you think it s possible to open an iris to an emanation realm?<br /> Do you think it involves mastery of prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T06:19:20-07:00","id":1418352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418325#post1418325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been said that mastery over an arcana allow the creation of an iris to the appropriate realm (underworld for death, ecc).<br /> Do you think it s possible to open an iris to an emanation realm?<br /> Do you think it involves mastery of prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it requires mastery of whatever Arcana is the focus of the Emanation. So Prime could open one to Mars, Time creates one to the Mists, Spirit to Yggdrasil and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:12:11-07:00","id":1418373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418352#post1418352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say it requires mastery of whatever Arcana is the focus of the Emanation. So Prime could open one to Mars, Time creates one to the Mists, Spirit to Yggdrasil and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>At minimum yes, but being Emanation a sort of magical realms don t you think that it would require some level of Prime also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:49:18-07:00","id":1418379,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Underworld: Death allows a mage to open an Iris into it. Suppose that Iris closed/expired. What are some ways you can get out? Can Death do it?<br /> <br /> Also, what published resources provide details about the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:57:00-07:00","id":1418383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418379#post1418379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Underworld: Death allows a mage to open an Iris into it. Suppose that Iris closed/expired. What are some ways you can get out? Can Death do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just cast the same spell again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418379#post1418379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what published resources provide details about the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>For updated information relevant to second edition, it's definitely the Geist 2e core book you want. Otherwise there's the now outdated 1e blue supplement Book of the Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T18:08:58-07:00","id":1418454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418373#post1418373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At minimum yes, but being Emanation a sort of magical realms don t you think that it would require some level of Prime also?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess not unless its the featured Arcanum. For example, the Walkers in Mists utilize Time and Space ( the Lords of Mars I theorize use Prime and Death). They are the specialists in accessing the Emanation of the Mists and imposing its power upon other parts of reality.<br /> <br /> Most of them require appropriate symbolism to enter, but not necessarily Prime. While Prime is how magic knows and defines itself, knowledge of that Arcanum is not required for magical phenomena to manifest. You can just cast a Death spell without Prime making its change True. In much the same way, I theorize all you would need is to either synchronize with its symbol to open the Iris, use a Weaving to open it without the effort or a Making to create a point of access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T20:21:45-07:00","id":1418472,"title":"","content":"Mind spells can work on anything that has a mind right? Ghost, spirits, abyssal entities, supernal entities, etc... basically any antagonist that isn't a simple golem or similar mechanism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T20:45:46-07:00","id":1418473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418472#post1418472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind spells can work on anything that has a mind right? Ghost, spirits, abyssal entities, supernal entities, etc... basically any antagonist that isn't a simple golem or similar mechanism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Does it mean you can plan for your Sleepwalker aid to become Claimed, then astrally project the original spirit's mind and seal it in a dream catcher, leaving your loyal follower with unfettered access to his ephemeral powers ? Why certainly, after all, its a just reward for your exorcism services.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T09:45:50-07:00","id":1418538,"title":"","content":"Q: I am not sure if I am playing paradox wrong. If a mage tries to contain paradox by rolling wisdom the worst that can happen is a Paradox Condition? It sounds pretty weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T09:57:27-07:00","id":1418540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>empe999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418538#post1418538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: I am not sure if I am playing paradox wrong. If a mage tries to contain paradox by rolling wisdom the worst that can happen is a Paradox Condition? It sounds pretty weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox conditions are designed to either cause wisdom loss or further conditions. You also, of course, take resistant bashing damage when containing paradox, which can matter in a fight (or the fight after the fight if your ST is vicious).<br /> <br /> And some of those conditions are pretty bad if you allow them to lapse. That being said, if you feel as if paradox doesn't have enough teeth, there are plenty of ways to make it worse, not all of them requiring mechanical changes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T10:03:17-07:00","id":1418542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>empe999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418538#post1418538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: I am not sure if I am playing paradox wrong. If a mage tries to contain paradox by rolling wisdom the worst that can happen is a Paradox Condition? It sounds pretty weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Falcon777 already touched on, the Paradox Conditions in the book are only examples. You should feel free to make up your own and make them hurt plenty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T10:32:25-07:00","id":1418547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>empe999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418538#post1418538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: I am not sure if I am playing paradox wrong. If a mage tries to contain paradox by rolling wisdom the worst that can happen is a Paradox Condition? It sounds pretty weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be terrifyingly effective once you realize how quickly the mage can lose control of the situation.<br /> <br /> If you allow the Paradox Condition to resolve, you made your life more complicated by taking on the consequences of it. <br /> <br /> If you allow it to lapse, the every single spell you cast in the meantime gains a Paradox dice, starting the accumulation cascade. <br /> <br /> The higher your Wisdom is, the less often this will happen, but when it does, it lasts longer. Plus you have to actively strive to maintain high Wisdom and be able to deal with the resistant bashing damage when it actually contains the Paradox. If you aren't the most physically fit, it can get very nasty, very quickly. Especially if you are containing a spell tainted by the Paradox cascade mentioned above.<br /> <br /> You can scour the Condition, but cause a point of resistant lethal damage and uses up a daily scouring.<br /> <br /> Then finally add the individual details of the Condition itself and you have a domino effect of doom. If the mage is in a situation where they need to cast quickly and often (difficult social encounter, breaking into a ruin or Sanctum, combat, navigating through a Realm Invisible, etc), where they don't have the time and/or resources to reduce Paradox risk at every turn, then the threat of the Abyss will be an ever present companion. <br /> <br /> All it takes is one moment of desperation to make them release a Paradox they cannot contain, bringing new threats that cannot be into the Fallen World. For madness is like gravity, all it takes is a little push.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-16-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T19:57:34-07:00","id":1418628,"title":"","content":"Do the Underworld and Arcadia count as Lower Depths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1578-patricl_gleason","name":"Patricl_Gleason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1578_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T20:12:59-07:00","id":1418629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Patricl_Gleason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1418628#post1418628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Underworld and Arcadia count as Lower Depths?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, though the former is heavily corrupted by probable denizens of one or more Depths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:57:05-07:00","id":1419028,"title":"","content":"Q: If I cast dispel magic on a subject protected by wards and signs, do I have to beat the potency of wards and signs itself as a withstand rating? Or does it only shields the subject but not the spells on him/her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T10:33:41-07:00","id":1419035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>empe999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419028#post1419028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: If I cast dispel magic on a subject protected by wards and signs, do I have to beat the potency of wards and signs itself as a withstand rating? Or does it only shields the subject but not the spells on him/her?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Dispel Magic</i> is cast on a spell, not a person, so unless <i>Wards and Signs</i> was cast on the spell you're trying to dispel the withstand is just the Arcanum rating of the spell's caster.<br /> <br /> [Edit] A more clever mage might cast <i>Wards and Signs</i> with a small area of effect centered on themself so that it does affect all spells on them, but this is not the default and might not work depending on your ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T10:50:22-07:00","id":1419041,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to make magically created goods, alchemical potions, or Perfected Materials to be permanent, that is Lasting. I was thinking something like the magic comes and goes but the result, the Perfected Material, is now fundamentally real. <br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, I can add the &quot;+2 Reach: Add one point of Mana and the effect of the spell becomes Lasting&quot; effect to say the spell to create Perfected Materials or whatnot but I was wondering if there was another way to go about it. <br /> <br /> I don't mind it being difficult or whatnot but I do think, with effort, a mage should be able to create materials that once conjured or formed don't need active magic to stay around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:24:14-07:00","id":1419047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419041#post1419041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to make magically created goods, alchemical potions, or Perfected Materials to be permanent, that is Lasting. I was thinking something like the magic comes and goes but the result, the Perfected Material, is now fundamentally real.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, I can add the &quot;+2 Reach: Add one point of Mana and the effect of the spell becomes Lasting&quot; effect to say the spell to create Perfected Materials or whatnot but I was wondering if there was another way to go about it.<br /> <br /> I don't mind it being difficult or whatnot but I do think, with effort, a mage should be able to create materials that once conjured or formed don't need active magic to stay around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfected Materials can be created by moving the material in to and out of Twilight or some other realm multiple times (with rest periods in between) to slowly remove its metaphysical impurities, this is a long process but results in a permanent, non-magical change.<br /> <br /> For magical items: some Enhanced Items are created via spells that already have the &quot;+2 Reach &amp; a Mana for Lasting&quot; option; for those that don't, and for Imbued Items, it doesn't make sense to <i>have</i> a Lasting effect, an Imbued Item, especially, is fundamentally an item actively sustained by magic.<br /> <br /> If by &quot;alchemical potions&quot; you mean <i>Spell Potion</i>, that's a one-off Imbued Item and, as such, would require active magical maintenance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:25:56-07:00","id":1419048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419041#post1419041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to make magically created goods, alchemical potions, or Perfected Materials to be permanent, that is Lasting. I was thinking something like the magic comes and goes but the result, the Perfected Material, is now fundamentally real. <br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, I can add the &quot;+2 Reach: Add one point of Mana and the effect of the spell becomes Lasting&quot; effect to say the spell to create Perfected Materials or whatnot but I was wondering if there was another way to go about it. <br /> <br /> I don't mind it being difficult or whatnot but I do think, with effort, a mage should be able to create materials that once conjured or formed don't need active magic to stay around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean. You could arguably cast with enough duration to make it indefinite. The Permanence Attainment from Matter makes this a lot easier. The problem is that each item would consume Willpower to unsafely relinquish and the spell could warp after a while. At that point, you would need to look into alternative relinquishment methods, such as via breaking points, destroying a soul, having someone else pay the price (a spirit, ghost, summoned entity, other mage, etc) or simply take on the XP burden on board. <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> goes into more detail on making magical items and on alternative relinquishment costs.<br /> <br /> Lasting means the effect is part of the natural world. Now it doesn't warp, provoke Clash of Wills and more importantly, does not trigger Quiescence or Disbelief. <br /> <br /> The final and simplest solution is to have a crafting focused Legacy. An Attainment uses no spell slots, plus is immune to Quiescence and Dispellation. Even those with less than indefinite duration make up for it by sheer availability.<br /> <br /> For those purposes, I recommend the Anima Meccanica for nanotech styled magical items, the Thaumatech Engineers for steampunk gadgets, the Clockwork Knights for power armor (all of them are posted in the forum) and this version of the Transhuman Engineers for cyberpunk creations:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/10/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-legacy.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/1...egacy.html?m=1</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-19-2020, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:36:05-07:00","id":1419053,"title":"","content":"The Moros splat hints around the idea that Moros have natural access to wealth (&quot;they can make you rich,&quot; &quot;they can't be bribed,&quot; etc...). Where's that coming from? Unless I misunderstand Matter spells, they only turn trash into treasure on a temporary basis; Matter basically just grants brief access to various forms of counterfeit money. Doesn't seem wise to pay some Sleeper off with bars of gold that turn back into lead after a few days (let alone another mage). Are Moros actually somehow better set up for wealth accrual than other paths?<br /> <br /> Sometimes published spells are intended to be Lasting but it's not explicitly stated (e.g. Teleportation); I'm wondering if missed some such cases in Matter. Any Arcanum can be leveraged to make money with enough creativity, but the fluff text gave me the impression that it's somehow easier or more straightforward with Matter and/or Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 10-19-2020, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:47:50-07:00","id":1419055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419053#post1419053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Moros splat hints around the idea that Moros have natural access to wealth (&quot;they can make you rich,&quot; &quot;they can't be bribed,&quot; etc...). Where's that coming from? Unless I misunderstand Matter spells, they only turn trash into treasure on a temporary basis; Matter basically just grants brief access to various forms of counterfeit money. Doesn't seem wise to pay some Sleeper off with bars of gold that turn back into lead after a few days (let alone another mage). Are Moros actually somehow better set up for wealth accrual than other paths?<br /> <br /> Sometimes published spells are intended to be Lasting but it's not explicitly stated (e.g. Teleportation); I'm wondering if missed some such cases in Matter. Any Arcanum can be leveraged to make money with enough creativity, but the fluff text gave me the impression that it's somehow easier or more straightforward with Matter and/or Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter lets you easily find valuable raw materials. Looking for oil? Matter. Looking for a gold or silver mine to open? Matter. Looking for pearls (before they were easy to farm)? Matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:57:29-07:00","id":1419059,"title":"","content":"Might want to combine it with Fate to find a resource that hasn't been claimed by an international conglomerate already. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:58:21-07:00","id":1419062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419053#post1419053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Moros splat hints around the idea that Moros have natural access to wealth (&quot;they can make you rich,&quot; &quot;they can't be bribed,&quot; etc...). Where's that coming from? Unless I misunderstand Matter spells, they only turn trash into treasure on a temporary basis; Matter basically just grants brief access to various forms of counterfeit money. Doesn't seem wise to pay some Sleeper off with bars of gold that turn back into lead after a few days (let alone another mage). Are Moros actually somehow better set up for wealth accrual than other paths?<br /> <br /> Sometimes published spells are intended to be Lasting but it's not explicitly stated (e.g. Teleportation); I'm wondering if missed some such cases in Matter. Any Arcanum can be leveraged to make money with enough creativity, but the fluff text gave me the impression that it's somehow easier or more straightforward with Matter and/or Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Knowing of Matter can detect precious substances in the soil, a Ruling can make mining them trivial. Purifying water, polluted rivers and even metals can be done with those two practices. <br /> <br /> Perfected tools mixed with shaping make creating finely crafted treasures very simple. Finding out the secrets of the dead, either as payment or in search of loot, is also profitable. <br /> <br /> Lastly, creating Matter (notice the spell never says the material vanishes after duration ends or that it needs to be a previously existing substance) or transmuting it into precious materials (due to Permanence making it very easy) means they should be pretty rich.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the wealth theme is based on their two roles. Master alchemist were supposed to unlock the power to transmute lead into gold via the philosopher's stone, making them very wealthy. The image of the necromancer's tomb, filled with innumerable treasures from ages past is also very prominent. So I guess the Moros inherited those expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-19-2020, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T12:22:43-07:00","id":1419068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419047#post1419047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfected Materials can be created by moving the material in to and out of Twilight or some other realm multiple times (with rest periods in between) to slowly remove its metaphysical impurities, this is a long process but results in a permanent, non-magical change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just wish that the actual Honing spell had the +2 Lasting option. I mean, personally, in a house rule sense, I am adding it. I want Mages to be able to make the materials last forever without tying it to the Indefinite Duration.<br /> <br /> I just think there is no real reason to say that the Adamant you created needs your active magic to sustain itself one its formed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For magical items: some Enhanced Items are created via spells that already have the &quot;+2 Reach &amp; a Mana for Lasting&quot; option; for those that don't, and for Imbued Items, it doesn't make sense to <i>have</i> a Lasting effect, an Imbued Item, especially, is fundamentally an item actively sustained by magic. </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Item remains a magically active item, I just don't think it should be something that the caster is penalized for having as part of his control rating. But I have to read more about Imbued Items as I might be missing something that is already there.<br /> <br /> I will say this, I really like 2e version of how the various magic item merits work. I love how they decouple the dots max from the whole standard rating. I also like how they describe it being set up, so I think its brilliant.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think more effects should be allowed to have the +2 Lasting then in the book. But its very very easy for me to add that in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If by &quot;alchemical potions&quot; you mean <i>Spell Potion</i>, that's a one-off Imbued Item and, as such, would require active magical maintenance. </div> </div> </div>So I get that, I just don't really like that. I mean I know that say Harry Potter isn't Awakening. But the idea that someone like Severus Snape in Awakening terms would have multiple spell potions connected to him through the control system bothers me.<br /> <br /> I much rather the idea that you create the potion, cast the spell in it (obviously pay Mana), and then the potion remains usable for x amount of time unrelated to anything you personally as the mage who made it would do.<br /> <br /> Though maybe upon reading the details to a bit more depth I might actually be able to get what I want. This might require a loosening of the difficulties in spell relinguishing but I'm probably gonna be fine with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419048#post1419048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on what you mean. You could arguably cast with enough duration to make it indefinite. The Permanence Attainment from Matter makes this a lot easier. The problem is that each item would consume Willpower to unsafely relinquish and the spell could warp after a while. At that point, you would need to look into alternative relinquishment methods, such as via breaking points, destroying a soul, having someone else pay the price (a spirit, ghost, summoned entity, other mage, etc) or simply take on the XP burden on board. <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> goes into more detail on making magical items and on alternative relinquishment costs.<br /> <br /> Lasting means the effect is part of the natural world. Now it doesn't warp, provoke Clash of Wills and more importantly, does not trigger Quiescence or Disbelief.<br /> <br /> The final and simplest solution is to have a crafting focused Legacy. An Attainment uses no spell slots, plus is immune to Quiescence and Dispellation. Even those with less than indefinite duration make up for it by sheer availability.<br /> <br /> For those purposes, I recommend the Anima Meccanica for nanotech styled magical items, the Thaumatech Engineers for steampunk gadgets, the Clockwork Knights for power armor (all of them are posted in the forum) and this version of the Transhuman Engineers for cyberpunk creations:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/10/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-legacy.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/1...egacy.html?m=1</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps</div> </div> </div> </div>While yeah an Indefinite duration is still a magic tied to you, and thus not gone.<br /> <br /> I do like the Permanence Attainment from Matter as a method of reducing the Reach re, but its a pity it doesn't let the subject created by the spell remain even after the spell is made.<br /> <br /> On Lasting, yeah, the magic that creates it comes and goes but the effect remains 'real' and fundamental. Its like how you heal someone and the damage removed remains removed - the active magic is the healing not the act of being healed.<br /> <br /> To me the active magics is making the Perfected Materials and not the Perfected Materials themselves. Thus the materials as an item is Lasting, there is no magic to remove as the magic that made them is gone, leaving just the material itself.<br /> <br /> Basically, you conjure stone, but the stone stays after the spell goes, the stone is no longer magical, its real, and so it doesn't disapear.<br /> <br /> It all does help, and I appreciate the information as it helps me to figure out the system as is and what I want it to do, and thus any potential adaptations or changes I would need to make to it to get what I want.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419062#post1419062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> Lastly, creating Matter (notice the spell never says the material vanishes after duration ends or that it needs to be a previously existing substance) or transmuting it into precious materials (due to Permanence making it very easy) means they should be pretty rich.<br /> <br /> ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, really? Oh. lol<br /> <br /> I honestly thought that because Lasting wasn't there the item vanishes. But if the conjured stuff stays even after the magic ends (and the fact Potency not Duration is the primary would indicate that) then a lot of my issues are gone. hehe<br /> <br /> It means I can create a spell like Conjure the Wizard's Tower that would basically create a massive tower out of magic that stays even after the spell ends. Hmm. I should figure out the elements of that spell. hehe<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-19-2020, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T13:44:14-07:00","id":1419081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419068#post1419068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I just wish that the actual Honing spell had the +2 Lasting option. I mean, personally, in a house rule sense, I am adding it. I want Mages to be able to make the materials last forever without tying it to the Indefinite Duration.<br /> <br /> I just think there is no real reason to say that the Adamant you created needs your active magic to sustain itself one its formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if the spell could easily create Lasting Perfected Materials, why do it the hard way?<br /> <br /> The spell is if you're in a situation where you need the Perfected Material <i>now</i> and it doesn't matter if the material only lasts a few turns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that the Item remains a magically active item, I just don't think it should be something that the caster is penalized for having as part of his control rating. But I have to read more about Imbued Items as I might be missing something that is already there. </div> </div> </div>That's what relinquishing is for, to remove the spells Imbued into the item from your control. And, yes, the current system makes it costly the Imbue items and safely relinquish it, but Imbued Items aren't supposed to be super common, anyway.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying the system is perfect, I have some homebrew stuff around Imbued Items: a spell that creates a magical schematic that allows you to have the rote quality on Imbuement rolls (Prime 4 Patterning, this one has the +2 Reach &amp; Mana for Lasting option similar to <i>Scribe Grimoire</i>); the Thaumatech Engineers Legacy has as its fourth optional Attainment an exceptional success on imbuement rolls on three successes instead of five; and the option to roll until you've rolled Gnosis + Prime times, even if you hit the success threshold already. These are all aimed at making getting an exceptional success easier, so that the spells imbued can be relinquished for a Willpower point instead of a Willpower <i>dot</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will say this, I really like 2e version of how the various magic item merits work. I love how they decouple the dots max from the whole standard rating. I also like how they describe it being set up, so I think its brilliant.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think more effects should be allowed to have the +2 Lasting then in the book. But its very very easy for me to add that in. </div> </div> </div>Just keep in mind that Lasting effects should only be those that aren't inherently magical by their very existence, and don't otherwise &quot;cheat&quot; in the creation of something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I get that, I just don't really like that. I mean I know that say Harry Potter isn't Awakening. But the idea that someone like Severus Snape in Awakening terms would have multiple spell potions connected to him through the control system bothers me.<br /> <br /> I much rather the idea that you create the potion, cast the spell in it (obviously pay Mana), and then the potion remains usable for x amount of time unrelated to anything you personally as the mage who made it would do. </div> </div> </div>You can do that, with a Legacy Attainment! In fact, the Thaumatech Engineers Legacy I made <i>does</i> have that option as one of its Attainments.<br /> <br /> But even if you discount Legacy Attainments, Relinquishing is a still a thing, and for something with a short shelf-life like a single-use potion, it makes sense to unsafely relinquish; as long as you don't exceed your safe reach the ST is only rolling a chance die once a chapter to see if it starts to go bad. Also, this is where a merit would make sense, something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Potion Maker (ooo)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Able to cast <i>Energize Object</i>, <i>Spell Potion</i>, or <i>Stored Spell</i><br /> Whenever a Mage with this merit unsafely relinquishes a spell placed in aLimited Use Item, that item rolls for Paradox once a Story rather than once a Chapter.<br /> <br /> As an aside: I think that <i>Energize Object</i> and <i>Spell Potion</i> shouldn't have been separate spells, but instead 2-dot Forces and Matter options of <i>Stored Spell</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though maybe upon reading the details to a bit more depth I might actually be able to get what I want. This might require a loosening of the difficulties in spell relinguishing but I'm probably gonna be fine with that. </div> </div> </div>I would play with it for a while before getting too in depth on trying to do house rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T20:59:54-07:00","id":1419114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419081#post1419081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because if the spell could easily create Lasting Perfected Materials, why do it the hard way?<br /> <br /> The spell is if you're in a situation where you need the Perfected Material <i>now</i> and it doesn't matter if the material only lasts a few turns.<br /> <br /> That's what relinquishing is for, to remove the spells Imbued into the item from your control. And, yes, the current system makes it costly the Imbue items and safely relinquish it, but Imbued Items aren't supposed to be super common, anyway.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying the system is perfect, I have some homebrew stuff around Imbued Items: a spell that creates a magical schematic that allows you to have the rote quality on Imbuement rolls (Prime 4 Patterning, this one has the +2 Reach &amp; Mana for Lasting option similar to <i>Scribe Grimoire</i>); the Thaumatech Engineers Legacy has as its fourth optional Attainment an exceptional success on imbuement rolls on three successes instead of five; and the option to roll until you've rolled Gnosis + Prime times, even if you hit the success threshold already. These are all aimed at making getting an exceptional success easier, so that the spells imbued can be relinquished for a Willpower point instead of a Willpower <i>dot</i>.<br /> <br /> Just keep in mind that Lasting effects should only be those that aren't inherently magical by their very existence, and don't otherwise &quot;cheat&quot; in the creation of something.<br /> <br /> You can do that, with a Legacy Attainment! In fact, the Thaumatech Engineers Legacy I made <i>does</i> have that option as one of its Attainments.<br /> <br /> But even if you discount Legacy Attainments, Relinquishing is a still a thing, and for something with a short shelf-life like a single-use potion, it makes sense to unsafely relinquish; as long as you don't exceed your safe reach the ST is only rolling a chance die once a chapter to see if it starts to go bad. Also, this is where a merit would make sense, something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Potion Maker (ooo)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Able to cast <i>Energize Object</i>, <i>Spell Potion</i>, or <i>Stored Spell</i><br /> Whenever a Mage with this merit unsafely relinquishes a spell placed in aLimited Use Item, that item rolls for Paradox once a Story rather than once a Chapter.<br /> <br /> As an aside: I think that <i>Energize Object</i> and <i>Spell Potion</i> shouldn't have been separate spells, but instead 2-dot Forces and Matter options of <i>Stored Spell</i>.<br /> <br /> I would play with it for a while before getting too in depth on trying to do house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the comments, they are interesting and thought provoking. <br /> <br /> That said though, upon further looking at some old versions and posts and such it seems the spells in question had &quot;+2 Reach: For one point of Mana the effect is Lasting&quot; on them but had that feature removed during the discussion phase. As the removal was for thematic reasons rather than mechanical I have no negative feelings towards adding the effect back in. So I am going to do so. <br /> <br /> I think mages should be able to permanently make magical substances that survive outside of keeping the spell that made them active, and so I am happy to add that feature back. <br /> <br /> That said your points are interesting. I will definetly look up the details of that Legacy. Though as the number of legacy attainments are limited (at least it seems so) this doesn't really solve the issues I have. <br /> <br /> That Merit is cool, a nice way to go about certain potion methods. <br /> <br /> Honestly, the more I delve into 2e Mage the more I love it. Soooo much potential. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In fact I already went and bought the pod/pdf of Signs of Sorcery cause it looked very interesting. And I am glad I did because there are many elements in it that are fun, especially the last chapter where they talk about variant Awakenings. I have an image of mages who go from say a World of Mundanity and find themselves in a World of Magic due to the effects of their Awakening changing history. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T08:37:17-07:00","id":1419170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419068#post1419068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I just wish that the actual Honing spell had the +2 Lasting option. I mean, personally, in a house rule sense, I am adding it. I want Mages to be able to make the materials last forever without tying it to the Indefinite Duration.<br /> <br /> I just think there is no real reason to say that the Adamant you created needs your active magic to sustain itself one its formed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree that the Item remains a magically active item, I just don't think it should be something that the caster is penalized for having as part of his control rating. But I have to read more about Imbued Items as I might be missing something that is already there.<br /> <br /> I will say this, I really like 2e version of how the various magic item merits work. I love how they decouple the dots max from the whole standard rating. I also like how they describe it being set up, so I think its brilliant.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think more effects should be allowed to have the +2 Lasting then in the book. But its very very easy for me to add that in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I get that, I just don't really like that. I mean I know that say Harry Potter isn't Awakening. But the idea that someone like Severus Snape in Awakening terms would have multiple spell potions connected to him through the control system bothers me.<br /> <br /> I much rather the idea that you create the potion, cast the spell in it (obviously pay Mana), and then the potion remains usable for x amount of time unrelated to anything you personally as the mage who made it would do.<br /> <br /> Though maybe upon reading the details to a bit more depth I might actually be able to get what I want. This might require a loosening of the difficulties in spell relinguishing but I'm probably gonna be fine with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While yeah an Indefinite duration is still a magic tied to you, and thus not gone.<br /> <br /> I do like the Permanence Attainment from Matter as a method of reducing the Reach re, but its a pity it doesn't let the subject created by the spell remain even after the spell is made.<br /> <br /> On Lasting, yeah, the magic that creates it comes and goes but the effect remains 'real' and fundamental. Its like how you heal someone and the damage removed remains removed - the active magic is the healing not the act of being healed.<br /> <br /> To me the active magics is making the Perfected Materials and not the Perfected Materials themselves. Thus the materials as an item is Lasting, there is no magic to remove as the magic that made them is gone, leaving just the material itself.<br /> <br /> Basically, you conjure stone, but the stone stays after the spell goes, the stone is no longer magical, its real, and so it doesn't disapear.<br /> <br /> It all does help, and I appreciate the information as it helps me to figure out the system as is and what I want it to do, and thus any potential adaptations or changes I would need to make to it to get what I want.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, really? Oh. lol<br /> <br /> I honestly thought that because Lasting wasn't there the item vanishes. But if the conjured stuff stays even after the magic ends (and the fact Potency not Duration is the primary would indicate that) then a lot of my issues are gone. hehe<br /> <br /> It means I can create a spell like Conjure the Wizard's Tower that would basically create a massive tower out of magic that stays even after the spell ends. Hmm. I should figure out the elements of that spell. hehe<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, a Dr Fate styled Tower of Fate or Dr Strange type of Sanctum Sanctorum is an entire project. The fast way of doing it is by having an archmage create a chanrty, but becoming one or convincing one to make one is improbable.<br /> <br /> I think the easiest way is using the Quarantine spell to secure an Paradox free zone, with indefinite diration and relinquished safely (advanced Potency might also be a good idea). Then build the basic mundane infrastructure using Matter.<br /> <br /> Next have the cabal trade favors for safe relinquishments (there is a Prime 3 spell to transfer spell control). Another option is to use a Fate 3 spell to modify the reward of an Obligation to include safe relinquishment. So long as the one who cast the spell fulfilled their vow, then it should work. <br /> <br /> Once you have a way to earn safe relinquishments, you can start expanding upon it by creating Golems, a Spirit Manse (or maybe a library if you add conjunctional Mind 3), Hallows, a portal network and much more. <br /> <br /> Its a big undertaking that will require a lot of investment from all players, but you can build an incredible base of operations. It might also be the focus of a story to seek out a vanished cabal's amazing Sanctum or inherit one, having to correct whatever problems made them vanish before one can build upon them. For example, have them inherit the one if the Thunder-Perfect Brotherhood and seek out the secrets of the Gaolers of Ialdabaoth. They can be found in Grimmoire of Grimmoires, which is a really cool read. Maybe throw in some bits from Constantine's mansion from Thief to make things interesting or make it into John Constantine's House of Mystery.<br /> <br /> That will certainly make the cabal renowned or feared. Hopefully they are careful enough not to tempt rivals, enemies and political interest into seizing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-20-2020, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T09:00:59-07:00","id":1419174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419170#post1419170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In theory, a Dr Fate styled Tower of Fate or Dr Strange type of Sanctum Sanctorum is an entire project. The fast way of doing it is by having an archmage create a chanrty, but becoming one or convincing one to make one is improbable.<br /> <br /> I think the easiest way is using the Quarantine spell to secure an Paradox free zone, with indefinite diration and relinquished safely (advanced Potency might also be a good idea). Then build the basic mundane infrastructure using Matter.<br /> <br /> Next have the cabal trade favors for safe relinquishments (there is a Prime 3 spell to transfer spell control). Another option is to use a Fate 3 spell to modify the reward of an Obligation to include safe relinquishment. So long as the one who cast the spell fulfilled their vow, then it should work.<br /> <br /> Once you have a way to earn safe relinquishments, you can start expanding upon it by creating Golems, a Spirit Manse (or maybe a library if you add conjunctional Mind 3), Hallows, a portal network and much more.<br /> <br /> Its a big undertaking that will require a lot of investment from all players, but you can build an incredible base of operations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting stuff here. Lots of potential to create a base of operation that will be honored through the ages.<br /> <br /> I will say this paying a Willpower DOT to safely relinquish an indefinite Duration base creation spell would totally be worth it. So yeah, I totally see the benefit of that. <br /> <br /> Though, all that said, I still think a variant of Ex Nilhilo could be used to make a structure from nothing that will remain even once the spell stops. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might also be the focus of a story to seek out a vanished cabal's amazing Sanctum or inherit one, having to correct whatever problems made them vanish before one can build upon them. For example, have them inherit the one if the Thunder-Perfect Brotherhood and seek out the secrets of the Gaolers of Ialdabaoth. They can be found in Grimmoire of Grimmoires, which is a really cool read. Maybe throw in some bits from Constantine's mansion from Thief to make things interesting or make it into John Constantine's House of Mystery.<br /> <br /> That will certainly make the cabal renowned or feared. Hopefully they are careful enough not to tempt rivals, enemies and political interest into seizing it. </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an amazing central element of a greater campaign, one I totally totally love and now want to play. Imagine, a group of young mages uncover the ruins of an abandoned house somewhere near but also out of range of others and quickly discover that there is more to it then meets the eye. Maybe they get a vision, or maybe they have a dream, or maybe something or someone informs them, or shows them, the site at its height - that it was once a vast complex with towering skyscrapers, majestic domes, even mammoth pyramids. Now though there is only ruins. But wait, they perform a particular spell they discover in a tome and it causes a wave of energy and light and before their eyes part of the place repairs itself, giving them access to a stairwell that opens to a massive cave containing x amount of floating crsystals, with all but one dark. One crystal can easily be lit, granting them access to a new section of the mansion. <br /> <br /> Now they have to hunt for clues and solve puzzles and uncover the mystery of how to get this sanctum or all sanctums, this veritable Hogwarts (without it being that), back to a usable state. <br /> <br /> Obviously they might find themsleves being hunted or harassed or effected by things both mundane and supernatural, and maybe even abyssal or supernal. <br /> <br /> Such an interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T01:58:27-07:00","id":1419331,"title":"","content":"Q: Do ephemeral beings add their Resistance trait to withstand? Reading the rulebook it would seem they only use their rank, usually a rather low withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T05:00:11-07:00","id":1419352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>empe999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419331#post1419331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: Do ephemeral beings add their Resistance trait to withstand? Reading the rulebook it would seem they only use their rank, usually a rather low withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not. Recall that Rank's normal contribution to attempts to supernaturally bind an ephemeral being is half the penalty it would impose on Awakened magic through spell factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T14:57:44-07:00","id":1419651,"title":"","content":"If a spell is Duration primary, does it mean by default it does nothing if it can be Withstood ? For example, String of Fate is Withstood by Resolve, so rather than Resolve diminishing the duration of the effect, it always reduces Potency. Should Potency become zero it completely nullifies it, is that correct ? Therefore, you would need to get it to 3 for it to even affect an average human ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T15:29:02-07:00","id":1419657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419651#post1419651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a spell is Duration primary, does it mean by default it does nothing if it can be Withstood ? For example, String of Fate is Withstood by Resolve, so rather than Resolve diminishing the duration of the effect, it always reduces Potency. Should Potency become zero it completely nullifies it, is that correct ? Therefore, you would need to get it to 3 for it to even affect an average human ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The spell is still active and if the Withstand rating changes the Potency adjusts, but otherwise it's just a spell whose impact is being a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T17:00:42-07:00","id":1419676,"title":"","content":"So speaking of Withstand, for those who have actually played in games, how does the rules translate to practice. What I mean is does the Withstand rules as is cause players to have a lot of their effects fizzle or do they still apply a lot. Because I gotta say with the way that the rules are written it seems that a lot f castings would fail, and that seems more annoying than fun for a player of a mage who wants to actually use the magic they are supposed to be able to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T17:45:28-07:00","id":1419684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419676#post1419676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So speaking of Withstand, for those who have actually played in games, how does the rules translate to practice. What I mean is does the Withstand rules as is cause players to have a lot of their effects fizzle or do they still apply a lot. Because I gotta say with the way that the rules are written it seems that a lot f castings would fail, and that seems more annoying than fun for a player of a mage who wants to actually use the magic they are supposed to be able to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this hasn\u2019t been my experience. The easiest ways to get around it are to ritual cast and/or find better yantras for a stronger bonus. Mages who are prepared naturally do better at casting strong spells, which is a feature of the system mechanics rather than a flaw. When trying to cast stronger spells, reach effects let you really bump up duration and scale quickly, so it tempts players to use more and more reach to accomplish better spells. You can also ignore withstand as an option when you get an exceptional success on a casting roll, so praxes (which only need 3 successes) and rotes (which grant up to +5 from one yantra alone) are also great ways for fledgling mages to overcome withstand ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T21:45:32-07:00","id":1419713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419657#post1419657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. The spell is still active and if the Withstand rating changes the Potency adjusts, but otherwise it's just a spell whose impact is being a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, thank you. For some reason I always thought the main factor was Withstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T21:46:16-07:00","id":1419714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419676#post1419676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So speaking of Withstand, for those who have actually played in games, how does the rules translate to practice. What I mean is does the Withstand rules as is cause players to have a lot of their effects fizzle or do they still apply a lot. Because I gotta say with the way that the rules are written it seems that a lot f castings would fail, and that seems more annoying than fun for a player of a mage who wants to actually use the magic they are supposed to be able to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It all depends on the time available and level of discretion required.<br /> <br /> You need to cast a Postcognition in a safe area ? High Speech and Concentration. Need to scry on someone remotely while amidst a party ? Use cup of wine/water to represent a scrying pool and your phone to represent capturing an image.<br /> <br /> Need to cure someone of a powerful curse ? Spend ritual time annoiting them with salt or water (shinto based cleansing yantra), use high speech, sacrifice a handmade health charm (+2 sacrament yantra) and inscribe runes into them using a pen.<br /> <br /> The more powerful the mage, the more likely they will acquire or create specialized tools to help them, such as a Moros making tools from perfected metals, a Thyrsus creating specific plants/animals or an Acanthus making lucky trinkets. Some pick a Shadow Name that synergizes with them and cultivate it, or otherwise create one of their own. <br /> <br /> Lastly, there is always the option of finding rare sacraments for potent spells, but there is always the question whether spending or seeking out an uncommon resource is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-23-2020, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T00:12:59-07:00","id":1419729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419676#post1419676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So speaking of Withstand, for those who have actually played in games, how does the rules translate to practice. What I mean is does the Withstand rules as is cause players to have a lot of their effects fizzle or do they still apply a lot. Because I gotta say with the way that the rules are written it seems that a lot f castings would fail, and that seems more annoying than fun for a player of a mage who wants to actually use the magic they are supposed to be able to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> regarding what I've played, withstand against non-supernal or mage entities has been mostly irrelevant. A psychic domination rote for example, starting with mind 3, is going to be potency 3 and have a lot of dices on the cast due to the rote (generally +3 or more dices) and willpower (+3). Realistically how how will the withstand be without supernal defense? 3, maybe 4? Just up the potency a bit and you are fine.<br /> <br /> The only effects that suffer from withstand are spells like degrading the form, but I've never seem them cast. why bother when you can cast something much better or buff you up to strenght 10 with life 3 and a rote in honing the form instead of spending turns de-buffing the enemy with a withstood spell.<br /> <br /> This applies for other supes too. Vampires can get to stupid high stamina withstand level as Resilience affects stamina, but anything targeting composure or resolve is gonna have the usual 3 or 4 points in withstand. If they are frenzing and also have high blood potency it becomes really harder, but you can always affect stuff around them instead that targeting them directly. turn the air around the vamp in fire, use matter to shape a cage or form a wall in front of them, trap them in a ban and so forth. Or just have life 3 and mind 3 and straight up murder any frenzying vampire ever pumping you up to strenght 10, brawl/weaponry 10 and athletics 10 before the fight. All you need is either preparation or creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T02:26:30-07:00","id":1419748,"title":"","content":"Usually when a spell fails because of Withstand in my games, it is because the player actually forgot to even consider Withstand when preparing the spell. Otherwise they usually raise it more than high enough to get past any Withstand. What empe999 says about Withstand on debuffs is true though. The system does not lend itself very well to debuffs because they are relatively ineffectual. In many cases buffing your own is going to translate to roughly the same impact as debuffing the enemy, but the former is much easier. Of course not all Arcana offer buffs for every situation, while debuffs are more widespread over the Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T03:28:43-07:00","id":1419755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419676#post1419676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So speaking of Withstand, for those who have actually played in games, how does the rules translate to practice. What I mean is does the Withstand rules as is cause players to have a lot of their effects fizzle or do they still apply a lot. Because I gotta say with the way that the rules are written it seems that a lot f castings would fail, and that seems more annoying than fun for a player of a mage who wants to actually use the magic they are supposed to be able to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience is that most spells aren't Withstood because they're cast on yourself or your cabalmates who'd naturally choose not to apply their personal Withstand rating, or because it's cast on the environment/objects without requiring a Withstand rating. When Withstood spells are cast, they're generally Potency primary, and it's relatively easy to guess (ephemeral Rank or probable Resistance Attribute for a Sleeper) or even know (Sympathetic Withstand) what the Withstand rating is going to be so you just adjust it accordingly if your spell doesn't automatically overcome it. In doubt, you could even cast spells to figure it out.<br /> Casting on enemies that can buff their Withstand ratings (enemy mages, certain other supers) was uncommon, and the spell failing was simply a risk you'd have to take.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr the vast majority of spells will succeed, either because they're simply not Withstood or because it's very easy to just compensate if needed. The only spell I remember casting that failed because of spell factors was when I failed to take Size into account.<br /> I don't get why you'd think it'd be common for spells to fail unless you fail to take into account the dice bonuses of Yantras. Especially Personas and Mudras can add tons of dice without taking more than one slot each, and a simple Mantra or other +2 Yantra can fill out any excess Yantra slots. Also, +3 from Willpower is a great way to increase the dice pool further without spending either time or a Yantra slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-23-2020, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T04:02:17-07:00","id":1419757,"title":"","content":"I was actually under the impression that, when forming the imago, you'd know how much withstand there would be. But that seems to not be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:08:41-07:00","id":1419765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>empe999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419757#post1419757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually under the impression that, when forming the imago, you'd know how much withstand there would be. But that seems to not be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that is where Mages' information gathering powers are meant to come in. Using Knowing spells and Mage Sight to know Withstand before you cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:24:10-07:00","id":1419768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419748#post1419748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually when a spell fails because of Withstand in my games, it is because the player actually forgot to even consider Withstand when preparing the spell. Otherwise they usually raise it more than high enough to get past any Withstand. What empe999 says about Withstand on debuffs is true though. The system does not lend itself very well to debuffs because they are relatively ineffectual. In many cases buffing your own is going to translate to roughly the same impact as debuffing the enemy, but the former is much easier. Of course not all Arcana offer buffs for every situation, while debuffs are more widespread over the Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you buff a character, it means only they become a bigger threat with their attacks that round. But debuff the giant spirit and it will have the same effect as buffing the entire cabal and their allies, should they focus attacks on it, all while requiring lower scale on the cast. I imagine that Withstand combined with the spell stacking rules are there to discourage debuffing as a first order strategy, especially since its not a particularly inventive one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T20:21:14-07:00","id":1420067,"title":"","content":"One of my player Mages has a Goetic Familiar, and the Cabal has access to a Synese that they will probably be using to shortcut into the Astral on a regular basis. So the question is: can the familiar use the Synese? If not, is there some other straightforward way of getting a Familiar into the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 10-24-2020, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T23:04:59-07:00","id":1420084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1420067#post1420067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my player Mages has a Goetic Familiar, and the Cabal has access to a Synese that they will probably be using to shortcut into the Astral on a regular basis. So the question is: can the familiar use the Synese? If not, is there some other straightforward way of getting a Familiar into the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory the familiar is already in &quot;though form&quot;, similar to a meditating or sleeping person. So if they use the Key or have a Mind mage Weave it open, they should be able to pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-25-2020, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T08:53:00-07:00","id":1420269,"title":"","content":"Suppose your players want to found a new Nameless Order. What would you make them go through to define Order Tools that function as yantras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T11:33:30-07:00","id":1420298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1420269#post1420269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose your players want to found a new Nameless Order. What would you make them go through to define Order Tools that function as yantras?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the building equipment rules, specifically the building an organization section, could be used.<br /> Exp point spent in the mystery cult merit would then &quot;calcify&quot; the group customs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T13:10:43-07:00","id":1420316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1420269#post1420269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose your players want to found a new Nameless Order. What would you make them go through to define Order Tools that function as yantras?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make it into a 3 dot merit called Nameless Order (X):<br /> <br /> 1 dot: Membership grants a free dot in Occult<br /> 2 dots: Gain a specialty in an Order skill (like Sculpting for crafts)<br /> 3 dots: Gain a 2 dot merit<br /> <br /> Beyond that would require them to become a full Diamond Order. In other words, &quot;4 dots&quot; means Order sized organization and &quot;5 dots&quot; means there is probably someone in the archmage weight class backing the organization.<br /> <br /> Should they wish to progress to a full global conspiracy type of Order, they need to define what they think magic is and then explore its Mysteries until they link to its symbolism. The 3 main methods that come to mind are:<br /> <br /> 1- Reclamation: Find Supernal proof of your thesis, likely by looking into a lost ruin, Verge, Emanation, etc.<br /> <br /> 2- Illumination: Have a mighty patron (archmage, Kerberos, True Fae, etc) give it weight with their involvement. Beating/tricking a True Fae, having an archmage perfect the idea (this is how the Mysterium was created)<br /> <br /> 3- Corroboration: Make their thesis into Truth by an event of enough magnitude to make the Supernal accept it, like The Great Refusal (aka create a Crowning Moment of Awesome)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, Orders have a lot of adherents and history powering their symbolism, making something with as much metaphysical weight should probably be a challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-26-2020, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T13:32:24-07:00","id":1420320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1420316#post1420316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would make it into a 3 dot merit called Nameless Order (X):<br /> <br /> 1 dot: Membership grants a free dot in Occult<br /> 2 dots: Gain a specialty in an Order skill (like Sculpting for crafts)<br /> 3 dots: Gain a 2 dot merit<br /> <br /> Beyond that would require them to become a full Diamond Order. In other words, &amp;quot;4 dots&amp;quot; means Order sized organization and &amp;quot;5 dots&amp;quot; means there is probably someone in the archmage weight class backing the organization.<br /> <br /> Should they wish to progress to a full global conspiracy type of Order, they need to define what they think magic is and then explore its Mysteries until they link to its symbolism. The 3 main methods that come to mind are:<br /> <br /> 1- Reclamation: Find Supernal proof of your thesis, likely by looking into a lost ruin, Verge, Emanation, etc.<br /> <br /> 2- Illumination: Have a mighty patron (archmage, Kerberos, True Fae, etc) give it weight with their involvement. Beating/tricking a True Fae, having an archmage perfect the idea (this is how the Mysterium was created)<br /> <br /> 3- Corroboration: Make their thesis into Truth by an event of enough magnitude to make the Supernal accept it, like The Great Refusal (aka create a Crowning Moment of Awesome)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, Orders have a lot of adherents and history powering their symbolism, making something with as much metaphysical weight should probably be a challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nameless and accursed treats nameless orders as Mystery cult initiation merits from 1 to 5 dots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T10:30:00-07:00","id":1420843,"title":"","content":"Q: is there anything written on how a tremere hollowing could be reversed? I don't seem to find anything, and my players met a tremere NPC who isn't that bad and they would get her out of the hollowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T08:30:01-07:00","id":1420982,"title":"","content":"Ritual Focus mentions that secondary actors instead contribute Potency to a teamworked spell's ritual pool. Does that extend to Sleepwalkers as well ? So would an area under the effect full of a Mystery Cult's members could possibly create a very powerful effect ? <br /> <br /> As a follow up question, can Ritual Focus help in summonings ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T08:33:17-07:00","id":1420983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1420982#post1420982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ritual Focus mentions that secondary actors instead contribute Potency to a teamworked spell's ritual pool. Does that extend to Sleepwalkers as well ? So would an area under the effect full of a Mystery Cult's members could possibly create a very powerful effect ?<br /> <br /> As a follow up question, can Ritual Focus help in summonings ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepwalkers don't teamwork the spell. They can be used as a Yantra, but since they don't roll anything the spell would have no effect. Ritual Focus also explicitly mentions Awakened participants. (Could work mechanically if the Sleepwalkers have the Ritual Savvy Merit, but I really don't think it's applicable.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-30-2020, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T13:05:03-07:00","id":1421043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1420983#post1420983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sleepwalkers don't teamwork the spell. They can be used as a Yantra, but since they don't roll anything the spell would have no effect. Ritual Focus also explicitly mentions Awakened participants. (Could work mechanically if the Sleepwalkers have the Ritual Savvy Merit, but I really don't think it's applicable.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I explained that poorly. I didn't mean Sleepwalker ritualists casting things completely by themselves. What I meant is that if a mage had a Mystery Cult full of Sleepwalkers, could they use Ritual Focus to allow the Sleepwalkers to add Potency to the dice pool rather than simply acts as an environment yantra ? The wording of the spell seemed to leave that possibility open and I just wondered if that could allow for a Mystery Cult that does that to create spells that help keep some kind of ancient horror in check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-30-2020, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:56:57-07:00","id":1421111,"title":"","content":"Can someone please remind me how one achieves an exceptional success on an extended action?<br /> <br /> Also, when determining the maximum number of roles on an extended action, how does Specialty figure in? Is it just a flat +1 if the roll aligns with the character's specialty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T22:03:10-07:00","id":1421113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421111#post1421111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please remind me how one achieves an exceptional success on an extended action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as on a regular action. If there's a specific outcome from completing an extended action with five or more successes beyond the required number (i.e. finishing with an exceptional success), it will say so in the roll results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, when determining the maximum number of roles on an extended action, how does Specialty figure in? Is it just a flat +1 if the roll aligns with the character's specialty? </div> </div> </div>Yup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T00:09:18-07:00","id":1421128,"title":"","content":"So for an extended action, when aiming for &quot;apply the exceptional success result of the action when you complete your goal,&quot; once a player has met the required number of successes but still has rolls remaining, can the player simply spend more time rolling to accrue an exceptional success so long as she doesn't exceed the maximum number of rolls?<br /> <br /> Or does &quot;apply the exceptional success result of the action when you complete your goal&quot; require an exceptional success on the final roll where the player achieved the required number of successes?<br /> <br /> If the latter is true: Suppose the player requires two more successes for an extended action. On her next roll, the player achieves 5 success. Is that an exceptional success? Or did she need 7 successes for an exceptional success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 10-31-2020, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T06:59:49-07:00","id":1421152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421128#post1421128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for an extended action, when aiming for &quot;apply the exceptional success result of the action when you complete your goal,&quot; once a player has met the required number of successes but still has rolls remaining, can the player simply spend more time rolling to accrue an exceptional success so long as she doesn't exceed the maximum number of rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because once you've crossed the threshold of required successes the extended action is over, and also because an exceptional success is a result on a singular roll. You can no more get an exceptional success by rolling five successes over two or more rolls than you can damage a Durability 3 object barehanded by rolling two successes on two separate Brawl rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or does &quot;apply the exceptional success result of the action when you complete your goal&quot; require an exceptional success on the final roll where the player achieved the required number of successes? </div> </div> </div>The latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the latter is true: Suppose the player requires two more successes for an extended action. On her next roll, the player achieves 5 success. Is that an exceptional success? Or did she need 7 successes for an exceptional success? </div> </div> </div>Historically, it's varied, because this is a particular exceptional success result rather than a general rule for extended actions. In the context of the 2e ruleset, the latter would be necessary for an action that specified you needed to exceed the required success count, but getting five successes on the last roll would still produce the normal results of an exceptional success on an extended action (speedier completion/lowered threshold/Condtion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T07:18:36-07:00","id":1421156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421043#post1421043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I explained that poorly. I didn't mean Sleepwalker ritualists casting things completely by themselves. What I meant is that if a mage had a Mystery Cult full of Sleepwalkers, could they use Ritual Focus to allow the Sleepwalkers to add Potency to the dice pool rather than simply acts as an environment yantra ? The wording of the spell seemed to leave that possibility open and I just wondered if that could allow for a Mystery Cult that does that to create spells that help keep some kind of ancient horror in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sleepwalkers are Sleepwalkers and interact with magic as Sleepwalkers do. Being in a Mystery Cult has no bearing on that, and I see nothing in the spell that would imply otherwise. Sleepwalkers are inherently unable to form an Imago, and thus unable to directly contribute dice to the dice pool. Their presence during a ritual is only good as a Yantra because their bearing on the spell is dependent on the mage using them to reinforce part of the spell.<br /> A similar spell to Ritual Focus could grant the Ritual Savvy Merit to a Sleepwalker, but that's a bit different as it's about preparations to the ritual rather than participation in it.<br /> <br /> Edit: You could also cast a spell to make them a better Yantra, like As Above, So Below. But for balancing purposes I recommend either as a dice trick or as a fixed bonus (increasing from +1 to +2 is a bit low, but +2 is a good level for a Yantra you've spent some extra effort on) rather than dice equal to Potency because that's one of the most slippery of imbalanced slopes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-31-2020, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T06:21:53-08:00","id":1421284,"title":"","content":"I am getting back into running a Mage game and I\u2019m a bit rusty. I will probably have more questions, but these are two that I had so far. <br /> <br /> (1) If I cast Wards and Signs, does it replace the standard Withstand rating or does it follow the standard rules for multiple Withstand ratings? For example, let\u2019s say someone casts a spell on a subject that is Withstood my Resolve, and assume they have Resolve 2 and an active Wards and Signs spell at Potency 3. Would the subject have Withstand 3 or 4?<br /> <br /> (2) Can someone walk me through a basic example of how the mechanics of sympathetic casting works? I feel like I understand it but there\u2019s also some confusing aspects of how it works. <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say I want to Scry on a subject with whom I have no sympathetic connection. Let\u2019s say I have a picture of them on my cell phone but don\u2019t know their sympathetic name. How does the casting work?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, let\u2019s say I snuck an object into their pocket to which I have a Strong connection (like a lock of my hair). What would I need to do to Scry now? Is this easier or harder than the first example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T10:04:02-08:00","id":1421308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421284#post1421284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am getting back into running a Mage game and I\u2019m a bit rusty. I will probably have more questions, but these are two that I had so far. <br /> <br /> (1) If I cast Wards and Signs, does it replace the standard Withstand rating or does it follow the standard rules for multiple Withstand ratings? For example, let\u2019s say someone casts a spell on a subject that is Withstood my Resolve, and assume they have Resolve 2 and an active Wards and Signs spell at Potency 3. Would the subject have Withstand 3 or 4?<br /> <br /> (2) Can someone walk me through a basic example of how the mechanics of sympathetic casting works? I feel like I understand it but there\u2019s also some confusing aspects of how it works. <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say I want to Scry on a subject with whom I have no sympathetic connection. Let\u2019s say I have a picture of them on my cell phone but don\u2019t know their sympathetic name. How does the casting work?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, let\u2019s say I snuck an object into their pocket to which I have a Strong connection (like a lock of my hair). What would I need to do to Scry now? Is this easier or harder than the first example?</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Wards and Signs substitutes its Potency for Withstand wholesale.<br /> <br /> 2- You cast the spell that Reached for sympathetic range, then spend a mana to activate the Attainment and using a yantra slot for the sympathetic link. Next you determine Withstand, to calculate the base value:<br /> <br /> a) If the spell is not Withstood by the target: the effect is Withstood by the Sympathetic Range (found in page 173). By that chart, a photo is a Weak link and a hair sample is a Strong one, the value is adjusted accordingly.<br /> <br /> b) If the spell is Withstood: take the greatest value between the Sympathetic Range Withstand and the target's Withstand, to tjis value you add 1 due to account for multiple sources <br /> <br /> Now you take that base vale and should you not know the target's sympathetic name, then add 1 to that value. Spellcasting otherwise proceeds as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T10:28:14-08:00","id":1421310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421308#post1421308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2- You cast the spell that Reached for sympathetic range, then spend a mana to activate the Attainment and using a yantra slot for the sympathetic link. Next you determine Withstand, to calculate the base value:<br /> <br /> a) If the spell is not Withstood by the target: the effect is Withstood by the Sympathetic Range (found in page 173). By that chart, a photo is a Weak link and a hair sample is a Strong one, the value is adjusted accordingly.<br /> <br /> b) If the spell is Withstood: take the greatest value between the Sympathetic Range Withstand and the target's Withstand, to tjis value you add 1 due to account for multiple sources<br /> <br /> Now you take that base vale and should you not know the target's sympathetic name, then add 1 to that value. Spellcasting otherwise proceeds as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so this is the part that I get confused about then. In the first example, if I'm just trying to use the photo as a material sympathy Yantra, do I need to Borrow Threads to establish a connection to the subject directly? Don't I need to have a personal connection between me and the subject to cast sympathetically? Or can I just target them by holding something that has a link to them and using it as a Yantra?<br /> <br /> It makes more sense to me in the example of using my own hair. I have a Strong connection to my hair sample itself, so if I'm scrying on the hair, that should be pretty easy by comparison, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T10:34:38-08:00","id":1421312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421284#post1421284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1) If I cast Wards and Signs, does it replace the standard Withstand rating or does it follow the standard rules for multiple Withstand ratings? For example, let\u2019s say someone casts a spell on a subject that is Withstood my Resolve, and assume they have Resolve 2 and an active Wards and Signs spell at Potency 3. Would the subject have Withstand 3 or 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421284#post1421284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let\u2019s say I want to Scry on a subject with whom I have no sympathetic connection. Let\u2019s say I have a picture of them on my cell phone but don\u2019t know their sympathetic name. How does the casting work?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't cast a sympathetic spell on that subject because you don't have a sympathetic connection to them.<br /> Quick edit: Unfortunately a photo also has no inherent sympathetic connection to what or who it depicts, so you can't cast Borrow Threads on it to gain a Sympathetic Connection to the intended subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421284#post1421284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, let\u2019s say I snuck an object into their pocket to which I have a Strong connection (like a lock of my hair). What would I need to do to Scry now? Is this easier or harder than the first example?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can cast the Scrying spell on the lock of hair. It'd have a Withstand rating of 1. Unfortunately you won't get any information from outside the pocket unless your ST is more generous about what the spell reveals, or allows a Reach option for &quot;zooming out&quot;. Or, you could just cast a second Scrying spell on the person whose pocket you're witnessing, as a remote spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421284#post1421284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(2) Can someone walk me through a basic example of how the mechanics of sympathetic casting works? I feel like I understand it but there\u2019s also some confusing aspects of how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need three things to cast sympathetic spells:<br /> 1.) Space 2+ for the Sympathetic Range Attainment.<br /> 2.) A Sympathetic Connection to the intended subject.<br /> 3.) A Sympathetic Yantra for the intended subject.<br /> <br /> The first one is pretty obvious.<br /> The second one can be a lot tougher, but there are spells for borrowing or even creating Sympathetic Connections so it's relatively easy to circumvent. You can also prep a subject by casting a different spell on them first in order to create a Weak Sympathetic Connection to be used in the future.<br /> The third one is easy provided you have access to anything you can draw on as you could just draw the subject. It does not have to be a good drawing, as long as it contains something that is tied to the person. You could also use the Sympathetic Name if you know it.<br /> <br /> When you cast the spell, you need to use one Reach to bring the spell to Sensory Range, and then one Mana to bring it to Sympathetic Range. And finally, you need to use a Sympathetic Yantra tied to the subject. This Yantra does not grant any bonus dice even if it normally would.<br /> The strength of the Sympathetic Connection adds a Withstand rating. When casting on a person, this Withstand rating increases by one if you don't know their Sympathetic Name. A Sympathetic Name is a valid Yantra for sympathetic magic but you only need to <i>know it</i> to avoid the extra Withstand. (But if you do know it, there's rarely any point in not using it.)<br /> <br /> Real example from my game (I don't remember the actual numbers so I fudged them into something that's probably close): Irminsul (Mastigos, Space 3, Gnosis 4) wants to provide a clean getaway for his cabal after having broken into the cellar of a Seer pylon's headquarters. He has prepared by casting Web-Weaver on a clearing in a nearby park to gain a Strong connection. He's also taken a photograph of the park on his phone.<br /> He intends to cast Co-Location which he knows as a Rote, and spends his three free Reaches on the following: Instant casting, sensory range, and Advanced Duration so he has time to bring everyone through. He spends one Mana to bring it to Sympathetic Range so he can cast both here and on the clearing. On his phone he has a photo of the clearing, which serves as his sympathetic Yantra, but it grants no dice because it's a Sympathetic Range spell. He also spends a turn applying the Mudra for an additional 3 dice (due to his Athletics 3).<br /> With a dice pool of 10 (Space 3+Gnosis 4+Mudra 3), he starts looking over spell factors. He needs to increase the Potency two steps up to Potency 3 because he needs Potency 2 for the spell to work, and the Withstand rating is 1 because of the Strong connection. With a final dice pool of 6, he succeeds and the spell is cast successfully.<br /> As Father Albertus (the cabal's Obrimos) is buying some time by monologuing at the surprised Seers in the next room, Irminsul spends two turns casting Co-Location in this room and on the prepared clearing, and then a few turn showing the rest of his cabal mates and some kidnapped Sleepwalkers through the Iris (because only Irminsul has Space Sight and can interact with it), before Albertus legs it into the room and is pulled through by Irminsul who reflexively ends the spell to prevent the Seers from following. Exfiltration successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-01-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T11:02:42-08:00","id":1421316,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> - Your example and responses are incredibly helpful. This makes more sense to me. I think I was gettinc confused about the difference between the Sympathetic connection, and the Sympathetic Yantra. So a photo could be used as a material Sympathetic Yantra, but because it has no inherent symbolic connection to the person, I can't Borrow Threads on it. Got it.<br /> <br /> I know I've read before that casting creates a Weak connection on a subject. How long does that actually last, or where can I find guidance as a ST on how long to rule that a connection might exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T11:40:31-08:00","id":1421320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421316#post1421316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - Your example and responses are incredibly helpful. This makes more sense to me. I think I was gettinc confused about the difference between the Sympathetic connection, and the Sympathetic Yantra. So a photo could be used as a material Sympathetic Yantra, but because it has no inherent symbolic connection to the person, I can't Borrow Threads on it. Got it.<br /> <br /> I know I've read before that casting creates a Weak connection on a subject. How long does that actually last, or where can I find guidance as a ST on how long to rule that a connection might exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find a clarification to this in page 193, the Attainment specifically calls for a yantra to be used. In the case of your hair, you are the yantra to &quot;person carrying my hair&quot;. In the case of the picture, it is the yantra to &quot;person in this picture&quot;.<br /> <br /> Borrow Threads allows you to take and give sympathetic connections without using material links. So if you have a piece of your hair, you can make the subject have a strong connection to you without placing it on them and risking them turning it against you (either by magic or detective work). Similarly, you could take the connection on the picture and store it on a keychain for future use. With some clever mix of that spell and a veiling, you could make sympathetic attacks against the subject redirext into a tree or a heavily warded magical item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T12:50:27-08:00","id":1421327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421156#post1421156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sleepwalkers are Sleepwalkers and interact with magic as Sleepwalkers do. Being in a Mystery Cult has no bearing on that, and I see nothing in the spell that would imply otherwise. Sleepwalkers are inherently unable to form an Imago, and thus unable to directly contribute dice to the dice pool. Their presence during a ritual is only good as a Yantra because their bearing on the spell is dependent on the mage using them to reinforce part of the spell.<br /> A similar spell to Ritual Focus could grant the Ritual Savvy Merit to a Sleepwalker, but that's a bit different as it's about preparations to the ritual rather than participation in it.<br /> <br /> Edit: You could also cast a spell to make them a better Yantra, like As Above, So Below. But for balancing purposes I recommend either as a dice trick or as a fixed bonus (increasing from +1 to +2 is a bit low, but +2 is a good level for a Yantra you've spent some extra effort on) rather than dice equal to Potency because that's one of the most slippery of imbalanced slopes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I need to think more on that spell idea. Ritual Focus does something similar to the Egregore merit, but perhaps it can be adapted into a way for Sleepwalkers to make a better contribution without it being broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T15:00:56-08:00","id":1421342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421320#post1421320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can find a clarification to this in page 193, the Attainment specifically calls for a yantra to be used. In the case of your hair, you are the yantra to &quot;person carrying my hair&quot;. In the case of the picture, it is the yantra to &quot;person in this picture&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>More specifically, you are a fitting material Yantra to your lock of hair. That would not allow you to cast spells directly on anyone holding the lock of hair. You can still use it to establish a sympathetic connection to whoever holds the hair with creative use of additional spells, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421320#post1421320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Borrow Threads allows you to take and give sympathetic connections without using material links.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most often you do need some material link to cast Borrow Threads on in order to gain the necessary sympathetic connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421320#post1421320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you have a piece of your hair, you can make the subject have a strong connection to you without placing it on them and risking them turning it against you (either by magic or detective work). Similarly, you could take the connection on the picture and store it on a keychain for future use. With some clever mix of that spell and a veiling, you could make sympathetic attacks against the subject redirext into a tree or a heavily warded magical item.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get what you're getting at here. Regardless, you can't <i>redirect</i> any sympathetic magic just by transferring sympathetic connections back and forth. If someone has transferred a sympathetic connection between a mage and an intended subject away from that subject and onto a tree, then any spell that mage would cast using Sympathetic Range on the intended subject would simply fail. The tree is not subject to any spells unless it's specifically targeted and the mage uses a sympathetic Yantra tied to that tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T08:00:02-08:00","id":1421623,"title":"","content":"Could someone please post a complete rewrite of Ghost Gate that is clear, detailed, and unambiguous, either here or in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread?<br /> <br /> I've read every thread I can find about that spell on the forum and seen a number of different interpretations; the most recent was more than two years ago. There are so many ambiguous/controversial elements in it that I'd prefer to see someone's coherent vision for the spell entire than ask about various elements of it piecemeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T10:48:56-08:00","id":1421650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421623#post1421623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone please post a complete rewrite of Ghost Gate that is clear, detailed, and unambiguous, either here or in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread?<br /> <br /> I've read every thread I can find about that spell on the forum and seen a number of different interpretations; the most recent was more than two years ago. There are so many ambiguous/controversial elements in it that I'd prefer to see someone's coherent vision for the spell entire than ask about various elements of it piecemeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the general idea is:<br /> <br /> 1- Living and ephemeral beings, plus anything they would be arguably wearing or carrying makes it to Death Twilight normally.<br /> <br /> 2- Everything else is destroyed and becomes Death ephemera as it crosses over. Exceptions include exceptionally powerful items,such as Artifacts, in addition to anything under the spell Death Touched Item. <br /> <br /> The Reach option skips the portal and just &quot;teleports&quot; the target.<br /> <br /> So the magically enhances sword, the fetish and the imbied item will all be destroyed as they cross through and only retain their base mundane utility in Twilight, unless someone is carrying it with them.<br /> <br /> I think that is the intended use. Technically Death Twilight is &quot;safer&quot; because while ghosts are more numerous than spirits, they are bound to their anchors. I think that keeps the spell useful without having to cast Death Touched Item all the time and still makes the spell distinct from its Spirit counterpart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T12:56:31-08:00","id":1421664,"title":"","content":"I've always played it that if you don't use the +1 Reach option, the spell opens a portal for as long as the spell lasts. All clothes and personal posessions turn into ephemera when you enter along with your body, as you and your belongings are transformed to Death-attuned Twilight. If you walk back out, all of those mundane, material objects are destroyed. Whe the duration runs out, the portal disappears, which has no bearing on the state of the person; you're either stuck in Twilight, or you're back in the flesh, depending on whether you came back through it. The transformation itself is effectively Lasting.<br /> <br /> Alternatively if you use the +1 Reach option, there is no gate; the subject, along with their possessions and clothing, is transformed to Death-attuned Twilight at the time of casting. When the duration ends, the subject and all of their personal possessions exit Twilight wherever they are. This is significantly more useful for purposes of keeping your equpiment intact, but it also has drawbacks such as spell control and ability to be dispelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:12:30-08:00","id":1421667,"title":"","content":"I have another question for myself, one that I feel should be simple but I can't find a straightforward answer anywhere. If a Gulmoth is summoned (either intentionally or unintentionally) into the Fallen World, and it suffers lethal damage equal to its Corpus, is it discorporated but hibernating, much like a spirit would? Or does it slip back into the Abyss, like a Supernal being would?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:55:05-08:00","id":1421681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1421667#post1421667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question for myself, one that I feel should be simple but I can't find a straightforward answer anywhere. If a Gulmoth is summoned (either intentionally or unintentionally) into the Fallen World, and it suffers lethal damage equal to its Corpus, is it discorporated but hibernating, much like a spirit would? Or does it slip back into the Abyss, like a Supernal being would?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably hibernation on the simple principle that Abyssal entities are tricky like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T05:07:31-08:00","id":1422221,"title":"","content":"Do 2e Seers have the same relationship with the Abyss as in 1e? They want to widen it to reduce the number of awakenings and the overall availability of magical power in the Fallen World to prevent anyone from being able to challenge the Exarchs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T05:33:56-08:00","id":1422225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1422221#post1422221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do 2e Seers have the same relationship with the Abyss as in 1e? They want to widen it to reduce the number of awakenings and the overall availability of magical power in the Fallen World to prevent anyone from being able to challenge the Exarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Regulate the Abyss&quot; is a tenet of the Seers in both editions; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971430#post971430\">as Dave has pointed out</a>, their particular institutional flaws mean they are nevertheless highly susceptible to Scelestus infiltration, but that's a different thing from them ever having been told to make the thing bigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T06:29:22-08:00","id":1422235,"title":"","content":"What happens if a spell that reduces an object's Durability reduces to or below zero? It suffers <i>extra</i> Structure loss when attacked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T06:32:50-08:00","id":1422237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1422235#post1422235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a spell that reduces an object's Durability reduces to or below zero? It suffers <i>extra</i> Structure loss when attacked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Durability doesn't go below zero and the only effect there is that it doesn't subtract any damage from the Structure lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T06:36:59-08:00","id":1422239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1422225#post1422225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Regulate the Abyss&quot; is a tenet of the Seers in both editions; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971430#post971430\">as Dave has pointed out</a>, their particular institutional flaws mean they are nevertheless highly susceptible to Scelestus infiltration, but that's a different thing from them ever having been told to make the thing bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm looking in the 1e Seers source book where there are <i>many </i>mentions of the Seer's desiring to widen the Abyss:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> &quot;Regardless of the reasons, the Seers developed two closely entwined mandates. They first and foremost dedicated themselves to widening the Abyss and attempting to eliminate or convert Awakened mages who opposed the Exarchs.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> &quot; Most hope that by helping to increase mortal disbelief in all forms of supernatural activity, they will help widen the Abyss and limit the power of all other supernatural beings&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Although many Seers believe that widening the Abyss is one of the most effective ways of preventing further Awakenings, the Seers still need to be careful about Abyssal intrusions into the Fallen World.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> &quot;Since the Fall of Atlantis, the Exarchs have been working towards strengthening the Abyss, so that there is no chance of the Supernal and the Fallen World ever rejoining. As the Abyss widens, the amount of magical knowledge and power available to mages shrinks. Without the power of the ancient mages, modern mages stand no chance of ever being able to truly threaten the Exarchs\u2019 reign.&quot;<br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T17:19:15-08:00","id":1422675,"title":"","content":"Oneiros and Hallows<br /> <br /> I would like the collective thoughts on using the Create Truth Spell to create a Hallow inside a mage's Oneiros. I assume it's possible in the Shadow and the Underworld. Is the Oneiros a potential spot for a Hallow? If so what might be the point cost for such a Hallow? Just curious<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T18:30:27-08:00","id":1422679,"title":"","content":"The Oneiros is only a location in a metaphorical sense, so I'd say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T19:20:36-08:00","id":1422684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1422675#post1422675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oneiros and Hallows<br /> <br /> I would like the collective thoughts on using the Create Truth Spell to create a Hallow inside a mage's Oneiros. I assume it's possible in the Shadow and the Underworld. Is the Oneiros a potential spot for a Hallow? If so what might be the point cost for such a Hallow? Just curious<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e book Astral Realms discusses this idea. Short version: you can, but there are vaguely defined &quot;consequences&quot;. Mages who put a Hallow in their own Oneiros are said to become increasingly erratic and dangerous until either disappearing mysteriously or having to get put down. The possibility of putting one in a Sleeper's Oneiros is raised, with some believing that it will lead to the Sleeper's awakening, but more likely the Hallow will just fade away from Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T19:43:46-08:00","id":1422687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1422239#post1422239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking in the 1e Seers source book where there are <i>many </i>mentions of the Seer's desiring to widen the Abyss</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. You understand that that's a different thing from them being told to do that, right?<br /> <br /> Like, the literal first paragraph that this topic comes up in highlights the distinction that the core mandate the Seers have from the Exarchs re: the Abyss is just that it should be prevented from being made smaller. There's also repeated mentions of the Abyss &quot;widening&quot; being something that is happening without the Seers' input, and they've had a well-established history of querying the Exarchs through indirect means with no detectable footprint like casting lots or reading omens with mundane practice, to say nothing of how &quot;the Seers as a sect are heavily compromised by Abyssal infiltration&quot; sees its most direct representation in the Gatekeepers.<br /> <br /> They're self-serving infighting powers-behind-the-throne who have a bad habit of thinking that they should cheat reality for their own advancement because they can, which is and has been a flaw exploited by Scelesti and other forces of the Abyss as these activities further empower the forces Outside \u2014 as with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1353225#post1353225\">Ammut and the Judges in Mummy</a>, there's a moral compromise angle that can be looked at there \u2014 but any corruption along the sect's institutional timeline from &quot;stop the Abyss from shrinking&quot; to &quot;make the Abyss bigger&quot; is nearly impossible to chart an origin point for when the Seers have such a long-running tendency toward rewriting history, reassigning credit and blame, and otherwise making the Iron Pyramid a right mess to exist in even without getting magic involved.<br /> <br /> If the Exarchs have changed their tune, or had their tune changed by centuries of Seer momentum, it's about as hard to identify the difference between those two things just like pinning down why the Abyss has changed the tenor of its interface with the world through history, because timeless god-magic is involved and we've got a rough enough task figuring out regular history. Regardless, this seems to be largely consistent between the two editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1422675#post1422675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like the collective thoughts on using the Create Truth Spell to create a Hallow inside a mage's Oneiros. I assume it's possible in the Shadow and the Underworld. Is the Oneiros a potential spot for a Hallow? If so what might be the point cost for such a Hallow? Just curious</div> </div> </div> </div>As Scriptorian notes, Astral Realms' discussion of the Arcana in Astral space talks about this in its Prime writeup \u2014 to summarize, they're not naturally occurring in the Astral, <i>but</i> you can definitely make one with magic, <i>but</i> the consequences are pretty dire; besides the rumors of mages with internal Hallows destabilizing, Temenos realms start to disconnect from the wider collective unconscious and Hallows in the Anima Mundi get scrubbed by the local in relatively short order.<br /> <br /> Create Truth, as a 2e spell with additional details of how Hallows work (altering the local ley lines, accumulating odd supernatural quirks, and otherwise being definitionally unique or extreme features of the environment that manifest and crystalize Supernal Truth into the world), suggests to me that putting one in your soul is a fast track to becoming Enraptured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T09:51:47-08:00","id":1422767,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and Scriptorium<br /> Thanks for the responses. Just got the astral book. Basically Create Truth is the ultimate weapon against things you don't like in the astral plane . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T06:16:52-08:00","id":1423046,"title":"","content":"More questions that I would love help with:<br /> <br /> (1) I know I've read before that casting a spell creates a Weak connection on a subject. How long does that actually last, or where can I find guidance as a ST on how long to rule that a connection might exist?<br /> <br /> (2) Per Mage p. 257, when ephemeral entities are discorporated due to losing their Corpus to lethal or aggravated damage, &quot;If it has even a single Essence or Mana point remaining, it reforms in a safe place (a Conditioned location, usually), hibernating.&quot; Can a hibernating ephemeral entity be damaged or destroyed, or do you have to wait for the entity to reform?<br /> <br /> (3) Does intentionally destroying an ephemeral entity risk an Act of Hubris by default, or is that at the ST's discretion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T09:54:54-08:00","id":1424759,"title":"","content":"Can a mage use Rewrite History to, at least temporarily, kill someone? (Eg, <i>When you were a teenager, you mistook a coral snake for a milk snake.</i>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T10:13:52-08:00","id":1424767,"title":"","content":"Yeah, although I'd consider it an Act of Hubris to kill someone even temporarily using magic and I also rule that this spell is &quot;obvious magic&quot; from the perspective of a Sleeper subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T11:17:19-08:00","id":1424784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1423046#post1423046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More questions that I would love help with:<br /> <br /> (1) I know I've read before that casting a spell creates a Weak connection on a subject. How long does that actually last, or where can I find guidance as a ST on how long to rule that a connection might exist?<br /> <br /> (2) Per Mage p. 257, when ephemeral entities are discorporated due to losing their Corpus to lethal or aggravated damage, &quot;If it has even a single Essence or Mana point remaining, it reforms in a safe place (a Conditioned location, usually), hibernating.&quot; Can a hibernating ephemeral entity be damaged or destroyed, or do you have to wait for the entity to reform?<br /> <br /> (3) Does intentionally destroying an ephemeral entity risk an Act of Hubris by default, or is that at the ST's discretion?</div> </div> </div> </div>1- I would say until their Nimbus fades from the subject <br /> <br /> 2- Yep, and it can't fight back until it reaches a threshold. So those without a Spirit caster can just sabotage the source of Essence and starve it until they are permanently killed or keep killing it (either with its Ban or something like Ephemeral Enchantment ). If they have a Familiar with a compatible purview and the Drain Numina, even better, they get an Essence appetizer and a full meal. If they want to gain political clout, they serve this chance to their rivals.<br /> <br /> 3- It does fall into Understanding Wisdom as a form of killing. Certain powerful mages would view beings that live in a less real strata of existence as illusory and therefore there is no crime in killing dreams, illusions or echoes of reality. These mages are the Exarchs and the less real beings are the residents of the Fallen World. So mages killing ephemeral entities just because &quot;more will eventually appear&quot; can be seen as a microcosmic version of that. So its certainly hubristic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-18-2020, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T13:36:24-08:00","id":1424813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1424767#post1424767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, although I'd consider it an Act of Hubris to kill someone even temporarily using magic and I also rule that this spell is &quot;obvious magic&quot; from the perspective of a Sleeper subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally fair on both points.<br /> <br /> It could be an interesting strategy to cast Rewrite History in that way to temporarily kill another mage, thus causing all their active spells to relinquish unsafely. I'm not sure whether or not they would revert back when the Duration runs out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T15:55:22-08:00","id":1424823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1424813#post1424813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally fair on both points.<br /> <br /> It could be an interesting strategy to cast Rewrite History in that way to temporarily kill another mage, thus causing all their active spells to relinquish unsafely. I'm not sure whether or not they would revert back when the Duration runs out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Patterning could give the option, because it can change anything into any other form within its purview. So Fate can make a target take parallel actions at the same time and choose which, if any, happen at the end. Matter can change apple cider into tungsten. For Rewrite History, you could make the historical changes only affect the target (just like Quarantine suspends the subject in its own &quot;outside space&quot;) or make them be part of the &quot;main&quot; timeline. When the effect ends, the spell can either bring them back to the &quot;start point&quot; or add any additional changes as well (such as cuts and bruises they received while in this state). It all depends on the intent of the caster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T16:26:06-08:00","id":1424826,"title":"","content":"My opinion is that Time is the most tightly constrained Arcana, with very few options for Creative Thaumaturgy. I think it's very hard to devise a new Time spell that does not overlap so heavily with one of the published spells that you really ought to just use the published spell. And those spells tend to be tightly locked down with explicit restrictions and much of the functionality consigned to expensive Reach options. I think that the developers wanted making significant changes to the past to be difficult and prone to paradox in comparison to directly changing the present.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To clarify, that is to say that I don't think you can Creative Thaumaturgy &quot;basically Rewrite History but it's intrinsically Lasting and has some of the Reach options build in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone who sees this post as throwing down the gauntlet on Time Creative Thaumaturgy, I'd love to see what original and distinctive Time spells you can post in the appropriate thread. There's a relative dearth of Time spells there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 11-18-2020, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T18:22:20-08:00","id":1424841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1424826#post1424826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion is that Time is the most tightly constrained Arcana, with very few options for Creative Thaumaturgy. I think it's very hard to devise a new Time spell that does not overlap so heavily with one of the published spells that you really ought to just use the published spell. And those spells tend to be tightly locked down with explicit restrictions and much of the functionality consigned to expensive Reach options. I think that the developers wanted making significant changes to the past to be difficult and prone to paradox in comparison to directly changing the present.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To clarify, that is to say that I don't think you can Creative Thaumaturgy &quot;basically Rewrite History but it's intrinsically Lasting and has some of the Reach options build in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone who sees this post as throwing down the gauntlet on Time Creative Thaumaturgy, I'd love to see what original and distinctive Time spells you can post in the appropriate thread. There's a relative dearth of Time spells there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find Forces is the most difficult for me, by a wide margin, its domain is very locked down. I have been trying to make a Forces and Space Mastigos Legacy of the Mysterium as a personal challenge and coming up with spells that don't already exist has been quite the ordeal, much less ones mixed with Space. Current ideas are to tie them to an Emanation, such as one inspired by The Music of Eric Zann or The Fauna of Mirrors.<br /> <br /> Time is much more intuitive for me to work with and I have posted a few spells there, including:<br /> <br /> * Temporal invisibility by falsifying your presence in the present, creating an afterimage in a loop animation <br /> * Decrease healing time to gain werewolf like recovery <br /> * Perfect your combat instincts with minor divinations to dodge due to perfect positioning (always in Dodge rather than defending while its active)<br /> * Speeding up any independent process by days/months/years (synthesizing medicine, fermentation, etc)<br /> * Creating a zero weight storage of infinite capacity (stutters the content to the future and discerns what you want to store/retrieve via Fate)<br /> * Creating an illusory disguise by simulating an older version of yourself (or younger via temporal sympathy), which accounts for any specific parameter (scarred from a difficult life, aged gracefully, etc)<br /> <br /> Some ideas I have been toying with:<br /> <br /> * Possess someone in the past with conjunctional Mind 4<br /> * Make someone do actions in a loop with Ruling (they always think they need to repeat what they just did and are oblivious to the times they did it before)<br /> * Make someone's perceptions be stuck at the time you cast the spell (everyone is &quot;frozen&quot; even as the battle rages on and they have no idea they have been attacked)<br /> * Increase bleed out time for lethal and aggravated damage (place this in a lunargent bullet with Weaving and any werewolf will go splat long before they can do anything about it)<br /> * Make bad things not get better, an inverted Veil of Moments called Time Salts All Wounds, preventing Conditions from ending or wounds from naturally healing<br /> * Gaining dots in Anonimity and/or Alternate Identity by Veiling your own past<br /> * D\u00e9j\u00e0 Fu (inspired by the Discworld martial art of the same name), a Patterning which allows you to roll for actions that happen in a splintered timeline. When the spell ends, they all resolve in the present one (building a fort, attacking multiple times a target, etc)<br /> * Create an absolute shield with a Patterning that shifts any incoming attacks (non sensory or sympathetic spells) to &quot;dummy&quot; splinters in the timeline (the presents your actions didn't choose to be canon).<br /> * Use a Weaving to gain circular aging, connecting your current age to your prime. That way time attacks actually work in your favor since you can't be aged to death and would be sent to your healed prime instead. It also means areas with shattered or unstable time can't turn you to dust.<br /> * Some kind of temporal bungee jumping or time teleportation from the casting point and the present/future, using an anchored temporal stutter. Inspired by the mission A Crack in the Slab from Dishonored 2, but at the moment its still a very nebulous idea.<br /> * An Unmaking that renders the targets stuck looping into the next (or last depending on the caster's preference) [Potency] turns for the duration, everything resetting after each loop elapses (mana, damage, but not memories). Inspired by how Dr Strange defeated Dormammu in the MCU.<br /> * An insidious variation of prophecy that falsifies a contest, trapping the unknowing target in a vision of it where the foe is implacable, yet just tough enough that victory seems at hand and they exhaust themselves fighting the apparition only they can see. Inspired by phase 1 of Lady Butterfly in Sekiro and Batman's Agamemnon Contingency for Wonder Woman.<br /> <br /> Hope those help inspire some ideas, Time is one of my favorite Arcana. If you have any ideas for the Forces and Space Legacy, please let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-19-2020, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T14:25:24-08:00","id":1425013,"title":"","content":"In the chronicle I'm working on I'd like to have a prominent Consilium mastigos, maybe a herald, be possessed by something goetic. Would a goetic daimon or demon be capable of potentially possessing a careless mastigos in this way? What chain of events would or could lead to that happening? And finally, how long could the goetic entity hope to keep this up and could they use supernal magic while possessing their dreamer? They'd be trying to pass as non-goetic, as if nothing had changed if that's at all possible or explainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26531-sleepwalker","user":"Sleepwalker","date":". 11-19-2020, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26531-sleepwalker","name":"Sleepwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T15:17:54-08:00","id":1425023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sleepwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1425013#post1425013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the chronicle I'm working on I'd like to have a prominent Consilium mastigos, maybe a herald, be possessed by something goetic. Would a goetic daimon or demon be capable of potentially possessing a careless mastigos in this way? What chain of events would or could lead to that happening? And finally, how long could the goetic entity hope to keep this up and could they use supernal magic while possessing their dreamer? They'd be trying to pass as non-goetic, as if nothing had changed if that's at all possible or explainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically they cannot, since goetia don't have Manifestations, save for either a certain property of a Mystery (such as New York) or if a mage goes out of their way to allow them to (with a Weaving of Mind and Spirit/Death). So a very ambitious Clavicularius or Bene Asmodai would probably do it.<br /> <br /> Another option is for the goetia to stealthfully enter the mage's Oneiros when they enter/exit it (or should a Mind mage open the path for them). From there they could engage in carefully and stealthily modifying the mage's mind to align with the goetia's goals (since the native goetia and especially the Daimon would normally not abide by its actions), rendering them into a copy or unknowing lackey of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T23:06:42-08:00","id":1425093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sleepwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1425013#post1425013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the chronicle I'm working on I'd like to have a prominent Consilium mastigos, maybe a herald, be possessed by something goetic. Would a goetic daimon or demon be capable of potentially possessing a careless mastigos in this way? What chain of events would or could lead to that happening? And finally, how long could the goetic entity hope to keep this up and could they use supernal magic while possessing their dreamer? They'd be trying to pass as non-goetic, as if nothing had changed if that's at all possible or explainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use a Goetia that is a familiar of another mage.<br /> As kaiser has said, a mind mage can force manifestation on a goetia.<br /> Also this mage could use the familiar senses to cast his spell remotely, maintaining the facade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T10:22:57-08:00","id":1425183,"title":"","content":"If I did this in a story, the Mastigos would have done it to himself and the mystery would be about what he was trying to achieve in doing so (probably an attempt at drastic mental self-reinvention).<br /> <br /> &quot;Natural&quot; goetia outside of the Astral are extremely uncommon and largely impotent. Mind Twilight is basically there for symmetry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T12:45:24-08:00","id":1425224,"title":"","content":"I like both Kaiser and Galivet's ideas enough that I think I want to use them together.<br /> <br /> A mastigos dislikes something about himself, obsessively so. He finds himself wanting to be more like another person so he goes into that person's oneiros and spirits away a goetic entity of theirs back to his own astral. Is that an idea that makes sense, even if it's destined to end in tragedy? The person he stole the goetia from would start to experience changes based on its loss, right? And the mastigos would start to be changed in the opposite direction? Would the mastigos's native goetia be hostile to the implant? Would the transplanted goetia be aware of what's happening and what's been done to it?<br /> <br /> I've wanted to run Mage for a long time but this is my first time doing it and I'm trying to make sure my ideas gel with how things work in the system and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26531-sleepwalker","name":"Sleepwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T13:15:43-08:00","id":1425232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1425183#post1425183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Natural&quot; goetia outside of the Astral are extremely uncommon and largely impotent. Mind Twilight is basically there for symmetry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Numina still function and are the only thing goetia can spend their Numina slots on; likewise, Influences may be limited, but a goetia is guaranteed to have an Influence commensurate with its Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T17:17:49-08:00","id":1425412,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to use Time alone to slow down the speed at which a Mystery is contaminated by a mage's Nimbus ? Either on the investigator or examined subject ? Much like Veil of Moments, the idea is to arrest or slow down the speed at which it happens.<br /> <br /> In addition, can Fate apply boons to Focused Mage Sight ? If so what Practice would be required? I would guess it would be treated as any other spellcasting action.<br /> <br /> Lastly, can either Fate or Mind affect a Clash of Wills ? I am trying to figure out what Arcana could help with Focused Sight besides Prime and those seem to be the most likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T18:12:38-08:00","id":1425421,"title":"","content":"I would not permit any magic specifically to prevent Nimbus contamination of a Mystery; it just doesn't make sense to me based on what the mechanics are trying to model. That said,<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> The boon may also affect spellcasting rolls <b>and other powers</b> at the cost of +2 Reach.</div>I have historically taken &quot;and other powers&quot; to include occasions where no spell is cast per se but Gnosis or Arcanum rating appears in a dice pool.<br /> <br /> I don't immediately see how Mind or Prime could help with Clash of Wills. I'd also be nervous about allowing any spells that directly influence Clash of Wills resolution. Like... you might get into an infinitely recursive situation where two spells that both impact Clash of Wills effectiveness have a Clash of Wills with each other. Also Clash of Wills has an important role in handling conflicts between Splats, and being able to influence that mechanic via more spellcasting seems wrong. Like double-dipping. Sorry I can't provide anything more specific than FUD; my knee-jerk &quot;no&quot; is strong here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I would permit homebrew Merits that impact Nimbus contamination and Clash of Wills rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 11-21-2020, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T18:25:04-08:00","id":1425424,"title":"","content":"Oh, another work-around: As a player I have used time travel to Scrutinize a mystery several times in the same Turn (Scrutinize, travel back, Scrutinize, travel back, etc...). This would mitigate nimbus contamination as the Mystery is &quot;fresh&quot; for each Scrutiny role but the character retains the knowledge of the Mystery represented by its reduced Opacity. There's a natural limit to this enforced by Potency spell factors and then Reach limits; the character has to spend at least a turn casting Shifting Sands and so each successive attempt requires traveling back one turn further to arrive at the Mystery in its &quot;fresh&quot; state.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Kind of like in that move Groundhog Day where Bill Murray gets better and better at playing the piano by taking piano lessons during the day he lives over and over and over. For the piano teacher, it's always the first piano lesson she's given Bill, but from Bill's perspective he's seen her hundreds of times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 11-21-2020, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T20:57:06-08:00","id":1425447,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see the confusion. In the Clash of Wills, I was considering only Fate and Mind. It stemmed from thinking about the Gift of Strength's Unchained Facet. It grants the werewolf the ability to break all restraints and bindings. So not only are they able to escape a pocket dimension, they gain rote property on the Clash of Wills. I was trying to figure out how a mage who needed to detain that target would prepare for that. The simplest answers seemed to enhance the effect of Willpower via Mind or apply a boon.<br /> <br /> Regarding Opacity, Prime seemed to focus the bulk of spells that help with Opacity. But in Mage there is never only one way to do anything, so I thought it was an interesting problemsolving exercise to consider how other Paths do it. <br /> <br /> The first solution is to just throw a lot of mana at the problem, but again that returns to Prime.<br /> <br /> Another one is to suspend or increase the time for the Nimbus to bleed out into the Mystery, summon its uncorrupted version from the past or travel to the past.<br /> <br /> The third solution is based on how activating Focused Mage Sight requires directed will, amounts to hallucinating answers and interpreting them. All could be streamlimed or enhanced with Mind.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Fate could make the mage be looking at the right symbol at the best time to gain knowledge.<br /> <br /> I am curious what alternatives there are to Prime when dealing with a high Opacity Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T13:37:23-08:00","id":1425777,"title":"","content":"Is there possible to a spell to counter the effects of attainments? More precisely: a fraying Prime spell could reduce a Mage Armor rating, or spells are not intended to interact with attainments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T13:41:14-08:00","id":1425778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redzone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1425777#post1425777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there possible to a spell to counter the effects of attainments? More precisely: a fraying Prime spell could reduce a Mage Armor rating, or spells are not intended to interact with attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells can interact with Attainments, but not because they are Attainments. If they interact, it's because they interact with the effects of the Attainments. As such a generic counter to Attainments could not work, but a spell which grants a supernatural Armour Piercing quality to a source of damage would definitely work against Mage Armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T03:13:29-08:00","id":1426946,"title":"","content":"Dumb question time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What happens if you cast a spell like Divination with advanced duration? Do you get to ask a new set of questions again at a later time based on your ritual casting interval? Or could you choose to structure the Imago in such a way that you can ask your questions later rather than at the time of casting? Or would it be both, if the duration is long enough (say, a day or a month)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T05:31:28-08:00","id":1426957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1426946#post1426946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What happens if you cast a spell like Divination with advanced duration? Do you get to ask a new set of questions again at a later time based on your ritual casting interval? Or could you choose to structure the Imago in such a way that you can ask your questions later rather than at the time of casting? Or would it be both, if the duration is long enough (say, a day or a month)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at page 113 in the core book, it says <i>&quot;If a spell would logically have an immediate effect, but is cast with advanced duration, the effect recurs at every multiple of the character\u2019s Gnosis-based ritual casting time, until the Duration runs out&quot;</i>. I always ruled the answers to Divination as happening instantly, so you don't need to extend duration just to hear longer answers. In this case specifically, I would say you can ask up to [Potency] questions at any time and you get a refresh on the number available on your Gnosis based interval. So if its one hour and you casted at Potency 3, you can ask all 3 instantly and make the spell &quot;do nothing&quot; for an hour or spread your questions around during that interval or use less questions than the max and get back to 3 every hour. The benefit is that you are able to divine what a target does during that time, even when they are outside of sensory range, which can be a major advantage to any chessmaster type of mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T07:57:50-08:00","id":1428089,"title":"","content":"I need two Beasts and a Promethean to enter a Qliphoth\u2019s Verge togheter with two mages.<br /> Do you think it would be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T08:20:29-08:00","id":1428091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428089#post1428089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need two Beasts and a Promethean to enter a Qliphoth\u2019s Verge togheter with two mages.<br /> Do you think it would be possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the story needs it to happen, then it's possible; more generally, Verges can be accessed by anyone meeting the entry requirements (which could be as simple as &quot;entering the place the Verge exists&quot;).<br /> <br /> [Edit] read up specifically on Qliphothic Verges, getting pulled in requires Paradox to occur, with Sleepers being pulled in by Quiescence. Personally, I'd just hand wave it and say that the Paradox suffered by the Mage pulls the rest of the party in, too. If you intentionally want it to be harder: the Beasts could find a Nasnas and use the Nasnas as an Astral-Abyssal bridge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 12-11-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T08:22:15-08:00","id":1428092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428089#post1428089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need two Beasts and a Promethean to enter a Qliphoth\u2019s Verge togheter with two mages.<br /> Do you think it would be possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>If its intentional, they could have a Space mage use a Weaving on the party so they can only be teleported together or have their Fate tied together. <br /> <br /> Another option is to give the Qlipoth a Dread Power to drag an entire area into Abyss if they complete a ritual. They could have an Abyssal Artifact that lets them do it. <br /> <br /> Lastly, there could be an Abyssal Verge that leads to it. The mages vanish and the others find a &quot;backdoor&quot; in the Verge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T09:42:40-08:00","id":1428184,"title":"","content":"In order to cast Co-Location to overlap places the mage is seeing with those their Familiar is watching, they can Reach for sensory range and spend a mana ? In other words, can the Familiar's senses be used for sympathetic casting or is double Reaching for remote viewing the only way to do it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T10:03:22-08:00","id":1428185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428184#post1428184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to cast Co-Location to overlap places the mage is seeing with those their Familiar is watching, they can Reach for sensory range and spend a mana ? In other words, can the Familiar's senses be used for sympathetic casting or is double Reaching for remote viewing the only way to do it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you describe has nothing to do with Sympathetic Range unless you're targeting the <i>familiar itself</i> at Sympathetic Range. Nothing it sees or interacts with has any inherent sympathetic connection to the familiar, and much less to you. If whatever it sees has a sympathetic connection to you, then it would have that regardless of the presence of your familiar.<br /> Also, don't forget that you also need a sympathetic Yantra when casting at Sympathetic Range, as well as have Potency enough to beat Withstand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T14:10:52-08:00","id":1428204,"title":"","content":"Cool, then remote viewing is the way to go, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T06:11:38-08:00","id":1428336,"title":"","content":"What does the spell Corridors of time send back in the past actually, only the mind of the subject or also his soul?<br /> In other words, if a mage is sent back to a time before his awakening, could he still cast spells and counts as a mage?<br /> Also, the core book states that if he dies during the trip the changes becomes lasting, but i don t understand if the mage would reawaken in a world whitout memories of him or if he simply dies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 12-14-2020, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T09:40:15-08:00","id":1428358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428336#post1428336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the spell Corridors of time send back in the past actually, only the mind of the subject or also his soul?<br /> In other words, if a mage is sent back to a time before his awakening, could he still cast spells and counts as a mage?<br /> Also, the core book states that if he dies during the trip the changes becomes lasting, but i don t understand if the mage would reawaken in a world whitout memories of him or if he simply dies</div> </div> </div> </div>In page 185 of the core book, under &quot;The Past can be Rewritten&quot;, it suggests that the mage would return to a present that doesn't know them, even if they died. In this way, their Time magic defies causality and resolves the temporal paradox.<br /> <br /> Because Unmaking can do everything Patterning can do and more, it means that based on Rewrite History, that the caster can choose to send either to the past. The main restriction is that they cannot make this choice for those born to their powers, such as werewolves or spirits. So they can choose to wield magic when they would have been Sleepers.<br /> <br /> What happens if the moment they are in overlaps with their time of Awakening and they aren't in the right circumstances? Probably nothing to them, since an Awakening is an act of Imperium done by one of the mightiest Talismans in existence. Some random Traveler's meddling in Time magic probably stands no chance of messing with a sealed rite. So they likely &quot;don't experience it&quot; because the Watchtower already has their signature.<br /> <br /> It would, however, likely create a big domino effect on their history. &quot;No Awakening&quot; means no alert sound to nearby mages, leading to no Order finding them, locating them later or someone/something else getting to them first. It could also lead to a very confused past version trying to solve this Mystery.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if they somehow figure out how to experience their Awakening again in the past, but this time with the answers, then it likely leads to one direction: Bad Things happen. Very, very, VERY Bad Things. Exarchial interference, archmage meddling, Harrowing or worse. Then their biggest concern then would be fixing it somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-14-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:07:49-08:00","id":1428372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428336#post1428336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the spell Corridors of time send back in the past actually, only the mind of the subject or also his soul?<br /> In other words, if a mage is sent back to a time before his awakening, could he still cast spells and counts as a mage?<br /> Also, the core book states that if he dies during the trip the changes becomes lasting, but i don t understand if the mage would reawaken in a world whitout memories of him or if he simply dies</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I play it as a flashback where the player controls their historical self as they were at that point in time. The only thing they bring from the future is their knowledge of what choices they wanted to make differently. Thematically, the point of the spell is to make different choices, not overcome obstacles using power or skill you didn't possess at the time.<br /> <br /> I'll also note that sheer dice pool and reach restrictions make it inconvenient to visit a point in time when the subject was vastly different for more than a couple of turns anyway.<br /> <br /> As a general rule I employ the most restrictive interpretation of time travel rules I can. Players tend not to like it when the cabal Acanthus goes on a substantial solo mission to the past to upend large parts of the story that the cabal has built. Nothing ruins a story quite like &quot;Oh, <i>he's</i> behind it all? I time travel back to that scene a few months back where we were all chatting in the pub and murder him.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 12-14-2020, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T06:34:47-08:00","id":1428463,"title":"","content":"One thing I found confusing about the Kitchen Alchemist's writeup is that their first Attainment is Serendipity with the Reach used for skill substitution. However, there would be only one turn for the effect to happen. So does that imply that, since Serendipity is Potency primary, the Reach effects do not require the spell to be active at the time the roll is made in order to work ? The errata for Shifting the Odds suggests that as a general rule they do, but this Attainment would probably not have time to act then. Is Serendipity some kind of special case ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-15-2020, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T08:18:52-08:00","id":1428474,"title":"","content":"The Reach effect for Serendipity is a Lasting consequence of casting the spell. Casting Serendipity with the Reach effect causes the subject to know something about how a skill may come in handy in the future in an unexpected way. Mechanically, that results in the skill substitution whenever that foreseen circumstance arrives. From the in-game perspective of the character, the omen foretells exactly what skills will come in handy and when. However from the player's perspective it's not decided until they want to spend the bonus.<br /> <br /> It's a Knowing spell. To quote a meme, &quot;if you know, you know.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 12-15-2020, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T08:33:29-08:00","id":1428478,"title":"","content":"Is Clash of Wills the best way to resolve Levitate vs. Gravitic Supremacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T08:45:00-08:00","id":1428480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428474#post1428474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Reach effect for Serendipity is a Lasting consequence of casting the spell. Casting Serendipity with the Reach effect causes the subject to know something about how a skill may come in handy in the future in an unexpected way. Mechanically, that results in the skill substitution whenever that foreseen circumstance arrives. From the in-game perspective of the character, the omen foretells exactly what skills will come in handy and when. However from the player's perspective it's not decided until they want to spend the bonus.<br /> <br /> It's a Knowing spell. To quote a meme, &quot;if you know, you know.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool, that makes it a lot clearer, thank you. One more question please. In Signs of Sorcery and Imperial Mysteries it says Emanation Realms are shards of Supernal Truths. So they are attuned to one Supernal Realms, have one key arcana and embody one archtype. Gehinnom's is sin, Tapana's is fire and Mars' is forgotten might. But what constitutes a focus for one ? I am having a bit of trouble groking that.<br /> <br /> For example, lets say you have one themed on mirrors. Its Arcana is Forces, with fractal distortions of space and the shifting laws of physics creating a maze, which in part is due to its connection to Pandemonium. Think the mirror maze from Baten Kaitos for an approximation of the general idea. Its theme is Self Reflection, with the mirrors, scrying windows, portals and the like bringing the self into focus, showing the connections that compose the mirror of the soul and the Realm being especially good for finding pieces that are &quot;missing&quot; or &quot;shattered&quot; from those &quot;mirrors of the self&quot;. Would that be a valid Emanation or is it more in line with the themes of a Verge ? I am having a bit of trouble drawing the line distinguishing them both (part from Emanations being their own infinite dimension).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-15-2020, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T09:12:29-08:00","id":1428482,"title":"","content":"The main things to consider when deciding on Verge vs Emanation:<ul><li>City-sized at maximum, or boundless?</li> <li>Accessibly by walking into it, or only by Thurae or other rare circumstances?</li> <li>Inhabited by (mostly) cryptids, or by supernal entities?</li> <li>Shadow, or no Shadow? Note that this is super important for Spirit mages because Emanations just don't have native spirits. There's no Shadow and they're inhabited by supernal beings.</li> <li>The rules don't mention this, but I personally also rule that Emanations are disconnected from the Underworld and there are no ghosts.</li> </ul>Regarding the last two points, I guess you can say some Emanation has it's own versions of the Shadow and/or Underworld and it's own versions of spirits and ghosts for Spirit and Death magic to work on if thematically appropriate. But I keep those as facets of the Fallen World only. If I want a ghost-themed setting I would just use the Underworld itself rather than an Emanation anyway.<br /> <br /> The narrative purpose of both Verges and Emanations is to enable the ST to have weird settings with fun themes like &quot;Dinosaur World,&quot; &quot;Steampunk City,&quot; etc... Like if as the ST you want something akin to the Shadow or the Underworld but with a different theme and you don't want to have to come up with the whole cosmology of its complex relationship to the Fallen World. So first you design your setting and then you pick whether it's a Verge or Emanation according the above factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 12-15-2020, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T11:30:23-08:00","id":1428495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428478#post1428478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Clash of Wills the best way to resolve Levitate vs. Gravitic Supremacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gravitic Supremacy affects gravity. Levitation ignores gravity. Levitation thus simply ignores the effects of Gravitic Supremacy.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not calling you out specifically, but I think there's a tendency among players to default to Clash of Wills when two supernatural effects are in some opposition rather than exploring other options, and I think that's not a good thing. The default stance should be to resolve the conflict using the rules of those powers, and only use the CoW rules if it's the only option.<br /> For example, a magically sharpened sword vs a magically reinforced suit of armour should really not use the CoW rules just because a power that increases damage comes into conflict with a power that increases armour. You'd naturally resolve it using the rules for how damage and armour interacts. On the other hand, if the sword is enhanced to ignore all armour and the armour is enhanced to resist all attacks (two terrible effects for game balance, but whatever) then you get a conflict that can't be resolved. That's when the CoW rules should come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-15-2020, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T11:36:37-08:00","id":1428496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1428482#post1428482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main things to consider when deciding on Verge vs Emanation:<ul><li>City-sized at maximum, or boundless?</li> <li>Accessibly by walking into it, or only by Thurae or other rare circumstances?</li> <li>Inhabited by (mostly) cryptids, or by supernal entities?</li> <li>Shadow, or no Shadow? Note that this is super important for Spirit mages because Emanations just don't have native spirits. There's no Shadow and they're inhabited by supernal beings.</li> <li>The rules don't mention this, but I personally also rule that Emanations are disconnected from the Underworld and there are no ghosts.</li> </ul>Regarding the last two points, I guess you can say some Emanation has it's own versions of the Shadow and/or Underworld and it's own versions of spirits and ghosts for Spirit and Death magic to work on if thematically appropriate. But I keep those as facets of the Fallen World only. If I want a ghost-themed setting I would just use the Underworld itself rather than an Emanation anyway.<br /> <br /> The narrative purpose of both Verges and Emanations is to enable the ST to have weird settings with fun themes like &amp;quot;Dinosaur World,&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Steampunk City,&amp;quot; etc... Like if as the ST you want something akin to the Shadow or the Underworld but with a different theme and you don't want to have to come up with the whole cosmology of its complex relationship to the Fallen World. So first you design your setting and then you pick whether it's a Verge or Emanation according the above factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking for an area with a Mirror Twilight, accesed via following special steps from the Hall of Mirrors in the Hedge, sending you to an infinite continent of illusion. Think of the continent of Mira from Baten Kaitos, the Mirror Dimension from the Dr Strange movie or games like Antichamber, Manifold Garden or the Stone Temple from Majora's Mask. But guided by a sense of the geometry reflecting the visitor at themselves. <br /> <br /> I think that would be an Emanation, correct ? Its boundless, has its own means of access and special rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T11:55:12-08:00","id":1428497,"title":"","content":"Eh, maybe I missed an important factor: Verges align with a Supernal Realm while Emanations align with a single Arcanum. If what you have in mind is mixing Space (scrying) and Mind (illusions) then it might be a better fit for a Pandemonic Verge. The &quot;real&quot; size of a place that is all about illusions probably doesn't matter; it can seem as big as it needs too (like a Star Trek holodeck).<br /> <br /> And, just because Verges can be accessed from the Fallen World without any special mechanisms doesn't mean that they're easy to find or that there aren't other more certain ways in from more esoteric realms.<br /> <br /> Honestly based on what you describe I don't think it even matters which term you use. Seems like a case where a rose by any name is gonna smell the same way.<br /> <br /> The distinction is a lot more important when e.g. you want to develop rival kingdoms of Paragons with thousands of years of history engaged in complex planet-wide alliances and wars, and you just can't build that setting inside of a Verge. You need Emanations when you want to build a game based on the Mage ruleset but with a radically different and vastly-scoped setting. When you just need an unusual location to visit as part of a typical Mage story then the distinction doesn't matter as much aside from pedantic characters insisting on the use of the proper theroetical term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 12-15-2020, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T08:57:36-08:00","id":1429628,"title":"","content":"Question: Can imperial practices be cast using teamwork bonuses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:16:38-08:00","id":1429681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1429628#post1429628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Can imperial practices be cast using teamwork bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing mechanically would seem to not allow it, but most non-AM's helping would be rolling only gnosis at -3 as they wont have the required Arcana levels.<br /> <br /> However the Pax might not allow it, now i think about. Something about not meddling in lower mages stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:47:36-08:00","id":1429684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1429681#post1429681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However the Pax might not allow it, now i think about. Something about not meddling in lower mages stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be lower mages meddling with Archmaster stuff (as long as the spell isn't for any of the lower mages, that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:50:33-08:00","id":1429685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1429681#post1429681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing mechanically would seem to not allow it, but most non-AM's helping would be rolling only gnosis at -3 as they wont have the required Arcana levels.<br /> <br /> However the Pax might not allow it, now i think about. Something about not meddling in lower mages stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that an archmaster could use ochemata as assistants to avoid violating the pax, or else erase the mages' memory afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T05:20:58-08:00","id":1429930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1429685#post1429685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that an archmaster could use ochemata as assistants to avoid violating the pax, or else erase the mages' memory afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs and Sorcery has this gem <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;They\u2019re often employed as ritual partners,<br /> supervisors for an important project, or guardians for Artifacts<br /> and places of power.&quot; </div> </div> </div> So it seems that is exactly what some AM's use them for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T11:24:41-08:00","id":1430099,"title":"","content":"What happens if a mage uses Perfect Recall on a Mummy, does it help with achieving Sebayt ? Does it require conjunctional Time to be effective ? I am not very familiar with 2ed, but I do remember some fascinating mentions of the Arisen now having a unique, non-linear perception of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T12:06:35-08:00","id":1430104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430099#post1430099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a mage uses Perfect Recall on a Mummy, does it help with achieving Sebayt ? Does it require conjunctional Time to be effective ? I am not very familiar with 2ed, but I do remember some fascinating mentions of the Arisen now having a unique, non-linear perception of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arisen explicitly never possess Eidetic Memory, no-sell any use of Fate or Time besides the Practices of Knowing and Unveiling, and apply Paradox dice equal to the highest of those two Arcana used even within those Practices. (It's not entirely clear whether conjunctional use of those Arcana would be subject to this effect, since the relevant sidebar says &quot;spells from Arcana other than Fate or Time&quot; don't.) Their relationship with time is such that all of their Descents have already happened, but a given interaction with a mummy might mean that a given Descent hasn't happened <i>yet</i> for them, which is mostly relevant because you're asking about their memory.<br /> <br /> Their souls cannot be tampered with due to being made inviolate and marked as the property of the Judges by the Rite of Return. The things they can remember are limited by their Memory rating \u2014 dramatically so, before Memory 7 opens it up from two previous Descents and your job, loved ones, and death in Irem to every Descent and the basics of Iremite knowledge \u2014 and since that's a function of their soul reclaiming bits of itself from the Judges I don't think Awakened magic circumvent that.<br /> <br /> Mummies most relevantly gain Reminisce Beats from uncovering hidden truths of the Nameless Empire and discovering secrets from your past or future Descents; gaining a dot of Memory, doing well in the Trials of Duat, or being exposed to unusual temporal phenomena might grant them the Echoes of Descent Condition, which allows them to temporarily gain insight (and Traits) from future experiences. My understanding of Perfect Recall is that it doesn't obviate the need for you to know what you're trying to remember so much as improve your recollection.<br /> <br /> tl;dr You're not likely to get them to remember stuff they weren't already aware of at some level, though giving them the ability to go over something from a previous Descent to notice an important detail might facilitate their attempts to regain Memory, which in turn is liable to prompt a Descent roll if they're actually gaining a dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T12:32:42-08:00","id":1430113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430104#post1430104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arisen explicitly never possess Eidetic Memory, no-sell any use of Fate or Time besides the Practices of Knowing and Unveiling, and apply Paradox dice equal to the highest of those two Arcana used even within those Practices. (It's not entirely clear whether conjunctional use of those Arcana would be subject to this effect, since the relevant sidebar says &quot;spells from Arcana other than Fate or Time&quot; don't.) Their relationship with time is such that all of their Descents have already happened, but a given interaction with a mummy might mean that a given Descent hasn't happened <i>yet</i> for them, which is mostly relevant because you're asking about their memory.<br /> <br /> Their souls cannot be tampered with due to being made inviolate and marked as the property of the Judges by the Rite of Return. The things they can remember are limited by their Memory rating \u2014 dramatically so, before Memory 7 opens it up from two previous Descents and your job, loved ones, and death in Irem to every Descent and the basics of Iremite knowledge \u2014 and since that's a function of their soul reclaiming bits of itself from the Judges I don't think Awakened magic circumvent that.<br /> <br /> Mummies most relevantly gain Reminisce Beats from uncovering hidden truths of the Nameless Empire and discovering secrets from your past or future Descents; gaining a dot of Memory, doing well in the Trials of Duat, or being exposed to unusual temporal phenomena might grant them the Echoes of Descent Condition, which allows them to temporarily gain insight (and Traits) from future experiences. My understanding of Perfect Recall is that it doesn't obviate the need for you to know what you're trying to remember so much as improve your recollection.<br /> <br /> tl;dr You're not likely to get them to remember stuff they weren't already aware of at some level, though giving them the ability to go over something from a previous Descent to notice an important detail might facilitate their attempts to regain Memory, which in turn is liable to prompt a Descent roll if they're actually gaining a dot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it means an Acanthus would have an especially tough time against them, since the most they could do is understand the mummy at some rudimentary level. Its pretty disappointing that they no sell both major Arcana of the Path almost entirely, Geists shut down a lot of things a Moros can do, but not to such an extreme degree. Hexes, oath, prophecies, even attack spells, all of them just made irrelevant. Even if you do the only thing allowed, you get a major mechanical punishment for doing it, so its a Mystery they shouldn't even try to solve ? That is an odd choice, its a strong mechanical incentive towards non-interaction. If the cabal finds an Arisen, it means the Acanthus will have their hands tied in just about everything that requires direct action. Is that from Contagion, the 2ed core book or from some other reference ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-27-2020, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T13:35:51-08:00","id":1430124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430113#post1430113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it means an Acanthus would have an especially tough time against them, since the most they could do is understand the mummy at some rudimentary level. Its pretty disappointing that they no sell both major Arcana of the Path almost entirely, Geists shut down a lot of things a Moros can do, but not to such an extreme degree. Hexes, oath, prophecies, even attack spells, all of them just made irrelevant. Even if you do the only thing allowed, you get a major mechanical punishment for doing it, so its a Mystery they shouldn't even try to solve ? That is an odd choice, its a strong mechanical incentive towards non-interaction. If the cabal finds an Arisen, it means the Acanthus will have their hands tied in just about everything that requires direct action.</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate what I said the last time this came up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1376899#post1376899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To reframe the things Tessie's already brought up, &quot;here's some Paradox&quot; <i>is</i> the magic having unpredictable consequences.<br /> <br /> Attempting to interfere with a mummy's Name at more than a cursory level doesn't work, and attempting to interact with it magically at all draws the influence of alien demon-gods made of pain and suffering just the same as if you'd exposed your Astral self to the raw currents of the world-soul and experienced a dreaming death \u2014 &quot;something powerful's got its tendrils in your magic, and that's represented with the same system as a normal Paradox&quot; goes clear back to 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further: There's a <i>big fucking difference</i> between casting spells on something and &quot;solving&quot; its Mysteries. (Mysteries do not work that way. You study them and gain information about them, chiefly through the universal tool the Awakened template hands you that doesn't risk Paradox at all.)<br /> <br /> Attempting to interfere with the history and destiny of a timeless creature who not only exists at the center of calm spots in an otherwise riotous expanse of temporal weirdness, but is also the personal property of a god, <i>should</i> prompt a kick in the face from anyone who hasn't got a beachhead in Heaven to yank on.<br /> <br /> You can still study the phenomenon, but a volatile paradox-monster running on the stolen power of manifest existence \u2014 which crossover material has seen the Awakened compare to <i>handling raw plutonium barehanded</i> \u2014 is not the sort of thing to expect to sit still. The Hedge can make your Mage Sight lie to you, why would a less hands-off piece of fateful god-magic be kinder?<br /> <br /> Besides which: The Acanthus have always gotten along just fine by being indirect or granting themselves boons and bonuses, which are not subject to the limitations of direct casting on an external target with the Arisen's level of protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that from Contagion, the 2ed core book or from some other reference ? </div> </div> </div>Mummy 2e Core from the Kickstarter draft. To my knowledge the Contagion material covering crossover interactions does not yet exist in a public-facing form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-27-2020, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T17:30:12-08:00","id":1430289,"title":"","content":"How would legacy creation look like in game by a character? Not at character creation, but a midgame character creating their own legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T19:51:56-08:00","id":1430297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430289#post1430289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would legacy creation look like in-game by a character? Not at character creation, but a midgame character creating their own legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the character, the legacy? Since each legacy requires indoctrination (even self-created ones) each ritual/idea or method to create one is different. There are probably many self created legacies that are very very similar created in different parts of the world but have different methods of joining it.<br /> <br /> The text is very wooly on how long it takes etc so just decide for yourself for your campaign, it should require some effort but need not be super hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T20:41:18-08:00","id":1430306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430289#post1430289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would legacy creation look like in game by a character? Not at character creation, but a midgame character creating their own legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would play out as the creator becoming the living embodiment of something that is meaningful to them. It requires them to understand and engrave its symbols into their soul.<br /> <br /> They must explore its Mysteries, codifying their philosophy for engaging with them. They create spells that embody this ethos, using them often enough to become Praxis, refining them with almost instinctual ease. In time they master these Imagos to the level where they are inscribed into the soul and shape it, creating Attainments that become incorporated into their Gnosis. Their habits become oblations. The tools, scenarios and willful complications they employ (such as the Eleventh Question gaining power from debilitating drugs) become yantras.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, beyond proactively exploring the Legacy's theme on the mundane and supernatural levels, there needs to be a moment of revelation. A eureka moment, a personal moment of satori regarding its Mystery. This will help symbolically codify their initiation. Moments of similar significance might even aid in figuring out or finalizing the creation of new Attainments.<br /> <br /> Then they keep learning, refining their methods, seeking kindred spirits and building the infrastructure to support it. By the time they reach the third Attainment, they can start teaching others, leveraging the infrastructure they created to start building the Organization (traditions, habits, hierarchy, events, etc) and trying to draw new recruits. This is why a cabal where everyone created a Legacy would be seen as a legendary feat, creating even one requires commitment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-29-2020, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:33:13-08:00","id":1430846,"title":"","content":"The spell Ectoplasm (Death 2) says:<br /> <br /> Ectoplasm (Death \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Expression, Academics<br /> The mage can create ectoplasm (see Ectoplasmic Shaping, above) from one of his own orifices, or the orifice of a corpse \u2014 normally the nose or mouth, but sometimes the tear ducts or ears. The mage can shape the ectoplasm into any shape he wish-es. The ectoplasm retains its shape for the Duration of the spell. <br /> <br /> The way it's written suggests to me the plasm loses it's molded shape at the end of duration, but doesn't cease to exist, impling once created, it is just a sub product of the spell, not dependant on the spell itself.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to get at is: can my Sin-Eater character's Moros friend fill an entire aquarium with plasm so she can just drink and fill other vials from the thing whenever she wants and have essentially unlimited Plasm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T09:47:38-08:00","id":1430880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1313922-plasm-vs-ectoplasm?p=1314040#post1314040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're the same thing. Mage was written when Geist 2e was still a glint in Travis' eye, but yeah - the goop Death spells can make is the goop Bound can eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct, Moros can be incredibly useful allies for the Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T10:45:22-08:00","id":1430889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430846#post1430846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell Ectoplasm (Death 2) says:<br /> <br /> Ectoplasm (Death \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Expression, Academics<br /> The mage can create ectoplasm (see Ectoplasmic Shaping, above) from one of his own orifices, or the orifice of a corpse \u2014 normally the nose or mouth, but sometimes the tear ducts or ears. The mage can shape the ectoplasm into any shape he wish-es. The ectoplasm retains its shape for the Duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> The way it's written suggests to me the plasm loses it's molded shape at the end of duration, but doesn't cease to exist, impling once created, it is just a sub product of the spell, not dependant on the spell itself.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to get at is: can my Sin-Eater character's Moros friend fill an entire aquarium with plasm so she can just drink and fill other vials from the thing whenever she wants and have essentially unlimited Plasm?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Plasm is technically lasting because the spell draws out/generates Plasm from a separate source (rather than just creating it or transforming something into Plasm), note that Plasm itself doesn't last that long. Any unused/unconsumed Plasm dissipates at the end of the scene. The spell doesn't mention this rule, but it's included in Geist 2e which should be considered more authorative regarding the properties of Plasm in a Mage/Geist crossover game.<br /> Also note that having an aquarium filled with Plasm is one hell of an Open invitation (hehe) for any and all ghosts who might pass by the location of said aquarium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T01:19:45-08:00","id":1430962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430889#post1430889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the Plasm is technically lasting because the spell draws out/generates Plasm from a separate source (rather than just creating it or transforming something into Plasm), note that Plasm itself doesn't last that long. Any unused/unconsumed Plasm dissipates at the end of the scene. The spell doesn't mention this rule, but it's included in Geist 2e which should be considered more authorative regarding the properties of Plasm in a Mage/Geist crossover game.<br /> Also note that having an aquarium filled with Plasm is one hell of an Open invitation (hehe) for any and all ghosts who might pass by the location of said aquarium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hadn't caught that part. I'd seen it mentioned in some instances, like the Plasm generated from Manifestations which have ended, but I didn't know it was a general thing. I guess it kind of makes sense, ~as sad as I am for my aquarium~. Although I think I could convince my st to allow something like an area spell in which Plasm doesn't evaporate. <br /> <br /> About the Open Condition thing, yeah, I'm very aware of that hahahahaah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T09:48:20-08:00","id":1431015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1430962#post1430962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, hadn't caught that part. I'd seen it mentioned in some instances, like the Plasm generated from Manifestations which have ended, but I didn't know it was a general thing. I guess it kind of makes sense, ~as sad as I am for my aquarium~. Although I think I could convince my st to allow something like an area spell in which Plasm doesn't evaporate.<br /> <br /> About the Open Condition thing, yeah, I'm very aware of that hahahahaah</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I swear Mr Sentinel, this is only to study the marine thanatology of the Underworld. That walking ghost amplifier that is a breach of the Veil waiting to happen is just an unexpected coincidence&quot;<br /> <br /> A Shielding of entropy should do it, or a ruling to prevent it from dissolving. Although you can just use a Fraying to make the ectoplasm simply not work for Manifestations, a Shielding can prevent it from being harnessed by full ghosts (so only Geists can use them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-04-2021, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T20:20:23-08:00","id":1431248,"title":"","content":"In IM, it says that other beings with 6+ attributes may participate in Imperium, but spirits may not. Why are spirits excluded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T05:58:46-08:00","id":1431281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431248#post1431248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In IM, it says that other beings with 6+ attributes may participate in Imperium, but spirits may not. Why are spirits excluded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason magical automata can't participate: they're the sum of their parts and don't strictly possess free will, in specific contrast to Spirit-based Supernal beings and characters with souls, who are the main participants in Imperium.<br /> <br /> More prosaically, it prevents an archmage from simply offloading the risks of Imperium onto a god they built to take the fall if it screws up; Rank 6+ and Influence 6+ are not quite the same as Gnosis 6+ and a supernatural power rated at 6+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T13:13:40-08:00","id":1431313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431248#post1431248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In IM, it says that other beings with 6+ attributes may participate in Imperium, but spirits may not. Why are spirits excluded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point out where it says that? Are you confusing the imperium for the Pax Arcana maybe? Pretty sure Rank 6+ spirits participate in the Pax Arcana and have equivalent powers to the imperial practices.<br /> <br /> If you mean the chapter called Inperium then that's about Archmaster's games to change the cosmos so its natural that spirits don't get to play in it, not being archmasters and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-06-2021, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T13:42:11-08:00","id":1431319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431313#post1431313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point out where it says that? Are you confusing the imperium for the Pax Arcana maybe? Pretty sure Rank 6+ spirits participate in the Pax Arcana and have equivalent powers to the imperial practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Province of Gods and Sages,&quot; pp75-6:<br /> <br /> &quot;At the Storyteller's discretion, other beings may also play at Imperium if they possess a supernatural power equivalent to Gnosis 6 or higher, a supernatural power rated at six dots or higher, and free will. Spirits and magical automata may not participate. The candidate must also possess the ability to directly influence the Supernal Realms, but might possess a special nature that allows them to do this from afar.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T16:55:35-08:00","id":1431337,"title":"","content":"Page 90 of Signs of Sorcery suggests that a mage can cast on a soul stone in the same was as a Familiar, using the remote viewing factor. Does that mean that so long as the sympathetic level is Connected, it can be used for that range factor ? For example a lock of hair, a fingernail or Daimonomikon of a Legacy Pedagogue","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T17:46:27-08:00","id":1431341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431337#post1431337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 90 of Signs of Sorcery suggests that a mage can cast on a soul stone in the same was as a Familiar, using the remote viewing factor. Does that mean that so long as the sympathetic level is Connected, it can be used for that range factor ? For example a lock of hair, a fingernail or Daimonomikon of a Legacy Pedagogue</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's limited to using a Familiar or Soul Stone rather than being a broad application of Connected Sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T18:36:22-08:00","id":1431343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431341#post1431341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's limited to using a Familiar or Soul Stone rather than being a broad application of Connected Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I initially thought as well, but both are used as examples of connected sympathy and the core book describes that level as &quot;The two subjects are metaphysically one&quot;. So technically you are viewing a subject remotely by seeing a part of it. The main conveniences Space mages enjoy are that they can use sympathetic casting to avoid the extra Reach and aren't exclusively limited to connected sympathy, at the disadvantage of having to deal with Withstands, wards and the mana cost. Signs of Sorcery is worded in such a way that made me wonder if that was the case.<br /> <br /> On a side question, is anything seen with the 2 Reach effect of The Outward and Inward Eye considered to be in sensory range, such as targets hiding somewhere past a scrying window ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-06-2021, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T03:32:30-08:00","id":1431379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431343#post1431343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is what I initially thought as well, but both are used as examples of connected sympathy and the core book describes that level as &quot;The two subjects are metaphysically one&quot;. So technically you are viewing a subject remotely by seeing a part of it. The main conveniences Space mages enjoy are that they can use sympathetic casting to avoid the extra Reach and aren't exclusively limited to connected sympathy, at the disadvantage of having to deal with Withstands, wards and the mana cost. Signs of Sorcery is worded in such a way that made me wonder if that was the case.<br /> <br /> On a side question, is anything seen with the 2 Reach effect of The Outward and Inward Eye considered to be in sensory range, such as targets hiding somewhere past a scrying window ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Prefer to just think that that spell is a mistake and should at least say it requires Space 2's attainment. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the mage has a Connected link to her own soul stone, this spell doesn\u2019t require sympathetic range to cast. </div> </div> </div> Is this statement wrong? ( i mean the withstand is 0 but that doesn't mean the attainment is not needed.) Since when has having a connected link to something mean you don't require sympathetic range (or a link). if Web weaving spell allows you to raise a connection to connected (it only says up to strong though, thank god) then one could improve your connection then cast any other spell without sympathetic range...<br /> <br /> It does start by saying &quot;this spell&quot; so it only applies to this spell rightly, but it just struck me as a aberration when i read it the first time. As not requiring space 2's attainment when casting on a soulstone would open up a huge can of worms (remote Aoe Spell soulstone grenades ahoy)<br /> <br /> As for OIEye then things through a portal would still count as remote viewing, because while its in realtime its still using a<br /> <i>&quot;magic scrying window, requires an additional Reach.</i>&quot; and viewing it through a scrying window breaks the sense from being directly viewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-08-2021, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T08:44:28-08:00","id":1431402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431343#post1431343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is what I initially thought as well, but both are used as examples of connected sympathy and the core book describes that level as &quot;The two subjects are metaphysically one&quot;. So technically you are viewing a subject remotely by seeing a part of it. The main conveniences Space mages enjoy are that they can use sympathetic casting to avoid the extra Reach and aren't exclusively limited to connected sympathy, at the disadvantage of having to deal with Withstands, wards and the mana cost. Signs of Sorcery is worded in such a way that made me wonder if that was the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just looked at the Sympathy table in the 2e core book.<br /> <br /> Only Soul Stones and familiars are listed as examples of Connected sympathy, bodily samples are Strong sympathy. Based on that, I'd say a Daimonomikon authored by a Legacy Pedagogue would offer the same benefits re: remote spellcasting as a Soul Stone or familiar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a side question, is anything seen with the 2 Reach effect of The Outward and Inward Eye considered to be in sensory range, such as targets hiding somewhere past a scrying window ? </div> </div> </div>From the spell <i>Scrying</i>: &quot;Casting spells on subjects the mage can see through the window counts as viewing them remotely.&quot;<br /> <br /> I see no reason that would change. Ergo, casting on someone through a Scrying Window would require 1 reach for Sensory Range and 1 reach for Remote Viewing, for a total of 2 Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 01-07-2021, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T02:27:30-08:00","id":1431454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431402#post1431402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just looked at the Sympathy table in the 2e core book.<br /> <br /> Only Soul Stones and familiars are listed as examples of Connected sympathy, bodily samples are Strong sympathy. Based on that, I'd say a Daimonomikon authored by a Legacy Pedagogue would offer the same benefits re remote spellcasting as a Soul Stone or familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's limited to using a Familiar or Soul Stone rather than being a broad application of Connected Sympathy. </div> </div> </div><br /> So the familiar condition does also mention this benefit. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (casting magic through a Familiar requires a Reach for remote viewing, but does not require the Sympathetic Range Attainment) </div> </div> </div>However, nowhere in the core book can I find where it gives this benefit to soulstones (or the connected level of sympathy) and I'm happy to just let only the &quot;Soul Window&quot; spell from Sos gain this benefit instead of every spell though a soulstone as a broad application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-08-2021, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T02:53:23-08:00","id":1431456,"title":"","content":"The thing about Familiars is that you can cast on things you view remotely through them. The fact that you are viewing them remotely is what allows you to do so; there's no reason you should be able to cast remotely on the familiar before you've chosen to share senses (but the fact that it's reflexive makes it a moot point, practically speaking).<br /> But even if we were to assume that you always can do that because the Familiar has Connected Sympathy, the advantage is still not the same as that stated in Soul Windows because you still need to use a Reach for remote viewing. The other difference is that you can cast <i>through</i> your Familiar while Soul Windows only states you can cast on the soulstone itself.<br /> <br /> Soul Windows references a rule that doesn't exist. The best thing to do is to either consider it a feature of that particular spell alone, or just ignoring it because it's not an actual rule. I'm personally leaning heavily towards the latter because I very much prefer consistency in how the rules of magic are applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T10:14:28-08:00","id":1431474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431454#post1431454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So the familiar condition does also mention this benefit.<br /> <br /> However, nowhere in the core book can I find where it gives this benefit to soulstones (or the connected level of sympathy) and I'm happy to just let only the &quot;Soul Window&quot; spell from Sos gain this benefit instead of every spell though a soulstone as a broad application.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the <i>Soul Window</i> spell:<br /> <br /> &quot;Since the mage has a Connected link to her own<br /> soul stone, this spell doesn\u2019t require sympathetic range to cast.&quot;<br /> <br /> Connected Sympathy allows you to cast on the thing with which you have Connected Sympathy without the Sympathetic Range Attainment. Viewing a thing remotely and in real time allows you to cast Remotely by spending two Reach total (one for Sensory Range, and an additional for Remote) without having the Sympathetic Range Attainment.<br /> <br /> A Familiar has both Connected Sympathy <i>and</i> the ability to be sensed through, by default. A Soul Stone has Connected Sympathy by default, but no method of sensing through unless you cast <i>Soul Window</i>. Ergo, a Legacy Pedagogue would be able to cast any spell on a Daimonomikon they scribed without the Sympathetic Range Attainment, but would have to cast a spell similar to <i>Soul Window</i> to sense through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T10:34:39-08:00","id":1431476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431474#post1431474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Connected Sympathy allows you to cast on the thing with which you have Connected Sympathy without the Sympathetic Range Attainment..</div> </div> </div> </div>Cant find any reference to this anywhere. Familiar and &quot;Soul windows&quot; mention it and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T10:55:03-08:00","id":1431479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431476#post1431476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cant find any reference to this anywhere. Familiar and &quot;Soul windows&quot; mention it and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is <i>Soul Window</i> not rules text? The sentence is pretty clear that the reason the Sympathetic Range Attainment isn't required is due to the Connected Sympathy property.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that there just aren't that many ways to have Connected Sympathy: Mage and their familiar, Mage and their soul stone(s), and Legacy Pedagogue and Daimonomikon are the only &quot;naturally&quot; occurring examples. The only other way is via Space 5's <i>Create Sympathy.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T12:11:12-08:00","id":1431486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431479#post1431479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is <i>Soul Window</i> not rules text? The sentence is pretty clear that the reason the Sympathetic Range Attainment isn't required is due to the Connected Sympathy property.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a rule is described within a specific spell, it's either specific to that spell or a reminder of a general rule. The reason given for the rule is not specific to the spell and there exists no such general rule for it to act as a reminder of, so it's a very dubious ruling which I would not accept at face value.<br /> My guess is that the writer confused the rule that Connected Sympathy isn't Withstood with the idea that it doesn't require Sympathetic Range at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T09:36:03-08:00","id":1431584,"title":"","content":"Hello all. I was wondering, how would one kill an archmage? When their body is destroyed, they just reappear inside their golden road since they are meditating out of it. Would one have to attack the golden road itself? Or breach the golden road and attack the archmage in that realm? This brings up another question, what is the difference between an archmage and their road?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T11:34:37-08:00","id":1431595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431584#post1431584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all. I was wondering, how would one kill an archmage? When their body is destroyed, they just reappear inside their golden road since they are meditating out of it. Would one have to attack the golden road itself? Or breach the golden road and attack the archmage in that realm? This brings up another question, what is the difference between an archmage and their road?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can totally kill an archmage. Their ability to instantly (and loudly) return to their Road from outside of it makes the process difficult even before accounting for any spells and superhuman Traits they have, but their Health and damage to it is real. The Road is just the home dimension of the archmage that forged it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T16:46:21-08:00","id":1431628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431595#post1431595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can totally kill an archmage. Their ability to instantly (and loudly) return to their Road from outside of it makes the process difficult even before accounting for any spells and superhuman Traits they have, but their Health and damage to it is real. The Road is just the home dimension of the archmage that forged it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their health and damage are real until they excise them and then they might not be.<br /> <br /> Im unsure if in 2e its now implied that archmages project some form of other body outside their golden road instead of leaving physically but either way catching one unawares outside its golden road is going to be tough so the best bet is to try to kill them inside their golden road with all the problems that might involve (getting there, fighting defenders + the AM itself). And after all, that if they have excised themselves so that they don't die when their health boxes say they should...then your shit out of luck.<br /> <br /> So yes you can kill a AM until you cant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-09-2021, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T16:50:09-08:00","id":1431631,"title":"","content":"As Tessie and i have said a few times now, it says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Since the mage has a Connected link to her own<br /> soul stone,<b> this spell</b> doesn\u2019t require sympathetic range to cast.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The bolded &quot;this spell&quot; part is what we are talking about, personally I'm fine with soul window on its own allowing this. I'm not fine with allowing any spell to ignore sympathetic range because of a connected connection. Being able to cast an area scale Celestial Fire spell on your soulstone and everything in its range without space 2's attainment just because it is your soulstone is not ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-09-2021, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T00:02:19-08:00","id":1431658,"title":"","content":"(never mind, not worth it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 01-10-2021, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T06:05:14-08:00","id":1431679,"title":"","content":"That is not the point I was making.<br /> The &quot;this spell&quot; phrasing does mean the effect applies to this spell (though necessarily exclusively), but the reason given is phrased as a general rule (or, as is more appropriate for individual spells, a reminder for a general rule).<br /> &quot;Since the mage has a Connected link to her own soul stone,[..]&quot; outright states that having Connected Sympathy is the reason this spell doesn't require Sympathetic Range. That means anything else the mage has Connected Sympathy with should be treated the same, or it would demonstrably <b>not</b> be the reason for why Soul Windows ignores Sympathetic Range.<br /> <br /> Given that general rules should never be given in spells, and the fact that spells cast on subjects with Connected Sympathy aren't Withstood, I think the most likely explanation is that it's supposed to be a reminder text rather than a newly introduced rule but that the writer mixed up Connected Sympathy spells not being Withstood with the mistaken notion that they don't require Sympathetic Range at all, meaning it's a reminder text for a rule that doesn't exist.<br /> Thus I heavily recommend ignoring that sentence outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:12:53-08:00","id":1431714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431679#post1431679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not the point I was making.<br /> The &quot;this spell&quot; phrasing does mean the effect applies to this spell (though necessarily exclusively), but the reason given is phrased as a general rule (or, as is more appropriate for individual spells, a reminder for a general rule).<br /> &quot;Since the mage has a Connected link to her own soul stone,[..]&quot; outright states that having Connected Sympathy is the reason this spell doesn't require Sympathetic Range. That means anything else the mage has Connected Sympathy with should be treated the same, or it would demonstrably <b>not</b> be the reason for why Soul Windows ignores Sympathetic Range.<br /> <br /> Given that general rules should never be given in spells, and the fact that spells cast on subjects with Connected Sympathy aren't Withstood, I think the most likely explanation is that it's supposed to be a reminder text rather than a newly introduced rule but that the writer mixed up Connected Sympathy spells not being Withstood with the mistaken notion that they don't require Sympathetic Range at all, meaning it's a reminder text for a rule that doesn't exist.<br /> Thus I heavily recommend ignoring that sentence outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty compelling argument.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I don't think it breaks anything to allow non-Sympathetic Casting on things with Connected Sympathy since there's only three.<br /> <br /> I'll probably just see if it ever comes up in my game before I even make a ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T19:43:23-08:00","id":1431782,"title":"","content":"Another Geist (and Vampire, for that matter) and Mage crossover related question, this one might not be too simple, but here it goes:<br /> <br /> What would you do for buf/heal/other spells that would usually relate to Life (Knit, Mend, the attributes buf one I forgot the name of etc.) on Geists and Vampires? <br /> <br /> If I were the st in the game that made me prompt that question, I'd probably require solving a Mystery for each type of supernatural which isn't obviously targeted by such spells, because I like the idea of using Mysteries for that.<br /> <br /> But I ask more as the concrete nature of the problem. That is: is a Sin-Eater &quot;alive enough&quot; to be targeted by Life? Is it &quot;dead enough&quot; to be targeted by Death?<br /> <br /> The concrete arguments I have for Sin-Eaters being targeted for death is, well, they died. They are the product of a complicated (dare I say ~mysterious~) Manifestation from an undead being tainted by the Underworld. A lot of Death here. <br /> <br /> Arguments against it are: their organs, as far as I understand, work just fine. Their whole physiology really looks to be pretty much that of &quot;a living person&quot; when not using Plasm.<br /> <br /> Vampires, on the other hand, are dead bodies preserved and moving due to their shenanigans. Only when they use Vitae do their organs &quot;come alive&quot;.<br /> <br /> So one could argue even though their souls are dead in both cases, a Sin-Eaters body is technically alive most of the time (with a few things, like the dead condition, making it temporarily dead again), whereas a vampires body is dead most of the time, only coming technically alive when using Vitae.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Death could be used to affect vampires not under the effects of Vitae for this purpose, while Life could affect Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't remember much from &quot;life energy&quot; as a concept in the game lines, but I assume it has everything to do with if Death or Life could be used to affect something is such ways. I'm asking here mostly to see if anyone could remember anything about it/has ever dealt with the same questions.<br /> <br /> Edit: in fact, same goes for Prometheans, even adding Matter to the conundrum in the case of the Unfleshed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","user":"Andrew Kaninchen","date":". 01-10-2021, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T21:50:08-08:00","id":1431788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431782#post1431782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Geist (and Vampire, for that matter) and Mage crossover related question, this one might not be too simple, but here it goes:<br /> <br /> What would you do for buf/heal/other spells that would usually relate to Life (Knit, Mend, the attributes buf one I forgot the name of etc.) on Geists and Vampires?<br /> <br /> If I were the st in the game that made me prompt that question, I'd probably require solving a Mystery for each type of supernatural which isn't obviously targeted by such spells, because I like the idea of using Mysteries for that.<br /> <br /> But I ask more as the concrete nature of the problem. That is: is a Sin-Eater &quot;alive enough&quot; to be targeted by Life? Is it &quot;dead enough&quot; to be targeted by Death?<br /> <br /> The concrete arguments I have for Sin-Eaters being targeted for death is, well, they died. They are the product of a complicated (dare I say ~mysterious~) Manifestation from an undead being tainted by the Underworld. A lot of Death here.<br /> <br /> Arguments against it are: their organs, as far as I understand, work just fine. Their whole physiology really looks to be pretty much that of &quot;a living person&quot; when not using Plasm.<br /> <br /> Vampires, on the other hand, are dead bodies preserved and moving due to their shenanigans. Only when they use Vitae do their organs &quot;come alive&quot;.<br /> <br /> So one could argue even though their souls are dead in both cases, a Sin-Eaters body is technically alive most of the time (with a few things, like the dead condition, making it temporarily dead again), whereas a vampires body is dead most of the time, only coming technically alive when using Vitae.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Death could be used to affect vampires not under the effects of Vitae for this purpose, while Life could affect Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't remember much from &quot;life energy&quot; as a concept in the game lines, but I assume it has everything to do with if Death or Life could be used to affect something is such ways. I'm asking here mostly to see if anyone could remember anything about it/has ever dealt with the same questions.<br /> <br /> Edit: in fact, same goes for Prometheans, even adding Matter to the conundrum in the case of the Unfleshed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say vampires become alive when using vitae, they mimic being alive but are still dead. Therefore under the purview of death instead of life. Any life effect requires death instead.<br /> <br /> Arnt sin eaters in 2e counted as living beings melded with a geist (yes they died but the geist brought them back to life) instead of 1e? If that's the case then Life should effect their body normally, maybe needing clashes vs anything the geist is doing to it also. If a mage wanted to mess with the geist separately then that would probably only require death The way i see it is that they are normal living people with extra abilities provided by the geist but still count enough for the Life Arcana.<br /> <br /> I think Prime is usually the Arcana that gets mapped to Prometheans a lot? But then you can heal them using Forces Electricity...(not read enough of 2e to know or care about Prometheans in 2e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T22:13:32-08:00","id":1431793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431788#post1431788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arnt sin eaters in 2e counted as living beings melded with a geist (yes they died but the geist brought them back to life) instead of 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bound are metaphysically dead, despite what their biological processes would have you believe \u2014 their remembrance of a ghost grants no Essence, and one of the first things the game tells you in the &quot;Truth and Lies&quot; sidebar at the front of the book is &quot;magic that specifically affects the living does not work on them[.]&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T23:48:39-08:00","id":1431800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431793#post1431793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bound are metaphysically dead, despite what their biological processes would have you believe \u2014 their remembrance of a ghost grants no Essence, and one of the first things the game tells you in the &quot;Truth and Lies&quot; sidebar at the front of the book is &quot;magic that specifically affects the living does not work on them[.]&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How does using life on a werewolf in human form work? (cba checking, Can you only use spirit on all Werewolves in any form or need both life/spirit or only spirit? Form probably shouldn't matter as they are living in all forms too?) I'm sure it's been thrashed out and would apply the same to Sineaters if they also count as a hybrid thingy.<br /> <br /> In the same way mind can cross over various things by proxy of them having a mind, i think Life can too, Werewolves are living so life should work on them, Sineaters are too, but then sineaters also being deathly means they get shafted by death too and werewolves with spirit? Meh good. Needing to add +2 spirit or +2 death may work too. I don't think there's any hard rules (until maybe contegion books) so decide for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-11-2021, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T02:41:28-08:00","id":1431808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431782#post1431782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Geist (and Vampire, for that matter) and Mage crossover related question, this one might not be too simple, but here it goes:</div> </div> </div> </div>In general:<br /> Geists are basically just ghosts in 2e. (In 1e I believe they were kinda ghost/spirit hybrids.)<br /> <br /> The Bound (aka Sin-Eaters) are metaphysically dead, but have fully functional biological bodies. The Life Arcanum governs both the concept of being alive and biology in general. As such, Life spells should work as long as they only relate to the body of the Bound rather than any higher concepts of &quot;life&quot;.<br /> For example: You can cast Knit to heal a Bound because that's just using the body's natural and still functional ability to heal, but if you cast Web of Life they would not ping because they're not alive.<br /> <br /> Vampires are walking corpses. Life spells generally affect them the same way they'd affect regular corpses. The exception is when the vampire uses Blush of Health to restart some biological functions. Life can interact with biological functions (but not the underlying ability of being able to use Blush of Life).<br /> For example: They would not ping for Web of Life (regardless of whether they use Blush of Life or not) and Knit wouldn't have any effect because they don't have a natural healing process anymore, but you could cast a Life Veiling spell to make them look alive just like how you could cast such a spell on a corpse to make it look alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431800#post1431800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does using life on a werewolf in human form work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are both easier and more difficult to use Life on. They are alive so any higher concept Life spells relating to &quot;life&quot; works on them just fine (the Life Knowing spell above would definitely ping for werewolves), but because they are shapeshifters and regenerators it means you can have trouble affecting their bodies since spells aren't allowed to mess around with other templates' powers.<br /> Whether or not you need to add Spirit to biology-based Life spells depends on how you interpret &quot;where&quot; the spiritual half of werewolves are, and whether it's necessary to interact with that when you wish to interact with their bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T09:32:27-08:00","id":1431842,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12306\" data-vbnamecard=\"12306\">Andrew Kaninchen</a> <br /> Re: Vampires and Sin-Eaters: Death all the way. as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> mentioned, the Bound are metaphysically dead, and that means they're affected by the Death Arcanum and not the Life Arcanum. Most of a Sin-Eater's power set is also Death aligned; conversely, most of the non-physical Disciplines for a Vampire are Mind.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> <br /> Re: Werewolves: Life to affect their physical forms (which are alive); Spirit would interact with Werewolves in a way similar to the way Prime interacts with Mages: it can reveal their Primal Urge, how much Essence they have, what Gifts and Rites they posses, what their Renown is, &amp;c. Could probably also provide 8- or 9-Again on power activation, or even rote-quality on Rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T12:07:50-08:00","id":1431855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431842#post1431842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> Re: Vampires and Sin-Eaters: Death all the way. as <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> mentioned, the Bound are metaphysically dead, and that means they're affected by the Death Arcanum and not the Life Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this ignores that Life works on more stuff than just living beings. It's one of the most limited Arcana in that regard, but any Life spells that doesn't deal with the fact that the subject is alive would work just as fine on a Bound as on a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T12:58:28-08:00","id":1431865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431855#post1431855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this ignores that Life works on more stuff than just living beings. It's one of the most limited Arcana in that regard, but any Life spells that doesn't deal with the fact that the subject is alive would work just as fine on a Bound as on a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>What other than living beings does Life work on? The only not-really-alive things that Life can affect are viruses.<br /> <br /> Are you saying spells like <i>Heighten Senses</i> should work on Sin-Eaters? What about Vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T13:16:37-08:00","id":1431866,"title":"","content":"I already gave an example: Life Veiling on a corpse to make it look alive. Purge Illness doesn't specify how it works, but I'd definitely allow it to affect non-living subject (corpses, foodstuff, etc). A Sheilding spell should definitely be able to prevent the spread of contagious diseases in both living and dead matter, or prevent decomposition based on biological processes. Food is even listed under the purview of Life, and most food tend to be dead long before it's considered food (or at least edible food).<br /> While Life is one of the most focused Arcana (up there with Spirit, poor Thyrsus), it does not necessarily have to be exclusively about the living, just like how Death definitely and demonstrably isn't exclusively about the dead.<br /> <br /> Edit: The name of an Arcanum reflects its themes, but it does not determine what's a valid subject for that Arcanum. No other Arcana works like that. Every spell has to be about Life in some way, but you can do that without a living subject. Compare to Space which is rarelt cast on an actual physical space rather than on a subject like an individual or an object. The nature of Life as an Arcanum makes spells on non-living subjects extremely rare, but that is no reason to believe it's a hard rule rather than a common consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-11-2021, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T13:38:43-08:00","id":1431871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431866#post1431866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already gave an example: Life Veiling on a corpse to make it look alive. Purge Illness doesn't specify how it works, but I'd definitely allow it to affect non-living subject (corpses, foodstuff, etc). A Sheilding spell should definitely be able to prevent the spread of contagious diseases in both living and dead matter, or prevent decomposition based on biological processes. Food is even listed under the purview of Life, and most food tend to be dead long before it's considered food (or at least edible food).<br /> While Life is one of the most focused Arcana (up there with Spirit, poor Thyrsus), it does not necessarily have to be exclusively about the living, just like how Death definitely and demonstrably isn't exclusively about the dead.<br /> <br /> Edit: The name of an Arcanum reflects its themes, but it does not determine what's a valid subject for that Arcanum. No other Arcana works like that. Every spell has to be about Life in some way, but you can do that without a living subject. Compare to Space which is rarelt cast on an actual physical space rather than on a subject like an individual or an object. The nature of Life as an Arcanum makes spells on non-living subjects extremely rare, but that is no reason to believe it's a hard rule rather than a common consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if I'm understanding you right, you're saying Life can affect the undead so long as there's functional biology? So it could boost a Vampire using blush of life, or a Sin-Eater, because both have functioning biology even though they're not really &quot;alive&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T13:46:41-08:00","id":1431872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1431871#post1431871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I'm understanding you right, you're saying Life can affect the undead so long as there's functional biology? So it could boost a Vampire using blush of life, or a Sin-Eater, because both have functioning biology even though they're not really &quot;alive&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on what you do, yes. The vampire is obviously more limited since they're temporarily pushing a few biological functions, but the Bound is a fully functional biological individual, physically speaking. Like I've already posted, Knit (which heals by boosting a body's own capacity to heal itself) couldn't work on the vampire because natural healing is not something the vampire is capable of, not even under the effects of Blush of Health. But it most definitely should work on the Bound because their body does heal naturally and healing is listed within the purview of Life.<br /> That said, and I'm repeating myself yet again, the Bound is still metaphysically dead so any Life spell which depends on the subject being alive will simply not work at all. Meaning that Life-Force Assault does not work on the Bound because they literally have no &quot;life-force&quot; to assault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T13:42:38-08:00","id":1432247,"title":"","content":"Does the astral in 2e work the same way it does in 1e? Like do non-mind spells still have the effect they do in the astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T14:38:05-08:00","id":1432253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1432247#post1432247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the astral in 2e work the same way it does in 1e? Like do non-mind spells still have the effect they do in the astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Astral Realms proper are made of thoughts, emotions, and other ephemeral creations of the soul, but the Arcana affect their creations using the same rules as they do on the material realm. Matter affects visions of stone, for instance.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T14:44:06-08:00","id":1432254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1432253#post1432253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The Astral Realms proper are made of thoughts, emotions, and other ephemeral creations of the soul, but the Arcana affect their creations using the same rules as they do on the material realm. Matter affects visions of stone, for instance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So they do. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T10:34:08-08:00","id":1433166,"title":"","content":"Hello kids! Quick question. Can a 1st dot Mind Spell allow you to perceive and communicate with Goetias in Twilight? I'm not talking about adding Mind 1 to the Spirit 1 spell &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T14:32:18-08:00","id":1433182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433166#post1433166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello kids! Quick question. Can a 1st dot Mind Spell allow you to perceive and communicate with Goetias in Twilight? I'm not talking about adding Mind 1 to the Spirit 1 spell &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wondered about that. In practice I just let it work; didn't see any obvious reason to require Spirit 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T16:35:42-08:00","id":1433192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433166#post1433166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello kids! Quick question. Can a 1st dot Mind Spell allow you to perceive and communicate with Goetias in Twilight? I'm not talking about adding Mind 1 to the Spirit 1 spell &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, that's how I imagine it works. To look through twilight is a spirit arcanum thing to do mind just lets you focus on goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T04:25:01-08:00","id":1433249,"title":"","content":"Technically a general Chronicles question, but mage is the most likely game line where this issue might come up: Is there an official rule how to handle one effect Clashing against multiple defenses from the same character, like a spell clashing against multiple layers of Shielding or Veiling spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T05:54:10-08:00","id":1433251,"title":"","content":"Who would win a clash of wills between a newly Awakened mage using Pneuma and an Archmaster?<br /> <br /> Both templates say that they automatically win a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T06:33:39-08:00","id":1433253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433166#post1433166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello kids! Quick question. Can a 1st dot Mind Spell allow you to perceive and communicate with Goetias in Twilight? I'm not talking about adding Mind 1 to the Spirit 1 spell &quot;Exorcist's Eye&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding Mind 1 to Exorcist's Eye means you can see both Goetia and spirits in Twilight. The general consensus seems to be that all spells that can be extended from one type of ephemeral entity to the others can just be wholly replicated using only the Arcanum relevant to the type of entity you wish to affect. I.e. yes, you can just cast a Mind Unveiling spell to see Goetia in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433249#post1433249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically a general Chronicles question, but mage is the most likely game line where this issue might come up: Is there an official rule how to handle one effect Clashing against multiple defenses from the same character, like a spell clashing against multiple layers of Shielding or Veiling spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no specific rules for handling stacked Clashes of Wills. So technically, if all spells are part of the same conflict, just roll for everyone and the winner has their effect take place. If there are multiple different conflicts, resolve them separately. I.e. if there's both a Shielding spell that would nullify incoming spells of a certain type as well as a Veiling spell that would provide false information, they create two different Clashes of Wills if a Knowing/Unveiling spell is cast that would trigger both protections. If the first CoW is won, then no information is gained at all. If the first CoW is lost but the second CoW is won, then false information is gained. Which is why you couldn't condense it to a single roll because the Shielding and the Veiling spells don't do the same thing and aren't in conflict with each other.<br /> <br /> However, <i>spells</i> have specific rules for stacking. As such, you generally can't end up in the first situation. When two different spells does the same thing, only the spell with the highest Potency is applied, meaning the attacker only has to win over a single opponent in the contested roll-off. Only if one of the protections comes from a non-spell source would you end up having to roll against multiple opponents like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433251#post1433251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would win a clash of wills between a newly Awakened mage using Pneuma and an Archmaster?<br /> <br /> Both templates say that they automatically win a clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider both to be one tier above, allowing them to win against all &quot;lesser&quot; beings but not to those on the same tier. In practice, however, the Archmaster will basically always win because their minimum dice pool is greater than the maximum dice pool a newly Awakened can scrape together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-24-2021, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T12:28:36-08:00","id":1433287,"title":"","content":"I think they'd just Clash - same as two archmasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T17:18:55-08:00","id":1433434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433287#post1433287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they'd just Clash - same as two archmasters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So archmasters don't have to spend mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T18:36:20-08:00","id":1433446,"title":"","content":"Hello all, if ascension takes both body and soul into the supernal, then is a wending sort of like a soul sarira?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12468,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","user":"Letalis","date":". 01-25-2021, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T19:03:49-08:00","id":1433447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433446#post1433446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, if ascension takes both body and soul into the supernal, then is a wending sort of like a soul sarira?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. A Sarira is solidified Resonance in the form of the Ascended character's body, whereas a Wending is the unstable remnants of an archmage's Golden Road, whether it was abandoned by their Ascension or their death. If there's a comparison to be made between them and anything, it's the abandoned Lustrums of Supernal gods cast down during the time of the Celestial Ladder, but most characters won't encounter those without tagging along with an archmaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T22:25:28-08:00","id":1433463,"title":"","content":"If the Golden Road is part of the Archmaster's soul, why is it not ascended? Is it only a portion of the soul (i.e. the oneiros and any reflection that they might have in the temenos) that is ascended? It seems odd that something so integral to the archmaster remains while something trivial like the physical body is drawn into the supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T22:49:23-08:00","id":1433464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433463#post1433463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Golden Road is part of the Archmaster's soul,</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not. It's the archmaster's connection to the Supernal, which runs <i>through</i> her soul just like the Astral Path she used to form through meditation, which is why Wendings are so much more fragile and unstable than an occupied Road is.<br /> <br /> Once they've Ascended, the Golden Road is basically vestigial; the thing you may be thinking of is the Cintamani, which serves as the Supernal endpoint of the Golden Road where the symbols of &quot;I'm an archmaster&quot; and later &quot;I'm Ascended&quot; live along with whatever their Noumenon was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T05:38:14-08:00","id":1433491,"title":"","content":"I feel as though archmasters of all people would not view the physical body as trivial; not when one looks at why they favour the term Phenomenal World over Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Souls require bodies to function, as the Supernal requires the Phenomenal to have meaning. This isn't straight Gnosticism where everything physical is profane and disgusting and the product of a faulty God; even mages regard the world as predating their demiurges, who employed other means of imprisoning humanity.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I think it is perfectly fitting for the entirety of the mage to Ascend (barring a shell of resonance and unnecessary Supernal connection).<br /> <br /> That and the element of Ascension kind of editing them out of the world, even if it was conceived as the soul being a seperable thing that floats off leaving the body behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T16:16:34-08:00","id":1433663,"title":"","content":"I suppose that my misunderstanding stems from that. I thought that the astral path (also golden road) was part of the awakened soul. Is the personal soul then just the oneiros? Which is then tethered to humanity's soul (temenos) and world soul (dreamtime) via the connection that is the astral path (golden road)?<br /> <br /> Edit: Just rechecked IM, as I remembered where I got that notion from. There, the Golden Road is described as being the inside of a transhuman soul on pg. 12.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12468,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","user":"Letalis","date":". 01-27-2021, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T23:07:53-08:00","id":1433684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1433663#post1433663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that my misunderstanding stems from that. I thought that the astral path (also golden road) was part of the awakened soul. Is the personal soul then just the oneiros? Which is then tethered to humanity's soul (temenos) and world soul (dreamtime) via the connection that is the astral path (golden road)?<br /> <br /> Edit: Just rechecked IM, as I remembered where I got that notion from. There, the Golden Road is described as being the inside of a transhuman soul on pg. 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>In truth, neither the Oneiros is the personal soul, if you remove a soul from someone the oneiros persists, but start to collapse.<br /> So we can say that personal souls are like oneiros foundations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T13:54:49-08:00","id":1434036,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your replies. Another question that has been bugging me is the love-hate relationship that many game lines in chronicles of darkness seem to have with level 6+ entities. I don't understand why they have &quot;stats&quot; explicitly mentioned (i.e. spirit rank goes from 1 - 10) but at the same time they (for the most part) seem to find it abhorrent to discuss any mechanics besides level for such beings. I realize that they should mostly be a vehicle for ST fiat, but why not give them a more skeletal framework to be fleshed out from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T14:20:21-08:00","id":1434043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1434036#post1434036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your replies. Another question that has been bugging me is the love-hate relationship that many game lines in chronicles of darkness seem to have with level 6+ entities. I don't understand why they have &amp;quot;stats&amp;quot; explicitly mentioned (i.e. spirit rank goes from 1 - 10) but at the same time they (for the most part) seem to find it abhorrent to discuss any mechanics besides level for such beings. I realize that they should mostly be a vehicle for ST fiat, but why not give them a more skeletal framework to be fleshed out from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're plot devices. Imperial Mysteries provides mechanics to use in their interaction with similarly powerful beings, but most of them just work through smaller-scale actors and do the occasional big unique miracle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T19:53:33-08:00","id":1434075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1434036#post1434036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why they have &amp;quot;stats&amp;quot; explicitly mentioned (i.e. spirit rank goes from 1 - 10)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think rank going that high is to just give a sense of hierarchy projecting upwards; a framework for how Firstborn is beneath Wolf is beneath Luna/Helios is beneath Gaia maybe is beneath God only knows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">at the same time they (for the most part) seem to find it abhorrent to discuss any mechanics besides level for such beings. I realize that they should mostly be a vehicle for ST fiat, but why not give them a more skeletal framework to be fleshed out from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one is running into a problem where stats might either undersell the thing or else be arbitrarily high enough that they might as well not be specified.<br /> <br /> Other than that, their narrative role is probably more suited to producing effects that create crisis in the story, rather than direct contest or affliction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key"