ks their souls. They have to roll for a Breaking Point and then suffer Quiescence. That is why The Sleeping Curse is insidious. You can believe in magic, know its real, but the raw Truth is too much for their soul to process.<br /> <br /> The way to make someone safe to be around magic is to use Stealing Fire with indefinite duration. But unless that was cast using a Legacy's Attainment, then there will always be the risk of it being dispelled (by rival mages, walking into an Ansho, having the Imago eaten by a resident of a Lower Depth, etc). When that happens, their sanity will shatter like a fine thread of glass, which can be devastating if they saw a lot of supernatural phenomena. Best case scenario, you end up with a babbling maniac. Worst case scenario, maybe they could become Slashers or even Banishers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a lot mate. That's what I was hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T03:55:31-08:00","id":1434674,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know how the Piercing Glance Merit from Signs of Sorcery works?<br /> Does the character have to actively use it, or does it passively trigger if a concealing effect is in the vicinity?<br /> <br /> Edit: also, if it has to be actively used, I assume the character chooses which arcanum to roll with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T04:18:45-08:00","id":1434677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1434674#post1434674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how the Piercing Glance Merit from Signs of Sorcery works?<br /> Does the character have to actively use it, or does it passively trigger if a concealing effect is in the vicinity?<br /> <br /> Edit: also, if it has to be actively used, I assume the character chooses which arcanum to roll with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it s the second one, if the charachter was supposed to use it actively it would be no more useful than turning on active mage sight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T08:27:16-08:00","id":1434688,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to use Temporal Sympathy with Shifting Sands to target the moments you want to rewrite without using multiple rewind Reaches ? I always thought it was curious to use Reaches instead, since being limited to [Potency] turns means you have very little ways to deal 